E["npc:anduin-wrynn"] = {t="npc",n="Anduin Wrynn",z="multi",s="Stormwind's throne rests with ten-year-old Anduin Wrynn while his father, King Varian Wrynn, is missing. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the royal court bear the work of governing.",h="Stormwind's throne rests with ten-year-old Anduin Wrynn while his father, King Varian Wrynn, is missing.",sec={{t="A Boy on the Throne",b="Anduin Wrynn was born in the peace after the Second War. His name honors his grandfather, King Llane, and Sir Anduin Lothar, the legendary knight. When King Varian Wrynn vanished on the way to a diplomatic summit in Theramore, Anduin was crowned to keep the kingdom steady. Clever and compassionate, he is still only ten and has little say in affairs of state. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and royal councilor Lady Katrana Prestor share the work of ruling the realm.",sp=0},{t="A Pawn in the Court",b="Stormwind Keep holds Anduin as tension grows at court. Highlord Bolvar watches over the kingdom's defenses and works to keep it whole. Lady Katrana Prestor presses her counsel upon the court and undermines troop deployments to outlying human settlements. Anduin feels how fragile his court has become and longs for his father. For now, nobles with designs of their own and guardians surround the young king.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a child ruling Stormwind?",a="King Varian Wrynn vanished under mysterious circumstances while sailing to a diplomatic summit in Theramore. To prevent a succession crisis and preserve order across the realm, ten-year-old Prince Anduin was crowned king, and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon was named regent to govern in his place.",al={"why is anduin king","where is varian","who is the kid king"},sp=1},{q="Who actually runs the kingdom right now?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is Regent of Stormwind. He commands the realm's armies and holds executive power until Anduin comes of age. Lady Katrana Prestor is a senior advisor whose influence reaches deep into the royal court and the House of Nobles.",al={"who rules stormwind","who is in charge","stormwind regent"}},{q="Who is Anduin named after?",a="Anduin's name honors two heroes of Stormwind's history: his grandfather, the fallen King Llane Wrynn, and Sir Anduin Lothar, the Lion of Azeroth who led the Alliance during the First and Second Wars.",al={"anduin name origin","anduin namesake","why named anduin"}},{q="Where is Anduin located in the city?",a="King Anduin sits on the royal throne in the throne room of Stormwind Keep. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and Lady Katrana Prestor are close beside him.",al={"where is anduin","anduin location","anduin wrynn location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="To Alliance citizens and soldiers, King Anduin is an innocent emblem of the realm's resilience. Many fear his youth leaves the throne open to court intrigue.",["race:Human"]="For Stormwind's people, the boy-king keeps the Wrynn dynasty alive while his father, Varian, is missing."},kw={"anduin","bolvar","boy-king","prestor","prince","stormwind","throne room","wrynn"},rel={"subzone:stormwind-keep","npc:bolvar-fordragon","topic:varian-wrynn","npc:onyxia","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:1431"},src={"Anduin Wrynn"}}
E["npc:blanchy"] = {t="npc",n="Blanchy",z="multi",s="Near the Jansen Stead, Blanchy rests beside the Furlbrows’ wagon in Westfall. The gentle mare travels through the troubled countryside with Theodore and Verna Furlbrow.",h="Near the Jansen Stead, Blanchy rests beside the Furlbrows’ wagon in Westfall.",sec={{t="A Faithful Farmhand",b="Before Blanchy drew the Furlbrows’ wagon through Westfall, she worked their farm in Stormwind’s breadbasket. She was sweet-tempered and known for behaving well. Years of hard labor have worn her down, and the journey away from troubled homesteads has left her exhausted. Yet her appetite remains hearty. Verna offers Blanchy’s treasured blanket and feed pouch to travelers who bring nourishing handfuls of oats from nearby fields.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns Blanchy?",a="Theodore and Verna Furlbrow own Blanchy, and they travel through Westfall. She is their draft horse and beloved companion.",al={"blanchy owner","who does blanchy belong to","furlbrow horse"}},{q="Where did Blanchy originally come from?",a="No record tells where Blanchy was foaled. As far as anyone in Westfall knows, she has long belonged to the Furlbrows and worked their farm until the family had to take to the road.",al={"blanchy origins","where is blanchy from","young blanchy"}},{q="Why does Verna Furlbrow need oats for Blanchy?",a="Years of labor and the long journey along Westfall’s dangerous roads have drained Old Blanchy. Verna asks travelers to gather the remaining bags of oats from nearby farmlands to restore the horse’s strength.",al={"blanchy oats","why feed blanchy","furlbrows horse tired"}},{q="Where can Blanchy be found?",a="Old Blanchy stands hitched beside the Furlbrow wagon along the main road near the Jansen Stead in northern Westfall.",al={"blanchy location","where is old blanchy","blanchy map"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler heading south from Elwynn Forest into Westfall, you may help feed Old Blanchy among your first acts of kindness for the struggling local refugees."},kw={"blanchy","furlbrow","jansen stead","oats","old blanchy","verna furlbrow","westfall"},rel={"npc:verna-furlbrow","subzone:jansen-stead","zone:westfall"},src={"Blanchy"}}
E["quest:1048"] = {t="quest",n="Into The Scarlet Monastery",z="general",s="Varimathras in the Undercity asks you to strike at Scarlet leaders and champions. Their defeat matters enough that he expects you to report back.",h="Varimathras in the Undercity asks you to strike at Scarlet leaders and champions.",sec={{t="A Report for Varimathras",b="Varimathras sends you against five Scarlet figures: High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion, and Houndmaster Loksey. Once they are slain, you are to report back to him in the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this assignment?",a="Varimathras gives it and expects you to report back to him in the Undercity.",al={"who sent me","varimathras task"}},{q="Who am I supposed to defeat?",a="The named targets are High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion, and Houndmaster Loksey.",al={"who to kill","scarlet targets"}},{q="Where do I report back?",a="Report back to Varimathras in the Undercity.",al={"report to varimathras","where to return"}}},kw={"herod","houndmaster loksey","mograine","scarlet","scarlet champion","scarlet monastery","undercity","varimathras","whitemane"},rel={"zone:undercity","npc:varimathras","npc:houndmaster-loksey","npc:herod","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine"},m={id=1048},src={"In-game quest text: Into The Scarlet Monastery"},fv=true}
E["quest:1050"] = {t="quest",n="Mythology of the Titans",z="general",s="In Ironforge, Librarian Mae Paledust seeks Mythology of the Titans, a book said to have rested in Tirisfal's old Monastery. Its study may show what the past can teach about the unknown ahead.",h="In Ironforge, Librarian Mae Paledust seeks Mythology of the Titans, a book said to have rested in Tirisfal's...",sec={{t="A Lost Volume",b="Before trouble came to Lordaeron, the old Monastery in Tirisfal Glades kept a library of knowledge. Mae asks you to bring her a book called Mythology of the Titans. It is said to be there, and she hopes its study will uncover secrets of the past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the book?",a="Librarian Mae Paledust in Ironforge asks you to bring her Mythology of the Titans.",al={"who wants it","Mae Paledust book","librarian Mae"}},{q="Where is Mythology of the Titans said to be?",a="The book is rumored to be in the library of the old Monastery in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where book","monastery book","titan book location"}},{q="What is Mythology of the Titans?",a="Mythology of the Titans is a book said to have been kept in the old Monastery's library in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what's the book","titan mythology","mythology book"}},{q="Why does Mae want the book?",a="Mae hopes studying the book may reveal secrets of the past and help prepare for the unknown.",al={"why get it","why Mae needs it","what's it for"}}},kw={"book","ironforge","librarian mae paledust","mae paledust","mythology of the titans","old monastery","tirisfal glades","titans"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:ironforge","subzone:library-ironforge","topic:titan","topic:lordaeron"},m={id=1050},src={"In-game quest text: Mythology of the Titans"},fv=true}
E["quest:106"] = {t="quest",n="Young Lovers",z="general",s="Maybell Maclure loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, though their families are bitter rivals. She asks you to carry her letter to him by the river.",h="Maybell Maclure loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, though their families are bitter rivals.",sec={{t="A Forbidden Romance",b="The Stonefields and the Maclures have held their grudge for years in southern Elwynn's farm country. Maybell cannot visit Tommy Joe without stirring her family's anger. So she trusts travelers to carry her letters across the line between the two farms.",sp=0},{t="The Riverbank Rendezvous",b="Tommy Joe stays beyond his relatives' sight on the quiet riverbank just west of Stonefield Farm. A letter from Maybell brings relief and fresh longing. Being apart grows more than he can bear, and the pair begin seeking ways to meet in secret.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Young Lovers?",a="Maybell Maclure gives it at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. She loves Tommy Joe Stonefield, but their families are bitter rivals, so they cannot meet openly.",al={"who gives young lovers","who starts young lovers","young lovers questgiver"}},{q="Where can Tommy Joe Stonefield be found?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield waits on the riverbank just west of Stonefield Farm, which lies due west of the Maclure Vineyards. There he stays out of his family's sight.",al={"where is tommy joe stonefield","find tommy joe","tommy joe location"}},{q="Why are Maybell and Tommy Joe kept apart?",a="The Stonefields and the Maclures have held a grudge against each other for years. Neither family lets its children mix, so the young couple writes secret letters.",al={"why are families fighting","stonefield maclure feud","why can't maybell and tommy joe see each other"}},{q="What item do you deliver during this quest?",a="You carry Maybell's Love Letter to Tommy Joe Stonefield at the river. It tells him of her affection and devotion, feud or no feud.",al={"what is maybell's letter","what do you deliver in young lovers","love letter elwynn"}},{q="How does Tommy Joe react to the letter?",a="Tommy Joe is thrilled and calls Maybell the light of his dull life. Her words make being apart more than he can bear, so he begins looking for a way for them to meet.",al={"how does tommy joe react","tommy joe response","what happens when you deliver the letter"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The story unfolds in southern Elwynn Forest, between the Maclure Vineyards and the river by Stonefield Farm. This quiet farming corner of the human kingdom is troubled by a petty family quarrel.",al={"where does young lovers take place","young lovers zone","stonefield farm location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member passing through Elwynn, you may carry messages between the feuding Stonefields and Maclures. Even with the kingdom in danger, small heartaches go on.",["race:Human"]="As a human who knows Elwynn, you have heard of the old grudge between the Stonefields and the Maclures. Maybell and Tommy Joe's romance is a delicate scandal among the neighbors."},kw={"elwynn forest","feud","love letter","maclure vineyards","maybell maclure","stonefield farm","tommy joe stonefield","young lovers"},rel={"npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","subzone:stonefield-farm"},m={id=106},src={"In-game quest text: Young Lovers"},fv=true}
E["quest:107"] = {t="quest",n="Note to William",z="general",s="In southern Elwynn, Mildred asks William Pestle to help two young lovers. Her note travels to the apothecary in Goldshire, where she hopes he can help Maybell and Tommy Joe unite despite their families’ feud.",h="In southern Elwynn, Mildred asks William Pestle to help two young lovers.",sec={{t="Star-Crossed in Elwynn",b="Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure hide their love from their feuding families. The Stonefields and Maclures have lived as neighbors in southern Elwynn Forest for years. Yet their bitter rivalry makes even ordinary relations difficult. Gramma Mildred Stonefield pities the young lovers and seeks another way to bring them together.",sp=0},{t="An Appeal to Goldshire",b="Mildred sends a courier north to the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where William Pestle works as an alchemist and apothecary. She has known him for many years, and believes persuasion alone cannot sway the feuding families. Her message asks for his help. When William receives it, Maybell and Tommy Joe's plight moves him, and he resolves to use his alchemical knowledge on their behalf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is William Pestle?",a="William Pestle is an alchemist and apothecary at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. He has known Gramma Mildred Stonefield for many years and makes herbal remedies and specialized draughts.",al={"who is william pestle","william pestle goldshire","alchemist goldshire"}},{q="Who sent the note to William?",a="Gramma Mildred Stonefield wrote the note and sent it to William Pestle. She hopes he can find a way to help Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who sent note","gramma stonefield note","mildred stonefield"}},{q="Why are Maybell and Tommy Joe unable to be together openly?",a="Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield love each other, but their families are locked in a bitter rivalry that has lasted for years. Gramma Stonefield hopes William Pestle can find a potion or plan to help them be together despite that hostility.",al={"why help maybell and tommy joe","young lovers quest elwynn","stonefield maclure feud"}},{q="Where can William Pestle be found?",a="William Pestle stays at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, a town in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where is william pestle","pestle location","lion's pride inn alchemist"}},{q="What is Gramma Stonefield's real name?",a="Her first name is Mildred. William Pestle says he has not seen Mildred in years when he receives her letter.",al={"what is gramma stonefield first name","gramma stonefield name"}},{q="How does William Pestle react to the note?",a="William says he has not seen Mildred in years, then wonders what her note has to say. She hopes his alchemical craft can help the young lovers.",al={"what does william do with note","william pestle reaction"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in Elwynn Forest, you may help local farming families with personal troubles while the guards focus on military threats.",["race:Human"]="As a human in Elwynn, you see how the Stonefield and Maclure feud divides neighbors. Sympathetic elders rely on discreet couriers."},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","gramma stonefield","lion's pride inn","maybell maclure","mildred stonefield","note to william","tommy joe stonefield","william pestle"},rel={"npc:william-pestle","npc:gramma-stonefield","quest:106","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn","subzone:goldshire"},m={id=107},src={"In-game quest text: Note to William"},fv=true}
E["quest:1109"] = {t="quest",n="Going, Going, Guano!",z="general",s="Master Apothecary Faranell seeks guano from the Kraul Bats of Razorfen Kraul. The Royal Apothecary Society needs it for its experiments.",h="Master Apothecary Faranell seeks guano from the Kraul Bats of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="A Rare Substance",b="Master Apothecary Faranell oversees the Royal Apothecary Society’s alchemical work in the Undercity. He needs guano from Kraul Bats, a rare species found in Razorfen Kraul. You are asked to bring him a pile so the Society can begin its work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who needs Kraul Guano?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell of the Royal Apothecary Society needs it for the Society’s work.",al={"who wants guano","faranell guano","apothecary guy"}},{q="Where do Kraul Bats live?",a="Kraul Bats are found in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"kraul bats location","where bats","bat guano"}},{q="What is Kraul Guano for?",a="Faranell needs it so the Royal Apothecary Society can begin its alchemical work.",al={"why guano","what's guano for","apothecary experiments"}},{q="Where do I bring the guano?",a="Bring the pile of Kraul Guano to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",al={"where bring guano","deliver guano","faranell location"}}},kw={"going going guano","kraul bats","kraul guano","master apothecary faranell","razorfen kraul","royal apothecary society","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:razorfenkraul","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:razorfen"},m={id=1109},src={"In-game quest text: Going, Going, Guano!"},fv=true}
E["quest:1113"] = {t="quest",n="Hearts of Zeal",z="general",s="Master Apothecary Faranell needs Hearts of Zeal for a dangerous experiment. He asks you to gather them from Scarlet Crusade disciples at the Scarlet Monastery.",h="Master Apothecary Faranell needs Hearts of Zeal for a dangerous experiment.",sec={{t="Faranell's Experiment",b="Faranell seeks a rare kind of guano for his experiment in the Undercity. He plans to combine opposing chemical substances with a toxic agent. At the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, you are to bring him the zealous hearts of the Scarlet Crusade's disciples.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the Hearts of Zeal?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity wants the Hearts of Zeal for an experiment.",al={"who wants hearts","Faranell hearts"}},{q="Where are the Scarlet Crusade disciples?",a="The disciples gather at the Scarlet Monastery in the northeastern peaks of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where find disciples","Scarlet Monastery hearts"}},{q="What does Faranell plan to do with the hearts?",a="Faranell is conducting an experiment with opposing chemical substances and a toxic agent, and wants the zealous hearts.",al={"why hearts of zeal","what's Faranell making"}},{q="How many Hearts of Zeal does Faranell need?",a="Faranell asks for twenty Hearts of Zeal.",al={"how many hearts","heart count"}}},kw={"experiment","hearts of zeal","master apothecary faranell","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:381"},m={id=1113},src={"In-game quest text: Hearts of Zeal"},fv=true}
E["quest:1136"] = {t="quest",n="Frostmaw",z="general",s="In the Alterac Mountains, a rare yeti hunt calls you far from home. Melor Stonehoof sends you after Frostmaw and awaits his mane in Thunder Bluff.",h="In the Alterac Mountains, a rare yeti hunt calls you far from home.",sec={{t="A Distant Hunt",b="Melor Stonehoof sends you far from home to hunt Frostmaw in the Alterac Mountains. The yeti’s white coat blends with the mountain snow, and he rarely shows himself. Melor gives you a scroll explaining how to lure him. Bring Frostmaw’s mane back to Melor in Thunder Bluff, and your journey will be complete.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Frostmaw?",a="Frostmaw is a yeti in the Alterac Mountains. His white coat blends with the snow, and he rarely appears.",al={"frostmaw who","what is frostmaw"}},{q="Where can I find Frostmaw?",a="You can find Frostmaw in the Alterac Mountains, where his white coat blends with the snow.",al={"frostmaw location","where is frostmaw"}},{q="How do I lure Frostmaw?",a="Melor Stonehoof gives you a scroll with instructions for luring Frostmaw.",al={"lure frostmaw","frostmaw scroll"}},{q="What does Melor want from Frostmaw?",a="Melor Stonehoof asks you to bring Frostmaw’s mane to him in Thunder Bluff.",al={"melor frostmaw","frostmaw mane"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","frostmaw","mane","melor stonehoof","scroll","thunder bluff","yeti"},rel={"npc:melor-stonehoof","zone:alterac","zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=1136},src={"In-game quest text: Frostmaw"},fv=true}
E["quest:1164"] = {t="quest",n="To Steal From Thieves",z="general",s="Genavie Callow in Undercity asks you to confront the Dabyrie family at their farmstead in Arathi. Her grievance turns a dispute over stolen belongings into a demand for vengeance.",h="Genavie Callow in Undercity asks you to confront the Dabyrie family at their farmstead in Arathi.",sec={{t="A Bitter Grievance",b="Genavie Callow says the plague took her family and the war left her estate looted and burned. She accuses Kenata and her children of taking the few belongings she still treasured. Now she asks you to bring her the heads of Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie from the Dabyrie Farmstead in Arathi.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Genavie Callow in Undercity asks you to bring her the heads of Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie.",al={"who gave this","who wants this","genavie"}},{q="Why is Genavie angry at the Dabyries?",a="Genavie says the plague took her family, the war cost her estate, and the Dabyries stole the belongings she had left.",al={"why mad at them","genavie grievance","dabyrie trouble"}},{q="Where is the Dabyrie Farmstead?",a="The Dabyrie Farmstead is in Arathi, northeast of Refuge Point.",al={"dabyrie farm location","where is the farm","farmstead"}},{q="Who are Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie?",a="They are the three people Genavie names in her demand: Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie.",al={"who are dabyries","kenata family","dabyrie names"}}},kw={"arathi","dabyrie farmstead","fardel","genavie callow","kenata","marcel dabyrie","refuge point","to steal from thieves"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},m={id=1164},src={"In-game quest text: To Steal From Thieves"},fv=true}
E["quest:1248"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="You follow the trail of a kidnapped Stormwind diplomat to Menethil Harbor. An intercepted docket confirms the abduction but leaves the diplomat's identity and the conspirators' destination unknown.",h="You follow the trail of a kidnapped Stormwind diplomat to Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Trail to the Wetlands",b="You have a docket that confirms a diplomat was taken from Stormwind. It names neither the diplomat nor the conspirators' destination. So the trail leads beyond Stormwind's gates to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, where you can search among the harbor crowds and their secret dealings.",sp=0},{t="Discreet Contacts in Menethil",b="Mikhail, a former associate of Elling Trias, retired from Stormwind several years ago and now tends the tavern in Menethil. You seek him to find Slim, who may know where the captive was taken or who arranged the abduction.\n\nIn the crowded tavern, discretion matters. Mention Trias's name, and Mikhail urges immediate silence before the conspirators notice your inquiry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mikhail?",a="Mikhail was a former associate of Elling Trias who left Stormwind several years ago to retire in Menethil Harbor. He now works there as a bartender, and Trias points you to him as a trustworthy contact who can help find Slim.",al={"who is mikhail","mikhail wetlands","menethil bartender"}},{q="Who is Slim and why are they looking for him?",a="Slim is a figure in Menethil Harbor believed to know something about the kidnapped diplomat. Mikhail can help you find Slim and learn what they know.",al={"who is slim","find slim","missing diplomat slim"}},{q="Who is the kidnapped diplomat?",a="The kidnapped diplomat's identity remains uncertain, even to the investigators. The intercepted docket confirms the abduction but leaves out the diplomat's identity and the conspirators' plans after the capture.",al={"who was kidnapped","kidnapped diplomat identity","who is missing diplomat"}},{q="Why does the trail lead to Menethil Harbor?",a="The trail leads to Menethil Harbor because Elling Trias's retired contact Mikhail tends bar there. The harbor is a port town on the coast of the Wetlands, and leads about the abduction pass through it.",al={"where is menethil harbor","why wetlands","why go to menethil"}},{q="What does the docket reveal about the plot?",a="The intercepted docket confirms the diplomat's abduction but leaves out where the captive was taken and what the abductors intend to do next.",al={"what docket","trias docket","what does the docket say"}},{q="What is Trias's involvement in this mission?",a="Elling Trias directs the investigation from Stormwind. He sends you to Mikhail, his old associate, who promised to help on Trias's word alone and without drawing public attention.",al={"who sent us to mikhail","trias connection","why mention trias"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The kidnapped diplomat's abduction touches Stormwind's high-level security and reaches of conspirators across Alliance territories.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can draw on covert skills to unravel secret dockets, find retired contacts, and question suspects discreetly in crowded taverns."},kw={"docket","menethil harbor","mikhail","slim","stormwind","the missing diplomat","trias","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1248},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1249"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="Stormwind's envoy is missing, and you follow the trail from the capital to Menethil Harbor. There, the inquiry crosses paths with underworld figures and operatives tied to Stormwind's intelligence network.",h="Stormwind's envoy is missing, and you follow the trail from the capital to Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Undercurrents in Menethil Harbor",b="You follow the missing Stormwind envoy's trail north to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Its docks and taverns hide shady dealers and covert runners, all working under the local guard's nose. To follow the leads through this port, you must deal with people who know the darker side of Alliance territory.",sp=0},{t="A Familiar Rogue",b="Catching Slim brings a sudden answer to the search. Local informants are surprised to learn he was entangled in the affair. His capture gives you critical answers, but it also stirs old memories for retired operatives in the Wetlands. They must weigh helping the Crown against being drawn back into Stormwind's underworld schemes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Slim?",a="Slim is a shady contact in Menethil Harbor whom you catch during the search for the missing diplomat. Local contacts are surprised to learn he was involved.",al={"who is slim","slim missing diplomat","caught slim"}},{q="Who is Elling?",a="Elling Trias is an influential figure in Stormwind City who keeps an underground network of former rogues and informants across Alliance lands.",al={"elling trias","who is elling","elling stormwind"}},{q="Where does this part of the investigation take place?",a="You follow this part of the investigation in Menethil Harbor, a Wetlands port connecting Ironforge to distant shores and Stormwind trade routes.",al={"where does this happen","menethil harbor missing diplomat","wetlands diplomat"}},{q="What is the Missing Diplomat quest chain about?",a="You investigate the disappearance of an important Stormwind envoy, following covert operatives, conspirators, and underworld contacts across the kingdom and beyond.",al={"what is the missing diplomat","missing diplomat quest","who is missing"}},{q="Why does the contact warn against mentioning this to Elling?",a="A Menethil Harbor contact once worked with Elling Trias in Stormwind's underground circles. He avoids telling Elling that he misses the old life, for fear Elling will summon him back to the capital.",al={"why is elling mentioned","trias cheese","elling trias connection"}},{q="What happened with the investigation in Menethil Harbor?",a="You follow leads to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and catch Slim. The encounter confirms local suspicions about illicit underground activity in town.",al={"what happened in menethil harbor","menethil lead","slim caught"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you follow the missing diplomat's trail into an underworld linking Stormwind's political circles to the Wetlands docks.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know that operatives and handlers like Elling Trias rely on quiet legwork and street contacts to find those who slip through the cracks."},kw={"elling trias","menethil harbor","missing diplomat","slim","stormwind","the missing diplomat","wetlands"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1249},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1250"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="Jahn says the Defias took the king from his ship while it lay moored. You are sent to Mikhail in the Wetlands as the search for Hendel continues.",h="Jahn says the Defias took the king from his ship while it lay moored.",sec={{t="A Witness Speaks",b="Jahn says the Defias put a man named Hendel aboard the king's ship while it was moored. The king was bound for Theramore to meet Jaina Proudmoore. Jahn believes the Defias worked with someone else, so you are asked to speak with Mikhail in the Wetlands as the search for Hendel begins.",sp=0},{t="Mikhail's Response",b="Mikhail is startled to hear the king is missing and sends word to Elling. Jahn, he says, was never someone he expected to betray Stormwind for coin. Still, Mikhail offers help finding Hendel.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jahn?",a="Jahn is a Defias conspirator who helped put Hendel aboard the king's ship.",al={"jahn who","who is jahn","defias jahn"}},{q="Who is Hendel?",a="Hendel is the man Jahn says he placed aboard the king's ship.",al={"hendel guy","who's hendel","king ship man"}},{q="What happened to the king?",a="Jahn says the Defias took the king from his ship while it was moored.",al={"where king","stormwind king missing","king kidnapped"}},{q="Why was the king going to Theramore?",a="The king was on his way to Theramore to meet Jaina Proudmoore.",al={"king theramore","jaina meeting","why theramore"}},{q="Who does Jahn say is involved besides the Defias?",a="Jahn believes the Defias worked with someone else, but says he does not know who.",al={"who working with defias","defias partner","who else involved"}},{q="Who is Mikhail?",a="Mikhail is the person you are asked to speak with in the Wetlands. He offers help finding Hendel.",al={"mikhail wetlands","who mikhail","talk to mikhail"}}},kw={"defias","hendel","jahn","jaina proudmoore","mikhail","stormwind king","the missing diplomat","theramore","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:rogue"},m={id=1250},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1264"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="A tavern keeper sends you to Commander Samaul in Theramore, where Hendel may still be stationed.",h="A tavern keeper sends you to Commander Samaul in Theramore, where Hendel may still be stationed.",sec={{t="A Lead in Theramore",b="The tavern keeper believes Hendel is among the Kul Tiras Marines who visit regularly. They are paid at the beginning of each month and usually leave Theramore afterward. Commander Samaul may know if Hendel is still stationed there. Mention Elling's name, and Samaul may help discreetly.",sp=0},{t="Samaul's Warning",b="Commander Samaul is the officer in charge of Miss Proudmoore's forces in Theramore. He is busy, but offers to answer your questions. The marsh beyond the city holds ogres, orcs and murlocs. Black dragons dwell in its southern reaches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hendel?",a="Hendel is a Kul Tiras Marine who may be among the regular visitors to a tavern. The tavern keeper thinks Commander Samaul in Theramore may know if Hendel is still stationed there.",al={"hendel","marine Hendel","who's Hendel"}},{q="Who is Commander Samaul?",a="Commander Samaul is in charge of Miss Proudmoore's forces in Theramore.",al={"Samaul","commander guy","Theramore commander"}},{q="Why am I looking for Samaul?",a="The tavern keeper believes Samaul may help you find Hendel if Hendel is still stationed in Theramore.",al={"find Samaul","why Samaul","missing diplomat quest"}},{q="Who is Elling?",a="The tavern keeper advises you to mention Elling's name when you ask Commander Samaul about Hendel.",al={"Elling","drop Elling's name","Elling name"}},{q="When do the Kul Tiras Marines leave Theramore?",a="The Kul Tiras Marines are paid at the beginning of each month and usually leave Theramore afterward.",al={"Marines leave","payday","when do they go"}},{q="What dangers does Samaul mention?",a="Samaul warns of ogres, orcs and murlocs in the marsh beyond the city, and black dragons in its southern reaches.",al={"Theramore dangers","what's in the swamp","marsh threats"}}},kw={"black dragons","commander samaul","dustwallow marsh","elling","hendel","kul tiras marines","miss proudmoore","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:kul-tiras","topic:murloc"},m={id=1264},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1265"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="Elling sends you to find Private Hendel, and a local officer fears the reason may be troubling. Hendel was stationed at Sentry Point, the first tower outside Theramore, where you are asked to seek signs of him.",h="Elling sends you to find Private Hendel, and a local officer fears the reason may be troubling.",sec={{t="At the Tower",b="A local officer knows Private Hendel and says he was stationed at Sentry Point, the first tower outside Theramore. The officer fears Elling sent you there first because your business may be troubling. Tell the officer what you can share. The watch must protect these lands, so any disturbance matters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Private Hendel?",a="Private Hendel is the man Elling sent you to find. A local officer says Hendel was stationed at the first tower outside Theramore.",al={"private hendel","hendel who","hendel backstory"}},{q="Where should I look for Hendel?",a="Look for signs of Private Hendel at Sentry Point, the first tower outside Theramore.",al={"hendel location","where hendel","sentry point hendel"}},{q="Who sent me to find Hendel?",a="Elling sent you to find Private Hendel.",al={"who sent me","elling hendel","hendel search"}},{q="Why is the officer concerned?",a="The officer fears Elling sent you there first because your business may be troubling. The officer wants to know what you can share to protect the lands.",al={"why concerned","officer worried","what's troubling"}}},kw={"elling","hendel","officer","private hendel","sentry point","theramore","tower"},rel={"subzone:sentry-point"},m={id=1265},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1266"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Diplomat",z="general",s="Theramore's people are watching Brackenwall and other dangers near their borders. You are sent west through Dustwallow Marsh to find Private Hendel.",h="Theramore's people are watching Brackenwall and other dangers near their borders.",sec={{t="West Along the Road",b="A guard detail waits west of you in Dustwallow Marsh, where Private Hendel watches over Theramore's infiltrators. They have been observing Brackenwall and searching for other threats near the borders. Look for the tents along the road to find Hendel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Private Hendel?",a="Private Hendel is on guard duty, protecting Theramore's infiltrators while they rest.",al={"private hendel","hendel who","who is hendel"}},{q="What are the infiltrators watching?",a="They have been keeping tabs on Brackenwall, the Horde base, and looking for other threats to Theramore's borders.",al={"what are they watching","brackenwall watch","infiltrators"}},{q="Where can I find Private Hendel?",a="Private Hendel is west of you, by the tents along the road in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where hendel","find hendel","hendel location"}},{q="Why are the infiltrators there?",a="They are watching Brackenwall and looking for other dangers near Theramore's borders.",al={"why infiltrators","theramore spies","what are they doing"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you are sent to find a Theramore guard watching the Horde base at Brackenwall and other threats to the borders."},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow marsh","horde base","infiltrators","private hendel","the missing diplomat","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:horde"},m={id=1266},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Diplomat"},fv=true}
E["quest:1302"] = {t="quest",n="James Hyal",z="general",s="Across the Great Sea, James Hyal's family waits for word from Kalimdor. He sailed there with Lady Jaina Proudmoore's expedition and set out to open an inn on the frontier. Now his family looks to Theramore's records for news.",h="Across the Great Sea, James Hyal's family waits for word from Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Across the Great Sea",b="During the Third War, many left their homes in the Eastern Kingdoms to follow Lady Jaina Proudmoore across the Great Sea. James Hyal went with them, known at home for his gift in the kitchen. After the fighting ended and Theramore Isle was founded, he sought a living on Kalimdor. He planned to open an inn for travelers and fellow settlers.",sp=0},{t="In Search of a Brother",b="Back in the Eastern Kingdoms, James's brother grows worried. No letters have come from across the sea, though he hopes James is busy running a roadside taproom. He asks travelers to seek his brother out. The search begins in Theramore, where Clerk Lendry keeps records of expedition members who have ventured into the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Hyal?",a="James Hyal is a human settler and gifted cook who crossed the Great Sea with Lady Jaina Proudmoore's expedition. After the fighting ended, he set out to make a living by opening an inn on Kalimdor.",al={"who is james hyal","james hyal lore","who is james"}},{q="Where can I find James Hyal?",a="James set out to open an inn somewhere on Kalimdor after arriving with Lady Proudmoore's expedition. His family has not heard from him recently, and Clerk Lendry in Theramore Isle keeps records that may give word of his whereabouts.",al={"where is james hyal","find james hyal","james hyal location"}},{q="Who is Clerk Lendry?",a="Clerk Lendry handles local records in Theramore Isle. Travelers seeking settlers such as James Hyal can ask Lendry to check those records.",al={"who is clerk lendry","clerk lendry location","theramore clerk"}},{q="Why did James travel to Kalimdor?",a="James sailed with Lady Jaina Proudmoore's expedition during the Third War, among those leaving the Eastern Kingdoms. After the fighting ended, he chose to stay on Kalimdor and open an inn for travelers and settlers.",al={"why did james go to kalimdor","james hyal expedition"}},{q="Who is looking for James Hyal?",a="James's brother in the Eastern Kingdoms is looking for him after receiving no word for some time. He remembers James as a fine cook and thinks he may be busy establishing his inn.",al={"who gives james hyal quest","who is james brother"}},{q="Is James Hyal in any danger?",a="James's brother thinks he may be occupied with his new business. His family has received no direct word from him for some time.",al={"is james hyal safe","what happened to james hyal"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="James sailed west with Lady Jaina Proudmoore during the Third War, and his family ties the Eastern Kingdoms to Theramore Isle across the Great Sea.",["profession:Cooking"]="James was known at home as a gifted cook. He went to Kalimdor to make a living running an inn and feeding travelers."},kw={"clerk lendry","cook","innkeeper","jaina proudmoore","james hyal","kalimdor","theramore"},m={id=1302},src={"In-game quest text: James Hyal"},fv=true}
E["quest:1434"] = {t="quest",n="Befouled by Satyr",z="general",s="Takata Steelblade in Desolace asks you to confront several kinds of Hatefury satyr. Their presence is the problem he needs you to address.",h="Takata Steelblade in Desolace asks you to confront several kinds of Hatefury satyr.",sec={{t="Takata's Request",b="Takata Steelblade asks for your help in Desolace. Hatefury Rogues, Felsworn, Betrayers, and Hellcallers are the satyr he names. He needs you to slay seven of each, then return to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for help with the Hatefury satyr?",a="Takata Steelblade asks you to confront the Hatefury satyr in Desolace.",al={"who is Takata","Takata Steelblade"}},{q="Which Hatefury satyr does Takata name?",a="Takata names Hatefury Rogues, Felsworn, Betrayers, and Hellcallers.",al={"Hatefury types","satyrs list"}},{q="How many of each kind does Takata ask you to slay?",a="Takata asks you to slay seven of each kind he names.",al={"how many satyrs","number of each"}},{q="Where do you return after dealing with the satyr?",a="Takata asks you to return to him in Desolace.",al={"where to go back","return to Takata"}}},kw={"befouled by satyr","betrayer","desolace","felsworn","hatefury","hellcaller","rogue","satyr","takata steelblade"},rel={"npc:takata-steelblade","zone:desolace","topic:rogue"},m={id=1434},src={"In-game quest text: Befouled by Satyr"},fv=true}
E["quest:1505"] = {t="quest",n="Veteran Uzzek",z="general",s="Just south of Far Watch Post, recruits turn to Veteran Uzzek for lessons in combat. His years of experience teach young Horde warriors that strength calls for discipline and study.",h="Just south of Far Watch Post, recruits turn to Veteran Uzzek for lessons in combat.",sec={{t="The Path of the Warrior",b="Strength alone cannot make a Horde warrior a champion. The finest fighters stay humble students of their craft. Through discipline and study, they sharpen their instincts. Young warriors ready to pass beyond basic training seek veterans who have survived the trials of war.",sp=0},{t="The Veteran at the Border",b="Between Durotar and the Barrens, young fighters seek deeper guidance in combat. Far Watch Post watches the eastern frontier. Just south of the orc garrison, Veteran Uzzek teaches promising recruits combat and survival tactics. He has endured countless bloody conflicts and now guides the next generation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veteran Uzzek?",a="Near the Durotar and Barrens frontier, Veteran Uzzek teaches young Horde warriors combat. He shares lessons learned through countless conflicts from his camp.",al={"who is uzzek","uzzek lore","who is the veteran"}},{q="Where can Uzzek be found?",a="Uzzek is south of Far Watch Post, the orc garrison on the eastern border between Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"where is uzzek","uzzek location","find uzzek"}},{q="What is Far Watch Post?",a="Far Watch Post is an orc garrison on the Barrens' eastern frontier. It guards the crossing from Durotar and protects the Horde's border.",al={"what is the far watch post","far watch post purpose"}},{q="Why are young warriors sent to Uzzek?",a="Young warriors seek Uzzek for combat instruction. The Horde prizes strength, but its finest fighters also master discipline, study, and martial technique.",al={"why visit uzzek","what does uzzek teach","warrior instruction"}},{q="What does Uzzek say when you arrive?",a="Uzzek welcomes young warriors to his post. He is ready to assess their commitment and teach them the ways of war.",al={"what happens when you speak to uzzek","uzzek quest turn in"}},{q="How does the Horde view its warriors?",a="The Horde honors warriors for their strength and devotion to battle. Its traditions also teach that mastery takes discipline and learning from seasoned veterans.",al={"who honors warriors","horde warrior culture"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you learn from Uzzek that brute force is not enough. True strength comes from disciplined study of combat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you honor martial skill and rely on veteran fighters at frontier outposts to guide the next generation."},kw={"barrens","combat instruction","durotar","far watch post","horde","uzzek","veteran uzzek","warrior"},rel={"npc:uzzek","subzone:far-watch-post","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","topic:warrior","topic:horde"},m={id=1505},src={"In-game quest text: Veteran Uzzek"},fv=true}
E["quest:1519"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="The earth calls a shaman to begin a patient trial of communion. By accepting an earthen sapta, the seeker steps onto a path of spiritual rebirth and learns to hear the foundation of life.",h="The earth calls a shaman to begin a patient trial of communion.",sec={{t="The Foundation of All Things",b="A shaman learns to commune with the primal force of earth through a formative rite. Earth is the most stubborn and wise of the elements, the steady bedrock beneath existence. It moves through slow cycles of erosion and rebirth. Mountains wear into deserts, and rivers carve canyons over ages. To hear the earth's voice, an initiate needs that same patience.",sp=0},{t="The Sapta and Rebirth",b="Answering the call changes a seeker beyond return to former ignorance. When the initiate proves readiness and respect for the laws of the Earth Mother, they receive an earthen sapta. The elixir opens a new way of seeing, and the shaman begins to grasp earth's secrets of strength, stamina, and elemental protection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Earth?",a="Call of Earth tests an aspiring shaman's patience and readiness to commune with earth. The seeker must heed its enduring wisdom.",al={"what is call of earth","earth quest shaman","purpose of call of earth"}},{q="What does the earth element represent in shamanic tradition?",a="Earth is the foundation of all things, embodying strength, stamina, and patience. It is the most stubborn and wise element, teaching that all things erode and are reborn over time.",al={"what does earth represent","element of earth lore","earth meaning shaman"}},{q="What is a sapta?",a="A sapta is an elemental draught prepared by a shaman mentor. Accepting it opens a spiritual path and attunes the seeker's senses to elemental spirits.",al={"what is a sapta","earth sapta","what does sapta do"}},{q="Who is the Earth Mother mentioned in the trial?",a="The Earth Mother is the source of life and balance, especially revered by tauren shamans. She protects those who honor her laws and grants wisdom to seekers who respect the land.",al={"who is earth mother","earth mother lore","earth mother connection"}},{q="What happens upon answering the call?",a="Answering the call prepares the seeker for the next step of their path. It brings spiritual rebirth, after which a shaman cannot return to ignorance and new secrets of earth come into view.",al={"what happens when you complete it","after call of earth","call of earth rebirth"}},{q="Why is patience required to commune with the earth?",a="Earth moves through cycles of erosion and rebirth. Mountains wear into deserts and rivers carve canyons, so a shaman needs patience and stamina to attune to these enduring rhythms.",al={"why does earth require patience","patience and earth"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, this rite marks a turning point in your training. Communion with earth brings strength, stamina, and deep spiritual insight.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, reverence for the Earth Mother lies at the heart of your culture. This trial honors beliefs held by your ancestors.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, your shamanic traditions draw on the elements. Your path begins with the grounded resilience of earth."},kw={"call of earth","earth mother","elements","patience","rebirth","sapta","shaman","stamina"},rel={"topic:earth-mother"},m={id=1519},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:1522"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="A shaman sees your strength in earth and sends you north to Kranal Fiss. There, you can learn the ways of fire.",h="A shaman sees your strength in earth and sends you north to Kranal Fiss.",sec={{t="Kranal Fiss",b="Kranal Fiss lives north of the Crossroads. The shaman says he is easy to find, but warns you not to go too far, lest you reach the elves' lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kranal Fiss?",a="Kranal Fiss is a shaman in the Barrens who can teach you the ways of fire.",al={"who's Kranal","Kranal"}},{q="Where can I find Kranal?",a="Kranal lives north of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"Kranal location","where's Kranal"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Kranal?",a="The shaman sees your strength in earth and believes you are ready to speak with Kranal, who can teach you the ways of fire.",al={"why Kranal","fire training"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you are sent to Kranal Fiss to learn the ways of fire after showing strength in earth."},kw={"barrens","call of fire","crossroads","earth","fire","kranal fiss","shaman"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads"},m={id=1522},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:1642"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Stormwind, The Tome of Divinity guides the first steps of paladin training. Its teachings call champions of the Holy Light to humility, compassion, and patience, not godhood or strength alone.",h="In Stormwind, The Tome of Divinity guides the first steps of paladin training.",sec={{t="The Nature of Divinity",b="The Tome of Divinity’s sacred texts teach paladin initiates what it means to serve the Light. Divinity means neither seeking godhood nor claiming rule over others. Instead, champions reflect the Light’s grace through pure intent and goodness in every deed. Paladins take up arms against evil, but strength without moral purpose means little. Their true distinction lies in how they treat ordinary people across Azeroth, keeping power bound to righteousness and humility.",sp=0},{t="Trials of Compassion and Patience",b="Scripture is only the beginning of a paladin’s service. After an initiate studies the Tome of Divinity, Duthorian Rall in Stormwind tests whether its lessons have taken root in the candidate’s heart and mind. The Light asks for more than the slaying of beasts. It calls for patience, bravery, and understanding.\n\nIn the city and the surrounding lands, people suffer and humble tasks go without glory. By aiding the less fortunate and comforting those in despair, an initiate proves they have the sound mind and selfless spirit to bear the Light’s blessings responsibly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of Divinity?",a="Paladins in Stormwind study the Tome of Divinity as a sacred guide to their calling. Its teachings reject godhood and personal glory, urging them to reflect the Holy Light through goodness, compassion, and patience.",al={"what is tome of divinity","tome of divinity quest","paladin tome of divinity"}},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a paladin leader in Stormwind who guides young paladins’ study of the Tome of Divinity. He oversees their spiritual and martial trials, testing their resolve through practical service to the kingdom and its people.",al={"who is duthorian rall","duthorian rall location","stormwind duthorian rall"}},{q="What virtues does the Tome of Divinity emphasize?",a="The Tome of Divinity teaches that compassion, patience, and bravery matter as much to a holy warrior as skill in combat. Paladins must smite wickedness, but their nobility lies in aiding the vulnerable and reflecting the Light’s benevolence.",al={"paladin virtues tome of divinity","what does the tome teach","virtues of the light"}},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall test aspiring paladins?",a="Duthorian Rall tests initiates to see whether they have truly taken the Tome of Divinity’s teachings to heart. They must show sound judgment and patience in serving the less fortunate, proving their devotion rests on service rather than pride.",al={"why does duthorian test paladins","duthorian rall trials","purpose of paladin trials"}},{q="Does the Tome of Divinity teach paladins to seek godhood?",a="No. The Tome of Divinity rejects the pursuit of godhood and teaches paladins to seek goodness in every deed. The Light grants them strength to protect and support others, not to place themselves above fellow mortals.",al={"do paladins seek godhood","strive for godhood paladin","meaning of divinity paladin"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The trials take place in the human kingdom of Stormwind. Initiates study the sacred teachings and report to Duthorian Rall in the city, then undertake trials of charity, patience, and valor through the streets and surrounding lands.",al={"where is the tome of divinity quest","tome of divinity stormwind location","where to turn in tome of divinity"}},{q="Why is patience so important for a paladin of the Light?",a="Patience shows that a holy warrior is disciplined, humble, and sound of mind. Serving the downtrodden often means taking on humble, difficult, or unglamorous tasks, which call for emotional steadfastness and genuine empathy as well as courage in battle.",al={"why patience paladin","importance of patience light","paladin patience test"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For a paladin, the Tome of Divinity sets out the moral heart of the calling: compassion and patience matter as much as readiness for combat.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind’s paladins form the Alliance’s spiritual and martial backbone. They anchor the realm’s defense in moral integrity and humble service to ordinary citizens.",["race:Human"]="For Stormwind’s humans, studying the holy tome is a sacred rite of passage that reinforces civic duty and devotion to the Holy Light."},kw={"cathedral of light","compassion","divinity","duthorian rall","holy light","paladin","patience","stormwind","the tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","topic:light","quest:1641","quest:2997","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1642},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1643"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Stormwind, initiates of the Light are sent to help someone in need. They seek a citizen of pure heart and noble motive, and find Stephanie Turner in the Trade District.",h="In Stormwind, initiates of the Light are sent to help someone in need.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Humility and Service",b="Initiates of the Light begin this sacred trial by walking Stormwind’s streets. They seek someone of noble intent and pure motive who depends on the kindness of strangers. Before deeper instruction in holy duties, they learn that service to the vulnerable matters more than glorious combat.",sp=0},{t="Aid in the Trade District",b="In Stormwind’s Trade District, Stephanie Turner makes clothing for children in the city’s orphanage with her husband. More tradesmen have come to the city, and competition for cloth and leather has made donations harder to find. Her husband has gone to Ironforge to seek support. Stephanie remains in Stormwind, carrying on their work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of The Tome of Divinity trial?",a="The trial teaches aspiring paladins to serve the Holy Light through humble aid. Initiates seek someone in Stormwind who is pure of heart and needs help, rather than proving themselves in combat or through grand deeds.",al={"what is the tome of divinity","tome of divinity purpose","why do the tome of divinity"}},{q="Who is Stephanie Turner?",a="Stephanie Turner lives in Stormwind’s Trade District and sews clothing for children at the city’s orphanage. She depends on cloth and leather donations to provide for them.",al={"who is stephanie turner","stephanie turner stormwind","where is stephanie turner"}},{q="Why has Stephanie Turner's husband gone to Ironforge?",a="Stephanie Turner’s husband has traveled to Ironforge to seek support for their work at the orphanage. While he is away, she gathers supplies and sews clothes in Stormwind.",al={"stephanie turner husband","who is stephanies husband","husband in ironforge"}},{q="What difficulties is Stephanie Turner facing?",a="More tradesmen in Stormwind have increased competition for cloth and leather. With fewer people willing to donate those materials, Stephanie struggles to gather enough to make clothes for the orphans.",al={"why is stephanie struggling","cloth shortage stormwind","orphanage clothing problem"}},{q="Why does this trial specifically direct initiates to Stephanie Turner?",a="Stephanie Turner has noble intent, a pure heart, and a real need for help. Aiding her gives an initiate a chance to serve someone devoted to caring for others.",al={"why help stephanie turner","why does the quest send you to stephanie"}},{q="What lesson does this trial impart to servants of the Light?",a="The trial teaches servants of the Light to show compassion and serve the vulnerable. Before using holy power in battle, they must learn to be kind to citizens in need.",al={"what does the light teach here","lesson of the tome of divinity"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin learning to serve the Holy Light, you begin with humble charity rather than martial glory.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance citizen, you see Stormwind’s struggle to support its orphans and the ties with Ironforge as people seek help amid economic strain."},kw={"holy light","ironforge","orphanage","paladin","stephanie turner","stormwind","the tome of divinity","tome of divinity","trade district"},rel={"subzone:trade-district","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:ironforge"},m={id=1643},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1644"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="Stephanie Turner in Stormwind needs help clothing children orphaned by the Scourge. Her husband John is gathering supplies as an aspiring paladin brings linen cloth to her home.",h="Stephanie Turner in Stormwind needs help clothing children orphaned by the Scourge.",sec={{t="The Orphans of War",b="Stephanie Turner cares for children whose families were lost to the Scourge in the northern lands over the last decade. Her husband John is away gathering supplies. So Stephanie must keep the children fed, warm, and sheltered while finding time to make them clothes.",sp=0},{t="A Trial of Compassion",b="An aspiring paladin proves compassion by bringing linen cloth to Stephanie. With the cloth, she can sew shirts and pants for the children while tending to their food and shelter. Such humble aid shows how the Light's protectors guard the weak.",sp=0},{t="Strains on the Capital",b="Stephanie says this year has grown harsher. John must make long, difficult journeys as far as Ironforge to gather supplies. Even within Stormwind's high stone walls, the pain of recent tragedies in the north is still felt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Stephanie Turner?",a="Stephanie Turner lives in Stormwind and cares for children orphaned by the Scourge. She works to feed, clothe, and shelter them, with help from charity and her husband John.",al={"who is stephanie turner","stephanie turner stormwind","orphanage caretaker"}},{q="Why does Stephanie Turner need linen cloth?",a="Stephanie needs linen cloth to sew shirts and pants for the orphaned children. With food and shelter to manage, she has little time to gather materials herself.",al={"why linen cloth","what is linen used for","cloth for stephanie"}},{q="Who is John and where has he gone?",a="John is Stephanie Turner's husband. He travels from Stormwind to gather supplies, going as far as Ironforge, though he dislikes being away from his family.",al={"who is john","where is john","stephanie turners husband"}},{q="Why are there so many orphaned children in Stormwind?",a="Most of the children in Stephanie's care lost their families in Scourge attacks across the northern kingdoms over the past decade. Refugees and survivors brought many of them south to Stormwind.",al={"why are there orphans in stormwind","scourge orphans stormwind","what happened to children parents"}},{q="How does helping Stephanie relate to the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity tests an aspiring paladin's virtues, especially charity and compassion. Giving basic supplies to a caretaker shows a servant of the Light will protect the humble as well as face monsters.",al={"tome of divinity meaning","why is this a paladin quest","paladin charity quest"}},{q="What does Stephanie mean about 'something in the air'?",a="Stephanie says this year has felt rougher than past years, as if something in the air signals a great change. She cannot say what it is.",al={"bad year stormwind","something in the air","stormwind troubles"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you show compassion and devotion to the Light by caring for the vulnerable and offering charity in Stormwind.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Stephanie Turner sews shirts and pants for the orphaned children with bolts of linen cloth.",["faction:Alliance"]="War orphans in Stormwind show the human cost of recent Scourge attacks across the northern Alliance realms."},kw={"charity","john turner","linen cloth","orphans","paladin","scourge","stephanie turner","stormwind","tome of divinity"},rel={"topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:scourge","zone:ironforge"},m={id=1644},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1646"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge teaches young paladins what the Light asks of them. The Tome of Divinity says devotion calls for patience, compassion, and humble service to the needy, alongside martial strength.",h="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge teaches young paladins what the Light asks of them.",sec={{t="The Measure of Divinity",b="For a paladin, strength in battle must serve a higher purpose. Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge gives initiates the Tome of Divinity to teach them why they wield their arms. It turns their thoughts from dominion and godhood toward moral goodness. A paladin's calling is to serve as a steady instrument of the Light.",sp=0},{t="Trials of Service and Compassion",b="The tome teaches that smiting evil is not enough to make a paladin. Compassion, patience, and humility set these warriors apart from common combatants. After studying its words, initiates undertake trials in Ironforge and nearby lands. Through charity and service, they show sound judgment and unwavering devotion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity teaches novice paladins that divinity means striving to do good, aid the less fortunate, and show compassion, patience, and bravery rather than seeking godhood.",al={"what is the tome of divinity","tome of divinity paladin","what does the tome teach"}},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a paladin mentor in Ironforge. She guides novices through their first trials and teaches them to balance righteous combat with selfless service.",al={"who is tiza battleforge","tiza battleforge location","where is tiza"}},{q="Why must paladins study patience and compassion?",a="A paladin's power reflects the Light, so battle strength alone is not enough. Patience and compassion help paladins defend and uplift others.",al={"why read the tome","paladin virtues","why patience and compassion"}},{q="What tests follow reading the book?",a="After reading the tome, paladins demonstrate their virtues through practical trials. Mentors send them across Ironforge and nearby lands to help the needy and prove their devotion to the Light.",al={"what happens after reading the tome","tome of divinity trials","next trial after reading"}},{q="Where does this trial take place?",a="After studying the tome, paladins return to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge, the dwarven capital.",al={"where is this quest turned in","ironforge paladin quest"}},{q="What does it mean to strive for divinity?",a="Striving for divinity means choosing to do good in all things, not seeking godhood. Paladins use the Light to support and protect the people of Azeroth.",al={"what does striving for divinity mean","paladin godhood"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you learn that compassion and service matter as much as martial skill.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you receive this instruction in Ironforge from mentors such as Tiza Battleforge, who teach you to guide strength with patience and virtue."},kw={"compassion","holy light","ironforge","paladin","patience","the tome of divinity","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","topic:light","zone:ironforge"},m={id=1646},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1647"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="At Ironforge's temple, an initiate seeks a lesson in the Light through service. Sent by a mentor into the outer ring, you search for someone with pure intent and a genuine need. There, John Turner shows how compassion and selfless work belong on the path of the Light.",h="At Ironforge's temple, an initiate seeks a lesson in the Light through service.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Compassion",b="Initiates of the Light stationed in Ironforge face a trial of compassion. Their mentor sends them into the dwarven city to find someone truly in need of aid. The search calls for discernment: you must recognize a pure heart, noble intent, and a real need for kindness. Humble service lies at the heart of this calling.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of John Turner",b="In Ironforge's outer ring, a humble worker named John Turner plies his trade. Startled by your approach, he calls out about the Orphanage of Stormwind, then tells you why he works so hard. Separated from his beloved wife by long hours of toil, Turner labors so orphaned children can have clothes and food. Help him, then return to the temple to continue your journey in the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Tome of Divinity quest?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a sacred trial for aspiring servants of the Light in Ironforge. You seek out and help someone of pure heart and noble motive before continuing your spiritual teachings.",al={"what is tome of divinity","tome of divinity purpose","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is John Turner?",a="John Turner is a hardworking man in Ironforge's outer ring, where he plies his trade. He works long hours away from his beloved wife to gather resources and feed and clothe orphans.",al={"who is john turner","john turner ironforge","where is john turner"}},{q="Why does the mentor send you to find someone in need?",a="The mentor sends you to test your understanding of compassion and service. You learn to recognize noble intent, offer kindness, and guide those who labor quietly for others.",al={"why find someone in need","purpose of helping john turner","why do this test"}},{q="Where is John Turner located in Ironforge?",a="John Turner walks along Ironforge's outer ring as he goes about his demanding daily work for the orphanage.",al={"where to find john turner","john turner location","how to find john turner"}},{q="What happens once you speak with John Turner?",a="After hearing John Turner's plight, you return to the mentor in the temple. There, you reflect on what it means to follow the Light and prepare for the next step of your calling.",al={"what happens after finding john turner","return to temple of the light","tome of divinity next step"}},{q="Why was John Turner shouting about an orphanage?",a="When first approached, John Turner shouts about the Orphanage of Stormwind, then catches himself and apologizes. He works to provide food and clothing for the orphaned children who rely on charity.",al={"what orphanage is john turner shouting about","stormwind orphanage ironforge","why did john turner shout"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you learn that devotion to the Light begins with selfless help for ordinary people in need.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you take this trial in Ironforge, your own capital, among the halls of your home city.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see compassion, charity, and care for the vulnerable among the virtues upheld in cities like Ironforge."},kw={"ironforge","john turner","light","orphanage","paladin","temple","the tome of divinity","tome of divinity"},rel={"zone:ironforge","topic:light"},m={id=1647},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1648"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Ironforge, The Tome of Divinity calls servants of the Light to show compassion. John Turner seeks aid for the Stormwind orphanage he runs with his wife, caring for children left parentless by the Scourge. The trial asks an initiate to choose charity over martial glory.",h="In Ironforge, The Tome of Divinity calls servants of the Light to show compassion.",sec={{t="Charity in the Great Forge",b="For an initiate walking the path of the Light, the trial in Ironforge calls for charity rather than arms. John Turner has come to the dwarven halls seeking help. He and his wife oversee an orphanage in Stormwind, where they care for children left without parents by the Scourge's rampages over the past decade. His journey to Ironforge speaks to the hardships shared by the Alliance's common folk.",sp=0},{t="The Scars of the Scourge",b="Provisions are hard to gather across borders. More tradesmen have come to work across Azeroth, and local supplies have grown scarce. John Turner has spent weeks in Ironforge appealing to civic groups and citizens, with little to show for it. His wife needs linen cloth to make clothes for the children. Giving it freely shows the selfless devotion at the heart of a servant of the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is John Turner?",a="John Turner is a human caretaker who runs a Stormwind orphanage with his wife. About once a month, he travels to Ironforge to seek supplies and charity from dwarven citizens and merchant guilds for children orphaned by war.",al={"who is john turner","john turner lore","ironforge turners"}},{q="Why does John Turner need linen cloth?",a="John Turner needs linen cloth so his wife in Stormwind can sew warm clothes for the orphaned children. More tradesmen across Azeroth and shifting trade have made basic cloth scarce and hard to find.",al={"why linen","why does john turner need cloth","linen for orphanage"}},{q="Why are there so many orphans in Stormwind?",a="The children in the Turners' care lost their parents in the Scourge's devastating assaults over the past decade. The Third War shattered families across the human kingdoms and left many young people without homes.",al={"stormwind orphanage orphans","why are there orphans","scourge orphans"}},{q="Why did John Turner travel to Ironforge?",a="John Turner travels across the mountains to Ironforge to ask dwarven citizens and trade groups for donations and supplies that are hard to find in Stormwind.",al={"why is john turner in ironforge","why ironforge for stormwind orphanage"}},{q="How does helping an orphanage relate to the Holy Light?",a="The Holy Light calls for selflessness, mercy, and service to those in despair. Helping a weary caretaker provide for war orphans tests an aspiring paladin's humility and charity.",al={"what does this have to do with the light","paladin connection","why do paladins do this quest"}},{q="Why has John Turner's trip to Ironforge been so difficult?",a="John Turner's trip has been slow and unproductive because supplies are scarce and few groups have offered help. He cannot return home until he secures a shipment.",al={"is john turner stuck","why is the trip slow"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="A paladin faces this trial through selfless aid to the innocent, not steel or combat. Such compassion is a virtue at the heart of the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this reveals the Scourge's deep wounds in human homes and the reliance between Stormwind and Ironforge."},kw={"holy light","ironforge","john turner","linen cloth","paladin","scourge orphans","stormwind orphanage","the tome of divinity"},rel={"topic:light","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:scourge"},m={id=1648},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1656"] = {t="quest",n="A Task Unfinished",z="general",s="On Red Cloud Mesa, a young tauren cannot finish a family chore alone. Their coming-of-age trials and their father's request leave them too exhausted to carry furs to Innkeeper Kauth in Bloodhoof Village.",h="On Red Cloud Mesa, a young tauren cannot finish a family chore alone.",sec={{t="Trials on the Mesa",b="Young tauren on Red Cloud Mesa face rites that prove they are ready for the wider world. The trials demand strength, while tribal chores still need doing. One youth must finish the Rite of Strength and answer an urgent request from their father. Too tired to carry a bundle of furs down the mesa, they ask you for help.",sp=0},{t="Hearth and Shelter",b="Bloodhoof Village lies in the open plains below, where Innkeeper Kauth receives the furs. He intends to make them into warm blankets for weary wanderers. The plains tauren welcome travelers, and their support helps those facing solitary trials of strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest A Task Unfinished?",a="An exhausted young tauren on Red Cloud Mesa asks you to carry furs to Innkeeper Kauth in Bloodhoof Village. They are still undertaking the Rite of Strength.",al={"what is a task unfinished","task unfinished quest info","who gives a task unfinished"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Kauth?",a="Innkeeper Kauth runs the inn in Bloodhoof Village, Mulgore. He offers weary travelers shelter, warm blankets, and hospitality as they cross the plains from the high mesas.",al={"who is innkeeper kauth","where is kauth","bloodhoof village innkeeper"}},{q="Why are the furs being delivered to the inn?",a="The young tauren's father asked for the furs to be delivered to Innkeeper Kauth. Kauth intends to make them into warm blankets for guests seeking shelter and rest at his inn in Bloodhoof Village.",al={"why deliver furs","what are the furs for","bundle of furs mulgore"}},{q="Why couldn't the young tauren deliver the furs themselves?",a="The young tauren is undertaking the Rite of Strength on Red Cloud Mesa and is too exhausted to travel to Bloodhoof Village. They cannot make the journey without failing the sacred rite or collapsing from fatigue.",al={"why can't the quester deliver the furs","why does the youth need help"}},{q="What is the Rite of Strength?",a="The Rite of Strength is a coming-of-age trial for young tauren on the mesa. It tests their stamina and resilience, and shows whether they can become protectors of their tribe.",al={"what is the rite of strength","rite of strength tauren trial"}},{q="Where is Bloodhoof Village situated?",a="Bloodhoof Village is a main settlement in Mulgore's rolling plains, below the sheltered heights of Red Cloud Mesa. The village has an open inn, crafting supplies, and trade outposts.",al={"where is bloodhoof village","bloodhoof village location"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren, you face demanding trials on Red Cloud Mesa to prove your maturity and strength. Family and tribal duties test your endurance alongside the rites.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Bloodhoof Village as a gathering place for travelers in Mulgore. It offers shelter and warm hearths to those crossing the plains."},kw={"a task unfinished","bloodhoof village","bundle of furs","innkeeper kauth","mulgore","red cloud mesa","rite of strength","tauren"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village","quest:757"},m={id=1656},src={"In-game quest text: A Task Unfinished"},fv=true}
E["quest:1678"] = {t="quest",n="Vejrek",z="general",s="In the foothills south of Frostmane Hold, you face Vejrek to prove your mettle. Muren Stormpike wants proof you can handle real foes. Your success begins a lesson in strong defense.",h="In the foothills south of Frostmane Hold, you face Vejrek to prove your mettle.",sec={{t="A Test of Mettle",b="Muren Stormpike says you need toughness before he can teach you new moves. Vejrek is the toughest troll in these parts, and his hut lies in the foothills south of Frostmane Hold. Muren asks you to bring back Vejrek’s head as proof you can handle real foes.",sp=0},{t="The Lesson",b="Muren accepts Vejrek’s head and says you have what it takes. He is ready to teach you strong defense, which helps you stay standing against foes that would fell others and supports your allies.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Vejrek?",a="Vejrek is described as the toughest troll in these parts. His hut lies in the foothills south of Frostmane Hold.",al={"who's vejrek","vejrek troll","that troll"}},{q="Why does Muren send me after Vejrek?",a="Muren wants proof that you can handle real foes before he teaches you new moves.",al={"why kill vejrek","muren's test","prove mettle"}},{q="Where is Vejrek's hut?",a="Vejrek’s hut is in the foothills south of Frostmane Hold.",al={"vejrek location","where's his hut","foothills troll"}},{q="What does Muren want brought back?",a="Muren asks you to bring back Vejrek’s head as proof of your mettle.",al={"vejrek head","what to bring","muren wants what"}},{q="What does Muren teach after the test?",a="Muren begins teaching strong defense after accepting Vejrek’s head. The lesson covers how it helps you stay standing against foes.",al={"muren lesson","what's the lesson","strong defense"}}},kw={"frostmane hold","ironforge","mettle","muren stormpike","strong defense","troll","vejrek"},rel={"quest:1679","quest:287","zone:ironforge","topic:troll"},m={id=1678},src={"In-game quest text: Vejrek"},fv=true}
E["quest:1680"] = {t="quest",n="Tormus Deepforge",z="general",s="In Ironforge, Tormus Deepforge waits for fighters sent by Muren Stormpike. Before he forges a weapon for them, he asks them to face a perilous trial.",h="In Ironforge, Tormus Deepforge waits for fighters sent by Muren Stormpike.",sec={{t="The Blacksmith's Anvil",b="Tormus Deepforge is a master dwarven weaponsmith in Ironforge. Warriors who show their growing skill to Muren Stormpike are sent across the city to consult him. Tormus is known for sturdy, potent arms, but he does not give fine blades or bludgeons to every passerby. A warrior must earn his work through action.",sp=0},{t="A Perilous Trial",b="Before Tormus agrees to forge a weapon, he asks the adventurer to promise him a favor. He speaks plainly about the danger ahead and warns that it could cost a life. To him, peril is no reason to turn back. It is the proper test of a warrior's mettle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tormus Deepforge?",a="Tormus Deepforge is an accomplished weaponsmith in Ironforge. He can forge exceptional weapons for warriors who prove their courage and ability through dangerous deeds.",al={"who is tormus","tormus deepforge ironforge","who is tormus deepforge"}},{q="Who sends you to speak with Tormus Deepforge?",a="Muren Stormpike sends promising fighters to Tormus Deepforge when they are ready for a weapon suited to their growing martial skill.",al={"who sent me to tormus","why talk to tormus","muren stormpike referral"}},{q="What does Tormus Deepforge ask in return for making a weapon?",a="Tormus agrees to forge a fine weapon after the adventurer does him a favor. He asks for a perilous undertaking that could mean death, the kind of challenge he believes an aspiring warrior seeks.",al={"tormus favor","what weapon will tormus make","what does tormus want"}},{q="Why does Tormus emphasize that the job is dangerous?",a="Tormus warns that the undertaking is perilous because it could cost a life. He believes danger is the proper test for anyone worthy of his craft.",al={"is tormus deepforge dangerous","what is tormus task","ironforge warrior quest tormus"}},{q="Where can Tormus Deepforge be found?",a="Tormus Deepforge works near the Great Forge in Ironforge. Fellow smiths, anvils, and roaring smelters surround him.",al={"where is tormus","tormus deepforge location"}},{q="Which adventurers does Tormus Deepforge work with?",a="Tormus works with warriors sent by their trainers. He seeks fighters with the grit and resolve to face life-threatening dangers.",al={"which class gets tormus quest","is tormus warrior only"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Muren Stormpike sends promising warriors to Tormus Deepforge in Ironforge. There, they prove their mettle and seek a weapon forged for their calling.",["faction:Alliance"]="Ironforge's master smiths test promising Alliance fighters with dangerous undertakings before they forge fine weapons for them."},kw={"dwarf smith","great forge","ironforge","muren stormpike","tormus deepforge","warrior quest","weaponsmith"},m={id=1680},src={"In-game quest text: Tormus Deepforge"},fv=true}
E["quest:1712"] = {t="quest",n="Cyclonian",z="general",s="At the summoning site, Cyclonian waits for a champion bold enough to face him. A special parchment names the rare materials needed to call forth the wind lord, whose whirlwind heart can strengthen a formidable weapon.",h="At the summoning site, Cyclonian waits for a champion bold enough to face him.",sec={{t="The Slumbering Wind Lord",b="A watcher has kept vigil at the summoning site for ages. The raging elemental wind lord awaits a combatant with the raw martial prowess to challenge and destroy him.",sp=0},{t="Summoning the Tempest",b="A special parchment names the rare materials needed to summon Cyclonian. Once the wind lord is called forth, you face him in direct combat. You may defeat him, or fall to his howling gale.",sp=0},{t="The Whirlwind Heart",b="Cyclonian's whirlwind heart is sought from the defeated elemental. Severed from him, its fierce elemental energies can be bound and infused into a weapon fit for an accomplished champion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cyclonian?",a="Cyclonian is a powerful elemental wind lord and a grave threat. Observers have watched him for ages, waiting for a champion strong enough to challenge and defeat him.",al={"who is cyclonian","cyclonian lore","what is cyclonian"}},{q="Why must Cyclonian be summoned?",a="Cyclonian is summoned so a worthy champion can challenge and slay him. The victor can claim his whirlwind heart and have its power infused into a formidable weapon.",al={"why summon cyclonian","cyclonian purpose","why fight cyclonian"}},{q="What is the Whirlwind Heart?",a="The Whirlwind Heart is Cyclonian's core essence. Torn from the defeated wind lord, its tempestuous energies can be infused into a weapon of great martial power.",al={"what is whirlwind heart","heart of cyclonian","whirlwind heart purpose"}},{q="Who has been watching Cyclonian?",a="Bath'rah the Windwatcher in the Alterac Mountains has kept vigil over the site for ages. He searches endlessly for a true champion who can topple Cyclonian and master his tempestuous heart.",al={"who wants cyclonian dead","who watches cyclonian"}},{q="How is Cyclonian brought forth?",a="A special parchment records the rare reagents needed to summon Cyclonian and draw the wind lord into the world to be challenged.",al={"how to summon cyclonian","cyclonian ingredients"}},{q="What weapon is forged from Cyclonian?",a="The champion who gathers the necessary components, summons Cyclonian, and slays him earns a weapon infused with the latent fury of the elemental's whirlwind heart.",al={"cyclonian reward","what weapon from cyclonian"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, defeating Cyclonian tests your strength and martial mastery. Claim his whirlwind heart and use it to forge a potent weapon."},kw={"champion","cyclonian","elemental","summoning","whirlwind heart","wind lord"},m={id=1712},src={"In-game quest text: Cyclonian"},fv=true}
E["quest:1713"] = {t="quest",n="The Summoning",z="general",s="At Bath'rah Windwatcher's camp, a warrior faces a trial against Cyclonian, the wind lord. Slay the elemental and claim the Whirlwind Heart, whose storm force can be bound into a weapon.",h="At Bath'rah Windwatcher's camp, a warrior faces a trial against Cyclonian, the wind lord.",sec={{t="Calling the Tempest",b="Bath'rah Windwatcher has prepared an ancient ritual to summon Cyclonian into the mortal realm. The fearsome elemental is known as the wind lord. There will be no bargain with the tempest. An able champion must strike it down as soon as it takes form.",sp=0},{t="The Heart of the Storm",b="Cyclonian's Whirlwind Heart sustains his physical form. When the wind lord falls, Bath'rah wrenches the heart free and harnesses the gale within. Its volatile power can imbue a weapon with the force of the storm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cyclonian?",a="Cyclonian is a powerful elemental known as the wind lord. Bath'rah Windwatcher's ritual calls him forth as a fierce tempest, and he must be defeated to claim the essence sealed in his core.",al={"who is cyclonian","what is cyclonian","cyclonian lore"}},{q="What is the Whirlwind Heart?",a="The Whirlwind Heart is Cyclonian's elemental core. Bath'rah Windwatcher needs it to bind the wind lord's swirling, destructive power into a weapon.",al={"what is whirlwind heart","why need whirlwind heart","whirlwind heart use"}},{q="Who is Bath'rah Windwatcher?",a="Bath'rah Windwatcher is a troll mystic who lives in the wilderness and knows how to summon Cyclonian. He guides warriors through the ritual, then uses the fallen elemental's heart to forge mighty weapons.",al={"who is bathrah","bathrah windwatcher","quest giver the summoning"}},{q="Why is Cyclonian being summoned?",a="Cyclonian is summoned so a warrior can face and slay the wind lord, then claim his elemental heart. Its power can be bound into a weapon.",al={"why summon cyclonian","purpose of the summoning","reason to summon"}},{q="What happens after Cyclonian is defeated?",a="After Cyclonian falls, Bath'rah can harness the elemental power in his Whirlwind Heart to empower a weapon with Cyclonian's stormcraft.",al={"what happens after defeating cyclonian","cyclonian reward lore","after the summoning"}},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The ritual takes place at Bath'rah Windwatcher's camp. There, the mystic gathers the primal focus needed to draw Cyclonian from the elemental realm into the physical world.",al={"where does the ritual happen","the summoning location"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, facing Cyclonian and claiming the Whirlwind Heart is a proving ground. It yields a weapon infused with the raw power of the tempest.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know Bath'rah Windwatcher's primal arts reach far beyond civilization. His command of wind elementals reflects the deep mystical traditions of troll shamans and witch doctors."},kw={"bath'rah windwatcher","bathrah","cyclonian","elemental","the summoning","warrior quest","whirlwind heart","wind lord"},rel={"quest:1712"},m={id=1713},src={"In-game quest text: The Summoning"},fv=true}
E["quest:1714"] = {t="quest",n="Essence of the Exile",z="general",s="At the cauldron, Essence of the Exile draws travelers with its beckoning vapors. Charms set off a violent reaction that reveals molten rock.",h="At the cauldron, Essence of the Exile draws travelers with its beckoning vapors.",sec={{t="A Beckoning Cauldron",b="A bubbling cauldron sends out vapors that draw travelers to its churning depths. Specific enchanted charms stir an intense reaction within the vessel.",sp=0},{t="The Molten Crucible",b="The charms sink slowly through the liquid. Then a large bubble rises and bursts, revealing a churning lump of molten rock forged from the combined materials.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Essence of the Exile?",a="Essence of the Exile is a transmutation ritual performed at a bubbling cauldron. Charms set off a violent reaction that yields a churning lump of molten rock.",al={"what is essence of the exile","essence of the exile quest"}},{q="What happens when charms are placed in the cauldron?",a="The cauldron's vapors draw travelers close. Charms sink to the bottom, then a large bubble bursts at the surface and leaves molten stone behind.",al={"what happens at the cauldron","how does the cauldron work"}},{q="What does the cauldron produce?",a="When a large bubble bursts at the surface, a churning lump of molten rock is revealed inside the cauldron.",al={"what is produced from the cauldron","what do you get from essence of the exile"}},{q="Where is the cauldron used for this ritual?",a="The ritual takes place at a boiling cauldron whose hot vapors beckon travelers. There, the vessel transforms its contents.",al={"cauldron location","where do i find the cauldron"}},{q="Why are charms placed into the cauldron?",a="The charms are consumed as reagents in the cauldron's depths. Their presence in the heated liquid helps form the molten rock.",al={"what are the charms for","why do charms go in the cauldron"}},{q="Why is the cauldron constantly bubbling?",a="The bubbling liquid and beckoning vapors mark an active reaction within the vessel. It is ready to transform whatever enters its depths.",al={"why is it bubbling","what are the vapors"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Alchemical cauldrons and elemental transmutations can bind separate essences into solid form through volatile magic.",["class:Shaman"]="Even when bubbling cauldrons churn molten rock, working with elemental essences calls for understanding the primal forces at play."},kw={"bubble","cauldron","charms","essence of the exile","molten rock","transmutation","vapors"},rel={"quest:1712"},m={id=1714},src={"In-game quest text: Essence of the Exile"},fv=true}
E["quest:1778"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge teaches initiates what service to the Holy Light demands. They aid someone in need, then return to tell her how they served.",h="In Ironforge, Tiza Battleforge teaches initiates what service to the Holy Light demands.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Holy Light",b="Paladins begin their trials by learning humility, duty, and charity. Tiza Battleforge does not ask for feats of arms. A servant of the Holy Light must understand the troubles ordinary people face and offer help without seeking praise or gain.",sp=0},{t="Accounting Before Ironforge",b="After helping someone in Ironforge, an aspiring paladin returns to Tiza Battleforge. The initiate tells her how they spent their time away and whose burdens they helped bear. When she is satisfied that they acted with charity and duty, Tiza commends them. Such selfless service is what it means to follow the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity tests novice paladins in compassion, charity, and self-sacrifice. Its trials ask more of them than strength in battle.",al={"what is the tome of divinity","tome of divinity trial","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a paladin mentor in Ironforge. She guides initiates and judges whether their deeds follow the Holy Light.",al={"who is tiza battleforge","where is tiza battleforge","ironforge paladin trainer"}},{q="Who is Stephanie?",a="Stephanie Turner is John Turner's wife in Stormwind. They run an orphanage together, and John hopes to return to her after gathering supplies in Ironforge.",al={"who is stephanie","stephanie stormwind"}},{q="What does Tiza Battleforge ask of returning initiates?",a="Tiza Battleforge listens to how a returning initiate served others. She asks how they helped a noble cause and aided ordinary citizens before granting her blessing.",al={"what lesson does tiza test","what does tiza want","paladin charity test"}},{q="Why must initiates report to Ironforge?",a="Initiates return to Ironforge to tell Tiza Battleforge what they did. By helping John Turner in the city, they show compassion and selflessness.",al={"why speak to tiza in ironforge","ironforge tome of divinity"}},{q="Why is self-sacrifice central to this trial?",a="Paladin teachings place the welfare of others above one's own. Tiza teaches that selfless sacrifice will be rewarded in time.",al={"how does the light reward sacrifice","paladin sacrifice"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you learn that the Holy Light calls for selflessness, charity, and lasting duty to ordinary citizens before martial glory.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf paladin, you report to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge after your trials in Dun Morogh. You account for your deeds in the wider world.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see close ties between Ironforge and Stormwind in the mentors and travelers who pass between these great cities."},kw={"charity","holy light","ironforge","paladin trial","stephanie","stormwind","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","zone:ironforge","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1778},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1779"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Ironforge, The Tome of Divinity tests paladin initiates in holy power and martial devotion. Entrusted with the Symbol of Life, an initiate is sent to aid Muiredon Battleforge, wounded after a deadly encounter with Dark Iron dwarves.",h="In Ironforge, The Tome of Divinity tests paladin initiates in holy power and martial devotion.",sec={{t="A Trial of Faith and Power",b="In Ironforge, paladin initiates face a trial of martial skill and holy power. They have already shown humility, patience, and charity. Now they are entrusted with the Symbol of Life and sent into the city to help those suffering from conflicts beyond its gates.",sp=0},{t="A Brother Fallen",b="Muiredon Battleforge lies badly wounded after a clash with Dark Iron dwarves. A priest tends his immediate injuries as he prepares to tell what became of his expedition and his companion Narm. The initiate must answer that need with the Light’s gift of renewal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a rite of passage for young paladins learning the ways of the Holy Light. After proving charitable and patient, an initiate receives the Symbol of Life and is sent to aid a wounded dwarf in Ironforge.",al={"what is this quest","tome of divinity purpose","what does this quest do"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a sacred token entrusted to paladin initiates during their trials. It carries the Holy Light’s power to heal and restore those fallen while defending their people.",al={"what is symbol of life","symbol of life item"}},{q="Who is Muiredon Battleforge?",a="Muiredon Battleforge is a dwarven fighter wounded in a clash with Dark Iron dwarves. A priest tends him in Ironforge while his wife sends promising paladins to hear his tale.",al={"who is muiredon battleforge","who is the wounded dwarf"}},{q="Who gives you the Symbol of Life?",a="Muiredon Battleforge’s wife, a paladin mentor in Ironforge, gives you the Symbol of Life. After seeing your charity and patience, she sends you to aid her wounded husband and test your power, readiness for combat, and willingness to help.",al={"who sends you to muiredon","who gives this quest"}},{q="What happened to Muiredon Battleforge?",a="Muiredon and his companion Narm were ambushed by Dark Iron dwarves. Muiredon escaped and returned to Ironforge with grave injuries that need spiritual and physical mending.",al={"who attacked muiredon","what happened to muiredon"}},{q="Who is Narm?",a="Narm is Muiredon Battleforge’s best friend and fellow paladin. He accompanied Muiredon into battle against the Dark Iron dwarves, but did not escape the clash, leaving a paladin’s aid needed on his behalf.",al={"who is narm","what happened to narm"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you carry the Symbol of Life to comfort the wounded. The trial prepares you for the sacred duty of resurrection.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you face this trial in the heart of Ironforge. It recalls the close bonds among defenders who brave ambushes by hostile Dark Iron clans."},kw={"dark iron","holy light","ironforge","muiredon battleforge","narm","paladin","symbol of life","tome of divinity"},rel={"zone:ironforge","topic:light","topic:priest"},m={id=1779},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1780"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall guides paladins through a trial of devotion to the Holy Light. They prove their worth through charity, selflessness, and a duty to protect those in need.",h="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall guides paladins through a trial of devotion to the Holy...",sec={{t="A Trial of Virtue",b="Paladins in the service of the Holy Light face a defining trial in Stormwind City. At the Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall sends initiates to prove their devotion through moral conduct and selfless deeds for the kingdom's citizens. Martial glory alone will not suffice.",sp=0},{t="The Virtue of Selflessness",b="After aiding the vulnerable, initiates return to Duthorian Rall. They have brought needed relief to children and earned their heartfelt gratitude. Their mentor sees the value in putting others first. He teaches that charity, compassion, and duty to the people of Azeroth mark the path of the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a series of trials for aspiring paladins. Guided by mentors at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, initiates show moral virtue, charity, and duty by helping citizens in need across the kingdom.",al={"what is tome of divinity","tome of divinity quest","paladin trial quest"}},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a senior paladin trainer at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. He guides fledgling paladins in their spiritual education and moral trials, judging whether their deeds uphold the virtues of the Holy Light.",al={"who is duthorian rall","paladin trainer stormwind","duthorian rall role"}},{q="What is the lesson behind this trial?",a="The trial teaches that wielding the Light calls for humility, selfless sacrifice, and service to others. It prizes compassion, charity, and moral duty to the people of Azeroth alongside martial skill.",al={"tome of divinity purpose","why do paladins do this","what does this quest teach"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The trial centers on the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. Initiates go out to help the populace, then return to report their deeds to Duthorian Rall at the cathedral.",al={"where does this quest take place","where to turn in tome of divinity","cathedral of light quest"}},{q="Who did the quest help?",a="The trial brings aid to those in dire need, including young children. The recipient gives heartfelt thanks and reminds paladins in Stormwind never to turn away from the innocent and destitute.",al={"who was helped in this quest","children charity quest","who received aid"}},{q="Why does Duthorian Rall emphasize charity?",a="Duthorian Rall emphasizes charity because the Holy Light calls for generosity and the defense of the innocent. He teaches that a paladin must sacrifice for others and value their well-being above their own.",al={"why does charity matter to paladins","paladins and the poor","charity holy light"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you prove your devotion to the Holy Light through charity and protection for ordinary citizens. The Tome of Divinity tests your commitment to serve others.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you are reminded that Stormwind's spiritual strength rests in safeguarding the vulnerable among your people."},kw={"cathedral of light","charity","duthorian rall","holy light","paladin trial","stormwind","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1780},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1781"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, a trial awaits paladin initiates: they must focus the holy Symbol of Life. Those who prove their virtue are sent to aid Gazin Tenorm, who barely escaped a Defias ambush near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest.",h="At Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, a trial awaits paladin initiates: they must focus the holy Symbol of Life.",sec={{t="A Test of Devotion",b="In Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, patient and charitable paladin initiates receive the Symbol of Life. Duthorian Rall entrusts them with this holy vessel to test their devotion to the Light. Only a worthy champion can focus one of the Light's greatest gifts, the power to restore life to the fallen.",sp=0},{t="Ambush at Heroes' Vigil",b="Gazin Tenorm shows why the Symbol is needed. He crawled back to Stormwind after Defias bandits attacked him near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest. Priests tend his severe wounds at the cathedral altar. His companion Henze remains in danger where the outlaws struck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is an associate of Duthorian Rall. He barely escaped a Defias ambush near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest and was brought to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light with severe wounds. Local priests are treating him.",al={"who is gazin tenorm","gazin elwynn defias","wounded man stormwind altar"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a holy relic entrusted to patient and charitable paladin initiates. It tests whether a rising champion has the spiritual focus and fortitude to channel one of the Holy Light's greatest gifts: the restoration of life.",al={"what does symbol of life do","symbol of life paladin","paladin resurrection artifact"}},{q="What happened at Heroes' Vigil?",a="At Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, Defias outlaws ambushed Gazin Tenorm and his companion Henze. Gazin fled to Stormwind with grievous wounds, while Henze remains in danger.",al={"where is heroes vigil","heroes vigil elwynn defias","gazin ambush location"}},{q="Who is Henze?",a="Henze is Gazin Tenorm's companion. Defias bandits attacked them near Heroes' Vigil in Elwynn Forest, and Henze was left behind while Gazin reached Stormwind alive.",al={"who is henze","henze faulk","gazin friend defias"}},{q="Who sends you to speak with Gazin Tenorm?",a="Duthorian Rall sends you to speak with Gazin Tenorm. A leader among Stormwind's Cathedral of Light paladins, he first confirms that an initiate has shown patience and charity, then directs them to Gazin at the altar.",al={"who sends you to gazin","duthorian rall tome of divinity","stormwind paladin trainer quest"}},{q="Why are Defias bandits attacking travelers near Heroes' Vigil?",a="Defias outlaws and highwaymen ambush travelers across Elwynn Forest, even within striking distance of the capital. Gazin Tenorm's attack shows how brazen and deadly their operations have become.",al={"defias threat elwynn","why are defias near heroes vigil","defias brotherhood stormwind"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a milestone in your training at Stormwind. The trial tests whether you have the spiritual strength to wield the Symbol of Life.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Defias attacks near Heroes' Vigil threaten travelers and citizens across Elwynn Forest. The church must intervene."},kw={"cathedral of light","defias","duthorian","duthorian rall","gazin tenorm","henze","heroes vigil","symbol of life","the tome of divinity","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:gazin-tenorm","subzone:heroes-vigil","topic:light","topic:priest","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1781},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1783"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="A paladin initiate carries the Symbol of Life to the frigid shores south of Helm's Bed Lake in Dun Morogh. There, the initiate must find Narm Faulk, a brave scout who fell holding off Dark Iron dwarves, and call him back with the Light.",h="A paladin initiate carries the Symbol of Life to the frigid shores south of Helm's Bed Lake in Dun Morogh.",sec={{t="Ambush at the Lake",b="South of Helm's Bed Lake, dwarven scouts Muiredon and Narm Faulk watched Dark Iron dwarves entrench themselves. When they saw an enemy commander issuing orders, they struck at several foes and tried to secure a script. The Dark Irons overwhelmed them with unexpected ferocity. Muiredon fled for reinforcements while Narm held the line.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Faith",b="With the Symbol of Life, a paladin initiate searches Dun Morogh's snowy reaches for Narm Faulk. Narm fell beneath the Dark Iron assault, but the holy relic draws his spirit back just as the Light was ready to embrace him fully. In that moment, the initiate answers the first call of a paladin: restoring life to the fallen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The Tome of Divinity tests a young paladin's devotion and worthiness. An initiate receives the Symbol of Life and is sent to save a fallen scout, calling on the Light to bring someone back from death.",al={"what is the tome of divinity","tome of divinity purpose","paladin resurrection quest"}},{q="Who is Narm Faulk?",a="Narm Faulk is an Alliance scout ambushed by Dark Iron dwarves south of Helm's Bed Lake. He gave up his chance to flee so his partner Muiredon could escape, and fell in battle before the Light restored him.",al={"who is narm faulk","where is narm","fallen dwarf narm"}},{q="Who is Muiredon?",a="Muiredon is the scout who fled the Dark Iron ambush at Narm Faulk's urging. He returns for reinforcements and directs the paladin to save his fallen comrade with the Symbol of Life.",al={"who is muiredon","quest giver muiredon","who gives the quest"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="Tiza and Muiredon bestow the Symbol of Life upon the paladin with instructions. This sacred relic can resurrect the dead when a worthy servant of the Light channels its power.",al={"what is the symbol of life","resurrection item","symbol of life lore"}},{q="What were Narm and Muiredon doing near Helm's Bed Lake?",a="Muiredon and Narm Faulk were spying on Dark Iron dwarves entrenched south of Helm's Bed Lake. They saw an enemy leader issuing orders and tried to recover sacred scripts before the dwarves overwhelmed them.",al={"what were they doing south of helms bed lake","why spy on dark iron","dark iron helms bed lake"}},{q="Who is Tiza?",a="Tiza helps dispatch aid and prepares the Symbol of Life with Muiredon for the rescue.",al={"who is tiza","tiza paladin"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a trial of the Light. The Symbol of Life lets you restore a fallen ally.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you face the Dark Iron dwarves entrenched south of Helm's Bed Lake in Dun Morogh.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect dwarven scouts and keep sacred scripts from the Dark Iron dwarves."},kw={"dark iron","dun morogh","helm's bed lake","muiredon","narm faulk","paladin","resurrection","symbol of life","tome of divinity"},rel={"zone:dunmorogh","subzone:helm-s-bed-lake","topic:light"},m={id=1783},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1784"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Dun Morogh, injured scouts need help exposing Dark Iron spies near Helm's Bed Lake. Their orders may persuade Ironforge's skeptical council to heed the danger.",h="In Dun Morogh, injured scouts need help exposing Dark Iron spies near Helm's Bed Lake.",sec={{t="A Trial of Service",b="Young dwarven paladins answer the call to defend Dun Morogh when an expedition near Helm's Bed Lake goes wrong. Narm Faulk and Muiredon Battleforge set out to ambush Dark Iron scouts. Narm fell wounded, while Muiredon returned to Ironforge to recover.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Council",b="Rumors of Dark Iron infiltrators have reached Ironforge, yet some council members refuse to believe they have entered Dun Morogh. Near Helm's Bed, the paladin can track down the spies and recover a Dark Iron Script from their captain. The orders offer proof of enemy movements and plots near the capital's gates.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Hearth",b="Bringing the intercepted orders to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge brings relief. Narm has been rescued, and the documents go to Muiredon's wife to present before the council. The paladin's bravery and devotion to the Light help guard the dwarven realm from hidden treachery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives The Tome of Divinity quest?",a="Narm Faulk gives you the charge to retrieve enemy scripts and report to his companion Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge. He is an injured dwarf, wounded fighting Dark Iron spies near Helm's Bed Lake.",al={"who gives this quest","tome of divinity questgiver","who is narm"}},{q="Who is Muiredon Battleforge?",a="Muiredon Battleforge is a dwarf in Ironforge. He scouted the Dark Iron spies near Helm's Bed Lake with Narm Faulk, then returned to the city to recover from his wounds.",al={"who is muiredon battleforge","where is muiredon","muiredon battleforge location"}},{q="What is the Dark Iron Script?",a="The Dark Iron Script contains written orders passed between Dark Iron spies and their captain near Helm's Bed Lake. It offers evidence of hostile infiltration for Ironforge's skeptical council.",al={"what is dark iron script","why get dark iron script","dark iron script purpose"}},{q="Why does the council in Ironforge need proof of the Dark Irons?",a="Some members of Ironforge's council doubt Dark Iron dwarves have entered Dun Morogh. The recovered scripts prove their movements and reveal their secret plans.",al={"why council deny dark irons","ironforge council dark iron proof"}},{q="Where are the Dark Iron spies located?",a="The Dark Iron spies operate near Helm's Bed Lake in eastern Dun Morogh, east of Kharanos. They work near a small house, passing covert battle orders.",al={"where is helms bed lake","helms bed dark irons","dark iron location dun morogh"}},{q="What role does this quest play for paladins?",a="The Tome of Divinity trials test an aspiring paladin's service, compassion, and courage. By helping fallen comrades such as Narm and defending Dun Morogh, you prove your devotion to the Light.",al={"what does the tome of divinity teach","paladin tome of divinity lore"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face an early trial in the Tome of Divinity. Protecting the kingdom and rescuing comrades in need show your devotion to the Light.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, uncovering Dark Iron spies near Ironforge is vital to the kingdom's defense. It proves to skeptical councilors that an old enemy has entered Dun Morogh.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, exposing Dark Iron sabotage near Ironforge protects the dwarf capital and strengthens northern defenses against covert threats."},kw={"dark iron dwarves","dark iron script","dun morogh","helm's bed lake","ironforge","muiredon battleforge","narm faulk","tome of divinity"},rel={"subzone:helm-s-bed-lake","zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","topic:light"},m={id=1784},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1785"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Ironforge, holy champions face a final trial before Tiza Battleforge. The Tome of Divinity shows whether they are ready to wield the Symbol of Life and call fallen allies back to life.",h="In Ironforge, holy champions face a final trial before Tiza Battleforge.",sec={{t="A Sacred Rite in Ironforge",b="You have crossed the kingdom's trials, and now you come to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge. She is a revered teacher of the holy arts. Her husband watches with pride as you approach, eager to see the dwarven people acknowledge your readiness before the Holy Light.",sp=0},{t="The Blessing of Resurrection",b="Tiza Battleforge's final blessing tests whether your heart is ready to wield the Symbol of Life. The relic answers only to one prepared to channel the Light's greatest gifts. Prove your worth, and Tiza grants you a sacred scroll that lets you call fallen comrades back from death. Ironforge needs this power against the Scourge and the Dark Iron clan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a sacred trial for holy champions in Ironforge. By proving your spiritual readiness, you learn to channel the Light and bring fallen companions back to life.",al={"what is tome of divinity","tome of divinity quest","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who is Tiza Battleforge?",a="Tiza Battleforge is a revered dwarven teacher of the Light in Ironforge. She gives the final blessing to champions ready to wield the power of resurrection.",al={"who is tiza battleforge","where is tiza battleforge","find tiza battleforge"}},{q="Who sends you to Tiza Battleforge?",a="After you complete an earlier trial in the field, Tiza Battleforge's husband directs you to her. He is already in Ironforge and sends you to his wife with pride and encouragement.",al={"who gives this quest","tiza husband","who sent me to tiza"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a holy item used in a paladin's trials. It answers only to a champion whose devotion makes them worthy to call a fallen ally back from death.",al={"what is symbol of life","symbol of life paladin","how does resurrection work"}},{q="What ability do you learn from completing this quest?",a="When you present yourself to Tiza Battleforge, she blesses you with a sacred scroll that teaches Redemption, the power to restore fallen allies to life.",al={"what power do i learn","resurrect spell quest","paladin revive quest"}},{q="Why are champions of the Light needed by Ironforge?",a="Ironforge needs champions of the Light against the Scourge and the Dark Iron dwarves. Their healing and holy defense help protect the realm.",al={"who are ironforge enemies","why fight dark irons and scourge","battlefield enemies"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you complete a sacred rite in Ironforge and receive the Light's power to raise the fallen.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you undertake this trial in Ironforge and earn the Battleforge family's gratitude on behalf of the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you train in the Light to face the Scourge and the Dark Iron clan."},kw={"ironforge","paladin","redemption","resurrection","symbol of life","the tome of divinity","tiza battleforge","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:tiza-battleforge","zone:ironforge","topic:light","topic:scourge"},m={id=1785},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1786"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Elwynn, faith and sacrifice are tested when a Defias ambush leaves Henze Faulk dead at Heroes' Vigil. With the Symbol of Life, you are sent to restore him and hinder the brotherhood's schemes.",h="In Elwynn, faith and sacrifice are tested when a Defias ambush leaves Henze Faulk dead at Heroes' Vigil.",sec={{t="Ambush at Heroes' Vigil",b="Henze Faulk and Gazin traveled to Heroes' Vigil after hearing that Defias Brotherhood agents had crossed into northeastern Elwynn Forest. The island lies in the middle of Stone Cairn Lake. The scouts sought proof to present to the king's royal advisors, so they tried to ambush two conspirators reviewing plans.\n\nDefias spellcasters soon joined the fight, and the scouts were overwhelmed. Henze stood his ground against the mages, sacrificing himself to give Gazin time to escape with his life.",sp=0},{t="The Gift of Resurrection",b="Ordinary medicine cannot restore Henze; only the Holy Light can. With the Symbol of Life, you are sent to find his fallen body on the island in Stone Cairn Lake.\n\nYour faith, channeled through the sacred artifact, brings Henze back to life. This test shows a paladin's spiritual bond and readiness to serve the Light in Stormwind's defense.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Henze Faulk?",a="Henze Faulk is a defender who went with Gazin to Heroes' Vigil on Stone Cairn Lake to find proof of Defias infiltration. He held off the mages so Gazin could escape, and fell to their spells. The Symbol of Life later restored him to life.",al={"who is henze faulk","henze faulk","where is henze"}},{q="Where is Heroes' Vigil?",a="Heroes' Vigil is an island in the middle of Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn Forest. Defias mages and rogues have made an outpost there, where they pore over plans.",al={"where is heroes vigil","heroes vigil location","heroes vigil island"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a holy item that channels a paladin's faith to restore the fallen. It needs true spiritual conviction, making its use on Henze Faulk a test of a paladin's calling.",al={"what is symbol of life","how to rez henze","symbol of life use"}},{q="Who directs the rescue of Henze Faulk?",a="Gazin Tenorm asks for help after escaping the Defias on the island. Wounded, he lies near the altar in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He is a friend of Duthorian Rall, the paladin leader who sent the initiate to him.",al={"who sent me to henze","duthroian or gazin","quest giver tome of divinity"}},{q="What are the Defias doing at Heroes' Vigil?",a="Defias operatives have crossed into northeastern Elwynn and gathered at Heroes' Vigil to study documents and coordinate their operations. Henze and Gazin sought those documents as proof for the king's advisors.",al={"why defias at heroes vigil","what are defias doing stone cairn lake","defias plans elwynn"}},{q="Why did Henze and Gazin go to Stone Cairn Lake?",a="Henze Faulk and Gazin went to Stone Cairn Lake after hearing reports of Defias infiltrators. They meant to ambush the conspirators and recover written proof of their plans for King Anduin's advisors in Stormwind.",al={"why were henze and gazin there","henze and gazin mission"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you prove your faith and bond with the Light by wielding the Symbol of Life to restore a fallen ally.",["faction:Alliance"]="Defias spellcasters in northeastern Elwynn threaten Stormwind's heartland. Gathering intelligence at Heroes' Vigil matters to the Alliance."},kw={"defias","duthorian","gazin","henze faulk","heroes vigil","paladin","resurrection","stone cairn lake","symbol of life","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:henze-faulk","subzone:heroes-vigil","subzone:stone-cairn-lake"},m={id=1786},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1787"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="You are proving your devotion to the Light through a trial for Alliance paladins. After helping an injured scout in Elwynn Forest, you face Defias Rogue Wizards and seek papers that threaten the realm.",h="You are proving your devotion to the Light through a trial for Alliance paladins.",sec={{t="A Paladin's Trial",b="As a paladin in training, you are being tested in Elwynn Forest. Henze was injured while watching illicit activity on an island. Help him learn how far the Defias have spread there.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrators in Elwynn",b="Henze found Defias Rogue Wizards studying secret papers on the island, but his injuries leave him unable to fight. You are sent to defeat the rogue spellcasters and recover their script. Then bring the intelligence safely to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.",sp=1},{t="Defending the Kingdom",b="The Defias Script confirms the brotherhood threatens nearby lands, including Heroes' Vigil. Bring the stolen intelligence to the Cathedral of Light. Your return proves your devotion to the Light and that Henze survived.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is involved in this quest?",a="You meet Henze Faulk, who lies injured on an island in Elwynn Forest. Afterward, report to Gazin Tenorm in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind.",al={"who gives this quest","who gives tome of divinity","where do i get tome of divinity"}},{q="Who is Henze?",a="Henze is an ally in the paladin trials who was injured while watching Defias activity. Unable to fight, he sends you to secure proof of the brotherhood's infiltration.",al={"who is henze","henze faulk lore","who is the injured guy"}},{q="Who is Gazin Tenorm?",a="Gazin Tenorm is Henze's friend and a friend of Duthorian Rall. He can be found near the altar in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He barely escaped the Defias at Heroes' Vigil and wants to know Henze is safe.",al={"who is gazin tenorm","where is gazin tenorm","gazin stormwind"}},{q="Why are Defias Rogue Wizards operating on the island?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has positions throughout Elwynn Forest. Its rogue wizards study plans and coordinate operations, and their documents show what they intend in the region.",al={"why are defias in elwynn","defias rogue wizards","defias script"}},{q="What is Heroes' Vigil?",a="Heroes' Vigil is a place in Elwynn Forest threatened by Defias operations. Gazin Tenorm hopes that stopping nearby rogue wizards and taking their papers will protect it from further harm.",al={"what is heroes vigil","heroes vigil elwynn","is heroes vigil safe"}},{q="What is the Defias Script?",a="The Defias Script is written orders or correspondence carried by Defias Rogue Wizards. It proves their infiltration and details their immediate schemes in Elwynn Forest.",al={"what is defias script","what are the papers","defias papers elwynn"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a trial of devotion and courage. It tests your resolve to protect the innocent and uphold the Light against threats such as the Defias Brotherhood.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help uncover Defias movements and documents in Elwynn Forest. This intelligence goes to Stormwind's defenders."},kw={"defias rogue wizards","defias script","elwynn forest","gazin tenorm","henze faulk","heroes' vigil","paladin quest","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:gazin-tenorm","subzone:heroes-vigil","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1787},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1788"] = {t="quest",n="The Tome of Divinity",z="general",s="In Stormwind, paladins face a trial of faith in The Tome of Divinity. An initiate proves mastery of the Symbol of Life by restoring a fallen ally, then earns Duthorian Rall's blessing to wield resurrection.",h="In Stormwind, paladins face a trial of faith in The Tome of Divinity.",sec={{t="Return to the Cathedral",b="After restoring the fallen Henze with the Symbol of Life in the field, an aspiring paladin returns to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. The Defias papers recovered from the island are to go to the King's advisors through Gazin Tenorm. First, Duthorian Rall awaits word of the initiate's success.",sp=0},{t="The Gift of Resurrection",b="Calling on the Light to restore the dead is no small gift. Duthorian Rall sees mastery of the Symbol of Life as proof that an initiate has the faith and spiritual strength for one of the paladin order's highest callings: resurrection. With this rite mastered, the paladin can safeguard allies on battlefields across the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Tome of Divinity?",a="The Tome of Divinity is a culminating trial for paladins learning to wield the Holy Light. Here, an initiate reports to Duthorian Rall after proving capable of channeling the Light to restore the fallen.",al={"tome of divinity","what is this quest","tome of divinity paladin"}},{q="Who is Duthorian Rall?",a="Duthorian Rall is a high-ranking paladin trainer at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. He oversees paladin initiates and judges their readiness to wield sacred rites.",al={"who is duthorian","duthorian rall role","where is duthorian"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a sacred focus for calling on the Light to restore the dead. Mastering its power proves an initiate is ready to wield the paladin's power of resurrection.",al={"symbol of life purpose","what did symbol of life do"}},{q="Who was Henze?",a="Henze is an ally who fell in the field and was restored with the Symbol of Life during an initiate's trials. The deed showed the paladin's resolve and faith to reverse death.",al={"who is henze","henze lore","henze paladin quest"}},{q="How does a paladin earn the power of resurrection?",a="Resurrection is one of a paladin's highest honors. Through deep faith and attunement to the Holy Light, a paladin learns to call fallen companions back from death's threshold.",al={"paladin resurrection lore","how do paladins revive"}},{q="Why is the script being taken to the King's advisors?",a="The script is the Defias papers taken from the island. Once Duthorian Rall has looked them over, Gazin Tenorm will carry them to the King's advisors as proof that the Defias have infiltrated Elwynn.",al={"kings advisors script","what script goes to stormwind"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, this trial marks your passage into true service to the Light. You master the sacred power to return fallen companions to life.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you train among Stormwind's paladins at the Cathedral of Light. Their work preserves the lives of Alliance defenders and strengthens the kingdom's defenses."},kw={"duthorian","duthorian rall","henze","paladin","resurrection","stormwind","symbol of life","the tome of divinity","tome of divinity"},rel={"npc:duthorian-rall","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=1788},src={"In-game quest text: The Tome of Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:1792"] = {t="quest",n="Whirlwind Weapon",z="general",s="A warrior's chosen weapon awaits the storm Cyclonian left behind. The whirlwind heart can bind the elemental's fury into a forged vessel.",h="A warrior's chosen weapon awaits the storm Cyclonian left behind.",sec={{t="Infusing the Storm",b="After Cyclonian falls and the warrior claims its heart, a craftsperson prepares a weapon to hold the storm's power. The heart is fused into the chosen arm, turning forged metal into a channel for elemental fury.",sp=0},{t="The Power of Cyclonian",b="Cyclonian's heart holds the violence of howling winds and tempestuous gales. Bound into a forged weapon, it lends the wielder the living might of the storm alongside their own martial skill. Each strike carries the force of the defeated elemental, whose storm now rages in the hands of its vanquisher.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Whirlwind Weapon quest?",a="A warrior can bind Cyclonian's whirlwind heart into a chosen weapon, joining the elemental's power with the warrior's own strength.",al={"what is whirlwind weapon","whirlwind weapon lore","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is Cyclonian?",a="Cyclonian is an elemental manifestation of wind and storm. Its defeat yields the whirlwind heart, which can bind primal wind energy into a physical weapon.",al={"who is cyclonian","cyclonian lore","what is cyclonian"}},{q="What is the whirlwind heart?",a="The whirlwind heart is Cyclonian's core, claimed when the elemental is defeated. It holds the tempest's fury and can be bound into a forged vessel chosen by the warrior.",al={"what is whirlwind heart","cyclonian heart","heart of cyclonian"}},{q="How is the weapon empowered?",a="The warrior chooses a forged weapon and has Cyclonian's whirlwind heart bound into it. The elemental's fury then courses through the steel.",al={"how is whirlwind weapon made","vessel of choice","forging whirlwind weapon"}},{q="What choices are offered for the weapon?",a="A warrior chooses the weapon that will receive Cyclonian's storm essence.",al={"which weapon can i pick","whirlwind choices","what weapons are offered"}},{q="Why is Cyclonian's power sought after?",a="Warriors seek Cyclonian's power to command the fury of a living gale through their weapons.",al={"why does warrior want whirlwind weapon","whirlwind weapon importance"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can claim a weapon infused with the tempestuous force of Cyclonian."},kw={"cyclonian","elemental","storm","vessel","warrior weapon","whirlwind heart","whirlwind weapon"},rel={"quest:1712"},m={id=1792},src={"In-game quest text: Whirlwind Weapon"},fv=true}
E["quest:1884"] = {t="quest",n="Ju-Ju Heaps",z="general",s="On the Echo Isles, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy Zalazane's ju-ju heaps. Their corruption threatens Durotar's flow of magic.",h="On the Echo Isles, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy Zalazane's ju-ju heaps.",sec={{t="Tainted Heaps",b="From Sen'jin Village, Un'thuwa asks you to destroy the heaps Zalazane placed among his huts on the main Echo Isle. The tainted fetishes corrupt wildlife and strengthen warlocks and infernal creatures. Left alone, they may change Durotar's flow of magic forever.",sp=0},{t="Un'thuwa's Sense",b="Un'thuwa senses the heaps have been destroyed. With time and luck, she believes Durotar's magic will return to its normal flow. She praises your deed for your people and says you have proved your worth to the Horde's classes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who placed the ju-ju heaps?",a="Zalazane, a warlock of the Echo Isles, placed the tainted heaps among his huts on the main isle.",al={"who made the heaps","zalazane heaps","ju ju source"}},{q="What do the heaps do?",a="The heaps corrupt wildlife and strengthen warlocks and infernal creatures.",al={"what are juju heaps","heaps effect","why destroy juju"}},{q="Where are the ju-ju heaps?",a="Zalazane placed them among his huts on the main Echo Isle.",al={"where heaps","echo isle heaps","ju ju location"}},{q="Who asks me to destroy them?",a="Un'thuwa in Sen'jin Village asks you to destroy the ju-ju heaps.",al={"who gives this","unthuwa request","who wants heaps gone"}},{q="Why does Durotar's magic matter here?",a="The heaps disrupt Durotar's normal flow of magic. If they remain, that flow may change forever.",al={"magic flow","durotar magic","why care about magic"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Un'thuwa calls this a deed for your people and says you have proved your worth to the Horde's classes."},kw={"durotar","echo isles","ju-ju heaps","magic","sen'jin village","tainted fetishes","un'thuwa","zalazane"},rel={"quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:warlock"},m={id=1884},src={"In-game quest text: Ju-Ju Heaps"},fv=true}
E["quest:1920"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Blue Recluse",z="general",s="Jennea Cannon asks you to investigate strange invisible creatures in the Blue Recluse tavern. She fears a mana rift has opened there.",h="Jennea Cannon asks you to investigate strange invisible creatures in the Blue Recluse tavern.",sec={{t="At the Blue Recluse",b="Jennea Cannon reports a disturbance at the Blue Recluse in the Mage Quarter. Invisible creatures now wander the tavern, and she fears a mana rift has formed. You are asked to make the creatures visible and capture them in containment coffers. Jennea needs the captured creatures for study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is happening at the Blue Recluse?",a="Invisible creatures are wandering the Blue Recluse, and Jennea Cannon fears a mana rift has formed there.",al={"blue recluse disturbance","what's wrong at the tavern"}},{q="Who sent me to investigate?",a="Jennea Cannon asks you to investigate the disturbance at the Blue Recluse.",al={"who asked me","jennea blue recluse"}},{q="Why does Jennea want the creatures?",a="Jennea wants to study the creatures to determine why they arrived.",al={"why capture them","what are the creatures for"}},{q="How do I make the creatures visible?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation makes the creatures visible inside the tavern.",al={"cantation use","make creatures visible"}},{q="What does Jennea fear has happened?",a="Jennea fears a mana rift has formed at the Blue Recluse.",al={"mana rift tavern","rift at blue recluse"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you bring the captured creatures to Jennea Cannon so they can be studied."},kw={"blue recluse","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","invisible creatures","jennea cannon","mage quarter","mana rift"},rel={"subzone:mage-quarter","npc:jennea-cannon","topic:mage","item:cantation-of-manifestation","item:chest-of-containment-coffers","item:filled-containment-coffer"},m={id=1920},src={"In-game quest text: Investigate the Blue Recluse"},fv=true}
E["quest:1947"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to the Marsh",z="general",s="Your class sends you to Dustwallow Marsh, where Tabetha’s knowledge can help you earn your wand.",h="Your class sends you to Dustwallow Marsh, where Tabetha’s knowledge can help you earn your wand.",sec={{t="Tabetha’s Cottage",b="West of Theramore and just north of the Stonemaul Ruins, Tabetha lives in a cottage. Your class asks you to speak with the hermit and learn from her vast knowledge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tabetha?",a="Tabetha is a hermit in Dustwallow Marsh, known for her vast knowledge.",al={"tabetha","marsh hermit","who is the hermit"}},{q="Where is Tabetha’s cottage?",a="Tabetha’s cottage is west of Theramore and just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tabetha location","where is tabetha","tabetha shack"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Tabetha?",a="Speaking with Tabetha begins your effort to earn your class’s wand.",al={"why tabetha","wand quest","earn my wand"}}},kw={"cottage","dustwallow marsh","journey to the marsh","stonemaul ruins","tabetha","theramore","wand"},rel={"npc:tabetha","zone:dustwallow","subzone:stonemaul-ruins"},m={id=1947},src={"In-game quest text: Journey to the Marsh"},fv=true}
E["quest:201"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Camp",z="general",s="Krazek has heard Hemet Nesingwary may be in Stranglethorn Vale. He asks you to find the hunters' camp near Lake Nazferiti and confirm the report.",h="Krazek has heard Hemet Nesingwary may be in Stranglethorn Vale.",sec={{t="Reports in the Jungle",b="Booty Bay reports place a hunters' camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale. Krazek has heard it lies along the river, just beyond the Venture Company's mining claim near Lake Nazferiti. The jungle is lawless, with dangers and competing interests. An armed camp draws notice.",sp=0},{t="A Renowned Marksman",b="Hemet Nesingwary may be among the hunters at the camp. The renowned dwarven marksman is known across the lands as an elite explorer with influential ties. Krazek sends you upriver to learn whether the legendary hunter has arrived.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the task to investigate the camp?",a="Krazek, an operative in Booty Bay, sends you to find the camp and report where it lies.",al={"who wants camp investigated","who gave this quest","krazek booty bay"}},{q="Who is Hemet Nesingwary?",a="Hemet Nesingwary is a renowned dwarven big-game hunter and explorer. Reports in Booty Bay place him among hunters camping near Lake Nazferiti, and his reputation and connections have drawn interest.",al={"hemet nesingwary stranglethorn","who is hemet nesingwary","famous dwarf hunter stranglethorn"}},{q="Where is the hunters' camp located?",a="The hunters' camp lies upriver from the Venture Company's mining operations, along Lake Nazferiti in northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"hunters camp location","where is nesingwary camp","where is the camp upriver"}},{q="Why is Krazek interested in this hunting camp?",a="Reports say Hemet Nesingwary may be at the camp. His influence and connections make Krazek cautious and curious.",al={"why does krazek care","why investigate hunters","krazek motive"}},{q="What is the hunters' relationship to the Venture Company?",a="The hunters are separate from the Venture Company. Their camp lies upriver from the company's mining outfit near Lake Nazferiti, which marks its location.",al={"venture company connection","are hunters with venture co","venture co lake nazferiti"}},{q="To whom do you report after finding the camp?",a="After you find and scout the riverside camp, return south to Booty Bay and report directly to Krazek.",al={"what do you do after finding camp","who to report to","where to turn in investigate camp"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may be drawn to the rumored gathering led by Hemet Nesingwary. There, you can test your tracking and marksmanship in the jungle.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may take pride in Hemet Nesingwary, one of the most famous dwarven marksmen and adventurers. His reported presence in Stranglethorn Vale's distant southern wilds may stir your curiosity."},kw={"booty bay","hemet nesingwary","hunters camp","investigate the camp","krazek","lake nazferiti","stranglethorn vale","venture company"},rel={"quest:5762","subzone:lake-nazferiti","subzone:booty-bay","topic:venture-company","topic:hunter"},m={id=201},src={"In-game quest text: Investigate the Camp"},fv=true}
E["quest:2158"] = {t="quest",n="Rest and Relaxation",z="general",s="From Northshire, new Alliance adventurers follow the road south to Goldshire for rest and welcome. At the Lion's Pride Inn, Innkeeper Farley offers food, drink, and a place by the hearth.",h="From Northshire, new Alliance adventurers follow the road south to Goldshire for rest and welcome.",sec={{t="A Haven on the Road",b="Weary travelers leave Northshire and follow the road south to Goldshire. It leads straight to the Lion's Pride Inn, where Innkeeper Farley welcomes those setting out into Elwynn Forest. For new adventurers, the inn is the first major outpost beyond the Abbey, with shelter and hot meals.",sp=0},{t="Farley's Hearth and Hospitality",b="Innkeeper Farley welcomes those who are tired and cold. Mention your referral, and you can settle by the open fire for a warm meal, sturdy ale, and a rest before continuing through Elwynn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="The Lion's Pride Inn is in Goldshire, south along the main road from Northshire Valley. Follow the road south to the tavern at the heart of town.",al={"where is lions pride inn","how to get to lion's pride inn","find lions pride"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Farley?",a="Innkeeper Farley runs the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. A close friend of contacts in Northshire, he welcomes weary adventurers with food, drink, and a warm hearth.",al={"who is innkeeper farley","farley lion's pride"}},{q="What is the purpose of Rest and Relaxation?",a="You travel from Northshire to Goldshire, where Innkeeper Farley offers food, drink, and lodging at the Lion's Pride Inn.",al={"what is the purpose of this quest","why go to lion's pride inn"}},{q="Does Innkeeper Farley really offer discounted food and drink?",a="Mention your referral to Innkeeper Farley, and you can ask about discounted food and drink while you recover from your travels.",al={"discount at lions pride","do i get cheaper food farley"}},{q="Why is rest important for traveling adventurers?",a="Travel across Elwynn is hard and dangerous. At an inn, you can shelter from the wilderness, warm yourself by the fire, recover, and replenish supplies before setting out again.",al={"why do adventurers need rest","rest and relaxation lore"}},{q="What is the motto of the Lion's Pride Inn?",a="Innkeeper Farley says the Lion's Pride Inn's motto is 'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.' Weary guests can find comfort by his hearth.",al={"what is lions pride inn motto","lions pride slogan"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Lion's Pride Inn is a haven and gathering place for Alliance travelers in Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="As a human recruit leaving Northshire Valley, you follow the southern road to Goldshire. There, Innkeeper Farley offers familiar hospitality near Stormwind."},kw={"alliance tavern","elwynn forest","goldshire","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","northshire","rest and relaxation"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-farley","subzone:lion-s-pride-inn"},m={id=2158},src={"In-game quest text: Rest and Relaxation"},fv=true}
E["quest:2218"] = {t="quest",n="Road to Salvation",z="general",s="Hogral Bakkan sends you to Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge. Hulfdan tests whether you think yourself a scoundrel fit to join his chosen few.",h="Hogral Bakkan sends you to Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.",sec={{t="Hulfdan's Test",b="Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge wants to know whether you see yourself as a scoundrel. He is considering you for a place among the Hidden Circle's chosen few. His answer depends on how highly you think of yourself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking to speak with me?",a="Hogral Bakkan sends you to speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.",al={"who is hulfdan","hulfdan blackbeard"}},{q="What is the Hidden Circle?",a="The Hidden Circle is an organization with chosen members and officers. Hulfdan Blackbeard is looking for scoundrels to join its chosen few.",al={"hidden circle","what circle"}},{q="Why does Hulfdan call me a scoundrel?",a="Hulfdan asks whether you think yourself a scoundrel fit to join the Hidden Circle's chosen few.",al={"hulfdan scoundrel","why scoundrel"}},{q="What does Hulfdan want from me?",a="Hulfdan wants to speak with you about becoming one of the Hidden Circle's chosen few.",al={"what hulfdan wants","blackbeard recruit"}}},kw={"chosen few","hidden circle","hulfdan blackbeard","ironforge","road to salvation","scoundrel"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=2218},src={"In-game quest text: Road to Salvation"},fv=true}
E["quest:231"] = {t="quest",n="A Daughter's Love",z="general",s="Sarah Ladimore asks you to bring her ring to Morgan Ladimore’s grave. The meeting there bears on Morgan’s troubled soul.",h="Sarah Ladimore asks you to bring her ring to Morgan Ladimore’s grave.",sec={{t="At the Grave",b="A voice on the wind answers when you bring Sarah Ladimore’s ring to Morgan Ladimore’s grave. Morgan wonders whether Sarah still lives, and says the ring lifts a weight from his shoulders. He entrusts you with his sword, Archeus, and asks you to keep the ring as he speaks to Lys, his love.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens when I take Sarah’s ring to Morgan’s grave?",a="A voice on the wind responds. Morgan wonders if Sarah is still alive and says the ring lifts a weight from his shoulders.",al={"sarah ring grave","morgan ladimore ring","a daughter's love ending"}},{q="Who is the voice at the grave?",a="Morgan Ladimore speaks as a ghostly voice on the wind.",al={"ghost voice","who speaks at the grave","morgan ghost"}},{q="What does Morgan give me?",a="Morgan gives you his sword, Archeus.",al={"morgan sword","archeus sword","take archeus"}},{q="What does Morgan ask me to keep?",a="Morgan asks you to keep Sarah’s ring.",al={"keep the ring","morgan's ring","ring at grave"}},{q="Who is Lys?",a="Morgan calls Lys his love.",al={"lys morgan","morgan's love","lys ladimore"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Morgan says Archeus was forged to do good and asks you to carry on the Light through it."},kw={"a daughter's love","archeus","grave","lys","morgan ladimore","ring","sarah ladimore"},rel={"topic:light"},m={id=231},src={"In-game quest text: A Daughter's Love"},fv=true}
E["quest:2342"] = {t="quest",n="Reclaimed Treasures",z="general",s="Patrick Garrett asks you to recover his family treasure from Uldaman. He is waiting for it in the Undercity.",h="Patrick Garrett asks you to recover his family treasure from Uldaman.",sec={{t="A Family Chest",b="The family chest is in Uldaman's South Common Hall. Patrick Garrett waits in the Undercity for the treasure kept inside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the treasure?",a="Patrick Garrett asks you to bring him his family treasure in the Undercity.",al={"patrick garrett","who wants it"}},{q="Where is the family chest?",a="The family chest is in the South Common Hall of Uldaman.",al={"chest location","where's the treasure"}},{q="Where do I bring the treasure?",a="Bring Patrick Garrett's family treasure to him in the Undercity.",al={"where to take it","undercity treasure"}}},kw={"family chest","family treasure","patrick garrett","reclaimed treasures","south common hall","uldaman","undercity"},rel={"subzone:uldaman","zone:undercity"},m={id=2342},src={"In-game quest text: Reclaimed Treasures"},fv=true}
E["quest:2360"] = {t="quest",n="Mathias and the Defias",z="general",s="In Westfall, SI:7 has found the Defias unusually active. You are sent to Agent Kearnen near an abandoned Alliance watch tower for a debriefing.",h="In Westfall, SI:7 has found the Defias unusually active.",sec={{t="The Watch Tower",b="The Defias have seized an abandoned Alliance watch tower southeast of Sentinel Hill. SI:7 reports they use it as a base to smuggle goods from the Redridge supply route. You are sent to Westfall to find Agent Kearnen, hidden near the tower, and hear her debriefing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is happening in Westfall?",a="SI:7 reports unusually heavy Defias activity in Westfall. The Defias have taken an abandoned Alliance watch tower and use it to smuggle goods from the Redridge supply route.",al={"defias in westfall","westfall defias activity"}},{q="Where is the Defias base?",a="The Defias base is an abandoned Alliance watch tower southeast of Sentinel Hill.",al={"defias tower","where is their base"}},{q="Who is Agent Kearnen?",a="Agent Kearnen is the SI:7 agent you are sent to find near the tower for a debriefing.",al={"kearnen","who is kearnen"}},{q="What does SI:7 want me to do?",a="SI:7 sends you to Westfall to find Agent Kearnen, hidden near the tower, and receive a debriefing.",al={"si7 task","find kearnen"}},{q="What are the Defias smuggling?",a="The Defias are smuggling goods from the Redridge supply route.",al={"defias goods","redridge supplies"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Defias have taken an abandoned Alliance watch tower in Westfall and use it as a base for smuggling."},kw={"agent kearnen","defias","mathias","redridge","sentinel hill","si:7","watch tower","westfall"},rel={"quest:2300","zone:westfall","subzone:sentinel-hill","topic:alliance"},m={id=2360},src={"In-game quest text: Mathias and the Defias"},fv=true}
E["quest:2383"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Parchment",z="general",s="A message waits for you in the Valley of Trials, sent while you were away. Frang, your class trainer, is outside the Den.",h="A message waits for you in the Valley of Trials, sent while you were away.",sec={{t="A Message from Frang",b="The parchment asks you to read its words and speak with Frang. Your class trainer waits outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the parchment?",a="The parchment appears to have come from Frang, your class trainer.",al={"parchment sender","who wrote it"}},{q="Where can I find Frang?",a="Frang waits outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where's Frang","Frang location"}},{q="What does Frang want?",a="Frang has words for you when you are ready.",al={"why Frang wants me","parchment message"}},{q="What should I do with the parchment?",a="Read the parchment, then speak with Frang in the Valley of Trials.",al={"read parchment","simple parchment"}}},kw={"class trainer","den","frang","parchment","simple parchment","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={id=2383},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Parchment"},fv=true}
E["quest:2608"] = {t="quest",n="The Touch of Zanzil",z="general",s="Doc Mixilpixil examines you and seeks a cause for your alarming condition. He asks to draw blood before consulting his colleagues about a cure.",h="Doc Mixilpixil examines you and seeks a cause for your alarming condition.",sec={{t="The examination",b="Doc Mixilpixil thinks you look worse than death and says he needs a blood sample to help you. You can lie down for his examination, though his warning suggests the treatment may hurt. Once he has examined you, he calls Dr. Montgomery and Mr. Noarm to confer about your case.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is examining me?",a="Doc Mixilpixil examines you and asks to draw blood so he can look for the cause of your condition.",al={"doc mixilpixil","who's the doctor","mixilpixil"}},{q="Why does Doc Mixilpixil want my blood?",a="Doc Mixilpixil says he needs a blood sample to find the cause and help you.",al={"blood sample","why blood","draw blood"}},{q="Who are Dr. Montgomery and Mr. Noarm?",a="Dr. Montgomery and Mr. Noarm are Doc Mixilpixil's colleagues, whom he calls to confer about your case.",al={"montgomery and noarm","doc's colleagues","noarm"}},{q="What happens after the examination?",a="After examining you, Doc Mixilpixil calls Dr. Montgomery and Mr. Noarm to confer.",al={"after the exam","what next","doctor conference"}}},kw={"blood","cure","doc mixilpixil","dr. montgomery","examination","mr. noarm","the touch of zanzil","zanzil"},m={id=2608},src={"In-game quest text: The Touch of Zanzil"},fv=true}
E["quest:2609"] = {t="quest",n="The Touch of Zanzil",z="general",s="Doc Mixilpixil asks you to gather supplies for the 'itis'. He says the ailment will not cure itself.",h="Doc Mixilpixil asks you to gather supplies for the 'itis'.",sec={{t="A Doctor's Request",b="Doc Mixilpixil needs you to bring him Simple Wildflowers, a Leaded Vial, a Bronze Tube, and a Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread. He says the 'itis' needs a cure, and these are the supplies he asks you to bring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for these supplies?",a="Doc Mixilpixil asks you to bring the supplies.",al={"who wants them","doc mixilpixil request"}},{q="What does Doc Mixilpixil need?",a="He needs Simple Wildflowers, a Leaded Vial, a Bronze Tube, and a Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread.",al={"what items","supplies list"}},{q="What is the 'itis'?",a="Doc Mixilpixil calls the ailment the 'itis'.",al={"what illness","itis"}}},kw={"bronze tube","doc mixilpixil","itis","leaded vial","light chartreuse silk thread","simple wildflowers","zanzil"},m={id=2609},src={"In-game quest text: The Touch of Zanzil"},fv=true}
E["quest:271"] = {t="quest",n="Vyrin's Revenge",z="general",s="At Farstrider Lodge, a hunter asks you to settle an old score with Ol' Sooty. The bear scarred Daryl the Youngling during a hunt a year ago.",h="At Farstrider Lodge, a hunter asks you to settle an old score with Ol' Sooty.",sec={{t="An Old Scar",b="A hunter at Farstrider Lodge asks you to face Ol' Sooty, the bear that scarred Daryl the Youngling. The lodge's hunters had failed to bring it down, and Daryl tried his luck a year ago. His attempt left him with the mark over his eye. Ol' Sooty keeps to its lair in the hills above Thelsamar.",sp=0},{t="At the Lodge",b="At Farstrider Lodge, you bring Daryl the Youngling proof of Ol' Sooty's end. He recognizes the bear's head and touches his scar. Then he begins to shake and begs you to take it away.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ol' Sooty?",a="Ol' Sooty is the bear that scarred Daryl the Youngling during a hunt a year ago.",al={"ol sooty bear","sooty","bear scarred daryl"}},{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl the Youngling is a skilled hunter at Farstrider Lodge. Ol' Sooty left him with a scar over his eye.",al={"daryl backstory","who's daryl","daryl scar"}},{q="Where does Ol' Sooty live?",a="Ol' Sooty can be found around its lair in the hills above Thelsamar.",al={"where is ol sooty","sooty location","bear lair"}},{q="Why does the hunter want Ol' Sooty killed?",a="Ol' Sooty scarred Daryl during a hunt a year ago, and a hunter at Farstrider Lodge wants payback.",al={"why kill sooty","vyrin revenge why","daryl revenge"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you are asked to face the bear that eluded the hunters of Farstrider Lodge and scarred Daryl."},kw={"bear","daryl the youngling","farstrider lodge","ol' sooty","scar","thelsamar","vyrin's revenge"},rel={"subzone:farstrider-lodge","subzone:thelsamar","npc:daryl-the-youngling","topic:hunter"},m={id=271},src={"In-game quest text: Vyrin's Revenge"},fv=true}
E["quest:272"] = {t="quest",n="Trial of the Sea Lion",z="general",s="Druids in Moonglade seek the sea lion’s spirit through a sacred rite. They recover two scattered pendant halves for agility and endurance, then unite them at the Shrine of Remulos to prepare for Aquatic Form.",h="Druids in Moonglade seek the sea lion’s spirit through a sacred rite.",sec={{t="The Path to Aquatic Form",b="Druid initiates in Moonglade undergo trials of attunement as they prepare to navigate Azeroth’s deep waters. The Trial of the Sea Lion follows earlier preparations in their spiritual training. Dendrite Starblaze oversees it in Nighthaven, where initiates learn to balance the sea lion’s graceful speed with its resilient stamina. Both are needed to take its form and withstand the ocean depths.",sp=0},{t="Agility and Endurance",b="The trial centers on reuniting the two halves of the Pendant of the Sea Lion. One represents the sea lion’s agility as it glides through turbulent currents. The other represents its endurance, the fortitude to dive long into freezing water without faltering. Initiates seek guidance from Moonglade’s inhabitants as they search across the world for the scattered relics.",sp=0},{t="The Shrine of Remulos",b="Once both halves are found, the initiate brings them near the Shrine of Remulos, where they can be joined into one talisman. The shrine’s energies bind agility and endurance in harmony. The initiate then presents the restored pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven. With the pendant, the druid shows readiness to embrace the sea lion aspect and awaken Aquatic Form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Trial of the Sea Lion?",a="Druids in Moonglade recover two pendant halves and unite them at the Shrine of Remulos. The halves represent agility and endurance, and the restored pendant is presented to Dendrite Starblaze as part of the path to Aquatic Form.",al={"trial of the sea lion quest","what is trial of the sea lion","sea lion trial"}},{q="Who gives the Trial of the Sea Lion quest?",a="Warden Tajarri at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade gives the trial. Initiates seek guidance from local residents, join the pendant halves near the shrine, then take the finished pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven.",al={"who gives trial of the sea lion","where to start trial of the sea lion","trial of the sea lion quest giver"}},{q="What do the two pendant halves represent?",a="The halves represent the sea lion’s agility and endurance. One reflects the grace and swiftness to glide through deep water; the other, the stamina and resilience for long journeys underwater. Druids must respect and embody both traits equally to master their shapeshifting arts.",al={"what are the pendant halves","pendant halves meaning","agility and endurance halves"}},{q="Where are the pendant halves located?",a="Initiates learn where the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance are hidden by speaking with Moonglade’s residents. Local druids and villagers give clues about the distant waters where each half was lost or concealed.",al={"how to find pendant halves","where to find the pendant halves","pendant of the sea lion halves location"}},{q="Where do you assemble the Pendant of the Sea Lion?",a="The halves must be joined near the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade. The shrine’s sacred aura helps unite agility and endurance in one talisman.",al={"how to combine pendant halves","where to fuse pendant halves","where is shrine of remulos pendant"}},{q="Why must druids balance agility and endurance?",a="Dendrite Starblaze teaches that agility and endurance must be balanced beneath the water. Speed without stamina brings exhaustion, while endurance without swiftness leaves a swimmer helpless against strong currents. Druids need both traits to embody the sea lion’s spirit.",al={"why agility and endurance","sea lion traits druid","meaning of the sea lion trial"}},{q="What is gained by completing the trial?",a="Completing the trial earns the restored Pendant of the Sea Lion and fulfills a major trial required to earn Aquatic Form. Mastering agility and endurance gives the initiate a spiritual foundation for taking a form that can breathe and swim swiftly underwater.",al={"what do you get from trial of the sea lion","sea lion trial reward","does this give aquatic form"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="This rite is exclusive to druids. It tests their spiritual maturity and balance before they may commune with aquatic spirits and adopt the sea lion’s form.",["race:NightElf"]="As long-standing custodians of Moonglade and the Cenarion Circle, night elf druids revere Dendrite Starblaze’s teachings and the sacred ground around the Shrine of Remulos.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren druids newly welcomed into the Cenarion Circle, undertaking the trial in Moonglade strengthens their communion with nature spirits and deepens their ties with their night elf mentors."},kw={"aquatic form","dendrite starblaze","half pendant of aquatic agility","half pendant of aquatic endurance","moonglade","nighthaven","pendant of the sea lion","shrine of remulos","trial of the sea lion"},rel={"item:pendant-of-the-sea-lion","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:31","npc:remulos","subzone:nighthaven","quest:5921"},m={id=272},src={"In-game quest text: Trial of the Sea Lion"},fv=true}
E["quest:28"] = {t="quest",n="Trial of the Lake",z="general",s="Tajarri awaits the result of a trial at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade. A Shrine Bauble from Lake Elune'ara is at its heart.",h="Tajarri awaits the result of a trial at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",sec={{t="At the Shrine",b="At the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade, Tajarri asks you to complete a trial. Find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara and bring it to the shrine. Use it there, then speak with Tajarri to complete the trial.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Tajarri ask me to do?",a="Tajarri asks you to find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara, use it at the Shrine of Remulos, then speak with Tajarri.",al={"tajarri trial","what do i need","lake trial"}},{q="Where is the Shrine of Remulos?",a="The Shrine of Remulos is in northwestern Moonglade.",al={"remulos shrine location","where's the shrine","shrine location"}},{q="Where do I find the Shrine Bauble?",a="The Shrine Bauble is in Lake Elune'ara.",al={"bauble location","find bauble","lake bauble"}},{q="What do I do with the Shrine Bauble?",a="Take the Shrine Bauble to the Shrine of Remulos and use it there.",al={"use bauble","bauble at shrine","shrine bauble"}},{q="Who do I speak with after using the bauble?",a="Speak with Tajarri at the shrine after using the Shrine Bauble.",al={"talk to tajarri","after the shrine","finish trial"}}},kw={"lake elune'ara","moonglade","shrine bauble","shrine of remulos","tajarri","trial of the lake"},rel={"quest:5921","subzone:lake-elune-ara","npc:remulos"},m={id=28},src={"In-game quest text: Trial of the Lake"},fv=true}
E["quest:284"] = {t="quest",n="The Search Continues",z="general",s="The search for the Menethil Statuette continues among nearby Murloc hovels. These shelters hold no sign of it, so you turn to two more.",h="The search for the Menethil Statuette continues among nearby Murloc hovels.",sec={{t="Empty Hovels",b="You search this cluster of Murloc hovels, but find no trace of the Menethil Statuette. Two nearby shelters to the north and northeast may hold clues.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What am I searching for?",a="You are searching for the Menethil Statuette.",al={"statuette search","menethil statue","what statuette"}},{q="What do I find in these hovels?",a="You find no trace of the Menethil Statuette in this cluster of Murloc hovels.",al={"murloc hovels","empty hovels","anything here"}},{q="Where should I look next?",a="Look in the nearby hovels to the north and northeast for more clues.",al={"next hovels","where look","north huts"}},{q="What is in the barrel?",a="The barrel holds damp, pungent cheese that is still tasty.",al={"barrel contents","cheese barrel","what's in barrel"}}},kw={"barrel","cheese","hovels","menethil statuette","murloc","search"},rel={"item:menethil-statuette","topic:murloc"},m={id=284},src={"In-game quest text: The Search Continues"},fv=true}
E["quest:285"] = {t="quest",n="Search More Hovels",z="general",s="Among the Murloc hovels, you have found no sign of the Menethil Statuette. So you press farther north, seeking the next clue.",h="Among the Murloc hovels, you have found no sign of the Menethil Statuette.",sec={{t="Northward Search",b="You believe the Menethil Statuette lies in one of the hovels to the north. So you continue your search among the Murloc dwellings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What am I searching for?",a="You are searching the Murloc hovels for the Menethil Statuette.",al={"statuette search","menethil statue","what am i looking for"}},{q="Did these hovels have the statuette?",a="A thorough search of this group of hovels reveals nothing.",al={"empty hovels","find anything here","what did the hovels show"}},{q="Where might the statuette be?",a="You believe one of the Murloc hovels farther north may hold the Menethil Statuette.",al={"where is the statuette","north hovels","statuette location"}}},kw={"barrel","menethil statuette","murloc hovels","north hovels","search more hovels"},rel={"topic:murloc","item:menethil-statuette"},m={id=285},src={"In-game quest text: Search More Hovels"},fv=true}
E["quest:286"] = {t="quest",n="Return the Statuette",z="general",s="Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor needs the Menethil Statuette brought back. It was found inside a barrel pulled from the muck, and its return will ease the Blind Princess's captain.",h="Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor needs the Menethil Statuette brought back.",sec={{t="The Figurine",b="The statuette lay packed in fine straw inside the barrel. It shows a young, long-haired Paladin raising a hammer. Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor is waiting for it. The Blind Princess's captain will be relieved to know the cargo is safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Menethil Statuette?",a="The Menethil Statuette is a silvery figurine showing a young, long-haired Paladin with a raised hammer.",al={"statuette","menethil figurine","what's in the barrel"}},{q="Where was the statuette found?",a="The statuette was packed in fine straw inside a barrel pulled from the muck.",al={"barrel statuette","where was it","straw barrel"}},{q="Who is waiting for the statuette?",a="Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor is waiting for the Menethil Statuette.",al={"who gets the statuette","return statuette","Karl Boran"}},{q="Who will be relieved when it is returned?",a="The captain of the Blind Princess will be relieved that the precious cargo has been recovered.",al={"captain relieved","Blind Princess cargo","who owns the cargo"}},{q="What does the statuette depict?",a="The statuette depicts a young, long-haired Paladin with a hammer raised.",al={"who is on the statuette","Paladin figurine","hammer statuette"}}},kw={"barrel","blind princess","karl boran","menethil harbor","menethil statuette","paladin","statuette"},rel={"item:menethil-statuette","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:paladin"},m={id=286},src={"In-game quest text: Return the Statuette"},fv=true}
E["quest:29"] = {t="quest",n="Trial of the Lake",z="general",s="In Moonglade, an initiate faces the Trial of the Lake, a timed test of speed and dexterity. You dive into Lake Elune'ara for an unstable Shrine Bauble, then hurry to the Shrine of Remulos before it decays. Success earns Tajarri's recognition and honors the Cenarion Circle's devotion to balance.",h="In Moonglade, an initiate faces the Trial of the Lake, a timed test of speed and dexterity.",sec={{t="A Test of Dexterity",b="Moonglade's guardians oversee this rite for initiates. You dive into Lake Elune'ara to find a delicate Shrine Bauble resting along the sunken lakebed. It begins to decay as soon as you disturb it, so you need a sure touch, keen senses, and swift movement to carry it overland before its magic fades.",sp=0},{t="Tribute to the Keeper",b="Once you have the bauble, you must hurry to the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade. The monument honors Keeper Remulos, who guides the Cenarion Circle in preserving nature and world balance. Activating the bauble there marks its importance to the Circle. Warden Tajarri greets initiates who beat the time limit and the competition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Trial of the Lake?",a="The Trial of the Lake tests an initiate's agility and focus in Moonglade. You dive into the cold depths of Lake Elune'ara to retrieve a Shrine Bauble that decays rapidly, then race across the haven to the Shrine of Remulos before its energy dissipates.",al={"what is trial of the lake","purpose of trial of the lake","what is this quest"}},{q="Where is the Shrine of Remulos located?",a="The Shrine of Remulos stands in northwestern Moonglade. It honors Keeper Remulos, who guides the Cenarion Circle, and warden Tajarri guards and maintains it.",al={"where is shrine of remulos","shrine location","remulos shrine moonglade"}},{q="Who is Tajarri?",a="Tajarri is a trusted warden of Moonglade who tends the Shrine of Remulos. She oversees the Trial of the Lake and welcomes initiates who bring the bauble to honor the shrine.",al={"who is tajarri","tajarri moonglade","shrine warden tajarri"}},{q="What is a Shrine Bauble?",a="A Shrine Bauble is a relic found along the bed of Lake Elune'ara. Once taken from the water, it decays rapidly, so its bearer must race to activate it at the Shrine of Remulos as tribute before its energy dissipates.",al={"what is shrine bauble","why does bauble decay","shrine bauble purpose"}},{q="Why is Keeper Remulos honored at this shrine?",a="Keeper Remulos is a revered keeper of the grove who guides the Cenarion Circle in preserving nature and maintaining balance. The shrine in northwestern Moonglade honors his leadership and principles.",al={"who is keeper remulos","remulos lore","why honor remulos"}},{q="What does offering the bauble at the shrine signify?",a="Activating the bauble at the Shrine of Remulos pays tribute to the sacred balance the Cenarion Circle maintains and acknowledges the shrine's lasting spiritual importance in Moonglade.",al={"what does using bauble do","why activate bauble at shrine"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you face a test of swiftness and adaptability in Moonglade. The rite of passage honors Keeper Remulos."},kw={"cenarion circle","lake elune'ara","moonglade","remulos","shrine bauble","shrine of remulos","tajarri","trial of the lake"},rel={"subzone:lake-elune-ara","npc:remulos","topic:cenarion-circle","quest:5921","topic:elune"},m={id=29},src={"In-game quest text: Trial of the Lake"},fv=true}
E["quest:297"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering Idols",z="general",s="At an excavation site, troggs clutch the carved idols Magmar Fellhew seeks. The relics have driven them into a violent frenzy.",h="At an excavation site, troggs clutch the carved idols Magmar Fellhew seeks.",sec={{t="The Unearthed Relics",b="Researchers uncovered a large cache of strange, carved stone idols shortly before savage troggs surfaced and overran the excavation site. The attack drove the expedition from the ruins before any formal study could begin. Now the troggs clutch the relics and prowl the site, barring a peaceful return.",sp=0},{t="A Savage Frenzy",b="The troggs seem deeply affected by the idols, beyond merely taking them. Their strange carvings exert an unsettling power that drives the creatures into an uncontrollable rage. Magmar Fellhew wants to study the idols safely and quell the frenzy gripping the area, so he seeks to take them from trogg hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magmar Fellhew?",a="Magmar Fellhew is an excavator seeking to recover carved stone idols from an excavation site troggs overran.",al={"who is magmar fellhew","quest giver","magmar"}},{q="What are the carved stone idols?",a="The idols are mysterious carved stone relics unearthed at an excavation site. Their unsettling power drives nearby troggs into a berserk frenzy.",al={"what are carved stone idols","strange idols","excavated idols"}},{q="Why do the idols make the troggs go berserk?",a="The idols exert a strange, inexplicable influence on troggs. When the creatures possess them, wild fury drives them berserk.",al={"why troggs berserk","idols make troggs crazy","trogg rage"}},{q="Why does Magmar Fellhew want the idols collected?",a="Magmar Fellhew wants the idols recovered safely so he can study their origins and properties, and remove the volatile relics from trogg hands.",al={"why get idols","purpose of gathering idols","magmar study"}},{q="What happened at the excavation site?",a="Troggs surfaced abruptly from the excavation site shortly after the idols were discovered. They drove the excavators from the ruins.",al={"who surfaced at the site","trogg invasion","excavation overrun"}},{q="Where are the idols found?",a="Troggs carry the carved stone idols at the excavation site where the relics were first unearthed.",al={"where to find idols","who has idols","carved stone idol location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you join excavators seeking ancient artifacts in trogg-infested ruins and the secrets they hold.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you help dwarven expeditions secure dangerous relics before savage troggs cause more havoc."},kw={"berserk","carved stone idols","excavation","gathering idols","magmar fellhew","ruins","troggs"},rel={"topic:trogg"},m={id=297},src={"In-game quest text: Gathering Idols"},fv=true}
E["quest:30"] = {t="quest",n="Trial of the Sea Lion",z="general",s="Tajarri asks you to seek two pendant halves in Moonglade and bring the joined Pendant of the Sea Lion to Dendrite Starblaze. Clues from the residents point toward the halves, and the Shrine of Remulos is where they can be joined.",h="Tajarri asks you to seek two pendant halves in Moonglade and bring the joined Pendant of the Sea Lion to...",sec={{t="Tajarri's Request",b="Tajarri at the Shrine of Remulos asks you to find two halves of a pendant in Moonglade. The residents may know where the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance can be found. Bring the joined Pendant of the Sea Lion to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven.",sp=0},{t="At the Shrine",b="The two pendant halves can be joined near the Shrine of Remulos. Once formed, the Pendant of the Sea Lion is to be brought to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Dendrite Starblaze want?",a="Dendrite Starblaze waits in Nighthaven for the joined Pendant of the Sea Lion. Tajarri sends you to find the two pendant halves in Moonglade and join them near the Shrine of Remulos.",al={"dendrite request","what does dendrite need"}},{q="Where can I find clues about the pendant halves?",a="The residents of Moonglade may have clues about where the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance are located.",al={"pendant clues","where are the halves"}},{q="Where do I join the two halves?",a="The two pendant halves can be joined in proximity to the Shrine of Remulos.",al={"join pendant","shrine pendant"}},{q="Where is Dendrite Starblaze waiting?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is in the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade.",al={"dendrite location","where is dendrite"}}},kw={"aquatic agility","aquatic endurance","dendrite starblaze","moonglade","nighthaven","pendant","sea lion","shrine of remulos","trial of the sea lion"},rel={"quest:5921","subzone:nighthaven","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:remulos","item:pendant-of-the-sea-lion"},m={id=30},src={"In-game quest text: Trial of the Sea Lion"},fv=true}
E["quest:3090"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Parchment",z="general",s="A tainted parchment waits for you after your absence, and your teacher Nartok asks to speak with you. Its words challenge Thrall’s rule and warn of the dangers warlocks face.",h="A tainted parchment waits for you after your absence, and your teacher Nartok asks to speak with you.",sec={{t="A message waits",b="The tainted parchment is believed to come from Nartok, your new teacher. Read it, then speak with him in the Den in the Valley of Trials. He calls the orcs a proud people and says Thrall turns away from power that could make the land theirs.",sp=0},{t="A place among them",b="Nartok says you have joined their ranks, yet warlock power will not make you welcome. Thrall allows warlocks into Orgrimmar because they remain orcs. Nartok warns that recklessness can be fatal. He remains ready to teach you spellcasting if you need instruction.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent the parchment?",a="The parchment is believed to come from Nartok, your new teacher.",al={"who sent this","parchment from who"}},{q="Where can I speak with Nartok?",a="Nartok is in the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is nartok","nartok location"}},{q="What does Nartok think of Thrall?",a="Nartok says Thrall turns away from power that could make the land theirs.",al={"thrall opinion","why criticize thrall"}},{q="Why does Thrall allow warlocks into Orgrimmar?",a="Nartok says Thrall allows warlocks into Orgrimmar because they are still orcs.",al={"warlocks in orgrimmar","why thrall allows warlocks"}},{q="What warning does Nartok give?",a="Nartok warns that warlock power does not ensure acceptance, and recklessness can be fatal.",al={"nartok warning","warlock danger"}},{q="Can Nartok teach me spells?",a="Nartok remains available if you need instruction in spellcasting.",al={"spell lessons","warlock training"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face the danger Nartok warns of: wielding your power recklessly may prove fatal."},kw={"den","nartok","orgrimmar","spellcasting","tainted parchment","thrall","valley of trials","warlock"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=3090},src={"In-game quest text: Tainted Parchment"},fv=true}
E["quest:3091"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Note",z="general",s="At Camp Narache, Harutt Thunderhorn calls young tauren warriors to defend their people. His summons reminds them that warriors stand beside druids and shamans in guarding the tribal borders from centaur.",h="At Camp Narache, Harutt Thunderhorn calls young tauren warriors to defend their people.",sec={{t="A Summons to Battle",b="At Camp Narache, a messenger brings young warriors a summons from Harutt Thunderhorn. The veteran trainer calls each fighter to report and begin training to defend the tribe.",sp=0},{t="The Defender's Burden",b="The Shu'halo revere their spiritual leaders, yet Harutt teaches that warriors bear an equal burden. They patrol tribal borders and hunt predatory centaur packs to protect their peaceful kin from attack. Battle may bring glory, but warriors remain humble and complete the same traditional rites as shamans and druids.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote the Simple Note?",a="Harutt Thunderhorn wrote the summons and sent it through a messenger to young tauren ready for martial training.",al={"who sent simple note","who wrote the note","sender simple note"}},{q="Who is Harutt Thunderhorn?",a="Harutt Thunderhorn is a tauren warrior trainer at Camp Narache in Mulgore. He trains new warriors in battle and the ancestral ways of tribal warfare.",al={"who is harutt","harutt thunderhorn","where is harutt"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Simple Note?",a="The note calls newly awakened warriors to meet their trainer. It reminds them that defenders and hunters are as vital to the tribe as druids and shamans.",al={"why is the note important","what does the note say"}},{q="Why are warriors called upon to hunt centaur?",a="Hostile centaur packs threaten Mulgore's borders. Harutt trains warriors to hunt them and protect the camp.",al={"why fight centaur","tauren centaur conflict"}},{q="Where is Camp Narache located?",a="Camp Narache lies at the edge of Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. It is the ancestral training camp and starting settlement of the young tauren of the Hawkwind tribe.",al={"camp narache location","where is camp narache"}},{q="What are the tribal rites Harutt mentions?",a="The text does not name the rites. It says every tribal member, from warriors and hunters to shamans and druids, must undergo them to prove strength, humility, and dedication to their people.",al={"tauren rites of passage","what rites do tauren take"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For young tauren beginning in Red Cloud Mesa, the note shows that protecting the tribe matters as much as spiritual callings such as shamanism and druidism.",["class:Warrior"]="Harutt Thunderhorn teaches novice tauren warriors to temper their pride and defend Camp Narache from centaur."},kw={"camp narache","centaur","harutt thunderhorn","mulgore","red cloud mesa","simple note","tauren","warrior"},rel={"subzone:camp-narache","topic:centaur","topic:shaman","topic:druid"},m={id=3091},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Note"},fv=true}
E["quest:3095"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Scroll",z="general",s="A sealed scroll bearing Dannal Stern’s mark finds you while you deal with the Scourge. It calls you to Deathknell, where Dannal speaks of your freedom and offers to teach you.",h="A sealed scroll bearing Dannal Stern’s mark finds you while you deal with the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Sealed Message",b="While you were away dealing with the mindless Scourge, a scroll arrived for you. Its seal bears Dannal Stern’s mark. He is the warrior trainer in Deathknell, and the message asks you to read it and speak with him before setting out again.",sp=0},{t="Freedom and Training",b="Dannal says others escaped death and fled to town. He sees promise in their resilience. He credits Sylvanas with freeing you in body and spirit, though the plague still afflicts you. He offers to teach you as you gain experience. Sylvanas will need people of your class to help save the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent me the scroll?",a="The scroll bears Dannal Stern’s seal. He is the warrior trainer in Deathknell.",al={"scroll sender","who sent this","Dannal scroll"}},{q="Why did the scroll arrive?",a="The scroll asks you to read it and speak with Dannal Stern in Deathknell.",al={"why scroll","what's this scroll for","simple scroll"}},{q="What does Dannal say about Sylvanas?",a="Dannal credits Sylvanas with freeing you in body and spirit, though the plague still afflicts you.",al={"Sylvanas freedom","what did Sylvanas do","Sylvanas and me"}},{q="What does Dannal offer?",a="Dannal offers to teach you as you gain experience and invites you to seek him out.",al={"Dannal teaching","can Dannal train me","warrior trainer"}},{q="What does Sylvanas need from me?",a="Dannal says Sylvanas will need people of your class to help save the Forsaken.",al={"Sylvanas needs","my class role","Forsaken future"}}},kw={"dannal stern","deathknell","forsaken","scourge","simple scroll","sylvanas","training"},rel={"subzone:deathknell"},m={id=3095},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Scroll"},fv=true}
E["quest:3099"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Scroll",z="general",s="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken warlocks receive a summons bearing Maximillion's name. It calls them back to the ruined settlement to weigh freedom, power, and servitude.",h="In Deathknell, newly awakened Forsaken warlocks receive a summons bearing Maximillion's name.",sec={{t="A Dark Summons",b="Newly risen Forsaken are clearing mindless Scourge remnants around Deathknell when a sealed scroll arrives. It bears the mark of Maximillion, the local warlock trainer. The message asks its recipient to consider servitude and freedom, then return to the ruined settlement and speak with him.",sp=0},{t="The Philosophy of Control",b="Maximillion teaches that escaping the Lich King's mindless grasp does not end slavery if another master holds the reins. A slave remains a slave until they claim true authority. He says mastering demonic servants does not betray Sylvanas. To Maximillion, it is the natural end of the Forsaken struggle for self-determination and respect.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent the Tainted Scroll?",a="The scroll bears Maximillion's personal seal. He is the warlock trainer in Deathknell and seeks newly awakened practitioners of the dark arts.",al={"who sends tainted scroll","who gave me tainted scroll","tainted scroll sender"}},{q="Who is Maximillion?",a="Maximillion trains newly raised Forsaken in Deathknell. He teaches them to summon and control demonic entities.",al={"who is maximillion","maximillion deathknell","warlock trainer deathknell"}},{q="What is written on the Tainted Scroll?",a="The scroll calls newly awakened warlocks to consider freedom, power, and servitude. It urges them to visit Maximillion for deeper instruction.",al={"what is tainted scroll","what does scroll say","scroll message"}},{q="Is Maximillion a traitor to Lady Sylvanas?",a="Maximillion says he is no traitor to Lady Sylvanas. He believes the Banshee Queen would understand his view, since she too pursued freedom from the Scourge.",al={"is maximillion a traitor","does maximillion betray sylvanas","maximillion loyalty"}},{q="Where can I find Maximillion?",a="You can find Maximillion in Deathknell, the ruined settlement in Tirisfal Glades where newly risen Forsaken first emerge from their graves.",al={"where to find maximillion","maximillion location"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The summons calls newly raised Forsaken warlocks to begin training with their local mentor in Deathknell.",al={"why warlock quest tainted scroll","tainted scroll purpose"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you meet Maximillion in Deathknell. He presents demonology and command of servants as a way to claim mastery and freedom.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you share a dark parallel: breaking free of the Scourge and commanding demonic servants for your own survival."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","maximillion","scourge","sylvanas","tainted scroll","tirisfal glades","warlock"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={id=3099},src={"In-game quest text: Tainted Scroll"},fv=true}
E["quest:3100"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Letter",z="general",s="At Northshire Abbey, new warriors are sent to Llane Beshere for training. Their letter calls them to aid the valley's troubled residents.",h="At Northshire Abbey, new warriors are sent to Llane Beshere for training.",sec={{t="A Call to Arms",b="New warriors arriving in Northshire Valley are directed by letter to Llane Beshere, the trainer at Northshire Abbey. They are to meet their instructor and learn the lay of the surrounding land. Then they can prepare for the demands of martial life.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Valley",b="The Knights of the Silver Hand guard Northshire Abbey, yet trouble reaches people beyond its protection. Llane Beshere tells new warriors that valley residents need able protectors. He urges them to master their weapons and defend those who live there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Letter?",a="Warriors returning from the kobold camps receive the Simple Letter in Northshire Valley. It sends them to Llane Beshere, the local trainer, to begin martial instruction.",al={"what is simple letter","simple letter quest","starter letter human warrior"}},{q="Who is Llane Beshere?",a="Llane Beshere trains warriors at Northshire Abbey. He teaches novices combat and welcomes recruits sent to him with orders or recommendations.",al={"who is llane beshere","beshere location","where is warrior trainer northshire"}},{q="Where do I deliver the Simple Letter?",a="Bring the letter to Llane Beshere at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. The holy order protects the abbey grounds.",al={"where to turn in simple letter","simple letter hand in","llane beshere location"}},{q="What role do the Knights of the Silver Hand play in Northshire?",a="The Knights of the Silver Hand guard Northshire Valley. Their protection keeps the abbey and its immediate grounds relatively secure while recruits, farmers, and clergy carry on amid growing local tensions.",al={"what are paladins doing in northshire","silver hand northshire abbey","paladins elwynn"}},{q="Why are the local citizens in need of assistance?",a="Local residents face encroachments and shortages, though the abbey itself is fairly well defended. Llane Beshere urges new arrivals to explore the surrounding land and lend strength to those in need.",al={"why does beshere want me to help citizens","northshire problems","who needs help northshire"}},{q="When should I return to Llane Beshere after delivering the letter?",a="Llane Beshere is at the abbey day and night, training warriors as they gain combat experience and need more advanced martial skills.",al={"when should i return to llane beshere","more warrior training northshire","beshere training"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="At Northshire Abbey, Llane Beshere trains warriors. The letter calls newly arrived fighters to begin martial training.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you receive your first guidance at Northshire Abbey before setting out into Elwynn Forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you are called to aid troubled residents beyond the Silver Hand's shelter at Northshire Abbey."},kw={"elwynn forest","knights of the silver hand","llane beshere","northshire abbey","northshire valley","simple letter","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},m={id=3100},src={"In-game quest text: Simple Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:3101"] = {t="quest",n="Consecrated Letter",z="general",s="At Northshire Abbey, the Consecrated Letter calls new initiates of the Holy Light to training. It sends each bearer to a class trainer and reminds them that their conduct reflects their faith.",h="At Northshire Abbey, the Consecrated Letter calls new initiates of the Holy Light to training.",sec={{t="A Sacred Calling",b="In Northshire Valley, the Consecrated Letter begins an initiate’s journey in the Holy Light. It calls those newly arrived to find their trainer at Northshire Abbey. There, they can formalize their instruction and take up their duties in the Kingdom of Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="Carrying the Light",b="The letter reminds each initiate of the weight of their calling. Those who channel the Holy Light shine before all, symbols of hope to allies and clear targets to adversaries. Their trainer teaches that such power demands discipline. Others will judge the faith by their conduct.",sp=0},{t="Guidance and Discipline",b="The letter begins a lasting bond between student and mentor. As the initiate tests their mettle against threats around Northshire, they are expected to return often to the abbey grounds. There, their trainer guides them toward deeper understanding of combat and divine grace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Consecrated Letter?",a="The Consecrated Letter calls an initiate of the Holy Light in Northshire Valley to begin training. It directs the bearer to a class trainer at Northshire Abbey and recalls their sacred duties.",al={"what is consecrated letter","consecrated letter quest"}},{q="Where does the Consecrated Letter come from?",a="After a new paladin returns from the kobold camps, someone at Northshire Abbey hands over the letter. Sealed with Brother Sammuel’s insignia, it tells the paladin to come see him.",al={"who gives consecrated letter","who sends consecrated letter"}},{q="Who receives the Consecrated Letter?",a="Brother Sammuel, the paladin trainer near the entrance of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest, receives the letter.",al={"who turns in consecrated letter","who reads consecrated letter"}},{q="What role does the trainer play after reading the letter?",a="The trainer mentors the initiate in the ways of the Holy Light. They teach martial techniques, defensive blessings, and sacred spells as the initiate gains practical combat experience in the valley.",al={"what does the trainer teach","why train with the trainer"}},{q="Why does the letter mention being a symbol?",a="Those who channel the Holy Light are visible paragons of faith and virtue. Friends and foes alike recognize its power, so their conduct reflects upon the faith itself.",al={"why am i a symbol","holy light symbol"}},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="Northshire Abbey lies in Elwynn Forest’s peaceful northern valley. It is a sanctuary of faith and the chief grounds for recruiting defenders of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where is northshire abbey","where do i take the letter"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you wield the Holy Light and embody its virtues. In Northshire and beyond, your allies look to you as a beacon of hope.",["race:Human"]="As a human beginning your service at Northshire Abbey, you are called to act as an honorable symbol in a Kingdom troubled by recent trials.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance representative of the Holy Light, you are expected to act with honor and uphold the Alliance’s moral standing and defense."},kw={"brother sammuel","consecrated letter","elwynn forest","holy light","northshire","northshire abbey","paladin","trainer"},rel={"topic:light"},m={id=3101},src={"In-game quest text: Consecrated Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:3102"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Letter",z="general",s="At Northshire Abbey, Jorik Kerridan summons promising rogues to meet him in secret. His letter points them toward a quiet stable and counsel for the dangers ahead.",h="At Northshire Abbey, Jorik Kerridan summons promising rogues to meet him in secret.",sec={{t="A Discreet Summons",b="Northshire Abbey looks peaceful, yet covert talents are recruited within its walls. After dealing with the kobolds, promising novices receive a letter bearing Jorik Kerridan's seal. It is addressed discreetly, away from the priests and paladins. The bearer is sent to a secluded meeting in the stables behind the Abbey.",sp=0},{t="Shadows in Northshire",b="Jorik Kerridan keeps to the stables because they are quiet and draw little notice. When newcomers arrive unseen, he speaks plainly about the wider world. Stormwind's SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood both seek stealthy operatives. Jorik urges each novice to keep their freedom and resist powerful groups that would push them around. A clever rogue holds the cards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the Encrypted Letter?",a="Jorik Kerridan sent the letter, which bears his personal insignia. Promising novices receive it after scouting nearby kobold camps.",al={"who sent encrypted letter","who gave me encrypted letter","who wrote the encrypted letter"}},{q="Where is Jorik Kerridan located?",a="Jorik Kerridan stays in the quiet stable behind Northshire Abbey. He keeps out of sight while tending to his covert work.",al={"where is jorik","where to find jorik kerridan","jorik location"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Letter?",a="The letter discreetly invites rising rogues to meet their local trainer. Its encrypted words keep training matters from prying eyes around the Abbey.",al={"why encrypted letter","what is encrypted letter for","why is letter encrypted"}},{q="Which organizations are looking to recruit rogues?",a="Jorik Kerridan says many factions seek skilled rogues, including Stormwind's covert agency SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood. The Defias seek spies inside Stormwind.",al={"who wants rogues","factions interested in rogues","who covets rogue skills"}},{q="What advice does Jorik Kerridan give?",a="Jorik urges you to remain your own person and refuse to be bullied into work against your will. Rogues hold the cards before the game is done.",al={"jorik advice","what does jorik tell you","rogue advice jorik"}},{q="Why does Jorik Kerridan stay in the stable?",a="Jorik Kerridan stays in the quiet stable behind Northshire Abbey because it draws little attention. There, trainers and operatives can meet beyond the notice of the Abbey's clergy and guards.",al={"why hide in stables","why is jorik behind abbey","why quiet in stables"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you meet Jorik Kerridan and hear his counsel on dealing with SI:7 and the Defias Brotherhood while keeping your independence.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even within Northshire Abbey, Stormwind's shadow operatives recruit and train promising agents for the conflicts ahead."},kw={"defias brotherhood","encrypted letter","jorik kerridan","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rogue trainer","si:7"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","quest:2300","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:kobold","quest:65"},m={id=3102},src={"In-game quest text: Encrypted Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:320"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Bellowfiz",z="general",s="You bring Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh. After the local hunting, the thirsty driver awaits a fresh drink.",h="You bring Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh.",sec={{t="A Cask for the Depot",b="After helping with local hunting, you receive a fresh cask of Evershine for Pilot Bellowfiz. Carry it through snowy Dun Morogh to Steelgrill's Depot. Such favors help people on the cold frontier look after one another.",sp=0},{t="Thirsty Aviators",b="Steelgrill's Depot lies just outside Kharanos. Gnomes test machinery, tend vehicles, and practice their craft there. The pilots face freezing winds and welcome a strong local drink. When you arrive with the cask, Pilot Bellowfiz is eager to uncork a bottle and taste the brew made by locals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Return to Bellowfiz?",a="You carry a fresh cask of Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh.",al={"what is return to bellowfiz","bellowfiz quest"}},{q="Who is Pilot Bellowfiz?",a="Pilot Bellowfiz is a dwarven siege-engine driver stationed at Steelgrill's Depot, just outside Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He is eager to try a fresh delivery of Evershine.",al={"who wants evershine","who is bellowfiz"}},{q="What is the cask of Evershine?",a="Evershine is a potent local brew made in Dun Morogh and kept in a sturdy cask. Thirsty pilots and locals prize it.",al={"what is evershine","cask of evershine"}},{q="Where do you deliver the cask?",a="Take the cask to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot, an engineering hub and workshop just east of Kharanos in Dun Morogh.",al={"where is bellowfiz","bellowfiz location"}},{q="Why was the Evershine sent to Bellowfiz?",a="After you help with hunting in the region, you receive a cask of Evershine for Pilot Bellowfiz. He eagerly awaits a taste.",al={"why deliver evershine","evershine delivery reason"}},{q="What happens when Bellowfiz receives the Evershine?",a="When Pilot Bellowfiz receives the cask, he says it will do just fine and moves at once to open a bottle for a taste.",al={"what does bellowfiz do with brew","bellowfiz reaction"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know stout Evershine is in high demand across Dun Morogh. Bringing it safely to thirsty comrades comes naturally.",["race:Gnome"]="Pilot Bellowfiz is a dwarven siege-engine driver at Steelgrill's Depot. Keeping hardworking engineers refreshed helps the machines run smoothly.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help morale and camaraderie among forces in Dun Morogh by carrying favors between dwarven hunters and pilots."},kw={"cask of evershine","dun morogh","evershine","kharanos","pilot bellowfiz","return to bellowfiz","steelgrill's depot"},rel={"npc:pilot-bellowfiz","subzone:steelgrill-s-depot","quest:318"},m={id=320},src={"In-game quest text: Return to Bellowfiz"},fv=true}
E["quest:34"] = {t="quest",n="An Unwelcome Guest",z="general",s="In Lakeshire, Martie Jainrose asks you to stop Bellygrub for good. The wild boar wrecked her garden and trampled her daffodils, and she offers a bounty for his tusk.",h="In Lakeshire, Martie Jainrose asks you to stop Bellygrub for good.",sec={{t="Trouble in the Garden",b="Martie Jainrose lives in Lakeshire, a town by the lake beneath the gathering shadows over the Redridge Mountains. A wild boar keeps breaking into her garden and ruining the peace of her home. Bellygrub has trampled her daffodils beyond recovery for the season. Now Martie asks travelers to end the animal's rampage.",sp=0},{t="The Menace of Bellygrub",b="Marshal Marris, who leads Lakeshire's town guard, gave the boar his name: Bellygrub. He spends most of his time rooting through the fields southwest of town. His hunger and boldness bring him close to homes, where he ruined Martie's flower beds. The damage has left her wanting him gone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest An Unwelcome Guest?",a="Martie Jainrose asks for help in Lakeshire, the lakeside town in the Redridge Mountains. Her garden has suffered repeated damage, and she wants the boar responsible hunted down.",al={"who gives an unwelcome guest","where to get an unwelcome guest","martie jainrose quest"}},{q="Who or what is Bellygrub?",a="Bellygrub is an aggressive boar that terrorizes the grounds around Lakeshire. Marshal Marris, the town guard leader, gave him that name.",al={"who is bellygrub","what is bellygrub","why is bellygrub called that"}},{q="Where can Bellygrub be found?",a="Bellygrub usually forages in the open fields southwest of Lakeshire. He often wanders closer to town and into residents' gardens.",al={"bellygrub location","where is bellygrub","find bellygrub","where does bellygrub spawn"}},{q="Why does Martie Jainrose want Bellygrub killed?",a="Bellygrub repeatedly trampled Martie Jainrose's garden and ruined her daffodils for the season. She wants him killed to stop the damage.",al={"why does martie want bellygrub dead","why kill bellygrub","what did bellygrub do"}},{q="What proof is needed to complete the quest?",a="Martie Jainrose asks you to bring her Bellygrub's tusk as proof that the boar has been dealt with. She will reward you for it.",al={"bellygrub proof","unwelcome guest turn in","what to bring martie jainrose"}},{q="Who is Marshal Marris and what is his connection to the beast?",a="Marshal Marris leads Lakeshire's town guard. He named the boar Bellygrub, while Martie Jainrose seeks vengeance for her ruined daffodils.",al={"who is marshal marris","marshal marris bellygrub"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping Martie Jainrose brings relief and order to Lakeshire, where townspeople already face greater threats in Redridge.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track Bellygrub, the named beast roaming southwest of Lakeshire, through the Redridge Mountains.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know the care Martie Jainrose gave her flower patch. Bellygrub's rampage ruined her seasonal daffodils and damaged the town's domestic plant life."},kw={"an unwelcome guest","bellygrub","boar","daffodils","lakeshire","marshal marris","martie jainrose","redridge","redridge mountains"},rel={"npc:martie-jainrose","subzone:lakeshire","npc:marshal-marris"},m={id=34},src={"In-game quest text: An Unwelcome Guest"},fv=true}
E["quest:359"] = {t="quest",n="Forsaken Duties",z="general",s="Magistrate Sevren needs word from Tirisfal Glades' eastern border. He fears Scourge may slip past The Bulwark and threaten nearby settlements.",h="Magistrate Sevren needs word from Tirisfal Glades' eastern border.",sec={{t="Vigilance on the Border",b="Magistrate Sevren watches over Brill and the countryside, keeping wary eyes on Tirisfal Glades' eastern border. The Scourge swarm across the Western Plaguelands, so sentries must report what they see. Sevren sends you south along the main road, then east, to bring back Deathguard Linnea's assessment.",sp=0},{t="Reports from the Front",b="Deathguard Linnea watches the frontier from an outpost beside the eastern road. Her report confirms Sevren's fears. The Bulwark holds the main Scourge host, but small groups sometimes slip past its defenses. Those strays gather around nearby Balnir Farmstead, threatening Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Forsaken Duties?",a="Magistrate Sevren in Brill asks you to bring back an updated report from the eastern Deathguard outpost.",al={"who gives forsaken duties","who starts forsaken duties","sevren quest"}},{q="Who is Deathguard Linnea?",a="Deathguard Linnea is stationed at the Deathguard waystation east of Brill. She watches the road and guards the approaches to the Plaguelands.",al={"who is linnea","deathguard linnea location","where is linnea"}},{q="What is The Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark is a fortified border outpost between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. Its defenders keep the Scourge from overrunning Forsaken lands.",al={"what is the bulwark","bulwark defense","why is the bulwark important"}},{q="Where are Scourge slipping past the border?",a="Small Scourge groups sometimes slip past The Bulwark and gather around Balnir Farmstead, east of the waystation.",al={"scourge in tirisfal","balnir farmstead scourge","where are the scourge leaking through"}},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want a status report?",a="Magistrate Sevren wants to keep the Scourge from gaining a strong foothold in Tirisfal Glades. The Deathguard must stay vigilant.",al={"why does sevren need a report","sevren concern"}},{q="How do you get to Deathguard Linnea's post?",a="From Brill, follow the road south, then turn east at the fork toward Tirisfal Glades' eastern reaches.",al={"where is the waystation","how to reach linnea"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know a breach in the border threatens Brill and the Forsaken's newly claimed Undercity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that guarding Tirisfal Glades against Scourge incursions preserves a reliable foothold in northern Lordaeron."},kw={"balnir farmstead","brill","deathguard linnea","forsaken duties","magistrate sevren","scourge","the bulwark","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:deathguard-linnea","subzone:bulwark","subzone:balnir-farmstead","topic:scourge","quest:1882"},m={id=359},src={"In-game quest text: Forsaken Duties"},fv=true}
E["quest:3633"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Engineering",z="general",s="Among master inventors, Goblin Engineering offers a path to command explosive power and volatile concussive ordnance. Its craft relies on high-yield blasting powders and relentless firepower, making it a destructive choice beside intricate tinkering.",h="Among master inventors, Goblin Engineering offers a path to command explosive power and volatile concussive...",sec={{t="The Art of the Detonation",b="Azeroth's engineers follow two distinct philosophies. Goblin tinkerers favor violent combustion, while other inventors make delicate clockwork and subtle devices. Goblins harness blasting powder to build tools of great devastation, turning fire, shrapnel, and concussive force toward practical problems.",sp=0},{t="Volatility and Power",b="Goblin engineers make no secret of the hazards. Recruits work with volatile compounds, heavy incendiaries, and prototypes that may singe their creator's eyebrows or level an opposing barricade. They prize maximum yield and destructive power, and welcome engineers who choose decisive firepower over fragile safety rules.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Goblin Engineering?",a="Goblin Engineering is a discipline devoted to high-yield explosions. Its practitioners craft powerful explosives, bombs, and heavy destructive devices instead of the intricate gadgets favored by gnomish engineers.",al={"what is goblin engineering","goblin spec","goblin engineering quest"}},{q="How does goblin engineering differ from gnomish engineering?",a="Gnomish engineering favors strange utility devices, complex tinkering, and inventive gadgets. Goblin engineering puts firepower, blasting powders, and destructive yield first. Goblin inventions are aggressive and effective, though hazardous to handle.",al={"goblin vs gnome engineering","gnomish or goblin","difference goblin gnome engineering"}},{q="Who teaches the goblin engineering discipline?",a="Master goblin engineers teach the discipline to recruits willing to work with explosions and blasting powder. Master Engineer Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan is a prominent trainer who tests candidates before teaching them the trade.",al={"who teaches goblin engineering","where to learn goblin engineering","goblin engineering trainer"}},{q="Is goblin engineering dangerous to practice?",a="Goblin inventors accept danger as part of the craft. Their designs maximize explosive output and concussive force, bringing unpredictable malfunctions, sudden detonations, and personal risk to the artisan handling them.",al={"goblin engineering danger","do goblin explosives blow up","is goblin engineering safe"}},{q="Can both factions learn goblin engineering?",a="Engineers of both the Alliance and Horde can learn goblin engineering once they are sufficiently skilled. Goblin tinkerers work mainly through neutral cartels such as the Steamwheedle Cartel, which welcomes anyone with steady hands, enough coin, and a love of explosive force.",al={"can anyone learn goblin engineering","alliance goblin engineering","horde goblin engineering"}},{q="Why would an engineer choose the goblin discipline?",a="Engineers choose goblin engineering for its unmatched destructive capability. It produces lethal combat explosives, mortar guns, land mines, and portable rockets made to obliterate opposition on the battlefield.",al={"why pick goblin engineering","what does goblin engineering make","goblin engineering items"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Goblin engineering is one of the two major specialized traditions open to master engineers. It focuses on volatile munitions, heavy explosive yield, and catastrophic destruction.",["profession:Mining"]="Engineers who pursue goblin craft rely heavily on refined ores, blasting powders, and solid stones to make incendiaries and bombs."},kw={"blasting powder","bombs","engineering","explosives","gadgetzan","goblin engineering","nixx sprocketspring","steamwheedle cartel"},m={id=3633},src={"In-game quest text: Goblin Engineering"},fv=true}
E["quest:416"] = {t="quest",n="Rat Catching",z="general",s="In the western foothills, tunnel rat kobolds trouble the roads into Thelsamar. Mountaineer Kadrell calls on travelers to drive them back and bring proof of the cull for a bounty.",h="In the western foothills, tunnel rat kobolds trouble the roads into Thelsamar.",sec={{t="Vermin in the Foothills",b="West of Thelsamar, tunnel rat kobolds have made dens in the foothills of Loch Modan. They foul the surrounding ground and trouble the roads leading into town. Their warrens threaten the safety and cleanliness of those roads.",sp=0},{t="A Mountaineer's Bounty",b="Mountaineer Kadrell has set a bounty on the tunnel rat kobolds. He asks passing travelers to bring their severed ears as proof of the cull. Then he pays coin and compensation, though the trophies are foul to inspect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Rat Catching quest?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell offers the bounty in Thelsamar. He asks travelers to cull the vermin coming from the nearby mountainside.",al={"who gives rat catching","where to get rat catching","kadrell quest"}},{q="What are tunnel rat kobolds?",a="Tunnel rat kobolds are a breed of kobolds that have dug dens in the western foothills near Thelsamar. They foul the mountainside.",al={"what are tunnel rats","kobolds in loch modan","tunnel rat kobold"}},{q="Where can the tunnel rat kobolds be found?",a="Tunnel rat kobolds and their dens lie directly west of Thelsamar, scattered along the mountainside and foothills.",al={"where are the tunnel rats","rat catching location","dens west of thelsamar"}},{q="Why does Kadrell ask for Tunnel Rat Ears?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell asks for tunnel rat ears as proof of the kill before paying the town's bounty.",al={"why collect ears","why does kadrell want ears","proof of kill loch modan"}},{q="Why is the Mountaineer concerned about the kobold infestation?",a="The kobolds have moved into the foothills outside Thelsamar, where they make dens and foul the surrounding dwarven lands. Kadrell wants them driven out to secure the area.",al={"why clear tunnel rats","thelsamar rat problem","why kill kobolds in loch modan"}},{q="Does Rat Catching lead to a larger questline?",a="This is a local bounty to clear pests around Thelsamar. Kadrell pays once the ears are delivered.",al={"does rat catching have follow up","rat catching chain","quest after rat catching"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As defenders of Khaz Modan, Dwarves have a direct stake in keeping the foothills around Thelsamar clear of vermin and subterranean invaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mountaineer Kadrell speaks for Loch Modan's local dwarven authorities. He offers bounties to Alliance travelers willing to safeguard their settlements."},kw={"bounty","kobold","loch modan","mountaineer kadrell","rat catching","thelsamar","tunnel rat","tunnel rat ears"},rel={"npc:mountaineer-kadrell","subzone:thelsamar","topic:kobold"},m={id=416},src={"In-game quest text: Rat Catching"},fv=true}
E["quest:490"] = {t="quest",n="Bounty: Gnarlpine Furbolg",z="general",s="Outside Darnassus, the Alliance bounty on Gnarlpine furbolg remains in force. Corruption spreads through Teldrassil, and Shayla Nightbreeze asks hunters to bring back the beasts’ fangs.",h="Outside Darnassus, the Alliance bounty on Gnarlpine furbolg remains in force.",sec={{t="A Decree from the Sentinels",b="Outside Darnassus, Shayla Nightbreeze carries the Sentinels’ orders to place a bounty on the Gnarlpine furbolg. They once lived peacefully in the ancient forests. Now corruption has stripped away their reason and made them vicious threats to travelers and Teldrassil’s natural sanctity.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Encampments",b="Hunters cull the Gnarlpine across the boughs of the World Tree and collect their fangs as proof. Ban'ethil Hollow lies south of the road west of Dolanaar, and it is one of their two major strongholds. The other is the ruined Starbreeze Village to the east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the bounty on the Gnarlpine furbolg?",a="Shayla Nightbreeze offers the bounty from the road outside Darnassus, Teldrassil’s capital.",al={"who gives bounty gnarlpine furbolg","where to get gnarlpine bounty","shayla nightbreeze location"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolg being hunted?",a="Corruption has stripped the Gnarlpine of reason and made them aggressive threats to travelers, night elf settlements, and Teldrassil’s natural wildlife.",al={"why kill gnarlpine","why are gnarlpine hostile","what happened to gnarlpine furbolg"}},{q="Where can the Gnarlpine furbolg be found?",a="The Gnarlpine gather in Ban'ethil Hollow, west of Dolanaar and south of the main path, and in Starbreeze Village farther east.",al={"gnarlpine furbolg locations","where are gnarlpine on teldrassil","where to find furbolg"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Shayla Nightbreeze requires Gnarlpine fangs as physical proof that the furbolg threats have been removed from the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"proof of bounty gnarlpine","what proof shayla wants","gnarlpine fangs proof"}},{q="Who authorized the bounty on the Gnarlpine?",a="The Sentinels authorized the bounty through direct orders to secure Teldrassil’s boughs. They are the night elves’ military protectors.",al={"who ordered gnarlpine bounty","who authorized furbolg bounty"}},{q="Were the Gnarlpine always hostile to the night elves?",a="Furbolgs once allied with the night elves and lived peacefully beside them. Corruption has twisted their minds and broken that peace.",al={"were furbolgs always enemies","did furbolg used to be friendly"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once peaceful neighbors and allies to the Kaldorei. Their corruption now threatens Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Sentinels call on Alliance adventurers to secure the night elf homeland from corruption by clearing dangerous furbolg encampments across the boughs.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see how the Gnarlpine have lost their harmony with nature. Their hostility now endangers the balance of the glade you are sworn to preserve."},kw={"ban'ethil hollow","bounty","corruption","darnassus","furbolg","gnarlpine","gnarlpine fangs","sentinels","shayla nightbreeze","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus","subzone:ban-ethil-hollow","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar"},m={id=490},src={"In-game quest text: Bounty: Gnarlpine Furbolg"},fv=true}
E["quest:4921"] = {t="quest",n="Lost in Battle",z="general",s="At the Crossroads, Mankrik searches for his wife, lost in a Bristleback ambush at a tauren camp. Wounded and unable to look for her himself, he asks travelers to search the Barrens for any sign of her.",h="At the Crossroads, Mankrik searches for his wife, lost in a Bristleback ambush at a tauren camp.",sec={{t="Ambush at the Camp",b="Mankrik, an orc warrior at the Crossroads, fought beside his wife at a small tauren camp. Bristleback quilboar suddenly swarmed them. His wife held off three attackers alone, but fresh reinforcements cut her off from Mankrik in the fight.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Search",b="Mankrik faced the advancing quilboar in a blind rage, but their numbers soon brought him down. A passing tauren druid found him near death on the Gold Road and tended his wounds. Still too injured to search for his wife, Mankrik asks travelers passing through the Crossroads to look across the Barrens and bring back any sign of her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mankrik?",a="Mankrik is an orc warrior recovering at the Crossroads in the Barrens. Quilboar separated him from his wife, and he asks travelers to search the scrublands for any sign of her.",al={"who is mankrik","who gives this quest","mankrik backstory"}},{q="What happened to Mankrik's wife during the battle?",a="Mankrik and his wife were fighting together at a small tauren camp when Bristleback quilboar ambushed them. She held off three attackers alone before fresh reinforcements overwhelmed her and separated her from Mankrik.",al={"what happened to mankriks wife","where is his wife","mankrik wife attack"}},{q="How did Mankrik survive the quilboar ambush?",a="A wandering tauren druid found Mankrik on the Gold Road after the quilboar overwhelmed him. The druid tended his life-threatening wounds and saved him.",al={"who saved mankrik","how did mankrik survive","druid on gold road"}},{q="Who attacked Mankrik and his wife?",a="Bristleback quilboar swarmed a small tauren camp and attacked Mankrik and his wife. Their numbers overcame them despite their fierce resistance.",al={"who attacked them","quilboar in the barrens","bristleback attackers"}},{q="Where should travelers look for Mankrik's wife?",a="Mankrik was found on the Gold Road after falling near a small tauren camp overrun by Bristlebacks. Travelers can search the quilboar-infested areas across the Barrens for his wife.",al={"where do i look for her","where to search for mankriks wife"}},{q="Where can Mankrik be found now?",a="Mankrik is recovering at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He waits for news or any sign of his missing wife.",al={"why crossroads","where is mankrik now"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Mankrik's plea shows the danger Horde settlers and patrols face from Bristleback quilboar while traveling through the Barrens.",["race:Orc"]="Mankrik fought fiercely in an orcish battle-rage to defend his mate, but the quilboar swarm overwhelmed him.",["race:Tauren"]="The ambush happened at a small tauren camp. A wandering tauren druid tended Mankrik's wounds along the Gold Road and saved his life.",["class:Druid"]="A tauren druid passing along the Gold Road found Mankrik as he collapsed. The druid tended his severe wounds and kept him alive."},kw={"bristleback","crossroads","gold road","lost in battle","mankrik","mankriks wife","quilboar","tauren camp"},rel={"npc:mankrik","subzone:crossroads","subzone:gold-road","topic:tauren","topic:druid"},m={id=4921},src={"In-game quest text: Lost in Battle"},fv=true}
E["quest:54"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Goldshire",z="general",s="Marshal McBride sends you south to Goldshire with dispatches for Marshal Dughan. Beyond Northshire's sheltered valley, Stormwind's nobles give Elwynn Forest less and less thought.",h="Marshal McBride sends you south to Goldshire with dispatches for Marshal Dughan.",sec={{t="From Northshire to the Greater Forest",b="You've proved yourself against Northshire's troubles, and McBride releases you from the valley's guard. His transfer papers send you past the border gates and down the road to Goldshire. From there, your duty reaches across the wider forest.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of the Marshals",b="Marshal Dughan waits in Goldshire to receive McBride's dispatches and make you an Acting Deputy of the Stormwind Marshals. His welcome carries a grim warning: beside the dangers roaming Elwynn, Northshire is a peaceful garden. Stormwind's royal army is bound up in distant nobles' politics, instead of guarding home ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands the Stormwind Marshals in Goldshire. He oversees Elwynn Forest's defenses and patrols.",al={"who is marshal dughan","where is dughan","dughan role"}},{q="Why are recruits sent to Goldshire?",a="When recruits have dealt with trouble in Northshire Valley, Marshal McBride sends those who prove capable south to Goldshire. The dangers there stretch across all of Elwynn Forest.",al={"why go to goldshire","leaving northshire","next step after northshire"}},{q="What does Acting Deputy Status mean?",a="Acting Deputy is a field rank granted with Marshal McBride's papers. It brings promising recruits into the Stormwind Marshals to help keep the law.",al={"acting deputy","what is acting deputy status","deputy status meaning"}},{q="Where is the Stormwind army?",a="Marshal Dughan says most of Stormwind's standing army is away. The court nobles keep it busy with their duties instead of patrolling the towns and farms at home.",al={"where is stormwind army","stormwind army missing","why is elwynn unprotected"}},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride commands the garrison at Northshire Abbey. He trains new defenders and sends those who prove themselves to the front line at Goldshire.",al={"who is mcbride","mcbride role"}},{q="How do you find Goldshire from Northshire?",a="Follow the main road south out of Northshire Valley, past the border gates and into Elwynn Forest's heart. Goldshire lies along the road.",al={"goldshire road","how to get to goldshire","direction to goldshire"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, your move from Northshire to Goldshire is your first real recognition from Stormwind's military.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Stormwind's army sent elsewhere, Elwynn's defense rests more and more on newly deputized recruits and volunteers like you."},kw={"acting deputy","elwynn forest","goldshire","marshal dughan","marshal mcbride","northshire","report to goldshire","stormwind marshals"},rel={"npc:marshal-dughan","npc:marshal-mcbride","subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=54},src={"In-game quest text: Report to Goldshire"},fv=true}
E["quest:565"] = {t="quest",n="Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak",z="general",s="In Southshore, Bartolo Ginsetti gathers materials for Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak. The eccentric artisan claims his mantle is renowned throughout the Alliance and calls for tailoring supplies, a leatherworker's cloak, and raw yeti fur.",h="In Southshore, Bartolo Ginsetti gathers materials for Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak.",sec={{t="The Grand Tailor of Southshore",b="Travelers in coastal Southshore can commission a Yeti Fur Cloak from Bartolo Ginsetti. The artisan boasts that no finer garment exists anywhere on the planet. His work draws on materials gathered from the local wilderness and the skill of allied trades.",sp=0},{t="Components of the Craft",b="Bartolo needs more than a pelt and needle to make his cloak. Bring him a Bolt of Wool, Fine Thread, a Hillman's Cloak, and ten clumps of Yeti Fur from beasts roaming the foothills. With those goods in hand, he works the raw materials into his cold-weather mantle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bartolo Ginsetti?",a="Bartolo Ginsetti is an eccentric, boastful craftsman in Southshore, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He claims to have made an unrivaled, world-famous Yeti Fur Cloak.",al={"who is bartolo","bartolo ginsetti","who gives this quest"}},{q="What materials does Bartolo require to make the cloak?",a="Bartolo needs a Bolt of Wool, a Hillman's Cloak made by a leatherworker, Fine Thread, and ten clumps of Yeti Fur.",al={"cloak ingredients","what items for bartolo","yeti fur cloak materials"}},{q="Where does Bartolo make his cloaks?",a="Bartolo makes his cloaks in Southshore, a coastal human town and the main Alliance hub in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He welcomes travelers passing through the region.",al={"why southshore","where is southshore","where does this happen"}},{q="Where do adventurers obtain Yeti Fur in Hillsbrad?",a="Wild yetis in the foothills and mountains of Hillsbrad and Alterac carry clumps of Yeti Fur. Their coats are dense and insulating.",al={"where to get fur","which yetis","where do yeti furs drop"}},{q="How is the Hillman's Cloak acquired?",a="A skilled leatherworker patterns and stitches the Hillman's Cloak that Bartolo uses as his base garment. He adds wool, Fine Thread, and fur to it.",al={"who makes hillmans cloak","hillmans cloak craft","leatherworking cloak"}},{q="Why does Bartolo claim his cloak is world famous?",a="Bartolo says no finer cloak exists anywhere on the planet. He boasts that it is renowned throughout the Alliance and offers unmatched warmth, luxury, and prestige.",al={"why is the cloak famous","best cloak in the world","is bartolo's cloak good"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Bartolo boasts that his Yeti Fur Cloak is renowned throughout the Alliance. He offers his tailoring from Southshore, an Alliance stronghold.",["profession:Tailoring"]="The garment calls for a Bolt of Wool and Fine Thread, along with exotic beast pelts."},kw={"bartolo ginsetti","bolt of wool","fine thread","hillmans cloak","hillsbrad foothills","southshore","yeti fur","yeti fur cloak"},rel={"subzone:southshore","topic:alliance"},m={id=565},src={"In-game quest text: Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak"},fv=true}
E["quest:5658"] = {t="quest",n="Touch of Weakness",z="general",s="A priestess welcomes you back and offers a lesson in weakness. Her words make clear that she expects you to return ready to learn.",h="A priestess welcomes you back and offers a lesson in weakness.",sec={{t="A Lesson Offered",b="A priestess greets you when you return and says she is glad to see you. She offers to teach you a lesson she expects you to remember. The lesson itself remains ahead, and she asks if you are ready.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to learn?",a="A priestess welcomes you back and offers to teach you a lesson.",al={"who gives this","priestess lesson","touch of weakness giver"}},{q="What does the priestess want to teach me?",a="She offers a lesson she says you would do well to remember.",al={"what lesson","weakness lesson","what is touch weakness"}},{q="What happens when I return?",a="The priestess is glad you have returned and asks whether you are ready for a lesson.",al={"return to priestess","what happens here","touch of weakness"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you are addressed as a young priestess and offered a lesson."},kw={"lesson","priestess","return","touch of weakness","weakness"},m={id=5658},src={"In-game quest text: Touch of Weakness"},fv=true}
E["quest:5924"] = {t="quest",n="Heeding the Call",z="general",s="Mathrengyl Bearwalker awaits you in Darnassus, where he calls you to learn the ways of the bear. This is your first step toward serving nature and preserving balance.",h="Mathrengyl Bearwalker awaits you in Darnassus, where he calls you to learn the ways of the bear.",sec={{t="A Call in Darnassus",b="In the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus, Mathrengyl Bearwalker welcomes you and calls you to take a first step into a wider world. He teaches that Cenarius' children are called to serve nature, with animals and plants both friends and charges. You begin by learning the ways of the bear and the strength of body and heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to come here?",a="Mathrengyl Bearwalker awaits you in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",al={"who wants me","who is mathrengyl","mathrengyl"}},{q="Where do I find Mathrengyl Bearwalker?",a="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",al={"where is mathrengyl","mathrengyl location","cenarion enclave"}},{q="What does Mathrengyl want me to learn?",a="He calls you to learn the ways of the bear and strength of body and heart.",al={"what do i learn","bear ways","heeding call"}},{q="What is the call of Cenarius' children?",a="Cenarius' children are called to serve nature and preserve balance for the sake of plants and animals, as well as their own.",al={"cenarius call","serve nature","why nature"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Mathrengyl calls you to learn the ways of the bear and serve nature by preserving balance."},kw={"balance","cenarion enclave","cenarius","darnassus","heeding the call","mathrengyl bearwalker","nature","ways of the bear"},rel={"quest:6001","npc:mathrengyl-bearwalker","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:darnassus","topic:cenarius"},m={id=5924},src={"In-game quest text: Heeding the Call"},fv=true}
E["quest:5925"] = {t="quest",n="Heeding the Call",z="general",s="Mathrengyl Bearwalker calls a young night elf druid to Darnassus to continue their training. As Archdruid Fandral Staghelm's direct assistant, he prepares the initiate for the trials of the bear.",h="Mathrengyl Bearwalker calls a young night elf druid to Darnassus to continue their training.",sec={{t="A Summons to Darnassus",b="As your basic instruction among Teldrassil's boughs comes to an end, word arrives that Mathrengyl Bearwalker wishes to speak with you. He is the direct assistant to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and one of the Cenarion Enclave's wisest elders. His summons calls you beyond basic wardenship and toward the deeper arts of nature.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Bear",b="You travel to the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus and climb to the second floor of Archdruid Staghelm's great tree. Bearwalker welcomes you and reminds you that those who answer Cenarius' call must honor plants and beasts as companions and charges. To preserve nature's balance, you need more than quiet reflection. You must learn the ways of the wild bear and master strength of body and heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mathrengyl Bearwalker?",a="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is a wise druid and the direct assistant to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm. He oversees advanced instruction for promising druids in Darnassus.",al={"who wants to talk to me","who is mathrengyl","who is mathrengyl bearwalker"}},{q="Where is Mathrengyl Bearwalker located?",a="Mathrengyl Bearwalker is on the second floor of Fandral Staghelm's tree in the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Senior members of the Cenarion Circle convene there on Teldrassil.",al={"where do i find bearwalker","where is mathrengyl","cenarion enclave location"}},{q="Why was I summoned to speak with Mathrengyl?",a="Your basic training is complete, and your path as a druid is ready to widen. Mathrengyl will guide you into nature's deeper disciplines.",al={"why am i being called","what is this quest for","why heed the call"}},{q="What will I learn from Mathrengyl Bearwalker?",a="Mathrengyl begins teaching you the ways of the bear. You learn strength of body and heart to help protect nature's balance.",al={"what will mathrengyl teach me","what do i learn next","what form do i get"}},{q="What does it mean to be among 'Cenarius' children'?",a="Cenarius is the patron demigod of nature and teacher of the first druids. His followers believe all druids share a duty to protect Azeroth's wild plants and beasts.",al={"who is cenarius","children of cenarius meaning"}},{q="What is Fandral Staghelm's tree?",a="Fandral Staghelm's tree is a grand, hollow living tree in Darnassus's Cenarion Enclave. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and his inner circle direct Cenarion affairs across Teldrassil from there.",al={"what tree is he in","fandral tree location"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you leave basic novice training and begin learning nature's deeper forms under Archdruid Staghelm's direct assistant.",["race:NightElf"]="At the heart of Darnassus, the Cenarion Enclave shows how deeply Cenarion druidism is woven into Kaldorei society.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you join night elf druids answering the Cenarion call in Darnassus. Their work strengthens the Alliance's ancient magical and natural foundations on Kalimdor."},kw={"bear form","cenarion enclave","darnassus","druid training","fandral staghelm","heeding the call","mathrengyl bearwalker","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:mathrengyl-bearwalker","npc:fandral-staghelm","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:darnassus","quest:6001","quest:6381","quest:940","topic:druid"},m={id=5925},src={"In-game quest text: Heeding the Call"},fv=true}
E["quest:5928"] = {t="quest",n="Heeding the Call",z="general",s="Turak Runetotem calls you to begin learning the ways of the bear. He teaches that druids serve nature and preserve balance.",h="Turak Runetotem calls you to begin learning the ways of the bear.",sec={{t="A Call to Learn",b="Turak Runetotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff asks you to speak with him. He says the time has come for you to take a first step into a larger world.\n\nHe teaches that Cenarius' children serve nature, caring for animals and plants as friends and charges. Your first lesson is the ways of the bear, and strength of body and heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to come here?",a="Turak Runetotem asks you to speak with him on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"who sent me","turak who","who is turak"}},{q="What does Turak want me to learn?",a="Turak says your first step is to learn the ways of the bear and strength of body and heart.",al={"what am i learning","bear lesson","learn bear"}},{q="What does Turak say druids do?",a="Turak says Cenarius' children serve nature and preserve balance for the sake of animals, plants, and themselves.",al={"druid calling","serve nature","why nature"}},{q="Where do I speak with Turak?",a="Turak Runetotem is on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"where is turak","elder rise","turak location"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Turak's teaching begins with service to nature and learning the ways of the bear."},kw={"bear","cenarius","druid","elder rise","heeding the call","nature","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:6002","npc:turak-runetotem","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:cenarius"},m={id=5928},src={"In-game quest text: Heeding the Call"},fv=true}
E["quest:5929"] = {t="quest",n="Great Bear Spirit",z="general",s="In Moonglade, druids are sent north to seek the Great Bear Spirit. Communion with this ancient guide teaches the bear’s nature and strength, a vital part of a druid’s spiritual and martial training.",h="In Moonglade, druids are sent north to seek the Great Bear Spirit.",sec={{t="The Noble Mentor of Moonglade",b="In northwestern Moonglade, the Great Bear Spirit dwells apart from Nighthaven’s quiet paths. This ancient and noble mentor teaches every initiate who seeks to understand the bear’s nature. Druids have long sought its blessing and wisdom as part of the path of the wild.",sp=0},{t="A Rite of Primal Focus",b="Dendrite Starblaze guides young druids from Nighthaven into the hills to meet the spirit. Communion brings primal wisdom and an awareness of natural strength. When the druids return, Dendrite tests their focus. The encounter gives them raw strength and knowing intent, but they must learn to direct that power in their daily work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can the Great Bear Spirit be found?",a="The Great Bear Spirit dwells in the northwestern wilds of Moonglade, apart from Nighthaven and its settled paths.",al={"where is the bear spirit","find bear spirit moonglade","bear spirit location"}},{q="Who sends druids to seek out the Great Bear Spirit?",a="Dendrite Starblaze, an elder druid in Nighthaven, directs initiates to commune with the spirit as part of their natural training.",al={"who sends you to bear spirit","dendrite starblaze role","quest giver bear spirit"}},{q="What is the Great Bear Spirit?",a="The Great Bear Spirit is a wise and noble guide, tutor, and mentor who teaches practicing druids the primal nature of the bear.",al={"what is the bear spirit","bear spirit lore","who is great bear spirit"}},{q="Why must druids commune with the Great Bear Spirit?",a="Initiates commune with the spirit to learn the bear’s nature and take in its raw strength, resilience, and wisdom before returning to put those qualities to work.",al={"why talk to bear spirit","bear spirit quest purpose","what do you learn from bear spirit"}},{q="What happens after the Great Bear Spirit is satisfied?",a="After communing with the spirit, initiates return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven. Dendrite recognizes their new understanding and prepares them to focus that power.",al={"what happens after bear spirit","dendrite after spirit","after visiting bear spirit"}},{q="Do all druids need to seek the spirit's wisdom?",a="Every druid must seek the Great Bear Spirit’s counsel. Communion is a fundamental step toward attuning to animal forms and natural power.",al={"do all druids visit bear spirit","is bear spirit mandatory","who visits bear spirit"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you commune with the Great Bear Spirit to gain natural wisdom and the spiritual grounding needed to take on the bear’s resilience."},kw={"bear form","dendrite starblaze","druid quest","great bear spirit","moonglade","nighthaven"},rel={"npc:dendrite-starblaze","topic:druid","subzone:nighthaven","quest:5921"},m={id=5929},src={"In-game quest text: Great Bear Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:5930"] = {t="quest",n="Great Bear Spirit",z="general",s="In Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze sends you to the Great Bear Spirit to learn about the bear’s nature. He believes your strength and intent are ready to be focused.",h="In Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze sends you to the Great Bear Spirit to learn about the bear’s nature.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Bear Nature",b="Dendrite Starblaze waits in Nighthaven, Moonglade, with a lesson in mind. He asks you to seek the Great Bear Spirit in the northwest and learn what it can share about the bear’s nature. When you have finished, return to Dendrite; he sees strength and intent in you, and says you can learn to focus both through the bear’s nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to the Great Bear Spirit?",a="Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven asks you to seek the Great Bear Spirit.",al={"who asks me","Dendrite's request"}},{q="Where is the Great Bear Spirit?",a="The Great Bear Spirit is in northwestern Moonglade.",al={"bear spirit location","where's the spirit"}},{q="What am I meant to learn?",a="Dendrite asks you to learn what the Great Bear Spirit has to share about the nature of the bear.",al={"bear nature lesson","what does the spirit teach"}},{q="Where do I return afterward?",a="After speaking with the Great Bear Spirit, return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",al={"where to go back","return to Dendrite"}}},kw={"bear","dendrite starblaze","great bear spirit","moonglade","nature of the bear","nighthaven"},rel={"quest:5921","subzone:nighthaven","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:5929"},m={id=5930},src={"In-game quest text: Great Bear Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:6069"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunter's Path",z="general",s="Thotar at Razor Hill can guide you toward earning a beast companion. You are sent to speak with him.",h="Thotar at Razor Hill can guide you toward earning a beast companion.",sec={{t="A Beast Companion",b="A trainer sees promise in your skill with beasts and sends you to Thotar at Razor Hill. He can guide you toward earning a pet of your own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who should I speak with?",a="Speak with Thotar at Razor Hill.",al={"who do I talk to","where do I go","Thotar quest"}},{q="What can Thotar help me with?",a="Thotar can guide you toward earning a pet of your own.",al={"what does Thotar do","get a pet","hunter pet"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Thotar?",a="A trainer believes you are skilled enough to handle and train a beast as a companion.",al={"why Thotar","what's the point","hunter path"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you are judged skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion."},kw={"beast","companion","hunter","hunter's path","pet","razor hill","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","topic:hunter"},m={id=6069},src={"In-game quest text: The Hunter's Path"},fv=true}
E["quest:6393"] = {t="quest",n="Elemental War",z="general",s="In Stonetalon Mountains, Tsunaman sends you against fire elementals in Neptulon’s name. The water envoy at Sun Rock Retreat asks you to enter the Charred Vale and gather Incendrite cores from the blazing elementals you destroy. Their struggle reaches beyond mortal borders, bound to the ancient rivalry between elemental forces.",h="In Stonetalon Mountains, Tsunaman sends you against fire elementals in Neptulon’s name.",sec={{t="Primal Rivalry in the Mountains",b="At Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains, Tsunaman speaks for the Tribunal of the Tides. You carry out Neptulon the Tidehunter’s will against the fiery kin of his water elementals. Their enmity reaches far beyond mortal borders. It is an ancient struggle between the primal forces of Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="The Ash and the Flame",b="Southern Stonetalon Mountains hold the Charred Vale, where ash and smoke mark the land. Fire elementals gather there and threaten the surrounding regions. Tsunaman sends you to destroy them and gather the Incendrites they leave behind. These blazing cores prove to the Tribunal that the elementals are gone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tsunaman?",a="Tsunaman is an envoy of the Tribunal of the Tides at Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains. Under Neptulon the Tidehunter’s authority, he wages war on fire elementals and sends you to destroy them.",al={"who is tsunaman","tsunaman quest giver","sun rock retreat elemental"}},{q="Why does Neptulon want the fire elementals destroyed?",a="Neptulon the Tidehunter bears an ancient enmity toward fire elementals and seeks their destruction. The Tribunal of the Tides sent Tsunaman to carry out this campaign in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"why fight fire elementals","elemental war reason","neptulon fire elementals"}},{q="Where is the Charred Vale located?",a="The Charred Vale lies in southern Stonetalon Mountains. Fiery elementals and other dangerous beasts born of flame and ruin overrun its ash-covered basin.",al={"where is charred vale","fire elemental location stonetalon","where to find incendrites"}},{q="What are Incendrites?",a="Incendrites are burning remnants left when the fire elementals of the Charred Vale are destroyed. Tsunaman gathers these cores as proof of their destruction and to win favor with the Tribunal of the Tides.",al={"what are incendrites","fire elemental drops","incendrite lore"}},{q="What is the Tribunal of the Tides?",a="The Tribunal of the Tides is an authority among water elementals that serves Neptulon the Tidehunter. It directs elemental forces and envoys such as Tsunaman to carry out the Tidehunter’s will against rival elemental domains.",al={"tribunal of tides lore","who are tribunal of tides","water elemental faction"}},{q="Who is Neptulon the Tidehunter?",a="Neptulon the Tidehunter is the Elemental Lord of water and ruler of the oceans, seas, and all water elementals. Like the other elemental lords, he wages an ancient, unending conflict against rival elements, especially fire.",al={"who is neptulon","water elemental lord","neptulon tidehunter"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you witness primal forces clash as Neptulon’s servants fight the fire elementals.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can aid the elemental fight while passing through Stonetalon Mountains. Tsunaman is stationed at Sun Rock Retreat."},kw={"charred vale","elemental war","fire elementals","incendrites","neptulon","stonetalon mountains","sun rock retreat","tribunal of the tides","tsunaman"},rel={"npc:tsunaman","subzone:charred-vale","subzone:sun-rock-retreat"},m={id=6393},src={"In-game quest text: Elemental War"},fv=true}
E["quest:6394"] = {t="quest",n="Thazz'ril's Pick",z="general",s="Foreman Thazz'ril needs his enchanted pick back from the northern cavern. Beasts now prowl the Burning Blade Coven, where the glowing tool lies.",h="Foreman Thazz'ril needs his enchanted pick back from the northern cavern.",sec={{t="A Lost Tool",b="Foreman Thazz'ril directs work in the Valley of Trials. He entered the northern cavern to search for mineral veins and left his favorite pick behind. When he returned, vicious beasts and hostile inhabitants had taken over. Now he seeks capable hands to bring back the tool.",sp=0},{t="Glow in the Dark",b="Thazz'ril enchanted his favorite pick to glow in the dark, making it easier to use in dim caverns. Its light marks the tool in a waterfall chamber inside the Burning Blade Coven. Dangerous creatures prowl the shadows. Thazz'ril hopes to put the pick back to work and find new mining prospects across the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril oversees labor and resource gathering in the Valley of Trials. He directs peons as they clear timber and prepare the land for mining.",al={"who is thazzril","thazzril role","foreman thazzril"}},{q="Why does Thazz'ril's pick glow?",a="Thazz'ril enchanted his favorite pick to glow in the dark, so it is easier to spot in pitch-black caverns.",al={"why is the pick special","glowing pick","enchanted pick"}},{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven is a dark cave network north of the peon lumber camp in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is burning blade coven","coven location","pick cave"}},{q="How did Thazz'ril lose his pick?",a="Thazz'ril left his favorite pick behind while surveying the northern cave for minerals. When he returned, vicious beasts and dark cultists had infested the cavern.",al={"how did thazzril lose his pick","why leave the pick","pick left behind"}},{q="Where inside the cave was the pick left?",a="Thazz'ril left the pick deep in the cave, in a subterranean chamber with waterfalls, where he had been surveying the rock walls.",al={"where inside cave","pick room","waterfall chamber"}},{q="What does Thazz'ril plan to do after getting his pick back?",a="Thazz'ril plans to find a productive cave to mine after his peons finish cutting down the surrounding timber in the Valley of Trials.",al={"thazzril future plans","what will thazzril mine"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know why Foreman Thazz'ril relies on his enchanted pick to survey minerals across Durotar. He hopes to open new mining prospects once the local timber is cleared.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure basic tools and drive off threats like the Burning Blade Coven. That strengthens the Horde's foothold in the Valley of Trials."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","mining","pick","thazz'ril","valley of trials","waterfall"},rel={"npc:foreman-thazz-ril","subzone:burning-blade-coven"},m={id=6394},src={"In-game quest text: Thazz'ril's Pick"},fv=true}
E["quest:642"] = {t="quest",n="The Princess Trapped",z="general",s="Across the Arathi Highlands, an iridescent shard carries Myzrael’s plea from deep underground. She calls herself a princess of the earth, imprisoned by giants, and asks travelers to strengthen a crystal cluster in Drywhisker Gorge.",h="Across the Arathi Highlands, an iridescent shard carries Myzrael’s plea from deep underground.",sec={{t="A Voice from the Stone",b="Strange shards lie scattered across the Arathi Highlands, humming with distant power. Near them, Myzrael’s voice rises from deep beneath the ground. She calls herself a princess of the earth, cast down and bound underground by ancient giants. Cut off from the lands above, she uses the crystals to carry her plea to anyone willing to listen.",sp=0},{t="The Drywhisker Connection",b="Myzrael directs you east to Drywhisker Gorge, where she asks you to strengthen your contact with her. Drywhisker kobolds infest the gorge, and she calls them allies of the giants who hold her captive. They carry Motes of Myzrael and guard a cluster of iridescent shards. Take the motes from the kobolds and use their energy on the formation. That will strengthen the crystal cluster and deepen your communication with the trapped princess.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Myzrael?",a="Myzrael is the voice speaking through the crystal. She calls herself a princess of the earth, imprisoned deep beneath the Arathi Highlands, and calls to passing travelers for help reaching the surface.",al={"who is the trapped princess","who is talking through the crystal","who is myzrael"}},{q="Who trapped Myzrael beneath the highlands?",a="Myzrael says giants imprisoned her beneath Arathi. They bound her deep underground, so she relies on shards scattered across the region to speak with those above.",al={"who imprisoned myzrael","who trapped the princess","why is myzrael underground"}},{q="What are the Motes of Myzrael?",a="Motes of Myzrael are crystalline or elemental fragments carried by Drywhisker kobolds. Myzrael says they hold enough latent earth power to activate the shard clusters and strengthen her link to the surface.",al={"why do the kobolds have motes","drywhisker gorge motes","what are motes of myzrael"}},{q="How are the Drywhisker kobolds connected to Myzrael's captors?",a="Myzrael says the Drywhisker kobolds in Drywhisker Gorge are allies of the giants who imprisoned her. They guard a crystal shard cluster in the gorge, between the princess and the surface.",al={"why are kobolds involved","drywhisker kobolds giants","kobolds working with giants"}},{q="How is Myzrael able to speak from underground?",a="Myzrael sends her voice through iridescent crystal shards that protrude from the soil of the Arathi Highlands. The shards carry her voice through the depths to people on the surface.",al={"how does myzrael speak","iridescent shards arathi","what are the crystal shards"}},{q="Where is Drywhisker Gorge located?",a="Drywhisker Gorge is a rugged cleft in eastern Arathi Highlands. Drywhisker kobolds live there and surround the iridescent shard cluster Myzrael asks you to empower with the gathered motes.",al={"where is drywhisker gorge","where do i take the motes","drywhisker shards location"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you commune with elemental spirits and may recognize Myzrael’s claim to be an earth princess. Her imprisonment underground calls for careful scrutiny of the elements.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the resonant shards and motes of earth energy a curious way to communicate and channel power across great distances.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you may encounter Drywhisker kobolds near the gorge and in underground veins in Arathi. You may also find the enchanted crystal shards tied to the princess."},kw={"arathi highlands","drywhisker gorge","drywhisker kobolds","earth princess","iridescent shards","motes of myzrael","myzrael","princess of the earth","the princess trapped"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:drywhisker-gorge","topic:kobold"},m={id=642},src={"In-game quest text: The Princess Trapped"},fv=true}
E["quest:655"] = {t="quest",n="Hammerfall",z="general",s="At Hammerfall, the Horde holds a camp won at the cost of Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer's life. Gor'mul remembers the captives' escape and why the stronghold bears its name.",h="At Hammerfall, the Horde holds a camp won at the cost of Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer's life.",sec={{t="Blood and Broken Chains",b="In the Arathi Highlands, the Alliance once held orcs captive behind wood and steel. Young Thrall and Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer led an assault on the camp's enclosures and freed their kin. Many captives escaped as the defenses fell. Then a mounted lance struck Doomhammer from behind. He died where Hammerfall now stands.",sp=0},{t="The Lingering Shadow of Defeat",b="Gor'mul was among those who did not find freedom that day. In the battle's chaos and the earth's tremors, he watched the Warchief fall and lost the will to fight. His brethren fled, leaving him behind. For years, Gor'mul wandered the highlands in grief. The Horde has reclaimed the site as a fortified base, yet survivors still carry the memory of Doomhammer's death.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul was an orc captive at the internment camp where Hammerfall now stands. Thrall and Doomhammer led an assault to free the captives, but Gor'mul was left behind during the escape. He wandered alone in despair for years.",al={"who is gormul","gor mul backstory","what happened to gormul"}},{q="How did Orgrim Doomhammer die?",a="Orgrim Doomhammer died in the battle to free the Arathi internment camp. An Alliance knight on horseback struck him from behind with a lance.",al={"how did doomhammer die","who killed doomhammer","doomhammer death story"}},{q="Why is the outpost named Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall bears the name of Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell there while freeing his people from human captivity. The Horde returned to the ruined camp and made it a permanent base.",al={"why is it called hammerfall","origin of hammerfall name","hammerfall history"}},{q="Who is Tor'gan?",a="Tor'gan is a Horde representative stationed at Hammerfall. He helps care for the encampment and understands the lingering trauma of former captives like Gor'mul.",al={"who is tor'gan","torgan hammerfall","torgan quest"}},{q="Did Thrall take part in the battle here?",a="Yes. Thrall fought beside Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer in the assault on the Arathi internment camp. They broke its defenses and freed captive orcs, but Doomhammer died in the battle.",al={"thrall and doomhammer arathi","liberation of hammerfall","did thrall fight at hammerfall"}},{q="Why is Gor'mul so despondent?",a="Gor'mul watched Doomhammer fall, and the sight crushed his spirit. When the other captives escaped into the wilderness, Gor'mul was left behind to wander without hope until the Horde returned to build Hammerfall.",al={"why is gormul so sad","gormul depression","why did gormul lose hope"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Hammerfall recalls the liberation of the orcish internment camps and Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer's sacrifice.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, Doomhammer's fall in Arathi remains one of history's most painful moments. It marked the end of an era and the rise of Thrall's new Horde.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can remember Orgrim Doomhammer as a legendary fighter. The ground where he fell carries the weight of that battle."},kw={"arathi highlands","doomhammer","gor'mul","hammerfall","internment camp","orgrim doomhammer","thrall","tor'gan"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","npc:thrall"},m={id=655},src={"In-game quest text: Hammerfall"},fv=true}
E["quest:65593"] = {t="quest",n="Hearts of the Lovers",z="general",s="Carendin Halgar seeks the hearts of Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson to draw an incubus. Their longing for one another makes them an especially potent lure.",h="Carendin Halgar seeks the hearts of Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson to draw an incubus.",sec={{t="A Scrying's Choice",b="Carendin Halgar seeks two hearts for his work at the Temple of the Damned. His scrying points to Avelina Lilly in Ambermill and Isaac Pearson in Ratchet. Avelina serves the fallen wizards with her tailoring, while Isaac hopes to make his mark in the seaside town. Though they toil far apart, each longs for the other. Carendin asks you to bring him their hearts as a lure for an incubus.",sp=0},{t="The Hearts",b="Carendin receives the hearts of Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson. He holds one in each hand and brings them together gently, then calls the lovers idiots.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson?",a="Avelina Lilly provides tailoring services to the fallen wizards in Ambermill, and Isaac Pearson hopes to make his mark in Ratchet. Their hearts yearn for each other.",al={"avelina and isaac","who are the lovers"}},{q="Why does Carendin want their hearts?",a="Carendin says an incubus is drawn to lovers' hearts, and that the deepest longing makes the strongest lure.",al={"incubus hearts","why hearts"}},{q="Where are the two lovers?",a="Avelina Lilly is in Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, while Isaac Pearson is in Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"where is avelina","where is isaac"}},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is at the Temple of the Damned, where he asks you to bring him Avelina and Isaac's hearts.",al={"carendin","temple of the damned"}}},kw={"ambermill","avelina lilly","carendin halgar","hearts of the lovers","incubus","isaac pearson","lovers","ratchet"},rel={"zone:silverpine","zone:barrens","subzone:ambermill","subzone:ratchet","npc:carendin-halgar"},m={id=65593},src={"In-game quest text: Hearts of the Lovers"},fv=true}
E["quest:65597"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="general",s="Carendin Halgar in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter asks you to use the Lovers’ Hearts to summon and subdue an incubus. He needs the hearts returned afterward.",h="Carendin Halgar in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter asks you to use the Lovers’ Hearts to summon and subdue an...",sec={{t="A Summoning in the Undercity",b="Carendin Halgar asks for your aid in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. The Lovers’ Hearts are to be used to summon and subdue an incubus, then brought back to him. The hearts remain in Carendin’s keeping when you return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Carendin Halgar, in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter, asks for your help.",al={"who wants this","who gave it","carendin halgar"}},{q="What are the Lovers’ Hearts for?",a="You use the Lovers’ Hearts to summon and subdue an incubus.",al={"lovers hearts use","what do hearts do","hearts for incubus"}},{q="What happens after the summoning?",a="You return the Lovers’ Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter.",al={"where return hearts","return lovers hearts","what next"}}},kw={"carendin halgar","incubus","lovers' hearts","magic quarter","summoning","the binding","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={id=65597},src={"In-game quest text: The Binding"},fv=true}
E["quest:65601"] = {t="quest",n="Love Hurts",z="general",s="Gan'rul sends you along Orgrimmar's main drag to find Magar. His longing for Krilge may reveal the object Gan'rul needs to lure an incubus into the world.",h="Gan'rul sends you along Orgrimmar's main drag to find Magar.",sec={{t="Magar's Search",b="East of the Cleft of Shadow, Magar longs for Krilge to return. He asks you to search for something precious. Bring that object to Gan'rul, who needs a token of love and devotion to summon an incubus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magar?",a="Magar lives along Orgrimmar's main drag and longs for Krilge to return.",al={"Magar who","who's Magar"}},{q="Who is Krilge?",a="Krilge is Magar's mate, and Magar longs for Krilge's return.",al={"Krilge who","Magar's mate"}},{q="What is an incubus?",a="An incubus is a male sayaad, profoundly evil and single-minded.",al={"incubus meaning","sayaad male"}},{q="What does Gan'rul need?",a="Gan'rul needs an object that represents great love and devotion to lure an incubus into the world.",al={"Gan'rul needs what","incubus item"}},{q="Where can I find Magar?",a="Magar lives east of the Cleft of Shadow along Orgrimmar's main drag.",al={"Magar location","where Magar"}}},kw={"cleft of shadow","gan'rul","incubus","krilge","love hurts","magar","orgrimmar","sayaad"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","subzone:drag"},m={id=65601},src={"In-game quest text: Love Hurts"},fv=true}
E["quest:65602"] = {t="quest",n="What Is Love?",z="general",s="Gakin the Darkbinder seeks a wooden figurine whose age and history make it fit for an incubus ritual. Its devotion may draw the creature close.",h="Gakin the Darkbinder seeks a wooden figurine whose age and history make it fit for an incubus ritual.",sec={{t="An Old Keepsake",b="Gakin the Darkbinder has located a figurine with his scrying. He says it once belonged to a young couple thousands of years ago, and its owners are gone. You are asked to bring the keepsake from a house beyond Maestra's Post in Ashenvale to Gakin in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",sp=0},{t="The Figurine's Power",b="When you return the wooden figurine, Gakin senses its emotional force remains strong despite the passage of time. He says the incubus will be drawn to it, making it the reagent he needs for the ritual.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Gakin want me to find?",a="Gakin asks you to retrieve a wooden figurine that he believes will draw an incubus to his ritual.",al={"what figurine","wooden figurine","gakin's item"}},{q="Where is the figurine?",a="Gakin says it is in a house beyond Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",al={"figurine location","where is it","house in ashenvale"}},{q="Who owned the figurine?",a="The figurine belonged to a young couple thousands of years ago.",al={"old owners","couple figurine","who had it"}},{q="Why does Gakin want the figurine?",a="Gakin senses emotional energy in the figurine and says it will attract an incubus for his ritual.",al={"why figurine","incubus reagent","what is it for"}}},kw={"ashenvale","gakin the darkbinder","incubus","maestra's post","ritual","stormwind","what is love","wooden figurine"},rel={"npc:gakin-the-darkbinder","zone:ashenvale","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:mage"},m={id=65602},src={"In-game quest text: What Is Love?"},fv=true}
E["quest:65604"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="general",s="Gan'rul Bloodeye sends you to summon an incubus with the Withered Scarf and subdue it. The binding tests your mastery of a demon's charms and power.",h="Gan'rul Bloodeye sends you to summon an incubus with the Withered Scarf and subdue it.",sec={{t="At the Circle",b="Gan'rul Bloodeye reads love in the threads of the Withered Scarf and believes it will draw an incubus. In Neeru's tent in Orgrimmar, you are to use it at the summoning circle and prove your mastery over the demon. Gan'rul warns that an incubus will not yield quietly, and asks you to bring the scarf back after it is subdued.",sp=0},{t="The Scarf Returned",b="Gan'rul receives the scarf after the incubus is subdued. He says he will teach you to summon the demon and return the scarf to Magar. The cloth reminds him that warlocks may wield demonic darkness, but demons must never wield them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives you The Binding?",a="Gan'rul Bloodeye gives you the Withered Scarf and asks you to summon and subdue an incubus.",al={"who is gan'rul","gan'rul binding","who gives the scarf"}},{q="What does the Withered Scarf do?",a="Gan'rul senses love woven into the scarf's threads and believes it will draw an incubus.",al={"scarf purpose","withered scarf","why scarf"}},{q="Where is the summoning circle?",a="The summoning circle is in Neeru's tent in Orgrimmar.",al={"incubus circle","where summon","neeru tent"}},{q="What is an incubus?",a="An incubus is a sayaad. Gan'rul warns that sayaad dominate minds and torture souls, and that an incubus can charm its prey.",al={"incubus meaning","sayaad","what demon"}},{q="What does Gan'rul ask you to do?",a="Gan'rul asks you to summon an incubus with the Withered Scarf, subdue it, and return the scarf to him.",al={"binding task","what do i do","incubus binding"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you are being tested in the summoning and subduing of an incubus. Gan'rul warns that demons can turn their charms against you."},kw={"gan'rul bloodeye","incubus","magar","neeru's tent","sayaad","summoning circle","the binding","withered scarf"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye","topic:warlock","quest:1713"},m={id=65604},src={"In-game quest text: The Binding"},fv=true}
E["quest:65610"] = {t="quest",n="Wish You Were Here",z="general",s="A mooncloth maker in Ashenvale asks you to find Krilge, who vanished while guarding civilians. His comrades call him a deserter, but the maker believes he held his post.",h="A mooncloth maker in Ashenvale asks you to find Krilge, who vanished while guarding civilians.",sec={{t="A Missing Friend",b="A mooncloth maker met Krilge while making mooncloth in Ashenvale. Krilge was stationed there to protect civilians, then disappeared. They often met at Fallen Sky Lake, until aggressive bog beasts overran it. The maker still hopes to learn what became of him.",sp=0},{t="At the Lake",b="You are asked to search Fallen Sky Lake and report your findings to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar. Krilge's comrades have stopped looking for him. Perhaps the lake still holds a sign of what became of him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Krilge?",a="Krilge was stationed in Ashenvale to protect civilians before he disappeared. He and the mooncloth maker often met at Fallen Sky Lake.",al={"krilge","missing mooncloth maker's friend"}},{q="Why is Krilge being called a deserter?",a="Krilge vanished from his post. Those who served with him stopped searching and call him a deserter.",al={"krilge deserter","why they stopped looking"}},{q="Who asks you to look for Krilge?",a="A mooncloth maker who met Krilge in Ashenvale asks you to search for a sign of him.",al={"who sent me","mooncloth maker"}},{q="Where did Krilge and the maker meet?",a="Krilge and the maker often met at Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale, before aggressive bog beasts overran the area.",al={"krilge meeting place","where is fallen lake"}},{q="Where should you report your findings?",a="You are asked to report your findings to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.",al={"report to gan'rul","where do i report"}}},kw={"ashenvale","bog beasts","deserter","fallen sky lake","gan'rul bloodeye","krilge","missing","mooncloth"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","zone:orgrimmar","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"},m={id=65610},src={"In-game quest text: Wish You Were Here"},fv=true}
E["quest:6626"] = {t="quest",n="A Host of Evil",z="general",s="Myriam Moonsinger asks you to confront Razorfen Downs’ defenders and cultists. Their presence is the problem she sends you to address.",h="Myriam Moonsinger asks you to confront Razorfen Downs’ defenders and cultists.",sec={{t="Myriam’s Request",b="Near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, Myriam Moonsinger asks you to face the Razorfen Battleguard, Razorfen Thornweavers, and Death's Head Cultists within. She expects you to return to her after dealing with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for help at Razorfen Downs?",a="Myriam Moonsinger, near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, asks you to confront its defenders and cultists.",al={"who is myriam","myriam moonsinger"}},{q="Which enemies does Myriam name?",a="Myriam names Razorfen Battleguard, Razorfen Thornweavers, and Death's Head Cultists.",al={"who do i fight","razorfen enemies"}},{q="Where do I return to Myriam?",a="Return to Myriam Moonsinger near the entrance to Razorfen Downs.",al={"where is myriam","myriam location"}}},kw={"a host of evil","death's head cultists","myriam moonsinger","razorfen battleguard","razorfen downs","razorfen thornweavers"},rel={"subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:razorfen"},m={id=6626},src={"In-game quest text: A Host of Evil"},fv=true}
E["quest:6661"] = {t="quest",n="Deeprun Rat Roundup",z="general",s="At the Deeprun Tram, Monty asks passing travelers to round up the rats. His flute’s charming melody draws the living Deeprun rats along.",h="At the Deeprun Tram, Monty asks passing travelers to round up the rats.",sec={{t="Vermin Beneath the Rails",b="Monty keeps pests from overrunning the Deeprun Tram. He speaks in salty sea slang and treats the tramway like a ship’s deck. Vermin scurry through the underground station. So Monty asks travelers passing along the line to help gather them.",sp=0},{t="A Questionable Delicacy",b="Monty gives helpers an enchanted Rat Catcher’s Flute. Its charming melody draws Deeprun rats to follow, and they must be brought back alive. Monty’s brother needs fresh rats for rat kabobs before the meat turns sour.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the Deeprun Rat Roundup quest?",a="Monty asks passing travelers for help at the Deeprun Tram. He needs extra hands to manage the vermin along the underground line.",al={"who gives deeprun rat roundup","monty deeprun tram","rat quest guy"}},{q="Why does Monty need the rats captured alive?",a="Monty’s brother needs living Deeprun rats to make rat kabobs before the meat turns sour. If they die too soon, the meat spoils.",al={"why catch rats alive","what does monty do with rats","rat kabob lore"}},{q="How do you charm and round up the rats?",a="Monty provides an enchanted Rat Catcher’s Flute. Play its melody near the rats, and they will follow you back to Monty’s station.",al={"how to catch deeprun rats","what is the flute for","rat catcher flute deeprun"}},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The Deeprun Tram runs underground between Stormwind and Ironforge. Monty is stationed along its platforms.",al={"where is deeprun rat roundup","monty location","deeprun tram rats"}},{q="Who is Monty's brother?",a="Monty mentions a brother who cooks rat kabobs but gives no name. His brother needs a steady supply of fresh, living rats so the meat does not go rancid.",al={"who is montys brother","monty brother cook","kabob brother"}},{q="Why does Monty talk like a pirate?",a="Monty speaks in heavy nautical slang and treats the tram like a ship’s deck. He has taken up pest control duties in the underground railway.",al={"why is a pirate in the tram","monty pirate deeprun"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Monty’s brother uses freshly captured Deeprun rats to make rat kabobs. The rats must stay alive until cooking, or the meat spoils."},kw={"deeprun rat","deeprun rat roundup","deeprun tram","monty","rat catchers flute","rat kabob","vermin"},m={id=6661},src={"In-game quest text: Deeprun Rat Roundup"},fv=true}
E["quest:6662"] = {t="quest",n="Me Brother, Nipsy",z="general",s="On the Deeprun Tram, Monty sends live rats to his brother Nipsy in Stormwind. Nipsy runs a rat kabob stall at the far terminal, while Monty's odd manner hints at Gnomeregan's tragedy.",h="On the Deeprun Tram, Monty sends live rats to his brother Nipsy in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Subterranean Delivery",b="At the Ironforge station, Monty asks you to carry live rats through the Deeprun Tram to his brother Nipsy at the Stormwind depot. The short trip links the dwarven and human capitals beneath the mountains. Curious trades carry on along the way.",sp=0},{t="The Rat Kabob Trade",b="The crate is labeled Carton of Mystery Meat, but inside are live Deeprun rats. Nipsy runs a rat kabob stall at the Stormwind terminal and needs the rats before they spoil. When the crate arrives intact and twitching, he is relieved to have food for travelers passing through the station.",sp=0},{t="Scars of Gnomeregan",b="Monty speaks in exaggerated pirate slang and warns travelers to keep their limbs aboard the tram. Nipsy says Monty has never seen an ocean in his life. Monty uses his pirate manner to cope with the lingering trauma of Gnomeregan's radioactive fall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Me Brother, Nipsy?",a="Monty is an eccentric gnome at the Ironforge side of the Deeprun Tram. Deeply affected by Gnomeregan's catastrophe, he has taken up a pirate's speech and manner, though he has never seen an ocean. He catches live rats to send across the tramline.",al={"who gives me brother nipsy","who is monty","monty tram"}},{q="Who is Nipsy?",a="Nipsy is Monty's brother and runs a food stall at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot. He relies on Monty to send live rats across the tram tunnel for his rat kabob business.",al={"who is nipsy","where is nipsy","nipsy location"}},{q="What is inside the Carton of Mystery Meat?",a="The Carton of Mystery Meat holds live Deeprun rats caught by Monty. Nipsy needs them to arrive alive so they will not spoil before he makes them into kabobs.",al={"what is carton of mystery meat","mystery meat crate","what is in the box"}},{q="Why does Monty speak like a pirate?",a="Monty speaks like a pirate to cope with the trauma of the Gnomeregan disaster. Nipsy says Monty has never seen an ocean, though he clings to pirate mannerisms and warns travelers about losing limbs on the tram rails.",al={"why does monty talk like a pirate","is monty a pirate","monty pirate lore"}},{q="What does Nipsy do with the rats?",a="Nipsy makes and sells rat kabobs to travelers at the Stormwind depot. Fresh Deeprun rats arriving by tram keep his stall supplied.",al={"what does nipsy do with the rats","rat kabob operation","nipsy food"}},{q="Where do you deliver the shipment?",a="You carry the shipment on the Deeprun Tram from the Ironforge depot to the Stormwind terminal. The tram runs through the underwater tunnel to Nipsy's station on the Stormwind side.",al={"how to get to nipsy","where do i take the meat","tram ride to nipsy"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Monty's pirate manner and eccentric delusions come from the trauma of the Gnomeregan incident. They show the personal toll the city's fall took on surviving gnomes.",["profession:Cooking"]="Nipsy skewers fresh Deeprun rats into kabobs for travelers between Ironforge and Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Deeprun Tram links Stormwind and Ironforge with a high-speed route. Local vendors serve travelers at both depots."},kw={"deeprun tram","gnomeregan","ironforge depot","me brother, nipsy","monty","mystery meat","nipsy","rat kabob","stormwind depot"},rel={"subzone:deeprun-tram","zone:gnomeregan","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:pirate"},m={id=6662},src={"In-game quest text: Me Brother, Nipsy"},fv=true}
E["quest:671"] = {t="quest",n="Foul Magics",z="general",s="In the Arathi Highlands, Tor'gan follows a demonic presence to Northfold Manor. From Hammerfall, he seeks help recovering bloodstone amulets from the summoners.",h="In the Arathi Highlands, Tor'gan follows a demonic presence to Northfold Manor.",sec={{t="A Simmering Rage",b="Demonic energy stirs in the Arathi Highlands, and Tor'gan feels it from his post at Hammerfall. The pull draws the orc west toward Northfold Manor. There, he finds signs of demonic summoning, but the lingering corruption makes his blood boil and stirs an involuntary rage tied to the blood curse's history. He retreats before the influence overwhelms his senses, then seeks help from others.",sp=0},{t="The Bloodstone Amulets",b="At Northfold Manor, Tor'gan found a bloodstone amulet on the ground. It showed that dark rituals were being performed there. Such charms help channel and steady demonic summonings, but the amulet he recovered had lost its magic. It held too little power for a thorough study. Tor'gan asks Horde travelers to retrieve ten intact amulets from the manor's practitioners, so he can examine the rituals and learn what entities were summoned.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Foul Magics?",a="Tor'gan gives the request from Hammerfall, the Horde stronghold in the Arathi Highlands. Sensing a demonic presence nearby, he asks travelers to investigate Northfold Manor.",al={"foul magics quest giver","who starts foul magics","torgan quest arathi"}},{q="Where is Northfold Manor located?",a="Northfold Manor lies west of Hammerfall, in the northern hills of the Arathi Highlands. Once a human homestead, it is now the site of covert demonic summonings using bloodstone charms.",al={"northfold manor location","where is northfold manor","find northfold manor arathi"}},{q="What are Bloodstone Amulets used for?",a="Bloodstone amulets help practitioners channel dark magic during demonic summonings. When a summoning drains an amulet's power, the charm is depleted.",al={"what is bloodstone amulet","bloodstone amulet purpose","why bloodstone amulets"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan feel rage near Northfold Manor?",a="Lingering demonic summoning energies near Northfold Manor stir Tor'gan's rage. Fel magic makes his blood boil and ignites an uncontrollable rage.",al={"why torgan blood boils","torgan rage northfold","why does torgan get angry"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan refuse to return to Northfold Manor?",a="Tor'gan fears the residual demonic power will stir dangerous rage in him. Worried he could lose control or succumb to its corrupting influence, he asks others to recover the amulets.",al={"why wont torgan go to northfold","why torgan doesnt go back","why cant torgan get amulets"}},{q="How many Bloodstone Amulets are needed?",a="Tor'gan asks for ten bloodstone amulets from Northfold Manor. The one he found was depleted, so he needs multiple charged specimens to study and understand the rituals there.",al={"how many bloodstone amulets","bloodstone amulet count","foul magics objective count"}},{q="Who is summoning demons at Northfold Manor?",a="Dark practitioners at Northfold Manor conduct demonic summonings. Their rituals and the fel residue drew Tor'gan's attention from Hammerfall and led to the Horde's investigation.",al={"who is at northfold manor","who is summoning demons northfold","northfold manor cultists"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you carry a deep and painful history of demonic corruption. Residual fel magic can make your blood boil and stir unnatural rage, as Tor'gan feels near Northfold Manor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Hammerfall is its lone outpost in the Arathi Highlands. Dark summoners just west of the settlement pose a direct security threat.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know the rituals and binding reagents needed to summon demons. The bloodstone amulets at Northfold Manor are objects of particular interest."},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","bloodstone amulet","demonic summoning","foul magics","hammerfall","northfold manor","tor'gan"},rel={"subzone:northfold-manor","subzone:hammerfall"},m={id=671},src={"In-game quest text: Foul Magics"},fv=true}
E["quest:672"] = {t="quest",n="Raising Spirits",z="general",s="Tor'gan seeks a way to lift Gor'mul's spirits at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. Tales of Orgrimmar and Warchief Thrall have brought no comfort, so Tor'gan turns to the Horde's newly rediscovered shamanic traditions.",h="Tor'gan seeks a way to lift Gor'mul's spirits at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Heavy Heart in Hammerfall",b="At Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, Gor'mul has fallen into deep melancholy. His companions have told him of Kalimdor, the mighty city of Orgrimmar, and Warchief Thrall's leadership. Yet none of these tales has eased his gloom or given him hope.",sp=0},{t="Spirits of the Wild",b="Tor'gan turns to the Horde's revived spiritual traditions to help Gor'mul. He gathers the eyes of highland raptors roaming Arathi and makes an amulet blessed with their spirits. Through this rite, he hopes the predators' vital force will awaken Gor'mul's will to live.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tor'gan?",a="Tor'gan is a troll shaman stationed at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. He hopes to help Gor'mul with an amulet made through the Horde's newly rediscovered shamanic traditions.",al={"who is tor'gan","torgan hammerfall","quest giver raising spirits"}},{q="Who is Gor'mul and why does he need cheering up?",a="Gor'mul is an orc at Hammerfall, sunk in despondency and lethargy. Tales of Orgrimmar and Warchief Thrall have not lifted his spirits.",al={"who is gormul","why is gormul sad","orc depressed hammerfall"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan need highland raptor eyes?",a="Tor'gan uses the eyes of Highland Striders and Highland Thrashers to make a shamanic amulet. He hopes their spirits will lend Gor'mul strength and tenacity, and rekindle his fighting spirit.",al={"why raptor eyes","raptor eyes amulet","purpose of raptor eyes"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="Hammerfall is the Horde outpost in the Arathi Highlands. It is named for former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer and is a fortified haven for orcs remaining in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"where is hammerfall","hammerfall location","orcs in arathi"}},{q="What is the newly found shamanistic magic mentioned by Tor'gan?",a="Orcs lost their spiritual bond with the elements and ancestor spirits during demonic corruption and internment. Under Warchief Thrall, the Horde has reclaimed the ancient shamanic path, guided by spiritual harmony rather than fel magic.",al={"shaman magic orcs","orc shamanism new horde","why new shaman magic"}},{q="What stories failed to cheer up Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul's companions told him of Orgrimmar, the new capital across the sea in Kalimdor, and of Warchief Thrall wielding Orgrim Doomhammer's armor and legendary warhammer.",al={"stories about thrall","what stories did they tell gormul","orgrimmar tales gormul"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see the Horde's revived traditions brought to bear against Gor'mul's despondency. Tor'gan calls on animal spirits to rekindle his will to live.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know internment and the loss of old ways have burdened veterans like Gor'mul with despair and lethargy. Some struggle to embrace Thrall's new Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see comrades at remote outposts like Hammerfall caring for despondent brothers-in-arms."},kw={"arathi highlands","gor'mul","hammerfall","highland raptor eyes","orgrimmar","raising spirits","shamanism","thrall","tor'gan"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=672},src={"In-game quest text: Raising Spirits"},fv=true}
E["quest:674"] = {t="quest",n="Raising Spirits",z="general",s="A Horde emissary hopes Raising Spirits will help Gor'mul find his fighting spirit again. The Raptor Talon Amulet is meant to rekindle it, but Gor'mul remains bitter and doubts any trinket can restore the Horde's former glory.",h="A Horde emissary hopes Raising Spirits will help Gor'mul find his fighting spirit again.",sec={{t="A Spark for a Fallen Flame",b="An emissary brings Gor'mul a Raptor Talon Amulet, hoping its power will reach him. The talisman channels the wild strength and ferocity of raptors. It is meant to rekindle the flame that once burned fiercely within the orc warrior.",sp=0},{t="Bitterness and Despair",b="Gor'mul answers the gift with bitter grief. He remembers the mightiest champions struck down by cowardly hands and rejects the talisman as polished bone. He doubts any trinket can restore the Horde to its former glory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Raising Spirits?",a="A Horde emissary brings Gor'mul a Raptor Talon Amulet, hoping it will rekindle the despondent warrior's fighting spirit.",al={"what is raising spirits","raising spirits quest"}},{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul is a warrior consumed by despair after the mightiest champions fell to cowardly hands. He dismisses tokens and doubts the Horde can regain its former glory.",al={"who is gormul","gor mul"}},{q="Why is the Raptor Talon Amulet brought to Gor'mul?",a="The Raptor Talon Amulet is crafted from polished bone and raptor talons. It is brought to Gor'mul in hope that it can channel raptors' natural strength and ferocity to awaken his inner flame.",al={"why bring amulet","what does raptor talon amulet do"}},{q="Why is Gor'mul despondent?",a="Gor'mul despairs after seeing the mightiest champions slain by cowardly hands. Their fall leaves him convinced that honor and strength can be snuffed out, breaking his will to fight.",al={"why is gormul sad","why is gormul depressed"}},{q="How does Gor'mul react to the amulet?",a="Gor'mul rejects the gift as mere polished bone. He believes it cannot restore the Horde or undo the tragedy he laments.",al={"does gormul like the amulet","gormul reaction"}},{q="What does Gor'mul say about the Horde?",a="Gor'mul doubts the Horde can reclaim its former glory, seeing little hope when treachery can strike down even the greatest heroes.",al={"can the horde be restored","gormul horde glory"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear Gor'mul mourn its fallen might and question whether a simple trinket can restore its lost glory.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you hear of an orc whose fighting spirit has been extinguished by despair and grief over a cowardly strike."},kw={"gor'mul","gormul","horde","raising spirits","raptor amulet","raptor talon amulet","warrior"},rel={"topic:horde","topic:warrior"},m={id=674},src={"In-game quest text: Raising Spirits"},fv=true}
E["quest:675"] = {t="quest",n="Raising Spirits",z="general",s="Tor'gan hopes ancestral magic can restore Gor'mul's pride and will to live. The shaman seeks to lift an old orc veteran from despair.",h="Tor'gan hopes ancestral magic can restore Gor'mul's pride and will to live.",sec={{t="A Broken Spirit",b="Gor'mul grieves that he survived when his fallen Warchief did not. Many orc veterans bear the weight of past wars, but Gor'mul believes fate denied him an honorable death beside his leader. Tor'gan, a shaman, hopes to ease that sorrow by recalling his people's spiritual strength. He prepares an enchanted amulet and trusts ancestral power to rekindle the old warrior's pride.",sp=0},{t="The Limits of the Amulet",b="Tor'gan's amulet reaches Gor'mul, but brings no comfort. Gor'mul casts it into the dirt and asks why anyone would show him mercy when fate denied him an honorable end. Tor'gan accepts that one charm cannot overcome years of sorrow. Still, he remains committed to helping Gor'mul, believing the growing practice of shamanism can guide him back to his former honor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul is an embittered orc veteran who survived the older Horde's conflicts after his Warchief fell. He believes fate cruelly denied him an honorable death beside that leader and rejects ordinary sympathy.",al={"who is gormul","gormul backstory","what is wrong with gormul"}},{q="Who is Tor'gan and why is he helping Gor'mul?",a="Tor'gan is a shaman trying to lift Gor'mul from despair. He believes ancestral ways can restore broken spirits and shamanism can bring former warriors to spiritual rebirth. He crafts infused charms to remind them of their people's strength.",al={"who is torgan","what does torgan want","torgan purpose"}},{q="What was the purpose of the amulet?",a="Tor'gan prepared the enchanted amulet to awaken Gor'mul's warrior spirit through shamanic energy. Gor'mul rejected it and threw it to the ground, believing its magic could not dispel his bitterness.",al={"what is the amulet","why did gormul throw the amulet","did the amulet work"}},{q="Which Warchief does Gor'mul mourn?",a="Gor'mul does not name the Warchief he mourns. He curses fate for denying him death beside his fallen leader in battle.",al={"which warchief died","who was gormuls warchief","who did gormul serve"}},{q="What does Tor'gan plan to do after the amulet fails?",a="Tor'gan accepts that the amulet lacked enough power on its own. He remains patient and believes shamanism's true power can rekindle Gor'mul's lost pride.",al={"does torgan give up","what happens after raising spirits","will gormul recover"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan use shamanism to help Gor'mul?",a="Tor'gan uses shamanism to mend wounded minds and pride among his people. Shamans heal those wounds and channel the elements for war.",al={"what does this show about shamans","why use shaman magic here"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see how orcish shamanism can restore the spirits of veterans still burdened by trauma.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may recognize the dishonor Gor'mul feels at being denied an honorable death beside his former Warchief.",["faction:Horde"]="Under Thrall's leadership, the Horde seeks to reintegrate and uplift embittered veterans rather than abandon them to despair."},kw={"amulet","gor'mul","mercy","orc","raising spirits","shaman","tor'gan","veteran","warchief"},rel={"topic:shaman"},m={id=675},src={"In-game quest text: Raising Spirits"},fv=true}
E["quest:677"] = {t="quest",n="Call to Arms",z="general",s="Drum Fel calls the Horde to strike from Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. The Witherbark have joined the Boulderfist ogres, and the Horde means to hold its foothold there.",h="Drum Fel calls the Horde to strike from Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="Defending Hammerfall",b="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel rallies the Horde from its fortified outpost in the Arathi Highlands. Old human ruins and hostile powers surround the settlement. The Witherbark forest trolls and Boulderfist ogres have made a pact, putting the Horde's foothold at risk. Drum Fel calls on champions to strike first and keep their enemies from deciding the struggle's course.",sp=0},{t="The Witherbark Threat",b="South of Hammerfall, the Horde's first strikes reach Witherbark territory. The forest trolls have rejected diplomacy and joined the Boulderfist ogres in trying to drive the Horde from the highlands. Hammerfall targets their axe throwers, headhunters and witch doctors to weaken their leaders and show that the Horde intends to stay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Call to Arms?",a="Drum Fel, an orc at Hammerfall in the northeastern Arathi Highlands, calls the Horde to fight. He directs defensive and offensive strikes to protect the outpost from nearby threats.",al={"who gives call to arms","where is drum fel","quest giver call to arms"}},{q="Why is Hammerfall targeting the Witherbark trolls?",a="The Witherbark forest trolls have joined the Boulderfist ogres in trying to drive the Horde from the Arathi Highlands. Their hostility puts Hammerfall's foothold at risk.",al={"why kill witherbark","why attack trolls arathi","what did witherbark do"}},{q="Where are the Witherbark trolls located?",a="The Witherbark trolls live in settlements and camps south of Hammerfall, including deep in Witherbark Village near the mountains.",al={"where are witherbark trolls","witherbark camp location","where to find axe throwers arathi"}},{q="What role do the Boulderfist ogres play in this conflict?",a="The Boulderfist are a brutal ogre clan in the Arathi Highlands. Drum Fel says they have joined the Witherbark trolls in trying to drive the Horde from the highlands.",al={"who are boulderfist","ogres in arathi","boulderfist troll alliance"}},{q="What is Hammerfall and why does it need defending?",a="Hammerfall is the Horde's main outpost in the Arathi Highlands, named for Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. It occupies an old Alliance internment camp and gives the Horde a hard-won sanctuary and military base in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"what is hammerfall","hammerfall lore","why is horde in arathi"}},{q="Are the Witherbark trolls part of the Horde?",a="No. The Witherbark are forest trolls native to the Eastern Kingdoms, while the Darkspear jungle trolls belong to the Horde. The Witherbark reject outsiders and have violently refused the Horde's offers.",al={"are witherbark in the horde","are forest trolls friendly to horde","darkspear vs witherbark"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall is isolated in the Arathi Highlands, with hostile forces around it. Defending the outpost matters as the Horde tries to hold a place in human lands.",["race:Orc"]="Hammerfall occupies the grounds of a former Second War internment camp. As an orc, defending this new settlement against hostile neighbors carries the weight of liberation.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll serving Thrall's Horde, you face the hostile Witherbark forest trolls. Their rejection of the new Horde marks a sharp divide between your peoples."},kw={"arathi highlands","axe thrower","boulderfist","call to arms","drum fel","hammerfall","headhunter","witch doctor","witherbark"},rel={"npc:drum-fel","subzone:hammerfall","topic:troll"},m={id=677},src={"In-game quest text: Call to Arms"},fv=true}
E["quest:678"] = {t="quest",n="Call to Arms",z="general",s="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel sends proven warriors against the Boulderfist ogres. Their attacks threaten the Horde's foothold in Arathi.",h="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel sends proven warriors against the Boulderfist ogres.",sec={{t="A Test of Mettle",b="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel calls on travelers who have aided the outpost to face a real threat. Boulderfist ogres have harassed the Horde expedition and tested its defenders. Fel sends warriors against these foes, not minor skirmishers. He expects them to return alive or with honor, and promises praise for their tenacity in battle.",sp=0},{t="The Boulderfist Threat",b="Southwest of Hammerfall, the Boulderfist clan has dug in near the dwarven bridge between Arathi and the Wetlands. Brutes fight alongside cunning magi, bringing crushing strength and deadly magic. Their aggression threatens Horde supply lines and control of the region. Drum Fel orders warriors to defeat ten Boulderfist brutes and four magi. Their defeat will weaken the clan and show that Hammerfall will not yield ground or tolerate rivals in Arathi.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Call to Arms quest?",a="Drum Fel, an officer at Hammerfall in the northeastern Arathi Highlands, gives the call. He sends proven fighters against dangerous foes to protect the outpost and test their strength.",al={"who gives call to arms","drum fel quest","call to arms questgiver"}},{q="Where is the Boulderfist lair located?",a="The Boulderfist lair lies southwest of Hammerfall, along the way to Thandol Span, the dwarven bridge to the Wetlands. Brutes and magi gather in earthen dens and mounds in the highlands.",al={"boulderfist location","where are the ogres","boulderfist lair arathi"}},{q="Which enemies need to be defeated for this task?",a="Drum Fel calls for ten Boulderfist Brutes and four Boulderfist Magi to be defeated before returning to Hammerfall. Brutes attack at close range, while magi cast arcane spells from afar.",al={"call to arms kill count","which ogres to kill","call to arms targets"}},{q="Why are the Boulderfist ogres considered a threat to Hammerfall?",a="The Boulderfists have dug in across Arathi and repeatedly challenged Hammerfall's Horde garrison. Their position near routes to the southern dwarven bridge threatens Horde scouting and supply lines, so Drum Fel wants their strength contained.",al={"why fight boulderfists","are boulderfists hostile to horde","ogre threat in arathi"}},{q="What does Drum Fel mean by returning in body or in spirit?",a="Drum Fel expects his fighters to return alive after succeeding, but honors those who fall fighting valiantly against formidable foes. Facing the ogres with tenacity and fearlessness brings honor, whether a warrior survives or not.",al={"drum fel quote","return in spirit meaning","come in body or spirit"}},{q="Can Alliance players undertake this quest?",a="No. Drum Fel gives this call only to the Horde at Hammerfall. Alliance forces operate from Refuge Pointe to the west and regard Hammerfall's defenders and the Boulderfist ogres as hostile rivals for control of the Arathi Highlands.",al={"is call to arms horde only","alliance call to arms arathi","can alliance do this quest"}},{q="Why does Drum Fel target both brutes and magi?",a="The brutes form the front line and absorb blows, while the magi attack from the rear with destructive magic. Defeating both kinds weakens the Boulderfists' combined strength and keeps them from mounting an organized counterattack against Hammerfall.",al={"why kill magi","boulderfist magi importance","boulderfist brute and magus"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Hammerfall's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms by driving back the aggressive Boulderfist ogres.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you have a personal stake in Hammerfall, named for Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, and in driving out the rival brutes threatening this memorial stronghold.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face a direct test of endurance and honor against brute force and arcane power.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you face Boulderfist Magi who wield arcane energies for destructive ends."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist brute","boulderfist magi","call to arms","drum fel","hammerfall","ogres","thandol span"},rel={"npc:drum-fel","subzone:hammerfall"},m={id=678},src={"In-game quest text: Call to Arms"},fv=true}
E["quest:684"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Marez Cowl",z="general",s="At Stromgarde, Marez Cowl advises Syndicate leaders and traffics with demons. Her influence threatens Alliance forces in the Arathi Highlands.",h="At Stromgarde, Marez Cowl advises Syndicate leaders and traffics with demons.",sec={{t="A Price on Syndicate Leadership",b="At Refuge Pointe, Alliance commanders offer a bounty on a high-ranking Syndicate leader. Marez Cowl advises the Syndicate and directs its work in Stromgarde’s ruins as a field operative. The bounty aims to break the group’s local command.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock of Stromgarde",b="Marez Cowl is a warlock among the Syndicate’s brigands and dispossessed nobles. She deals openly with demonic powers to enforce her will and defend Syndicate territory. To reach her lair in Stromgarde, you must face armed criminals and the demons she commands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marez Cowl?",a="Marez Cowl is a high-ranking Syndicate advisor and operative. She wields influence in the organization and is a dangerous warlock who traffics with demons.",al={"who is marez cowl","marez cowl background","who is she"}},{q="Where is Marez Cowl located?",a="Marez Cowl is in the Syndicate-held part of ruined Stromgarde, in the Arathi Highlands. Criminal forces are entrenched there, and you must find your way through them to reach her lair.",al={"where to find marez cowl","marez cowl location","where is marez"}},{q="Who posted the bounty on Marez Cowl?",a="The Alliance military in the Arathi Highlands offers the bounty. Captain Nials, commander of the Alliance stronghold at Refuge Pointe, oversees it.",al={"who posted bounty marez cowl","who wants marez cowl dead","who pays bounty"}},{q="Why is there a bounty on her head?",a="Marez Cowl is wanted for her Syndicate leadership and her use of demonic summoning in Stromgarde. She threatens the Alliance garrison trying to reclaim the ruined kingdom.",al={"why is marez cowl wanted","why bounty on marez cowl","why kill marez cowl"}},{q="What kind of magic does Marez Cowl use?",a="Marez Cowl uses warlock magic to summon and bargain with demons. Take extreme care when confronting her and the demons she commands.",al={"what makes marez cowl dangerous","marez cowl powers","is marez cowl strong"}},{q="Where do you turn in the bounty for Marez Cowl?",a="After Marez Cowl is slain, deliver her head to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe, the Alliance outpost in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where turn in marez cowl bounty","where is captain nials","turn in marez head"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance garrison at Refuge Pointe, led by Captain Nials, fights to reclaim Stromgarde. High-ranking Syndicate leaders like Marez Cowl are strategic priorities.",["class:Warlock"]="Marez Cowl belongs to the Syndicate’s darker occult wing. Her use of demonic summoning shows how political renegades turn to demons to extend their influence.",["class:Paladin"]="As a warlock who deals openly with demons in the ruins of an ancient human kingdom, Cowl affronts the Holy Light and Stromgarde’s defense."},kw={"arathi highlands","bounty","captain nials","marez cowl","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","warlock"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","topic:syndicate","topic:warlock"},m={id=684},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Marez Cowl"},fv=true}
E["quest:685"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Otto and Falconcrest",z="general",s="In the Arathi Highlands, the Stromgarde Militia has marked Lord Falconcrest and Otto for death. Falconcrest leads the local Syndicate forces, and Otto guards him with deadly skill. Their deaths would weaken the Syndicate's hold in the region. Proof must reach Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.",h="In the Arathi Highlands, the Stromgarde Militia has marked Lord Falconcrest and Otto for death.",sec={{t="A Desperate Bounty",b="From Refuge Pointe, Stromgarde's defenders seek to break the Syndicate's hold over their ancestral lands. The militia has placed a bounty on Lord Falconcrest and Otto, his bodyguard. Bring both targets' heads to Captain Nials to claim the reward.",sp=0},{t="Commander and Enforcer",b="Lord Falconcrest directs the Syndicate's push into the Arathi Highlands. His death would disrupt the criminal network's work in the region. Otto is a brutally effective bodyguard. His blades have killed dozens of Stromgarde's remaining militia soldiers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Falconcrest?",a="Lord Falconcrest is a noble who commands the Syndicate's operations in the Arathi Highlands. He organizes their bid to seize the broken kingdom of Stromgarde, making him a chief target of the local human militia.",al={"who is lord falconcrest","falconcrest lore","who is falconcrest"}},{q="Who is Otto?",a="Otto is Lord Falconcrest's deadly personal bodyguard. A ferocious combatant rather than a strategist, he has slain dozens of Stromgarde defenders in the highlands.",al={"who is otto","falconcrest bodyguard","otto syndicate"}},{q="Why has the Stromgarde Militia placed a bounty on them?",a="The Stromgarde Militia seeks to cripple the Syndicate's leadership in the Arathi Highlands. Falconcrest's death would disrupt their regional command, while Otto's death would remove a lethal threat who has killed many Alliance fighters.",al={"why bounty on falconcrest","why kill otto and falconcrest","stromgarde bounty"}},{q="Who offers the reward for Otto and Falconcrest?",a="Captain Nials, an officer of the Stromgarde Militia at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, collects the bounties for Lord Falconcrest and Otto.",al={"where turn in otto falconcrest","who is captain nials","falconcrest bounty turn in"}},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in the Arathi Highlands?",a="The Syndicate is made up of fallen Alteraci nobles and rogue elements seeking land and riches amid northern Lordaeron's collapse. From the Arathi Highlands, they have moved into Stromgarde's ruins to wrest control from its surviving defenders.",al={"what is the syndicate arathi","syndicate role arathi"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Bring the severed heads of Lord Falconcrest and Otto directly to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe as proof of their deaths.",al={"where to take otto head","proof of bounty"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lord Falconcrest and his Syndicate operatives threaten Stromgarde's remnants. This bounty matters to the effort to reclaim the highlands.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face a personal fight. Bringing down the Syndicate's traitorous human nobles helps avenge your fallen kingdom."},kw={"arathi highlands","bounty","captain nials","falconcrest","otto","refuge pointe","stromgarde militia","syndicate"},rel={"topic:syndicate","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi"},m={id=685},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Otto and Falconcrest"},fv=true}
E["quest:701"] = {t="quest",n="Guile of the Raptor",z="general",s="Tor'gan seeks to awaken Gor'mul's dormant warrior spirit through the guile of the raptor. He gathers Highland Fleshstalker hearts to make an enchanted charm and restore Gor'mul's fighting resolve.",h="Tor'gan seeks to awaken Gor'mul's dormant warrior spirit through the guile of the raptor.",sec={{t="Awakening the Dormant Warrior",b="Tor'gan wants to draw Gor'mul out of his listlessness and restore the warrior spirit that lies dormant. He turns to primal magic instead of persuasion, hoping a charm filled with wild predators' essence will stir Gor'mul to action. Through the charm, he seeks to renew Gor'mul's martial resolve and show him the strength of this power.",sp=0},{t="The Heart of the Predator",b="Tor'gan needs Highland Fleshstalker hearts to call on the instincts of a cunning hunter. In shamanic and primal traditions, a predator's heart carries its ferocity and guile. Tor'gan uses these trophies to make a physical token and weave a spell. He hopes they will give Gor'mul a predator's cunning and help him rediscover his calling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tor'gan?",a="Tor'gan is a spiritual figure who seeks to help Gor'mul. He believes Gor'mul has lost touch with his inner strength, so he gathers reagents for an item infused with beast magic to rouse him.",al={"who is tor'gan","torgan","quest giver"}},{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="Gor'mul has lost his fighting spirit, and the warrior within him lies dormant. Tor'gan means to infuse him with primal predator essence, so Gor'mul can witness new power and rise to fight again.",al={"who is gormul","why help gormul","dormant warrior"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan need raptor hearts?",a="Tor'gan needs twelve raptor hearts to make a physical talisman and weave the enchantment meant to infuse Gor'mul. Primal magic draws on predators' hearts to channel their instincts, guile, and power.",al={"why raptor hearts","what are hearts for","raptor magic"}},{q="Where do the raptor hearts come from?",a="The hearts come from Highland Fleshstalkers, predatory raptors known for relentless hunting and cunning. Tor'gan believes their hearts can fuel the spell that will awaken Gor'mul.",al={"where to get hearts","which raptors","highland fleshstalkers"}},{q="What does the guile of the raptor signify?",a="The guile of the raptor means a predator's cunning, swift reflexes, and lethal instinct. Tor'gan believes this nature can break through Gor'mul's lethargy and revive his combat instincts.",al={"what is guile of the raptor","what power","raptor guile meaning"}},{q="What is the ultimate goal of the ritual?",a="Tor'gan uses the gathered hearts to make an item and weave a spell. He hopes to show Gor'mul new power and awaken his dormant warrior identity, so Gor'mul can reclaim his path.",al={"is gormul cured","what happens after ritual","does it work"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know Tor'gan hopes to rouse Gor'mul's dormant warrior spirit with raptors' cunning and ferocity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see a tradition of drawing on primal beasts and natural spirits to restore purpose to a listless or troubled comrade."},kw={"dormant warrior","gor'mul","guile of the raptor","highland fleshstalkers","raptor hearts","tor'gan","warrior"},rel={"topic:warrior"},m={id=701},src={"In-game quest text: Guile of the Raptor"},fv=true}
E["quest:736"] = {t="quest",n="The Star, the Hand and the Heart",z="general",s="In the Undercity, Keeper Bel'dugur tests those who seek to lead their own circle. To found a new chapter, they need Yagyin's Digest, but he asks for three unnamed items of power.",h="In the Undercity, Keeper Bel'dugur tests those who seek to lead their own circle.",sec={{t="A Test of Brotherhood",b="Practitioners who hope to lead their own circle come to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity. To found a chapter and gather followers, they need Yagyin's Digest, a work of ritual lore in his keeping. Bel'dugur will aid a brother, but first he asks for proof of worthiness before entrusting him with such knowledge.",sp=0},{t="The Unspoken Relics",b="Keeper Bel'dugur asks for three items of power in exchange for Yagyin's Digest. Their names carry peril or sacred weight, so he will not speak them aloud. Instead, he writes them on a private note. Finding all three proves a practitioner worthy of founding a chapter of their own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur lives in the Undercity and aids members of his dark brotherhood. He guards potent lore and asks candidates to prove their worth before entrusting them with sacred texts.",al={"who is keeper bel'dugur","bel'dugur role","beldugur undercity"}},{q="What is Yagyin's Digest?",a="Yagyin's Digest is a work of ritual lore needed to found a new chapter or gather followers within a secretive occult order.",al={"what is yagyin's digest","yagyins digest purpose","yagyin digest book"}},{q="What items does Keeper Bel'dugur ask for?",a="Bel'dugur asks for three items of power. He writes their names on a private note because he will not speak them aloud.",al={"what items does bel'dugur need","beldugurs note items","three items of power"}},{q="Why are the names of the requested items not spoken aloud?",a="Bel'dugur will not speak the names of the three relics aloud. Their peril or sacred significance calls for discretion.",al={"why can't bel'dugur say the item names","cannot utter names","unspoken item names"}},{q="What does it mean to gather another flock?",a="Gathering a flock means recruiting followers and founding an independent chapter of the brotherhood, ready to guide other practitioners.",al={"what does gathering a flock mean","opening a chapter","our order chapter"}},{q="Where is this quest centered?",a="The story centers on Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity, the subterranean Forsaken capital.",al={"where does this quest take place","bel'dugur location","quest hand in location"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you seek Yagyin's Digest to gather a new flock and extend your order's occult mastery.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you find Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity, where he guides Forsaken practitioners seeking forbidden rites."},kw={"bel'dugur's note","keeper bel'dugur","order","the star the hand and the heart","three items of power","undercity","yagyin's digest"},rel={"npc:keeper-bel-dugur","zone:undercity"},m={id=736},src={"In-game quest text: The Star, the Hand and the Heart"},fv=true}
E["quest:744"] = {t="quest",n="Preparation for Ceremony",z="general",s="Eyahn Eagletalon is making a headdress for his brother, who soon stands before Chief Cairne Bloodhoof. He asks you to gather the vibrant feathers from harpies beyond Thunder Bluff while he tans the leather bands.",h="Eyahn Eagletalon is making a headdress for his brother, who soon stands before Chief Cairne Bloodhoof.",sec={{t="Honoring the Chieftain",b="Among the tauren, standing before Chief Cairne Bloodhoof brings pride and reverence. Families honor the occasion by preparing proper attire. The traditional headdress is made from treated leather and symbolic plumage, with each part chosen to show dignity and respect before the leader of the united tribes.",sp=0},{t="Feathers of the Crags",b="A ceremonial headdress needs a leather band and feathers for its crown. While the leather straps are tanned, long, pristine feathers must be gathered. Harpies roost in the craggy hills north and northwest of Thunder Bluff, so you must venture into their hostile nests to find feathers of the needed size and color.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What ceremony is being prepared for?",a="The ceremony marks a tauren appearing before Chief Cairne Bloodhoof. His sibling is making a headdress from tanned leather and vibrant feathers for the occasion.",al={"what ceremony is this","what is the ceremony","who stands before bloodhoof"}},{q="Who is Chief Bloodhoof?",a="Chief Cairne Bloodhoof leads the united tauren tribes from Thunder Bluff. Standing before him is an honor for any tauren.",al={"who is chief bloodhoof","cairne bloodhoof","who is bloodhoof"}},{q="Why are harpy feathers needed for the headdress?",a="The headdress needs feathers of a particular size and color. Its design calls for azure and bronze plumage while the leather straps are tanned.",al={"why do we need harpy feathers","why harpy feathers","why feathers"}},{q="Where are the harpies located?",a="The harpies live in rugged lands north and northwest of Thunder Bluff, in Mulgore.",al={"where do harpies live","where to find harpies","where are azure and bronze feathers"}},{q="What role do harpies play in Mulgore?",a="Harpies are vicious, avian-humanoid creatures that nest in Mulgore’s rocky crags. They threaten travelers and the tribes, while their large, colorful plumage provides material for ceremonial ornaments.",al={"why are harpies hunted","what are harpies"}},{q="Who is crafting the ceremonial headdress?",a="Eyahn Eagletalon tans the leather straps and makes the headdress for his brother, who is preparing to appear before the chieftain.",al={"who makes the headdress","who crafts the headdress"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know that natural headdresses are bound to honor and rites of passage before the high chieftain. Helping make such regalia shows the tribes’ shared pride and spirit.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you honor the customs of your tauren allies atop Thunder Bluff’s mesas when you help with their ceremonial duties."},kw={"cairne bloodhoof","ceremony","feathers","harpy","headdress","mulgore","preparation for ceremony","tauren","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","topic:harpy"},m={id=744},src={"In-game quest text: Preparation for Ceremony"},fv=true}
E["quest:750"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunt Continues",z="general",s="Grull Hawkwind sends young hunters into the southern hills of Red Cloud Mesa for mountain cougar pelts. The hides will clothe the tribe's children and help mend its tents.",h="Grull Hawkwind sends young hunters into the southern hills of Red Cloud Mesa for mountain cougar pelts.",sec={{t="The Purpose of the Hunt",b="At Camp Narache, Grull Hawkwind sends young hunters south into the hills of Red Cloud Mesa to hunt mountain cougars. This is no search for trophies. The hunt teaches young hunters to provide for their community.",sp=0},{t="Shelter for the Tribe",b="Camp Narache needs the pelts to make clothing for the tribe's children and mend worn hide tents. When you bring them back, the elders will be grateful for your contribution. Grull promises to tell his father, Chief Hawkwind, what you have done.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does the tribe need mountain cougar pelts?",a="The tribe needs mountain cougar pelts to make clothing for its children and repair the village tents at Camp Narache. Grull Hawkwind says the hides are needed for both.",al={"why hunt cougars","what are cougar pelts for","mountain cougar pelts use"}},{q="Who offers this quest?",a="Grull Hawkwind offers the hunt at Camp Narache. He is a prominent hunter and the son of Chief Hawkwind, and he guides young hunters in supporting the settlement.",al={"who gives the hunt continues","quest giver camp narache"}},{q="Where are the mountain cougars found?",a="Mountain cougars roam the hills south of Camp Narache on Red Cloud Mesa.",al={"where are the cougars","mountain cougars location","where to find mountain cougar"}},{q="What is Grull Hawkwind's connection to Chief Hawkwind?",a="Grull Hawkwind is the son of Chief Hawkwind, the tribal leader at Camp Narache. Grull promises to speak to his father about your deeds if you bring the needed pelts.",al={"how to impress chief hawkwind","chief hawkwind son"}},{q="What does this hunt teach about tauren tradition?",a="Among the tauren, hunting is not sport or a search for trophies. Using a beast's hide, meat, and bone to sustain the community honors the plains and helps the tribe survive.",al={"tauren hunting philosophy","why hunt in mulgore"}},{q="Why are mountain cougar pelts considered highly valued?",a="Mountain cougar pelts are thick and durable, suited to withstand the elements on the plains. They warm the children and help patch dwellings, so village elders prize them.",al={"are cougar pelts valuable","why are cougar pelts prized"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren coming of age on Red Cloud Mesa, you learn to use every part of a beast for the tribe, from food to clothing and shelter. This is an essential rite of passage.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn the plains' way of the hunt: stalk beasts with purpose, take only what is needed, and never treat them as sport or trophies."},kw={"camp narache","chief hawkwind","grull hawkwind","mountain cougar pelts","red cloud mesa","tauren hunting","the hunt continues"},rel={"npc:grull-hawkwind","subzone:camp-narache","npc:chief-hawkwind"},m={id=750},src={"In-game quest text: The Hunt Continues"},fv=true}
E["quest:755"] = {t="quest",n="Rites of the Earthmother",z="general",s="On Red Cloud Mesa, young tauren begin their spiritual journey under Chief Hawkwind's care. He sends them south of Camp Narache to Seer Graytongue, who guides their first steps toward the trials.",h="On Red Cloud Mesa, young tauren begin their spiritual journey under Chief Hawkwind's care.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Trials",b="On Red Cloud Mesa, Chief Hawkwind sends young tauren to Seer Graytongue in the hills south of Camp Narache. The seer guides the youth as their spiritual path begins. This journey carries them beyond everyday camp life and toward the duties their tribal customs demand.",sp=0},{t="Embracing the Earthmother",b="The Earthmother shapes tauren beliefs about creation and daily life. Her rites test maturity, resilience, and spiritual depth. Seer Graytongue warns those who reach his sanctuary that the trials call for full devotion to the traditions of the mesa.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Rites of the Earthmother?",a="Chief Hawkwind directs young tauren from Camp Narache to seek Seer Graytongue in the surrounding hills.",al={"who starts rites of the earthmother","quest giver"}},{q="Where can I find Seer Graytongue?",a="Seer Graytongue lives in the hills directly south of Camp Narache, on Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore.",al={"where is seer graytongue","graytongue location","find graytongue"}},{q="What are the Rites of the Earthmother?",a="The Rites of the Earthmother are sacred traditional trials where tauren youths prove their wisdom, strength, and devotion to their people and beliefs.",al={"what are rites of the earthmother","earthmother trials lore"}},{q="Who is Seer Graytongue?",a="Seer Graytongue is a respected spiritual elder who lives south of Camp Narache and guides initiates through the Earthmother's sacred trials.",al={"who is seer graytongue","graytongue role"}},{q="Who is Chief Hawkwind?",a="Chief Hawkwind leads Camp Narache on Red Cloud Mesa and prepares young tauren before sending them to the seers.",al={"who is chief hawkwind","hawkwind role"}},{q="What is required to complete this task?",a="You travel south from Camp Narache into the hills and speak with Seer Graytongue to report that you are ready for the trials.",al={"what do i need to do","how to complete quest"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you begin a spiritual journey through the Rites of the Earthmother. They test your readiness to serve your tribe and revere the Earthmother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see the spiritual heart of your tauren allies, who have recently joined the Horde, in these sacred trials.",["class:Shaman"]="As an aspiring shaman, you begin with rites blessed by tribal seers. They are an essential first step toward communion with the elements and the spirits of Mulgore.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you begin your path toward harmony with nature by honoring the sacred guidance of tribal elders and seers."},kw={"camp narache","chief hawkwind","earthmother","red cloud mesa","rites of the earthmother","seer graytongue","tauren"},rel={"npc:seer-graytongue","npc:chief-hawkwind","subzone:camp-narache","quest:763"},m={id=755},src={"In-game quest text: Rites of the Earthmother"},fv=true}
E["quest:76156"] = {t="quest",n="Stalk With The Earthmother",z="general",s="Boarton Shadetotem sees a talent for subtlety in you and asks you to enter the Venture Company mine. He wants Seaforium Mining Charges taken from the mine’s supply carts.",h="Boarton Shadetotem sees a talent for subtlety in you and asks you to enter the Venture Company mine.",sec={{t="A Subtle Approach",b="Boarton Shadetotem, in Thunder Bluff, believes you can work with subtlety. He gives you a mask and asks you to enter the nearby Venture Company mine. There, you are to take Seaforium Mining Charges from carts of blasting supplies and bring them back to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks me to enter the mine?",a="Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff asks you to enter the Venture Company mine.",al={"who is Boarton","Boarton Shadetotem","who gave this"}},{q="What am I looking for in the mine?",a="You are asked to take Seaforium Mining Charges from carts of blasting supplies.",al={"what to steal","mine supplies","seaforium charges"}},{q="Why does Boarton give me a mask?",a="Boarton gives you a mask for entering the nearby Venture Company mine.",al={"mask disguise","why the mask","infiltrate mine"}},{q="Where is the Venture Company mine?",a="The mine is southeast of Thunder Bluff.",al={"mine location","where is the mine","venture company mine"}},{q="Who are the supplies taken from?",a="The supplies are in the Venture Company mine.",al={"who owns supplies","venture company supplies","company mine"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Boarton believes you have a talent for subtlety and asks you to enter the Venture Company mine."},kw={"blasting supplies","boarton shadetotem","mask","mine","seaforium mining charges","subtlety","thunder bluff","venture company"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","topic:venture-company","topic:rogue"},m={id=76156},src={"In-game quest text: Stalk With The Earthmother"},fv=true}
E["quest:76160"] = {t="quest",n="Stalk With The Earthmother",z="general",s="Boarton Shadetotem asks you to make a salve from Windfury Cones found north of Thunder Bluff. He hopes it will make a blade's wounds burn with bitter force.",h="Boarton Shadetotem asks you to make a salve from Windfury Cones found north of Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Bitter Salve",b="Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff wants a venomous salve, made from cones gathered near the Harpies' nests to the north. You are to crush the Windfury Cones with a mortar and pestle, then bring him the result. He warns that the finished salve may hurt even on the skin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the salve?",a="Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff asks you to prepare a salve from Windfury Cones.",al={"who wants the salve","Boarton Shadetotem request"}},{q="Where do the Windfury Cones grow?",a="The Harpies north of Thunder Bluff nest in a tree that produces the toxic resin. Fallen cones lie around their nests.",al={"where find cones","Windfury Cone location"}},{q="What is the salve meant to do?",a="Applied to a blade, the salve is meant to make an opponent's wounds burn and turn their blood to salt.",al={"what does salve do","poison blade salve"}},{q="Why does Boarton warn about touching it?",a="Boarton says even skin contact with the finished salve could be painful.",al={"salve skin warning","is the salve dangerous"}}},kw={"boarton shadetotem","harpies","mortar and pestle","salve","stalk with the earthmother","thunder bluff","windfury cones"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","topic:harpy"},m={id=76160},src={"In-game quest text: Stalk With The Earthmother"},fv=true}
E["quest:76240"] = {t="quest",n="Stalk With The Earthmother",z="general",s="Boarton Shadetotem asks you to fillet a Raw Brilliant Smallfish in Thunder Bluff. He hopes the exercise will reveal a talent for subtle arts.",h="Boarton Shadetotem asks you to fillet a Raw Brilliant Smallfish in Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Final Trial",b="Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff asks you to show what comes naturally with his Knife Set. Bring him a Raw Brilliant Smallfish and fillet it before him. He hopes this less direct test will uncover hidden talent.",sp=0},{t="Parting Words",b="Boarton Shadetotem sees that you lack the rogueish precision he sought. He offers a parting gift and sends you on your travels, wishing the Horde heroes like you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to fillet a fish?",a="Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff asks you to fillet a Raw Brilliant Smallfish with his Knife Set.",al={"who is boarton","boarton shadetotem","fish knife quest"}},{q="Why does Boarton want me to fillet a fish?",a="Boarton hopes the exercise will bring out a hidden talent for subtle arts.",al={"why fillet fish","what is boarton testing","smallfish test"}},{q="What fish does Boarton ask for?",a="Boarton asks for a Raw Brilliant Smallfish.",al={"which fish","raw smallfish","brilliant fish"}},{q="Where do I fillet the fish?",a="Fillet the Raw Brilliant Smallfish in front of Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.",al={"where fish task","thunder bluff fish","where use knife set"}}},kw={"boarton shadetotem","knife set","raw brilliant smallfish","stalk with the earthmother","subtle arts","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","topic:horde"},m={id=76240},src={"In-game quest text: Stalk With The Earthmother"},fv=true}
E["quest:7792"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="In Darnassus, wool cloth is gathered to support the city's stores. Your sixty pieces earn recognition for your generosity.",h="In Darnassus, wool cloth is gathered to support the city's stores.",sec={{t="Wool Stores",b="Darnassus needs sixty pieces of wool cloth from you. Others across the realm are expected to provide the rest of its stores. Your donation earns full recognition for your generosity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Darnassus need?",a="Darnassus needs wool cloth to support its stores.",al={"wool donation","what cloth does Darnassus want"}},{q="How much wool do I need to donate?",a="You need to donate sixty pieces of wool cloth.",al={"how many wool","sixty wool"}},{q="Why is Darnassus collecting wool?",a="Darnassus is gathering wool cloth to support its stores.",al={"why wool","wool drive"}},{q="What do I get for donating wool?",a="Your donation of sixty pieces earns full recognition from Darnassus for your generosity.",al={"wool donation recognition","donate wool reward"}}},kw={"darnassus","donation","recognition","stores","wool","wool cloth"},rel={"zone:darnassus"},m={id=7792},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:7802"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="At Ironforge, wool donations help support its stores. Sixty pieces bring full recognition for your generosity.",h="At Ironforge, wool donations help support its stores.",sec={{t="Wool Stores",b="Ironforge asks you for sixty pieces of wool cloth. Its stores need only that much from you. Others are expected to give enough to support the drive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How much wool does Ironforge need from me?",a="Sixty pieces of wool cloth, for Ironforge.",al={"wool donation amount","how many wool","sixty wool"}},{q="What do I get for donating wool?",a="Give Ironforge sixty pieces of wool cloth, and you earn full recognition for your generosity.",al={"wool donation reward","what for wool","ironforge recognition"}},{q="Why is Ironforge collecting wool?",a="Ironforge gathers wool cloth to support its stores.",al={"wool drive","why wool donation","ironforge wool"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, your wool donation earns recognition from Ironforge."},kw={"donation","ironforge","recognition","sixty pieces","stores","wool","wool cloth"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=7802},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:7807"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="Across the realm, A Donation of Wool calls for aid to the Gnomeregan Exiles. Driven from Gnomeregan, they need wool cloth to sustain their displaced people. Sixty pieces earn formal recognition among the gnomes.",h="Across the realm, A Donation of Wool calls for aid to the Gnomeregan Exiles.",sec={{t="A Displaced People's Needs",b="Gnomeregan's fall to trogg invaders and radioactive contamination drove its surviving gnomes from their high-tech city. They now live as refugees, hosted chiefly by their dwarven cousins in Ironforge.\n\nOutside their ancestral halls, the Gnomeregan Exiles face severe strain in supplying their people. Regular drives for cloth and other basics help keep them clothed, supplied, and organized.",sp=0},{t="The Textile Drive",b="The drive asks each volunteer for exactly sixty pieces of wool cloth. By gathering modest contributions from across the realm, the exiles can collect the textiles they need for bedding, bandages, and clothing without overburdening any one supplier. Those who aid their recovery receive formal recognition among their people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Gnomeregan Exiles need wool cloth?",a="The Gnomeregan Exiles are gathering basic textile supplies. Driven from their home city, their refugee population needs wool cloth to sustain its people and ongoing operations.",al={"why wool","what is the wool for","wool donation purpose"}},{q="How much wool cloth is needed?",a="The drive asks each contributor for sixty pieces of wool cloth. The organizers count on contributions from across the realm to meet their supply needs.",al={"how much wool","donation amount","wool required"}},{q="Who is organizing this donation drive?",a="Representatives of the Gnomeregan Exiles organize the collection and receive donations for the displaced gnomes sheltering among their allies.",al={"who takes donation","who is accepting wool","donation recipient"}},{q="Can you donate wool cloth more than once?",a="Each donor is asked for one contribution of sixty pieces. The exiles need that fixed amount from you and rely on contributors across the realm to meet their quota.",al={"can i donate again","is it repeatable","more wool donations"}},{q="What recognition do the Gnomeregan Exiles offer?",a="Donating sixty pieces earns recognition and gratitude from the Gnomeregan Exiles. It shows your loyalty and support for their displaced people in a time of crisis.",al={"gnomeregan exiles standing","gnome reputation","exile recognition"}},{q="Why are the gnomes currently in exile?",a="The gnomes fled their subterranean home in Gnomeregan after a catastrophic disaster and trogg invasion. As refugees, they depend on temporary encampments, aid from allies, and material drives.",al={"why are gnomes in exile","where is gnomeregan","gnome refugee crisis"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Contributing raw materials strengthens Alliance solidarity and helps sustain a vital ally displaced from its mountain home.",["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, gathering wool helps resupply your displaced kin as they survive and rebuild outside Gnomeregan.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors who gather or weave wool cloth have an ample supply of textiles that refugee populations need for basic garments and supplies."},kw={"cloth drive","donation of wool","gnome","gnomeregan","gnomeregan exiles","textiles","wool cloth"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan"},m={id=7807},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:78124"] = {t="quest",n="Nar'thalas Almanac",z="general",s="Scholars seek the Nar'thalas Almanac to preserve ancient magical study. Its recovery brings forgotten lore into a library where researchers can study it.",h="Scholars seek the Nar'thalas Almanac to preserve ancient magical study.",sec={{t="A Relic of Ancient Study",b="A rare work of arcane study, the Nar'thalas Almanac comes from the ancient traditions of pre-Sundering night elven scholarship. For caretakers of great archives, securing the volume rescues centuries-old lore from obscurity and adds an important piece of history to their shelves. Those who uncover neglected works help bridge forgotten antiquity and modern scholarship.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Archives",b="Across Azeroth, archivists and researchers seek lost treatises, field notes, and chronicles. Bringing the Nar'thalas Almanac to a dedicated library lets its keepers safeguard, catalog, and study it, rather than leave it to rot in ruins or fall into careless hands. Each recovered volume offers fresh insight into the arcane arts of past eras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Nar'thalas Almanac?",a="The Nar'thalas Almanac is a rare ancient manuscript of magical scholarship sought by curators for their historical archives. Those who recover it place its insights in scholarly care, where they can be preserved and cataloged.",al={"what is the narthalas almanac","narthalas almanac quest","almanac info"}},{q="Who is collecting the Nar'thalas Almanac?",a="Library scholars interested in ancient magical texts and historical archives collect the almanac. Curators actively seek additions to expand their shared knowledge of the world's arcane heritage.",al={"who wants the almanac","where does the almanac go","almanac turn in"}},{q="What does the name Nar'thalas refer to?",a="Nar'thalas was an ancient Kaldorei center of learning and magical study before the Great Sundering. Texts bearing its name preserve fragments of pre-Sundering arcane arts and elven knowledge.",al={"what is narthalas","narthalas lore","where is narthalas"}},{q="Why are magical texts being collected for the library?",a="Historical records and magical treatises were displaced, lost, or buried in ruins across Azeroth. Scholars study recovered writings to broaden their understanding of arcane currents and guard fragile records against being lost entirely.",al={"why collect magical works","library purpose","why books matter"}},{q="Can other magical works be brought to the library?",a="Treatises, tomes, and forgotten manuscripts can shed light on arcane theory and ancient history. Scholars continually seek additions to enrich their shelves.",al={"more magical books","other tomes","more texts"}},{q="Is the Nar'thalas Almanac dangerous to handle?",a="The almanac is a compiled record of study, not a volatile forbidden artifact. Historians and practitioners can use it as a valuable reference on historical magic.",al={"is the almanac dangerous","does almanac have dark magic","safe to read"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the scholarly value of texts on ancient arcane traditions. Adding recovered works to a library's magical collection matters deeply.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you know Nar'thalas as an ancient center of Kaldorei arcane scholarship before the Sundering shattered the old world. An almanac bearing its name links you to ancient night elven history.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can help scholars and curators in Alliance archives seek rare manuscripts and expand the realm's gathered lore."},kw={"almanac","arcane","book","library","magical works","nar'thalas","narthalas","tome"},m={id=78124},src={"In-game quest text: Nar'thalas Almanac"},fv=true}
E["quest:78127"] = {t="quest",n="The Dalaran Digest",z="general",s="The librarian asks you to bring magical works for the collection. Each book adds knowledge to the library.",h="The librarian asks you to bring magical works for the collection.",sec={{t="The Collection",b="The librarian welcomes magical works that may benefit the library. You bring a book to join the collection, helping its knowledge grow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the librarian want?",a="The librarian asks you to bring magical works that may benefit the collection.",al={"what to bring","library book","magical works"}},{q="Where do I bring the book?",a="Bring the book to the librarian who asked you to add it to the collection.",al={"where is the librarian","library location"}},{q="Why is the librarian collecting magical works?",a="Your contribution brings more knowledge to the collection.",al={"why collect books","library purpose"}}},kw={"collection","dalaran digest","knowledge","librarian","library","magical works"},m={id=78127},src={"In-game quest text: The Dalaran Digest"},fv=true}
E["quest:78142"] = {t="quest",n="Bewitchments and Glamours",z="general",s="In Ironforge, the library is seeking magical works for its shelves. You can help its keepers widen their knowledge by bringing in books that may benefit the collection.",h="In Ironforge, the library is seeking magical works for its shelves.",sec={{t="A Growing Collection",b="Bring magical works to the library in Ironforge, where each addition can broaden what its keepers know.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the library want?",a="The library seeks magical works that may benefit its collection.",al={"what do they want","library books","magical works"}},{q="Where do I bring the magical works?",a="Bring the magical works to the library.",al={"where bring books","where is the library","ironforge library"}},{q="Why are they collecting magical works?",a="The library says the works will expand its knowledge.",al={"why collect magic books","what is the collection for"}}},kw={"bewitchments and glamours","books","collection","ironforge","library","magical works"},m={id=78142},src={"In-game quest text: Bewitchments and Glamours"},fv=true}
E["quest:78143"] = {t="quest",n="Secrets of the Dreamers",z="general",s="A library's scholars seek writings tied to the Dreamers and other magical lore. Travelers bring forgotten works from across the realm, where they can be studied and kept in the archives.",h="A library's scholars seek writings tied to the Dreamers and other magical lore.",sec={{t="Recovering Forgotten Lore",b="Scholars across the realm depend on travelers to recover rare magical texts and historical treatises. These works lie in ancient ruins or private hoards, far from the archives. So adventurers carry them safely to those who study Azeroth's arcane mysteries and preserve its lore.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Archives",b="When travelers bring in treatises, archivists add them to the library's permanent collection. Researchers seek obscure writings on the Emerald Dream and arcane theory. Their work continues, and they welcome further magical texts found in the field.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Secrets of the Dreamers?",a="Travelers recover magical writings and obscure knowledge, then bring them to a library's scholars to enrich the archives.",al={"what is secrets of the dreamers","secrets of dreamers quest","what do you do in this quest"}},{q="Who collects these magical texts?",a="A scholar overseeing a library's collection gathers the texts, asking travelers to bring in magical works.",al={"who wants secrets of the dreamers","who gives this quest","where to turn in secrets of the dreamers"}},{q="Where are the recovered works stored?",a="The writings go into an institutional library's growing archives, where Alliance scholars and researchers can catalog and preserve rare lore and magical discoveries.",al={"what is the collection","which library is this for","where do the books go"}},{q="What does the title refer to by \"the Dreamers\"?",a="The Dreamers refers to druids attuned to the Emerald Dream or ancient sleeping entities bound to nature's slumber. Writings bearing their secrets preserve mysterious primal power.",al={"who are the dreamers","dreamers lore","why is it called dreamers"}},{q="Can you bring more magical works after finishing the quest?",a="The archivists welcome further contributions. When you find magical writings that may aid the collection, you can bring them in for continued research.",al={"can i turn in more books","is this repeatable","more magical works"}},{q="Why is collecting these magical writings important to scholars?",a="Scholars seek to widen their understanding of arcane, natural, and obscure lore. Lost or scattered treatises may hold insights into the world's deeper history and mysteries.",al={"why gather magical books","why does the library need magic tomes"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can seek obscure tomes and magical texts to enrich scholarly archives.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, writings tied to nature magic and the Emerald Dream hold deep meaning in the Cenarion arts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scholars, especially those who keep great repositories, depend on champions to recover lost knowledge from dangerous places."},kw={"arcane","dreamers","library","magical works","scholars","secrets of the dreamers","tomes"},m={id=78143},src={"In-game quest text: Secrets of the Dreamers"},fv=true}
E["quest:78145"] = {t="quest",n="Arcanic Systems Manual",z="general",s="The Arcanic Systems Manual is a magical work sought for a library's collection. Adding it helps the library expand its knowledge.",h="The Arcanic Systems Manual is a magical work sought for a library's collection.",sec={{t="A Place in the Library",b="The library welcomes magical works that can benefit its collection. You bring one to add, and your contribution helps its knowledge grow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Arcanic Systems Manual?",a="It is a magical work sought for a library's collection.",al={"arcanic manual","what manual"}},{q="Who wants the manual?",a="A librarian asks you to bring magical works that may benefit the collection.",al={"who asked for it","manual for who"}},{q="Why bring the manual to the library?",a="The library's knowledge grows through contributions of magical works.",al={"why donate it","what's it for"}}},kw={"arcanic","arcanic systems manual","collection","ironforge","library","magical works","manual"},m={id=78145},src={"In-game quest text: Arcanic Systems Manual"},fv=true}
E["quest:78146"] = {t="quest",n="Goaz Scrolls",z="general",s="The librarian asks you to bring Goaz Scrolls for the collection. Your contribution adds to the library’s knowledge.",h="The librarian asks you to bring Goaz Scrolls for the collection.",sec={{t="A Growing Collection",b="The librarian thanks you for contributing Goaz Scrolls. More magical works could help the library too, and the librarian welcomes them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Goaz Scrolls for?",a="Goaz Scrolls add to the library’s collection and knowledge.",al={"goaz scrolls purpose","why bring scrolls","scrolls library"}},{q="Who asks for the Goaz Scrolls?",a="A librarian asks you to bring Goaz Scrolls for the collection.",al={"who wants goaz scrolls","scrolls giver","library person"}},{q="Where are the scrolls going?",a="The Goaz Scrolls are for the library’s collection.",al={"where bring scrolls","goaz scrolls location","library scrolls"}},{q="What else would benefit the library?",a="The librarian welcomes other magical works that might benefit the library.",al={"other magical works","more library books","what else to bring"}}},kw={"collection","goaz scrolls","knowledge","library","magical works","scrolls"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=78146},src={"In-game quest text: Goaz Scrolls"},fv=true}
E["quest:78147"] = {t="quest",n="Crimes Against Anatomy",z="general",s="A librarian asks you to add magical works to the collection in Ironforge. Your discoveries help expand the library’s knowledge.",h="A librarian asks you to add magical works to the collection in Ironforge.",sec={{t="For the Collection",b="The library in Ironforge seeks magical works that could benefit its collection. You can bring discoveries to the librarian, whose knowledge grows through these contributions. More works may yet be of use to the library.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for magical works?",a="A librarian in Ironforge asks you to bring magical works that could benefit the collection.",al={"who wants books","library request"}},{q="Where do I bring the works?",a="Bring them to the librarian in the Library in Ironforge.",al={"where is the library","bring books where"}},{q="Why collect magical works?",a="The works help expand the library’s knowledge.",al={"why books","what for magical works"}}},kw={"collection","crimes against anatomy","ironforge","librarian","library","magical works"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=78147},src={"In-game quest text: Crimes Against Anatomy"},fv=true}
E["quest:78148"] = {t="quest",n="Runes of the Sorcerer-Kings",z="general",s="The Library in Ironforge welcomes magical works for its collection. Your discoveries help expand its knowledge.",h="The Library in Ironforge welcomes magical works for its collection.",sec={{t="The Collection",b="The library's keeper thanks you as its collection grows through your efforts. More magical works may add to its knowledge, and the keeper welcomes them for the library.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the library want?",a="The library welcomes magical works that may benefit its collection.",al={"what do they want","library books","magical works"}},{q="Where is the library?",a="The library is in Ironforge.",al={"library location","where's the library","ironforge library"}},{q="Why bring magical works?",a="Your efforts expand the library's knowledge.",al={"why books","what for","help the library"}}},kw={"collection","ironforge","knowledge","library","magical works","runes","sorcerer-kings"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=78148},src={"In-game quest text: Runes of the Sorcerer-Kings"},fv=true}
E["quest:78149"] = {t="quest",n="Fury of the Land",z="general",s="The Library in Ironforge seeks magical works for its collection. Your findings help expand its knowledge.",h="The Library in Ironforge seeks magical works for its collection.",sec={{t="A Place for Knowledge",b="In Ironforge's Library, you are asked to bring magical works that may benefit its collection. The librarian welcomes what you have found, and invites you to bring more if you discover it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the library want?",a="The Library seeks magical works that may benefit its collection.",al={"what do they need","library books","magical works"}},{q="Where should I bring magical works?",a="Bring them to the librarian in the Library in Ironforge.",al={"where to take books","library location","bring works"}},{q="Why are they collecting magical works?",a="The librarian says each contribution expands their knowledge.",al={"why collect magic books","library collection","what for"}}},kw={"collection","fury of the land","ironforge","knowledge","library","magical works"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=78149},src={"In-game quest text: Fury of the Land"},fv=true}
E["quest:7820"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="Thunder Bluff seeks wool cloth, and you can earn its full recognition by giving sixty pieces. Other donors are expected to bring enough supplies to support the drive.",h="Thunder Bluff seeks wool cloth, and you can earn its full recognition by giving sixty pieces.",sec={{t="A Cloth Donation",b="Thunder Bluff is gathering wool cloth. Give sixty pieces to earn full recognition for your generosity. Other donors in the realm are expected to bring enough to support the drive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Thunder Bluff want donated?",a="Thunder Bluff is accepting wool cloth donations.",al={"wool donation","what cloth do they need","donate wool"}},{q="How much wool cloth should I give?",a="Give sixty pieces of wool cloth to earn full recognition from Thunder Bluff.",al={"how many wool","sixty cloth","donation amount"}},{q="What do I get for donating wool?",a="Your gift of sixty pieces of wool cloth earns full recognition from Thunder Bluff.",al={"wool donation recognition","what's the recognition","donation reward"}},{q="Why is Thunder Bluff collecting wool?",a="Thunder Bluff expects other donors in the realm to provide enough wool cloth to support the donation drive.",al={"wool drive why","what is wool for","why collect cloth"}}},kw={"cloth drive","donation","recognition","sixty pieces","thunder bluff","wool","wool cloth"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=7820},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:7826"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="In Orgrimmar, A Donation of Wool asks for help gathering cloth. The city has wool in its stores and expects more donors to bring in enough for the drive.",h="In Orgrimmar, A Donation of Wool asks for help gathering cloth.",sec={{t="Wool for Orgrimmar",b="Orgrimmar asks you to give sixty pieces of wool cloth. In return, the city promises recognition. Its stores already hold some wool, and other donors are expected to help support the drive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Orgrimmar asking for?",a="Orgrimmar is accepting donations of wool cloth.",al={"what do they want","wool donation"}},{q="How much wool do I need to donate?",a="Orgrimmar asks for sixty pieces of wool cloth.",al={"how many wool","sixty wool"}},{q="What do I get for donating wool?",a="You earn full recognition from Orgrimmar for donating sixty pieces of wool cloth.",al={"donation recognition","wool reward"}},{q="Why is Orgrimmar collecting wool?",a="Orgrimmar is gathering wool to support its donation drive.",al={"wool drive","why wool"}},{q="Does Orgrimmar already have wool?",a="Yes. Orgrimmar has wool in its stores and expects other donors to bring in enough for the drive.",al={"wool stores","how much wool"}}},kw={"a donation of wool","donation","orgrimmar","recognition","sixty pieces","wool","wool cloth"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=7826},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:78261"] = {t="quest",n="The Horn of Xelthos",z="general",s="A note from C asks you to retrieve the Horn of Xelthos from Shadowfang Keep alone. Veenix in the Stonetalon Mountains may help you through the courtyard gate.",h="A note from C asks you to retrieve the Horn of Xelthos from Shadowfang Keep alone.",sec={{t="A Quiet Approach",b="C leaves the note near Pyrewood Village and names Veenix as a contact in the Stonetalon Mountains. The Horn of Xelthos lies somewhere inside Shadowfang Keep, where entering usually calls for backup. C wants the work kept quiet, so you are to go alone and bring the horn back to the dead drop.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the Horn of Xelthos?",a="C leaves a note asking you to retrieve the Horn of Xelthos and return it to the dead drop near Pyrewood Village.",al={"who is C","who wants the horn","C horn job"}},{q="Where is the Horn of Xelthos?",a="The Horn of Xelthos is somewhere inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"where horn","horn location","find Xelthos"}},{q="Why do I have to go alone?",a="C says the work requires a low profile, so you are to enter Shadowfang Keep alone.",al={"why solo","go alone why","no backup"}},{q="Who is Veenix?",a="Veenix is C's contact in the Stonetalon Mountains, and may help you get past Shadowfang Keep's courtyard gate.",al={"Veenix help","who Veenix","gate contact"}},{q="Where do I return the horn?",a="Return the horn to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village.",al={"where return horn","dead drop location","turn in horn"}}},kw={"c","dead drop","horn of xelthos","pyrewood village","shadowfang keep","stonetalon mountains","veenix","xelthos"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","zone:stonetalon","subzone:pyrewood-village"},m={id=78261},src={"In-game quest text: The Horn of Xelthos"},fv=true}
E["quest:7833"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="A Darkspear troll gathers wool donations, and your sixty pieces of Wool Cloth join a larger collection.",h="A Darkspear troll gathers wool donations, and your sixty pieces of Wool Cloth join a larger collection.",sec={{t="A Shared Collection",b="The Darkspear trolls are gathering Wool Cloth to replenish their stores. The collector can take your sixty pieces now, while help from others is expected to complete the collection.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is being collected?",a="The Darkspear trolls are gathering Wool Cloth.",al={"what do they need","wool donation"}},{q="How much Wool Cloth do they need from me?",a="The collector needs sixty pieces of Wool Cloth from you.",al={"how much wool","60 cloth"}},{q="Why are the trolls collecting wool?",a="The trolls are gathering wool to replenish their stores.",al={"why wool","what for"}},{q="Can I give the cloth now?",a="Yes. The collector can accept your sixty pieces of Wool Cloth now.",al={"where give wool","donate now"}}},kw={"collection","darkspear","donation","stores","trolls","wool","wool cloth"},m={id=7833},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:789"] = {t="quest",n="Sting of the Scorpid",z="general",s="At the Den in the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new Horde recruits after scorpids northwest of camp. Ten tails will prove they can face danger in battle.",h="At the Den in the Valley of Trials, Gornek sends new Horde recruits after scorpids northwest of camp.",sec={{t="Trial of the Stinger",b="Gornek tests novice Horde recruits against the Valley of Trials' wildlife. Scorpid workers roam the rocks northwest of the Den. Their venom has humbled seasoned warriors and clumsy initiates alike. Recruits must face them and bring back ten tails as proof of their skill.",sp=0},{t="Venom and Vigilance",b="Scorpids are dangerous, yet their venom also helps save injured initiates. The Den keeps antivenom brewed from extracted scorpid venom to treat fallen novices. Gornek teaches recruits to stay watchful in battle. Even a small foe can wield enough venom to fell a mighty warrior.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns Sting of the Scorpid?",a="Gornek oversees novice training at the Den in the Valley of Trials. He assigns the hunt to young warriors and adventurers.",al={"who gives sting of the scorpid","scorpid quest giver","gornek quest"}},{q="Where are the scorpids located?",a="Scorpid workers roam northwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"where to find scorpids","scorpid location","valley of trials scorpids"}},{q="What does Gornek require from the hunt?",a="Gornek requires ten Scorpid Worker Tails as proof that a recruit has faced the venomous beasts and won.",al={"what do scorpids drop","scorpid quest item","scorpid tails"}},{q="How is the antidote for scorpid venom created?",a="The Den brews antivenom from venom extracted from scorpid stingers. It keeps stores on hand to treat novices who underestimate their prey.",al={"scorpid venom cure","antidote lore","how is scorpid antidote made"}},{q="What lesson does Gornek want recruits to learn?",a="Gornek teaches recruits that any opponent, large or small, can be lethal. Overconfidence against a seemingly minor foe can prove fatal.",al={"gornek lesson","why hunt scorpids","scorpid trial purpose"}},{q="Does Gornek offer further training after this hunt?",a="After you deliver the tails, Gornek says he has nothing left to teach you at the Den. He sends you onward into Durotar to serve the Horde.",al={"what after sting of the scorpid","gornek next quest","does gornek teach more"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As a young orc coming of age in the Valley of Trials, you face an essential test of endurance and battlefield awareness under Gornek's eye.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll training alongside the Horde in the Valley of Trials, you prove your skill against local scorpids before venturing deeper into Durotar.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you learn from Gornek that decisive strikes can overcome tough carapaces. Arrogance toward smaller foes invites defeat."},kw={"antidote","durotar","gornek","scorpid","scorpid worker","sting of the scorpid","the den","valley of trials","venom"},rel={"npc:gornek","topic:warrior"},m={id=789},src={"In-game quest text: Sting of the Scorpid"},fv=true}
E["quest:79007"] = {t="quest",n="... and that note you found",z="general",s="At a recent campsite, cooling embers and scattered supplies are all that remain. A scorched parchment bears a riddle about finding a twin land, the only clue left behind.",h="At a recent campsite, cooling embers and scattered supplies are all that remain.",sec={{t="Embers in the Wild",b="A recent campfire is dying beside scattered provisions and a blistered piece of paper. Whoever stayed here left recently, and the parchment narrowly escaped the flames. The supplies remain exposed, as though the traveler departed in haste or was interrupted.",sp=0},{t="A Cryptic Riddle",b="The surviving scrap bears one instruction: “Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.” No signature, coordinates, or further context survived the fire. The riddle is the only trail left for whoever finds it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the note found at the campsite say?",a="The charred, blistered note reads: “Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.” It is the only clue left at the abandoned campsite.",al={"what does the note say","note text","blistered note"}},{q="Who left the note behind?",a="The note's author is unknown. It was found among scattered provisions beside the dying embers of a recent campfire, suggesting whoever wrote or carried it left recently or was forced to depart in haste.",al={"where did the note come from","who wrote the note","who made the fire"}},{q="What does 'the twin land' refer to?",a="The note's “twin land” means a matching or mirrored place. The charred fragment gives no further explanation, leaving its meaning for travelers to unravel.",al={"what is twin land","twin land clue"}},{q="How do you follow the clues on the note?",a="The charred note is your only guide, with no destination marked on a map. Its riddle points you to seek a land or place that echoes its description.",al={"what to do with the note","where does this quest go"}},{q="Why was the campsite abandoned?",a="The campsite shows signs of a sudden departure or disturbance. Scattered provisions lie beside fading embers, and no other identifying gear or signs remain beyond the blistered scrap.",al={"who abandoned the provisions","scattered provisions campsite"}},{q="Are there any other clues at the fire?",a="No other writings or markers remain intact at the campfire. The flames destroyed almost everything, leaving only the blistered paper as evidence of whoever rested there.",al={"does the fire reveal anything else","campsite clues"}}},kw={"and that note you found","blistered note","charred note","embers","recent fire","scattered provisions","twin land"},m={id=79007},src={"In-game quest text: ... and that note you found"},fv=true}
E["quest:7905"] = {t="quest",n="The Darkmoon Faire",z="general",s="You carry a Free Ticket Voucher to Gelvas Grimgate inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival. The voucher is meant for him.",h="You carry a Free Ticket Voucher to Gelvas Grimgate inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival.",sec={{t="A Voucher for Gelvas",b="Gelvas Grimgate is inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival, and you carry a Free Ticket Voucher for him. The voucher awaits delivery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the voucher for?",a="The Free Ticket Voucher is for Gelvas Grimgate, who is inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival.",al={"voucher for who","Gelvas voucher"}},{q="Where is Gelvas Grimgate?",a="Gelvas Grimgate is inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival.",al={"where's Gelvas","Gelvas location"}},{q="What do I bring to Gelvas?",a="Bring the Free Ticket Voucher to Gelvas Grimgate.",al={"what voucher","ticket voucher"}}},kw={"carnival","darkmoon faire","free ticket voucher","gelvas grimgate","voucher"},m={id=7905},src={"In-game quest text: The Darkmoon Faire"},fv=true}
E["quest:79091"] = {t="quest",n="Archmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography",z="general",s="In Ironforge, you seek Archmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography. The rare volume holds the late Kirin Tor leader's own account and offers insight into Dalaran's history and high arcane scholarship.",h="In Ironforge, you seek Archmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography.",sec={{t="The Words of the Grand Magus",b="Archmage Antonidas led the Kirin Tor for decades and ruled Dalaran. One of Azeroth's most brilliant minds, he rose through the ranks of the Violet Citadel and mastered the arcane. His unabridged autobiography records his leadership during the Second and Third Wars. For scholars and practitioners of magic, it offers a firsthand view of Dalaran's inner workings and the arcane arts.",sp=0},{t="From the Great Library of Ironforge",b="Before reaching its new home, the rare manuscript rested in Ironforge's grand library. In the Hall of Explorers, dwarven archivists kept it beside ancient titan relics and dwarven histories. Their vast collections hold texts gathered from ruins and foreign kingdoms across Azeroth. Yet arcane scholars elsewhere seek such works for their own collections, sure the busy archivists will never notice one missing volume.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Archmage Antonidas?",a="Archmage Antonidas led the Kirin Tor for many years and ruled the magical city-state of Dalaran. A legendary master of the arcane, he was a key councilor to the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. He warned King Terenas about the plague before falling in defense of Dalaran during the Third War.",al={"who was antonidas","archmage antonidas lore","antonidas backstory"}},{q="What is the unabridged autobiography?",a="Archmage Antonidas wrote the comprehensive autobiography himself, recounting his life, scholarship, and leadership within Dalaran. As head of the Kirin Tor, his writings are an invaluable record of history and magic.",al={"what is this book","unabridged autobiography book","antonidas tome"}},{q="Where did this book come from?",a="The volume came from the library in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. Dwarven explorers and archivists often collect historical and magical texts from across the eastern continents.",al={"where is the book from","did this come from ironforge","ironforge library book"}},{q="Why is this book being sought after?",a="Scholars and librarians seek powerful or historic magical texts to expand their archives and preserve arcane knowledge. Works by legendary magi are especially sought after, lest they be lost or hidden in foreign collections.",al={"why collect magical books","who wants antonidas book","why does the library want this"}},{q="What happened to Archmage Antonidas?",a="Archmage Antonidas perished during the Third War when the fallen Prince Arthas Menethil and the Scourge invaded Dalaran. Antonidas raised a powerful magical barrier to defend the city and its secrets. Arthas breached the defenses and struck him down to claim the Book of Medivh.",al={"did antonidas die","how did antonidas die","what happened to antonidas"}},{q="Will the Ironforge library notice the book is gone?",a="The recipient dismisses concern that the dwarves will notice the book's absence. The Ironforge archives are so vast that one missing tome will likely go unnoticed.",al={"will ironforge miss the book","stealing from ironforge library"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Archmage Antonidas was one of the Kirin Tor's greatest leaders and a paragon of arcane scholarship. His life and personal writings offer vital insight to any practitioner of the arcane arts.",["race:Dwarf"]="The tome comes from the great library in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. The scholars receiving it seem unconcerned about depriving the dwarven archivists of such a rare volume.",["race:Human"]="Antonidas was a revered human archmage who led the Kirin Tor and Dalaran through the Second and Third Wars. His unabridged autobiography is a precious piece of human history.",["faction:Alliance"]="Antonidas was a pillar of the Alliance of Lordaeron against the Orcish Horde and the Scourge. His personal memoirs are a treasured historical record across Alliance lands."},kw={"antonidas","arcane","archmage antonidas","autobiography","dalaran","hall of explorers","ironforge","kirin tor","library","mage"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge","zone:ironforge"},m={id=79091},src={"In-game quest text: Archmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography"},fv=true}
E["quest:79092"] = {t="quest",n="Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal",z="general",s="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus keeps a journal of his investigations. Now you carry its magical insights to the scholars of the Ironforge Library, where they can join the dwarven archive.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Archmage Theocritus keeps a journal of his investigations.",sec={{t="A Master's Field Notes",b="Archmage Theocritus is an esteemed spellcaster known throughout the Alliance. He is stationed at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest, where he has studied alone for years. His investigations range from curious artifacts and ley line anomalies to nearby magical threats.\n\nHe records his findings in detailed journals. This volume offers a rare chance to study the personal observations of a senior Kirin Tor archmage.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Ironforge Archives",b="The Explorers' League and the caretakers of the Ironforge Library maintain one of the continent's greatest archives. You bring Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal to them, helping preserve and catalog its arcane insights beside the historic volumes of Khaz Modan. The librarians welcome further magical discoveries that can broaden their shared wisdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal?",a="Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal is a scholarly record of his research. You bring it to the Ironforge Library to preserve arcane knowledge and enrich its archives.",al={"theocritus journal turn in","what is theocritus journal"}},{q="Who is Archmage Theocritus?",a="Archmage Theocritus is an esteemed human mage stationed at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. He studies ancient magical disturbances and artifacts.",al={"who is theocritus","archmage theocritus lore"}},{q="Where is this journal brought?",a="You bring the journal to the archivists at the Library in Ironforge. They collect rare documents and magical manuscripts.",al={"where do i turn in theocritus journal","who wants theocritus journal"}},{q="Why does the library want this journal?",a="The Ironforge Library's scholars want to preserve arcane knowledge and study rare works by master spellcasters. These works expand their historical records.",al={"why collect magical journals","purpose of theocritus journal"}},{q="Can more magical works be delivered to the library?",a="Yes. The curators encourage you to seek more magical works and historical texts for their archives.",al={"more journals to turn in","are there other books for library"}},{q="What kind of research is contained in the journal?",a="The journal holds notes and observations from Archmage Theocritus' extensive investigations into magical phenomena and arcane lore.",al={"what is in theocritus journal","contents of theocritus journal"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know that notes from prominent figures like Archmage Theocritus help safeguard historical magical works in Ironforge's archives.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help enrich Ironforge's great repository of knowledge for Alliance scholars."},kw={"arcane knowledge","archmage theocritus","ironforge","ironforge library","research journal","theocritus","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=79092},src={"In-game quest text: Archmage Theocritus' Research Journal"},fv=true}
E["quest:79093"] = {t="quest",n="Rumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works",z="general",s="A compiled work by Rumi of Gnomeregan is sought for a library’s collection. Its pages preserve gnomish writings and knowledge that might otherwise be lost.",h="A compiled work by Rumi of Gnomeregan is sought for a library’s collection.",sec={{t="Preserving Gnomish Thought",b="Gnomish writings were scattered, buried, or left in danger when troggs overran Gnomeregan. Now scholars and archivists seek surviving manuscripts, treatises, and compiled works. They hope to keep the wisdom and ingenuity of gnomish thinkers alive.",sp=0},{t="Archival Recovery",b="When travelers find collected works in the field and bring them to the archives, curators add them to their growing collections. Each recovered manuscript widens what scholars can study. Archivists welcome more magical and historical texts, keeping them within reach of scholars, mages, and historians who guard Azeroth’s learning.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works?",a="Rumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works is a compilation of gnomish writings sought for a library. An adventurer brings it to a scholar so its knowledge can be preserved and studied.",al={"rumi of gnomeregan quest","what is rumi of gnomeregan","who is rumi"}},{q="Where are these collected works delivered?",a="The collected works go to a curator or scholar who tends a library’s collection. They seek significant writings and magical treatises for the archives.",al={"where do i turn in rumi works","who takes rumi books","rumi collection turn in"}},{q="Why does the library want these collected works?",a="The library wants the works to preserve important scholarship. Scholars and archivists gather rare texts, historical treatises, and magical manuscripts, especially writings from Gnomeregan.",al={"why collect rumi books","purpose of rumi of gnomeregan","why library wants rumi"}},{q="Who is Rumi of Gnomeregan?",a="Rumi of Gnomeregan is an intellectual or magical author whose collected writings archivists seek. With Gnomeregan largely overrun, surviving works preserve the gnomes’ scholarly traditions.",al={"who was rumi of gnomeregan","rumi lore","rumi author"}},{q="Can more books be brought to the library after this?",a="Yes. Archivists welcome more discoveries, and curators encourage travelers to bring rare magical treatises and historical works for the collection.",al={"are there more books to find","can i bring more texts","more magical works library"}},{q="Who can complete this task?",a="Alliance adventurers can help scholars safeguard historical and arcane writings. Anyone who recovers these texts can bring them to the archives to aid research.",al={"rumi quest requirements","who can turn in rumi works","alliance only rumi"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, preserving the collected writings of thinkers like Rumi helps keep your culture and intellectual heritage alive after Gnomeregan’s fall.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you value rare writings from across Azeroth that deepen understanding of magical theory and history.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help scholars and curators protect valuable literature and magical texts for the Alliance’s shared knowledge."},kw={"collected works","gnomeregan lore","gnomish writings","library","magical works","rumi of gnomeregan"},m={id=79093},src={"In-game quest text: Rumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works"},fv=true}
E["quest:79094"] = {t="quest",n="The Lessons of Ta'zo",z="general",s="Ta'zo asks you to bring magical works to the library in Ironforge. Each addition helps expand its collection and knowledge.",h="Ta'zo asks you to bring magical works to the library in Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Library's Collection",b="Ta'zo asks you in the Library of Ironforge to bring something for its collection. Magical works that might benefit the library are welcome, and your efforts help expand its knowledge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for magical works?",a="Ta'zo asks you to bring magical works that might benefit the library in Ironforge.",al={"who is ta'zo","ta'zo library","ta'zo"}},{q="What does Ta'zo want brought to the library?",a="Ta'zo asks for magical works that might benefit the library's collection.",al={"what to bring ta'zo","magical books","library collection"}},{q="Where does Ta'zo keep the collection?",a="The collection is in the Library of Ironforge.",al={"where is ta'zo","ironforge library","library location"}},{q="Why does Ta'zo ask for magical works?",a="Ta'zo says the library's knowledge expands through your efforts.",al={"why magical works","expand knowledge","help library"}}},kw={"collection","ironforge","knowledge","lessons","library","magical works","ta'zo"},rel={"subzone:library-ironforge"},m={id=79094},src={"In-game quest text: The Lessons of Ta'zo"},fv=true}
E["quest:79095"] = {t="quest",n="The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer",z="general",s="Curators seek The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer to enrich their archives. Its delivery helps preserve rare alchemical and arcane theory for researchers and spellcasters.",h="Curators seek The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer to enrich their archives.",sec={{t="A Scholar's Acquisition",b="Curators welcome The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer for its study of esoteric and magical principles. Owen Thadd adds the text directly to his working collection of magical references.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Archives",b="Owen Thadd's collection in Undercity preserves specialized treatises. By bringing him rare primers on arcane and alchemical theory, you help keep metaphysical insights safe in the archives and accessible to researchers instead of leaving them lost in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer?",a="Curators seek The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer as a rare scholarly text for their collection of magical literature and study of metaphysical sciences.",al={"what is the apothecaries metaphysical primer","metaphysical primer quest","what is this book"}},{q="Who wants this primer delivered to them?",a="Owen Thadd in Undercity wants the primer delivered to him. He seeks magical works and arcane treatises to preserve knowledge for researchers and spellcasters.",al={"who wants this book","where do i turn in the primer","who takes the primer"}},{q="Why does the library collect works like this?",a="Libraries and archives gather metaphysical and magical works to expand their lore. These works help scholars, alchemists, and arcanists study arcane principles.",al={"why library want primer","purpose of collecting primer","why collect magical books"}},{q="Can you bring more magical works to the library?",a="Scholars who catalog magical literature welcome further arcane and scholarly discoveries you find for their archives.",al={"are there more books to turn in","can i bring other books","more library books"}},{q="What kind of lore is contained in a metaphysical primer?",a="In magical scholarship, metaphysics concerns the nature of magical energies, the unseen forces governing reality, and how physical reagents interact with arcane forces.",al={"what does metaphysical mean wotlk classic","metaphysics lore wow","what is apothecary metaphysics"}},{q="Who wrote The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer?",a="The records do not name the apothecary who wrote the primer. Apothecaries and scholars often compile primers on practical alchemy, herbal mixtures, and mystical formulas.",al={"who wrote apothecary primer","apothecary primer author","who is the apothecary"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Owen Thadd in Undercity recover rare treatises for the library's arcane collections.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you value metaphysical primers for their insights into magical theory, alchemical interactions, and the foundations of spellcraft."},kw={"alchemy","apothecary","undercity","library","magical works","metaphysical primer","tome"},rel={"zone:undercity"},m={id=79095},src={"In-game quest text: The Apothecary's Metaphysical Primer"},fv=true}
E["quest:79096"] = {t="quest",n="Ataeric: On Arcane Curiosities",z="general",s="Ataeric seeks rare magical writings to enlarge a library's collection. Scholars hope these works will deepen their study of the arcane and keep its lore safe.",h="Ataeric seeks rare magical writings to enlarge a library's collection.",sec={{t="Preserving Arcane Knowledge",b="Across Azeroth, scholars rely on travelers to recover rare tomes and treatises from dangerous ground. Ataeric seeks magical writings to broaden an institution's study of the arcane. Each volume can help scholars piece together practices that might otherwise be scattered or lost.",sp=0},{t="An Expanding Archive",b="The curator adds each curiosity to the archive. The library remains eager for further magical writings found across the world, so its collection can grow with ongoing scholarship.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Ataeric seeks magical writings to add to a library's collection of arcane lore.",al={"what is this quest","ataeric quest","arcane curiosities turn in"}},{q="Who collects these arcane writings?",a="Ataeric wrote the treatise. A researcher or curator gathers magical works and rare volumes for a library's archives.",al={"who wants this","who gets the book","who is ataeric"}},{q="Which library benefits from these curiosities?",a="The curiosities are sought for an academic collection at a scholarly library.",al={"what library is this","where do these books go"}},{q="Are there more magical works to collect?",a="Yes. The scholar welcomes any further magical works found during your travels to broaden the library's lore.",al={"can you turn in more","repeatable magical works","more books for library"}},{q="Why does the library seek arcane curiosities?",a="The library seeks rare treatises to deepen the study of the arcane and preserve mystical knowledge.",al={"what does the library study","why collect arcane books"}},{q="Why is recovering arcane works important?",a="Recovering arcane works brings obscure knowledge into a library where it can be kept and studied instead of remaining lost in the field.",al={"is this dangerous","arcane magic risk"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you have a natural interest in arcane study. Recovering magical treatises and contributing to scholarly libraries suit your craft.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the value of written records, artifacts, and obscure lore. Dwarven scholars and the Explorers' League prize them."},kw={"arcane","arcane curiosities","ataeric","library","magical works","scholars"},m={id=79096},src={"In-game quest text: Ataeric: On Arcane Curiosities"},fv=true}
E["quest:79097"] = {t="quest",n="Baxtan: On Destructive Magics",z="general",s="At the library, Baxtan: On Destructive Magics joins the works scholars gather to understand dangerous arcane power.",h="At the library, Baxtan: On Destructive Magics joins the works scholars gather to understand dangerous arcane...",sec={{t="A Tome of Ruinous Arts",b="Scholars seek to preserve what is known of arcane lore. When you find a text on destructive magic, its place is in careful academic keeping. There, its power and peril can be understood instead of lost.",sp=0},{t="Curating the Library's Lore",b="The library holds works on history, science, and the arcane. Its scholar welcomes travelers who recover forgotten treatises from dangerous corners of the world. Each volume adds to the library's knowledge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest 'Baxtan: On Destructive Magics'?",a="You bring Baxtan's treatise on destructive magics to a library scholar, adding a work of magic to the collection.",al={"what is baxtan on destructive magics","what is this quest","baxtan quest"}},{q="Who is Baxtan?",a="Baxtan wrote On Destructive Magics. The scholar who receives it gathers important tomes and magical treatises for the library.",al={"who is baxtan","baxtan npc","where is baxtan"}},{q="What kinds of books is Baxtan looking for?",a="The library's scholar seeks works of learning and magic for the collection, including treatises you find across the world.",al={"what kind of books does baxtan want","baxtan book collection","more books for baxtan"}},{q="Where does this magical knowledge end up?",a="The gathered texts enter the library's collection, where scholars preserve them for study of the arcane and its dangers.",al={"where does the book go","which library","ironforge library collection"}},{q="Why does the library collect works on destructive magic?",a="Scholars catalog destructive magic to understand the hazards, workings, and forms of potent arcane energies.",al={"why study destructive magic","destructive magics lore"}},{q="Can you bring more magical works to Baxtan?",a="Yes. The scholar welcomes more magical works you uncover as part of an ongoing effort to gather lore.",al={"are there more quests for baxtan","can i turn in more books"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may value treatises on destructive magic as you study arcane power and its dangers.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may recognize why scholars seek to understand volatile or forbidden powers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you benefit when Alliance libraries expand the knowledge held for all."},kw={"arcane","baxtan","book","destructive magics","library","magic","tome"},m={id=79097},src={"In-game quest text: Baxtan: On Destructive Magics"},fv=true}
E["quest:79236"] = {t="quest",n="Cherry for Your Thoughts?",z="general",s="In Booty Bay, Tokal offers a drink for the truth about attacks on human and dwarven outposts. Rumors blame the Horde, but her band served a private mercenary contract.",h="In Booty Bay, Tokal offers a drink for the truth about attacks on human and dwarven outposts.",sec={{t="The Whispers in Booty Bay",b="Tokal keeps out of sight in Booty Bay and watches for law enforcement. Recent raids devastated human and dwarven camps, and rumors blame the Horde. When travelers come who clearly do not work for the marshal asking questions, Tokal gives another account. She offers to tell it in exchange for a drink.",sp=0},{t="Private Mercenaries",b="Tokal admits she joined the pillaging of human and dwarven outposts, but says the Horde did not carry out the raids. Her band worked under a private contract for an unnamed third party. Tokal insists on a Cherry Grog before she names who paid for the operation and why.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tokal?",a="Tokal is a mercenary hiding in Booty Bay. A marshal is investigating raids on human and dwarven settlements, and Tokal offers to tell who hired her for a Cherry Grog.",al={"who is tokal","tokal booty bay","cherry grog quest giver"}},{q="Why does Tokal want a Cherry Grog?",a="Tokal wants a Cherry Grog before discussing her past contracts. Then she will explain who privately funded the raids on Alliance camps.",al={"why buy cherry grog","cherry grog tokal","what does tokal want"}},{q="Was the Horde responsible for pillaging the human and dwarven camps?",a="Tokal says the Horde did not order the raids on human and dwarven camps. Rumors blame the Horde, but her group worked under a private mercenary contract.",al={"who hired tokal","did horde attack alliance camps","was horde behind the raids"}},{q="Why is Tokal worried about a marshal?",a="Tokal fears a marshal investigating the pillaging of human and dwarven settlements. She checks that anyone approaching her in Booty Bay was not sent to bring her to justice.",al={"who is the marshal","is tokal hiding from marshal","marshal looking for tokal"}},{q="Where do you get Cherry Grog for Tokal?",a="Tavern keepers and barkeepers in Booty Bay sell Cherry Grog. Bringing Tokal a mug meets her demand and prompts her to tell her story.",al={"where to get cherry grog","cherry grog location","booty bay grog"}},{q="Why is Tokal staying in Booty Bay?",a="Booty Bay is a freebooter port beyond the strict jurisdiction of the Alliance and Horde. It gives a mercenary hiding after raids on human and dwarven camps a place to lie low.",al={"why is tokal in booty bay","tokal hiding place"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can learn that a private patron hired the raiders who struck human and dwarven camps. The Horde did not hire them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you can learn from Tokal that private mercenary contracts led to the attacks on Alliance camps. They were not official Horde aggression."},kw={"booty bay","cherry for your thoughts","cherry grog","marshal","mercenary","pillaging","private contract","tokal"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","topic:horde","topic:human"},m={id=79236},src={"In-game quest text: Cherry for Your Thoughts?"},fv=true}
E["quest:79361"] = {t="quest",n="Storm, Earth, and Fire",z="general",s="Prate Cloudseer asks you to help stop the quilboar from flooding Thousand Needles through twisted shamanism. A tome meant for your training may help disperse the coming storm.",h="Prate Cloudseer asks you to help stop the quilboar from flooding Thousand Needles through twisted shamanism.",sec={{t="A Storm Approaches",b="Prate Cloudseer had planned to continue your training, but the threat in Thousand Needles cannot wait. You have seen that the quilboar are not to be taken lightly. Prate gives you a tome meant for study and asks you to gather twisted fire, earth, air, and water totems. The tome may hold a way to disperse the storm they are bringing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Prate Cloudseer asks you to gather twisted totems in Thousand Needles.",al={"who is Prate","Prate Cloudseer","cloudseer"}},{q="What are the quilboar trying to do?",a="Prate says the quilboar mean to flood Thousand Needles through twisted shamanism.",al={"quilboar plan","why the totems","quilboar storm"}},{q="What does Prate give me?",a="Prate gives you a tome that was meant for study and may help disperse the coming storm.",al={"tome","what is the book","study tome"}},{q="Which totems does Prate need?",a="Prate asks you to gather twisted fire, earth, air, and water totems.",al={"totem types","fire earth air water","what totems"}}},kw={"prate cloudseer","quilboar","storm earth and fire","thousand needles","tome","twisted shamanism","twisted totems"},rel={"quest:91209","zone:thousandneedles","topic:quilboar"},m={id=79361},src={"In-game quest text: Storm, Earth, and Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:79362"] = {t="quest",n="Grant's Shield",z="general",s="Sirra Von’Indie seeks Grant Valor’s mace in Raven Hill Cemetery, where his spirit still battles the undead. The weapons may help her learn more about the proud hero.",h="Sirra Von’Indie seeks Grant Valor’s mace in Raven Hill Cemetery, where his spirit still battles the undead.",sec={{t="A Fallen Hero",b="Sirra Von’Indie in Darkshire asks you to find Grant Valor’s mace among the skeletons in Raven Hill Cemetery. Grant’s shield was left behind by his specter, and his spirit still fights the undead there. The mace may point to the creature that injured him, and Sirra wants to study the weapons.",sp=0},{t="The Weapons",b="In Darkshire, Sirra Von’Indie reflects on how a simple creature brought Grant Valor low. She says a single slip can cripple a person for life. The weapons, she believes, tell much about their owner, and she takes time to study them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Grant Valor?",a="Grant Valor was the father of the Valor family and a hero of Raven Hill. His specter still battles the undead.",al={"grant valor","who is grant","grant backstory"}},{q="Where is Grant's mace?",a="Grant’s mace is on one of the skeletons in Raven Hill Cemetery.",al={"grant mace","find grant's mace","mace location"}},{q="Why am I looking for Grant's mace?",a="Sirra Von’Indie asks you to find the mace so she can learn more from Grant’s weapons.",al={"why find mace","grant shield quest","what does sirra want"}},{q="Where do I take the mace?",a="Return Grant’s mace to Sirra Von’Indie in Darkshire.",al={"return mace","sirra location","where is von'indie"}},{q="What happened to Grant?",a="Grant was injured by a creature in Raven Hill Cemetery. His spirit still battles the undead there.",al={"grant injured","how was grant hurt","grant valor shield"}}},kw={"darkshire","grant valor","grant's mace","grant's shield","raven hill cemetery","sirra von'indie","undead","valor family"},rel={"quest:96139","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","subzone:darkshire","topic:scourge"},m={id=79362},src={"In-game quest text: Grant's Shield"},fv=true}
E["quest:79363"] = {t="quest",n="Silvia's Sword",z="general",s="Silvia Valor's sword, left by her spirit, points you to the Defias near Raven Hill. The blade belonged to a guard who protected civilians and their homes.",h="Silvia Valor's sword, left by her spirit, points you to the Defias near Raven Hill.",sec={{t="A Guard's Blade",b="The spirit of Silvia Valor, Raven Hill's guard, has left her sword behind. Silvia spent her life defending civilians and their homes. Her spirit still visits farmsteads, and the Defias have taken up residence at Addle's Stead, south of Raven Hill. Driving them out may be her unfinished business, and Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire waits to hear what comes of it.",sp=0},{t="The Blade's Study",b="At Addle's Stead, the Defias are the first lead in Silvia Valor's unfinished business. When you return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire, she recognizes Silvia as a fine warrior and defender, though one with a narrow view of who deserved protection. Sirra cannot tell what Silvia wants from the sword, so she studies the blade further.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Silvia Valor?",a="Silvia Valor was a guard at Raven Hill who spent her life protecting civilians and their homes.",al={"Silvia Valor backstory","who is Silvia","Raven Hill guard Silvia"}},{q="Why is Silvia's spirit visiting farmsteads?",a="Silvia's spirit still visits farmsteads, and her unfinished business may involve the Defias at Addle's Stead.",al={"Silvia ghost why","why is she haunting farms","Silvia unfinished business"}},{q="Who asks about Silvia's sword?",a="Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire takes up the sword's story. You return to her for more about Silvia Valor once the Defias at Addle's Stead are dealt with.",al={"who gave Silvia's sword","Sirra Von'Indi sword","Darkshire sword giver"}},{q="Where have the Defias taken up residence?",a="The Defias have taken up residence at Addle's Stead, south of Raven Hill.",al={"Defias Addle's Stead","where are Defias","Raven Hill Defias"}},{q="What does Sirra think of Silvia?",a="Sirra calls Silvia a fine warrior and defender, though she says Silvia had a narrow view of who deserved protection.",al={"Sirra opinion Silvia","Silvia warrior","what kind of guard was Silvia"}},{q="What does Sirra do with the sword?",a="Sirra studies Silvia Valor's blade further.",al={"what happens to the blade","Sirra studies sword","Silvia sword next"}}},kw={"addle's stead","darkshire","defias","guard","raven hill","silvia valor","silvia's sword","sirra von'indi","unfinished business"},rel={"quest:163","subzone:addle-s-stead","subzone:darkshire","npc:sirra-von-indi"},m={id=79363},src={"In-game quest text: Silvia's Sword"},fv=true}
E["quest:79364"] = {t="quest",n="Eyes on the Sky",z="general",s="A note warns that the Razormane are carrying out an unseen ritual in Thousand Needles. You are asked to seek an answer to the threat of storms and rising tides.",h="A note warns that the Razormane are carrying out an unseen ritual in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Gathering Threat",b="The note you found points to the Razormane in Thousand Needles, where an unseen ritual is underway. Raging storms and rising tides raise the fear that the canyon may be flooded. The quilboar may be drawing on elemental power learned from Hirzek, a shaman. Return to your allies and speak with Prate Cloudseer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the note say?",a="It says the Razormane have burrowed into Thousand Needles for an unseen ritual, amid raging storms and rising tides.",al={"note in Thousand Needles","what note","razormane note"}},{q="Who is Hirzek?",a="Hirzek is a shaman who taught the quilboar sorcery that twists the elements.",al={"Hirzek","Hirzek shaman","who's Hirzek"}},{q="What threat do the quilboar pose?",a="The feared danger is that the quilboar could use elemental power to flood the canyon.",al={"quilboar threat","razormane ritual","what are quilboar doing"}},{q="Who should I speak with?",a="You are asked to speak with Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.",al={"where to go","who to find","Prate Cloudseer"}}},kw={"elemental sorcery","eyes on the sky","hirzek","prate cloudseer","quilboar","razormane","rising tides","ritual","storms","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:quilboar","topic:shaman"},m={id=79364},src={"In-game quest text: Eyes on the Sky"},fv=true}
E["quest:79624"] = {t="quest",n="Anyone Can Cook",z="general",s="An illegible recipe appears to describe a meat dish, and you suspect ogre writing. Find an ogre who can read it.",h="An illegible recipe appears to describe a meat dish, and you suspect ogre writing.",sec={{t="A Strange Recipe",b="The recipe is written in a language you cannot read, and its subject seems to be a meat dish. Ogre is your best guess, given where it came from and what it describes. You hope to find an ogre who can translate it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the recipe for?",a="It appears to be for some sort of meat dish.",al={"recipe purpose","what dish","meat recipe"}},{q="What language is the recipe written in?",a="You do not understand the language. Ogre is your best guess.",al={"recipe language","what writing","can't read recipe"}},{q="Who can read the recipe?",a="You are looking for an ogre who can read it.",al={"translate recipe","who can read it","ogre reader"}},{q="Who is Skonk?",a="Skonk is an ogre who is listening for the recipe.",al={"Skonk","who skonk","ogre Skonk"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you have a reason to wonder what sort of meat dish the illegible recipe describes."},kw={"anyone can cook","illegible recipe","meat dish","ogre","recipe","skonk","translation"},m={id=79624},src={"In-game quest text: Anyone Can Cook"},fv=true}
E["quest:79677"] = {t="quest",n="A Quick Grocery Run",z="general",s="Skonk asks you to gather ingredients for a dish in Arathi Highlands. He learned to cook after other ogres mocked his size and fighting ability.",h="Skonk asks you to gather ingredients for a dish in Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="Skonk's Ingredients",b="Skonk, an ogre in Arathi Highlands, needs ingredients for a dish he knows how to make. Other ogres laughed at his size and called him weak, so he turned to cooking. You gather the ingredients and bring them to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Skonk?",a="Skonk is an ogre who learned to cook after other ogres mocked his size and fighting ability.",al={"skonk","who's skonk"}},{q="Why does Skonk cook?",a="Other ogres laughed at Skonk for being smaller and called him weak, so he learned to cook instead of fight.",al={"why cook","skonk cooking"}},{q="What does Skonk need?",a="Skonk needs ingredients for a dish he can make.",al={"ingredients","what ingredients"}},{q="Where do I bring the ingredients?",a="Bring the ingredients to Skonk in Arathi Highlands.",al={"where skonk","bring ingredients"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can help Skonk gather ingredients for a dish he knows how to make."},kw={"arathi highlands","cooking","dish","ingredients","ogre","skonk","teasing"},rel={"zone:arathi"},m={id=79677},src={"In-game quest text: A Quick Grocery Run"},fv=true}
E["quest:79974"] = {t="quest",n="Wet Job",z="general",s="On a mountainside, Wet Job sends you to recover an emergency reserve stash. Someone prepared it for a hasty escape and hid it near a high cliffside perch.",h="On a mountainside, Wet Job sends you to recover an emergency reserve stash.",sec={{t="An Emergency Cache",b="In dangerous country, a reserve can make a quick escape possible. You search the rugged heights for a stash someone left there in case plans went wrong. Its supplies are waiting to be recovered.",sp=0},{t="The Eagle's Nest",b="The directions lead to a high mountain perch, described as carved from the waterfalls of time. There, at the eagle's nest, a weathered messenger bag lies partly buried in the earth. Inside, provisions and parchment have endured beneath the soil, protected by dwarven craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Wet Job about?",a="You recover a hidden emergency stash, prepared with supplies for a hasty escape.",al={"what is wet job","wet job quest","what kind of quest is wet job"}},{q="Who left the reserve stash?",a="Someone left the stash as an emergency reserve in case they had to flee in a hurry. It holds a messenger bag with parchment and supplies, made with dwarven craft.",al={"who left the stash","whose supplies are these","who hid the reserve stash"}},{q="Where is the stash hidden?",a="The stash lies high on a mountainside, at an eagle's nest on the rock face described as carved from the waterfalls of time. A messenger bag is partly buried there.",al={"where is the stash","wet job location","eagles nest location"}},{q="What is found in the messenger bag?",a="The buried messenger bag holds provisions and parchment, protected by dwarven craft.",al={"what is inside the stash","wet job items","what do you find"}},{q="Why is the task called Wet Job?",a="The name refers to the mountain landmarks, with waterfalls of time and damp soil around the hidden bag.",al={"why is it called wet job","wet job name meaning"}},{q="How is dwarven engineering involved?",a="The cache's construction and reliability show dwarven engineering, made to withstand burial outdoors.",al={"dwarven engineering connection","is this dwarven"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can admire the dwarven ingenuity behind a dependable emergency stockpile hidden in rugged terrain.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can take pride in the enduring quality of the mountain craft praised when the cache is recovered.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the value of hidden emergency stashes, kept ready in case a hasty flight is needed."},kw={"dwarven engineering","eagles nest","messenger bag","mountainside","parchment","reserve stash","supplies","wet job"},m={id=79974},src={"In-game quest text: Wet Job"},fv=true}
E["quest:79975"] = {t="quest",n="Eagle's Fist",z="general",s="At a misty overlook, Eagle's Fist keeps a lonely watch over a weathered barricade. A letter speaks of loyalty to the Old Kingdoms and the Eagle and Fist, though its writer has left in haste.",h="At a misty overlook, Eagle's Fist keeps a lonely watch over a weathered barricade.",sec={{t="A Hidden Perch",b="A folded letter lies inside a toolbox at a high overlook. From here, its writer says, one can call the shots or launch a parachute glider across the land. Misty spray dampens this lonely post, but the view reaches across historic lands.",sp=0},{t="Loyalty to the Old Kingdoms",b="The letter's writer pledges lasting loyalty to the Eagle and Fist. To serve that cause well, the writer says, one must keep a measured distance. The nearby barricade has fallen into disrepair, like the Old Kingdoms it once shielded from danger. Still, the watcher vows never to abandon the post.",sp=0},{t="A Hasty Departure",b="The sentry left the overlook in a hurry. The campfire was fed with fresh wood only recently, yet the watcher is gone. Tools, burning embers and a cryptic letter remain behind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Eagle's Fist?",a="Eagle's Fist is a lonely lookout over a weathered barricade, where a toolbox holds a folded letter. Its writer has left in haste.",al={"what is eagle's fist","eagles fist quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who wrote the letter found in the toolbox?",a="An unidentified scout or sentry wrote the letter. The writer serves the Old Kingdoms and the Eagle and Fist, keeping watch at a lonely barricade.",al={"who wrote the note","who left the letter","toolbox letter author"}},{q="What does 'the Eagle and Fist' refer to?",a="The Eagle and Fist is an allegiance named in the letter. It calls for keeping a measured distance in service, and is tied to guarding what remains of the Old Kingdoms.",al={"what is the eagle and fist","eagle and fist meaning","who is eagle and fist"}},{q="Why is the campsite abandoned?",a="The scout left in haste, though the campfire had only recently been fed with fresh wood. The writer praised the overlook as a place to launch a parachute glider.",al={"where did the scout go","why did they leave","who fed the campfire"}},{q="What barricade is being defended?",a="The letter's writer says the barricade is worn, like the fallen Old Kingdoms of humanity it once defended. Still, the watcher vows never to abandon it.",al={"what barricade","which old kingdoms","barricade lore"}},{q="What kind of lookout post is this?",a="The perch offers an incredible view, and water spray dampens the air. It may be a high cliff or overlook near a great waterfall or cascading river.",al={"where is this located","why is there water spray","eagles fist location"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The lookout's note calls the spot an ideal place to launch a parachute glider. Engineers may appreciate the chance for aerial reconnaissance and mechanical flight."},kw={"barricade","campfire","eagle's fist","folded letter","lookout","old kingdoms","parachute glider","toolbox"},m={id=79975},src={"In-game quest text: Eagle's Fist"},fv=true}
E["quest:79976"] = {t="quest",n="This Must Be The Place",z="general",s="At This Must Be The Place, a camper has vanished moments before anyone could catch up. A torn note says the writer has taken their work underground to keep it from the wrong hands.",h="At This Must Be The Place, a camper has vanished moments before anyone could catch up.",sec={{t="A Hasty Departure",b="Someone broke camp at this secluded spot only moments ago. An inadequately secured sleeping bag unrolls underfoot, while heavy canvas lies bundled over assorted gear. A small scrap of paper holds a hurried parting message, but whoever camped here has vanished before anyone could catch up.",sp=0},{t="Into the Underground",b="The torn note says its author has taken their work underground to keep it from the wrong hands. Whether these are final words or a clue to the researcher's next hidden shelter remains unknown. The equipment lies abandoned for whoever found the campsite.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote the torn note?",a="The note does not name its author. The writer says only that they have taken their work underground to keep it from the wrong hands, leaving the campsite and equipment behind.",al={"who wrote the note","note author","who left the message"}},{q="What work is being taken underground?",a="The note does not reveal what work the author is taking underground. The writer says they want to keep it safe from unspecified adversaries.",al={"what underground work","why take work underground","what work"}},{q="Where did the campsite's occupant go?",a="The occupant left moments before anyone arrived, and their destination is unknown. The note hints they may have gone to another hidden shelter.",al={"did i miss them","where did they go","where is the author"}},{q="What was left behind at the campsite?",a="The traveler left an inadequately secured sleeping bag that unrolls on the ground, heavy canvas bundled over assorted gear, and a discarded pack containing miscellaneous gear.",al={"what is left behind","supplies at camp","what was in the pack"}},{q="Is this a clue leading to another hideout?",a="The note could be a farewell or a clue to the author's next underground shelter. It does not settle which.",al={"is there another hideout","next camp","more clues"}},{q="Who are the 'wrong hands' mentioned in the note?",a="The note does not identify the wrong hands. The author feared pursuit or theft and left before their work could be compromised.",al={"who are the wrong hands","wrong hands meaning","who is chasing the author"}}},kw={"abandoned camp","equipment pack","hideout","sleeping bag","this must be the place","torn note","underground"},m={id=79976},src={"In-game quest text: This Must Be The Place"},fv=true}
E["quest:79980"] = {t="quest",n="Scramble",z="general",s="A scavenger's note sends travelers down a steep cliff in search of Scramble's hidden supplies. One hundred paces north, they find provisions and a dirty parchment.",h="A scavenger's note sends travelers down a steep cliff in search of Scramble's hidden supplies.",sec={{t="The Northward Trail",b="A note points the way to a hidden supply cache. Its writer offers a few informal words of encouragement, then gives precise directions: go one hundred paces due north down the treacherous cliffside. Provisions wait there to keep a traveler going.",sp=0},{t="Unearthing the Messenger Bag",b="Following the directions down the steep cliff face leads to a buried messenger bag. Inside are practical survival supplies and another dirty parchment. The note points onward along a larger trail.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Scramble?",a="Scramble sends travelers along a scavenged trail to a hidden cache. A note directs them one hundred paces north down a treacherous cliff to buried supplies.",al={"scramble quest","what is scramble","scramble stash"}},{q="Where is the hidden stash located?",a="The note places the cache about one hundred paces due north, down a steep cliffside. Careful footing is needed on the way down.",al={"where is stash","how to find stash","stash location"}},{q="Who left the note and the cache?",a="The note does not name its author. Its informal, practical directions help an explorer find emergency provisions, and the stash remains intact.",al={"who wrote scramble note","who left stash","scramble author"}},{q="What is inside the buried stash?",a="The buried messenger bag holds survival supplies and a dirty parchment tucked among them.",al={"scramble rewards","what is in scramble cache","bag contents"}},{q="What is the dirty parchment found with the supplies?",a="The dirty parchment is inside the buried messenger bag, alongside the provisions. It is found when the bag is pulled from the ground.",al={"dirty parchment scramble","what does parchment say","scramble note"}},{q="What hazards are involved in reaching the cache?",a="The steep northern descent is the chief hazard. A misstep can mean broken ankles or a serious fall.",al={"danger scramble","cliff scramble","scramble cliffside"}}},kw={"cache","cliffside","messenger bag","parchment","scramble","stash","supplies"},m={id=79980},src={"In-game quest text: Scramble"},fv=true}
E["quest:815"] = {t="quest",n="Break a Few Eggs",z="general",s="Cook Torka is waiting on fresh eggs from the Echo Isles before the next meal. You carry them back unbroken so the kitchen can keep to its schedule.",h="Cook Torka is waiting on fresh eggs from the Echo Isles before the next meal.",sec={{t="Endless Meals",b="At Razor Hill in Durotar, Cook Torka prepares meals from morning through evening. Breakfast gives way to lunch, then dinner, with little time to leave the stove for provisions. So Torka sends you to the Echo Isles for Taillasher eggs before the next meal service falls behind. Bring them back whole, and the cook can keep the kitchen working on time.",sp=0},{t="A Cook's Gratitude",b="Cook Torka has little time for praise while meals wait to be made. Eggs need a gentle touch, since a cracked shell spoils an ingredient the kitchen needs. When you bring the eggs back unbroken, Torka sends you on your way and returns to work over the fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Break a Few Eggs?",a="Cook Torka needs you to bring Taillasher eggs back unbroken from the Echo Isles, so the kitchen can keep to its schedule.",al={"break a few eggs quest","what is break a few eggs","egg quest"}},{q="Who is the cook in Break a Few Eggs?",a="Cook Torka prepares meals throughout the day at Razor Hill in Durotar. Torka speaks bluntly and is in a hurry, relying on you to fetch Taillasher eggs from the Echo Isles without cracking them before mealtime.",al={"who gives break a few eggs","egg quest cook","who is cooking"}},{q="Why does the cook need eggs?",a="Cook Torka needs eggs for meals prepared throughout the day, from breakfast through dinner. Fresh eggs keep the kitchen's work on schedule.",al={"why eggs","what are eggs for","why need eggs"}},{q="Why does the cook comment on not being clumsy?",a="Eggs can break on the way back. Cook Torka needs the shells and yolks intact for the coming meal service.",al={"why careful with eggs","dont break eggs","why not clumsy"}},{q="What does the title Break a Few Eggs refer to?",a="The title echoes the proverb about making an omelet and breaking eggs. It suits the work of carrying fragile ingredients to a busy kitchen.",al={"break a few eggs meaning","phrase meaning","why is it called break a few eggs"}},{q="Why is the cook so impatient?",a="Cook Torka is busy preparing meals from breakfast through dinner. With more cooking to do, Torka has little patience for chitchat and wants to return to the stove.",al={"cook attitude","why is the cook rude","grumpy cook"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know the pressure of keeping people fed. Bringing fragile ingredients back unbroken is part of the work in any kitchen."},kw={"break a few eggs","breakfast","cook","cooking","eggs","kitchen","meals"},m={id=815},src={"In-game quest text: Break a Few Eggs"},fv=true}
E["quest:8193"] = {t="quest",n="Master Angler",z="general",s="Every Sunday, an angling contest seeks the greatest anglers. Bring Tastyfish from Stranglethorn’s coastal schools among the first fifty to be declared a Master Angler.",h="Every Sunday, an angling contest seeks the greatest anglers.",sec={{t="Sunday’s Contest",b="The contest is open each Sunday, and you can earn the title of Master Angler by bringing Tastyfish to the organizer among the first fifty people. The fish come from schools along the coasts of Stranglethorn, and they spoil quickly.",sp=0},{t="A Second Offer",b="If you arrive too late for the first fifty places, the organizer’s apprentice will still pay you for Tastyfish. The fish do not keep until the next Sunday.",sp=0}},faq={{q="When is the angling contest?",a="The contest takes place every Sunday.",al={"master angler day","what day is fishing contest"}},{q="Where do I find Tastyfish?",a="Tastyfish schools are found along the coasts of Stranglethorn.",al={"tastyfish location","where fish tastyfish"}},{q="How do I become a Master Angler?",a="Bring Tastyfish to the contest organizer among the first fifty people.",al={"master angler requirements","win fishing contest"}},{q="What if I arrive too late?",a="The organizer’s apprentice will pay you for Tastyfish if you are too late to be among the first fifty.",al={"missed the contest","too slow fishing"}},{q="Can I save Tastyfish for next week?",a="No. Tastyfish spoil quickly, so they cannot be saved for the next Sunday.",al={"do tastyfish spoil","keep fish until sunday"}}},kw={"angling contest","fishing","fishing schools","master angler","stranglethorn","sunday","tastyfish"},m={id=8193},src={"In-game quest text: Master Angler"},fv=true}
E["quest:8312"] = {t="quest",n="Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!",z="general",s="For Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!, an ailing child asks travelers to gather holiday sweets. Innkeepers in the cities and Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village share treats, and Spoops offers magical candy in return.",h="For Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!, an ailing child asks travelers to gather holiday sweets.",sec={{t="A Bedridden Holiday",b="Spoops is too ill to join Hallow's End outdoors. While others celebrate, Spoops asks travelers to gather holiday treats. In return, Spoops offers candy that changes whoever eats it into strange shapes.",sp=0},{t="Tricks and Treats Across the Realm",b="Travelers can find holiday treats in settlements across the realm. Innkeepers in major cities ask visitors to perform tricks before sharing their sweets. Kali Remik also gives out treats in Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Spoops?",a="Spoops is a sick young person who cannot go trick-or-treating during Hallow's End. Hoping to take part, Spoops asks travelers to collect seasonal treats from innkeepers and vendors across the world.",al={"who is spoops","spoops","what is spoops"}},{q="Why can't Spoops go trick-or-treating?",a="Spoops is too ill to go outside for Hallow's End. Bedridden by illness, Spoops relies on travelers to visit city innkeepers and gather holiday sweets.",al={"why cant spoops go trick or treating","why is spoops staying in","spoops sick"}},{q="What candy does Spoops offer in exchange?",a="Spoops offers magical candies that transform whoever eats them. They can turn you into shapes that are both funny and frightening.",al={"what candy does spoops give","spoops reward candy","special candy"}},{q="Where do you find the treats for Spoops?",a="Innkeepers in the capital cities share holiday candy after travelers perform tricks. Kali Remik also hands out sweets in Sen'jin Village.",al={"where do i get candy","who gives treats","candy locations"}},{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a troll in Sen'jin Village, Durotar. During Hallow's End, Kali Remik gives holiday candy to travelers who stop by.",al={"who is kali remik","kali remik candy","senjin village candy"}},{q="Why do innkeepers ask for tricks?",a="During Hallow's End, innkeepers in major settlements ask visitors to show their holiday spirit with silly tricks or gestures before sharing their sweets.",al={"what do innkeepers want","innkeeper tricks","how to get innkeeper candy"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you gather treats in the major cities and visit Sen'jin Village, the Darkspear settlement, on behalf of an ailing child.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can find Kali Remik handing out seasonal sweets in Sen'jin Village during Hallow's End."},kw={"candy","hallow's end","innkeeper","kali remik","sen'jin village","spoops","treats","trick or treat"},rel={"npc:kali-remik","subzone:sen-jin-village","topic:troll"},m={id=8312},src={"In-game quest text: Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!"},fv=true}
E["quest:837"] = {t="quest",n="Encroachment",z="general",s="At Razor Hill in central Durotar, Gar'Thok sends you west against Razormane camps. Their fortified dens still threaten the young orc homeland.",h="At Razor Hill in central Durotar, Gar'Thok sends you west against Razormane camps.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="When Thrall brought the orcs to Kalimdor and founded Durotar, the Razormane already ranged across much of the harsh, arid land. These aggressive, boar-like quilboar became a constant danger to the new settlement. The Horde drove most of them back through sustained military efforts. Yet fortified pockets remain in thorned redoubts west of Razor Hill.",sp=0},{t="Gar'Thok's Offensive",b="Gar'Thok, an officer at Razor Hill, leads the effort to remove the remaining Razormane. He sends seasoned defenders into the western bramble camps to kill their scouts, warriors, and dustrunners. Gar'Thok and the Horde leadership fear any quilboar foothold near Razor Hill could bring disaster. They see this strike as the first step toward securing Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Brambles",b="Once the quilboar defenders are gone, Horde forces can burn the bramble dens and keep the Razormane from reclaiming the western foothills. The fire destroys an enduring menace and secures Durotar's western perimeter. It also protects the vital supply roads between Razor Hill and the wider realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Encroachment?",a="Gar'Thok, an orc officer stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar, gives the order.",al={"who gives encroachment","where to get encroachment","encroachment questgiver"}},{q="Why is the Horde fighting the Razormane quilboar in Durotar?",a="When the orcs arrived in Durotar, the Razormane quilboar held much of the region. The Horde drove most of them back, but fortified pockets remain west of Razor Hill and threaten the safety of the new orc homeland.",al={"why fight quilboar durotar","why attack razormane","quilboar conflict durotar"}},{q="Where are the Razormane camps located?",a="The Razormane camps lie west of Razor Hill, among dense tangles of thorny brambles.",al={"where are the quilboar camps","how to find razormane camps","encroachment location"}},{q="Who are the Razormane?",a="The Razormane are a hostile tribe of quilboar native to Kalimdor's arid plains. They build defensive bramble dens and fiercely resist the Horde's settlement of Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"who are the razormane","razormane lore","what is razormane"}},{q="What happens once the quilboar are defeated?",a="After the quilboar are defeated, Gar'Thok sends word to burn their cleared brambles and structures. This strengthens Horde control of the area and secures Durotar's borders.",al={"what happens after encroachment","encroachment turn in","fate of quilboar camps"}},{q="What is Razor Hill's role in this conflict?",a="Razor Hill is a fortified orc settlement in central Durotar. It is a military and logistical hub between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar.",al={"where is razor hill","what is razor hill"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need to secure Durotar from the native Razormane quilboar to establish a safe, lasting homeland.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you claim Durotar as your new homeland. The Razormane bramble dens still threaten your settlements."},kw={"brambles","durotar","encroachment","gar'thok","quilboar","razor hill","razormane"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","subzone:razor-hill","topic:quilboar","zone:durotar"},m={id=837},src={"In-game quest text: Encroachment"},fv=true}
E["quest:8373"] = {t="quest",n="The Power of Pine",z="general",s="During Hallow’s End, Sergeant Hartman asks you to clear Forsaken stink bombs from Southshore. A pine-scented cleaner helps keep the village clean.",h="During Hallow’s End, Sergeant Hartman asks you to clear Forsaken stink bombs from Southshore.",sec={{t="Southshore’s Stink",b="During Hallow’s End, the Forsaken foul Southshore with stink bombs. The bombs mar the celebration of liberation. Sergeant Hartman asks you to remove any that have landed in the village with a Stink Bomb Cleaner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks me to clean up the stink bombs?",a="Sergeant Hartman in Southshore asks you to clear the Forsaken stink bombs.",al={"who gave me this","sergeant hartman"}},{q="Where are the stink bombs?",a="The stink bombs are in Southshore.",al={"stink bombs location","where clean"}},{q="Who uses stink bombs on Southshore?",a="The Forsaken use stink bombs on Southshore during Hallow’s End.",al={"who stink bombs","forsaken bombs"}},{q="What does the cleaner do?",a="The Stink Bomb Cleaner uses pine to fight foul smells.",al={"pine cleaner","stink bomb cleaner"}},{q="Why is Southshore being cleaned?",a="The Forsaken stink bombs make a smelly mess during Southshore’s Hallow’s End celebration.",al={"why clean southshore","hallow's end stink"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help Sergeant Hartman keep Southshore clean of Forsaken stink bombs."},kw={"forsaken","hallow's end","pine cleaner","sergeant hartman","southshore","stink bomb cleaner","stink bombs"},rel={"subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},m={id=8373},src={"In-game quest text: The Power of Pine"},fv=true}
E["quest:8386"] = {t="quest",n="Fight for Warsong Gulch",z="general",s="A call to fight for Warsong Gulch helps preserve Ashenvale's natural defenses. Your efforts keep them intact for another day.",h="A call to fight for Warsong Gulch helps preserve Ashenvale's natural defenses.",sec={{t="Ashenvale's Defenses",b="In Ashenvale, you are asked to fight for Warsong Gulch. Your work helps keep the area's natural defenses intact for another day.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why fight for Warsong Gulch?",a="Your efforts help preserve Ashenvale's natural defenses for another day.",al={"warsong gulch fight","why warsong"}},{q="What does this help protect?",a="The fight helps keep Ashenvale's natural defenses intact for another day.",al={"what defenses","ashenvale protection"}},{q="Where is Warsong Gulch?",a="Warsong Gulch is the battlefield that forms a natural barrier between Ashenvale and the Barrens.",al={"warsong location","where warsong gulch"}}},kw={"ashenvale","defenses","fight for warsong gulch","natural defenses","warsong gulch"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","zone:warsonggulch"},m={id=8386},src={"In-game quest text: Fight for Warsong Gulch"},fv=true}
E["quest:8426"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Warsong Gulch",z="general",s="A Horde Warbringer asks you to bring three Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor. The marks are the proof requested for this call.",h="A Horde Warbringer asks you to bring three Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor.",sec={{t="A Mark Returned",b="You carry the three Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds. The Warbringer asks for these marks, and that is all this call requires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Warbringer ask for?",a="The Horde Warbringer asks you to bring three Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor.",al={"what marks","warbringer wants","bring what"}},{q="Where do I bring the marks?",a="Bring the marks to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.",al={"where warbringer","turn in marks","where to bring"}},{q="How many marks are needed?",a="The Warbringer asks for three Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor.",al={"how many marks","number of marks","three marks"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can bring the Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer."},kw={"battlegrounds","horde","marks of honor","warbringer","warsong gulch"},rel={"zone:warsonggulch","topic:horde"},m={id=8426},src={"In-game quest text: Battle of Warsong Gulch"},fv=true}
E["quest:86576"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodfury Trinkets",z="general",s="Mor'rogal asks you to bring him sunstones from the Bloodfury harpies in the Charred Vale. He says they are bound to the lights of the skies.",h="Mor'rogal asks you to bring him sunstones from the Bloodfury harpies in the Charred Vale.",sec={{t="Harpies' Stones",b="The Bloodfury harpies gather shiny things, among them golden-yellow sunstones. Mor'rogal is up on the hills above you and has mentioned using them. He asks you to bring him any Glittering Sunstones you find.",sp=0},{t="Light in Stone",b="Mor'rogal says sunstones reflect the sun's majesty. They can adorn shrines and homes with small motes of light. At night, the moon lends them its silver beauty. To him, they recall a bond with the lights of the skies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Bloodfury harpies collecting?",a="The Bloodfury harpies gather shiny objects, including golden-yellow sunstones.",al={"harpy shiny things","bloodfury trinkets","what do harpies gather"}},{q="Who wants the sunstones?",a="Mor'rogal, who is up on the hills above you, has mentioned using sunstones.",al={"who needs sunstones","mor rogal trinkets","sunstone giver"}},{q="What does Mor'rogal use sunstones for?",a="Mor'rogal says sunstones can adorn shrines and homes with small motes of light.",al={"why morrogal wants stones","sunstone use","what are stones for"}},{q="What do the sunstones mean to Mor'rogal?",a="The sunstones remind Mor'rogal of a bond with the lights of the skies.",al={"sunstone meaning","lights of skies stones","why are stones special"}}},kw={"bloodfury harpies","bloodfury trinkets","charred vale","glittering sunstones","lights of the skies","mor'rogal","shrines","sunstones"},rel={"subzone:charred-vale","npc:mor-rogal","topic:harpy"},m={id=86576},src={"In-game quest text: Bloodfury Trinkets"},fv=true}
E["quest:86585"] = {t="quest",n="Banner of the Fallen",z="general",s="In trogg territory, Mountaineer Ylva’s search for missing comrades ended beneath the trampled standard of Ironforge. Raising it again draws out the trogg that struck her down.",h="In trogg territory, Mountaineer Ylva’s search for missing comrades ended beneath the trampled standard of...",sec={{t="The Trampled Standard",b="Mountaineer Ylva’s trampled Ironforge standard marks where the Alliance scout met her end. She entered trogg territory to find comrades who had vanished on patrol, carrying the city’s banner as a sign of defiance. A powerful trogg struck with enough force to shatter her defenses. The standard was left in the dirt.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance for Ylva",b="Headsplitter, the brute responsible for Ylva’s death, recognized the Ironforge standard and the threat it posed. Raising the fallen banner openly challenges the trogg and draws it back to defend its kill. Once Headsplitter is slain, the battered standard can be returned to Captain Rugelfuss. He arranges for Ylva’s weapon to be passed on and the banner to be cleaned and preserved in her honor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the fallen mountaineer?",a="Mountaineer Ylva was an independent-minded dwarf who entered trogg country to search for mountaineers who never returned from patrol. She carried an Ironforge standard and sought to show dwarven resolve against the troggs before they struck her down.",al={"who was the mountaineer","ylva lore","who died with the banner"}},{q="What is the quest Banner of the Fallen about?",a="You find Mountaineer Ylva’s body and the trampled Ironforge standard she carried. Raising the banner draws out her killer, the trogg Headsplitter, so you can avenge her and return the standard to Captain Rugelfuss.",al={"what is banner of the fallen","what happens in banner of the fallen","ironforge banner quest"}},{q="Who killed Mountaineer Ylva?",a="A trogg known as Headsplitter killed Ylva. It may have used a heavy spiked club to deliver the fatal blow to her skull and knock off her helm. Raising the Ironforge standard provokes the creature to return.",al={"who killed ylva","which trogg killed the mountaineer","headsplitter trogg"}},{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is the dwarven officer overseeing mountaineer operations, and he receives Ylva’s recovered banner. He recognizes her bravery and fierce independence, and promises to clean and display the standard in her honor.",al={"who is rugelfuss","where do i turn in the banner","captain rugelfuss banner"}},{q="Why did Mountaineer Ylva go into trogg territory alone?",a="Ylva went alone to investigate the disappearance of mountaineers who had not returned from a patrol through trogg country. Fiercely independent, she carried the banner to show that Ironforge would never bow to troggs.",al={"why did ylva go into trogg territory","why was ylva alone","ylva missing patrol"}},{q="How is the trogg Headsplitter lured out?",a="Headsplitter remembers the Ironforge standard from striking down Mountaineer Ylva. Planting and raising the trampled banner again provokes the trogg to return and finish what it started.",al={"how do you summon headsplitter","call out headsplitter","raising the standard"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Mountaineer Ylva died defending Ironforge’s honor while searching for missing kin. Recovering her trampled banner and avenging her death strikes at the heart of dwarven pride and duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Ironforge standard represents dwarven allegiance and defiance in trogg territory. Securing it honors the fallen soldiers who hold the line for the Alliance."},kw={"banner of the fallen","captain rugelfuss","headsplitter","ironforge banner","ironforge standard","mountaineer ylva","troggs","ylva"},rel={"npc:captain-rugelfuss","topic:trogg","zone:ironforge"},m={id=86585},src={"In-game quest text: Banner of the Fallen"},fv=true}
E["quest:86613"] = {t="quest",n="Excavation Tools",z="general",s="Magmar Fellhew asks you to return tools abandoned when troggs drove the dwarves from their excavation. The tools can help the excavators resume work once the invasion is under control.",h="Magmar Fellhew asks you to return tools abandoned when troggs drove the dwarves from their excavation.",sec={{t="Tools Left Behind",b="Magmar Fellhew needs the excavation tools the dwarves left behind when troggs overran their camp. You can return them to the excavators, whose work has been stalled by the invasion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Magmar need the excavation tools?",a="The dwarves left most of their tools behind when troggs overran their camp. The tools will help the excavators work again once the invasion is under control.",al={"why tools","magmar tools","excavation tools"}},{q="Who is Magmar Fellhew?",a="Magmar Fellhew is the excavator who asks you to return the abandoned tools.",al={"who magmar","Magmar","tool guy"}},{q="Why did the dwarves leave the tools?",a="The dwarves had to leave most of their tools behind when troggs overran their camp.",al={"dwarves fled","why abandoned","troggs tools"}},{q="What is the excavation's problem?",a="Troggs overran the camp, forcing the dwarves to leave most of their tools behind and halt their work until the invasion is under control.",al={"dig site problem","what happened at camp","excavation issue"}}},kw={"camp","dig site","dwarves","excavation","excavation tools","magmar fellhew","troggs"},rel={"topic:trogg"},m={id=86613},src={"In-game quest text: Excavation Tools"},fv=true}
E["quest:86614"] = {t="quest",n="Silver of the Waves",z="general",s="A lost silver hair clip waits among fishing debris, and its owner is caught up in daily chores. Its return brings relief and restores a keepsake thought lost to the water.",h="A lost silver hair clip waits among fishing debris, and its owner is caught up in daily chores.",sec={{t="A Keepsake in the Flotsam",b="Among discarded fishing debris, you find an ornate silver hair clip marked with the initials K.D. Rusted hooks and broken wire spools lie nearby. Moisture has tarnished the clip, but its fine work still shows beneath the corrosion.",sp=0},{t="Restoring the Shine",b="The clip belongs to a hardworking local, busy with daily chores. You return the keepsake, which its owner had thought lost to the water for good. A little polishing will restore its shine, and the grateful owner welcomes its return.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Silver of the Waves?",a="You find the tarnished silver hair clip among discarded fishing debris, then seek its owner. The piece bears the initials K.D.",al={"silver of the waves","what is silver of the waves","hair clip quest"}},{q="Whose hair clip is found in the debris?",a="The hair clip bears the initials K.D. Its owner recognizes it when you return it, and is grateful to recover a keepsake thought gone forever.",al={"kd monogram","whose hair clip is it","who is kd"}},{q="Where was the hair clip lost?",a="The hair clip lies among discarded fishing debris, near broken wire spools and rusty hooks. The entry does not say exactly where it was lost.",al={"where was the hair clip found","hair clip location"}},{q="What condition is the hair clip in?",a="The ornate silver hair clip is tarnished by moisture and weather, but its craftsmanship remains visible. A little polishing will restore its shine.",al={"silver clip condition","is the hair clip broken"}},{q="How does this quest begin?",a="You find the monogrammed hair clip among discarded fishing refuse, broken wire spools, and rusty hooks. Then you seek its owner.",al={"who gives the quest","how do you start silver of the waves"}},{q="Why is returning the hair clip significant?",a="The owner had thought the keepsake lost to the water for good. Its return brings relief, and the grateful owner welcomes the recovery of a treasured possession.",al={"hair clip reward","why return the hair clip"}}},kw={"chores","fishing debris","hair clip","k.d.","monogram","silver keepsake","silver of the waves"},m={id=86614},src={"In-game quest text: Silver of the Waves"},fv=true}
E["quest:86667"] = {t="quest",n="Snowbound",z="general",s="In Loch Modan, Grenhild studies the local elementals while Norric Lochthane asks for snow from South Gate Pass. His request carries a deeper hope: the aging shaman longs to see his former student again.",h="In Loch Modan, Grenhild studies the local elementals while Norric Lochthane asks for snow from South Gate...",sec={{t="An Unusual Request",b="Grenhild is studying Loch Modan's local elementals when a minor elemental arrives with a message from Norric Lochthane, her former mentor. He urgently needs fresh, unmelted snow for his shamanic workings. Grenhild asks a traveler to fetch it so she can stay with her studies. The snow comes from South Gate Pass, where cold drafts preserve the drifts year-round, and must be sealed in a specially crafted ceramic jar to keep the valley heat at bay.",sp=0},{t="Teacher and Pupil",b="Norric Lochthane lives in a quiet cottage on the Loch's northwest coast, away from the settlements. When the jar arrives, he is pleased to have the cold reagent for his mystical research. Yet he laments that Grenhild did not come herself. His request was for more than a magical ingredient: the aging shaman hoped to reconnect with his former student, now following her own path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Norric Lochthane?",a="Norric Lochthane is an experienced shaman who lives in a cottage on the northwest coast of the Loch in Loch Modan. He once taught Grenhild and still pursues shamanic workings in private. He can call on minor elementals to carry messages through the wilderness.",al={"norric lochthane lore","who is norric","norric loch modan"}},{q="Who is Grenhild?",a="Grenhild is an elemental researcher stationed in Loch Modan. She studied magic under Norric Lochthane and respects his craft, but devotes her fieldwork to local elementals and has little time to travel.",al={"who is grenhild","grenhild loch modan","grenhild mentor"}},{q="Why does Norric need a jar of snow?",a="Norric needs the snow for his shamanic workings and mystical research. He also hoped Grenhild would take the request as a reason to visit him in person.",al={"why does norric want snow","snow for shamanic workings","jar of snow purpose"}},{q="Where is the snow gathered for this quest?",a="Gather snow near the tunnel entrance at South Gate Pass, high in the mountains between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. The cold elevation keeps snow there throughout the year, so travelers can pack it in an insulated ceramic jar.",al={"where to find snow","south gate pass snow location","how to get jar of snow"}},{q="Why couldn't Grenhild deliver the snow herself?",a="Grenhild is busy observing and studying Loch Modan's local elementals. Her fieldwork keeps her at her post, away from the trek to South Gate Pass and down to Norric's lakeside home.",al={"why cant grenhild go","why does grenhild need help","grenhild busy"}},{q="How did Norric send his request to Grenhild?",a="Norric summoned a minor elemental and sent it to carry his message to Grenhild. The unusual courier shows his ease with elemental arts and shamanic practice.",al={"norric courier","elemental messenger","how did norric contact grenhild"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Norric Lochthane's use of minor elemental couriers and frozen reagents reflects the shamanic traditions and elemental studies found in Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="Norric Lochthane and Grenhild's exchange offers a glimpse of dwarven mentorship and elemental scholarship around Loch Modan's peaks and shores."},kw={"grenhild","jar of snow","loch modan","minor elemental","norric lochthane","shamanic workings","snowbound","south gate pass","the loch"},rel={"topic:shaman","subzone:the-loch","subzone:south-gate-pass"},m={id=86667},src={"In-game quest text: Snowbound"},fv=true}
E["quest:86757"] = {t="quest",n="Slowing the Orc Advance",z="general",s="Shandrina asks you to help drive orcs from eastern Ashenvale. Their scouts and grunts make it unsafe for her kind to travel through the woods.",h="Shandrina asks you to help drive orcs from eastern Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Orcs in the Woods",b="In Ashenvale, Shandrina seeks your help as orcs spread through the eastern forest. Their scouts and grunts now lurk throughout the woods, making travel unsafe for her kind. You are asked to bring her the jagged swords and curved knives the orcs use, so she can salvage and repurpose them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Shandrina need?",a="Shandrina asks you to bring her the jagged swords and curved knives used by the orcs.",al={"what does she want","shandrina needs","items for shandrina"}},{q="Why is Ashenvale unsafe?",a="Orcs have taken over the eastern forest, and their scouts and grunts lurk through the woods.",al={"why unsafe","orcs in ash forest","what's happening in ashenvale"}},{q="What will Shandrina do with the weapons?",a="Shandrina plans to salvage and repurpose the orc weapons.",al={"weapon purpose","what for swords","reuse orc weapons"}},{q="Who are the orcs in the woods?",a="The orcs have taken over the eastern forest, where their scouts and grunts now lurk.",al={"orc scouts","orc grunts","who took over east"}}},kw={"ashenvale","curved knives","grunts","jagged swords","orcs","scouts","shandrina","weapons"},rel={"zone:ashenvale"},m={id=86757},src={"In-game quest text: Slowing the Orc Advance"},fv=true}
E["quest:86758"] = {t="quest",n="Twisting the Knife",z="general",s="Marek asks you to hunt Daggerfang, the crocolisk that took his knife. The beast prowls along the lake’s edge, where other hunters may be at risk.",h="Marek asks you to hunt Daggerfang, the crocolisk that took his knife.",sec={{t="Marek’s Knife",b="Marek tells you that a crocolisk nearly took his hand and left him scrambling from the lake. He thinks his knife is still somewhere nearby. He calls the beast Daggerfang and asks you to find it along the lake’s edge, where other hunters may be in danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daggerfang?",a="Daggerfang is a crocolisk Marek says hunts along the edge of the lake.",al={"daggerfang","daggerfang croc","big crocolisk"}},{q="What happened to Marek’s knife?",a="Marek thinks he left his knife near the lake after using it against a crocolisk.",al={"marek knife","lost knife","where knife"}},{q="Why does Marek want Daggerfang hunted?",a="Marek believes Daggerfang may threaten the other hunters near the lake.",al={"why kill daggerfang","croc danger","hunt the croc"}},{q="Where is Daggerfang?",a="Marek says Daggerfang hunts along the edge of the lake.",al={"daggerfang location","lake croc","where is the croc"}},{q="What does Marek ask me to bring back?",a="Marek asks you to find and defeat Daggerfang and bring back his knife.",al={"what to bring back","knife and croc","marek request"}},{q="What does Marek say about the crocolisk?",a="Marek says the crocolisk nearly took his hand, and he used his knife against it to escape.",al={"marek croc story","almost lost hand","knife in jaw"}}},kw={"crocolisk","daggerfang","hunt","hunters","knife","lake","marek"},rel={"topic:hunter"},m={id=86758},src={"In-game quest text: Twisting the Knife"},fv=true}
E["quest:86776"] = {t="quest",n="Ingredients for the Forge",z="general",s="In Thelsamar, Morhan Coppertongue needs bronze bars to fill his dwindling workshop stores. Far from Ironforge's steady trade, the settlement depends on travelers to bring the metals its forge needs.",h="In Thelsamar, Morhan Coppertongue needs bronze bars to fill his dwindling workshop stores.",sec={{t="Supply Strains in Thelsamar",b="Thelsamar keeps a quieter pace than Ironforge's Great Forge. Far from the capital, supplies can be hard to come by. Morhan Coppertongue, the local blacksmith, makes the hardware, pots, and tools the township needs. Yet bronze and other raw metals often run short. Without regular shipments from the city, passing travelers and prospectors help keep the local anvils at work.",sp=0},{t="Keeping the Fires Burning",b="Bronze bars let Morhan resume making goods for daily use. But the forge still faces shortages, and Loch Modan has no reliable merchant route bringing coal to town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers Ingredients for the Forge?",a="Morhan Coppertongue, a dwarven craftsman, offers it at the forge in Thelsamar, in Loch Modan.",al={"who gives ingredients for the forge","morhan coppertongue quest","thelsamar blacksmith quest"}},{q="What materials does Morhan Coppertongue need?",a="Morhan needs bronze bars for his workshop. He uses them to make everyday goods such as pots, kettles, and tools for local residents.",al={"what does morhan need","materials for ingredients for the forge","what bars for thelsamar forge"}},{q="Why is Thelsamar running out of metal?",a="Thelsamar lacks Ironforge's great workshops and steady trade. Its craftspeople can run short of raw metal.",al={"why does thelsamar lack bronze","why doesn't thelsamar have metal"}},{q="What does Morhan forge with the bronze?",a="Morhan uses bronze to make useful goods for the home and workplace, including cookware, kettles, pots, and tools for the townsfolk.",al={"what is bronze used for in thelsamar","what does morhan make"}},{q="What other supplies does the forge struggle to get?",a="Morhan also needs a regular trader to bring coal into town. The forge depends on fuel to keep its fires burning.",al={"what fuel does morhan need","thelsamar coal problem"}},{q="Where is this quest completed?",a="It takes place in Thelsamar, Loch Modan's chief dwarven settlement in the hills east of Dun Morogh.",al={"where does ingredients for the forge take place","ingredients for the forge location"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Morhan Coppertongue depends on smiths and metalworkers to supply Thelsamar with everyday goods, from kettles and cooking pots to field tools.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners who smelt copper and tin into bronze bars provide the materials that keep Loch Modan's rural workshops working.",["race:Dwarf"]="Even a small dwarven settlement like Thelsamar depends on its forge, so a shortage of metal concerns the whole community."},kw={"blacksmith","bronze bars","forge","ingredients for the forge","loch modan","morhan coppertongue","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:ironforge"},m={id=86776},src={"In-game quest text: Ingredients for the Forge"},fv=true}
E["quest:87288"] = {t="quest",n="Soft Saber Pelts",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Soft Saber Pelts come from cats that threaten travelers on the roads. Their thick coats make warm blankets and shawls.",h="Across Azeroth, Soft Saber Pelts come from cats that threaten travelers on the roads.",sec={{t="Securing the Wilderness Roads",b="Saber cats prowl the roads used by couriers, merchants, and lone travelers across Azeroth. People may admire their grace, yet growing numbers near trade routes bring sudden attacks. Hunters keep those roads safe for everyone who depends on them.",sp=0},{t="Warmth from the Hunt",b="The hunt yields more than pelts. Frontier camps value saber cats’ dense coats for their warmth and strength. Skilled hands make the pelts into shawls and heavy blankets, giving shelter from harsh weather.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are travelers asked to hunt sabers?",a="Saber cats near the roads threaten travelers and merchants. Hunting them keeps the routes safer for those passing through.",al={"why hunt sabers","why kill sabers","saber threat"}},{q="What are the saber pelts used for?",a="Their thick fur makes durable, warm blankets and shawls that help guard against the weather.",al={"what are pelts for","saber pelt craft","blankets and shawls"}},{q="Who seeks to trade for these saber pelts?",a="Local merchants and crafters trade with hunters for useful materials. For quality pelts, they offer sturdy, soft goods made through their craft.",al={"saber pelt trade","who takes pelts"}},{q="Do wild sabers pose a real threat to the roads?",a="Yes. Large saber cats hunt across wide territories that can overlap with frontier roads. Couriers and caravans risk sudden attacks where the cats roam.",al={"are sabers dangerous","saber road danger"}},{q="What is given in return for the pelts?",a="The hunter receives a soft, durable keepsake in thanks for the pelts. It recalls the great cats hunted along the frontier.",al={"soft and sturdy reward","remembrance reward"}},{q="How do local traders view the hunting of such majestic beasts?",a="Traders may regret killing such regal creatures, but they see the hunt as necessary to protect travelers and make practical use of the warm pelts.",al={"is hunting sabers justified","regret hunting sabers"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can turn saber pelts into sturdy, soft blankets and shawls for cold travel on the frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you respect saber predators and hunt them when they threaten the roads."},kw={"blankets","pelts","roads","saber","shawls","soft saber pelts","trade"},m={id=87288},src={"In-game quest text: Soft Saber Pelts"},fv=true}
E["quest:87491"] = {t="quest",n="Spark of Freedom",z="general",s="The fire elemental has spent its strength in a blazing display. The Dark Irons held its attention, and the rest of the group is relieved it never turned on them.",h="The fire elemental has spent its strength in a blazing display.",sec={{t="After the Flames",b="The fire elemental's display leaves the onlooker amazed, then relieved when the creature runs out of strength. The Dark Irons had drawn its attention. Had it turned on the rest of the group, they too could have been in danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the fire elemental?",a="The fire elemental ran out of strength after its pyrotechnic display.",al={"fire elemental","elemental ran out of steam","what happened here"}},{q="Who was the elemental going after?",a="The fire elemental had been going after the Dark Irons.",al={"dark irons target","elemental and dark irons","who was it attacking"}},{q="Why is the onlooker relieved?",a="The onlooker is relieved because the elemental did not turn on the rest of the group.",al={"why relieved","elemental danger","could it attack us"}}},kw={"dark irons","fire elemental","pyrotechnic display","spark of freedom"},m={id=87491},src={"In-game quest text: Spark of Freedom"},fv=true}
E["quest:87760"] = {t="quest",n="Holy Diver",z="general",s="A Darnassian seeks your help stopping naga from controlling sea creatures near the Ruins of Mathystra. Find their beastmistress and recover the tool used to compel the creatures.",h="A Darnassian seeks your help stopping naga from controlling sea creatures near the Ruins of Mathystra.",sec={{t="A Beastmistress's Rod",b="A Darnassian asks you to stop the naga in the Ruins of Mathystra, where they are seizing threshers from the shore. Animal samples showed that the naga forced sea creatures to serve as mounts and beasts of burden. Those they could not use were driven away. Find the Stormscale Beastmistress and bring back her Rod of Deep Dominion; the creatures remain under the naga's control until it is taken.",sp=0},{t="The Creatures' Peace",b="In the Ruins of Mathystra, you take the Rod of Deep Dominion from the naga. The Darnassian says it will be destroyed, so the threshers and sea turtles can live in peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the naga doing to the sea creatures?",a="The naga compel sea creatures to serve as mounts and beasts of burden, and drive away those they cannot use.",al={"naga and threshers","sea creature mounts","what happened to the animals"}},{q="Where are the naga forces?",a="The naga have forces in the Ruins of Mathystra.",al={"naga location","mathystra naga","where is beastmistress"}},{q="Who are you looking for?",a="A Stormscale Beastmistress is the target named by the Darnassian.",al={"beastmistress","stormscale woman","who has the rod"}},{q="What is the Rod of Deep Dominion?",a="It is the rod the naga use to compel sea creatures into their service.",al={"deep dominion rod","naga control tool","rod name"}},{q="Which creatures are affected?",a="The Darnassian names threshers and sea turtles as creatures that can live in peace once the rod is destroyed.",al={"threshers and turtles","animals in danger","sea creatures"}}},kw={"holy diver","naga","rod of deep dominion","ruins of mathystra","sea creatures","sea turtles","stormscale beastmistress","threshers"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","topic:naga","zone:darnassus"},m={id=87760},src={"In-game quest text: Holy Diver"},fv=true}
E["quest:88756"] = {t="quest",n="Bring Back a Bang",z="general",s="A construction site has lost blasting powder to Dark Iron dwarves camped east on Direforge Hill. Their marked barrels could bring danger to the surrounding lands.",h="A construction site has lost blasting powder to Dark Iron dwarves camped east on Direforge Hill.",sec={{t="Theft at the Construction Site",b="Dark Iron dwarves camp east on Direforge Hill. They raided a nearby construction site and carried its vital blasting powder back to their tents.",sp=0},{t="Volatile Hands",b="Blasting powder in malicious Dark Iron hands threatens the surrounding lands. The stolen barrels bear red markings that set them apart from common supplies. Recover them before the dwarves put the powder to destructive use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who stole the explosives?",a="Dark Iron dwarves raided a nearby construction site and carried barrels of blasting powder to their tents east on Direforge Hill.",al={"who stole explosives","who took the barrels","stolen powder"}},{q="Where did the Dark Irons take the barrels?",a="The Dark Iron dwarves hauled the stolen barrels east to their camps on Direforge Hill.",al={"where are explosives","direforge hill camps","where is stolen powder"}},{q="How can you identify the stolen explosives?",a="Red markings distinguish the stolen construction barrels from ordinary supplies.",al={"what do barrels look like","how to identify powder","red marked barrels"}},{q="Why do the explosives need to be recovered?",a="The construction workers cannot spare the materials, and blasting powder in malicious Dark Iron hands threatens everyone nearby.",al={"why retrieve powder","what is dark iron threat","why stop dark irons"}},{q="What is Direforge Hill?",a="Direforge Hill lies east of the local worksite, where hostile Dark Iron dwarf camps have taken hold.",al={"what is direforge hill","direforge hill lore"}},{q="Who are the Dark Iron dwarves?",a="Dark Iron dwarves are a treacherous faction, known for malice, dark sorcery, and lasting hostility toward their kin and neighbors.",al={"who are dark iron dwarves","why are dark irons hostile"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the destructive power of mining explosives, especially when they fall into the hands of your bitter Dark Iron kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know blasting powder and volatile compounds need careful handling and containment. Unsecured stores can bring disaster."},kw={"blasting powder","bring back a bang","construction site","dark iron dwarf","direforge hill","stolen explosives"},rel={"subzone:direforge-hill","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf"},m={id=88756},src={"In-game quest text: Bring Back a Bang"},fv=true}
E["quest:91282"] = {t="quest",n="A Second Home",z="general",s="Newly risen Forsaken are being invited to join an order in Tirisfal Glades. They are directed to Bandarion Keep, a monastery on the bluffs northwest of the Solliden Farmstead near the Whispering Woods. The order offers community, shared faith, and mutual support as they make a place in their new unlife.",h="Newly risen Forsaken are being invited to join an order in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Gathering of the Risen",b="Newly risen Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades are urged to find fellowship among their peers. Together, they can face unlife through mutual faith and community, and discover their full potential.",sp=0},{t="Sanctuary on the Bluffs",b="Travelers are directed to Bandarion Keep, a monastery on the bluffs northwest of the Solliden Farmstead. Beside the Whispering Woods, it offers the new order a refuge to study, practice, and establish roots in Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest A Second Home?",a="Newly risen Forsaken are invited to join a new class order in Tirisfal Glades. They are directed to a monastery where like-minded practitioners can gather, find fellowship, and explore their shared potential.",al={"what is a second home","quest a second home","a second home quest"}},{q="Where can Bandarion Keep be found?",a="Bandarion Keep stands on the bluffs northwest of the Solliden Farmstead in Tirisfal Glades, beside the Whispering Woods.",al={"where is bandarion keep","bandarion keep location","how to get to bandarion keep"}},{q="Who established the monastery at Bandarion Keep?",a="Bandarion Keep is the monastery of Tyr's Watch, a Forsaken paladin order in Tirisfal Glades. It gathers newly risen brethren around community and shared faith.",al={"who runs bandarion keep","who formed bandarion keep","bandarion keep order"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken being invited to Bandarion Keep?",a="The founders believe newly risen undead can reach their full potential through community and shared purpose. Bandarion Keep offers their order a sanctuary and a place to learn.",al={"why go to bandarion keep","bandarion keep purpose"}},{q="What is the connection to the Solliden Farmstead?",a="The Solliden Farmstead lies in western Tirisfal Glades, southeast of the bluffs where Bandarion Keep overlooks the edge of the Whispering Woods.",al={"where is solliden farmstead","solliden farmstead bandarion"}},{q="What kind of order is gathering at Bandarion Keep?",a="Tyr's Watch is a newly formed Forsaken paladin order gathering at Bandarion Keep. It aims to support its kin as they adjust to their new unlife.",al={"what order is at bandarion keep","bandarion keep class order"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Newly risen Forsaken often feel adrift after breaking free from the Scourge. An order founded on community and shared faith offers a rare chance to rebuild.",["faction:Horde"]="Stronger ties among Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades help secure the Horde's presence in the northern Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"a second home","bandarion keep","forsaken order","monastery","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","whispering woods"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","subzone:solliden-farmstead"},m={id=91282},src={"In-game quest text: A Second Home"},fv=true}
E["quest:91285"] = {t="quest",n="Murlocs at the Gates",z="general",s="Breton Samuels asks you to drive back murlocs troubling the keep. Their attacks make rebuilding harder.",h="Breton Samuels asks you to drive back murlocs troubling the keep.",sec={{t="The Murloc Problem",b="Murlocs still trouble the keep after you and the others drove them from their spawning grounds. Their attacks are growing harder to manage, so Breton Samuels asks you to drive back some of them. They lurk in the bluffs along the eastern road and in camps around the lake to the west.",sp=0},{t="The Attacks",b="Breton Samuels expects the attacks to continue. He hopes pushing back the Vile Fin attackers and seers will slow them down. The keep is already hard to rebuild while murlocs strike at its people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Breton Samuels asks you to drive back some of the murlocs troubling the keep.",al={"who gives this","breton samuels","who wants help"}},{q="Why are the murlocs a problem?",a="The murlocs have troubled the keep since its people drove them from their spawning grounds. Their attacks are becoming harder to manage.",al={"why murlocs","murloc problem","what are they doing"}},{q="Where are the murlocs?",a="They lurk in the bluffs along the road to the east and in camps around the lake to the west.",al={"where murlocs","murlocs location","where to find them"}},{q="Which murlocs are involved?",a="The Vile Fin attackers and Vile Fin seers are troubling the keep.",al={"murloc types","vile fins","who to fight"}},{q="Why does the keep need help?",a="The keep is being rebuilt, and murloc attacks make that work harder.",al={"why help","keep rebuilding","what's at stake"}}},kw={"attacker","breton samuels","keep","murloc","murlocs at the gates","seer","spawning grounds","vile fin"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={id=91285},src={"In-game quest text: Murlocs at the Gates"},fv=true}
E["quest:91294"] = {t="quest",n="Touring the Grounds",z="general",s="Breton asks you to walk Bandarion Keep after the murloc attacks come under control. Meeting Danitha Morr is your first step toward settling among the residents.",h="Breton asks you to walk Bandarion Keep after the murloc attacks come under control.",sec={{t="At the Keep",b="Breton asks you to meet Bandarion Keep’s residents and look around the stronghold. Once you have finished, Danitha Morr can help you settle in. The keep is still small, but its people call it home.",sp=0},{t="A Commander",b="Danitha Morr introduces herself as the closest thing Bandarion Keep has to a commander. She welcomes those seeking fellowship with people still loyal to the Light. The keep needs help before it can be fully established.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to look around?",a="Breton encourages you to explore Bandarion Keep after the murloc attacks come under control.",al={"who sent me around","breton touring grounds"}},{q="Who leads Bandarion Keep?",a="Danitha Morr is the closest thing Bandarion Keep has to a commander.",al={"who is danitha","keep leader"}},{q="Why should I speak to Danitha Morr?",a="Danitha Morr can help you settle in among the keep’s residents.",al={"where do i go after touring","talk to danitha"}},{q="What is Bandarion Keep like?",a="Bandarion Keep is a small stronghold whose residents call it home.",al={"what's the keep like","bandarion keep"}},{q="Who is welcome at the keep?",a="Danitha welcomes those seeking fellowship with people who remain loyal to the Light.",al={"who can join","loyal to the light"}}},kw={"bandarion keep","breton","danitha morr","grounds","light","murloc attacks","residents"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:light","topic:murloc"},m={id=91294},src={"In-game quest text: Touring the Grounds"},fv=true}
E["quest:91316"] = {t="quest",n="Making Repairs",z="general",s="At the fortress, a shortage of building materials has made restoration difficult. You are sent to Shadowvale to search for lumber.",h="At the fortress, a shortage of building materials has made restoration difficult.",sec={{t="Supplies at Shadowvale",b="Shadowvale is a ruined village in the Whispering Forest, southwest of the fortress. Search an old root cellar in one of its buildings for usable materials. The fortress lies far from settled lands, so bringing in supplies is difficult. Its repairs depend on what can be found there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are building materials needed?",a="The fortress needs building materials to help restore it. Its distance from the Undercity makes supplies difficult to bring in.",al={"why need lumber","fortress repairs"}},{q="Where is Shadowvale?",a="Shadowvale lies in ruins in the Whispering Forest, southwest of the fortress.",al={"shadowvale location","where is the village"}},{q="Where might usable materials be found?",a="Usable materials may be stored in an old root cellar in one of Shadowvale's buildings.",al={"root cellar materials","where to look"}},{q="What is the fortress short of?",a="The fortress is short of building materials needed for its restoration.",al={"what supplies are missing","lumber shortage"}}},kw={"building materials","fortress","making repairs","root cellar","shadowvale","sturdy lumber","undercity","whispering forest"},rel={"subzone:whispering-forest","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity"},m={id=91316},src={"In-game quest text: Making Repairs"},fv=true}
E["quest:91317"] = {t="quest",n="The Tarnished",z="general",s="At Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades, the Tarnished threaten a fledgling order's place among the Forsaken. Their attacks deepen mistrust and put the order's future at risk.",h="At Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades, the Tarnished threaten a fledgling order's place among the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Tarnished Order",b="Some risen still bear prejudices from their former lives, and now attack their fellow Forsaken. The Tarnished have gathered at Shadowvale, southwest of here. Their violence must end, and Commander Rudolph Gelhardt’s head must be brought back.",sp=0},{t="A Place Among Them",b="The Tarnished’s attacks give those who distrust the order more reason to turn against it. Stopping them may help the order earn a place among the Forsaken. Acceptance could still take years or decades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Tarnished?",a="The Tarnished are risen who kept prejudices from their former lives and now attack fellow Forsaken.",al={"tarnished who","who are these tarnished"}},{q="Where are the Tarnished?",a="A number of the Tarnished have settled at Shadowvale, southwest of here in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"tarnished location","where tarnished"}},{q="Why are the Tarnished a threat?",a="Their attacks on fellow Forsaken deepen mistrust of the order among the Forsaken.",al={"why stop tarnished","tarnished attacks"}},{q="Who leads the Tarnished?",a="Commander Rudolph Gelhardt leads the Tarnished.",al={"tarnished leader","rudy gelhardt"}},{q="Why does the order need the Forsaken's trust?",a="The order is mistrusted because the Forsaken remember persecution by the living in the name of the Light. The Tarnished’s attacks deepen that mistrust.",al={"order trust","forsaken mistrust"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you face risen who attack their own people. Their violence worsens mistrust toward a fledgling order.",["faction:Horde"]="The order hopes to earn a place among the Horde, but its leader expects acceptance may take years or decades."},kw={"commander rudolph gelhardt","fledgling order","forsaken","mistrust","shadowvale","tarnished drudges","tarnished zealots","the tarnished","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:light"},m={id=91317},src={"In-game quest text: The Tarnished"},fv=true}
E["quest:91723"] = {t="quest",n="Delicate Instruments",z="general",s="Hamish Bergwort's instruments at the Tower of Azora falter as surges of magic rise from the north. Their source is Jasperlode Mine, where kobold geomancers stir the earth.",h="Hamish Bergwort's instruments at the Tower of Azora falter as surges of magic rise from the north.",sec={{t="Disrupted Calibrations",b="At the Tower of Azora, Hamish Bergwort's arcane apparatus needs careful calibration. Uncontrolled surges keep unsettling his measurements. He cannot make precise adjustments while the interference continues.",sp=0},{t="The Interference from Jasperlode",b="The magical pulses lead north to Jasperlode Mine. Kobolds have taken its tunnels, where their geomancers work crude earth magic. Their frequent rituals send ripples through the stone. Those tremors unsettle the Tower of Azora's sensitive instruments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hamish Bergwort?",a="Hamish Bergwort is an arcane researcher at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. His sensitive instruments need precise calibration and are easily disturbed by magical fluctuations.",al={"who is hamish bergwort","quest giver delicate instruments","hamish bergwort tower of azora"}},{q="Why are the arcane instruments malfunctioning?",a="Magical surges from Jasperlode Mine to the north disrupt the instruments. Kobolds there create the surges with crude earth magic.",al={"why are instruments disrupted","cause of arcane surges","what is interfering with azora"}},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine lies north of the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. Kobolds occupy its tunnels, where geomantic rituals send ripples through the surrounding woods.",al={"what is jasperlode mine","where are the geomancers","jasperlode kobolds"}},{q="What are Kobold Geomancers?",a="Kobold geomancers are spellcasters among the kobold packs who wield crude elemental earth magic. Their rituals together create disturbances that interfere with sensitive arcane equipment.",al={"what are kobold geomancers","kobold magic users","geomancy kobold"}},{q="How does eliminating the geomancers resolve the issue?",a="Stopping the geomancers' rituals in Jasperlode Mine ends the elemental surges. Then researchers at the Tower of Azora can calibrate their devices without interference.",al={"why kill geomancers","delicate instruments purpose","stopping the surges"}},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane study spire in eastern Elwynn Forest. Scholars and mages there observe regional phenomena and maintain finely tuned magical apparatus.",al={"what is tower of azora","azora tower lore","elwynn mage tower"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the Tower of Azora's delicate apparatus needs steady surroundings. Crude geomantic magic can disrupt careful arcane study.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help protect Elwynn Forest's scholarly enclaves by aiding the researchers at the Tower of Azora against the kobolds' disruptive magic."},kw={"arcane","delicate instruments","elwynn forest","geomancy","hamish bergwort","jasperlode mine","kobold","kobold geomancer","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:jasperlode-mine","topic:kobold"},m={id=91723},src={"In-game quest text: Delicate Instruments"},fv=true}
E["quest:91724"] = {t="quest",n="Delicate Instruments",z="general",s="At the Tower of Azora, Defias magic troubles Delicate Instruments. Hamish Bergwort's equipment suffers from erratic spellcasting near Stone Cairn Lake. The disturbance must end before his instruments can work properly.",h="At the Tower of Azora, Defias magic troubles Delicate Instruments.",sec={{t="Interference at the Tower",b="Hamish Bergwort studies arcane questions in the Tower of Azora. His work depends on precise readings, and even a slight change in local magic can ruin hours of careful study. He suspects crude spells nearby are causing the interruptions.",sp=0},{t="Banditry and the Arcane",b="Defias rogue wizards practice magic near Stone Cairn Lake, and their casting causes the interference. Their unchecked spellcraft brings unstable magic into Elwynn. End their casting, and the disturbance will cease, allowing Bergwort's instruments to give clean readings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Delicate Instruments?",a="Hamish Bergwort offers Delicate Instruments from the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He needs stable magical conditions for his research.",al={"who gives delicate instruments","delicate instruments questgiver","where is hamish bergwort"}},{q="What is disrupting Hamish Bergwort's instruments?",a="Crude spells from Defias bandits near Stone Cairn Lake interfere with the instruments in the Tower of Azora.",al={"what is disrupting the instruments","why are instruments disrupted","delicate instruments interference"}},{q="Where can the Defias Rogue Wizards be found?",a="The Defias rogue wizards gather along the shores and surrounding grounds of Stone Cairn Lake, just north of the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest.",al={"where are the rogue wizards","stone cairn lake rogue wizards","where to find defias rogue wizards"}},{q="Why are Defias bandits practicing magic?",a="The Defias Brotherhood has recruited renegade dabblers in the arcane. These rogue wizards practice magic without sanction and cause erratic disturbances in the region.",al={"why do defias have wizards","defias spellcasters","rogue wizards lore"}},{q="What is the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Azora is an arcane spire in eastern Elwynn Forest. Human magi and scholars study ley lines, magical anomalies, and regional security there.",al={"what is tower of azora","azora tower elwynn","who runs tower of azora"}},{q="Does eliminating the rogue wizards fix the problem?",a="Yes. Once you cull the Defias rogue wizards casting at Stone Cairn Lake, the magical resonance calms and Hamish Bergwort's apparatus works properly again.",al={"does stopping the wizards work","delicate instruments outcome","hamish bergwort instruments fixed"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know careless spells from amateurs like the Defias rogue wizards can send wild fluctuations across Elwynn and disrupt sensitive magical research.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep eastern Elwynn Forest secure from Defias encroachment by maintaining order around the Tower of Azora."},kw={"defias brotherhood","defias rogue wizard","delicate instruments","elwynn forest","hamish bergwort","stone cairn lake","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:stone-cairn-lake"},m={id=91724},src={"In-game quest text: Delicate Instruments"},fv=true}
E["quest:91725"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Enchanting Supplies",z="general",s="Near the Tower of Azora, Blixie Fitzwink has lost the supplies she was carrying after a gnoll ambush. The enchanting reagents are scattered among camps around Stone Cairn Lake. Their return could spare her weeks of chore duty and keep Master Theocritus's arcane studies supplied.",h="Near the Tower of Azora, Blixie Fitzwink has lost the supplies she was carrying after a gnoll ambush.",sec={{t="An Ambush on the Road",b="Blixie Fitzwink was carrying supplies from a trading post to the Tower of Azora when gnolls ambushed her on the road. She fled, leaving the cargo scattered among their camps along Stone Cairn Lake. The valuable reagents were meant for Master Theocritus, whom Blixie assists. Now she asks travelers to recover them, fearing weeks of cleanup duty after her arcane polymorph experiments.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Errands and Local Hazards",b="Master Theocritus conducts sensitive magical research at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. His work depends on delicate reagents brought from local trading posts. Gnoll packs around Stone Cairn Lake have grown bolder, making the route dangerous. The lost supplies could interrupt his studies, while their return may spare his beleaguered assistant further trouble.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Stolen Enchanting Supplies?",a="Blixie Fitzwink asks for help near the Tower of Azora. She assists Master Theocritus and was ambushed by gnolls while carrying supplies back from a local trading post.",al={"who gives stolen enchanting supplies","who is blixie fitzwink","quest giver blixie"}},{q="Who is Master Theocritus?",a="Master Theocritus is a senior human wizard who lives at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He oversees arcane investigations in the region and relies on assistants to bring him enchanting reagents and research materials.",al={"who is master theocritus","theocritus role","tower of azora mage"}},{q="What supplies were taken by the gnolls?",a="The gnolls took enchanting reagents gathered at a trading post for Master Theocritus's arcane work. The ambush scattered the cargo, and the items ended up in gnoll camps around Stone Cairn Lake.",al={"what are the supplies","what did gnolls steal","enchanting reagents"}},{q="Where did the gnolls take the supplies?",a="Stone Cairn Lake lies in eastern Elwynn Forest, north of the Tower of Azora. Gnoll packs camp along its shores and on surrounding islands, threatening travelers on nearby roads.",al={"where is stone cairn lake","where are gnolls holding supplies","lake gnolls elwynn"}},{q="Why is Blixie Fitzwink worried about losing the package?",a="Blixie fears Master Theocritus will give her weeks of cleaning duty after his polymorph experiments. Apprentices at the tower face mundane or messy chores when errands or magical duties go wrong.",al={"what happens if blixie fails","blixie punishment","polymorph cleanup"}},{q="Why are gnolls attacking travelers in eastern Elwynn?",a="Gnoll packs prowl eastern Elwynn Forest, with hostile camps around Stone Cairn Lake and raids on nearby roads. They disrupt trade and ambush travelers moving between settlements and arcane outposts.",al={"why are gnolls near tower of azora","gnoll threat elwynn","riverpaw stone cairn lake"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the supply route to the Tower of Azora secure helps Stormwind's frontline mages stay equipped against threats in Elwynn Forest and beyond.",["class:Mage"]="The Tower of Azora's arcane research depends on delicate materials. Recovered enchanting reagents matter to mages studying under Master Theocritus.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome apprentice, you may find yourself doing menial work for human archmages. A mistake can bring humiliating chore duty."},kw={"blixie fitzwink","elwynn forest","enchanting supplies","gnolls","master theocritus","polymorph","stone cairn lake","tower of azora"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:stone-cairn-lake","npc:theocritus","topic:gnoll"},m={id=91725},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Enchanting Supplies"},fv=true}
E["quest:91732"] = {t="quest",n="Good Steel",z="general",s="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Hagar Lowe seeks good steel for the tools worn by its woodcutters. With fine metal scarce after the wars, he sends adventurers to Jasperlode Mine for picks whose steel can be reused.",h="At Eastvale Logging Camp, Hagar Lowe seeks good steel for the tools worn by its woodcutters.",sec={{t="A Kingdom's Scarcity",b="After the wars that battered the human kingdoms, good steel grows scarce in Elwynn Forest. At Eastvale Logging Camp, woodcutters rely on sturdy axes, saws, and other tools. Constant use and poor metal have worn them down. Without steady shipments from Stormwind's foundries, craftsman Hagar Lowe must keep the camp working with what he can find.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Past",b="North of Eastvale Logging Camp, Jasperlode Mine lies abandoned after its fall. Miners once worked its rich veins with finely made picks, forged when steel was plentiful and expertly tempered. Hagar sends adventurers into the infested tunnels to bring those picks back to Eastvale. Their sound metal can be melted down and made into tools for the camp's lumberjacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Good Steel?",a="Hagar Lowe, a craftsman at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, asks adventurers to salvage good steel equipment from abandoned workings. The camp needs reliable tools.",al={"who gives good steel","where do i turn in good steel","who is hagar lowe"}},{q="Why does Hagar Lowe need mining tools from Jasperlode Mine?",a="Wars have left quality steel scarce, and the camp's tools badly worn. Hagar wants the finely made picks abandoned in Jasperlode Mine so he can reuse their steel for tools used in lumbering.",al={"why get picks","why does hagar want mining tools","purpose of mining tools"}},{q="What is Jasperlode Mine?",a="Jasperlode Mine is an old mining site in north-eastern Elwynn Forest, north of Eastvale Logging Camp. It was overrun and abandoned, leaving finely made mining equipment in its depths.",al={"what is jasperlode mine","where are the tools","jasperlode lore"}},{q="Why is good steel in short supply?",a="The Third War and prolonged conflicts disrupted production, supply lines, and trade across the human kingdoms. Resources are stretched thin as the realm is defended and rebuilt, so outlying places like Eastvale salvage durable metal from old tools.",al={"why is steel scarce","steel shortage elwynn","after the war metal shortage"}},{q="What is Eastvale Logging Camp?",a="Eastvale Logging Camp is Stormwind's main timber settlement, on Elwynn Forest's eastern border near the Redridge Mountains. Its woodcutters supply raw lumber to Stormwind and nearby communities, so reliable tools matter to their work.",al={"where is eastvale logging camp","eastvale camp purpose","eastvale lumber camp"}},{q="What makes the tools in Jasperlode Mine so special?",a="The picks left in Jasperlode Mine were forged when craftsmanship was higher and steel was more plentiful. Their lasting shine and durability show Hagar they were made with better steel than is available today.",al={"who makes the picks","why are the picks good","mining tools quality"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="With high-grade steel scarce in post-war Elwynn, smiths and craftsmen must scrounge for metal and reuse it from old, abandoned tools.",["profession:Mining"]="The picks left behind in Jasperlode Mine show an older, finer standard of metalworking that workers in Elwynn struggle to match today.",["faction:Alliance"]="Strained supplies across Stormwind's outlying lands leave settlements like Eastvale Logging Camp salvaging abandoned tools to keep working."},kw={"eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","good steel","hagar lowe","jasperlode mine","mining tools","post-war shortages","repurposing steel"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:eastvale-logging-camp"},m={id=91732},src={"In-game quest text: Good Steel"},fv=true}
E["quest:91733"] = {t="quest",n="Downstream",z="general",s="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Ormin Pelford's wagon has overturned, and the river has carried his woodworking tools downstream. Murlocs and wolves guard the banks where they lie.",h="Near Eastvale Logging Camp, Ormin Pelford's wagon has overturned, and the river has carried his woodworking...",sec={{t="A Mishap on the Road",b="Laborer Ormin Pelford was bringing a shipment back from a local trading post when his wagon tipped near Eastvale Logging Camp. Its gear spilled into the river, and the current swept it downstream before he could secure it. Without the woodworking tools, the loggers face delays in their timber work.",sp=0},{t="Perils Along the Riverbank",b="Ormin Pelford's lost cargo lies along banks where murlocs and wolves roam. Aggressive murlocs claim the muddy shoals downstream, while predatory wolves prowl the surrounding woods. Ormin cannot face those dangers alone. He needs hardy travelers to search the riverbanks, recover the submerged saw, axe, and toolbox, and bring them back safely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Downstream?",a="Ormin Pelford asks for help near Eastvale Logging Camp. He is a laborer whose supply wagon overturned in the river while he was hauling goods from a trading post.",al={"who gives downstream","downstream quest giver","who is ormin pelford"}},{q="What supplies were lost in the water?",a="Ormin Pelford lost a Waterlogged Axe, a Waterlogged Saw, and a Waterlogged Toolbox. They fell into the river when his wagon tipped over.",al={"what fell in the river","lost supplies downstream","what items downstream"}},{q="Where did the supplies wash up?",a="The crates and tools drifted downstream along the river south of Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"where are the tools","where do supplies wash up","downstream location"}},{q="Why can't Ormin Pelford retrieve the supplies himself?",a="Ormin Pelford cannot face the riverbanks alone, where river murlocs and forest wolves prowl near the cargo.",al={"why can't ormin get supplies","why ormin pelford needs help"}},{q="What dangers lurk along the riverbanks?",a="Aggressive murlocs claim the downstream riverbanks, and wolves prowl nearby. Salvage is dangerous there.",al={"downstream river hazards","threats downstream"}},{q="Why are these tools important to Eastvale?",a="The axes, saws, and toolboxes are essential to the woodsmen at Eastvale Logging Camp. They provide raw timber for Elwynn Forest and Stormwind.",al={"why are tools important eastvale","logging camp timber tools"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Eastvale Logging Camp supplied with tools helps its timber reach Stormwind and Elwynn's settlements."},kw={"downstream","eastvale logging camp","elwynn forest","murloc","ormin pelford","waterlogged axe","waterlogged saw","waterlogged toolbox"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","topic:murloc"},m={id=91733},src={"In-game quest text: Downstream"},fv=true}
E["quest:91736"] = {t="quest",n="Applejack Still",z="general",s="At the Applejack Still, cider becomes a clear, potent spirit. Apple vapor rises as the coils turn it into liquor.",h="At the Applejack Still, cider becomes a clear, potent spirit.",sec={{t="The Distillation Device",b="Fermented cider passes through the still and emerges as strong spirit. Near the apparatus, apple vapor stings the nostrils. Pipes and coils draw the fruit's essence and condense it into liquor.",sp=0},{t="A Clear Pour",b="Alcohol vapor condenses inside the still and becomes a clear spirit. Applejack flows from the outlet into a waiting bottle, ready to drink or store. Even in rough field conditions, the apparatus produces a clear, potent brew.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Applejack Still?",a="The Applejack Still distills fermented apples into applejack, a potent spirit. Coils condense the vapor into clear liquor that pours into a bottle.",al={"what is applejack still","what is this device","what does the still do"}},{q="Why is the apple scent so strong around the still?",a="Concentrated apple vapor gives the still its sharp scent, strong enough to sting the nostrils. The vapor rises as alcohol evaporates and condenses inside the metal coils.",al={"what does it smell like","why does it burn","still scent"}},{q="What kind of liquid does the machine dispense?",a="The still pours a clear spirit into a bottle. This applejack is a potent fruit brandy made by distilling fermented apples.",al={"what liquid comes out","clear liquid still","what does it dispense"}},{q="How does the distillation device operate?",a="The still heats fermented apple cider or wash, separating alcohol vapor from water and fruit solids. Coils condense the vapor, and the spirit collects at the spout before filling a waiting bottle.",al={"how does applejack still work","distillation process"}},{q="What exactly is applejack?",a="Applejack is a strong alcoholic drink made by distilling fermented apple cider. It is clear and aromatic, with more alcohol than ordinary cider or ale.",al={"what is applejack","applejack drink"}},{q="Is operating the still hazardous?",a="The still gives off alcoholic vapors strong enough to sting the nose. It dispenses clear liquor, but high-proof vapor and pressure call for caution.",al={"is the still safe","is it dangerous"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can distill and brew strong spirits from orchard fruit, a craft known among rustic cooks and tavern keepers across Azeroth.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how mechanical condensation and plumbing turn fermented cider into concentrated liquor automatically."},kw={"alcohol","apparatus","applejack","brewing","cider","distillery","liquor","still"},m={id=91736},src={"In-game quest text: Applejack Still"},fv=true}
E["quest:91738"] = {t="quest",n="An Apple Treat",z="general",s="A sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack after months without any. He says it should cheer the troops.",h="A sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack after months without any.",sec={{t="A Welcome Bottle",b="A sergeant recognizes your Thunder Applejack and says the troops will be glad of it. He thanks you for bringing it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the sergeant want?",a="The sergeant welcomes a bottle of Thunder Applejack, which he says should bring the troops some cheer.",al={"what does he need","sergeant applejack","apple treat"}},{q="How long has it been since he saw Thunder Applejack?",a="The sergeant says he has not seen Thunder Applejack in months.",al={"applejack how long","months without it","when last applejack"}},{q="Who is the bottle for?",a="The sergeant says the bottle should put a smile on the troops' faces.",al={"who gets the applejack","applejack for troops","who wants the bottle"}}},kw={"an apple treat","bottle","sergeant","thunder applejack","troops"},m={id=91738},src={"In-game quest text: An Apple Treat"},fv=true}
E["quest:91740"] = {t="quest",n="Croaky's Head",z="general",s="At Ridgepoint Tower, Croaky's death brings grim relief to a grieving Stormwind garrison. The murloc leader terrorized eastern Elwynn's roads. Proof of his death gives the guards hope as they struggle to secure the waterways.",h="At Ridgepoint Tower, Croaky's death brings grim relief to a grieving Stormwind garrison.",sec={{t="Terror on the Eastvale Roads",b="Murlocs along Elwynn Forest's rivers and streams have grown bolder. They ambush travelers and threaten trade routes. Croaky was a particularly aggressive chieftain who rallied other murlocs to attack near local roads. Merchants, farmers, and travelers between Elwynn and Redridge now face deadly roads. Croaky's death ends his ambushes and removes a threat to Stormwind's hold on the eastern woodland outskirts.",sp=0},{t="The Watch at Ridgepoint Tower",b="Ridgepoint Tower guards Elwynn Forest's eastern edge and the strategic crossing into the Redridge Mountains. Officer Merell Ross leads the guards, though dangers around the outpost have stretched them thin. Murloc attacks recently killed two watchmen on patrol.\n\nThe deaths shook the garrison and exposed the vulnerable border. Bringing Croaky's severed head to Ross proves the chieftain is dead. Now the guards have reason to hope they can drive the raiders back from Elwynn's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Croaky?",a="Croaky was a notorious murloc leader who terrorized travelers and patrols along eastern Elwynn Forest's waterways. His particularly aggressive ambushes near roads threatened regional peace until an adventurer hunted him down.",al={"who is croaky","croaky lore","what kind of murloc is croaky"}},{q="Who is Merell Ross?",a="Merell Ross is a member of the Stormwind city watch stationed at Ridgepoint Tower on Elwynn Forest's eastern border. Ross oversees border security and seeks to rally the garrison after murloc raids killed guards. The watch protects the high road into the Redridge Mountains.",al={"merell ross","who is officer ross","ridgepoint tower commander"}},{q="Where is Ridgepoint Tower located?",a="Ridgepoint Tower guards the far eastern edge of Elwynn Forest and the road into the Redridge Mountains. East of the Eastvale Logging Camp, the stone garrison houses Stormwind guards facing hostile creatures and highway bandits.",al={"where is ridgepoint tower","ridgepoint tower location","how to find ridgepoint tower"}},{q="Why did the guards at Ridgepoint Tower want Croaky dead?",a="Murlocs recently killed two Ridgepoint Tower patrol members in the surrounding woods and waters. The guards want Croaky dead to stop the road ambushes and begin a concerted effort to drive the murlocs out of Elwynn.",al={"why kill croaky","why do guards want croakys head","murloc attack on ridgepoint watch"}},{q="What does turning in Croaky's Head accomplish for Elwynn Forest?",a="Bringing Croaky's Head to Ridgepoint Tower proves a dangerous organizer of roadside raids is dead. The guards hope to regain the offensive, secure eastern trade paths, and gradually push murloc tribes from Elwynn's riverbanks.",al={"croakys head purpose","what happens when you kill croaky","turn in croakys head"}},{q="Why are murlocs such a threat along Elwynn's roads?",a="Murlocs commonly nest along Elwynn Forest's rivers, lakes, and streams, and key roads run beside those waterways. Their tribes ambush travelers, trade caravans, and isolated patrols, overwhelming defenders with unpredictable numbers and fierce raids.",al={"why are murlocs attacking roads","elwynn murloc problem","murloc threat in elwynn"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you aid Stormwind's overextended forces by eliminating dangerous leaders who prey on travelers. Securing the eastern border road reinforces Alliance authority between Elwynn and Redridge.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Elwynn, you face murloc incursions that threaten homesteads and claim the lives of local town guardsmen. Slaying Croaky brings justice for two fallen watchmen and defends the realm's heartland.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the brutal reality of frontline combat and the cost paid by fallen watchmen. Felling an aggressive chieftain relieves a hard-pressed defensive line."},kw={"croaky","croaky's head","eastvale","elwynn forest","merell ross","murloc","ridgepoint tower","stormwind guard"},rel={"subzone:ridgepoint-tower","topic:murloc"},m={id=91740},src={"In-game quest text: Croaky's Head"},fv=true}
E["quest:91741"] = {t="quest",n="Nibbled-On Book",z="general",s="In Northshire Valley, Nibbled-On Book has been chewed by kobolds. Brother Paxton hopes to see it returned to Northshire Abbey's modest collection.",h="In Northshire Valley, Nibbled-On Book has been chewed by kobolds.",sec={{t="A Chewed Tome",b="Kobolds in Northshire Valley scavenge what they find left unguarded. You recover a chewed tome from a slain kobold, its cover torn and its parchment marked by teeth. The book came from the library shelves of nearby Northshire Abbey. Valley kobolds have been taking volumes from there.",sp=0},{t="Brother Paxton's Plight",b="Brother Paxton tends the small library inside Northshire Abbey, where the Brotherhood of Northshire reads and studies. Kobolds from the valley slip inside and snatch books from the shelves. Paxton is grateful to have this nibbled volume back. Yet he worries about the rest of his collection still missing in kobold hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Nibbled-On Book?",a="Kobolds stole the volume from Northshire Abbey. Its cover bears tooth marks, as though the scavengers mistook its parchment and leather binding for food.",al={"what is this book","nibbled book lore","what book did the kobold drop"}},{q="Why did the kobolds try to eat the book?",a="The tooth marks suggest the kobolds tried to chew or eat the book. They scavenge what they find, and Brother Paxton says they steal his books to gnaw on them.",al={"why do kobolds want books","why are kobolds eating books","kobold diet books"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey who cares for its modest library. Kobolds sneaking into the abbey and taking books from his shelves distress him.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton northshire","abbey librarian"}},{q="Where did the book originally come from?",a="The book came from the small library Brother Paxton keeps inside Northshire Abbey, in Northshire Valley of Elwynn Forest.",al={"where did the book come from","where does paxton keep books","northshire library"}},{q="Are there other missing books from the abbey's library?",a="Yes. Brother Paxton worries that kobolds have repeatedly stolen from his shelves. He wonders what to do about the rest of his missing collection.",al={"are more books missing","rest of the collection","did kobolds steal more books"}},{q="Who should the book be returned to?",a="Return the recovered book to Brother Paxton inside Northshire Abbey. He inspects its tooth-marked cover and takes it back into his care.",al={"how to get the book back","who wants the nibbled book","return book to paxton"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit in Elwynn Forest, you help secure Northshire Valley by recovering property stolen from Northshire Abbey.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share an interest in Northshire Abbey's library, which preserves clerical and historical knowledge for the kingdom of Stormwind."},kw={"abbey library","brother paxton","elwynn forest","kobold","nibbled-on book","northshire abbey","stolen book"},rel={"topic:kobold","quest:344"},m={id=91741},src={"In-game quest text: Nibbled-On Book"},fv=true}
E["quest:91743"] = {t="quest",n="Rascally Rodents",z="general",s="Kobolds are carrying books away from Brother Paxton’s library in Northshire Valley. He fears they are devouring the abbey’s collection.",h="Kobolds are carrying books away from Brother Paxton’s library in Northshire Valley.",sec={{t="A Threat to the Library",b="Brother Paxton fears the kobolds that have spread from the hills and mines into Northshire Valley’s sacred grounds. He believes they are devouring books from his collection. With the library at risk, he asks young adventurers to hunt the kobolds and recover whatever volumes they can.",sp=0},{t="An Unexplained Appetite",b="Brother Paxton finds that the eight recovered volumes have not been eaten. The kobolds took and hoarded the books for reasons he cannot explain. Many volumes are still missing from the valley, and their strange interest in the books leaves him unsettled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Rascally Rodents?",a="Brother Paxton, a resident of the abbey in Northshire Valley, asks for help protecting its library from the kobolds.",al={"who gives rascally rodents","quest giver rascally rodents","paxton book quest"}},{q="Why are the kobolds stealing books?",a="Brother Paxton thinks the kobolds are eating his books, but the recovered volumes are untouched. Why the kobolds take and hoard them remains unknown.",al={"why kobolds taking books","do kobolds eat books","why do kobolds want books"}},{q="Where do you find the Stolen Books?",a="You find the Stolen Books among the kobolds in Northshire Valley, in their camps and mine workings.",al={"where to find stolen books","stolen books location","kobold books northshire"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton belongs to the Northshire brotherhood and cares deeply for the abbey’s books. He relies on passing initiates to recover them from scavengers.",al={"who is brother paxton","brother paxton lore"}},{q="What does Brother Paxton give you as a reward?",a="When you return eight stolen volumes, Brother Paxton gives you one of his how-to books, which he says he does not need. Many volumes remain missing.",al={"what reward paxton gives","how to book reward"}},{q="Are all the stolen books recovered?",a="No. Brother Paxton says many volumes are still missing from the valley, and the kobolds’ interest in them remains unexplained.",al={"are all books recovered","are all books saved"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human initiate training in Northshire Valley, you help defend the abbey’s treasures and books from pests and invaders.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest aiding the Abbey of Northshire, you help protect the Holy Light’s scholars and their books from destruction.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know written knowledge is precious, even when kobolds threaten it."},kw={"brother paxton","kobolds","library","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rascally rodents","stolen books"},rel={"quest:344","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:kobold"},m={id=91743},src={"In-game quest text: Rascally Rodents"},fv=true}
E["quest:91745"] = {t="quest",n="Mining Consultant",z="general",s="At Echo Ridge Mine, Kelsey Fargo watches the kobolds from her post outside the entrance. Their strange movements have drawn local attention.",h="At Echo Ridge Mine, Kelsey Fargo watches the kobolds from her post outside the entrance.",sec={{t="Trouble at the Mine",b="Kobold trouble at Echo Ridge Mine has taken an odd turn. The creatures defend their underground claims and gather candles, but now their coordinated disturbances have caught the authorities’ attention. You are sent to Kelsey Fargo, a mining apprentice stationed near the entrance. From her post outside the tunnels, she has watched the kobolds closely.",sp=0},{t="Scholarly Scavengers",b="Kelsey Fargo has seen kobolds scampering back and forth with heavy books and arguing as they go. She believes they stole the volumes from the library inside Northshire Abbey. What the tunnel dwellers want with books they cannot read remains unclear.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kelsey Fargo?",a="Kelsey Fargo is a mining apprentice stationed just outside Echo Ridge Mine in Northshire Valley. From her post, she can watch the local kobolds’ movements and habits.",al={"who is kelsey fargo","kelsey fargo role","mining apprentice northshire"}},{q="Why are kobolds carrying books?",a="Kelsey Fargo has seen kobolds running back and forth with books while arguing. She suspects they stole the volumes from the library inside Northshire Abbey, but their purpose is unknown.",al={"why are kobolds stealing books","kobolds reading","books in echo ridge mine"}},{q="Where is Echo Ridge Mine?",a="Echo Ridge Mine lies in the hills northwest of Northshire Abbey, in northwestern Northshire Valley. Kobolds have heavily infested it and disrupted mining operations.",al={"where is echo ridge mine","echo ridge mine location"}},{q="Where are the kobolds getting these books?",a="The books are believed to have come from the library inside Northshire Abbey. Local human clergy and scholars keep records, scriptures, and historical volumes there.",al={"where do the books come from","abbey library kobolds"}},{q="What is the purpose of consulting the mining apprentice?",a="You are sent to speak with Kelsey Fargo outside the mine about the strange kobold activity. From her post, she can tell you what she has witnessed.",al={"mining consultant quest purpose","why talk to kelsey"}},{q="What strange behavior have the kobolds exhibited?",a="Kobolds around Echo Ridge Mine have been seen yelling at one another and carrying off written texts. Their behavior is unusually erratic compared with their usual digging and defense of their territory.",al={"what are the kobolds doing","kobold behavior northshire"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can speak with Kelsey Fargo, an apprentice stationed just outside Echo Ridge Mine. She is a local contact for learning about mineral work and conditions nearby.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you begin in Northshire Valley, a training ground for new adventurers. The abbey’s archives and nearby mines matter to the region, and kobolds threaten them both."},kw={"echo ridge mine","kelsey fargo","kobold","library","mining","mining consultant","northshire abbey","northshire valley"},rel={"subzone:echo-ridge-mine","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:kobold"},m={id=91745},src={"In-game quest text: Mining Consultant"},fv=true}
E["quest:91746"] = {t="quest",n="Elmpaw's Head",z="general",s="At Elmpaw's Head, the hunt is over, and a wealthy collector awaits its prize. The beast’s head goes to a handler who prepares and mounts trophies for affluent patrons.",h="At Elmpaw's Head, the hunt is over, and a wealthy collector awaits its prize.",sec={{t="The Fallen Beast",b="Elmpaw has fallen, and hunters prize the beast’s head as proof of victory. Trackers regard the hunt as an impressive feat, a hard-won end to the chase.",sp=0},{t="A Collector's Prize",b="A handler rewards you for Elmpaw’s severed head. Then the handler prepares and mounts it for wealthy patrons who want fierce wild trophies on their mantles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who or what is Elmpaw?",a="Elmpaw is a formidable creature, and hunters regard bringing it down as an impressive feat. Its head proves the victory.",al={"who is elmpaw","what is elmpaw","elmpaw boss"}},{q="Why does the quest giver want Elmpaw's head?",a="The handler wants Elmpaw’s head to prepare and mount as a trophy for wealthy collectors who display such prizes on their mantles.",al={"why want head","elmpaw head turn in","what is trophy for"}},{q="Who are the collectors interested in the trophy?",a="The collectors are wealthy patrons who value exotic beast trophies for their homes. Once mounted, Elmpaw’s head can fetch a high price.",al={"who buys trophy","elmpaw buyers","who wants elmpaw head"}},{q="Is Elmpaw a dangerous target?",a="Elmpaw is a notable challenge, and hunters regard bringing the beast down as an impressive feat.",al={"how hard is elmpaw","is elmpaw tough"}},{q="What kind of task is Elmpaw's Head?",a="You hunt Elmpaw in the wild and bring its head to an interested handler. The handler rewards you and prepares the trophy for sale.",al={"is elmpaw head a bounty","who posted elmpaw quest"}},{q="Where can Elmpaw be found?",a="Elmpaw roams wilderness where hunters encounter dangerous beasts. After the hunt, bring its head back to the handler.",al={"elmpaw location","where to find elmpaw"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the skill it takes to bring down a formidable beast like Elmpaw and claim its trophy."},kw={"beast","collector","elmpaw","head","hunter","mantle","trophy"},m={id=91746},src={"In-game quest text: Elmpaw's Head"},fv=true}
E["quest:91751"] = {t="quest",n="Rough Wolf Pelts",z="general",s="Near Goldshire, Rough Wolf Pelts are needed for Helene Peltskinner's leather orders. Her husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey, so she asks for help skinning local wolves.",h="Near Goldshire, Rough Wolf Pelts are needed for Helene Peltskinner's leather orders.",sec={{t="A Skinner's Need",b="Just outside Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner supplies travelers and residents with cured leather and furs. Her husband usually hunts Elwynn Forest's timber wolves for her. Now his duties near Northshire Abbey keep him away, while customer orders wait. So Helene asks passing apprentices to skin the local wolves.",sp=0},{t="Prowlers of the Forest",b="Timber wolves prowl Elwynn Forest's woodlands, farmlands, and roads. Skinning them gives novice skinners practice harvesting hides. Their pelts help Helene continue her leatherwork and keep trade moving through Goldshire. Hunters, too, sharpen their woodcraft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Helene Peltskinner?",a="Helene Peltskinner is a skinner and leatherworker based just outside Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. She prepares hides and fills craft orders for travelers and locals. Her husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey, so she needs help gathering wolf hides for her work.",al={"who is helene peltskinner","helene peltskinner","who gives rough wolf pelts"}},{q="Why does Helene need wolf pelts?",a="Helene needs wolf pelts to fill her backlog of leather orders near Goldshire. Her husband usually hunts wolves for her work, but his duties elsewhere in Elwynn leave her short on hides. Passing travelers can help by skinning local wolves.",al={"why need rough wolf pelts","why collect pelts","what does helene do with pelts"}},{q="Where is Helene's husband?",a="Helene's husband is occupied near Northshire Abbey. He usually hunts wolves and gathers skins for her, so his absence leaves Helene needing help to keep up with her orders.",al={"where is helene husband","helene husband","who is helene husband"}},{q="Where are the wolves found in Elwynn Forest?",a="Timber wolves roam Elwynn Forest's woodlands around Goldshire and Northshire. Skinners harvest their pelts and bring them to Helene's leatherworking post.",al={"where to find rough wolf pelts","which wolves drop pelts","wolf locations elwynn"}},{q="Is skinning required to harvest these pelts?",a="Yes. Helene offers travelers practice in skinning, and the pelts come from skinning slain wolves. Hunting them alone does not provide the hides she needs.",al={"do i need skinning for rough wolf pelts","rough wolf pelts skinning requirement","skinning quest goldshire"}},{q="Where can Helene Peltskinner be found?",a="Helene Peltskinner works near Goldshire, the central settlement of Elwynn Forest. Her work is close to the township, where hunters and travelers on the King's Road can bring her hides from the forest.",al={"where is helene peltskinner located","helene peltskinner location","where to find helene"}}},kw={"elwynn forest","goldshire","helene peltskinner","leatherworking","pelts","rough wolf pelts","skinning","timber wolves"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn"},m={id=91751},src={"In-game quest text: Rough Wolf Pelts"},fv=true}
E["quest:91752"] = {t="quest",n="The Big Picture",z="general",s="In Northshire Valley, kobolds carry stolen illustrated books into the mine for Shinyfinder Narf. The volumes are to be returned to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey.",h="In Northshire Valley, kobolds carry stolen illustrated books into the mine for Shinyfinder Narf.",sec={{t="The Kobold Book Thief",b="Kobolds in Northshire Valley have been seen fleeing with books and crying, “Picture for Narf!” Most gather candles and shiny trinkets, but Shinyfinder Narf seeks illustrated tomes. He has collected a sack of them in his hideout beneath the mine.",sp=0},{t="Recovering the Abbey's Tomes",b="The deeper shafts hold tougher, meaner kobolds who guard Narf and his strange hoard. To recover the stolen books, you face those darker tunnels and confront him. Then the sack goes to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey, who sees that the valuable volumes return to Brother Paxton.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Shinyfinder Narf?",a="Shinyfinder Narf leads kobolds deep in the mine near Northshire Valley. He hoards stolen books and calls for picture books, so local authorities have ordered his cache recovered.",al={"who is narf","shinyfinder narf lore","narf kobold"}},{q="Why are the kobolds stealing books?",a="Kobolds from the mine have been seen shouting, “Picture for Narf!” as they snatch books. Narf seeks illustrated works and keeps them in a sack deep in the tunnels.",al={"why do kobolds want picture books","what is picture for narf","why books stolen"}},{q="Whose books were stolen?",a="The stolen books belong to Brother Paxton, who lives at Northshire Abbey. Marshal McBride receives the recovered sack and arranges for the books to return to Brother Paxton's collection.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton books"}},{q="Who is Marshal McBride?",a="Marshal McBride is the law enforcement officer stationed just inside Northshire Abbey. He keeps order, protects the abbey grounds and organizes defense against the local kobolds.",al={"who is marshal mcbride","where is mcbride"}},{q="Where can Shinyfinder Narf be found?",a="Shinyfinder Narf lives in the deeper, more dangerous reaches of the mine in Northshire Valley. Meaner kobolds surround him and guard his hoard.",al={"where is narf","where to find narf","mine location"}},{q="How dangerous is the mine where Narf lives?",a="The kobolds deeper in the mine with Narf are meaner and more hostile than the common scavengers outside. Narf and his den are dangerous for anyone traveling alone.",al={"is narf dangerous","can you solo narf"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you help keep Northshire Valley peaceful and recover stolen goods from the encroaching vermin.",["race:Human"]="As a human adventurer, you begin your service at Northshire Abbey, protecting Stormwind's outlying territories."},kw={"brother paxton","kobold","marshal mcbride","narf","northshire abbey","picture books","shinyfinder narf","the big picture"},rel={"npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:344","topic:kobold"},m={id=91752},src={"In-game quest text: The Big Picture"},fv=true}
E["quest:91753"] = {t="quest",n="An Enchanting Lesson",z="general",s="At the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, Kitta Firewind gives An Enchanting Lesson to apprentice enchanters. Kobold geomancers bind simple magic into crude wax effigies, showing why practice matters alongside arcane theory.",h="At the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, Kitta Firewind gives An Enchanting Lesson to apprentice enchanters.",sec={{t="Theory and Practice",b="Kitta Firewind, an enchanter at the Tower of Azora, challenges apprentice enchanters to look beyond polished libraries. She asks them to examine magic where it appears naturally. Even the uneducated kobolds beneath Elwynn Forest channel cantrips into everyday talismans, proof that magical instinct can thrive without formal schooling.",sp=0},{t="Primitive Cantrips",b="Kobold geomancers shape Crude Wax Effigies with simple folk enchantments. Students obtain the effigies and carefully unravel their bound magic through disenchantment, extracting Luminous Residue. By taking these primitive charms apart, they learn how raw magic behaves in the field. Enchantment's fundamental threads are found through observation as well as in grimoires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest An Enchanting Lesson?",a="Kitta Firewind, an enchanter at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, offers this lesson to adventurers. She teaches that scholarly theory and hands-on practice belong together.",al={"who gives an enchanting lesson","quest giver enchanting lesson","kitta firewind quest"}},{q="Where is the Tower of Azora located?",a="The Tower of Azora stands in eastern Elwynn Forest. It is a bastion of magical study and wizardry amid the farmlands and woods of the human kingdom.",al={"where is tower of azora","tower of azora location"}},{q="How do kobolds know how to use magic?",a="Kobolds have no formal schooling or scholarly traditions, yet geomancers have an instinctive knack for binding basic cantrips and enchantments into crude wax effigies.",al={"can kobolds do magic","kobold geomancers magic","do kobolds have enchantments"}},{q="What are the wax effigies used for?",a="Crude Wax Effigies are primitive items fashioned by kobold geomancers. Though unsophisticated, they hold bound magic that can be unraveled and studied through disenchanting.",al={"what are wax effigies","crude wax effigies","kobold wax magic"}},{q="What is Luminous Residue?",a="Luminous Residue is the essence obtained by deconstructing and disenchanting the crude wax effigies carried by kobold geomancers. It is tangible proof of their innate cantrips.",al={"what is luminous residue","how to get luminous residue"}},{q="What is the main takeaway of Kitta Firewind's lesson?",a="Kitta Firewind teaches that theoretical knowledge and practical experimentation are inseparable. She urges students to study practical magic wherever it appears.",al={"lesson of the quest","what does kitta firewind teach"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Scholarly mages often scoff at subterranean vermin, yet Kitta Firewind reminds them that even primitive creatures can reveal unexpected truths about raw magical currents.",["faction:Alliance"]="Studying at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest gives Alliance adventurers insight into academic wizardry and the surprisingly magical pests infesting their lands."},kw={"an enchanting lesson","disenchanting","elwynn forest","kitta firewind","kobold geomancer","luminous residue","tower of azora","wax effigy"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-azora","topic:kobold"},m={id=91753},src={"In-game quest text: An Enchanting Lesson"},fv=true}
E["quest:91758"] = {t="quest",n="Follow That Kobold!",z="general",s="A kobold has fled Northshire's mines with Brother Paxton's books, and the abbey calls on Tordrin Sternblade to track it. Follow That Kobold! begins with a theft from the local mines.",h="A kobold has fled Northshire's mines with Brother Paxton's books, and the abbey calls on Tordrin Sternblade...",sec={{t="The Book Thief of Northshire",b="Kelsey saw a kobold flee the Northshire Abbey mine tunnels with a heavy sack of books. The workers and clerics thought the vermin in the mines were under control. The books belong to Brother Paxton, who needs them back in the abbey's collection.",sp=0},{t="Calling in the Mountaineer",b="The kobold is a nimble scavenger from below ground. Tracking it through Northshire Abbey's wooded grounds calls for special skill. You are sent behind the abbey to the stables, where Tordrin Sternblade can be found. The dwarven Hunter trainer has newly arrived from Ironforge, and his wilderness knowledge can help pick up the kobold's scent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Follow That Kobold! about?",a="A kobold fled Northshire Valley's mine with a heavy sack of Brother Paxton's stolen books. The abbey wants them returned.",al={"what is follow that kobold","quest follow that kobold"}},{q="Who is Tordrin Sternblade?",a="Tordrin Sternblade is a dwarven Hunter trainer newly arrived from Ironforge. He is behind Northshire Abbey near the stables, where his tracking skill can help recover the books.",al={"who is tordrin sternblade","where is tordrin","hunter trainer northshire"}},{q="What did the kobold steal?",a="Kelsey reports that a kobold slipped out of the Northshire mine tunnels with a large sack of books. The human tomes belong to Brother Paxton, and the abbey needs them returned.",al={"why did kobold steal books","what did kobold take","sack of books"}},{q="Who reported the theft?",a="Kelsey Fargo, the new mining apprentice who works right outside the Northshire mine, reported the theft. She noticed a kobold leaving the tunnels with a sack stuffed with books.",al={"who is kelsey","kelsey northshire"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey. The stolen library materials belong to him or his sacred duties, so the abbey calls for an experienced tracker to recover them.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton books"}},{q="How do you track the thieving kobold?",a="You are warned against charging blindly into the woods and sent to consult Tordrin Sternblade behind the abbey. His wilderness knowledge can help you track the thief.",al={"how do i track the kobold","tracking the thief"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you meet Tordrin Sternblade, a veteran Hunter trainer newly arrived from Ironforge to assist Northshire Abbey.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you bring traditional dwarven tracking expertise from Ironforge to help the humans of Northshire.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Stormwind's holy abbey and an Ironforge mountaineer support one another."},kw={"brother paxton","follow that kobold","hunter trainer","ironforge","kelsey","kobold","northshire","tordrin sternblade"},rel={"topic:hunter","topic:kobold","zone:ironforge","quest:344"},m={id=91758},src={"In-game quest text: Follow That Kobold!"},fv=true}
E["quest:91772"] = {t="quest",n="Shhh! We're Hunting Kobolds",z="general",s="Kobolds are moving from Northshire Valley toward Elwynn Forest. You follow their trail with a tracking kit and report what you find to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.",h="Kobolds are moving from Northshire Valley toward Elwynn Forest.",sec={{t="Tracking the Vermin",b="Kobolds have spread beyond Northshire Valley and the abbey grounds. With a tracking kit, you follow their trail to learn where they gather. Your report will help Goldshire prepare for threats across Elwynn Forest.",sp=0},{t="The Fargodeep Connection",b="The tracks run southwest from Northshire and across Elwynn Forest toward Fargodeep Mine. Marshal Dughan commands Goldshire's garrison and already knows the mine is heavily infested with kobolds. Your report confirms the threat, and the mine remains overrun.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this task?",a="You follow kobolds moving beyond Northshire Valley with a tracking kit. Find where they are gathering, then report what you find to the Stormwind authorities in Goldshire.",al={"quest purpose","what is this quest","why hunt kobolds"}},{q="Who is concerned about the kobold movements?",a="Marshal McBride, commander of Northshire Valley, is concerned about the kobolds' movements. A local guide gives you a tracking kit so you can follow their trail out of the valley and into Elwynn Forest.",al={"who gives tracking kit","who is concerned about kobolds"}},{q="Where do the kobold tracks lead?",a="The tracks lead out of Northshire toward Fargodeep Mine in central Elwynn Forest. Kobolds have gathered there in force.",al={"where do tracks go","kobold destination","where are kobolds heading"}},{q="Who is Marshal Dughan?",a="Marshal Dughan commands the Stormwind guard garrison in Goldshire. He coordinates Elwynn Forest's local defenses and receives reports of threats moving into the region.",al={"who is marshal dughan","where is dughan","report to dughan"}},{q="Why are the kobolds heading to Fargodeep Mine?",a="Fargodeep Mine is already infested with kobolds. More of them heading there means greater danger for local workers and nearby settlements.",al={"why fargodeep mine","fargodeep kobolds"}},{q="What happens once you reach Goldshire?",a="When you report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, he confirms that kobolds infest Fargodeep Mine. He is not surprised and prepares to recruit fighters to confront them.",al={"what happens after reporting","dughan reaction"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer leaving Northshire, you help protect Elwynn's supply lines and settlements. Goldshire's garrison needs to know when threats gather.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know a tracking kit can help you follow vermin trails through the woods."},kw={"elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","goldshire","kobold tracking kit","kobolds","marshal dughan","marshal mcbride","northshire","shhh we're hunting kobolds"},rel={"subzone:fargodeep-mine","quest:62","npc:marshal-dughan","subzone:goldshire","npc:marshal-mcbride","topic:kobold"},m={id=91772},src={"In-game quest text: Shhh! We're Hunting Kobolds"},fv=true}
E["quest:91775"] = {t="quest",n="Book Return",z="general",s="In Elwynn, Marshal Dughan sends you to Fargodeep Mine for Brother Paxton’s lost books. One volume, “Fun with Elementals,” could place dangerous instructions in kobold hands.",h="In Elwynn, Marshal Dughan sends you to Fargodeep Mine for Brother Paxton’s lost books.",sec={{t="Lost Pages in the Dark",b="Marshal Dughan sends you into Fargodeep Mine for books belonging to Brother Paxton of Northshire Abbey. Kobolds have overrun the mine, and Paxton fears they might read “Fun with Elementals.” Its simple instructions could teach them to summon an elemental in the tunnels.",sp=0},{t="Knowledge in Peril",b="Fargodeep Mine once brought gold to the kingdom of Stormwind. Now kobolds overrun its lower levels, while Elwynn’s defenders are stretched thin. The damp, dangerous caverns threaten the books. You carry the recovered volumes in a protective book bag, keeping Paxton’s records safe and arcane lessons beyond the kobolds’ reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Book Return?",a="Marshal Dughan in Goldshire sends you into Fargodeep Mine for books belonging to Brother Paxton. One is “Fun with Elementals,” a magical primer Paxton is especially anxious to recover.",al={"what is book return","book return quest","who gives book return"}},{q="Why are Brother Paxton's books inside Fargodeep Mine?",a="Kobolds who stole Brother Paxton’s books from Northshire were tracked to Fargodeep Mine. Kobolds now overrun its tunnels, and Paxton wants the books gathered before they are ruined or misused.",al={"why paxton books in mine","how did books get into fargodeep","why are books in fargodeep mine"}},{q="What is the book 'Fun with Elementals'?",a="“Fun with Elementals” is an introductory book about conjuring that Brother Paxton is desperate to recover. He fears its simple instructions could let even a kobold summon an elemental servant deep in the mine.",al={"fun with elementals","what is fun with elementals","paxton elemental book"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey devoted to study, records, and literature. Some books he has lost contain potent, basic magic.",al={"who is brother paxton","paxton lore","librarian paxton"}},{q="Why is Marshal Dughan involved in retrieving books?",a="Marshal Dughan oversees Elwynn Forest’s defense from Goldshire. As he sends you to investigate kobolds in Fargodeep Mine, he also seeks to help Brother Paxton recover his books before the kobolds become a greater magical threat.",al={"why dughan care about books","marshal dughan books"}},{q="Could a kobold really summon an elemental?",a="Brother Paxton fears a simple guide could teach the kobolds to conjure elemental forces. Their growing presence in the mine already threatens Elwynn.",al={"can kobolds use magic","can kobolds summon elementals"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know careless handling of arcane books like “Fun with Elementals” can put dangerous knowledge within reach of kobolds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Northshire Abbey and Goldshire’s garrison working together to protect books and dangerous magical texts from Elwynn’s pests."},kw={"book return","brother paxton","elwynn forest","fargodeep mine","fun with elementals","goldshire","kobold","marshal dughan"},rel={"quest:62","quest:344","subzone:fargodeep-mine","npc:marshal-dughan","topic:kobold"},m={id=91775},src={"In-game quest text: Book Return"},fv=true}
E["quest:91777"] = {t="quest",n="Rare Books",z="general",s="In Northshire Valley, Rare Books sends you after two primers taken by kobolds. Brother Paxton needs them back at Northshire Abbey.",h="In Northshire Valley, Rare Books sends you after two primers taken by kobolds.",sec={{t="Missing from the Abbey",b="Brother Paxton has lost two books from the library at Northshire Abbey. Kobolds carrying books and other things have taken them into Jasperlode Mine. The missing volumes are Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards and Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words. Both are primers on magic.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Kobolds in Jasperlode",b="Kobolds in Jasperlode Mine are studying the stolen books. An apprentice has already tried to summon an elemental. No one knows what a more practiced geomancer might call forth from those lessons.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Rare Books?",a="You are asked to recover the last two books missing from Brother Paxton's catalog. Kobolds have taken them into Jasperlode Mine.",al={"rare books quest","what is rare books","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is Brother Paxton?",a="Brother Paxton is a cleric at Northshire Abbey who cares for its books and documents. Kobolds have taken volumes from the library, and he needs them returned.",al={"who is paxton","brother paxton lore","abbey librarian"}},{q="Which books need to be recovered?",a="The missing books are Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards and Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words. Both introduce arcane and magical theory.",al={"which books are missing","stolen book titles","missing library books"}},{q="Where are the missing books located?",a="The missing books are in Jasperlode Mine in Northshire Valley. Kobold diggers and geomancers occupy the gold mine.",al={"where are the books","book locations","where to find the books"}},{q="Why did the kobolds take books on magic?",a="Kobolds in Jasperlode Mine appear to be using the books to study geomancy and spellcasting. An apprentice has tried to summon an elemental.",al={"why do kobolds have books","can kobolds read","kobold wizards"}},{q="Why does Brother Paxton reward weapons intended for the militia?",a="Brother Paxton gives helpers spare weapons set aside for the Northshire militia. He believes adventurers facing threats in the valley can put them to better use.",al={"paxton reward weapons","why militia weapons","abbey weapons"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize the basic principles in these primers. Their lessons have reached kobolds beneath the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help recover books stolen from Northshire Abbey and aid the local militia."},kw={"arcane explainer","brother paxton","geomancy","jasperlode mine","kobold","northshire abbey","northshire valley","rare books"},rel={"subzone:jasperlode-mine","quest:344","quest:76","topic:kobold"},m={id=91777},src={"In-game quest text: Rare Books"},fv=true}
E["quest:91858"] = {t="quest",n="Diplomatic Incident",z="general",s="Two Earthen Ring dignitaries have gone missing in Silverpine Forest while traveling to Tarren Mill. Danitha sends you to Trevan Rol at the Sepulcher to learn more and help secure the Horde’s legitimacy.",h="Two Earthen Ring dignitaries have gone missing in Silverpine Forest while traveling to Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="Missing Travelers",b="Danitha sends you to Trevan Rol at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Two Earthen Ring dignitaries vanished while traveling toward Tarren Mill, and little is known beyond rumors of a diplomatic incident. Their recovery could help the Horde gain legitimacy. Trevan says you have walked into a serious mess.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who went missing in Silverpine?",a="Two dignitaries from the Earthen Ring went missing in Silverpine Forest while traveling to Tarren Mill.",al={"missing dignitaries","earthen ring travelers","who disappeared"}},{q="Where do I go for information?",a="Danitha sends you to speak with Trevan Rol at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is trevan rol","find trevan","sepulcher"}},{q="Why does Danitha want the travelers found?",a="Recovering the missing Earthen Ring dignitaries could help the Horde gain legitimacy.",al={"why find them","horde legitimacy","diplomatic incident"}},{q="What happened to the dignitaries?",a="They went missing in Silverpine Forest while traveling toward Tarren Mill. Their whereabouts are unknown.",al={"what happened in silverpine","why are they missing","dignitaries whereabouts"}}},kw={"danitha","dignitaries","diplomatic incident","earthen ring","horde","missing travelers","sepulcher","silverpine forest","tarren mill","trevan rol"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:horde","quest:95349"},m={id=91858},src={"In-game quest text: Diplomatic Incident"},fv=true}
E["quest:91860"] = {t="quest",n="A Grim Fate",z="general",s="A patrol sighting on Fenris Isle raises concern for an elf and an Earthen Ring traveling party. You are asked to investigate the party’s fate.",h="A patrol sighting on Fenris Isle raises concern for an elf and an Earthen Ring traveling party.",sec={{t="A Pyre on the Shore",b="A patrolman saw gnolls place a large body on a pyre along Fenris Isle’s shore. He saw no elf or smaller bodies, and fears for the traveling party. You are asked to search the isle and learn what became of them.",sp=0},{t="The Body",b="On Fenris Isle, the body is Tauren, and it has been heavily gnawed. The elf woman is nowhere in sight. She may still be deeper in the nearby fortress, so her fate remains uncertain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What did the patrolman see?",a="A patrolman saw gnolls placing a large body on a pyre on Fenris Isle’s shore.",al={"patrol sighting","gnolls and a pyre","what was on the shore"}},{q="Who is the traveling party?",a="The party is described as an Earthen Ring traveling party.",al={"earthen ring party","who was traveling","traveling group"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Fenris Isle?",a="You are asked to investigate Fenris Isle and learn the fate of the Earthen Ring traveling party.",al={"why fenris isle","what am i looking for","a grim fate quest"}},{q="Was the elf seen on the shore?",a="The patrolman saw no elf among those at the pyre.",al={"where is the elf","elf on fenris","did they see her"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, the patrolman appeals to your sense of oaths, though he doubts this search is worth the danger."},kw={"a grim fate","earthen ring","elf","fenris isle","gnolls","pyre","tauren","traveling party"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","topic:gnoll","topic:tauren","quest:95349"},m={id=91860},src={"In-game quest text: A Grim Fate"},fv=true}
E["quest:91861"] = {t="quest",n="Into Fenris Keep",z="general",s="A lone body leaves hope that a missing member of the Earthen Ring party may still be alive. You are asked to search Fenris Keep for the captive.",h="A lone body leaves hope that a missing member of the Earthen Ring party may still be alive.",sec={{t="A Search in Fenris Keep",b="A member of the Earthen Ring party is missing, and you are asked to search Fenris Keep for them. Trevan and Hadrec described a High Elf inside the nearby fortress. Since only one body was found, there is hope the missing party member is still alive.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Help",b="Inside Fenris Keep, you find the missing High Elf asking a Forsaken for help to escape. Time is short for the captive.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who am I looking for in Fenris Keep?",a="You are searching for a missing member of the Earthen Ring party, described by Trevan and Hadrec as a High Elf.",al={"missing person fenris","who is missing","earthen ring party"}},{q="Why is there hope the missing person is alive?",a="Only one body was found, leaving hope that the missing High Elf is still inside Fenris Keep.",al={"only one body","is the elf alive","fenris keep body"}},{q="Who asks me to search Fenris Keep?",a="The request is to investigate Fenris Keep and try to locate the missing member of the Earthen Ring party.",al={"who sent me","who wants me to search","fenris keep request"}},{q="What does the captive ask for?",a="The captive asks a Forsaken for help to get free, saying time is short.",al={"free me","help captive","what does the elf want"},sp=1}},kw={"captive","earthen ring","fenris keep","hadrec","high elf","into fenris keep","missing member","trevan"},rel={"subzone:fenris-keep","topic:forsaken","quest:95349"},m={id=91861},src={"In-game quest text: Into Fenris Keep"},fv=true}
E["quest:91899"] = {t="quest",n="A Sealed Crate",z="general",s="Trade handlers seek lost cargo as bandits disrupt the roads. You can recover sealed crates from the wilderness and outlaw camps to help keep supplies moving.",h="Trade handlers seek lost cargo as bandits disrupt the roads.",sec={{t="Endangered Trade Routes",b="Highway crime has risen of late. Organized bandits and rogue thieves prey on trade routes, ambushing wagons, pack trains, and lone couriers. Their cargo is scattered across wilderness roads or carried off to outlaw camps. These raids threaten the supply lines between settlements.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming Lost Cargo",b="Traders and cargo handlers rely on independent adventurers to recover lost freight and keep supplies moving. Sealed crates rescued from bandits or found abandoned in the brush can be brought to trade handlers. There, the goods help secure supplies, curb illicit trade, and restore safety to regional commerce.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is A Sealed Crate?",a="A Sealed Crate holds lost or intercepted merchant goods recovered from wilderness routes. Handing it in keeps cargo from thieves and helps restore secure commerce.",al={"sealed crate quest","what is a sealed crate","crate turn in"}},{q="Why are trade routes being raided by bandits?",a="Bandits and outlaws have recently made travel dangerous on roads and trade routes. They target caravans and couriers, leaving cargo scattered in the wilds.",al={"why are bandits stealing crates","trade route bandits","who is attacking caravans"}},{q="Who collects these recovered crates?",a="Trade handlers and quartermasters accept recovered crates to catalog merchant property and build stockpiles safe from roaming thieves. They compensate adventurers and scavengers who retrieve them.",al={"who takes the sealed crates","where do sealed crates go","crate delivery"}},{q="Can you bring in multiple sealed crates?",a="Yes. Trade handlers encourage travelers to bring in any additional crates found on roads or in the wilds while bandits continue to disrupt deliveries.",al={"can you repeat sealed crate","more crates","are there more crates"}},{q="What is inside a sealed crate?",a="The crates hold recovered trade supplies and commercial cargo intercepted in transit. The courier delivering one has not opened it; it returns to trade stockpiles to limit losses to highwaymen.",al={"whats inside sealed crate","inside a sealed crate","what is in the crates"}},{q="Where do these recovered crates come from?",a="Crates may be found abandoned along dangerous trade routes, near bandit camps, or taken from outlaws who intercepted shipments.",al={"where to find sealed crates","how to get sealed crates","bandit crates"}}},kw={"bandits","caravan","cargo","delivery","sealed crate","supplies","thieves","trade routes"},m={id=91899},src={"In-game quest text: A Sealed Crate"},fv=true}
E["quest:91900"] = {t="quest",n="A Sealed Crate",z="general",s="Bandits and thieves are raiding the roads, and lost shipments lie scattered across the wilds. Local merchants will pay you to bring a sealed crate back.",h="Bandits and thieves are raiding the roads, and lost shipments lie scattered across the wilds.",sec={{t="Disrupted Trade Routes",b="Caravans and couriers now face ambushes along the old trade highways. Many leave wagons and crates behind when they flee, and the goods sit in the brush until someone finds them. Merchants and depot keepers depend on travelers to bring that cargo home.",sp=0},{t="Cargo Recovery",b="Carry a sealed crate to a receiving depot and you earn a bounty on the spot. Handlers sort the freight and send it on its way, so commerce keeps moving despite the brigands. While the roads stay contested, lost cargo remains steady work for any traveler passing through.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside a sealed crate?",a="The crate contains recovered trade goods that were intercepted or lost along trade routes. Merchants and recipients pay couriers and adventurers to retrieve and return them unopened rather than letting the contents fall into criminal hands.",al={"what is in the crate","crate contents","whats inside a sealed crate"}},{q="Why are people asking for sealed crates to be delivered?",a="A recent uprising of bandits and thieves has disrupted active trade routes, leaving cargo scattered or stolen. Traders and local organizers offer bounties and compensation for anyone willing to recover and return these lost shipments.",al={"why return crates","who wants sealed crates","crate delivery reason"}},{q="Can you turn in multiple sealed crates?",a="Yes. Due to ongoing bandit raids on commercial routes, abandoned and stolen crates continue to turn up across troubled paths. Couriers are encouraged to bring any additional crates they discover back for further compensation.",al={"can i find more crates","where to get crates","more sealed crates"}},{q="Who is intercepting the trade routes?",a="Local thieves and bandits have increasingly targeted transport routes, ambushing caravans and intercepting commerce. While many different rogue outfits operate across the region, their common effect is leaving shipments discarded or seized along roads.",al={"who stole the crates","bandit uprising trade routes","who is attacking shipments"}},{q="Can you open a sealed crate yourself?",a="Whether you can open the crate yourself is unclear. Return recovered crates to the recipient to receive payment for the delivery.",al={"can i open the crate","open sealed crate","why keep crate sealed"}},{q="Who pays for recovering these shipments?",a="Local trade handlers and depot keepers receive the recovered cargo and provide compensation on the spot, managing the inventory and directing further retrieval efforts.",al={"who pays for the crates","who gives crate reward","crate compensation"}}},kw={"bandits","cargo","compensation","delivery","sealed crate","shipment","thieves","trade routes"},m={id=91900},src={"In-game quest text: A Sealed Crate"},fv=true}
E["quest:91904"] = {t="quest",n="A Sealed Crate",z="general",s="Trade caravans lose sealed crates to thieves along the roads. Merchants seek the missing goods and pay to have them returned, restoring regional supplies.",h="Trade caravans lose sealed crates to thieves along the roads.",sec={{t="Stolen Cargo and Imperiled Roads",b="Bandits and thieves strike trade caravans on roads and shipping lanes. Haulers and couriers can lose their shipments in an ambush, leaving sealed crates beside wild roads and paths until someone finds them.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Supply Chain",b="Merchants and supply coordinators pay for merchandise returned safely. Bring recovered crates to regional collection points, and the goods can flow through disrupted supply lines again. You are paid for protecting trade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a sealed crate?",a="Sealed crates hold cargo intercepted or lost along commercial routes. Return recovered goods to merchants and local recipients to restore freight and earn payment.",al={"sealed crate purpose","what is a sealed crate","what are sealed crates for"}},{q="Why are these crates lying around?",a="Banditry and organized theft have surged along regional trade routes. Highwaymen ambush caravans and haulers, leaving stolen or abandoned shipments along the road.",al={"who lost the crates","why are crates lost","why crates on the road"}},{q="Who wants these crates returned?",a="Caravan coordinators, quartermasters, and merchants accept recovered crates. They gather and sort the cargo back into regular supply lines, then pay those who recover their missing goods.",al={"who buys sealed crates","who wants sealed crates","crate turn in"}},{q="Can you look inside a sealed crate?",a="The crates stay locked and sealed in transit to protect their merchandise. Return them intact so handlers can process the goods and pay you without tampering.",al={"can i open a sealed crate","whats inside the crate","open sealed crate"}},{q="Can you return more sealed crates in the future?",a="Yes. Highway robbery remains widespread along major roads, and merchants seek recovered freight. Bring them any other missing crates you find in the wild.",al={"more crates","can i turn in more crates","are crates repeatable"}},{q="Who is intercepting the trade routes?",a="Thieves and cutpurses target merchant shipments across trade territories. They steal valuable goods and disrupt commerce between settlements.",al={"bandit attacks trade routes","thieves stealing goods","who is raiding the roads"}}},kw={"a sealed crate","bandits","caravan","cargo","crate","delivery","merchants","sealed crate","thieves","trade routes"},m={id=91904},src={"In-game quest text: A Sealed Crate"},fv=true}
E["quest:91905"] = {t="quest",n="A Sealed Crate",z="general",s="Trade recipients seek A Sealed Crate after bandits disrupt the roads. Recovered cargo helps keep local stores supplied and out of outlaw hands.",h="Trade recipients seek A Sealed Crate after bandits disrupt the roads.",sec={{t="Disrupted Trade Routes",b="Bandits and thieves have struck established trade routes, leaving merchant cargo scattered. Their ambushes put caravans and supply lines at risk. Across contested lands, lost shipments are a common sight. Recovering the crates helps local trade endure the lawlessness.",sp=0},{t="Recovered Cargo",b="Merchants and handlers rely on couriers to bring lost goods back to storage depots. Each returned crate adds to local stores and denies outlaws the gains of highway robbery. In return, salvage workers receive fair pay for facing dangerous roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the sealed crate?",a="The crate holds commercial cargo, though its exact contents are not given. Merchants and handlers want the goods secured away from thieves.",al={"what is inside the sealed crate","crate contents","whats in the crate"}},{q="Why are these crates lying around?",a="Bandits and thieves have struck trade routes, scattering shipments and leaving crates abandoned or stolen across the region.",al={"why are crates lost","who is stealing crates","bandits stealing trade goods"}},{q="Who wants these crates returned?",a="Local merchants and trade coordinators receive the recovered crates. They add the goods to secure stores and pay adventurers who salvage them from danger.",al={"who takes the crates","where do the crates go","turn in crates"}},{q="Can more sealed crates be recovered?",a="Yes. Bandits continue to disrupt overland travel, so local handlers pay adventurers to recover other crates scattered along trade routes.",al={"can i find more crates","repeatable crates","more sealed crates"}},{q="What is threatening the trade routes?",a="Bandits and outlaws prey on unguarded caravans, threatening trade routes. Merchants pay for cargo recovered from the roads.",al={"bandit trade routes","trade disruptions","why are roads unsafe"}},{q="Why is the crate sealed?",a="The reason for the seal is not given. You return the lost cargo to the handlers, who add it to their pile and pay you.",al={"sealed crate purpose","why seal the crate"}}},kw={"bandits","cargo","crate","delivery","merchants","salvage","sealed crate","thieves","trade routes"},m={id=91905},src={"In-game quest text: A Sealed Crate"},fv=true}
E["quest:91920"] = {t="quest",n="Wild Eyes",z="general",s="In Silverpine Forest, Wild Eyes brings an ailing Forsaken scout to a desperate choice. Apothecary Renferrel's heart-based draughts have failed, and the scout seeks another way to stave off a second death.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Wild Eyes brings an ailing Forsaken scout to a desperate choice.",sec={{t="Desperate Measures",b="In Silverpine Forest, a Forsaken Deathstalker feels their body failing and faces a second death. Apothecary Renferrel's draughts have brought no relief. So the scout risks Renferrel's wrath and seeks another cure along the creature-ridden shores of Lake Lordamere.",sp=0},{t="New Reagents at the Sepulcher",b="The Deathstalker suspects Renferrel's focus on hearts has kept him from trying other reagents. So the scout asks you to gather murloc eyes and bring them to Renferrel at the Sepulcher. The strange organs broaden the apothecary's experiments, and he restores the fading scout.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks you to gather murloc eyes?",a="An ailing Forsaken Deathstalker in Silverpine Forest asks you to help restore their strength. With a second death looming and Renferrel's draughts failing, the scout gambles on different ingredients.",al={"who gives wild eyes","wild eyes quest giver","who asks for murloc eyes"}},{q="Why does the quest require murloc eyes?",a="The Deathstalker sees murlocs infesting Lake Lordamere's shores and proposes using their eyes. The scout hopes this new ingredient will draw Renferrel beyond his fixation on hearts.",al={"why murloc eyes","what are murloc eyes for","murloc eyes potion"}},{q="How does Apothecary Renferrel react to the delivery?",a="Renferrel first scoffs and blames the potion's failure on too few hearts. Yet he admits he had not considered murloc anatomy and agrees to use it to restore the Deathstalker.",al={"renferrel reaction","what does renferrel say","does renferrel like the eyes"}},{q="Where is Apothecary Renferrel located?",a="Apothecary Renferrel conducts his research at the Sepulcher, the main Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is apothecary renferrel","renferrel location","where to turn in wild eyes"}},{q="Why did Renferrel's original potion fail to work?",a="Renferrel says the potion failed because he received only three hearts, though the recipe calls for six. The ailing Deathstalker noticed no improvement from the formula.",al={"why did potion fail","why did renferrels potion not work","deathstalker potion failure"}},{q="What is Apothecary Renferrel obsessed with?",a="Renferrel is fixated on animal hearts in his restorative mixtures. That focus keeps him from considering other specimens until the Deathstalker brings murloc eyes.",al={"renferrel heart obsession","why does renferrel want hearts"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken soldiers contend with the bodily decay of undeath. They rely on the Royal Apothecary Society's grim concoctions to sustain their failing strength.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken war effort in Silverpine Forest relies on Apothecary Renferrel's work at the Sepulcher. His research sustains frontline scouts and Deathstalkers.",["class:Rogue"]="Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's elite scouts and assassins. Restoring their strength is a priority in the region."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","deathstalker","forsaken alchemy","lake lordamere","murloc eyes","sepulcher","silverpine forest","wild eyes"},rel={"npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","topic:murloc"},m={id=91920},src={"In-game quest text: Wild Eyes"},fv=true}
E["quest:91921"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Quinn (Again)",z="general",s="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick needs a remedy before his affliction claims his mind and body. A courier brings him a mixture brewed from six hearts, restoring his strength for the travels ahead.",h="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick needs a remedy before his affliction claims his mind and body.",sec={{t="A Desperate Remedy",b="North of the Sepulcher, Quinn Yorick rests at the Ivar Patch in Silverpine Forest. His affliction threatens both mind and body, so a special alchemical mixture brewed from six hearts is sent to his camp. For the Forsaken and their allies, bringing remedies to wandering kin can hold back rot and madness.",sp=0},{t="Averting Degeneration",b="Quinn Yorick feared he was nearing a grim end, becoming a mindless ghoul. He drinks the freshly brewed potion, and its effects come at once. His strength returns, and he can prepare to travel across the plagued land.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Quinn Yorick?",a="Quinn Yorick is an afflicted traveler at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He needs special alchemical mixtures to stave off physical decline and regain enough strength to travel.",al={"who is quinn","quinn yorick lore","who is quinn yorick"}},{q="What is Quinn's Potion and why does he need it?",a="Quinn's Potion is a special mixture made to aid his recovery and keep his condition from worsening. Without it, he feared he would deteriorate into a mindless ghoul.",al={"what does the potion do","quinns potion purpose","why does quinn need a potion"}},{q="Where is the Ivar Patch located?",a="The Ivar Patch lies directly north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. It is Quinn Yorick's temporary shelter while he recovers.",al={"where is ivar patch","ivar patch location"}},{q="What are the ingredients in Quinn's potion?",a="Quinn's remedy is an alchemical mixture brewed from extracts of six whole hearts. It is meant to halt his bodily decay.",al={"potion ingredients","what is quinn potion made of","hearts potion"}},{q="Does the potion successfully cure Quinn Yorick?",a="The potion takes effect as soon as Quinn drinks it. He says he will soon be strong enough to travel again instead of becoming a ghoul.",al={"what happens to quinn","does quinn turn into a ghoul","quinn recovery"}},{q="Who brews the potion for Quinn?",a="Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher brews Quinn's potion from the extract of six whole hearts. Impatient with paperwork, he hands it over and is eager to dismiss the courier.",al={"who makes quinn potion","apothecary quinn"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Quinn Yorick fears becoming a mindless ghoul. His plight shows how the Forsaken struggle to preserve their free will and physical faculties.",["faction:Horde"]="Helping distressed travelers and outcasts in Silverpine Forest strengthens Horde influence in the plagued lands north of the Sepulcher."},kw={"ghoul","ivar patch","quinn yorick","quinn's potion","return to quinn","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"npc:quinn-yorick","item:quinn-s-potion","subzone:ivar-patch","subzone:sepulcher"},m={id=91921},src={"In-game quest text: Return to Quinn (Again)"},fv=true}
E["quest:92109"] = {t="quest",n="My First Alchemy Set",z="general",s="A young alchemist in Moonbrook asks you for basic supplies. She wants to begin learning despite her father's warning about herbs.",h="A young alchemist in Moonbrook asks you for basic supplies.",sec={{t="A Young Alchemist",b="The child in Moonbrook's barn has been told not to handle her father's herbs. She hopes to learn alchemy while she is still young, and asks you to bring her empty vials, Silverleaf, and Peacebloom. She is waiting to see what she can make with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for the alchemy supplies?",a="A young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn in Moonbrook asks you for supplies.",al={"who wants supplies","moonbrook alchemist girl"}},{q="Why does she want these things?",a="She wants to start learning alchemy, but her father will not let her handle his herbs because he considers them dangerous.",al={"why alchemy stuff","why does she need supplies"}},{q="What supplies is she asking for?",a="She asks for five Empty Vials, five Silverleaf, and five Peacebloom.",al={"what items","alchemy supplies"}},{q="Where can I find the young alchemist?",a="She is inside the barn in Moonbrook, Westfall.",al={"where is the girl","moonbrook barn"}},{q="What does she plan to do with the supplies?",a="She says she will see what she can make with the supplies.",al={"what will she make","does she make potions"}}},kw={"alchemy","empty vials","moonbrook","my first alchemy set","peacebloom","silverleaf","westfall","young alchemist"},rel={"zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","quest:567"},m={id=92109},src={"In-game quest text: My First Alchemy Set"},fv=true}
E["quest:92110"] = {t="quest",n="My First Real Potion",z="general",s="A child asks you to bring murloc eyes for My First Real Potion. She is eager to mix it herself.",h="A child asks you to bring murloc eyes for My First Real Potion.",sec={{t="A First Attempt",b="The child is glad to see the murloc eyes. While you were away, she gathered more herbs and found empty vials downstairs. Now she asks you to mix the ingredients as she watches. The potion turns sickly orange when the eyes go in.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the child want?",a="The child wants murloc eyes for her first real potion, along with herbs and empty vials.",al={"what she wants","child potion","potion ingredients"}},{q="Who mixes the potion?",a="You mix the potion while the child watches.",al={"who does the mixing","mix potion","potion maker"}},{q="What color does the potion turn?",a="The mixture turns sickly orange within seconds of adding the murloc eyes.",al={"potion color","orange potion","what does it look like"}},{q="Does the child drink it?",a="No. The child says she would not drink the potion, but gives you her recipe.",al={"drink potion","would she drink it","is it safe"}}},kw={"child","herbs","murloc eyes","my first real potion","orange potion","potion","vials"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={id=92110},src={"In-game quest text: My First Real Potion"},fv=true}
E["quest:92401"] = {t="quest",n="A Frightened Request",z="general",s="Edward Heartweaver’s wife waits in fear after he vanishes in the Ruins of Lordaeron. Since their son was lost when the capital fell, Edward has gone each week to search the graveyard for his remains. Now his usual journey has lasted several days.",h="Edward Heartweaver’s wife waits in fear after he vanishes in the Ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Father's Grief",b="When the Scourge destroyed Lordaeron during the Third War, the Heartweavers lost their young son. His body was never found in the ruin. So Edward Heartweaver went each week to the capital’s graveyard, still hoping to find some trace of his child.\n\nGrief and guilt kept Edward from letting go. The graveyard lay within the ruined capital, where the search was perilous.",sp=0},{t="The Perils of the Ruins",b="The surface ruins of Lordaeron are overrun by hostile creatures and lurking horrors. They are no place for ordinary citizens. Edward’s frightened wife warned him and begged him to stop going, but he kept to his weekly search.\n\nThen Edward failed to return for several days. His wife turned to capable adventurers and asked them to brave the ruins and learn what had become of him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Edward Heartweaver?",a="Edward Heartweaver is a grieving father whose son was lost when the Scourge destroyed Lordaeron. He searched the ruined capital’s graveyard each week for the child’s remains, then vanished.",al={"who is edward","edward heartweaver lore","husband in ruins"}},{q="Why did Edward go to the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="Edward went to the Ruins of Lordaeron to search for his son’s remains. The boy was lost when Prince Arthas and the Scourge destroyed the capital, and Edward kept searching despite his wife’s warnings.",al={"why did edward go to lordaeron","edward heartweaver graveyard","why search lordaeron ruins"}},{q="Why are the Ruins of Lordaeron so dangerous?",a="The surface ruins of Lordaeron are overrun by hostile creatures and dangerous horrors. Ordinary citizens cannot safely travel there, making a long search perilous.",al={"why are lordaeron ruins dangerous","what is in lordaeron ruins","ruins of lordaeron threats"}},{q="Who offers the quest A Frightened Request?",a="Edward Heartweaver’s frightened wife asks for help after he fails to return from his weekly search. She turns to capable adventurers to find out what happened to him.",al={"who gives a frightened request","a frightened request questgiver","edward wife quest"}},{q="What happened to Edward's son?",a="The Heartweavers’ son was lost when Prince Arthas and the Scourge destroyed Lordaeron. His body was never found, leaving Edward grieving and searching for his remains.",al={"what happened to the son","edward heartweaver son","lost son in lordaeron"}},{q="What is the objective of A Frightened Request?",a="Edward’s wife asks you to search the dangerous Ruins of Lordaeron and discover what happened to Edward Heartweaver.",al={"what do i do in a frightened request","a frightened request goal","how to complete a frightened request"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="The fall of Lordaeron remains a deep tragedy in human memory. As a human, you can see Edward’s desperate search as a reminder of the families torn apart when Prince Arthas destroyed his own people.",["race:Undead"]="The ruins above the Undercity are held by the Forsaken, who rose from the kingdom’s ashes. As an undead, you know living humans still wander the shattered capital’s graveyard, in lands the Forsaken now hold.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can understand the grief that drives a father to search a graveyard for his lost son."},kw={"a frightened request","arthas","edward heartweaver","heartweaver","lordaeron graveyard","missing husband","ruins of lordaeron","scourge"},rel={"zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},m={id=92401},src={"In-game quest text: A Frightened Request"},fv=true}
E["quest:92421"] = {t="quest",n="Light's Justice",z="general",s="In the Undercity, Morbin Lightbane sends warriors above to gather what the Forsaken need. Intact limbs from the Scourge in the Ruins of Lordaeron help repair wounded Forsaken and sustain their ranks.",h="In the Undercity, Morbin Lightbane sends warriors above to gather what the Forsaken need.",sec={{t="The Scourge Above",b="Above the Undercity, Scourge remnants still prowl the ruined streets of Lordaeron's former capital. Though the Dark Lady has defeated the dreadlords and founded the Forsaken kingdom, clearing the surface remains costly work. The undead threaten the gateway below and drain the forces sent to reclaim the fallen kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Flesh and Bone",b="Forsaken bodies do not mend on their own. Rotting tissue and shattered sinew cannot knit again, so Morbin Lightbane sends warriors to gather intact limbs from destroyed Scourge in the ruins above. Those parts can repair wounded Forsaken and help them endure and fight again.",sp=0},{t="A Captain's Legacy",b="Morbin Lightbane honors his late commander, Captain Garek Bandarion, by carrying on this work. Bandarion pledged to heal their people and free Lordaeron from Scourge occupation. To Morbin, destroying their mindless enemies and restoring their kin is justice in the service of the Banshee Queen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Morbin Lightbane?",a="Morbin Lightbane is a Forsaken paladin who lives in the Undercity. He carries out Lady Sylvanas's will by tending to his kin's physical survival and honoring his fallen captain, Garek Bandarion.",al={"who gives lights justice","who is morbin lightbane","quest giver"}},{q="Why are intact limbs needed?",a="Forsaken flesh decays and cannot heal or knit itself together. Intact limbs gathered from fallen undead in the ruins above can repair damaged bodies and help keep their fighting forces active.",al={"why intact limbs","why do forsaken need limbs","why harvest body parts"}},{q="Who was Captain Garek Bandarion?",a="Captain Garek Bandarion was a commander devoted to cleansing Lordaeron of Scourge remnants and healing his Forsaken kin. His followers carry on that work in his memory.",al={"who was captain bandarion","captain garek bandarion lore","garek bandarion"}},{q="Where are the Scourge forces located?",a="Scourge forces wander the Ruins of Lordaeron, the surface city directly above the Undercity. Forsaken efforts to purge them continue, but the invaders remain dangerous in number.",al={"where do scourge roam","where are intact limbs found","ruins of lordaeron scourge"}},{q="Are there paladins among the Forsaken?",a="Morbin Lightbane calls himself a paladin of the Forsaken. He directs his martial devotion toward serving Sylvanas Windrunner and protecting his people.",al={"can forsaken be paladins","undead paladins lore","forsaken paladin"}},{q="What does 'Light's Justice' signify for the Forsaken?",a="For Morbin Lightbane, justice means driving the mindless Scourge from Lordaeron's capital and using their remains to save the Forsaken.",al={"what does lights justice mean","why is it called lights justice","quest name meaning"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken bodies cannot regrow decaying flesh on their own. Gathering limbs from Scourge remnants is a grim necessity to keep wounded Forsaken and soldiers whole.",["class:Paladin"]="Morbin Lightbane calls himself a paladin of the Forsaken. His example shows holy warfare and martial duty enduring in undeath under the Dark Lady's service.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity protects the Horde's vital northern capital and strengthens its fragile hold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"forsaken paladin","garek bandarion","intact limbs","light's justice","morbin lightbane","ruins of lordaeron","scourge","undercity"},rel={"zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:paladin","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:light"},m={id=92421},src={"In-game quest text: Light's Justice"},fv=true}
E["quest:92422"] = {t="quest",n="The Wrath of Rath'mael",z="general",s="In the Ruins of Lordaeron, a fog hides Scourge movements above the Undercity. Rath'mael, a Scourge necromancer, has shrouded the ruined streets and graveyard. Deathguard Kristof in Brill calls for you to strike him down.",h="In the Ruins of Lordaeron, a fog hides Scourge movements above the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Shroud Over the Ruins",b="Scout reports from Lordamere Overlook tell of a sinister presence in the Ruins of Lordaeron. An unholy fog now covers the ruined streets and nearby graveyard, hiding lingering Scourge forces. Rath'mael cast the shroud. His spells conceal the undead above the heart of Forsaken territory.",sp=0},{t="The Defense of Tirisfal",b="Deathguard Kristof in Brill sends you to rally your allies and strike Rath'mael down. The Forsaken cannot let this menace take root unchecked. The Scourge may replace him, but his fall will disrupt their coordination, disperse the fog, and give Tirisfal Glades room to breathe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rath'mael?",a="Rath'mael is a Scourge necromancer who has risen among the undead in the Ruins of Lordaeron. His dark sorcery conjures an unholy fog that conceals Scourge movements in the streets and graveyard near Lordamere Overlook.",al={"who is rathmael","who is rath'mael","rathmael lore"}},{q="What is the unholy fog in the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="The unholy fog over the ruined capital's streets and graveyard is conjured by Rath'mael. It conceals lingering Scourge forces from Forsaken patrols.",al={"what is the fog in lordaeron","why is there fog in ruins of lordaeron","unholy fog ruins"}},{q="Who offers this mission?",a="Deathguard Kristof, a Forsaken soldier, offers the call from Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He watches the approaches to the Capital City ruins and calls for Rath'mael's death before the Scourge threat grows too great.",al={"who gives wrath of rathmael","where is deathguard kristof","kristof brill"}},{q="Where is Rath'mael located?",a="Rath'mael operates in the Ruins of Lordaeron, around its streets and graveyard and near Lordamere Overlook above the lake.",al={"where is rathmael found","where to find rath'mael","rathmael location"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Rath'mael destroyed?",a="The Forsaken fear the Scourge gathering forces and hiding their movements above the Undercity. Rath'mael's fog threatens Forsaken defenses and travelers throughout Tirisfal.",al={"why kill rathmael","why fight rathmael"}},{q="Does Rath'mael's death permanently secure the ruins?",a="No. The Scourge will replace fallen lieutenants with another dark spellcaster. Rath'mael's death slows their immediate advance, thins their numbers, and lifts the fog for a time.",al={"does killing rathmael end the scourge","will scourge be gone after rathmael"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you live in the Undercity beneath the ruined capital. Scourge forces in the courtyards and graveyards above threaten your doorstep.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you have a foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms. Securing Lordaeron's surrounding lands helps preserve it against the relentless undead."},kw={"brill","deathguard kristof","lordamere overlook","rath'mael","rathmael","ruins of lordaeron","scourge necromancer","the wrath of rath'mael","tirisfal glades","unholy fog"},rel={"zone:ruinsoflordaeron","subzone:brill","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron"},m={id=92422},src={"In-game quest text: The Wrath of Rath'mael"},fv=true}
E["quest:92456"] = {t="quest",n="A Green Sample",z="general",s="In Stormwind City, Shylamiir seeks a living plant from Dalaran’s guarded garden. The cutting is wanted for study of mana-fed growth, but it brings back a darker surprise.",h="In Stormwind City, Shylamiir seeks a living plant from Dalaran’s guarded garden.",sec={{t="An Errand to Dalaran",b="Shylamiir in Stormwind City seeks a traveler willing to enter restricted lands. The Kirin Tor’s interest in botany has caught Shylamiir’s attention, and a living plant from Dalaran’s central garden is wanted for study. The secluded sorcerers keep their borders closed to outsiders. Reaching the garden calls for someone able to slip past their defenses.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Roots",b="The cutting from Dalaran’s central garden is a Fel Infused Blossom. Fel taint has touched its growth, where pure arcane energy was expected. The discovery catches Shylamiir off guard and suggests the Kirin Tor face darker troubles than their outward appearance reveals. That taint makes the blossom more compelling to study than ordinary arcane herbs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Green Sample?",a="In Stormwind City, Shylamiir asks an outsider to enter Dalaran and gather a plant sample.",al={"who gives a green sample","quest giver green sample","shylamiir location"}},{q="What does Shylamiir ask you to retrieve?",a="Shylamiir asks you to retrieve vegetation from Dalaran’s central garden, expecting a mana-infused plant.",al={"what does shylamiir want","a green sample objective","green sample item"}},{q="Where is the requested sample found?",a="The requested sample grows in Dalaran’s central garden, within the secluded magocracy that guards its borders from outsiders.",al={"where is central garden","how to get fel infused blossom","dalaran garden location"}},{q="Why is the blossom fel-infused instead of mana-infused?",a="The sample is a Fel Infused Blossom, its fel taint in place of healthy mana-infused growth. Shylamiir sees the corruption as a sign that the Kirin Tor face darker troubles than expected.",al={"why fel infused","is dalaran fel corrupted","dalaran plant fel"}},{q="Why is Shylamiir interested in Dalaran's flora?",a="Shylamiir is interested in how the Kirin Tor tend mana-infused plants. Dalaran’s interest in botany is unusual for a magocracy.",al={"why does shylamiir want dalaran plants","dalaran botany reason"}},{q="What is Shylamiir's reaction to the delivered blossom?",a="The blossom’s fel taint startles Shylamiir, yet also intrigues them. Shylamiir praises you for completing the dangerous errand.",al={"how does shylamiir react","green sample turn in"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you know scholars have long been intrigued by the Kirin Tor’s secluded experiments and Dalaran’s botany. Unexpected corruption hints at hidden troubles within the mage enclave.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how to slip past defenses and enter places where you are not welcome. That is why Shylamiir seeks your help.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a practitioner of Herbalism, you learn that unnatural energies can corrupt ordinary vegetation into fel-infused blossoms in Dalaran’s central garden."},kw={"a green sample","botany","central garden","dalaran","fel infused blossom","kirin tor","shylamiir","stormwind city"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:stormwind","topic:mage","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=92456},src={"In-game quest text: A Green Sample"},fv=true}
E["quest:92457"] = {t="quest",n="Starving Arcane",z="general",s="Archmage Modera asks you to clear rogue elementals from the City of Dalaran. A breach has unsettled the city's enchantments and defenses, and the Kirin Tor needs room to tend its wards.",h="Archmage Modera asks you to clear rogue elementals from the City of Dalaran.",sec={{t="Arcane Fragments",b="The breach has disturbed factotums and enchantments across Dalaran. Some of those enchantments protect the city's defenses. Fragmented arcane energy has drawn Seeking Remnants, Saturated Remnants, and Mana Echoes. They gather to fill themselves with its free-flowing magic. Archmage Modera asks you to thin their numbers while the Kirin Tor tends the wards and other incidents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are elementals gathering in Dalaran?",a="Fragmented arcane energy from the breach has drawn rogue elementals seeking to fill themselves with its free-flowing magic.",al={"why elementals here","dalaran elementals","arcane elementals"}},{q="Who asks me to clear the elementals?",a="Archmage Modera asks you to thin the elementals inside the city. She is outside Dalaran.",al={"who gave this","Modera task","archmage Modera"}},{q="What did the breach affect?",a="The breach disturbed factotums and enchantments throughout Dalaran, including some tied to the city's defenses.",al={"breach damage","what broke","dalaran wards"}},{q="Which elementals are involved?",a="Seeking Remnants, Saturated Remnants, and Mana Echoes make up the elemental throng.",al={"which remnants","elemental types","what am I clearing"}}},kw={"arcane energy","archmage modera","breach","dalaran","elementals","kirin tor","mana echoes","saturated remnants","seeking remnants","starving arcane"},rel={"subzone:dalaran"},m={id=92457},src={"In-game quest text: Starving Arcane"},fv=true}
E["quest:92458"] = {t="quest",n="Heart of Disruption",z="general",s="The Image of Archmage Modera needs help containing an arcane disruption in Dalaran. The Violet Citadel’s wards are under strain, and the Kirin Tor need time to bring the crisis under control.",h="The Image of Archmage Modera needs help containing an arcane disruption in Dalaran.",sec={{t="A Way Inside",b="At the top of the Violet Citadel, a thunderous crash sounded from the parlors. The disturbance began there, and rampant arcane power now threatens the wards. The Kirin Tor are occupied inside, so you receive a key and are asked to find a less public way into the city before the disruption worsens.",sp=0},{t="The Mote",b="Modera asks you to collect an Arcane Mote. She does not ask what you saw in the citadel. Her concern is containing the mote and ending the disruption. The Kirin Tor must now take up that work while the wards hold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="The Image of Archmage Modera asks you to help contain the arcane disruption in Dalaran.",al={"who needs help","modera help","who gave this"}},{q="What caused the disruption?",a="The disturbance began at the top of the Violet Citadel after a thunderous crash sounded from the parlors above.",al={"what happened in the citadel","why are the wards strained","arcane disturbance"}},{q="Why are the wards in danger?",a="Rampant arcane power has overrun the citadel, leaving the Kirin Tor struggling to keep the wards in place.",al={"what's wrong with the wards","why is dalaran overrun","rampant arcane power"}},{q="What does Modera ask me to collect?",a="Modera wants you to gather an Arcane Mote.",al={"what am i collecting","arcane mote","mote task"}},{q="Why do I need a key?",a="Modera gives you a key so you can take a less public approach to entering the city.",al={"what is the key for","how do i get inside","citadel key"}},{q="What happens after I bring back the mote?",a="Modera says the Kirin Tor must contain the mote and end the disruption.",al={"what does modera do with it","mote ending","what happens next"}}},kw={"arcane mote","archmage modera","dalaran","heart of disruption","kirin tor","leylines","violet citadel","wards"},rel={"subzone:dalaran"},m={id=92458},src={"In-game quest text: Heart of Disruption"},fv=true}
E["quest:92466"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="Initiates gather what their instructor asks of them in Call of Earth. Their effort shows whether they are ready to continue their training.",h="Initiates gather what their instructor asks of them in Call of Earth.",sec={{t="A Test of Resolve",b="An initiate faces a test of resolve when the instructor asks for particular materials. The gathering tests patience and endurance. By meeting the earth’s demands, the student shows the strength needed to commune with its enduring power.",sp=0},{t="The Next Step",b="When the initiate returns with the requested offerings, the instructor sees their grit. The student has held firm through the trial and is ready for the next step in spiritual training.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Earth?",a="Call of Earth asks spiritual initiates to gather requested items and prove their perseverance before advancing in training.",al={"what is call of earth","call of earth quest"}},{q="What does finishing this trial demonstrate?",a="Finishing the trial shows your grit and determination to your mentor. It proves your focus is strong enough for greater spiritual responsibilities.",al={"what did i prove","grit and determination"}},{q="What happens after completing the Call of Earth?",a="After Call of Earth, your instructor considers you ready for the next step toward communion with the elements.",al={"whats next","next quest"}},{q="Why must an initiate commune with earth?",a="An initiate proves endurance before communing with earth spirits, whose nature reflects stability and strength.",al={"why earth","earth spirits meaning"}},{q="Who oversees the Call of Earth?",a="A spiritual teacher or shaman mentor guides initiates through the trial and judges their discipline and readiness to bond with the spirits.",al={"who gives this quest","call of earth trainer"}},{q="Who is eligible to undertake this trial?",a="Call of Earth tests those learning to attune themselves to the elements.",al={"can anyone do call of earth","is call of earth for shamans"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you prove your resolve before gaining deeper insight into communion with the spirits of stone and soil.",["faction:Horde"]="Among the Horde, you encounter shamanistic trials such as Call of Earth as a foundational rite for spiritual practitioners."},kw={"call of earth","determination","earth","elements","shaman","spirits","trial"},rel={"quest:92472"},m={id=92466},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:92467"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="At the Rise of Spirits, you drink an Earth Sapta and meet an elemental guide. The earth's strength may help you seek the winds again.",h="At the Rise of Spirits, you drink an Earth Sapta and meet an elemental guide.",sec={{t="The Nature of the Sapta",b="Shamans drink saptas to open their sight to the elemental world. Each brew attunes a mortal spirit to one realm and reveals spirits usually hidden from view. Only those with enough resolve can bear their power. Select practitioners guard the knowledge of these brews.",sp=0},{t="The Rise of Spirits",b="You travel northeast through a pass to the Rise of Spirits, where initiates commune with the earth. Saptas are drunk only at sacred sites. On consecrated ground, the draught lets you pierce the veil and see what the spirits choose to reveal.",sp=0},{t="Strength of the Earth",b="After you drink the Earth Sapta, an elemental guide greets you as a child of the four winds. You seek to learn why they have departed. The earth spirit cannot explain the wind spirits' motives, but teaches you strength and steadfast resolve.\n\nEven high above, amid an endless sea of clouds, you must first anchor yourself to the earth. Only then can you speak with the winds again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="An Earth Sapta is a magical brew that attunes your spirit to the element of earth. With enough resolve, you can see elemental spirits hidden from ordinary sight.",al={"what is earth sapta","sapta explanation","what does sapta do"}},{q="Where must the Earth Sapta be consumed?",a="Drink the Earth Sapta at the Rise of Spirits, northeast through a pass. Saptas are consumed only on sacred ground.",al={"where to drink earth sapta","rise of spirits location","where is rise of spirits"}},{q="Why must saptas only be drunk in sacred places?",a="Saptas are potent brews that join mortal spirits with the elements. Shamanic tradition requires drinking them at sacred sites to commune with the spirits.",al={"why drink sapta at sacred place","can i drink sapta anywhere"}},{q="Why does the spirit address the seeker as a 'child of the four winds'?",a="The earth spirit greets you as a child of the four winds because you seek to learn why the winds have departed.",al={"who is child of the four winds","why child of four winds"}},{q="Why have the spirits of the winds left?",a="Even the earth spirit at the Rise of Spirits does not know why the wind spirits have grown distant or where they have gone.",al={"why did the winds leave","where did winds go"}},{q="How does communing with the earth help someone reconnect with the winds?",a="The earth teaches strength and resolve. Even amid an endless sea of clouds, you remain tethered to the earth. Learning its steadiness is the first step toward speaking with the four winds again.",al={"why earth first","how does earth help with winds"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you use saptas to attune your spirit to an element and commune with its spirits.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you may be adrift high in an endless sea of clouds and estranged from the four winds. The earth gives you a steady foundation for understanding."},kw={"call of earth","earth sapta","elements","four winds","rise of spirits","shaman","spirits"},rel={"quest:1462"},m={id=92467},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:92468"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="An earth spirit sends you to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove with a shard of Rough Quartz. There, the shard becomes the heart of your first Earth Totem and begins your study of the elemental forces.",h="An earth spirit sends you to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove with a shard of Rough Quartz.",sec={{t="The Earth's Gift",b="An earth spirit gives you a shard of Rough Quartz as proof of your communion. It sends you to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove with the shard. Even the smallest fragment can endure. The spirits grant favor and respect to those who show patience, resilience, and wisdom.",sp=0},{t="The Four Elements and the Totem",b="Windshaper Boros sets the Rough Quartz at the heart of your Earth Totem. He reminds you that the elemental path has four parts. You may long to hear and sing the songs of the wind. Yet mastery begins with understanding all four forces, starting with the unyielding ground beneath your feet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Windshaper Boros?",a="Windshaper Boros, also called Boro, lives in Thendal Grove. An elder practitioner and crafter, he guides initiates in understanding the elemental spirits and shapes their focal totems from elemental gifts.",al={"who is boro","windshaper boros location","where is thendal grove"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Rough Quartz?",a="An earth spirit gives you the Rough Quartz as proof of your meeting and communion. Windshaper Boros uses it as the foundation and heart of your Earth Totem.",al={"what is rough quartz","shard of earth","quartz use"}},{q="Why is an Earth Totem necessary?",a="An Earth Totem gives you a personal focus for communing with earth spirits and channeling earth-based spells. It marks you as an initiate and anchors you to the world's elemental foundations.",al={"what does earth totem do","totem purpose","why need totem"}},{q="Why must one commune with earth before speaking with the winds?",a="The winds are only one part of the world's elemental balance. Before seeking their songs, you study all four elements, beginning with the earth's stability, patience, and strength.",al={"why start with earth","seeking the winds","all four elements"}},{q="Where is Thendal Grove located?",a="Thendal Grove is the sanctuary where Windshaper Boros tends to elemental matters and instructs novices beginning their shamanic journey.",al={"where is thendal grove","thendal grove zone"}},{q="What wisdom does the earth spirit impart?",a="The earth spirit teaches that even the smallest stone can endure after greater things crumble. It asks for patience, inner strength, and the pursuit of wisdom in exchange for mutual respect and harmony.",al={"what elements ask","earth philosophy"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, receiving your first totem begins your communion with the elemental forces. It gives you a physical focus for earth-aligned spells and rites.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you begin your return to the winds by mastering the earth and grounding yourself in its solid foundations."},kw={"call of earth","earth totem","elements","rough quartz","shaman","thendal grove","windshaper boro","windshaper boros"},rel={"item:rough-quartz"},m={id=92468},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:92479"] = {t="quest",n="A Scribbled Letter",z="general",s="At Northshire Abbey, adventurers receive a summons from Tordrin Stemblade after clashes with nearby kobolds. It calls promising recruits to seek his training as Stormwind faces growing dangers.",h="At Northshire Abbey, adventurers receive a summons from Tordrin Stemblade after clashes with nearby kobolds.",sec={{t="A Summons in Northshire",b="After clashes with kobold camps in the valley, adventurers at Northshire Abbey receive a hasty letter sealed by Tordrin Stemblade. It asks them to give it prompt attention before taking up other business. The summons brings budding champions to formal mentorship within the abbey’s protective grounds.",sp=0},{t="Guidance in Perilous Times",b="Tordrin Stemblade says times have changed. Unfamiliar folk now take up weapons to defend the realm. As the wilderness around Northshire grows more dangerous by the day, he offers travelers counsel day or night. He guides them as they master their skills and help Stormwind’s beleaguered people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is A Scribbled Letter?",a="After clashes with kobold camps, adventurers at Northshire Abbey receive a letter sealed by Tordrin Stemblade. It directs them to seek his mentorship and training in the valley.",al={"what is the scribbled letter","scribbled letter quest","letter from tordrin"}},{q="Who sent the letter?",a="Tordrin Stemblade sent the letter. He is a local trainer at Northshire Abbey, where he instructs fledgling adventurers learning their craft.",al={"who sent the letter","who wrote the letter","author scribbled letter"}},{q="Where can Tordrin Stemblade be found?",a="Tordrin Stemblade can be found at Northshire Abbey in Northshire Valley. He remains there day and night, ready to offer travelers instruction and advice.",al={"where is tordrin stemblade","tordrin location","find tordrin stemblade"}},{q="Why did Tordrin Stemblade send the letter?",a="After an adventurer proves capable against local kobolds, Tordrin sends word so they can receive proper training. He aims to prepare them for the growing dangers threatening Northshire’s residents and the wider realm of Stormwind.",al={"why did tordrin send a letter","tordrin stemblade purpose","why summons"}},{q="What threats are currently affecting Northshire?",a="Northshire Valley faces incursions from aggressive kobold camps and dangerous man-eating beasts roaming the surrounding woods. Local mentors muster and drill capable fighters in response.",al={"what threats are in northshire","dangers in northshire abbey","kobolds northshire"}},{q="What does Tordrin Stemblade offer after receiving the letter?",a="Tordrin offers continuous training and guidance. He urges adventurers to learn the lay of the land and assist local folk with the kingdom’s many troubles.",al={"what does tordrin offer","tordrin training","what happens after meeting tordrin"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Tordrin Stemblade mentors hunters at Northshire Abbey. He notes how times have changed as new races take up the bow to defend Stormwind from beasts and vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Training skilled defenders at Northshire Abbey helps secure Elwynn Forest against encroaching kobolds and other growing threats to Stormwind."},kw={"a scribbled letter","hunter trainer","kobold camps","northshire abbey","northshire valley","scribbled letter","tordrin stemblade"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:kobold"},m={id=92479},src={"In-game quest text: A Scribbled Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:92489"] = {t="quest",n="Power Overwhelming",z="general",s="High Sorcerer Andromath sends aid from Stormwind to Dalaran, where arcane power has turned dangerous. The Kirin Tor rebuild behind closed borders, and a Mana Elemental threatens their work.",h="High Sorcerer Andromath sends aid from Stormwind to Dalaran, where arcane power has turned dangerous.",sec={{t="A City in Seclusion",b="After Archimonde destroyed Dalaran in the Third War, the Kirin Tor drew inward. Scholars and sorcerers once came from across the world to its doors. Now the surviving magi keep outsiders away as they rebuild their ruined city behind closed borders.",sp=0},{t="Wayward Arcane Forces",b="As the Kirin Tor restore Dalaran, arcane energy has grown dangerous. Volatile leaks surge out of control and take shape as beings of pure mana. High Sorcerer Andromath fears internal turmoil could undo the city’s recovery, or that Dalaran could abandon its old ties to the Alliance. So he sends champions from Stormwind to quell the Mana Elemental and remind the Kirin Tor that their allies still stand with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Power Overwhelming?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath sends aid from Stormwind as the Kirin Tor rebuild Dalaran. A Mana Elemental formed from wayward arcane energy threatens their work.",al={"what is power overwhelming","power overwhelming quest","dalaran mana elemental quest"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="High Sorcerer Andromath asks champions in Stormwind City to journey to Dalaran and aid the Kirin Tor.",al={"who gives power overwhelming","andromath quest","where to start power overwhelming"}},{q="Why is Dalaran reclusive and distrusting?",a="Archimonde devastated Dalaran during the Third War. As the Kirin Tor rebuild their home, its surviving magi remain wary of outsiders.",al={"why dalaran secluded","what happened to dalaran","why are dalaran mages distrustful"}},{q="What is causing the disturbance in Dalaran?",a="Volatile arcane energy has surged out of control during Dalaran’s reconstruction and formed hostile mana elementals.",al={"dalaran arcane outbreak","why are there mana elementals in dalaran","what is going on in dalaran"}},{q="What is the Mana Elemental?",a="A Mana Elemental is a being formed from pure mana. Its appearance shows the arcane disturbance threatening Dalaran is stronger than first reports suggested.",al={"what is the mana elemental","dalaran elemental lore","creature of pure mana"}},{q="Why is Stormwind sending help to Dalaran?",a="The Kirin Tor have long been allies of the Alliance. High Sorcerer Andromath sends aid because he fears Dalaran could fall to chaos or leave the Alliance while vulnerable.",al={"why stormwind helping dalaran","why does alliance care about dalaran"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of the Kirin Tor, you know Stormwind is eager to strengthen its bond by aiding Dalaran as it rebuilds.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the Kirin Tor share a kinship with your calling, and that unstable arcane manifestations endanger Dalaran."},kw={"arcane energy","archimonde","dalaran","high sorcerer andromath","kirin tor","mana elemental","power overwhelming","stormwind"},rel={"quest:1939","subzone:dalaran","zone:stormwind","topic:alliance","topic:mage","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=92489},src={"In-game quest text: Power Overwhelming"},fv=true}
E["quest:92514"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome to Shen'dar Village",z="general",s="At Shen'dar Village, newcomers are sent to meet its elder and innkeeper. Local tensions share the frontier with a growing bandit threat.",h="At Shen'dar Village, newcomers are sent to meet its elder and innkeeper.",sec={{t="First Steps in Shen'dar",b="Newcomers in Shen'dar Village first meet the people who guide daily life there. Those touched by the spirits are directed to Elder Illaya Amberwind near the village square. Coriella Calmbreeze welcomes visitors at the village inn, where lodging and supplies are available. These introductions help travelers learn the village's customs before they take up arms.",sp=0},{t="Factions and Frontier Trouble",b="Disputes in Shen'dar Village stay civil, though the Windshapers and the High Order disagree. Their ideological friction runs through the region, but both groups know survival comes first. Bandits are pressing into the area. That danger gives the village reason to set smaller quarrels aside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Welcome to Shen'dar Village?",a="Welcome to Shen'dar Village guides newcomers to meet the people who lead and serve the settlement. Travelers are directed to the resident Windshaper elder and the village innkeeper before they help with local troubles such as bandits.",al={"what is shen'dar village quest","welcome to shendar quest overview","what to do in shendar village"}},{q="Who is Illaya Amberwind?",a="Illaya Amberwind is Shen'dar Village's Windshaper elder. She is near the town center and guides those touched by the spirits amid local political friction.",al={"who is illaya amberwind","illaya amberwind location","windshaper elder shendar"}},{q="Who is Coriella Calmbreeze?",a="Coriella Calmbreeze runs Shen'dar Village's inn, offering lodging, rest, and provisions to travelers and locals.",al={"who is coriella calmbreeze","shendar village innkeeper","where is the inn in shendar village"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are practitioners touched by the spirits, marked by a charge of static in the air around them. They and the High Order keep relations civil in Shen'dar Village despite their tensions and the wider threats.",al={"what are windshapers","spirit touched windshaper lore","high order vs windshapers"}},{q="What is the tension between the High Order and the Windshapers?",a="The High Order and the Windshapers are in political and ideological conflict. In Shen'dar Village, both sides keep the peace and attend to shared, more urgent concerns.",al={"what is the high order","conflict in shendar village","high order vs windshapers tension"}},{q="What problems is Shen'dar Village currently facing?",a="Shen'dar Village faces local bandits in the surrounding territory, alongside the philosophical dispute between the Windshapers and the High Order.",al={"shendar village troubles","what threat faces shendar village","bandits in shendar village"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can sense the faint static in the air around spirit-touched Windshapers like Illaya Amberwind in Shen'dar Village."},kw={"bandits","coriella calmbreeze","high order","illaya amberwind","shen'dar village","spirit-touched","welcome to shen'dar village","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=92514},src={"In-game quest text: Welcome to Shen'dar Village"},fv=true}
E["quest:92515"] = {t="quest",n="The Problem With Prideclaws",z="general",s="The Shen'dar Highlands village faces danger from prideclaws, bandits, and cultists. The beasts press toward the settlement, and culling them guards the people while providing useful pelts.",h="The Shen'dar Highlands village faces danger from prideclaws, bandits, and cultists.",sec={{t="A Growing Wild Menace",b="Prideclaws are pressing toward the village in the Shen'dar Highlands. Bandits roam the hills, and unhinged cultists trouble the region. Villagers face danger from several sides. As the beasts grow bolder and their territory spreads, the settlement draws nearer to their reach.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borders",b="Villagers have organized a culling before the wandering predators can snatch pets or children. Driving prideclaws back from the borders helps guard the settlement. Their sturdy pelts also give village craftsmen material for useful goods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are prideclaws?",a="Prideclaws are fierce predators of the hills and highlands of Shen'dar. Their pelts are valuable, and their growing numbers bring them closer to settlements.",al={"what are prideclaws","prideclaw lore","prideclaws"}},{q="Where are the prideclaws located?",a="Prideclaws roam the hills of the Shen'dar Highlands. Their growing numbers carry them toward the local village and its inhabitants.",al={"where is this quest","where do prideclaws live","prideclaw location"}},{q="Why does the village need the prideclaws culled?",a="Bandits and mad cultists already menace the region. As prideclaw numbers grow, the beasts draw near the village, putting children and domestic animals at risk.",al={"why kill prideclaws","why cull prideclaws","village danger"}},{q="What will be done with the prideclaw pelts?",a="Village crafters use prideclaw pelts to make practical goods and supplies.",al={"what happens to pelts","prideclaw pelt use","pelts purpose"}},{q="What other threats plague the surrounding hills?",a="Roaming bandits and unstable cultists trouble the hills around the settlement, alongside the wild prideclaws.",al={"other threats shendar","what else threatens the village","local threats"}},{q="How do the locals view the prideclaws?",a="The villager overseeing the culling finds prideclaws somewhat cute, even from behind armed guards. Still, keeping the village safe matters before tragedy strikes.",al={"who gives the problem with prideclaws","quest giver thoughts"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking and culling predators near settlements is familiar work. Prideclaws in these numbers still demand respect."},kw={"cull","prideclaw pelts","prideclaws","shen'dar","shen'dar highlands","the problem with prideclaws","village borders"},m={id=92515},src={"In-game quest text: The Problem With Prideclaws"},fv=true}
E["quest:92516"] = {t="quest",n="Hippogryph Harassment",z="general",s="Near Shen'dar Village, Hippogryph Harassment puts travelers in danger. A wild flock nests southeast of the village in the Shen'dar Highlands and attacks those on the nearby road. You are asked to cull its young, protectors, and matriarch so travelers can pass safely.",h="Near Shen'dar Village, Hippogryph Harassment puts travelers in danger.",sec={{t="Peril on the Road",b="Travelers near Shen'dar Village face danger from the skies. A wild flock nests southeast of the settlement, in the Shen'dar Highlands. Across Kalimdor, hippogryphs are known as noble beasts, and some are bonded to elven riders. Untamed flocks, though, fiercely guard their territory.\n\nWagons and lone travelers on the paths below have become targets of aerial ambushes. The attacks disrupt passage and could leave the village isolated if the creatures go unchecked.",sp=0},{t="Culling the Flock",b="The flock's nesting grounds in the Shen'dar Highlands must be confronted to end the danger. To make the high roads safe, kill the young before they reach maturity and overcome the vigilant protectors guarding the perimeter.\n\nThe matriarch directs attacks on passersby. Travelers can use the roads safely again only when the nest is struck and she is felled.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the hippogryphs attacking travelers near Shen'dar Village?",a="The hippogryphs have established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village in the Shen'dar Highlands. Their territory lies beside the main travel route, and they attack those who come near to defend their brood and hunting grounds.",al={"why hippogryphs attacking","why are hippogryphs hostile","hippogryph harassment cause"}},{q="Where is the hippogryph flock located?",a="The flock nests southeast of Shen'dar Village in the Shen'dar Highlands. Its roost overlooks the road, where the young, protectors, and matriarch gather among the cliffs and ridges.",al={"where are the hippogryphs","hippogryph location","shen'dar highlands location"}},{q="Which hippogryphs must be slain to complete the task?",a="To restore safe travel, slay eight hippogryph youths, six sturdy hippogryph protectors, and the hippogryph matriarch who directs the roost in the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"which hippogryphs do i kill","hippogryph harassment targets","hippogryph objectives"}},{q="Who is the leader of the hippogryph flock?",a="A powerful Hippogryph Matriarch leads the flock in the Shen'dar Highlands. She directs the roost and its defense of the nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village, so her death is needed to break the flock's hold on the roadway.",al={"who leads the hippogryphs","hippogryph matriarch","boss hippogryph"}},{q="Why must the hippogryph youths be culled?",a="The youths are the flock's future growth and continued expansion. Culling them alongside the mature protectors keeps the roost from quickly replenishing its strength or establishing a lasting reign of terror over the local highways.",al={"why kill hippogryph youths","why target young hippogryphs","culling hippogryph young"}},{q="Are these hippogryphs tame or allied with anyone?",a="No. These are wild, untamed creatures that established a roost in the Shen'dar Highlands on their own. Unlike the disciplined mounts raised by the night elves, this feral flock treats any passing humanoid as an intruder or prey encroaching on its territory.",al={"are the hippogryphs tamed","are these night elf hippogryphs","friendly hippogryphs"}},{q="What danger do these hippogryphs pose to the local settlement?",a="The flock nests overlooking the road leading southeast from Shen'dar Village. The beasts swoop down on supply carts, messengers, and wandering travelers, threatening safe overland travel and risking the village's isolation from the surrounding lands.",al={"what threat do hippogryphs pose","danger to shendar village","why are hippogryphs a problem"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere hippogryphs as sacred companions of Elune. Culling an aggressive wild flock is a somber task when wilderness clashes with traveler safety.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you understand the predatory instincts of aerial beasts and the hierarchy of a wild roost. Killing the matriarch is the surest way to break the flock's aggression.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you seek harmony with the wild. You can see this culling as an unfortunate necessity to restore balance after the beasts began preying on travelers."},kw={"hippogryph","hippogryph harassment","hippogryph matriarch","hippogryph protector","hippogryph youth","kalimdor","matriarch","shen'dar highlands","shen'dar village"},m={id=92516},src={"In-game quest text: Hippogryph Harassment"},fv=true}
E["quest:92517"] = {t="quest",n="The Criminal Element",z="general",s="The Highlands Bandits terrorize the Shen'dar Highlands from a cave behind a waterfall. A new cult has arrived, and local defenders are stretched thin. So outside help is needed against the gang's leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic.",h="The Highlands Bandits terrorize the Shen'dar Highlands from a cave behind a waterfall.",sec={{t="Outlaws Behind the Falls",b="The Highlands Bandits have made their den in a hidden cave behind a northern waterfall in the Shen'dar Highlands. Their leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic, commands cutthroats who troubled the locals long before an enigmatic cult arrived. Since then, their lawlessness has grown into terror. Local defenders are stretched thin and cannot spare forces, so you are sent to break the gang and bring Bennic down.",sp=0},{t="A Shift in the Shadows",b="After \"Badwind\" Bennic is eliminated, the Highlands Bandits lose their hold and the locals gain a brief respite. Yet surviving outlaws may seek shelter with the nearby cult. If it takes in these seasoned highwaymen, its ranks could swell and deepen the threat across the region.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Badwind\" Bennic?",a="\"Badwind\" Bennic leads the Highlands Bandits from a hidden cave behind a waterfall in the Shen'dar Highlands. His gang has long plagued the area, and the recent turmoil has made them an even greater terror.",al={"who is badwind bennic","bennic","badwind"}},{q="Where are the Highlands Bandits hiding?",a="The Highlands Bandits hide in a cave behind a waterfall to the north in the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"where are the bandits","bandit cave location","waterfall cave"}},{q="What is the cult mentioned in the area?",a="The cult is a new and alarming faction whose followers gather at Falaath Village to the south, and whose numbers are growing. The bandits were here before the cult arrived, but its presence has made the region more dangerous. Local forces worry that surviving bandits may seek refuge with the cult and strengthen its ranks.",al={"what cult","cult connection","who is the cult"}},{q="Why can't local forces handle the bandits themselves?",a="Local forces are stretched thin by the emerging cult and lack the manpower to clear out the bandits. Bringing Bennic down and scattering his gang removes an active threat from the region.",al={"why kill the bandits","bandit problem"}},{q="What happens to the bandits after Bennic is defeated?",a="With Bennic defeated, the bandits' hideout is scattered, but surviving outlaws may seek protection with the nearby cult and swell its already alarming numbers.",al={"what happens to surviving bandits","did all bandits die"}},{q="Where does this conflict take place?",a="The Highlands Bandits roam the Shen'dar Highlands, where they keep a hidden cave behind a waterfall.",al={"where is shendar highlands","shen'dar highlands"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know hidden caves behind waterfalls make familiar bandit hideouts. \"Badwind\" Bennic and his crew lack the care to stay out of the locals' sight and escape their anger."},kw={"badwind bennic","bennic","cult","highlands bandits","shen'dar highlands","the criminal element","waterfall cave"},m={id=92517},src={"In-game quest text: The Criminal Element"},fv=true}
E["quest:92519"] = {t="quest",n="Ward Restocking",z="general",s="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor is short of remedies, antidotes, and elixirs for the infirmary. The missing tonics are at Go'Shek Farm.",h="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor is short of remedies, antidotes, and elixirs for the infirmary.",sec={{t="A Shortage in the Ward",b="Doctor Gregory Victor tends Hammerfall’s wounded and ailing in the medical ward. The nearby Forsaken apothecary usually supplies the infirmary with remedies, antidotes, and elixirs. When those deliveries stop, Victor turns to capable travelers to keep the clinic stocked.",sp=0},{t="The Recluse of Go'Shek Farm",b="Apothecary Jorell works in a cramped shack at Go'Shek Farm, south and west of Hammerfall. Doctor Victor says Jorell is often absent. The eccentric Forsaken chemist may neglect his duties or succumb to his own noxious concoctions. Couriers sent for the packaged tonics should find the medicine waiting, whether Jorell is there or not.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Ward Restocking?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor oversees Hammerfall’s medical ward and infirmary. When regular deliveries fail, he asks dependable travelers to retrieve supplies.",al={"who gives ward restocking","quest giver ward restocking","doctor gregory victor quest"}},{q="Where is Apothecary Jorell located?",a="Apothecary Jorell works from a small shack at Go'Shek Farm, south and slightly west of Hammerfall along the road in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where is apothecary jorell","jorell lab location","where to find tonics"}},{q="Why does Doctor Gregory Victor send you to Go'Shek Farm?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor sends you to Go'Shek Farm because Apothecary Jorell failed to deliver an urgently needed crate of antidotes and elixirs to the Hammerfall infirmary.",al={"why go to goshek farm","what is at goshek farm"}},{q="What supplies are needed for the ward?",a="The ward needs a case of Packaged Tonics containing Apothecary Jorell’s antidotes and elixirs. They will replenish the Hammerfall medical ward’s dwindling stocks.",al={"what are packaged tonics","what items do you pick up"}},{q="Why hasn't Apothecary Jorell delivered the supplies himself?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor suspects Jorell either poisoned himself again while brewing concoctions in his poorly ventilated shack or neglected his duties to the ward.",al={"what happened to jorell","is jorell dead","why didn't jorell deliver"}},{q="Where must the supplies be delivered?",a="Bring the case of tonics from Go'Shek Farm to Doctor Gregory Victor at the medical ward in Hammerfall.",al={"where do tonics go","who to turn in ward restocking"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Hammerfall needs steady shipments of tonics and medicine. They help keep its soldiers, defenders, and travelers standing against threats in the Arathi Highlands.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know Apothecary Jorell carries the Royal Apothecary Society’s presence into Arathi. His erratic behavior and toxic experiments at Go'Shek Farm frustrate even his allies."},kw={"apothecary jorell","arathi highlands","doctor gregory victor","go'shek farm","hammerfall","packaged tonics","ward restocking"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","subzone:go-shek-farm","npc:doctor-gregory-victor"},m={id=92519},src={"In-game quest text: Ward Restocking"},fv=true}
E["quest:92528"] = {t="quest",n="Among the Faithful",z="general",s="At Falaath Village, you pass among the Faithful of Al'Akir in the Shen'dar Highlands. Their growing ranks and storm magic draw close scrutiny, while their leaders gather with plans that threaten nearby settlements and outposts.",h="At Falaath Village, you pass among the Faithful of Al'Akir in the Shen'dar Highlands.",sec={{t="Infiltrating Falaath Village",b="You enter Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands as an eager recruit among the Faithful of Al'Akir. The cultists boast that their ranks are growing. They claim their devotion gives the storm its shape and fury. New arrivals are usually sent to Skypriest Aanders for scrutiny, but an unexpected meeting at the village inn interrupts that routine.",sp=0},{t="The Secret Guest",b="Skypriest Aanders hosts a distinguished guest on the north side of town. While he is occupied, you can move through the settlement without his watch. Eavesdropping on the leaders reveals their immediate plan: a coordinated military push across the Shen'dar Highlands.",sp=1},{t="Lorthuna's Scheme",b="Lorthuna is the mysterious guest at the inn and the supreme commander of the entire cult. Her presence points to an aggressive strike against Shen'dar Village and the western watchtower. Shen'dar Village is a clear population center. Yet local scouts cannot understand why the remote lookout tower is a target or what lies behind the cult's storm-driven offensive.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who are the Faithful of Al'Akir?",a="The Faithful of Al'Akir are a cult devoted to the Windlord, Al'Akir. They are based around Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands, wield storm magic, and answer to Lorthuna.",al={"who are the faithful of alakir","what cult is this","alakir cult"}},{q="Who is Skypriest Aanders?",a="Skypriest Aanders is a ranking officer of the cult at Falaath Village. He assesses and inducts new recruits, though he is occupied at the village inn receiving an important guest during your infiltration.",al={"who is skypriest aanders","aanders","cult assessment guy"}},{q="Who is Lorthuna?",a="Lorthuna is the supreme leader of the cult of Al'Akir. Her covert presence at the Falaath Village inn reveals that the cult is arranging an imminent, high-level offensive in the highlands.",al={"who is lorthuna","cult leader lorthuna","guest at the inn"}},{q="Why is the cult targeting the western watchtower?",a="The cult plans simultaneous strikes on Shen'dar Village and the western watchtower. The village is an understandable target, but the watchtower's purpose in the attack remains a mystery to highland defenders.",al={"why attack the watchtower","western watchtower cult","cult targets"}},{q="Where does this take place?",a="Falaath Village lies in the Shen'dar Highlands. It is a major base and staging ground for the Faithful of Al'Akir and their new recruits.",al={"where is falaath village","falaath village location"}},{q="What are the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands?",a="The cult seeks to expand its influence and unleash storm magic across the Shen'dar Highlands. Under Lorthuna's leadership, its immediate assault targets Shen'dar Village and the western watchtower.",al={"what are the cults goals in shendar highlands","cult plans shendar"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you follow familiar holy or shadow faiths. At Falaath Village, the cultists follow Skypriests devoted to Al'Akir the Windlord and channel the storm's primal strength.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the elemental forces the cult of Al'Akir worships and commands through its mastery of storm energies."},kw={"al'akir","among the faithful","falaath village","lorthuna","shen'dar highlands","skypriest aanders","western watchtower","windlord"},rel={"quest:92529"},m={id=92528},src={"In-game quest text: Among the Faithful"},fv=true}
E["quest:92529"] = {t="quest",n="Falaath Village",z="general",s="At Falaath Village, marked recruits gather to seek the Windlord's favor. They come from Shen'dar Village to report to Missionary Jasaan and join the faithful.",h="At Falaath Village, marked recruits gather to seek the Windlord's favor.",sec={{t="Contrition for the Windlord",b="In Shen'dar Village, Sania Silverstream says her people grew prideful and took the bounty of the air for granted. The wind spirits abandoned them, and stagnation followed. Now penitent recruits receive the Mark of Akir and travel to Falaath Village. There, they join others who hope their acts of contrition will restore the wind's favor.",sp=0},{t="The Mission at Falaath",b="At Falaath Village, Missionary Jasaan welcomes initiates bearing the Mark of Akir. Jasaan sees each new acolyte as a blessing from the four winds. Those who arrive may seek the elemental grace of Al'Akir.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Falaath Village?",a="Marked recruits travel from Shen'dar Village to Falaath Village and report to Missionary Jasaan. There, they seek fellowship with the faithful.",al={"what is falaath village quest","falaath village overview","falaath village quest"}},{q="Who is Missionary Jasaan?",a="Missionary Jasaan is an acolyte near the entrance to Falaath Village. Jasaan welcomes recruits sent by Sania Silverstream to seek Al'Akir's blessings.",al={"who is missionary jasaan","jasaan lore","falaath missionary"}},{q="Who is Sania Silverstream?",a="Sania Silverstream is one of the faithful in Shen'dar Village. She gives new recruits the Mark of Akir and directs them to Falaath Village.",al={"who is sania silverstream","sania lore","sister sania"}},{q="Why are the shen'dorei worshipping Al'Akir?",a="The followers believe their people grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The spirits abandoned them, and through acts of contrition they seek to regain Al'Akir's favor.",al={"why worship alakir","windlord alakir worship","who is the windlord"}},{q="What is the Mark of Akir?",a="The Mark of Akir is a sign Sania Silverstream gives recruits in Shen'dar Village. It identifies them as members of the faithful before they enter Falaath Village.",al={"what is mark of akir","lost mark of akir","recruits mark"}},{q="Who are the shen'dorei mentioned in the quest?",a="The shen'dorei Sania speaks of are elves facing stagnation after the wind spirits withdrew their favor. Some seek atonement through devotion to the elements.",al={"who are the shendorei","shen dorei lore"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a shen'dorei seeking to restore your bond with the winds, you join the faithful at Falaath Village in shared contrition. There, you hope to regain Al'Akir's favor.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you seek harmony with elemental spirits. The faithful approach Al'Akir through penitence and religious devotion, hoping to reclaim the winds that abandoned them."},kw={"al'akir","falaath village","mark of akir","missionary jasaan","sania silverstream","shen'dar village","shen'dorei","windlord"},m={id=92529},src={"In-game quest text: Falaath Village"},fv=true}
E["quest:92550"] = {t="quest",n="Havoc in the Highlands",z="general",s="In the highlands, Shen'dar Village moves against Al'Aketh forces at Falaath Village. Its defenders mean to stop an assault before it begins and protect their home.",h="In the highlands, Shen'dar Village moves against Al'Aketh forces at Falaath Village.",sec={{t="A Preemptive Strike",b="Zealous cultists are preparing to assault Shen'dar Village. So its leaders send you into the ruins of Falaath Village to strike first, before the Al'Aketh forces can begin their attack.",sp=0},{t="Assault on Falaath Village",b="Al'Aketh zealots gather at Falaath Village and wield chaotic elemental power. You break their ranks by defeating Al'Aketh Stormcallers and shattering Living Lightning. Then you find Commander Cyclas and behead him.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Highlands",b="Commander Cyclas is slain, and his vanguard lies devastated. Shen'dar Village gains a vital reprieve. As the citizens take up arms, Sania Silverstream slips out of town unnoticed. She flees while the local defense gathers strength.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Havoc in the Highlands?",a="Shen'dar Village strikes first against Al'Aketh cultists in the ruins of Falaath Village. Its defenders hope to stop an assault before it begins.",al={"havoc in the highlands quest","what is havoc in the highlands","highlands quest"}},{q="Who is threatening Shen'dar Village?",a="The Al'Aketh threaten Shen'dar Village. They worship elemental storms and field Stormcallers, bound Living Lightning, and Commander Cyclas, their leader.",al={"who are the enemies","what cult is this","who attacks shendar"}},{q="Where are the cultists massing?",a="The cultists gather in the ruins of Falaath Village. Commander Cyclas and his Al'Aketh followers use it as their staging ground.",al={"where is commander cyclas","falaath village ruins","where to go"}},{q="Who is Commander Cyclas?",a="Commander Cyclas leads the Al'Aketh forces gathered in the ruins of Falaath Village. They prepare to march on Shen'dar.",al={"who is commander cyclas","cyclas lore","cyclas cult"}},{q="Why did Sania Silverstream flee Shen'dar Village?",a="Sania Silverstream slips out of Shen'dar Village just before its defenders rally. She likely flees after seeing the locals take up arms and organize their defense.",al={"sania silverstream fleeing","why did sania leave","who is sania silverstream"}},{q="Does the strike successfully secure Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village turns back the immediate threat by breaking the cultists' forward ranks and beheading Commander Cyclas. Returning zealots will find the highlands ready to resist.",al={"did shendar survive","aftermath of the attack","is shendar safe"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know Al'Aketh Stormcallers and their summoned Living Lightning wield the elements. The cultists twist wind and storm into weapons of fanatical aggression."},kw={"al'aketh","commander cyclas","falaath village","havoc in the highlands","living lightning","sania silverstream","shen'dar village","stormcallers"},rel={"quest:92529"},m={id=92550},src={"In-game quest text: Havoc in the Highlands"},fv=true}
E["quest:92551"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Supplies",z="general",s="Caravans bound for the Shen'dar Highlands are under attack, and their stolen goods gather in Falaath Village. Food and windstones grow scarce in the highland settlements, leaving some skyborne close to starvation.",h="Caravans bound for the Shen'dar Highlands are under attack, and their stolen goods gather in Falaath Village.",sec={{t="Raids on the Highland Lifeline",b="For months, raiders have attacked caravans on the road between the lowlands and the Shen'dar Highlands. Their wagons carry food and windstones that highland settlements depend on. As fewer deliveries arrive, townsfolk struggle to get by, and some draw close to starvation.",sp=0},{t="The Falaath Cache",b="The Al'Aketh blame common bandits for the attacks. Yet the missing supplies keep turning up in Falaath Village, where the Al'Aketh store the stolen packs. The recovered goods go to the local authorities and constable, who send them straight to the skyborne in greatest need.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What supplies were stolen from the caravans?",a="Caravans between the lowlands and highlands carried food and windstones. Regular deliveries help keep local townsfolk fed and supplied.",al={"what was stolen","supplies taken","what goods were stolen"}},{q="Who is responsible for raiding the caravans?",a="The Al'Aketh have raided the supply caravans for months. They blame ordinary bandits, yet stolen packs keep turning up in Falaath Village.",al={"who stole the supplies","who raided the caravans","caravan attackers"}},{q="Where are the stolen supply caches being held?",a="The Al'Aketh store the stolen supply packs in Falaath Village, within the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"where are the supplies","where to find supplies","stolen caches location"}},{q="Why are these supply caravans being targeted?",a="The caravans carry food and windstones between the lowlands and highlands. The raids leave local skyborne short of supplies while highland goods gather in Falaath Village.",al={"why steal windstones and food","why caravan raids"}},{q="What happens to the supplies once they are recovered?",a="Once recovered, the supplies go to the local constable and authorities. They redistribute them to the townsfolk most in need of food and relief.",al={"who gets the supplies back","supplies redistribution","what happens after recovery"}},{q="Why do the Al'Aketh blame bandits for the raids?",a="The Al'Aketh blame roving bandits to deflect responsibility. Yet stolen cargo keeps turning up in their settlement at Falaath Village.",al={"why blame bandits","al aketh bandits excuse"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="The raids break the lifeline between the highlands and lowlands. Without regular deliveries of food and windstones, skyborne townsfolk go hungry."},kw={"al'aketh","caravans","constable","falaath village","shen'dar highlands","skyborne","stolen supplies","windstones"},rel={"quest:92529","topic:skyborne"},m={id=92551},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Supplies"},fv=true}
E["quest:92553"] = {t="quest",n="Restocking the Larders",z="general",s="In the Shen'dar Highlands of Zephras, a village cook needs help keeping the food stores full. Danger keeps the villagers from foraging, so the cook turns to you for eggs and strider meat.",h="In the Shen'dar Highlands of Zephras, a village cook needs help keeping the food stores full.",sec={{t="Dangers in the Highlands",b="Rising dangers make life harder in the Shen'dar Highlands. Villagers can no longer safely enter the wilderness to forage or hunt, and the communal stores are nearly empty. So local cooks rely on travelers willing to brave the wild trails and help keep the settlement fed.",sp=0},{t="Sustenance and Comfort",b="The cook asks you to find strider meat and fresh small eggs among the highlands' wildlife. In return, the cook shares knowledge of local game and its recipes. Small eggs fried in ursera tallow offer comfort, with dried peacebloom for a quiet pipe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What supplies are needed for Restocking the Larders?",a="The local cook needs three Small Eggs and eight cuts of Strider Meat to feed the village while danger keeps ordinary foragers indoors.",al={"restocking larders objective","what to collect restocking larders"}},{q="Where can the ingredients be found?",a="Wild creatures throughout the Shen'dar Highlands on Zephras provide the strider meat and small eggs.",al={"where get strider meat zephras","egg locations shendar"}},{q="Why is the village running low on food?",a="Rising dangers make it too perilous for ordinary villagers to hunt or forage, leaving the food stores depleted.",al={"why need food zephras","why village hungry shendar"}},{q="What reward does the cook offer for the food?",a="The cook offers culinary tips, techniques, and training in local recipes in exchange for fresh provisions.",al={"what does quest giver offer","cooking training quest"}},{q="What are the Shen'dar Highlands and Zephras?",a="The Shen'dar Highlands lie on Zephras, where locals face mounting threats while trying to sustain their daily lives.",al={"what is zephras","where is shendar highlands"}},{q="How does the cook prepare the eggs?",a="The cook fries freshly gathered small eggs in ursera tallow, a comfort on Zephras.",al={"tallow cooking secret","how are eggs cooked zephras"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, gathering strider meat and small eggs gives you practical experience and recipes suited to Zephras wildlife."},kw={"cooking","restocking the larders","shendar highlands","small eggs","strider meat","ursera tallow","zephras"},m={id=92553},src={"In-game quest text: Restocking the Larders"},fv=true}
E["quest:92579"] = {t="quest",n="To Valanaar",z="general",s="Aonda sends an urgent report across the island to Valanaar, where the peacekeepers prepare for a growing threat. Their leader, Valennia Stormfist, must ready her people as conflict with the cult draws near.",h="Aonda sends an urgent report across the island to Valanaar, where the peacekeepers prepare for a growing...",sec={{t="An Urgent Dispatch",b="After you help defend Shen'dar and its pylon, Aonda entrusts you with urgent word for Valennia Stormfist. Valanaar lies at the island's southeastern edge, where the peacekeepers keep their headquarters under Valennia's command. Aonda warns that the peaceful days are ending. Valennia must prepare her people for an inevitable clash with the aggressive, expanding cult.",sp=0},{t="The Gathering Storm",b="The peacekeepers avoided direct conflict with the mysterious cult until its incursions drove tensions to a breaking point. After reading Aonda's report, Valennia knows they must gather their remaining forces and plan a defense. The cult may turn its attention to Valanaar itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Valanaar?",a="Aonda, a highlander in Shen'dar, sends you to Valanaar. After you help secure the village and pylon from the looming cultist threat, she entrusts you with an urgent written report to carry across the island.",al={"who gives to valanaar","quest giver to valanaar","who sends me to valanaar"}},{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist leads the island's peacekeepers from their headquarters in Valanaar. She is responsible for local defense and order, including responses to the cult's aggressive expansion.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","valennia leader","valennia"}},{q="What is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is a settlement at the island's southeastern edge. It is the peacekeepers' base under Valennia Stormfist, as well as a refuge and community hub for townsfolk.",al={"what is valanaar","where is valanaar","valanaar location"}},{q="What is the purpose of Aonda's report?",a="Aonda's report describes the cult's growing threat and the events that put Shen'dar and its pylon at risk. The peacekeepers avoided direct conflict, but the cult's rapid expansion makes a clash inevitable. Valanaar must prepare its defenses.",al={"why deliver report","what is aonda report","what is in the letter"}},{q="What threat does the cult pose to the island?",a="The report warns that an unnamed cult is expanding rapidly across the island. The peacekeepers kept their distance to avoid open warfare, but the cult's recent aggressive moves against places such as Shen'dar mean conflict can no longer be avoided.",al={"what cult to valanaar","who is the cult","cult threat island"}},{q="What happens once you reach Valanaar?",a="When Valennia receives the grim news, she must confer with her remaining peacekeepers and plan a defense against future cult attacks. As she coordinates their plans, she invites travelers to help the townsfolk around Valanaar.",al={"what to do after delivering report","what next to valanaar"}}},kw={"aonda","cult","peacekeepers","shen'dar","to valanaar","valanaar","valennia stormfist"},m={id=92579},src={"In-game quest text: To Valanaar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92595"] = {t="quest",n="The Windshapers",z="general",s="Among the wind spirits, The Windshapers seek a way to keep Zephras and the Shen'dorei alive. Illaya Amberwind welcomes new recruits to their work, as dangers gather in Skywall.",h="Among the wind spirits, The Windshapers seek a way to keep Zephras and the Shen'dorei alive.",sec={{t="Mandate of the Windshapers",b="Illaya Amberwind welcomes new recruits into the Windshapers, who commune with the wind spirits and protect the Shen'dorei. The order seeks those born with spiritual perception. They hope to mend the growing rift between their people and the elemental forces that sustain their aerial realm. Every Windshaper bears that burden.",sp=0},{t="Trials on Zephras",b="The Al'Aketh bring turmoil within Skywall, and the elemental plane holds dangers of its own. The Windshapers believe Zephras can endure and the Shen'dorei can weather the storm only if they restore their bond with the spirits of the winds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers commune with the wind spirits and protect the Shen'dorei. Guided by Illaya Amberwind, they seek people gifted with skysight to restore their bond with the spirits and preserve their imperiled homeland.",al={"who are windshapers","windshapers faction","what do windshapers do"}},{q="What is skysight?",a="Skysight is an inborn spiritual sensitivity that lets a person connect with the aerial elements. Formal shaman training is not needed, but commanding skysight is essential to reaching the spirits of the winds.",al={"what is skysight","skysight lore"}},{q="Who is Illaya Amberwind?",a="Illaya Amberwind guides the Windshapers and recognizes spiritual gifts in travelers. She welcomes those with skysight and explains the order's work, the peril facing Zephras, and the trials confronting the Shen'dorei.",al={"who is illaya","illaya amberwind"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is an aerial land or settlement enduring severe hardships and internal unrest. The Windshapers struggle to protect it and preserve a future for their people there.",al={"what is zephras","zephras lore"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are a hostile faction within, troubling the Windshapers and the Shen'dorei. Their threat adds to the dangers of surviving within Skywall.",al={"who are the al'aketh","alaketh threat"}},{q="Who are the Shen'dorei?",a="The Shen'dorei are the people the Windshapers seek to protect. The Al'Aketh and perilous conditions in Skywall threaten their survival, so the Windshapers seek to secure it by restoring balance with the winds.",al={"who are shendorei","shen'dorei lore"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may commune with the elements through training, but skysight can appear in others too. The Windshapers share this spiritual duty with elemental callers.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you know the Windshapers fight for the Shen'dorei's survival and home amid the perils of Skywall and Zephras."},kw={"al'aketh","illaya amberwind","shen'dorei","skysight","skywall","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"topic:skywall","topic:shaman"},m={id=92595},src={"In-game quest text: The Windshapers"},fv=true}
E["quest:92596"] = {t="quest",n="The High Order",z="general",s="On Zephras, Rathiril Sunlance tells newcomers why the shen'dorei must now stand alone. Their elemental benefactors are gone, so these Highborne descendants of Eldre'Thalas turn to ancient arcane magic to protect their people.",h="On Zephras, Rathiril Sunlance tells newcomers why the shen'dorei must now stand alone.",sec={{t="A People on Their Own",b="The shen'dorei on Zephras are working to reclaim their strength and choose their own path. For a long time, elemental benefactors protected them. Now those patrons are gone, leaving the people exposed to strife within and dangers around them. Rathiril Sunlance seeks those gifted in arcane magic to help preserve their people and build their strength on their own.",sp=0},{t="Legacy of Eldre'Thalas",b="The shen'dorei carry the legacy of Eldre'Thalas and an innate wellspring of arcane energy. Even those never formally trained in wizardry share that power. The High Order sees it as the destiny of Highborne descendants to wield these ancient gifts. With them, the shen'dorei hope to resist the Al'Aketh within and face the many threats to their home on Zephras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the High Order?",a="Among the shen'dorei on Zephras, the High Order works for their people's survival. Founded by descendants of the Highborne of Eldre'Thalas, it seeks to wield their ancient arcane gifts so their society can defend itself and endure on its own.",al={"who are the high order","what is high order","high order purpose"}},{q="Who is Rathiril Sunlance?",a="Rathiril Sunlance is an elf associated with the High Order on Zephras. He teaches newcomers about local arcane energies, the shen'dorei's plight, and their resolve to survive without their former elemental patrons.",al={"who is rathiril","rathiril sunlance lore","sunlance"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is a floating isle in Skywall where Rathiril Sunlance and his kin now live. Arcane energies fill the isle, and the shen'dorei face dangers within their people and uncertainty about their security from outside threats.",al={"where is the high order","what is zephras","zephras lore"}},{q="Who are the shen'dorei?",a="The shen'dorei are elf descendants of the Highborne from Eldre'Thalas. Now living on Zephras, they have an innate bond with arcane magic and seek to stand on their own.",al={"who are the shendorei","shen dorei","shendorei lore"}},{q="Who were the elemental benefactors?",a="The elemental benefactors were powerful elemental beings who once aided and protected the shen'dorei. They are gone, so the people of Zephras must rely on their own magic and resourcefulness.",al={"who are the elementals","elemental patrons","elemental benefactors"}},{q="What are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are an internal faction or threat that endangers the shen'dorei on Zephras. The High Order organizes defenses in part to face such threats from within.",al={"what is alaketh","al aketh threat","internal threats zephras"}},{q="What is the connection between the High Order and Eldre'Thalas?",a="The shen'dorei's ancestors came from Eldre'Thalas, the ancient Highborne city in Kalimdor known to many in the years after the Third War as Dire Maul. The High Order honors this heritage by preserving and wielding their ancient arcane gifts.",al={"eldrethalas connection","are they from dire maul","highborne origins"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Rathiril says that even adventurers without formal mage training carry strong arcane auras. Their shared magic is an inborn heritage, not only a learned discipline.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you descend from the ancient Highborne of Eldre'Thalas. You must master your arcane gifts to stand on your own now that your elemental patrons are gone."},kw={"al'aketh","arcane","eldre'thalas","highborne","rathiril sunlance","shen'dorei","the high order","zephras"},rel={"topic:highborne","topic:mage"},m={id=92596},src={"In-game quest text: The High Order"},fv=true}
E["quest:92640"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Times",z="general",s="Valennia Stormfist waits in Valanaar with a plan to strike the cult at its shrine. Lorthuna must be stopped there, but the Windshapers and the High Order must first set aside their deep tensions.",h="Valennia Stormfist waits in Valanaar with a plan to strike the cult at its shrine.",sec={{t="A Direct Strike",b="The cult cannot be safely faced in the open, so the defenders need a bolder plan. They will strike at the cult's shrine instead of fighting a long battle on unfavorable ground. If they eliminate Lorthuna before she completes her part in the cult's grand scheme, they can cripple the threat at its source.",sp=0},{t="Uniting Divided Factions",b="In Valanaar, Valennia Stormfist has spent time planning an assault on the shrine. The attack needs substantial reinforcements and strength united across the factions. Yet the Windshapers and the High Order remain divided by severe political tensions, putting their alliance at risk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist is in Valanaar, where she has been planning an assault on the cult's shrine. The attack depends on cooperation between rival factions.",al={"who is valennia","valennia stormfist","where is valennia"}},{q="Who is Lorthuna?",a="Lorthuna is a key figure in the hostile cult. She is directing a critical scheme at the shrine, making her the target of the planned strike.",al={"who is lorthuna","lorthuna lore","cult leader lorthuna"}},{q="Why must the shrine be attacked directly?",a="The cult cannot be safely confronted in the open. The plan is to strike at the shrine and stop Lorthuna before her scheme comes to fruition.",al={"why attack shrine","cult attack reason"}},{q="What is the issue between the Windshapers and the High Order?",a="Tensions run high between the Windshapers and the High Order. Neither faction can carry out the assault on the shrine alone, so both must cooperate.",al={"high order windshapers tension","why are factions fighting","windshaper dispute"}},{q="Where is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is where Valennia Stormfist is coordinating the plan and rallying allies for a strike against the cult's shrine.",al={"where is valanaar","valanaar location"}},{q="What is the overall goal of this mission?",a="The goal is to find Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, learn the details of her planned strike, and help secure cooperation between the divided factions.",al={"desperate times objective","what is the plan desperate times"}}},kw={"cult","desperate times","high order","lorthuna","shrine","valanaar","valennia stormfist","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=92640},src={"In-game quest text: Desperate Times"},fv=true}
E["quest:92642"] = {t="quest",n="Disrupting Logistics",z="general",s="At the Gustberry Lowlands, Al'Aketh cultists are pressing a full-scale assault. Their healers keep the brawlers fighting, and the defenders need help before their lines give way.",h="At the Gustberry Lowlands, Al'Aketh cultists are pressing a full-scale assault.",sec={{t="A Desperate Defense",b="A fierce assault is bearing down on the defenders above the Gustberry Lowlands. Enemy forces are gathering, and the local lines are near breaking. The commanders expected substantial reinforcements from Valennia, but they must rely on whatever capable hands arrive. Strikes against the enemy's support may be the only way to hold the defense together.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Cultist Line",b="Al'Aketh brawlers press forward in ranks, sustained by healers who mend their wounds. In the Gustberry Lowlands, taking out those healers can break the cultists' push. That gives the defenders a chance to rally and drive back the invasion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Disrupting Logistics?",a="Disrupting Logistics is a desperate defense against the Al'Aketh assault in the Gustberry Lowlands. A lone defender needs help taking out the enemy's front-line support before the defense collapses.",al={"what is disrupting logistics","disrupting logistics quest","gustberry lowlands quest"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh cultists attacking the lowlands?",a="Al'Aketh cultists are attacking the Gustberry Lowlands with brawlers and healers. Their organized front depends on healing support to keep pressure on the local defenders.",al={"who are alaketh","who is attacking gustberry lowlands","who are the cultists"}},{q="Why are the Al'Aketh healers specifically targeted?",a="The Al'Aketh healers keep the vanguard fighters pressing forward. Taking them out may break the assault's momentum and give the defenders a chance to rally and push the cultists back.",al={"why kill healers","why target alaketh healers"}},{q="Where does this assault take place?",a="The assault is taking place in the Gustberry Lowlands, directly down the hill from the defensive outpost. Al'Aketh brawlers and healers have overrun the lowlands and are pressing their attack.",al={"where is gustberry lowlands","gustberry lowlands location"}},{q="Who is Valennia?",a="Valennia appears to organize aid and reinforcements. The defender is exasperated that Valennia sent only one adventurer against a massive assault.",al={"who is valennia","valennia reinforcements"}},{q="Who commands the defense against the Al'Aketh?",a="A beleaguered defender offers the call for aid as their people near defeat before the Al'Aketh. The defender reveres 'the winds' and needs any fighting force that can turn the battle.",al={"who gives disrupting logistics","who are my people holding out"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know how healing support can sustain an offensive line. The Al'Aketh healers are the linchpin of the cultist assault.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the value of slipping behind enemy lines to eliminate healers and disrupt reinforcements."},kw={"al'aketh","brawlers","cultists","disrupting logistics","gustberry lowlands","healers","valennia"},m={id=92642},src={"In-game quest text: Disrupting Logistics"},fv=true}
E["quest:92643"] = {t="quest",n="The Turncoat",z="general",s="A cultist of the Al'Aketh offers to defect and reveal what the cult intends for the island. You are sent to bring him from a secluded highland retreat northwest of Valanaar, where the meeting may be a trap.",h="A cultist of the Al'Aketh offers to defect and reveal what the cult intends for the island.",sec={{t="A Broken Oath",b="A cultist within the Al'Aketh ranks claims to know the cult's true intentions for the island. He offers to defect, but demands firm assurances of protection. The cult guards its plans closely, so reaching out may be worth the danger.",sp=0},{t="The Highland Hideout",b="The defector waits alone in a secluded residence in the highlands northwest of Valanaar. You must reach him with care. The meeting may be an Al'Aketh ambush meant to draw out those who pry into the cult's affairs.",sp=0},{t="Silence in the Highlands",b="The defector lies dead inside the secluded highland house. Assassins tracked him down and struck before an escort could arrive. Outside, fallen assassins mark the aftermath. A gleam on the dead turncoat's body hints that he left an answer behind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the turncoat?",a="The turncoat was a former member of the Al'Aketh cult who claimed to know the cult's true intentions for the island. He offered to defect and share what he knew in exchange for protection.",al={"who is the turncoat","who was the defector","turncoat identity"}},{q="What is the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are an enigmatic cult operating in the region. Their plans for the island remain hidden behind secrecy and zealotry, so local authorities risk much to reach deserters willing to speak.",al={"who are the alaketh","alaketh cult","what is alaketh"}},{q="Where is the defector hiding?",a="The defector hid in a secluded residence in the highlands northwest of Valanaar. He waited there for an escort, trusting in promises of protection.",al={"where is the turncoat hiding","turncoat location","where to find the turncoat"}},{q="What happened to the defector?",a="By the time anyone reached the secluded highland residence, assassins had tracked down and slain the defector. He was found dead inside the house, beyond questioning.",al={"what happened to the turncoat","did the defector die","who killed the turncoat"}},{q="What did the turncoat leave behind?",a="After the assassins outside were dealt with, a glint on the dead defector's body caught the eye. The shiny item remained, and may hold a clue to the secrets he carried.",al={"what shiny object","turncoat shiny item","shiny reflection body"}},{q="Why did the cultist decide to defect?",a="The cultist claims to know the Al'Aketh's true intentions for the island and will defect only with assurances of protection. What drove him to leave the cult is not known.",al={"why did the cultist defect","turncoat motive","why betray alaketh"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Infiltration, defection, and ambush are familiar to a Rogue. Cultists who break ranks risk silence or a blade. The assassins outside show how secrecy can cut both ways in the highlands."},kw={"al'aketh","cultist","defector","highlands","the turncoat","turncoat","valanaar"},m={id=92643},src={"In-game quest text: The Turncoat"},fv=true}
E["quest:92644"] = {t="quest",n="Unfortunate News",z="general",s="You find the turncoat dead before they can speak. A damaged blue crystal remains beneath the body, and you carry it to High Elder Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",h="You find the turncoat dead before they can speak.",sec={{t="A Broken Rendezvous",b="You reach the rendezvous and find the defecting cultist already slain. Their body is still warm. Beneath it lies a small, glowing blue crystal, damaged but still humming. You carry it to High Elder Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",sp=0},{t="Shadowsong's Investigation",b="You return to Valanaar alone and tell High Elder Talanaanis Shadowsong that the turncoat died before giving testimony. The loss of a living contact is a serious setback. Yet the damaged blue crystal catches the High Elder's eye. He finds it interesting and takes it from you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Unfortunate News?",a="You find the defecting cultist dead before they can speak. Beneath the body lies a damaged, glowing blue crystal, which you carry to High Elder Talanaanis Shadowsong.",al={"what is unfortunate news","unfortunate news quest","unfortunate news wow forever"}},{q="Who was the turncoat cultist?",a="The turncoat was a defecting cultist you were sent to meet. They were killed before they could speak or escape, leaving a still-warm body and a damaged crystal.",al={"who is the dead turncoat","who died in unfortunate news","turncoat cultist"}},{q="Who is High Elder Shadowsong?",a="Talanaanis Shadowsong is an elf and the High Elder in Valanaar. He directs investigations into the cultists and receives the damaged crystal from the turncoat's body.",al={"who is shadowsong in valanaar","where is talanaanis shadowsong","talanaanis shadowsong"}},{q="What is the damaged blue crystal?",a="The damaged blue crystal is a small, glowing crystal found beneath the fallen turncoat. High Elder Shadowsong finds it interesting and takes it from you.",al={"what is the glowing crystal","blue crystal from cultist","damaged crystal unfortunate news"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="Valanaar is where High Elder Talanaanis Shadowsong resides. You return there with your report and the recovered crystal.",al={"where is valanaar","valanaar location","turn in unfortunate news"}},{q="How does this quest connect to The Turncoat?",a="This follows The Turncoat, in which you set out to find the defecting cultist. You arrive too late to save them.",al={"what quest comes before unfortunate news","unfortunate news prequel","the turncoat quest"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you may recognize the damaged, glowing blue crystal as an artifact. High Elder Shadowsong investigates the cultists and takes the crystal for study."},kw={"cultist","glowing crystal","shadowsong","talanaanis shadowsong","turncoat","unfortunate news","valanaar"},rel={"quest:92643"},m={id=92644},src={"In-game quest text: Unfortunate News"},fv=true}
E["quest:92645"] = {t="quest",n="Breaking the Breaker",z="general",s="In the Gustberry Lowlands, cultists press the defenders hard. Commander Belguilos leads the assault from her hillside villa, and striking her there may be the defenders’ only chance to survive.",h="In the Gustberry Lowlands, cultists press the defenders hard.",sec={{t="A Desperate Defense",b="Cultists assault the Gustberry Lowlands, driving the local defenders to the brink. Repelling them seems nearly impossible while Commander Belguilos directs the attack. All fear her as “the Breaker.”\n\nHer villa is the operation’s base. Slaying her there is perilous, near-suicidal, yet passivity leaves the defenders doomed.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Peacekeeper",b="Before she commanded the cultists, Belguilos kept order as a peacekeeper. Even then, those around her found something deeply unsettling in her manner. When the cult’s influence spread beyond control, she embraced its extremism. Now she commands the cultists and is a terror.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Belguilos the Breaker?",a="Belguilos, called “the Breaker,” commands the cultist attack. Before joining the cult, she served as a peacekeeper, though those around her found her unsettling even then.",al={"who is belguilos","who is the breaker","cult commander"}},{q="Where can Commander Belguilos be found?",a="Commander Belguilos is at the villa at the base of the hill in the Gustberry Lowlands. From there, she coordinates the cultist assault on the local defenders.",al={"where is belguilos","belguilos location","where to find the breaker"}},{q="Why must Belguilos be eliminated?",a="The cultists’ onslaught is nearly impossible to repel while Belguilos directs it. Eliminating her breaks the cult’s leadership and gives the defenders a real chance to survive.",al={"why kill belguilos","cult attack reason","why is breaker dangerous"}},{q="What was Belguilos's past before joining the cult?",a="Before the cult’s influence spread beyond control, Belguilos served as a peacekeeper. Those who knew her found something deeply unsettling in her even then.",al={"what was belguilos before","was belguilos good","peacekeeper cultist"}},{q="What is the significance of the blessing of the four winds?",a="The blessing of the four winds is an expression of profound relief and gratitude among the defenders after the terrifying cult commander has been permanently stopped.",al={"four winds meaning","who says four winds bless you"}},{q="What are the Gustberry Lowlands?",a="The Gustberry Lowlands are contested ground where the cult assault unfolds. Commander Belguilos can be found at a villa at the base of the hill.",al={"what is gustberry lowlands","where is breaker quest"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="The defenders invoke the four winds to bless the hero after the cultists are stopped.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Commander Belguilos, a former peacekeeper feared as “the Breaker.”"},kw={"belguilos","breaking the breaker","commander belguilos","cult commander","gustberry lowlands","peacekeeper","the breaker","villa"},m={id=92645},src={"In-game quest text: Breaking the Breaker"},fv=true}
E["quest:92646"] = {t="quest",n="Confront Lorthuna",z="general",s="Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger pursue High Priestess Lorthuna through a portal into the Rohashi Spires above Zephras. They call for your aid before she can escape justice or strengthen her power.",h="Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger pursue High Priestess Lorthuna through a portal into the Rohashi...",sec={{t="Pursuit into the Spires",b="High Priestess Lorthuna flees through a mystic gateway into the Rohashi Spires above Zephras. An injured ally remains behind at the portal's threshold. Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger follow her into the heights and call for your help before she escapes justice or strengthens her power.",sp=0},{t="The Cost of the Battle",b="After the clash in the spires, Valennia and her surviving forces need a healer's care. They are escorted to recover within the High Elder's residence. Lorthuna has met them in combat, and the coalition is battered with its resources stretched thin.",sp=1},{t="An Island Left Vulnerable",b="After the battle, Muln confers on the Windshapers and their continuing mission, then departs for mainland Azeroth. Zephras remains critically vulnerable. The leaders left behind must urgently plan defenses against the dangers that still threaten the island.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is High Priestess Lorthuna?",a="High Priestess Lorthuna is a powerful adversary who flees through a portal to the Rohashi Spires above Zephras. Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale pursue her there.",al={"who is lorthuna","what is lorthuna","high priestess lorthuna lore"}},{q="What are the Rohashi Spires?",a="The Rohashi Spires are heights above the island of Zephras. High Priestess Lorthuna flees there through a portal, and her pursuers follow.",al={"what are rohashi spires","where is the portal going","rohashi spires location"}},{q="Who pursued Lorthuna into the portal?",a="Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger pursue High Priestess Lorthuna through the portal as she flees to the spires. They call for your aid.",al={"who went after lorthuna","ayessa and elaadrin","who enters the portal"}},{q="What happened to Valennia and her forces?",a="Valennia and her surviving forces need immediate care after the fighting. Healers tend them, and they are escorted to recover in the High Elder's residence.",al={"who is valennia","what happened to valennia","valennia forces"}},{q="What is Muln's role in these events?",a="Muln is an ally associated with the Windshapers who departs for mainland Azeroth after discussing their future and continuing mission.",al={"who is muln","muln leaving zephras","where did muln go"}},{q="Is the island of Zephras safe after Lorthuna is confronted?",a="Zephras remains critically vulnerable after the confrontation. Its leaders must urgently plan defenses against the dangers threatening the island.",al={"what happens to zephras","is zephras safe now","state of zephras island"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you face High Priestess Lorthuna, a corrupted spiritual leader among the spires. The battle against her carries weight for those who defend against dark doctrine.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you share a spiritual stake in the Windshapers' work to guide elemental balance on Zephras. You can help ensure that harmony survives Lorthuna's threat."},kw={"ayessa dawnsinger","confront lorthuna","elaadrin evengale","high priestess lorthuna","lorthuna","muln","rohashi spires","valennia","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","quest:92595"},m={id=92646},src={"In-game quest text: Confront Lorthuna"},fv=true}
E["quest:92679"] = {t="quest",n="Blood Tithe",z="general",s="In Valanaar, Alvarion Windfield seeks aid for the orchard that sustains his family. Pain keeps the Skyborne farmer from his work, so he sends travelers west to his wife, Aamelia, who tends their lowland farm.",h="In Valanaar, Alvarion Windfield seeks aid for the orchard that sustains his family.",sec={{t="A Plea in Valanaar",b="Alvarion Windfield has come from his homestead to Valanaar in search of capable fighters. Pain leaves him visibly injured, and he fears for the livelihood his farm provides. He asks you to travel west into the lowlands, where his wife Aamelia tends their family orchard.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Lowlands",b="The Windfield Orchard lies in the lowlands west of Valanaar. Alvarion is too ill to tend the farm, so Aamelia Windfield bears its burdens alone. Reach the western valley, learn what threatens the orchard, and lend the family your strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alvarion Windfield?",a="Alvarion Windfield is a Skyborne farmer in Valanaar who seeks fighters to protect his home. Though severe pain troubles him, he sends travelers to his wife, Aamelia, at their orchard.",al={"who is alvarion","alvarion windfield lore","who gives blood tithe"}},{q="Where is the Windfield Orchard located?",a="The Windfield Orchard lies in the lowlands west of Valanaar. Alvarion directs travelers there to find his wife, Aamelia Windfield, who oversees the farm's defense.",al={"where is windfield orchard","aamelia windfield location","how to find the orchard"}},{q="Why is Alvarion in pain?",a="Alvarion's affliction is unknown when travelers meet him. Intense, debilitating pain troubles him as he speaks, lending urgency to his plea for help.",al={"why is alvarion hurting","what is wrong with alvarion","alvarion pain"}},{q="Who is Aamelia Windfield?",a="Aamelia Windfield is Alvarion's wife and tends their family orchard west of Valanaar. He sends willing travelers to help her defend their land.",al={"who is aamelia","aamelia windfield lore","alvarion wife"}},{q="What is the task in Blood Tithe?",a="Alvarion Windfield seeks help in Valanaar for his struggling farm. He asks you to find his wife, Aamelia, at their lowland orchard.",al={"blood tithe quest summary","what is blood tithe about","farm under attack valanaar"}},{q="What is Valanaar's significance here?",a="Valanaar is a settlement where travelers and Skyborne gather. Alvarion comes there seeking capable fighters to save his orchard from peril.",al={"valanaar lore","where does blood tithe take place","what is valanaar"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne farmer, Alvarion Windfield suffers and calls desperately for aid. His hardship shows what Skyborne face beyond Valanaar."},kw={"aamelia windfield","alvarion windfield","blood tithe","skyborne","valanaar","windfield orchard"},rel={"topic:skyborne","quest:92579"},m={id=92679},src={"In-game quest text: Blood Tithe"},fv=true}
E["quest:92682"] = {t="quest",n="Make Yourself Useful",z="general",s="At Windfield Orchard, Ferauu's bandits are taking stormapples before their share is due. Some hungry outlaws have broken ranks to pick the trees early. Drive them off, and the orchard keeper will respect you.",h="At Windfield Orchard, Ferauu's bandits are taking stormapples before their share is due.",sec={{t="Trouble at Windfield Orchard",b="Windfield Orchard gives Ferauu's bandits a regular share of its fruit harvest. Ferauu leads the crew, but some outlaws cannot wait for his scheduled visit. They slip into the orchard early to pick stormapples for themselves.",sp=0},{t="Thieves Among Thieves",b="The orchard caretaker puts ambitious newcomers to work before Ferauu arrives. The keeper asks you to secure the ripe stormapples and drive off hungry bandits trespassing among the trees. They have gone behind Ferauu's back to take his share. The keeper says Ferauu would likely execute them for it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ferauu?",a="Ferauu leads the bandits who demand a regular share of Windfield Orchard's harvest. He rules his crew with ruthless discipline, though some hungry bandits have slipped in early behind his back.",al={"who is ferauu","ferauu lore","ferauu bandit leader"}},{q="What is Windfield Orchard?",a="Windfield Orchard is a local farm that grows stormapples. Ferauu's bandits demand part of its fruit harvest in exchange for leaving the orchard in peace.",al={"what is windfield orchard","windfield orchard lore","stormapple orchard"}},{q="Why are hungry bandits prowling the stormapple trees?",a="Hungry bandits in Ferauu's crew entered the orchard before the scheduled harvest pickup to steal stormapples for themselves. They broke ranks and tampered with the crop, so the orchard keeper asks you to drive them out.",al={"why kill hungry bandits","why are bandits at the orchard","hungry bandits lore"}},{q="What are stormapples?",a="Stormapples are a fruit grown at Windfield Orchard. They feed people and make up the harvest tribute Ferauu's bandits demand.",al={"what are stormapples","ripe stormapples"}},{q="Does Ferauu know his bandits are sneaking into the orchard?",a="Ferauu does not know these bandits came early. The orchard keeper says they went rogue, and Ferauu would likely execute them if he caught them taking fruit before his arrival.",al={"does ferauu know about the bandits","ferauu double cross"}},{q="Who tasks you with Make Yourself Useful?",a="The orchard caretaker offers you work at Windfield Orchard and watches the groves from a nearby window. Faced with bold newcomers looking for work or food, the keeper tests your mettle by sending you against the intruding bandits.",al={"who gives make yourself useful","make yourself useful quest giver"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can spot the lack of discipline among amateur thieves when bandits betray their crew to steal stormapples early."},kw={"bandits","ferauu","hungry bandits","make yourself useful","orchard","ripe stormapples","stormapples","windfield orchard"},rel={"topic:rogue"},m={id=92682},src={"In-game quest text: Make Yourself Useful"},fv=true}
E["quest:92683"] = {t="quest",n="Flutterfly Dust",z="general",s="In the Gustberry Lowlands, Flutterfly Dust draws a homesteader's interest. Travelers gather it from giant flutterflies while bandits threaten anyone who ventures alone into the fields.",h="In the Gustberry Lowlands, Flutterfly Dust draws a homesteader's interest.",sec={{t="The Giants of Gustberry",b="Giant flutterflies drift through the outer fields and orchards of the Gustberry Lowlands. Their wings shed fine dust, and you can gather it in bulk. Nearby homesteaders want the powder for practical household needs. Yet the insects remain wild.",sp=0},{t="Swatters and Shakes",b="A Flutterfly Swatter brings dust down with a blunt strike. Most flutterflies panic, take to the air, and shake loose piles of powder. Some turn and strike back when provoked. Usually, they are docile.",sp=0},{t="Unspoken Applications",b="The dust is messy to gather and clings to clothing and gear for weeks. The homesteader eagerly awaits its delivery, since bandits make solo trips into the fields too dangerous. Ask what the powder is for, and the resident offers only vague words about general stuff and things.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is flutterfly dust used for?",a="The resident says the dust has practical household uses, but keeps its purpose vague, calling it general stuff and things.",al={"what is flutterfly dust","flutterfly dust use","what is the dust for"}},{q="Where are flutterflies found?",a="Giant flutterflies roam the outer fields near the local orchard, especially across the Gustberry Lowlands. Bandits nearby make gathering there dangerous for anyone alone.",al={"where are flutterflies","flutterfly location","gustberry lowlands bugs"}},{q="Are flutterflies aggressive?",a="Flutterflies are usually docile and flee when disturbed. Some defend themselves when swatted or provoked, then release their wing dust.",al={"are flutterflies dangerous","do flutterflies attack","flutterfly behavior"}},{q="How is flutterfly dust collected?",a="A Flutterfly Swatter delivers a firm blow to the oversized insects. As they react, some shake their rumps and scatter piles of wing dust for gathering.",al={"how to get dust","flutterfly swatter","collect flutterfly dust"}},{q="Why does the resident need someone else to gather the dust?",a="The resident lives alone and cannot easily leave the homestead to gather the dust. Bandits across the surrounding lowlands make a trip far into the fields too dangerous.",al={"why need help","bandit threat gustberry","why quest giver asks"}},{q="Why is the resident evasive about the dust's true purpose?",a="The resident refuses to explain the dust's household use and waves off questions with talk of things and stuff. Its purpose remains unexplained.",al={"why so secret","secret dust recipe"}}},kw={"bandits","flutterfly","flutterfly dust","flutterfly swatter","gustberry lowlands","orchard","wing dust"},m={id=92683},src={"In-game quest text: Flutterfly Dust"},fv=true}
E["quest:92684"] = {t="quest",n="Ornery Ornery Galestriders",z="general",s="In the Gustberry Lowlands, an orchard farmer's poor harvest is under threat from galestriders raiding the stormapples. Drive off the boldest birds to save the remaining fruit and bring home tenderloins for dinner.",h="In the Gustberry Lowlands, an orchard farmer's poor harvest is under threat from galestriders raiding the...",sec={{t="Defending the Orchard",b="A poor harvest has left Gustberry Lowlands farmers with little to spare. Now wild galestriders strip ripe stormapples from orchard branches and threaten what fruit remains. The farmer needs the boldest birds driven off or culled before the crop is gone.",sp=0},{t="Lowland Terrors",b="Lowlands galestriders are larger and more bad-tempered than their highland kin. Take care near these towering birds, traveler; one powerful kick can badly hurt or kill a fighter. Their tenderloins give hungry locals a rare, substantial meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the galestriders causing problems for the farmer?",a="Galestriders raid the orchard for stormapples. With the harvest already meager, their feeding threatens the local food supply.",al={"what are galestriders stealing","why kill galestriders","stormapple orchard"}},{q="How dangerous are lowlands galestriders?",a="Lowlands galestriders are larger and more aggressive than their highland kin. Their powerful kicks can kill a traveler caught off guard.",al={"how dangerous are galestriders","galestrider attacks","are galestriders strong"}},{q="What does the farmer want from the galestriders?",a="The farmer wants travelers to cull aggressive lowlands galestriders and collect their tenderloins for dinner.",al={"galestrider meat","what do galestriders drop","tenderloin quest"}},{q="Where are these galestriders found?",a="Ornery lowlands galestriders roam the Gustberry Lowlands, especially near farmsteads and orchards where they forage for stormapples.",al={"where are galestriders found","galestrider location","gustberry lowlands"}},{q="How do lowlands galestriders compare to highlands galestriders?",a="Lowlands galestriders are larger and more ill-tempered than their highland kin. Their kicks can badly injure a traveler.",al={"highlands vs lowlands galestriders","galestrider varieties"}},{q="What are stormapples?",a="Stormapples are an orchard crop grown in the region. With the harvest scarce, the remaining trees need protection from foraging galestriders.",al={"what are stormapples","orchard harvest"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Lowlands galestriders yield hearty tenderloins for a substantial hot meal, a welcome change from lean harvests and fruit.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, watch for the powerful kicks and aggressive temper of lowlands galestriders. They differ from their highland kin."},kw={"galestrider","gustberry lowlands","lowlands galestrider","orchard","ornery galestriders","stormapples","tenderloin"},m={id=92684},src={"In-game quest text: Ornery Ornery Galestriders"},fv=true}
E["quest:92685"] = {t="quest",n="The Hills Have Eyes",z="general",s="Aamelia faces a bandit assault in the Gustberry Lowlands, and Ferauu’s raid draws near. She sends travelers to strike a camp in the northern hills before the bandits gather.",h="Aamelia faces a bandit assault in the Gustberry Lowlands, and Ferauu’s raid draws near.",sec={{t="A Preemptive Strike",b="Aamelia faces an approaching attack in the Gustberry Lowlands. Ferauu leads the outlaws threatening her farm. She asks you to strike their camp in the hills to the north. Thin the highwaymen’s ranks before they gather, and Aamelia hopes to weaken their attack and gain time before they arrive.",sp=0},{t="Renewed Hope and Retribution",b="Aamelia asks you to bring back blood-stained masks from the fallen highwaymen as proof of the ambush. Grimly, she jokes about stitching them into a blanket for Ferauu. She is glad her tormentors met fierce resistance.\n\nThe strike on the northern camp ends weeks of hopeless waiting. Aamelia has new courage to face Ferauu and his main band when they arrive.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is The Hills Have Eyes?",a="Aamelia asks travelers to strike a bandit camp in the northern hills before Ferauu’s highwaymen attack her farm. She also asks for blood-stained masks from the fallen bandits.",al={"hills have eyes quest","what is this quest","what is the hills have eyes"}},{q="Who gives the quest The Hills Have Eyes?",a="Aamelia gives the request from her farm in the Gustberry Lowlands. Weeks of waiting for the bandits have left her dreading their attack.",al={"who gives the hills have eyes","who is aamelia","quest giver aamelia"}},{q="Who is Ferauu?",a="Ferauu leads the highwayman bandits around the Gustberry Lowlands. His gang threatens Aamelia’s farm and is preparing to attack.",al={"who is ferauu","ferauu boss","bandit leader ferauu"}},{q="Where are the highwayman bandits located?",a="Highwayman Bandits have camps throughout the Gustberry Lowlands, including a small camp in the hills directly north of Aamelia’s farm.",al={"gustberry lowlands bandits","where are the bandits","bandit camp hills"}},{q="Why does Aamelia want blood-stained bandit masks?",a="Aamelia asks for blood-stained masks as proof of the ambush. The strike on the bandits’ camp helps even the odds before Ferauu’s attack.",al={"why collect masks","why blood stained masks","what are the masks for"}},{q="What happens after completing the quest?",a="After the hill camp is struck, Aamelia finds hope for her farm. Ferauu and his remaining bandits are due to arrive at any moment, and she must face their attack.",al={"what happens after the hills have eyes","next quest aamelia","ferauu attack"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Aamelia grimly jokes about stitching a blanket from blood-stained bandit masks for Ferauu."},kw={"aamelia","bandit masks","blood-stained bandit masks","ferauu","gustberry lowlands","highwayman bandits","the hills have eyes"},m={id=92685},src={"In-game quest text: The Hills Have Eyes"},fv=true}
E["quest:92693"] = {t="quest",n="Standing Our Ground",z="general",s="Aamelia Windfield gives you one last chance to retreat to Valanaar before the bandits close in. You have helped the local defenders prepare, yet the coming fight still seems doomed.",h="Aamelia Windfield gives you one last chance to retreat to Valanaar before the bandits close in.",sec={{t="A Desperate Last Stand",b="Aamelia Windfield gives you one last chance to return safely to Valanaar. You have helped the local defenders prepare for the bandits, but the fight ahead looks grim. Will you stand with them, or leave before the clash?",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Bandit Leader",b="When you signal that you are ready, you go with Aamelia Windfield to face the bandit leader. Defeating the brigand ends the immediate threat. Aamelia can hardly catch her breath, shocked and relieved that their gamble succeeded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Standing Our Ground?",a="Aamelia Windfield gives you one last chance to retreat before you face the bandit leader.",al={"who gives standing our ground","quest giver standing our ground","standing our ground npc"}},{q="Who do you fight in Standing Our Ground?",a="You face the bandit leader threatening the local defenders. Aamelia gathers her resolve and confronts the leader with you.",al={"who is the bandit leader standing our ground","standing our ground boss","bandit leader standing our ground"}},{q="What is Valanaar in relation to this quest?",a="Valanaar is the nearby settlement where Aamelia offers you a chance to retreat if you do not want to risk your life in the fight.",al={"where is valanaar standing our ground","standing our ground retreat town","valanaar quest"}},{q="Why does Aamelia describe the battle as a lost cause?",a="Aamelia and her companions believe the odds are against them. They see the standoff as a desperate last stand, and survival seems almost impossible without outside help.",al={"why is standing our ground a lost cause","standing our ground story","aamelia windfield struggle"}},{q="What happens once the confrontation is over?",a="The bandit leader is defeated. Aamelia Windfield is shocked and relieved that the ordeal is over, and struggles to steady her racing heart.",al={"what happens after beating bandit leader standing our ground","standing our ground turn in","does aamelia survive"}},{q="What leads up to this final stand?",a="You helped the defenders prepare for the bandit threat, giving them a fighting chance before the final confrontation.",al={"standing our ground prerequisites","quests before standing our ground"}}},kw={"aamelia windfield","bandit leader","bandits","lost cause","standing our ground","valanaar"},rel={"quest:92579"},m={id=92693},src={"In-game quest text: Standing Our Ground"},fv=true}
E["quest:92698"] = {t="quest",n="What Is My Purpose?",z="general",s="In the orchard fields, a Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct wanders without purpose. Its broken speech has repeated for decades, since the wind elementals departed. Aamelia Windfield knows what locals remember of its past.",h="In the orchard fields, a Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct wanders without purpose.",sec={{t="The Wandering Construct",b="A Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct paces through the fields, caught in a broken loop. Muffled fragments come from beneath its armor, repeating errors and questions about its purpose. Decades alone have left its old instructions corrupted or forgotten. It looks imposing, but threatens no one who passes. Its broken voice carries over the soil as it wanders without purpose.",sp=0},{t="Forgotten Labor and the Windshapers",b="Aamelia Windfield says the construct has roamed the fields for decades, apparently since the wind elementals departed. Alvarion guessed it once hauled harvests to distant markets or tended livestock, centuries ago, before the land became an orchard. The Windshapers built and maintained cyclone constructs in earlier ages. Orchard workers have talked of asking them to repair the machine, but the matter has never seemed urgent. So it continues to roam, largely ignored.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct?",a="The Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct is an ancient armored machine that wanders the local fields. The Windshapers once maintained it, but decades without care have left it in disrepair. From beneath its armor, it repeats broken words and errors while asking about its purpose.",al={"what is the construct","cyclone construct","giant construct in fields"}},{q="Who is Aamelia Windfield?",a="Aamelia Windfield lives near the orchard. She says the construct has paced the fields for decades, apparently since the wind elementals departed. The Windshapers once cared for such machines.",al={"aamelia windfield","who is aamelia","orchard npc"}},{q="What was the construct's original purpose?",a="The construct's original purpose is unknown. Aamelia Windfield says Alvarion thought it might have hauled harvests to market or tended livestock centuries ago, before the orchard existed.",al={"construct purpose","what did the construct do","construct job"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are an ancient group who built and maintained cyclone constructs. Local farmhands have discussed asking them for help, but the construct has caused no urgent concern.",al={"windshapers","who made the construct","who maintains cyclone constructs"}},{q="Why is the construct repeating fragmented words?",a="The construct repeats fragmented words because its operation is broken. It has gone without care for decades, since the wind elementals departed. Its speech includes questions about its purpose and reports of errors.",al={"why is construct talking","function error construct","what is it saying"}},{q="Why haven't the locals repaired or dismantled the construct?",a="Locals have not repaired or dismantled the construct because it poses no threat as it wanders peacefully among the orchard's trees and crops. Aamelia Windfield and other residents have discussed asking the Windshapers to maintain it, but no urgent need has arisen.",al={"why ignore the construct","why not fix construct","is the construct dangerous"}},{q="Who is Alvarion?",a="Alvarion is a local whom Aamelia Windfield mentions when discussing the construct's past. He thought it might once have hauled harvests to market or tended livestock, before the land became an orchard.",al={"alvarion","who is alvarion","alvarion theory"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may find the construct's old mechanisms intriguing. Their logic still loops after centuries of wear and no maintenance.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may take interest in the construct's decline. Local accounts tie its abandonment and failure to the wind elementals' departure."},kw={"aamelia windfield","alvarion","construct","cyclone construct","malfunctioning cyclone construct","orchard","what is my purpose","wind elementals","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=92698},src={"In-game quest text: What Is My Purpose?"},fv=true}
E["quest:92699"] = {t="quest",n="The Supreme Magister",z="general",s="In Valanaar, Elaadrin Evengale draws new arrivals toward the High Order. From a lodge in the settlement’s southeast, the order seeks allies as it faces hostile Windshapers and a nearby cult.",h="In Valanaar, Elaadrin Evengale draws new arrivals toward the High Order.",sec={{t="The High Order of Valanaar",b="New arrivals of promise in Valanaar are directed to the High Order. Supreme Magister Elaadrin Evengale leads it from a lodge in the settlement’s far southeast. He watches newcomers closely, seeking the strength, resolve, and arcane aura to face the dangers threatening their home.",sp=0},{t="Rival Factions and Looming Cults",b="Peace in Valanaar is fragile. The High Order and the Windshapers are bitter enemies, so newcomers are warned to keep their distance from the Windshapers lest violence break out in the streets. A dangerous cult lurks nearby. With threats outside the town, its leaders cannot afford bloodshed within.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elaadrin Evengale?",a="Elaadrin Evengale leads the High Order as its Supreme Magister. From a lodge in Valanaar’s southeast, he seeks people with the arcane aptitude and resolve to defend their home.",al={"who is elaadrin evengale","elaadrin evengale","who is the supreme magister"}},{q="Where can Elaadrin Evengale be found?",a="Elaadrin Evengale and his followers work from a lodge in Valanaar’s far southeast.",al={"where is supreme magister","where to find elaadrin evengale","valanaar lodge location"}},{q="What is the High Order?",a="The High Order is an arcane organization in Valanaar, led by Supreme Magister Elaadrin Evengale. Its members wield arcane power to defend their home, though their numbers are dwindling and tensions in the settlement are rising.",al={"what is high order","high order lore"}},{q="Why is there conflict between the High Order and the Windshapers?",a="The High Order and the Windshapers are bitter rivals in Valanaar. Local leaders urge them to keep apart and prevent violence in the streets, especially with cult activity threatening the settlement.",al={"why do high order and windshapers fight","windshapers conflict","valanaar tensions"}},{q="Who is Rathiril?",a="Rathiril directs promising newcomers to the High Order in Valanaar through magical missives. These messages alert Elaadrin Evengale to people of notable potential.",al={"who is rathiril","rathiril missive"}},{q="What cult threatens Valanaar?",a="A mysterious cult active around Valanaar threatens the settlement. Local authorities work to quell conflict between groups such as the High Order and the Windshapers to keep Valanaar secure.",al={"what cult in valanaar","cult threat valanaar"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you carry an arcane aura that Elaadrin recognizes. He values the rare aptitude and resolve needed to master the arcane and preserve your homeland."},kw={"arcane","cult","elaadrin evengale","high order","rathiril","the supreme magister","valanaar","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92596","quest:92595"},m={id=92699},src={"In-game quest text: The Supreme Magister"},fv=true}
E["quest:92700"] = {t="quest",n="The Grand Skyseer",z="general",s="In Valanaar, the Windshapers seek travelers gifted with spiritual sight. They send you to Ayessa Dawnsinger at their lodge, while rivalries and a threatening cult strain the settlement.",h="In Valanaar, the Windshapers seek travelers gifted with spiritual sight.",sec={{t="Arrival in Valanaar",b="You arrive in Valanaar and are sent to the central lodge. There, the Windshapers gather beneath Grand Skyseer Ayessa Dawnsinger. Elder Amberwind has heard of your deeds in Shen'dar Village and welcomes you among those attuned to the spirits. Dangers press from beyond the town and within it, so tread carefully through its fragile politics.",sp=0},{t="Rivalries and Looming Cults",b="Peace in Valanaar hangs by a thread. The Windshapers and the High Order openly oppose one another, and street skirmishes threaten the settlement. A shadowy cult also menaces the region. Local leaders have ordered both factions to keep their distance and face this shared danger instead of fighting over territory.",sp=0},{t="The Fading Skysight",b="Grand Skyseer Ayessa Dawnsinger says skysight is growing rare among the people of Zephras. Those who arrive with a strong aura and harmony with the spirits are vital allies. The Windshapers need them as they guide their land through hard times.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Grand Skyseer?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger leads the Windshapers in Valanaar as their spiritual guide. She receives travelers at the lodge near the settlement's center, especially those who resonate with the spirits and bear the rare gift of skysight.",al={"who is grand skyseer","ayessa dawnsinger who is she","who is ayessa"}},{q="Where can Ayessa Dawnsinger be found?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger can be found at the Windshaper lodge near the center of Valanaar. She awaits travelers from Shen'dar Village who bring word of their recent deeds from Elder Amberwind.",al={"where find ayessa dawnsinger","where is grand skyseer lodge","ayessa location valanaar"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are a spiritual collective in Valanaar, led there by Grand Skyseer Ayessa Dawnsinger. They study the skies and commune with the spirits, even as tensions with the High Order run high.",al={"what are windshapers","windshaper faction valanaar"}},{q="Why do the Windshapers clash with the High Order?",a="The Windshapers and the High Order clash over the wind spirits. The High Order distrusts their motives and seeks to understand Skywall's powers. The Windshapers trust the elementals and take that doubt as an insult. Street violence is forbidden, especially with a cult threatening the region.",al={"windshapers high order conflict","why high order mad at windshapers","high order valanaar"}},{q="What is the gift of skysight?",a="Skysight is a rare spiritual perception found in few people of Zephras. It lets them sense spiritual auras and commune with unseen forces. Ayessa says the gift is growing rarer, making those who possess it vital in these hard times.",al={"what is skysight","skysight gift zephras"}},{q="Who is Elder Amberwind?",a="Elder Amberwind is a respected elder in Shen'dar Village. Elder Amberwind judges travelers and sends word of their deeds and spiritual resonance to Valanaar. The elder directs the worthy to Grand Skyseer Ayessa Dawnsinger.",al={"who is elder amberwind","amberwind shendar village"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may find an important contact in Ayessa Dawnsinger. She recognizes travelers attuned to the spirits and gifted in spiritual matters.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find kindred thought among the Windshapers. They sense spiritual auras and watch subtle shifts in the skies."},kw={"ayessa dawnsinger","elder amberwind","high order","shen'dar village","skysight","the grand skyseer","valanaar","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","quest:92595"},m={id=92700},src={"In-game quest text: The Grand Skyseer"},fv=true}
E["quest:92701"] = {t="quest",n="To Valanaar",z="general",s="At Valanaar, Valennia Stormfist must face the cult's growing threat. Aonda sends urgent news from Shen'dar, where the village and its pylon were defended.",h="At Valanaar, Valennia Stormfist must face the cult's growing threat.",sec={{t="Dispatch from Shen'dar",b="After Shen'dar and its pylon were defended, Aonda sends a trusted messenger across the island. The message is bound for Valanaar on the island's southeastern edge. There, the commander of the peacekeepers must hear how quickly the cult is advancing.",sp=0},{t="The Gathering Storm",b="Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers have long tried to avoid open conflict with the cult spreading across the island. Yet the events at Shen'dar mark a change. The cult's influence is growing, and Valennia can no longer hold back from a clash. Her dwindling force must ready Valanaar for an assault.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist commands the peacekeepers stationed at Valanaar. She is charged with protecting the island's people, while her small garrison faces growing cult activity.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","valennia","leader of peacekeepers"}},{q="Who is Aonda?",a="Aonda is a highlander stationed in Shen'dar. After securing a pylon and defending the village from cultists, she entrusts a traveler with her written report for Valennia.",al={"who sent the report","crafty highlander","aonda"}},{q="What is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar lies at the southeastern edge of the island. It is the base of Valennia Stormfist and the peacekeepers who defend the island's people.",al={"what is valanaar","where is valanaar","valanaar location"}},{q="What is the cult threatening the island?",a="A rapidly growing cult is spreading across the island and pressing into settlements and sacred pylons. The peacekeepers once avoided direct clashes, but now Valanaar's defenders must prepare to fight.",al={"what cult","who is attacking","cult expansion"}},{q="What is Shen'dar?",a="Shen'dar is a village near a vital pylon on the island. Its people recently repelled cultists to protect the village and pylon, and its leaders keep close ties with the peacekeepers at Valanaar.",al={"what is shendar","shen'dar","pylon village"}},{q="What is contained in Aonda's report?",a="Aonda's written report tells of the defense of Shen'dar and its pylon. It warns Valennia that the cult is spreading too quickly for direct conflict to be avoided.",al={"what is in aondas report","written report contents","what does letter say"}}},kw={"aonda","cult","peacekeepers","pylon","shen'dar","to valanaar","valanaar","valennia stormfist"},m={id=92701},src={"In-game quest text: To Valanaar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92703"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver the News",z="general",s="At the Windfield orchard, Aamelia sends word that her family is safe. Alvarion waits in Valanaar, where he went to seek help.",h="At the Windfield orchard, Aamelia sends word that her family is safe.",sec={{t="Relief at the Orchard",b="Aamelia thanks you for saving the Windfield family orchard. Her home is safe, but Alvarion Windfield has gone to Valanaar to plead for help. He needs to know his family and home are out of danger.",sp=0},{t="A Secret for the Future",b="Aamelia asks Alvarion to find a skilled windshaper once he has recovered. A construct remains at the orchard, and an expert must examine it to make sure it poses no threat.\n\nAamelia is expecting a child. She asks you to keep the news from Alvarion until he returns home safely in person.",sp=1},{t="A Hero in Valanaar",b="Alvarion Windfield is overcome with emotion when you tell him his family and home are safe. He went to Valanaar believing his search for help was a desperate, nearly vain hope. Your success recalls the legendary heroes his people remembered from before they arrived in Skywall. The Windfield family welcomes you into their home for good.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Deliver the News?",a="Aamelia asks you to go to Valanaar and tell her partner, Alvarion Windfield, that she is safe and the danger at the orchard has passed.",al={"deliver the news quest","what is deliver the news","who gives deliver the news"}},{q="Who is Alvarion Windfield?",a="Alvarion Windfield lives in Skywall and is recovering in Valanaar. He left for the city to seek help for his family's orchard, fearing hope was lost before you arrived.",al={"who is alvarion windfield","where is alvarion","alvarion location"}},{q="Who is Aamelia?",a="Aamelia lives at the Windfield homestead and tends the orchard with Alvarion. Grateful for your help, she asks you to bring him news of their safety in Valanaar.",al={"who is aamelia","quest giver aamelia"}},{q="What does Aamelia keep secret from Alvarion?",a="Aamelia tells you she is expecting a child. She asks you to keep the news from Alvarion until he is back on his feet and returns home.",al={"what is aamelias secret","aamelia touches belly","is aamelia pregnant"}},{q="Why does Aamelia want a windshaper brought to the orchard?",a="Aamelia wants Alvarion to bring a windshaper to the orchard after he recovers. The specialist can inspect a construct there and make sure it poses no danger to their growing family.",al={"why windshaper construct","what construct does aamelia mention","windfield construct"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The story takes you from the Windfield orchard to Valanaar, a settlement in Skywall where these settlers have made their home.",al={"where does deliver the news take place","valanaar skywall quest"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you hear Alvarion recall the heroes his people knew from stories before they arrived in Skywall. Their memory recalls your people's roots and heritage before the migration."},kw={"aamelia","alvarion windfield","construct","deliver the news","orchard","skywall","valanaar","windfield","windshaper"},rel={"quest:92579","topic:skywall"},m={id=92703},src={"In-game quest text: Deliver the News"},fv=true}
E["quest:92708"] = {t="quest",n="A Grand Adventure",z="general",s="On Zephras Isle, Ayessa Dawnsinger and the Windshapers seek a way to save their home. The isle lies in Skywall, where wind spirits have vanished without explanation.",h="On Zephras Isle, Ayessa Dawnsinger and the Windshapers seek a way to save their home.",sec={{t="The Crisis on Zephras Isle",b="Wind spirits have vanished from Zephras Isle, and the trouble keeps growing. The Windshapers have investigated the disturbances and uncovered truths about their missing kin and the fate of their elemental home. Ayessa Dawnsinger asks you to heed what they have learned and prepare for an undertaking unlike any before.",sp=0},{t="A Venture Beyond Skywall",b="Ayessa Dawnsinger believes Skywall lacks the power and knowledge to save Zephras Isle. She has concluded that salvation lies below, in the mortal world of Azeroth. Leaving their homeland breaks with tradition. The island's future depends on those willing to venture into the unknown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest A Grand Adventure?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger asks for help as wind spirits vanish from Zephras Isle. The Windshapers believe saving their home means venturing beyond Skywall to Azeroth.",al={"what is this quest","grand adventure quest","what is a grand adventure"}},{q="Who is Ayessa Dawnsinger?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger is a Windshaper on Zephras Isle. She investigates the crisis and asks capable adventurers to heed what the Windshapers have learned.",al={"who is ayessa","dawnsinger","who is ayessa dawnsinger"}},{q="What crisis is taking place on Zephras Isle?",a="Wind spirits have vanished from Zephras Isle without explanation. The Windshapers investigate the disturbances and seek a way to save their home.",al={"what is zephras isle crisis","what happened on zephras isle","zephras problem"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers investigate the disturbances and missing wind spirits threatening Zephras Isle.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshapers zephras"}},{q="Why do the Windshapers need to travel to Azeroth?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger believes Skywall lacks the power and knowledge to save Zephras Isle. She believes they must seek salvation in Azeroth below.",al={"why go to azeroth","why leave skywall","path to salvation"}},{q="What is Skywall?",a="Skywall is the elemental home realm of the Windshapers and Zephras Isle, above the mortal world of Azeroth.",al={"what is skywall","where is skywall"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne of Skywall, you face a great change. You leave your elemental home to seek salvation for Zephras Isle in Azeroth."},kw={"a grand adventure","ayessa dawnsinger","azeroth","skywall","wind spirits","windshapers","zephras isle"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","zone:zephras","quest:92595","topic:skywall"},m={id=92708},src={"In-game quest text: A Grand Adventure"},fv=true}
E["quest:92709"] = {t="quest",n="A Grand Adventure",z="general",s="In Valanaar, Elaadrin Evengale asks you to hear the High Order’s plans. Their search for ancient magic may shape Zephras Isle’s future.",h="In Valanaar, Elaadrin Evengale asks you to hear the High Order’s plans.",sec={{t="A Lost Heritage",b="Elaadrin speaks of your Highborne lineage and the young people who may help save their home. The High Order seeks the ancient magic of its forebears, and what has been lost over many millennia.",sp=0},{t="The Way Ahead",b="Elaadrin says Azeroth is key to the search. The Kirin Tor will show the High Order the way. As its members prepare to leave, you can speak with others in Valanaar. Many need help with their work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to listen?",a="Elaadrin Evengale in Valanaar asks you to hear the High Order’s plans.",al={"who is Elaadrin","Elaadrin Evengale","who wants to talk"}},{q="What is the High Order trying to rediscover?",a="The High Order seeks its forebears’ ancient magic and what was lost over many millennia.",al={"what are they looking for","ancient magic","high order plans"}},{q="Why does the High Order seek ancient magic?",a="Elaadrin says rediscovering ancient magic is key to unlocking Zephras Isle’s secrets and securing its future.",al={"why ancient magic","save Zephras","isle future"}},{q="Who will show them the way?",a="Elaadrin says the Kirin Tor will show the High Order the way.",al={"Kirin Tor","who guides them","azeroth plan"}},{q="What can I do while they prepare to leave?",a="While they prepare to leave, you can speak with other members of the High Order in Valanaar. Most need help with their work.",al={"help in Valanaar","other High Order members","what next"}}},kw={"a grand adventure","ancient magic","elaadrin evengale","high order","highborne","kirin tor","valanaar","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras","topic:highborne","quest:92596"},m={id=92709},src={"In-game quest text: A Grand Adventure"},fv=true}
E["quest:92727"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Scholar",z="general",s="Fillion Flamebreeze is missing after setting out to study atmospheric magic on Zephras. The High Order sent the scholar toward the Shen'dar Highlands, and concern grows as the road from Valanaar yields no word of his return.",h="Fillion Flamebreeze is missing after setting out to study atmospheric magic on Zephras.",sec={{t="The High Order's Mission",b="The High Order gathers and preserves knowledge across Zephras. Yet field research on the island has grown perilous. Fillion Flamebreeze set out for the Shen'dar Highlands to study atmospheric arcane phenomena, but never reported back. His peers now fear the dangers along the frontier roads have claimed him.",sp=0},{t="Traces on the Western Road",b="Fillion Flamebreeze left Valanaar and traveled west toward the Shen'dar Highlands. There, he meant to study windborne magic pooling among the peaks. He vanished before completing the journey. Along the route, a search finds only his personal satchel in the dirt. Dried blood stains it, and his survival is in grave doubt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fillion Flamebreeze?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze is a scholar of the High Order on Zephras. He set out to study windborne magic in the Shen'dar Highlands, then disappeared along the road.",al={"who is fillion flamebreeze","fillion flamebreeze lore","who is the missing scholar"}},{q="What happened to Fillion Flamebreeze?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze never reached his destination. His discarded satchel lies along the western road toward the Shen'dar Highlands, marked with his embroidered name and specks of dried blood that suggest an attack.",al={"what happened to fillion","did fillion die","fillion flamebreeze fate"}},{q="What is the High Order?",a="The High Order gathers and preserves knowledge across Zephras. Its work has grown more perilous amid wild magical phenomena and threats along the roads.",al={"high order mandate","what does high order do","high order zephras"}},{q="Why was Fillion travelling to the Shen'dar Highlands?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze traveled to the Shen'dar Highlands to record unusual windborne magic pooling and flowing across parts of the highlands.",al={"where was fillion going","wind magic shendar","why did he go to the highlands"}},{q="Where was Fillion Flamebreeze last seen?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze's bloodstained satchel lies along the westward road from Valanaar as it climbs toward the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"where is the satchel","fillion satchel location","road from valanaar"}},{q="What is the windborne magic of the Shen'dar Highlands?",a="Windborne magic is made up of atmospheric arcane currents that gather naturally in certain high places on Zephras. The Shen'dar Highlands are a chief subject of arcane research.",al={"what is windborne magic zephras","wind magic highlands"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you share Flamebreeze's curiosity about the windborne arcane currents gathering in Zephras's highlands.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you know Zephras's winds and atmospheric magic hold great interest. Hidden dangers make the terrain perilous even for scholars."},kw={"bloodstained satchel","fillion flamebreeze","high order","shen'dar highlands","the missing scholar","valanaar","windborne magic","zephras"},rel={"quest:92596"},m={id=92727},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Scholar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92741"] = {t="quest",n="Unwelcome Visitors",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, shrieklings are pressing toward the woods' edge. Iaadaria Bitterwind in Valanaar asks travelers to gather their talons for the High Order.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, shrieklings are pressing toward the woods' edge.",sec={{t="The Shriekling Surge",b="Shadowgale Forest is a dangerous woodland that ordinary adventurers are forbidden to enter. Now its shrieklings have multiplied in numbers never seen before. They are pressing toward the forest's edge and extending their hunting grounds beyond the canopy. If they keep spreading, settled lands and travel routes will face a growing danger.",sp=0},{t="Scholarly Culling",b="In Valanaar, Iaadaria Bitterwind of the High Order sees both danger and opportunity in the shrieklings' growing numbers. The Order usually leaves pest control and trapping to others. Yet shriekling talons have rare alchemical properties, making an exception worthwhile. Travelers are asked to enter Shadowgale Forest and bring back eight talons. The High Order can then help protect the region and study the reagents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Unwelcome Visitors?",a="Iaadaria Bitterwind gives the request in Valanaar. She is a researcher with the High Order and asks travelers to hunt shrieklings nearby, gathering materials for her alchemical studies.",al={"who gives unwelcome visitors","unwelcome visitors quest giver","where to pick up unwelcome visitors"}},{q="What is the High Order's interest in the shrieklings?",a="The High Order is interested in the shrieklings' talons, which have distinct alchemical properties. Though the Order usually leaves trapping and pest control to others, Iaadaria Bitterwind sees a chance to study valuable reagents while helping protect the region.",al={"why does high order want talons","high order shrieklings","iaadaria bitterwind motive"}},{q="Why must the shriekling population be culled?",a="The shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest have multiplied greatly in recent months. They are moving beyond their usual woodland territory, threatening neighboring areas if their spread continues.",al={"why kill shrieklings","shriekling threat","why are shrieklings a problem"}},{q="Where is Shadowgale Forest located?",a="Shadowgale Forest lies near Valanaar. Its dangerous woods are usually forbidden to ordinary travelers and inexperienced adventurers because of the violent wildlife within.",al={"where is shadowgale forest","shadowgale forest location","how to get to shadowgale forest"}},{q="What are shrieklings?",a="Shrieklings are vicious predatory beasts native to Shadowgale Forest. Their talons have alchemical properties, and in recent months their numbers have grown so greatly that they are pushing beyond the forest's edge.",al={"what is a shriekling","shriekling lore","what kind of beasts are shrieklings"}},{q="What items are required to complete Unwelcome Visitors?",a="Travelers must bring eight Shriekling Talons from Shadowgale Forest to Iaadaria Bitterwind in Valanaar. The talons will aid her scholarly and alchemical research.",al={"unwelcome visitors objectives","what do i need for unwelcome visitors","shriekling talons needed"}},{q="Why is Shadowgale Forest off-limits to normal adventurers?",a="Shadowgale Forest is forbidden to ordinary adventurers because its wildlife is deadly and the woods are treacherous. Those who enter, including travelers asked to cull the shrieklings, must be ready for severe danger.",al={"why is shadowgale off limits","shadowgale forest danger","can anyone enter shadowgale forest"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track and thin the overpopulated shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest. You take up the work of wardens and trappers, a duty the High Order disdains.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the shrieklings' sudden growth and spread as a disturbance in Shadowgale Forest. Swift action is needed to restore the forest's natural balance."},kw={"alchemical properties","iaadaria bitterwind","shadowgale forest","shriekling","shriekling talons","the high order","unwelcome visitors","valanaar"},rel={"quest:92596"},m={id=92741},src={"In-game quest text: Unwelcome Visitors"},fv=true}
E["quest:92834"] = {t="quest",n="Avenged Tenfold",z="general",s="Elaadrin turns from diplomacy to retribution after the Al'Aketh cult answers his appeal with violence. The High Order scholar had sent his dear friend Belathaan Brightwish to seek peace at the Shrine of Akir, north of Valanaar.",h="Elaadrin turns from diplomacy to retribution after the Al'Aketh cult answers his appeal with violence.",sec={{t="The Diplomatic Overture",b="The Al'Aketh cult's violence brought armed posturing from factions like the Peacekeepers and Windshapers. Elaadrin spoke for the High Order and saw such displays as a foolish escalation. His order prizes pragmatism and avoids conflict, so he still believed reasoned dialogue could work. He sent his close friend, Belathaan Brightwish, to the Shrine of Akir to negotiate peace.",sp=0},{t="A Ghoulish Rejection",b="The Al'Aketh cult answered with a package bearing Belathaan's severed tongue, coated in silver pigment. Elaadrin was horrified and burdened by guilt. He saw that taking the high road had cost his dear friend's life, and admitted the Windshapers were right to reject negotiations. He abandoned diplomacy and called on travelers to hunt the cultists across the Gustberry Fields and the Shrine of Akir, collecting their Al'Aketh Windstone Charms.",sp=1},{t="Prudence and Arcane Wrath",b="The High Order puts logic before sentiment and holds that avoiding bloodshed is usually the prudent path. Yet Elaadrin shows how cold logic cuts both ways when foes mistake restraint for helplessness. Crackling arcane energy gathers around him. The High Order favors peace, but those who butcher its emissaries face overwhelming retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elaadrin?",a="Elaadrin represents the High Order and first sought peace with the Al'Aketh cult. After they murdered his envoy and close friend Belathaan Brightwish, he abandoned diplomacy and ordered the cultists destroyed.",al={"who is elaadrin","quest giver avenged tenfold","who gives this quest"}},{q="What happened to Belathaan Brightwish?",a="Belathaan Brightwish was Elaadrin's close friend and envoy to the Shrine of Akir, sent to open peaceful dialogue with the Al'Aketh cult. The cult murdered him and returned a box to Elaadrin containing his severed tongue, painted with silver pigment.",al={"what happened to belathaan","who is belathaan brightwish","why did belathaan die"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh cultists?",a="The Al'Aketh are a violent cult active north of Valanaar, around the Gustberry Fields and Shrine of Akir. They carry prayer charms called Al'Aketh Windstone Charms and reject peaceful overtures from outsiders with violence.",al={"who are alaketh","who are the cultists","al'aketh cult"}},{q="What is the High Order?",a="The High Order prizes pragmatism, intellect, and logic. Its members generally favor avoiding conflict and preserving life, but can answer a grave offense with fierce magical retribution.",al={"what is the high order","high order beliefs"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers and Peacekeepers are factions that first answered the Al'Aketh cult's violence with forceful displays and posturing. Elaadrin called their response reckless, but later conceded they were right to dismiss diplomatic appeals.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshapers peacekeepers"}},{q="Where are the Al'Aketh cultists found?",a="The Al'Aketh cultists gather north of Valanaar, in the Gustberry Fields and around the Shrine of Akir. Belathaan Brightwish was sent to the Shrine before his death.",al={"where is shrine of akir","where are gustberry fields","where are the cultists"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Elaadrin channel crackling arcane power when provoked. The High Order's devotion to logic rests alongside formidable magical force."},kw={"al'aketh","avenged tenfold","belathaan brightwish","elaadrin","gustberry fields","high order","shrine of akir","windshapers","windstone charms"},rel={"quest:92596","quest:92595"},m={id=92834},src={"In-game quest text: Avenged Tenfold"},fv=true}
E["quest:92840"] = {t="quest",n="Catching Wind",z="general",s="At the Overlook Standing Stones, the High Order seeks readings that may help save Zephras. Its expedition faces fierce opposition from the Windshapers in the Shen'dar Highlands.",h="At the Overlook Standing Stones, the High Order seeks readings that may help save Zephras.",sec={{t="Measuring the Gales",b="The High Order studies the wild elemental flows of the Shen'dar Highlands in hopes of saving Zephras. At the Overlook Standing Stones, its researchers use an Index Esoteria, a tool made to draw data from the great windstone formations. The Windshapers see these probes as profane trespass against the wind.",sp=0},{t="Clash of Dogma and Inquiry",b="The High Order's expedition and the Windshapers soon clash at the stones. The Windshapers call the study and taking of elemental energy a desecration of their sacred ways. The High Order sees them as narrow in their beliefs, much like the violent Al'Aketh. It will not let their resistance halt its work to save the realm.",sp=0},{t="The Standing Stone Massacre",b="At the Overlook Standing Stones, the High Order meets hostile resistance, and the clash leaves blood among the windstones. The High Order secures its readings with the Index Esoteria. The Windshapers call the fighting a massacre, and the feud casts a shadow over Valanaar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Catching Wind about?",a="The High Order sends an operative to study elemental energy at the Overlook Standing Stones in the Shen'dar Highlands. The operative carries an Index Esoteria to gather data from the windstones despite opposition from the Windshapers.",al={"what is catching wind","catching wind quest"}},{q="What is an Index Esoteria?",a="The Index Esoteria is a High Order instrument made to extract, measure, and record elemental energy from the great windstone formations at the Overlook Standing Stones.",al={"what is the index esoteria","index esoteria device"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers defend their sacred sites and traditional beliefs about elemental magic. They see the High Order's research and devices as desecration and fight to keep outsiders from the windstones.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshapers lore"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are a violent group the High Order compares with the Windshapers. The High Order considers both groups dangerous zealots bound by inflexible beliefs, though it calls the Al'Aketh more violent.",al={"who are al'aketh","al aketh"}},{q="Where are the Overlook Standing Stones located?",a="The Overlook Standing Stones lie in the Shen'dar Highlands. Their great windstone formations channel strong elemental currents, making the site important to the High Order's research.",al={"where are overlook standing stones","overlook standing stones location"}},{q="Who is Fillion?",a="Fillion is a High Order operative or researcher sent to study elemental energy at the Overlook Standing Stones. After confrontation with the Windshapers, the High Order sent an adventurer with the Index Esoteria to secure the data.",al={"what happened to fillion","who is fillion"}},{q="Why does the High Order need the windstone data?",a="The High Order believes knowledge of the realm's elemental forces is vital to saving Zephras. It sees research as necessary to overcome threats that traditional beliefs cannot resolve.",al={"why does high order want data","saving zephras"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may feel torn between the Windshapers' reverence for elemental currents and the High Order's measured taking of elemental power.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may value the Index Esoteria's careful measurements and see elemental forces as a field of study."},kw={"al'aketh","catching wind","fillion","high order","index esoteria","overlook standing stones","shen'dar highlands","valanaar","windshapers","windstone formations","zephras"},rel={"quest:92596","quest:92595"},m={id=92840},src={"In-game quest text: Catching Wind"},fv=true}
E["quest:92849"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Scholar",z="general",s="You follow the trail of Fillion Flamebreeze, missing after an assignment at the Overlook Standing Stones. The search leads north to a cave, where he was dragged by a winged beast.",h="You follow the trail of Fillion Flamebreeze, missing after an assignment at the Overlook Standing Stones.",sec={{t="The Vanished Researcher",b="You find signs of trouble along the trail Fillion Flamebreeze took on his travels. They point to foul play. Following them leads north to a dark cave. The missing scholar may still be alive inside, waiting for help.",sp=0},{t="Ambush by the Windshapers",b="Fillion Flamebreeze was returning from an assignment at the Overlook Standing Stones when Windshapers ambushed him. They battered him, dragged him to the cave entrance, and left him bleeding. Helpless, he faced whatever waited within.",sp=1},{t="Lair of the Winged Beast",b="As Fillion lay fading at the cavern’s threshold, a massive winged beast emerged from the dark and dragged him inside. It carried him deep into its lair as prey for its younglings. Timely rescue spared him that fate.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fillion Flamebreeze?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze is a scholar who was returning from an assignment at the Overlook Standing Stones when Windshapers ambushed him. Left bleeding and unconscious outside a nearby cave, he was dragged inside by a massive winged predator.",al={"who is fillion","fillion flamebreeze","missing scholar npc"}},{q="What was Fillion doing at the Overlook Standing Stones?",a="The Overlook Standing Stones were the site of Fillion Flamebreeze’s scholarly assignment. His journey back from the stones led to an ambush by Windshapers. The precise nature of his research is unclear.",al={"what are overlook standing stones","overlook stones assignment","fillion mission"}},{q="Who attacked Fillion Flamebreeze?",a="Windshapers ambushed and battered Fillion Flamebreeze. They forced him to the mouth of a nearby cave and left him bleeding and barely conscious.",al={"who attacked fillion","what are windshapers","windshaper ambush"}},{q="What creature took Fillion into the cave?",a="A massive winged beast in a cave north of the ambush site took Fillion from the cave entrance. It dragged him into its lair to feed itself and its hungry younglings.",al={"what cave beast","winged monster fillion","what took fillion"}},{q="Where can Fillion Flamebreeze be found?",a="Clues at the site of Fillion Flamebreeze’s misfortune point to a cave just to the north. Inside, he is trapped in the beast’s nesting grounds and awaits rescue before he is devoured.",al={"how to find fillion","where is the missing scholar","fillion cave location"}},{q="What was the fate of the missing scholar?",a="Fillion survives his ordeal because someone intervenes in the cave in time. Without an adventurer finding and helping him, he would have become dinner for the winged beast and its offspring.",al={"did fillion survive","what happens to fillion flamebreeze","save missing scholar"}}},kw={"fillion","fillion flamebreeze","overlook standing stones","the missing scholar","windshapers","winged beast"},m={id=92849},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Scholar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92850"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Scholar",z="general",s="Fillion Flamebreeze is stranded near a dangerous den, and Valanaar needs the threat ended. Once he can travel, he asks you to slay the Shriekling Matriarch nearby.",h="Fillion Flamebreeze is stranded near a dangerous den, and Valanaar needs the threat ended.",sec={{t="A Perilous Nesting Ground",b="After his ordeal, Fillion Flamebreeze can travel back toward the safety of Valanaar. Yet a brood of shrieklings has nested close to the settlement. Fillion asks you to enter the Shriekling Den and slay the Shriekling Matriarch before the beasts threaten the town.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to the Magister",b="When you bring the Matriarch’s head to Fillion in Valanaar, he thanks you. Yet the shrieklings are only the least of their troubles. Fillion prepares to report on his mission and the surrounding area to the Supreme Magister.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fillion Flamebreeze?",a="Fillion Flamebreeze is a scholar skilled in the arcane arts. He was on an assignment near Valanaar before becoming stranded near a nest of dangerous beasts.",al={"who is fillion flamebreeze","who is the scholar","who gives the missing scholar"}},{q="What are shrieklings?",a="Shrieklings are hostile beasts nesting in a nearby den close to Valanaar. Their presence threatens anyone traveling in the area.",al={"what are shrieklings","where do shrieklings nest","shriekling threat"}},{q="Who is the Supreme Magister?",a="The Supreme Magister is Elaadrin Evengale, who leads the High Order in Valanaar. Fillion reports the events at the den and the status of his mission to them.",al={"who is the supreme magister","fillion report","who does fillion answer to"}},{q="What is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is the nearby settlement where Fillion is stationed. He returns there once he has recovered enough to travel.",al={"what is valanaar","where is valanaar"}},{q="What is the Shriekling Matriarch?",a="The Shriekling Matriarch leads the shrieklings nesting in the Shriekling Den. Fillion asks you to slay her and bring back her head to end the immediate danger to Valanaar.",al={"shriekling matriarch target","who to kill in shriekling den"}},{q="Why does Fillion consider the shrieklings the least of their troubles?",a="The shrieklings threaten Valanaar because they nest so close to the settlement. When you return, Fillion says they are only the least of their troubles.",al={"why least of our troubles","greater danger valanaar"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you share Fillion Flamebreeze’s training in the arcane arts. He relies on that training to recover and travel safely."},kw={"fillion flamebreeze","shriekling","shriekling den","shriekling matriarch","supreme magister","the missing scholar","valanaar"},rel={"quest:92699","quest:92579"},m={id=92850},src={"In-game quest text: The Missing Scholar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92860"] = {t="quest",n="In Service of Zephras",z="general",s="The High Order now offers Valanaar its full military and diplomatic support against the Al'Aketh cult. Hostile movements across the island have ended its policy of avoiding direct confrontation.",h="The High Order now offers Valanaar its full military and diplomatic support against the Al'Aketh cult.",sec={{t="The Gathering Threat",b="The High Order once tried to avoid open conflict with the secretive Al'Aketh cult. Reports of large troop movements and clear hostility have ended that effort. The cultists are mobilizing, and every settlement on the island faces a threat to its peace and safety. So the High Order has chosen to act. It sends an emissary to join with local defenders before the Al'Aketh strike.",sp=0},{t="Alliance with Valanaar",b="Valennia Stormfist receives the High Order's offer of unconditional aid for Valanaar's resistance against the Al'Aketh. Together, the two sides can form a united defense and prepare joint military efforts across the region. The emissary also brings word of Belathaan's death. Valennia's cousin was a devoted servant of Zephras. She mourns him and vows vengeance, then turns to preparations for the campaign ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest In Service of Zephras about?",a="The High Order sends an emissary to Valennia Stormfist to pledge support for Valanaar. It had tried to avoid direct violence with the Al'Aketh, but hostility and reports of large troop movements across the island forced a change. The offer brings the High Order into Valanaar's defense and carries news of Belathaan's death.",al={"in service of zephras overview","what happens in service of zephras","in service of zephras quest"}},{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist leads defensive efforts against the Al'Aketh in Valanaar. She receives the High Order's offer of mutual aid. Belathaan, her cousin and a servant of Zephras, has died, and Valennia vows vengeance against those threatening her people.",al={"valennia stormfist lore","who is valennia","valennia stormfist"}},{q="Who was Belathaan?",a="Belathaan was Valennia Stormfist's cousin and a devoted servant of Zephras. His death came before the emissary brought word of it to Valennia. The news deepens the conflict's personal cost and strengthens her vow to avenge him.",al={"who is belathaan","belathaan lore","what happened to belathaan"}},{q="What is the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh is a hostile cult active on the island. Its hostile acts and troop movements threaten the people of Zephras. The High Order's effort to avoid direct conflict has given way to an armed alliance against the cult.",al={"who are the al'aketh","al'aketh cult","what is alaketh"}},{q="What is the High Order's role in this conflict?",a="The High Order first sought to avoid direct war with the Al'Aketh. Their hostile actions and reports of large troop movements convinced its leaders to act. The High Order now sends a courier to Valennia Stormfist, pledging its full strength to Valanaar's resistance.",al={"high order involvement","why is the high order fighting","high order zephras"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is the island, also called Zephras Isle, that the High Order, Valanaar, and its defenders seek to protect. The Al'Aketh's growing movements threaten its people, and Belathaan is remembered as a faithful servant of Zephras. Their safety is why the High Order joins the defense.",al={"where is zephras","who is zephras","zephras lore"}}},kw={"al'aketh","belathaan","cult of al'aketh","high order","in service of zephras","stormfist","valanaar","valennia stormfist","zephras"},rel={"quest:92596"},m={id=92860},src={"In-game quest text: In Service of Zephras"},fv=true}
E["quest:92871"] = {t="quest",n="In Service of Zephras",z="general",s="Across Zephras, the Al'Aketh cult is gathering for a wider conflict. The Windshapers send an emissary to assure Valennia Stormfist that they will aid her peacekeepers.",h="Across Zephras, the Al'Aketh cult is gathering for a wider conflict.",sec={{t="Rumors on the Island",b="Reports of Al'Aketh activity are spreading across Zephras. Valennia Stormfist's peacekeepers have guarded the island for a long while, but the cult now seems to be preparing for a larger conflict. So the Windshapers pledge to stand with Valanaar's forces if open fighting begins.",sp=0},{t="Pledging Support",b="You are sent to Valennia Stormfist to assure her that the Windshapers are ready to aid her peacekeepers. Valennia welcomes their swift pledge. She is ready to speak with you about the cult's worsening threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist leads the peacekeepers who protect Zephras. She directs the island's defense, including Valanaar's campaign against the Al'Aketh.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","valennia stormfist"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are allies on Zephras who aid Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers. They offer full support to Valanaar's forces against the growing threat of the Al'Aketh.",al={"what are the windshapers","windshapers lore"}},{q="What are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are a cult active across Zephras. Reports say they are making larger moves and preparing for conflict.",al={"who are alaketh","what is alaketh","al aketh cult"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is an island defended by Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers. The Windshapers aid them against the Al'Aketh cult.",al={"what is zephras","zephras island"}},{q="What is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is a settlement on Zephras and home to Valennia Stormfist's peacekeepers. The Windshapers fully support its fight against the Al'Aketh.",al={"what is valanaar","who is valanaar"}}},kw={"al'aketh","in service of zephras","valanaar","valennia stormfist","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=92871},src={"In-game quest text: In Service of Zephras"},fv=true}
E["quest:92880"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Valanaar",z="general",s="Yorna's report brings word to Valanaar that the eastern watchtower has held. Its perimeter is stable, and the remaining attackers are being cleared away.",h="Yorna's report brings word to Valanaar that the eastern watchtower has held.",sec={{t="Word from the Outpost",b="After the attack on the outpost, Yorna sends word to Valanaar. The attackers have been broken, and the defenders are clearing away those who remain. You carry Yorna's Report to ease the leaders waiting in town for news.",sp=0},{t="Relief in Valanaar",b="You bring the eastern watchtower's report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar. The tower has held, and its perimeter is stable. Valennia gives thanks to the winds, relieved that the frontier remains secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Valanaar?",a="Yorna sends you to Valanaar after the outpost's hard-fought defense. She asks you to carry a report to the settlement's leaders.",al={"who gives return to valanaar","who sends you back to valanaar","yorna quest giver"}},{q="Who do you report to in Valanaar?",a="You report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar. She awaits news of the outlying defenders and their safety.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","where is valennia stormfist","hand in return to valanaar"}},{q="What is Yorna's Report?",a="Yorna's Report says the defenders have stabilized their position and are clearing away the attackers who remain.",al={"what is yornas report","what does yorna report say"}},{q="Which watchtower was under attack?",a="Yorna and her forces defended the eastern watchtower, a key position watching the approaches to Valanaar.",al={"what tower was attacked","which watchtower is yorna at"}},{q="What is the status of the eastern watchtower?",a="The defenders have secured the eastern watchtower and stabilized the situation. They are still clearing away attackers who remain.",al={"is the watchtower safe","did the defenders win"}},{q="Why do the defenders speak of the four winds?",a="The defenders of Valanaar honor the four winds and the elements. Their blessing and Valennia's thanks to the winds show that reverence.",al={"four winds meaning","may the four winds bless you"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you share the defenders' and leaders' ties to the four winds, reflected in their blessing."},kw={"eastern watchtower","four winds","return to valanaar","valanaar","valennia stormfist","yorna","yorna's report"},rel={"quest:92579"},m={id=92880},src={"In-game quest text: Return to Valanaar"},fv=true}
E["quest:92881"] = {t="quest",n="The High Elder's Request",z="general",s="In Valanaar, High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong calls for help after coordinated assaults strike the region's watchtowers. Reports from the western watchtower point to a hostile cult targeting the local anchor pylons.",h="In Valanaar, High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong calls for help after coordinated assaults strike the region's...",sec={{t="Trouble at the Watchtowers",b="Coordinated assaults on the western and eastern watchtowers reveal a troubling pattern. What seemed like scattered skirmishes now points to a planned attack on the local anchor pylons. A report from the western watchtower tells how a skypriest revealed the cult's interest in these structures. Now the towers' defense is an urgent concern.",sp=0},{t="Audience in Valanaar",b="The threat to the anchor pylons is growing, so leaders send you to speak with High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. He has a promising lead on the cult's movements and seeks experienced allies to track the enemy. The cult may be preparing a ritual or sabotage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Elder Shadowsong?",a="High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong is a leader in Valanaar. Coordinated cult activity has struck the region's watchtowers, and he seeks capable allies to pursue leads on the cult's intentions.",al={"who is talaanis shadowsong","high elder shadowsong","where is shadowsong"}},{q="Where is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is where High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong is stationed. He coordinates defenses and investigates cult incursions against local anchor pylons and towers.",al={"what is valanaar","valanaar location"}},{q="Why were the watchtowers attacked?",a="Coordinated attacks struck both the western and eastern watchtowers. Defenders suspect deliberate maneuvers aimed at the nearby anchor pylons, not random raids.",al={"why were watchtowers attacked","western and eastern watchtowers","watchtower attacks"}},{q="What are the anchor pylons?",a="Anchor pylons are important defensive or regional structures. Reports from the western watchtower suggest a hostile cult means to interfere with them or subvert them.",al={"what are anchor pylons","cult anchor pylons","why anchor pylons"}},{q="Who was the skypriest at the western watchtower?",a="A skypriest was involved in the incident at the western watchtower. Reports from that encounter led leaders to suspect the cult has a broader scheme involving the anchor pylons.",al={"who was the skypriest","western watchtower skypriest","skypriest role"}},{q="What cult is targeting the watchtowers?",a="A hostile cult carried out simultaneous strikes on the region's watchtowers. Its nature and motives remain under investigation as High Elder Shadowsong works to uncover its plans.",al={"what cult is this","who attacked the towers"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For priests studying divine or ritual manipulation, the cult's interest in anchor pylons and the skypriest's involvement at the western watchtower are troubling signs."},kw={"anchor pylons","eastern watchtower","shadowsong","skypriest","talaanis shadowsong","the high elder's request","valanaar","western watchtower"},rel={"quest:93926"},m={id=92881},src={"In-game quest text: The High Elder's Request"},fv=true}
E["quest:92909"] = {t="quest",n="Harvesting the Harvesters",z="general",s="At Saldean's Farm in Westfall, Ozwin Ironsprocket is trapped by haywire harvest golems. The visiting gnome tinkerer needs salvaged parts to build a way out.",h="At Saldean's Farm in Westfall, Ozwin Ironsprocket is trapped by haywire harvest golems.",sec={{t="A Miscalculated Endeavor",b="Ozwin Ironsprocket came south from Ironforge when its workshops heard of haywire harvesters in Westfall. The gnomish engineer believed he could diagnose and recalibrate the farm machines. He hoped to bring peace to the region's farmlands, already troubled by outlaws and now overrun by rampaging harvesters.",sp=0},{t="Pinned in the Stable",b="Near Saldean's Farm, Ozwin found the harvest golems far more violent than his schematics suggested. Their sharp blades and erratic swings drove him into a nearby stable. Trapped there, he cannot safely return to the fields. He needs daring travelers to salvage isosprings and gyrostabilizers from the machines so he can build a device to escape.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ozwin Ironsprocket?",a="Ozwin Ironsprocket is a gnome tinkerer from Ironforge who came to Westfall to recalibrate the rampaging harvest golems. Their hostility drove him into a stable at Saldean's Farm.",al={"who is ozwin ironsprocket","ozwin","quest giver"}},{q="Why are the harvest golems so aggressive?",a="The harvest golems in Westfall's abandoned fields are wildly aggressive toward passersby. Their ferocity far exceeds what Ozwin expected when he thought routine recalibration would fix them.",al={"why are harvesters attacking","why are golems aggressive","what is wrong with harvesters"}},{q="Where can Ozwin Ironsprocket be found?",a="Ozwin Ironsprocket is hiding in a stable at Saldean's Farm in Westfall, sheltering from harvest golems in the nearby fields.",al={"where is ozwin ironsprocket","where to turn in harvesting the harvesters","ozwin location"}},{q="What does Ozwin intend to build with the collected parts?",a="Ozwin needs golem isosprings and harvester gyrostabilizers to build a mechanical contraption that will let him flee the stable safely.",al={"what does ozwin need parts for","why collect isosprings","escape device parts"}},{q="Why did Ozwin travel from Ironforge to Westfall?",a="Ozwin traveled from Ironforge to Westfall after hearing that rogue machinery was terrorizing the countryside. He believed he could recalibrate the harvesters.",al={"why did ozwin come to westfall","why leave ironforge"}},{q="Where do the required golem parts come from?",a="The isosprings and gyrostabilizers come from the hostile harvest golems and harvesters in the fields around Saldean's Farm in Westfall.",al={"where do parts drop","how to get isosprings and gyrostabilizers"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Ozwin's ambition to tinker with complex machinery is familiar. He misjudged the machines' aggression and ended up cornered in a farm stable.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can salvage isosprings and gyrostabilizers from rogue harvest golems and use them as raw parts for an escape device.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler at Saldean's Farm, you can help a visiting gnome scholar stranded after his attempt to fix Westfall's rogue harvesters went wrong."},kw={"golem isosprings","harvest golems","harvester gyrostabilizers","harvesting the harvesters","ironforge","ozwin ironsprocket","saldean's farm","westfall"},rel={"subzone:saldean-s-farm","zone:westfall","quest:897","zone:ironforge"},m={id=92909},src={"In-game quest text: Harvesting the Harvesters"},fv=true}
E["quest:92910"] = {t="quest",n="Harvesting the Harvesters",z="general",s="A salvaged harvester part may interest someone who studies harvest golems. You are asked to bring it to Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm.",h="A salvaged harvester part may interest someone who studies harvest golems.",sec={{t="A Salvaged Part",b="Someone at Saldean's Farm may want to examine the part you salvaged from a harvester. It appears mostly intact, and Ozwin Ironsprocket is waiting to see it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do I take to Ozwin?",a="You bring Ozwin Ironsprocket the Precessive Autocognition Assembly, a part salvaged from a harvester.",al={"harvester part","what item","autocognition assembly"}},{q="Where do I bring the salvaged part?",a="Bring the Precessive Autocognition Assembly to Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm.",al={"where ozwin","saldean farm","where to take it"}},{q="Why might someone want the part?",a="The salvaged part appears mostly intact, and someone interested in harvest golems may want to see it.",al={"why harvesters","who wants this","harvester interest"}}},kw={"harvest golem","harvester","harvesting the harvesters","ozwin ironsprocket","precessive autocognition assembly","saldean's farm","salvaged part"},rel={"subzone:saldean-s-farm"},m={id=92910},src={"In-game quest text: Harvesting the Harvesters"},fv=true}
E["quest:92911"] = {t="quest",n="Harvesting the Harvesters",z="general",s="At Saldean's Farm, Ozwin Ironsprocket needs parts for a device meant to briefly override the harvesters' systems. He continues working on the assembly while you gather what he needs.",h="At Saldean's Farm, Ozwin Ironsprocket needs parts for a device meant to briefly override the harvesters'...",sec={{t="Parts for Ozwin",b="Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm is studying what makes the harvesters work. He believes he can briefly override their systems. You are gathering parts for his device while he continues tinkering with the assembly.",sp=0},{t="The Finished Device",b="Ozwin completes the device and asks you to try it. He stays at the farm, which is beginning to feel like home to him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for parts?",a="Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm needs parts for a device.",al={"who needs parts","ozwin parts"}},{q="What is Ozwin building?",a="Ozwin is building a device intended to briefly override the harvesters' systems.",al={"what device","harvester device"}},{q="What parts does Ozwin need?",a="Ozwin needs Golem Isosprings, Copper Modulators, and a Crude Scope.",al={"parts list","what does ozwin need"}},{q="Where is Ozwin working?",a="Ozwin Ironsprocket is working at Saldean's Farm.",al={"where ozwin","ozwin location"}}},kw={"copper modulators","crude scope","device","golem isosprings","harvesters","harvesting the harvesters","ozwin ironsprocket"},rel={"subzone:saldean-s-farm"},m={id=92911},src={"In-game quest text: Harvesting the Harvesters"},fv=true}
E["quest:92947"] = {t="quest",n="Making Our Move",z="general",s="At the Shrine of Akir, a strike force moves against the Al'Aketh and their High Priestess. A frontal charge will draw the defenders while the main force approaches from the flank.",h="At the Shrine of Akir, a strike force moves against the Al'Aketh and their High Priestess.",sec={{t="A Coordinated Pincer",b="At the Shrine of Akir, the assault depends on timing and divided forces. A small band of elite fighters charges the front gates to raise the alarm and draw out the defenders. Meanwhile, the commander leads the main strike team in from the flank. Their push divides the defenders' attention and opens a path toward the shrine's leadership.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Al'Aketh Lines",b="The Al'Aketh defend the Shrine of Akir with armored Guardians, mystical Spiritcallers and martial Blademasters. The strike force must break through their front lines to reach the inner sanctum, where the High Priestess directs her followers. Once the outer defenders are beaten, you meet the force's second-in-command, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, at the shrine steps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the objective of the assault in Making Our Move?",a="The strike force aims to breach the Shrine of Akir and reach the High Priestess. Fighters charge the front to draw the defenders while the main team flanks their position.",al={"making our move","quest making our move","shrine of akir quest"}},{q="Who is Hyusaa Quickbreeze?",a="Hyusaa Quickbreeze is the strike force's second-in-command. After you thin the Al'Aketh defenders at the shrine, you are to meet Quickbreeze near its steps.",al={"who is hyusaa","hyusaa quickbreeze","where is hyusaa"}},{q="Who is the High Priestess targeted in the attack?",a="The High Priestess commands the Al'Aketh within the Shrine of Akir. The strike force flanks the enemy lines to reach and defeat her.",al={"who is high priestess akir","high priestess alaketh","target high priestess"}},{q="What is the Shrine of Akir?",a="The Shrine of Akir is a fortified religious site held by the Al'Aketh. Guardians, Spiritcallers and Blademasters defend its central sanctuary, where their leadership resides.",al={"what is shrine of akir","shrine of akir lore","where is shrine of akir"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh forces holding the shrine?",a="The Al'Aketh are the hostile defenders of the Shrine of Akir. Their ranks include frontline Guardians, spellcasting Spiritcallers and agile Blademasters who guard the way to their High Priestess.",al={"who are alaketh","al'aketh defenders","alaketh mobs"}},{q="Why is a frontal distraction used in the assault?",a="A handful of seasoned fighters enters through the shrine's front entrance to draw the defenders and cause chaos. This gives the main force a chance to flank the compound and push toward the inner shrine.",al={"why diversion","shrine attack plan","attack strategy making our move"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="The assault targets the Al'Aketh leadership at the Shrine of Akir, including the hostile High Priestess and her Spiritcallers."},kw={"al'aketh","al'aketh blademaster","al'aketh guardian","al'aketh spiritcaller","high priestess","hyusaa quickbreeze","making our move","shrine of akir"},m={id=92947},src={"In-game quest text: Making Our Move"},fv=true}
E["quest:93036"] = {t="quest",n="Infiltrating the Cult",z="general",s="In Shen'dar Village, Sania Silverstream draws followers as its uneasy peace begins to fray. The village asks a newcomer to approach her and learn what the Order of the Al'Aketh intends for the settlement.",h="In Shen'dar Village, Sania Silverstream draws followers as its uneasy peace begins to fray.",sec={{t="A Precarious Peace",b="In Shen'dar Village, an uneasy truce with the Order of the Al'Aketh is starting to unravel. Local authorities have long tolerated Sania Silverstream, a self-proclaimed missionary living among them. The Order claims to be a peaceful religious movement and sends gentle recruiters to draw in unsuspecting followers. Village leaders let Sania recruit to keep the cult from open conflict. Now that fragile peace is wearing thin.",sp=0},{t="Beneath the Missionary's Veil",b="Sania Silverstream is a junior priestess of the Order of the Al'Aketh, devoted to Al'Akir the Windlord, ruler of the air elementals. She invites newcomers to learn of her sovereign and promises them a place at his table. Shen'dar's residents know her too well to approach safely. So village leaders turn to a newcomer to earn her confidence and uncover what the cult plans for their home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sania Silverstream?",a="Sania Silverstream is a junior priestess of the Order of the Al'Aketh who lives in Shen'dar Village and presents herself as a missionary. She gently recruits locals to worship Al'Akir the Windlord.",al={"who is sania","sania silverstream lore","priestess sania"}},{q="What is the Order of the Al'Aketh?",a="The Order of the Al'Aketh is a cult that presents itself as a conventional religious movement. Its members revere Al'Akir the Windlord, ruler of the air elementals, and quietly recruit converts from nearby settlements to expand their influence.",al={"who are the alaketh","what is alaketh","order of alaketh"}},{q="Why has Shen'dar Village tolerated Sania Silverstream?",a="Shen'dar Village's leaders tolerate Sania Silverstream's missionary work to preserve a fragile peace and avoid open conflict with the cult. That truce is fraying, so they have chosen to investigate her quietly.",al={"why let sania stay","why not kill sania","why is sania in the village"}},{q="Who is the Windlord Al'Akir?",a="Al'Akir the Windlord is the Elemental Lord of the skies, storms, and air. The Order of the Al'Aketh reveres him as its sovereign and promises a place at his table to those who repent and join.",al={"who is the windlord","alakir lore","who is alakir"}},{q="Why are you asked to infiltrate the cult instead of a local?",a="As a newcomer to Shen'dar Village, you are unfamiliar to Sania and the Al'Aketh. They are less likely to suspect you work for village leaders, so you can approach her as an interested recruit without drawing suspicion.",al={"why me","why send an adventurer","infiltrating quest reason"}},{q="What are the Al'Aketh planning for Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village's leaders suspect the Al'Aketh's recruiting hides broader, aggressive plans for the settlement. They want to uncover those plans before the fragile peace collapses.",al={"cult plan for village","what do the alaketh want","alaketh intentions"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may recognize that Sania Silverstream's faith is pledged to an Elemental Lord, not the Holy Light or Elune. Her pleasant religious manner conceals elemental worship.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can use your talents for espionage, deception, and reconnaissance to approach the cult through its unsuspecting recruiter."},kw={"al'aketh","al'akir","alaketh","alakir","infiltrating the cult","sania silverstream","shen'dar village","windlord"},m={id=93036},src={"In-game quest text: Infiltrating the Cult"},fv=true}
E["quest:93065"] = {t="quest",n="Prepare for Battle",z="general",s="The Peacekeepers are gathering in town to march into the surrounding territory. You are called to make your final preparations and meet Valennia Stormfist in the Gustberry Lowlands before the company departs.",h="The Peacekeepers are gathering in town to march into the surrounding territory.",sec={{t="A Call to Muster",b="The Peacekeepers, the local defense forces, have called their troops and volunteers to arms as tensions rise. Secure your equipment, ready your weapons, and join the company as it forms for an organized march into the surrounding territory.",sp=0},{t="The Gathering at Gustberry Lowlands",b="The company gathers along the eastern road leading north out of town into the Gustberry Lowlands. There, organizer Valennia Stormfist inspects the fighters and calls the roll. Then the company marches into danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist organizes the Peacekeepers' muster in the Gustberry Lowlands. She oversees final preparations along the eastern road leading north out of town before the forces depart.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","valennia stormfist","stormfist"}},{q="Who are the Peacekeepers?",a="The Peacekeepers are an organized local defense force. They are gathering to face a looming threat outside of town.",al={"who are the peacekeepers","peacekeepers","peacekeeper force"}},{q="Where are the Gustberry Lowlands?",a="The Gustberry Lowlands is where local defense forces gather. Their staging ground lies along the road leading north out of town.",al={"where is gustberry lowlands","gustberry lowlands location","gustberry lowlands"}},{q="What are the Peacekeepers preparing for?",a="The Peacekeepers are preparing to march out in force. They call on capable allies to check their gear and gather at the edge of town before the company departs.",al={"what are they preparing for","why prepare for battle","what is the battle"}},{q="Where is the rendezvous point for the march?",a="The company meets along the eastern road leading north out of town. There, its members can gather in formation before marching into the field.",al={"where is the muster point","where to meet valennia","rendezvous point"}},{q="What happens once everyone is assembled?",a="Valennia Stormfist inspects the assembled ranks and calls the roll. Then the forces march into danger.",al={"how does the muster finish","what does valennia say","we are as ready as we will ever be"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a front-line fighter, you know this gathering comes before combat. Check your gear and form ranks beside your allies as the company prepares to march."},kw={"eastern road","gustberry lowlands","mobilization","peacekeepers","prepare for battle","valennia stormfist"},m={id=93065},src={"In-game quest text: Prepare for Battle"},fv=true}
E["quest:93089"] = {t="quest",n="What Comes Next",z="general",s="On Zephras Isle, the High Order seeks your blessing before departing with its Kirin Tor allies. Their expedition depends on finding an arcane answer to the island’s instability.",h="On Zephras Isle, the High Order seeks your blessing before departing with its Kirin Tor allies.",sec={{t="The Departure",b="High Elder Shadowsong has blessed the expedition, and its preparations are ready. Ansirem has worked to establish skycutter travel between Dalaran and Zephras Isle. Now the vanguard is preparing to depart. Speak with Elaadrin Evengale when you are ready to leave the island.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who do I speak with before leaving Zephras Isle?",a="Speak with Elaadrin Evengale when you are ready to leave Zephras Isle.",al={"who do i talk to","leave zephras isle","elaadrin departure"}},{q="Where is the High Order going?",a="The High Order is preparing an expedition, with skycutter transport linking Dalaran and Zephras Isle.",al={"where are they going","high order destination","next stop"}},{q="Who is helping the High Order?",a="The Kirin Tor are helping the High Order. Ansirem has worked on skycutter transport between Dalaran and Zephras Isle.",al={"who are the allies","kirin tor help","high order friends"}},{q="What is the expedition seeking?",a="The expedition hopes to find an arcane solution to bring stability to Zephras Isle.",al={"what are they looking for","arcane solution","why leave the island"}},{q="What happened to the cult?",a="Elaadrin says the cult has been defeated, and preparations for the expedition are complete.",al={"cult status","is the cult defeated","what about the cult"}}},kw={"ansirem","dalaran","elaadrin evengale","high order","kirin tor","skycutter","what comes next","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras","subzone:dalaran","quest:92596"},m={id=93089},src={"In-game quest text: What Comes Next"},fv=true}
E["quest:93090"] = {t="quest",n="What Comes Next",z="general",s="On Zephras Isle, the expedition prepares to cross the skies for Kalimdor. The local cult is defeated, and High Elder Shadowsong has given his blessing. Skycutters now carry travelers between the island and Mulgore.",h="On Zephras Isle, the expedition prepares to cross the skies for Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Departure from Zephras Isle",b="High Elder Shadowsong has blessed the expedition's onward journey from Zephras Isle, where the local cult has been defeated and safety restored. The expedition now looks beyond the island, with its focus set on travel across the open skies toward Kalimdor. Ayessa Dawnsinger coordinates the final departure for those ready to leave.",sp=0},{t="Skycutters to Mulgore",b="Muln worked to secure steady skycutter travel between Zephras Isle and Mulgore. Test voyages succeeded, and an advance party has already crossed over. They wait on the other side to make contact with the shaman of the Earthen Ring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest What Comes Next?",a="The expedition is preparing to leave Zephras Isle after earning High Elder Shadowsong's blessing and defeating the local cult. Travelers are ready to cross the skies by skycutter to Kalimdor.",al={"what is what comes next","what comes next quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Where does the expedition travel?",a="Skycutters connect Zephras Isle with Mulgore, a grassy mesa region in central Kalimdor. The Earthen Ring makes its home there, and advance members of the expedition are already waiting.",al={"where are we going","skycutter destination","where does the skycutter fly"}},{q="Who is Ayessa Dawnsinger?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger coordinates the departure from Zephras Isle. Preparations are in place, test flights have succeeded, and High Elder Shadowsong has blessed the expedition's departure.",al={"who is ayessa dawnsinger","ayessa dawnsinger","ayessa"}},{q="Who is Muln?",a="Muln worked to establish steady skycutter travel between Zephras Isle and Mulgore. He conducted test voyages to ensure safe passage across the skies.",al={"who is muln","muln skycutter","muln zephras"}},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an organization of shamans devoted to keeping harmony among the elemental spirits. Its members are the expedition's contacts and hosts in Mulgore.",al={"what is the earthen ring","earthen ring mulgore","who are the earthen ring"}},{q="Why is the expedition leaving Zephras Isle?",a="The local cult is defeated, and High Elder Shadowsong has blessed the expedition. With those tasks complete, the expedition can leave Zephras Isle and continue to the mainland.",al={"why leave zephras isle","is zephras finished","why go to mulgore"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you travel to Mulgore to meet the Earthen Ring, a revered shamanic organization devoted to soothing Azeroth's elemental spirits.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you travel to Mulgore, your people's ancestral homeland. The Earthen Ring keeps its operations there."},kw={"ayessa dawnsinger","earthen ring","high elder shadowsong","mulgore","muln","skycutter","what comes next","zephras isle"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","zone:zephras","zone:mulgore","quest:95349"},m={id=93090},src={"In-game quest text: What Comes Next"},fv=true}
E["quest:93159"] = {t="quest",n="The Strange Hermit",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, a hooded hermit keeps to himself beneath the trees. Though years alone have made him shy, he shares something of his handmade life and the forest spirits who sing to him.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, a hooded hermit keeps to himself beneath the trees.",sec={{t="A Recluse in the Woods",b="Deep beneath Shadowgale Forest's canopy, you find a hooded recluse far from towns and trade routes. He is known simply as the Strange Hermit. Years without ordinary company have left him nervous and awkward in conversation. Even a greeting seems strange to him.",sp=0},{t="Spirits and Simple Things",b="The hermit says he has the company and provisions he needs. He once lived elsewhere, then chose a life here among handmade trinkets and the local forest spirits. They often sing to him, though their songs cannot answer him as another person can.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the strange hermit?",a="The Strange Hermit is an eccentric, hooded recluse in Shadowgale Forest. Unused to company, he tends his handmade possessions and spends time with local woodland spirits instead of other people.",al={"strange hermit","hermit identity","who is the hermit"}},{q="Where does the hermit live?",a="The hermit lives deep among the trees of Shadowgale Forest, far from towns and trade routes where few travelers pass.",al={"where is the hermit","shadowgale forest location","hermit zone"}},{q="Why does the hermit live by himself?",a="The hermit says he lived somewhere else before choosing to settle in the forest. He keeps his past vague and makes his life among handmade things and the wild spirits of the woods.",al={"why is the hermit alone","hermit isolation","hermit backstory"}},{q="Can the hermit speak with forest spirits?",a="The local forest spirits sing to the hermit, though they do not speak with him. He enjoys their songs, but they cannot answer as another person can.",al={"hermit talking to spirits","forest spirits shadowgale","hermit friends"}},{q="What has the hermit built in the forest?",a="The hermit has made several handcrafted items and structures to occupy himself. He finds comfort and contentment in these simple belongings.",al={"hermit crafts","what did hermit build"}},{q="What happens during the quest 'The Strange Hermit'?",a="You approach the nervous hermit in Shadowgale Forest and hear what he chooses to share about his life in seclusion.",al={"strange hermit quest","speak to hermit"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may value the hermit's bond with the local forest spirits, though their songs offer less than the deeper communion you know.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may understand the comfort the hermit finds in building by hand to furnish his lonely dwelling."},kw={"forest spirits","handcrafted","hermit","hooded figure","loner","shadowgale forest","strange hermit"},m={id=93159},src={"In-game quest text: The Strange Hermit"},fv=true}
E["quest:93160"] = {t="quest",n="The Forest's Bounty",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, a forager needs help gathering fallen acorns. Raptor-like predators prowl the deeper woods, and the harvest can be roasted into a forest meal.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, a forager needs help gathering fallen acorns.",sec={{t="A Perilous Foraging Run",b="A cautious forager in Shadowgale Forest has gathered the acorns near safety. Fierce, raptor-like creatures prowl among the trees and keep the forager from reaching the wilder groves. So passing travelers are needed to gather what lies deeper in the woods, and help ensure neither goes hungry.",sp=0},{t="Roasting the Harvest",b="Shadowgale Acorns make hearty food when prepared with care. Raw, they can be bitter or tough, but roasting them over a fire turns the wild harvest into a rich treat. To gather them, you must brave the timber where predatory birds prowl.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks you to gather the acorns?",a="A nervous forager near Shadowgale Forest asks you to gather acorns. They have collected those nearby, but need help reaching woods where dangerous wildlife roams.",al={"who gives the forest bounty quest","who wants acorns","quest giver forests bounty"}},{q="Where are the acorns found?",a="Shadowgale Acorns lie scattered beneath Shadowgale Forest's canopy. Search the forest floor and watch for predators among the trees.",al={"where are shadowgale acorns","acorn location","shadowgale forest acorns"}},{q="Why is collecting acorns dangerous here?",a="Predatory, raptor-like birds prowl the forest floor. Without martial training, ordinary folk risk danger if they stray far from camp.",al={"why dangerous shadowgale forest","what raptor birds","why is gathering acorns dangerous"}},{q="What are the acorns used for?",a="The acorns are hearty wild food. Roast them over a fire for a warm snack to share with those willing to brave the forest beasts.",al={"what are shadowgale acorns for","roasted acorns","why gather acorns"}},{q="What are the raptor-bird creatures mentioned in the forest?",a="The forager describes dangerous “raptor-bird things” hunting in Shadowgale Forest. These avian or reptilian predators are large and vicious enough to prey on an unwary traveler.",al={"what raptor bird thing","raptor birds in shadowgale","forest raptors"}},{q="How are the acorns prepared for eating?",a="Shadowgale Acorns can be tough or bitter raw. Roasting them over heat makes them a delicious treat.",al={"are shadowgale acorns edible raw","how to cook shadowgale acorns","eating forest acorns"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can roast Shadowgale acorns into simple forest fare."},kw={"acorns","cooking","foraging","raptor-bird","shadowgale acorns","shadowgale forest","the forest's bounty"},m={id=93160},src={"In-game quest text: The Forest's Bounty"},fv=true}
E["quest:93165"] = {t="quest",n="Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears",z="general",s="In the wilds around Shadowgale Forest, the Nightclaw survivors seek vengeance against the Al'Aketh. After a terrible tragedy at the cultists' hands, they offer coin and a promise of access to their hidden lore for trophies taken from slain enemies. Their feud now reaches across Shadowgale Forest and the surrounding territories.",h="In the wilds around Shadowgale Forest, the Nightclaw survivors seek vengeance against the Al'Aketh.",sec={{t="Blood for Blood",b="The Nightclaw enclave and the Al'Aketh cultists are locked in a bitter feud. A terrible tragedy has left the survivors with no hope of peace. They seek vengeance for their fallen kin and turn to wandering adventurers and mercenaries for help. The enclave offers coin and the promise of deeper trust to those who kill cultists and bring back their ears as proof.",sp=0},{t="The Al'Aketh Menace",b="The Al'Aketh spread their influence through the Gustberry Lowlands, Shadowgale Forest, and the ancient Shrine of Akir. Their dark practices and fanatical ways have earned the hatred of local inhabitants. Striking the cult's camps across these lands can weaken its reach and earn favor with the secretive Nightclaw. The enclave keeps its mysteries close until an outsider proves their loyalty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears?",a="The Nightclaw enclave offers coin and deeper trust to those who kill Al'Aketh cultists and bring back their ears. The survivors seek vengeance after a terrible tragedy.",al={"mercy falls on deaf ears quest","what is this quest","quest overview"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are a sect of accursed cultists whose actions have brought ruin and tragedy to neighboring settlements. They operate across the Gustberry Lowlands, Shadowgale Forest, and the Shrine of Akir, provoking blood feuds with the people of those lands.",al={"who are the alaketh","alaketh cultists lore","who are al'aketh"}},{q="Where can Al'Aketh cultists be found?",a="Al'Aketh cultists can be found in Shadowgale Forest, around the Shrine of Akir, and throughout the Gustberry Lowlands. The Nightclaw seek proof from those who kill them.",al={"where are alaketh cultists","alaketh locations","where to find cultists"}},{q="Why does the quest giver collect cultist ears?",a="The Nightclaw demand cultist ears as proof that their enemies are dead. After a severe tragedy at the Al'Aketh's hands, the enclave seeks vengeance and proof for every bounty paid.",al={"why ears","why do they want cultist ears","ears proof"}},{q="Who are the Nightclaw?",a="The Nightclaw are a secretive enclave that has suffered heavy losses at the hands of the Al'Aketh. They guard their lore closely, but promise outsiders access to their mysteries if they prove their loyalty by fighting the cultists.",al={"nightclaw faction","who are nightclaw","nightclaw secrets lore"}},{q="What tragedy did the Al'Aketh cause?",a="The Al'Aketh caused a great tragedy for the Nightclaw enclave, sparking an uncompromising blood feud. The bounty gives no details of the incident or its casualties, but the survivors demand total vengeance.",al={"what did the alaketh do","what happened to the enclave","alaketh tragedy"}},{q="What are the Nightclaw's secrets?",a="The Nightclaw keep their secrets within the enclave and do not reveal them to outsiders at once. They promise access to this hidden knowledge to those who keep aiding their fight against the Al'Aketh and prove themselves true friends.",al={"nightclaw secrets","what secrets does nightclaw have","what does nightclaw reveal"}}},kw={"al'aketh","blood feud","cultists","ears","gustberry lowlands","mercy falls on deaf ears","nightclaw","shadowgale forest","shrine of akir"},m={id=93165},src={"In-game quest text: Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears"},fv=true}
E["quest:93172"] = {t="quest",n="Free the Hollows",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, the wind hollows’ sorrowful song carries through ancient ruins. An old tragedy binds these ghost-like spirits, and travelers seek to give them peace.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, the wind hollows’ sorrowful song carries through ancient ruins.",sec={{t="Hauntings of Shadowgale",b="Elves across the island have long feared Shadowgale Forest as a haunted grove. In its northeastern woods, old stone ruins lie beneath the overgrowth. Ghost-like wind hollows drift there without rest, but they show no malice. Their sorrow points to a disaster that befell the ruins ages ago.",sp=0},{t="The Mournful Song",b="On quiet nights, travelers near the ruins hear strange singing on the breeze. No mortal song sounds like it, and its deep melancholy unsettles those who hear it. Compassionate travelers believe the shades suffer in their endless lament. They seek the wind hollows to break their spectral bonds and grant them peace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the wind hollows?",a="Wind hollows are sorrowful, ghost-like spirits haunting old elven ruins in northeastern Shadowgale Forest. Bound by an ancient tragedy, they sing mournfully through the trees at night.",al={"what are wind hollows","hollows lore","what are the hollows"}},{q="Why do the wind hollows need to be freed?",a="The spirits are believed to remain bound by a terrible catastrophe and trapped in sorrow. Destroying them is seen as an act of mercy that releases their lingering forms from the ruins.",al={"why free hollows","why kill hollows","free the hollows purpose"}},{q="Where are the spirits found?",a="The spirits gather among ancient ruins in the northeastern woods of Shadowgale Forest, an island woodland inhabited by elves.",al={"where is shadowgale forest","shadowgale ruins","ruins location"}},{q="What is the strange singing heard in the woods?",a="The wind hollows sing a sorrowful melody unlike any ordinary tune. Their song is thought to come from their tragic end and their endless confinement among the island’s ruins.",al={"hollow singing","ghost song","why are ghosts singing"}},{q="Who asks you to free the hollows?",a="An island observer who pities the trapped spirits asks you to free them, mindful that local elves fear the haunted woods.",al={"who gives free the hollows","questgiver free the hollows"}},{q="What happened at the ruins to create the hollows?",a="The exact details are lost to time, but locals know a terrible event took place at the northeastern ruins and bound the spirits there in endless sorrow.",al={"what happened at shadowgale ruins","why are the ruins haunted"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As an island elf, you know Shadowgale Forest has long been feared as haunted, its spirits bound to ancient ruins.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see the wind hollows as sorrowful spirits trapped by tragedy. Destroying them is seen as mercy, releasing souls bound in anguish.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the unquiet spirits in Shadowgale Forest disturb the wilderness and call for balance and release."},kw={"free the hollows","ghosts","hollows","ruins","shadowgale","shadowgale forest","wind hollows"},m={id=93172},src={"In-game quest text: Free the Hollows"},fv=true}
E["quest:93176"] = {t="quest",n="My Little Friends",z="general",s="A keeper offers you a package to begin studying three small creatures. The Entomology Starter Kit holds the notes and materials for the work.",h="A keeper offers you a package to begin studying three small creatures.",sec={{t="A Keeper’s Offer",b="A keeper who has spent many hours studying a small menagerie offers to share the hobby with you. The package contains notes and materials to begin. With the Entomology Starter Kit, you can seek an Arbor Tarantula, a Hay Weevil Specimen, and a Flesh Picker.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the keeper want me to do?",a="Use the Entomology Starter Kit to find and catch an Arbor Tarantula, a Hay Weevil Specimen, and a Flesh Picker.",al={"my little friends task","what do i collect"}},{q="What is in the package?",a="The package contains notes and materials to get you started with the keeper’s hobby.",al={"starter kit contents","what's in the package"}},{q="What is the keeper studying?",a="The keeper studies the anatomy, diets, and social rituals of the creatures in a small menagerie.",al={"little menagerie","what is he studying"}},{q="What happens if I lose the kit?",a="The keeper says you will need to purchase another package for a small fee.",al={"lost starter kit","kit replacement"}}},kw={"arbor tarantula","entomology","flesh picker","hay weevil specimen","menagerie","my little friends","starter kit"},m={id=93176},src={"In-game quest text: My Little Friends"},fv=true}
E["quest:93317"] = {t="quest",n="Crab Season",z="general",s="On Zephras, foragers hurry to gather Windsong crawlers before the brief season ends. Cultists have made the shores perilous, so locals call for help.",h="On Zephras, foragers hurry to gather Windsong crawlers before the brief season ends.",sec={{t="A Fleeting Harvest",b="For a few weeks each year, Windsong crawlers appear along Windsong Lake’s freshwater shores and the rivers that feed it. Their meat is a rare harvest, but the season soon passes.",sp=0},{t="Peril by the Waters",b="Cultists patrol the wilderness around Zephras, putting local foragers in danger. The journey to Windsong Lake is too hazardous for gatherers alone. Unless you brave the shores and the ill-tempered crabs, this brief harvest may be lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Windsong crawlers?",a="Windsong crawlers are aggressive crabs found only around Windsong Lake on Zephras. They can be gathered for just a few weeks each year.",al={"what are windsong crawlers","windsong crabs","lake crabs zephras"}},{q="Why do the crabs need to be harvested right now?",a="Windsong crawlers are available for only a few weeks each year. Once the season closes, their meat cannot be gathered again until the next year.",al={"why harvest crawlers now","crawler season window","why limited time crabs"}},{q="Why can't the local harvester gather the crabs themselves?",a="Cultist activity has made the journey to Windsong Lake too dangerous for local foragers to make before the short season ends.",al={"why cant locals gather crabs","cultists zephras","windsong cult activity"}},{q="Where are Windsong crawlers found?",a="Windsong crawlers live along the shores of Windsong Lake on Zephras and the nearby connecting riverbanks.",al={"windsong crawler locations","where are crabs on zephras","windsong lake shores"}},{q="Are Windsong crawlers dangerous to hunt?",a="Windsong crawlers are aggressive and snap at anyone trying to gather them.",al={"are windsong crawlers dangerous","crab temperament","mean crabs"}},{q="What is Windsong crawler meat used for?",a="Locals gather Windsong crawler meat as seasonal food during the few weeks it is available. Cultists blocking the paths have led them to seek help from adventurers.",al={"windsong crawler meat purpose","why collect crab meat","what is crawler meat for"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can prepare seasonal Windsong crawler meat gathered from Zephras’s lake."},kw={"crab season","crabs","cult activity","windsong crawler meat","windsong crawlers","windsong lake","zephras"},m={id=93317},src={"In-game quest text: Crab Season"},fv=true}
E["quest:93318"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Vulgara the Insatiable",z="general",s="In the Shen'dar Highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable terrorizes travelers and nearby settlements. Constable Aonda has called for a Peacekeeper bounty, with Vulgara's head to be brought to Danarii Bellowveil.",h="In the Shen'dar Highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable terrorizes travelers and nearby settlements.",sec={{t="The Highland Scourge",b="Constable Aonda has named Vulgara the Insatiable an immediate danger to the highlands. The massive winged vuldren roosts southwest of Shen'dar Village, where she terrorizes travelers and local settlements. The Peacekeepers call on bounty hunters to end the threat.",sp=0},{t="Pressured Protectors",b="Bandits and a shadowy cult trouble the Peacekeepers across the region. Slaying Vulgara would ease the danger to local people and keep the skies over Shen'dar safe. Then the defenders could focus on civil defense.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vulgara the Insatiable?",a="Vulgara the Insatiable is a massive, winged vuldren terrorizing the Shen'dar Highlands. Local authorities call her a scourge, and her ravenous appetite and violence endanger travelers and nearby settlements.",al={"who is vulgara","vulgara lore","what kind of monster is vulgara"}},{q="Who placed the bounty on Vulgara?",a="Constable Aonda of the local Peacekeepers issued the bounty to protect local citizens. Hunters are to bring proof of Vulgara's death to Danarii Bellowveil.",al={"who posted vulgara bounty","who wants vulgara dead","constable aonda"}},{q="Where can Vulgara the Insatiable be found?",a="Vulgara prowls a hilltop southwest of Shen'dar Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"vulgara location","where does vulgara spawn","find vulgara"}},{q="Who is Danarii Bellowveil?",a="Danarii Bellowveil handles the bounty's fulfillment. With bandits and cultists pressing the Peacekeepers, Danarii inspects Vulgara's severed head and dispenses the promised reward.",al={"who is danarii bellowveil","danarii turn in"}},{q="What kind of creature is a vuldren?",a="A vuldren is a dangerous, predatory winged beast found in the highlands. Vulgara is particularly massive and vicious, and her predation threatens local settlements.",al={"what is a vuldren","vuldren beast"}},{q="What other threats plague the Shen'dar Highlands?",a="The Peacekeepers in the Shen'dar Highlands are stretched thin by an entrenched cult and bandits preying on local citizens. Predatory beasts like Vulgara trouble them as well.",al={"what threats are in shendar highlands","shendar cult and bandits"}}},kw={"bounty","constable aonda","danarii bellowveil","peacekeepers","shen'dar highlands","shen'dar village","vuldren","vulgara","vulgara the insatiable"},m={id=93318},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Vulgara the Insatiable"},fv=true}
E["quest:93319"] = {t="quest",n="Pilfered Windstones",z="general",s="On Zephras, stolen windstones have left emergency stores short. The Highlands Bandits took them while Aonda's few peacekeepers guard against growing cultist numbers at Falaath Village.",h="On Zephras, stolen windstones have left emergency stores short.",sec={{t="The Stolen Caches of Zephras",b="Windstones keep daily life moving on Zephras. Each settlement keeps emergency stores for times of crisis, but village supplies began to run short. Then captured bandits from the northern Shen'dar Highlands were found carrying the stones. For months, the Highlands Bandits had slipped into local stockpiles, taking what they could while security was thin.",sp=0},{t="Stretched Defenses and Looming Threats",b="Aonda is responsible for village defense, and has refused to approve a raid on the northern cave. The settlement has too few peacekeepers to spare. To the south, cultists are multiplying at Falaath Village, so the guards must hold their posts against that threat. With the peacekeepers pinned down, independent adventurers must face the bandits and recover the stolen windstones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are windstones used for on Zephras?",a="Residents on Zephras rely on windstones for daily life and survival. Settlements keep reserve caches for emergencies.",al={"what are windstones used for","why need windstones","windstone purpose"}},{q="Who stole the windstones?",a="The Highlands Bandits stole the windstones. Captured bandits from a cave in the Shen'dar Highlands were found carrying them, and locals believe the thieves had been breaking into village storehouses for months.",al={"who stole the windstones","who took windstones","windstone thieves"}},{q="Where are the Highlands Bandits located?",a="The Highlands Bandits camp in a cave north of the settlement, in the Shen'dar Highlands. They keep goods taken from village stores there.",al={"where is the bandit cave","highlands bandits location","shendar bandits"}},{q="Why hasn't the village cleared out the bandit cave?",a="Aonda oversees the settlement's defense and has declined to organize a raid on the northern cave because the village has few peacekeepers. Sending them away would leave the settlement vulnerable to growing cultist numbers at Falaath Village to the south.",al={"why not attack the bandit cave","why aonda wont attack","village defense bandits"}},{q="What is the threat at Falaath Village?",a="Cultist numbers are growing at Falaath Village, south of the settlement. Their presence keeps the peacekeepers guarding their home instead of pursuing bandits.",al={"what is falaath village threat","cultists falaath","falaath cultists"}},{q="Does recovering the windstones solve the settlement's shortage?",a="Recovering the stolen stones gives emergency stores temporary relief, but supply route disruptions remain urgent. Without secure supply lines, shortages will continue to threaten the settlement.",al={"are windstones secure now","supply routes zephras","windstone shortage fixed"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can see how the Highlands Bandits exploit a settlement stretched thin by cultist threats.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you know daily life on Zephras depends on windstones. Recovering and defending these caches matters to local settlements."},kw={"aonda","bandit cave","falaath village","highlands bandits","pilfered windstones","shen'dar highlands","windstones","zephras"},rel={"quest:92529"},m={id=93319},src={"In-game quest text: Pilfered Windstones"},fv=true}
E["quest:93320"] = {t="quest",n="Tower Defense",z="general",s="At the fortified position, Tower Defense holds against overwhelming numbers. The defenders have kept the line for now, but exhaustion threatens to break it.",h="At the fortified position, Tower Defense holds against overwhelming numbers.",sec={{t="A Beleaguered Defense",b="The garrison holds back the first assault at a fortified position. Yet the attackers outnumber them and keep pressing forward. The surviving fighters are growing tired, and the line between survival and defeat grows thin.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Attrition",b="The garrison keeps its perimeter, but time favors the attackers. Prolonged skirmishes against superior numbers drain the defenders’ strength. They need a decisive move to break the stalemate before their lines buckle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Tower Defense about?",a="Tower Defense is a desperate defense against overwhelming numbers. The line still holds, but exhaustion threatens to break it unless the stalemate ends.",al={"what is tower defense","tower defense quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who are the defenders fighting?",a="The attackers outnumber the defenders and press hard enough to wear down the garrison. The cult is attacking the pylon watchtower outside town.",al={"who attacks in tower defense","who are we fighting","tower defense enemy"}},{q="What is the current status of the defenders?",a="The defenders are tiring from prolonged combat under relentless assault. Without relief, the garrison risks losing ground unless the stalemate breaks soon.",al={"why are defenders tired","stalemate at the tower","status of the fight"}},{q="Does holding the line resolve the battle?",a="Holding off the assault buys only a little time. Fatigue will wear down the defenders unless they find a way to break the deadlock.",al={"did we win tower defense","how does tower defense end","what happens after holding them off"}},{q="Where does this defense take place?",a="The defense takes place at a fortified outpost under siege. Constant pressure from numerous attackers has stretched the defenders thin.",al={"where is tower defense located","tower defense zone","what tower is this"}},{q="What is needed to turn the tide?",a="The defenders need a swift plan to break the siege before their exhausted frontline gives way.",al={"what needs to be done next","how to win the siege","breaking the stalemate"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know a hold against superior numbers tests stamina as much as skill. Discipline on the frontline can keep the defense from collapsing."},kw={"defenders","exhaustion","fortification","outpost","siege","stalemate","tower defense"},m={id=93320},src={"In-game quest text: Tower Defense"},fv=true}
E["quest:93461"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome to Shen'dar Village",z="general",s="In Shen'dar Village, newcomers with Highborne blood are welcomed under a fragile truce. The High Order and Windshapers keep peace within the settlement, while old rivalries simmer beyond its borders.",h="In Shen'dar Village, newcomers with Highborne blood are welcomed under a fragile truce.",sec={{t="A Fragile Hearth",b="Newcomers with traces of Highborne blood go to the main lodge to pay respects to Rathiril Sunlance, elder of the High Order. They also seek a room from Coriella Calmbreeze, the local innkeeper. Different elven factions share this haven, but their truce remains tense.",sp=0},{t="Rivalries of the Wilds",b="Daily life brings rooms and odd jobs, yet friction persists between the High Order and the Windshapers. In the village square, both groups observe civility. Beyond the settlement, away from prying eyes, old rivalries go unchecked.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Welcome to Shen'dar Village?",a="You are welcomed to Shen'dar Village and introduced to its key figures and fragile peace. You meet Rathiril Sunlance, the High Order elder, and Coriella Calmbreeze at the village inn before taking on local work.",al={"what is this quest","welcome to shendar village info","shendar village intro"}},{q="Who is Rathiril Sunlance?",a="Rathiril Sunlance is an elder of the High Order who lives in Shen'dar Village. He is in the main village lodge, around the corner from the one who first welcomes you, and is a contact for those with Highborne lineage or dealings with the High Order.",al={"who is rathiril sunlance","high order elder","where is rathiril"}},{q="Who is Coriella Calmbreeze?",a="Coriella Calmbreeze runs the local inn in Shen'dar Village. She offers travelers food, lodging, and supplies before they venture into the surrounding wilds.",al={"who is coriella calmbreeze","shendar innkeeper","where to get lodging shendar"}},{q="What is the tension between the High Order and the Windshapers?",a="The High Order and the Windshapers follow different traditions and ambitions, and tensions run high between them. They keep a civil peace within Shen'dar Village, but beyond its edge, conflict can spill into violence in the wilds.",al={"high order vs windshapers","why is there tension","village conflict"}},{q="What is the High Order look mentioned by the questgiver?",a="Those descended from the Highborne have a distinct twinkle in their eyes. This arcane inheritance lets observant locals recognize the look of the High Order.",al={"high order look","highborne eyes","highborne twinkle"}},{q="Is Shen'dar Village safe from conflict?",a="Civility is kept between the High Order and Windshapers inside Shen'dar Village. Outside the settlement, the peace ends, and open hostility flares away from watchful eyes.",al={"is shendar safe","violence outside shendar","wilds danger"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find Shen'dar Village tied to ancient Highborne bloodlines and legacy, a reminder of the pride and arcane heritage that divided elven society.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage with ties to Highborne traditions, you may recognize your lineage in the High Order. Its elders, including Rathiril Sunlance, command respect in Shen'dar."},kw={"coriella calmbreeze","high order","highborne","main lodge","rathiril sunlance","shendar village","windshapers"},rel={"topic:highborne","quest:92595"},m={id=93461},src={"In-game quest text: Welcome to Shen'dar Village"},fv=true}
E["quest:93735"] = {t="quest",n="The Broken Construct",z="general",s="In Valanaar, a damaged construct threatens one of the island’s last working relics. Riaani Nightwind has gone to the city’s western edge to examine it. The old machines carry a history reaching back to the spirits of the wind.",h="In Valanaar, a damaged construct threatens one of the island’s last working relics.",sec={{t="Gifts of the Wind Spirits",b="Long ago, the spirits of the wind gave the island’s people magical instruments, devices, and animated constructs. Across generations, the Windshapers cared for these gifts. Then the spirits departed, and their patronage ended. Most creations fell into disrepair. Only a handful still work.",sp=0},{t="A Crisis in Valanaar",b="One of Valanaar’s last working constructs has been damaged. Its loss would further diminish the island’s dwindling heritage. Artisan Riaani Nightwind was sent to the city’s western edge to examine the machine and try to repair it. These ancient devices are fragile, and she needs aid.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are local caretakers entrusted with tending the magical instruments, devices, and constructs gifted by the spirits of the wind. Since the spirits departed, they have worked to preserve the few relics that still function.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshapers lore","what do windshapers do"}},{q="Where did the magical constructs come from?",a="The spirits of the wind gave the island’s inhabitants magical constructs, instruments, and devices. Since the spirits departed, very few of these creations still function.",al={"who built constructs","construct origins","where did the constructs come from"}},{q="Who is Riaani Nightwind?",a="Riaani Nightwind is an artisan sent to Valanaar’s western edge to inspect and repair one of the city’s few working constructs after it was damaged.",al={"who is riaani nightwind","riaani location","artisan in valanaar"}},{q="Why are most of the island's constructs broken?",a="Most of the island’s constructs fell into disrepair after the spirits of the wind departed and their ancient patronage ended. Only a handful remain in working order.",al={"why are constructs broken","why did constructs fail","wind spirits leaving"}},{q="What is Valanaar's connection to the constructs?",a="Valanaar is home to some of the island’s last working constructs gifted by the wind spirits. One was recently damaged on the city’s western end, and Riaani Nightwind was sent to examine and repair it.",al={"what is valanaar","valanaar city","where is the construct"}},{q="What needs to be done for The Broken Construct?",a="You are asked to travel to Valanaar’s western edge, find artisan Riaani Nightwind, and help him repair the damaged construct.",al={"broken construct quest goal","what do i do broken construct","where to go broken construct"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the delicate magical devices tended by the Windshapers especially interesting.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see the old bond between the island’s people and the spirits of the wind in the constructs they gifted before departing.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the mechanical and magical challenges artisans face when keeping ancient enchanted constructs working without their original spirit patrons."},kw={"artisan","broken construct","construct","riaani nightwind","valanaar","wind spirits","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=93735},src={"In-game quest text: The Broken Construct"},fv=true}
E["quest:93736"] = {t="quest",n="Unwelcome Spirits",z="general",s="The Windshapers seek the spirits of the wind, gone from their reach. Now hollows appear in Shadowgale Forest, and the order gathers their essences to learn what drove the true spirits away.",h="The Windshapers seek the spirits of the wind, gone from their reach.",sec={{t="The Vanished Spirits",b="The Windshapers have lost communion with the spirits of the wind. They seek to learn why the spirits left and what might bring them back. Their departure has left a void in the local elemental atmosphere.",sp=0},{t="Shadows in Shadowgale",b="After the wind spirits departed, strange sprites called hollows appeared in Shadowgale Forest to the north. The Windshapers had not known of them before the spirits vanished. The hollows seem tied to the spirits’ absence, and their essences may help reveal what they are.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are an order seeking to learn why the spirits of the wind abandoned them and how to bring them back. Their inquiries now focus on strange occurrences that began after the spirits disappeared.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshaper faction","what do windshapers want"}},{q="What are the hollows?",a="Hollows are strange wind sprites that appeared in Shadowgale Forest after the original wind spirits departed. Their origins and nature remain unknown, so scholars gather their essences for study.",al={"what are hollows","wind hollow lore","hollow sprites"}},{q="Where is Shadowgale Forest?",a="Shadowgale Forest lies to the north. Strange wind hollows have appeared there since the area's elemental spirits departed.",al={"where is shadowgale forest","shadowgale location"}},{q="Why did the wind spirits leave?",a="No one knows why the spirits of the wind vanished. The Windshapers seek the cause and hope to restore communion with them.",al={"why did wind spirits leave","where did the spirits go"}},{q="Why are Wind Hollow Essences being gathered?",a="The Windshapers gather essences from dispersed hollows for study. They hope these remains will reveal what brought the beings into existence after the spirits departed.",al={"why collect hollow essences","wind hollow essence purpose"}},{q="Are the hollows considered hostile?",a="The hollows are unwelcome intruders that appeared when the natural spirits were gone. Their spread through Shadowgale Forest calls for dispersal so the region is protected and specimens can be gathered.",al={"are hollows dangerous","hollow sprite threat"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For those who commune with the elements, the natural wind spirits' departure and the hollows' arrival point to a deep disturbance in the local balance of air."},kw={"hollows","shadowgale forest","sprites","unwelcome spirits","wind hollow essence","wind hollows","wind spirits","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=93736},src={"In-game quest text: Unwelcome Spirits"},fv=true}
E["quest:93737"] = {t="quest",n="The Broken Construct",z="general",s="Ayessa has sent you to help Riaani Nightwind with a disabled construct. Hear his plans and learn what he needs done to set the machine right.",h="Ayessa has sent you to help Riaani Nightwind with a disabled construct.",sec={{t="Assisting the Artisan",b="Ayessa sends you to help Riaani Nightwind with a damaged construct. He is deep among its inner parts, searching for the cause of the trouble. Surprised by your arrival, Riaani doubts an untrained traveler can manage delicate mechanical work. Once he climbs out, he agrees to explain what needs doing.",sp=0},{t="Troubleshooting Machinery",b="A construct depends on precise assembly and careful calibration. When it breaks down, its engineer faces serious work. Riaani Nightwind is shoulder-deep in mechanical parts and needs another pair of hands to gather materials or test the machine in the field. Listen to his briefing to learn how you can help bring the inert construct back to working order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Riaani Nightwind?",a="Riaani Nightwind is a tinkerer working on a disabled mechanical construct. He doubts newcomers sent to help, but needs assistance to get the machine working again.",al={"who is riaani nightwind","riaani","construct mechanic"}},{q="Who is Ayessa?",a="Ayessa is an associate who sends travelers to help Riaani Nightwind with his mechanical troubles. Her referral persuades him to consider putting a newcomer to work.",al={"who sent me to riaani","ayessa","who is ayessa"}},{q="What is the broken construct?",a="The broken construct is a mechanical creation that has stopped working properly. Riaani Nightwind is inside it, searching for the parts and tasks needed for repairs.",al={"what is the construct","what machine is riaani fixing","broken machine"}},{q="What does Riaani need help with?",a="Ayessa has sent you to help Riaani. He needs time to climb out of the construct's inner workings and explain what help he needs.",al={"what does riaani want me to do","broken construct task","how to help riaani"}},{q="Why is Riaani skeptical of your help?",a="Riaani is absorbed in technical work and impatient when interrupted. He sees most adventurers as untrained novices until they show they can follow mechanical instructions.",al={"why does riaani call me a novice","is riaani rude","riaani dialogue"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the frustration of troubleshooting a construct with complicated mechanical parts."},kw={"ayessa","broken construct","construct","engineering","riaani nightwind","the broken construct"},m={id=93737},src={"In-game quest text: The Broken Construct"},fv=true}
E["quest:93738"] = {t="quest",n="The Broken Construct",z="general",s="A Windshaper asks you to tell Ayessa Dawnsinger what you learned about the broken construct. The High Order’s work with wind spirit magic has drawn concern.",h="A Windshaper asks you to tell Ayessa Dawnsinger what you learned about the broken construct.",sec={{t="Return to Ayessa",b="Take what you learned to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar. The High Order has tested the Windshapers’ patience with its experiments in wind spirit magic. It has also touched knowledge under Windshaper purview. Ayessa can decide what should happen next.",sp=0},{t="A Troubling Name",b="Ayessa believes the High Order was responsible for the construct breaking down. She knows Belathaan as Valennia Stormfist’s cousin, and says his mother was a Windshaper. His involvement leaves her disappointed. She needs time to reflect.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who should I report to?",a="Report what you learned to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",al={"report to ayessa","where report","ayessa daw sinsinger"}},{q="Why are the Windshapers concerned about the High Order?",a="The High Order has experimented with wind spirit magic and meddled with knowledge under Windshaper purview, though it is forbidden to do so.",al={"high order trouble","why windshapers mad","high order wind magic"}},{q="What happened to the construct?",a="Ayessa believes the High Order was responsible for the construct breaking down.",al={"broken construct","construct broke","why construct broken"}},{q="Who is Belathaan?",a="Belathaan is Valennia Stormfist’s cousin, and his mother was a Windshaper.",al={"belathaan","belathaan family","belathaan cousin"}}},kw={"ayessa dawnsinger","belathaan","broken construct","high order","valanaar","valennia stormfist","wind spirits","windshaper"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","quest:92596"},m={id=93738},src={"In-game quest text: The Broken Construct"},fv=true}
E["quest:93739"] = {t="quest",n="Exploring the Horde",z="general",s="From Grommash Hold, you travel to meet the leaders who guide the Horde. The journey carries you from Orgrimmar to the Darkspear trolls, the tauren and the Forsaken.",h="From Grommash Hold, you travel to meet the leaders who guide the Horde.",sec={{t="Orders from Grommash Hold",b="Nazgrel sends you from Grommash Hold into the wider Horde lands. The fortress stands at the heart of Orgrimmar, where Nazgrel and the Warchief's council oversee military affairs. You leave Durotar's red canyons behind to learn how far the peoples beneath the red banner are joined.",sp=0},{t="An Alliance of Survival",b="You meet the leaders of the Horde's allied peoples: Shadow Hunter Vol'jin of the Darkspear trolls, High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof of the tauren, and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, queen of the Forsaken. Speaking with each in person lets you see the ties between Kalimdor and Lordaeron, across the Great Sea, where plague has scarred the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Exploring the Horde?",a="You report to Nazgrel in Grommash Hold, then travel across Horde lands to meet Vol'jin, Cairne Bloodhoof and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"what is exploring the horde","exploring the horde quest","what do you do in this quest"}},{q="Who is Nazgrel and where is he located?",a="Nazgrel is an orc warrior and trusted lieutenant in Grommash Hold, within Orgrimmar. He advises the Horde and directs aspiring champions to commanders and allies across its lands.",al={"who is nazgrel","where is nazgrel","nazgrel role"}},{q="Which leaders are you sent to meet?",a="You meet Shadow Hunter Vol'jin of the Darkspear trolls, High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof of the tauren in Mulgore, and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen of the Forsaken in the Undercity.",al={"which leaders do i talk to","leaders to visit","who to speak with"}},{q="Why are adventurers instructed to visit each leader?",a="The Horde's peoples are bound by shared survival and pacts of brotherhood. Meeting Vol'jin, Cairne and Sylvanas shows you the alliance's reach, from Durotar and Mulgore to Lordaeron.",al={"why visit all leaders","purpose of visiting horde leaders","diplomacy reason"}},{q="Where can each of the leaders be found?",a="Vol'jin is among the Darkspear trolls in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. Cairne Bloodhoof holds court atop the mesas of Thunder Bluff in Mulgore. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner resides in the Undercity's Royal Quarter beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"where are the leaders located","leader locations","how to find voljin cairne sylvanas"}},{q="What is Grommash Hold?",a="Grommash Hold is the central fortress in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. Named for Grom Hellscream, it is where Warchief Thrall and his advisors, including Nazgrel, oversee Horde affairs.",al={"what is grommash hold","where is grommash hold","orgrimmar hold"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="You meet the leaders guiding the Horde across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Orc"]="Nazgrel advises Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar and guides young orc warriors making their mark.",["race:Troll"]="Speaking with Shadow Hunter Vol'jin strengthens the bond between the Darkspear tribe and their orc allies in the Valley of Spirits.",["race:Tauren"]="Meeting High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff brings you to the spiritual heart and strength of the tauren.",["race:Undead"]="Traveling to the Undercity to meet the Dark Lady Sylvanas Windrunner shows the Forsaken's strategic, if tense, alliance with Kalimdor's Horde."},kw={"cairne bloodhoof","darkspear","exploring the horde","forsaken","grommash hold","nazgrel","orgrimmar","sylvanas windrunner","tauren","thunder bluff","undercity","vol'jin"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold","npc:vol-jin","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","npc:sylvanas-windrunner"},m={id=93739},src={"In-game quest text: Exploring the Horde"},fv=true}
E["quest:93740"] = {t="quest",n="Blood for Blood",z="general",s="Several Windshaper novices lie dead in the Highlands, and the Windshapers suspect the Al'Aketh. Ayessa sends you north to the Gustberry Lowlands to answer the killings and bring back the fallen cultists' windstone prayer charms.",h="Several Windshaper novices lie dead in the Highlands, and the Windshapers suspect the Al'Aketh.",sec={{t="A Grim Discovery",b="Several Windshaper novices have been found slain in the Highlands. Proof is scarce, yet the Windshapers suspect the Al'Aketh cultists. Their zealotry makes them the chief suspects. The Windshapers' creed demands an eye for an eye, so they will not let the killings go unanswered.",sp=0},{t="Demands of Retribution",b="Ayessa calls for you to strike at any Al'Aketh you find north in the Gustberry Lowlands. She asks you to bring back the windstone prayer charms carried by the fallen cultists, as proof of their deaths. The Windshapers see this strike as an answer to the cultists' long fanaticism.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are cultists whom the Windshapers regard as bloody zealots. The Windshapers suspect them of slaying novices in the Highlands.",al={"who are the alaketh","alaketh cultists","who are we fighting"}},{q="Why are the Windshapers seeking retribution?",a="Several Windshaper novices were found dead in the Highlands, and the Windshapers suspect the Al'Aketh. Their creed calls for vengeance in return.",al={"why kill alaketh","windshaper novices dead","why revenge"}},{q="Who is Ayessa?",a="Ayessa represents the Windshapers. She directs their retribution against the Al'Aketh and collects the prayer charms taken from fallen cultists.",al={"who is ayessa","quest giver","ayessa windshaper"}},{q="What are the windstone prayer charms?",a="Al'Aketh cultists carry windstone prayer charms. Ayessa asks for them as proof that the cultists responsible for the killings have been slain.",al={"what are windstone charms","prayer charms","proof of the deed"}},{q="Where can the Al'Aketh be found?",a="The Al'Aketh are to the north in the Gustberry Lowlands, where they carry out their practices.",al={"where are the alaketh","where are cultists","gustberry lowlands location"}}},kw={"al'aketh","ayessa","blood for blood","cultists","gustberry lowlands","highlands","windshapers","windstone prayer charms"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=93740},src={"In-game quest text: Blood for Blood"},fv=true}
E["quest:93791"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Belann",z="general",s="In Valanaar, aspiring spellcasters are sent to meet Belann Windwood. The High Order honors the making of a personal spell focus as a long-held tradition.",h="In Valanaar, aspiring spellcasters are sent to meet Belann Windwood.",sec={{t="A Rite of Growing Power",b="As students grow in command of magic, the High Order turns to an ancient custom to test and strengthen their talents. Making a spell focus of their own, whether a wand or staff, is one of the order’s most enduring traditions. It is for students who wish to bind their growing power to an implement they have made themselves.",sp=0},{t="The Craftsman of Valanaar",b="In Valanaar, initiates seek Belann Windwood for help with this craft. He has spent more than a century forging staves and wands for the High Order. A trusted mentor, Belann welcomes dedicated students and guides them through the craft and history of their magical tools.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Belann Windwood?",a="Belann Windwood is a master craftsman who lives in Valanaar. For more than a century, he has made staves and wands for members of the High Order.",al={"who is belann","belann windwood","belann"}},{q="What is the High Order?",a="The High Order is an ancient organization of practitioners. Its traditions include guiding young spellcasters as they make and master their own spell focuses.",al={"what is the high order","high order lore"}},{q="What is a spell focus?",a="A spell focus, such as a wand or staff, channels magical energies. For developing spellcasters in the High Order, making one is among the oldest rites of passage.",al={"what is a spell focus","purpose of spell focus"}},{q="Where can Valanaar be found?",a="Valanaar is the settlement where Belann Windwood keeps his workshop and helps High Order students craft focuses.",al={"where is valanaar","valanaar location"}},{q="Why are you sent to speak with Belann?",a="As an aspiring wielder of magic, you are sent to study under Belann, whose expertise spans more than a century, and begin shaping your own magical implement.",al={"why visit belann","why craft a focus"}},{q="What happens after you meet Belann?",a="When you introduce yourself to Belann in Valanaar, he welcomes you and prepares to explain the next stages of assembling your spell focus.",al={"what happens next","after speaking with belann"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, making a personal spell focus marks a vital rite of passage and honors the ancient traditions of the High Order."},kw={"belann","belann windwood","high order","spell focus","staves","valanaar","wands"},rel={"quest:92472","quest:92596"},m={id=93791},src={"In-game quest text: Speak with Belann"},fv=true}
E["quest:93797"] = {t="quest",n="Boughs in the Wind",z="general",s="In Valanaar, Belann Windwood guides apprentices through the old rite of shaping a spell focus. They seek a wind-touched branch near Falaath Village, as fewer people in Zephras are born with a gift for magic.",h="In Valanaar, Belann Windwood guides apprentices through the old rite of shaping a spell focus.",sec={{t="A Rite of Passage",b="Young spellcasters in Zephras begin this old rite when they show a gift for magic. In Valanaar, Belann Windwood guides apprentices as they gather a fallen branch from the region’s oldest trees. The boughs keep traces of wind, making them fit to channel spells.",sp=0},{t="Whispers at the Wind Shrine",b="The strongest boughs lie near the wind shrine just south of Falaath Village, where elemental currents gather. Tradition says a branch may choose its spellcaster, and some say it sings softly to those able to wield its power. For elders like Belann, each apprentice who completes the rite helps carry their culture forward. Fewer people in Zephras are born with a gift for magic each passing year.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Boughs in the Wind?",a="Apprentices gather a wind-touched fallen branch to shape a spell focus. This old rite helps preserve Zephras’s magical heritage.",al={"what is boughs in the wind","boughs in the wind quest","spell focus quest"}},{q="Who is Belann Windwood?",a="Belann Windwood is a mentor in Valanaar who guides young spellcasters as they shape their spell focuses. He worries that fewer people show a gift for magic each passing year.",al={"who is belann windwood","belann questgiver","belann valanaar"}},{q="Where do you find the Wind-Infused Bough?",a="The boughs fall from the oldest trees near the wind shrine just south of Falaath Village. Belann directs apprentices there because ancient wood retains traces of elemental currents.",al={"where to find wind bough","where is wind-infused bough","bough location"}},{q="Why do young spellcasters create a spell focus?",a="Apprentices shape their own spell focus after showing a gift for magic. It channels elemental energies and marks their passage into an old cultural rite.",al={"why make spell focus","purpose of spell focus","spell focus lore"}},{q="Why does Belann ask if the branch sang to you?",a="Belann Windwood says tradition holds that a branch often chooses its spellcaster. A fitting bough may seem to sing to someone sensitive to elemental winds.",al={"branch picks the caster","singing branch","does the branch choose you"}},{q="What is happening to magic in Zephras?",a="Fewer people in Zephras are born with a natural gift for magic each passing year. Belann believes keeping the old rites alive matters all the more.",al={"where is zephras","magic fading zephras","zephras magic lore"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As fewer youths show a gift for magic each passing year, shaping a traditional spell focus helps preserve your people’s ancestral culture in Zephras.",["class:Mage"]="Shaping a spell focus from a wind-touched bough marks an early rite for spellcasters learning to channel elemental resonance."},kw={"belann windwood","boughs in the wind","falaath village","spell focus","valanaar","wind shrine","wind-infused bough","zephras"},rel={"quest:92529"},m={id=93797},src={"In-game quest text: Boughs in the Wind"},fv=true}
E["quest:93835"] = {t="quest",n="Confront Lorthuna",z="general",s="An injured mage needs you to follow Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale through a portal to the Rohashi Spires. There, they face High Priestess Lorthuna and need your help.",h="An injured mage needs you to follow Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale through a portal to the Rohashi...",sec={{t="Through the portal",b="Lorthuna fled through a portal to the spires above. Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale followed moments ago, but their companion is too badly hurt to go with them. Join the two mages through the portal as they face the High Priestess.",sp=0},{t="After the clash",b="The remaining mages were sent to help Valennia and her forces escape. Valennia is resting at High Elder Shadowsong's residence. Ansirem has returned to Azeroth after discussing the High Order's next steps. Zephras survived the day, but remains dangerously vulnerable, and plans must be made for what comes next.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to go after Lorthuna?",a="An injured mage asks you to follow Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale through the portal and help them face High Priestess Lorthuna.",al={"who sent me","injured mage","who needs help"}},{q="Where did Lorthuna go?",a="Lorthuna fled through a portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead.",al={"where is lorthuna","lorthuna portal","where'd she flee"}},{q="Who went after Lorthuna?",a="Ayessa Dawnsinger and Elaadrin Evengale went through the portal after Lorthuna.",al={"ayessa and elaadrin","who followed her","who's up there"}},{q="Why can't the injured mage go with them?",a="The mage took too many hits and must stay behind.",al={"why am i going alone","mage too hurt","why stay behind"}},{q="Where is Valennia?",a="Valennia is resting at High Elder Shadowsong's residence after the remaining mages helped her and her forces escape.",al={"valennia location","where did she go","valennia safe"}},{q="What is at risk now?",a="Zephras is dangerously vulnerable, and the High Order must plan for what comes next.",al={"zephras vulnerable","what happened to zephras","high order next"}}},kw={"ayessa dawnsinger","elaadrin evengale","high order","lorthuna","portal","rohashi spires","valennia","zephras"},rel={"npc:ayessa-dawnsinger","quest:92596"},m={id=93835},src={"In-game quest text: Confront Lorthuna"},fv=true}
E["quest:93836"] = {t="quest",n="The Fate of Zephras",z="general",s="After Lorthuna falls, word of danger reaches Valanaar. Zephras Isle's wards have failed, and Ayessa proposes a journey to Azeroth. High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong must hear what has happened.",h="After Lorthuna falls, word of danger reaches Valanaar.",sec={{t="A Precarious Victory",b="Lorthuna has fallen after the battle above the Shrine of Akir. Yet Zephras Isle has paid dearly for the victory. Its ancient wards, which hid it from Al'Akir, have collapsed. The floating sanctuary now lies exposed in the Windlord's domain. A messenger crosses the isle with word for Valanaar.",sp=0},{t="The Word to Valanaar",b="High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong hears that Lorthuna is dead and the wards have broken. He also learns that Ayessa means to lead an expedition to Azeroth. With their magical veil gone, the islanders look beyond their home for a way to protect it. Shadowsong weighs fear against hope. Al'Akir is a terrible menace, yet elemental gods move across vast stretches of time. That may leave the islanders precious time to act.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest The Fate of Zephras about?",a="Lorthuna has fallen at the Shrine of Akir, and word of the danger goes to Valanaar. The island's protective wards have failed, and Ayessa proposes an expedition to Azeroth. High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong receives the news.",al={"fate of zephras quest","what is the fate of zephras","what happens in the fate of zephras"}},{q="Why is Zephras Isle in danger from Al'Akir?",a="Zephras Isle lies within the elemental domain of Al'Akir, the Windlord. Ancient wards once hid the sanctuary from his sight. Now they are gone, leaving the island exposed should Al'Akir turn his wrath upon it.",al={"why is zephras in danger","why attack zephras","zephras elemental threat"}},{q="Who is Talaanis Shadowsong?",a="Talaanis Shadowsong is the High Elder of the Skyborne in Valanaar on Zephras Isle. He oversees his people's rule and survival, and receives reports of threats and choices facing their home.",al={"who is talaanis shadowsong","high elder shadowsong","where is talaanis shadowsong"}},{q="What is Ayessa's plan?",a="Ayessa plans to lead an expedition from Zephras Isle to Azeroth. She seeks answers and allies beyond their domain to help protect her people from Al'Akir.",al={"who is ayessa","ayessa plan","what is ayessa doing"}},{q="Who was Lorthuna and what happened to her?",a="Lorthuna led the cult on Zephras Isle. She was slain above the Shrine of Akir, breaking the cult's leadership as the island's protective wards fell.",al={"who is lorthuna","cult leader lorthuna","what happened to lorthuna"}},{q="Who is Muln?",a="Muln is an advisor or scholar who knows about the elemental lords. He warned Zephras's defenders of Al'Akir's great power and danger, and confirmed their vulnerability without magical concealment.",al={"who is muln","muln lore"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne of Zephras Isle, you face the loss of the wards and the threat of Al'Akir. Your people now look beyond their floating home for a way to protect it.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the Windlord Al'Akir's elemental domain surrounds Zephras. With the ancient wards gone, the island lies exposed."},kw={"al'akir","ayessa","fate of zephras","lorthuna","muln","shrine of akir","talaanis shadowsong","valanaar","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras"},m={id=93836},src={"In-game quest text: The Fate of Zephras"},fv=true}
E["quest:93926"] = {t="quest",n="The Western Watch",z="general",s="At the outpost southwest of the settlement, cultists press the defenders, and local leaders call them back. They judge the tower too costly to hold and turn to protecting the village.",h="At the outpost southwest of the settlement, cultists press the defenders, and local leaders call them back.",sec={{t="A Costly Outpost",b="The western watchtower guards the frontier southwest of the settlement. Cultists have renewed their assault, and local leaders decide the isolated post costs too many lives to defend. So they prepare orders recalling the peacekeepers. They hope to spare more lives and gather every defender to protect the village and its people.",sp=0},{t="Too Late to Retreat",b="Peacekeeper Vaaniel commanded the garrison at the western watch. The withdrawal order arrived too late. Storm-wielding cult spellcasters had overrun the tower before messengers reached it. Vaaniel and his garrison lay dead among scorched stone and lightning burns.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Peacekeeper Vaaniel?",a="Peacekeeper Vaaniel commands the peacekeepers at the western watchtower. Cultists are attacking, and you are sent to find him and tell him to bring his garrison back to the village quickly.",al={"who is vaaniel","vaaniel lore","peacekeeper vaaniel"}},{q="Why were the peacekeepers ordered to abandon the watchtower?",a="Local leaders ordered the peacekeepers to leave because the cult assaults were costing too many lives. They want the defenders gathered at the village to protect its people.",al={"why abandon tower","why leave watchtower","western watch order"}},{q="What killed Peacekeeper Vaaniel?",a="Storm-wielding cult spellcasters killed Peacekeeper Vaaniel. Lightning and elemental magic left burns and scorch marks on him and the tower's defenders.",al={"how did vaaniel die","who killed vaaniel","peacekeeper killed by what"}},{q="Who attacked the western watchtower?",a="A hostile cult attacked the western watchtower with destructive storm magic. Local commanders do not know why the cult wants the tower, but the attack threatens nearby settlements.",al={"who is attacking the tower","cult attack western tower","what cult is this"}},{q="Where is the western watchtower located?",a="The western watchtower stands southwest of the local settlement, guarding the western approaches. Its isolation left it vulnerable to cult assaults.",al={"where is the watchtower","western watchtower location"}},{q="What happened to the garrison at the tower?",a="The watchtower had fallen by the time runners arrived with orders to evacuate. Cult spellcasters killed Peacekeeper Vaaniel and the other defenders shortly before aid could reach them.",al={"what happens at the tower","watchtower outcome","did any peacekeepers survive"}}},kw={"cult","peacekeeper vaaniel","peacekeepers","storm spellcasters","the western watch","watchtower","western watchtower"},m={id=93926},src={"In-game quest text: The Western Watch"},fv=true}
E["quest:93927"] = {t="quest",n="A Last Request",z="general",s="On Zephras, a fallen peacekeeper carries a message that may reveal his final moments. His bloodstained note points to the duty he left unfinished.",h="On Zephras, a fallen peacekeeper carries a message that may reveal his final moments.",sec={{t="A Grim Discovery",b="You find a dead peacekeeper in the field with a bloodstained note in his hands. When you examine him, the note slips free. On Zephras, peacekeepers risk their lives to keep order. His last words may tell what happened to him.",sp=0},{t="The Final Message",b="The bloodied parchment holds the peacekeeper's final plea or instructions. Whoever killed him left his duty unfinished. Read the clues and complete his final mission. The note points the way to answer his dying call.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the dead peacekeeper?",a="The fallen peacekeeper's identity is unknown when you find him. He kept order, and his duty ended violently. Only an urgent message remains in his hands.",al={"who is the dead peacekeeper","dead peacekeeper","peacekeeper identity"}},{q="What is written on the bloody note?",a="The note recounts the peacekeeper's final account. The cult surprised his post. Raani never saw it coming, Arvensus took a sword to the gut, and a lightning bolt felled the writer. Left for dead, he expected his wounds to finish what the cult began.",al={"what is the bloody note","what does the note say","peacekeeper note"}},{q="How is this request discovered?",a="You find the peacekeeper's body in the field and examine it. The bloody note in his hands holds his final plea.",al={"how to start a last request","where is a last request found"}},{q="What happened to the peacekeeper?",a="The cult ambushed the peacekeeper's post without warning. His fellows fell, and a lightning bolt struck him, leaving him for dead. He lived long enough to record what happened in the note found in his hands.",al={"why was peacekeeper killed","who killed peacekeeper"}},{q="What is the peacekeeper's last request?",a="The peacekeeper died before he could finish his mission or deliver his message. You can retrieve and read his bloodstained note, decipher his final instructions, and fulfill his dying wish.",al={"what is the peacekeeper's request","last request purpose"}},{q="What role do peacekeepers serve?",a="Peacekeepers protect settlements and roads, keeping order and defending them from danger. When one falls in the field, their duties remain unfinished and their allies unwarned unless someone recovers their final report.",al={"who are peacekeepers","peacekeeper lore"}}},kw={"a last request","bloody note","dead peacekeeper","peacekeeper","peacekeeper note"},m={id=93927},src={"In-game quest text: A Last Request"},fv=true}
E["quest:93948"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver the Signet",z="general",s="A traveler carries the recovered Shadowsong Family Signet to High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. Its return confirms his nephew's death on Zephras Isle, and Talaanis points the traveler toward the local peacekeepers.",h="A traveler carries the recovered Shadowsong Family Signet to High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",sec={{t="A Somber Errand",b="A traveler carries the Shadowsong Family Signet to Valanaar, recovered from an isolated tower. The grim token is meant for Talaanis Shadowsong, the High Elder of Zephras Isle. His people love him, though hardship weighs on the settlement. The ring confirms his nephew has perished, and Talaanis receives the heirloom with condolences.",sp=0},{t="Grief and Duty in Valanaar",b="In Valanaar, High Elder Talaanis thanks the traveler for returning the signet, though grief shadows him. He recognizes the traveler's skill and points them to Captain Valennia Stormfist, who leads the Valanaar peacekeepers. The settlement faces strained circumstances and mounting pressures. Its protectors welcome capable hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talaanis Shadowsong?",a="Talaanis Shadowsong is the High Elder of Zephras Isle. His community respects and loves him, and the returned signet confirms his nephew's death.",al={"who is talaanis","high elder talaanis","talaanis shadowsong lore"}},{q="What is the Shadowsong Family Signet?",a="The Shadowsong Family Signet is a family ring recovered from a tower. Its return to Talaanis Shadowsong confirms that his nephew has perished.",al={"what is the signet ring","nephews ring","shadowsong signet"}},{q="Where is Valanaar located?",a="Valanaar is a settlement on Zephras Isle. High Elder Talaanis Shadowsong lives there, and Captain Valennia Stormfist leads its peacekeepers.",al={"where is valanaar","valanaar settlement","talaanis location"}},{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist leads the peacekeepers in Valanaar. High Elder Talaanis directs capable travelers to speak with her because the settlement needs help.",al={"who is valennia stormfist","captain valennia","valanaar peacekeeper captain"}},{q="Who are the shen'dorei mentioned by Talaanis?",a="Talaanis calls capable young travelers coming down from the highlands shen'dorei, a name that reflects the elven presence and heritage on Zephras Isle.",al={"who are the shendorei","shendorei highlands"}},{q="What happened to Talaanis Shadowsong's nephew?",a="Talaanis's nephew died at a tower, where the family signet was lost. Returning the ring to Valanaar tells the High Elder of his nephew's death.",al={"what happened to talaanis nephew","how did nephew die"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the Shadowsong name carries deep history among elven lineages. On Zephras Isle, High Elder Talaanis and the local shen'dorei face their own struggles."},kw={"deliver the signet","shadowsong family signet","shen'dorei","talaanis shadowsong","valanaar","valennia stormfist","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras","quest:92579"},m={id=93948},src={"In-game quest text: Deliver the Signet"},fv=true}
E["quest:93949"] = {t="quest",n="Bugged",z="general",s="In Valanaar, seasonal skyhopper swarms now threaten the settlement. High Order mages found listening enchantments on slain insects, and local cultists are suspected of spying through them.",h="In Valanaar, seasonal skyhopper swarms now threaten the settlement.",sec={{t="Eavesdroppers in the Swarm",b="When skyhopper season comes, lowland insects swarm around Valanaar. High Order mages inspected several slain skyhoppers and found listening enchantments on them. Local cultists are suspected of using the seasonal pests to eavesdrop on the city.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Air",b="The enchanted skyhoppers look like ordinary insects, so Valanaar's protectors must cull the whole swarm. Clearing them out denies the hostile cult intelligence and ends its magical surveillance of the city.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are skyhoppers?",a="Skyhoppers are winged pests native to the lowlands around Valanaar. They swarm in great numbers during their seasonal surge.",al={"what are skyhoppers","skyhopper bug"}},{q="Who enchanted the insects?",a="Local cultists are suspected of placing listening spells on skyhoppers to eavesdrop on Valanaar.",al={"who enchanted the bugs","cult listening bugs","who is spying in valanaar"}},{q="How do you tell which skyhoppers are enchanted?",a="Enchanted skyhoppers look just like ordinary insects. The whole swarm must be cleared to uncover and eliminate the spies.",al={"how to tell enchanted skyhoppers","which bugs are enchanted"}},{q="Where does this take place?",a="The infestation and spying take place around Valanaar, an aerial city near the lowlands where seasonal swarms rise.",al={"where is bugged quest","valanaar bugs"}},{q="What kind of enchantment was placed on the skyhoppers?",a="High Order mages found listening spells bound to slain skyhoppers. The enchantments turn them into roving watchers.",al={"what spell is on the bugs","skyhopper enchantment"}},{q="Why do all the skyhoppers need to be exterminated?",a="Enchanted skyhoppers cannot be distinguished from ordinary pests by sight. Clearing the swarms is necessary to purge the cult's listening posts and protect Valanaar.",al={"why kill skyhoppers","bugged quest goal"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="High Order mages found listening enchantments on ordinary skyhoppers, turning the seasonal swarm into a threat to Valanaar."},kw={"bugged","cult","enchanted skyhoppers","high order","listening spell","skyhoppers","valanaar"},rel={"topic:mage"},m={id=93949},src={"In-game quest text: Bugged"},fv=true}
E["quest:93951"] = {t="quest",n="A Little Beauty",z="general",s="In the Shen'dar Highlands, the Skyborne gather hippogryph down near Zephras. Its bright plumes bring beauty and small joys to the village through hard times.",h="In the Shen'dar Highlands, the Skyborne gather hippogryph down near Zephras.",sec={{t="Plumes of the Highlands",b="Wild hippogryphs nest on Zephras Isle, southwest of the village in the Shen'dar Highlands. They are territorial and can trouble travelers nearby. Yet they shed vibrant, silky soft down, which the Skyborne gather to weave into hair ornaments.",sp=0},{t="Finding Joy in Small Things",b="For Zephras's artisan, gathering feathers for hair is more than vanity. Even in hard times, small joys shared with others help keep the community's spirit alive. Beauty gives each day in the village something to celebrate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are hippogryph feathers being collected?",a="The Skyborne gather wild hippogryph down to make hair adornments. The vibrant, silky soft plumes have fallen from the birds, which can trouble travelers near the settlement.",al={"why gather feathers","what are feathers for","feather purpose"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is the island home of the Skyborne. Its artisan crafts hair adornments from gathered feathers to bring happiness and lighthearted moments to residents.",al={"who is Zephras","what town is this","where does this happen"}},{q="Where do the hippogryphs nest?",a="Wild hippogryphs nest southwest of the village in the Shen'dar Highlands. They are territorial and keep unwanted guests away from their nesting grounds.",al={"where are the nests","where are hippogryphs","shendar highlands location"}},{q="Why are small luxuries like hair adornments important in times like these?",a="The artisan believes small joys and beauty matter, especially in difficult times. Bringing happiness to others makes the effort worthwhile.",al={"are feathers important","why hair decorations","vain triviality"}},{q="Are the hippogryphs hostile to visitors?",a="The wild hippogryphs southwest of the village defend their nesting grounds from intruders. Gathering their fallen feathers can be hazardous for unwary travelers.",al={"why hippogryphs dangerous","are hippogryphs wild"}},{q="Is decorating hair with feathers common among the Skyborne?",a="Yes, many Skyborne weave vibrant plumes into their hair. Hippogryph down is exceptionally soft and well suited to these adornments.",al={"skyborne feathers","do skyborne wear feathers"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you can gather vibrant hippogryph down to adorn your hair with soft plumes. This custom brings small joys to Zephras through hardship."},kw={"a little beauty","down feathers","feathers","hippogryph","plumes","shen'dar highlands","skyborne","zephras"},rel={"topic:skyborne"},m={id=93951},src={"In-game quest text: A Little Beauty"},fv=true}
E["quest:93958"] = {t="quest",n="The Inner Sanctum",z="general",s="At the Shrine of Akir, Valennia Stormfist's assault has gone silent. Her force breached the deepest chamber amid fierce fighting, and now allies outside fear for those within.",h="At the Shrine of Akir, Valennia Stormfist's assault has gone silent.",sec={{t="A Sudden Silence",b="Valennia Stormfist led her detachment into the inner sanctum of the Shrine of Akir after a hard assault. Fighting sounded from deep within the chambers, fierce and desperate. Then the noise stopped without warning. Allies waiting outside can only fear the worst.",sp=0},{t="The Cost of the Breach",b="Valennia Stormfist is found gravely wounded inside the quiet sanctum. Her vanguard's fate remains uncertain in the aftermath of the battle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Valennia Stormfist?",a="Valennia Stormfist commands the assault into the depths of the Shrine of Akir. She led her forces through the breach into the inner sanctum, where the fighting soon fell silent.",al={"who is valennia","who is valennia stormfist","valennia"}},{q="What is the Shrine of Akir?",a="The Shrine of Akir holds an inner sanctum now under assault. Valennia's troops broke through its defenses amid heavy fighting, making the shrine the heart of a deadly clash.",al={"what is shrine of akir","shrine of akir lore","akir shrine"}},{q="What happened to Valennia's forces inside?",a="Heavy fighting rang out inside after the breach, then stopped all at once. The silence leaves allies outside fearing Valennia's vanguard may have been overwhelmed or killed.",al={"why is it quiet","what happened to valennias forces","valennia soldiers"}},{q="Is Valennia Stormfist still alive?",a="Valennia Stormfist survives the assault, gravely wounded inside the Shrine of Akir's inner sanctum after the fighting ends.",al={"is valennia alive","did valennia die","valennia fate"}},{q="What is the objective inside the inner sanctum?",a="The inner sanctum is the deepest chamber in the Shrine of Akir. You are sent in alone to assess the aftermath and find Valennia and any fighters who survived.",al={"what is the inner sanctum","inner sanctum quest purpose"}},{q="Who sends you into the inner sanctum?",a="An ally keeping watch at the rear outside the inner sanctum sends you in. They hold the perimeter and watch your back as you go to join Valennia's vanguard.",al={"who sends you to valennia","quest giver inner sanctum"}}},kw={"inner sanctum","shrine of akir","stormfist","the inner sanctum","valennia","valennia stormfist"},m={id=93958},src={"In-game quest text: The Inner Sanctum"},fv=true}
E["quest:94003"] = {t="quest",n="The Skybreaker Bulwark",z="general",s="At the Shrine of Akir, Zaal Stormshield holds the Skybreaker Bulwark. The last of the Skybreakers seeks its return from the cultist who took it.",h="At the Shrine of Akir, Zaal Stormshield holds the Skybreaker Bulwark.",sec={{t="A Fallen Lineage",b="On Zephras Isle, the Al'Aketh have slain the Skybreakers, leaving one survivor. The last of the family bears deep sorrow and bitter shame over the loss of their greatest heirloom. The cultist Zaal Stormshield took the Skybreaker Bulwark and now lurks at the Shrine of Akir.",sp=0},{t="The Sacred Shield",b="By family tradition, the Skybreaker Bulwark protects anyone truly worthy to wield it. The last Skybreaker believes Zaal unworthy of its divine favor. So the survivor seeks an adventurer to strike down the thief at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim the ancestral shield. In return, the Skybreaker offers training in the Skybreaker Defense technique.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Skybreakers?",a="The Skybreakers are an ancient lineage on Zephras Isle, nearly wiped out by the Al'Aketh. The one who asks for the shield is the sole survivor.",al={"who are the skybreakers","skybreaker family"}},{q="What is the Skybreaker Bulwark?",a="The Skybreaker Bulwark is an ancestral shield of the Skybreaker line on Zephras Isle. Family tradition says no harm can befall anyone worthy to wield it.",al={"what is the skybreaker bulwark","the shield","skybreaker shield lore"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh slew the Skybreaker family on Zephras Isle, leaving one survivor to mourn their loss.",al={"who killed the skybreakers","what are the alaketh","alaketh"}},{q="Who is Zaal Stormshield?",a="Zaal Stormshield is a cultist who took the Skybreaker Bulwark after the Skybreaker family was slain. He lurks with the heirloom at the Shrine of Akir on Zephras Isle.",al={"who has the shield","zaal","stormshield"}},{q="Where is the Shrine of Akir?",a="The Shrine of Akir is on Zephras Isle. Zaal Stormshield lurks there with the stolen Skybreaker Bulwark.",al={"where is zaal","shrine of akir location","where to find shield"}},{q="Why must the Bulwark be reclaimed?",a="The last Skybreaker seeks the Bulwark's return to right the family's shame and take the sacred relic from unworthy hands. In return, the survivor teaches the Skybreaker Defense technique.",al={"why recover shield","what is skybreaker defense","shield reward"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can learn the Skybreaker Defense technique by recovering the ancestral shield.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may value the work of reclaiming a blessed heirloom from a corrupt cultist."},kw={"al'aketh","shrine of akir","skybreaker","skybreaker bulwark","skybreaker defense","the skybreaker bulwark","zaal stormshield","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras"},m={id=94003},src={"In-game quest text: The Skybreaker Bulwark"},fv=true}
E["quest:94006"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Ursera Spirit",z="general",s="A druid sends you to meet Urs'endris, a spirit on Zephras who has taught druids the ursera shape for generations. His domain is withering, and Urs'endris can guide your studies further.",h="A druid sends you to meet Urs'endris, a spirit on Zephras who has taught druids the ursera shape for...",sec={{t="The Great Spirit",b="A druid sends you to Urs'endris near the falls northeast of Valanaar. Your druidic studies have brought you to a meeting with one of Zephras's great spirits. Urs'endris has taught druids to take the ursera shape for generations, and his domain is withering into the sky.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Urs'endris?",a="Urs'endris is a wise spirit on Zephras who has taught druids to take the ursera shape for generations.",al={"urs'endris who","great spirit urs","ursera spirit"}},{q="Where can I find Urs'endris?",a="Urs'endris is near the falls northeast of Valanaar, near the Shrine of Akir.",al={"urs'endris location","where is urs'endris","meet the spirit"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Urs'endris?",a="Your druidic studies have progressed enough for you to meet one of Zephras's great spirits, and Urs'endris can instruct you further.",al={"why meet urs'endris","druid spirit quest","ursera studies"}},{q="What is happening to Urs'endris's domain?",a="Urs'endris's domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky.",al={"withering domain","zephras falling","what's wrong there"}},{q="What is the ursera shape?",a="The ursera shape is a form Urs'endris has taught druids to take for generations.",al={"ursera form","way of the claw","ursera"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, your studies have brought you to Urs'endris, who has taught druids the ursera shape for generations."},kw={"druid","falls","shrine of akir","spirit","urs'endris","ursera","valanaar","zephras"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94006},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Ursera Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:94007"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="In Valanaar, Quel'ana Quickgale can teach you to tame a beast. Your time in the highlands has prepared you to seek an animal companion.",h="In Valanaar, Quel'ana Quickgale can teach you to tame a beast.",sec={{t="A New Companion",b="Your host believes you are ready to seek an animal companion after your time in the highlands. Go to Valanaar and speak with Quel'ana Quickgale. He will teach you the art of beast taming.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches beast taming?",a="Quel'ana Quickgale teaches you to tame beasts in Valanaar.",al={"who is Quel'ana Quickgale","beast taming teacher"}},{q="Where do I find Quel'ana Quickgale?",a="Quel'ana Quickgale is in Valanaar, the port to the southeast.",al={"where is Quel'ana","Valanaar taming"}},{q="Why am I going to Valanaar?",a="You are sent to Valanaar to speak with Quel'ana Quickgale and begin learning to tame beasts.",al={"why Valanaar","taming beast quest"}},{q="What am I learning?",a="Quel'ana Quickgale will teach you to tame a beast so you can seek an animal companion.",al={"what is beast taming","animal companion"}}},kw={"animal companion","beast taming","highlands","quel'ana quickgale","taming the beast","valanaar"},m={id=94007},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94013"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="Quel'ana Quickgale gives you one last trial in taming a Vuldren Alpha. Mastering it prepares you for the deeper teachings of your class.",h="Quel'ana Quickgale gives you one last trial in taming a Vuldren Alpha.",sec={{t="The Final Trial",b="Quel'ana gives you a Taming Rod and sends you to the Gustberry Lowlands. There, you are to tame a Vuldren Alpha. Then return the rod to him in Valanaar. This trial proves your mastery and prepares you for deeper class teachings.",sp=0},{t="A New Lesson",b="After you return, Quel'ana says you have learned the basics. He offers to teach you to form a lasting bond with an animal companion. He urges you to carry that knowledge forward for the good of the class Zephras Isle needs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Quel'ana ask me to tame?",a="Quel'ana asks you to tame a Vuldren Alpha with the Taming Rod in the Gustberry Lowlands.",al={"vuldren alpha taming","what beast","tame alpha"}},{q="Where do I find the Vuldren Alpha?",a="The Vuldren Alpha is in the Gustberry Lowlands.",al={"alpha location","gustberry lowlands","where tame beast"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod for?",a="Quel'ana gives you the Taming Rod to tame a Vuldren Alpha.",al={"rod purpose","taming rod quest","how use rod"}},{q="Where do I return the Taming Rod?",a="Return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.",al={"return rod","quelana location","where return taming rod"}},{q="What will I learn after this?",a="Quel'ana says he can teach you to form a lasting bond with an animal companion.",al={"next lesson","animal companion bond","what comes after"}}},kw={"animal companion","gustberry lowlands","quel'ana quickgale","taming rod","taming the beast","valanaar","vuldren alpha","zephras isle"},rel={"item:taming-rod","zone:zephras"},m={id=94013},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94050"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="general",s="In Valanaar, you meet Quel'dora Quickgale to learn how to train your pet. Her teaching helps you care for and guide it.",h="In Valanaar, you meet Quel'dora Quickgale to learn how to train your pet.",sec={{t="Quel'dora's Teaching",b="Your fellow hunter sends you to his sister, Quel'dora Quickgale, in Valanaar. You already know how to tame a pet. Now Quel'dora can teach you to train your companion.",sp=0},{t="A Hunter's Charge",b="Quel'dora teaches you to guide your pet, teach it new abilities, feed it, and revive it if it falls in battle. She urges you to respect the balance and remain in awe of the nature around you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Quel'dora Quickgale?",a="Quel'dora Quickgale is the sister of the hunter who sends you to learn pet training.",al={"who is queldora","quel'dora","quickgale"}},{q="Where can I find Quel'dora?",a="Quel'dora Quickgale is in Valanaar.",al={"where queldora","quel'dora location","valanaar trainer"}},{q="What does Quel'dora teach?",a="Quel'dora teaches you to train and guide your pet, teach it abilities, feed it, and revive it if it falls in battle.",al={"pet training","train my pet","what can pet trainer teach"}},{q="Can I already tame a pet?",a="The hunter who sends you to Quel'dora says you already have the power to tame a pet.",al={"tame pet","pet taming","can hunter tame"}},{q="What does the hunter ask me to do?",a="The hunter asks you to speak with Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.",al={"training the beast","pet trainer quest","speak to queldora"}},{q="What does Quel'dora say about nature?",a="Quel'dora urges you to respect the balance and live in awe of the nature around you.",al={"respect nature","balance","quel'dora advice"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you are learning to train and guide a pet you can already tame."},kw={"feed pet","hunter","pet training","quel'dora quickgale","revive pet","tame pet","training the beast","valanaar"},m={id=94050},src={"In-game quest text: Training the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94214"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Shadow Protection Potion",z="general",s="A transferable writ requests one Shadow Protection Potion and gives details for delivery and payment. The transaction depends on bringing the writ with you.",h="A transferable writ requests one Shadow Protection Potion and gives details for delivery and payment.",sec={{t="A Written Request",b="A faded note asks you to provide one Shadow Protection Potion. It also gives the delivery place and payment details, and says the writ can pass from hand to hand. You need the writ with you to complete the exchange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ request?",a="The writ requests one Shadow Protection Potion.",al={"what do they want","potion request","writ item"}},{q="Where do I deliver it?",a="The delivery location is marked on your map.",al={"delivery spot","where to take potion","marked location"}},{q="Does the writ say how I will be paid?",a="The writ includes information about payment.",al={"payment details","how much do they pay","writ payment"}},{q="Can I give the writ to someone else?",a="Yes. The note says the writ is transferable.",al={"is it transferable","pass the writ","transfer writ"}},{q="Do I need to keep the writ with me?",a="Yes. You must have the writ with you to complete the transaction.",al={"need writ to deliver","must I carry it","writ required"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","payment","potion","shadow protection potion","transferable","writ"},m={id=94214},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Shadow Protection Potion"},fv=true}
E["quest:94219"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Draught of Water Breathing",z="general",s="A transferable writ requests one Draught of Water Breathing and gives delivery and payment details. You need the writ to complete the exchange.",h="A transferable writ requests one Draught of Water Breathing and gives delivery and payment details.",sec={{t="A Written Request",b="The faded note asks you for one Draught of Water Breathing. It also gives the delivery place and payment, and can pass from one holder to another.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ request?",a="It requests one Draught of Water Breathing.",al={"what do they want","draught request","writ item"}},{q="Where do I deliver it?",a="The writ gives a delivery location, marked on your map.",al={"delivery place","where to take it","writ location"}},{q="What payment is offered?",a="The writ includes information about payment.",al={"how much pay","writ payment","what do I get"}},{q="Can the writ be transferred?",a="Yes. The note says the writ can be transferred.",al={"transferable writ","can someone else carry it","pass the writ"}},{q="Do I need the writ to complete the exchange?",a="Yes. You must have the writ with you to complete the transaction.",al={"need the note","writ required","can I deliver without it"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","draught of water breathing","payment","water breathing","writ"},m={id=94219},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Draught of Water Breathing"},fv=true}
E["quest:94220"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Pearl-Handled Dagger",z="general",s="A transferable writ requests a Pearl-Handled Dagger and gives terms for its delivery and payment. You need the writ to complete the exchange.",h="A transferable writ requests a Pearl-Handled Dagger and gives terms for its delivery and payment.",sec={{t="The Writ",b="The note is written in faded ink, and it names a Pearl-Handled Dagger among the items wanted. Its lower lines give a delivery place and payment terms. The writ can pass from hand to hand, but you need to hold it when you complete the exchange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ ask for?",a="The writ requests a Pearl-Handled Dagger.",al={"pearl dagger writ","what item is wanted"}},{q="Where do I deliver the item?",a="The delivery location is marked on your map.",al={"delivery place","where to take it"}},{q="What does the customer offer?",a="The writ includes information about payment.",al={"payment terms","how much pay"}},{q="Can I transfer this writ?",a="Yes. The writ says it can be transferred.",al={"pass writ along","is the note transferable"}},{q="Do I need to keep the writ?",a="Yes. You need the writ in your possession to complete the transaction.",al={"need writ to finish","must hold note"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","dagger","delivery","payment","pearl-handled dagger","writ"},m={id=94220},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Pearl-Handled Dagger"},fv=true}
E["quest:94222"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Iridescent Hammer",z="general",s="A customer awaits one Iridescent Hammer, with delivery and payment details set down in a writ. Its transferable mark lets the holder complete the exchange.",h="A customer awaits one Iridescent Hammer, with delivery and payment details set down in a writ.",sec={{t="The Writ",b="The customer asks for one Iridescent Hammer. Bring the writ to complete the exchange at the marked location.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the customer want?",a="One Iridescent Hammer is what the customer wants.",al={"iridescent hammer writ","what item is requested"}},{q="Where do I deliver it?",a="The writ gives the delivery details, and the location is marked on your map.",al={"writ delivery place","where to take hammer"}},{q="Does the writ need to be with me?",a="Yes. Keep the writ with you to complete the exchange.",al={"need writ to deliver","writ required"}},{q="Can someone else use the writ?",a="Yes. The writ is marked as transferable.",al={"transferable writ","pass writ along"}},{q="Does the writ say how payment works?",a="Yes. The writ includes payment information.",al={"hammer payment","how much payment"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","hammer","iridescent hammer","payment","transferable","writ"},m={id=94222},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Iridescent Hammer"},fv=true}
E["quest:94226"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Green Iron Gauntlets",z="general",s="MacKinley’s writ asks you to bring him Green Iron Gauntlets. The transferable note includes delivery and payment details.",h="MacKinley’s writ asks you to bring him Green Iron Gauntlets.",sec={{t="A Written Order",b="The faded writ names Green Iron Gauntlets and gives a delivery place and payment. You need the writ with you to complete the exchange. MacKinley waits for the goods, though his greeting hints that something is amiss.",sp=0},{t="At the Exchange",b="MacKinley says he wanted green iron knuckles, not gauntlets. He accepts the gauntlets while he waits for a replacement, then pays you less than you expected.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does MacKinley ask for?",a="The writ requests one pair of Green Iron Gauntlets, though MacKinley says he meant to ask for green iron knuckles.",al={"mckinley wants what","green iron writ"}},{q="Where do I deliver the gauntlets?",a="The writ gives a delivery location, marked on your map.",al={"where to deliver","writ location"}},{q="Do I need the writ with me?",a="Yes. The writ must be in your possession to complete the exchange.",al={"need writ","forgot the writ"}},{q="What does the writ say about payment?",a="The note includes information about payment, but gives no amount in its text.",al={"how much pay","payment details"}},{q="Can someone else carry the writ?",a="Yes. The note says the writ is transferable.",al={"transferable writ","can i give writ"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","green iron gauntlets","green iron knuckles","mackinley","payment","transferable"},m={id=94226},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Green Iron Gauntlets"},fv=true}
E["quest:94242"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Pilferer's Gloves",z="general",s="A transferable writ requests Pilferer's Gloves and gives the details for delivery and payment. You need the writ to complete the transaction.",h="A transferable writ requests Pilferer's Gloves and gives the details for delivery and payment.",sec={{t="A Written Order",b="A faded note requests one pair of Pilferer's Gloves. It includes where to deliver them and how payment is arranged, and the writ can pass from hand to hand.",sp=0},{t="The Transaction",b="You need the writ with you when you bring the requested gloves to the marked location. The note ties the delivery and payment details to this written order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ ask for?",a="The writ requests one pair of Pilferer's Gloves.",al={"pilferer's gloves writ","gloves order","what item"}},{q="Where do I deliver the gloves?",a="The delivery location is marked on your map.",al={"delivery place","where to take gloves","marked location"}},{q="What do I need to complete the transaction?",a="You need the writ in your possession to complete the transaction.",al={"need the writ","writ requirement","complete transaction"}},{q="Does the writ say how payment works?",a="The writ includes information about payment.",al={"payment details","how much payment","gloves payment"}},{q="Can someone else carry the writ?",a="Yes. The writ is transferable.",al={"transferable writ","pass the note","can i give it away"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","gloves","payment","pilferer's gloves","transferable","writ"},m={id=94242},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Pilferer's Gloves"},fv=true}
E["quest:94243"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Quiver",z="general",s="A faded Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Quiver asks you to bring one Heavy Quiver to a marked location and gives payment details.",h="A faded Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Quiver asks you to bring one Heavy Quiver to a marked location and gives...",sec={{t="The Writ",b="The note asks you to acquire one Heavy Quiver and bring it to the place marked on your map. Keep the writ with you to complete the exchange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ request?",a="The customer requests one Heavy Quiver.",al={"heavy quiver request","what item is wanted"}},{q="Where do I deliver it?",a="The delivery place is marked on your map.",al={"delivery location","where to take quiver"}},{q="Do I need to carry the writ?",a="Yes. Carry the writ with you to complete the exchange.",al={"need the writ","writ required"}},{q="Can I give this writ to someone else?",a="Yes. The writ can be transferred to someone else.",al={"transfer writ","can someone else use it"}},{q="Does the writ mention payment?",a="The writ gives payment details, but no amount is stated.",al={"how much payment","quiver payment"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","heavy quiver","payment","quiver","transferable"},m={id=94243},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Quiver"},fv=true}
E["quest:94246"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Red Whelp Gloves",z="general",s="A transferable writ requests one pair of Red Whelp Gloves. It names a delivery place and payment for the exchange.",h="A transferable writ requests one pair of Red Whelp Gloves.",sec={{t="A Written Request",b="A faded note requests one pair of Red Whelp Gloves and gives a delivery location and payment. You need to hold the writ to complete the exchange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ ask for?",a="The writ requests one pair of Red Whelp Gloves.",al={"red whelp gloves writ","what item is requested"}},{q="Where do I deliver the gloves?",a="The writ provides a delivery location marked on your map.",al={"delivery location","where to take gloves"}},{q="What do I need to complete the exchange?",a="You need the writ in your possession to complete the exchange.",al={"what do i need","writ requirement"}},{q="Can the writ be transferred?",a="Yes. The note says the writ is transferable.",al={"transferable writ","can someone else take it"}},{q="Does the writ mention payment?",a="Yes. The writ includes information about payment.",al={"how much payment","payment for gloves"}}},kw={"craftsman's writ","delivery","payment","red whelp gloves","transferable","writ"},m={id=94246},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Red Whelp Gloves"},fv=true}
E["quest:94249"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Azure Silk Hood",z="general",s="A faded Craftsman’s Writ requests an Azure Silk Hood and gives terms for its delivery and payment. You need the writ to complete the exchange.",h="A faded Craftsman’s Writ requests an Azure Silk Hood and gives terms for its delivery and payment.",sec={{t="The Written Terms",b="The note is penned in faded ink and names one item: an Azure Silk Hood. It also gives the place for delivery and the payment. The writ can pass from one bearer to another, but you need it with you to complete the transaction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ ask for?",a="The customer requests one Azure Silk Hood.",al={"azure hood writ","what item is wanted","craftsman writ"}},{q="Where do I deliver the hood?",a="The delivery location is marked on your map.",al={"delivery location","where to take it","marked place"}},{q="What do I need for the transaction?",a="You need the requested item and the writ in your possession.",al={"what to bring","need the writ?","complete exchange"}},{q="Does the writ say how payment works?",a="The note includes information about payment, but the text here does not specify the amount.",al={"how much payment","payment terms","what do i get"}},{q="Can someone else carry the writ?",a="Yes. The writ is marked as transferable.",al={"transferable writ","can i pass it on","who can hold it"}}},kw={"azure silk hood","craftsman's writ","delivery","payment","silk hood","transferable","writ"},m={id=94249},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Azure Silk Hood"},fv=true}
E["quest:94253"] = {t="quest",n="Craftsman's Writ: Colorful Kilt",z="general",s="A customer seeks a disguise for slipping into Zul'Gurub, and Craftsman's Writ: Colorful Kilt names the garment they want.",h="A customer seeks a disguise for slipping into Zul'Gurub, and Craftsman's Writ: Colorful Kilt names the...",sec={{t="A disguise",b="The transferable writ asks you to bring one Colorful Kilt to the marked location. The customer plans to pass through Zul'Gurub's gates dressed as one of its ritualists, and says the kilt suits the disguise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the writ ask for?",a="The writ requests one Colorful Kilt, to be delivered to the location marked on your map.",al={"colorful kilt writ","what item is needed"}},{q="Why does the customer want a colorful kilt?",a="The customer plans to sneak into Zul'Gurub dressed as one of its ritualists and says the kilt will help.",al={"why kilt","kilt disguise"}},{q="Can I transfer this writ?",a="Yes. The writ says it is transferable.",al={"transfer writ","give writ away"}},{q="Where should I deliver the kilt?",a="The writ directs you to the location marked on your map.",al={"delivery place","where to bring it"}}},kw={"colorful kilt","craftsman's writ","delivery","disguise","ritualist","zul'gurub"},rel={"subzone:zul-gurub"},m={id=94253},src={"In-game quest text: Craftsman's Writ: Colorful Kilt"},fv=true}
E["quest:94369"] = {t="quest",n="The Fate of Zephras",z="general",s="In Valanaar, you bring Talaanis Shadowsong word of the danger facing Zephras. The fallen wards leave the isle exposed to Al'Akir, and its people must decide how to protect their home.",h="In Valanaar, you bring Talaanis Shadowsong word of the danger facing Zephras.",sec={{t="A warning for Talaanis",b="You tell Talaanis what happened above the Shrine of Akir. You share Elaadrin's plan to leave Zephras Isle. High Elder Shadowsong needs to understand the danger and why you were sent to Azeroth. The people of Zephras must find a way to save their home.",sp=0},{t="What remains",b="Talaanis weighs the news. Lorthuna is gone, and the cult has lost its leader. Zephras has not been invaded. Yet Al'Akir may turn his attention to the isle in years or decades, and fear now stands beside cause for celebration.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do I speak with?",a="You speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",al={"who to talk to","talaanis","where do i report"}},{q="What do I tell Talaanis?",a="You tell Talaanis what happened above the Shrine of Akir and of Elaadrin's plan to leave Zephras Isle.",al={"what happened at shrine","what do i report","shrine of akir news"}},{q="Why are the people of Zephras afraid of Al'Akir?",a="The wards that hid Zephras have fallen. Al'Akir may choose to attack while the people are in his domain.",al={"why fear al'akir","windlord danger","al akir threat"}},{q="What does High Elder Shadowsong need to know?",a="High Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger and what the people of Zephras intend to do on their mission to Azeroth.",al={"what talaanis needs","high elder news","intentions for azeroth"}}},kw={"al'akir","elaadrin","lorthuna","shrine of akir","talaanis shadowsong","valanaar","wards","windlord","zephras"},rel={"zone:zephras"},m={id=94369},src={"In-game quest text: The Fate of Zephras"},fv=true}
E["quest:94373"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="At Anvilmar, Teo Hammerstorm tests initiates who seek the earth's favor. They face Frostmane trolls to the south and claim bear pendants before receiving an earthen sapta.",h="At Anvilmar, Teo Hammerstorm tests initiates who seek the earth's favor.",sec={{t="The Wisdom of Stone",b="In Coldridge Valley, Teo Hammerstorm guides initiates at Anvilmar along the earth's rugged path. He teaches young wanderers to heed the mountains and see the land as firm ground. Stone can shield those who respect it. The earth shares its wisdom only with those who show grit and patience.",sp=0},{t="Trial in the Frostmane Den",b="To prove they are ready, initiates face Frostmane trolls in a cave south of Anvilmar. The trolls make coarse pendants from Iceclaw bears that roam the frozen heights. Recovering two bear pendants from the den proves the stubborn resolve and strength the elemental spirits expect.",sp=0},{t="The Earthen Sapta",b="After the initiate presents the pendants, Teo Hammerstorm praises patience, the earth's finest virtue. Patience outlasts crumbling peaks and rivers carving valleys. Then Teo prepares an earthen sapta, which lets the initiate perceive and walk the true path of the elements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the Call of Earth quest?",a="Teo Hammerstorm, an elder guide at Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley, offers the trial. He teaches initiates the ways of stone and asks them to prove their resolve to the earth spirits.",al={"who gives call of earth","quest giver call of earth","teo hammerstorm quest"}},{q="What does Teo Hammerstorm ask you to do?",a="You travel south of Anvilmar to a cave inhabited by Frostmane trolls and recover two Frostmane Bear Pendants. The trolls make them from Iceclaw bears, and you bring them to Teo Hammerstorm.",al={"call of earth objectives","what do i need for call of earth","frostmane pendants quest"}},{q="Where do you find the Frostmane Bear Pendants?",a="Frostmane trolls carry the pendants in a cave south of Anvilmar. They make the talismans from Iceclaw bears and wear them in their den.",al={"where are frostmane bear pendants","how to get frostmane bear pendants","frostmane cave anvilmar"}},{q="What reward does Teo Hammerstorm prepare upon completion?",a="Teo prepares an earthen sapta, a ceremonial draught that attunes you to the elemental spirits. It lets you walk the true path of the earth.",al={"what is a sapta","earth sapta dwarf","what does teo hammerstorm craft"}},{q="Why must initiates face the Frostmane trolls for this trial?",a="Facing the Frostmane trolls shows the grit and resilience needed to commune with the earth. Taking the bear pendants from their den proves the initiate's resolve.",al={"why kill frostmane trolls","why frostmane pendants"}},{q="What does Teo Hammerstorm teach about the nature of earth?",a="Teo teaches that patience is the earth's greatest virtue. It endures as mountains crumble and rivers carve valleys. He says stone shields those who respect it, though even bedrock can shift when slighted.",al={"earth virtues teo hammerstorm","wisdom of the mountain"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you begin communion with the spirits of stone and soil through this initiation. Teo prepares an earthen sapta for you.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you find this trial near Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley. It joins your mountain heritage and fortitude with the earth's patience.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face Frostmane trolls in caves south of Anvilmar."},kw={"anvilmar","call of earth","coldridge valley","earth totem","frostmane","frostmane bear pendant","iceclaw bear","sapta","shaman","teo hammerstorm"},rel={"subzone:anvilmar","topic:troll"},m={id=94373},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:94374"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="At a mountain Spirit Stone, an initiate drinks Earth Sapta and binds spirit to the world's enduring foundations. The draught opens the way to elemental awareness, teaching humility and patience amid snow and rock.",h="At a mountain Spirit Stone, an initiate drinks Earth Sapta and binds spirit to the world's enduring...",sec={{t="The Draught of Vision",b="At an isolated mountain shrine, you drink Earth Sapta, an enchanted brew. Ancient elemental magic gives it power to show mortal eyes elemental spirits and subtle currents beyond ordinary sight. Its strength makes the shrine the only safe place to drink it, where spirit and stone can form their bond.",sp=0},{t="The Spirit Stone in the Snow",b="High on a snow-swept mountain, the Spirit Stone waits at the end of a secluded path. You travel through bitter cold to stand humbly before the ancient rock. The living earth welcomes those who come without pride. Mountains give lasting physical strength, while the vast, steady plains teach patience.",sp=0},{t="Strength and Stillness",b="Communion with stone is a foundational rite for spiritual pathfinders. Wind, fire, and crashing water carry restless fury, while earth teaches discipline and quiet resilience. You absorb earth's still essence, preparing mind and body for the conflicting, chaotic dualities of the more volatile elements that roar across the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Earth Sapta?",a="Earth Sapta is a potent mystical brew crafted with magic to bind a practitioner’s spirit directly to the elements. It is not meant for the weak-willed. Drinking it pierces ordinary mortal sight, revealing spirits and elemental truths others cannot perceive.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta lore","what does sapta do"}},{q="Where must the sapta be consumed?",a="You must drink the brew only at a dedicated sacred site. For this rite, you travel north up the mountain along a hidden path to find the ancient Spirit Stone among the crags.",al={"where do i drink sapta","spirit stone location","where is the spirit stone"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Call of Earth rite?",a="The rite is a foundational trial of communion and humility. At the Spirit Stone, drinking sapta teaches you to draw strength from the mountains and patience from the plains. It attunes your mortal spirit to the living world before you face more turbulent elements.",al={"why do this quest","meaning of call of earth","call of earth lore"}},{q="Who knows how to brew Earth Sapta?",a="Only a select few initiated shamans know how to brew sapta. Brewing it requires knowledge and spiritual preparation. Its recipe is guarded with great reverence because the draught connects mortal awareness directly to primal forces.",al={"who knows sapta recipe","can anyone make sapta"}},{q="How does the element of earth differ from the other elements?",a="Other elemental forces clash, burn, and roar with violent unrest, while earth brings steadfast stillness, patience, and an unyielding foundation. You first learn humility before stone, then face the volatile dual nature of the other elements.",al={"earth vs other elements","how does earth compare to fire water air"}},{q="What setting is this rite performed in?",a="The rite takes place high in a cold, snowbound mountain range. You follow a secluded path through snow and stone to commune with the spirits of the land despite the biting frost.",al={"where is call of earth set","frozen land earth quest"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you take part in an essential communion that binds spirit to stone and grants vision beyond mortal perception through sapta’s ritual draught.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hear this sacred communion in the rough cadence of your people, amid frozen mountain peaks. It ties communion with the earth to Dun Morogh’s snowy heights.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see an elemental rite practiced among snowy mountain crags, where shamanic traditions take root within Alliance lands."},kw={"call of earth","dun morogh","earth sapta","elemental rite","hidden path","sapta","shaman","spirit stone"},rel={"quest:1462","subzone:hidden-path","quest:99141"},m={id=94374},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:94375"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="Young shaman in Dun Morogh seek the earth spirits’ favor through Call of Earth. They carry rough quartz to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar, where he shapes it into the heart of an Earth Totem.",h="Young shaman in Dun Morogh seek the earth spirits’ favor through Call of Earth.",sec={{t="The Whispering Stone",b="In Dun Morogh, young shaman begin their spiritual path by seeking the earth spirit and listening to its teachings. The spirit gives them rough quartz, a humble stone meant to become the heart of an Earth Totem. The rite calls for humility, patience, strength, and resolve. An initiate learns from the earth and does not measure worth by size.",sp=0},{t="The Mountain's Favor",b="Teo Hammerstorm waits in Anvilmar for the initiate to bring back the rough quartz. He judges whether the mountain spirits have acknowledged them, and sends away anyone who arrives without the stone. Bring him the quartz, and he shapes it into an Earth Totem. The totem binds the young shaman to the strength of the world's roots.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rough Quartz for?",a="An earth spirit gives you rough quartz as proof of communion. Teo Hammerstorm uses it to make your Earth Totem.",al={"rough quartz purpose","what is rough quartz","why do i need rough quartz"}},{q="Who is Teo Hammerstorm?",a="Teo Hammerstorm is a mentor in Anvilmar, in Dun Morogh. He tests aspiring shaman by asking for proof of communion with the elements before making their totems.",al={"who is teo hammerstorm","teo hammerstorm location","where is teo"}},{q="What is the Call of Earth?",a="Through Call of Earth, young shaman seek communion with the earth spirits and earn their first Earth Totem.",al={"call of earth questline","what is call of earth","earth totem quest"}},{q="What does the earth spirit ask of the initiate?",a="The earth spirit asks you to stay strong and patient as you seek wisdom. It teaches that small things can outlast others, and that true power comes through mutual respect with the earth.",al={"earth spirit lesson","what does earth ask","shaman earth philosophy"}},{q="Where is Anvilmar located?",a="Anvilmar lies in Coldridge Valley, in Dun Morogh. Young dwarven initiates train there and commune with the surrounding mountains.",al={"what is anvilmar","anvilmar lore","where does call of earth take place"}},{q="Why is the Earth Totem important?",a="A totem connects a shaman with the elemental spirits. The Earth Totem binds your will to the mountains’ steadfast strength and resilience.",al={"why totem matters","shaman totem lore","what does an earth totem do"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you begin your path by communing with the earth spirits and earning an Earth Totem.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can join your people’s ties to stone and mountain with the shamanic path by communing with earth spirits in Dun Morogh.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance shaman, you find elemental spiritualists offering guidance around Anvilmar, within Ironforge lands."},kw={"anvilmar","call of earth","coldridge valley","dun morogh","earth totem","rough quartz","shaman","teo hammerstorm","totem"},rel={"item:rough-quartz","subzone:anvilmar"},m={id=94375},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:94411"] = {t="quest",n="Meddlesome Mages",z="general",s="In the Shen'dar Highlands, High Order apprentices gather at sacred stones and meddle with magic. Their spells threaten the fragile forces that hold the island together.",h="In the Shen'dar Highlands, High Order apprentices gather at sacred stones and meddle with magic.",sec={{t="Encroachment at the Stones",b="North of the village, High Order apprentices gather around ancient standing stones. Repeated warnings have not turned them from the sacred sites. They press on with their arcane studies, while local leaders hesitate to shed the blood of their shen'dorei kin. So they call for outside help to drive the apprentices away before lasting harm is done.",sp=0},{t="The Fragile Island",b="Delicate mystical forces bind the island's land together and keep it safe. The defenders fear the High Order gives little thought to the danger in its spellcraft. One careless spell could break those bindings. Then ruin would come to everyone who lives there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Meddlesome Mages about?",a="You are asked to drive away High Order Apprentices gathered at sacred standing stones north of the village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"what is meddlesome mages","meddlesome mages quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who are the High Order Apprentices?",a="The High Order is a faction of mages whose apprentices have ignored warnings and intruded on sacred ground to experiment with magic. The locals regard them as shen'dorei brothers and sisters.",al={"who are the high order apprentices","what is high order","high order mages"}},{q="Why must the High Order Apprentices be dispersed?",a="The apprentices have ignored repeated warnings to avoid the standing stones. Their reckless spellcraft threatens the fragile forces binding the island and could bring destruction to the homeland.",al={"why disperse high order","why fight the apprentices","standing stones problem"}},{q="Where are the High Order Apprentices gathering?",a="The High Order Apprentices gather at standing stones north of the village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",al={"where is this quest","shen'dar highlands location","standing stones north of village"}},{q="Who are the shen'dorei mentioned in the quest?",a="The shen'dorei are kin to the people who ask for help. Conflict among their own people weighs on the local leaders, yet they feel compelled to act against the High Order to protect their homeland.",al={"who are shendorei","shendorei brothers and sisters","what are shen'dorei"}},{q="What danger do the mages pose to the island?",a="Delicate forces bind the island together, and they are vulnerable. Unchecked arcane meddling could break them and destroy the island.",al={"what is the danger","island fragile forces","what could happen to the island"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see the danger in the High Order's reckless spellcasting. Their apprentices disregard the delicate balance that holds the island together."},kw={"arcane meddling","high order","high order apprentices","meddlesome mages","shen'dar highlands","shen'dorei","standing stones"},rel={"topic:mage"},m={id=94411},src={"In-game quest text: Meddlesome Mages"},fv=true}
E["quest:94413"] = {t="quest",n="A Magical Affront",z="general",s="On Zephras, A Magical Affront sets the local order against the Windshapers. The order seeks to harness and study the surfaced leylines, while the Windshapers see them as scars to heal. Their conflict has reached the southwestern forest.",h="On Zephras, A Magical Affront sets the local order against the Windshapers.",sec={{t="Unveiled Currents",b="Ancient conduits of raw magic have recently broken through the earth on Zephras. For scholars and practitioners of the local order, this is a rare boon. Direct contact with the leylines gives them new insight into the arcane currents across the region and deepens their mastery of magic.",sp=0},{t="Scars and Strife",b="The Windshapers see the exposed energies as open wounds and scars across Zephras. They gather at the rupture sites to suppress or mend the leylines and heal the earth.\n\nThe order depends on that raw power, so it sees their efforts as a threat. It sends you southwest into the forest to drive the Windshapers back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are a group on Zephras who see the surfaced leylines as unnatural wounds in the land. They seek to heal them, putting them at odds with orders that study and channel the leylines.",al={"who are the windshapers","what are windshapers","windshapers zephras"}},{q="Why does the order want the Windshapers driven off?",a="The order needs access to the surfaced leylines to deepen its understanding of magic. The Windshapers try to suppress or mend them, so the order sees their efforts as a threat and sends you to drive them off.",al={"why kill windshapers","why fight the windshapers","windshaper conflict"}},{q="What are the leylines on Zephras?",a="Leylines are conduits of mystical energy that traverse the world. On Zephras, they have recently broken through the earth, exposing raw magic and giving arcane practitioners direct access to study it.",al={"what are leylines zephras","zephras leylines","surface leylines"}},{q="Where is the contested leyline located?",a="The contested leyline lies in the forest southwest on Zephras. Windshapers have gathered there to close or mend the exposed surge of magic.",al={"where is the leyline forest","leyline location","forest to southwest"}},{q="Why do the Windshapers consider the leylines scars?",a="The Windshapers see the sudden rupture of raw subterranean energy through the earth as violent scars across Zephras. They believe mending those tears will restore natural balance, which puts them at odds with spellcasters who want the leylines left open.",al={"why do windshapers want to heal leylines","are leylines harmful zephras","healing the scars"}},{q="What is the significance of Zephras in this conflict?",a="Zephras is where the leylines have recently emerged at the surface. Their raw magic has made the land a flashpoint between those who seek to master its arcane power and those who see the breaches as wounds to heal.",al={"what is zephras","where does a magical affront take place","zephras lore"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you may see the surfaced leylines on Zephras as a rare chance to study raw mystical energy directly. Their preservation matters to your arcane craft.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you may feel the tension in the Windshapers’ view of the exposed leylines as wounds across the natural land, in need of healing.",["class:Shaman"]="As a Shaman, you may share the Windshapers’ elemental and natural stewardship as they seek to calm and heal disturbances across Zephras. That puts their aims at odds with orders harnessing raw magical flows."},kw={"a magical affront","arcane","leyline","leylines","scars","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=94413},src={"In-game quest text: A Magical Affront"},fv=true}
E["quest:94427"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="Your order sends you to Tanis Alderwood in Undercity’s Trade Quarter. There, a chance to show grace comes through good deeds.",h="Your order sends you to Tanis Alderwood in Undercity’s Trade Quarter.",sec={{t="A Call for Grace",b="Your order teaches that divinity means doing good for its own sake, not seeking godhood. It says tragedy brought you here. Now it asks you to find Tanis Alderwood in Undercity’s Trade Quarter. Tanis is in need and may benefit from your grace.",sp=0},{t="Tanis’s Plea",b="When you approach Tanis Alderwood, they fear you may hurt them. They insist they have no quarrel with you or your order. Then they beg you to leave them be.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tanis Alderwood?",a="Tanis Alderwood is someone in need in Undercity’s Trade Quarter.",al={"Tanis","who's Tanis","Trade Quarter person"}},{q="Why am I sent to Tanis?",a="Your order says Tanis Alderwood may benefit from your grace.",al={"why Tanis","help Tanis","what's the point"}},{q="What does divinity mean to my order?",a="Your order defines divinity as doing good for its own sake, rather than seeking godhood.",al={"divinity meaning","good for its own sake","what is divinity"}},{q="Where can I find Tanis Alderwood?",a="You can find Tanis Alderwood in Undercity’s Trade Quarter.",al={"Tanis location","where's Tanis","Trade Quarter"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, your order defines divinity as doing good for its own sake. It says tragedy can threaten the grace that defined you in life."},kw={"a lesson in divinity","divinity","grace","panhandling","tanis alderwood","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter"},m={id=94427},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94434"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="In the Undercity, Tanis Alderwood asks you for fresh cloth. His wife is falling apart, and he hopes to wrap her until an apothecary is free.",h="In the Undercity, Tanis Alderwood asks you for fresh cloth.",sec={{t="A Beggar's Plea",b="The apothecaries are occupied with the Dark Lady's business. So Tanis asks you to bring linen for his wife. He hopes the cloth will hold her together while they wait for help.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Tanis Alderwood, a beggar in the Undercity, asks you to help his wife.",al={"who is Tanis","Tanis Alderwood","beggar guy"}},{q="What's wrong with Tanis's wife?",a="Tanis says she is literally falling apart and needs a wrapping to hold her together.",al={"wife falling apart","what happened to his wife","Tanis wife"}},{q="Why can't the apothecaries help?",a="Tanis says the apothecaries are occupied with the Dark Lady's business.",al={"apothecaries busy","why no apothecary","Dark Lady business"}},{q="What does Tanis need?",a="Tanis asks you to bring fresh cloth so he can wrap his wife while they wait for the apothecaries.",al={"what cloth does he need","linen for Tanis","help beggar"}}},kw={"a lesson in divinity","apothecaries","beggar","dark lady","linen cloth","tanis alderwood","undercity","wife"},rel={"zone:undercity"},m={id=94434},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94435"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="Tanis Alderwood thanks you for your help and calls you a friend. Danitha Morr sees this small act of service as a way to strengthen the Forsaken’s connection to the Light.",h="Tanis Alderwood thanks you for your help and calls you a friend.",sec={{t="A Small Service",b="Danitha Morr says your help may strengthen the Forsaken’s connection to the Light. Mistrust and conspiracies linger among the Dark Lady’s followers. The Forsaken must meet that fear with courage and righteousness. Danitha gives you a symbol for what comes next.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is thanking me?",a="Tanis Alderwood thanks you for helping him and says you will always have a friend in him.",al={"tanis alderwood","who is tanis","tanis thanks"}},{q="What does Danitha say my help means?",a="Danitha says even a small act of service may strengthen the Forsaken’s connection to the Light.",al={"why help danitha","small act meaning","light connection"}},{q="Why does Danitha mention mistrust?",a="Danitha says the Dark Lady and some in her service mistrust them, and that some even conspire against them.",al={"forsaken mistrust","dark lady fear","why are they mistrusted"}},{q="What does Danitha give me?",a="A symbol from Danitha, for what comes next.",al={"what symbol","danitha item","symbol for next"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you hear Danitha describe the Forsaken’s effort to help their people prosper again.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you hear Danitha call for courage and righteousness in helping your people prosper again."},kw={"a lesson in divinity","danitha morr","dark lady","forsaken","light","mistrust","symbol","tanis alderwood"},rel={"topic:light","topic:forsaken","subzone:bandarion-keep"},m={id=94435},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94436"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="In A Lesson in Divinity, Danitha Morr asks you to show what a priest can do with the Symbol of Life. Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep has come seeking aid for a friend.",h="In A Lesson in Divinity, Danitha Morr asks you to show what a priest can do with the Symbol of Life.",sec={{t="A Plea for Aid",b="Billmuth says the priests turned him away, and his friend may have no one else to turn to. He is not proud to ask you, but he needs aid for the Forsaken. The Symbol of Life is meant to show your ability to channel the Light. Handling it may cause discomfort. Its power can still be your ally and guide, even to the Forsaken, whose creation is tied to a force opposed to the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep has come seeking help for a friend.",al={"billmuth help","who needs aid"}},{q="Why does Billmuth ask a priest?",a="Billmuth says the priests turned him away, and you may be his friend's only chance.",al={"why priest","priests turned him away"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life?",a="The Symbol of Life is a talisman of the Light that Danitha Morr gives you to show your ability to channel the Light.",al={"symbol of life","light talisman"}},{q="Why might the Symbol of Life hurt to handle?",a="Danitha warns that the talisman may cause discomfort because the Light is opposed to the force that created the Forsaken.",al={"symbol pain","light hurts"}},{q="Where can I find Deathguard Billmuth?",a="Deathguard Billmuth is downstairs at Bandarion Keep.",al={"billmuth location","bandarion keep"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, Danitha asks you to show your ability to channel the Light with the Symbol of Life."},kw={"a lesson in divinity","bandarion keep","danitha morr","deathguard billmuth","forsaken","light","priest","symbol of life"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:light","topic:forsaken","topic:priest"},m={id=94436},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94438"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="Danitha Morr sends you to Venomweb Vale to find Deathguard Falgan. He and his companion were separated after learning the Scarlet Crusade plans an attack on Brill.",h="Danitha Morr sends you to Venomweb Vale to find Deathguard Falgan.",sec={{t="Falgan's Return",b="Deathguard Falgan went with Billmuth to scout Scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. They learned the Scarlet Crusade plans some kind of attack. Now Falgan asks whether you will help the Forsaken further.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to find Falgan?",a="Danitha Morr asks you to find Deathguard Falgan and help him if you can.",al={"who sent me","Danitha Morr","quest giver"}},{q="Where is Falgan?",a="Falgan is at Venomweb Vale.",al={"Falgan location","where falgan","find deathguard"}},{q="What happened to Falgan?",a="Falgan stayed behind after a noise alerted Scarlet forces to him and his companion. His companion reached Brill without him.",al={"Falgan missing","what happened","save falgan"}},{q="What did Falgan and Billmuth discover?",a="Falgan and Billmuth learned that the Scarlet Crusade plans some kind of attack.",al={"scarlet orders","what did they find","attack plans"}},{q="What is the Symbol of Life for?",a="The Symbol of Life is used to bring Deathguard Falgan back to life.",al={"resurrect falgan","symbol life","how save falgan"}},{q="What does Falgan ask after returning?",a="After returning, Falgan asks whether you are willing to help the Forsaken further.",al={"help forsaken","what next","Falgan asks"}}},kw={"a lesson in divinity","billmuth","brill","danitha morr","deathguard falgan","scarlet crusade","symbol of life","venomweb vale"},rel={"subzone:venomweb-vale","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken"},m={id=94438},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94440"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="Deathguard Billmuth needs you to recover Scarlet Crusade attack plans from Venomweb Vale. The Deathguard expects an assault and hopes the plans will help prepare an ambush.",h="Deathguard Billmuth needs you to recover Scarlet Crusade attack plans from Venomweb Vale.",sec={{t="Orders for the Keep",b="Scarlet Crusaders carry deployment orders in their satchels, and the Deathguard expects an attack. Bring a copy of the plans to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep. Then the Deathguard can prepare an ambush.",sp=0},{t="A Friend Saved",b="Billmuth thanks you for saving his friend and says he will take the plans to his commander. Your actions have shown him you are Forsaken through and through, despite the mistrust some of his people hold toward your class.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Billmuth need?",a="Deathguard Billmuth asks you to recover the Scarlet Crusade's attack plans from Venomweb Vale.",al={"what does billmuth want","billmuth plans","plans for billmuth"}},{q="Where are the attack plans?",a="The Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale carry the attack plans.",al={"where plans","scarlet plans location","find attack plans"}},{q="Why does the Deathguard want the plans?",a="The Deathguard expects an attack and wants the plans so it can prepare an ambush.",al={"why get plans","what are plans for","deathguard ambush"}},{q="Who should receive the plans?",a="Bring the plans to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.",al={"who gets plans","return plans to","billmuth where"}}},kw={"a lesson in divinity","attack plans","bandarion keep","deathguard billmuth","forsaken","scarlet crusade","venomweb vale"},rel={"quest:381","subzone:bandarion-keep","subzone:venomweb-vale","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={id=94440},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94441"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson in Divinity",z="general",s="A fellow Forsaken asks you to thank Danitha Morr for the paladins’ service at Bandarion Keep. Your work has earned the Deathguard’s gratitude and brings a gift of redemption.",h="A fellow Forsaken asks you to thank Danitha Morr for the paladins’ service at Bandarion Keep.",sec={{t="Thanks at the Keep",b="A fellow Forsaken asks you to carry their thanks to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep. The rest of the Deathguard will hear of the service you and the other paladins performed. They are proud to count you among the Forsaken and trust the Dark Lady watches over you.",sp=0},{t="A Gift of Light",b="Danitha says a paladin ready to receive one of the Light’s greatest blessings can use the Symbol of Life. She bestows redemption upon you, letting you resurrect fallen companions. Your service matters to the Forsaken and the paladins of Bandarion Keep. The Deathguard hopes such acts will win the hearts and minds of fellow Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do I thank?",a="You are asked to thank Danitha Morr for the paladins’ service at Bandarion Keep.",al={"who is Danitha","thank Danitha","Danitha Morr"}},{q="Who will hear about the service?",a="The rest of the Deathguard will hear of the paladins’ service at Bandarion Keep.",al={"Deathguard thanks","who gets told","keep service"}},{q="What does the Symbol of Life do?",a="The Symbol of Life can be used by a paladin ready to receive one of the Light’s greatest blessings.",al={"Symbol of Life","life symbol","what does it do"}},{q="Why is the Deathguard proud of me?",a="The Deathguard is proud to count you among the Forsaken and values the service you performed with the paladins of Bandarion Keep.",al={"Forsaken proud","why proud","Deathguard proud"}}},kw={"a lesson in divinity","bandarion keep","danitha morr","deathguard","forsaken","light","redemption","symbol of life"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:light","topic:forsaken"},m={id=94441},src={"In-game quest text: A Lesson in Divinity"},fv=true}
E["quest:94449"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="In Dun Morogh, an elder sends shaman initiates to Bruegs Kindleborn to test their readiness for the fire sapta. They have already learned patience and grounding through earth.",h="In Dun Morogh, an elder sends shaman initiates to Bruegs Kindleborn to test their readiness for the fire...",sec={{t="The Burning Trial",b="After proving patience and grounding through earth, shamans face a more volatile force: the fire elemental spirit. Stone holds steady, but fire promises chaos, ruin, and fierce energy. So an elder sends the initiate across Dun Morogh’s snow-laden peaks to seek guidance before trying to harness its wild heat.",sp=0},{t="The Recluse of the Peaks",b="Bruegs Kindleborn keeps watch in a secluded cave high in the mountains above South Gate Outpost. When an initiate arrives with an elder’s recommendation, Bruegs prepares them for the sapta of fire. He warns that flame’s hunger to burn and consume is easily stirred. To master it, a shaman must know when to hold back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bruegs Kindleborn?",a="Bruegs Kindleborn mentors shamans in a mountain cave high above South Gate Outpost in Dun Morogh. Elders send initiates to him, and he judges whether they have the maturity and discipline to receive the fire sapta.",al={"who is bruegs kindleborn","bruegs kindleborn lore","where is bruegs"}},{q="What is the sapta of fire?",a="A sapta is an elemental draught or preparation that lets a shaman commune with spirits of that element. The sapta of fire grants communion with flame and its raw power, and calls for mental focus and prior grounding in stone.",al={"what is sapta of fire","fire sapta","sapta meaning"}},{q="Where is Bruegs Kindleborn located?",a="Bruegs Kindleborn lives far east in the snowy mountains of Dun Morogh, sheltered in a cave overlooking South Gate Outpost.",al={"where to find bruegs kindleborn","south gate outpost cave","where is call of fire turn in"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Call of Fire?",a="Call of Fire brings shamans who have shown patience and mastered earth before the chaotic power of destruction. Bruegs Kindleborn watches over their trial.",al={"what is call of fire","fire totem quest dun morogh"}},{q="Why must a shaman learn the lessons of stone before fire?",a="Earth teaches steadfast patience, stability, and control. Without stone’s grounding, a shaman risks being overwhelmed by fire’s volatile hunger and destructive passions.",al={"why stone first","remember what stone taught you"}},{q="What prerequisites are required before undertaking the Call of Fire?",a="Before this rite, an initiate has shown patience and grounding in earth through earlier trials. The elder sends a student to Bruegs Kindleborn only when their discipline is proven solid.",al={"call of fire prereq","patience quest connection"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face a spiritual trial that carries you from stone’s endurance to fire’s fierce, destructive power.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance shaman, you follow your elders’ guidance in the mountains of Dun Morogh to awaken communion with the elements of fire.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you face this trial high above South Gate Outpost in Dun Morogh, where your discipline is tested against flame’s burning hunger."},kw={"bruegs kindleborn","call of fire","dun morogh","earth sapta","fire totem","sapta of fire","shaman","south gate outpost"},rel={"zone:dunmorogh","subzone:south-gate-outpost"},m={id=94449},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:94465"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="You carry the Torch of the Dormant Flame through Loch Modan to seek Braldir Ashmantle. The trial tests whether an initiate is ready to wield elemental flame.",h="You carry the Torch of the Dormant Flame through Loch Modan to seek Braldir Ashmantle.",sec={{t="The Path Beyond the Valley of Kings",b="To earn the totem of fire, you carry the unlit Torch of the Dormant Flame into the crags of Loch Modan. Beyond the stone carvings of the Valley of Kings, a steep path climbs to an isolated mountain summit. There the elements hold sway, far from the roads travelers know.",sp=0},{t="The Shrine of the Dormant Flame",b="Braldir Ashmantle watches over the Shrine of the Dormant Flame on a high, windswept peak. Unprepared wanderers and fortune hunters find only silence and bare stone. But when you arrive as a true initiate bearing the sacred torch, Braldir reveals the elemental power sleeping within the shrine's brazier, waiting to be rekindled.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Fire quest?",a="The Call of Fire is a trial for an initiate seeking to earn a fire totem. You travel into the crags of Loch Modan and bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle at a sacred mountain peak.",al={"what is call of fire","shaman fire quest loch modan","fire totem quest"}},{q="Who is Braldir Ashmantle?",a="Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine of the Dormant Flame high in the crags of Loch Modan. He turns away ordinary travelers and treasure seekers, and welcomes those who bear the Torch of the Dormant Flame.",al={"who is braldir ashmantle","shrine keeper loch modan"}},{q="Where is the Shrine of the Dormant Flame located?",a="The Shrine of the Dormant Flame rests high in the crags of Loch Modan. A hidden path winds there beyond the Valley of Kings.",al={"where is shrine of the dormant flame","dormant flame location"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="Initiates carry the Torch of the Dormant Flame to show their earnest intent and readiness to commune with elemental fire. Braldir Ashmantle requires you to present it before granting an audience.",al={"what is the torch of the dormant flame","torch of the dormant flame purpose"}},{q="Why must the petitioner travel to Loch Modan?",a="You travel to Loch Modan because the secluded elemental peak that holds the Shrine of the Dormant Flame rises beyond the Valley of Kings, away from casual travelers.",al={"why go to loch modan","why is the fire shrine in loch modan"}},{q="How is the fire totem earned through this trial?",a="After you reach Braldir Ashmantle and prove your intent with the torch, you kindle the shrine's brazier. You return with the flame burning and earn the totem of fire.",al={"what happens after finding braldir","how to get fire totem"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As an aspiring shaman, you prove your dedication to the elemental spirits of fire by carrying a sacred torch to an isolated peak in Loch Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hear dwarven speech as the path leads beyond the Valley of Kings into the rugged crags of Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Across Alliance lands, common travelers see only barren mountain stone. Keepers of the shrine guard ancient elemental secrets from ordinary eyes."},kw={"braldir ashmantle","call of fire","fire totem","loch modan","shaman","shrine of the dormant flame","torch of the dormant flame","valley of kings"},rel={"item:torch-of-the-dormant-flame","zone:lochmodan","topic:alliance"},m={id=94465},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:94466"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="In Loch Modan, initiates seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem it grants. Braldir Ashmantle guides them through a trial that calls for reagents from kobolds and troggs. They prepare a fire sapta and learn that flame can forge and give life as well as destroy.",h="In Loch Modan, initiates seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem it grants.",sec={{t="The Path to the Flame",b="In Loch Modan, Braldir Ashmantle guides initiates who seek the power of flame. Before they can commune with fire spirits, they must attune their mortal spirits with a sacred draught called a fire sapta. Without it, the Eternal Flame would consume them instead of enlightening them. Braldir asks each petitioner to gather two reagents from hostile valley dwellers and prove their resolve.",sp=0},{t="Reagents of the Earth and Spark",b="A fire sapta needs substances rich in elemental power. In the north, Tunnel Rat Geomancers gather sticky fire tar in their warrens to fuel their subterranean magic. In the south, Stonesplinter Seers carry reagent pouches filled with primitive elemental charms across the hills. Claiming these items means facing two of Loch Modan’s most entrenched pests, and gaining what is needed to bind an initiate’s soul to flame.",sp=0},{t="The Tempering of Wisdom",b="Once the reagents are gathered, Braldir Ashmantle teaches patience alongside the power to destroy. To him, fire means more than fury and ash. It is life, the craft of the forge, and the breath of creation. Mastery calls for balance: shadow gives meaning to light, and flame keeps stone from being only a cold memory. To master fire, an initiate must learn when to blend rather than burn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Call of Fire?",a="Aspiring shaman undertake Call of Fire to seek communion with the Eternal Flame. First, they prepare a fire sapta to bind their mortal spirit to the element.",al={"what is call of fire","what is this quest","call of fire purpose"}},{q="Who is Braldir Ashmantle?",a="Braldir Ashmantle guides initiates in Loch Modan. He teaches the balance of fire and prepares a fire sapta once they gather the needed reagents.",al={"who gives call of fire","who is braldir ashmantle","braldir ashmantle location"}},{q="What is a fire sapta?",a="A fire sapta is a preparation made from reagents bound to flame. It attunes and binds a shaman’s spirit to fire, making communion with the Eternal Flame possible.",al={"what is a fire sapta","what does a sapta do","why need sapta"}},{q="Where is the fire tar found?",a="Tunnel Rat Geomancers carry fire tar in their caves in northern Loch Modan. They use it in their primitive fire crafts.",al={"where do i get fire tar","fire tar location","kobold caves fire tar"}},{q="Where is the Stonesplinter reagent pouch found?",a="Stonesplinter Seers carry reagent pouches in the southern hills of Loch Modan. The trogg mystics use them to hold reagents tied to elemental magic.",al={"where do i get reagent pouch","stonesplinter seer pouch","stonesplinter pouch location"}},{q="How does Braldir Ashmantle view the element of fire?",a="Braldir teaches that fire is more than destruction: it is forge, life, and the breath of creation. In balance with other forces, it tempers cold stone and gives warmth and purpose to existence.",al={"braldir view on fire","meaning of fire loch modan","dwarven fire philosophy"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="To commune with fire spirits and seek the Eternal Flame, you forge an elemental bond with a fire sapta. This path leads toward the fire totem.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you find Braldir Ashmantle guiding initiates in Loch Modan. He sees fire as the breath of the forge and creation, not mere destruction.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Alliance lands, you face local trogg and kobold threats as you take part in shamanic rites in Loch Modan."},kw={"braldir ashmantle","call of fire","eternal flame","fire sapta","fire tar","fire totem","loch modan","stonesplinter seer","tunnel rat geomancer"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","item:fire-tar","item:reagent-pouch-shaman","topic:kobold"},m={id=94466},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:94467"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="At the shrine, an initiate drinks fire sapta to face the trial called Call of Fire. The rite asks them to subdue a spirit and offer its embers to the sacred brazier.",h="At the shrine, an initiate drinks fire sapta to face the trial called Call of Fire.",sec={{t="The Rite of Flame",b="An initiate receives prepared fire sapta, guided by elemental lore. The draught awakens their senses to the unseen world. After drinking at the shrine, they climb toward the peak, where mortal sight gives way to primal forces. There, a dormant manifestation of fire awaits their challenge.",sp=0},{t="Facing the Manifestation",b="The Minor Manifestation of Fire tests an initiate's resolve and endurance. It does not attack until challenged, then grows fiercer with each passing moment. When subdued, it yields glowing embers. Carry them to the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame to kindle the torch and win the spirit's lasting favor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Fire?",a="Call of Fire is a sacred rite in which an initiate drinks prepared fire sapta, faces a spirit of flame, and offers its ember to a brazier to earn fire's favor.",al={"what is call of fire","call of fire quest","fire totem trial"}},{q="What is the purpose of the fire sapta?",a="Fire sapta is a prepared draught that opens an initiate's spiritual sight, revealing the elemental spirit waiting at the mountain peak.",al={"fire sapta purpose","why drink sapta","what does sapta do"}},{q="What spirit appears during the trial?",a="A Minor Manifestation of Fire awaits the initiate atop the peak. It does not fight until struck.",al={"what spirit do i fight","call of fire mob","fire manifestation"}},{q="Why must the fire spirit be defeated quickly?",a="The elemental spirit grows fiercer and hotter as the battle wears on. A swift, decisive strike can subdue it before its flames overwhelm the initiate.",al={"why hit it quick","call of fire fight","fire spirit timer"}},{q="What is done with the glowing embers?",a="After the Minor Manifestation of Fire is defeated, its glowing embers are carried to the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame to kindle the ritual torch.",al={"where do embers go","call of fire brazier","shrine of eternal flame brazier"}},{q="What does earning the fire's favor mean?",a="Kindling the torch earns the direct favor and communion of the fire elementals. The rite establishes a bond with the flames.",al={"what is the reward","what does the ritual give","fire favor"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you undertake a foundational trial in communion with fire. Sacred sapta lets you perceive and confront the spirits of flame."},kw={"brazier","call of fire","fire sapta","glowing ember","minor manifestation of fire","shaman trial","shrine of eternal flame"},rel={"item:glowing-ember"},m={id=94467},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:94468"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="Above Loch Modan, an initiate kindles the flame that must reach Dun Morogh. Bruegs Kindleborn awaits its return and judges the traveler's command of the elements.",h="Above Loch Modan, an initiate kindles the flame that must reach Dun Morogh.",sec={{t="The Flame Over the Loch",b="An initiate lights the Torch of Eternal Flame on a mountain ridge above Loch Modan. The flame marks the beginning of a deeper bond with the elements. From there, the initiate carries it down the trails and into the snowy vales of Dun Morogh.",sp=0},{t="The Flameborn's Reward",b="In Dun Morogh, Bruegs Kindleborn awaits the traveler. He is an elemental mentor who judges whether the traveler's inner fire has taken hold. The blazing torch proves the initiate's will and reverence for fire. Bruegs then grants the Fire Totem, welcoming the flameborn into a lineage of elemental guidance for their kin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Fire?",a="Call of Fire is a spiritual trial for shamans in Khaz Modan. The initiate lights the Torch of Eternal Flame at a brazier overlooking Loch Modan, then carries it through the mountains to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.",al={"what is call of fire","call of fire quest","what do you do in call of fire"}},{q="Who is Bruegs Kindleborn?",a="Bruegs Kindleborn is an elemental mentor who lives in Dun Morogh. He oversees the rites of flame and gives initiates who complete the trek their Fire Totem.",al={"who is bruegs kindleborn","where is bruegs kindleborn","bruegs kindleborn location"}},{q="What is the Torch of Eternal Flame?",a="The Torch of Eternal Flame is a ceremonial torch lit at a brazier overlooking Loch Modan. It marks an initiate's bond with elemental fire and must be carried safely to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.",al={"what is torch of eternal flame","torch of eternal flame","where do you get the torch"}},{q="What do you receive upon completing this trial?",a="When you deliver the Torch of Eternal Flame safely to Bruegs Kindleborn, he acknowledges your blazing spirit and gives you your Fire Totem. The totem marks you as flameborn.",al={"what reward for call of fire","do you get fire totem","call of fire totem"}},{q="Where does this journey take place?",a="The journey begins at an overlook above Loch Modan, where the torch is lit. The mountain path leads into Dun Morogh, where Bruegs Kindleborn awaits.",al={"where does call of fire take place","call of fire path","where to take the torch"}},{q="Why does Bruegs mention Madoran?",a="Bruegs mentions Madoran in an oath, referring to Madoran Bronzebeard. He was the revered dwarven leader who led the Bronzebeard clan during the War of the Three Hammers.",al={"why by madorans beard","madoran meaning","who is madoran bruegs mentions"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you complete the trial of fire in Khaz Modan and earn the Fire Totem. It lets you channel flame and commune with the fire spirits.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you carry the flame from the heights above Loch Modan into Dun Morogh. The journey joins your spiritual seeking to the elemental forces of your mountain home.",["faction:Alliance"]="Within Alliance lands in Khaz Modan, spiritual callings take root. Bruegs Kindleborn guides new initiates as they learn the elemental arts."},kw={"bruegs kindleborn","call of fire","dun morogh","fire totem","flameborn","loch modan","shaman","torch of eternal flame"},rel={"zone:dunmorogh","zone:lochmodan"},m={id=94468},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:94484"] = {t="quest",n="Unnerving Silence",z="general",s="In northeastern Shadowgale Forest, a druid enclave has gone silent. Since Ban'aethall fell into ruin, unrest has spread through the territory.",h="In northeastern Shadowgale Forest, a druid enclave has gone silent.",sec={{t="Silence in the Canopy",b="After Ban'aethall fell into ruin, unrest stirred through the territory. Regular messages from the druid conclave in a cave in northeastern Shadowgale Forest have now stopped. Their allies have heard nothing, and worry grows as the forest grows more unsettled.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Enclave",b="You are sent into northeastern Shadowgale Forest to find Elegael Thornpaw, a prominent druid of the enclave. Has the conclave withdrawn deeper into communion with nature, or have the dangers that tore through Ban'aethall reached the cave? No one knows the enclave's fate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Unnerving Silence about?",a="You are asked to learn why messages from a druid conclave in Shadowgale Forest have stopped. Search the cave in the forest's northeast and discover what has happened to the secluded order.",al={"unnerving silence quest","what is unnerving silence"}},{q="Where can Elegael Thornpaw be found?",a="Elegael Thornpaw is in a cave in northeastern Shadowgale Forest. She is the point of contact for the secluded druid conclave there.",al={"where is elegael thornpaw","elegael thornpaw location","find thornpaw"}},{q="Who is Elegael Thornpaw?",a="Elegael Thornpaw belongs to the druid conclave in a cave in northeastern Shadowgale Forest. Her silence and the missed scheduled messages have raised concern for the enclave's safety.",al={"who is elegael thornpaw","thornpaw lore"}},{q="What is Shadowgale Forest?",a="Shadowgale Forest is a wooded expanse with a hidden druid conclave in a cave in its northeastern region. Since Ban'aethall fell and turmoil spread through the territory, contact with the forest's people has grown uncertain.",al={"what is shadowgale forest","shadowgale forest conclave"}},{q="What is Ban'aethall?",a="Ban'aethall was a village deep in Shadowgale Forest, now fallen into ruin. Its destruction and unrest across the territory have raised fears for nearby camps, including the Shadowgale conclave.",al={"what happened to banaethall","banaethall ruins lore","ban'aethall fallen"}},{q="Why has the druid conclave gone silent?",a="The druids' scheduled messages and reports from Shadowgale Forest have stopped without explanation. With Ban'aethall in ruins and tension rising, their allies fear disaster or hostile forces may have overtaken the enclave.",al={"why did druids stop sending messages","why are druids quiet"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may worry for your kin and the balance of the wild when a secluded enclave in Shadowgale Forest falls silent. Finding Elegael Thornpaw may reveal what disrupted their communion."},kw={"ban'aethall","druid","druid conclave","elegael thornpaw","shadowgale forest","unnerving silence"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94484},src={"In-game quest text: Unnerving Silence"},fv=true}
E["quest:94485"] = {t="quest",n="Tears of the Lady",z="general",s="In Shadowgale, Lady's Tear moss may keep Elegael's wounded companions alive. They are trapped in Nightclaw Den, and Elegael needs medicine from nearby trees.",h="In Shadowgale, Lady's Tear moss may keep Elegael's wounded companions alive.",sec={{t="Desperate Remedies in Shadowgale",b="Elegael needs your help in Shadowgale. Wounded companions are trapped inside Nightclaw Den, critically injured and waiting for aid. Ordinary supplies are scarce, so you gather medicine from the surrounding woods. Their wounds cannot wait.",sp=0},{t="The Healing Moss",b="Elegael needs Lady's Tear, a spindly moss clinging to tree bases across Shadowgale. Its secretion is viscous and sticky, with natural antiseptic properties. It seals open gashes and shields traumatic wounds from worsening in the damp wild. With enough moss, Elegael can prepare dressings to stabilize the fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Tears of the Lady about?",a="Elegael needs help treating wounded companions trapped in Nightclaw Den. Gather Lady's Tear moss in Shadowgale so Elegael can prepare a poultice to keep them alive.",al={"what is tears of the lady","tears of the lady quest info"}},{q="What is Lady's Tear?",a="Lady's Tear is a spindly moss that grows near tree bases throughout Shadowgale. Its secretion is viscous and sticky, with natural antiseptic properties that can seal open wounds.",al={"what is ladys tear","ladys tear moss","what is lady's tear moss"}},{q="Who is Elegael?",a="Elegael organizes medical aid in Shadowgale. Wounded companions are trapped in Nightclaw Den, and Elegael needs supplies to treat them.",al={"who is elegael","quest giver tears of the lady"}},{q="What is the Nightclaw Den?",a="Nightclaw Den is where several of Elegael's injured allies are stranded near Shadowgale. Their condition is precarious as Elegael seeks healing ingredients.",al={"what is nightclaw den","where is nightclaw den"}},{q="Why does Elegael need Lady's Tear moss?",a="Elegael needs Lady's Tear's antiseptic secretion to prepare a poultice. The viscous, sticky substance seals open gashes and protects traumatic wounds from worsening.",al={"why need ladys tear","what does the moss do"}},{q="Where is Lady's Tear moss found?",a="Lady's Tear clings to tree bases throughout Shadowgale. Elegael has gathered what was immediately reachable, and more moss lies in the surrounding woods.",al={"where does ladys tear grow","finding ladys tear"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know Lady's Tear for its sticky antiseptic secretion. It can bind open flesh and help prevent infection in wilderness emergencies.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you channel the Light to mend mortal injuries. Natural poultices like Lady's Tear can dress wounds when magical relief is stretched thin."},kw={"elegael","lady's tear","moss","nightclaw den","poultice","shadowgale","tears of the lady"},m={id=94485},src={"In-game quest text: Tears of the Lady"},fv=true}
E["quest:94486"] = {t="quest",n="Feathers for Binding",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, healers need young shrieklings’ feathers to bind a healing poultice. The usually docile birds now attack travelers, making the plumage dangerous to gather.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, healers need young shrieklings’ feathers to bind a healing poultice.",sec={{t="Remedies of the Forest",b="Field healers in Shadowgale Forest treat grave injuries with moss and antiseptic tree sap. Harsh weather can dry the sap or rob it of its strength. So they bind the poultice with young Shadowgale shrieklings’ feathers, which shield the wound and hold the medicine in place.",sp=0},{t="Uncharacteristic Hostility",b="Gathering the soft feathers has grown dangerous. Young Shadowgale shrieklings are usually docile woodland dwellers, but lately they have turned inexplicably aggressive. Their strong talons can inflict lethal wounds. Now the fledglings strike at passersby.",sp=0},{t="A Regrettable Necessity",b="Local caretakers mourn the need to cull young beasts. Yet emergencies threaten the region, and the shrieklings grow more dangerous. Thinning their numbers gathers vital curative materials and curbs a rising threat along forest paths. Each feather is treated with respect, so the beasts’ sacrifice is not wasted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Shadowgale shriekling feathers needed for the poultice?",a="Young Shadowgale shrieklings’ feathers insulate the poultice. Laid over moss and antiseptic sap, they keep the sap from drying and shield wounds from harsh weather.",al={"purpose of feathers","why shriekling feathers","poultice feathers"}},{q="How dangerous are the juvenile shrieklings?",a="Shadowgale shrieklings are usually docile, but lately they have grown unusually hostile. Even the young have large, vicious talons that can disembowel an unwary traveler.",al={"shriekling danger","are shrieklings dangerous","shriekling aggression"}},{q="Why must juvenile shrieklings be hunted instead of adults?",a="The caretakers regret culling young shrieklings, but their sudden aggression and competing wilderness emergencies make thinning their numbers a painful necessity. Gathering their feathers also helps meet urgent medical needs.",al={"why kill young shrieklings","killing young shrieklings"}},{q="Where are the Shadowgale shrieklings found?",a="Shadowgale shrieklings roam the canopies and underbrush of Shadowgale Forest. Travelers must venture carefully through the woods to find them.",al={"where is shadowgale forest","shriekling location","where are shrieklings"}},{q="What other ingredients are being used alongside these feathers?",a="The poultice uses local moss and antiseptic sap, bound and insulated with feathers from young shrieklings.",al={"poultice ingredients","what is in the poultice"}},{q="Why have the shrieklings become so hostile lately?",a="No one knows the exact cause of the shrieklings’ sudden hostility. The normally peaceful young creatures have grown aggressive, adding to the crises facing local caretakers.",al={"why are shrieklings angry","what caused shriekling aggression"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and natural healers can value the balance of moss, antiseptic tree sap, and insulating feathers in a field dressing or medicinal poultice.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may share the caretakers’ sorrow over slaying young woodland beasts, even when rising aggression and urgent medical need leave few alternatives."},kw={"antiseptic sap","feathers for binding","poultice","shadowgale forest","shadowgale shriekling","shriekling","shrieklings"},m={id=94486},src={"In-game quest text: Feathers for Binding"},fv=true}
E["quest:94487"] = {t="quest",n="Unwanted and Unworthy",z="general",s="On Zephras, bloodshed in Shadowgale Forest drives Elegael to seek vengeance and recover stolen heirlooms for the High Elder.",h="On Zephras, bloodshed in Shadowgale Forest drives Elegael to seek vengeance and recover stolen heirlooms for...",sec={{t="Ambush in Shadowgale Forest",b="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambush the local druids in Shadowgale Forest. Elegael had thought these zealots harmless dreamers, with clouds between their ears. Now druid blood stains the forest floor, and Elegael demands swift retribution against the Footsoldiers and Stormchasers responsible.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Heirlooms and Lost Youth",b="Elegael believes the cultists' betrayal has cost them their heritage. They no longer deserve the name shen'dorei, nor do their remains deserve the winds of their homeland. Many were young, their promising futures cut short by fanaticism.\n\nTheir bloodied heirlooms must return to the High Elder. There, the sacred items await a wiser and more worthy generation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Al'Aketh Cultists?",a="The Al'Aketh Cultists are storm-obsessed cultists on Zephras. Elegael once thought them foolish dreamers, with clouds between their ears, but they turned to brutal violence against the local druids.",al={"who are alaketh","alaketh cult","who are the cultists"}},{q="Who is Elegael?",a="Elegael is a shen'dorei protector or druid on Zephras. The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed Elegael, and the betrayal and bloodshed of young lives have left Elegael distressed. Elegael seeks retribution and the recovery of stolen ancestral heirlooms.",al={"who is elegael","quest giver elegael"}},{q="What are the bloodied heirlooms?",a="The bloodied heirlooms belonged to young shen'dorei drawn into the Al'Aketh Cult. Elegael gathers them to return to the High Elder's collection, where they can pass to a more worthy future generation.",al={"bloodied heirlooms","why collect heirlooms","what are the heirlooms"}},{q="What are the shen'dorei?",a="The shen'dorei are the people who inhabit Zephras. Elegael believes the Al'Aketh Cultists forfeited their right to the name through violent betrayal and desecration of the island's harmony.",al={"shendorei meaning","who are shendorei"}},{q="Where is Shadowgale Forest?",a="Shadowgale Forest is a wooded region on Zephras. Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Stormchasers operate there, and the cultists ambushed the druids there.",al={"shadowgale forest location","where is shadowgale"}},{q="Why did the Al'Aketh Cultists ambush the druids?",a="Elegael does not know the cultists' exact motives. Once dismissed as harmless zealots, they rose in sudden, vicious violence and shattered the delicate balance on the island.",al={"why did cultists attack","cult motives","why ambush druids"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="On Zephras, the Al'Aketh Cultists spilled local druids' blood in an unprovoked assault. As a druid, you answer with vengeance and defend nature's balance."},kw={"al'aketh","bloodied heirlooms","elegael","footsoldiers","heirlooms","shadowgale forest","shen'dorei","stormchasers","zephras"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94487},src={"In-game quest text: Unwanted and Unworthy"},fv=true}
E["quest:94488"] = {t="quest",n="The Ties That Bind",z="general",s="Elegael Thornpaw faces a traitor among Shadowgale Forest’s druids. Haalien vanished months ago, then joined the attacking cultists and rose to command them. Now Elegael orders his execution.",h="Elegael Thornpaw faces a traitor among Shadowgale Forest’s druids.",sec={{t="Betrayal in the Forest",b="Druids face a vicious cultist attack in Shadowgale Forest. Elegael Thornpaw finds Haalien’s scent over the slaughter. Haalien was a druid of the circle who vanished months ago, but he did not perish in the wilds. He joined the invading cultists and now commands their violent campaign against his former kin.",sp=0},{t="Blood and Kinship",b="Haalien betrayed more than his vows to the Cenarion Circle. When Elegael sees the fallen commander’s severed head, she reveals that Haalien was her cousin. Fury at his atrocities could not ease the burden of striking down her own kin, so she could not bear it alone. His death ends the life of a renegade whose malice cost numerous innocent lives.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest The Ties That Bind?",a="Elegael Thornpaw is a druid stationed in Shadowgale Forest. As cultists attack, she directs you to hunt down Commander Haalien after discovering his part in the bloodshed.",al={"who gives ties that bind","quest giver shadowgale","who is elegael thornpaw"}},{q="Who is Commander Haalien?",a="Commander Haalien was a druid of the Cenarion Circle who vanished months before the cultist attacks. He willingly joined the hostile cultists and rose to command their forces against his kin.",al={"who is haalien","commander haalien lore","haalien background"}},{q="Why does Elegael want Commander Haalien dead?",a="Haalien left his druidic circle to command cultists who slaughtered innocents and spilled the blood of his brethren. Elegael orders his execution because of his crimes and the danger he poses to the forest.",al={"why kill haalien","haalien crime","what did haalien do"}},{q="What is the connection between Elegael Thornpaw and Haalien?",a="Commander Haalien is Elegael Thornpaw’s cousin. Enraged by his crimes, she admits that killing her own kin would have been a bitter burden, so she asks you to help.",al={"elegael haalien related","how do elegael and haalien know each other"}},{q="Why are cultists present in the Shadowgale Forest?",a="Even the local druids do not know exactly why the cultists came to Shadowgale Forest. Former circle members like Haalien lead them, directing violence and bloodshed against the forest’s defenders.",al={"shadowgale forest cultists","why are cultists in shadowgale"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The events unfold in Shadowgale Forest, where Elegael Thornpaw investigates the cultist attack and confronts her cousin’s betrayal.",al={"where does ties that bind happen","shadowgale forest location"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the Cenarion Circle holds balance and kinship sacred. Haalien’s betrayal and the bloodshed among fellow druids are grave offenses against the order."},kw={"cenarion circle","commander haalien","cultists","druid","elegael thornpaw","haalien","shadowgale forest","the ties that bind"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94488},src={"In-game quest text: The Ties That Bind"},fv=true}
E["quest:94489"] = {t="quest",n="The Wounds of Betrayal",z="general",s="In Shadowgale Forest, Elegael cares for the shen'dorei druids wounded in a terrible assault. Poultices are ready for Nightfang Den, north across the clearing, while her mate Jorel Windsinger is missing.",h="In Shadowgale Forest, Elegael cares for the shen'dorei druids wounded in a terrible assault.",sec={{t="Aid for the Shen'dorei",b="Elegael tends the shen'dorei druids hurt in the assault on Shadowgale Forest. She has prepared poultices for her brethren sheltering in Nightfang Den, just north across the clearing. Few shen'dorei druids remain, and every survivor matters to their fragile enclave.",sp=0},{t="The Search for Jorel Windsinger",b="Elegael asks you to find her mate, Jorel Windsinger, and bring care to the seven battered druids in the cave. When she fled the fighting to prepare medicines, Jorel was already clinging to life. Nightfang Den holds the full devastation wrought upon the sanctuary, and Jorel's fate lies in its dark recesses.",sp=1},{t="A Vow of Retribution",b="After learning Jorel's end and seeing the terrible toll on her brethren, Elegael's grief turns to fury. She casts off despair and chooses retribution. Anyone allied with the Al'Aketh will face her unrelenting wrath for the slaughter of her people.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Wounds of Betrayal?",a="Elegael, a shen'dorei druid, asks you to tend her wounded brethren after a violent attack in Shadowgale Forest.",al={"who gives the wounds of betrayal","quest giver the wounds of betrayal","who is elegael"}},{q="Where is Nightfang Den located?",a="Nightfang Den lies north across the clearing in Shadowgale Forest. Injured shen'dorei druids have taken refuge in the cave.",al={"where is nightfang den","nightfang den location","where are the wounded druids"}},{q="Who is Jorel Windsinger?",a="Jorel Windsinger is Elegael's mate. Badly injured in the attack, he remained in Nightfang Den, where you learn his fate.",al={"who is jorel windsinger","jorel windsinger fate","where is jorel"}},{q="What are the shen'dorei druids?",a="The shen'dorei are a rare people with few druids among them. Elegael says every survivor is precious.",al={"what are the shendorei","who are shendorei druids","shendorei druid lore"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are enemies responsible for the attack on the druids, or allies of those responsible. After learning Jorel's fate and seeing the devastation, Elegael vows vengeance on them and anyone allied with them.",al={"who are the alaketh","al aketh","why does elegael hate al aketh"}},{q="What happens to Jorel Windsinger in the quest?",a="When you find Jorel Windsinger in Nightfang Den, his condition has taken a tragic turn. News of his fate and the surviving druids' dire state leaves Elegael grief-stricken and furious, and she vows revenge.",al={"what happens to jorel windsinger","does jorel live","jorel outcome"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the weight of seeing fellow caretakers of the wilds suffer betrayal and grievous injury. The shen'dorei druids are few.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere druidic traditions. The suffering of kindred druids in Shadowgale Forest and their struggle against treachery may weigh heavily on you."},kw={"al'aketh","druid","elegael","jorel windsinger","nightfang den","shadowgale forest","shen'dorei","the wounds of betrayal"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94489},src={"In-game quest text: The Wounds of Betrayal"},fv=true}
E["quest:94490"] = {t="quest",n="Ripped Missive",z="general",s="Haalien bears a bloodied letter after an attack on a druid den in Shadowgale Forest. Its words reveal what the cultists sought and point toward danger within Valanaar.",h="Haalien bears a bloodied letter after an attack on a druid den in Shadowgale Forest.",sec={{t="Bloodstained Orders",b="Haalien's missive gives a glimpse of the violence in Shadowgale Forest. Found after a fierce skirmish, the torn scrap bears grim news of cultists who attacked a local druid den. Its words offer clues to those seeking justice for the fallen.",sp=0},{t="Senseless Slaughter",b="Elegael Thornpaw learns why the cultists struck the den. They sought a mysterious pylon, not a feud with the druids. The den's inhabitants died because they stood in the way. Enraged by the slaughter, Elegael vows vengeance on any cultists still in the forest.",sp=1},{t="Treachery in Valanaar",b="Orders from within Valanaar lie behind the attack. The missive points to a directive from the settlement, where a traitor may be at work. To uncover the conspiracy before more lives are lost, the letter must reach Lotheluum in Valanaar without delay.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What is the Ripped Missive?",a="The missive is a torn, bloodstained letter found behind Haalien's bracer after a battle. It reveals why cultists attacked a druid den in Shadowgale Forest.",al={"what is ripped missive","ripped missive quest","bloodstained note haalien"}},{q="Where is the missive recovered from?",a="The missive was found behind Haalien's bracer after a violent confrontation. The battle left the letter torn and bloodstained.",al={"who dropped the ripped missive","where did ripped missive come from","who is haalien"}},{q="Who should receive the Ripped Missive?",a="Elegael Thornpaw in Shadowgale Forest should receive the missive first. After reading it, Elegael directs that it be carried swiftly to Lotheluum in Valanaar.",al={"who wants the ripped missive","who do i give ripped missive to","elegael thornpaw missive"}},{q="Why did the cultists attack the druid den?",a="The cultists attacked the druid den to secure a pylon there. They killed the druids because they stood in the way.",al={"why did cultists attack the druid den","cultist motive druid den","why did haalien attack"}},{q="Where did the attack orders originate?",a="The missive points to orders from Valanaar, where a traitor may be directing the cultists' work.",al={"where did the orders come from","who sent haalien","valanaar traitor"}},{q="Who is Lotheluum and why must they be notified?",a="Lotheluum is a contact in Valanaar. Elegael Thornpaw orders the missive delivered there to warn that the deadly orders trace back to someone hidden in the settlement.",al={"who is lotheluum","why take missive to lotheluum","lotheluum valanaar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The letter brings bitter news: druids at the den were slaughtered because they stood in the way of cultists seeking a pylon."},kw={"cultist","druid den","elegael thornpaw","haalien","lotheluum","pylon","ripped missive","shadowgale forest","valanaar"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94490},src={"In-game quest text: Ripped Missive"},fv=true}
E["quest:94491"] = {t="quest",n="The Fate of the Den",z="general",s="At the druid den, survivors mourn their fallen after the cultist assault. The Fate of the Den reaches Lotheluum in Valanaar with a recovered missive and word of heavy losses. The dispatch reveals that someone in Valanaar has been feeding vital information to the enemy.",h="At the druid den, survivors mourn their fallen after the cultist assault.",sec={{t="Tragedy at the Den",b="Cultists struck the druid den and left its defenders battered and grieving for fallen comrades. Outside aid brought the immediate danger under control, but the physical and emotional devastation remains immense. The dead cannot be brought back, and the wounded survivors are too weak for the long trek. Lingering cultists still roam nearby.",sp=0},{t="Treachery in Valanaar",b="The recovered missive shows the cultists chose their target with purpose. Someone hidden within Valanaar has been feeding them intelligence. When Lotheluum hears of the slaughter and reads the dispatch, grief for his fallen fellows gives way to alarm. A traitor still walks free in the settlement. He takes the evidence to the High Elder so their sacrifice will not be forgotten.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lotheluum?",a="Lotheluum lives in Valanaar and receives reports about the druid den. News of the assault and the recovered missive grieve him for his fallen fellows, so he takes evidence of betrayal to the High Elder.",al={"lotheluum","who is lotheluum","lotheluum npc"}},{q="What happened at the druid den?",a="Cultists devastated the druid den and killed many defenders. An adventurer helped bring the immediate danger under control, and the battered survivors found evidence that an insider had guided the attack.",al={"what happened at the den","druid den attack","fate of the den backstory"}},{q="What does the recovered missive reveal?",a="The missive reveals that someone hidden in Valanaar has secretly fed intelligence to the cult. It suggests local sabotage and espionage enabled the deadly raid on the den.",al={"what does the missive say","den missive","traitor missive"}},{q="Who is the High Elder mentioned by Lotheluum?",a="The High Elder is an authority in Valanaar to whom Lotheluum answers. Facing heavy casualties and the threat of a traitor, Lotheluum brings the missive and news of the tragedy to the High Elder.",al={"who is the high elder","valanaar high elder","high elder"}},{q="Who was responsible for attacking the druid den?",a="Members of a cult operating in the region attacked the druid den. An informant sheltered in Valanaar guided them, and the assault cost the den's inhabitants dearly.",al={"who attacked the den","who attacked druid den","den cultists"}},{q="Why could the survivor at the den not deliver the missive personally?",a="The survivor was too badly wounded by the attack to make the trek to Valanaar. The survivor stayed behind to eliminate remaining cultists and sent an adventurer to raise the alarm.",al={"why do we deliver the missive","quest giver injured","why cant the survivor go to valanaar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you feel the weight of this tragedy. Those who fell were your fellows, and hostile cultists betrayed their secluded refuge."},kw={"cultists","druid den","high elder","lotheluum","missive","the fate of the den","traitor","valanaar"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=94491},src={"In-game quest text: The Fate of the Den"},fv=true}
E["quest:94493"] = {t="quest",n="A Sacrifice in Vain",z="general",s="Elegael Thornpaw fears the Al'Aketh Cultists will overwhelm the wounded in her den. A message meant for Valanaar has not reached them, leaving her to ask for help.",h="Elegael Thornpaw fears the Al'Aketh Cultists will overwhelm the wounded in her den.",sec={{t="A Plea for Aid",b="The Al'Aketh Cultists fell upon Elegael Thornpaw's fellows with almost no warning. Many in her den are wounded or dying, and she does not know how long they can survive the attack. She had tried to send word to Valanaar, but the message did not get through. With no reinforcements in sight, Elegael asks you to help.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Elegael Thornpaw asks for help as the Al'Aketh Cultists attack her fellows.",al={"who needs help","Elegael Thornpaw","Elegael"}},{q="What happened to the people in the den?",a="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed them with little warning. Many are wounded or dying.",al={"den wounded","what happened here","cultist attack"}},{q="Why did Valanaar not send reinforcements?",a="Elegael's message did not reach Valanaar, so reinforcements have not arrived.",al={"where are reinforcements","Valanaar message","message to Valanaar"}},{q="What does Elegael need?",a="Elegael asks you to help her wounded fellows survive the Al'Aketh Cultists' attack.",al={"how can I help","help Elegael","what does she ask"}}},kw={"a sacrifice in vain","al'aketh cultists","den","elegael thornpaw","reinforcements","valanaar","wounded"},m={id=94493},src={"In-game quest text: A Sacrifice in Vain"},fv=true}
E["quest:94494"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In Loch Modan, Norric Lochthane calls a shaman toward water's purity. Having found harmony with wind, earth, and flame, the initiate is ready to commune with water.",h="In Loch Modan, Norric Lochthane calls a shaman toward water's purity.",sec={{t="The Path of Purity",b="A shaman who has found balance with earth, wind, and flame now turns to water. Its lesson reaches beyond a force to wield. Water offers a spiritual image of purity and resilience.",sp=0},{t="Ascent into the Elements",b="Norric Lochthane urges the initiate onward without delay. Communion with the elements demands effort and endurance, and the way climbs through rugged country. The mountain waits for no one. Understanding begins with the ascent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Water?",a="Call of Water begins a shaman's communion with water. Having learned from earth, wind, and fire, the initiate now seeks water's deeper truth.",al={"what is call of water","call of water quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who guides this step of the journey?",a="Eldrun Stormbreaker, the shaman trainer in Ironforge, sends the initiate to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. Norric urges a decisive first step, for neither the elements nor the heights wait for hesitation.",al={"who gives call of water","who says the mountain waits for no one","call of water mentor"}},{q="What does it mean that the mountain waits for no one?",a="The saying urges the initiate to begin a demanding ascent. Shamanic journeys lead into high peaks and remote wilderness where the spirits dwell, and they call for resolve.",al={"what does mountain waits for no one mean","the mountain waits for no one","mountain meaning"}},{q="What is the truth of water's purity?",a="Water teaches cleansing, fluidity, and purity. Stone offers stability and fire fuels resolve, while water's wisdom helps balance the spirits within oneself.",al={"why water purity","truth of waters purity","water element meaning"}},{q="How does water relate to the other elements here?",a="Earth, wind, and fire are foundations the initiate has already felt in boot, breath, and belly. Harmony calls for balance among the elements, not pursuit of one power alone.",al={"which elements come first","prerequisites for water","call of water elements"}},{q="Where does the initiate go after hearing these words?",a="Norric Lochthane sends the initiate to the Wetlands to seek the water sapta from Hervdana Saegrund. She dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.",al={"what happens next call of water","where do i go now","next step call of water"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you take a fundamental step toward communion with the elemental spirits. You move from earth and fire toward water's fluidity and purity.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hear a mentor's gruff cadence as you follow rugged mountain paths toward communion with nature."},kw={"call of water","elements","mountain","purity","shaman","totem trial","water totem"},m={id=94494},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94495"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In the Wetlands, seekers learn what pure water can do and search for the water sapta. Beneath the southern falls, Hervdana Saegrund welcomes those who brave the wilderness.",h="In the Wetlands, seekers learn what pure water can do and search for the water sapta.",sec={{t="The Nature of Water",b="Pure water gives life anew, carves stone, and washes away impurities. Tainted water brings the threat of ruin. Those who seek communion with water are sent into the wild to obtain a water sapta from those who dwell beside the element.",sp=0},{t="Shelter Beneath the Falls",b="Hervdana Saegrund and her family make their home in a secluded cave directly beneath the southern waterfalls of the Wetlands. Ironforge guards are far away, and Dark Iron dwarves lurk in the surrounding swamps. Still, Hervdana and her kin keep their isolated home by the falls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hervdana Saegrund?",a="Hervdana Saegrund is a dwarf who lives with her family in a cave beneath the southern falls of the Wetlands. She helps shamans seeking communion with water and the secrets of the water sapta.",al={"who is hervdana","hervdana saegrund","where is hervdana"}},{q="What is the water sapta?",a="A water sapta is a ceremonial elixir shamans use to commune with water spirits. In the eastern realms, seekers are directed to Hervdana Saegrund near the southern falls to obtain one.",al={"what is water sapta","sapta meaning","why get water sapta"}},{q="Where can Hervdana Saegrund be found?",a="Hervdana Saegrund and her family live in a secluded cave directly beneath the southern waterfalls in the Wetlands.",al={"where does hervdana live","where is the cave","southern falls location"}},{q="Why does Hervdana live in the dangerous Wetlands?",a="Hervdana and her kin have chosen the solitude of the waterfall cave for their own reasons, despite the Dark Iron dwarves in the marshes and the absence of city guards.",al={"why live in wetlands","wetlands dangers","dark irons wetlands"}},{q="What is the lesson of water taught here?",a="Pure water brings rebirth, carves stone, washes away impurities, and soothes the weary. Corrupted or tainted water threatens ruin.",al={"what does water mean","philosophy of water","water lesson"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Call of Water quest?",a="Shamans undertake the Call of Water to learn water’s nature and seek the water sapta from guides who live apart.",al={"what kind of quest is this","who is this quest for","dwarf shaman quest"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you learn water’s nature and seek a water sapta to commune with its spirits.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Hervdana recognizes you as kin braving the dangerous marshlands, where Dark Iron dwarves lurk nearby.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you journey deep into the perilous Wetlands, far from dwarven or Alliance guard patrols."},kw={"call of water","dwarf","hervdana saegrund","shaman","southern falls","water sapta","wetlands"},rel={"quest:972","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},m={id=94495},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94497"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In the Wetlands, an initiate gathers water to earn the sapta through Call of Water. The marsh is dangerous, but its waters show how water's energies shape and sustain the land.",h="In the Wetlands, an initiate gathers water to earn the sapta through Call of Water.",sec={{t="The Way of the Sapta",b="Hervdana guides initiates through the search for water in its many forms. They learn how it moves, changes lives, and sustains the land. Their path toward the sapta and communion with the spirits begins at an estuary, where ocean tides meet fresh runoff from the highlands.",sp=0},{t="Where Fresh Meets Brackish",b="Below Hervdana's cave, waterfalls carry highland springwater into the marsh. There it meets saltwater pushed inland by the coastal tides. The ocean brings sediment, minerals, and energies unlike those in clear mountain snowmelt. An initiate can find wisdom in the land's natural ways where these waters meet.",sp=0},{t="Shadows in the Marsh",b="Dangerous marsh creatures make gathering water risky. Dark Iron dwarves have also pushed far north into the Wetlands. Hervdana regrets the hostility between the dwarven clans. She sees how much dwarfkind might achieve if they set aside their feuds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the sapta?",a="The sapta is a sacred draught that lets an initiate commune with elemental spirits. To earn it, an initiate seeks water in its many forms and learns how it shapes the land and nourishes life.",al={"what is the sapta","sapta meaning","why seek sapta"}},{q="Who is Hervdana?",a="Hervdana guides initiates from her cave above the Wetlands waterfalls. She directs them to gather water samples and attune themselves to the element.",al={"who gives call of water","where is hervdana","hervdana cave"}},{q="Why gather water where the fresh meets the brackish?",a="At the estuary, highland snowmelt and springwater meet ocean tides. Their waters carry sediment, minerals, and spiritual wisdom.",al={"why estuary water","brackish water wetlands","fresh meets salt"}},{q="What dangers lurk near the waterfalls?",a="Dangerous marsh creatures and Dark Iron dwarves threaten travelers near the waterfalls. The dwarves have pushed north into the Wetlands.",al={"dark iron in wetlands","why are dark iron dwarves here","dark iron threat"}},{q="What does it mean to become a vessel?",a="A vessel is an initiate who seeks wisdom in the waters and carries offerings gathered from nature to deepen elemental harmony.",al={"what is a vessel","vessel of water"}},{q="What is the Empty Brown Waterskin used for?",a="Hervdana provides the Empty Brown Waterskin to collect a brackish sample at the base of the waterfalls in the marsh.",al={"empty brown waterskin use","what skin is used"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you seek the sapta by learning water's nature across different lands. You attune your spirit to its many forms.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hear Hervdana lament the division between the clans. Dark Iron dwarves press north as far as the Wetlands."},kw={"call of water","dark iron","estuary","hervdana","sapta","waterskin","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","item:empty-brown-waterskin"},m={id=94497},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94499"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="Hervdana Saegrund sends you from the Wetlands to test the waters at Stonewatch Falls in Redridge. What you bring back will serve in your spiritual trials.",h="Hervdana Saegrund sends you from the Wetlands to test the waters at Stonewatch Falls in Redridge.",sec={{t="A Suspect Cascade",b="Hervdana Saegrund sends you south from the Wetlands to examine the waters at Stonewatch Falls in Redridge. Lake Everstill supplies clean water to Lakeshire, but murlocs lurk beneath the cascade. They have grown unusually large and twisted. Hervdana suspects venom, foul sorcery, or seepage from the old fortress above. She asks you to gather a sample in an Empty Red Waterskin.",sp=0},{t="The True Source of Corruption",b="Hervdana Saegrund finds the water from Everstill clean and untouched by pollution. Dark sorcery from shadowseers near Stonewatch has twisted the Nightcrawler murlocs, not tainted water. The sample proves the falls are pure and that you are devoted to your trials. It is also a vital reagent for brewing a spiritual sapta.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where are they located?",a="Hervdana Saegrund gives it from the Wetlands. She studies water sources and the reagents needed to craft a sapta for an aspiring shaman's spiritual trials.",al={"who gives call of water","quest giver hervdana"}},{q="Why are you sent to collect water from Stonewatch Falls?",a="Hervdana suspects venom, dark magic, or corruption may be seeping over Stonewatch Falls from the old fort above and deforming the murlocs below. She asks you to bring back a fresh sample for her to examine.",al={"why fill waterskin redridge","stonewatch falls purpose"}},{q="Is the water at Stonewatch Falls actually tainted?",a="No. The water is pure and uncontaminated. Hervdana finds that local shadowseers' dark magic twists the murlocs.",al={"are stonewatch waters tainted","is lake everstill corrupted"}},{q="Why are the murlocs around Stonewatch Falls so large and twisted?",a="Nightcrawler murlocs near the falls are larger and more twisted than those in the Loch or Wetlands. Hervdana traces the change to the foul magic of local shadowseers.",al={"why are redridge murlocs mutated","stonewatch murlocs difference"}},{q="What is the water sample used for?",a="A sapta lets a shaman pierce the veil and perceive elemental spirits. Hervdana gathers pure water from various sources to brew the reagent for your spiritual trials.",al={"what is sapta","call of water reward purpose"}},{q="Who is Norric?",a="Norric is an associate or mentor involved in the shamanic trials. Hervdana says Norric will be pleased when you return with pure water.",al={"who is norric","norric call of water"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you gather water for a sapta and prove your devotion and perception across distant waterways before you commune with the water spirits."},kw={"call of water","hervdana saegrund","lake everstill","nightcrawler murlocs","redridge","sapta","shadowseers","stonewatch falls","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:stonewatch-falls","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:stonewatch","subzone:lakeshire","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc","item:empty-red-waterskin","subzone:the-loch"},m={id=94499},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94500"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In Ashenvale, you gather pure water from the lake beside Astranaar. It is the last sample you need before returning to Norric.",h="In Ashenvale, you gather pure water from the lake beside Astranaar.",sec={{t="The Search for Pure Water",b="You are sent to fill a waterskin with Ashenvale's uncorrupted water. Astranaar is a haven beside the lake, whose ancient waters lap against sunken ruins. This is the last liquid sample the giver needs before sending you on to Norric.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Astranaar",b="To reach Ashenvale from the Eastern Kingdoms, cross the sea by ship from Menethil Harbor toward Auberdine. The ship puts in at Southshore along the way. From Auberdine's docks, follow the road inland beneath Ashenvale's green boughs. Stay alert among the watchful shadows of the trees.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Call of Water?",a="You carry an empty waterskin into Ashenvale's ancient forest to gather pure water from the lake beside Astranaar. The sample may be enchanted, and you return it to the giver.",al={"what is call of water","call of water quest","call of water objective"}},{q="Where do I collect the water for this quest?",a="Gather water from the lake beside Astranaar, deep in Ashenvale. It remains uncorrupted, and ancient sunken ruins lie beneath its surface.",al={"where to find pure water","where to fill waterskin","call of water location"}},{q="How do I travel to Ashenvale for this quest?",a="Cross the sea by boat from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine. The boat stops at Southshore along the way. From Auberdine on the Darkshore coast, travel south through Ashenvale's deep woods to Astranaar.",al={"how to get to astranaar","travel to ashenvale","boat to astranaar"}},{q="What makes the water at Astranaar special?",a="The lake beside Astranaar holds water untouched by corruption. Sunken stone ruins suggest an ancient era of elven civilization and give the water its pure, potentially enchanted qualities.",al={"what lake in astranaar","astranaar water ruins","ruins in astranaar lake"}},{q="Who is Norric?",a="Norric is waiting for you after you gather the final liquid sample. The giver collects the pure Ashenvale water before sending you back to Norric.",al={"who is norric","return to norric"}},{q="What dangers should I expect in Ashenvale?",a="Ashenvale is an ancient, dense forest full of perils. The giver warns you to stay alert beneath its green canopy, where watchful eyes do not blink.",al={"danger in ashenvale","ashenvale threats"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross the sea from the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor, sailing from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine. From there, you reach Astranaar, a Night Elf settlement.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you are sent to gather water from the pure lake beside Astranaar, in the heartlands of the Kaldorei in Ashenvale. Ancient ruins still lie undisturbed there."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","auberdine","call of water","menethil","norric","southshore","waterskin"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","subzone:auberdine","subzone:southshore"},m={id=94500},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94501"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="At Loch Modan, seekers prepare to commune with water spirits. Hervdana blesses pure water for Norric Lochthane as aspiring shamans draw nearer to the water totem rites.",h="At Loch Modan, seekers prepare to commune with water spirits.",sec={{t="The Path to the Water Totem",b="You seek harmony with water through patience and reverence. Hervdana blesses the water you gather, and you carry it to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Birthing the Sapta",b="Norric Lochthane uses Hervdana’s blessed water to brew a water sapta. The draught lets you perceive the water spirits at Stendel’s Pond near Moonbrook. Every drop matters, and the dampened stopper has its place in the rites.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Norric Lochthane?",a="Norric Lochthane mentors candidates in Loch Modan as they seek communion with the elements. He oversees the preparations and rites for earning the water totem.",al={"who is norric","norric loch modan","who is norric lochthane"}},{q="Who is Hervdana?",a="Hervdana Saegrund lives with her family in a cave by the southern falls in the Wetlands. She guides aspiring shamans and blesses sacred water for making water sapta.",al={"who is hervdana","blessed by hervdana","hervdana water"}},{q="What is a sapta used for?",a="A sapta is a draught prepared with sacred water. Drinking it lets a shaman perceive elusive water spirits in natural pools.",al={"what is water sapta","sapta purpose","what does sapta do"}},{q="Where is Stendel's Pond located?",a="Stendel’s Pond lies in Westfall near Moonbrook. Water spirits dwell there, and a shaman seeks them after drinking a prepared sapta.",al={"where is stendels pond","stendel pond location","water spirits stendel"}},{q="Why is the Vial of Purest Water important?",a="The Vial of Purest Water holds blessed water needed to brew the water sapta and perform the rites for earning a water totem. Norric warns that every drop matters.",al={"why need pure water","vial of purest water purpose"}},{q="What are the water totem rites?",a="The water totem rites are spiritual trials that attune shamans to water. Shamans show respect and balance before receiving a water totem.",al={"what are water totem rites","how to get water totem"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face a trial of communion with the elements. You earn the water totem rites and make the sapta needed to perceive elemental spirits.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can seek guidance from elemental mentors such as Norric Lochthane across Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance shaman, you seek communion with water spirits across the eastern lands, between Loch Modan and Westfall."},kw={"call of water","hervdana","loch modan","moonbrook","norric lochthane","shaman","stendel's pond","vial of purest water","water sapta","water totem"},rel={"item:vial-of-purest-water","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stendel-s-pond","subzone:moonbrook"},m={id=94501},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94502"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="You travel from Loch Modan to Westfall, where a corrupted spring has silenced the water spirits. At Stendel's Pond, you can cleanse the corruption and awaken an old shrine to seek their favor and the Water Totem.",h="You travel from Loch Modan to Westfall, where a corrupted spring has silenced the water spirits.",sec={{t="A Spring Tainted by Shadow",b="Near Moonbrook, Stendel's Pond lies under a dark taint spreading across Westfall. Its waters were once clear, but now the local water spirits are silent. An old shrine stands neglected along the shore, covered in dust and cobwebs. You can seek to awaken the powers sleeping within it.",sp=0},{t="The Rite of Cleansing",b="Norric in Loch Modan guides you through the rite to restore balance. At Stendel's Pond, you face the foul entity polluting the water and take its bracers to the stone shrine. There, you offer them with drops of an alchemical draught and speak the incantation. Its vapors summon a cleansed spirit, which imparts wisdom and proves you worthy of the Water Totem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Water quest?",a="For shamans seeking communion with the water elements, the Call of Water is a spiritual trial. You cleanse the corruption at Stendel's Pond in Westfall and use its old shrine to summon a cleansed water spirit and seek your Water Totem.",al={"what is call of water","water totem quest","water quest westfall"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Norric gives you the Call of Water in Loch Modan. He instructs you in elemental rites, provides special potions, and guides you in cleansing corrupted elemental waters.",al={"who gives call of water","norric loch modan","quest giver"}},{q="Where is Stendel's Pond?",a="Stendel's Pond lies just outside Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall. Once a pure spring, it has grown still and murky under dark, corrupting influences.",al={"where is stendels pond","stendel pond location","pond near moonbrook"}},{q="How do you cleanse the corruption at Stendel's Pond?",a="You cleanse Stendel's Pond by defeating the corrupting presence and taking its bracers. Place them on the old shrine with the remaining potion drops, then speak the incantation Norric taught you.",al={"how to cleanse pond","cleanse stendels pond","shrine ritual"}},{q="What do you earn for completing this quest?",a="After you complete the trial and bring proof of the cleansing to Norric in Loch Modan, he gives you the Water Totem. It grants you command over water's elemental powers.",al={"what reward call of water","water totem reward"}},{q="Why is Stendel's Pond corrupted?",a="No one knows what caused the darkness at Stendel's Pond. The pool lies unnaturally still among the bones of beasts. Did Westfall's spreading malaise poison it, or is the pond itself a fountainhead of corruption?",al={"why is stendels pond corrupted","what corrupted the pond"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you undertake a rite of passage to attune with the water spirits and earn the Water Totem. It shows harmony and mastery over elemental forces.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance shaman, you travel from Loch Modan into Westfall to purify its corrupted waters."},kw={"call of water","loch modan","moonbrook","norric","shaman","stendel's pond","water totem","westfall"},rel={"subzone:stendel-s-pond","zone:westfall","zone:lochmodan","subzone:moonbrook"},m={id=94502},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94503"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In Westfall, you drive restless spirits from the waters before a Minor Manifestation of Water can speak with you.",h="In Westfall, you drive restless spirits from the waters before a Minor Manifestation of Water can speak with...",sec={{t="Cleansing the Tainted Waters",b="Corrupt spirits disturb Westfall's waters and their natural balance. You speak sacred words, and radiant light scatters the restless essences into ash and quiet mist.",sp=0},{t="The Spirit's Warning",b="Once the corrupt spirits are driven back, a Minor Manifestation of Water can emerge. It warns that the land's vital energies still wane, and that preserving life demands constant care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Call of Water?",a="In Westfall, you face a spiritual trial against corrupt spirits. A sacred invocation drives them back with radiant light, freeing the troubled waters so you can speak with a Minor Manifestation of Water.",al={"what is call of water","call of water westfall","westfall water quest"}},{q="Where can the Minor Manifestation of Water be found?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water appears in Westfall after the corrupt spirits nearby are subdued and dispelled. It waits to speak with those who aided the waters.",al={"where is the minor manifestation of water","manifestation location","water spirit westfall"}},{q="What happens when the corrupted spirits are cleansed?",a="When the invocation ends, brilliant light scatters the corrupt spirits. Their tainted essence unravels into ash as the water hisses into gentle mist.",al={"what happens during ritual","corrupt spirits call of water"}},{q="Is the land fully restored after completing the task?",a="The immediate corruption ebbs, but the elemental warns that the land's vitality continues to wane. Mortals still bear the enduring duty of protecting life.",al={"is corruption gone","did we save the water"}},{q="Who is called upon to assist the manifestation?",a="You are called to cleanse the spirits and shoulder the duty of protecting dwindling life. The manifestation thanks your class for stepping forward.",al={"who can do call of water","class requirement water quest"}},{q="Why were the water spirits corrupted in Westfall?",a="Corrupt spirits have disturbed Westfall's natural waters. Their precise origin is unclear, but their malevolent presence saps the area's living vitality.",al={"why is water corrupted westfall","westfall water problem"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you commune with primal elements and cleanse tainted water spirits. This rite reminds you of your enduring duty to balance nature.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find the manifestation in Westfall, where local spirits endure the creeping blight touching the land."},kw={"call of water","cleansing","corruption","elemental","minor manifestation of water","water spirit","westfall"},rel={"npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:westfall"},m={id=94503},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94505"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="general",s="In Westfall, you learn what water can give and what corruption can take. Bring a Shard of Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan, and he grants you a water totem.",h="In Westfall, you learn what water can give and what corruption can take.",sec={{t="The Path of Water",b="You travel to Westfall and return to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan with a Shard of Water. The journey tests your dedication to water and your understanding of its power to give life and purge corruption. Those who prove themselves receive a water totem and take an essential step on their elemental path.",sp=0},{t="Giver of Life",b="Water gives life, and corruption brings it to an end. Norric Lochthane teaches you to use water's restorative strength to protect the vulnerable and preserve living things. Its gifts reach beyond mending the body. They bring endurance, renewal, and spiritual balance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Norric Lochthane?",a="Norric Lochthane is a shaman mentor in Loch Modan. He guides initiates through trials to understand water spirits and tests their resolve with a journey to Westfall. When they bring proof of their communion, he gives them a water totem.",al={"who is norric lochthane","who gives water totem","norric loch modan"}},{q="What is the Shard of Water?",a="The Shard of Water is proof you bring from Westfall to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. It shows you have communed with water, understood its life-giving nature, and learned to fight corruption.",al={"what is shard of water","shard of water use","shard of water quest item"}},{q="Why does the trial lead to Westfall?",a="You travel to Westfall to learn water's life-giving power and see how corruption threatens it. Even modest victories in that troubled land show your ability to protect life.",al={"why go to westfall","westfall water quest","journey to westfall call of water"}},{q="What is the significance of the water totem?",a="A water totem embodies your bond with water. Its pure water can soothe and mend wounds, while its spiritual gifts also preserve and sustain life.",al={"what does water totem do","why do shamans need water totem","water totem lore"}},{q="What lesson does the trial teach about water?",a="The trial teaches you that water gives life, while corruption ends it. You are charged with using water's power to nurture and protect living things and restore balance where corruption threatens them.",al={"what is water is life","call of water philosophy","shaman water teachings"}},{q="What comes after completing the Call of Water?",a="Norric Lochthane says your next elemental trial will not come right away. He encourages you to practice and explore water's deeper mysteries before taking further trials.",al={"what trial comes next","next shaman trial","what happens after call of water"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you undergo a rite of passage that brings communion with water spirits and grants you a water totem to heal and sustain life.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance initiate, you report to mentors like Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan and face trials in places like Westfall, unlike Horde shamans of Kalimdor."},kw={"call of water","loch modan","norric lochthane","shaman","shard of water","water totem","westfall"},rel={"item:shard-of-water","zone:lochmodan","zone:westfall"},m={id=94505},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:94568"] = {t="quest",n="The Cult's True Plans",z="general",s="The cult's informant has died before sharing what he knew. Talaanis Shadowsong must help investigators find another way to oppose the cult.",h="The cult's informant has died before sharing what he knew.",sec={{t="A Silenced Defector",b="A frightened insider left the cult and hoped to seek help beyond it. Before he could reveal what he knew, he was killed. His warnings remain, but the cult's plans do not.",sp=0},{t="Rethinking the Approach",b="The informant's death leaves the leadership without its chief source of knowledge. They consult Talaanis Shadowsong and reconsider how to confront the cult. An open attack with peacekeepers is judged a losing battle, so the investigators must find another way forward.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the turncoat mentioned in this quest?",a="The turncoat was a cult insider who sought help after becoming terrified of the cult's schemes. He was killed before he could reveal what he knew.",al={"who died in the cults true plans","who is the dead turncoat","turncoat cult secrets"}},{q="Who is Talaanis Shadowsong?",a="Talaanis Shadowsong is the contact consulted after the informant's death. You observe a strategic discussion with Talaanis about how to proceed against the cult.",al={"talaanis shadowsong role","who is talaanis shadowsong","speak with talaanis"}},{q="Why can't peacekeepers simply attack the cult directly?",a="Peacekeepers are not expected to fare well in an open clash with the cult. The investigators judge that a direct attack would be a losing battle.",al={"why not fight the cult","peacekeepers vs cult","direct assault cult"}},{q="What are the cult's actual plans?",a="The cult's plans remain unknown because the informant died before sharing what he knew. Whatever they intend was frightening enough to drive a member to seek help.",al={"what is the cult planning","cult scheme","cult true plans meaning"}},{q="What is the next step after speaking with Talaanis?",a="After the informant's death and the decision against open battle, the leadership must find another way to uncover and thwart the cult's plans.",al={"what happens after the cults true plans","next steps cult quest"}},{q="What happens during The Cult's True Plans?",a="You speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe a council about the informant's death. The discussion considers why the peacekeepers cannot be relied on to stop the cult by force.",al={"the cults true plans quest summary","what do you do in the cults true plans"}}},kw={"cult","defector","peacekeepers","talaanis shadowsong","the cult's true plans","turncoat"},rel={"quest:92643"},m={id=94568},src={"In-game quest text: The Cult's True Plans"},fv=true}
E["quest:94616"] = {t="quest",n="Water Sapta",z="general",s="In Westfall, you take the Water Sapta to seek a troubled pond. The ceremonial draught sharpens your sight to water spirits and hidden corruption, so you can investigate the imbalance.",h="In Westfall, you take the Water Sapta to seek a troubled pond.",sec={{t="The Sight of the Waters",b="Shamans prepare a sapta to let them see beyond the physical world. The Water Sapta attunes your senses to water, revealing disturbances and spirits hidden from ordinary travelers. Without that changed sight, an elemental presence might seem like no more than ripples.",sp=0},{t="Disturbance in Westfall",b="The Water Sapta leads you to Westfall, an arid Alliance realm troubled by unrest and neglect. A pond there holds spiritually polluted water. With the sapta's sight, you seek the corrupted water, uncover the disturbance, and restore harmony to the local water spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Water Sapta?",a="A Water Sapta is a ceremonial brew that attunes your spiritual sight to water spirits and disturbances hidden from mortal eyes.",al={"what is a water sapta","water sapta purpose","what does water sapta do"}},{q="Where is the tainted pond in Westfall?",a="The tainted pond lies within Westfall. The Water Sapta guides you there to find the corrupted water and address the spiritual disturbance.",al={"where is the tainted pond","tainted pond westfall","tainted pond location"}},{q="Why does the water sapta lead to Westfall?",a="The Water Sapta leads you to Westfall because a pond there holds tainted water. You investigate the corruption and seek to restore balance to the troubled spirits.",al={"why go to westfall","westfall water corruption","why is westfall water tainted"}},{q="Who uses the water sapta?",a="Shamans use Water Saptas during trials of elemental communion. The draught attunes their senses to water spirits, helping them perceive hidden elementals and inspect tainted pools.",al={"who drinks water sapta","who uses water sapta","shaman sapta drink"}},{q="What happens when you bring the sapta to the tainted pond?",a="Near the tainted pond in Westfall, the Water Sapta grants elemental sight. It reveals the water's spiritual state or summons hidden spirits tied to the local water trial.",al={"what happens after using sapta","sapta elemental sight"}},{q="How do elemental saptas work in shamanic tradition?",a="Saptas are ceremonial draughts that attune shamans to an element and bridge the physical world and spirit realm. Shamans use them in trials for earth, fire, water, or air.",al={"how do saptas work","sapta lore"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can use a sapta to attune your spiritual senses to elemental spirits hidden from ordinary sight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you investigate corrupted waters in Westfall and bring elemental cleansing rites into Alliance lands."},kw={"elemental attunement","sapta","shaman trial","tainted pond","water sapta","water spirits","westfall"},rel={"quest:972","zone:westfall"},m={id=94616},src={"In-game quest text: Water Sapta"},fv=true}
E["quest:94638"] = {t="quest",n="Strength and Mercy",z="general",s="Ur'endra's mate asks you to end her suffering after she loses herself to madness. Your resolve earns a blessing to take the shape of his kin.",h="Ur'endra's mate asks you to end her suffering after she loses herself to madness.",sec={{t="A Heavy Plea",b="A druid asks you to end Ur'endra's suffering in the Shen'dar Highlands. She is his mate, but madness has turned her against her own kin. The loss of the winds' magic has driven many creatures to lose themselves, and Ur'endra is among them. Her lair lies in a cave west of here, along the bluffs between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.",sp=0},{t="The Blessing",b="In the Shen'dar Highlands, Ur'endra's mate grieves her loss and calls it necessary for the balance. He sees your resolve in accepting so terrible a price. He grants you a blessing that lets you take the shape of his kin, and charges you to aid those who lack strength and defend those in need.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ur'endra?",a="Ur'endra is the mate of the druid who asks you to end her suffering.",al={"ur'endra","urendra who","druid's mate"}},{q="Why is Ur'endra attacking her kin?",a="Ur'endra has lost herself to madness. The loss of the winds' magic has caused many creatures to lose themselves.",al={"why urendra mad","urendra attacking","what happened to urendra"}},{q="Where is Ur'endra's lair?",a="Ur'endra makes her lair in a cave west of the druid, in the bluffs between the Shen'dar Highlands and the Gustberry Lowlands.",al={"urendra cave","where is urendra","shen'dar cave"}},{q="What does the druid ask me to do?",a="The druid asks you to end Ur'endra's suffering.",al={"urendra task","what do i do","kill urendra"}},{q="What blessing does the druid grant?",a="The druid grants you a blessing that lets you take the shape of his kin.",al={"shape blessing","way of the claw","druid blessing"}},{q="Why does the druid ask for this?",a="The druid considers ending Ur'endra's suffering necessary for the balance.",al={"why kill urendra","why this is necessary","balance"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are asked to prove your resolve before receiving a blessing to take the shape of the druid's kin."},kw={"druid blessing","gustberry lowlands","shape of the claw","shen'dar highlands","strength and mercy","ur'endra","winds' magic"},m={id=94638},src={"In-game quest text: Strength and Mercy"},fv=true}
E["quest:94773"] = {t="quest",n="Divine Grace",z="general",s="A lesson called Divine Grace thanks you for serving the Light. Your example matters to travelers in dangerous lands.",h="A lesson called Divine Grace thanks you for serving the Light.",sec={{t="A Lesson of Thanks",b="After your service, the Light is praised for the example you set among travelers in dangerous lands. You are offered a lesson in thanks for what you have done.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Divine Grace about?",a="Divine Grace thanks you for serving the Light and setting an example for travelers in dangerous lands.",al={"divine grace","what's divine grace","divine grace quest"}},{q="Who is this lesson for?",a="The lesson is offered to you in thanks for your service to the Light.",al={"who gets the lesson","lesson for me","divine grace reward"}},{q="What example did I set?",a="You became an example to travelers in dangerous lands and beyond.",al={"my example","shining example","what did i do"}}},kw={"dangerous lands","divine grace","lesson","light","travelers"},rel={"topic:light"},m={id=94773},src={"In-game quest text: Divine Grace"},fv=true}
E["quest:94774"] = {t="quest",n="Divine Grace",z="general",s="High Priestess Laurena calls you to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light because your superiors have approved further training. Your lessons in the ways of the Light are ready to begin.",h="High Priestess Laurena calls you to Stormwind’s Cathedral of Light because your superiors have approved...",sec={{t="A Call to Stormwind",b="Your superiors send you to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind after judging that you have proven yourself. There, High Priestess Laurena is ready to guide your further training. She says there are lessons every servant of the Light must learn, and she is prepared to discuss them with you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why am I being sent to Stormwind?",a="Your superiors believe you have proven yourself and have approved further training in the ways of the Light.",al={"why Stormwind","sent to Cathedral","why go there"}},{q="Who is High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind and is ready to guide your training.",al={"Laurena who","who is Laurena","high priestess"}},{q="Where do I find High Priestess Laurena?",a="High Priestess Laurena is at the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind.",al={"Laurena location","where is Laurena","cathedral location"}},{q="What training is Laurena offering?",a="Laurena is prepared to discuss lessons that all servants of the Light must learn.",al={"Light training","what lessons","learn the Light"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, your superiors have approved further training in the ways of the Light."},kw={"cathedral of light","divine grace","high priestess laurena","light","servant of the light","stormwind","training"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:high-priestess-laurena","topic:light","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=94774},src={"In-game quest text: Divine Grace"},fv=true}
E["quest:94789"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Air",z="general",s="A shaman is sent to Veyric Thundervein in the northern hills of Arathi Highlands. He will teach you more about mastering air.",h="A shaman is sent to Veyric Thundervein in the northern hills of Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="The Northern Hills",b="A shaman sends you north into Arathi Highlands to find Veyric Thundervein. The element of air is difficult to master, and he can teach you more. Your growing skill has brought you this far; now your training turns to wind and the spirits of air.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veyric Thundervein?",a="Veyric Thundervein is in the northern hills of Arathi Highlands, where he can teach you more about air.",al={"Veyric","who is Veyric","air trainer"}},{q="Where do I find Veyric?",a="Find Veyric Thundervein in the northern hills of Arathi Highlands.",al={"Veyric location","where's Veyric","Arathi air trainer"}},{q="What is Call of Air about?",a="A shaman sends you to Veyric Thundervein so he can teach you more about the element of air.",al={"Call of Air quest","air training","wind spells"}},{q="Why am I going to Arathi Highlands?",a="Veyric Thundervein is in the northern hills of Arathi Highlands, and he will teach you more about air.",al={"why Arathi","go north quest","find Veyric"}},{q="What does Veyric teach?",a="Veyric teaches you to focus wind spells and call upon the spirits of air.",al={"Veyric training","spirits of air","focus wind spells"}}},kw={"air","arathi highlands","call of air","shaman","spirits of air","veyric thundervein","wind spells"},rel={"zone:arathi"},m={id=94789},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Air"},fv=true}
E["quest:94792"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="Josephine Carson is teaching aspiring hunters in Taming the Beast how to care for a wild companion. The trial uses a Rockhide Boar and a Taming Rod, with nature’s balance in mind.",h="Josephine Carson is teaching aspiring hunters in Taming the Beast how to care for a wild companion.",sec={{t="Bonding with Beasts",b="Traveling alone in the wild can be dangerous. An animal companion offers protection in battle and company on long journeys. For aspiring hunters and trackers, forming that bond is a vital step. Josephine Carson guides novices through a trial with a Rockhide Boar and a Taming Rod. To calm and direct the beast, they must stay composed and focused without giving in to fear or causing needless bloodshed.",sp=0},{t="The Balance of Nature",b="Josephine Carson warns her pupils not to exploit beasts recklessly. Taming calls for patience and discipline, never cruelty or dominance, and nature’s balance must be kept. The enchanted rod lets novices practice handling a formidable Rockhide Boar without permanently depleting local wildlife. Once they learn to command and soothe the beast, they return the rod. Respect for nature comes before pride.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Taming the Beast?",a="Taming the Beast teaches aspiring hunters how to bond with wild creatures. Josephine Carson shows them how to approach and pacify a Rockhide Boar with a Taming Rod. The trial teaches survival skills and respect for nature’s balance.",al={"taming the beast quest","what is taming the beast","hunter pet quest"}},{q="Who is Josephine Carson?",a="Josephine Carson mentors adventurers in caring for animal companions. She lends students a Taming Rod so they can practice patience and skill with beasts. She teaches that the work takes practice and respect for nature’s balance.",al={"josephine carson","who gives taming the beast","taming rod quest giver"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod used for?",a="The Taming Rod is an enchanted tool for safely handling a formidable beast. It lets novices practice commanding and soothing a Rockhide Boar without permanently depleting local wildlife. They return the rod once they learn the fundamentals.",al={"taming rod","what does the taming rod do","how to use taming rod"}},{q="Why do hunters need animal companions?",a="An animal companion offers protection, watchfulness, and aid in combat. A loyal beast can guard the front line and keep a traveler company on long, hazardous journeys through wild lands.",al={"why get a pet","beast companion benefits","why tame beasts"}},{q="What creature must be tamed during this trial?",a="The trial calls for a Rockhide Boar, a sturdy beast suited to testing basic animal handling. The exercise teaches composure and discipline when facing aggressive wildlife. Afterward, adventurers report their progress to Josephine Carson.",al={"which boar do i tame","rockhide boar target","taming the beast mob"}},{q="Why does Josephine Carson emphasize the balance of nature?",a="Josephine Carson warns against greed and force when handling wild beasts. Reckless use disrupts nature’s balance, and beasts are not disposable tools. True mastery means respecting their place in nature.",al={"balance of nature meaning","nature balance taming","why respect nature"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, taming wild beasts is a defining rite of passage. A loyal companion offers protection and watchfulness in battle, forging an enduring partnership between tracker and beast.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that care and restraint help preserve nature’s balance. Treating forest wildlife with respect honors the natural order you are sworn to protect."},kw={"animal companion","balance of nature","beast taming","hunter pet","josephine carson","rockhide boar","taming rod","taming the beast"},rel={"item:taming-rod","quest:456"},m={id=94792},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94793"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="general",s="In Goldshire, Training the Beast shows young hunters how to care for a tamed companion. Isaac Chan teaches them to feed and revive their beasts, then train them for life at their side.",h="In Goldshire, Training the Beast shows young hunters how to care for a tamed companion.",sec={{t="The Responsibilities of the Hunt",b="You seek Isaac Chan, an experienced woodsman in Goldshire, to learn how to train your beast. A tamed creature needs care and discipline before it can become a steady ally. Without Chan's guidance, your companion may remain unruly in the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Woodsman's Guidance",b="Isaac Chan teaches you to care for your animal companion. You learn to feed it and revive it if it falls in battle. He also teaches commands that help it fight, and reminds you that power over wildlife calls for respect. Honor nature's balance and live in awe of the world around you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Isaac Chan?",a="Isaac Chan is a lifelong woodsman who lives in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest. He knows wildlife and wilderness survival, and teaches novice hunters to guide, feed, revive, and teach abilities to their animal companions.",al={"who is isaac chan","goldshire beast trainer","isaac chan lore"}},{q="What is the purpose of Training the Beast?",a="Hunters learn to care for a tamed beast and maintain their bond. Isaac Chan teaches them to feed their companion, revive it if it falls in battle, and teach it new combat abilities.",al={"what does this quest do","why train beast","purpose of training the beast"}},{q="Where can Isaac Chan be found?",a="Isaac Chan lives in Goldshire, the central township of Elwynn Forest, south of Northshire Valley and southwest of Stormwind City.",al={"where is isaac chan","where do i turn this in","isaac chan location"}},{q="What skills does Isaac Chan teach?",a="Isaac Chan teaches the basics of caring for and training an animal companion. You learn to feed your beast, revive it if it falls in combat, and teach it new abilities as it grows alongside you.",al={"what skills do you get","pet abilities learned","what does isaac chan teach"}},{q="Why does Isaac Chan remind hunters to respect nature?",a="Isaac Chan teaches hunters humility before the wild. He asks them to honor nature's balance and live in awe of the world around them, so their bond with a beast rests on stewardship rather than exploitation.",al={"why respect nature","respect the balance hunter"}},{q="Who undertakes this quest?",a="Hunters who can already tame beasts seek Isaac Chan's woodland discipline to sustain and train an animal companion.",al={"who can do this quest","is training the beast hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you move beyond capturing beasts to build a lasting, disciplined bond. Feed, revive, and train your companion.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hunter in Elwynn Forest, you can learn the basics of beast handling from veteran woodsmen like Isaac Chan in Goldshire."},kw={"elwynn forest","feed pet","goldshire","hunter pet","isaac chan","pet training","revive pet","training the beast","woodsman"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={id=94793},src={"In-game quest text: Training the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94822"] = {t="quest",n="Confounding Flash",z="general",s="Your superiors send you to Ironforge to continue your training with High Priestess Mims. Your service to the Light has earned their notice.",h="Your superiors send you to Ironforge to continue your training with High Priestess Mims.",sec={{t="A Further Lesson",b="Your superiors send you to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. They judge that your service has prepared you for more training. Mims is to guide you, and the lesson awaits your arrival.",sp=0},{t="Before Mims",b="High Priestess Mims receives you in Ironforge and notes your late arrival. She excuses the delay in light of your service to the Light, then asks you to heed her lesson.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent me to Ironforge?",a="Your superiors asked you to travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge for further training.",al={"who sent me","who are my superiors"}},{q="Who is High Priestess Mims?",a="High Priestess Mims is the one your superiors direct you to find in Ironforge. She can guide your further training.",al={"who is mims","mims"}},{q="Why am I being sent for training?",a="Your superiors believe you have proven yourself through your service to the Light.",al={"why training","why me"}},{q="Where do I find High Priestess Mims?",a="Find High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge.",al={"where is mims","hall of mysteries"}}},kw={"confounding flash","hall of mysteries","high priestess mims","ironforge","light","superiors","training"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:hall-of-mysteries","topic:light"},m={id=94822},src={"In-game quest text: Confounding Flash"},fv=true}
E["quest:94863"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="Josephine Carson guides you through Taming the Beast as you learn to handle a boar before facing a Gray Forest Wolf. With a Taming Rod, you seek the fiercer creature's trust.",h="Josephine Carson guides you through Taming the Beast as you learn to handle a boar before facing a Gray...",sec={{t="The Path of the Hunter",b="Josephine Carson watches as you take another step in learning to handle beasts. You have practiced with simple boars; now you enter the forest to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. The enchanted rod she gives you helps calm the predator. Patience and respect matter as much as tracking and marksmanship when you seek a wild creature's trust.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Instinct and Trust",b="Josephine Carson gives you a specialized Taming Rod to calm dangerous wildlife. Approach the wolf with patience and precision, and overcome its aggression without lethal force. After practicing your bond with the beast, return the rod to Josephine as proof of your growing skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Taming the Beast?",a="Taming the Beast is a hunter's training trial, where you use an enchanted Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf.",al={"taming the beast quest","gray forest wolf quest","tame wolf lesson"}},{q="Who gives and completes this quest?",a="Josephine Carson instructs you and gives you the Taming Rod. After the trial, you return it to her.",al={"who gives taming the beast","who is josephine carson","where to turn in taming the beast"}},{q="What creature do you have to tame?",a="You are instructed to tame a Gray Forest Wolf, a fiercer forest predator than the boars you handled before.",al={"what do i tame","which beast","target of taming the beast"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod used for?",a="Josephine Carson gives you the Taming Rod to soothe a wild Gray Forest Wolf and form a temporary bond without causing permanent harm.",al={"what does taming rod do","why use taming rod","taming rod lore"}},{q="What did the hunter tame before this trial?",a="Before facing the Gray Forest Wolf, you practiced handling a forest boar.",al={"taming previous lesson","what was tamed before wolf"}},{q="Do you keep the Gray Forest Wolf as a permanent companion?",a="No. After practicing your beast-bonding skills, you return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.",al={"do you keep wolf","is wolf permanent pet"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn the patience and respect needed to bond with fierce wild predators."},kw={"beast taming","gray forest wolf","hunter","hunter training","josephine carson","taming rod","taming the beast"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={id=94863},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94864"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="In Elwynn Forest, hunters face Taming the Beast, the final trial Josephine Carson oversees. After taming a boar and a wolf, each hunter uses a Taming Rod to earn a Young Forest Bear’s trust. The test deepens the hunter’s bond with beasts and teaches respect for the woodland’s balance.",h="In Elwynn Forest, hunters face Taming the Beast, the final trial Josephine Carson oversees.",sec={{t="The Final Trial of the Hunt",b="Hunters in Elwynn Forest learn to live among the wild creatures around them. After taming a wolf and a boar, they face one last test of courage and patience. Josephine Carson sends each hunter to a Young Forest Bear, the strongest of the forest’s common predators. The hunter must endure the bear’s strength and earn its trust, rather than force it to submit.",sp=0},{t="Respect and Balance in Elwynn",b="Taming wildlife in Elwynn calls for respect, not dominion. Forest bears embody the woodland’s strength and vitality, and help keep its natural order. With a Taming Rod, hunters learn to calm a bear’s aggression and form a bond through understanding. Earning the trust of such a powerful animal deepens a hunter’s bond with the wild and completes the first lessons Josephine Carson oversees.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns this trial to hunters?",a="Josephine Carson assigns the trial to hunters training in Elwynn Forest. After they tame lesser beasts, she gives them guidance and the Taming Rod for the forest bear. When the trial is done, they return the rod to her.",al={"who gives taming the beast","taming the beast quest giver","josephine carson quest"}},{q="Which beasts must be tamed before this challenge?",a="Hunters first tame a boar and a wolf before facing a Young Forest Bear. Those trials show they can handle resilient and pack-oriented beasts before attempting to earn a bear’s trust.",al={"prerequisite beasts for taming","what did i tame before bear","beasts tamed before this"}},{q="Why are hunters sent after a Young Forest Bear?",a="A Young Forest Bear tests a hunter against the brawn and might of Elwynn Forest’s wildlife. After handling the quick wolf and resilient boar, the hunter must show endurance, respect, and courage to earn the bear’s trust.",al={"why tame young forest bear","young forest bear purpose","why bears in elwynn"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Taming Rod?",a="Josephine Carson gives hunters a Taming Rod to help calm wild animals. It helps soothe an aggressive Young Forest Bear without killing it and lets the hunter form a peaceful bond. Hunters return the rod to Carson when the trial is complete.",al={"taming rod purpose","what does taming rod do","why use taming rod"}},{q="How does taming beasts help Elwynn Forest?",a="Hunters learn to preserve Elwynn Forest’s natural balance by treating wildlife with respect and restraint. They guide dangerous beasts peacefully instead of hunting them down, preserving harmony between local wildlife and humanoid settlements.",al={"why does elwynn balance matter","elwynn forest balance","taming and forest balance"}},{q="What does completing this lesson signify for a hunter?",a="Completing the final trial deepens a hunter’s bond with wild beasts. Earning the trust of Elwynn’s mightiest creature teaches the understanding needed for lifelong partnerships with animal companions across Azeroth.",al={"what happens after taming the bear","hunter training completion","attunement to beasts meaning"}},{q="Where are Young Forest Bears found?",a="Young Forest Bears roam the wooded areas of Elwynn Forest, among dense trees and alongside wolves and spiders. Hunters leave nearby settlements and track the bears through the undergrowth, following Carson’s final direction with the Taming Rod.",al={"young forest bear location","where to find bears in elwynn","forest bear elwynn"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you move beyond tracking and toward a deeper, more understanding bond with wild beasts.",["race:Human"]="As a human hunter training in Elwynn Forest, you learn to live alongside the kingdom’s natural predators instead of trying to destroy them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance beast master, you can give wilderness scouts disciplined companions to defend homesteads and patrol trade roads across Stormwind’s territories."},kw={"attunement to beasts","beast training","elwynn forest","hunter quest","josephine carson","taming rod","taming the beast","young forest bear"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={id=94864},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94896"] = {t="quest",n="Aid For The Refugees",z="general",s="After Ban'aethal fell, its survivors have little left to call their own. The settlement deep in Shadowgale Forest began to fall into the sky in the middle of the night, and danger keeps the refugees from retrieving what they left behind.",h="After Ban'aethal fell, its survivors have little left to call their own.",sec={{t="A Desperate Plea",b="Ealaane and the other refugees fled their homes deep in Shadowgale Forest. With almost nothing gathered around them, they ask travelers to brave the dangers they left behind.",sp=0},{t="The Calamity of Ban'aethal",b="Ban'aethal began to fall into the sky in the dead of night. Its inhabitants had only moments to escape, leaving their personal possessions behind. The surrounding woods grew hostile and dangerous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ealaane?",a="Ealaane fled Ban'aethal with others when their settlement began to collapse. She asks travelers heading toward Shadowgale Forest to recover the belongings left in the ruins.",al={"who gave aid for the refugees","quest giver aid for the refugees","ealaane"}},{q="What happened to Ban'aethal?",a="Ban'aethal was a settlement deep within Shadowgale Forest. Its residents fled in the middle of the night when a sudden catastrophe struck.",al={"what is banaethal","where is banaethal","ban aethal village"}},{q="Why did the villagers have to evacuate Ban'aethal?",a="Ban'aethal began to fall into the sky in the middle of the night, forcing its residents to flee. The village and surrounding forest became too dangerous for them to stay or return.",al={"why evacuate banaethal","falling into sky","ban aethal disaster"}},{q="Why are the villagers asking for their belongings to be retrieved?",a="The catastrophe came suddenly in the middle of the night, leaving the villagers little time to flee with their belongings. The forest and ruins are now too dangerous, so they depend on travelers to recover what was left behind.",al={"why need belongings","abandoned belongings","why recover belongings"}},{q="What is Shadowgale Forest?",a="Shadowgale Forest is the wooded region where Ban'aethal stood. Since the disaster tore the village apart, the forest has become extremely hazardous for ordinary folk.",al={"where is shadowgale forest","shadowgale forest lore"}},{q="Can the refugees return to their homes?",a="No. Ealaane says Shadowgale Forest and the ruins of Ban'aethal are too dangerous for the refugees to return on their own.",al={"can refugees go back","is banaethal safe"}}},kw={"aid for the refugees","ban'aethal","banaethal","belongings","ealaane","refugees","shadowgale forest"},rel={"topic:refugee"},m={id=94896},src={"In-game quest text: Aid For The Refugees"},fv=true}
E["quest:94897"] = {t="quest",n="The Fate of a Loved One",z="general",s="Resaan has been gone from the Ruins of Ban'aethal for more than a week, and his partner waits for news. Travelers bound there are asked to bring him home or return his cherished heirloom.",h="Resaan has been gone from the Ruins of Ban'aethal for more than a week, and his partner waits for news.",sec={{t="A Desperate Plea",b="Resaan's partner pleads with him to stay as he prepares to return to the Ruins of Ban'aethal. Yet he feels compelled to brave the ruins for supplies. His partner is left waiting for word.",sp=0},{t="Vanished in the Ruins",b="More than a week has passed since Resaan set out, far longer than a swift return should take. His partner asks travelers bound for Ban'aethal to search the ruins. If Resaan lives, bring him home. If tragedy has taken him, recover his family heirloom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Resaan?",a="Resaan returned to the Ruins of Ban'aethal to gather supplies despite his partner's pleas that he stay. More than a week has passed without word, and his partner fears the worst.",al={"who is resaan","where is resaan","find resaan"}},{q="What are the Ruins of Ban'aethal?",a="The Ruins of Ban'aethal are where Resaan went in search of supplies. His partner fears he may not have survived a week there alone.",al={"what is banaethal","ruins of banaethal lore","where is banaethal"}},{q="Why did Resaan return to Ban'aethal?",a="Resaan returned to Ban'aethal to retrieve supplies despite his partner's pleas that he stay.",al={"why did resaan go back","why resaan in banaethal"}},{q="What does the questgiver ask you to bring back?",a="Resaan's partner asks travelers to bring him safely home if he is alive. If he has perished in the ruins, they ask for his personal heirloom as a keepsake.",al={"what does questgiver want","what happens if resaan dead"}},{q="How long has Resaan been missing?",a="Resaan has been missing for more than a week since setting out for the Ruins of Ban'aethal. The dangers there leave his partner fearing the worst.",al={"how long resaan missing","how long has resaan been gone"}},{q="Who offers this quest?",a="Resaan's grieving partner asks passing travelers heading toward Ban'aethal for help, desperate to learn what became of him.",al={"who gives fate of a loved one","fate of a loved one questgiver"}}},kw={"ban'aethal","heirloom","resaan","ruins of ban'aethal","supplies","the fate of a loved one"},m={id=94897},src={"In-game quest text: The Fate of a Loved One"},fv=true}
E["quest:94911"] = {t="quest",n="Child of Nature",z="general",s="A fellow Skyborne sees promise in your druidic arts and points you toward Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. He can teach you how to reach the Cenarion Circle’s stronghold in Moonglade.",h="A fellow Skyborne sees promise in your druidic arts and points you toward Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Druid’s Welcome",b="Your teacher believes the druids of the Cenarion Circle will welcome you and share their knowledge. Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff can show you how to reach their stronghold in Moonglade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who should I speak with?",a="Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. He can teach you how to reach Moonglade.",al={"who do I talk to","Turak Runetotem","who is Turak"}},{q="Where is the Cenarion Circle’s stronghold?",a="The Cenarion Circle’s stronghold is in Moonglade on Kalimdor.",al={"where is the circle","Cenarion Circle location","Moonglade"}},{q="Why am I being sent to Moonglade?",a="The druids of the Cenarion Circle can share their knowledge with you.",al={"why Moonglade","learn druid","druid training"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you are told the Cenarion Circle’s druids will welcome you and share their knowledge.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are directed to Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff, who can teach you how to reach the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade."},kw={"cenarion circle","child of nature","druid","moonglade","skyborne","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:5921","zone:thunderbluff","npc:turak-runetotem","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:skyborne"},m={id=94911},src={"In-game quest text: Child of Nature"},fv=true}
E["quest:94912"] = {t="quest",n="Child of Nature",z="general",s="In Stormwind, Sheldras Moontree can show you the way to Moonglade. There, the Cenarion Circle’s druids have wisdom to share with a child of nature.",h="In Stormwind, Sheldras Moontree can show you the way to Moonglade.",sec={{t="A Far Stronghold",b="Sheldras Moontree, a night elf in Stormwind, can show you how to reach Moonglade on Kalimdor. The Cenarion Circle keeps its stronghold there. It is an ancient order of naturalists and druids, with much to teach you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sheldras Moontree?",a="Sheldras Moontree is a night elf in Stormwind who can show you how to reach Moonglade.",al={"sheldras","night elf in stormwind","who teaches me moonglade"}},{q="What is the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle is an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts.",al={"cenarion circle","druid order","nature circle"}},{q="Where is the Cenarion Circle's stronghold?",a="The Cenarion Circle keeps its stronghold in Moonglade on Kalimdor.",al={"cenarion stronghold","where is moonglade","moonglade"}},{q="What can I learn from the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle’s druids have much wisdom to share with you.",al={"cenarion teachings","what can they teach","druid wisdom"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you are among the first of your people to arrive in Azeroth, and you are welcomed.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are directed toward the Cenarion Circle, an ancient order whose members practice the druidic arts."},kw={"cenarion circle","child of nature","druid","kalimdor","moonglade","sheldras moontree","skyborne","stormwind"},rel={"quest:5921","topic:cenarion-circle","quest:94911"},m={id=94912},src={"In-game quest text: Child of Nature"},fv=true}
E["quest:94914"] = {t="quest",n="Moonglade",z="general",s="Your teacher opens a way to Moonglade, where Dendrite Starblaze awaits. There, you can speak with him about the path you have begun.",h="Your teacher opens a way to Moonglade, where Dendrite Starblaze awaits.",sec={{t="A First Lesson",b="Your teacher welcomes druids to Moonglade. Keeper Remulos watches over those who rest there. You receive Teleport: Moonglade, a spell that carries you there when you seek knowledge or solace. Your first lesson is to speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you now follow.",sp=0},{t="The Bear Form",b="Dendrite Starblaze recognizes that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. He sees you well on your way.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who should I speak to in Moonglade?",a="Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you are on.",al={"who do i talk to","dendrite starblaze","nighthaven druid"}},{q="How do I get to Moonglade?",a="Your teacher gives you Teleport: Moonglade, a spell that carries you there.",al={"moonglade teleport","how reach moonglade","teleport spell"}},{q="Who watches over druids in Moonglade?",a="Keeper Remulos watches over druids who rest in Moonglade.",al={"keeper remulos","moonglade guardian","who guards moonglade"}},{q="What does Dendrite say about my progress?",a="Dendrite recognizes that you have already mastered the form of the Bear.",al={"bear form","did i master bear","dendrite response"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, your teacher welcomes you to Moonglade and teaches you a spell to travel there."},kw={"bear form","dendrite starblaze","druid","keeper remulos","moonglade","nighthaven","teleport"},rel={"quest:5921","subzone:nighthaven","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:remulos"},m={id=94914},src={"In-game quest text: Moonglade"},fv=true}
E["quest:94946"] = {t="quest",n="The Magical City of Dalaran",z="general",s="A mage in Valanaar sends you from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City, where several mages await your people's arrival. The city offers a place to begin exploring Azeroth, but the lands beyond can be dangerous without preparation and experience.",h="A mage in Valanaar sends you from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City, where several mages await your people's...",sec={{t="Arrival in Dalaran",b="Recent events with the cult keep the speaker in Valanaar for now. Several mages wait in Dalaran for your people, so you are sent to the dock outside the lodge. There, you board a skycutter bound for Dalaran City.\n\nWhen you arrive, speak with Danaaris Stargale. Your people are still making their home in the city, and the country beyond its safety can prove dangerous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is waiting in Dalaran?",a="Several mages await your people's arrival in Dalaran. When you reach the city, you are asked to speak with Danaaris Stargale.",al={"mages in dalaran","who's in dalaran","dalaran mages"}},{q="Where do I travel from?",a="You travel from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City aboard the skycutter at the dock outside the lodge.",al={"how get to dalaran","from zephras","skycutter"}},{q="Why is the speaker staying in Valanaar?",a="Recent events with the cult changed the speaker's plans, so they intend to remain in Valanaar for a time.",al={"why stay valanaar","cult changed plans","valanaar mage"}},{q="Is it safe outside Dalaran?",a="The land beyond Dalaran can be dangerous without proper preparation and experience.",al={"outside dalaran safe","danger near dalaran","dalaran outskirts"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you travel from Zephras Isle to join the mages awaiting your people's arrival in Dalaran."},kw={"cult","dalaran","dalaran city","danaaris stargale","mages","skycutter","valanaar","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras","subzone:dalaran"},m={id=94946},src={"In-game quest text: The Magical City of Dalaran"},fv=true}
E["quest:94947"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome to Azeroth",z="general",s="You arrive in Stormwind through the Skyborne Portal and are welcomed by its regent. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon grants you leave to travel across Alliance lands.",h="You arrive in Stormwind through the Skyborne Portal and are welcomed by its regent.",sec={{t="Arrival in the Capital",b="You step through the Skyborne Portal into Stormwind, the human capital. From there, you make your way along the city's grand thoroughfares to Stormwind Keep, where the regency awaits your arrival.",sp=0},{t="An Audience with the Regent",b="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon receives the arriving members of the High Order in the throne room. A Kirin Tor courier had warned him they were coming. It has been some time since high elves walked the halls of Stormwind Keep, yet Bolvar welcomes them as guests and grants them free passage across Alliance territories on behalf of the King.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this quest about?",a="You arrive in Stormwind through the Skyborne Portal and present yourself to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon at Stormwind Keep.",al={"what is welcome to azeroth","welcome to azeroth quest"}},{q="Who is Bolvar Fordragon?",a="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs Stormwind as regent from Stormwind Keep. He rules on behalf of the young King Anduin Wrynn while King Varian remains missing.",al={"who is bolvar fordragon","regent of stormwind"}},{q="Why is Bolvar receiving the Skyborne?",a="A Kirin Tor messenger told Bolvar Fordragon that members of the High Order would arrive. He welcomes them as guests of the crown and grants them leave to travel freely across Alliance lands.",al={"why are skyborne in stormwind","high elves stormwind"}},{q="What is the High Order?",a="The High Order is the group associated with the Skyborne high elves. The Kirin Tor announced their arrival to Stormwind's leaders.",al={"who is high order","high order lore"}},{q="Where does the Skyborne Portal lead?",a="The Skyborne Portal brings travelers directly into Stormwind, the human capital. From there, newcomers can go to Stormwind Keep to seek an audience with the crown.",al={"skyborne portal destination","where does portal go"}},{q="Are the Skyborne allowed throughout Alliance territory?",a="Bolvar Fordragon welcomes the Skyborne as the King's guests and grants them leave to travel unhindered throughout Alliance lands.",al={"are skyborne alliance","skyborne welcome alliance"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you are welcomed into Stormwind and granted passage across Alliance territory when you arrive through the portal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon officially welcomes the High Order on behalf of King Anduin Wrynn, granting them leave to freely traverse Alliance lands."},kw={"bolvar fordragon","high elf","high order","kirin tor","portal","skyborne","stormwind keep","welcome to azeroth"},rel={"npc:bolvar-fordragon","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:skyborne","quest:92596","topic:alliance","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:95350"},m={id=94947},src={"In-game quest text: Welcome to Azeroth"},fv=true}
E["quest:94978"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="Quel'ana Quickgale teaches you the bond between beast and master. You begin by taming a Windsong Crawler near the waters of Zephras.",h="Quel'ana Quickgale teaches you the bond between beast and master.",sec={{t="First Bond",b="You have the Taming Rod and a Windsong Crawler to tame. Find one near a body of water and practice your skills. Then return the rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar. This creature is your first step toward mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Quel'ana ask me to tame?",a="Quel'ana asks you to tame a Windsong Crawler near a body of water on Zephras.",al={"what beast","taming target","crawler quest"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod for?",a="You use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler.",al={"how rod works","taming tool","rod quest"}},{q="Where do I find a Windsong Crawler?",a="Windsong Crawlers live near bodies of water on Zephras.",al={"crawler location","where crawler","zephras beast"}},{q="Who gave me the Taming Rod?",a="Quel'ana Quickgale gives you the Taming Rod in Valanaar.",al={"quest giver","who is quelana","quelana quickgale"}},{q="Why am I learning to tame a beast?",a="Learning the bond between beast and master is the first step toward mastery of your class.",al={"why tame crawler","beast mastery","first taming"}}},kw={"beast taming","quel'ana quickgale","taming rod","taming the beast","valanaar","windsong crawler","zephras"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={id=94978},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:94979"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="general",s="In the Gustberry Lowlands, Quel'ana Quickgale asks you to tame a galestrider. Your skill on open ground will prepare you for trials ahead.",h="In the Gustberry Lowlands, Quel'ana Quickgale asks you to tame a galestrider.",sec={{t="Across the Plains",b="You've already shown you can tame the river's crawler. Now Quel'ana Quickgale gives you a Taming Rod and sends you to the lowlands of Zephras. There, a proud, winged galestrider runs swiftly across the plains. Earn its trust and practice your skill. Then bring the rod back to Quel'ana in Valanaar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Quel'ana want me to tame?",a="Quel'ana asks you to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands.",al={"tame what","galestrider tame","what beast"}},{q="Where do I find the galestrider?",a="You can find the Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands, in the plains of Zephras.",al={"where galestrider","galestrider location","lowlands where"}},{q="What is the Taming Rod for?",a="Quel'ana gives you the Taming Rod so you can tame an Ornery Galestrider.",al={"taming rod use","rod for what","how tame beast"}},{q="Who gave me this assignment?",a="Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar asks you to tame an Ornery Galestrider and bring back the Taming Rod.",al={"who sent me","quelana who","quickgale"}}},kw={"galestrider","gustberry lowlands","ornery galestrider","quel'ana quickgale","taming rod","taming the beast","valanaar","zephras"},rel={"item:taming-rod"},m={id=94979},src={"In-game quest text: Taming the Beast"},fv=true}
E["quest:95034"] = {t="quest",n="The Debt",z="general",s="Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher recounts the attack that left Banon gravely wounded. Her account names a worgen as the creature that struck them on the road.",h="Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher recounts the attack that left Banon gravely wounded.",sec={{t="A Wound on the Road",b="Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher tells you what happened on the road. A giant, wolf-like worgen attacked her party and killed its guards. Banon stepped between the creature and Lumina, who drove it off with a spell. By then Banon was badly bitten. He urged her to leave him, but she stayed, and the two limped onward before gnolls found them.",sp=0},{t="Banon's Last Moments",b="Banon in the Sepulcher was pierced by many gnoll blades before he turned on Lumina. She saw that he still recognized her, though he could not control himself. Lumina believes the worgen doomed him, and vows to kill it so it cannot bring the same horror to another living being.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who attacked Lumina and Banon on the road?",a="A giant, wolf-like worgen attacked Lumina and Banon on the road.",al={"what attacked them","worgen attack","road attacker"}},{q="What happened to the guards?",a="The worgen dispatched the guards who accompanied Lumina and Banon.",al={"guards fate","what about the guards","road guards"}},{q="How did Lumina drive off the worgen?",a="Lumina managed to cast a spell that startled the worgen and caused it to flee.",al={"how worgen flee","lumina spell","what scared it"}},{q="Why was Banon bitten?",a="Banon threw himself in the worgen's path to protect Lumina, and the creature badly bit him.",al={"banon bite","how hurt banon","what happened to banon"}},{q="Where does Lumina tell you what happened?",a="Lumina Windsinger tells you her account in the Sepulcher.",al={"where find lumina","lumina location","sepulcher"}}},kw={"banon","gnolls","lumina windsinger","road attack","sepulcher","the debt","worgen"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","topic:worgen","topic:gnoll"},m={id=95034},src={"In-game quest text: The Debt"},fv=true}
E["quest:95036"] = {t="quest",n="A Moon-Kissed Blade",z="general",s="Trevan warns you that worgen threaten Silverpine Forest. Old Fire-Eye resists death through unknown magic, and Trevan asks you to learn what a special blade will require.",h="Trevan warns you that worgen threaten Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A smith's list",b="Old Fire-Eye is the worgen who attacked Trevan and his companions. Trevan will give you a list of materials for a weapon against him. The materials are gathered, and Trevan believes he knows a smith who can craft the blade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Old Fire-Eye?",a="Old Fire-Eye is the largest and meanest of the worgen. He attacked Trevan and his companions.",al={"old fire-eye","fire eye worgen","big worgen"}},{q="Why does Old Fire-Eye keep coming back?",a="Unknown magic keeps Old Fire-Eye from staying dead.",al={"why wont fire-eye die","old fire eye magic","worgen that wont stay dead"}},{q="What does Trevan need from me?",a="Trevan will give you a list of materials needed to forge a special weapon.",al={"what does Trevan want","Trevan list","blade materials"}},{q="Why is a special blade needed?",a="Old Fire-Eye resists death through unknown magic. Trevan says a special weapon is needed to put him down.",al={"moon kissed blade why","weapon for Old Fire-Eye","kill fire eye"}},{q="Who can craft the blade?",a="Trevan thinks he knows a smith able to craft the blade.",al={"smith for the blade","who makes moon blade","blade blacksmith"}}},kw={"a moon-kissed blade","blade materials","old fire-eye","silverpine forest","special weapon","trevan","worgen"},rel={"zone:silverpine","topic:worgen","quest:95140","topic:light"},m={id=95036},src={"In-game quest text: A Moon-Kissed Blade"},fv=true}
E["quest:95042"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking the Kor Gem",z="general",s="In Ashenvale, Ulric Frostveil sees your search for a Kor Gem as familiar work for Alliance spellcasters. He points you north to Blackfathom Deeps, where naga still use the gems.",h="In Ashenvale, Ulric Frostveil sees your search for a Kor Gem as familiar work for Alliance spellcasters.",sec={{t="A Gem in Ashenvale",b="Ulric asks you to bring him a Kor Gem from the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, north of Ashenvale. The naga below still use the gems. They can empower magical weapons and implements, but Ulric warns you not to go alone.",sp=0},{t="Ulric's Interest",b="Ulric Frostveil recognizes corruption in the gem. He says he can dispel the evil infused into it by the naga witches. Then he asks whether you would sell it to him for his academic pursuits.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ulric Frostveil?",a="Ulric Frostveil is a Forsaken in Ashenvale who asks you to bring him a Kor Gem.",al={"ulric frostveil","who is ulric","forsaken in ashenvale"}},{q="Where can I find a Kor Gem?",a="Ulric directs you north to Blackfathom Deeps, where naga still use Kor Gems.",al={"kor gem location","where gem","blackfathom gem"}},{q="What are Kor Gems used for?",a="Kor Gems can empower magical weapons and implements.",al={"kor gem use","gem magic","what does kor gem do"}},{q="Why does Ulric want a Kor Gem?",a="Ulric asks you to bring him a Kor Gem. He says he may value it for his academic pursuits.",al={"ulric wants gem","why gem","frostveil gem"}},{q="Who still uses Kor Gems?",a="The naga in Blackfathom Deeps still use Kor Gems.",al={"naga gems","who uses kor gems","blackfathom naga"}}},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","forsaken","kor gem","naga","ulric frostveil"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","zone:blackfathom","topic:naga","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance"},m={id=95042},src={"In-game quest text: Seeking the Kor Gem"},fv=true}
E["quest:95111"] = {t="quest",n="An Underrated Talent",z="general",s="In Silverpine Forest, Trevan Rol gives Ott a chance to make a blade to your design. Ott’s simple weapons have earned praise from smiths in the Undercity.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Trevan Rol gives Ott a chance to make a blade to your design.",sec={{t="A Smith's Chance",b="Trevan Rol asks you to carry materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him a commission. Ott sells simple blades to travelers. Trevan bought one and later took it to the Undercity for maintenance. There, local smiths praised its quality and mistook it for the work of a famous master. Now Ott has the chance to forge a blade to your specifications.",sp=0},{t="Ott's Answer",b="Ott says no one has asked him to make a custom weapon before. He usually crafts humble, functional weapons in his own style and seeks no acclaim. Still, he is willing to try. He wonders why you chose him when smiths in the Undercity also take custom work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ott?",a="Ott is a weaponsmith in Tarren Mill who sells simple blades to travelers.",al={"ott smith","who's ott","tarren mill smith"}},{q="Why does the Undercity smith want me to find Ott?",a="The smith bought one of Ott’s blades and was surprised when Undercity smiths praised its quality. The smith wants Ott to have a chance to make something special.",al={"why ott","undercity smith order","ott commission"}},{q="What am I bringing to Ott?",a="You are taking materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offering him a commission to forge your blade.",al={"materials for ott","what do i take","ott materials"}},{q="Does Ott make custom weapons?",a="Ott says no one has asked him to make a custom weapon before, but he is willing to try.",al={"ott custom blade","can ott forge for me","ott commissions"}},{q="Why does Ott ask why I chose him?",a="Ott says smiths in the Undercity take custom work, and wonders why you sought him instead.",al={"why choose ott","ott wonders why","why not undercity smith"}}},kw={"commission","custom blade","ott","smith","tarren mill","undercity","weaponsmith"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:undercity"},m={id=95111},src={"In-game quest text: An Underrated Talent"},fv=true}
E["quest:95125"] = {t="quest",n="Ott's Masterwork",z="general",s="Ott is ready to forge a blade for you from fine materials. You may watch him at work.",h="Ott is ready to forge a blade for you from fine materials.",sec={{t="At the Forge",b="Ott values the fine materials and hopes his work will meet your expectations. He forges a blade for you, then offers it for your travels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is making my blade?",a="Ott is forging your blade from the fine materials you provided.",al={"who forges it","otts blade","ott smith"}},{q="Can I watch Ott forge it?",a="Ott asks you to stand back as he begins forging. You are asked to watch him work.",al={"watch ott forge","see blade made","forge process"}},{q="What does Ott say when the blade is finished?",a="Ott calls the blade his finest work and hopes it serves you well in your travels.",al={"ott completion","what does ott say","blade done"}}},kw={"blacksmith","blade","forging","masterwork","materials","ott"},m={id=95125},src={"In-game quest text: Ott's Masterwork"},fv=true}
E["quest:95126"] = {t="quest",n="The Moonsilver Blade",z="general",s="In Silverpine Forest, Trevan Rol awaits the blade that will complete his work before he faces a beast.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Trevan Rol awaits the blade that will complete his work before he faces a beast.",sec={{t="The Blade",b="Ott thanks you for the chance to help and asks you to carry his gratitude to Trevan. You bring Ott's Masterwork back to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.",sp=0},{t="Trevan's Approval",b="Trevan Rol examines the blade and approves of Ott's work. Only the beast remains. When you are ready, he directs you to speak with Lumina.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who made Ott's Masterwork?",a="Ott made Ott's Masterwork and sent it with you to Trevan Rol.",al={"who made the blade","ott blade","masterwork maker"}},{q="Who is Trevan Rol?",a="Trevan Rol receives and inspects Ott's Masterwork in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is trevan","trevan blade","trevan rol"}},{q="Where do I bring the blade?",a="Bring Ott's Masterwork to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where blade go","take ott's masterwork where","blade destination"}},{q="What does Trevan think of the blade?",a="Trevan Rol inspects the blade and says it will do nicely.",al={"trevan like blade","is ott's blade good","trevan approval"}},{q="Who should I speak with after Trevan?",a="When you are ready, Trevan Rol directs you to speak with Lumina.",al={"what next","who is lumina","speak to lumina"}}},kw={"beast","lumina","moonsilver blade","ott","ott's masterwork","silverpine forest","trevan rol"},rel={"quest:95125","zone:silverpine"},m={id=95126},src={"In-game quest text: The Moonsilver Blade"},fv=true}
E["quest:95140"] = {t="quest",n="Old Fire-Eye",z="general",s="Lumina Windsinger sends you after Old Fire-Eye in Silverpine Forest with the Moonsilver Blade. The Windshapers await his death, and Lumina hopes the blade will guide you well.",h="Lumina Windsinger sends you after Old Fire-Eye in Silverpine Forest with the Moonsilver Blade.",sec={{t="A Blade's Purpose",b="The Windshapers have given you the Moonsilver Blade. Locals say Old Fire-Eye hunts across a wide stretch south of here, usually near the gates to Gilneas. Lumina asks you to find him and use the blade to end him. The Windshapers' gratitude depends on his death.",sp=0},{t="After the Hunt",b="When you return, Lumina thanks you and says Banon may rest in peace. Then she lays a small measure of her people's magic upon the bloodstained blade, hoping the winds will guide it well.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to hunt Old Fire-Eye?",a="Lumina Windsinger asks you to hunt Old Fire-Eye with the Moonsilver Blade.",al={"who sent me","lumina task","windsinger"}},{q="Where can I find Old Fire-Eye?",a="Locals say Old Fire-Eye hunts across a wide area south of Lumina, usually near the gates to Gilneas.",al={"fire eye location","where is old fire-eye","gilneas gates"}},{q="What should I use against Old Fire-Eye?",a="Lumina asks you to use the Moonsilver Blade to end Old Fire-Eye.",al={"blade for fire-eye","moonsilver weapon","what weapon"}},{q="Why does Lumina want Old Fire-Eye slain?",a="Lumina says the Windshapers will be grateful when Old Fire-Eye is dead.",al={"why kill fire-eye","why hunt him","fire-eye reason"}},{q="Who is Banon?",a="Lumina says Banon may rest in peace after Old Fire-Eye is slain.",al={"banon who","banon peace","who is banon"}},{q="What does Lumina do with the blade?",a="Lumina lays a small measure of her people's magic upon the bloodstained Moonsilver Blade.",al={"blade magic","lumina enchants blade","wind magic"}}},kw={"banon","gilneas","lumina windsinger","moonsilver blade","old fire-eye","silverpine forest","windshapers"},rel={"quest:95126","quest:92595","zone:silverpine"},m={id=95140},src={"In-game quest text: Old Fire-Eye"},fv=true}
E["quest:95141"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Rog'mar",z="general",s="An Orc directs you to Rog'mar, an outpost in the embattled Riverglades. Report to Krom'rosh, whose experience has helped the outpost endure repeated attacks.",h="An Orc directs you to Rog'mar, an outpost in the embattled Riverglades.",sec={{t="An Outpost Endures",b="The Riverglades lie northeast of Stonard along the eastern coast. Many have tried to claim the land, though few have managed it. Rog'mar is a small outpost that has survived countless attacks. You are sent there to report to Krom'rosh, an old ally whose battle experience has helped the outpost endure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Rog'mar?",a="Rog'mar lies in the Riverglades, northeast of Stonard along the eastern coast.",al={"rog'mar location","where is rogmar","rog'mar outpost"}},{q="Who am I reporting to?",a="You are to report to Krom'rosh at the Rog'mar outpost.",al={"report to who","who is krom'rosh","kromrosh"}},{q="What is Rog'mar?",a="Rog'mar is a small outpost in the Riverglades that has endured countless attacks.",al={"rogmar what","riverglades outpost","small outpost"}},{q="Why is Krom'rosh at Rog'mar?",a="Krom'rosh's experience battling enemies has helped the outpost endure.",al={"why kromrosh there","krom'rosh role","who runs rogmar"}},{q="What kind of land are the Riverglades?",a="The Riverglades are an embattled land along the eastern coast, northeast of Stonard.",al={"riverglades","what is riverglades like","embattled land"}}},kw={"attacks","eastern coast","krom'rosh","outpost","riverglades","rog'mar","stonard"},rel={"zone:riverglades","subzone:stonard"},m={id=95141},src={"In-game quest text: Report to Rog'mar"},fv=true}
E["quest:95204"] = {t="quest",n="Crest of Lordaeron",z="general",s="The Forsaken preserve what little remains of Lordaeron in Undercity. A weathered crest bears the fallen kingdom’s emblem, a rare link to its past.",h="The Forsaken preserve what little remains of Lordaeron in Undercity.",sec={{t="A Surviving Symbol of the Fallen Kingdom",b="The Third War shattered Lordaeron. Ash, ruins, and Scourge desolation swallowed much of the kingdom, leaving few emblems behind. To the Forsaken beneath the ruins of the Capital City, those that survive are precious links to the civilization they once belonged to.",sp=0},{t="Preserving Forsaken Heritage",b="The weathered crest is brought from the wider world to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity. Oran tests the metal with a bite, then confirms it is genuine and mostly intact. For Oran and the Forsaken archivists, each recovered piece helps restore a history the Scourge sought to erase.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crest of Lordaeron?",a="The Crest of Lordaeron is a weathered emblem of the fallen human kingdom. Few physical relics survived the Scourge’s destruction, so it preserves a rare piece of Lordaeron’s past.",al={"what is crest of lordaeron","lordaeron crest quest","crest item"}},{q="Who wants the crest in Undercity?",a="Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity receives the crest. Oran inspects and safeguards artifacts tied to the old kingdom.",al={"who gets the crest","where to turn in crest","crest turn in undercity"}},{q="Why does Oran Snakewrithe bite the crest?",a="Oran Snakewrithe bites the crest to test its metal and verify that it is genuine. Oran confirms it is a mostly intact relic of Lordaeron.",al={"why bite the crest","oran bites crest"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken value relics of Lordaeron?",a="The Forsaken are the undead remnants of Lordaeron’s former people. Relics of their ruined homeland remain tangible links to their history and identity.",al={"why do forsaken care about lordaeron","forsaken relics"}},{q="What will happen to the crest after it is turned in?",a="Oran Snakewrithe takes custody of the crest and keeps it safe. It helps the Forsaken preserve and remember their kingdom’s heritage.",al={"what happens to the crest","crest preservation"}},{q="How rare are surviving relics from Lordaeron?",a="Surviving emblems and relics from before the Third War are exceptionally scarce. The Scourge’s invasion left few physical signs of Lordaeron behind.",al={"is the crest rare","how many crests left"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a former citizen of Lordaeron, you treasure relics of the fallen kingdom as rare remnants of your past and heritage.",["faction:Horde"]="You help Forsaken archivists in Undercity preserve Lordaeron’s legacy amid the ruins left by the Scourge."},kw={"crest of lordaeron","forsaken","lordaeron","oran snakewrithe","relic","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:lordaeron","quest:95189"},m={id=95204},src={"In-game quest text: Crest of Lordaeron"},fv=true}
E["quest:95212"] = {t="quest",n="Never Saddle on Quality",z="general",s="At Amberstill Ranch, handlers prepare rams for the Alliance expedition in Alterac. They need pristine mountain leopard pelts to make warm saddles for the beasts, so mounts and riders can face the northern mountains' biting frost.",h="At Amberstill Ranch, handlers prepare rams for the Alliance expedition in Alterac.",sec={{t="Mounting the Expedition",b="The handlers of Amberstill Ranch in Dun Morogh are readying sturdy mountain rams for Alterac. But the work has stalled: they lack the material needed to make durable, cold-weather saddles for the rams.",sp=0},{t="Warmth for the High Passes",b="The expedition's mounts need thick insulation to endure the freeze of the Alterac mountains. Hunters are sent to the eastern crags to track the largest, fiercest mountain leopards in Dun Morogh and bring back pristine pelts. The Alliance forces need gear that can withstand the high passes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Never Saddle on Quality?",a="At Amberstill Ranch in Dun Morogh, a breeder needs high-quality leopard pelts for warm, sturdy saddles. The saddles are for a team of rams being readied as reinforcements for the Alterac expedition.",al={"what is this quest","never saddle on quality quest","what is never saddle on quality"}},{q="Why are leopard pelts needed?",a="Leopard pelts provide the thick fur needed to make durable, warm saddles for the expedition's mounts. The insulation protects riders and beasts from Alterac's biting mountain chill.",al={"why leopard pelts","what are pelts for","why pristine pelts"}},{q="Where are the rams being sent?",a="The mounts are bound for Alliance forces in the Alterac expedition. Well-equipped riding rams are vital support in the harsh weather and ongoing operations in the high passes.",al={"where are the rams going","who gets the rams","alterac reinforcements"}},{q="What is Amberstill Ranch's role here?",a="Amberstill Ranch lies in Dun Morogh, east of Kharanos. It is the main breeding and training ground for dwarven mountain rams.",al={"where is amberstill ranch","amberstill ranch location"}},{q="Where do the leopards roam?",a="The leopards roam the snowy ridges and eastern crags of Dun Morogh, east of Amberstill Ranch. Hunters seek the largest beasts there for their pristine hides.",al={"where find leopards","where are leopards dun morogh"}},{q="Why is cold weather protection so important for the expedition?",a="Alterac's kingdom and peaks are freezing and windswept. Without thick, high-quality saddle material, mounts and riders risk frostbite and exhaustion in the mountains.",al={"is alterac cold","why warm saddles"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Amberstill Ranch breeds rams to reinforce Alliance forces in Alterac's freezing heights.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Morogh's hardy mountain rams are iconic dwarven mounts. Their breeders at Amberstill Ranch refuse to equip them with substandard gear.",["class:Hunter"]="Skilled trackers and hunters are needed to seek out Dun Morogh's fiercest mountain leopards and secure pristine pelts."},kw={"alterac","alterac expedition","amberstill ranch","dun morogh","leopard pelts","never saddle on quality","pristine leopard pelts","rams","saddles"},rel={"subzone:amberstill-ranch","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={id=95212},src={"In-game quest text: Never Saddle on Quality"},fv=true}
E["quest:95213"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Blasting Powder",z="general",s="Near Gol'Bolar Quarry, an empty keg of hazardous blasting powder has turned up among troggs. Its return to Quarrymaster Thesten reveals a breach in the quarry's security and explosive stores.",h="Near Gol'Bolar Quarry, an empty keg of hazardous blasting powder has turned up among troggs.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Discovery",b="At Gol'Bolar Quarry, a warning stamped on an empty keg shows that hazardous blasting powder has slipped out of authorized hands. The explosives are reserved for controlled quarrying, with the quarrymaster's direct approval. The keg was found among hostile troggs, and that points to a threat beyond ordinary trouble for the miners.",sp=0},{t="The Quarrymaster's Alarm",b="When the empty keg reaches Quarrymaster Thesten, the dwarven overseers' worst fears are confirmed. Thesten turns pale: the blasting powder is gone, and subterranean troggs swarming the area have handled it. Now the quarry leaders must learn what the creatures mean to blast next.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Stolen Blasting Powder?",a="Stolen Blasting Powder concerns an empty keg stamped with hazardous warnings, found among troggs near Gol'Bolar Quarry. It alerts Quarrymaster Thesten to the theft of volatile mining supplies.",al={"what is stolen blasting powder","powder keg quest","empty powder keg lore"}},{q="Who should receive the empty powder keg?",a="Bring the empty powder keg directly to Quarrymaster Thesten, who oversees operations at Gol'Bolar Quarry in Dun Morogh.",al={"where to bring the keg","who is thesten","quarrymaster location"}},{q="Why is the stolen blasting powder dangerous?",a="The keg bears quarrymaster authorization warnings and held hazardous blasting powder. Troggs with heavy explosives threaten the quarry excavation and nearby settlements.",al={"why is powder dangerous","troggs with explosives","why do troggs have powder"}},{q="What is Gol'Bolar Quarry?",a="Gol'Bolar Quarry is a dwarven excavation site in Dun Morogh that quarries stone and minerals for Ironforge.",al={"where is gol bolar","quarry location","golbolar dun morogh"}},{q="Why does Quarrymaster Thesten turn pale?",a="Quarrymaster Thesten turns pale at the sight of the empty keg and asks where it was found. He knows its dangerous contents have already fallen into hostile trogg hands.",al={"why thesten pale","thesten reaction","what does thesten say"}},{q="What are troggs doing near Gol'Bolar Quarry?",a="Troggs have infested the lower reaches and outskirts of Gol'Bolar Quarry. They disrupt dwarven miners and scavenge equipment and explosive powder from the dig site.",al={"are troggs in the quarry","trogg infestation dun morogh","why are troggs taking powder"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Gol'Bolar Quarry provides stone and resources vital to Ironforge. For a dwarf, the security of its mining explosives is an urgent concern.",["profession:Engineering"]="Blasting powder is volatile and dangerous. As an engineer, you know the havoc troggs could cause with unauthorized explosives.",["profession:Mining"]="Quarry operations depend on controlled demolitions to extract stone. Missing powder kegs signal grave danger inside the excavation pits.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, securing Dun Morogh's supply lines and mining outposts from trogg incursions is essential to operations across Khaz Modan."},kw={"blasting powder","dun morogh","empty powder keg","gol'bolar quarry","powder keg","quarrymaster thesten","stolen blasting powder","thesten","troggs"},rel={"subzone:gol-bolar-quarry","topic:trogg"},m={id=95213},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Blasting Powder"},fv=true}
E["quest:95214"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Blasting Powder",z="general",s="At Gol'Bolar Quarry, Stolen Blasting Powder has gone east with the troggs. Quarrymaster Thesten needs help recovering the missing munitions before the brutes set them off by accident.",h="At Gol'Bolar Quarry, Stolen Blasting Powder has gone east with the troggs.",sec={{t="A Missing Stockpile",b="At Gol'Bolar Quarry in Dun Morogh, dwarves use heavy blasting charges to break stone and open deep veins. But primitive troggs from the nearby crags stole a bulk shipment of high-grade powder. Quarrymaster Thesten needs capable hands before the pack causes an accidental detonation.",sp=0},{t="A Powder Keg in the Crags",b="The missing keg holds enough force to reduce King Magni Bronzebeard's grand throne room to an open-air courtyard. The troggs carried the powder east to their rough foothill camps. Left alone, they may soon discover fire or strike stone against spark.",sp=0},{t="Quiet Resolution",b="After the stolen charges are recovered from the troggs and returned to the quarry depot, Quarrymaster Thesten can breathe easy. He rewards you, then quietly asks that you tell no one about the incident.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Quarrymaster Thesten?",a="Quarrymaster Thesten oversees excavation at Gol'Bolar Quarry in Dun Morogh. After a great stockpile of industrial blasting powder goes missing under his watch, he needs help recovering it.",al={"who is thesten","quarrymaster thesten","who gives this quest"}},{q="Where can the stolen blasting powder be found?",a="The troggs carried the powder to the crags and dens immediately east of Gol'Bolar Quarry. You are sent to recover the volatile kegs and sacks before disaster strikes.",al={"where is stolen blasting powder","trogg location","powder location"}},{q="Why did the troggs steal the blasting powder?",a="The entry gives no reason for the troggs' theft. They scavenged the powder kegs from quarry workers, and Quarrymaster Thesten fears they may ignite the explosives through clumsy experimentation.",al={"why troggs steal powder","what do troggs want with powder"}},{q="How dangerous is the stolen blasting powder?",a="Quarrymaster Thesten says the missing keg could blast King Magni's throne room into an open-air courtyard. If it detonates in the enclosed quarry or caverns, the force would be devastating.",al={"how powerful is powder","magni throne room powder","is the powder dangerous"}},{q="Why does Quarrymaster Thesten want the incident kept quiet?",a="When you return the powder, Quarrymaster Thesten pays you and asks you to keep the incident quiet. He gives no reason, but losing so much explosive to the troggs is something he would rather conceal.",al={"why keep it secret","thesten secret","dont mention incident"}},{q="What is Gol'Bolar Quarry?",a="Gol'Bolar Quarry is a dwarven excavation site in eastern Dun Morogh. It quarries stone for construction and engineering across the realm, while troggs emerge from the rock into its deep pits.",al={"what is gol bolar","gol bolar quarry","where is golbolar"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Gol'Bolar Quarry supports Ironforge's stonecraft and excavation. Letting troggs weaponize mining explosives so near King Magni's doorstep is a humiliating failure for a dwarven supervisor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dun Morogh's supply lines and stone works matter to the Alliance's mountain stronghold. Guarding dangerous munitions helps keep the nearby High Seat in Ironforge safe.",["profession:Mining"]="Blasting powder clears rock and opens veins in deep digs, but it takes discipline to handle. Losing bulk kegs to wild cave-dwellers is every quarrymaster's nightmare."},kw={"blasting powder","dun morogh","explosives","gol'bolar quarry","ironforge","king magni","quarrymaster thesten","thesten","troggs"},rel={"subzone:gol-bolar-quarry","topic:trogg","quest:95213"},m={id=95214},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Blasting Powder"},fv=true}
E["quest:95216"] = {t="quest",n="The New Plague",z="general",s="In the Undercity, Theodore Griffs studies reports of a lethal creature in the ruins above. Its venom consumes even undead flesh, and he seeks to learn how its toxins work.",h="In the Undercity, Theodore Griffs studies reports of a lethal creature in the ruins above.",sec={{t="The Apothecary's Ambition",b="The Royal Apothecary Society gathers dangerous substances from across Azeroth. Theodore Griffs is one of its researchers. He tracks strange beasts and deadly contaminants to advance Forsaken alchemy. Now rumors tell of a venomous creature in the shattered stone above, so Griffs sends you to bring back a sample before the chance is lost.",sp=0},{t="A Flesh-Dissolving Toxin",b="Witherfang is the venomous arthropod stalking the surface ruins of Lordaeron. Its venom breaks down living tissue and dead, preserved flesh alike. Griffs wants to learn how it overcomes the resistance of dead flesh, knowledge that could help refine biological weapons and protect the Forsaken kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Reverse Engineering the Ichor",b="Theodore Griffs is frustrated that Witherfang was killed instead of captured alive. Still, the gathered ichor gives him enough to study. By breaking down the creature’s bodily fluids, he hopes to learn how its venom works and add to the Undercity’s growing chemical knowledge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Theodore Griffs?",a="Theodore Griffs is a researcher with the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity’s Apothecarium. He studies potent toxins and strange specimens to make compounds for the Forsaken, and has little patience for those who fail to value careful alchemical work.",al={"who gives the new plague","theodore griffs","who is theodore griffs"}},{q="What is Witherfang?",a="Witherfang is a venomous arthropod found in the Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity. Its toxin can dissolve even resilient undead flesh.",al={"what is witherfang","where is witherfang","ruins of lordaeron arthropod"}},{q="Why does Theodore Griffs want Witherfang's venom?",a="Theodore Griffs wants to learn how Witherfang’s venom eats through undead flesh. He hopes to recreate its effects for the Forsaken’s alchemical arsenal.",al={"what does theodore want with witherfang","why collect the highly toxic strain"}},{q="Why is Theodore Griffs upset when you return?",a="Theodore Griffs hoped you would keep Witherfang intact or gather its venom carefully. He is annoyed that it was slain, but recovered enough ichor from its remains to study.",al={"why was theodore angry","did i ruin the sample"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Apothecarium?",a="The Apothecarium is the Royal Apothecary Society’s research center beneath Lordaeron. There, its members test dangerous strains, make alchemical weapons, and experiment on strange creatures. It is the Undercity’s most vital quarter.",al={"apothecarium purpose","why is the apothecarium important"}},{q="How does Theodore believe virulent strains are best transmitted?",a="Theodore Griffs believes the surest way to spread a potent strain is to put it directly into the bloodstream.",al={"how is the venom transmitted","transmission method"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks toxins that can harm the living and the dead. It pursues Forsaken supremacy and protection for its young nation.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde accepts the Forsaken as allies in the Eastern Kingdoms, yet the Apothecarium’s grim experiments often trouble its more honorable members."},kw={"apothecarium","ichor","ruins of lordaeron","the new plague","theodore griffs","toxic strain","undercity","witherfang"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},m={id=95216},src={"In-game quest text: The New Plague"},fv=true}
E["quest:95217"] = {t="quest",n="The Quarry's Smith",z="general",s="At the quarry, The Quarry's Smith, Frast Dokner, needs metal and leather for camp repairs. With a supply shipment late, he asks travelers to bring the materials. In return, Dokner offers practical smithing techniques.",h="At the quarry, The Quarry's Smith, Frast Dokner, needs metal and leather for camp repairs.",sec={{t="Shortages at the Quarry",b="An excavation needs steady care. Pickaxes must be sharpened, worn brackets replaced, and camp gear reinforced. When a vital shipment misses its schedule, work begins to grind to a halt. Without fresh stock from the major trade routes, the craftsmen must improvise and look to passing travelers for help.\n\nFrast Dokner works the forge through these delays. He asks anyone willing to gather basic metals and hides to help keep the camp running, rather than wait for transport wagons that may be far behind.",sp=0},{t="An Apprentice's Bargain",b="Dwarven blacksmithing guilds prize discipline and guard their methods, rarely sharing trade secrets with casual wanderers. Dokner weighs that custom against the camp's immediate needs. He lacks workable copper and durable leather for patching tools and camp gear.\n\nBring the raw materials to his anvil, and he will teach you his personal smithing techniques. The bargain trades useful craft knowledge for materials the camp needs to endure and keep its gear in repair.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Frast Dokner?",a="Frast Dokner is an experienced blacksmith at a quarry encampment. He maintains tools, structural fittings, and equipment for the workers there. When delays cut off his regular supply line, he asks passing travelers to gather the raw materials he needs.",al={"frast dokner lore","who is the quarry smith","quarry blacksmith"}},{q="Why does the quarry need copper bars and boar hides?",a="Quarry work and camp upkeep use great amounts of sturdy materials. Copper is an accessible, workable metal for replacement fittings, nails, fasteners, and bands that reinforce broken tools. Boar hides provide tough leather for bellows, tool wraps, straps, and protective aprons against sparks and the grinding work.",al={"why copper bars and boar hides","materials needed quarry smith","quarry repair materials"}},{q="Why is the supply shipment late?",a="Frast Dokner does not explain why the shipment is late. Overland routes across snowy crags and mountain passes often face blizzards, roaming wildlife, and hostile trogg or bandit ambushes. Remote mining camps and quarries feel the strain first when transport wagons fall behind.",al={"late supply shipment","what happened to the supplies","why are supplies delayed"}},{q="What does Frast Dokner offer in exchange for the materials?",a="Frast Dokner offers more than coin: he promises to share his personal blacksmithing techniques with whoever gathers the needed supplies. An aspiring artisan can learn practical metalworking and equipment care from a seasoned field craftsman, lessons city guildhalls rarely teach novices.",al={"quarry smith reward lore","what does frast teach","blacksmithing techniques frast"}},{q="Where is this quarry located?",a="Frast Dokner works at Gol'Bolar Quarry in Dun Morogh, south of Kharanos. The dwarven excavation lies in snowy foothills and faces harsh winter weather and aggressive subterranean troggs, who harass miners and disrupt trade convoys from Ironforge.",al={"which quarry is this","where is frast dokner","quarry smith location"}},{q="Is Frast Dokner affiliated with Ironforge?",a="Frast Dokner and the quarry camp are under the Bronzebeard clan and the Kingdom of Ironforge. Quarrying stone and mining ore in Dun Morogh support the kingdom's construction projects and defenses. Blacksmiths such as Dokner help sustain Ironforge's industry.",al={"frast dokner ironforge","is the quarry part of ironforge","quarry dwarf allegiance"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can learn from Frast Dokner, a field mentor for apprentice smiths. He trades his hard-won forging techniques to anyone who supplies the raw metal and leather that keep his anvil hot.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner working the surrounding deposits, you have a buyer close at hand for your smelted copper bars. They go toward practical training and camp repairs.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Bronzebeard industry at Gol'Bolar Quarry, where dwarven resolve keeps the forges burning when supply caravans run late.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help keep the remote dwarven quarry running and its equipment ready in the snowy high country."},kw={"blacksmithing","copper bars","dun morogh","dwarf","frast dokner","gol'bolar quarry","ironforge","the quarry's smith","toughened boar hides"},m={id=95217},src={"In-game quest text: The Quarry's Smith"},fv=true}
E["quest:95250"] = {t="quest",n="Abominable Creatures",z="general",s="At Lordaeron's fallen capital, Captain Truman waits anxiously for reinforcements and news of his missing commander. He believes the revered Grand Marshal still fights in the nearby ruins, and asks a capable traveler to find him. The search reveals the defenders' grim fate and deep hostility among the loyalists.",h="At Lordaeron's fallen capital, Captain Truman waits anxiously for reinforcements and news of his missing...",sec={{t="A Desperate Vigil",b="Captain Truman keeps watch outside Lordaeron, anxious for long-overdue reinforcements. He calls his superior a renowned Grand Marshal, tall and statuesque, and believes him a formidable fighter. Ordered to hold the line while his commander charged into battle, Truman remains bound by duty.\n\nHe distrusts outsiders and scorns those he calls lesser breeds, refusing to rely on local irregulars. When a capable traveler arrives, he asks you to enter the ruins, check on his master's well-being, and learn how the battle fares.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Lordaeron",b="The search takes you into the Ruins of Lordaeron, the shattered capital that fell to the Scourge during the Third War. Captain Truman expects his glorious leader to stand triumphant over the fallen, but the blighted city tells a grimmer story.\n\nHorrors, undead remnants, and abominations roam its broken stone plazas. The ruined streets show what became of the defenders who entered the city. No immaculate knight holds the line; the commander has met a tragic, twisted end among the monstrosities in the courtyards.",sp=0},{t="A Horrifying Revelation",b="The missing commander, whom Captain Truman calls the Baron, has become a grotesque undead monstrosity. You slay the creature and carry the Head of the Baron back to Captain Truman. The severed head of his former lord leaves Truman shocked and horrified, overcome with revulsion.\n\nUnable to accept his commander's fate, he turns on you in bitter outrage and accuses you of siding with monsters. He declares that the true sons of Lordaeron will reclaim their land and purge all beasts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Abominable Creatures?",a="Captain Truman, a human loyalist, makes the request from his post outside the fallen kingdom. He waits anxiously for reinforcements and news of his commander, a revered Grand Marshal who charged into the nearby Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"who gives abominable creatures","abominable creatures quest giver","where to start abominable creatures"}},{q="Where does the quest Abominable Creatures take place?",a="The search takes you into the Ruins of Lordaeron, the shattered capital overrun by Scourge horrors and undead remnants. Captain Truman keeps watch outside the blighted city and asks travelers to find his missing superior there.",al={"abominable creatures location","where is abominable creatures completed","abominable creatures zone"}},{q="Who is Captain Truman's master?",a="Captain Truman calls his master the Grand Marshal and praises him as a tall, statuesque military hero. The missing man is also called the Baron, a high-ranking aristocrat and military commander leading the realm's defense.",al={"who is truman's commander","grand marshal identity truman","who is the baron"}},{q="What happened to the Grand Marshal in the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="The Grand Marshal was slain and transformed into a monstrous undead creature in the Ruins of Lordaeron. You find an abomination called the Baron, slay him, and take his severed head.",al={"what happened to the baron","grand marshal fate","is the grand marshal dead"}},{q="Why does Captain Truman get angry when you turn in the quest?",a="Captain Truman expects his statuesque commander to be alive and victorious. The grotesque, mutated head of the Baron fills him with horror and revulsion. He furiously accuses you of playing a sick joke and consorting with vile beasts.",al={"why is truman mad","truman reaction abominable creatures","why does truman yell at you"}},{q="What does Captain Truman mean by the 'true sons of Lordaeron'?",a="By “true sons of Lordaeron,” Captain Truman means the rightful human survivors who seek to reclaim their shattered homeland and purge it of all beasts. The phrase reveals his belief that the land belongs to those human survivors.",al={"true sons of lordaeron meaning","who are the true sons of lordaeron","truman true sons"}},{q="Why does Captain Truman refuse to trust 'half breeds'?",a="Captain Truman distrusts non-human races and irregular allies, calling them untrustworthy half-breeds and filth. His disdain keeps him from confiding in anyone he does not consider a worthy representative of the realm.",al={"truman half breeds","why is captain truman racist","truman xenophobia"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Lordaeron's fallen leadership meet a grim fate: even an esteemed Grand Marshal has become a grotesque undead horror. Captain Truman's grief and nationalistic zeal reflect the trauma of human survivors desperate to reclaim their ancestral home.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see how perilous and isolated the loyalist remnants are in northern Lordaeron's blighted ruins. Their detachments struggle with dwindling hope and the toll of facing overwhelming monstrosities.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see the Baron's grotesque transformation as a reminder of how the Scourge mutilated Lordaeron's finest defenders into monstrous abominations. Captain Truman's words reveal the hostility living loyalists hold toward the Undercity's people."},kw={"abominable creatures","captain truman","grand marshal","head of the baron","lordaeron","ruins of lordaeron","the baron","true sons of lordaeron"},rel={"zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},m={id=95250},src={"In-game quest text: Abominable Creatures"},fv=true}
E["quest:95328"] = {t="quest",n="Whispering Horror Residue",z="general",s="Beneath the Whispering Forest, Whispering Horror Residue is carried to Undercity for study. Father Lankester awaits it in the War Quarter.",h="Beneath the Whispering Forest, Whispering Horror Residue is carried to Undercity for study.",sec={{t="An Unsettling Harvest",b="Beneath the Whispering Forest, you recover a strange beast’s twitching remains. The unsettling material is carried to Undercity, where researchers may study it.",sp=0},{t="Studies in Shadow",b="In Undercity’s War Quarter, Father Lankester receives the remains. He says the Whispering Forest has long been touched by the void. Its physical traces may help him study the mysteries of shadow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Whispering Horror Residue?",a="The residue is the squirming remains of a strange beast defeated beneath the Whispering Forest. Shadow scholars value it for arcane and occult study.",al={"what is the residue","what is whispering horror residue","residue item"}},{q="Who wants the Whispering Horror Residue?",a="Father Lankester, a Forsaken figure in Undercity’s War Quarter, wants the residue. He welcomes the chance to study shadow and void-touched phenomena.",al={"who takes the residue","who is father lankester","where to turn in residue"}},{q="Where did this specimen come from?",a="The specimen came from beneath the Whispering Forest, west of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. Father Lankester says the area is touched by the void.",al={"where does horror come from","whispering forest lore","under whispering forest"}},{q="Why does Father Lankester want the residue?",a="Father Lankester wants to study shadow and the void. Physical remains from void-touched creatures give practitioners of forbidden arts material for study.",al={"why lankester want this","undercity shadow research","why study residue"}},{q="Where can Father Lankester be found?",a="Father Lankester can be found in Undercity’s War Quarter, beneath the ruins of Lordaeron’s capital. Forsaken warriors, scholars, and military planners gather there.",al={"where is war quarter","where is lankester located","undercity lankester location"}},{q="Is the Whispering Forest touched by the void?",a="Father Lankester says the Whispering Forest has long been touched by the void. The woods and the spaces beneath them are known for that corruption.",al={"is whispering forest cursed","void corruption whispering forest","what touches whispering forest"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest among the Forsaken, you may share Father Lankester’s scholarly and religious interest in void specimens. Strange remains can be objects of study rather than mere abominations.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you know Undercity’s people study forbidden magic and unnatural corruption across Lordaeron. They seek ways to use dark forces to strengthen their hold on the kingdom.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you recover unsettling specimens from hidden places in Tirisfal Glades for study beneath the ruins of the capital."},kw={"father lankester","shadow","tirisfal","undercity","void","war quarter","whispering forest","whispering horror residue"},rel={"subzone:whispering-forest","subzone:war-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={id=95328},src={"In-game quest text: Whispering Horror Residue"},fv=true}
E["quest:95349"] = {t="quest",n="The Earthen Ring",z="general",s="From Zephras, the Windshapers of The Earthen Ring reach Azeroth as an advance vanguard. After cult activity delays the rest in Valanaar, they board a skycutter outside the lodge and make landfall in Mulgore to meet Alaana Stormwalker and adjust to a vast, dangerous world.",h="From Zephras, the Windshapers of The Earthen Ring reach Azeroth as an advance vanguard.",sec={{t="Departure from Valanaar",b="Cult activity in Valanaar has disrupted the Windshapers’ plans to travel to Azeroth. Their senior leaders stay behind at the lodge to finish urgent business and quell the threat, while a small vanguard sets out ahead. At the docks just outside the lodge, the pioneers board a skycutter bound across the skies.\n\nTheir commanders promise to join them soon. Until then, the advance group must establish a presence before the rest can follow.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Mulgore",b="In Mulgore, Alaana Stormwalker welcomes the arriving adventurers from Zephras. Establishing a foothold in Azeroth will take time, so newcomers are encouraged to scout the surrounding territory and grow accustomed to it.\n\nThe winds favor the expedition, but Azeroth is unfamiliar and perilous. Travelers should learn the local terrain, wildlife, and neighboring inhabitants before those still in Valanaar arrive to join them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Windshapers traveling to Azeroth?",a="The Windshapers send a vanguard ahead to establish a presence on Azeroth while their leaders remain in Valanaar. Cult activity there disrupted the original plans and delayed the rest of the group, so the advance party travels alone until reinforcements can follow.",al={"why go to azeroth","windshaper mission","why are windshapers in mulgore"}},{q="Who is Alaana Stormwalker?",a="Alaana Stormwalker welcomes Windshapers arriving from Zephras in Mulgore. She says establishing a secure presence in these new lands will take time and advises newcomers to explore the surrounding region and prepare for Azeroth’s dangers.",al={"who is alaana","alaana stormwalker role","where is alaana stormwalker"}},{q="Why was the main departure delayed?",a="Cult activity in Valanaar delayed the main departure. Expedition leaders stay behind at the lodge to settle the trouble, while a small vanguard boards a skycutter and travels ahead to Azeroth.",al={"why the delay","what cult delayed travel","why stay in valanaar"}},{q="How do travelers journey from Valanaar to Mulgore?",a="Travelers board a skycutter at the docks just outside the lodge in Valanaar. It carries the vanguard across the sky to Mulgore, connecting Zephras with Azeroth during the initial expedition.",al={"how to reach mulgore","where is the ship","how do you travel to azeroth"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is the home of the adventurers arriving aboard the skycutter. In Mulgore, Alaana Stormwalker welcomes newcomers from Zephras and says favorable winds guided their crossing into unfamiliar, dangerous Azeroth.",al={"where is zephras","what is zephras","zephras lore"}},{q="What should adventurers do upon arriving in Mulgore?",a="New arrivals are encouraged to scout the surrounding lands of Mulgore. Learning the nearby terrain, creatures, and local threats will help them as they establish a presence in this unfamiliar, hazardous world.",al={"what to do in mulgore","next steps after arriving","what to do next"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne adventurer leaving Valanaar, you make the historic journey to Azeroth as part of its advance vanguard. You leave the cult troubles behind and set foot on Mulgore’s plains.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren native to Mulgore, you witness travelers from Zephras descending upon your ancestral plains. Welcoming these visitors offers an early connection to allies seeking a foothold in your lands.",["class:Shaman"]="As a Shaman, you share the Windshapers’ reverence for the elements and their reliance on the winds to guide their crossing. Arriving under The Earthen Ring connects you to elemental traditions taking root in Mulgore."},kw={"alaana stormwalker","banu-alah","cult","mulgore","skycutter","the earthen ring","valanaar","windshapers","zephras"},rel={"zone:mulgore"},m={id=95349},src={"In-game quest text: The Earthen Ring"},fv=true}
E["quest:95350"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome to Azeroth",z="general",s="In Kalimdor, the Windshapers reach beyond their isolated home to seek allies. Guided by their ties to the Earthen Ring, an emissary travels from Thunder Bluff to meet Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar.",h="In Kalimdor, the Windshapers reach beyond their isolated home to seek allies.",sec={{t="Allies in a Broader World",b="The Windshapers look beyond their isolated origins to the peoples of Kalimdor. They know isolation cannot shield them from Azeroth’s threats, so they seek companions to face the wilderness together. Their search reaches the neighboring tauren city of Thunder Bluff and the orcish bastions to the east.",sp=0},{t="An Audience with the Warchief",b="The envoys travel first to the soaring towers of Thunder Bluff, then across the barrens to Orgrimmar, the Horde’s capital. Warchief Thrall waits in the tranquil Valley of Wisdom. An audience with him draws the Windshapers into Kalimdor’s political and spiritual life, joining them to the Horde through shared purpose and respect for the elements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest Welcome to Azeroth?",a="An emissary travels for the Windshapers to meet Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. The meeting introduces them to the wider Horde and Kalimdor’s surface world.",al={"what is this quest","welcome to azeroth quest","purpose of welcome to azeroth"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers reach out from above to surface allies, seeking survival through fellowship with the Earthen Ring and the Horde. They send travelers to speak directly with Horde leadership in Durotar.",al={"who are windshapers","what are windshapers"}},{q="Why are you sent to speak with Thrall?",a="Thrall is the Horde’s Warchief and a revered shamanic leader who oversees the coalition’s major alliances from the Valley of Wisdom. Meeting him formalizes relations between the Windshapers and the Horde.",al={"why visit thrall","speak with thrall orgrimmar","why go to orgrimmar"}},{q="How do you travel from Thunder Bluff to Orgrimmar?",a="Travelers take flight from Thunder Bluff’s central roost with the flight master, crossing Kalimdor’s plains eastward to Orgrimmar’s canyon fortress.",al={"how to reach orgrimmar","thunder bluff flight master","getting to orgrimmar from thunder bluff"}},{q="How does the Earthen Ring fit into this mission?",a="The Earthen Ring is aligned with the Horde’s coalition of like-minded peoples. It helps join shamanic factions with the nations of Kalimdor.",al={"earthen ring horde role","is earthen ring horde"}},{q="Where is Thrall located in Orgrimmar?",a="Warchief Thrall resides in the Valley of Wisdom, a quiet spiritual sanctuary in western Orgrimmar where shamans and tribal advisors gather.",al={"where is thrall","valley of wisdom thrall location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This diplomatic journey formalizes ties with the Horde, bringing newcomers before Warchief Thrall as allies in Kalimdor’s struggle for survival.",["race:Skyborne"]="Leaving the high heights for the surface world below, you reach out from among the Skyborne Windshapers to Thunder Bluff and Orgrimmar, seeking a place among new allies.",["class:Shaman"]="With guidance from the Earthen Ring and the blessing of the winds, you link spiritual kin with shamanic leadership in the Valley of Wisdom."},kw={"earthen ring","horde","orgrimmar","thrall","thunder bluff","valley of wisdom","welcome to azeroth","windshapers"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","zone:thunderbluff","topic:horde","quest:92595"},m={id=95350},src={"In-game quest text: Welcome to Azeroth"},fv=true}
E["quest:95494"] = {t="quest",n="Bruised Pride and Lion Hides",z="general",s="An injury leaves a hunter or tradesperson unable to gather lion hides for a local tanner. They turn to you to keep their trade agreement and their professional record intact.",h="An injury leaves a hunter or tradesperson unable to gather lion hides for a local tanner.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Dilemma",b="A hunter or tradesperson has been hurt and cannot safely track wild beasts. Their agreement with a neighborhood craftsman is still due, so they hire you to hunt wild lions and gather their pelts.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Arrangement",b="The raw hides go to a local tanner, who exchanges them for finished leather goods the giver needs for their livelihood. The giver’s pride is stung by needing help, but honoring the bargain keeps their professional reputation unbroken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this quest about?",a="A wounded huntsman or trader needs lion hides to supply a local tanner. In exchange, the giver receives finished leather goods essential to their livelihood.",al={"what is bruised pride and lion hides","quest goal","what are the lion hides for"}},{q="Why does the quest giver need help gathering hides?",a="An injury keeps the giver from hunting lions themselves. They rely on you to uphold a long-standing agreement with a local tanner.",al={"why need help","why can't they hunt"}},{q="Who receives the lion hides?",a="A local tanner receives the raw hides and processes them into finished leather goods the giver needs for regular trade and work.",al={"who gets the lion hides","where do hides go"}},{q="What does the name 'Bruised Pride and Lion Hides' mean?",a="The name refers to both a pride of lions to hunt and the injured hunter’s pride. The hunter has never failed to deliver on a contract, but their injury now limits them.",al={"bruised pride meaning","why is it called bruised pride"}},{q="Was the arrangement with the tanner at risk?",a="Yes. The injury puts the giver’s next delivery at risk. Gathering the lion hides lets them keep their bargain without coming up short.",al={"does tanner arrangement hold","trade deal broken"}},{q="How was the quest giver injured?",a="The giver suffered an injury that prevents them from hunting lions in the wild. Its exact cause is not given, and delivering the hides lets them preserve their reputation.",al={"quest giver injury","what happened to hunter"}}},kw={"bruised pride and lion hides","hunting","leather goods","lion hides","tanner","trade"},m={id=95494},src={"In-game quest text: Bruised Pride and Lion Hides"},fv=true}
E["quest:95495"] = {t="quest",n="The Hermit Tanner",z="general",s="You carry raw hides across the Barrens to The Hermit Tanner, who lives above the Dry Hills. Vrang cannot make the climb, so he sends you to his secluded trading partner.",h="You carry raw hides across the Barrens to The Hermit Tanner, who lives above the Dry Hills.",sec={{t="A Ridge in the Barrens",b="Across the Barrens, Vrang trades with a tanner who lives on a ridge above the Dry Hills. The steep, rocky climb is too hard for Vrang, so he asks passing travelers to carry raw hides to his partner's homestead.",sp=0},{t="An Unconventional Craftsman",b="Vrang warns you that the solitary tanner's unusual appearance may startle you, but says he is no danger to visitors. When you bring the hides to the ridge, the hermit welcomes you warmly. He regrets that Vrang could not come himself, for there is something he hoped to discuss with the trader.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this delivery?",a="Vrang sends you with a bundle of raw hides for his trading partner on the ridge above the Dry Hills.",al={"who gives hermit tanner","where start quest","vrang delivery"}},{q="Where does the hermit tanner live?",a="The hermit tanner lives alone on a secluded homestead atop a ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.",al={"hermit tanner location","where is hermit tanner","ridge hermit"}},{q="Why does Vrang warn you about the tanner's appearance?",a="Vrang warns you that the tanner's unusual appearance may startle you, but assures you that he poses no danger to visitors.",al={"hermit looks","why hermit scary","hermit appearance"}},{q="Why couldn't Vrang make the climb himself?",a="The steep, rocky climb is too taxing for Vrang to manage, so he asks a passing traveler to carry the hides.",al={"why need delivery","why vrang cant go"}},{q="What items are being delivered to the ridge?",a="You carry a bundle of raw hides for the hermit's tanning trade, which he and Vrang share.",al={"what is bundle of hides","quest items delivered"}},{q="What does the hermit tanner wish to discuss with Vrang?",a="The hermit regrets that Vrang could not come in person and says he has something to discuss with him.",al={"what does tanner want with vrang","tanner business with vrang"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Across the Barrens, you can help traders like Vrang carry goods over the rugged savanna."},kw={"barrens","bundle of hides","dry hills","hermit tanner","ridge","tanner","vrang"},rel={"subzone:dry-hills","zone:barrens"},m={id=95495},src={"In-game quest text: The Hermit Tanner"},fv=true}
E["quest:95507"] = {t="quest",n="Vrang's Game",z="general",s="Vrang sends you across a valley in the Barrens to check his traps. The small game they catch can help him, though other wildlife makes the area dangerous.",h="Vrang sends you across a valley in the Barrens to check his traps.",sec={{t="Vrang's Traps",b="Vrang has traps scattered across the valley, and he wants you to bring back any small game they have caught. Keep your attention on the wildlife too, for it can make the area dangerous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Vrang want?",a="Vrang wants you to check his traps and bring back any small game they have caught.",al={"vrang traps","vrang game","what does vrang need"}},{q="Where are Vrang's traps?",a="Vrang's traps are scattered across a valley in the Barrens.",al={"where traps","trap location","barrens traps"}},{q="What is dangerous around the traps?",a="Other wildlife around the traps can be dangerous if you are not paying attention.",al={"danger nearby","other animals","wildlife danger"}}},kw={"barrens","small game","trapped game","traps","valley","vrang","wildlife"},m={id=95507},src={"In-game quest text: Vrang's Game"},fv=true}
E["quest:95508"] = {t="quest",n="Unwelcome Guests",z="general",s="You helped someone survive an encounter with unwelcome guests, and they are grateful. What brought you together remains unclear.",h="You helped someone survive an encounter with unwelcome guests, and they are grateful.",sec={},faq={{q="What happened here?",a="You helped the speaker survive an encounter, though they give no details about it.",al={"what happened","unwelcome guests","guest trouble"}},{q="Who is thanking me?",a="The speaker who thanks you is not named.",al={"who is this","who thanked me","quest giver"}},{q="Why are they in my debt?",a="The speaker says you helped them survive, but does not explain what happened.",al={"why thank me","why do they owe me","helped them"}}},kw={"debt","help","survive","thanks","unwelcome guests"},m={id=95508},src={"In-game quest text: Unwelcome Guests"},fv=true}
E["quest:95534"] = {t="quest",n="Strahnbrad Mystery",z="general",s="A singed note asks you to investigate strange activity around the old bellows in Strahnbrad. Report what you learn in Hillsbrad.",h="A singed note asks you to investigate strange activity around the old bellows in Strahnbrad.",sec={{t="The Singed Note",b="A note found in Strahnbrad warns that the old bellows seem to move when no one watches. Its writer dismisses the tale as a ghost story, yet insists you uncover the truth before their return. They believe great power lies in Strahnbrad, and fire magic has burned away the rest of the message.",sp=0},{t="Your Findings",b="In Hillsbrad, the townsfolk hear your report about the old bellows in Strahnbrad. A fire elemental lived within them, though how it came to be there remains a mystery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is strange about the old bellows?",a="A singed note claims the old bellows in Strahnbrad spring to life when no one is watching.",al={"old bellows mystery","bellows moving","strahnbrad bellows"}},{q="Who left the note?",a="The note does not name its writer; it says they will return.",al={"who wrote the note","singed note author","mystery note"}},{q="What does the note say about Strahnbrad?",a="The writer believes great power lies in Strahnbrad.",al={"strahnbrad power","great power there","what's in strahnbrad"}},{q="Where do I report what I find?",a="You are asked to report your findings in town in Hillsbrad.",al={"where report findings","hillsbrad report","report in town"}}},kw={"fire elemental","fire magic","hillsbrad","old bellows","singed note","strahnbrad","strahnbrad mystery"},rel={"subzone:strahnbrad"},m={id=95534},src={"In-game quest text: Strahnbrad Mystery"},fv=true}
E["quest:95621"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble in the Valley",z="general",s="A squad of Kul Tiran soldiers is searching the valley, and their purpose is unknown. They have camped near a wrecked caravan to the south, drawing the attention of local scouts.",h="A squad of Kul Tiran soldiers is searching the valley, and their purpose is unknown.",sec={{t="Suspicious Activity in the Valley",b="A rifleman watching the lowlands spotted human soldiers searching the valley floor. Through his scope, he recognized the heraldry and livery of Kul Tiras. Armed foreigners rarely work so openly here, and their presence has raised alarm.",sp=0},{t="The Wrecked Caravan",b="The soldiers have camped near a ruined caravan to the south. What they seek among the wreckage remains unknown. Local observers consider their armed presence an immediate concern, so investigators are sent to eliminate them and uncover the purpose of their search.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Kul Tiran soldiers doing in the valley?",a="A sharpshooter spotted Kul Tiran soldiers searching the valley below. They camped near a wrecked caravan to the south, and local scouts are sent to investigate their purpose.",al={"why kul tirans here","kul tiras soldiers in valley","what are kul tirans doing"}},{q="Where is the Kul Tiran camp located?",a="The Kul Tiran soldiers camp near a ruined caravan south of the vantage point overlooking the valley.",al={"wrecked caravan location","where is kul tiras camp","caravan site"}},{q="How was the Kul Tiran presence discovered?",a="A scout watching the valley inspected the human group through a rifle scope and recognized Kul Tiras by its uniforms and insignia.",al={"how were they identified","kul tiras livery"}},{q="What is the objective of investigating the camp?",a="You are sent south to the wrecked caravan to confront the Kul Tiran soldiers and discover what brought them to search the area.",al={"what is the goal","trouble in the valley objectives"}},{q="Why are the Kul Tiran soldiers treated as enemies?",a="The soldiers are armed foreigners searching the land around a destroyed caravan without explanation. Scouts see them as a threat to be subdued so their intentions can be uncovered.",al={"why fight kul tiras","are kul tirans hostile"}},{q="Who detected the soldiers in the valley?",a="Walton, the hermit tanner watching the valley, spotted the soldiers through his rifle scope. He hired an adventurer to eliminate them and learn why they were there.",al={"who spotted soldiers","who gave quest"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you may recognize the sea green and anchor colors of Kul Tiras. Soldiers from this reclusive seafaring nation are a rare and unexpected sight in the valley."},kw={"caravan","kul tiras","soldiers","trouble in the valley","valley","wrecked caravan"},rel={"topic:kul-tiras","topic:human"},m={id=95621},src={"In-game quest text: Trouble in the Valley"},fv=true}
E["quest:95646"] = {t="quest",n="Horrors in the Highland",z="general",s="Rethiel the Greenwarden senses corruption flowing through a mountain gully into the Wetlands' freshwater. He sends you to the highland excavation sites for a Highland Horror's root core, then warns that digging stirs an ancient energy and endangers the whole region.",h="Rethiel the Greenwarden senses corruption flowing through a mountain gully into the Wetlands' freshwater.",sec={{t="Taint in the Gully",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden senses the land changing deep in the Wetlands. Through a mountain gully, foul taint reaches the highlands and infects their freshwater creatures. Lowland life has been shaped by brackish water, but these creatures have never known the sea's protective salt. Rethiel fears they cannot withstand the spreading evil. He asks you to climb to the excavation sites, slay a Highland Horror, and bring back its root core.",sp=0},{t="An Ancient Stirring",b="When you bring Rethiel the Highland Horror's root core, he confirms his fears: an ancient energy has begun to stir. The highland creatures suffer from no ordinary sickness. Recent digging has brought on the affliction. Rethiel warns the excavators to stop at once. Their curiosity could unleash something far worse upon the Wetlands and put everyone in the region at risk.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Horrors in the Highland?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden, an ancient protector of the Wetlands, offers the work after sensing corruption seeping through a nearby mountain gully.",al={"who gives horrors in the highland","horrors in the highland questgiver","rethiel quest"}},{q="Where can Highland Horrors be found?",a="Highland Horrors dwell at the excavation sites on higher ground above the lowlands, near the mountain gully where corruption seeps.",al={"where are highland horrors","highland horror location","where to find highland horror"}},{q="Why are the highland creatures so susceptible to corruption?",a="Highland freshwater creatures have never known the sea's protective salt, leaving them defenseless against the spreading corruption.",al={"why are the creatures tainted","why highland creatures corrupted","unsalted water corruption"}},{q="What is the root core of a Highland Horror?",a="A Highland Horror's root core is the heart of the corrupted creature. Rethiel needs it to examine the unnatural power spreading through the waterways and learn the nature of the corruption.",al={"what is the root core","highland horror core","why take the root core"}},{q="What does Rethiel discover when you return the root core?",a="When you return the root core, Rethiel discovers that an ancient energy has begun to stir from deep within the earth, likely disturbed by digging at the excavation sites.",al={"what does rethiel discover","ancient energy wetlands","excavation danger"}},{q="Why does Rethiel want the excavators to stop digging?",a="Rethiel warns the excavators to stop digging at once for their own safety. Their work risks releasing dangerous ancient forces.",al={"stop digging rethiel","what should excavators do","dwarf dig site warning"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can sense the natural balance shifting through roots and waterways. You may recognize how suddenly ancient corruption threatens freshwater life.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know that digging in the highlands has disturbed more than ancient relics. Rethiel urges the excavators to stop before worse evils awaken.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance explorer, you know that prospectors at mountain excavation sites risk disturbing ancient forces buried beneath the earth."},kw={"corruption","excavation sites","highland horror","horrors in the highland","rethiel","rethiel the greenwarden","root core","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:463","zone:wetlands"},m={id=95646},src={"In-game quest text: Horrors in the Highland"},fv=true}
E["quest:95647"] = {t="quest",n="Lost in the Thicket Things",z="general",s="Ardin Grassman is missing near an excavation site after following word of towering grasses. His alchemist wife asks travelers to find him, as dangerous wildlife has attacked the crew.",h="Ardin Grassman is missing near an excavation site after following word of towering grasses.",sec={{t="A Forager's Calling",b="Ardin Grassman's alchemist wife asks you to find her missing husband. He has a keen sense for nature and often braves cliffs and distant wilds to gather herbs and plants for her work. When an excavation crew spoke of towering grasses unlike any they had seen, Ardin's curiosity drew him toward the site.",sp=0},{t="Ambush at the Dig Site",b="Ardin reached the excavation site and found the crew in danger. The surrounding land had agitated the local wildlife, and hostile spiders swarmed the dig team. Ardin and the crew were trapped by the attacking beasts until travelers came to their aid.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ardin Grassman?",a="Ardin Grassman gathers herbs and has a rare instinct for sensing plants. He often searches cliffs and peaks for wild flora to supply his wife's alchemy. Rumors of towering grasses drew him toward an excavation site.",al={"who is ardin","ardin grassman lore","who is ardin grassman"}},{q="Why did Ardin wander off into the wild?",a="Ardin heard an excavation crew describe towering grasses unlike any they had seen. His instinct for unusual plants drew him out to see them, and he did not return home.",al={"why did ardin leave","why is ardin missing","what was ardin looking for"}},{q="Where did Ardin go?",a="Ardin went toward the nearby Excavation Sites after hearing a passing crew's report. Search the dig sites where the crew set up camp.",al={"where is ardin","ardin location","where to find ardin grassman"}},{q="What happened to Ardin at the excavation site?",a="Ardin reached the excavation camp as local wildlife turned aggressive. Giant spiders and other beasts ambushed the crew, trapping Ardin with them until travelers arrived to help.",al={"what happened to ardin","is ardin dead","what attacked ardin"}},{q="Who is looking for Ardin?",a="Ardin's wife, an alchemist, is looking for him. He gathered herbs for her shelves, but did not return after investigating reports of strange grass. So she asked travelers to find him.",al={"who gives lost in the thicket things","who started this quest","ardin wife"}},{q="Why did the wildlife attack the excavation crew?",a="The cause of the wildlife's sudden agitation near the excavation sites is unknown. Aggressive creatures, especially spiders, swarmed and overwhelmed the dig team.",al={"why are spiders attacking","what upset the animals","why are beasts angry"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you may recognize Ardin Grassman's gift for sensing plants and herbs. He often climbs difficult terrain to gather rare plants for alchemy.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may recognize Ardin's gift for sensing plants. The wildlife near the dig sites has grown agitated, disturbing the balance of the wilds."},kw={"alchemy","ardin","ardin grassman","excavation sites","herbalism","lost in the thicket things","spiders","towering grasses"},m={id=95647},src={"In-game quest text: Lost in the Thicket Things"},fv=true}
E["quest:95663"] = {t="quest",n="Dragonmaw Rumors",z="general",s="The Deathstalkers seek clearer word about Dragonmaw magic rumored in the Wetlands. You are sent to meet their agent in the hills above the clan's camp.",h="The Deathstalkers seek clearer word about Dragonmaw magic rumored in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Whispers in the Wetlands",b="A Deathstalker in the Wetlands needs your help as rumors gather around the Dragonmaw clan. They are said to command magic that binds dragons, and whispers claim they prepare a display of that power. Broken symbols offered no firm proof, so you are sent to meet an agent in the hills above their camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Dragonmaw rumored to be doing?",a="The rumor says the Dragonmaw are preparing a display of magic strong enough to make dragons serve.",al={"dragonmaw rumors","what are dragonmaw planning","dragonmaw magic"}},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers need help?",a="The Deathstalkers have only broken symbols and uncertain whispers about the Dragonmaw, so an agent needs assistance in the hills above the clan's camp.",al={"deathstalker needs help","why help deathstalkers","what do they need"}},{q="Where is the Deathstalker agent?",a="The agent is in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp in the Wetlands.",al={"agent location","where meet agent","deathstalker agent hills"}},{q="What did the broken symbols reveal?",a="The broken symbols carried only uncertain whispers about a rumored Dragonmaw display of magic.",al={"broken symbols","what symbols showed","symbols dragonmaw"}},{q="What happens when you meet the agent?",a="The Deathstalker agent will reveal the next steps when you meet her in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp.",al={"meet the agent","next steps","what does agent say"}}},kw={"broken symbols","deathstalker agent","deathstalkers","dragonbinding","dragonmaw","dragonmaw camp","dragonmaw rumors","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1886","quest:92472","zone:wetlands"},m={id=95663},src={"In-game quest text: Dragonmaw Rumors"},fv=true}
E["quest:95664"] = {t="quest",n="Elder Knowledge",z="general",s="A strange Titan Relic scatters light like a living prism, yet its nature remains uncertain. You carry it to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff to seek someone who can explain its ancient power.",h="A strange Titan Relic scatters light like a living prism, yet its nature remains uncertain.",sec={{t="A Shard of Light",b="The unusual composite shard in your keeping scatters light like a living prism. Its nature is uncertain, though its power feels ancient. You take the Titan Relic to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and seek someone who can tell you more.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Titan Relic?",a="It is an unusual composite shard that scatters light like a living prism. Its nature is uncertain, but its power feels ancient.",al={"titan relic","what's the relic","prism shard"}},{q="Where do I take the Titan Relic?",a="Take the Titan Relic to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and look for someone who can explain it.",al={"where relic go","elder rise relic","thunder bluff shard"}},{q="Why am I carrying the shard?",a="You are seeking someone at Elder Rise who can tell you more about the Titan Relic.",al={"why this relic","what do with shard","elder knowledge quest"}}},kw={"ancient power","composite shard","elder knowledge","elder rise","living prism","thunder bluff","titan relic"},rel={"subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:titan"},m={id=95664},src={"In-game quest text: Elder Knowledge"},fv=true}
E["quest:95682"] = {t="quest",n="Open the Maw",z="general",s="A Deathstalker Agent asks you to clear Dragonmaw from the Excavation Sites and bring back anything of note. The clan may be seeking a path back to power.",h="A Deathstalker Agent asks you to clear Dragonmaw from the Excavation Sites and bring back anything of note.",sec={{t="A Quiet Approach",b="A Deathstalker Agent outside the Excavation Site wants the Dragonmaw forces cleared away. The remnants of the dragon-wrangling clan believe they have found something that could restore their former power. Their ragtag presence must be removed so the Deathstalkers can enter unseen. Bring back anything notable you recover, and keep the matter between the agent and royal command.",sp=0},{t="The Recovered Scrawl",b="The Deathstalker Agent recognizes the orcish writing among the recovered items. It shows the Dragonmaw hope to appease Rend, their false warchief. The agent calls the effort fruitless, but the knowledge is valuable to the Dark Lady. The agent leaves the recovered items with you and warns you to say nothing of the mission.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent me to the Excavation Site?",a="A Deathstalker Agent outside the Excavation Site asks you to clear out the Dragonmaw and bring back anything of note.",al={"who wants dragonmaw cleared","deathstalker agent job","who sent me"}},{q="What are the Dragonmaw hoping to do?",a="The Dragonmaw remnants believe they have found something that could restore their former power.",al={"dragonmaw plan","why are dragonmaw here","dragonmaw back to power"}},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers want the site cleared?",a="They want to enter the Excavation Site undetected.",al={"why clear excavation site","deathstalkers move in","what do they need"}},{q="What should I bring back?",a="Bring the Deathstalker Agent anything of note you recover from the Dragonmaw.",al={"what to recover","dragonmaw items","what does agent want"}},{q="Who is the Dark Lady?",a="The agent uses that title for Sylvanas, who leads the Forsaken.",al={"dark lady meaning","who is dark lady","sylvanas title"}}},kw={"dark lady","deathstalker agent","dragonmaw","excavation site","forsaken","orcish scrawl","rend"},m={id=95682},src={"In-game quest text: Open the Maw"},fv=true}
E["quest:95697"] = {t="quest",n="Changing Tastes",z="general",s="At Borstan's Firepit, a new dish may bring travelers to Orgrimmar. Zamja's advice and tales of giant raptor talons lead Borstan to seek thicket raptor meat from the Wetlands across the sea.",h="At Borstan's Firepit, a new dish may bring travelers to Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Elevating Capital Cuisine",b="Borstan's Firepit in Orgrimmar hopes to widen its menu. Zamja suggests homestyle raptor cooking for travelers who miss the familiar meals of their birth villages. Borstan likes the thought of drawing new patrons with raptor, but simple village fare seems too modest for the Horde's great capital. He wants a bolder version of the old staple.",sp=0},{t="The Hunt in the Wetlands",b="A hunter returns to Orgrimmar with a massive talon from a thicket raptor of the Wetlands excavation sites. The beast's size and quality catch Borstan's interest. He arranges for adventurers to cross the sea to the Eastern Kingdoms, brave the excavation grounds, and bring back prime thicket raptor meat for his fires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Changing Tastes?",a="Changing Tastes is a culinary task in Orgrimmar. Borstan, owner of Borstan's Firepit, seeks thicket raptor meat from the distant Wetlands to raise his menu above basic village cooking.",al={"what is changing tastes","changing tastes quest"}},{q="Who is Zamja?",a="Zamja is an associate and fellow culinary worker who suggests homestyle raptor dishes for Borstan's Firepit, hoping to attract customers who do not usually visit.",al={"who is zamja","zamja cooking"}},{q="What is Borstan's Firepit?",a="Borstan's Firepit is an eatery in Orgrimmar, the Horde capital. It serves hearty cooked meats to locals and travelers alike.",al={"borstans firepit","where is borstan"}},{q="Why does Borstan want thicket raptor meat?",a="Borstan wants a grander take on familiar flavors than Zamja's homestyle raptor cooking. A hunter's tale of giant talons inspires him to seek thicket raptor meat from the Wetlands.",al={"why raptor meat","why thicket raptor"}},{q="Where are the thicket raptors located?",a="Thicket raptors live at excavation sites in the Wetlands, an Alliance-leaning region across the Great Sea in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"where do i find thicket raptors","wetlands excavation sites raptor"}},{q="Who gives the quest Changing Tastes?",a="Borstan, proprietor of Borstan's Firepit in Orgrimmar, offers Changing Tastes after Zamja's advice and a trophy brought back by an adventurous hunter inspire him.",al={"who gives changing tastes","borstan questgiver"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Borstan hopes to raise rustic meals to a grander height for the Horde capital, as tastes and tavern menus evolve beyond village staples.",["faction:Horde"]="Supplying Borstan's Firepit means crossing the sea into contested Wetlands to bring exotic meat back to Orgrimmar."},kw={"borstan","borstan's firepit","changing tastes","excavation sites","orgrimmar","thicket raptor","thicket raptor meat","wetlands","zamja"},rel={"npc:zamja","zone:orgrimmar","zone:wetlands","topic:hunter"},m={id=95697},src={"In-game quest text: Changing Tastes"},fv=true}
E["quest:95737"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Caitlin",z="general",s="An alchemist waits for word about a rare grass. She asks you to find Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor, whose husband has not reported back from an excavation.",h="An alchemist waits for word about a rare grass.",sec={{t="A Missing Report",b="The alchemist heard from Caitlin that her husband's excavation team found signs of a primordial grass. Caitlin does not know how much they found or whether it can be reached.\n\nNow the alchemist asks you to speak with Caitlin in Menethil Harbor. Both women are waiting to learn what happened to the promised seeds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Caitlin Grassman?",a="Caitlin Grassman is an alchemist in Menethil Harbor. Her husband joined an excavation team that found signs of a primordial grass.",al={"Caitlin","who is Caitlin","Caitlin Grassman"}},{q="What does the alchemist want me to do?",a="The alchemist asks you to speak with Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.",al={"find Caitlin","talk to Caitlin","Caitlin quest"}},{q="What did the excavation team find?",a="The team found signs of a long-lost primordial grass. How much there is and whether it can be reached remain unknown.",al={"primordial grass","rare grass","excavation find"}},{q="Why are they concerned?",a="Caitlin promised the alchemist that her husband would bring back grass seeds, but none have arrived. Both women suspect trouble at the excavation site.",al={"where are the seeds","missing grass seeds","why worried"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you are asked to check on Caitlin after her husband's team found signs of a rare primordial grass."},kw={"alchemist","caitlin grassman","excavation","grass seeds","menethil harbor","primordial grass","seeking caitlin","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={id=95737},src={"In-game quest text: Seeking Caitlin"},fv=true}
E["quest:95748"] = {t="quest",n="The Gurubashi Legends of Old",z="general",s="A troll scholar seeks a rubbing of an ancient tablet north of Vile Reef. Its legend may clarify the scale of lost I'lalai.",h="A troll scholar seeks a rubbing of an ancient tablet north of Vile Reef.",sec={{t="A Tablet by the Coast",b="The scholar compares a tablet piece you brought with the ruins off Vile Reef. Those ruins seem too small to match the sprawling civilization described in its words. So the scholar asks you to make a rubbing of a tablet in an ancient troll ruin on the coastal hills to the north.",sp=0},{t="An Old Memory",b="The scholar welcomes the rubbing and says the tablet is familiar from youth. Many moons have passed since it was last read, and the scholar's memory has faded.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the scholar want?",a="The scholar wants a rubbing of a tablet containing legends of the lost troll city of I'lalai.",al={"tablet rubbing","what does he need","rubbing request"}},{q="Where is the tablet?",a="It is in an ancient troll ruin on the coastal hills north of Vile Reef.",al={"tablet location","where tablet","north of reef"}},{q="Why does the scholar want a rubbing?",a="A tablet piece you brought describes I'lalai as a sprawling civilization, while the ruins off Vile Reef seem too small to match.",al={"why rubbing","I'lalai tablet","lost city legend"}},{q="What is I'lalai?",a="I'lalai is described in the tablet piece as a lost troll city and a sprawling civilization.",al={"I'lalai city","lost troll city","Ilalai"}},{q="What does the scholar say about the tablet?",a="The scholar has read the tablet before, when young, but says many moons have passed and memory has faded.",al={"scholar memory","read tablet before","old troll legend"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you are asked to help a scholar study legends of a lost troll city."},kw={"ancient ruin","gurubashi","i'lalai","legend","rubbing","tablet","troll","vile reef"},rel={"subzone:vile-reef","quest:629","topic:troll"},m={id=95748},src={"In-game quest text: The Gurubashi Legends of Old"},fv=true}
E["quest:95770"] = {t="quest",n="Locating the Lost City",z="general",s="Kin'weelay asks you to search the Vile Reef for a cavern tied to the lost city. Naga gathering there may have found something worth investigating.",h="Kin'weelay asks you to search the Vile Reef for a cavern tied to the lost city.",sec={{t="A Cavern in the Reef",b="Kin'weelay recalls diving among the Vile Reef ruins before murlocs settled there. He remembers a cavern and asks you to explore the reef for its entrance. Naga now gather in the region, and he wants to know what drew them there.",sp=0},{t="A Possible Discovery",b="When you return, Kin'weelay listens to what you saw. The naga are coming and going from the cavern ruin, though their purpose remains unclear. He wonders if it connects to I'lalai and the Lost City, long held as myth among trolls. Now he wants to investigate.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to search the Vile Reef?",a="Kin'weelay asks you to explore the Vile Reef and look for a cavern entrance.",al={"who sent me","kin weelay request","who wants this"}},{q="Why am I looking for a cavern?",a="Kin'weelay remembers a cavern among the Vile Reef ruins and suspects it may help locate the Lost City.",al={"why cavern","lost city clue","what am i looking for"}},{q="Why are the naga gathering there?",a="Kin'weelay has heard that naga are gathering in the region, but their reason is unknown.",al={"naga at reef","why naga","naga reason"}},{q="What happened to the Vile Reef ruins?",a="Murlocs settled among the Vile Reef ruins after Kin'weelay's younger years, when he used to dive there.",al={"vile reef ruins","murlocs there","who settled reef"}},{q="Where is the cavern entrance?",a="The cavern entrance is in the Vile Reef. Kin'weelay asks you to explore the reef for it.",al={"cavern location","find entrance","where cavern"}}},kw={"cavern","i'lalai","kin'weelay","locating the lost city","lost city","murlocs","naga","vile reef"},rel={"subzone:vile-reef","npc:kin-weelay","quest:629","topic:naga","topic:murloc","topic:troll"},m={id=95770},src={"In-game quest text: Locating the Lost City"},fv=true}
E["quest:95772"] = {t="quest",n="Songblade Search",z="general",s="Dorin Songblade waits for word from his brother Daewyn in the Wetlands. Daewyn joined an archaeological crew from Loch Modan to dig in unexplored hills, but his silence is unlike him.",h="Dorin Songblade waits for word from his brother Daewyn in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Brother's Unease",b="Dorin Songblade tends his workshop, buried in orders to refit girdles. His brother Daewyn has gone north with a dwarven excavation crew from Loch Modan. The hills they seek in the Wetlands have never felt a dwarven pickaxe. Daewyn usually writes as soon as he arrives, but no word has reached Dorin, and the silence unsettles him.",sp=0},{t="The Dig in the Wetlands",b="Daewyn Songblade digs at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands. He looks much like his brother Dorin and carries a rifle with DLS carved into its wooden stock. Those initials mark Daewyn at the remote excavation camp in the marshlands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Songblade Search?",a="Dorin Songblade asks travelers to check on his brother. Work refitting girdles fills the artisan's hands, so he could not join Daewyn's archaeological dig.",al={"who gives songblade search","songblade search quest giver","dorin songblade"}},{q="Who is Daewyn Songblade?",a="Daewyn Songblade is Dorin Songblade's brother. He left with an excavation crew from Loch Modan for the Wetlands hills, but has not sent word as he usually does.",al={"who is dorin brother","missing songblade dwarf","daewyn songblade"}},{q="Where can Daewyn be found?",a="Daewyn is at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands. His resemblance to Dorin and the DLS initials carved into his rifle's wooden stock identify him.",al={"where is daewyn","where to find daewyn songblade","songblade search location"}},{q="Why did Daewyn travel to the Wetlands?",a="Daewyn traveled to the Wetlands with a dwarven digging expedition from Loch Modan to excavate unexplored hills.",al={"why did daewyn go to wetlands","whelgars excavation purpose","why did the dwarfs go to wetlands"}},{q="What do the initials carved on the gun mean?",a="The initials DLS carved into the rifle stock belong to Daewyn Songblade. They identify the dwarf at the excavation site as Dorin's missing brother.",al={"what does dls stand for","dls gun carving","dls initials"}},{q="Why was Dorin worried about his brother?",a="Dorin worries because Daewyn usually writes promptly after setting out. No letters have come since Daewyn left for the Wetlands, and Dorin fears something has gone wrong.",al={"why is dorin worried","why look for daewyn","songblade search reason"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know expedition crews and archaeological digs are common across Khaz Modan. The Wetlands beyond Loch Modan are dangerous, and journeys there put kin at risk.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you may pass excavation sites on the way between Loch Modan and Menethil Harbor. There, you can aid stranded dwarven prospectors and artisans."},kw={"daewyn songblade","dls","dorin songblade","loch modan","songblade search","wetlands","whelgar's excavation site"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","zone:wetlands","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},m={id=95772},src={"In-game quest text: Songblade Search"},fv=true}
E["quest:95773"] = {t="quest",n="Enemies in the Water",z="general",s="Naga gather near old troll ruins off the coast, while the Horde is already pressed by attacks on its caravans. You are asked to answer this threat and show that you are proving your worth.",h="Naga gather near old troll ruins off the coast, while the Horde is already pressed by attacks on its caravans.",sec={{t="Reports from the Coast",b="The Horde has received reports of naga gathering near old troll ruins beneath the sea. Bloodscalp and ogre attacks are already straining its defenses, so a threat from the water gives little room for delay. You are asked to confront the Brinescale skirmishers and bring back their tridents as proof.",sp=0},{t="A Message at Grom’gol",b="At Grom’gol, the tridents you bring back are meant to be planted outside the gates. Their display will warn that the Horde is not to be trifled with, and your work earns the commander’s praise.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the naga near the coast?",a="Reports say the naga are gathering around old troll ruins beneath the sea.",al={"naga coast","naga in water","why naga here"}},{q="Who are the enemies here?",a="The threat comes from Brinescale skirmishers, a group of naga reported near the coast.",al={"water enemies","who naga","brinescale"}},{q="Why does the Horde want the naga dealt with?",a="The Horde is already stretched thin defending its caravans from Bloodscalp and ogre attacks, and fears a surprise assault from the sea.",al={"why kill naga","horde naga problem","sea attack"}},{q="What proof is requested?",a="You are asked to bring back Brinescale tridents as proof of your success.",al={"trident proof","what bring back","brinescale tridents"}},{q="What will happen to the tridents?",a="They will be planted outside Grom’gol’s gates as a warning that the Horde is not to be trifled with.",al={"trident message","plant tridents","gromgol tridents"}},{q="How does this prove my worth?",a="The commander praises your work and says you are quickly proving your worth to the Horde.",al={"prove worth","horde approval","why am i here"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde seeks to protect its caravans while keeping watch for a possible attack from the sea."},kw={"bloodscalp","brinescale","enemies in the water","grom'gol","horde","naga","ogres","tridents","troll ruins"},rel={"quest:323","topic:naga","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={id=95773},src={"In-game quest text: Enemies in the Water"},fv=true}
E["quest:95774"] = {t="quest",n="Her Name Is Olgra",z="general",s="Mankrik mourns Olgra and prepares a monument to keep her name alive. He asks you to seek her missing bone adornments among the nearby Razormane raiders.",h="Mankrik mourns Olgra and prepares a monument to keep her name alive.",sec={{t="Honoring the Fallen",b="A healer saved Mankrik, but Olgra died from her wounds on the battlefield. Grieving, Mankrik prepares a lasting tribute so her name and sacrifice will be remembered.",sp=0},{t="Lost Keepsakes",b="Olgra wore cherished ornaments made of polished bone, but they are missing from her resting place. Mankrik asks you to recover them from the nearby Razormane raiders, so they can rest beside the monument he is raising for her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Olgra?",a="Olgra fell in battle against the quilboar. The healer who saved Mankrik could not save her, and he intends to honor her memory forever.",al={"who is olgra","mankrik wife","who died"}},{q="What are Olgra's adornments?",a="Olgra's adornments are cherished pieces of jewelry made from polished bone. She wore them before she was slain.",al={"what are olgras adornments","olgra jewels","what are the adornments made of"}},{q="Why are the Razormane raiders being hunted?",a="The Razormane raiders have Olgra's ornaments. Mankrik sends you to recover them from the raiders near the place where she died.",al={"why kill razormane raiders","who stole olgras adornments","where are the adornments"}},{q="What will Mankrik do with the recovered adornments?",a="Mankrik plans to place the recovered bone jewelry beside the monument he is building for Olgra, so her memory will endure.",al={"mankrik memorial","what will mankrik do with the adornments","why does mankrik want the adornments"}}},kw={"adornments","mankrik","memorial","olgra","polished bone","quilboar","razormane raiders"},rel={"npc:mankrik","topic:quilboar"},m={id=95774},src={"In-game quest text: Her Name Is Olgra"},fv=true}
E["quest:95789"] = {t="quest",n="Shady Saltseers",z="general",s="A contact of Baron Revilgaz sends you to the Drowned City after the Saltseers, pirates who collect magical artifacts. Their stolen goods have drawn attention now that the sunken troll ruin has risen again.",h="A contact of Baron Revilgaz sends you to the Drowned City after the Saltseers, pirates who collect magical...",sec={{t="A Baron’s Request",b="A contact of Baron Revilgaz asks you to recover artifacts from the Saltseers in the Drowned City. The pirates collect magical objects, and the ruin’s return has left goods there for the taking. Their stolen artifacts are what Revilgaz’s contact seeks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the Saltseers’ artifacts?",a="A contact of Baron Revilgaz asks you to recover the artifacts.",al={"who sent me","baron revilgaz contact","who wants artifacts"}},{q="Who are the Saltseers?",a="The Saltseers are pirates who collect magical artifacts.",al={"saltseer pirates","who are saltseers","saltseers"}},{q="Where are the Saltseers?",a="They are in the Drowned City, a sunken troll ruin that has risen again.",al={"where is drowned city","saltseers location","drowned city"}},{q="What artifacts am I looking for?",a="You are asked to recover Voodoo Infused Artifacts stolen by the Saltseers.",al={"what to collect","voodoo artifacts","stolen goods"}}},kw={"baron revilgaz","drowned city","magical artifacts","pirates","saltseers","shady saltseers","troll ruin","voodoo infused artifacts"},rel={"npc:baron-revilgaz","topic:pirate","topic:troll"},m={id=95789},src={"In-game quest text: Shady Saltseers"},fv=true}
E["quest:95791"] = {t="quest",n="The Saltseer Captain",z="general",s="A rival hunter wants Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners removed from the Drowned City. Their crew keeps gathering the magical artifacts he seeks.",h="A rival hunter wants Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners removed from the Drowned City.",sec={{t="A Rival in the City",b="A rival hunter seeks your help in the Drowned City, where the Saltseer pirates have become a thorn in his side. Captain Dreadrise and his Saltseer Coroners gather the magical artifacts he wants. He asks you to remove the captain and three of his crew from the picture.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Dreadrise?",a="Captain Dreadrise leads the Saltseer pirates in the Drowned City.",al={"dreadrise","saltseer captain","captain guy"}},{q="Who are the Saltseer Coroners?",a="The Saltseer Coroners are crew members Captain Dreadrise works with in gathering magical artifacts.",al={"saltseer crew","coroners","dreadrise's crew"}},{q="Why does the giver want Dreadrise gone?",a="Captain Dreadrise and his crew keep gathering magical artifacts the giver has been seeking, and he is tired of the competition.",al={"why kill dreadrise","why remove captain","dreadrise rival"}},{q="Where are Captain Dreadrise and the Saltseers?",a="Captain Dreadrise and the Saltseer pirates are in the Drowned City.",al={"where is dreadrise","saltseer location","drowned city pirates"}},{q="What does the giver ask me to do?",a="The giver asks you to slay Captain Dreadrise and three Saltseer Coroners in the Drowned City.",al={"what do i do","dreadrise quest","saltseer task"}}},kw={"captain dreadrise","drowned city","magical artifacts","pirates","saltseer","saltseer coroners"},rel={"topic:pirate"},m={id=95791},src={"In-game quest text: The Saltseer Captain"},fv=true}
E["quest:95795"] = {t="quest",n="Fallen in the Fen",z="general",s="At the excavation, a fallen dwarf leaves grim news for his brother in Lakeshire. Dorin Songblade learns what became of his kin and faces the gifts he could not finish in time.",h="At the excavation, a fallen dwarf leaves grim news for his brother in Lakeshire.",sec={{t="Tragedy at the Dig",b="At the excavation sites, an adventurous dwarf lies dead. You cover his remains with his own cloak, then carry the grim news to Lakeshire and seek out his kin.",sp=0},{t="A Brother's Grief",b="Dorin Songblade is a dwarven craftsman in Lakeshire. When he learns his brother's fate, grief overwhelms him. For weeks, he worked at his forge on a surprise set of gear, but it was not ready before his brother's expedition. He regrets not going with him.\n\nDorin cannot bear to reforge, sell, or keep what he made with his own hands. So he gives the finished pieces to the one who brought him closure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Fallen in the Fen?",a="At the excavation sites, you find a fallen dwarf and cover his body with his own cloak. Then you carry word of his fate to his grieving brother, Dorin Songblade, in Lakeshire.",al={"what is fallen in the fen","fallen in the fen quest"}},{q="Who is Dorin Songblade?",a="Dorin Songblade is a dwarven smith in Lakeshire. He had been forging a surprise set of gear for his brother when he learned of the death at the excavation sites.",al={"who is dorin songblade","dorin in lakeshire","dorin songblade role"}},{q="Who is the fallen dwarf found at the excavation?",a="The fallen dwarf was Dorin Songblade’s brother. Before his expedition, he passed through Lakeshire to gather supplies, then met his death in the field.",al={"who died in the fen","dead dwarf excavation","whose body is in the excavation"}},{q="Where can Dorin Songblade be found?",a="Dorin Songblade lives in Lakeshire, the primary settlement in the Redridge Mountains. He works at the forge there.",al={"where is dorin songblade","dorin songblade location"}},{q="What was Dorin forging for his brother?",a="Dorin was forging equipment as a surprise gift for his brother. The work was unfinished when his brother left on his expedition. Dorin cannot bear to keep, reforge, or sell the gear.",al={"what was dorin forging","dorin surprise gift"}},{q="Why does Dorin give away the items he crafted?",a="Dorin regrets not accompanying his brother and cannot bear to keep, reforge, or sell the arms he made. He gives the finished pieces to the traveler who brought news of his kin.",al={"why did dorin give away the gear","why does dorin give you equipment"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the grief of losing a brother to ancient digs and untamed wilderness. You know crafted metal can outlive the hand meant to hold it.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you understand the care Dorin put into arms meant as a surprise for his kin. Now the gear recalls his brother’s untimely death.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can bring comfort to a grieving artisan in Redridge. A town resident seeks closure during troubled times for the kingdom."},kw={"blacksmith","dorin","dorin songblade","dwarf","excavation","excavation sites","fallen in the fen","lakeshire","songblade"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","topic:dwarf"},m={id=95795},src={"In-game quest text: Fallen in the Fen"},fv=true}
E["quest:95803"] = {t="quest",n="A Token of Good Faith",z="general",s="Danitha sends you to carry Rudolph Gelhardt’s head to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity. The delivery is meant to show the Forsaken that your people are devoted to their prosperity.",h="Danitha sends you to carry Rudolph Gelhardt’s head to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Show of Loyalty",b="Danitha says Sylvanas distrusts your people and openly disparages them. She asks you to bring Rudolph Gelhardt’s head as proof that you tend to your own house and stand with the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Lady’s Answer",b="Sylvanas doubts Danitha’s order can stop more of its members from turning the Light against their own people. She warns that she may no longer tolerate the order if it stops serving the Forsaken’s interests. The order will be watched.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks me to bring Rudolph Gelhardt’s head to Sylvanas?",a="Danitha asks you to carry Rudolph Gelhardt’s head to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.",al={"who sent me to Sylvanas","Danitha head delivery","head to the Dark Lady"}},{q="Why does Danitha want me to bring the head to Sylvanas?",a="Danitha wants the delivery to show Sylvanas that your people tend to their own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the Forsaken.",al={"why bring Rudolph's head","what is this delivery for","prove loyalty"}},{q="Why does Sylvanas mistrust Danitha’s people?",a="Danitha says Sylvanas greatly mistrusts your people and nearly openly disparages them.",al={"why Sylvanas distrusts us","Dark Lady mistrust","why does she disparage us"}},{q="Where do I take Rudolph Gelhardt’s head?",a="You are asked to bring Rudolph Gelhardt’s head to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.",al={"where is Sylvanas","head delivery location","take it to Undercity"}}},kw={"a token of good faith","danitha","dark lady","forsaken","light","rudolph gelhardt","sylvanas windrunner","undercity"},rel={"quest:91317","zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:forsaken","topic:light"},m={id=95803},src={"In-game quest text: A Token of Good Faith"},fv=true}
E["quest:95805"] = {t="quest",n="Grace of An'she and Mu'sha",z="general",s="On Red Cloud Mesa, An'she and Mu'sha receive honor as the Earthmother's eyes. You carry smoldering incense to a shrine in the southeastern hills, where its smoke rises toward the sun and moon that bring warmth, life, and direction to the plains.",h="On Red Cloud Mesa, An'she and Mu'sha receive honor as the Earthmother's eyes.",sec={{t="The Eyes of the Earthmother",b="Tauren honor An'she and Mu'sha as the sun and moon, the Earthmother's twin eyes. Elemental spirits dwell in Azeroth's stones, winds, and waters, while the celestial twins watch from the heights of heaven. As they cross the sky, they mark day and night and bring warmth, guidance, and hope to living creatures. For tauren, honoring them is a spiritual duty. Balance calls for reverence toward the land beneath your feet and the light above.",sp=0},{t="An Offering on the Heights",b="Carry smoldering incense into the southeastern hills overlooking Red Cloud Mesa, just south of the prickly quilboar grounds. Make the journey with speed and care. Keep the embers dry and reach the shrine before they burn to cold ash. At the elevated shrine, cast them into the sacred fire. Their fragrant smoke carries your respect skyward, toward the sun and moon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are An'she and Mu'sha?",a="An'she and Mu'sha are the sun and moon in tauren belief, honored as the Earthmother's twin eyes. They shine from above, unlike the spirits dwelling in Azeroth's soil, air, fire, and water. An'she brings warmth and life, while Mu'sha offers guidance and solace through the night.",al={"who are anshe and musha","anshe and musha lore","tauren sun and moon gods"}},{q="Why do the tauren make offerings to the sun and moon?",a="Tauren teachings hold that balance is essential to existence. An'she and Mu'sha give living creatures energy, vision, and hope. By offering incense at a high place, tauren show respect for both celestial lights, whose constant benevolence mortal life depends on.",al={"why revere the sun and moon","tauren celestial worship","why honor anshe and musha"}},{q="Where is the shrine of An'she and Mu'sha located?",a="The shrine lies in the high hills southeast of Red Cloud Mesa, overlooking the plains and just south of the thorny quilboar territories. Its height gives a clear, unobstructed view of the open sky, where smoke can rise toward the heavens.",al={"where is the anshe shrine","shrine location mulgore","how to find the incense shrine"}},{q="What is the significance of the smoldering incense?",a="Smoldering incense carries a traveler's prayer and respect toward the sun and moon. Its fragrant smoke rises from the burning embers. Cast them into the shrine fire to complete the rite and bring the pilgrim a tranquil sense of spiritual fulfillment.",al={"what does the incense do","meaning of the incense offering","why burn smoldering incense"}},{q="Why must the incense be delivered quickly and kept dry?",a="The incense must still smolder when it reaches the shrine fire, so the journey calls for vigilance, speed, and care. Finish before the embers burn to cold ash, and keep them from water, which would extinguish them and spoil the offering.",al={"why is the incense timed","dont get it wet","incense burning down"}},{q="Do the quilboar threaten the pilgrimage to the shrine?",a="Quilboar tribes occupy defended thorn dens in the hills just north of the shrine. The shrine rests at a quiet overlook south of their grounds, but travelers must avoid the quilboar brambles, where an attack could delay or disrupt the journey.",al={"quilboar near the shrine","are quilboar a threat to pilgrims","quilboar south of the mesa"}},{q="How does Mu'sha compare to other cultures' views of the moon?",a="Tauren call the moon Mu'sha, the loving left eye of the Earthmother, gazing down on mortal life. Night elves revere the same luminous white moon as Elune, while tauren tradition binds Mu'sha to her solar twin, An'she.",al={"is musha elune","tauren moon versus elune","musha and the night elves"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you learn that life calls you to honor An'she and Mu'sha as faithfully as the Earthmother. Their reverence lies at the heart of tauren spiritual identity and reminds young braves of their duty.",["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you look to the sun and moon's eternal dance as nature's primal balance, guiding your understanding of its cosmic rhythms.",["class:Shaman"]="As a tauren shaman, you speak with the spirits of earth, fire, water, and air, and pay equal homage to the celestial twins whose light sustains living energy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see the sacred rites on Red Cloud Mesa and the nature-revering ways the nomadic tauren bring to their allies."},kw={"an'she","earthmother","moon","mu'sha","mulgore","red cloud mesa","shrine","smoldering incense","sun","tauren"},rel={"topic:light","topic:quilboar"},m={id=95805},src={"In-game quest text: Grace of An'she and Mu'sha"},fv=true}
E["quest:95809"] = {t="quest",n="Heartwoven",z="general",s="In the Wetlands, Ardin Grassman has survived the marsh’s dangers and sends word to Menethil Harbor. A traveler carries a reed heart to Caitlin Grassman.",h="In the Wetlands, Ardin Grassman has survived the marsh’s dangers and sends word to Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Signal from the Marshes",b="Ardin Grassman went to see the strange grasses at the Wetlands excavation sites, but became stranded among the marsh’s dangers. You clear a path through the wilderness, giving him room to rest and gather his harvest. Tired but determined, Ardin prepares to return toward the safety of the port.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Menethil",b="Before setting out for home, Ardin takes marsh reeds from his pack and braids them into a heart. He gives you the token to carry to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor. She has been waiting in worry. Word that Ardin survived and will soon return brings relief, along with the reed heart and the promise of a warm meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Heartwoven?",a="A traveler helps Ardin Grassman after he becomes stranded at the Wetlands excavation sites. Ardin makes a reed heart to carry word of his survival and affection to Caitlin Grassman, who waits in Menethil Harbor.",al={"heartwoven quest","what is heartwoven","wetlands heartwoven"}},{q="Who is Caitlin Grassman?",a="Caitlin Grassman waits anxiously in Menethil Harbor for her husband, Ardin. She fears for his life after he went to the Wetlands excavation sites, and feels relief when you bring word that he survived.",al={"who is caitlin grassman","caitlin menethil harbor","caitlin grassman"}},{q="What is the reed-woven heart?",a="The reed-woven heart is a token Ardin makes from marsh reeds in his pack. He sends it with you to reassure Caitlin that he is alive and returning home soon.",al={"what is the reed heart","heart woven from reeds","reed woven heart"}},{q="Where do you turn in Heartwoven?",a="You bring the reed heart to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor, the Alliance port town on the western coast of the Wetlands.",al={"where to turn in heartwoven","heartwoven turn in location","where is caitlin grassman"}},{q="Who gives you the quest Heartwoven?",a="Ardin Grassman gives you the heart to carry to Caitlin, his wife. After you clear a safe path through the Wetlands, he rests, gathers his bushels, and sends you ahead with the token.",al={"who gives heartwoven","who crafts the heart","the survivor heartwoven"}},{q="What happened to the stranded gatherer?",a="Ardin went to the excavation sites to see strange towering grasses, but agitated wildlife overwhelmed the excavation team, especially spiders. You clear a path through the surrounding threats, allowing Ardin to survive, gather his bushels, and head back to Menethil Harbor.",al={"what happened to the gatherer","is he alive","heartwoven survivor"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help keep the perilous marsh routes around Menethil Harbor safe for the civilians who rely on them.",["profession:Cooking"]="When Caitlin learns her partner survived, she sets out to prepare a warm, hearty meal to welcome him home."},kw={"caitlin grassman","grassman","heartwoven","menethil harbor","reed heart","reeds","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:light"},m={id=95809},src={"In-game quest text: Heartwoven"},fv=true}
E["quest:95810"] = {t="quest",n="Lost Relic Carry",z="general",s="You carry a broken rock-mech relic through the Wetlands toward Prospector Whelgar. Its strange material draws the eye of dwarven researchers.",h="You carry a broken rock-mech relic through the Wetlands toward Prospector Whelgar.",sec={{t="A Fragment of Ancient Craft",b="A rock-mech has left behind a fractured piece of its ancient craft. Its unfamiliar composite marks it as part of a sophisticated mechanism tied to the Titans.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Excavation",b="Prospector Whelgar studies ancient remains at the Wetlands excavation site. Bring the relic safely to him, and dwarven scholars will have physical evidence for their study of their ancient heritage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Titan Relic?",a="The Titan Relic is a fractured piece of an ancient rock-mech automaton. Its unknown composite formed part of an intricate mechanical device.",al={"what is the relic","what is the item","rock mech piece"}},{q="Who is Prospector Whelgar?",a="Prospector Whelgar is a dwarven researcher who oversees the excavation site in the Wetlands. He studies ancient earthen remains and relics uncovered across the region.",al={"who is whelgar","whelgar lore","excavation lead"}},{q="Where does the relic need to be delivered?",a="Bring the relic to Prospector Whelgar at his excavation site in the Wetlands. There, dwarven excavators investigate ancient ruins.",al={"where do i bring it","where is the turn in","whelgar location"}},{q="What created the rock-mech automaton?",a="The fragment is identified as a Titan relic. Dwarven lore ties ancient mechanical constructs and stone automatons to the enigmatic Titans who shaped the world.",al={"who made the rock mech","automaton origins","titan connection"}},{q="Why does Prospector Whelgar treat the relic with reverence?",a="Whelgar respects the danger of reaching the depths where these automatons lie. He says surviving the delve and returning with an intact piece earns genuine respect.",al={"why is whelgar impressed","perilous delve"}},{q="What is unusual about the automaton's material?",a="The automaton's material is an unfamiliar composite, unlike ordinary stone or forged metal. It shows the sophisticated craft of ancient Titan constructs.",al={"what is the material","strange composite"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you share your people's drive to unearth ancient relics from their makers. This fragment is a prized find for dwarven heritage.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how the rock-mech's composite material and intricate design point to mechanical principles beyond standard mortal engineering."},kw={"automaton","excavation site","explorers league","lost relic carry","prospector whelgar","rock-mech","titan relic","wetlands"},rel={"npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","topic:titan","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site"},m={id=95810},src={"In-game quest text: Lost Relic Carry"},fv=true}
E["quest:95883"] = {t="quest",n="The Tortured Soul",z="general",s="At Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest, a dark rite waits unfinished. An abandoned note names the last offerings still needed: blood and a soul marked by suffering.",h="At Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest, a dark rite waits unfinished.",sec={{t="A Hasty Rite",b="At Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest, an altar bears the remains of a hastily assembled dark rite. A scrawled note lies among the scattered materials. Most of the ingredients are already gathered, but the rite still calls for blood and a Tortured Soul.",sp=0},{t="Foul Energies Unleashed",b="The creatures dwelling among Beren's Peril's crags endure great agony, making them fit sources for the rite's needed essence. Bring that soul to the ominous offering stone, and foul magical energy surges from it. The rite moves closer to fulfillment.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is The Tortured Soul?",a="The Tortured Soul tells of an unfinished dark rite at Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest. An offering stone awaits blood and the soul of a tormented creature.",al={"what is the tortured soul quest","tortured soul silverpine","beren peril quest"}},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The ritual altar and its offering stone are at Beren's Peril, a perilous mountainous enclave in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is the ritual","where is beren's peril","offering stone location"}},{q="What components are required for the ritual?",a="A scrap of note at the altar says that nearly all the materials are gathered. The two still needed are blood and a Tortured Soul.",al={"what is needed for ritual","ritual components berens peril"}},{q="Where do you find the Tortured Soul?",a="Nearby creatures dwelling among Beren's Peril's crags are tortured enough to yield the essence the offering stone needs.",al={"where to get tortured soul","who has the soul"}},{q="What happens when the Tortured Soul is brought to the altar?",a="Bringing the tortured soul to the offering stone releases foul energy and brings the dark rite closer to completion.",al={"what happens when you bring soul","turn in tortured soul"}},{q="Who created the ritual at Beren's Peril?",a="No creator is named. The note and hurriedly gathered materials suggest someone assembled the altar in haste among Beren's Peril's hostile denizens.",al={"who made the ritual","who wrote the note"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Channeling tormented souls and preparing dark rites at ancient offering stones reflect the grim, manipulative nature of demonic and shadow magic.",["race:Undead"]="Silverpine Forest is Forsaken territory, where dark magic and lingering suffering threaten the borders of Lordaeron.",["class:Priest"]="The rite draws foul energy from suffering spirits, in stark opposition to the restorative principles of the Holy Light."},kw={"beren's peril","foul energy","offering of blood","offering stone","ritual","silverpine forest","the tortured soul"},rel={"quest:95884","quest:95885","quest:516","zone:silverpine"},m={id=95883},src={"In-game quest text: The Tortured Soul"},fv=true}
E["quest:95884"] = {t="quest",n="The Offering Stone",z="general",s="In Beren's Peril, a ritual offering is being prepared at the Offering Stone. Fragments of a weathered note point travelers to the altar in Silverpine Forest.",h="In Beren's Peril, a ritual offering is being prepared at the Offering Stone.",sec={{t="A Tattered Note",b="A weathered scrap found in Silverpine Forest holds fragments about a ritual and an offering stone nearby. Time and moisture have worn away most of its words. Follow the clues into Beren's Peril, and you can find the crude altar in the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="The Ritual Site",b="At Beren's Peril, strange implements and bizarre items lie scattered across the rough stone. Someone has been using the site to prepare an offering or dark rite, far from prying eyes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Offering Stone?",a="The Offering Stone is a rough altar in Beren's Peril, Silverpine Forest. Strange implements and items scattered across it point to preparations for an offering or dark rite.",al={"what is offering stone","offering stone silverpine","what is this stone"}},{q="Where can the Offering Stone be found?",a="You can find the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril, in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is offering stone","offering stone location","find offering stone"}},{q="Who created or uses the Offering Stone?",a="The damaged note does not name the ritualists. Tools and items left on the stone show that someone was preparing an offering or dark rite nearby.",al={"who made the offering stone","who uses offering stone","who is performing the ritual"}},{q="What does the mysterious note say?",a="Most of the note is weathered and illegible. The surviving fragments mention preparations for a ritual and point to an offering stone nearby.",al={"what note","scrap of note silverpine","what does the note say"}},{q="What is found on the Offering Stone?",a="Strange tools, ritual implements, and other items lie scattered across the rough stone, meant for an offering.",al={"what items are on the stone","what implements on stone","offering stone items"}},{q="What kind of ritual is being performed here?",a="The note does not fully describe the rite. The stone is prepared as an altar where items or sacrifices are laid out for a ritual.",al={"what ritual offering stone","why an offering stone","what offering silverpine"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer in Silverpine Forest, keep watch for suspicious rituals and cultist activity in the shadowed crags of Beren's Peril.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may read the dark implements on the offering stone as signs of ritual practice, worth close study."},kw={"beren's peril","implements","offering stone","ritual","scrap of note","silverpine forest","the offering stone"},rel={"quest:516","zone:silverpine"},m={id=95884},src={"In-game quest text: The Offering Stone"},fv=true}
E["quest:95885"] = {t="quest",n="The Offering of Blood",z="general",s="At Beren's Peril, the scrap of note calls for blood at the Offering Stone. You bring a Tortured Soul to answer it.",h="At Beren's Peril, the scrap of note calls for blood at the Offering Stone.",sec={{t="The Final Rite",b="Deep in Beren's Peril, the Offering Stone waits for a final offering. Scraps of note call for a willing sacrifice, and lead you to bring blood to the altar. As you approach with the restless essence, dread closes in.",sp=0},{t="Cracking the Stone",b="The Tortured Soul draws the stone's lingering power away. The rite drains the ancient monument instead of waking a greater terror. Its rough surface cracks, then collapses into rubble. Something glittering lies among the shattered fragments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The rite takes place at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril, within Silverpine Forest. Peril and shadowed magic haunt the area.",al={"where is this quest","where is offering of blood","beren's peril quest"}},{q="What is the Offering Stone?",a="The Offering Stone is an ancient monument in Beren's Peril. It calls for blood from a willing sacrifice to unlock or drain the power within.",al={"what is the offering stone","offering stone berens peril","altar in berens peril"}},{q="What is the Tortured Soul used for?",a="A Tortured Soul is given at the Offering Stone to answer the scrap of note's call for a willing sacrifice.",al={"who is the tortured soul","what is tortured soul","what sacrifice is needed"}},{q="What happens when the offering is completed?",a="The rite drains the power that animates the Offering Stone. The rough stone cracks and crumbles, leaving something glittering among its remains.",al={"what happens to the stone","does the stone break","what happens after the ritual"}},{q="Who created the stone and why?",a="No one knows who made the Offering Stone or why. The rite drains its power and destroys it, but its maker's purpose remains unknown.",al={"who built the offering stone","purpose of offering of blood","why was stone made"}},{q="What is Beren's Peril?",a="Beren's Peril is a rocky landmark in Silverpine Forest, where wild beasts and hidden dangers lurk. Dark rites and restless souls have also left their mark there.",al={"what is berens peril","berens peril lore","why is it called berens peril"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know dark rites and bargains with souls. Even a seasoned practitioner of the fel may feel a chill at offering blood to an ancient, unknown stone.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find the use of a tortured soul in an ominous blood rite troubling, whatever its fate."},kw={"beren's peril","blood ritual","offering of blood","offering stone","sacrifice","silverpine forest","the offering of blood","tortured soul"},rel={"quest:95884","quest:95883","quest:516"},m={id=95885},src={"In-game quest text: The Offering of Blood"},fv=true}
E["quest:95981"] = {t="quest",n="Watching the Roads",z="general",s="Shadow Priest Allister sends the Forsaken against Kirin Tor patrols near Ambermill. With Dalaran's barrier down, their wizards and watchers guard the roads into Silverpine Forest while carrying magical goods into Forsaken lands.",h="Shadow Priest Allister sends the Forsaken against Kirin Tor patrols near Ambermill.",sec={{t="Tensions Along the Ambermill Road",b="Near Ambermill, Kirin Tor wizards and sentries watch the roads into Silverpine Forest. Since the barrier around Dalaran fell, they have tightened their hold on travel across the border. From the Sepulcher, the Forsaken see the human magi using these roads to carry dangerous relics and enchanted pendants into contested lands.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Supply Line",b="Shadow Priest Allister wants to stop the flow of Dalaran's magical goods at its source. He sends agents after the Kirin Tor escorts on the roads near Ambermill. By striking Dalaran Wizards and Dalaran Watchers, the Forsaken aim to break the Kirin Tor's hold on regional travel and guard their eastern frontier from outside arcane meddling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Watching the Roads?",a="Shadow Priest Allister gives the order from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He sends champions against Kirin Tor patrols on the local roads.",al={"who gives watching the roads","quest giver watching the roads","where to turn in watching the roads"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking Dalaran patrols near Ambermill?",a="Shadow Priest Allister wants to stop magical relics and pendants from reaching Silverpine Forest from Dalaran. Striking the wizards and watchers near Ambermill cuts off their passage across Forsaken borders.",al={"why kill dalaran wizards","why attack ambermill roads","kirin tor silverpine purpose"}},{q="What is the situation with the barrier around Dalaran?",a="The barrier around Dalaran has fallen. The Kirin Tor have tightened their watch on nearby roads and patrol the Ambermill region with suspicion.",al={"what happened to dalaran barrier","dalaran dome down","barrier down dalaran"}},{q="Where can the Dalaran Wizards and Watchers be found?",a="Dalaran Wizards and Dalaran Watchers patrol the roads around Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. They watch travel and guard Kirin Tor personnel and enchanted items.",al={"where are dalaran watchers","ambermill patrol locations","where to find dalaran wizards"}},{q="What kind of items is Dalaran shipping along these roads?",a="The Kirin Tor carry enchanted pendants and other magical relics from Dalaran into Silverpine Forest. Allister wants to stop them before the artifacts spread farther through the territory.",al={"what relics dalaran shipping","what are the pendants","ambermill pendants"}},{q="Why are the Kirin Tor so vigilant along the Ambermill roads?",a="The Kirin Tor watch the roads into Silverpine Forest closely since Dalaran's magical barrier fell. Allister sees their suspicion and vigilance, but the Forsaken at the Sepulcher do not know their exact motives.",al={"why is kirin tor paranoid","why are dalaran guards patrolling","kirin tor road control"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you help secure Silverpine's roads and defend Forsaken borders from Dalaran's magical incursions.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help disrupt Dalaran's supply lines near Ambermill and hold the region against hostile human enclaves.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you see Shadow Priest Allister direct the offensive from the Sepulcher, where Forsaken clergy take an active part in border defense.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you face Dalaran's wizards and watchers, who use magical relics and patrols to guard passage. Their work makes them targets for rival spellcasters."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran watcher","dalaran wizard","kirin tor","pendants","relics","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","watching the roads"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","topic:priest"},m={id=95981},src={"In-game quest text: Watching the Roads"},fv=true}
E["quest:95998"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="At Sam’s fire, travelers learn to rest and endure the road. Then they can turn to tradeskills and work in the wild.",h="At Sam’s fire, travelers learn to rest and endure the road.",sec={{t="Lessons by the Fire",b="Sam welcomes restless travelers who cross Azeroth in search of fortune, danger, and renown. Ambition alone cannot keep a newcomer warm or ease the miles. By his fire, you learn when to rest, how to build a fire, and how to gather strength for the open road.",sp=0},{t="Fieldcraft and Trade",b="A campfire offers warmth against the night chill and a chance for boosted rest. Those who know the wild understand that endurance comes from resting between journeys. Once you have learned these basics, you can turn to tradeskills. Craftsmen and gatherers can learn to make camp fixtures suited to their work in the field.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sam?",a="Sam is an experienced outdoorsman and traveler who teaches newcomers to endure the wild. He welcomes them to share his fire and learn practical ways to face the road.",al={"who is sam","sam campfire quest","quest giver"}},{q="What is the purpose of sitting by the campfire?",a="Boosted Rest is the renewal that comes from resting beside a proper campfire in the wild. Its warmth and comfort help weary travelers recover and continue their journey.",al={"what is boosted rest","boosted rest buff","resting by fire"}},{q="Why are wilderness skills important for adventurers?",a="Wilderness skills help travelers endure the dangers and long miles beyond settlement walls. Fieldcraft lets them sustain themselves without succumbing to fatigue.",al={"why learn outdoorsman skills","why thrive in wilds","survival skills"}},{q="How do tradeskills relate to wilderness camping?",a="After you learn to make a basic camp, profession trainers can teach you to craft camp fixtures suited to your work in the field.",al={"tradeskills camping","camp fixtures","professions after this"}},{q="What should an adventurer do after completing this lesson?",a="After resting by Sam’s fire and learning basic campcraft, you can seek out profession trainers. A practical craft lets you build field stations suited to your trade.",al={"next steps","what after great outdoors","after campfire quest"}},{q="Who can undertake The Great Outdoors?",a="Any traveler setting out into the wider world can learn these lessons, whatever their background or allegiance.",al={"can anyone do this","who can take great outdoors","is this quest general"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, learning to make camp gives you a foundation for preparing meals in the open air.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, living off the land and resting by an open flame may feel familiar. Even seasoned scouts benefit from learning campcraft."},kw={"basic campfire","boosted rest","camp fixture","campcraft","outdoorsman","sam","the great outdoors","tradeskill"},m={id=95998},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96031"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="At a camp in the wilderness, leatherworkers put cured hides to use and make shelter of their own. A sound campsite needs a pitched tent and a fire, whose kindling is taught by cooking trainers.",h="At a camp in the wilderness, leatherworkers put cured hides to use and make shelter of their own.",sec={{t="Pitching Shelter in the Wild",b="For tradespeople who work with hides and leather, making a shelter of their own is an essential milestone. A sturdy leather tent shields travelers from harsh weather, wind and the chill of night on open ground. Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in crowded streets or market squares, so you need to pass beyond the city gates and into the wilderness to make camp.",sp=0},{t="The Warmth of a Campfire",b="A pitched tent is only half a campsite. A proper fire keeps back darkness and cold winds, and gives you a hearth in dangerous lands. Since cooking in the field begins with building and tending a fire, seek instruction from culinary masters and cooking trainers. They teach you to kindle a campfire before you establish camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can you pitch a camp tent?",a="Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in streets or city squares, so take your tent beyond the city gates and into the wilderness.",al={"camp tent use","where pitch tent","can i camp in town"}},{q="What else is required besides a tent to pitch a camp?",a="A tent alone is not a full camp. You also need a campfire burning beside it.",al={"need fire for camp","camp requirements","how to camp"}},{q="Where do adventurers learn to build a campfire?",a="Culinary masters and cooking trainers teach you to kindle a campfire as part of preparing food. Seek a cooking trainer to learn the basics.",al={"learn campfire","who teaches campfire","cooking fire"}},{q="How does leatherworking relate to crafting camp tents?",a="Leatherworkers use cured hides and pelts, joined with sturdy stitching, to make tent coverings that can withstand rough wilderness elements. This craft gives wanderers a reliable shelter from animal hides.",al={"camping 101 leatherworking","leather camp tent","tent crafting leatherworking"}},{q="Why do adventurers establish camps in the wilderness?",a="Wilderness camps give travelers a secure haven to rest and recuperate when they are far from settled outposts, inns and settlements. Portable shelter and a warm fire help against the elements and perilous terrain.",al={"why camp out","camping purpose","wilderness survival camp"}},{q="Why do townsfolk object to setting up tents inside town?",a="Townsfolk object because tents across public streets clutter thoroughfares and cause disturbances. Settlements have inns and private lodgings for travelers, so locals expect camps to remain in the wild.",al={"camping town rules","no tents in town","why cant i pitch tent in city"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A campfire is the heart of a wilderness campsite. Basic cooking teaches you to kindle a flame and sustain a camp in the wild."},kw={"camp tent","campfire","camping","cooking","leatherworking","shelter","tent","wilderness"},m={id=96031},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96044"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="Smiths bound for the wilderness are sent to Kharanos to learn from Tognus Flintfire. He teaches them to make a portable sharpening wheel for keeping weapons keen at camp.",h="Smiths bound for the wilderness are sent to Kharanos to learn from Tognus Flintfire.",sec={{t="Field Maintenance for the Open Road",b="You are sent to Kharanos to learn how a smith can serve far from a town forge. There, skilled hands turn raw metal into tools for camp. A blade kept keen is ready for the long road.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Kharanos",b="In Kharanos, Tognus Flintfire teaches capable smiths to make a sharpening wheel. Set one beside your campsite and warriors and rogues can grind nicks from their weapons and hone dull edges before the next march.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tognus Flintfire?",a="Tognus Flintfire teaches blacksmithing in Kharanos, in Dun Morogh. He trains smiths who have shown skill in their trade, teaching them to make gear for campsites.",al={"who is tognus flintfire","where is tognus","tognus flintfire location"}},{q="What is a Sharpening Wheel?",a="A sharpening wheel is a portable tool made by blacksmiths. At camp, it gives warriors, rogues and other weapon bearers a place to hone their blades in the field.",al={"what does sharpening wheel do","sharpening wheel camp","sharpening wheel purpose"}},{q="Why do warriors and rogues care about the Sharpening Wheel?",a="Warriors and rogues depend on sharp weapons in battle. A sharpening wheel lets them tend their blades, axes and daggers while traveling far from town forges.",al={"who needs sharpening wheel","warriors sharpening wheel","rogues sharpening wheel"}},{q="Where is Kharanos?",a="Kharanos lies southwest of Ironforge in the snowy peaks of Dun Morogh. Travelers, miners and craftsmen use the settlement as a stopping place while crossing the mountain passes.",al={"where is kharanos","kharanos location","finding kharanos"}},{q="What is required to learn this camping item?",a="Show basic skill at the anvil, and Tognus Flintfire will teach you to make campsite gear. Then you can learn to forge the portable wheel.",al={"camping 101 blacksmithing requirement","when can i learn sharpening wheel","smithing camp training"}},{q="Why do blacksmiths craft camping items?",a="Blacksmiths make camping tools to help adventuring parties beyond settled towns. A portable sharpening wheel lets companions maintain their weapons under the open sky, without returning to a city forge.",al={"why craft camp items","blacksmithing camping items","smithing utility in wild"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="You can learn to make field tools such as the sharpening wheel, taking your craft beyond city forges to help allies in the wild.",["class:Warrior"]="Keen weapons matter in battle, and a sharpening wheel at camp helps you keep your edge on an expedition.",["class:Rogue"]="A sharp dagger is essential to your trade, so a camp sharpening wheel is welcome between field contracts.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find Kharanos in the snowy foothills of Dun Morogh. Its smiths keep cold steel sharp for the road."},kw={"blacksmithing","blades","camp","camping 101","dun morogh","kharanos","sharpening wheel","tognus flintfire","weapons"},rel={"subzone:kharanos","topic:warrior","topic:rogue"},m={id=96044},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:96045"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="In Ironforge, Vosur Brakthel shows alchemists how to prepare for the road. With a Mana Well, they can give spellcasters and healers a place to recover while traveling.",h="In Ironforge, Vosur Brakthel shows alchemists how to prepare for the road.",sec={{t="Brewing for the Road",b="Vosur Brakthel trains alchemists in Ironforge to carry their craft beyond the city. Brewing vials in a quiet laboratory is only part of the work. Out in Azeroth's wild places, alchemists can use what they know to make a Mana Well for a camp, helping companions endure the journey.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness Campsites",b="A Mana Well can refresh healers and spellcasters, but it belongs at a wilderness camp, not on an Ironforge street. City folk frown on tents pitched within their walls. A proper camp also needs a fire, so seek a cooking trainer's guidance before heading into the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vosur Brakthel?",a="Vosur Brakthel is an alchemy trainer in Ironforge. He teaches alchemists to use their craft to make a Mana Well for companions in the field.",al={"who teaches camping 101 alchemy","vosur brakthel role","who is vosur brakthel"}},{q="What is a Mana Well?",a="A Mana Well is an alchemical fixture for a wilderness camp. It helps spellcasters and healers recover as they travel.",al={"what does a mana well do","mana well purpose","why make a mana well"}},{q="Can you set up a camp inside Ironforge?",a="No. City folk frown on camps pitched in Ironforge's streets, so take your Mana Well beyond the city to the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in ironforge","camping in town","where to place mana well"}},{q="What else is needed to set up a camp?",a="A camp also needs a campfire. If you do not know how to make one, seek a cooking trainer before heading out.",al={"campfire requirement","do i need cooking for camping","how to start a camp"}},{q="When can an alchemist learn to make a Mana Well?",a="Vosur Brakthel teaches alchemists who have taken up the profession and shown some skill in it. With that experience, they can learn to make a Mana Well.",al={"when can i learn mana well","mana well requirements","camping 101 requirements"}},{q="Who benefits most from a Mana Well at camp?",a="Spellcasters and healers benefit most from a Mana Well. It helps them replenish their mana while traveling far from town taverns and hearthstones.",al={"who benefits from mana well","mana well classes","who uses mana well"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A campsite needs a campfire, a practical skill taught by cooking trainers across the realms.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Ironforge, alchemists can seek Vosur Brakthel's guidance on preparing restorative concoctions for their journeys."},kw={"alchemy","campfire","camping","camping 101: alchemy","ironforge","mana well","vosur brakthel"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=96045},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:96046"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="Out beyond the guarded roads, miners learn to make a lodestone for a wilderness camp. The work pairs knowledge of stone with the firecraft needed to live outdoors.",h="Out beyond the guarded roads, miners learn to make a lodestone for a wilderness camp.",sec={{t="Fieldcraft for Miners",b="Beyond guarded roads, a miner must rely on fieldcraft. Mineral knowledge gives you the means to shape a lodestone, the anchor for a campsite in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Rules of the Wild",b="A campsite belongs beyond town limits, where travelers can pitch their shelters without troubling settled folk. Choose a place in the open wilds. A camp also needs a fire to ward off the night chill. Learning to build one is part of the same fieldcraft as working stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a lodestone used for?",a="A lodestone anchors a campsite in the wilderness.",al={"lodestone purpose","what is lodestone for","why craft lodestone"}},{q="Can I set up camp inside a town or city?",a="Townspeople and settlement authorities frown on tents in public squares and streets. Set up camp beyond the town limits.",al={"can i camp in town","camping in city","camp inside settlement"}},{q="What is required before setting up a camp?",a="A camp needs a warm fire burning nearby.",al={"do i need campfire","how to make camp","camp prerequisites"}},{q="Where do I learn how to build a campfire?",a="Cooking instructors and chefs across Azeroth teach the basic fire-starting skills used in cooking.",al={"where learn campfire","who teaches campfire","campfire trainer"}},{q="How does mining connect to crafting a lodestone?",a="Mining teaches you to work the minerals and stone needed to make a lodestone.",al={"why miners camp","mining lodestone connection","lodestone craft"}},{q="Where should I go to test my new camp?",a="Go beyond the city gates into the open wilderness, where you can find room to camp away from townsfolk.",al={"where to test camp","testing lodestone","camp outdoors"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you learn to shape earth and ore into a lodestone that anchors a wilderness camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn the firecraft a camp needs from cooking trainers."},kw={"campfire","camping","camping 101: mining","campsite","cooking","lodestone","mining","wilderness"},m={id=96046},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:96050"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="You’re preparing for wilderness fishing with a Fish Bowl and a campfire. Learn where to set up and what makes a resting place comfortable.",h="You’re preparing for wilderness fishing with a Fish Bowl and a campfire.",sec={{t="Wilderness Etiquette",b="Travel through Azeroth calls for a little knowledge of the wild. When you need a place to rest, keep your tent and gear beyond town borders. Townsfolk and guards dislike travelers spreading their belongings through settlements. Take your supplies into the open wilderness instead.",sp=0},{t="The Comforts of Camp",b="A proper campsite needs a few comforts. Start with a warm campfire; a cooking trainer can teach you how to make one. Once the fire is ready, set out a handcrafted Fish Bowl. Then your stop is fit for an angler.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do you learn from Camping 101: Fishing?",a="You learn to make a Fish Bowl and prepare a wilderness resting place for fishing. Set up away from settlements.",al={"what does this quest teach","fish bowl craft","camping fishing reward"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="Set up in the wilderness, beyond town borders. Townsfolk object when travelers spread their gear through public thoroughfares.",al={"where pitch camp","can i camp in town","camping location rules"}},{q="What do you need before pitching a camp?",a="Have a campfire ready for warmth. A campsite needs one to be complete.",al={"how to start camp","do i need a campfire","camp requirements"}},{q="How do you learn to build a campfire?",a="Cooking trainers teach you how to make a campfire. If you have not learned the basics of cooking, seek a cook for instruction.",al={"how make campfire","where learn campfire","who teaches fire"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Fish Bowl?",a="The Fish Bowl decorates an outdoor campsite and suits an angler resting by the water.",al={"what is fish bowl for","camping fish bowl use","fish bowl lore"}},{q="Why are camping lessons taught to adventurers?",a="Wilderness mentors teach practical frontier skills, including making fires and respecting settlement boundaries before you head into the wild.",al={"who offers camping 101","why camping lessons","camping survival guide"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Learn the basics of cooking before making camp. Cooking trainers teach travelers to build the campfire a campsite needs."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping","cooking","fish bowl","fishing","wilderness"},m={id=96050},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:96055"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="In Ironforge, herbalists can learn to make Incense Candles for life in camp. Reyna Stonebranch teaches the craft to gatherers ready to put wild herbs to practical use.",h="In Ironforge, herbalists can learn to make Incense Candles for life in camp.",sec={{t="Practical Field Botany",b="Gathering wild herbs can serve a camp as well as a traveling party. With skill, herbalists turn what they gather into useful aids for life outdoors.",sp=0},{t="Aromatics for the Hearth",b="In Ironforge, proficient herbalists can seek instruction from Reyna Stonebranch. Once they prove their skill, she teaches them to make an Incense Candle. Its soothing aroma lifts the spirits at camp and brings calm to spellcasters and healers on long expeditions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="Herbalists learn to put wild plants to practical use in camp. Reyna Stonebranch teaches the craft in Ironforge.",al={"what is camping 101 herbalism","herbalism camping quest","herbalism camp guide"}},{q="Who is Reyna Stonebranch?",a="Reyna Stonebranch teaches proficient herbalists in Ironforge how to make Incense Candles for camp.",al={"who teaches incense candle","where is reyna stonebranch","reyna stonebranch location"}},{q="What does an Incense Candle do?",a="An Incense Candle brings a soothing aroma to camp and lifts the spirits of travelers.",al={"what does incense candle do","incense candle camping","incense candle purpose"}},{q="Why are Incense Candles useful to spellcasters?",a="Its soothing aroma helps spellcasters and healers find a calmer place during long expeditions.",al={"who benefits from incense candle","is incense candle for casters"}},{q="Where must herbalists travel for this instruction?",a="Herbalists travel to Ironforge to meet Reyna Stonebranch after proving their skill in gathering herbs.",al={"where do i go for camping herbalism","which city for camping 101 herbalism"}},{q="What is required before learning to craft the candle?",a="Herbalists must prove their skill in gathering herbs before Reyna Stonebranch teaches them to make Incense Candles.",al={"when can i learn incense candle","herbalism camping requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can make Incense Candles from gathered wild herbs to aid spellcasters at camp.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance herbalist, you can seek Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge for instruction in fieldcraft.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find herbalism instructor Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge, where she teaches how to make Incense Candles."},kw={"camp","camping 101","herbalism","herbs","incense candle","ironforge","reyna stonebranch"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=96055},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:96056"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="In Ironforge, skilled skinners learn to make a Camp Chair from animal hides. Balthus Stoneflayer teaches the craft after they prove their skill.",h="In Ironforge, skilled skinners learn to make a Camp Chair from animal hides.",sec={{t="Harvesting the Wilds",b="Skinning fallen beasts gives armorers and crafters leather to work with. Hides from cats, bears, and other beasts have uses in the field, too. You are sent to turn those materials into something useful at camp instead of selling them.",sp=0},{t="The Artisan of Ironforge",b="Balthus Stoneflayer teaches skinners in Ironforge to make a Camp Chair from prepared pelts. First, you need to show him you know how to skin beasts. Only then will he share his crafting methods.",sp=0},{t="Rest and Readiness",b="A Camp Chair gives you a place to sit by the fire and unwind while traveling. Rest there, and you can meet the next danger with your senses sharp and your strength restored.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Skinning?",a="Skilled skinners go to Ironforge to learn how to make a Camp Chair from animal hides.",al={"what is camping 101 skinning","quest purpose","camping 101 skinning quest"}},{q="Who teaches you to craft the camping item?",a="Balthus Stoneflayer teaches you to make a Camp Chair in Ironforge. First, show him you can skin beasts.",al={"who to talk to","who teaches camp chair","balthus stoneflayer who"}},{q="Where do you need to go to complete this quest?",a="Go to Ironforge, the dwarven capital in the snowy peaks of Dun Morogh. Balthus Stoneflayer teaches skinners there who prove their skill.",al={"where to go","balthus location","ironforge trainer"}},{q="What item do skinners learn to craft for their camp?",a="You learn to make a Camp Chair from animal hides, giving you a place to rest in the field between dangers.",al={"what do you make","camp chair purpose","skinning camp craft"}},{q="Why is crafting a camp chair useful for an adventurer?",a="A Camp Chair gives you a place to rest on long wilderness treks and recover your focus before danger finds you.",al={"why make a chair","what does camp chair do","camp chair benefit"}},{q="What proficiency is required before Balthus will teach you?",a="Balthus Stoneflayer teaches you after you prove your skill at skinning beasts.",al={"requirements","when can i learn","proficiency needed"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Your path to making a Camp Chair leads to Ironforge, the dwarven mountain city and Alliance capital.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can find Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge and learn how skilled skinners make camp comforts from hides.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can skin your prey in the wild and make a Camp Chair for resting between long tracks."},kw={"balthus stoneflayer","camp chair","camping","camping 101: skinning","hides","ironforge","skinning"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=96056},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:96057"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="A tailor can learn from Uthrar Threx in Ironforge how to make a Rallying Banner for a camp. The banner is meant to bolster morale, and a campfire is needed to start a camp.",h="A tailor can learn from Uthrar Threx in Ironforge how to make a Rallying Banner for a camp.",sec={{t="A Banner for Camp",b="A teacher in Ironforge can show you how to make a banner for your camp once you have proved your tailoring skill. The banner is called a Rallying Banner. It can help keep you energized, and you will need a campfire before setting up camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches tailoring for camping?",a="Uthrar Threx in Ironforge can teach you to craft a camping item once you have shown proficiency in tailoring.",al={"who teaches this","tailoring teacher","Uthrar Threx"}},{q="What can I make with tailoring?",a="You can learn to craft a Rallying Banner for your camp.",al={"tailoring camp item","what banner","craft banner"}},{q="What does the Rallying Banner do?",a="An inspirational banner can help keep you energized, and morale is important to success on a battlefield.",al={"banner purpose","why banner","rally banner"}},{q="What do I need before starting a camp?",a="You need a campfire before setting up camp. A cook can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","camp requirements"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can learn to make a Rallying Banner for your camp once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",["profession:Cooking"]="A cook can teach you to make the campfire needed before setting up camp."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101","ironforge","morale","rallying banner","tailoring","uthrar threx"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=96057},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:96058"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Engineering",z="general",s="An engineer in Kharanos can learn to craft a Reagent Bot for a camp. The bot helps keep you supplied with materials for spells.",h="An engineer in Kharanos can learn to craft a Reagent Bot for a camp.",sec={{t="A Camp's Supplies",b="An engineer can learn from Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos how to make a Reagent Bot. You need to show proficiency in your engineering skill before he teaches you. The bot helps supply materials that you and your allies need for spells.",sp=0},{t="Ready for the Wilds",b="You can now craft a Reagent Bot. To test it, leave the town and head into the wilderness, where you can set up camp. Bring a campfire too; cooks can teach you how to make one.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Reagent Bot?",a="Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot once you show proficiency in engineering.",al={"Bronk bot lesson","who is Bronk Guzzlegear","reagent bot trainer"}},{q="What does a Reagent Bot do?",a="A Reagent Bot helps keep you and your allies supplied with materials needed for spells.",al={"what is reagent bot for","bot spell supplies","camp bot"}},{q="What do I need before I can learn this?",a="You need to show proficiency in your engineering skill before Bronk Guzzlegear teaches you to craft a Reagent Bot.",al={"engineering proficiency","how learn reagent bot","camping 101 engineering"}},{q="Where can I try out the Reagent Bot?",a="You can test the Reagent Bot in the wilderness, since most folk do not want camps set up in the center of town.",al={"where test bot","camp location","reagent bot wilderness"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. A camp needs a campfire, and most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how make campfire","camp cooking"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn from Bronk Guzzlegear to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make the campfire needed for a camp."},kw={"bronk guzzlegear","camp","campfire","camping 101","engineering","kharanos","reagent bot","spell materials"},rel={"subzone:kharanos"},m={id=96058},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Engineering"},fv=true}
E["quest:96059"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="An enchanter in Ironforge can learn to make an Enchanted Lute for camp after proving skill. Its magic offers entertainment during rests on the trail.",h="An enchanter in Ironforge can learn to make an Enchanted Lute for camp after proving skill.",sec={{t="A Lute for Camp",b="Your next lesson concerns a tune for the trail. In Ironforge, Thonys Pillarstone can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute once you have shown proficiency in enchanting. The magic gives you a way to find entertainment during downtime before you take to the road again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make an Enchanted Lute?",a="Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute after you show proficiency in enchanting.",al={"thonys pillarstone","who teaches enchanting camp item"}},{q="What is the Enchanted Lute for?",a="The Enchanted Lute is a camping item meant to provide entertainment during downtime.",al={"lute purpose","enchanted lute camp"}},{q="Why do I need enchanting skill?",a="You can learn to craft the camping item once you have shown proficiency in enchanting.",al={"enchanting proficiency","how to learn lute"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an enchanter, you can learn from Thonys Pillarstone to make an Enchanted Lute for camp once you have shown proficiency in your skill."},kw={"camp item","camping 101","enchanted lute","enchanting","ironforge","thonys pillarstone"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=96059},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:96101"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="Raan welcomes new wanderers and shows them how to endure the wild. Rest by his basic campfire to gain Boosted Rest, then visit nearby trade trainers to learn practical professions.",h="Raan welcomes new wanderers and shows them how to endure the wild.",sec={{t="Lessons in the Wild",b="Raan has traveled the wilds and teaches others how to survive beyond settlement walls. Ambition and steel alone will not carry you through harsh weather; practical campcraft matters. He welcomes those seeking fortune and glory, and offers guidance to anyone willing to learn.",sp=0},{t="The Warmth of the Hearth",b="Raan asks you to sit beside his basic campfire and rest until you gain Boosted Rest. Across Azeroth's wild places, knowing when to pause, make camp, and recover can mean the difference between life and death.\n\nAfter the lesson, Raan directs you to nearby village trainers. There you can learn a trade and craft specialized fixtures for your campsite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Great Outdoors?",a="Raan, an experienced traveler, teaches wandering adventurers how to survive in the open wilderness.",al={"who offers the great outdoors","quest giver the great outdoors","raan campfire quest"}},{q="What is the purpose of The Great Outdoors?",a="The lesson teaches wilderness survival. Rest beside a basic campfire to gain Boosted Rest before dangerous journeys.",al={"what does the great outdoors teach","the great outdoors purpose","what do i learn from raan"}},{q="How is the quest completed?",a="Sit beside Raan's basic campfire and rest until you gain Boosted Rest.",al={"how to complete the great outdoors","raan campfire objective","boosted rest objective"}},{q="What does Raan suggest doing after completing the quest?",a="After the campfire lesson, Raan encourages you to visit nearby village trainers and learn a practical trade. Craftsmen can create camp fixtures suited to their craft.",al={"what does raan advise next","where to go after the great outdoors","after completing the great outdoors"}},{q="What is Boosted Rest?",a="Boosted Rest is a restorative effect gained by resting beside an established campfire. It helps travelers recover while braving the elements.",al={"what is boosted rest","campfire boosted rest buff"}},{q="Do tradeskills allow adventurers to craft campsite fixtures?",a="Yes. Local trade trainers can teach you to craft useful camp fixtures suited to your craft, so you can maintain a specialized campsite outdoors.",al={"can professions make campfires","profession camp fixtures","trade camp items"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know a basic campfire helps a traveling party rest and recover in the wild.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know campcraft is essential for trackers and rangers who live beneath open skies."},kw={"basic campfire","boosted rest","camp fixture","campfire","raan","the great outdoors","tradeskill","wilderness survival"},m={id=96101},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96102"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="Tailoring training teaches you to make a Rallying Banner. Its test belongs in the wilderness, where a camp needs a campfire.",h="Tailoring training teaches you to make a Rallying Banner.",sec={{t="A Campfire First",b="You can now craft a Rallying Banner, and its completion note calls for a wilderness test. A camp needs a campfire before you set it up. Most cooks can teach you to make one, so ask a cooking trainer for the basics if you have not learned them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I make after this?",a="Tailoring training teaches you to craft your own Rallying Banner.",al={"what do i craft","banner recipe","tailoring banner"}},{q="Where should I test the banner?",a="Test your Rallying Banner in the wilderness. The completion note says townsfolk generally do not care for camps in the center of town.",al={"where to test it","camping where","test banner"}},{q="What does a camp need?",a="Before you set up a camp, you need a campfire.",al={"camp needs what","campfire needed","camping basics"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a campfire?",a="Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. A cooking trainer can teach you the basics.",al={"campfire trainer","who teaches fire","cooking fire"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can craft a Rallying Banner for a camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make a campfire."},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","rallying banner","tailoring","wilderness"},m={id=96102},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:96130"] = {t="quest",n="Chakuyak",z="general",s="Near the tree stands west of Stonebull Lake, Chakuyak threatens travelers crossing Mulgore. Local tribesfolk have marked the fierce wolf for hunting, and her pelt will be honored.",h="Near the tree stands west of Stonebull Lake, Chakuyak threatens travelers crossing Mulgore.",sec={{t="The Shadow of Stonebull Lake",b="Chakuyak prowls the tree stands west of Stonebull Lake, where prairie wolves roam Mulgore’s grassy plateaus and rolling hills. This fierce alpha female has become a danger to travelers arriving from abroad, so local hunters have marked her for removal before more wanderers are harmed.",sp=0},{t="Reverence and Necessity",b="For the local tribes, killing Chakuyak calls for solemn respect, not boasting. They see it as necessary to protect travelers and villagers. Her thick pelt is cured and put to use, honoring the wolf and ensuring her sacrifice is not wasted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who or what is Chakuyak?",a="Chakuyak is a large, unusually aggressive prairie wolf who threatens travelers in Mulgore.",al={"what is chakuyak","who is chakuyak","is chakuyak a wolf"}},{q="Where is Chakuyak located?",a="Chakuyak prowls the tree stands west of Stonebull Lake, among the wooded hills.",al={"where to find chakuyak","chakuyak spot","where does chakuyak roam"}},{q="Why must Chakuyak be hunted down?",a="Chakuyak has grown bold and aggressive, making her a danger to travelers arriving from abroad.",al={"why kill chakuyak","chakuyak threat"}},{q="What happens to Chakuyak's pelt after the hunt?",a="Her pelt is preserved and put to use, so nothing is wasted.",al={"what happens to chakuyak pelt","chakuyak fur"}},{q="Do I need a group to hunt Chakuyak?",a="Chakuyak is exceptionally fierce. Travelers often join small hunting parties to track and bring her down safely.",al={"should i group for chakuyak","is chakuyak hard to solo"}},{q="Who acknowledges your victory over Chakuyak?",a="The hunter who set the hunt promises to praise your deed to the tribe’s chief when you return with Chakuyak’s pelt.",al={"who rewards chakuyak hunt","chakuyak chief"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the balance between reverence for nature and the duty to protect your tribe. Using a slain beast’s pelt honors it.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need patience and keen senses to track a fierce, solitary alpha wolf through wooded hills. Treat the predator with respect."},kw={"chakuyak","mulgore","prairie wolf","stonebull lake","tauren hunt","travelers","wolf pelt"},rel={"subzone:stonebull-lake"},m={id=96130},src={"In-game quest text: Chakuyak"},fv=true}
E["quest:96137"] = {t="quest",n="Ira's Dagger",z="general",s="Sirra Von'Indi asks you to look into Ira's dagger and the worgs still harming travelers. Ira's spirit may have unfinished business in the forest.",h="Sirra Von'Indi asks you to look into Ira's dagger and the worgs still harming travelers.",sec={{t="A Ranger's Dagger",b="Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire asks you to deal with the worgs that continue to claim victims in the forest. Ira was a self-appointed ranger who kept the woods safe by stopping beasts from attacking travelers. Her spirit still wanders there, and the dagger belonged to her. Sirra seeks more information about the blade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Ira?",a="Ira was a self-appointed ranger who kept the forest safe by preventing beasts from attacking travelers.",al={"ira backstory","who is ira"}},{q="Why does Ira's spirit wander the forest?",a="Ira's spirit still wanders the woods, and she may have unfinished business there.",al={"ira ghost why","why is ira a ghost"}},{q="What is Ira's dagger?",a="It is a small dagger that belonged to Ira.",al={"ira dagger","dagger story"}},{q="Why are you dealing with worgs?",a="The worgs continue to claim victims throughout the forest, and Ira's unfinished business may be to clear them out.",al={"worgs in the forest","ira worg quest"}},{q="Who asks about the dagger?",a="Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire asks you to return to her with the dagger for more information.",al={"sirra dagger","who wants ira's dagger"}}},kw={"black ravager","darkshire","ira","ira's dagger","ranger","sirra von'indi","spirit","worg","young black ravager"},rel={"subzone:darkshire","npc:sirra-von-indi"},m={id=96137},src={"In-game quest text: Ira's Dagger"},fv=true}
E["quest:96138"] = {t="quest",n="Merrick's Bow",z="general",s="Sirra Von'Indi asks you to look into the ogres troubling Merrick Valor's spirit near Raven Hill. Merrick's bow may help shed light on the place's history.",h="Sirra Von'Indi asks you to look into the ogres troubling Merrick Valor's spirit near Raven Hill.",sec={{t="A spirit's concern",b="Near Raven Hill, Merrick Valor's spirit still wanders the roads. You have a bow he left behind, and his unfinished business may concern the ogres south of town. Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire can tell you more about the bow and Merrick's past.",sp=0},{t="Merrick's past",b="Sirra Von'Indi says Merrick always wanted to prove himself, and that something happened to him and his family. She thanks you for bringing the bow and hopes it will cast more light on Raven Hill's history.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Merrick Valor?",a="Merrick Valor was a famed Watcher who took pride in keeping roads safe from encroaching enemies.",al={"merrick","merrick valor"}},{q="Why is Merrick's spirit wandering?",a="Merrick's spirit still wanders the roads. His unfinished business may be tied to the ogres south of Raven Hill.",al={"merrick ghost","why spirit wandering"}},{q="What does Merrick's bow have to do with Raven Hill?",a="Sirra Von'Indi hopes Merrick's bow can shed more light on Raven Hill's history.",al={"merrick bow","bow raven hill"}},{q="Who is Sirra Von'Indi?",a="Sirra Von'Indi is in Darkshire and can tell you more about Merrick's bow.",al={"sirra","sirra von indi"}},{q="What happened to Merrick and his family?",a="Sirra Von'Indi says something happened to Merrick and his family, but gives no further details.",al={"merrick family","what happened merrick"}}},kw={"darkshire","merrick valor","merrick's bow","ogres","raven hill","sirra von'indi","splinter fist","watcher"},rel={"quest:163","subzone:darkshire","npc:sirra-von-indi"},m={id=96138},src={"In-game quest text: Merrick's Bow"},fv=true}
E["quest:96204"] = {t="quest",n="The Windshaper's Wrath",z="general",s="Lumina Windsinger asks you to help her escape Fenris Keep. Your aid gives her reason to trust paladins.",h="Lumina Windsinger asks you to help her escape Fenris Keep.",sec={{t="A Way Out",b="Lumina Windsinger is free inside Fenris Keep, but she wants to leave with you. She means to make the creatures who held her regret crossing a Windshaper. Stay with her as she makes her escape.",sp=0},{t="A New Friend",b="At Fenris Keep, Lumina tells you she has met Trevan and learned he sent you to find her. She has heard unkind things about paladins, but your help has changed her view. The Windshapers count you and your kind as friends.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lumina Windsinger?",a="Lumina Windsinger is a Windshaper who was held at Fenris Keep and seeks your help escaping.",al={"lumina","who is lumina","windsinger"}},{q="Where is Lumina trying to escape from?",a="Lumina Windsinger is trying to escape Fenris Keep.",al={"lumina escape","fenris keep","get lumina out"}},{q="Who sent me to find Lumina?",a="Lumina says Trevan sent you along her trail.",al={"who sent me","trevan","lumina trail"}},{q="Why does Lumina mention paladins?",a="Lumina has heard unkind things about paladins, but says those claims proved unfounded after your help.",al={"paladin thing","lumina paladins","does she trust paladins"}},{q="What does Lumina think of me?",a="Lumina says you and your kind have a friend among the Windshapers.",al={"lumina likes me","windshaper friend","what does lumina say"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Lumina has heard unkind things about your kind, but your help gives her cause to welcome you as a friend."},kw={"escape","fenris keep","lumina windsinger","paladin","trevan","windshaper"},m={id=96204},src={"In-game quest text: The Windshaper's Wrath"},fv=true}
E["quest:96241"] = {t="quest",n="Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon",z="general",s="Mazu'kon wants you to collect venom samples from the Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise. The strange toxins have caught his curiosity.",h="Mazu'kon wants you to collect venom samples from the Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise.",sec={{t="At Gloomrise",b="Mazu'kon has heard of strange new creatures crawling around Gloomrise. Their venom may have unusual properties, so he asks you to collect samples from the Gnawed Corpses with his extractor. He is curious to learn what makes the toxin different.",sp=0},{t="The Samples",b="Mazu'kon thanks you for bringing the toxin samples from Gloomrise. He says the venom's unusual properties were no joke, and notes that you seem unharmed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the toxin samples?",a="Mazu'kon asks you to collect venom samples from the Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise.",al={"who wants toxins","Mazu'kon toxin"}},{q="Why does Mazu'kon want the venom?",a="He has heard the creatures' venom may have unusual properties, and it has made him curious.",al={"why toxins","what's he curious about"}},{q="Where do I get the samples?",a="The samples come from Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise.",al={"toxin samples where","Gloomrise corpses"}},{q="What does Mazu'kon give you?",a="Mazu'kon gives you an extractor to gather the venom.",al={"extractor","how collect toxin"}},{q="How many toxin samples does he need?",a="Mazu'kon asks for five Gloomrise Toxin Samples.",al={"sample count","how many toxins"}}},kw={"extractor","gloomrise","gloomrise toxin samples","gnawed corpses","mazu'kon","toxin","venom"},m={id=96241},src={"In-game quest text: Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon"},fv=true}
E["quest:96243"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="general",s="In Coldridge Valley, the Call of Earth sends an initiate to seek Teo Hammerstorm at Anvilmar. There begins a shaman’s communion with the spirits of stone.",h="In Coldridge Valley, the Call of Earth sends an initiate to seek Teo Hammerstorm at Anvilmar.",sec={{t="The Voice of Stone",b="An initiate’s first communion with the elements begins when the earth calls. Other elemental energies may already stir, but speaking with stone brings balance. The earth teaches the initiate to find strength that will not yield. Firm footing comes beneath their boots and within their spirit.",sp=0},{t="The Holdfast of Anvilmar",b="In Dun Morogh’s snowy reaches, initiates find shelter and instruction at Anvilmar. The holdfast lies in Coldridge Valley, forged by hammer, fire, and will. Teo Hammerstorm waits within, teaching fledgling shamans to heed the rumbling earth and begin their elemental duties.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Call of Earth?",a="The Call of Earth summons an aspiring shaman to begin communion with the earth spirits. It directs the initiate to seek guidance and find grounding in the power of living stone.",al={"what is call of earth","call of earth quest","what is this quest"}},{q="Who is Teo Hammerstorm?",a="Teo Hammerstorm teaches initiates inside Anvilmar, the dwarven stronghold in Coldridge Valley. He guides them in communing with the earth and learning its steady strength.",al={"who is teo hammerstorm","where is teo hammerstorm","teo hammerstorm location"}},{q="What is Anvilmar?",a="Anvilmar is a dwarven holdfast in Coldridge Valley, in the snowy reaches of Dun Morogh. Forged by hammer, fire, and will, it is a redoubt where young heroes train.",al={"where is anvilmar","what is anvilmar","anvilmar location"}},{q="Why must a shaman heed the call of earth?",a="A shaman heeds the call of earth to ground their spirit and find firm footing beneath their soles. Communion with stone brings its steady power within reach.",al={"why speak to earth","purpose of call of earth","shaman earth connection"}},{q="Who undertakes this summons?",a="The summons is for shamans beginning their path in Dun Morogh. It directs them to experienced elemental trainers who can guide their bond with the spirits.",al={"who sends call of earth","who takes call of earth","who does this quest"}},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="The journey leads to Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley, within snowy Dun Morogh. Initiates go inside the holdfast to find their mentor.",al={"where does call of earth take place","call of earth zone","where to go"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, heeding the call of earth begins your path, binding you to deep stone and the steadfast spirits of the land.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, your bond with stone and earth can make communion with these spirits feel natural in Dun Morogh’s deep vaults.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance shaman in Dun Morogh, you begin your elemental journey at Anvilmar, the ancestral dwarven stronghold."},kw={"anvilmar","call of earth","coldridge valley","dun morogh","earth totem","elements","shaman","teo hammerstorm"},rel={"subzone:anvilmar","subzone:coldridge-valley","zone:dunmorogh"},m={id=96243},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:96259"] = {t="quest",n="Defending the Dead",z="general",s="At Gloomrise, spiders threaten Mulgore’s people and an ancient tauren burial ground. You are asked to help contain the infestation.",h="At Gloomrise, spiders threaten Mulgore’s people and an ancient tauren burial ground.",sec={{t="The Burial Ground",b="A camp asks you to protect Gloomrise, an ancient tauren burial ground northwest of the camp. Vicious spiders infest the site, threatening Mulgore’s people and damaging a place many tauren hold sacred.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold",b="Your efforts help the people of Mulgore establish a foothold against the spiders. Clearing the infestation completely may take time, so the burial ground remains at risk.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Gloomrise?",a="Gloomrise is an ancient tauren burial ground northwest of the camp.",al={"gloomrise burial ground","where is gloomrise"}},{q="Why is Gloomrise in danger?",a="Vicious spiders infest Gloomrise, threatening Mulgore’s people and damaging the sacred burial ground.",al={"spiders at gloomrise","why defend the dead"}},{q="Why is the burial ground sacred?",a="Many tauren consider Gloomrise sacred.",al={"tauren sacred site","why tauren burial ground"}},{q="Who asks for help?",a="A camp asks you to help protect Gloomrise from its spider infestation.",al={"who needs help","who gave this"}},{q="Has the infestation been cleared?",a="No. Your efforts create a foothold, but clearing the infestation completely may take time.",al={"are spiders gone","gloomrise infestation"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Gloomrise matters as an ancient burial ground that many of your people hold sacred."},kw={"defending the dead","gloomrise","hatchlings","mulgore","soldiers","spiders","tauren burial ground"},rel={"zone:mulgore","topic:tauren"},m={id=96259},src={"In-game quest text: Defending the Dead"},fv=true}
E["quest:96260"] = {t="quest",n="Stronger than Steel",z="general",s="At Gloomrise, a researcher seeks crystalline silk from the spreading giant spiders. The silk may yield a light cloth with strong defenses.",h="At Gloomrise, a researcher seeks crystalline silk from the spreading giant spiders.",sec={{t="Silk for Study",b="A researcher asks you for more crystalline silk after a scout returned from Gloomrise covered in it. Giant spiders have spread across the burial ground, and their venom is rumored to wake the dead. The silk's resilience may make it useful for cloth with defensive strength.",sp=0},{t="A New Weave",b="The samples prove sufficient for the researcher's needs. A cloak woven from silk already on hand is offered to you, with hopes it will aid your travels.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the researcher want?",a="The researcher wants more crystalline silk from the Gloomrise spiders for study.",al={"silk samples","crystalline silk","what silk"}},{q="Where is the silk found?",a="The crystalline silk comes from giant spiders at Gloomrise.",al={"where silk","gloomrise silk","spider silk place"}},{q="Why study the silk?",a="The silk may be made into lightweight, durable cloth with defensive properties.",al={"silk use","what can silk do","why silk"}},{q="What is rumored about the spiders' venom?",a="The spiders' venom is rumored to be strong enough to wake the dead.",al={"spider venom","wake dead","venom rumor"}},{q="What did the scout bring back?",a="One scout returned from investigating Gloomrise covered in resilient, crystalline spider silk.",al={"scout report","scout silk","what happened scout"}}},kw={"cloak","cloth","crystalline silk","gloomrise","spiders","stronger than steel","venom"},m={id=96260},src={"In-game quest text: Stronger than Steel"},fv=true}
E["quest:96261"] = {t="quest",n="The Broodmother",z="general",s="At Gloomrise, the Earthen Ring asks you to stop the spider infestation by confronting its broodmother. The threat puts the people of Mulgore at risk.",h="At Gloomrise, the Earthen Ring asks you to stop the spider infestation by confronting its broodmother.",sec={{t="The Gloomrise Nest",b="The Earthen Ring believes a powerful matriarch is driving the spider infestation at Gloomrise. You are asked to seek out Broodmother Valraxx and destroy her. The spiders seem unlike ordinary spiders, so the Ring warns you to be ready for anything.",sp=0},{t="Troubling Signs",b="Afterward, the Earthen Ring reports reanimated dead and a broodmother with a night elven form. These discoveries trouble them, though they set aside the question of what they mean. They thank you for helping the Ring and Mulgore's people.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is happening at Gloomrise?",a="A spider infestation is spreading at Gloomrise, and the Earthen Ring believes a powerful matriarch is leading it.",al={"gloomrise spiders","spider infestation","what's at gloomrise"}},{q="Who is Broodmother Valraxx?",a="Broodmother Valraxx is the broodmother at Gloomrise whom the Earthen Ring asks you to destroy.",al={"valraxx","broodmother","spider matriarch"}},{q="Why does the Earthen Ring want the broodmother gone?",a="The Ring believes the broodmother is driving the hostile spider population to spread.",al={"why kill broodmother","why valraxx","stop spiders"}},{q="Where is the broodmother?",a="Broodmother Valraxx is at Gloomrise.",al={"valraxx location","where broodmother","gloomrise location"}},{q="What does the Earthen Ring say about these spiders?",a="The Earthen Ring says these seem to be no ordinary spiders.",al={"strange spiders","ordinary spiders","spiders weird"}}},kw={"broodmother","earthen ring","gloomrise","infestation","mulgore","night elven form","spiders","valraxx"},rel={"quest:95349","zone:mulgore"},m={id=96261},src={"In-game quest text: The Broodmother"},fv=true}
E["quest:96264"] = {t="quest",n="Elemental Aid",z="general",s="A shaman is asked to investigate the quilboar gathering in Razorfen Kraul. The earth warns of a ritual, and the elements need aid against those who abuse their power.",h="A shaman is asked to investigate the quilboar gathering in Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="The Earth’s Warning",b="The earth carries a warning to a shaman: the quilboar are gathering in Razorfen Kraul for a ritual of terrible power. Your task is to investigate their kraul and return with information on their plans. The elements lend you their aid, and now they need yours.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the earth warn about?",a="The earth warns that the quilboar are gathering for a ritual of terrible power.",al={"earth warning","what's rumbling","quilboar ritual"}},{q="Where are the quilboar gathering?",a="The quilboar are gathering in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"where to investigate","quilboar location","kraul location"}},{q="Why does the shaman need to help the elements?",a="The elements help the shaman, and the shaman is asked to repay that aid by helping them against those who abuse their power.",al={"help the elements","elemental aid reason","why aid elements"}},{q="What information is needed?",a="You are asked to investigate Razorfen Kraul and bring back information on the quilboar's plans.",al={"what to find","quilboar plans","information needed"}},{q="Who gives the request?",a="The request comes from a speaker who calls you a shaman and says the elements need help.",al={"who asks","quest giver","who needs help"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you have mastered the elements, and this request calls on you to repay their aid."},kw={"charlga razorflank","earth","elemental aid","elements","quilboar","razorfen kraul","ritual","shaman"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","npc:charlga-razorflank","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen","topic:shaman"},m={id=96264},src={"In-game quest text: Elemental Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:96294"] = {t="quest",n="A Darker Truth",z="general",s="Muln Earthfury asks you to bring him a letter recovered at Gloomrise. It may shed light on the spiders there.",h="Muln Earthfury asks you to bring him a letter recovered at Gloomrise.",sec={{t="A Letter at Gloomrise",b="At Gloomrise, you have found that the Broodmother was a night elf druid in a twisted animal form. Questions remain about the spiders and their purpose. A note from her robe may hold answers, so you carry it to Muln Earthfury at Skywatcher Plateau.",sp=0},{t="Muln's Concern",b="Muln Earthfury finds the letter disturbing. It speaks of a “Wild King” and a “Pact,” though he does not know who or what they are. He plans to consult the Cenarion Circle, while taking comfort that the one controlling the spiders is gone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the Broodmother?",a="The Broodmother was a night elf druid who had taken a twisted animal form.",al={"broodmother identity","valraxx who","spider elf?"}},{q="What do I bring to Muln Earthfury?",a="You bring Muln Earthfury the letter recovered from Broodmother Valraxx's robe.",al={"what letter","muln letter","bring what?"}},{q="Where do I take the letter?",a="You take the letter to Muln Earthfury at Skywatcher Plateau.",al={"muln location","where's skywatcher","letter destination"}},{q="What does Muln make of the letter?",a="Muln finds it disturbing and wonders about its references to a “Wild King” and a “Pact.”",al={"muln reaction","why disturbing","letter says what"}},{q="Who will Muln consult?",a="Muln plans to speak with the druids of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"cenarion circle letter","who will he ask","druid council?"}}},kw={"a darker truth","broodmother valraxx","cenarion circle","gloomrise","muln earthfury","night elf druid","pact","skywatcher plateau","spiders","wild king"},rel={"quest:96261","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf","topic:druid"},m={id=96294},src={"In-game quest text: A Darker Truth"},fv=true}
E["quest:96339"] = {t="quest",n="Legacy Reward: Replica Ironforge Air Rifle",z="general",s="A parcel addressed to you waited in a caretaker’s hands until you came to claim it. Inside was a Replica Ironforge Air Rifle, left by a courier whose name is unknown.",h="A parcel addressed to you waited in a caretaker’s hands until you came to claim it.",sec={{t="A Package Awaiting Collection",b="The caretaker kept nothing in storage and had no wish to hold the parcel. The courier insisted you would come for it, then hurried away before the caretaker could refuse. You arrived just before the box was cast into the ocean with the evening’s refuse.",sp=0},{t="Dwarven Engineering in Miniature",b="Inside the parcel is a Replica Ironforge Air Rifle, a tribute to the firearm craft of the dwarven capital. Dwarven mountaineers and marksmen carry deadly weapons through Dun Morogh. Replicas like this recall the intricate barrelwork and pneumatic mechanisms perfected by Ironforge craftsmen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent this package?",a="The courier and original sender gave no name or explanation. The caretaker says someone left a parcel addressed to you, insisted you would claim it, then vanished before questions could be asked.",al={"who sent the package","sender of air rifle","who left the rifle"}},{q="What was almost done to the package?",a="The parcel nearly went into the sea with the nightly garbage. The caretaker said they do not keep things in storage and routinely throw unwanted clutter into the ocean.",al={"what was going to happen to the package","garbage in sea","package thrown away"}},{q="What is inside the parcel?",a="The parcel contains a Replica Ironforge Air Rifle, left for you as a tribute to dwarven firearm design.",al={"what is inside the package","replica rifle contents","package reward"}},{q="Why was the caretaker holding the package?",a="The caretaker does not keep mail or store parcels. The courier hurried away before there was a chance to refuse the delivery.",al={"why did they hold it","holding mail","does this place hold packages"}},{q="Why is this considered a legacy reward?",a="A mysterious benefactor left a special parcel for a seasoned adventurer at an outpost, where it waited to be collected upon arrival.",al={"why is it called legacy reward","legacy reward lore","what does legacy mean here"}},{q="Is the replica rifle a functional weapon?",a="The rifle is a replica of an Ironforge air rifle, modeled after finely engineered dwarven ranged weapons rather than a frontline battle rifle.",al={"is the rifle a real weapon","can you shoot it","replica function"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The parcel holds a replica Ironforge air rifle, honoring the famed firearms and mechanical craft of Khaz Modan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers and gunsmiths may appreciate the intricate firearm model. An indifferent courier brought it, and it nearly ended up at the bottom of the ocean."},kw={"air rifle","ironforge","ironforge air rifle","legacy reward","mysterious package","replica ironforge air rifle"},m={id=96339},src={"In-game quest text: Legacy Reward: Replica Ironforge Air Rifle"},fv=true}
E["quest:96394"] = {t="quest",n="The Restless Dead",z="general",s="Beneath the Hall of Thanes, restless spirits trouble the crypts where generations of dwarven dead lie at rest. The caretakers fear to enter the vaults, and the disturbance has reached the spirit of Anvilmar.",h="Beneath the Hall of Thanes, restless spirits trouble the crypts where generations of dwarven dead lie at rest.",sec={{t="Disturbance in the Deep Vaults",b="Generations of honored dwarves rest in the ancestral crypts beneath the Hall of Thanes. Their spirits usually sleep in peace, but something unseen has stirred them violently. Strange noises rise from the lower vaults and frighten the caretakers. They will not enter those chambers or perform their duties until order returns. Now adventurers are called to quiet the agitated souls.",sp=0},{t="Quieting the Ancestors",b="The spirits in the Hall of Thanes are light sleepers. Whatever disturbed the lower tombs roused Enraged Apparitions and Tormented Souls, turning sacred ground into a perilous haunt. The revered spirit of Anvilmar has awakened as well. A respectful but firm hand must quell the ancestors' fury and restore peace to the catacombs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is The Restless Dead quest about?",a="An unknown disturbance has stirred the spirits in the crypts beneath the Hall of Thanes. The keepers fear to enter while the apparitions remain agitated.",al={"what is the restless dead","what is this quest","restless dead quest overview"}},{q="Why have the spirits awakened?",a="An unknown disturbance in the deep vaults woke the entombed dead. The spirits in the Hall of Thanes are light sleepers, and whatever happened in the tombs roused them to rage and torment.",al={"why are the ghosts angry","who disturbed the tombs","why are apparitions awake"}},{q="Where does this disturbance take place?",a="The disturbance lies in the crypts and vaults beneath Ironforge's Hall of Thanes, an ancestral resting place where ancient dwarven spirits lie entombed.",al={"where is hall of thanes","where do restless dead spawn","hall of thanes location"}},{q="Who is the spirit of Anvilmar?",a="Anvilmar is an ancient and prominent spirit resting in the deep tombs of the Hall of Thanes. This great spirit awakened alongside lesser apparitions and must return to peaceful rest.",al={"who is spirit of anvilmar","spirit of anvilmar lore","who is anvilmar ghost"}},{q="Why do the keepers need an adventurer's help?",a="The keepers care for the crypts and perform their regular duties in the Hall of Thanes. Angry spirits roam the halls, so the keepers refuse to enter the lower vaults until the danger passes.",al={"who are the keepers","why do keepers need help","keepers hall of thanes"}},{q="What spirits haunt the Hall of Thanes?",a="Enraged Apparitions, Tormented Souls, and the great spirit of Anvilmar haunt the disturbed vaults. All were startled into an aggressive vigil within the burial chambers.",al={"what kinds of ghosts are down there","apparitions in hall of thanes","types of restless dead"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Hall of Thanes holds your people's honored dead and ancestors. Their sudden and violent stirring unsettles the heart of dwarven heritage.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you are called to commune with souls and guide troubled dead toward peaceful rest when spirits linger in torment or anger.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure the ancestral crypts beneath Ironforge so the keepers can carry out their sacred duties without fear of vengeful apparitions."},kw={"anvilmar","dwarf tombs","dwarven spirits","enraged apparitions","ghosts","hall of thanes","spirit of anvilmar","the restless dead","tormented souls"},rel={"zone:hallofthanes","subzone:anvilmar"},m={id=96394},src={"In-game quest text: The Restless Dead"},fv=true}
E["quest:96403"] = {t="quest",n="Important Heirlooms",z="general",s="In the Hall of Thanes, Dark Iron dwarves break into the vaults while Thom is caught inside. The nervous gnome asks you to gather the scattered dwarven relics before the invaders reach them.",h="In the Hall of Thanes, Dark Iron dwarves break into the vaults while Thom is caught inside.",sec={{t="Trouble in the Vaults",b="Thom is a gnome caught in the Hall of Thanes when Dark Iron dwarves tunnel up in mole machines. He cannot secure the vaults alone, so he asks passing adventurers to enter the hostile dig site. The dwarven relics lie scattered through the chambers. The invaders may seize or destroy them.",sp=0},{t="Cultural Preservation or Lucrative Plunder?",b="Thom says he was patrolling and wants to catalogue the relics for preservation. Yet he lets slip talk of priceless loot and appraising the haul. He pays you well to face the danger, but whether the treasures will reach a museum or an auction block remains unclear.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thom?",a="Thom is a nervous gnome near the vaults who asks for help retrieving relics. His slips about loot and appraisal suggest he cares more for plunder than vault security.",al={"who is quest giver","who is thom","quest giver"}},{q="What is the Hall of Thanes?",a="The Hall of Thanes is an underground dwarven vault holding ancient cultural relics and heirlooms. Dark Iron forces have breached it.",al={"what is hall of thanes","where is hall of thanes"}},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves in the vaults?",a="Dark Iron dwarves tunneled into the vaults from below in mole machines. Their purpose is unknown.",al={"why dark iron there","dark iron mole machines"}},{q="Is Thom really returning the heirlooms?",a="Thom says he will return the relics to places of honor, but his words raise doubts. He calls lurking patrol and cataloguing appraisal, and speaks of loot and a haul.",al={"is thom lying","does thom steal","thom trustworthy"}},{q="What are the Dwarven Heirlooms?",a="The Dwarven Heirlooms are ancient cultural relics kept in the Hall of Thanes. Historians prize them, while opportunists such as Thom see valuable loot.",al={"what are the heirlooms","dwarven heirlooms lore"}},{q="Why can't Thom retrieve the heirlooms himself?",a="Dark Iron mole machines caught Thom off guard while he was lurking in the vaults. He cannot safely gather the relics without an adventurer's protection.",al={"why does thom need help","why help thom"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Thom's clumsy cover story shows how curiosity can turn toward valuable relics.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may doubt Thom's sudden interest in ancestral relics when he keeps slipping into talk of loot and appraisal.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see through Thom's claim that he was patrolling the vaults. He is a scavenger caught off guard by an underground invasion."},kw={"dark iron","dwarven heirlooms","gnome","hall of thanes","important heirlooms","mole machine","thom","vaults"},rel={"zone:hallofthanes","topic:gnome"},m={id=96403},src={"In-game quest text: Important Heirlooms"},fv=true}
E["quest:96604"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="Brakk welcomes travelers beside his Basic Campfire and teaches them to rest in the wild. From there, they turn to practical crafts.",h="Brakk welcomes travelers beside his Basic Campfire and teaches them to rest in the wild.",sec={{t="Lessons in the Wild",b="Brakk greets aspiring adventurers with a hearty “Lok-tar” and welcomes those seeking fortune and glory. The road through Azeroth’s wilds asks for more than skill at arms; travelers must also endure the elements. Learning to make camp and regain strength is a first step toward surviving out there.",sp=0},{t="From Hearth to Craft",b="Rest beside Brakk’s Basic Campfire brings a restorative pause in the open air and teaches travelers how to recover. Once they know these basics, novice adventurers can visit craftsmen in a nearby village. There, they can study tradeskills and learn to build camp fixtures suited to their chosen craft.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Great Outdoors?",a="Brakk’s lesson teaches new adventurers to rest beside a campfire before taking up a profession.",al={"what is the great outdoors","the great outdoors quest"}},{q="Who is Brakk?",a="Brakk welcomes restless travelers seeking fortune and glory and teaches practical ways to survive in the wild and rest by a campfire.",al={"who is brakk","quest giver"}},{q="What is the Boosted Rest buff?",a="Resting near Brakk’s Basic Campfire grants the Boosted Rest buff and shows how an open flame can help an adventurer recover in the wild.",al={"boosted rest buff","campfire buff"}},{q="What should you do after completing the quest?",a="After learning how to rest in the wild, visit trainers in the nearby village to study a tradeskill and learn to build camp fixtures suited to that craft.",al={"next step after quest","what to do after campfire"}},{q="What are camp fixtures?",a="Camp fixtures are campsite installations taught by profession trainers in nearby villages. They let travelers adapt their camps to support their chosen tradeskills.",al={"camp fixtures","what are camp fixtures"}},{q="Who is this training intended for?",a="This lesson is for restless souls seeking fortune and glory in the wild, especially those just beginning their journey and preparing to choose a trade.",al={"who should do this quest","is this for horde"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="A traditional Orcish “Lok-tar” greets new Horde adventurers as they learn the basics of survival before setting out across treacherous territories."},kw={"boosted rest","brakk","camp fixture","campfire","the great outdoors","tradeskill","wilderness survival"},m={id=96604},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96605"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="At Kaga's wilderness camp, newcomers learn how to rest and recover. From the campfire, they go on to nearby artisans to learn tradeskills and craft camp fixtures.",h="At Kaga's wilderness camp, newcomers learn how to rest and recover.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Wild",b="Kaga shows newcomers how to endure the wilderness beyond civilization. Courage alone cannot keep you safe there. You also need to know how to make camp and withstand the open elements.",sp=0},{t="The Hearth and the Craft",b="Kaga's campfire gives weary travelers a place to rest. Sit beside it to gain the Boosted Rest buff. Once you know how to rest in the wilds, Kaga urges you to visit artisans in a nearby settlement. They can teach you tradeskills and how to craft camp fixtures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Great Outdoors?",a="Kaga teaches newcomers how to survive in the wilderness. She shows them how to rest by a campfire and prepare to learn trades.",al={"what is the great outdoors","the great outdoors quest"}},{q="Who offers this quest?",a="Kaga is a traveler who teaches newcomers the basics of wilderness survival. At her campfire, they can learn to rest and recover.",al={"who is kaga","kaga questgiver"}},{q="What is the Boosted Rest buff?",a="Boosted Rest is the state gained by sitting beside Kaga's Basic Campfire. It reflects the restorative effect of resting at a wilderness camp.",al={"boosted rest","what is boosted rest buff"}},{q="What are camp fixtures?",a="After learning the basics of resting in the wilds, you can learn from artisans in nearby settlements how to craft specialized camp fixtures.",al={"camp fixtures lore","trade camp fixtures"}},{q="Why does Kaga have you sit by the campfire?",a="Learning to make camp and recover stamina helps you survive beyond civilized towns. Sitting by Kaga's campfire lets you gain rested recovery between journeys.",al={"why rest at campfire","campfire resting"}},{q="What should you do after completing this lesson?",a="After learning to rest in the wilds, seek out profession trainers in the nearby village. They can teach you a trade and recipes for trade-specific camp fixtures.",al={"what next after great outdoors","after kaga quest"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Campfires and wilderness survival are the foundation of cooking in the field. Learning camp craft naturally complements your cooking."},kw={"boosted rest","camp fixture","campfire","kaga","survival","the great outdoors","tradeskill","wilderness"},m={id=96605},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96606"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="At Lyreena's campfire, hunters learn how to rest before traveling through the wilds. They can gain the Boosted Rest buff there.",h="At Lyreena's campfire, hunters learn how to rest before traveling through the wilds.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Wild",b="Lyreena is an experienced scout who guides hunters beyond civilization's borders. She welcomes you to rest beside her campfire between hunts. In Azeroth's wilds, knowing how to make camp and regain your strength matters as much as tracking quarry.",sp=0},{t="Campfire Respite",b="A campfire offers warmth and a quiet rest from travel. Sit near the flames to gain Boosted Rest and recover energy for the journey ahead. Rest helps you survive in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lyreena?",a="Lyreena is an experienced scout who guides hunters through the wilderness. She offers practical advice beside her campfire.",al={"who is lyreena","lyreena campfire","quest giver"}},{q="What is The Great Outdoors?",a="At Lyreena's campfire, hunters learn to rest before traveling through the wilds.",al={"what is the great outdoors","what is this quest","the great outdoors quest"}},{q="What is Boosted Rest?",a="Boosted Rest is a benefit you gain by sitting near a campfire. It helps you recover from travel and prepare for the journey ahead.",al={"boosted rest buff","boosted rest campfire","how to get boosted rest"}},{q="Why do you need to rest by a campfire?",a="Resting by a campfire gives you warmth and time to recover. It helps you prepare for dangerous journeys through the wilderness.",al={"campfire purpose","why sit by fire","resting at campfire"}},{q="Why is outdoor survival crucial for hunters?",a="Hunters travel through isolated wilds where taverns and safe towns may be far away. Basic campcraft helps you endure harsh conditions without exhaustion.",al={"hunter survival skills","outdoor survival","why hunter quest"}},{q="What must you do to complete the task?",a="Sit near Lyreena's campfire and wait briefly to gain the Boosted Rest buff.",al={"quest goal","how to finish the great outdoors","great outdoors objectives"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn why wilderness survival and campcraft matter while tracking through the wilds."},kw={"adventurer","boosted rest","campfire","hunter","lyreena","survival","the great outdoors","wilds"},rel={"topic:hunter"},m={id=96606},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96608"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Outdoors",z="general",s="Eric waits by his campfire to teach travelers how to rest in the wild.",h="Eric waits by his campfire to teach travelers how to rest in the wild.",sec={{t="Lessons of the Wild",b="Beyond settled places, ambition and a weapon or holy symbol are not enough. You need to know how to rest amid the elements. Eric has traveled far, and he welcomes you beside his campfire. There, he teaches why proper rest matters before you face the wilds.",sp=0},{t="From Campfire to Craft",b="A campfire begins a useful campsite for a long journey. Once you have learned how to recover in the wild, visit tradeskill trainers in nearby settlements. They can teach you to make camp fixtures for your trade. Then your craft can support your travels wherever the road leads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eric?",a="Eric is a seasoned traveler who teaches newcomers how to survive in the wilderness. He welcomes you beside his campfire and shares advice for life beyond city walls.",al={"who gives this quest","who is eric","who teaches outdoors"}},{q="What is the Boosted Rest buff?",a="Resting beside Eric's campfire gives you the Boosted Rest effect. It helps you recover and prepare for the trials ahead, away from the elements.",al={"what is boosted rest","how does the campfire help","rest buff at camp"}},{q="What are camp fixtures?",a="Camp fixtures are practical structures or tools for specific tradeskills that you can set up in the wild. Trainers in nearby settlements explain how your profession lets you establish a working camp.",al={"what are camp fixtures","profession fixtures","tradeskill camp item"}},{q="Why do you need to sit near Eric's campfire?",a="Sitting beside Eric's campfire gives you time to pause, warm up, and hear his guidance on wilderness survival. Resting there lets you gain the full benefit of shelter outdoors.",al={"why sit at fire","sit near campfire","campfire objective"}},{q="Where should an adventurer go after completing this lesson?",a="After learning to rest at camp, Eric suggests visiting the nearby village. Local trainers can teach you a tradeskill, then show you how to make camp fixtures suited to your craft.",al={"what to do after","where next","after the great outdoors"}},{q="Who is this survival lesson intended for?",a="Eric welcomes passing adventurers with a restless spirit and a readiness to seek fortune and glory across the world. His wilderness guidance can help you leave safety and venture into the open wilds.",al={"who can do this quest","priest only","is this for adventurers"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find your calling in sacred sanctuaries and chapels. Yet life on the road calls for practical survival skills alongside prayers and blessings."},kw={"boosted rest","camp fixture","campfire","eric","survival","the great outdoors","tradeskill","wilderness"},rel={"topic:priest"},m={id=96608},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Outdoors"},fv=true}
E["quest:96626"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="In Goldshire, Cook Tomas shows new travelers how cooking kindles a campfire. With that fire, they can make a simple camp in the wild.",h="In Goldshire, Cook Tomas shows new travelers how cooking kindles a campfire.",sec={{t="The Hearth in the Wild",b="A campfire gives you a place to prepare food and begin a camp in Azeroth's wilds. Learn to cook, and you learn to build that fire. Then an open stretch of wilderness can become a place to camp.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Goldshire",b="In Elwynn Forest, new travelers find Cook Tomas in Goldshire and learn the craft. His instruction gives you the skill to make a basic camp in the wild. At first, your camp holds few furnishings. Greater cooking skill lets you build larger fires, while other crafting trades give you more ways to furnish and shape your campsite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Cooking teaches you to build a basic campfire for a campsite in the wild.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","what does camping 101 teach","purpose of camping 101"}},{q="Who is Tomas and where can he be found?",a="Tomas teaches cooking in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest. Find him at the Lion's Pride Inn, where he teaches the basics of cooking and lighting a campfire.",al={"who is tomas","where is tomas","tomas goldshire"}},{q="Why is cooking required to establish a campsite?",a="Cooking teaches you to build the campfire at the heart of a wilderness camp, where you can rest and arrange furnishings.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","is cooking required to camp","cooking campfire relationship"}},{q="Can you make larger campfires as your skill improves?",a="Greater cooking skill lets you build larger, sturdier fires for your camp in the wild.",al={"how to upgrade campfire","can i build bigger campfires","bigger fires cooking"}},{q="How do you acquire furnishings for your campsite?",a="Other tradeskill trainers teach you ways to make campsite furnishings. Different crafting trades let you create items to decorate and improve a camp in the wild.",al={"how to add camp furnishings","where do camp furnishings come from","crafting camp items"}},{q="Where can an adventurer set up camp?",a="Once you know how to cook and build a campfire, you can make camp in the open wilderness. Your first campsites are modest and hold only a few furnishings until you expand your skills.",al={"can i camp anywhere","wilderness camping rules","camp placement limits"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking teaches you to build basic campfires at the heart of your camps in the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer new to Elwynn Forest, you are directed to Cook Tomas at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire to learn cooking and campfire building."},kw={"campfire","camping","camping 101: cooking","campsite","cooking","furnishings","goldshire","tomas"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={id=96626},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96629"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="In Dun Morogh, travelers learn to cook and make a fire for the wilds. Gremlock Pilsnor teaches novice adventurers in Kharanos. Cooking keeps food ready for the road and helps travelers light campfires at wilderness campsites.",h="In Dun Morogh, travelers learn to cook and make a fire for the wilds.",sec={{t="The Hearth in the Wild",b="Your first camp in Dun Morogh begins with a fire. In Kharanos, Gremlock Pilsnor teaches novice adventurers to cook. The skill keeps food ready for the road. A sturdy campfire gives an outdoor camp its center.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Campsite",b="Once you can build a campfire, you can pitch a humble camp in the open wilderness. A simple fire holds only a few furnishings, but greater cooking skill lets you build larger blazes. Artisans trained in other crafts can make furnishings, turning a basic rest stop into a fully outfitted encampment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Camping 101: Cooking?",a="You learn to cook and build campfires, the first steps toward setting up a wilderness camp.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","quest purpose","camping basics cooking"}},{q="Who is Gremlock Pilsnor?",a="Gremlock Pilsnor teaches novice adventurers to cook in Kharanos, in Dun Morogh.",al={"who teaches cooking in kharanos","gremlock pilsnor location","cooking trainer dun morogh"}},{q="Why is cooking necessary for camping?",a="Cooking teaches you to build a campfire, the base of a wilderness camp and its furnishings.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","campfire purpose","cooking and camps"}},{q="Where can a campsite be established?",a="Once you know how to build a fire, you can pitch a basic campsite in the wilderness and rest there on your travels.",al={"where can i make a camp","campsite rules","setting up camp"}},{q="How do you improve or expand a campsite?",a="Greater cooking skill lets you build larger campfires, while other crafting trades let you make more campsite furnishings.",al={"how to upgrade campsite","bigger fires","more camp decorations"}},{q="Can other professions contribute to camping?",a="Other crafting trades can add furnishings to your campsite when you have learned the skills to make them.",al={"who offers camping furnishings","tradeskill camp items","other camp trainers"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking teaches you to build the campfire needed for a wilderness campsite and its furnishings.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you need basic survival skills like building a fire when you travel far from temples and settlements.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer near Dun Morogh, you learn cooking and wilderness skills from the dwarven instructors in Kharanos."},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","dun morogh","furnishings","gremlock pilsnor","kharanos","wilderness"},rel={"subzone:kharanos","topic:priest"},m={id=96629},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96634"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="In the wild, you begin with cooking and a fire, and trainers such as Zarrin in Dolanaar can teach you the trade. A campfire anchors your camp and opens the way to outdoor survival.",h="In the wild, you begin with cooking and a fire, and trainers such as Zarrin in Dolanaar can teach you the...",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wild",b="When you travel through the wild, a campfire gives you a place to begin. Seek cooking training first. Cooking lets you prepare meals from wild game and teaches you to light a basic campfire. That fire anchors an outdoor camp. Without it to ward off the chill and keep darkness at bay, you cannot make a reliable campsite in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Expanding the Campsite",b="A basic campfire lets you make a modest camp in the wild. It holds only a few simple furnishings, but you can expand your camp as your skills grow. More cooking training teaches you to kindle larger, sturdier fires. Trainers in other trades can teach you to make furnishings and improve your camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Cooking training introduces you to wilderness survival. A campfire anchors your campsite in the wild.",al={"what does this quest do","camping 101 cooking purpose","why do camping 101"}},{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin teaches cooking in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He teaches beginners culinary basics and how to build a basic campfire.",al={"who is zarrin","zarrin dolanaar","where is cooking trainer dolanaar"}},{q="How do you establish a campsite in the wild?",a="Begin by learning to build a basic campfire through cooking training. Basic training lets you make a modest camp in the wild, while further training teaches larger fires and campsite improvements.",al={"how to build camp","how does camping work","making a campsite"}},{q="Can you add furnishings to your campsite?",a="Yes. Cooking gives your camp its anchoring fire, and trainers in other trades teach skilled artisans to make furnishings and improvements for their camps.",al={"furnishing campsite","camp decorations","campsite furnishings other professions"}},{q="Why is cooking required for camping?",a="Cooking teaches you to build and maintain a campfire in the wild. Since fire anchors an outdoor camp, learning to cook is the first step toward wilderness camping.",al={"why need cooking for camping","cooking connection to camping"}},{q="Can you make larger campfires?",a="Yes. More cooking training teaches you to build larger fires for your wilderness camps.",al={"can i make bigger campfires","how to upgrade campfire"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking gives you the campfire that anchors an outdoor campsite. As your cooking skill grows, you can learn to build larger, sturdier fires.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can learn bushcraft and firemaking from Zarrin in Dolanaar before traveling deeper into Teldrassil's wilds."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","campsite","cooking","dolanaar","furnishings","wilderness survival","zarrin"},rel={"npc:zarrin","subzone:dolanaar"},m={id=96634},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96646"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="At Shen'dar Village, Zerril Softbreeze shows you how to kindle a campfire. Camping 101: Cooking teaches you to make a fire and establish a campsite in the wilderness.",h="At Shen'dar Village, Zerril Softbreeze shows you how to kindle a campfire.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wild",b="A campfire gives you a place to rest in untamed lands. Learning to cook begins with making that fire. It is the first step toward establishing a safe campsite.",sp=0},{t="Foundations of the Campsite",b="Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn the fundamentals of cooking. Once you know how to kindle a campfire, you can establish a small campsite in the wilderness. A basic camp has only a few furnishings. As your cooking skill improves, you can kindle larger fires. Other tradeskills help furnish the site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Camping 101: Cooking teaches you to kindle a campfire and establish a campsite in the wilderness.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","camping cooking quest"}},{q="Who is Zerril Softbreeze?",a="Zerril Softbreeze teaches cooking and campfire making in Shen'dar Village.",al={"who is zerril softbreeze","cooking trainer shen'dar"}},{q="Why is cooking required to set up a camp?",a="Cooking teaches you to kindle the campfire at the heart of a wilderness campsite.",al={"why learn cooking for camping","why need cooking for camp"}},{q="Where is Zerril Softbreeze located?",a="Zerril Softbreeze is in Shen'dar Village.",al={"where is zerril softbreeze","shen'dar village location"}},{q="How can campsites be furnished?",a="A basic camp has few furnishings. Other tradeskills let you craft and set up more.",al={"campsite furnishings","how to furnish camp"}},{q="Can campfires be upgraded?",a="As your cooking skill improves, you can kindle larger campfires.",al={"bigger campfires","upgrade camp"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn to kindle a campfire at the heart of a wilderness campsite."},kw={"campfire","camping","campsite","cooking","furnishings","shen'dar village","zerril softbreeze"},m={id=96646},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96655"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="In Razor Hill, Cook Torka shows travelers how to cook and make a campfire. With those skills, they can establish camps in the wild.",h="In Razor Hill, Cook Torka shows travelers how to cook and make a campfire.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wild",b="Beyond a settlement's gates, surviving in the wild takes more than sharp steel and sturdy armor. In Razor Hill, Cook Torka teaches budding adventurers to cook. Across Durotar and beyond, cooking means more than preparing a hot meal. It also teaches travelers to light a reliable campfire, the heart of any campsite.",sp=0},{t="Building and Furnishing a Camp",b="Once travelers know the basics, they can pitch a modest camp almost anywhere on the frontier. A novice campfire supports only a few essential furnishings. Greater cooking skill lets travelers build larger blazes. Other trades teach them to craft what they need to furnish and improve a camp into a reliable shelter from the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Camping 101: Cooking teaches adventurers the basics of outdoor survival. Learning to cook and make a campfire lets them establish camps in the wild.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","camping 101 cooking quest","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who is Cook Torka?",a="Cook Torka is the Horde cooking trainer in Razor Hill, Durotar. He teaches aspiring adventurers cooking basics and how to light a campfire.",al={"who teaches cooking razor hill","who is cook torka","where is cook torka"}},{q="Why is cooking required for camping?",a="Cooking teaches travelers to build the campfire at the heart of a campsite. Without a fire, they cannot maintain a proper campsite in the wilderness.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","cooking campfire connection","does camping require cooking"}},{q="Where can an adventurer set up a campsite?",a="Once you learn the basics of cooking and making a campfire, you can set up a small campsite almost anywhere in the open wilderness. At first, it supports only a few furnishings.",al={"where can i camp","how does camping work","campsite placement"}},{q="How do you upgrade your campfire?",a="As you improve your cooking skill, you can learn to build larger, longer lasting campfires and expand what your campsite can support.",al={"bigger campfires","upgrade campfire","how to improve campsite"}},{q="How do you obtain furnishings for a campsite?",a="Cooking provides the campfire foundation, while other trade trainers across the world teach adventurers to craft and place furnishings for their campsites.",al={"campsite decorations","furnishing camp","camp furnishings trainers"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking is needed to build a basic campfire, the foundation for surviving in the wild and setting up a campsite.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer starting out in Durotar, you can visit Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn the basics of cooking."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","camping 101: cooking","campsite","cook torka","cooking","durotar","furnishings","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={id=96655},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96661"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Cooking",z="general",s="In Bloodhoof Village, Pyall Silentstride begins your lessons in cooking and campfires. Across Kalimdor, those skills help you make a campsite and prepare meals from hunted game.",h="In Bloodhoof Village, Pyall Silentstride begins your lessons in cooking and campfires.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Wild",b="When night falls, a campfire gives you a place to return to. Across Kalimdor, basic cooking teaches you to build a fire in the wild. It also shows you how to prepare nourishing meals from hunted game, making cooking part of surviving outdoors.",sp=0},{t="Building the Camp",b="In Bloodhoof Village, Mulgore, Pyall Silentstride teaches you the basics of cooking. With that training, you can kindle a campfire and pitch a simple camp in the wilderness. As your cooking skill grows, you learn to build larger fires. Other crafts can furnish your outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Cooking?",a="Cooking teaches you to kindle a campfire and establish a campsite in the wilderness.",al={"what is camping 101 cooking","camping cooking quest","camping basics cooking"}},{q="Who is Pyall Silentstride?",a="Pyall Silentstride teaches cooking in Bloodhoof Village, Mulgore. He shows novice adventurers how to cook and build basic campfires.",al={"who is pyall silentstride","pyall silentstride location","bloodhoof cooking trainer"}},{q="Why is cooking necessary to learn camping?",a="Cooking teaches you to kindle a campfire, the practical heart of a campsite, and prepare meals.",al={"why need cooking for camping","why learn cooking to camp","campfire camping connection"}},{q="Can you make bigger campfires as your skill improves?",a="As your cooking skill improves, you learn to build larger fires for more substantial campsites.",al={"can i upgrade campfires","bigger campfires","how to make larger fires"}},{q="How do you furnish a campsite?",a="Other crafts can provide furnishings for your campsite. You can make them if you have learned those crafts.",al={"how do campsite furnishings work","campsite decorations","furnishing campsites tradeskills"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="Once cooking has taught you to kindle a campfire, you can establish a simple camp in the open wilderness wherever you travel.",al={"where to place camp","can i camp anywhere","campsite restrictions"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn to kindle the campfire at the heart of a campsite and prepare food for the wilds.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler in Mulgore, you begin your survival training in Bloodhoof Village, where tauren craftsmen and cooks can guide you."},kw={"bloodhoof village","campfire","camping 101","campsite","cooking","furnishings","pyall silentstride","wilderness"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={id=96661},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Cooking"},fv=true}
E["quest:96773"] = {t="quest",n="The Coldbringer's Eye",z="general",s="The Kirin Tor seeks the Coldbringer’s Eye, a scrying orb used by a servant of the Lich King in Razorfen Downs. You are asked to recover it so the artifact can be studied.",h="The Kirin Tor seeks the Coldbringer’s Eye, a scrying orb used by a servant of the Lich King in Razorfen Downs.",sec={{t="A Kirin Tor Request",b="A servant of the Lich King dwells in Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar lair shelters him. The Kirin Tor says he uses the Coldbringer’s Eye to direct lesser minions elsewhere. You are asked to retrieve the orb for their study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Coldbringer’s Eye?",a="The Coldbringer’s Eye is a scrying orb used by a servant of the Lich King in Razorfen Downs.",al={"coldbringer eye","what's the eye","scrying orb"}},{q="Who wants the Coldbringer’s Eye?",a="The Kirin Tor wants the Coldbringer’s Eye so it can study the artifact and understand how it works.",al={"who wants the orb","kirin tor eye","who asked for it"}},{q="Where is the Coldbringer’s Eye?",a="The Coldbringer’s Eye is in Razorfen Downs.",al={"where's the eye","razorfen downs orb","eye location"}},{q="Who uses the orb?",a="A servant of the Lich King in Razorfen Downs uses the orb to direct lesser minions elsewhere.",al={"who has the eye","lich king servant","coldbringer user"}}},kw={"coldbringer","coldbringer's eye","kirin tor","lich king","quilboar","razorfen downs","scrying orb","servant"},rel={"subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:razorfen","topic:quilboar","topic:lich-king"},m={id=96773},src={"In-game quest text: The Coldbringer's Eye"},fv=true}
E["quest:96783"] = {t="quest",n="A Way In",z="general",s="A Syndicate trade draws you toward Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands. You need a disguise from Northfold Manor to enter without suspicion.",h="A Syndicate trade draws you toward Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Hidden Trade",b="A contact sends you to Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands, where the Syndicate holds important dealings behind its walls. Word has reached them of a trade between Syndicate members, and its details may be inside the keep. To enter without arousing suspicion, you need a Syndicate uniform from Northfold Manor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is happening at Stromgarde Keep?",a="The Syndicate uses Stromgarde Keep as one of its largest strongholds, and a trade between its members is taking place somewhere in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"stromgarde trade","what's at stromgarde","syndicate keep"}},{q="Why am I going to Northfold Manor?",a="You are looking for a Syndicate uniform at Northfold Manor to disguise yourself before entering Stromgarde Keep.",al={"northfold manor","why northfold","get disguise"}},{q="What do I need to enter the keep?",a="You need a Syndicate uniform from Northfold Manor to enter Stromgarde Keep without arousing suspicion.",al={"uniform","syndicate disguise","way into stromgarde"}},{q="What is the Syndicate trade about?",a="The trade is between Syndicate members somewhere in the Arathi Highlands. Its details may be found inside Stromgarde Keep.",al={"syndicate deal","what trade","trade details"}}},kw={"a way in","arathi highlands","northfold manor","stromgarde keep","syndicate","trade","uniform"},rel={"subzone:northfold-manor","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:syndicate"},m={id=96783},src={"In-game quest text: A Way In"},fv=true}
E["quest:96800"] = {t="quest",n="Past Due",z="general",s="A scholar needs a missing tome from the Scarlet Monastery to study Grim Batol’s ancient Wildhammer runemasters.",h="A scholar needs a missing tome from the Scarlet Monastery to study Grim Batol’s ancient Wildhammer...",sec={{t="An overdue book",b="The old Dalaran library’s ledgers show that Arcanist Doan borrowed the tome before the Third War and never returned it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who needs the book?",a="A scholar writing a thesis on the ancient Wildhammer runemasters of Grim Batol needs the book for that research.",al={"who wants the tome","scholar research"}},{q="What book was borrowed?",a="The borrowed book is called The Lost Magic of the Runemasters.",al={"which tome","lost runemasters book"}},{q="Who borrowed the book?",a="The old Dalaran library’s ledgers say a mage named Doan borrowed the book before the Third War.",al={"who checked it out","Doan book"}},{q="Where is the book?",a="The book is in the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, where Arcanist Doan is now.",al={"where's the tome","book location"}},{q="What is the research about?",a="The scholar is researching the ancient Wildhammer runemasters of Grim Batol.",al={"wildhammer runemasters","Grim Batol thesis"}}},kw={"arcanist doan","dalaran library","grim batol","past due","scarlet monastery","the lost magic of the runemasters","wildhammer runemasters"},rel={"subzone:grim-batol","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage"},m={id=96800},src={"In-game quest text: Past Due"},fv=true}
E["quest:96821"] = {t="quest",n="Legging It",z="general",s="The peons have halted their southward travel because dangers line the road. Their work waits until the way is safe again.",h="The peons have halted their southward travel because dangers line the road.",sec={{t="Securing the Line",b="Peons have left their assigned work undone and stopped traveling south. Perils along the road have made the journey too dangerous. Once the threats are pushed back, overseers can send their crews to work again.",sp=0},{t="Labor and Route Security",b="Peons do much of the Horde’s hard labor, from harvesting timber and quarrying to building outposts. They have little skill in battle, so roadside predators or hostile scouts can halt the movement of supplies. Clear routes keep settlements supplied and let the work continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Legging It?",a="Dangers along the road have frightened peons away from traveling south. Their duties wait until the way is safe.",al={"what is legging it","legging it quest info","legging it quest"}},{q="Why were the peons afraid to travel south?",a="The peons fear the dangers along the southern road. Without protection or a clear path, they refuse to travel to their assignments, bringing local work to a halt.",al={"why were peons scared","peon fear","why peons stopped working"}},{q="What is accomplished by completing the task?",a="When the southern route is clear and immediate dangers are pushed back, overseers can send peons to gather resources and work in the field.",al={"what happens after legging it","legging it outcome","clearing path result"}},{q="Who are the peons mentioned in the task?",a="Peons are the Horde’s labor force. They harvest lumber, mine, and build fortifications. They are essential to settlements but poorly suited to combat, and readily retreat from danger.",al={"who are the peons","peon role","what do peons do"}},{q="Where were the peons traveling?",a="The peons were traveling south along a path toward outlying work areas and resource deposits that need regular care. The journey had become dangerous enough to stop all traffic.",al={"where does the path lead","southern path","heading south"}},{q="Why do peons require adventurers to clear their routes?",a="Peons lack military training and combat gear, leaving them vulnerable to wilderness predators and hostile forces. Overseers rely on experienced adventurers to clear threats and keep work routes safe.",al={"why do peons need protection","peon safety","guarding peons"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde construction and resource gathering rely heavily on peons, so their routes need to stay safe.",["race:Orc"]="Peons do much of the work in orcish settlements. Overseers rely on warriors to clear threats from their paths so work can continue."},kw={"cleared the path","horde labor","legging it","overseer","peon labor","peons","southern path"},m={id=96821},src={"In-game quest text: Legging It"},fv=true}
E["quest:96822"] = {t="quest",n="For Honor",z="general",s="Fallen warriors live on in memory through For Honor. Their sacrifices endure in the minds of those who remember them.",h="Fallen warriors live on in memory through For Honor.",sec={{t="A Duty of Remembrance",b="Those who outlive fallen warriors carry their memory forward. Remembering those who gave everything is a duty.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Legacy",b="Your efforts keep the fallen fighters alive in memory. Those who remember them continue to honor their sacrifices.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest For Honor about?",a="For Honor asks you to remember fallen fighters. Your efforts keep their sacrifices from fading.",al={"what is for honor","for honor quest overview"}},{q="Who are the warriors mentioned upon completion?",a="The warriors are fallen fighters honored for their deeds. Your actions preserve their memory and the service they gave.",al={"who are the warriors","who is remembered"}},{q="Why is honoring these warriors important?",a="Remembering fallen warriors gives their sacrifice dignity. It keeps their courage acknowledged.",al={"why do this quest","for honor meaning"}},{q="Who asks for this task to be done?",a="Someone seeking to remember fallen comrades directs the work. When you return, they confirm it is done and acknowledge the warriors' memory.",al={"who gives for honor","quest giver for honor"}},{q="Does this quest lead to other tasks?",a="Nothing points to further work. For Honor honors fallen fighters and their sacrifices.",al={"is for honor part of a chain","what follows for honor"}},{q="What does the title For Honor signify?",a="For Honor names the duty of remembering fallen soldiers. Keeping their sacrifice and battlefield memory alive is a solemn duty for any fighter.",al={"what makes it honorable","meaning of for honor"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the weight of battlefield sacrifice. Remembering fallen combatants keeps their deeds alive."},kw={"fallen warriors","for honor","honor","memorial","quest","remembrance","warrior"},rel={"topic:warrior"},m={id=96822},src={"In-game quest text: For Honor"},fv=true}
E["quest:96825"] = {t="quest",n="This Fruit Could Bite Back",z="general",s="In Durotar, prickly pears feed Orgrimmar and promise more food ahead. Gathered with care, these hardy fruits can nourish the Horde capital and provide seeds for future crops.",h="In Durotar, prickly pears feed Orgrimmar and promise more food ahead.",sec={{t="Harvesting the Arid Wastes",b="Durotar is rugged and sun-baked, where traditional farming is nearly impossible. Its hardy prickly pears thrive in the arid soil, so inhabitants gather them to help feed Orgrimmar. Their protective spines call for care, and their fruit brings needed nourishment.",sp=0},{t="Cultivation and Sustenance",b="Prickly pears feed people now and can help supply food in the years ahead. Their flesh is prepared for dishes, while their seeds are carefully preserved for planting. The aim is to grow this resilient crop around Orgrimmar, creating a lasting food source close outside the fortress walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is This Fruit Could Bite Back?",a="You gather wild prickly pears in Durotar for cooking and save their seeds to plant across the dry land around Orgrimmar.",al={"what is this fruit could bite back","this fruit could bite back quest","bite back fruit quest"}},{q="Why are prickly pears being gathered?",a="Prickly pears provide food for local meals, and their seeds are saved for planting. The aim is to grow them across the arid land around Orgrimmar.",al={"why gather prickly pears","prickly pear purpose","what are prickly pears for"}},{q="Where will the seeds be planted?",a="The seeds are meant to be planted throughout the outskirts and lands around Orgrimmar, where they can help establish a resilient food supply in the harsh desert soil.",al={"where grow prickly pears","prickly pear planting orgrimmar"}},{q="Who wants these fruits gathered?",a="A local resident wants the harvest to improve local food stores, feed travelers, and grow crops suited to Durotar's harsh desert climate.",al={"who wants the prickly pears","quest giver bite back"}},{q="Why does the fruit 'bite back'?",a="Prickly pears have sharp spines and needles like other hardy desert cacti, so gatherers must take care.",al={"why bite back","why does fruit bite back"}},{q="Why is planting fruit around Orgrimmar important?",a="Durotar is mostly arid and rocky, making conventional farming difficult. Drought-tolerant prickly pears could help provide a lasting food supply for Orgrimmar.",al={"does orgrimmar lack food","orgrimmar agriculture","durotar farming"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know sustainable food sources like hearty desert fruits can help feed Orgrimmar and the Horde's growing population.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can prepare prickly pears into dishes, and the fruit can also supply city residents.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know how hardy desert plants can be and how much effort it takes to gather spiny wild fruits for cultivation."},kw={"cactus fruit","durotar","fruit","orgrimmar","prickly pear","prickly pears","seeds","this fruit could bite back"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=96825},src={"In-game quest text: This Fruit Could Bite Back"},fv=true}
E["quest:96874"] = {t="quest",n="This Is Spinal Axe",z="general",s="Ug’thok in Orgrimmar asks you to gather spines from the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge. He hopes to shape them into an axe head for your smithing lessons.",h="Ug’thok in Orgrimmar asks you to gather spines from the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge.",sec={{t="A smith’s idea",b="Ug’thok asks you to bring five Weathered Spines and five Rough Grinding Stones. He believes the spines could make a fine axe head, though Saru laughed at the idea.",sp=0},{t="Tough material",b="The spines are tougher than Ug’thok expected, which may make them difficult to work. He plans to keep shaping the design.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the spines?",a="Ug’thok in Orgrimmar asks you to gather Weathered Spines and Rough Grinding Stones.",al={"who wants spines","ugthok axe","smithing lesson"}},{q="What does Ug’thok want to make?",a="Ug’thok hopes to make an axe head from the beasts’ spines.",al={"spine axe","what is he crafting","axe head idea"}},{q="Where do the spines come from?",a="The Weathered Spines come from the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge.",al={"where are spines","thunder ridge beasts","spine location"}},{q="What else does Ug’thok need?",a="Ug’thok asks for Rough Grinding Stones along with the spines.",al={"grinding stones needed","what materials","rough stones"}},{q="Why does Ug’thok want the materials?",a="Ug’thok wants to try making an axe head from the spines as part of your smithing lessons.",al={"why spines","what are they for","ugthok materials"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a smithing student, you help Ug’thok gather materials for an axe head he hopes to make."},kw={"axe head","orgrimmar","rough grinding stones","saru","smithing","thunder ridge","ug’thok","weathered spines"},rel={"subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:orgrimmar","quest:96875"},m={id=96874},src={"In-game quest text: This Is Spinal Axe"},fv=true}
E["quest:96875"] = {t="quest",n="Beasts of Thunder Ridge",z="general",s="Across Durotar, Orgrimmar's builders need hides to keep the growing capital strong. Kamari sends you to Thunder Ridge for lizard hides and cured light hides.",h="Across Durotar, Orgrimmar's builders need hides to keep the growing capital strong.",sec={{t="A Growing Capital",b="Orgrimmar keeps growing as the Horde makes a home in Durotar. New homes, workshops, and defenses need lumber, stone, and animal skins. Timber comes from farther away, but Durotar's beasts provide sturdy hides for the peons and builders.",sp=0},{t="Beasts of the Canyon",b="The lizards of Thunder Ridge have tough hides, too thick and stiff for wearable armor. Properly harvested, their pelts line the walls and ceilings of Orgrimmar's timber and stone buildings. There, they shield the interiors from the harsh sun and sudden canyon winds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Orgrimmar need lizard hides from Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge lizard hides are too thick and coarse for wearable armor, but their toughness suits them for building. Orgrimmar's peons line new walls and roofs with the hides to guard against the elements.",al={"what are the hides for","why rough lizard hide","what are thunder ridge hides used for"}},{q="Who is Kamari?",a="Kamari is a leatherworker in Orgrimmar who supplies sturdy pelts and hides to the city's builders and peons. The hides are needed for ongoing construction.",al={"who is kamari","kamari orgrimmar","who gives beasts of thunder ridge"}},{q="Where is Thunder Ridge located?",a="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon in Durotar, where lizards have thick hides Kamari wants for Orgrimmar's new buildings.",al={"where is thunder ridge","thunder ridge location","thunder ridge durotar"}},{q="Why are cured light hides requested along with lizard hides?",a="Kamari requests cured light hides alongside the heavy lizard hides to complement those materials. The request also tests your broader familiarity and skill with leather processing.",al={"why cured light hides","what are the cured hides for"}},{q="Why is Orgrimmar expanding so rapidly?",a="Orgrimmar is the newly established Horde capital, and its ongoing construction must house growing numbers of orcs and their allies. That growth creates a constant need for raw materials.",al={"why is orgrimmar building","orgrimmar expansion"}},{q="Can the lizard hides from Thunder Ridge be made into armor?",a="Thunder Ridge lizard hides are generally too thick and rigid for flexible armor. Their chief practical use is in construction.",al={"can you wear lizard hides","is rough lizard hide armor"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde settles in Durotar, supplies from the wilderness help fortify and grow Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know that Durotar's elements call for rugged materials gathered by hunters and laborers."},kw={"beasts of thunder ridge","cured light hide","durotar","kamari","leatherworking","orgrimmar","peons","rough lizard hide","thunder ridge"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:thunder-ridge"},m={id=96875},src={"In-game quest text: Beasts of Thunder Ridge"},fv=true}
E["quest:96876"] = {t="quest",n="Ukor's Lost Pack",z="general",s="In southern Durotar, Ukor's Lost Pack lies abandoned in the wilds. Its owner fled a huge spider and left his supplies behind.",h="In southern Durotar, Ukor's Lost Pack lies abandoned in the wilds.",sec={{t="A Lost Belonging",b="In southern Durotar, you find a traveling bag with Ukor's name crudely stitched across its flap. In these harsh lands, discarded gear may point to trouble nearby.",sp=0},{t="Fleeing the Wilds",b="Ukor receives his pack in southern Durotar and tells how he lost it. A huge spider ambushed him, and he fled in panic, certain his supplies were gone. Finding the bag intact earns you Ukor's heartfelt gratitude and praise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor lives in southern Durotar. When a huge spider confronted him in the wilds, he abandoned his belongings to escape.",al={"who is ukor","ukor durotar"}},{q="Why did Ukor lose his pack?",a="Ukor dropped his pack while fleeing a huge spider in Durotar. He thought his belongings were gone for good until you found the bag.",al={"why was pack lost","where did ukor lose pack"}},{q="Where does the pack need to be taken?",a="Take the recovered pack to Ukor in southern Durotar, where he waits to greet returning travelers.",al={"where to return pack","ukor turn in"}},{q="How is the pack identified?",a="Ukor's name is crudely stitched across the bag's flap.",al={"how is pack identified","pack stitching"}},{q="What kind of creature chased Ukor?",a="A huge spider ambushed Ukor in southern Durotar. Terrified, he dropped his possessions and ran for safety.",al={"spider in durotar","what spider attacked ukor"}},{q="What happens when you return the pack to Ukor?",a="Ukor is astonished and deeply grateful to see his belongings again. He calls you a true hero for retrieving the bag.",al={"ukor reward","how does ukor react"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a young Horde adventurer in southern Durotar, you can help locals like Ukor by recovering belongings lost to dangerous wildlife."},kw={"durotar","horde","lost pack","southern durotar","spider","ukor","ukor's lost pack"},rel={"npc:ukor","zone:durotar"},m={id=96876},src={"In-game quest text: Ukor's Lost Pack"},fv=true}
E["quest:96877"] = {t="quest",n="Halikor's Hoof",z="general",s="In the wilds, Halikor's Hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of a hunter's triumph. The enormous severed hoof honors the hunter's victory over the formidable lizard.",h="In the wilds, Halikor's Hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of a hunter's triumph.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Mighty Beast",b="Halikor's vast size is plain in the hoof taken from its remains. Hunters and warriors in the wilds have long claimed a piece of a formidable beast to prove the kill. The hoof leaves no doubt of the lizard's great size and strength.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Capital",b="The heavy hoof is carried to Orgrimmar to announce the beast's defeat to the Horde. Strength and survival against the land's harsh predators matter in this warrior society. Presenting the trophy honors the hunter and assures the capital that a dangerous creature has been slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Halikor?",a="Halikor is a formidable lizard of immense size. Hunters claim its severed hoof as proof that the beast was slain.",al={"what is halikor","who is halikor","halikor lizard"}},{q="Why must the hoof be delivered to Orgrimmar?",a="The hoof is carried to Orgrimmar as proof of the beast's defeat and the hunter's triumph.",al={"why bring hoof to orgrimmar","halikor hoof deliver","where does the hoof go"}},{q="How is Halikor's Hoof obtained?",a="You claim Halikor's Hoof from the lizard's body after tracking down and slaying it in combat.",al={"how to get halikors hoof","halikor drop"}},{q="Why does a lizard have a hoof?",a="Halikor is a mighty beast of the wilds, and its enormous hoof proves you brought it down. No one has said why it bears a hoof.",al={"does halikor have hooves","why does a lizard have hooves"}},{q="Who in Orgrimmar wants Halikor's Hoof?",a="You carry the hoof to Orgrimmar as proof of your victory. No particular hunter or official is named to receive it.",al={"who accepts halikors hoof in orgrimmar","turn in halikor hoof orgrimmar"}},{q="What is the story behind the quest Halikor's Hoof?",a="The mighty lizard Halikor is slain, and its enormous severed hoof is carried to Orgrimmar. The trophy shows the hunter's prowess and brings the Horde word of the beast's death.",al={"what is halikors hoof quest","halikors hoof story"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Carrying proof of a mighty beast's defeat to Orgrimmar honors Horde traditions of strength and hunting prowess.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, bringing down the enormous Halikor shows the skill of the tracker and the thrill of the hunt."},kw={"halikor","halikor's hoof","horde","hunt","lizard","orgrimmar","trophy"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=96877},src={"In-game quest text: Halikor's Hoof"},fv=true}
E["quest:96895"] = {t="quest",n="The Argent Emissary",z="general",s="In Tirisfal Glades, two Argent Dawn emissaries hunt Scourge cultists near the Undercity. Both are Forsaken, yet local authorities distrust an armed neutral order in their territory.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, two Argent Dawn emissaries hunt Scourge cultists near the Undercity.",sec={{t="Wary Welcome",b="Two Forsaken emissaries of the Argent Dawn have recently reached Tirisfal Glades. Their arrival puts local authorities on edge. The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge, but the Forsaken distrust an armed neutral order acting without oversight in their territory. Even their shared heritage does little to ease that wariness.",sp=0},{t="Cultists at the Gates",b="The emissaries pursue Scourge cultists southeast of the Undercity, near its outskirts. They mean to root out the Lich King's agents before the cultists gain a foothold. One emissary watches their movements from near the city gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Argent emissaries?",a="Two Argent Dawn emissaries have recently come to Tirisfal Glades. Both are Forsaken who joined the holy, neutral order instead of serving only the Undercity.",al={"who are the emissaries","argent dawn visitors","who came to tirisfal"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn operating near the Undercity?",a="The emissaries track Scourge cultists seen near the outskirts southeast of the Undercity. The Argent Dawn hunts Scourge remnants wherever they appear, even near major Horde settlements.",al={"why are they near undercity","argent dawn mission tirisfal","what are emissaries doing"}},{q="Why are local Forsaken wary of the emissaries?",a="Local Forsaken distrust an armed neutral order operating without supervision in Tirisfal Glades. That wariness remains even when its emissaries share their undead condition.",al={"why nervous about argent dawn","can we trust argent dawn","forsaken view of argent dawn"}},{q="What is the threat posed by the cultists?",a="A cell of Scourge cultists has been seen lurking southeast near the city's outskirts. The Lich King remains a threat to free undead, so local scouts and the Argent Dawn have taken notice.",al={"cultists outside undercity","scourge in tirisfal","who are the cultists"}},{q="Where did the emissary go?",a="One emissary moved near the Undercity entrance to watch Scourge cultists operating just outside the city walls.",al={"where to find emissary","emissary location","find argent dawn member"}},{q="Do the Forsaken serve in the Argent Dawn?",a="Yes. The Argent Dawn welcomes anyone willing to fight the Scourge, including free-willed undead who devote themselves to the cause. The Scarlet Crusade does not.",al={"are forsaken allowed in argent dawn","argent dawn undead","can undead join argent dawn"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Argent Dawn is neutral, but Horde authorities watch its independent operations near the Undercity with care.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you can see fellow undead choose the Argent Dawn over the Undercity. Their choice shows divided loyalties among the free undead."},kw={"argent dawn","argent emissary","cultists","forsaken","scourge cultists","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:undercity","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},m={id=96895},src={"In-game quest text: The Argent Emissary"},fv=true}
E["quest:96896"] = {t="quest",n="A Righteous Cause",z="general",s="Leonid Barthalomew the Revered and Danitha Morr meet again to remember the Undercity's defense against Naxxramas. They speak of Garek Bandarion, a fallen undead hero who found the Holy Light again as a paladin, and of the Forsaken who carry his path onward.",h="Leonid Barthalomew the Revered and Danitha Morr meet again to remember the Undercity's defense against...",sec={{t="Reunion of Veterans",b="Leonid Barthalomew the Revered and Danitha Morr meet again after defending Lordaeron together. They survived Naxxramas's assault on the Undercity, though many comrades fell. Now they remember the dead and the hard road faced by Forsaken who still honor the Holy Light.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Garek Bandarion",b="Leonid and Danitha remember Garek Bandarion, the fallen hero whose name was given to the keep. Leonid believes Garek may have been the first Forsaken to wield the Holy Light again as a true paladin. Most Forsaken have turned from the Light. Danitha and her cohort keep Garek's legacy alive and explore what holy unlife may allow.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Plaguelands",b="After speaking with Danitha, Leonid prepares to leave the keep and return to the fight against the Scourge in the ravaged east. He is stationed at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands. There, he welcomes able-bodied adventurers ready to take up arms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Leonid Barthalomew the Revered?",a="Leonid Barthalomew the Revered is an undead member of the Argent Dawn. He works from Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands and keeps ties with former comrades in Lordaeron who fought beside him against the Scourge.",al={"who is leonid barthalomew","leonid the revered","leonid barthalomew lore"}},{q="Who is Danitha Morr?",a="Danitha Morr is a Forsaken leader who fought beside Leonid Barthalomew during the Scourge attack on the Undercity. She leads a cohort that carries on Garek Bandarion's teachings and holy legacy.",al={"who is danitha morr","danitha","danitha morr lore"}},{q="Who was Garek Bandarion?",a="Garek Bandarion was a Forsaken fighter who fell defending the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. Leonid believes he may have been the first Forsaken to wield the Holy Light again as a paladin.",al={"who is garek bandarion","garek bandarion lore","keep named after"}},{q="What happened during the attack on the Undercity?",a="When Naxxramas, a necropolis, attacked the Undercity, Forsaken champions including Danitha Morr, Leonid Barthalomew, and Garek Bandarion joined the city's defense against the Scourge. They suffered heavy losses.",al={"undercity naxxramas attack","defense of undercity","scourge attack undercity"}},{q="Can the Forsaken wield the Light as paladins?",a="Most Forsaken reject the Light, which brings excruciating pain to undead flesh. Garek Bandarion showed that an undead warrior can wield the Holy Light as a paladin. Danitha's cohort continues to study the practice.",al={"can forsaken be paladins","undead paladin lore","forsaken light wielders"}},{q="Where does Leonid Barthalomew go after this?",a="After visiting his friends and speaking with Danitha Morr, Leonid plans to return to Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands. The Argent Dawn coordinates its fight against the Scourge there.",al={"where is leonid going","find leonid later","lights hope chapel leonid"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Garek Bandarion and Danitha's cohort mark a rare path: Forsaken rediscovering how to wield the Holy Light as paladins despite their undead state.",["race:Undead"]="Leonid and Danitha seek a path back to the Light, though most Forsaken remain distant from or hostile to holiness in their unlife.",["faction:Horde"]="Leonid Barthalomew links the defenders of the Undercity with the Argent Dawn at Light's Hope Chapel in the Plaguelands."},kw={"danitha morr","forsaken","garek bandarion","leonid barthalomew","light's hope chapel","naxxramas","paladin","righteous cause","scourge","undercity"},rel={"topic:paladin","topic:light","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge"},m={id=96896},src={"In-game quest text: A Righteous Cause"},fv=true}
E["quest:96897"] = {t="quest",n="The Cult of the Damned",z="general",s="In Tirisfal Glades, living servants of the Scourge threaten the people once more. By culling Dark Neophytes and Dark Enforcers, you help keep the Lich King's agents from repeating the betrayals that shattered Lordaeron.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, living servants of the Scourge threaten the people once more.",sec={{t="Mortal Agents of the Scourge",b="The Scourge has living servants who swear fealty to the Lich King. They serve where the mindless dead cannot. In Tirisfal Glades, people already face roaming undead and the relentless zealots of the Scarlet Crusade. Now, newly discovered cells of Dark Neophytes and Dark Enforcers show the Scourge seeking a foothold again.",sp=0},{t="Lessons of the Fall",b="The marching dead were not the only cause of Lordaeron's fall. Neighbors betrayed neighbors as the Cult of the Damned infiltrated villages and poisoned granaries. From the shadows, they helped bring the kingdom down. Fresh Cult activity in Tirisfal threatens to repeat that history in the scarred lands of the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cult of the Damned?",a="The Cult of the Damned is made up of mortals who willingly serve the Lich King and the Scourge. These living acolytes spread plague, sabotage defenses, and practice necromancy by choice instead of being raised as mindless undead.",al={"what is cult of the damned","who are the cultists","who are dark neophytes"}},{q="Why are members of the Cult operating in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Tirisfal Glades remains contested, haunted by mindless undead, Scarlet Crusade zealots, and surviving Scourge influence. The Cult works in secret to undermine local resistance and advance the Scourge's dark designs.",al={"why are cultists in tirisfal","cult in tirisfal glades"}},{q="Who are the Dark Neophytes and Dark Enforcers?",a="Dark Neophytes are new initiates learning dark arts and rituals. Dark Enforcers guard the Cult's operations and enforce discipline. Together, they make up active cells in the region.",al={"who are dark enforcers","dark neophytes role"}},{q="Why are living servants considered worse than mindless undead?",a="Mindless undead act by instinct or direct command, while living cultists knowingly choose treachery. They can blend into mortal societies and infiltrate settlements, making them more insidious than roaming ghouls or skeletons.",al={"why living cultists worse","living servants scourge"}},{q="What does the quest mean by not letting Lordaeron's history repeat itself?",a="Lordaeron fell not only to invasion, but also when the Cult of the Damned poisoned grain and betrayed fellow citizens from within. If cultists gain a foothold, the same catastrophe could follow.",al={"lordaeron history repeat","fall of lordaeron cult"}},{q="How does the Cult relate to the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal?",a="The Scarlet Crusade fanatically hunts anything tainted by undeath, so the Scourge and the Cult are its targets. Their conflict leaves local inhabitants caught between mindless horrors, zealous crusaders, and covert cultists.",al={"scarlet crusade relation","cult vs scarlet crusade"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know how living cultists laid waste to Lordaeron and brought about your undeath. Stopping new Cult cells in Tirisfal helps secure your new kingdom.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you recognize how the Cult of the Damned twists faith. Its members trade sacred devotion for dark necromancy.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you swore to eradicate the shadow that broke Lordaeron. Living cultists devoted to the Scourge are sworn enemies of the Light."},kw={"cult of the damned","dark enforcers","dark neophytes","living servants","lordaeron","necromancy","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal","topic:lordaeron","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:381"},m={id=96897},src={"In-game quest text: The Cult of the Damned"},fv=true}
E["quest:96898"] = {t="quest",n="Remnants of War",z="general",s="Across Tirisfal Glades, remnants of war lie scattered beneath the soil. Naxxramas was driven from the Undercity at great cost to the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn. Its shattered necrotic focusing crystal remains a danger, and Scourge cultists seek its fragments for the dark magic within.",h="Across Tirisfal Glades, remnants of war lie scattered beneath the soil.",sec={{t="The Shadow Over the City",b="Naxxramas once loomed over Tirisfal Glades, seeking to wipe out the Undercity and the Forsaken. The Forsaken and the Argent Dawn fought off the floating fortress in a desperate defense. Both sides suffered heavy losses. During the battle, the immense necrotic focusing crystal atop Naxxramas was destroyed, scattering fragments across the glades.",sp=0},{t="Scattered Necromancy",b="Naxxramas was driven away, but pieces of its crystal remain in the soil. Scourge cultists search for the fragments, hoping to use the dark magic still within them. Gathering the shards keeps that power from the Scourge. Yet clearing every fragment from Tirisfal will take years.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the necrotic crystal fragments?",a="The necrotic crystal fragments are pieces of the great focusing crystal once mounted atop Naxxramas. The crystal was destroyed during the assault on the Undercity, and shards fell across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what are necrotic crystal fragments","what are the crystals","necrotic crystals"}},{q="Why did Naxxramas attack the Undercity?",a="Naxxramas came to Tirisfal Glades to destroy the Undercity and wipe out the Forsaken. The Forsaken and the Argent Dawn fought it off, though both suffered heavy losses.",al={"why naxxramas attack","naxxramas undercity attack","what did naxxramas do here"}},{q="Why are Scourge cultists collecting the crystal fragments?",a="Scourge cultists search Tirisfal Glades for the shattered fragments because necrotic magic remains within them. They hope to reclaim that power for the Scourge.",al={"why do cultists want the crystals","what do cultists want with shards","scourge cultists crystals"}},{q="Is handling the necrotic crystals dangerous?",a="Yes. Though broken and largely drained of their original charge, the fragments still hold volatile necrotic energy. Direct contact is dangerous.",al={"are the crystals dangerous to touch","crystal physical contact","can necrotic crystals hurt you"}},{q="Who helped the Forsaken fight off Naxxramas?",a="The Forsaken fought beside the Argent Dawn to defend the Undercity from Naxxramas. Both suffered heavy losses in the battle.",al={"who fought at naxxramas","who defended undercity","argent dawn undercity defense"}},{q="Will all the necrotic crystals ever be cleared from Tirisfal?",a="Clearing every crystal fragment from Tirisfal will take years. The crystal shattered above the glades and scattered shards far and wide. Residents will keep finding them in the soil.",al={"will tirisfal be clean of crystals","can they clear all the fragments","crystals left in tirisfal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know Naxxramas threatened the Undercity itself. Recovering the fragments helps protect your people from Scourge power on their doorstep.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Tirisfal Glades from lingering Scourge magic. You protect the Undercity and the Horde's foothold in northern Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, handle Naxxramas's broken necrotic crystals with care. Unstable magical energy remains within them.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you face the unholy corruption lingering in the shards. It threatens to defile the land further."},kw={"argent dawn","cultists","forsaken","naxxramas","necrotic crystal fragments","remnants of war","scourge","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:argent-dawn"},m={id=96898},src={"In-game quest text: Remnants of War"},fv=true}
E["quest:96899"] = {t="quest",n="Bandarion Keep",z="general",s="At Bandarion Keep, Commander Leonid Barthalomew waits for travelers in western Tirisfal Glades. The Argent Dawn once held the secluded fortress against the Scourge, and Danitha and her paladins now guard its walls.",h="At Bandarion Keep, Commander Leonid Barthalomew waits for travelers in western Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Keep",b="After you aid the Argent Dawn against Cult of the Damned activity, you are sent northwest across Tirisfal Glades. Commander Leonid Barthalomew waits at the fortress to speak with you about the order's ongoing crusade against darkness.",sp=0},{t="History and Stewardship",b="The Argent Dawn once used the stronghold as a staging post against Scourge incursions across Tirisfal Glades. Then the order turned its focus to the Eastern and Western Plaguelands. The fort was left behind and began to decay, until Paladin Danitha and her companions took stewardship of its walls.",sp=0},{t="Memories of a Mutual Friend",b="Leonid Barthalomew remembers the battles fought from the fortress ramparts. He is relieved the stronghold has not fallen into neglect. Danitha named it for a mutual friend.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Leonid Barthalomew?",a="Leonid Barthalomew commands the Argent Dawn. He once used Bandarion Keep as a base during Scourge incursions into Tirisfal Glades. Now he has returned to meet Danitha and her paladins.",al={"who is leonid barthalomew","where is leonid barthalomew","leonid bandarion keep"}},{q="What is Bandarion Keep?",a="In western Tirisfal Glades, Bandarion Keep is a fortress the Argent Dawn once held against Scourge assaults. The order withdrew to the Plaguelands and left the fort in disrepair. Danitha's paladins restored it and now hold it.",al={"what is bandarion keep","bandarion keep history","who holds bandarion keep"}},{q="Who is Danitha?",a="Danitha is a paladin who took stewardship of Bandarion Keep with her order after the Argent Dawn withdrew east to the Plaguelands. She named the keep for a mutual friend she shared with Leonid Barthalomew.",al={"who is danitha","danitha paladin","who runs bandarion keep"}},{q="Why is it called Bandarion Keep?",a="Danitha named the fortress for a mutual friend known to her and Commander Leonid Barthalomew.",al={"why was it named bandarion keep","who is bandarion","bandarion name meaning"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn interested in Bandarion Keep?",a="The Argent Dawn journeys to Bandarion Keep to coordinate with Danitha's paladins. Together they guard against Scourge forces and Cult of the Damned activity across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why go to bandarion keep","argent dawn tirisfal glades","bandarion keep argent dawn"}},{q="Why did the Argent Dawn previously abandon the keep?",a="The Argent Dawn left Bandarion Keep when it shifted its main forces east to battle the Scourge in the Plaguelands. The fort stood empty until Danitha and her paladins took it in hand.",al={"what happened to the keep after the war","why did argent dawn leave bandarion keep"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find Bandarion Keep under Danitha's care. Her fellow paladins hold its walls as a holy bastion against dark forces in Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"argent dawn","bandarion keep","cult of the damned","danitha","leonid barthalomew","paladin","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:argent-dawn","zone:tirisfal","topic:paladin","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:scourge","quest:96897","quest:376"},m={id=96899},src={"In-game quest text: Bandarion Keep"},fv=true}
E["quest:96984"] = {t="quest",n="Heart of Disruption",z="general",s="Magus Wordeen Voidglare lets you past his wards into Dalaran to seek an Arcane Mote. He fears the city’s fall could bring catastrophe to the Undercity as well.",h="Magus Wordeen Voidglare lets you past his wards into Dalaran to seek an Arcane Mote.",sec={{t="A Key Through the Wards",b="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill sends you into Dalaran with a key he has imbued to pass his wards. He fears that if the city falls, the Undercity will be threatened too. Find the Arcane Mote and meet him at the Violet Citadel, where this began; preventing catastrophe comes first.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Dalaran?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill sends you into Dalaran to find an Arcane Mote.",al={"who gave me this","Wordeen Voidglare","who is the magus"}},{q="Why am I going to Dalaran?",a="You are sent to find an Arcane Mote. Wordeen fears Dalaran’s fall could bring the Undercity down with it.",al={"why Dalaran","what am I looking for","Dalaran task"}},{q="How do I get past Wordeen's wards?",a="Wordeen imbues your key so it can pass his wards and let you enter the city.",al={"the key","Dalaran key","get past wards"}},{q="Where should I meet Wordeen?",a="Wordeen asks you to meet him at the Violet Citadel in Dalaran, where this began.",al={"meet the magus","Violet Citadel","where is Wordeen"}},{q="What is Wordeen's first priority?",a="Wordeen says preventing a catastrophe comes first.",al={"prevent catastrophe","what matters most","first priority"}}},kw={"arcane mote","dalaran","heart of disruption","magus wordeen voidglare","tarren mill","undercity","violet citadel","wards"},rel={"zone:undercity","subzone:dalaran","subzone:tarren-mill"},m={id=96984},src={"In-game quest text: Heart of Disruption"},fv=true}
E["quest:96986"] = {t="quest",n="The Grave Knight",z="general",s="In Tarren Mill, Melisara sends you after Atrexis, who raises the dead beneath Dalaran. She sees his work as an affront to the Forsaken.",h="In Tarren Mill, Melisara sends you after Atrexis, who raises the dead beneath Dalaran.",sec={{t="Melisara's Charge",b="Melisara calls Atrexis a traitor to the Forsaken. Beneath Dalaran, he raises an undead army. She asks you to defeat him, though she cares little for the mage city's fate. No one is beyond the Dark Lady's reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Grave Knight?",a="Atrexis is a necromancer in Dalaran, whom Melisara calls the Grave Knight.",al={"atrexis","atrexis grave knight","grave knight who"}},{q="Who sent me after Atrexis?",a="Melisara in Tarren Mill asks you to defeat Atrexis.",al={"who gave grave knight quest","melisara atrexis","who wants atrexis dead"}},{q="Why does Melisara want Atrexis defeated?",a="Melisara calls Atrexis a traitor to the Forsaken because he raises an undead army beneath Dalaran.",al={"why kill atrexis","why grave knight","forsaken reason atrexis"}},{q="Where is Atrexis?",a="Atrexis is in the City of Dalaran.",al={"atrexis location","grave knight location","where grave knight"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Melisara cares little for Dalaran's fate as she sends you after Atrexis.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know Melisara calls Atrexis a traitor to the Forsaken. She says his undead army defies what the Forsaken stand for."},kw={"atrexis","dalaran","forsaken","grave knight","melisara","necromancer","tarren mill","undead army"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dalaran","topic:forsaken","topic:mage"},m={id=96986},src={"In-game quest text: The Grave Knight"},fv=true}
E["quest:96987"] = {t="quest",n="Opportunistic Education",z="general",s="Rexxie Copperclutch asks you to fetch a tome from Dalaran’s library while its mages are occupied. She hopes to sell the book and share the profit with you.",h="Rexxie Copperclutch asks you to fetch a tome from Dalaran’s library while its mages are occupied.",sec={{t="A Book for Rexxie",b="Rexxie Copperclutch, near the sewer entrance, sees a chance to profit from Dalaran’s library. While its mages are occupied, she asks you to bring her the tome called Founding of Dalaran. She offers to split whatever it sells for.",sp=0},{t="The Book’s Worth",b="Rexxie judges the book you bring back to be worth little. She considers disguising it with gold spray and claiming it belonged to an archmage.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the book?",a="Rexxie Copperclutch, near Dalaran’s sewer entrance, asks you to bring her a tome from the city’s library.",al={"who wants the tome","rexxie copperclutch","who is rexxie"}},{q="Which book does Rexxie want?",a="Rexxie asks for Founding of Dalaran.",al={"what book","founding of dalaran","tome name"}},{q="Why does Rexxie want the tome?",a="Rexxie hopes to sell the tome and share the profit with you.",al={"why steal book","what's the book for"}},{q="Where is the book supposed to come from?",a="Rexxie asks you to find Founding of Dalaran in the City of Dalaran.",al={"where get tome","dalaran library","book location"}},{q="What is happening with Dalaran’s mages?",a="Rexxie says the mages are occupied while she asks you to look for a book.",al={"mages busy","why opportunistic","dalaran mages"}},{q="What does Rexxie think of the book you bring?",a="Rexxie judges the book to be worth little and considers spraying it with gold to make it seem valuable.",al={"is book valuable","what happens to tome","rexxie reaction"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, Rexxie calls you like-minded and welcomes you into her scheme."},kw={"dalaran","founding of dalaran","library","mages","opportunistic education","rexxie copperclutch","tome","undead"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","topic:mage"},m={id=96987},src={"In-game quest text: Opportunistic Education"},fv=true}
E["quest:96988"] = {t="quest",n="Source of Power",z="general",s="In Dalaran, rogue constructs have turned on their makers, and Doctor Martin Felben sees a chance for the Forsaken. He wants their arcane cores for his work in Undercity and hopes to catch the Dark Lady’s eye.",h="In Dalaran, rogue constructs have turned on their makers, and Doctor Martin Felben sees a chance for the...",sec={{t="An Opportunistic Harvest",b="Dalaran’s rogue arcane constructs are laying siege to the magi, and the Forsaken are eager to exploit the city’s turmoil. Doctor Martin Felben, an apothecary in Undercity, seeks to scavenge the cores that power the sentries rather than aid the besieged sorcerers. Dalaran has long guarded its magical research, but its vulnerable sentries now offer an opening to opportunistic researchers.",sp=0},{t="Ambition in the Apothecary Society",b="Doctor Felben wants the cracked sentry cores to advance his standing within the Royal Apothecary Society. He hopes to infuse Forsaken abominations with volatile Dalaran construct magic and raise a devastating army of arcane-powered flesh beasts. Such a breakthrough, he believes, would win Lady Sylvanas Windrunner’s undivided attention and show his alchemical genius. He hopes to rise in the Society, where ruthless cunning and potent results dictate survival and rank.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Source of Power?",a="Doctor Martin Felben gives it. He is an apothecary residing in Undercity, the Forsaken capital, and seeks to prove his alchemical talents to the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner by creating new military monstrosities.",al={"who gives source of power","source of power quest giver","martin felben quest"}},{q="What is happening in Dalaran during this quest?",a="Dalaran is under siege by its own arcane constructs, which have turned against their creators. The fighting creates an opening for outsiders to enter the city and salvage the magical components powering the rogue sentries.",al={"what happened in dalaran","dalaran under siege","why are constructs attacking dalaran"}},{q="Why does Doctor Felben want the construct cores?",a="Doctor Felben wants to use the arcane energy in Dalaran’s sentry cores to augment Forsaken abominations. By synthesizing arcane machinery with fleshcraft, he hopes to create an army of arcane-powered abominations and prove his alchemical mastery to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"why collect sentry cores","what does felben need cores for","felben sentry core plan"}},{q="What are the objectives for Source of Power?",a="You are sent into Dalaran to confront the rogue constructs and gather six Cracked Sentry Cores. Then you bring them to Doctor Martin Felben in Undercity for his ongoing experiments.",al={"source of power objectives","how many cores do i need","what to collect for source of power"}},{q="What is Doctor Felben's goal within the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="Doctor Martin Felben seeks recognition and rapid advancement among the Forsaken. He hopes a formidable force of arcane-infused abominations will impress Lady Sylvanas Windrunner enough for her to name him head of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"felben apothecaries goal","who leads the royal apothecary society","felben dark lady recognition"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken scavenging Dalaran's technology?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society and the Forsaken seek unconventional weapons and power sources to ensure their survival in Lordaeron. While Dalaran’s defenses collapse from within, Forsaken apothecaries can take its sophisticated arcane components without formally engaging the magi in open warfare.",al={"why forsaken want dalaran magic","undercity dalaran constructs","forsaken interest in dalaran"}},{q="Where are the Cracked Sentry Cores found?",a="Cracked Sentry Cores come from rogue constructs laying siege to Dalaran. You gather them from the hostile enchanted guardians across the city for Doctor Felben’s research in Undercity.",al={"where to find cracked sentry cores","cracked sentry core location","dalaran sentry core drops"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken rely on the Royal Apothecary Society’s ruthless innovations to survive in Lordaeron. Helping Doctor Felben advances the faction’s arcane fleshcraft research under the Dark Lady’s watch.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers in Lordaeron support the Forsaken’s efforts to secure advanced military assets against their rivals while Dalaran is crippled by its rogue creations.",["class:Mage"]="Mages may find grim irony in Dalaran’s constructs turning on their masters, while their arcane power sources are plundered for gruesome experiments in Undercity.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the craft behind Dalaran’s autonomous sentries, even as their delicate arcane cores are torn out to fuel horrific fleshcraft abominations."},kw={"abominations","arcane constructs","cracked sentry core","dalaran","doctor martin felben","royal apothecary society","source of power","sylvanas windrunner","undercity"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:dalaran","zone:undercity"},m={id=96988},src={"In-game quest text: Source of Power"},fv=true}
E["quest:97003"] = {t="quest",n="Chol'aruk the Ravener",z="general",s="In the Barrens, Gur'ak sends travelers after a colossal quilboar called Chol'aruk the Ravener. He believes the tales and asks them to return with its head.",h="In the Barrens, Gur'ak sends travelers after a colossal quilboar called Chol'aruk the Ravener.",sec={{t="The Legend of the Ravener",b="Razormane quilboar whisper of Chol'aruk, an enormous terror they call The Ravener. They say it lairs deep in a cavern at Thorn Hill, northeast of the local trails. By their account, it is roughly five times the size of an ordinary quilboar and driven by an unquenchable thirst for blood. Many dismiss the tales as campfire exaggeration. Gur'ak knows better from past battles with similar beasts.",sp=0},{t="Gur'ak's Warning",b="Gur'ak knows a beast of such size poses a real danger. He directs capable travelers to track Chol'aruk to its lair in Thorn Hill, end its threat, and bring back its head as proof. The Ravener is said to be ferocious and colossal. Gur'ak warns that only well-prepared groups should enter the cave to face it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chol'aruk the Ravener?",a="The Razormane call Chol'aruk an enormous quilboar known as The Ravener. They say it is roughly five times the size of an ordinary quilboar, thirsts endlessly for blood, and lairs in a deep cave in the Barrens.",al={"who is cholaruk","what is cholaruk","the ravener"}},{q="Where can Chol'aruk be found?",a="Chol'aruk lairs deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of Gur'ak's encampment in the Barrens. Travelers must enter Thorn Hill's caverns to reach it.",al={"where is cholaruk","cholaruk location","where is thorn hill cave"}},{q="Who offers the hunt for Chol'aruk?",a="Gur'ak, an orc in the Barrens, sends travelers after Chol'aruk. He believes the rumors because he has faced similar beasts before.",al={"who gives cholaruk quest","who is gurak","gurak barrens"}},{q="Why is Gur'ak hunting Chol'aruk?",a="Gur'ak wants Chol'aruk destroyed because it terrorizes the region. He asks for the beast's severed head as proof that the Ravener has fallen.",al={"why kill cholaruk","cholaruk bounty reason"}},{q="Should I fight Chol'aruk alone?",a="Gur'ak warns travelers not to face Chol'aruk alone. Its reported size and bloodlust make it a formidable foe, so he calls for a prepared hunting party.",al={"can i solo cholaruk","is cholaruk hard","bring group for cholaruk"}},{q="What is the connection between Chol'aruk and the Razormane quilboar?",a="The Razormane quilboar speak of Chol'aruk with dread and call it The Ravener. The Razormane are a quilboar tribe living in parts of the Barrens, and quilboar are boar-like humanoids native to central Kalimdor.",al={"what are quilboar","razormane cholaruk","why razormane fear him"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Gur'ak, an orc, calls Horde travelers to hunt a dangerous menace in the Barrens with the battle cry Blood and thunder.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, tracking a beast said to be five times larger than an ordinary quilboar calls for keen instincts and preparation for formidable prey.",["class:Warrior"]="As a Warrior, you face a brutal creature with an unquenchable bloodlust. Be ready to brace against its overwhelming physical fury."},kw={"barrens","chol'aruk","cholaruk","gur'ak","gurak","quilboar","razormane","the ravener","thorn hill"},rel={"zone:barrens","subzone:thorn-hill","topic:quilboar"},m={id=97003},src={"In-game quest text: Chol'aruk the Ravener"},fv=true}
E["quest:97220"] = {t="quest",n="Philmor's Favor",z="general",s="A delicate shipment is bound for the Gatehouse in Stormwind under Philmor's Favor. With dockhands scarce, travelers carry it to a stockroom entrance above Trias' Cheese in the Trade District.",h="A delicate shipment is bound for the Gatehouse in Stormwind under Philmor's Favor.",sec={{t="Strained Logistics in Stormwind",b="Stormwind's freight handlers are short of dockhands, and ordinary cargo schedules are strained. They rely on trustworthy travelers to carry sensitive crates into the city's commercial quarter and keep deliveries moving.",sp=0},{t="Discreet Deliveries at Trias' Cheese",b="The Gatehouse shipment is bound for an unusual destination. Carry the crate to the second floor of Trias' Cheese in the Trade District, where a concealed entrance opens onto a stockroom. Supplies and ceremonial gifts for the guard's officers pass through there, beyond prying eyes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who needs help with this delivery?",a="Stormwind's freight handlers need help keeping cargo schedules on track while dockhands are scarce.",al={"who gives philmor's favor","philmor quest giver"}},{q="Where is the delivery destination?",a="Take the shipment to the Gatehouse stockroom entrance on the second floor of Trias' Cheese in Stormwind's Trade District.",al={"where do i take the package","trias cheese delivery","where is the gatehouse entrance"}},{q="Who receives the shipment?",a="Elaine, mistress of Trias' Cheese, handles discreet cargo bound for the nearby Gatehouse stockroom.",al={"who is elaine","elaine trias cheese"}},{q="What is inside the Gatehouse shipment?",a="The shipment holds delicate goods for the Gatehouse. Local handlers use discretion with deliveries tied to ceremonial surprises for guard officers.",al={"what is in the package","gatehouse delivery contents"}},{q="Why is a military stockroom accessed through a cheese shop?",a="Trias' Cheese has an upstairs access point to the Gatehouse stockroom, letting cargo pass discreetly without using the main military entrance.",al={"why trias cheese gatehouse","secret entrance trias cheese"}},{q="Why are dockhands in short supply?",a="Dockside and cargo handlers are short-handed throughout the week, so logistics coordinators rely on travelers to keep deliveries on schedule.",al={"why short dockhands","stormwind dockhands shortage"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep deliveries moving through Stormwind's Trade District while dockhands are scarce."},kw={"elaine","gatehouse","gatehouse shipment","philmor","philmor's favor","stormwind","trade district","trias' cheese"},rel={"subzone:trade-district"},m={id=97220},src={"In-game quest text: Philmor's Favor"},fv=true}
E["quest:97222"] = {t="quest",n="Gatehouse Goods",z="general",s="In Stormwind, Gatehouse Goods moves from Trias' Cheese to the neighboring gatehouse. The route takes the shipment up the shop's stairs to a landing on the same floor, where guards can collect it outside the stockroom. Shared quarters link the city's shops and defenses.",h="In Stormwind, Gatehouse Goods moves from Trias' Cheese to the neighboring gatehouse.",sec={{t="Shared Quarters and Shared Floors",b="Couriers carry a gatehouse shipment up the stairs inside Trias' Cheese. The cheese shop is a separate business with its own inventory, yet its building shares a floor with the neighboring gatehouse. From the upper landing, couriers can move supplies between the two quarters without using the front avenues.",sp=0},{t="A Practical Drop-off",b="The crate is left outside the stockroom door rather than carried inside. Gatehouse guards watch for deliveries and arrange for someone to collect each package when returning to their posts. The door opens inward, so a crate outside will not block the entry or hinder anyone inside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Gatehouse Goods?",a="Gatehouse Goods is a Stormwind delivery between Trias' Cheese and the neighboring gatehouse. A courier carries the shipment upstairs and leaves it outside the gatehouse stockroom door.",al={"what is gatehouse goods","gatehouse goods quest"}},{q="Where is the shipment supposed to be delivered?",a="The shipment goes up the stairs inside Trias' Cheese. Though the shop is a separate business, its building shares a floor with the gatehouse, and the crate is left outside the stockroom.",al={"trias cheese gatehouse","where is delivery going"}},{q="Why is the crate left outside the door instead of brought inside?",a="The courier is told to leave the crate outside the stockroom. Gatehouse guards watch for deliveries and arrange for someone to carry them in when returning to their posts.",al={"why not deliver inside","who picks up the crate"}},{q="Why does the stockroom door open inward?",a="The stockroom door opens inward, so goods left outside will not block the doorway or hinder people inside.",al={"inward door trias","stockroom door hinge"}},{q="Is Trias' Cheese affiliated with the gatehouse?",a="No. Trias' Cheese is a separate business with its own inventory, though it shares a floor with the gatehouse.",al={"is trias cheese part of gatehouse","trias cheese stock"}},{q="Who oversees the delivery of the goods?",a="Local operators arrange the delivery and expect professional respect and discretion. After a successful drop-off that leaves the threshold clear, they acknowledge reliable couriers.",al={"who gives gatehouse goods","who accepts the delivery"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help move goods between Stormwind shopkeepers and the neighboring gatehouse through discreet deliveries at Trias' Cheese.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how to move quietly around Trias' Cheese and notice details like doors that open inward."},kw={"delivery","elling trias","gatehouse goods","gatehouse shipment","stockroom","stormwind","trias cheese"},m={id=97222},src={"In-game quest text: Gatehouse Goods"},fv=true}
E["quest:97223"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodtalon Matriarch",z="general",s="Near Sen'jin Village, handlers face a threat from the Bloodtalon Matriarch as they seek her young. Her pack is prized for speed and cunning, but adults resist taming. The Darkspear seek to secure her clutch and raise loyal companions from the egg.",h="Near Sen'jin Village, handlers face a threat from the Bloodtalon Matriarch as they seek her young.",sec={{t="The Bloodtalon Lineage",b="Along Durotar's coast, Bloodtalon raptors are prized for speed and cunning. Handlers in Sen'jin Village value those traits in dependable mounts and companions for the Darkspear tribe. Yet full-grown raptors have stubborn, violent instincts. Once grown, wild adults are scarcely tamed.",sp=0},{t="Preserving the Bloodline",b="Repeated attempts to capture and train the Matriarch have only made her more aggressive. Now she threatens the surrounding territory. The trolls seek to protect their tribe and preserve her bloodline. They must quell the dangerous mother and save her clutch, so the next generation can be raised from the egg as loyal allies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Bloodtalon Matriarch?",a="The Bloodtalon Matriarch is a fierce adult raptor whose pack is known for speed and cunning. Attempts to capture and train her failed as she grew too dangerous to handle. The Darkspear trolls seek to secure her eggs.",al={"who is bloodtalon matriarch","bloodtalon raptor matriarch","matriarch raptor"}},{q="Why must the Bloodtalon Matriarch be dealt with?",a="The Matriarch has become a danger to the surrounding territory, and adult raptors are difficult to tame. By quelling her and securing her clutch, handlers in Sen'jin Village can protect the tribe and preserve her bloodline.",al={"why kill matriarch","why capture eggs","why hunt the matriarch"}},{q="Why not tame the Matriarch instead?",a="Full-grown raptors have stubborn, violent instincts and are nearly impossible to tame. Handlers can raise the young from eggs as loyal companions instead.",al={"can you tame adult raptors","train adult raptor"}},{q="What will happen to the Matriarch's offspring?",a="The captured clutch is brought to Sen'jin Village to be incubated and raised. The trolls plan to train the young raptors from infancy as reliable allies and mounts for the tribe.",al={"what happens to the eggs","matriarch children","raptors in senjin"}},{q="Where is this quest centered?",a="The work centers near Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar. There, handlers seek to raise loyal raptors for the Darkspear tribe.",al={"where is this quest handed in","senjin village raptor quest"}},{q="What makes the Bloodtalon pack special?",a="The Bloodtalon pack is prized for speed and cunning. Those traits make its young desirable as companions and mounts, while full-grown raptors resist taming.",al={"bloodtalon raptor traits","why bloodtalon raptors"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know Sen'jin Village's handlers prize raptors as agile companions and war mounts. The Bloodtalon line is valued for cunning and speed.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that raising local predators as loyal allies helps protect the Darkspear settlement and strengthen the Horde's presence on the Durotar coast.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know how hard it is to tame a seasoned adult beast. Raising a predator from birth can forge a true bond."},kw={"bloodtalon","darkspear","matriarch","raptor","raptor eggs","raptors","sen'jin village","senjin","troll mounts"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village"},m={id=97223},src={"In-game quest text: Bloodtalon Matriarch"},fv=true}
E["quest:97225"] = {t="quest",n="Forgotten Loa Idols",z="general",s="The Darkspear seek the Forgotten Loa Idols so their sacred rites can continue. The relics preserve the tribe’s bond with its patron spirits.",h="The Darkspear seek the Forgotten Loa Idols so their sacred rites can continue.",sec={{t="Sacred Remnants of the Loa",b="The Darkspear honor the loa through sacred rites. These primal animal spirits and wild gods belong to the trolls’ ancestral heritage. The lost idols are needed for ceremonies in their honor. Without them, spiritual leaders cannot perform the rites that keep the tribe in harmony with its divine guardians.",sp=0},{t="The Darkspear Bond",b="The Darkspear approach the loa with respect and humble reverence. Other hostile troll factions across Azeroth practice blood sacrifice or try to command spirits by force. Losing their patrons’ favor would be a grave catastrophe for the Darkspear. So restoring the idols is vital to preserving the tribe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Forgotten Loa Idols?",a="The Darkspear need the missing sacred idols so their tribal rituals can resume and they can honor their wild spirits.",al={"forgotten loa idols","what is this quest","what is forgotten loa idols"}},{q="What are loa?",a="The loa are powerful, ancient primal spirits and animal deities revered by trolls. Trolls honor them with offerings, prayer, and ritual ceremonies, seeking protection, favor, and spiritual guidance.",al={"what are loa","troll gods","who are the loa"}},{q="How do the Darkspear view their loa compared to other troll tribes?",a="The Darkspear meet the loa with deep reverence, mutual respect, and a sense of spiritual duty. They believe their survival depends on keeping the spirits’ favor.",al={"darkspear loa relationship","why revere loa","other tribes loa"}},{q="Why are the idols needed for tribal rituals?",a="The idols are sacred objects needed for tribal rites. Without them, elders and spiritual leaders cannot properly commune with and honor their patron spirits.",al={"why need idols","loa idols purpose","why are idols important"}},{q="Why is keeping the loa's favor so vital to the Darkspear?",a="The Darkspear fear that without proper rites and offerings, they could lose the loa’s favor and protection, leaving the tribe vulnerable in a perilous world.",al={"what happens if not returned","falling out of favor","darkspear loa favor"}},{q="Who seeks the return of the Forgotten Loa Idols?",a="A Darkspear spiritual guide seeks the idols’ return and is anxious to resume communal ceremonies and secure blessings from the tribe’s ancestral patrons.",al={"who gives forgotten loa idols","quest giver","who asks for idols"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, communion with the loa is central to your spiritual life. Lost idols let vital rituals continue and help keep the tribe in the spirits’ good graces.",["class:Priest"]="As a troll priest, you rely on rituals and sacred items from your ancestors to channel spiritual power and honor the loa.",["class:Shaman"]="As a troll shaman, you invoke elemental forces while honoring the wild gods and ancestral loa tied to your tribe’s survival.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you belong to a faction whose foundational members include the Darkspear. Helping their holy elders preserve vital religious artifacts strengthens tribal unity."},kw={"darkspear","forgotten loa idols","idols","loa","reverence","rituals","spirits","troll"},m={id=97225},src={"In-game quest text: Forgotten Loa Idols"},fv=true}
E["quest:97234"] = {t="quest",n="Reading Room",z="general",s="At Roy's Book Club, members trade older literature for newer works from the Stormwind library. Wrapped books carry the exchange between the club and the librarian.",h="At Roy's Book Club, members trade older literature for newer works from the Stormwind library.",sec={{t="Literary Pursuits in Stormwind",b="Roy's Book Club gathers readers in Stormwind to discuss classical legends and provocative writings. To keep those talks fresh, members rotate their reading. They trade older or less popular works for newer volumes from the city's library.",sp=0},{t="The Library Exchange",b="Roy's Book Club keeps an established lending arrangement with the Stormwind library. Roy wraps the club's returned books in a distinctive way, and you carry them to the librarian. In return, the club receives a new list of modern tomes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Reading Room quest?",a="Roy's Book Club trades older books for modern tomes from the Stormwind library. You carry a wrapped bundle of less popular works to the library for the exchange.",al={"reading room quest","what is reading room","reading room story"}},{q="Who is Roy?",a="Roy runs a reading club where members discuss legends and literature. He arranges with the Stormwind library to rotate reading material and returns borrowed books in pristine condition.",al={"who is roy","roys book club","book club leader"}},{q="Where are the books being taken?",a="The books go to the library in Stormwind. The librarian recognizes Roy's club's distinctive wrapping and accepts the books in exchange for modern writing.",al={"where do books go","stormwind library drop off","wrapped reading material delivery"}},{q="Why are the books being exchanged?",a="The club trades less popular books for more modern and thought-provoking works through its borrowing arrangement with the city library.",al={"why trade books","why return tomes","exchange reading material"}},{q="How does the Stormwind librarian view the book club?",a="The Stormwind librarian is pleased with the arrangement. Roy's club returns loaned books in excellent condition and treats every text with care, even when its subject is provocative.",al={"what does librarian think","is book club allowed","library arrangement"}},{q="What are the club refreshments mentioned?",a="The club offers free refreshments to patrons and helpers who assist with book exchanges between the reading venue and the city archives.",al={"complimentary club refreshments","club perks","what refreshments"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can visit the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep. Civic and scholarly exchanges help sustain the city's intellectual life."},kw={"books","legends","librarian","reading room","roy's book club","stormwind library","tomes"},rel={"quest:579","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=97234},src={"In-game quest text: Reading Room"},fv=true}
E["quest:97236"] = {t="quest",n="Fang of Githyiss",z="general",s="Near Aldrassil, Githyiss’s hunt brings a rare specimen to the sanctuary. Scholars can study the giant spider’s fang and watch for predators in Shadowglen.",h="Near Aldrassil, Githyiss’s hunt brings a rare specimen to the sanctuary.",sec={{t="A Monstrous Specimen",b="Githyiss threatens travelers in Shadowglen’s wilds. The giant spider’s fang matters both as a danger and as a specimen worth studying. Scouts carry it through the underbrush to the sanctuary beneath the great tree.",sp=0},{t="Research in Aldrassil",b="In Aldrassil, night elf naturalists and scholars watch the wildlife on the forest floor. A fresh, intact fang from a spider as large as Githyiss can teach them about arachnids beneath Teldrassil’s canopy. Researchers welcome the find as they study the glade’s aggressive creatures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fang of Githyiss?",a="The fang is a fresh specimen from the great spider Githyiss. Its size gives researchers rare material to study arachnid predators near Aldrassil.",al={"what is fang of githyiss","githyiss fang quest","fang of githyiss item"}},{q="Who or what is Githyiss?",a="Githyiss is a large, dangerous spider that prowls the forests near Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Its size threatens travelers and draws the interest of local naturalists.",al={"who is githyiss","githyiss spider","where is githyiss"}},{q="Who wants the Fang of Githyiss?",a="A scholar in Aldrassil who studies spiders wants the fang. Fresh specimens help researchers learn more about local arachnids.",al={"who turns in fang of githyiss","where do i bring the fang","spider researcher aldrassil"}},{q="Where is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is Shadowglen’s great bough and central sanctuary, within the crown of the world tree Teldrassil. Young night elves train and find shelter there.",al={"where is aldrassil","aldrassil location"}},{q="Why are scholars in Aldrassil studying spider fangs?",a="Aldrassil’s scholars and naturalists study local spiders to understand Shadowglen’s ecology and watch the aggressive, oversized beasts beneath Teldrassil’s canopy.",al={"why do they study spiders in aldrassil","why study spider fangs"}},{q="Can Horde players turn in the Fang of Githyiss?",a="No. Shadowglen, the night elf starting enclave atop Teldrassil, is open to Alliance adventurers beginning their journey in Aldrassil.",al={"is this quest alliance only","can horde do fang of githyiss"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf adventurer in Shadowglen, you help defend Teldrassil by facing dangerous creatures and aiding Aldrassil’s researchers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you help researchers and young recruits learn about the dangerous wildlife near Aldrassil across Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you watch Teldrassil’s natural balance by studying unusual predators and overgrown spiders in the surrounding wilds."},kw={"aldrassil","fang of githyiss","githyiss","shadowglen","spider","spider study","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil"},m={id=97236},src={"In-game quest text: Fang of Githyiss"},fv=true}
E["quest:97237"] = {t="quest",n="Shelf Picked",z="general",s="In Stormwind, Roy Lewells sends a runner to gather books for a reading group in the Park.",h="In Stormwind, Roy Lewells sends a runner to gather books for a reading group in the Park.",sec={{t="An Errand for the Stacks",b="Roy Lewells has sent a note asking for several books from the Stormwind library. The librarian checks the list and confirms every title is in stock. The books are there for you to find and pull from the shelves. The librarian stays at the desk to keep the inventory records.",sp=0},{t="The Cellar Reading Club",b="Roy Lewells's note makes you an official courier, so you are not responsible for returning the borrowed books. That duty belongs to Lewells's establishment. Once you bring the volumes to the Park, Roy prepares them for lively after-hours discussions in a cellar. The books have an exotic smell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Shelf Picked?",a="A librarian overseeing the Stormwind library gives you the errand after receiving Roy Lewells's note. The librarian confirms the requested books are in stock and asks you to pull them from the shelves.",al={"who gives shelf picked","shelf picked quest giver","where does shelf picked start"}},{q="Who is Roy Lewells?",a="Roy Lewells organizes a local reading group based in Stormwind's Park. He sends couriers to collect books from the library for the group's after-hours discussions in a cellar.",al={"who is roy lewells","roy lewells park","who is lewells"}},{q="Where does the book collection take place?",a="The books are collected at a Stormwind library. The librarian keeps the inventory records while you search the shelves for Roy Lewells's requested titles.",al={"what library is this","where are the books picked","which library shelf picked"}},{q="Why does Roy Lewells need these books?",a="Roy Lewells needs the books for an informal book club whose members gather for lively discussions after hours in a cellar.",al={"why retrieve books for lewells","what is lewells book club","cellar after hours book club"}},{q="Are you responsible for returning the borrowed books?",a="No. With Roy Lewells's note, you act as an official courier. His establishment is responsible for returning the borrowed books.",al={"am i responsible for returning books","who returns shelf picked books","library book return accountability"}},{q="Where do you bring the books once retrieved?",a="You bring the collected books to Roy Lewells in Stormwind's Park.",al={"where do you turn in shelf picked","where to find roy lewells","shelf picked turn in"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Courier errands between Stormwind's libraries and local gathering places are part of everyday life in the capital, even amid wider tensions in the kingdom."},kw={"book club","courier","library","park","roy lewells","shelf picked","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:park","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=97237},src={"In-game quest text: Shelf Picked"},fv=true}
E["quest:97242"] = {t="quest",n="Yelmak's Medley",z="general",s="Tensions rise in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. Master alchemist Yelmak hopes a calming mixture made with local water plants will quiet his apprentice Whuut's clumsy frustration and stubborn pride.",h="Tensions rise in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",sec={{t="Trouble in the Laboratory",b="At Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions, young apprentice Whuut's pride is making trouble. Rather than ask for help when he is out of his depth, he breaks the shop's equipment in frustration. Master alchemist Yelmak seeks to calm the youth without bruising his fragile ego, so he devises a soothing concoction.",sp=0},{t="Soothing Local Flora",b="The recipe calls for fresh cattails and speargrass from the watercourses winding through the Valley of Honor. Kor'geld cannot leave the shop without alerting the suspicious apprentice, so someone discreet must gather the plants. The botanical mixture is meant to temper Whuut's attitude and restore peace to the alchemy shop.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Yelmak's Medley?",a="Kor'geld offers the task on behalf of the shop's master alchemist. He is found in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",al={"who gives yelmaks medley","quest giver yelmak medley"}},{q="Who is Whuut?",a="Whuut is an apprentice mixer training under Yelmak in the Valley of Honor. His stubborn pride leads him to break equipment rather than admit he needs guidance or help.",al={"who is whuut","yelmak apprentice","whuut orgrimmar"}},{q="What is the purpose of the home-brewed medley?",a="The home-brewed medley is meant to soothe Yelmak's proud apprentice and temper his sour mood. It uses fresh cattail and speargrass cuttings.",al={"what is yelmak's medley recipe","what does yelmak want to brew"}},{q="Where are the ingredients gathered?",a="Wild cattails and speargrass grow along the freshwater streams and pools flowing through Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",al={"where to find cattails and speargrass","valley of honor cuttings"}},{q="Why doesn't Kor'geld gather the cuttings personally?",a="Kor'geld cannot leave Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions without Whuut realizing the shop staff is catering to his difficult temperament.",al={"why does korgeld need help","why cant korgeld pick plants"}},{q="Where is Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions located?",a="Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions is in the Valley of Honor, an eastern district of Orgrimmar. Its waterways run among warrior barracks and artisan shops.",al={"where is yelmak alchemy and potions","yelmak shop location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help smooth tensions inside Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor and its alchemical trade.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you gather fresh cattails and speargrass along Orgrimmar's watercourses. Local plants can be used in concoctions and herbal brews."},kw={"alchemy","cattail","kor'geld","orgrimmar","speargrass","valley of honor","whuut","yelmak","yelmak's medley"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-honor"},m={id=97242},src={"In-game quest text: Yelmak's Medley"},fv=true}
E["quest:97243"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="In Skywall, initiates carry the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn for teaching. The shrine lies in the Gustberry Lowlands.",h="In Skywall, initiates carry the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn for teaching.",sec={{t="Voices Across the Elemental Plane",b="Skywall belongs to the air elementals, though its currents reach the wider Elemental Plane. Spirits of earth, water, and fire still speak to those who can hear them. Some Windshapers are especially open to these other forces. Olariaan Swiftburn, a shen'dorei among them, is deeply attuned to fire.",sp=0},{t="The Shrine of Flames",b="Initiates take the Torch of Dormant Flame to the Gustberry Lowlands. Far along the island rim, west of Valanaar, stands the Shrine of Flames, Olariaan Swiftburn's home. Olariaan receives the dormant flame and offers to teach aspiring students to heed fire's demanding call amid the air realm's churning currents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Olariaan Swiftburn?",a="Olariaan Swiftburn is a shen'dorei Windshaper, deeply attuned to fire. Olariaan lives at the Shrine of Flames, along the Gustberry Lowlands' edge west of Valanaar.",al={"who gives call of fire","who do i take the torch to","olariaan swiftburn"}},{q="Where is the Shrine of Flames?",a="The Shrine of Flames lies in the Gustberry Lowlands of Skywall. It sits along the edge of the floating island expanse, directly west of Valanaar.",al={"where is shrine of flames","gustberry lowlands location","how to find olariaan"}},{q="Why is fire being studied in Skywall?",a="Skywall belongs to air, yet remains part of the wider Elemental Plane. Spirits of all four elements still speak there to those attuned enough to listen.",al={"why fire in skywall","elemental plane fire","isnt skywall just air"}},{q="What is the Torch of Dormant Flame?",a="The Torch of Dormant Flame is an elemental focus carried to Olariaan Swiftburn. An initiate brings it to seek instruction in communing with fire.",al={"what is the dormant flame","torch of dormant flame","what item do i carry"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers practice navigating and shaping elemental forces in Skywall. Their ranks include people of varied origins, such as the shen'dorei.",al={"who are windshapers","windshaper faction"}},{q="What does this quest lead to?",a="Olariaan Swiftburn teaches disciples to heed the call of fire. Mastering primal forces in Skywall's demanding domain takes great perseverance.",al={"what does olariaan teach","fire training skywall"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Heeding the elements is fundamental to shamanic training. Even in Skywall, communing with fire calls for dedicated guidance and ancestral reverence.",["race:Skyborne"]="Though native to Skywall's winds, you and the Windshapers know that balance means honoring all four primal elements."},kw={"call of fire","elemental plane","gustberry lowlands","olariaan swiftburn","shen'dorei","shrine of flames","skywall","torch of dormant flame","valanaar","windshapers"},rel={"quest:1524","topic:skywall","topic:elemental-plane"},m={id=97243},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:97244"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="The Windshapers send you after a traitor who chose power over his order. Skypriest Faladiel has fled to the Gustberry Lowlands, and they need his heart for a ritual.",h="The Windshapers send you after a traitor who chose power over his order.",sec={{t="A Traitor Among the Flame",b="The Windshapers send you after Skypriest Faladiel, once one of their own. He left the order to join the Al'Aketh and traded his calling as a flame-caller for power. He betrayed his former brothers and sisters, and their blood stains his hands. Now the Windshapers send you to carry out their judgment.",sp=0},{t="Reckoning in the Lowlands",b="Faladiel hides at a farm in the Gustberry Lowlands, northeast past Valanaar and just south of the Shrine of Akir. The Windshapers seek more than vengeance. They need his heart for an upcoming ritual. They believe a betrayer's heart will lend their sacred flames unmatched intensity.",sp=0},{t="Blood Paid with Blood",b="The Windshapers hold to their creed: blood must answer for blood. Faladiel's heart is only one part of what must feed their ceremonial fire before their rites can be concluded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Skypriest Faladiel?",a="Skypriest Faladiel was once a devoted caller of the flame and a member of the Windshapers. He joined the Al'Aketh for power, betraying his former brothers and sisters and staining his hands with their blood.",al={"who is faladiel","faladiel backstory","skypriest faladiel lore"}},{q="Why do the Windshapers want Faladiel killed?",a="Faladiel betrayed the Windshapers for power and murdered his former brothers and sisters. Their creed calls for blood to answer for blood, so they seek his execution as retribution.",al={"why kill faladiel","why do windshapers want faladiel dead","faladiel betrayal"}},{q="Why do the Windshapers need Faladiel's heart?",a="The Windshapers need Faladiel's heart for a ritual. They believe a traitor's heart will make their flames burn hotter and with greater intensity.",al={"why faladiel heart","what is heart for","ritual reagent heart"}},{q="Where can Skypriest Faladiel be found?",a="Skypriest Faladiel hides at a farm in the Gustberry Lowlands, northeast past Valanaar and just south of the Shrine of Akir.",al={"where is faladiel","skypriest faladiel location","find faladiel"}},{q="What is the creed of the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers' creed holds that blood must be repaid in blood. They practice flame-calling and sacred elemental rituals.",al={"who are windshapers","windshaper creed","windshapers faction"}},{q="What is the Al'Aketh's connection to this mission?",a="The Al'Aketh include members who traded former allegiances and honor for personal power. Skypriest Faladiel is one such member.",al={"what are alaketh","faladiel alaketh","alaketh traitors"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may see Faladiel's fall from grace in his turn from calling the flame to betraying and murdering members of his own order.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman attuned to fire and elemental rites, you may recognize the primal nature of feeding a traitor's essence to the flames to intensify their sacred power."},kw={"al'aketh","call of fire","faladiel","faladiel's heart","gustberry lowlands","shrine of akir","skypriest faladiel","valanaar","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92595"},m={id=97244},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:97245"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="In the Shen'dar Highlands, Olariaan Swiftburn sends you to face Kuramaa, an ancient forest sprite. Flame can pierce its defenses, and its wooden mask is needed in the Gustberry Lowlands to kindle an eternal flame and commune with fire spirits.",h="In the Shen'dar Highlands, Olariaan Swiftburn sends you to face Kuramaa, an ancient forest sprite.",sec={{t="The Sprite of the Highlands",b="People in the Shen'dar Highlands speak of Kuramaa, an ancient forest sprite that dwells in a twisted tree stump. The stump stands atop a hill near the regional Anchor Pylon. Strike the bark with a bare fist, and Kuramaa comes forth to meet you in combat.",sp=0},{t="Fire and Wood",b="Kuramaa's natural wards turn aside most arcane and divine magic. Only searing flame pierces its ancient bark and brings it low. Defeat the sprite, and its wooden mask is yours, an artifact of great power. Yet Kuramaa is eternal. When called again, it reforms.",sp=0},{t="The Eternal Flame",b="In the Gustberry Lowlands, Olariaan Swiftburn awaits Kuramaa's mask. The enchanted relic is needed to kindle an eternal flame and commune with the spirits of fire. Defeating highland nature spirits opens the rite's path to ancient communion with the elements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kuramaa?",a="Kuramaa is an ancient forest sprite dwelling in the Shen'dar Highlands. Local residents say it lives in a twisted tree stump atop a hill near the Highlands Anchor Pylon.",al={"who is kuramaa","kuramaa lore","what is kuramaa"}},{q="Who is Olariaan Swiftburn?",a="Olariaan Swiftburn is a ritualist in the Gustberry Lowlands who sends you to confront Kuramaa. Olariaan needs the sprite's wooden mask for a sacred rite of fire.",al={"who gives call of fire","who is olariaan swiftburn","where turn in call of fire"}},{q="How do you summon Kuramaa?",a="Kuramaa dwells in a twisted tree stump atop a hill near the Anchor Pylon in the Shen'dar Highlands. Strike the stump's bark with a fist, and the sprite comes out to fight.",al={"how to summon kuramaa","where is kuramaa stump","summon forest sprite"}},{q="What is Kuramaa vulnerable to in combat?",a="Kuramaa resists most forms of magic. Flame alone can pierce its defenses and bring the ancient forest sprite low.",al={"kuramaa weaknesses","how to beat kuramaa","kuramaa magic immune"}},{q="Why does Olariaan Swiftburn need Kuramaa's mask?",a="Olariaan Swiftburn needs Kuramaa's powerful wooden mask to kindle an eternal flame and commune with fire spirits.",al={"why collect kuramaa mask","what does mask do","kuramaa mask purpose"}},{q="Is Kuramaa permanently destroyed when defeated?",a="No. Kuramaa is eternal. Its spirit endures after its physical form is defeated, then manifests again when called.",al={"is kuramaa dead","did i kill kuramaa","kuramaa respawn lore"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face a highland spirit with flame and gather power to commune with fire spirits.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you find that Kuramaa resists most forms of magic. Only fire magic can overcome the sprite."},kw={"anchor pylon","call of fire","forest sprite","gustberry lowlands","kuramaa","kuramaa's mask","olariaan swiftburn","shen'dar highlands"},m={id=97245},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:97246"] = {t="quest",n="Meal Appeal",z="general",s="In Orgrimmar, Thatog worries his young son Migi is skipping meals to play. He asks you to fetch lunch from Borstan's Firepit and find Migi behind Grommash Hold.",h="In Orgrimmar, Thatog worries his young son Migi is skipping meals to play.",sec={{t="A Parent's Duty in Orgrimmar",b="Thatog's daily duties keep him at his post in Orgrimmar. He has little time to watch Migi, his energetic young son. From morning until dusk, Migi races through the city with his friends. He often ignores his hunger until he comes home famished.",sp=0},{t="Delivery Behind the Hold",b="Thatog arranges a hot lunch for Migi at Borstan's Firepit and asks you to carry it. Migi would rather keep playing than stop to eat. So you take the meal to the yard behind Grommash Hold, where Migi and the neighborhood children play.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thatog?",a="Thatog is an orc parent in Orgrimmar whose daily duties keep him from watching Migi, his young son. Worried that Migi skips meals to play with friends, he asks you to collect and deliver the boy's lunch.",al={"who is thatog","quest giver thatog","thatog orgrimmar"}},{q="Where can Migi be found?",a="Migi spends his days playing with friends in Orgrimmar. Thatog says you can find the children behind Grommash Hold.",al={"where is migi","migi location","find migi"}},{q="What is Borstan's Firepit?",a="Borstan's Firepit is a place to get food in Orgrimmar. Thatog asks you to collect Migi's arranged lunch there and deliver it to him.",al={"where is borstan firepit","borstans firepit location","borstan lunch"}},{q="Why does Migi forget to eat?",a="Migi gets so caught up playing with friends behind Grommash Hold that he neglects to eat. He often comes home hungry at day's end.",al={"why does migi skip lunch","migi starving","why is migi not eating"}},{q="Who is Migi?",a="Migi is Thatog's young son. He spends his time playing with friends in Orgrimmar instead of coming home or collecting his prepared meals.",al={"who is migi","migi orc kid","thatogs son"}},{q="What is the objective of Meal Appeal?",a="You collect Migi's lunch from Borstan's Firepit and deliver it to him behind Grommash Hold, so he can eat while he plays.",al={"meal appeal quest goal","what to do meal appeal","meal appeal task"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Orgrimmar's daily life includes concerns beyond warfare and defense. Thatog worries about feeding children like Migi as they run through the Valley of Strength.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know how parents like Thatog worry when their children neglect meals to play in the streets of Durotar's capital."},kw={"borstan","borstans firepit","grommash hold","lunch delivery","meal appeal","migi","orgrimmar","thatog"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold"},m={id=97246},src={"In-game quest text: Meal Appeal"},fv=true}
E["quest:97249"] = {t="quest",n="Favorite Food",z="general",s="In Orgrimmar, Migi's parents worry that play keeps him from eating enough. Borstan of Borstan's Meats prepares varied lunches with a taste Migi loves, so he and his friends stop to eat.",h="In Orgrimmar, Migi's parents worry that play keeps him from eating enough.",sec={{t="An Appetite for Play",b="Behind Grommash Hold, young Migi and his friends spend their afternoons playing along Orgrimmar's dusty paths. His parents worry that he often neglects his meals and does not eat enough. So they ask Borstan's Meats to prepare daily packed lunches. They insist that Borstan vary the meals, hoping Migi will learn to enjoy more than one favorite dish.",sp=0},{t="The Sweetglaze Compromise",b="Migi loves sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches and comes for lunch when the smokehouse fills with their sweet aroma. Borstan finds a way to honor his parents' request while keeping Migi fed. He crumbles the leftover crispy glazed cracklings into a savory seasoning that can be sprinkled over any dish. Behind Grommash Hold, the topping persuades Migi and his companions to pause their play and share lunch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Migi?",a="Migi is a young resident of Orgrimmar who plays with friends behind Grommash Hold. His parents worry that he gets so caught up in play that he does not eat enough, so they arrange daily lunches from Borstan's Meats.",al={"migi orgrimmar","who is the kid behind grommash hold","migi lunch"}},{q="Who gives the quest Favorite Food?",a="Borstan of Borstan's Meats gives it in Orgrimmar. He prepares a varied meal after learning that Migi's parents worry about the boy's eating habits.",al={"favorite food quest giver","who starts favorite food","borstan favorite food"}},{q="Where can Migi be found?",a="Migi can be found behind Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, playing with other local children. They often pass along the road to the stronghold and recognize Borstan's daily meals by their scent.",al={"migi location","where is migi","where to deliver migis lunch","find migi orgrimmar"}},{q="What is Migi's favorite food?",a="Migi loves the sweetglazed hog belly sandwich made in the smoker at Borstan's Meats. When the smoker is running, its aroma draws him toward lunch behind Grommash Hold.",al={"what does migi like to eat","migis favorite meal","sweetglazed hog belly migi"}},{q="Why do Migi's parents request different meals?",a="Migi's parents ask Borstan to vary his meals so their son will learn to enjoy more than one dish. They want him to eat enough without relying only on sweetglazed pork.",al={"why change migis lunch","migis parents request","why not sweetglazed sandwiches every day"}},{q="How does Borstan get Migi to eat different foods?",a="Borstan crumbles leftover crispy glazed cracklings into a topping for different dishes. Its familiar sweetglaze flavor helps Migi enjoy the varied meals.",al={"borstans trick","how does borstan get migi to eat","sweetglaze crumbs"}},{q="What is Borstan's Meats?",a="Borstan's Meats is a smokehouse and butchery in Orgrimmar. Borstan smokes hog belly sandwiches and prepares packed meals for city residents, including neighborhood youths.",al={"borstans meats orgrimmar","where is borstans meats","what is borstan"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This shows everyday life in Orgrimmar, where tradesfolk and families look after the capital's children and make sure they are fed.",["profession:Cooking"]="In Orgrimmar, Borstan turns crispy smoked hog belly cracklings into a flavorful seasoning for daily meals."},kw={"borstan","borstan's meats","favorite food","grommash hold","hog belly","lunch","migi","orgrimmar","sweetglaze"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold"},m={id=97249},src={"In-game quest text: Favorite Food"},fv=true}
E["quest:97250"] = {t="quest",n="Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected",z="general",s="Along the eastern coast, Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected follows rising Horde and Alliance tensions after a roadside tavern is destroyed. The incident warns Alliance forces, while the question of who threatened a vital civilian trade route remains open.",h="Along the eastern coast, Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected follows rising Horde and Alliance tensions after a...",sec={{t="Friction on the Coast",b="Along the eastern coast, Horde and Alliance skirmishes are reaching contested ground. Then a tavern on a major thoroughfare is destroyed. Ordinary travelers now face danger, and the region's stability is at risk.",sp=0},{t="Doubt and Disruption",b="Local leaders doubt Horde forces destroyed the tavern, though suspicion first fell on the Horde. Civilians and merchants rely on that road to move goods, so the Horde has reason to keep it open. They call for a closer look at who ruined the tavern.",sp=1},{t="A Warning to the Alliance",b="The affair ends in victory for Horde forces in the area, though questions about the tavern remain. The result warns the Alliance that any move into Horde territory along the coast will meet immediate resistance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected about?",a="Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected follows rising Horde and Alliance tensions along the eastern coast after a roadside tavern is destroyed on a vital trade route.",al={"what is this quest","wrongly blamed justly corrected lore","what happened in wrongly blamed"}},{q="Did the Horde destroy the tavern?",a="Horde leaders doubt their forces destroyed the tavern. Horde civilians depend on the route for trade and everyday travel, so its destruction works against their interests.",al={"did horde destroy tavern","who burned the tavern","who destroyed the tavern"}},{q="Why does the destroyed tavern matter to the Horde?",a="The tavern lies along a major road used by civilian travelers and merchants. Its destruction disrupts trade and movement, making the road a concern for the Horde.",al={"why is tavern route important","why does the tavern matter"}},{q="What caused tensions on the eastern coast?",a="The cause of the tensions is unclear. Friction between the Horde and Alliance has been mounting along the eastern coast, and conflict has reached Horde territory.",al={"why fighting on eastern coast","eastern coast conflict"}},{q="What message does this outcome send to the Alliance?",a="The outcome warns the Alliance that incursions into Horde territory along the coast will meet resistance.",al={"what did horde achieve","why warning to alliance"}},{q="Is there further investigation into the tavern's destruction?",a="Horde leaders seek a closer look at who destroyed the tavern. Its ruin threatens civilian passage, and the circumstances remain suspicious.",al={"what to investigate","will the tavern be investigated"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The outcome is a Horde victory and a warning against Alliance incursions. It also raises concern about protecting the trade routes and civilian roads the Horde depends on.",["faction:Alliance"]="The outcome warns the Alliance against further presence and provocations along the eastern coast."},kw={"alliance warning","civilian route","eastern coast","horde trade","tavern","territorial conflict","wrongly blamed, justly corrected"},rel={"topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={id=97250},src={"In-game quest text: Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected"},fv=true}
E["quest:97253"] = {t="quest",n="Parts and Pieces",z="general",s="In Ratchet, Wrenix's machine lies in pieces after the pirates dismantled it. He sent it to face the raiders after five or six mercenaries failed to return alive. Now its scattered parts lie in the pirates' upper camp.",h="In Ratchet, Wrenix's machine lies in pieces after the pirates dismantled it.",sec={{t="A Mechanical Solution",b="Pirates along the coast south of Ratchet trouble the town's residents and tradesfolk. Wrenix the Wretched wanted to stop them without risking more coin on hired hands. Five or six mercenaries had already gone after the pirates and failed to return alive.\n\nSo Wrenix sent an automated machine to deal with the encampment on its own. He hoped the contraption could face the marauders without putting another living soul at risk.",sp=0},{t="Scimitars and Screwdrivers",b="The pirates south of Ratchet proved resourceful. They used their curved scimitars as makeshift screwdrivers and pried Wrenix's machine apart before he could send instructions to retreat toward town.\n\nIts delicate components now lie scattered in their upper camp. Wrenix needs someone to slip inside and gather five handfuls of the complicated parts from the dirt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wrenix the Wretched?",a="Wrenix the Wretched is an eccentric tinkerer in the port town of Ratchet. After five or six mercenaries failed to return alive from the pirates south of town, he sent an automated machine to face them. The pirates dismantled it, and its parts lie scattered in their upper camp.",al={"who is wrenix","wrenix the wretched lore","ratchet wrenix"}},{q="What happened to the earlier mercenaries Wrenix hired?",a="Wrenix hired five or six mercenaries to deal with the pirates south of Ratchet. None returned alive, so he turned to a machine instead.",al={"wrenix previous mercenaries","what happened to the other adventurers","who did wrenix send first"}},{q="Why did Wrenix send a machine to fight the pirates?",a="Wrenix sent a machine because five or six mercenaries he hired failed to return alive. He hoped an automated contraption could face the pirates without risking another living soul.",al={"why send a machine","wrenix robot plan","why did wrenix use a contraption"}},{q="How did the pirates dismantle Wrenix's machine?",a="The pirates used their curved scimitars as makeshift screwdrivers to pry Wrenix's machine apart. They scattered its components through their camp and dismantled the contraption down to its frame before Wrenix could send it instructions to retreat toward Ratchet.",al={"how was the machine destroyed","how did pirates dismantle the robot","pirates scimitar screwdrivers"}},{q="Where are the complicated parts located?",a="The complicated parts lie scattered on the ground in the pirates' upper camp along the coast south of Ratchet. They left the pieces there after taking Wrenix's machine apart. Five handfuls must be gathered.",al={"where are the parts","upper pirate camp location","handfuls of complicated parts location"}},{q="Why does Wrenix believe this retrieval mission is safer?",a="Wrenix believes gathering scattered parts is safer than sending mercenaries to eliminate the pirates. The earlier mercenaries did not return alive; this work calls for slipping into the upper camp and collecting five handfuls of components from the dirt.",al={"is parts and pieces safe","why does wrenix think you will survive","wrenix survival odds"}},{q="What are the Complicated Parts needed for?",a="The complicated parts are pieces of Wrenix's automated machine. He needs them recovered so his engineering work and materials do not go entirely to waste.",al={"what are complicated parts","why does wrenix need the parts","what does wrenix do with the parts"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers may see the irony in pirates taking apart a sophisticated machine. Wrenix's scattered parts show the danger of sending an automated prototype into a hostile camp without physical safeguards."},kw={"complicated parts","machine","parts and pieces","pirate","pirates","ratchet","scimitars","upper pirate camp","wrenix the wretched"},rel={"npc:wrenix-the-wretched","subzone:ratchet","topic:pirate"},m={id=97253},src={"In-game quest text: Parts and Pieces"},fv=true}
E["quest:97257"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="general",s="At Skywall, initiates face the Windshapers’ trial and seek a Fire Totem. They summon spirits of flame, bear the Eternal Flame to Valanaar, and kindle its brazier.",h="At Skywall, initiates face the Windshapers’ trial and seek a Fire Totem.",sec={{t="The Ritual of Flame",b="Olariaan of the Windshapers guides initiates through a sacred trial at Skywall. They gather at the Brazier of Offering and call to spirits of flame from the Firelands. If their offerings are worthy, the spirits kindle the altar with the Eternal Flame. A worthy initiate may then take up that flame.",sp=0},{t="The Journey to Valanaar",b="The Eternal Flame must be caught on a torch and carried across Skywall to Valanaar. In this elemental realm, its power from the Firelands fades in the swirling air. The initiate must reach the Brazier of Eternal Flames before the torch goes dark.",sp=0},{t="The Fire Totem",b="When an initiate rekindles the brazier at Valanaar, the Windshapers grant them a Fire Totem. It honors their discipline and respect for the elements. The elders teach that elemental power serves those who respect it, but consumes those who do not.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Call of Fire?",a="Call of Fire sends an aspiring shaman to summon spirits of flame and catch the Eternal Flame. Carrying it to Valanaar proves the initiate’s respect for the elemental plane and earns a Fire Totem.",al={"what is call of fire","call of fire quest","what is this quest about"}},{q="Who is Olariaan?",a="Olariaan leads the ceremony at the Brazier of Offering. He places materials on the altar and calls the spirits of flame to kindle the Eternal Flame.",al={"who is olariaan","olariaan role","who starts the ritual"}},{q="What is the Eternal Flame?",a="The Eternal Flame comes from spirits of flame called forth from the Firelands during the Windshaper ritual. Initiates catch it on a torch and use it to kindle the Brazier of Eternal Flames in Valanaar.",al={"what is the eternal flame","eternal flame skywall"}},{q="Why must the flame be carried quickly to Valanaar?",a="The flame comes from the Firelands, and its heat fades quickly in Skywall’s air. Initiates hurry so the torch stays lit until they reach Valanaar.",al={"why does eternal flame dissipate","why rush to valanaar","flames of firelands skywall"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are an order in Skywall who guide initiates through elemental trials. They honor the balance and power of the elemental planes and oversee the granting of totems.",al={"who are the windshapers","windshaper faction"}},{q="What is the reward for completing the trial?",a="An initiate who completes the ritual and rekindles the brazier in Valanaar earns a Fire Totem, a focus for channeling fiery elemental power.",al={"call of fire reward","fire totem reward","what do you get from call of fire"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you undergo this rite of initiation and earn a Fire Totem when you complete it. The totem grants you mastery over fire.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you follow a shamanic tradition in which the Windshapers of Skywall guide initiates in honoring the elemental planes."},kw={"call of fire","eternal flame","fire totem","firelands","olariaan","skywall","valanaar","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92579","quest:92595","topic:skywall","topic:elemental-plane"},m={id=97257},src={"In-game quest text: Call of Fire"},fv=true}
E["quest:97263"] = {t="quest",n="Your Package Has Arrived",z="general",s="A parcel from Aerie Peak lies beside a city mailbox, bound for Ironforge. Marked urgent for Eldrun Stormbreaker, it still waits to be delivered.",h="A parcel from Aerie Peak lies beside a city mailbox, bound for Ironforge.",sec={{t="Misplaced Freight",b="Several parcels lie abandoned beside a city mailbox. They were left there instead of being carried to their destinations. One urgent parcel came from Aerie Peak, the Wildhammer dwarves’ mountain redoubt in the Hinterlands. Deliveries between distant outposts across Khaz Modan and Lordaeron can go awry. An alert passerby can carry a mislaid package onward.",sp=0},{t="A Parcel for Eldrun Stormbreaker",b="The parcel is addressed to Eldrun Stormbreaker in Ironforge. Its urgent notice marks the shipment as important enough to travel from the Hinterlands to the dwarven capital without delay. The crate still needs to reach Eldrun before it is stolen or forgotten.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the package found by the mailbox?",a="It is an urgent parcel from Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands, addressed to Eldrun Stormbreaker in Ironforge. It was left beside a mailbox with several other packages instead of reaching its destination.",al={"what is the package","misplaced package","what was left by the mailbox","mailbox package"}},{q="Who is Eldrun Stormbreaker?",a="Eldrun Stormbreaker is the named recipient of the misplaced parcel in Ironforge. The label gives Eldrun’s name and marks the package urgent, but says little else until it reaches its recipient.",al={"who is eldrun stormbreaker","eldrun stormbreaker","who gets the package","package recipient"}},{q="Where was the parcel sent from?",a="The parcel came from Aerie Peak, the Wildhammer clan’s settlement and fortress in the mountains of the Hinterlands. It was bound for Ironforge before it was misplaced near a mailbox along the way.",al={"where did the package come from","package origin","where was it mailed from","aerie peak delivery"}},{q="Why was the parcel marked urgent?",a="The sender marked the crate urgent because its contents or arrival time mattered. A delay on the long journey from Aerie Peak to Ironforge could cause trouble for Eldrun Stormbreaker.",al={"why is it urgent","urgent delivery","what is inside the package","why urgent"}},{q="Why was the package left sitting by a mailbox?",a="Several parcels were left abandoned beside a mailbox instead of being sorted and delivered. The reason is unknown, and the packages remain misplaced.",al={"why was it abandoned","why was package dropped","lost mail","misplaced packages"}},{q="Where does this package need to be delivered?",a="The parcel is bound for Ironforge and addressed to Eldrun Stormbreaker. It needs to be carried to Eldrun inside the dwarven fortress city.",al={"where do i deliver it","package destination","delivery location","who do i bring the package to"}},{q="What connection exists between Aerie Peak and Ironforge?",a="Aerie Peak is home to the Wildhammer dwarves, and Ironforge is the seat of the Bronzebeard clan. The clans have distinct customs and homes, yet correspondence, trade, and kinship ties link the Hinterlands to the Great Forge beneath the mountain.",al={"aerie peak and ironforge","wildhammer and bronzebeard trade","ironforge aerie peak connection","why send mail from aerie peak"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the ties between the Bronzebeards of Ironforge and their Wildhammer cousins in Aerie Peak. Getting this parcel safely to its recipient honors those ties.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know reliable communication between the Hinterlands and Ironforge matters to Alliance interests across Khaz Modan and the northern territories."},kw={"aerie peak","eldrun stormbreaker","ironforge","mailbox","misplaced package","urgent delivery","wildhammer","your package has arrived"},rel={"zone:ironforge"},m={id=97263},src={"In-game quest text: Your Package Has Arrived"},fv=true}
E["quest:97265"] = {t="quest",n="Hate the Hatefury",z="general",s="Aka'rai in Shadowprey Village asks you to strike at the Hatefury satyr in Sargeron. His grievance comes from a bargain that left him seeking revenge.",h="Aka'rai in Shadowprey Village asks you to strike at the Hatefury satyr in Sargeron.",sec={{t="Aka'rai's Grievance",b="Aka'rai speaks of a bargain with a satyr that promised him power and knowledge. He says the Hatefury cast him aside, leaving him with less than before. Now he asks you to attack their camp northeast of Shadowprey Village, in Sargeron. Their blood is the price he seeks for his revenge.",sp=0},{t="The Blood Bargain",b="After the fighting, Aka'rai says one Hatefury escaped your assault. He names that satyr as the one who joined him in a ritual marked by spilled blood. The satyr holds Aka'rai's soulstone, so Aka'rai fears leaving Shadowprey Village while it remains in his hands. For now, he says your work is done.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Aka'rai in Shadowprey Village asks you to attack the Hatefury satyr at Sargeron.",al={"who is aka'rai","aka rai","hatefury giver"}},{q="Why does Aka'rai want the Hatefury attacked?",a="Aka'rai says the Hatefury cast him aside after a bargain that promised power and knowledge.",al={"why hatefury","aka'rai revenge","satyr grudge"}},{q="Where are the Hatefury?",a="The Hatefury camp is at Sargeron in Desolace, northeast of Shadowprey Village.",al={"hatefury location","sargeron satyr","where camp"}},{q="What did Aka'rai bargain for?",a="Aka'rai says the bargain promised power, knowledge beyond ordinary tomes, and an eager minion.",al={"aka'rai deal","satyr bargain","power deal"}}},kw={"aka'rai","desolace","hate the hatefury","hatefury","sargeron","satyr","shadowprey village","soulstone"},rel={"subzone:sargeron","subzone:shadowprey-village","zone:desolace","topic:satyr"},m={id=97265},src={"In-game quest text: Hate the Hatefury"},fv=true}
E["quest:97275"] = {t="quest",n="Whuut's the Rush",z="general",s="Yelmak sends you to carry a tonic to Whuut, whose eagerness has outrun his care. His apprentice reaches for rare herbs before learning what common plants can do.",h="Yelmak sends you to carry a tonic to Whuut, whose eagerness has outrun his care.",sec={{t="The Eager Prodigy",b="Whuut has a gift for alchemy, and the stirring rod comes naturally to him. Yet impatience leads him to spend the shop’s rarest reagents before he has mastered the basics. He reaches for legendary plants before learning how common herbs must be balanced, treating alchemy as a race.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in a Vial",b="Yelmak answers his apprentice’s haste with a lesson in a vial. He brews a refined tonic from common speargrass and cattail using a quick method. Whuut is daydreaming about Black Lotus and Mountain Silversage when the tonic reaches his hands. Its simple ingredients show how much skill, patience, and respect for everyday plants can matter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Whuut?",a="Whuut is Yelmak’s young apprentice and a gifted alchemist. Eager to experiment with rare herbs, he rushes past the trade’s fundamentals.",al={"who is whuut","whuut backstory","about whuut"}},{q="Who is Yelmak?",a="Yelmak is an experienced alchemist who mentors Whuut in the shop. He worries that the young alchemist is wasting precious supplies.",al={"who gives this quest","yelmak role","who is yelmak"}},{q="Why does Yelmak send you with a potion for Whuut?",a="Yelmak sends you with a tonic to teach Whuut patience and respect for the basics. He made it with speargrass and cattail, ordinary plants Whuut has been overlooking.",al={"what is yelmak's lesson","why does yelmak send the potion","point of the quest"}},{q="What ingredients did Yelmak use in his potion?",a="Yelmak used speargrass and cattail to brew the tonic. His careful method makes these common plants useful.",al={"what is in the potion","yelmak potion reagents","quick tonic ingredients"}},{q="Which rare reagents was Whuut trying to work with?",a="Whuut was reaching for Black Lotus and Mountain Silversage. He had passed over everyday ingredients in favor of these rare plants.",al={"what was whuut brewing","rare herbs whuut wants","what reagents did whuut use"}},{q="Does Whuut learn his lesson?",a="After tasting the tonic and hearing its recipe, Whuut is surprised that common plants could make such a brew. He admits Yelmak is right and resolves to pay closer attention to the everyday plants he had dismissed.",al={"does whuut change his mind","whuut reaction to potion","outcome of whuut's the rush"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know that learning the properties of everyday plants such as speargrass and cattail matters as much as seeking rare blooms.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can learn from Yelmak’s patience and resourcefulness with local Kalimdor ingredients."},kw={"alchemy","black lotus","cattail","herbalism","mountain silversage","potion","speargrass","whuut","yelmak"},m={id=97275},src={"In-game quest text: Whuut's the Rush"},fv=true}
E["quest:97277"] = {t="quest",n="Grund and Gozwin",z="general",s="At their camp in the northwestern hills, Grund and Gozwin face a snow leopard’s attack. Grund drives it off with his shotgun, but Gozwin loses his Mechanic's Log in the scramble.",h="At their camp in the northwestern hills, Grund and Gozwin face a snow leopard’s attack.",sec={{t="An Ambush by the Fire",b="You camp with Grund and Gozwin in the snowy hills for the evening. As Grund turns to prepare a boar over the fire, a snow leopard springs from the brush and seizes Gozwin in its jaws. Grund snatches up his shotgun and fires over the beast’s head. Startled, the leopard lets Gozwin go and flees into the cold crags.",sp=0},{t="A Tinkerer's Lost Work",b="Gozwin escapes with deep scratches, but the attack scatters the camp. In the scramble, he loses his prized Mechanic's Log, which holds schematics for his mecha-walker. The battered gnome fears someone may find his engineering secrets. He cannot rest until you search the hills northwest of camp for the log and the prowling leopard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are Grund and Gozwin?",a="Grund is a dwarf, and Gozwin is his gnomish companion and an engineer. A snow leopard attacks as they camp in the snowy hills, leaving Gozwin wounded and their belongings scattered.",al={"who are grund and gozwin","grund gozwin"}},{q="What attacked Gozwin at camp?",a="A snow leopard springs from the brush and grabs Gozwin in its jaws while Grund prepares a boar over the fire. Grund fires his shotgun over its head, frightening the beast away.",al={"what attacked gozwin","who attacked gozwin"}},{q="Why is Gozwin's Mechanic's Log so important to him?",a="Gozwin's Mechanic's Log holds technical schematics for his mecha-walker. He fears someone may discover his engineering secrets if the log is found.",al={"why is the log important","mechanic log gozwin"}},{q="How badly hurt was Gozwin in the attack?",a="Gozwin escapes with deep scratches after Grund fires his shotgun and frightens the leopard away. The battered gnome is anxious about his lost log.",al={"is gozwin okay","did gozwin survive"}},{q="Where is Grund and Gozwin's camp located?",a="Their camp is in the snowy hills to the northwest. You are asked to search there for the lost log and the prowling leopard.",al={"where is the camp","grund camp location"}},{q="What happened to the meal Grund was preparing?",a="The leopard flees after Grund fires his shotgun. The snow leopard made a meal of the boar Grund was preparing.",al={"what happened to the boar roast","leopard eating boar"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may understand Gozwin's worry over the lost schematics for his mecha-walker.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize how quickly Grund defends his gnomish companion.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know why Gozwin is anxious about the schematics and notes in his Mechanic's Log."},kw={"dwarf","gnome engineer","gozwin","grund","mecha-walker","mechanic's log","snow leopard prowler"},m={id=97277},src={"In-game quest text: Grund and Gozwin"},fv=true}
E["quest:97281"] = {t="quest",n="A Simmering Storm",z="general",s="In Durotar, the Dull Stormy Orb has caught Rezlak's attention. The goblin tinker sees reason to study the relic, recovered from the Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine.",h="In Durotar, the Dull Stormy Orb has caught Rezlak's attention.",sec={{t="A Spark in the Dust",b="Travelers who contend with the Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine may find the Dull Stormy Orb among their strange trinkets. Its worn surface gives off a steady electrical vibration. Dark mist churns within, split now and then by sharp sparks. The relic shows the harpies have handled storm magic.",sp=0},{t="Goblin Curiosity",b="Rezlak waits at the entrance to Drygulch Ravine, where the orb has caught his eye. Its discovery brings to mind advice from his employer, Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet. What the harpies meant to do with the miniature storm remains unknown. Now the orb is in goblin hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dull Stormy Orb?",a="The Dull Stormy Orb is a magical curiosity recovered from a harpy in Durotar. Its dull surface hides a faint electrical buzz, swirling dark mist, and occasional sparks.",al={"what is dull stormy orb","stormy orb","orb from harpies"}},{q="Who wants the Dull Stormy Orb?",a="Rezlak wants the Dull Stormy Orb. He is a goblin scout stationed just outside Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, with an eye for peculiar curiosities and salvage.",al={"who takes dull stormy orb","turn in stormy orb","where to bring orb"}},{q="Why did the harpies have this orb?",a="The harpies' purpose for the orb is unknown. The Dustwind harpies of Drygulch Ravine were using it to channel or contain electrical and stormy elemental forces.",al={"what were harpies doing with orb","why do harpies have storm orb","harpy orb purpose"}},{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin operative near Drygulch Ravine in northern Durotar. He is affiliated with the Steamwheedle Cartel and Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet.",al={"who is rezlak","rezlak durotar","goblin near drygulch"}},{q="Where is Drygulch Ravine?",a="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged canyon system in northern Durotar. Hostile Dustwind harpies infest it, harassing travelers and disrupting local trade and settlements.",al={"where is drygulch ravine","drygulch location","harpy canyon durotar"}},{q="What does Rezlak think of the orb?",a="The orb brings to Rezlak's mind lessons and remarks from his boss, Chief Engineer Gazlowe, about peculiar oddities that might prove profitable.",al={"what does rezlak say about gazlowe","rezlak gazlowe connection"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you help Rezlak secure mysterious magical artifacts recovered from hostile harpies threatening Durotar's canyons.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you recognize the miniature electrical storm as a reflection of primal elemental forces. Its crude vessel raises questions about the harpies' methods.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you share Rezlak's interest in odd curiosities that spark with erratic electrical charges and swirling internal mists."},kw={"a simmering storm","drygulch ravine","dull stormy orb","durotar","dustwind","gazlowe","harpy","rezlak"},rel={"subzone:drygulch-ravine","npc:rezlak","topic:harpy"},m={id=97281},src={"In-game quest text: A Simmering Storm"},fv=true}
E["quest:97282"] = {t="quest",n="Stormy Potential",z="general",s="Near Drygulch Ravine, Rezlak looks for a way to protect his caravan from harpies. He hopes to charge a drained orb with the electrical organs of Durotar's thunder lizards.",h="Near Drygulch Ravine, Rezlak looks for a way to protect his caravan from harpies.",sec={{t="Seizing Opportunity",b="Near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, harpies threaten Rezlak's caravan, and a sound magical orb has lost its power. Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, once advised Rezlak to seize opportunity when it knocks. Now the goblin plans to charge the dormant orb and answer both troubles at once.",sp=0},{t="Harnessing the Storm",b="Rezlak needs strong electricity to restore his drained orb. Thunder lizards live in the gorge west of Drygulch Ravine, and their organs generate and conduct deadly lightning. He asks you to bring him those charged organs. Rezlak hopes to channel their volatile current into the orb and defend his supply wagons from harpy ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Stormy Potential?",a="Rezlak, a goblin merchant and tinkerer near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar, asks for your help. Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, taught him to seize opportunity, and Rezlak hopes to restore a drained orb with the charge in local beasts' electrical organs.",al={"who gives stormy potential","where is rezlak","rezlak quest giver"}},{q="What is Rezlak trying to charge with the organs?",a="Rezlak hopes to charge an intact orb that has lost all its power. He plans to use thunder lizard organs to defend his caravan from harpies harassing the area.",al={"what is rezlak charging","why need thunder lizard organs","rezlak orb purpose"}},{q="Where are the thunder lizards found?",a="Thunder lizards live in a gorge west of Rezlak's position near Drygulch Ravine in Durotar. You can bring their electrical organs back to him.",al={"where find thunder lizards","thunder lizard location durotar","where are the organs"}},{q="Why are thunder lizards dangerous to harvest?",a="Thunder lizards are dangerous because they release bolts of lightning. Their electrical blasts can teach travelers a painful lesson they may get only once.",al={"why thunder lizards lightning","do thunder lizards use lightning"}},{q="Why does Rezlak fear the harpies?",a="Harpies from Drygulch Ravine ambushed Rezlak's caravan. He hopes the charged orb will deter them or serve as a weapon against further attacks on his shipments.",al={"why rezlak need defense","who attacked rezlak","harpy caravan attack"}},{q="What is Rezlak's connection to Gazlowe?",a="Rezlak looks to Gazlowe, Ratchet's chief engineer, as a mentor and business inspiration. Gazlowe's advice to seize opportunity guides Rezlak's plan for the orb.",al={"who is gazlowe to rezlak","rezlak gazlowe advice"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using thunder lizard organs to power dormant devices shows goblin ingenuity, though the safety margins are nearly nonexistent.",["faction:Horde"]="Rezlak's work supports the Horde's foothold and travel through Durotar, where marauding harpies from Drygulch Ravine threaten travelers and supply caravans."},kw={"charged organs","drygulch ravine","durotar","gazlowe","harpies","orb","rezlak","stormy potential","thunder lizard"},rel={"npc:rezlak","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},m={id=97282},src={"In-game quest text: Stormy Potential"},fv=true}
E["quest:97286"] = {t="quest",n="Research Access",z="general",s="Your actions have earned you a place in the library. Its doors are open for your study.",h="Your actions have earned you a place in the library.",sec={{t="Library Access",b="You have earned access to the library for your studies. Its doors are open to you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can I enter the library?",a="Your actions showed respect for knowledge, so the library is open to you for study.",al={"library access","why library open","study library"}},{q="What does the library offer me?",a="The library is open for your study.",al={"library for what","study access","what can i do"}},{q="What did my actions show?",a="Your actions showed respect for knowledge.",al={"respect knowledge","why accepted","what did i prove"}}},kw={"access","knowledge","library","research access","respect","study"},m={id=97286},src={"In-game quest text: Research Access"},fv=true}
E["quest:97288"] = {t="quest",n="Unending Torment",z="general",s="The head of a fallen abomination sets Unending Torment in motion. Its repeated stitching points toward deliberate dark experimentation in the Forsaken capital, and you bring it to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",h="The head of a fallen abomination sets Unending Torment in motion.",sec={{t="A Loose Stitch",b="When the towering abomination falls in battle, its head topples from its shoulders. The neck was severed, stitched, torn away, and reattached many times. Each repair left the seam more fragile, until the head barely clung to its shoulders.\n\nSuch persistent patchwork is unusual even for undead constructs. The repeated destruction and reassembly suggest this abomination was rebuilt again and again. Ordinary scavengers could not explain its craftsmanship. Only the skilled flesh-crafters of the Undercity could identify the creature's origins.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Lady's Jest",b="At the Apothecarium, Master Apothecary Faranell, leader of the Royal Apothecary Society, recognizes the severed head at once. He sees its repeated reassembly as an intentional, cruel joke devised by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, not an accident of necromancy.\n\nOnly the Dark Lady and her inner circle know what offense earned the creature this degrading punishment. Faranell gleefully accepts the battered head, confident the Royal Apothecary Society can put it to use in their ongoing alchemical and necromantic endeavors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Abominable Head?",a="The Abominable Head is the severed head of a unique construct, loosened when the creature is defeated. Its neck bears the scars of repeated reattachment, and each repair weakened the flesh and stitches. You bring it to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity for examination.",al={"abominable head lore","what is abominable head","abomination head quest item"}},{q="Why has the head been reattached so many times?",a="The head was stitched back after each fall or loss so the construct could be pieced together to continue serving or suffering. Its increasingly fragile neck eventually gave way again.",al={"why reattached head","why was the head sewn back on","unending torment head stitches"}},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society in the Apothecarium of the Undercity. Under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's authority, he oversees Forsaken apothecaries researching poisons, plagues, and anatomical alterations. His familiarity with the Dark Lady's projects lets him identify the stitched head's origins at once.",al={"who is faranell","master apothecary faranell lore","faranell undercity"}},{q="Why does Sylvanas consider this a cruel joke?",a="The cruelty lies in the endless cycle itself. Each time the creature falls, it is sloppily stitched back together to serve or suffer once more, and each repair leaves it weaker. This is how the Dark Lady punishes her enemies. Faranell does not say who the creature once was, or what it did to earn this.",al={"sylvanas joke","why dark lady joke","cruel joke by dark lady"}},{q="What will Faranell do with the head?",a="Faranell regularly repurposes necromantic remnants, flesh, and biological oddities to develop concoctions, plagues, and construct reinforcements for the Forsaken's ongoing conflicts. He accepts the head for the society's alchemical and necromantic work.",al={"what happens to the head","faranell use for head","what will the apothecaries do with it"}},{q="Where do you turn in the quest Unending Torment?",a="Bring the Abominable Head to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Apothecarium, in the Undercity's southern quadrant. He is surrounded by bubbling vats, assistants, and test subjects as he oversees the society's research.",al={"where to turn in unending torment","unending torment hand in","who takes abominable head"}},{q="Can Alliance players turn in this quest?",a="The delivery brings you to Master Apothecary Faranell inside the Apothecarium of the Undercity, so it is intended for Horde adventurers. Alliance adventurers who approach him would face hostile Undercity guards and death at the hands of the Forsaken upon entering their stronghold.",al={"is unending torment horde only","alliance unending torment","can alliance do unending torment"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the head shows how repeated repairs weaken an undead construct. It is a grim reminder of their queen's absolute authority and the Royal Apothecary Society's macabre ingenuity.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers who see the head glimpse the Forsaken's practice of repeated reanimation and flesh-crafting. These methods work, but they can unnerve peers who are more bound to honor."},kw={"abominable head","abomination","apothecarium","dark lady","master apothecary faranell","royal apothecary society","sylvanas windrunner","undercity","unending torment"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:undercity"},m={id=97288},src={"In-game quest text: Unending Torment"},fv=true}
E["quest:97289"] = {t="quest",n="Unending Torment",z="general",s="In the Undercity, the Forsaken prepare to question a fallen Alliance commander. They mean to give Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos a new body, and learn what he carried to his grave.",h="In the Undercity, the Forsaken prepare to question a fallen Alliance commander.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Conquest",b="Deep in the Undercity, Forsaken practitioners stitch abominations from discarded pieces of the dead. Among the preserved skulls lies one with a bitter history: the severed head of Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos. He led the surviving Alliance forces across Lordaeron, until the Dark Lady killed him.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Grave",b="The Forsaken plan to question Garithos, not keep his head as a trophy. Their necromancers prepare a cobbled abomination body as his new host, hoping to uncover Alliance secrets locked in his skull. When they bring the head to the lifeless construct, the abomination wakes in agony and relives its gruesome final moments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Othmar?",a="Othmar was Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos, a notorious commander who led Alliance remnants in Lordaeron after the Third War. Non-humans despised him. Master Apothecary Faranell says the Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching him herself.",al={"who is othmar","othmar identity","who was othmar"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken reanimating Othmar's remains?",a="The Forsaken hope to pry secrets from Garithos that he took to his grave. They place his preserved head near a prepared abomination host to draw information from his revived remains.",al={"why reanimate othmar","purpose of reviving head","what secrets othmar"}},{q="How did Othmar die?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell says Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Dark Lady, had the pleasure of killing Grand Marshal Garithos herself.",al={"who killed othmar","how did othmar die","othmar death"}},{q="Why is the quest item called the Head of the Baron?",a="The Baron is the name of the towering abomination in the Ruins of Lordaeron. Its head once belonged to Grand Marshal Garithos, Faranell reveals.",al={"head of the baron othmar","why called head of the baron"}},{q="Where is Othmar's new body located?",a="The headless abomination meant to receive Othmar's head is kept in an adjoining chamber within the Undercity. Forsaken practitioners await its reanimation.",al={"where is othmars body","abomination location undercity"}},{q="What happens when the construct awakens?",a="When the head is placed near the assembled construct, its stitched flesh twitches violently to life. The remains panic as they relive the terror of Garithos's final moments alive.",al={"what happens when body wakes","completion reaction othmar"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see the remains of Grand Marshal Garithos used in experiments that recall Lady Sylvanas's conquest of Lordaeron.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Alliance, you see the gruesome fate of Grand Marshal Garithos, an Alliance leader who crossed the Banshee Queen in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you see the Royal Apothecary Society conduct reanimation experiments in the Undercity. The work shows the Forsaken's dark craft and vengeance against former oppressors."},kw={"abomination","forsaken","garithos","grand marshal","head of the baron","othmar","sylvanas","undercity","unending torment"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:alliance"},m={id=97289},src={"In-game quest text: Unending Torment"},fv=true}
E["quest:97290"] = {t="quest",n="Unending Torment",z="general",s="At the Undercity, a defiant subject refuses the Royal Apothecary Society's demands. Master Apothecary Faranell welcomes the news, eager to break a difficult captive.",h="At the Undercity, a defiant subject refuses the Royal Apothecary Society's demands.",sec={{t="Defiance in the Shadows",b="A subject under the Royal Apothecary Society's scrutiny despises you. The captive calls you an abomination and refuses to help. Such hatred is familiar to the Forsaken, for many living beings and captives recoil from Lordaeron's undead.",sp=0},{t="Faranell's Ambition",b="You bring the subject's refusal to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. The head of the Royal Apothecary Society greets the news with wicked delight. To him, resistance makes the subject a challenge, fit for the cruel experiments of the Apothecarium.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Unending Torment?",a="Unending Torment sends you to face a defiant subject tied to the Royal Apothecary Society. The prisoner or hostile being calls you an abomination and refuses to help, so you report this failure to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",al={"unending torment quest","what is unending torment","unending torment lore"}},{q="Who gives the quest Unending Torment?",a="A defiant subject rejects your approach and calls you an abomination. The captive remains nameless in the exchange and sends you back to the Royal Apothecary Society's leadership with your findings.",al={"who starts unending torment","unending torment quest giver","where to get unending torment"}},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society in the Apothecarium, beneath the ruins of Lordaeron in the Undercity. He oversees Forsaken alchemists and researchers who develop plagues, concoctions, and poisons to defend the Forsaken and destroy their enemies across Azeroth.",al={"who is faranell","master apothecary faranell","apothecary faranell role"}},{q="Why does the speaker call the player an abomination?",a="The captive calls you an abomination out of disgust for the undead and their agents. Many living beings and enemies of the Forsaken share this horror of the animated dead in the Undercity.",al={"why abomination","who calls you abomination","why is the prisoner angry"}},{q="Where must you report after completing the task?",a="Report the subject's refusal directly to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. Deep in the Apothecarium, fellow researchers surround him as they make lethal concoctions for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",al={"where to turn in unending torment","unending torment turn in","who to report to unending torment"}},{q="How does Master Apothecary Faranell react to the subject's defiance?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell is pleased by the subject's stubborn refusal. He welcomes the impasse as an entertaining challenge and relishes testing difficult subjects with the Royal Apothecary Society's ruthless methods.",al={"faranell reaction","what does faranell say","does faranell get mad"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know the living may call you an abomination. Helping Master Apothecary Faranell supports the Royal Apothecary Society's grim work.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion in Lordaeron, you see the ruthlessness of your Forsaken allies. Faranell's delight in breaking stubborn captives reveals the dark pragmatism of the Undercity."},kw={"abomination","apothecarium","faranell","forsaken","master apothecary faranell","royal apothecary society","undercity","unending torment"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:undercity"},m={id=97290},src={"In-game quest text: Unending Torment"},fv=true}
E["quest:97291"] = {t="quest",n="Unending Torment",z="general",s="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell prepares a brew to bind a captive to the Dark Lady's will. He needs lethal reagents from across the Forsaken capital to finish it.",h="In the Undercity, Master Apothecary Faranell prepares a brew to bind a captive to the Dark Lady's will.",sec={{t="Binding the Will",b="Deep in the Undercity's Apothecarium, Master Apothecary Faranell conducts experiments to strengthen the Forsaken. He has reattached the severed head of a battered captive. Now he needs a special alchemical mixture to crush the creature's remaining resistance and bind its will to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Reagents",b="Faranell sends his agent across the Undercity to gather potent ingredients for his brew. A Toxic Skullcap comes from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Blisterweed is held by nearby herbalist trainers who owe him a debt, and a poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter sells Essence of Agony.",sp=0},{t="The Masterpiece",b="With the ingredients in hand, Faranell is grimly satisfied with the masterpiece he is about to make. He looks forward to testing the concoction on their 'honored guest.' He trusts the agonizing draught to strip away the captive's remaining bravado and return the stray creature obediently to the Dark Lady's service.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Unending Torment?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell offers it. He leads the Royal Apothecary Society and can be found in the Apothecarium within the Undercity.",al={"who gives unending torment","quest giver unending torment","unending torment start"}},{q="What reagents are needed for Faranell's concoction?",a="Faranell needs three ingredients: a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed from near the herbalism trainers in the Apothecarium, and Essence of Agony from a poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter.",al={"what are the ingredients","unending torment items","what reagents faranell need"}},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell experimenting on?",a="Faranell is experimenting on an unwilling captive whose severed head has just been reattached. He mockingly calls him a 'lost sheep' and an 'honored guest,' and seeks to crush the defiant bravado he clings to after severe beatings.",al={"who is the beast","who is the lost sheep faranell mentions","who is being tortured"}},{q="What is the goal of Faranell's potion?",a="Faranell's potion is meant to mentally break the subject and bind it to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's will. She is the Dark Lady of the Forsaken.",al={"why make this potion","purpose of unending torment potion","what does the concoction do"}},{q="Where can players find Tawny Grisette?",a="Tawny Grisette is in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, where she supplies specialty goods including the Toxic Skullcap the apothecaries need.",al={"where is tawny grisette","toxic skullcap vendor","find miss grisette"}},{q="Where is the Blisterweed located?",a="Blisterweed grows near the Undercity's herbalism trainers, the Alliestars, in the Apothecarium. Faranell says they owe him a favor, so adventurers may take what is needed.",al={"where to find blisterweed","alliestaers herbalism","herbalist trainer undrecity blisterweed"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, alchemical torment to bind reanimated remains to the Dark Lady's service is part of daily life in the Apothecarium.",["faction:Horde"]="The Royal Apothecary Society continues brewing sinister concoctions deep beneath Lordaeron's ruins and testing the limits of alchemical subjugation.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering Blisterweed from the Apothecarium's herbalist trainers shows how ordinary botanical study overlaps with the Society's darker alchemical work.",["class:Rogue"]="The work takes you into the Rogues' Quarter to buy Essence of Agony, a potent reagent favored by poison crafters and assassins."},kw={"apothecarium","blisterweed","essence of agony","faranell","master apothecary faranell","tawny grisette","toxic skullcap","undercity","unending torment"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","subzone:rogues-quarter","topic:rogue"},m={id=97291},src={"In-game quest text: Unending Torment"},fv=true}
E["quest:97292"] = {t="quest",n="Unending Torment",z="general",s="Master Apothecary Faranell sets a punishment in motion beneath the Undercity. In the Apothecarium, the Royal Apothecary Society turns Hissing Serum against Othmar’s remains, seeking lasting retribution for crimes against the Dark Lady.",h="Master Apothecary Faranell sets a punishment in motion beneath the Undercity.",sec={{t="Apothecary Retribution",b="In the Undercity’s Apothecarium, Master Apothecary Faranell conducts harsh experiments against the Forsaken’s enemies. He has prepared Hissing Serum, a caustic substance meant to drip without end onto a captive beneath an alchemical apparatus.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of Garithos",b="Grand Marshal Garithos lies beneath Faranell’s apparatus as Othmar, his remains held in a suspended framework. Faranell judges chemical torment fitting for crimes against the Dark Lady. The serum runs down over Othmar’s body, simmering his flesh as punishment and study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Othmar?",a="Othmar is Grand Marshal Othmar Garithos, the former human commander who made an uneasy alliance with Sylvanas Windrunner during Lordaeron’s reclamation. The Forsaken betrayed and killed him. Master Apothecary Faranell now holds his remains for continued torment and experiments.",al={"who is othmar","what othmar","othmar garithos"}},{q="Why is Othmar being tormented?",a="Othmar Garithos aided Sylvanas Windrunner in taking Capital City back from the dreadlords. Yet he despised non-humans and sought to claim all Lordaeron for humanity. The Forsaken hold him guilty of crimes against the Dark Lady and judge chemical torment fitting for his arrogance and deeds.",al={"why torturing othmar","what did othmar do","crimes against sylvanas"}},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell heads the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity’s Apothecarium. He oversees the making of serums, toxins, and plagues, and directs the operation against Othmar.",al={"faranell role","who gives unending torment","apothecary faranell"}},{q="What does the Hissing Serum do?",a="Hissing Serum is an alchemical brew by Master Apothecary Faranell. It simmers flesh and brings excruciating pain as it flows from an apparatus above Othmar’s suspended body.",al={"what is hissing serum","serum effects","faranell serum"}},{q="Is Othmar alive or undead?",a="Othmar is undead. The Dark Lady slew Garithos herself, and his head has been joined to an abomination’s body that twitches to life. Faranell calls him their “new guest” and intends to keep him suffering beneath the dripping serum.",al={"othmar dead or alive","is garithos alive","state of othmar"}},{q="What does Faranell plan to do with Othmar next?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell plans to keep Othmar’s flesh simmering beneath the dripping apparatus and watch him closely. He says he has extensive plans for Othmar’s future, with further experiments and retribution in store.",al={"faranell future plans","what happens to othmar next","othmar future"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity. For the Forsaken, punishing enemies of the Dark Lady like Garithos is central to their retribution.",["faction:Horde"]="By helping Faranell in the Undercity, you take part in the severe methods the Forsaken use against those who have crossed them and the Banshee Queen."},kw={"apothecarium","dark lady","garithos","hissing serum","master apothecary faranell","othmar","undercity","unending torment"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell"},m={id=97292},src={"In-game quest text: Unending Torment"},fv=true}
E["quest:97326"] = {t="quest",n="Rocks to Rests",z="general",s="Behind Grommash Hold, Thra and friends make room for games in Orgrimmar. They need smooth boulders to use as chairs and tables.",h="Behind Grommash Hold, Thra and friends make room for games in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Quiet Corner of Orgrimmar",b="Young orcs gather in a dirt clearing behind Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. There they can play away from the fortress guards. The open ground suits their miniature figures, but with no furniture, they sit in the dust.",sp=0},{t="Makeshift Furniture",b="Thra spots you passing and asks you to carry eight medium-sized, smooth boulders to the clearing. Their flat sides will make sturdy chairs and low tables. Then the youths can arrange their games without sitting in the dirt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Rocks to Rests?",a="Thra is a young orc playing games with friends in the clearing behind Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. Thra is observant and playful, and asks passersby to help improve the play area.",al={"who gives rocks to rests","thra orgrimmar","who is thra"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The clearing lies directly behind Grommash Hold, Warchief Thrall's seat in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom. The children gather in this relatively clear patch of dirt, away from the fortress's heavy traffic.",al={"where is rocks to rests","thra location","where behind grommash hold"}},{q="Why does Thra need smooth boulders?",a="Thra and the other youths need smooth, medium-sized rocks for chairs and tables. Without furniture, they sit in the dirt while arranging and playing their miniature games.",al={"why rocks","what are smooth boulders for","why boulders"}},{q="What game is being played behind Grommash Hold?",a="Thra and the other youths play an informal tabletop game with small figures spread across the ground. The smooth boulders will give them steady places for their figures and somewhere comfortable to sit.",al={"what game are they playing","thra game orgrimmar","figures behind grommash hold"}},{q="Does Rocks to Rests involve fighting?",a="No. This is a peaceful undertaking, with no fighting or military trial. You use your strength to haul heavy boulders to the children's game spot.",al={"is rocks to rests dangerous","any combat rocks to rests"}},{q="What do the children do with the boulders once delivered?",a="After you deliver the eight smooth boulders, Thra and the children move them around the clearing. Their flat sides make seats and tables for the figures in their tabletop game.",al={"what happens after rocks to rests","what does thra do with rocks"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Helping young orcs behind the Warchief's stronghold shows how community and everyday life matter in Orgrimmar, even in a warrior society.",["race:Orc"]="Orc youths making games behind Grommash Hold show how the next generation grows up in the heart of Durotar."},kw={"durotar","grommash hold","orcs","orgrimmar","rocks to rests","smooth boulders","tabletop","thra"},rel={"subzone:grommash-hold"},m={id=97326},src={"In-game quest text: Rocks to Rests"},fv=true}
E["quest:97328"] = {t="quest",n="Anything of Value",z="general",s="A zeppelin crash in Stranglethorn Vale leaves signs that a shipment was plundered. Its torn label still points toward Booty Bay.",h="A zeppelin crash in Stranglethorn Vale leaves signs that a shipment was plundered.",sec={{t="A Torn Label",b="In Stranglethorn Vale, the crash debris holds signs of a plundered supply shipment. Its labels are shredded, though one still bears the words Booty Bay. Two-toed footprints and divots in the earth lead toward the ruins of Zul'Kunda in the northwest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the shipment?",a="The supplies were plundered, and the shipping labels were torn apart.",al={"stolen shipment","zeppelin cargo","what was plundered"}},{q="Where did the footprints lead?",a="The footprints and divots lead toward the ruins of Zul'Kunda in the northwest.",al={"two toed tracks","where is the trail","footprints"}},{q="What does the surviving label say?",a="One torn label still shows the words Booty Bay.",al={"booty bay label","torn shipping label","where was it going"}},{q="Who needs the recovered shipments?",a="The shipments are to be returned to someone in Booty Bay.",al={"who wants the cargo","where do I take it","shipment return"}}},kw={"anything of value","booty bay","crash","footprints","shipment","stolen supplies","zeppelin","zul'kunda"},rel={"zone:stranglethorn","subzone:booty-bay","quest:98247"},m={id=97328},src={"In-game quest text: Anything of Value"},fv=true}
E["quest:97453"] = {t="quest",n="Weed Whacked",z="general",s="Gemmil asks you to deal with the Carnivorous Weeds south of Grom'gol. They frightened Gemmil while the young student was gathering plants, and the camp's safety is at stake.",h="Gemmil asks you to deal with the Carnivorous Weeds south of Grom'gol.",sec={{t="A Frightened Student",b="Gemmil was gathering plants outside the gates of the jungle camp when huge weeds appeared and spat at the young student. Gemmil escaped unharmed, but now cannot play outside the camp. You are asked to make the area south of Grom'gol safe and then speak with Gemmil's mother.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gemmil?",a="Gemmil is a young student of herbalism who hopes to become an alchemist.",al={"gemmil who","who's gemmil"}},{q="What happened to Gemmil?",a="While gathering plants outside the gates, Gemmil was frightened by huge weeds that spat at them. Gemmil escaped unharmed.",al={"gemmil attacked","weeds spitting"}},{q="Where are the Carnivorous Weeds?",a="The Carnivorous Weeds are south of Grom'gol.",al={"weed location","where weeds"}},{q="Why can't Gemmil play outside camp?",a="Gemmil's parents no longer let them play outside the camp after the weeds frightened them.",al={"gemmil can't play","why no outside"}},{q="Who should you speak with after making the area safe?",a="After making the area south of Grom'gol safe, you are asked to inform Gemmil's mother.",al={"tell gemmil's mum","gemmil's mother"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a student of herbalism, you can understand Gemmil's wish to study plants and become an alchemist."},kw={"alchemist","carnivorous weeds","gemmil","grom'gol","herbalism","jungle","weed whacked"},m={id=97453},src={"In-game quest text: Weed Whacked"},fv=true}
E["quest:97485"] = {t="quest",n="Traditions of the Bluff",z="general",s="A Tauren tradition asks you to scatter incense from Hunter’s Rise. The offering may honor the Earthmother, a hunt, an occasion, or a search for guidance.",h="A Tauren tradition asks you to scatter incense from Hunter’s Rise.",sec={{t="Incense to the Winds",b="A Tauren at Hunter’s Rise asks you to honor a tradition of scattering incense to the winds. You gather herbs, cedar twigs, sinew thread, and ceremonial flint and tinder from the named suppliers. At the ceremonial site, you combine them and scatter the incense from the south-facing cliff.",sp=0},{t="Many Occasions",b="Incense may be scattered to ask the Earthmother to watch over someone, bless a hunt, mark an occasion, or seek guidance from the ancestors. The act is reverent, though it need not follow a single ceremony. Different tribes observe different traditional steps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the tradition at Hunter’s Rise?",a="The tradition is to scatter incense to the winds from the south-facing cliff of Hunter’s Rise.",al={"incense tradition","scatter incense","bluff incense"}},{q="What can the incense offering be for?",a="It may ask the Earthmother to watch over someone, bless a hunt, celebrate an occasion, or offer guidance from the ancestors.",al={"why incense","incense for what","bless the hunt"}},{q="What do I need to make the incense?",a="The components are herbs, cedar twigs, sinew thread, and ceremonial flint and tinder.",al={"incense ingredients","what components","herbs cedar thread flint"}},{q="Where is the ceremonial site?",a="The ceremonial site is on the south-facing cliff of Hunter’s Rise.",al={"where to spread incense","ceremonial site location","south cliff"}},{q="Do all tribes perform the tradition the same way?",a="No. Different tribes may observe different traditional steps, and the act is not strictly ceremonial.",al={"different tribe customs","same ceremony","incense steps"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you honor a tradition that may invoke the Earthmother or seek guidance from your ancestors."},kw={"ancestors","cedar twigs","ceremonial flint","earthmother","hunter’s rise","incense","tauren tradition","traditions of the bluff"},rel={"npc:nida"},m={id=97485},src={"In-game quest text: Traditions of the Bluff"},fv=true}
E["quest:97538"] = {t="quest",n="Pigments for Paints",z="general",s="Tah Winterhoof needs red pigment for his paints, and you can help him replenish it. The color comes from mirkweed pods gathered in Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains.",h="Tah Winterhoof needs red pigment for his paints, and you can help him replenish it.",sec={{t="An Artisan's Need",b="Tah Winterhoof has run out of red pigment and cannot continue his work. He lives in Thunder Bluff, and his traveling days are behind him. So he asks you to make the long journey north into the Stonetalon Mountains and gather more coloring.",sp=0},{t="The Waters of Mirkfallon",b="Mirkfallon Lake lies in a mountain pass in the Stonetalon Mountains. Mirkweed grows beneath its waters, and its seed pods turn red when harvested and dried. Gather thirty pods, and Tah will have the raw material he needs to return to his work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Pigments for Paints?",a="Tah Winterhoof asks for help in Thunder Bluff. His traveling days are behind him, so he needs someone younger to gather materials for his craft.",al={"who gives pigments for paints","pigments quest giver","tah winterhoof location"}},{q="Where are Mirkweed Pods found?",a="Mirkweed grows in the waters of Mirkfallon Lake, a large, round lake in a mountain pass in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where to find mirkweed pods","mirkweed location","where is mirkfallon lake"}},{q="Why does Tah Winterhoof need mirkweed?",a="Tah Winterhoof has run out of red pigment for his artwork. Dried mirkweed pods turn red and provide dye for his paints.",al={"why collect mirkweed","what is mirkweed used for","why red pigment"}},{q="How many Mirkweed Pods are needed?",a="Tah Winterhoof needs thirty Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake to replenish his red pigment.",al={"how many pods needed","mirkweed count"}},{q="What is mirkweed?",a="Mirkweed is an aquatic plant that grows in Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Its pods dry into red pigment.",al={"what kind of plant is mirkweed","mirkweed details"}},{q="Where is Tah Winterhoof located?",a="Tah Winterhoof lives atop the mesa city of Thunder Bluff in Mulgore, where he practices his craft and prepares traditional paints.",al={"where is tah winterhoof","tah winterhoof thunder bluff"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see how Thunder Bluff artisans use natural plants to make traditional pigments and dyes.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know that aquatic plants such as mirkweed can provide useful pigments beyond medicinal herbs. Mirkfallon Lake's waters are dangerous.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the ties between Thunder Bluff and the rugged passes of the Stonetalon Mountains."},kw={"mirkfallon lake","mirkweed","mirkweed pods","pigments for paints","red pigment","stonetalon mountains","tah winterhoof","thunder bluff"},rel={"subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon","zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=97538},src={"In-game quest text: Pigments for Paints"},fv=true}
E["quest:97539"] = {t="quest",n="Silky Sutures",z="general",s="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor is turning to spider silk as infirmary supplies dwindle. Siege damage remains unrepaired, and the outpost's guards and laborers still need care.",h="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor is turning to spider silk as infirmary supplies dwindle.",sec={{t="The Crumbling Outpost",b="Hammerfall endures in the Arathi Highlands, though siege damage still mars its defenses. Doctor Gregory Victor, the outpost's physician, sees the neglect as official policy. With little support and crumbling fortifications around him, he keeps the infirmary running. Its care helps laborers and sentinel guards stay on their feet and ready for conflict.",sp=0},{t="Makeshift Medical Supplies",b="Medical supplies are running low at Hammerfall, so Doctor Victor seeks another way to stitch wounds. Tough highland spider silk can be twisted into resilient sutures when bandages and ordinary thread are scarce. Victor jokes that infection is the least of a wounded soldier's worries. The silk gives the infirmary thread to patch up defenders in hostile territory.",sp=0},{t="Gallows Humor in Hammerfall",b="Doctor Gregory Victor greets travelers with dry jokes about grave prognoses and stitches made from spider silk. His humor masks the hard truth of running a frontline clinic while Hammerfall remains isolated. Regular aid is rare in the highlands, and travelers can help keep the clinic supplied. Victor relies on improvised remedies and determination to care for the wounded as the outpost decays around him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor oversees Hammerfall's infirmary as its medical officer and trauma surgeon. He treats wounded guards and laborers with a blunt manner and mordant wit. Despite shortages and unrepaired siege damage, he keeps the ward working.",al={"who is victor","gregory victor lore","hammerfall doctor"}},{q="Why does Doctor Victor need spider silk?",a="Doctor Victor needs spider silk because Hammerfall's infirmary is nearly out of ordinary supplies. He twists strong highland spider silk into sutures to close wounds when proper thread is unavailable.",al={"why spider silk","surgical spidersilk use","spider silk sutures"}},{q="What condition is Hammerfall in during this quest?",a="Hammerfall shows clear signs of neglect and strain. Its siege damage remains unrepaired, and Doctor Victor sees that neglect as official policy. With little aid or supplies, the guards, laborers, and medical staff must make do.",al={"hammerfall status","why is hammerfall damaged","state of hammerfall"}},{q="Where do the spiders for this quest come from?",a="The spiders roam the wilderness of the Arathi Highlands around Hammerfall. They must be hunted across the highland plains to gather silk for Doctor Victor's sutures, then brought back to the clinic.",al={"arathi spiders","where to find spidersilk","surgical spidersilk location"}},{q="Why is Doctor Victor sarcastic about infection?",a="Doctor Victor jokes that infection is the least of a wounded soldier's worries when he stitches them with spider silk. His dark humor reflects the demands of frontline care, where stopping blood loss and treating grave wounds come before sterile conditions.",al={"doctor humor","spider silk infection","victor jokes"}},{q="Why are supplies so scarce at Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is isolated in a contested part of the Arathi Highlands and faces hostile threats. Reinforcements and supplies arrive infrequently, leaving the garrison and infirmary short of materials, tools, and healing supplies.",al={"why no supplies","hammerfall supply shortage","lack of help hammerfall"}},{q="Who does the infirmary in Hammerfall treat?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor's infirmary treats the laborers and guards stationed at Hammerfall. Keeping them healthy helps the outpost remain fortified and functional despite danger and structural damage.",al={"who does victor treat","hammerfall patients","clinic patients"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall is a vital Horde stronghold in the Arathi Highlands. Doctor Victor's work keeps its defenders healthy and ready to protect the faction's position there.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you bring the Forsaken's pragmatic, unsentimental medical knowledge to Hammerfall, using resources from the highlands to keep the clinic working."},kw={"arathi highlands","doctor gregory victor","field sutures","hammerfall","infirmary","silky sutures","spider silk","surgical spidersilk"},rel={"npc:doctor-gregory-victor","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi"},m={id=97539},src={"In-game quest text: Silky Sutures"},fv=true}
E["quest:97583"] = {t="quest",n="WRIGGLE.",z="general",s="In Undercity, WRIGGLE. dances with travelers, then tires and needs special sludge to recover. After feeding, it follows a new friend.",h="In Undercity, WRIGGLE.",sec={{t="A Dancing Slime",b="In Undercity, WRIGGLE. joins the dances of friendly travelers. The little slime starts full of energy, but soon tires and needs food to regain its strength.",sp=0},{t="Sustenance from the Canals",b="You can buy Nutritious Slime Sludge in Undercity's rancid canals. WRIGGLE. absorbs the foul treat and regains its energy. Then it bonds with the one who fed it and is ready to follow its new friend.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is WRIGGLE.?",a="You befriend WRIGGLE. by dancing with the lively little slime. It needs special food to keep up its energy.",al={"wriggle quest","what is wriggle","slime dance quest"}},{q="Where do you find Nutritious Slime Sludge?",a="A vendor sells Nutritious Slime Sludge in Undercity's canals, where alchemical waste and runoff are common.",al={"where to get sludge","nutritious slime sludge vendor","feed slime undrecity"}},{q="How do you catch the slime's attention if it seems tired?",a="Dance with the tired or distracted slime, and it mirrors your playful movements.",al={"how to get slime attention","tired slime","wake slime wriggle"}},{q="Why does the slime feed on sludge?",a="Slimes absorb alchemical ooze and sludge around them to stay strong and regain vitality after exertion.",al={"why slime eat sludge","what do slimes eat"}},{q="What happens once the slime is fed?",a="Once fed its preferred sludge, the revitalized slime bonds with you and seeks to follow you.",al={"does slime follow you","slime companion","wriggle reward"}},{q="Can Alliance players easily obtain the sludge?",a="Alliance travelers face great peril entering Undercity. Vendors in the canals of the Forsaken capital sell the sludge.",al={"can alliance do wriggle","alliance slime sludge"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the toxic runoff and animated slimes in Undercity's canals well. A slime companion feels at home with you.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you can trade with local vendors in the canals of Undercity, the Forsaken capital, to obtain the special sludge."},kw={"canals","excitable slime","nutritious slime sludge","slime","sludge","undercity","wriggle"},rel={"zone:undercity"},m={id=97583},src={"In-game quest text: WRIGGLE."},fv=true}
E["quest:97891"] = {t="quest",n="Prompt Potion Runner",z="general",s="In Undercity, a runner carries Alessandro’s brew across the slime canal before it spoils. The delivery must reach the Apothecarium in time.",h="In Undercity, a runner carries Alessandro’s brew across the slime canal before it spoils.",sec={{t="A Race Against Decay",b="Alessandro needs a swift courier in Undercity’s underground corridors. The Forsaken alchemist has made a volatile brew that will soon spoil. His undead joints are too frail for him to cross the toxic slime canal, so you carry it intact before it turns to useless sludge.",sp=0},{t="The Apothecarium's Demands",b="Doctor Martin Felben waits at the Apothecarium for the brew, which he needs for his ongoing research. He says the six potions Alessandro sent before this one destabilized in transit. A timely delivery lets the doctor continue his shadowy experiments without interruption. The unstable brew and Alessandro’s frail joints show the hazards of Forsaken alchemy and undeath.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Alessandro in Undercity needs you to carry the delivery. His undead knees pop out and rattle when he tries to run, so he cannot race across the slime canal himself.",al={"who gives prompt potion runner","who starts prompt potion runner","who is alessandro"}},{q="Where does the potion need to go?",a="Take the potion to Doctor Martin Felben at the Apothecarium in Undercity, where he conducts alchemical experiments.",al={"where do you take the potion","who is doctor martin felben","prompt potion runner turn in"}},{q="Why is the delivery timed?",a="The concoction is unstable and has a very short shelf life. Carry it quickly across the canal or it will destabilize and become useless.",al={"why timed","unstable potion shelf life","why hurry"}},{q="Have other delivery attempts failed?",a="Doctor Martin Felben says the six potions Alessandro tried to send before this one destabilized before reaching the Apothecarium.",al={"did other couriers fail","alessandro past attempts","how many potions failed"}},{q="Why can't Alessandro deliver the potion himself?",a="Alessandro says his knees rattle and pop out whenever he tries to run. These effects of undeath keep him from rushing the delivery himself.",al={"why cant alessandro deliver it","alessandro knees"}},{q="What are Doctor Felben's experiments?",a="Doctor Martin Felben is an apothecary who conducts experiments in the Apothecarium. The exact formula remains obscure, and he resumes his research when the stable mixture arrives.",al={"what does doctor felben do","what is the potion used for"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know brittle joints and decaying knees can hinder vital Royal Apothecary Society laboratory work.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help the Forsaken with dangerous alchemical work in Undercity, where travelers must cross toxic slime canals."},kw={"alessandro","apothecarium","doctor martin felben","prompt potion runner","royal apothecary society","slime canal","undercity","unstable potion"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium"},m={id=97891},src={"In-game quest text: Prompt Potion Runner"},fv=true}
E["quest:97899"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="An alchemist in Orgrimmar can learn to craft a Mana Well for a camp. It offers healers and spellcasters a refreshing drink, while setting it up calls for a campfire.",h="An alchemist in Orgrimmar can learn to craft a Mana Well for a camp.",sec={{t="A Well for Camp",b="Someone in Orgrimmar asks you to speak with Whuut once you have shown skill in alchemy. Whuut can teach you to craft a Mana Well, a camping item that draws healers and spellcasters seeking refreshment. To set up camp in the wilderness, you also need a campfire. A cooking trainer can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a Mana Well?",a="Whuut in Orgrimmar can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you have shown proficiency in alchemy.",al={"mana well trainer","whuut alchemy","who is whuut"}},{q="What does a Mana Well do?",a="A Mana Well is a camping item that offers a refreshing taste to healers and spellcasters.",al={"mana well use","what is mana well","camp mana"}},{q="Can I set up camp in town?",a="Most people do not care for camps set up in the center of town, so the completion text points you toward the wilderness to try out your Mana Well.",al={"camp in orgrimmar","mana well town","camping town"}},{q="What else do I need for a camp?",a="A campfire is needed as the basis of a camp. A cooking trainer can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","camp setup","fire for camp"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemy","campfire","camping","healers","mana well","orgrimmar","spellcasters","whuut"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=97899},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97900"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="In Razor Hill, Dwukk can teach you a camp craft suited to your blacksmithing skill. A Sharpening Wheel gives nearby fighters a way to hone their weapons.",h="In Razor Hill, Dwukk can teach you a camp craft suited to your blacksmithing skill.",sec={{t="A camp craft",b="Dwukk teaches you to craft a Sharpening Wheel once you show skill in blacksmithing. Set it up at a wilderness camp, where nearby fighters and rogues can hone their weapons.\n\nYou need a campfire to start your camp. Cooks can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Sharpening Wheel?",a="Dwukk in Razor Hill teaches you to craft a Sharpening Wheel once you show skill in blacksmithing.",al={"sharpening wheel trainer","dwukk blacksmithing","who teaches camping blacksmithing"}},{q="What does the Sharpening Wheel do?",a="Nearby fighters and rogues can use a Sharpening Wheel at your camp to hone their weapons.",al={"sharpening wheel use","what's the wheel for","hone weapons camp"}},{q="Where can I try out my camp?",a="Try out your camp in the wilderness. Camps should not be set up in the center of town.",al={"where to set up camp","camping location","camp in town"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. You need a campfire to start your camp, and cooks can teach you how to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","fire for camping"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can learn from Dwukk to craft a Sharpening Wheel for a wilderness camp.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can hone your weapons at a nearby Sharpening Wheel set up at camp."},kw={"blacksmithing","campfire","camping","dwukk","razor hill","rogues","sharpening wheel","weapons"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","topic:rogue"},m={id=97900},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97901"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="You can make an Enchanted Lute, but townsfolk dislike camps in town centers. To set up camp in the wilderness, you need a fire.",h="You can make an Enchanted Lute, but townsfolk dislike camps in town centers.",sec={{t="A Campfire First",b="A campfire gives you the basis for your camp. Most cooks can show you how to make one, so seek a cooking trainer if you have not learned the basics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I craft?",a="You can craft an Enchanted Lute.",al={"enchanted lute","make a lute","camping lute"}},{q="Where can I try it out?",a="You need to head into the wilderness to try it out. Most folks dislike camps in town centers.",al={"where to camp","camping spot","try the lute"}},{q="Why do I need a campfire?",a="Your camp begins with a campfire.",al={"need campfire","camp fire","camping fire"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a fire?",a="Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. Ask a cooking trainer if you have not learned the basics.",al={"learn fire","cooking trainer","make campfire"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make a fire for the basis of a camp."},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","enchanted lute","fire","wilderness"},m={id=97901},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97902"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Engineering",z="general",s="A teacher points you to Mukdrak in Razor Hill, who can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you prove your engineering skill. The bot helps keep a camp supplied with materials for spells.",h="A teacher points you to Mukdrak in Razor Hill, who can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you prove your...",sec={{t="A Bot for Camp",b="An engineer can learn to make a Reagent Bot from Mukdrak in Razor Hill once you show proficiency in your skill. The automaton helps keep you and your allies supplied with materials used to fuel spells. To try it at camp, head into the wilderness; townsfolk do not welcome camps in the center of town.",sp=0},{t="Ready the Fire",b="A camp also needs a campfire before it can be set up. Most cooks can teach you how to make one, so you can seek out someone who trains cooks if you need the basics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Reagent Bot?",a="Mukdrak in Razor Hill can teach you to craft a Reagent Bot after you show proficiency in engineering.",al={"mukdrak bot","who teaches reagent bot","reagent bot trainer"}},{q="What does the Reagent Bot do?",a="The Reagent Bot helps keep you and your allies supplied with materials used to fuel spells.",al={"what bot do","reagent bot use","bot for camp"}},{q="Where should I set up my camp?",a="The completion text advises heading into the wilderness to try the bot, since most folk dislike camps set up in the center of town.",al={"camp where","camping location","where test bot"}},{q="What else do I need before setting up camp?",a="You need a campfire before starting your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","camp setup","fire for camp"}},{q="Who can teach me the basics of making a campfire?",a="Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of making a campfire.",al={"campfire teacher","learn make fire","cooking fire"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101","engineering","mukdrak","razor hill","reagent bot"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={id=97902},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Engineering"},fv=true}
E["quest:97903"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="general",s="At Rawrk's camp in Razor Hill, capable travelers learn to make a First Aid Kit for the wilderness. The lesson covers where to camp and why a fire matters.",h="At Rawrk's camp in Razor Hill, capable travelers learn to make a First Aid Kit for the wilderness.",sec={{t="Survival on the Frontier",b="Rawrk in Razor Hill teaches capable travelers to make a First Aid Kit. With one, you can tend wounds far from an apothecary or infirmary, where help may be hard to find.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Campfire",b="Rawrk warns you against pitching a tent in the middle of Razor Hill or another settlement. Find an open place in the wild instead. A camp also needs a fire to see you through the night. Learn basic firemaking from a cooking instructor before you set out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rawrk and where is he found?",a="Rawrk teaches survival campcraft in Razor Hill, Durotar. He shows capable travelers how to make First Aid Kits for the wilderness.",al={"who teaches camping first aid","where is rawrk","camping 101 trainer"}},{q="What is required before setting up a wilderness camp?",a="Choose an open place in the wild and build a proper campfire. Rawrk warns against camping within town limits and advises you to learn firemaking from a cooking instructor first.",al={"what do i need to camp","how to make a camp","campfire requirement camping"}},{q="Can camps be pitched inside towns or settlements?",a="No. Residents object to tents in the middle of settlements, so find an open place in the wild for your camp.",al={"can i camp in razor hill","camping inside cities","where can i place my camp"}},{q="What does this training teach adventurers to craft?",a="The training teaches you to make a personal First Aid Kit for tending wounds on wilderness journeys.",al={"camping 101 first aid reward","what item does this teach","first aid kit crafting"}},{q="Why does Rawrk recommend learning cooking?",a="A proper camp needs a fire. Cooking instructors teach basic firemaking, so Rawrk recommends learning from one before you set out.",al={"why do i need cooking for camping","cooking campfire camping"}},{q="What prerequisites are needed before learning this craft?",a="You need to show basic proficiency in medical and survival skills before Rawrk teaches you to make a field First Aid Kit.",al={"prerequisites for camping 101 first aid","skill needed for camping first aid"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can learn this training in Razor Hill, Durotar, to help sustain yourself across Kalimdor's rugged frontiers.",["profession:Cooking"]="As someone who knows Cooking, you know campcraft needs fire. Rawrk says a proper camp requires a fire, a skill taught by cooking trainers."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","durotar","first aid kit","rawrk","razor hill","survival","wilderness camp"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={id=97903},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97904"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="At your camp, fishing can bring comfort to you and your companions. Near Sen'jin Village, Lau'Tiki can teach you to make a Fish Bowl.",h="At your camp, fishing can bring comfort to you and your companions.",sec={{t="A Camp Comfort",b="Once you have shown skill in fishing, speak with Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village. Lau'Tiki can teach you to make a Fish Bowl, a fixture for camp meant to bring joy to you and your fellow adventurers. A happier camp, the giver hopes, makes for stronger fighters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can fishing do for my camp?",a="Your fishing skill can help you learn to make a Fish Bowl for your camp.",al={"fishing camp item","camping fishing"}},{q="Who teaches me to make a Fish Bowl?",a="Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village can teach you to make a Fish Bowl once you have shown skill in fishing.",al={"fish bowl teacher","Lau'Tiki fishing"}},{q="What is the Fish Bowl for?",a="The Fish Bowl is a camping fixture meant to bring joy to you and your fellow adventurers.",al={"fish bowl use","camp fish fixture"}},{q="Where can I find Lau'Tiki?",a="Lau'Tiki is near Sen'jin Village.",al={"Lau'Tiki location","Sen'jin fishing"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a fisher, you can learn to make a Fish Bowl for your camp once you have shown skill in fishing."},kw={"camp fixture","camping","fish bowl","fisherman","fishing","lau'tiki","sen'jin village"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village"},m={id=97904},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97905"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="You learn to make incense candles from wild plants in Camping 101: Herbalism. First, though, a proper camp needs a fire, and your campsite belongs in the wilderness beyond town.",h="You learn to make incense candles from wild plants in Camping 101: Herbalism.",sec={{t="Aromatic Craft of the Wild",b="Herbalism lets you turn gathered plants into incense candles for comfort on the trail. Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in city streets, so these candles are meant for camps beyond guarded settlements.",sp=0},{t="The Heart of the Campsite",b="A campfire belongs at the heart of every campsite. Set one before you use an incense candle. Herbalists provide the aromatic burn, while cooking trainers across the land teach travelers the basics of starting a fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an incense candle?",a="Herbalists craft incense candles from wild plants. Burn one at a wilderness campsite beside a campfire.",al={"what is incense candle","incense candle use","camping herbalism item"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="You can set up camp in the open wilderness. Townsfolk object to tents spread across town thoroughfares.",al={"where to make camp","can i camp in town","camping in cities"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire to set up a camp?",a="A camp needs a campfire at its heart. Cooking trainers across Azeroth teach basic fire-building techniques.",al={"how to make campfire","campfire needed for camp","cook campfire camping"}},{q="Who teaches how to make a campfire?",a="Cooking trainers teach you to kindle a simple campfire. Learn the basics of cooking before you head into the wild.",al={"who teaches campfires","learn to build fire","cooking trainer fire"}},{q="How does herbalism tie into camping?",a="Herbalism provides the plants and resins for incense candles. Gathered from the wilds, they bring soothing aromas to your campsite.",al={"herbalism connection to camping","why herbalism camping","what does herbalism give for camps"}},{q="Do you need a campfire to use an incense candle?",a="A camp needs a proper campfire. Set one before you settle in to use an incense candle.",al={"can i light incense candle without fire","incense candle campfire requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you learn to make incense candles from gathered plants for use at wilderness camps.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you learn to kindle the campfire at the heart of every camp."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping","cooking","herbalism","incense candle","wilderness"},m={id=97905},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97906"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="In Orgrimmar, Karolek can teach you to craft a leatherworker’s tent once you have shown skill in your profession. A tent offers shelter on your travels, though setting camp also calls for a campfire.",h="In Orgrimmar, Karolek can teach you to craft a leatherworker’s tent once you have shown skill in your...",sec={{t="A Place to Camp",b="A leatherworker in Orgrimmar points you to Karolek, who can teach you to make a tent for your travels. It offers shade on hot days and shelter from rain, giving you a place to rest while journeying. Once you have shown proficiency in leatherworking, Karolek can teach you to craft this camping item.",sp=0},{t="Campfire First",b="Your tent is ready, but a campfire completes the camp. Cooks can teach you to make one, and a cooking trainer can show you the basics. To try your tent, leave the center of town and set it up in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a leatherworker’s tent?",a="Karolek in Orgrimmar can teach you to craft a tent after you show proficiency in leatherworking.",al={"tent trainer","who teaches leatherworking tent","karolek tent"}},{q="What does the tent do?",a="The tent gives you shelter from rain and shade on hot days, and offers a place to rest on your travels.",al={"what is the tent for","leatherworking camping item","tent use"}},{q="Can I set up my tent in town?",a="The completion text says most people do not care for tents set up in the center of town, so you need to go into the wilderness to try it out.",al={"tent in town","where can i camp","camping location"}},{q="What else do I need to start a camp?",a="You need a campfire as well as a tent. Cooks can teach you to make a fire.",al={"need campfire","camp fire how","what completes a camp"}},{q="Who can teach me the basics of cooking?",a="Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of the culinary arts.",al={"cooking trainer","learn culinary arts","campfire trainer"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn to make the campfire needed to complete a camp."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","camping item","cooking","karolek","leatherworking","orgrimmar","tent"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=97906},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97907"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="In Durotar, skilled miners can learn to forge a Lodestone for camps in the wild. Krunn in Razor Hill teaches the craft.",h="In Durotar, skilled miners can learn to forge a Lodestone for camps in the wild.",sec={{t="The Miner's Camp",b="Mining yields materials for travel and survival in the wild. With skill in pick and ore, you can learn to make gear for a campsite. In Durotar, Krunn in Razor Hill teaches skilled miners to forge a Lodestone for their travels.",sp=0},{t="Campfire Camaraderie",b="At a wilderness camp, a Lodestone gives the gathered fighters greater strength in battle. Set it beside the campfire, and martial fighters around the flames gain an edge. Townsfolk frown on tents pitched in city squares, so you need the open wild to put your craft to use.",sp=0},{t="Fire and Fieldcraft",b="A sturdy Lodestone needs a fire at the heart of camp. You need a basic campfire before setting up a resting place. If you do not know how to build one, seek a cooking instructor. Cooking teaches the basics for warmth and sustenance on expeditions beyond town walls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Mining?",a="Skilled miners can seek Krunn in Razor Hill and learn to craft a Lodestone for a campsite.",al={"what is camping 101 mining","camping mining quest","mining lodestone quest"}},{q="Who is Krunn?",a="Krunn trains skilled miners in Razor Hill, in Durotar. Once they show enough skill, he teaches them to make camp items such as the Lodestone.",al={"who is krunn","where is krunn","razor hill trainer"}},{q="What is a Lodestone used for?",a="Miners make Lodestones to place beside a wilderness campfire. Physical fighters gathered around it gain greater martial strength.",al={"what does a lodestone do","lodestone benefit","why craft lodestone"}},{q="Can you set up camp inside Razor Hill?",a="No. Townsfolk and settlement authorities frown on camps in populated streets. Head into the surrounding wilderness to pitch camp and place your Lodestone.",al={"can i camp in town","why cant i camp in razor hill","camping inside cities"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire before setting up camp?",a="A campfire forms the center of a working campsite. Cooking instructors teach you to build a basic fire, and cooking helps prepare you for camps in the wild.",al={"do i need a campfire","how to start camp","fire requirement camping"}},{q="Who can learn to craft a Lodestone?",a="Miners who show enough skill can learn to craft a Lodestone from Krunn in Razor Hill.",al={"who can make lodestones","can anyone make a lodestone"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can unearth raw minerals and make field gear such as a Lodestone to support your allies at camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn from cooking instructors to build the basic campfire at the heart of a wilderness campsite.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde miner traveling through Durotar, you can visit Krunn in Razor Hill to learn how to make Lodestones for your expeditions."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101: mining","cooking","durotar","krunn","lodestone","mining","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill"},m={id=97907},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97908"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="In Orgrimmar, new skinners are sent to Thuwd to learn the craft of camping. You make a Camp Chair from hides and pelts, then carry it beyond the city to open country.",h="In Orgrimmar, new skinners are sent to Thuwd to learn the craft of camping.",sec={{t="Comfort in the Wild",b="In Orgrimmar, Thuwd teaches capable skinners to make a Camp Chair from cured hides. The pelts and hides of fallen beasts can serve beyond armorcraft. A skinner can put them to use in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Rules of the Trail",b="Thuwd warns that guards and townsfolk frown on camps along busy city streets. A chair belongs in open country, away from settlement walls. A proper campsite needs a warm campfire, too. Cooks across Kalimdor teach the basics of making one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches skinners how to make camp items?",a="In Orgrimmar, Thuwd teaches skinners how to make camp items. Skinners speak with him after showing basic skill in their craft.",al={"who gives camping 101 skinning","who to speak to in orgrimmar","who is thuwd"}},{q="What camping item can skinners craft?",a="Skinners can make a Camp Chair from the hides and pelts of fallen beasts. It offers a comfortable seat while they rest in the wild.",al={"what do skinners make for camp","skinning camping craft","camp chair skinning"}},{q="Can you set up a camp chair inside a city?",a="City residents and guards frown on campsite equipment in town. Travel beyond settlement gates into the wilderness to pitch camp and set out your chair.",al={"can i camp in orgrimmar","camps in city","where to pitch camp"}},{q="What else is required to complete a camp?",a="A proper campsite needs a fire for warmth, visibility, and cooking. Before you pitch camp, ask a cooking trainer how to build a simple campfire.",al={"why need campfire","camp prerequisites","how to set up camp"}},{q="Why should an adventurer craft a camp chair?",a="A comfortable chair gives you a place to rest between hunts and recover from the road before your next skirmish.",al={"skinning benefit camping","why rest in camp chair","camp chair benefits"}},{q="When does Thuwd teach the Camp Chair pattern?",a="Thuwd shares the Camp Chair pattern after skinners prove basic skill at harvesting skins and hides from fallen beasts.",al={"when can i learn camp chair","camping 101 requirements","skinning skill needed"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Thuwd trains skinners in Orgrimmar, so Horde adventurers traveling from Durotar can learn this wilderness craft there.",["profession:Cooking"]="A proper campsite needs both a seat and heat. As a new skinner, you are encouraged to study cooking basics and learn to build a campfire."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping","camping 101: skinning","orgrimmar","skinning","thuwd"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar"},m={id=97908},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97915"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="An Alchemist can learn to craft a Mana Well from Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind. It gives healers and spellcasters a refreshing taste at camp.",h="An Alchemist can learn to craft a Mana Well from Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Camp for Brews",b="An Alchemist can ask Alchemist Mallory near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest to teach a camping craft. You need to show proficiency in your skill before learning to make a Mana Well. Healers and spellcasters can come to the camp for a refreshing taste.",sp=0},{t="Setting Up Camp",b="Once you know the craft, you can make your own Mana Well. Camps belong in the wilderness, and a campfire is needed before you start one. Someone who trains cooks can teach you the basics of making a fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches Alchemists to make a Mana Well?",a="Alchemist Mallory teaches the craft near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest, once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",al={"mana well trainer","alchemy camp craft","mallory alchemy"}},{q="What is a Mana Well for?",a="A Mana Well gives healers and spellcasters a refreshing taste at camp.",al={"mana well use","what does mana well do","alchemy camp item"}},{q="Where can I find Alchemist Mallory?",a="Alchemist Mallory is near Stormwind in Elwynn Forest.",al={"mallory location","where is mallory","alchemy trainer elwynn"}},{q="What do I need before starting a camp?",a="You need a campfire before starting your camp. Someone who trains cooks can teach you how to make a fire.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","camp basics"}},{q="Where should I try out my Mana Well?",a="Try it in the wilderness, since most folk do not care for camps in the center of town.",al={"mana well camping","camp in town","where test mana well"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemist mallory","alchemy","camp","campfire","camping","elwynn forest","healers","mana well","spellcasters","stormwind"},rel={"zone:elwynn","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=97915},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97916"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="In Goldshire, Smith Argus teaches skilled metalworkers to prepare for work in the wild. They learn to forge a portable Sharpening Wheel and to make camp in open country with a proper fire.",h="In Goldshire, Smith Argus teaches skilled metalworkers to prepare for work in the wild.",sec={{t="Forging for the Trail",b="Smith Argus of Goldshire shows skilled metalworkers how to carry their craft beyond the town anvils. Those ready for the work can learn to forge a Sharpening Wheel, keeping blades keen on long travels.",sp=0},{t="Life in the Field",b="Field gear alone does not make a proper camp. Goldshire townsfolk frown on camps within settlements, so crafters must head into the open frontier to use their equipment. A wilderness camp also needs a warm fire. Visit a local cook to learn the basics of making one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Blacksmithing?",a="Smith Argus teaches skilled blacksmiths to forge a portable Sharpening Wheel for use in the wilderness.",al={"what does this quest do","camping 101 blacksmithing purpose","what do i learn"}},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is the blacksmith and trainer in Goldshire, within Elwynn Forest. He teaches promising smiths basic metalworking and camping craft.",al={"who is smith argus","goldshire blacksmith trainer","argus goldshire"}},{q="What is a Sharpening Wheel?",a="A Sharpening Wheel is camping equipment that blacksmiths can forge to hone tools and weapons away from town forges.",al={"what is a sharpening wheel","camping sharpening wheel","blacksmith camp item"}},{q="Can you set up camp inside town?",a="Townsfolk frown on camps in settled places like Goldshire. Smiths need to head into the wilderness to set up their gear.",al={"can i camp in goldshire","pitch tent in town","where can i camp"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire to make camp?",a="A campfire completes a wilderness camp. Blacksmiths can visit a cooking trainer to learn basic fire-making before heading out.",al={"do i need cooking for camping","campfire for camp","how to make a camp"}},{q="When can you learn this camping craft?",a="Smith Argus teaches this camping craft to blacksmiths with sufficient skill.",al={"camping 101 requirements","blacksmith proficiency requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Blacksmiths learning their trade in Elwynn Forest can forge a Sharpening Wheel to maintain equipment and hone blades in the field.",["profession:Cooking"]="A proper campsite needs a reliable fire, so basic cooking training pairs well with metalworking in the wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance artisans starting out in Goldshire can ask Smith Argus how to prepare for long journeys beyond town."},kw={"blacksmithing","campfire","camping","camping 101","elwynn forest","goldshire","sharpening wheel","smith argus"},rel={"npc:smith-argus","subzone:goldshire"},m={id=97916},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97917"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="In Stormwind, Betty Quin teaches enchanters to bring a little magic to the campfire. With an Enchanted Lute, they can lift spirits and help travelers rest along the trail.",h="In Stormwind, Betty Quin teaches enchanters to bring a little magic to the campfire.",sec={{t="Magic on the Trail",b="Long roads across Azeroth call for more than steel and rations. Comfort and good spirits matter in the wild, too. Enchanters put their craft to work at camp, turning quiet hours into music and rest before the next stretch of trail.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Betty Quin",b="Betty Quin in Stormwind teaches enchanters to make special items for the campsite. Once they have shown skill in enchanting, she can teach them to craft an Enchanted Lute. Its charms lift spirits around the campfire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Enchanting?",a="Enchanters can learn to make magical supplies for camp from Betty Quin in Stormwind. She teaches those who have honed their craft.",al={"what is camping 101 enchanting","camping 101 enchanters","enchanting camp quest"}},{q="Who is Betty Quin?",a="Betty Quin teaches skilled enchanters in Stormwind how to make magical items for the road and for leisure.",al={"who is betty quin","stormwind enchanting trainer betty","where is betty quin"}},{q="What is an Enchanted Lute?",a="An Enchanted Lute is a magical instrument that brings music and lifts spirits during camp. It helps travelers face the hardships of the trail.",al={"what does enchanted lute do","why craft enchanted lute","enchanted lute purpose"}},{q="Why are enchanters valued at a campsite?",a="Enchanters bring magic to camp, making downtime a chance to rest, prepare, and enjoy some music before a hard journey.",al={"why enchanters in camp","enchanter camp usefulness"}},{q="Where do I go to complete this task?",a="Find Betty Quin in Stormwind, the capital of the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"where do i turn in camping 101 enchanting","betty quin location"}},{q="What skill is needed to learn camping enchanting recipes?",a="Betty Quin teaches campcraft to enchanters who have shown solid skill in enchanting, including how to make an Enchanted Lute.",al={"camping 101 enchanting requirements","when can i learn enchanted lute"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance enchanters traveling through their lands can find Betty Quin in Stormwind for lessons in campcraft."},kw={"betty quin","camp","camping 101","camping 101: enchanting","enchanted lute","enchanting","stormwind"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=97917},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97921"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers a new comfort for camp. They learn to make Incense Candles, whose fragrance lifts the spirits of spellcasters resting in the wild.",h="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers a new comfort for camp.",sec={{t="Botanical Utilities for the Road",b="A herbalist's craft can help a traveling party in more ways than brewing restorative draughts or selling flowers. With skill in gathering, you can help your companions endure the wilds. A camp needs more than a fire and dry bedroll. Weary travelers also need comforts that keep their minds keen. Some plants give off aromas that refresh tired minds, so herbalists can support a party far from civilization.",sp=0},{t="The Guidance of Herbalist Pomeroy",b="In Elwynn Forest, Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers to make campsite supplies from local plants. She shows them how to shape an Incense Candle, putting herbs to use beyond alchemy flasks. Burned at camp, its fragrance soothes tired travelers and lifts the spirits of companions who rely on mana. With Pomeroy's teaching, herbalists can bring comfort to parties traveling in the wild.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="Skilled herbalists can learn to make Incense Candles for campsites. Herbalist Pomeroy teaches this craft in Elwynn Forest.",al={"camping 101 herbalism quest","herbalism camping quest","what is camping 101 herbalism"}},{q="Who teaches the camping recipe for herbalists?",a="Herbalist Pomeroy teaches skilled gatherers in Elwynn Forest to make Incense Candles from local plants.",al={"who teaches herbalism camping","camping 101 trainer","where is herbalist pomeroy","herbalist pomeroy location"}},{q="What item do herbalists learn to craft from this quest?",a="Herbalists learn to make an Incense Candle. Its fragrance soothes travelers and lifts the spirits of companions who rely on mana while resting in the wild.",al={"what do herbalists make for camping","herbalism camp item","incense candle herbalism","what does camping 101 teach"}},{q="What are the requirements to start Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="You need skill in Herbalism and gathering before Herbalist Pomeroy will teach you camp craft.",al={"camping 101 herbalism requirements","when can i get camping 101 herbalism","herbalism skill needed for camping 101"}},{q="Why are Incense Candles useful for adventuring parties?",a="Incense Candles soothe travelers and lift the spirits of companions who rely on mana while resting in the wild.",al={"what does incense candle do","why make incense candle","incense candle benefits","herbalism incense candle use"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel to Elwynn Forest to meet Herbalist Pomeroy and learn to make campsite supplies.",al={"camping 101 herbalism zone","where to turn in camping 101 herbalism","elwynn forest herbalism quest"}},{q="Can non-herbalists craft the Incense Candle?",a="No. Making an Incense Candle requires Herbalism and knowledge of wild plants and aromatic materials, which Herbalist Pomeroy teaches.",al={"can anyone make incense candle","is incense candle herbalism only","do i need herbalism for incense candle"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can use your knowledge of plants to make Incense Candles that comfort your traveling companions at camp.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can rest near an Incense Candle and take heart from its fragrance during wilderness travel.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can benefit from an herbalist companion who makes Incense Candles for camp.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can seek Herbalist Pomeroy's instruction in Elwynn Forest."},kw={"camp","camping 101","campsite","elwynn forest","healers","herbalism","herbalist pomeroy","incense candle","spellcasters"},rel={"zone:elwynn"},m={id=97921},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97922"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="In Goldshire, Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers to make a tent for journeys beyond town. It shelters travelers from harsh weather and gives them a place to rest while camping in the wilderness.",h="In Goldshire, Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers to make a tent for journeys beyond town.",sec={{t="Shelter for the Open Road",b="Beyond the gates of Goldshire, shelter matters as much as armor. In Elwynn Forest, leatherworkers can visit Adele Fielder to learn more than simple belts and tunics. After they show skill with hide and needle, Adele teaches them to make a durable tent for long journeys overland. It is built to withstand harsh weather.",sp=0},{t="The Essentials of Campcraft",b="A finished tent covers a campsite and guards against the elements. It keeps travelers cool under scorching suns, dry in driving rain, and rested between dangerous encounters.\n\nGoldshire locals and city guards will not allow campsites in the town streets, so you need to head into the open wilderness to camp. Adele also reminds wanderers that a proper camp needs a campfire. A culinary trainer can teach you to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches leatherworkers how to craft tents?",a="Adele Fielder teaches leatherworkers in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest, to make sturdy tents after they show skill in their craft.",al={"who gives tent training","adele fielder location","leatherworking tent teacher"}},{q="What purpose does a crafted tent serve?",a="A crafted tent shelters travelers from harsh weather, keeping them cool on sweltering days and dry in heavy rain. It also gives adventurers rest in the wilderness.",al={"why make tent","what does tent do","tent benefits"}},{q="Can you pitch a tent inside a town?",a="You cannot pitch a tent in town streets or town centers. Take your gear into the wilderness to set up camp.",al={"can i pitch tent in town","where can i use tent","tent in stormwind or goldshire"}},{q="What else is needed alongside a tent to complete a camp?",a="Adele Fielder says a camp needs a campfire as well as a tent, for warmth and practical use in the wild.",al={"what else do i need for camp","tent campfire requirement","how to complete campsite"}},{q="Where can a traveler learn to build a campfire?",a="Culinary trainers and local cooks teach the basics of lighting a campfire. Learn from them so you can build a reliable fire wherever you roam.",al={"who teaches campfire","how to learn campfire","fire for camp"}},{q="When can a leatherworker learn to craft a camping tent?",a="A leatherworker must first show skill in the craft before Adele Fielder teaches tentmaking.",al={"tent skill requirements","how to get tent recipe","when can i craft tent"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Adele Fielder says a wilderness campsite needs a campfire and urges you to learn cooking so you can kindle one.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Goldshire, this training guides Alliance leatherworkers toward practical survival crafts for journeys across Azeroth."},kw={"adele fielder","campfire","camping","elwynn forest","goldshire","leatherworking","tent","wilderness survival"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={id=97922},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97923"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="In Stormwind, Gelman Stonehand teaches miners to shape a lodestone for camps in the wild. Set by a campfire, it strengthens the fighters gathered there.",h="In Stormwind, Gelman Stonehand teaches miners to shape a lodestone for camps in the wild.",sec={{t="The Earth's Resonant Power",b="Miners in Stormwind can shape the earth’s natural magnetism into a lodestone. At an expedition’s campsite, it bolsters the fighting strength of those gathered there. Gelman Stonehand, Stormwind’s mining instructor, teaches the craft to prospectors who prove their skill with a pickaxe.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness Camps and Campfires",b="A lodestone belongs in the wild, far from Cathedral Square and the Trade District. Townsfolk disapprove of travelers camping within city limits, so pioneers must head into the wild to make camp. The stone also needs a campfire. Cooks across the realm teach this basic wilderness skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Mining?",a="Gelman Stonehand teaches miners in Stormwind to craft a lodestone for a wilderness campsite. You must prove your mining skill to learn the craft.",al={"what is camping 101 mining","quest objective","what do i do"}},{q="Who teaches the Lodestone schematic?",a="Gelman Stonehand is a mining trainer in Stormwind City. He teaches qualified miners to make a lodestone for expeditions in the wild.",al={"who teaches lodestone","where is gelman stonehand","stonehand location"}},{q="What does a Lodestone do?",a="A lodestone set at a wilderness campsite strengthens warriors and other fighters gathered around its campfire.",al={"what does lodestone do","lodestone buff","why make lodestone"}},{q="Can I set up camp inside Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's townsfolk disapprove of camps in city squares and streets. Go beyond the settlement gates to make camp and set your lodestone in the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in town","where can i place camp","camping restrictions"}},{q="Why do I need a campfire to set up camp?",a="A campfire is the foundation of a campsite, and specialized gear like a lodestone is useless without one. Cooks teach travelers to start fires with wood and flint.",al={"do i need cooking for camping","how to make camp","campfire requirement"}},{q="Who benefits most from gathering around a Lodestone?",a="Anyone who fights with a blade, axe, or hammer can benefit from a lodestone. Fighters seek its added strength while resting by the flames before a dangerous battle.",al={"who benefits from lodestone","is lodestone for melee","lodestone classes"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can shape a lodestone to strengthen your wilderness campsite and aid allies resting beside you.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn to tend a campfire, the foundation for specialized camp equipment.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance tradesfolk, you can learn from Gelman Stonehand in Stormwind to turn earthcraft into practical field tools."},kw={"campfire","camping 101: mining","campsite","gelman stonehand","lodestone","mining","stormwind","wilderness"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=97923},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97924"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="In Elwynn Forest, skinners learn Camping 101: Skinning from Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire. She teaches them to shape harvested hides into a Camp Chair for rests beyond settled towns.",h="In Elwynn Forest, skinners learn Camping 101: Skinning from Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire.",sec={{t="Creature Comforts in the Wild",b="You can shape hides taken from beasts into a Camp Chair for rest in the wild. In Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make this seat for travelers on long journeys through dangerous lands.",sp=0},{t="Rules of the Campsite",b="Take your gear into the wilderness before making camp, for townspeople often object to camps in the town square. A field camp also needs a campfire. Many skinners learn basic culinary arts to master fire-building.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Skinning?",a="In Goldshire, Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make a Camp Chair from harvested hides.",al={"what is camping 101 skinning","what does this quest do","skinning camp chair quest"}},{q="Who teaches skinners how to craft a Camp Chair?",a="Helene Peltskinner teaches proficient skinners to make a Camp Chair in Goldshire.",al={"who teaches camp chair","helene peltskinner location","where to turn in camping 101 skinning"}},{q="What is the purpose of crafting a Camp Chair?",a="A Camp Chair gives travelers a seat where they can rest during wilderness journeys.",al={"what does a camp chair do","why make a camp chair","camp chair purpose"}},{q="Where can adventurers set up camp?",a="Town residents generally dislike camps in the middle of settlements, so set up your camp in the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in town","where can i place camp chair","camping in goldshire"}},{q="What else is required to build a complete campsite?",a="A campsite needs a basic campfire. If you do not know how to build one, learn culinary arts from a local cook.",al={"what do i need for a camp","do i need a fire to camp","campfire requirement"}},{q="Who is eligible to learn this camping craft?",a="Skinners proficient at harvesting hides from beasts can learn this craft and put those hides to practical use in the wild.",al={"who can learn camp chair","can non skinners do this","skinning requirement camping"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a skinner learning to make a field camp, consult a cook. A campsite needs a basic campfire for warmth and meal preparation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance skinner visiting Elwynn Forest, find Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire to learn this wilderness craft."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping 101: skinning","goldshire","helene peltskinner","skinning","wilderness camping"},rel={"subzone:goldshire"},m={id=97924},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97925"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="In Elwynn Forest, skilled clothworkers are sent to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp. He teaches them to weave a Faction Banner that inspires travelers and raises morale at wilderness camps.",h="In Elwynn Forest, skilled clothworkers are sent to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",sec={{t="A Weaver's Purpose in the Wild",b="Eldrin, an artisan at the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, guides skilled needleworkers. Tailoring makes garments and bags, but it can also sustain a journey. Those who have proven their skill with thread and loom can learn to make camp accessories for travel through the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Banners of Morale",b="The Faction Banner is the chief craft Eldrin teaches. It stands beside a traveler's fire, where its emblem can hearten those on dangerous journeys and in battle. A banner at camp gives weary travelers a familiar sign of resolve and helps them press on through hostile lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Camping 101: Tailoring?",a="Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest teaches skilled tailors to make a Faction Banner. The banner inspires travelers and raises morale at camp.",al={"what is camping 101 tailoring","tailoring camp item quest","how to get camp banner"}},{q="Who is Eldrin and where can he be found?",a="Eldrin is an artisan at the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. He teaches skilled tailors to craft faction banners for camps.",al={"who is eldrin","where is eldrin","eldrin location"}},{q="What does the Faction Banner do for a camp?",a="A Faction Banner inspires travelers and raises morale at camp. Its emblem offers weary travelers resolve as they journey through hostile lands.",al={"what does the tailoring banner do","faction banner camp","why craft a faction banner"}},{q="What requirements are needed to learn the craft from Eldrin?",a="Tailors must first prove their skill before Eldrin teaches them the craft. They need honed needlework to weave and assemble the banner.",al={"what skill do i need","camping banner requirements","can any tailor make a banner"}},{q="Where is the Eastvale Logging Camp located?",a="The Eastvale Logging Camp lies in the eastern woods of Elwynn Forest, along the road toward Redridge Mountains. Local craftspeople and workers gather at this logging hub.",al={"where is eastvale logging camp","eastvale logging camp elwynn"}},{q="Is this task exclusive to Alliance tailors?",a="Eldrin is in the heart of Elwynn Forest, within Alliance territory. The instruction there is for Alliance-aligned craftsmen from the eastern settlements.",al={"can horde do this quest","is this alliance only"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors can weave a Faction Banner to inspire travelers and raise morale at camp during long expeditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers are directed to Eldrin at the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to stitch a faction banner."},kw={"banner","camping","camping 101","eastvale logging camp","eldrin","elwynn forest","faction banner","tailoring"},rel={"subzone:eastvale-logging-camp","zone:elwynn"},m={id=97925},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:97927"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="Kray in Thunder Bluff can teach you to craft a Mana Well for your alchemist's camp. The well draws healers and spellcasters seeking refreshment.",h="Kray in Thunder Bluff can teach you to craft a Mana Well for your alchemist's camp.",sec={{t="A Well for Camp",b="An alchemist can learn to craft a Mana Well from Kray in Thunder Bluff. You have shown proficiency in your skill, and Kray can teach you this camping craft. Healers and spellcasters will come for a refreshing taste. To set up camp in the wilderness, you also need a campfire, which a cook can teach you to make.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to craft a Mana Well?",a="Kray in Thunder Bluff can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you have shown proficiency in alchemy.",al={"mana well trainer","who is Kray","Kray alchemy"}},{q="What is a Mana Well for?",a="A Mana Well is a camping craft for alchemists. Healers and spellcasters come to it for refreshment.",al={"mana well use","what does the well do","alchemy camp item"}},{q="Where do I learn this camping craft?",a="You speak with Kray in Thunder Bluff to learn the Mana Well craft.",al={"where is Kray","Thunder Bluff alchemy","mana well location"}},{q="What else do I need to set up camp?",a="A camp needs a campfire before it can be set up. A cook can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how to start camp","fire for camp"}},{q="Can I test the Mana Well in town?",a="The completion instructions say most folk do not care for camps in the center of town, so you need to head into the wilderness to test it.",al={"camp in town","where to try Mana Well","Mana Well test"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemy","campfire","camping","healers","kray","mana well","spellcasters","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=97927},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97928"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="You’re ready to make a Sharpening Wheel and try it in the wilderness. First, you’ll need a campfire to set up camp.",h="You’re ready to make a Sharpening Wheel and try it in the wilderness.",sec={{t="Ready to Camp",b="You can now craft a Sharpening Wheel. Take it into the wilderness to try it out, where you can set up camp away from the center of town. Bring a campfire along. A cook can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I craft now?",a="You can now craft your own Sharpening Wheel.",al={"sharpening wheel","blacksmithing craft","what do i make"}},{q="Where can I try the Sharpening Wheel?",a="You can try it in the wilderness, where camps can be set up away from the center of town.",al={"where to test it","sharpening wheel location","camping where"}},{q="What do I need before setting up camp?",a="You need a campfire before you can set up camp.",al={"campfire needed","how to start a camp","camping basics"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a campfire?",a="A cook can teach you to make a campfire.",al={"learn campfire","who teaches fire","cooking fire"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="You can now craft a Sharpening Wheel to use in the wilderness.",["profession:Cooking"]="A cook can teach you how to make a campfire."},kw={"blacksmithing","campfire","camping","cook","sharpening wheel","wilderness"},m={id=97928},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97931"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="general",s="You are ready to make a First Aid Kit, and now you need a place to try it.",h="You are ready to make a First Aid Kit, and now you need a place to try it.",sec={{t="A Place to Camp",b="You can make the kit, but most people would rather not camp in the middle of town. So take it out into the wilderness. Before you set up camp, you need a campfire. Most cooks can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I try the First Aid Kit?",a="Try the First Aid Kit in the wilderness, where people are less likely to object to a camp.",al={"where try kit","first aid kit place"}},{q="What do I need before setting up camp?",a="You need a campfire before you can set up camp.",al={"campfire needed","what for camping"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a campfire?",a="Most cooks can teach you how to make a campfire.",al={"make campfire","fire teacher"}}},kw={"campfire","camping","cooking","first aid","first aid kit","wilderness"},m={id=97931},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97932"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="In Mulgore, anglers can turn fishing into a comfort for camps in the wild. Show Uthan Stillwater in Bloodhoof Village your skill with rod and reel, and he teaches you to make a Fish Bowl for travelers resting outdoors.",h="In Mulgore, anglers can turn fishing into a comfort for camps in the wild.",sec={{t="Angling in the Wild",b="Anglers passing through Mulgore can put their quiet pastime to use around camp. If you have proved your skill with rod and reel, seek out Uthan Stillwater in Bloodhoof Village. He teaches skilled fishermen to make a Fish Bowl, a homely touch for a campsite.",sp=0},{t="Comforts of Camp",b="A Fish Bowl brings a little cheer to a hard journey. Its calm presence makes a resting place in the wild more pleasant and lifts the spirits of those gathered there. Better spirits mean sharper instincts and greater resilience in battle.",sp=0},{t="Campfire and Open Country",b="A campsite belongs in the open country, not in a settlement like Bloodhoof Village. The Fish Bowl can only be tried in the wilderness. A camp also needs a proper fire, so seek out a culinary trainer to learn basic fire-making before you set one up.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Fish Bowl do for a campsite?",a="A Fish Bowl is a camp fixture made by skilled fishermen. It brings comfort and cheer to travelers resting in the wilderness, lifting their spirits and helping them stay sharp in battle.",al={"fish bowl camp","fish bowl what do","fish bowl benefit"}},{q="Who teaches the Fish Bowl recipe?",a="Uthan Stillwater teaches the craft in Bloodhoof Village, in Mulgore. He teaches anglers who have already shown skill at fishing.",al={"where learn fish bowl","who teaches fish bowl","uthan stillwater location"}},{q="Why can't you pitch camp inside a settlement?",a="Settlements like Bloodhoof Village do not allow travelers to set up camps in town. Pitch your camp in the open wild instead.",al={"camp in town","why cant i camp in bloodhoof village","camping inside cities"}},{q="What else is required to set up a camp?",a="A proper campsite needs a campfire. If you do not know how to kindle one, seek out a cooking trainer to learn basic fire-making.",al={"campfire camping requirement","need fire for camp","camping basics fire"}},{q="What requirements are needed before learning the Fish Bowl?",a="You need to show fishing skill before Uthan Stillwater will teach you to make camp fixtures. If you are a novice angler, spend time honing your craft by the water first.",al={"fishing proficiency camping","when can i get fish bowl","camping 101 fishing requirements"}},{q="Why would an adventurer want a Fish Bowl while camping?",a="A Fish Bowl brings a touch of home to a hard, tiring life on the road. Watching a fish by the fire can bring joy and lift an adventurer's spirits.",al={"why bring fish bowl camping","camp fish bowl lore"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A proper campsite needs a campfire. Basic cooking training pairs naturally with a fisherman's camp in the wild.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde angler traveling through Mulgore, you can learn to make camp fixtures from Uthan Stillwater in Bloodhoof Village."},kw={"bloodhoof village","campfire","camping","camping 101: fishing","fish bowl","fishing","mulgore","uthan stillwater"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={id=97932},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97933"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="Komin Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff can teach you to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. Herbalism skill opens the way to a useful aid for healers and spellcasters.",h="Komin Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff can teach you to craft an Incense Candle for your camp.",sec={{t="A Candle for Camp",b="A teacher in Thunder Bluff asks you to put your herbalism skill to use in learning a camp craft. The Incense Candle can lift the spirits of healers and spellcasters. You leave with the knowledge to make one, but testing it calls for a camp beyond the town and a campfire to go with it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches the camp craft?",a="Komin Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff teaches you to craft an Incense Candle.",al={"camping herbalism trainer","who teaches incense candle"}},{q="What does herbalism have to do with camping?",a="Showing proficiency in herbalism lets you learn to craft an Incense Candle for your camp.",al={"herbalism camp item","herbalism camping"}},{q="What is an Incense Candle for?",a="An Incense Candle can boost the spirits of healers and spellcasters.",al={"incense candle use","camp candle"}},{q="Where can I try the candle?",a="You need to head into the wilderness to test it, since most folk do not care for camps in the center of town.",al={"where test incense candle","camp in town"}},{q="Do I need anything else for camp?",a="A campfire is needed before you start your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","what else for camp"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, your skill lets you learn to craft an Incense Candle for camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach the basics of making a campfire, which a camp needs."},kw={"campfire","camping","camping 101","herbalism","incense candle","komin winterhoof","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=97933},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97934"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="In Bloodhoof Village, leatherworkers can learn to make a tent for shelter on the road. Chaw Stronghide teaches the craft to those ready to handle heavier hides and rugged stitching.",h="In Bloodhoof Village, leatherworkers can learn to make a tent for shelter on the road.",sec={{t="Shelters for the Open Plains",b="Across Kalimdor, leatherworkers who know how to stitch a sturdy tent can shelter from the midday sun and prairie rain. A tent also gives weary travelers a place to rest and recover before crossing the open plains again.",sp=0},{t="The Craft of Chaw Stronghide",b="At Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore, Chaw Stronghide teaches leatherworkers who can handle heavier hides and rugged stitching. Once they prove their skill, he shows them how to make a durable tent for journeys far from civilization.",sp=0},{t="Camps in the Wild",b="Choose a camp with care and respect for local settlements. Village folk frown on travelers setting up along central paths and thoroughfares, so take your tent into the wild frontier. A proper camp also needs a fire. Ask a skilled cook how to kindle one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does this quest teach leatherworkers?",a="Leatherworkers learn to make a tent for their travels. It shelters them from harsh weather and gives them a place to rest in the wilderness.",al={"leatherworking tent quest","what does camping 101 teach","leatherworking camp item"}},{q="Who teaches leatherworkers how to craft camp tents?",a="Chaw Stronghide teaches tent making in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. He shares the craft once a leatherworker proves able to handle heavier hides and rugged stitching.",al={"who teaches tent crafting","chaw stronghide tent","leatherworking tent trainer"}},{q="Where can travelers set up their camp tents?",a="Pitch camp in the open wilderness, away from populated settlements. Town residents and village elders do not want private shelters in town squares or along roads.",al={"where can i pitch tent","can i camp in town","tent placement"}},{q="Why is a campfire needed alongside a tent?",a="A campfire brings warmth and protection to a wilderness camp. Visit a skilled cook to learn how to kindle one before traveling into the wild.",al={"why do i need a campfire","cooking campfire tent","tent and fire"}},{q="Where is Bloodhoof Village located?",a="Bloodhoof Village lies in central Mulgore, south of Thunder Bluff along the shores of Stonebull Lake. The tauren settlement serves hunters, gatherers and artisans, and offers training, trade supplies and guidance to travelers exploring the plains.",al={"where is bloodhoof village","bloodhoof village location","how to find chaw stronghide"}},{q="Do you need cooking skill to maintain a proper campsite?",a="Cooking is not needed to stitch a leather tent, but cooks teach travelers how to kindle campfires. A fire completes an outdoor camp, warms the night air and lets travelers prepare food on long journeys.",al={"is cooking needed for camping","do i need cooking","campfire cooking basics"}},{q="What benefits does a camp tent provide to a traveler?",a="A tent shelters travelers from intense heat and heavy rain. Resting inside helps them stay refreshed and alert as they explore distant territories.",al={"benefits of camping tent","why make a tent","what does tent do"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Making portable leather shelters suits the tauren tribes' nomadic traditions and wilderness survival heritage across Mulgore's plains.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers crossing Kalimdor's wide, arid lands rely on rugged camping gear far from fortified strongholds.",["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking trainers teach travelers to build a proper campfire, completing a leather tent's warm campsite."},kw={"bloodhoof village","campfire","camping 101","chaw stronghide","leatherworking","mulgore","shelter","tent"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={id=97934},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97935"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="In Thunder Bluff, miners can learn to carry their craft into the wild. Brek Stonehoof teaches them to shape a lodestone that gives strength to those resting by a campfire.",h="In Thunder Bluff, miners can learn to carry their craft into the wild.",sec={{t="Honest Labor in the Earth",b="Mining may lack the glamour of high arcana, but it is honest work found across Azeroth. Miners draw useful minerals and dense stone from deep rock faces. Those materials make weapons and armor, and now they serve a purpose in the field. A miner can shape stone into sturdy tools for a wilderness camp.",sp=0},{t="The Lodestone of Thunder Bluff",b="Brek Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff teaches miners to put their trade to use in the wild. Once they show skill with a pick, he teaches them to shape a camp lodestone. Set beside an open blaze, the stone lends vigor and an edge in battle to those preparing to wield a blade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the lodestone do for a campsite?",a="A lodestone set beside a campfire lends vigor and combat strength to those gathered there.",al={"lodestone camp benefit","lodestone bonus","what does lodestone do"}},{q="Who is Brek Stonehoof?",a="Brek Stonehoof lives in Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital. He teaches skilled miners to make camping tools from stone and ore.",al={"brek stonehoof location","where is brek stonehoof","who teaches mining camp item"}},{q="When can a miner learn how to craft a lodestone?",a="A miner must first show skill in the trade before Brek Stonehoof teaches the craft of shaping a lodestone.",al={"when can i learn lodestone","mining skill requirement lodestone"}},{q="Who benefits most from a miner's lodestone?",a="Anyone preparing to wield a weapon can benefit from the lodestone's strength while resting beside it.",al={"who benefits lodestone","is lodestone for melee"}},{q="How does mining tie into establishing a campsite?",a="Mining provides metal for smelters and blacksmiths, and lets travelers shape stone tools like lodestones to strengthen a wilderness camp.",al={"why mine for camping","how does mining help camp"}},{q="What is the purpose of Camping 101: Mining?",a="In Thunder Bluff, aspiring miners can learn from Brek Stonehoof to make field tools for survival in the wild.",al={"camping 101 mining overview","what is camping 101 mining"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can put your gathering craft to work in the wild by preparing a lodestone for an expedition camp.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can learn from Brek Stonehoof atop Thunder Bluff's mesas, drawing on tauren knowledge of stone and earthcraft.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can give those resting by your campfire a lodestone's strength for battles ahead."},kw={"brek stonehoof","camp","campfire","camping 101: mining","lodestone","mining","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=97935},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97936"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="In Mulgore, skinners learn to make a Camp Chair for wilderness rest. Yonn Deepcut teaches the craft in Bloodhoof Village, where skilled hide-gatherers prepare for camps beyond the settlements.",h="In Mulgore, skinners learn to make a Camp Chair for wilderness rest.",sec={{t="Hides of the Wild",b="Fallen beasts yield hides and pelts that skinners can turn into useful gear. Leather becomes armor, and animal skins can also make comforts for the wild. After long weeks crossing untamed lands, travelers can rest on gear made from those hides and stay sharp in combat.",sp=0},{t="Lessons in Bloodhoof Village",b="In Mulgore, skinners visit Bloodhoof Village to speak with Yonn Deepcut. Once they show they can harvest beast hides, Yonn teaches them to stitch together a Camp Chair. Towns and villages do not welcome travelers pitching tents in their streets, so the chairs are for wilderness use. A campfire completes the camp, and local cooks teach how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Skinning?",a="In Mulgore, Yonn Deepcut teaches skinners to make a Camp Chair in Bloodhoof Village. First, they show they can harvest beast hides.",al={"what is camping 101 skinning","camping skinning quest","what does this quest do"}},{q="Who teaches the Camp Chair recipe?",a="Yonn Deepcut teaches skinners to make a Camp Chair in Bloodhoof Village, Mulgore, after they demonstrate skill at harvesting beast hides.",al={"who teaches camp chair","who to talk to for camping skinning","where is yonn deepcut"}},{q="What is a Camp Chair used for?",a="A Camp Chair gives you a comfortable place to rest when you camp in the wild. Sitting helps you recover strength and stay ready for battle.",al={"what does a camp chair do","camp chair use","why make a camp chair"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="Set up camp in the wilderness. Townspeople do not welcome travelers pitching tents in settlements.",al={"where can i make a camp","can i camp in town","camp chair in city"}},{q="What else is required to set up a camp?",a="A camp also needs a campfire. Local cooks and culinary trainers teach you how to make one.",al={"what else do i need for camp","campfire needed","do i need a fire to camp"}},{q="Where is Bloodhoof Village located?",a="Bloodhoof Village lies in Mulgore. The tauren settlement is home to tradespeople, including skinning trainers.",al={"where is bloodhoof village","bloodhoof village location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde skinner in Mulgore, you can visit Bloodhoof Village and learn to make camp gear from the hides you gather.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren skinner, you can learn from Yonn Deepcut in the heart of Mulgore to make chairs from beast hides for wilderness rest.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn from culinary trainers to make a campfire for your camp."},kw={"bloodhoof village","camp chair","campfire","camping 101","camping 101: skinning","mulgore","skinning","yonn deepcut"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={id=97936},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97938"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="In Dolanaar, Cyndra Kindwhisper teaches alchemists how to tend a campsite. Her lesson joins potion craft with wilderness survival and shows how to make a Mana Well for traveling healers and casters.",h="In Dolanaar, Cyndra Kindwhisper teaches alchemists how to tend a campsite.",sec={{t="Field Craft for Alchemists",b="Alchemists learn to carry their craft beyond the workbench. Cyndra Kindwhisper shows them how to make useful camp fittings that can sustain a traveling party on long journeys through the wild.",sp=0},{t="The Mana Well of Dolanaar",b="In Dolanaar, alchemists who know the basics can seek Cyndra Kindwhisper. She teaches them to set up a Mana Well at camp. Its refreshing magic helps healers and spellcasters replenish their mana far from taverns and settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Alchemy?",a="Camping 101: Alchemy teaches novice alchemists in Dolanaar to use their craft at camp. They learn to make useful wilderness fittings with their potion-making skills.",al={"what is camping 101 alchemy","camping 101 alchemy quest","alchemy camp quest"}},{q="Who teaches this camping skill?",a="Cyndra Kindwhisper teaches alchemists in Dolanaar, the night elf settlement on Teldrassil. She instructs those who have shown skill in brewing and crafting specialized camping items.",al={"who is cyndra kindwhisper","cyndra kindwhisper location","where is cyndra kindwhisper"}},{q="What is a Mana Well?",a="A Mana Well is an alchemist's camp installation. It offers arcane refreshment to spellcasters and healers who need to replenish their reserves on the road.",al={"what does a mana well do","mana well camp item","mana well lore"}},{q="Where does this quest take you?",a="You travel to Dolanaar, a night elf village in central Teldrassil. It is a hub for young adventurers and tradecraft trainers leaving Shadowglen.",al={"where is dolanaar","how to get to dolanaar","dolanaar location"}},{q="Who benefits from an alchemist's camp installation?",a="Traveling healers and spellcasters benefit most from Mana Wells. The refreshing fonts help replenish them on taxing journeys far from towns.",al={"who benefits from mana wells","who uses mana wells","mana well spellcasters"}},{q="What is required before learning to craft a Mana Well?",a="Alchemists must first show skill in basic brewing and potion craft. Then Cyndra Kindwhisper teaches them to assemble camping fittings such as a Mana Well.",al={"when can i learn the mana well","camping 101 requirements","skill proficiency needed"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance alchemists traveling across Teldrassil are directed to Dolanaar to learn magical camp craft for wilderness survival.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf herbalist or alchemist in Dolanaar, you can join natural botany with camp craft to support spellcasters in the wild."},kw={"alchemy","camp","camping 101","camping 101: alchemy","cyndra kindwhisper","dolanaar","mana well","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar"},m={id=97938},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97940"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="A guide in the Oracle Glade points you toward learning an enchanting craft for camp. An Enchanted Lute can bring entertainment during a wilderness stay.",h="A guide in the Oracle Glade points you toward learning an enchanting craft for camp.",sec={{t="A Camp Craft",b="An enchanter can make a useful craft for your camp, and you are directed to Alanna Raveneye in the Oracle Glade. She can teach you to make an Enchanted Lute once you have shown proficiency in your skill. It is meant to bring entertainment during your downtime before you take to the trail again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me the Enchanted Lute?",a="Alanna Raveneye in the Oracle Glade can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",al={"alanna raveneye","who teaches lute","lute trainer"}},{q="What is the Enchanted Lute for?",a="The Enchanted Lute is a camping craft meant to provide entertainment during downtime in the wild.",al={"lute purpose","camp lute","why enchanted lute"}},{q="Why are enchanters welcome at camps?",a="Enchanters can make things better, so they are welcome at camps in the wild.",al={"enchanters camping","enchanting camp","camping enchanting"}},{q="Where do I learn this camping craft?",a="You can learn from Alanna Raveneye in the Oracle Glade in Teldrassil.",al={"oracle glade trainer","where alanna","enchanting location"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As an enchanter, you can learn to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"alanna raveneye","camp craft","camping","enchanted lute","enchanting","oracle glade","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade"},m={id=97940},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97942"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="general",s="In Dolanaar, travelers learn to prepare a First Aid Kit for camp. Byancie teaches how to tend wounds far from town healers and find a place to camp.",h="In Dolanaar, travelers learn to prepare a First Aid Kit for camp.",sec={{t="Field Medicine in the Wilds",b="Wild country brings bites from beasts and cuts from jagged ground. Rangers and other travelers may be far from town and its medical supplies. A First Aid Kit lets them tend minor wounds at a roadside camp before they grow grave beneath the open sky.",sp=0},{t="Lessons in Dolanaar",b="In Dolanaar, Byancie teaches travelers skilled in triage to pack medical supplies for rough trails. Townsfolk do not allow tents and scattered supplies in the center of a settlement. Campers need to head into the forest before making camp.",sp=0},{t="The Hearth of the Camp",b="An open flame begins a working camp. Set a campfire before laying out medical kits or bedding; it brings warmth and protection. Building and tending a fire is basic to surviving in the wild. Trainers recommend asking a cook to teach you to kindle one before tending a wilderness camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Byancie?",a="Byancie teaches in Dolanaar, a settlement on Teldrassil. She shows travelers skilled in medicine how to assemble First Aid Kits for wilderness camping.",al={"who is byancie","byancie location","where is byancie"}},{q="What is a camping First Aid Kit?",a="A camping First Aid Kit is a medical supply made by adventurers trained in First Aid. At an established camp, it gives them a place to tend wounds and provide healing in the field.",al={"what is first aid kit camp","how does first aid kit work","camping first aid kit"}},{q="Where can you set up a camp?",a="Set up camp in the open wilderness, away from town borders. Residents and guards do not welcome temporary camps in settlement centers or city squares.",al={"can i camp in town","why camp outside town","camp rules"}},{q="Why is a campfire required for a camp?",a="A campfire gives a wilderness camp heat, light, and safety. Cooks and culinary trainers can teach you to kindle one.",al={"why do i need campfire","cooking campfire camp","camp fire requirement"}},{q="Why is First Aid considered pragmatic for hunters?",a="Hunters often travel alone in remote wilds, far from healers and templars. First Aid lets them tend injuries while tracking game or surviving an ambush.",al={"why first aid for hunters","hunters healing"}},{q="How do you learn to craft a camping First Aid Kit?",a="Show basic skill in First Aid, then ask Byancie in Dolanaar to teach you how to assemble a camping First Aid Kit.",al={"how to get first aid kit","learn first aid kit craft"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can pair wilderness survival with First Aid to tend injuries far from civilization and town healers.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn the firecraft camp life needs for warmth, alongside the food that sustains you."},kw={"byancie","campfire","camping","dolanaar","field medic","first aid","first aid kit","hunter"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","topic:hunter"},m={id=97942},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97943"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="In Darnassus, anglers are directed to Astaia to learn how a Fish Bowl can brighten a wilderness camp. The craft rewards skilled fishermen with a touch of comfort for life outdoors.",h="In Darnassus, anglers are directed to Astaia to learn how a Fish Bowl can brighten a wilderness camp.",sec={{t="Comfort at the Campsite",b="Anglers crossing Kalimdor can put quiet hours by the water to use. In Darnassus, Astaia teaches experienced fishermen to turn their catches and skill into campsite comforts. One of these is a Fish Bowl, made to display at camp and bring cheer to weary travelers.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness Necessities",b="A wilderness camp needs more than fishing gear. You cannot pitch one in a crowded city center or urban district, so you must find open ground. Every camp also needs a warm fire. Visit a local cooking trainer to learn basic fire-making before settling down for the night.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches you how to craft camping items for fishing?",a="Astaia in Darnassus teaches experienced fishermen to craft a decorative Fish Bowl for camp once they show proficiency in fishing.",al={"who teaches camping fishing","where is astaia","fish bowl trainer"}},{q="What purpose does a Fish Bowl serve at camp?",a="A Fish Bowl brings comfort and joy to resting adventurers. A happy, well-rested camper fights with renewed vigor on outdoor journeys.",al={"what does fish bowl do","camp fish bowl use","fish bowl camp fixture"}},{q="Can you set up a camp inside Darnassus or other cities?",a="You cannot pitch a camp in the heart of a settlement or town center. Head into the wilderness to set up camp and place fixtures such as a Fish Bowl.",al={"can you camp in darnassus","where to make camp","camp in cities"}},{q="What is required before setting up a camp?",a="A basic campfire is required for a campsite. Visit a cooking trainer to learn how to kindle one before establishing a wilderness camp.",al={"what do you need for a camp","how to start camp","campfire required"}},{q="Do you need fishing skill to learn how to craft a Fish Bowl?",a="Yes. An adventurer must first demonstrate proficiency in fishing to learn the craft from Astaia.",al={"fishing proficiency camping","when can i learn fish bowl"}},{q="Why do adventurers set up camps in the wild?",a="A camp gives outdoor travelers a place to rest and find morale-boosting comforts such as a Fish Bowl, helping them stay rested and capable in the wilderness.",al={"why make camp wow forever","camping benefits"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance angler, you can visit Astaia in Darnassus to learn campsite craft.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, your basic training helps you make the campfire every camp needs."},kw={"astaia","campfire","camping","camping 101: fishing","campsite","darnassus","fish bowl","fishing"},rel={"zone:darnassus"},m={id=97943},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97944"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="In Dolanaar, herbalists learn to make camp goods from the plants they gather. Malorne Bladeleaf teaches skilled gatherers to craft Incense Candles, which bolster healers and spellcasters by the campfire.",h="In Dolanaar, herbalists learn to make camp goods from the plants they gather.",sec={{t="More Than Picking Flowers",b="Herbalism can serve a traveler beyond gathering flowers for sale or for alchemists. In the wilderness, harvested plants can become useful camp equipment. Preparing them for survival lets your gathered plants support longer journeys in the field.",sp=0},{t="The Soothing Flame of Dolanaar",b="At Dolanaar, Malorne Bladeleaf teaches skilled herbalists to make an Incense Candle. Its soothing flame creates a focused, high-spirited refuge around the campfire. Healers and spellcasters value its revitalizing presence as they restore their magical energies between perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="Skilled herbalists travel to Malorne Bladeleaf in Dolanaar to learn how to make camp goods from gathered plants.",al={"what is camping 101 herbalism","camping herbalism quest"}},{q="What does an Incense Candle do for a camp?",a="An Incense Candle lifts spirits and creates a soothing, focused atmosphere around a campfire.",al={"what does incense candle do","incense candle benefit"}},{q="Who is Malorne Bladeleaf?",a="Malorne Bladeleaf teaches skilled herbalists in Dolanaar to make camp supplies, including Incense Candles.",al={"who teaches incense candle","who is malorne bladeleaf","bladeleaf dolanaar"}},{q="Where does this quest take you?",a="You travel to Dolanaar, a night elf settlement on Teldrassil and a hub for travelers, trainers, and woodland crafters.",al={"where is dolanaar","dolanaar location"}},{q="Why are Incense Candles useful to magic users?",a="An Incense Candle creates a serene, focused place where healers and spellcasters can restore their spirits and magical strength during wilderness journeys.",al={"who benefits from incense candle","is incense candle for casters"}},{q="What is required before Malorne Bladeleaf will teach you?",a="You need enough practical skill in herbalism before Malorne Bladeleaf will teach you to make camp supplies.",al={"when can i learn incense candle","herbalism skill requirement camping"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can use gathered plants for wilderness survival as well as alchemy, making camp supplies such as Incense Candles.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance herbalist near Teldrassil, you can learn fieldcraft from local night elf practitioners in Dolanaar.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share a tradition of understanding the restorative properties of nature's herbs, taught in settlements such as Dolanaar."},kw={"camping","camping 101: herbalism","dolanaar","herbalism","incense candle","malorne bladeleaf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar"},m={id=97944},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97946"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="On Teldrassil, leatherworkers can learn to make a shelter for the trail. Find Nadyia Maneweaver on the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus, where she teaches the craft of tents that keep travelers dry and cool.",h="On Teldrassil, leatherworkers can learn to make a shelter for the trail.",sec={{t="Shelter in the Wilderness",b="Across Kalimdor, an open sky can bring hard weather. Skilled leatherworkers learn to shape hides and pelts into sturdy shelters, giving travelers a safe place to rest wherever the road leads. A tent lets wanderers find the rest they need far from the inns.",sp=0},{t="The Road from Dolanaar",b="Nadyia Maneweaver teaches proficient leatherworkers along the forest road between Dolanaar and Darnassus. She shows them how to stitch a sturdy tent for the trail. A tent needs a campfire to make a proper camp, and cooks teach that craft. Set the shelter in the open wilds, away from town streets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches this camping skill?",a="Nadyia Maneweaver teaches the camping skill along the road from Dolanaar toward Darnassus on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives camping 101 leatherworking","who teaches camping 101","nadyia maneweaver"}},{q="What do leatherworkers learn from this quest?",a="Leatherworkers learn to make a tent that keeps travelers cool in hot weather and dry in the rain.",al={"what does camping 101 teach","tent recipe","what do i learn from camping 101"}},{q="Where can you pitch a camp tent?",a="Pitch tents in the open wilderness, outside settlements and city centers.",al={"where can i pitch my tent","can i pitch a tent in town","camping in cities"}},{q="What else is required to set up a camp?",a="A camp needs a lit campfire as well as a tent. Cooking trainers teach the craft of making one.",al={"what do i need for a campsite","campfire requirement","do i need a campfire for tent"}},{q="Why is having a tent useful for travelers?",a="A tent shelters travelers from the weather and gives them rest, helping them stay alert far from inns.",al={"why build a tent","tent rest benefit","why camp"}},{q="Where is Nadyia Maneweaver located?",a="Nadyia Maneweaver is along the main road from Dolanaar toward Darnassus, the night elf capital.",al={"where is nadyia maneweaver","nadyia location","road to darnassus trainer"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you rely on rest and shelter in the wilds to stay sharp. A leather tent can help you find both.",["profession:Cooking"]="To make a proper camp, you need a warm campfire. Cooking trainers across the land teach you how to make one."},kw={"campfire","camping","darnassus","dolanaar","leatherworking","nadyia maneweaver","tent","wilderness"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","quest:487","topic:rogue"},m={id=97946},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97948"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="You’re sent to Auberdine to learn a new use for mining. There, Kurdram Stonehammer teaches skilled miners to craft a lodestone that strengthens allies gathered around a campfire.",h="You’re sent to Auberdine to learn a new use for mining.",sec={{t="The Practical Art of Earth and Stone",b="Mining has uses beyond smelting ingots and hammering armor. Experienced prospectors shape raw earth and magnetic ore into camping gear, so travelers can make well-fortified hearths in the wilderness. This introduction shows miners a practical use for their craft.",sp=0},{t="A Mentor in Auberdine",b="In Auberdine, the coastal town of Darkshore, promising miners seek out Kurdram Stonehammer. Once a miner proves dedication and skill, Kurdram teaches the method for making a camp lodestone. Set beside a fire, the stone strengthens the martial companions gathered nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Mining?",a="You’re sent to Auberdine to find Kurdram Stonehammer. Once you show your mining skill, he teaches you to make a lodestone that strengthens a camp.",al={"what is this quest","camping 101 mining objective","what do i do camping mining"}},{q="Who is Kurdram Stonehammer?",a="Kurdram Stonehammer is a craftsman in Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. He teaches qualified miners to make camping gear, including lodestones.",al={"who is kurdram stonehammer","auberdine mining trainer","kurdram stonehammer location"}},{q="What is a camp lodestone?",a="Miners craft a camp lodestone to set beside a campfire. It strengthens physical fighters gathered nearby.",al={"what does lodestone do","camp lodestone effect","camping oomph buff"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="Auberdine is a coastal port in Darkshore, an Alliance harbor and crossroads in northern Kalimdor. Kurdram Stonehammer lives there and teaches miners campcraft.",al={"where is auberdine","auberdine location","how to get to auberdine"}},{q="Who benefits from a camp lodestone?",a="Close-quarters fighters especially value a camp lodestone. Its power gives travelers gathered around the fire greater vigor in combat.",al={"who benefits from lodestone","is lodestone good for warriors","camp lodestone buff target"}},{q="When can you learn to craft the lodestone?",a="Kurdram Stonehammer teaches lodestone crafting once you show sufficient skill in mining.",al={"when can i learn lodestone","mining level for camp lodestone","proficiency requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can shape rough stone into a camp lodestone that aids travelers on the road and strengthens frontline fighters.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find Kurdram Stonehammer in Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore. He teaches campcraft to those passing through northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","campcraft","campfire","camping 101: mining","darkshore","kurdram stonehammer","lodestone","mining"},rel={"subzone:auberdine"},m={id=97948},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97949"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="Out in the wilds, you learn to make a Camp Chair and prepare a campsite. You need hides, open ground away from town, and a campfire.",h="Out in the wilds, you learn to make a Camp Chair and prepare a campsite.",sec={{t="Comforts of the Trail",b="Hides gathered on the road can be put to use. With the materials at hand, you learn to make a portable Camp Chair for journeys through Azeroth. Townsfolk object when travelers pitch camp in city centers, so take this craft into the open wilds.",sp=0},{t="The Essential Campfire",b="A campfire is the first need at a campsite in the wild. Its flames bring warmth and shelter from the elements. If you have not learned basic cooking, visit a cooking trainer to learn how to kindle a fire in the field.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do you learn from Camping 101: Skinning?",a="You learn to make a portable Camp Chair for resting in the wilderness.",al={"what do i get","what does camping 101 give","camp chair craft"}},{q="Can you set up a camp in town?",a="Townsfolk generally object to camps in town squares and city streets. Head into the wilds to pitch yours.",al={"can i camp in town","pitch tent in stormwind","camping inside cities"}},{q="Do you need a campfire to make camp?",a="Yes. A campsite needs a lit campfire. Cooking trainers across Azeroth can teach you to kindle one.",al={"need fire for camp","how to make campfire","fire for camp chair"}},{q="Where can you learn how to make a campfire?",a="Cooking trainers can teach you to prepare food and start a simple campfire with flint and wood.",al={"who teaches campfire","cooking fire trainer","where to learn cooking fire"}},{q="Why must you head into the wilderness to set up camp?",a="Open ground in the wilderness lets you pitch camp without disturbing town residents or blocking local roads and settlements.",al={"why need wilderness","where can i use camp chair","where to pitch camp"}},{q="How does skinning relate to making a camp chair?",a="Skinners work hides and leather taken from beasts. These materials suit portable outdoor seating such as a Camp Chair.",al={"skinning camping relation","why skinning for chair","skinning camp chair"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Learn basic cooking from a culinary trainer. Knowing how to build a campfire is essential when setting up a campsite in the wild."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping 101","camping 101: skinning","cooking","skinning","wilderness"},m={id=97949},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97950"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="A tailor can learn to make a Rallying Banner for a camp. Trianna in Darnassus teaches the pattern once you have shown skill in tailoring.",h="A tailor can learn to make a Rallying Banner for a camp.",sec={{t="A Banner for Camp",b="Someone who values tailoring points you to Trianna in Darnassus. She can teach you to craft a Faction Banner for your camp once you have shown proficiency in tailoring. A banner can lift inspiration and morale on a battlefield, and the craft is within reach for a skilled tailor.",sp=0},{t="Setting Up Camp",b="With Trianna's teaching, you can craft a Rallying Banner. To try it out, find a place in the wilderness, since most folk dislike camps in the middle of town. Bring a campfire too; a cook can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches tailoring a camp banner?",a="Trianna in Darnassus can teach you to craft a Faction Banner for your camp after you show proficiency in tailoring.",al={"tailor banner teacher","Trianna tailoring","camp banner trainer"}},{q="What can a tailor make for a camp?",a="A skilled tailor can learn to craft a Rallying Banner for a camp.",al={"tailor camp item","tailoring camp craft","what banner tailoring"}},{q="Why make a Rallying Banner?",a="An inspirational banner can help keep you energized, and inspiration and morale matter on a battlefield.",al={"banner purpose","rallying banner why","banner morale"}},{q="Where can I test my camp setup?",a="The completion advice is to try the banner in the wilderness, since most folk dislike camps in the center of town.",al={"where test banner","camping place","banner test location"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="A camp needs a campfire, and most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire for camp","fire needed","how make campfire"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can learn to craft a Rallying Banner for your camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"campfire","camping","darnassus","faction banner","rallying banner","tailoring","trianna"},rel={"zone:darnassus"},m={id=97950},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:97951"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="At your camp, alchemists can learn to craft a Mana Well. Carolai Anise in Brill teaches the craft once you have shown skill in alchemy.",h="At your camp, alchemists can learn to craft a Mana Well.",sec={{t="A camp for brews",b="Carolai Anise in Brill teaches alchemists to craft a Mana Well for their camp. Once you know the craft, you can make camp in the wilderness. First, you need a campfire, which cooks can teach you to make.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to craft a Mana Well?",a="Carolai Anise in Brill can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you have shown skill in alchemy.",al={"mana well trainer","who teaches mana well","carolai anise alchemy"}},{q="What is a Mana Well for?",a="A Mana Well is a camping item you can craft as an alchemist. Healers and spellcasters are drawn to its refreshing taste.",al={"mana well use","what does mana well do","mana camp item"}},{q="Where can I learn the Mana Well craft?",a="Carolai Anise in Brill can teach you the Mana Well craft.",al={"mana well location","brill alchemy trainer","where is carolai"}},{q="What do I need before starting a camp?",a="You need a campfire before you start your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","camp basics"}}},kw={"alchemist","alchemy","brill","camp","campfire","camping 101","carolai anise","mana well"},rel={"npc:carolai-anise","subzone:brill"},m={id=97951},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97952"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="A Blacksmith can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at camp. Basil Frye in Undercity can teach you once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",h="A Blacksmith can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at camp.",sec={{t="A Smith's Camp",b="Someone asks you to speak with Basil Frye in Undercity about a camping item for your Blacksmithing. You need to show proficiency in your skill before he teaches you to craft a Sharpening Wheel. At camp, the wheel lets Warriors and Rogues nearby hone their weapons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can Basil Frye teach me?",a="Basil Frye can teach you to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at camp, once you have shown proficiency in Blacksmithing.",al={"Basil Frye blacksmithing","sharpening wheel","camp blacksmith item"}},{q="What does a Sharpening Wheel do?",a="A Sharpening Wheel at your camp lets nearby Warriors and Rogues hone their weapons.",al={"what wheel do","sharpen weapons","sharpening wheel use"}},{q="Where do I find Basil Frye?",a="Basil Frye is in Undercity.",al={"Basil location","where is basil","Basil Frye Undercity"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Blacksmith, you can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at camp.",["class:Warrior"]="A Sharpening Wheel at camp lets you hone your weapon.",["class:Rogue"]="A Sharpening Wheel at camp lets you hone your weapon."},kw={"basil frye","blacksmithing","camp","rogue","sharpening wheel","undercity","warrior"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:warrior","topic:rogue"},m={id=97952},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97953"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="At Brill, Vance Undergloom teaches enchanters to make an Enchanted Lute for camp. First, show proficiency in your skill.",h="At Brill, Vance Undergloom teaches enchanters to make an Enchanted Lute for camp.",sec={{t="A Camp Companion",b="At a camp in the wilds, enchanters can learn to make an Enchanted Lute. Bring it along to lend some entertainment to your time away from the trail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I learn to craft?",a="You can learn to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp.",al={"enchanted lute","camping enchanting item","what does vance teach"}},{q="Who teaches me about the lute?",a="Vance Undergloom in Brill can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute.",al={"who is vance","vance undergloom","lute teacher"}},{q="Where do I find Vance Undergloom?",a="Vance Undergloom is in Brill.",al={"where is vance","vance location","brill enchanter"}},{q="What do I need before speaking with Vance?",a="Show proficiency in your skill before you learn to craft the camping item.",al={"skill requirement","show proficiency","enchanting requirement"}},{q="Why bring an Enchanted Lute to camp?",a="The Enchanted Lute brings entertainment to your time at camp.",al={"lute purpose","camp entertainment","why enchanted lute"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As an enchanter, you can learn to craft an Enchanted Lute for camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"brill","camp","camping 101","enchanted lute","enchanter","enchanting","vance undergloom"},rel={"subzone:brill"},m={id=97953},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:97955"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="general",s="At wilderness camps, Camping 101: First Aid helps healers prepare for injuries. In Brill, Nurse Neela teaches skilled practitioners to make a First Aid Kit for treating wounds far from settled lands.",h="At wilderness camps, Camping 101: First Aid helps healers prepare for injuries.",sec={{t="Medicine in the Field",b="Beyond guarded settlements, beasts and rival factions put travelers in danger. A healer trained in First Aid can learn to assemble a First Aid Kit for a wilderness camp. With it, travelers can tend wounds far from settled lands.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Brill",b="In Brill, Nurse Neela teaches travelers to put their medical skill to work at camp. Those skilled in bandaging and treatment can learn to make a portable First Aid Kit. First, travelers need a wilderness site and a basic campfire. Cooking instructors can teach them how to build one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nurse Neela?",a="Nurse Neela practices medicine in Brill, the Forsaken town in Tirisfal Glades. She teaches skilled First Aid practitioners to make kits for wilderness camps.",al={"who is nurse neela","where is nurse neela","nurse neela location"}},{q="What does a First Aid Kit do at a camp?",a="A First Aid Kit is a camp accessory made by First Aid practitioners. At a wilderness campsite, it supplies what travelers need to treat injuries.",al={"what is a first aid kit","first aid kit purpose","camp first aid kit"}},{q="Why do you need a campfire to set up camp?",a="A campfire must be in place before you can set up other camp amenities, including medical kits. Cooking instructors and cooks teach you to build a basic campfire.",al={"why need campfire","how to make campfire","cooking campfire camp"}},{q="Can you set up a camp inside a town?",a="You need to camp in the open wilderness. Town residents and local authorities generally object to tents and fires in the middle of town streets.",al={"can i camp in town","camping in brill","why camp in wilderness"}},{q="Who teaches how to make the First Aid Kit?",a="Nurse Neela in Brill teaches eligible travelers to make a First Aid Kit once they have enough First Aid skill.",al={"who teaches camping first aid","camping first aid trainer","first aid kit trainer"}},{q="What is the goal of Camping 101: First Aid?",a="Nurse Neela in Brill teaches you to use your field medicine skills to prepare medical supplies for outdoor camps.",al={"what is camping 101 first aid","camping 101 quest"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking instructors teach you to build a basic campfire. You need one before setting up a wilderness campsite or adding medical amenities.",["faction:Horde"]="Nurse Neela teaches in Brill, the Forsaken town in Tirisfal Glades, giving Horde travelers a local source of instruction.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can turn to Nurse Neela in Brill for help adapting your medicinal skills to survival in Lordaeron's ruined lands."},kw={"brill","campfire","camping","camping 101","first aid","first aid kit","nurse neela","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill"},m={id=97955},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97956"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="In Brill, someone hopes your fishing skill will bring cheer to camp. Clyde Kellen can teach you to make a fishbowl for it.",h="In Brill, someone hopes your fishing skill will bring cheer to camp.",sec={{t="A Camp Keepsake",b="Your fishing may brighten the camp. Once you've proved your skill, speak with Clyde Kellen in Brill. He can teach you to make a fishbowl for the camp.\n\nThe giver believes cheerful adventurers fight more strongly. They hope the fishbowl will bring joy to you and the others.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What am I being asked to do?",a="Prove your fishing skill, then speak with Clyde Kellen in Brill. He can teach you to make a fishbowl for your camp.",al={"what do i do","fishing camp task"}},{q="Who is Clyde Kellen?",a="Clyde Kellen is in Brill and can teach you to make a fishbowl for your camp.",al={"who's clyde","clyde kellen"}},{q="What is the fishbowl for?",a="The fishbowl is meant to bring joy to you and the other adventurers at camp.",al={"fishbowl purpose","camp fish bowl"}},{q="Why would fishing help the camp?",a="Your fishing skill can help you make a fishbowl. The giver hopes it will cheer the adventurers.",al={"fishing useful how","why fishing camp"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As an angler, you can use your fishing skill to make a fishbowl for your camp."},kw={"brill","camp","camping basics","clyde kellen","fishbowl","fishing"},rel={"subzone:brill"},m={id=97956},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97958"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="Shelene Rhobart can teach you to make a tent once you show your leatherworking skill. It offers shelter from heat and rain while you travel.",h="Shelene Rhobart can teach you to make a tent once you show your leatherworking skill.",sec={{t="A Leatherworker's Tent",b="A leatherworking trainer points you to Shelene Rhobart, who is on the road from Brill to Undercity. She can teach you to craft a camping item once you show proficiency in your skill. A tent can keep you cool on hot days and dry in the rain, giving you rest on your travels.",sp=0},{t="A Place to Camp",b="Your tent is meant for the wilderness, since most folk do not care for tents set up in the center of town. A campfire completes a camp, and cooks can teach you how to make one. If you need the basics of cooking, seek someone who can train you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a tent?",a="Shelene Rhobart can teach you to craft a camping item for leatherworking.",al={"tent trainer","who teaches tent","shelene tent"}},{q="Where is Shelene Rhobart?",a="Shelene Rhobart is on the road from Brill to Undercity.",al={"shelene location","where's shelene","road to undercity"}},{q="What does the tent do?",a="The tent can keep you cool on hot days and dry in the rain, so you can get rest while traveling.",al={"tent use","what's the tent for","camping tent"}},{q="Where should I set up the tent?",a="The tent is meant for the wilderness; most folk do not care for tents set up in the center of town.",al={"where to camp","tent in town","camping spot"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. A campfire completes a camp, and cooks can teach you how to make one.",al={"camp fire","need fire for camp","camping fire"}},{q="How do I learn to make a campfire?",a="Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you need the basics of cooking, seek someone who can train you.",al={"learn fire","cooking trainer","make a campfire"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach travelers how to make the campfire that completes a camp."},kw={"brill","camp tent","campfire","camping","cooking","leatherworking","shelene rhobart","tent","undercity"},rel={"npc:shelene-rhobart","subzone:brill","zone:undercity"},m={id=97958},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97959"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="You can now make a Lodestone and prepare to camp in the wilderness.",h="You can now make a Lodestone and prepare to camp in the wilderness.",sec={{t="A Place to Camp",b="You can now craft your own Lodestone. Try it in the wilderness, where folk are less likely to mind a camp. Before you start, you will also need a campfire. A cook can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can I make now?",a="From now on you can craft a Lodestone yourself.",al={"lodestone recipe","make lodestone"}},{q="Where should I try the Lodestone?",a="Head into the wilderness to try it; most folk do not want camps in the center of town.",al={"where to camp","test lodestone"}},{q="What do I need before starting a camp?",a="You need a campfire before starting your camp.",al={"campfire needed","camp setup"}},{q="Who can teach me to make a campfire?",a="A cook can teach you to make a campfire.",al={"learn campfire","who teaches fire"}}},kw={"campfire","camping","cook","lodestone","mining","wilderness"},m={id=97959},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97961"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="A tailoring trainer can show you how to make a Faction Banner for your camp. Bowen Brisboise teaches the craft once you prove your skill.",h="A tailoring trainer can show you how to make a Faction Banner for your camp.",sec={{t="A Banner for Camp",b="A tailoring trainer points you to Bowen Brisboise on the road from Deathknell to Brill. Prove your skill to him, and he can teach you to make a Faction Banner for your camp. A banner can help keep you encouraged in the field.",sp=0},{t="Setting Up Camp",b="Bowen Brisboise teaches you to make a Rallying Banner. To try it, you need to set your camp in the wilderness, since most folk dislike camps in town. You also need a campfire, which a cook can teach you to make.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who teaches tailoring camp crafts?",a="Bowen Brisboise can teach you to craft a Faction Banner once you prove your tailoring skill.",al={"who is bowen","bowen brisboise","tailoring teacher"}},{q="Where can I find Bowen Brisboise?",a="Bowen Brisboise is on the road from Deathknell to Brill.",al={"where's bowen","bowen location","road to brill"}},{q="What can tailoring make for a camp?",a="Tailoring can teach you to make a Faction Banner for your camp.",al={"tailoring camp item","banner craft","camp banner"}},{q="What is the banner called?",a="The banner you learn to craft is called a Rallying Banner.",al={"rallying banner","banner name","what banner"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. You need a campfire before setting up camp, and a cook can teach you to make one.",al={"camp fire needed","fire for camp","start a camp"}}},kw={"bowen brisboise","brill","campfire","camping","deathknell","faction banner","rallying banner","tailoring"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill"},m={id=97961},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:97963"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Alchemy",z="general",s="Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you show skill in Alchemy. The well draws healers and spellcasters to a camp for refreshment.",h="Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you show skill in Alchemy.",sec={{t="A Camp for Alchemists",b="An Alchemist can learn to make a Mana Well from Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village, once you have shown proficiency in your skill. Healers and spellcasters are drawn to its refreshing drink. To try it at camp, you need a campfire first; a cook can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What can Nyassa teach me?",a="Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Mana Well once you have shown proficiency in Alchemy.",al={"nyassa alchemy","mana well trainer","camping alchemy"}},{q="What does a Mana Well do?",a="A Mana Well draws healers and spellcasters to your camp for a refreshing drink.",al={"mana well use","what's mana well for","mana well"}},{q="Where do I learn to make a Mana Well?",a="Nyassa Swiftdraught teaches the recipe in Shen'dar Village.",al={"where nyassa","shen'dar village alchemy","mana well location"}},{q="What do I need before setting up camp?",a="You need a campfire to start your camp. A cook can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp","camping alchemy requirements"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A cook can teach you to make the campfire needed to start your camp."},kw={"alchemy","campfire","camping","healers","mana well","nyassa swiftdraught","shen'dar village","spellcasters"},m={id=97963},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Alchemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:97964"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Blacksmithing",z="general",s="As a Blacksmith, you can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at your camp. Aedi Thriceforged in Shen'dar Village can teach you once you have shown proficiency.",h="As a Blacksmith, you can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at your camp.",sec={{t="Aedi's Lesson",b="A Sharpening Wheel lets warriors and rogues nearby hone their weapons at your camp. In Shen'dar Village, Aedi Thriceforged can teach you its craft once you have shown proficiency in Blacksmithing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Sharpening Wheel?",a="Aedi Thriceforged in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Sharpening Wheel once you have shown proficiency in Blacksmithing.",al={"sharpening wheel teacher","who is aedi","aedi blacksmithing"}},{q="What does a Sharpening Wheel do?",a="At your camp, a Sharpening Wheel lets nearby warriors and rogues hone their weapons.",al={"sharpening wheel use","hone weapons","camp sharpening thing"}},{q="Where do I find Aedi Thriceforged?",a="Aedi Thriceforged is in Shen'dar Village.",al={"aedi location","where is aedi","aedi shendar"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Blacksmith, you can learn to craft a Sharpening Wheel for use at your camp.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior nearby, you can hone your weapon at a Sharpening Wheel set up at a camp.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue nearby, you can hone your weapon at a Sharpening Wheel set up at a camp."},kw={"aedi thriceforged","blacksmithing","camping 101","rogue","sharpening wheel","shen'dar village","warrior"},rel={"topic:warrior","topic:rogue"},m={id=97964},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Blacksmithing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97965"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: First Aid",z="general",s="At Shen'dar Village, you seek care for injuries far from civilization. Naleeia Tattermend teaches skilled practitioners to prepare medical kits for a wilderness camp.",h="At Shen'dar Village, you seek care for injuries far from civilization.",sec={{t="Healing in the Wilderness",b="A journey across Azeroth can bring violence, wild beasts, and hazards of the land. First Aid lets you bind cuts and broken bones without relying only on spellcraft. A First Aid Kit at a wilderness camp gives you a place to tend injuries and help companions recover. Then you can prepare to travel on.",sp=0},{t="The Mentor of Shen'dar Village",b="In Shen'dar Village, Naleeia Tattermend teaches practitioners to make durable medical supplies for a campsite. She shares her techniques after you show that you know basic medical care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who do I need to speak with for this quest?",a="Speak with Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village. She knows how to craft medical supplies for wilderness camps.",al={"who to talk to camping first aid","where is naleeia tattermend","camping 101 first aid turn in"}},{q="Where is Shen'dar Village located?",a="Shen'dar Village is on Zephras Isle, where Naleeia Tattermend lives. Practitioners travel there for further wilderness first aid training after honing their skills.",al={"where is shendar village","shen'dar village location","shendar village first aid"}},{q="What is the purpose of crafting a First Aid Kit for camp?",a="You learn to make a First Aid Kit for an adventurer's campsite. Supplies ready at camp let you treat injuries between journeys. They may mean the difference between life and death.",al={"what does camping first aid do","first aid kit camp","why craft first aid kit"}},{q="When will Naleeia Tattermend teach me to craft the kit?",a="Naleeia Tattermend teaches you after you show enough skill in First Aid. Practice bandaging and treatment before making field kits.",al={"when can i learn the first aid kit","naleeia tattermend requirement","camping 101 first aid requirement"}},{q="Why is First Aid considered both honorable and pragmatic?",a="Wounds and physical trauma threaten travelers across Azeroth. Bandages and medical care let travelers of every discipline tend their own wounds and stabilize companions without relying only on magic.",al={"why is first aid important","first aid lore","is first aid useful"}},{q="Can any adventurer craft a camping First Aid Kit?",a="Any adventurer who studies First Aid and proves their skill can learn from Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to make a First Aid Kit for camp.",al={"can anyone learn this kit","who can make first aid kit camp"}}},kw={"bandages","camping","camping 101: first aid","first aid","first aid kit","naleeia tattermend","shen'dar village","wilderness survival"},m={id=97965},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: First Aid"},fv=true}
E["quest:97967"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Fishing",z="general",s="You are learning how fishing can make wilderness camps more welcoming. In Shen'dar Village, skilled anglers can ask Fenn Fairweather to teach them the Fish Bowl craft.",h="You are learning how fishing can make wilderness camps more welcoming.",sec={{t="Comforts of the Hearth",b="A camp in the wild needs comfort along with sharp blades and sturdy armor. Good spirits help companions bear the strain of life in the field. Fishing brings provisions, and skilled anglers can put their craft to work improving a campsite. With live fish and a proper fixture, a traveler can make camp more welcoming.",sp=0},{t="The Artisan of Shen'dar",b="In Shen'dar Village, Fenn Fairweather shares fishing secrets with seasoned anglers who know the patience of rod and reel. Anglers with enough skill can learn to make a Fish Bowl, a simple fixture that brings cheer and rest to weary companions. Good spirits in the wild help a group stay focused and resolute when danger draws near.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches the Fish Bowl camping craft?",a="Fenn Fairweather teaches the Fish Bowl craft in Shen'dar Village. Show enough skill in fishing, and Fenn can teach you to make one for camp.",al={"who gives fish bowl","where is fenn fairweather","fish bowl trainer"}},{q="What purpose does a Fish Bowl serve at camp?",a="A Fish Bowl is a decorative fixture that brings comfort and cheer to you and your companions at camp. A well-kept camp and high spirits help you stay sharp and ready for danger in the field.",al={"what does fish bowl do","fish bowl buff","camping fish bowl effect"}},{q="Where is Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village is a gathering place for tradesfolk and instructors, including Fenn Fairweather. Anglers go there to learn practical camping crafts suited to their skills.",al={"where is shendar village","shen'dar village location"}},{q="What skill is required to learn this camping craft?",a="You need to show basic skill as an angler before learning this craft. Once your fishing is well honed, instructors in Shen'dar Village can teach you to make camp fixtures such as the Fish Bowl.",al={"camping fishing requirements","when can i learn fish bowl","how to start camping fishing"}},{q="Why does fishing matter for wilderness camping?",a="Fishing brings in food, and an angler's patience and keen eye can also improve camp life. A fresh catch displayed in a crafted bowl offers calm and lifts spirits during long wilderness journeys.",al={"why fishing for camping","fishing usefulness in camp"}},{q="Who is Fenn Fairweather?",a="Fenn Fairweather is an artisan and instructor in Shen'dar Village. Fenn knows the practical comforts of wilderness life and shares camp fixture craft with skilled anglers.",al={"who is fenn fairweather","fenn fairweather lore"}}},kw={"camping","camping 101: fishing","fenn fairweather","fish bowl","fishing","shen'dar village"},m={id=97967},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Fishing"},fv=true}
E["quest:97968"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Herbalism",z="general",s="At camps along the trail, Camping 101: Herbalism points gatherers toward instructors who teach them to make Incense Candles. Herbalists use gathered plants to bring comfort to spellcasters and healers on long journeys.",h="At camps along the trail, Camping 101: Herbalism points gatherers toward instructors who teach them to make...",sec={{t="Wild Flora on the Trail",b="Travelers can put roots and petals to use beyond selling fresh stems or brewing draughts. Gatherers meet instructors who teach them to make Incense Candles from wild aromatic plants. These candles support companions on the trail.",sp=0},{t="Soothing the Mind",b="Long journeys through hostile country wear down healers and spellcasters. At an active campsite, an Incense Candle gives off a soothing, revitalizing scent that lifts their spirits and helps them recover clarity and strength before danger calls again. Those who wield magic or tend the wounded value that comfort most.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Herbalism?",a="Camping 101: Herbalism connects skilled herb gatherers with instructors who teach them to make Incense Candles for wilderness camps.",al={"what is camping 101 herbalism","camping 101 herbalism quest","herbalism camping quest"}},{q="What is an Incense Candle used for?",a="An Incense Candle is made from gathered plants and burned at a campsite. Its soothing, revitalizing scent lifts resting companions’ spirits and gives healers and spellcasters a beneficial boost.",al={"what does incense candle do","incense candle camp effect","why make incense candle"}},{q="Who teaches how to make an Incense Candle?",a="Your instructor depends on where you begin: Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge, Malorne Bladeleaf in Dolanaar, Herbalist Pomeroy in Elwynn Forest, Jandi in Orgrimmar, Faruza in Brill, Komin Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff, or Syriel Nightrain in Valanaar.",al={"who teaches incense candle","incense candle trainer","where to learn incense candle"}},{q="Why are Incense Candles especially useful for magic users?",a="Casting spells and tending wounds drain physical energy and mental focus. The soothing smoke of an Incense Candle helps replenish both, keeping spirits high and casters ready for battle.",al={"why do spellcasters need incense","incense candle healers","incense candle magic users"}},{q="Do you need to be an herbalist to take this quest?",a="This instruction is for those skilled in gathering plants and herbs. It teaches how to find and use aromatic wild plants.",al={"can anyone learn incense candle","do i need herbalism for camping 101 herbalism","herbalism requirement camping candle"}},{q="How does Herbalism tie into camping?",a="Gathered plants have uses around camp beyond brewing concoctions and salves. They can be made into incense that refreshes weary companions.",al={"is herbalism just for potions","uses for herbs camping","herbalism camp items"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering plants in the wilderness provides the aromatic herbs needed for camp incense. That makes the work useful for survival as well as alchemy.",["class:Priest"]="Incense Candles lit at camp lift the spirits and replenish the mental reserves of holy healers between skirmishes.",["class:Mage"]="Spellcasters who spend their focus in battle value camp incense, whose soothing scent helps restore their minds and support arcane recovery."},kw={"camp","camping","camping 101: herbalism","healers","herbalism","herbs","incense candle","spellcasters"},m={id=97968},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Herbalism"},fv=true}
E["quest:97969"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Leatherworking",z="general",s="A leatherworker’s travels lead to lessons in making a shelter for the wilds. In Shen'dar Village, Indari Sunseam teaches skilled craftsmen to stitch tents that protect travelers and give them rest on long journeys.",h="A leatherworker’s travels lead to lessons in making a shelter for the wilds.",sec={{t="Shelter on the Road",b="Traveling leatherworkers need sturdy gear made from hide and pelt. Once they learn the craft, they are sent to Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village. There, she teaches them to make a proper camping tent. It keeps travelers dry in heavy rain and cool beneath a blazing sun, helping them rest on long journeys.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness Campsites",b="Townsfolk object when rough camps clutter their streets, so you pitch your tent in the wild. A campsite needs more than shelter; it also needs a warming campfire. Visit a local cook to learn basic firemaking before you set out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches leatherworkers how to craft a tent?",a="Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village teaches skilled leatherworkers to make camping tents.",al={"who teaches leatherworking tents","camp tent trainer","where is indari sunseam"}},{q="What is the purpose of crafting a tent?",a="A well-made tent shields travelers from heavy rain and blazing heat, helping them rest and stay alert on the road.",al={"what does a tent do","tent purpose","tent benefits"}},{q="Where can a camping tent be pitched?",a="You pitch a tent in the wilderness, away from town centers where locals object to camps.",al={"can i pitch tent in city","where to use tent","camp rules"}},{q="What else is needed to pitch a proper camp?",a="A proper camp also needs a campfire. A cooking trainer can teach you to build a basic fire.",al={"do i need a fire","camp requirements","what else for camp"}},{q="When does Indari Sunseam teach you the tent pattern?",a="Indari Sunseam teaches the tent pattern after you have practiced leatherworking and shown proficiency in the trade.",al={"when can i learn tent","tent requirements","leatherworking tent req"}},{q="What is Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village is where Indari Sunseam lives and works, teaching travelers to craft camping supplies.",al={"where is shen'dar village","shendar village location","indari sunseam town"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="A tent alone does not make a complete camp. You also need to learn basic campfire craft, usually from a cooking trainer."},kw={"camp tent","campfire","camping","cooking","indari sunseam","leatherworking","shen'dar village","tent","wilderness"},m={id=97969},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Leatherworking"},fv=true}
E["quest:97970"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Mining",z="general",s="A mining instructor in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Lodestone for your camp. It gives those gathered around the fire extra strength in combat.",h="A mining instructor in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Lodestone for your camp.",sec={{t="A Miner's Craft",b="Mining offers honest work, and you can learn a camp craft through Messana Crestwind in Shen'dar Village. Once you have shown proficiency in mining, she can teach you to make a Lodestone. Those who gather around your fire can draw extra strength from it, so the craft may bring sword-wielders to your camp.",sp=0},{t="A Place to Camp",b="With the craft learned, you can make your own Lodestone. Camps are unwelcome in the center of town, so take it into the wilderness to test it. A campfire is needed before you set up camp, and a cook can teach you how to make one.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make a Lodestone?",a="Messana Crestwind in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Lodestone after you show proficiency in mining.",al={"lodestone trainer","who teaches mining camp craft"}},{q="What does a Lodestone do?",a="It gives those gathered around your campfire extra strength in combat.",al={"lodestone use","what's lodestone for"}},{q="Where can I test my Lodestone?",a="You can test it in the wilderness; camps are unwelcome in the center of town.",al={"where test lodestone","lodestone camp"}},{q="Do I need a campfire?",a="Yes. You need a campfire before setting up camp, and a cook can teach you to make one.",al={"campfire needed","how start camp"}},{q="What do I need before Messana teaches me?",a="You need to show proficiency in mining before Messana Crestwind can teach you to craft a Lodestone.",al={"mining proficiency","how learn lodestone"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can show your proficiency to Messana Crestwind and learn to craft a Lodestone for your camp.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make the campfire needed to set up camp."},kw={"camp","campfire","camping 101","lodestone","messana crestwind","mining","shen'dar village"},m={id=97970},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Mining"},fv=true}
E["quest:97971"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Skinning",z="general",s="In Shen'dar Village, Mendalass Tattermend shows skinners how to prepare for rest in the wilds. The lesson joins skinning with survival and a place to sit at camp.",h="In Shen'dar Village, Mendalass Tattermend shows skinners how to prepare for rest in the wilds.",sec={{t="Comfort in the Wilds",b="You can shape hides from fallen beasts into more than armor. Mendalass Tattermend shows you how to make a portable Camp Chair, so you can rest in the wilds and regain your strength before battle.",sp=0},{t="The Teachings of Shen'dar Village",b="In Shen'dar Village, Mendalass Tattermend teaches proven skinners to make sturdy seats from collected pelts. Towns forbid camps within their limits. A campsite also needs a campfire, a skill local culinary instructors have traditionally taught.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Skinning about?",a="In Shen'dar Village, Mendalass Tattermend teaches skinners to make a Camp Chair from harvested hides. It gives you a place to rest while camping in the wilds.",al={"what is this quest","camping 101 purpose","why do this quest"}},{q="Who is Mendalass Tattermend?",a="Mendalass Tattermend is a skinning trainer in Shen'dar Village. The trainer teaches proficient skinners to make field seating from harvested hides.",al={"who is mendalass","who teaches camp chair","mendalass tattermend"}},{q="Where can Mendalass Tattermend be found?",a="Mendalass Tattermend is in Shen'dar Village, where skinners can show their skill and learn to make camp gear.",al={"where is mendalass","where is shendar village","where do i turn this in"}},{q="What item does this quest teach you to make?",a="Skinners learn to make a Camp Chair from hides gathered from fallen beasts. It gives you a place to rest in the wilds.",al={"what do skinners make","camp chair recipe","what item do i get"}},{q="Can you set up camp inside a town?",a="No. Towns forbid camps within their limits, so camps and chairs belong in the wilderness.",al={"can i camp in town","where can i pitch camp","where to use camp chair"}},{q="What else is required to make a proper camp?",a="A proper campsite needs a campfire. Culinary trainers traditionally teach the basics of starting one.",al={"what else do i need for camp","campfire needed","camp requirements"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Cooking and wilderness survival go hand in hand. A campsite needs a campfire, a skill culinary trainers traditionally teach."},kw={"camp chair","campfire","camping 101","hides","mendalass tattermend","shen'dar village","skinning","wilderness"},m={id=97971},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Skinning"},fv=true}
E["quest:97972"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="A tailor can learn to make a Faction Banner for your camp. You need to show proficiency in Tailoring before Taleen Shimmerthread can teach you.",h="A tailor can learn to make a Faction Banner for your camp.",sec={{t="A Banner for Camp",b="Someone who can teach you to make a Faction Banner is in Shen'dar Village. Taleen Shimmerthread can show you how to craft this camping item once you have proved your Tailoring skill. An inspiring banner can help keep you energized on the battlefield.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who can teach me to make a Faction Banner?",a="Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a Faction Banner for your camp once you show proficiency in Tailoring.",al={"banner teacher","who teaches tailoring banner","taleen banner"}},{q="What is the Faction Banner for?",a="The Faction Banner is a camping item. An inspirational banner can help keep you energized on the battlefield.",al={"banner purpose","why make a banner","camp banner"}},{q="What do I need before Taleen can teach me?",a="You need to show proficiency in Tailoring before Taleen Shimmerthread can teach you to craft the Faction Banner.",al={"tailoring requirement","how skilled for banner","banner skill"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can learn to craft a Faction Banner for your camp after showing proficiency in your skill."},kw={"camping","faction banner","profession","shen'dar village","tailoring","taleen shimmerthread"},m={id=97972},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:97973"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Tailoring",z="general",s="At Shen'dar Village, tailors can learn to make a Faction Banner for wilderness camps. The banner lifts spirits and helps sustain morale.",h="At Shen'dar Village, tailors can learn to make a Faction Banner for wilderness camps.",sec={{t="The Weaver's Contribution to Camp",b="A campsite in the wild calls for more than warm clothes. A well-made banner can give a camp a shared purpose, so clothworkers are urged to carry their craft beyond garments and bags. With further instruction, bolts of woven fabric become a sign of unity and fortitude.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Shen'dar Village",b="In Shen'dar Village, Taleen Shimmerthread teaches camping crafts to tailors with enough skill. She shows them how to fashion a Faction Banner. Stitched with care and planted at camp, it rallies allies and helps keep their spirits up through the trials ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Camping 101: Tailoring?",a="At Shen'dar Village, promising tailors can seek instruction in field craft. Show enough skill in tailoring and you can learn to make a Faction Banner for a wilderness campsite.",al={"what is this quest","camping 101 tailoring quest","tailoring camping banner"}},{q="Who is Taleen Shimmerthread?",a="Taleen Shimmerthread is a skilled tailor in Shen'dar Village. She teaches qualified crafters to make camping items, including banners that lift spirits at camp.",al={"taleen shimmerthread","who teaches tailoring banner","where is taleen shimmerthread"}},{q="Where is Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village is where Taleen Shimmerthread lives. Tailors go there to learn how to use their cloth-working craft to make camping gear.",al={"where is shendar village","shendar village location"}},{q="What camping item can tailors learn to craft?",a="Tailors can learn to make a Faction Banner for camp. Planting one gives those resting there an inspiring presence.",al={"faction banner camping","what does tailoring make for camp","tailoring camp item"}},{q="What are the requirements to learn the camping banner?",a="You need to show skill in tailoring before Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village will teach you to make a Faction Banner for camp.",al={"how to learn faction banner","tailoring requirements camping banner"}},{q="Why are faction banners valuable at camp?",a="Faction banners lift spirits and sustain morale on a campaign. Tailors stitch them as an energizing focal point for adventurers on grueling journeys.",al={"why make a faction banner","camping banner morale"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you can make Faction Banners that lift camp morale and energize allies in the field."},kw={"camp banner","camping","camping 101: tailoring","faction banner","shen'dar village","tailoring","taleen shimmerthread","tradeskill"},m={id=97973},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Tailoring"},fv=true}
E["quest:97977"] = {t="quest",n="Nature's Call",z="general",s="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella seeks the cause of the Gnarlpine's sudden hostility. Their carved totems may tell why they turned against their longtime night elf allies.",h="In Shadowglen, Tarindrella seeks the cause of the Gnarlpine's sudden hostility.",sec={{t="Investigating the Glen",b="The dryad Tarindrella asks you to search camps along Shadowglen's western border. The Gnarlpine furbolgs left them in haste, and she cannot believe they would cast aside centuries of friendship with the night elves without cause. Bring back intact engraved totems. Their carvings may tell what changed.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow and the Nightmare",b="The Gnarlpine totems tell of nightmares about an encroaching shadow that would wipe out their tribe. Fear grew into blind rage and warped their minds. They came to see their longtime elven neighbors as the very shadow they feared. Tarindrella hopes their story will shed light on the deeper malaise creeping through Teldrassil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Nature's Call?",a="Tarindrella, a dryad, watches over Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Alarmed by the Gnarlpine furbolgs' sudden hostility, she asks you to recover relics from their camps and seek the cause of their madness.",al={"who gives nature's call","who is tarindrella","tarindrella location"}},{q="Why did the Gnarlpine furbolgs turn hostile?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs suffered nightmares of a looming shadow that threatened to destroy them. Dread twisted into paranoia and fury, until they saw their longtime night elf allies as enemies.",al={"why did gnarlpine attack","why are gnarlpine mad","what happened to gnarlpine furbolgs"}},{q="Where are the Gnarlpine totems located?",a="Smaller Gnarlpine totems lie in abandoned furbolg camps along the glen's western edge. Grell and grellkin scavenging among the ruins have scattered some across the surrounding area.",al={"where are the gnarlpine totems","find gnarlpine totems","gnarlpine camp location"}},{q="Why can't players collect the larger totems in the camps?",a="Tarindrella advises you to leave the larger totems in the camps. She says that, as a dryad, she would not know what to do with such cumbersome carvings, and prefers smaller engraved totems that can be carried.",al={"why large totems ignored","can i loot big totems","big gnarlpine totem"}},{q="Who are the Gnarlpine furbolg?",a="The Gnarlpine are a furbolg tribe native to Teldrassil. They lived peacefully alongside the night elves, but creeping nightmares have recently turned them into aggressive foes.",al={"who are the gnarlpine","gnarlpine lore","are gnarlpine evil"}},{q="What is the great shadow mentioned in the totems?",a="The totems speak of an unseen Great Shadow haunting the furbolgs' dreams. Its origin remains unknown, and Tarindrella hopes their fate will help uncover the broader corruption afflicting Teldrassil.",al={"what shadow gnarlpine","what is the shadow in teldrassil","nightmares in teldrassil"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the Gnarlpine's fall from longtime companions into hostility and madness is a personal tragedy for Teldrassil's defenders.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are attuned to nature's balance and the spiritual corruption affecting Kalimdor's creatures. Nightmare-touched furbolg totems are cause for alarm.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Teldrassil's boughs and keep your newfound night elf allies anchored on Kalimdor."},kw={"furbolg","gnarlpine","grell","grellkin","nature's call","nightmares","shadowglen","tarindrella","teldrassil","totem"},rel={"npc:tarindrella","topic:furbolg","quest:940"},m={id=97977},src={"In-game quest text: Nature's Call"},fv=true}
E["quest:97979"] = {t="quest",n="The Goddess Provides",z="general",s="Beneath Teldrassil, young night elves begin a rite that teaches them to know Elune’s gifts. After the Long Vigil, they seek guidance in her radiance and shelter in her shadow.",h="Beneath Teldrassil, young night elves begin a rite that teaches them to know Elune’s gifts.",sec={{t="A Vigil Concluded",b="For millennia after the Sundering, the kaldorei kept apart from other peoples. During the Long Vigil, they watched over Kalimdor and guarded the sacred peaks of Mount Hyjal. The Third War brought devastation, and the defense of the World Tree ended their ancient seclusion.\n\nNow the night elves dwell beneath Teldrassil’s boughs and face an unfamiliar world. They reach across the ocean to make allies and take their place among Azeroth’s peoples.",sp=0},{t="Blessings of Mother Moon",b="Elune, the Mother Moon, remains at the heart of kaldorei faith, though the night elves now dwell in a new home and form new ties. From their earliest days, they learn to call on her gifts. Her radiance guides their strikes and clarifies their purpose. Her shadow hides them from enemy sight.\n\nThese inherited blessings bind the kaldorei to their goddess and prepare them for dangers beyond the Great Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Goddess Provides?",a="Young night elves learn to recognize and demonstrate Elune’s blessings in a rite beneath Teldrassil’s boughs.",al={"what is the goddess provides","the goddess provides quest"}},{q="Who is the goddess referenced in this quest?",a="The goddess is Elune, whom the kaldorei call Mother Moon. She is central to night elf culture and spiritual life, and they believe she grants her children protection, clarity, and stealth.",al={"who is the goddess","who is mother moon","night elf goddess"}},{q="What gifts does Elune provide to the kaldorei?",a="Elune grants radiance that guides a warrior’s strikes and the power to blend into surrounding shadows.",al={"what gifts does elune give","elune racial abilities","elune powers"}},{q="What was the Long Vigil?",a="The Long Vigil was the thousands of years when the night elves guarded Kalimdor in isolation. It ended after they defended Mount Hyjal against the Burning Legion, and the kaldorei then opened their borders.",al={"what was the long vigil","why did the long vigil end"}},{q="Why have the night elves joined the Alliance?",a="After defending Mount Hyjal, the night elves ended their long isolation and chose to forge ties with mortal races across the sea. They joined the Grand Alliance for mutual survival and camaraderie.",al={"why did night elves join alliance","kaldorei alliance"}},{q="Where does this instruction take place?",a="Teldrassil is a Great Tree off Kalimdor’s northern coast. After the Third War, its sheltered boughs became the night elves’ new home and sanctuary.",al={"where is teldrassil","what is teldrassil"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you inherit Elune’s blessings: moonlight to reveal hidden paths and shadows to conceal your presence.",["faction:Alliance"]="After the battle at Mount Hyjal, the night elves ended their long isolation and joined the Alliance. You share your people’s lunar powers in service of mutual defense.",["class:Priest"]="As a kaldorei priest, you devote yourself to Mother Moon and channel Elune’s grace as guiding radiance and divine protection."},kw={"elune","goddess provides","hyjal","kaldorei","long vigil","mother moon","shadowmeld","teldrassil"},rel={"topic:elune","quest:940","zone:hyjal","topic:alliance","quest:5672"},m={id=97979},src={"In-game quest text: The Goddess Provides"},fv=true}
E["quest:97985"] = {t="quest",n="Thundering Hearts",z="general",s="In Thousand Needles, the researcher seeks Stormheart’s massive heart for work on an abomination.",h="In Thousand Needles, the researcher seeks Stormheart’s massive heart for work on an abomination.",sec={{t="A Large Heart",b="A researcher studying abomination creation believes the work calls for a massive heart. Stormheart, a thunder lizard said to patrol the canyon edge in Thousand Needles, seems large enough. But Stormheart is not docile.",sp=0},{t="The Heart",b="Stormheart’s heart still carries electrical pulses. The researcher says it appears to match the size specified in the notes and will be added to the abomination.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants Stormheart’s heart?",a="A researcher studying abomination creation wants Stormheart’s heart for an abomination.",al={"who needs the heart","abomination researcher","who sent me"}},{q="Where is Stormheart?",a="Stormheart patrols along the canyon edge in Thousand Needles.",al={"stormheart location","where's the thunder lizard","stormheart where"}},{q="What is Stormheart?",a="Stormheart is a thunder lizard of impressive size.",al={"stormheart creature","big lizard","thunder lizard"}},{q="Why is a heart needed?",a="The researcher’s notes say abomination creation requires a massive heart.",al={"why heart","abomination heart","what's the heart for"}},{q="What does the researcher know about the heart?",a="The researcher says the heart still carries electrical pulses and appears to match the size specified in the notes.",al={"heart details","electrical heart","what's special about it"}}},kw={"abomination","creation","heart","stormheart","thousand needles","thunder lizard","thundering hearts"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles"},m={id=97985},src={"In-game quest text: Thundering Hearts"},fv=true}
E["quest:98013"] = {t="quest",n="Swelling Forces",z="general",s="At the Grove of the Ancients, Arbal sends defenders against the Stormscale naga in the northeast ruins. These cursed former Highborne threaten the surrounding woodlands as their numbers grow.",h="At the Grove of the Ancients, Arbal sends defenders against the Stormscale naga in the northeast ruins.",sec={{t="Serpents in the Sunken City",b="Arbal watches the northeast ruins from the Grove of the Ancients with grave concern. Cursed Highborne have become the serpent-like naga of the Stormscale tribe. They now occupy the remains of their old civilization, and their growing army could spread beyond the ruins into the wider forest. Arbal sends defenders there to cut down their numbers before that happens.",sp=0},{t="An Unholy Alliance",b="Arbal warns that the Stormscale naga aid the Twilight's Hammer cult. These former Highborne now desecrate and pillage the forests that once sheltered them, serving sinister masters. To Arbal, this is unforgivable. Their numbers must be curbed before the cult and its serpentine allies tighten their hold on the land.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Swelling Forces?",a="Arbal gives the order from the Grove of the Ancients, directing defenders against the hostile naga gathering in the northeast ruins.",al={"who gives swelling forces","arbal quest giver","where is arbal"}},{q="Why are the naga being targeted in this quest?",a="The Stormscale naga have occupied the nearby ruins and threaten the surrounding woodlands. They also aid the Twilight's Hammer cult, bringing violence to lands they once called home.",al={"why kill naga","naga in the ruins","stormscale threat"}},{q="What is the connection between the naga and the ruins?",a="The naga were once Highborne elves of ancient Kalimdor, changed by a terrible curse. They once lived in these cities and have returned as serpents seeking conquest and devastation.",al={"who are the stormscale naga","naga origins","cursed highborne"}},{q="What is the naga's connection to the Twilight's Hammer?",a="The Stormscale naga are assisting the Twilight's Hammer cult. Arbal warns that their alliance threatens further ruin for the ancient forests.",al={"twilights hammer naga","why naga working with cult"}},{q="Where do the Stormscale forces gather?",a="The Stormscale forces gather in ruins northeast of the Grove of the Ancients. Defenders are sent to curb their growing numbers there.",al={"where are the ruins","where to find stormscale"}},{q="Why does Arbal consider the naga's actions unforgivable?",a="Arbal considers it unforgivable that the naga pillage their ancient homeland at a dark master's command. Their former Highborne nobility has given way to cruelty and dark alliances.",al={"why does arbal hate naga","unforgivable arbal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The naga in these ruins were once Highborne kindred of the night elves. Their return to desecrate and pillage the ancient forests alongside dark cultists is a bitter betrayal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance forces defending the sacred forests around Darkshore and the Grove of the Ancients face a coordinated front of naga and Twilight's Hammer."},kw={"arbal","grove of the ancients","highborne","myrmidon","naga","sorceress","stormscale","swelling forces","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:952","topic:naga","topic:highborne","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},m={id=98013},src={"In-game quest text: Swelling Forces"},fv=true}
E["quest:98021"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to Sentinel Hill",z="general",s="At Sentinel Hill, Journey to Sentinel Hill brings Alliance travelers into Westfall’s troubled farmlands. The local commanders have pleaded with Stormwind for months without answer, and now put any willing traveler to work.",h="At Sentinel Hill, Journey to Sentinel Hill brings Alliance travelers into Westfall’s troubled farmlands.",sec={{t="Arrival on the Frontier",b="In Westfall, you arrive at Sentinel Hill, the outpost guarding the surrounding farmlands. Its garrison is short of soldiers and overlooked by the royal court. When travelers offer help, the local commander asks little about their standing. Any willing hands are welcome.",sp=0},{t="Pleas to Stormwind",b="For months, Sentinel Hill’s leaders have asked Stormwind for soldiers to defend Westfall from threats drawing near. With no reinforcements, local commanders accept whoever arrives. One commander expected an army and got a skinny elf instead. In Westfall, beggars cannot be choosers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Journey to Sentinel Hill?",a="Journey to Sentinel Hill brings Alliance travelers into Westfall, where defenders at Sentinel Hill have asked Stormwind for help without receiving enough soldiers.",al={"what is journey to sentinel hill","journey to sentinel hill quest","sentinel hill quest"}},{q="Why is Sentinel Hill asking for help?",a="Sentinel Hill’s leaders have asked Stormwind for soldiers for months to meet the troubles in Westfall. With no reinforcements, they rely on whichever travelers arrive.",al={"who is begging stormwind for aid","sentinel hill garrison","why sentinel hill needs help"}},{q="Why does the quest text mention a skinny elf?",a="The commander expected help from Stormwind after months of pleas, but got a skinny elf instead. Beggars cannot be choosers, so the commander puts the newcomer to work.",al={"skinny elf quote","why skinny elf","sentinel hill elf comment"}},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind sent proper reinforcements?",a="Sentinel Hill has appealed to Stormwind for months, but royal support has not arrived. The local commanders depend on volunteers.",al={"why won't stormwind help westfall","stormwind neglecting westfall","stormwind westfall aid"}},{q="What is Sentinel Hill?",a="Sentinel Hill is a military outpost guarding Westfall’s farmlands. It is the main defense against the region’s lawlessness, Defias bandits, and gnolls.",al={"where is sentinel hill","what is sentinel hill","sentinel hill location"}},{q="What happens after reaching Sentinel Hill?",a="When you report to Sentinel Hill, the local defenders put you to work at once. You help face the many threats across Westfall’s plains and farmlands.",al={"what to do in westfall","westfall next quests","what happens after arriving in westfall"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Westfall needs help, but Stormwind has left its commanders waiting for soldiers. They rely on whatever volunteers arrive.",["race:NightElf"]="At Sentinel Hill, the frontier commander may grumble that Stormwind sent a skinny elf instead of seasoned infantry. The outpost needs all the help it can get."},kw={"journey to sentinel hill","peoples militia","sentinel hill","skinny elf","stormwind","westfall"},rel={"zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=98021},src={"In-game quest text: Journey to Sentinel Hill"},fv=true}
E["quest:98024"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to the Crossroads",z="general",s="A newly arrived traveler from the elemental plane is sent to the Crossroads in the Barrens. There, Thork calls for aid as the Horde faces the dangers of Kalimdor's frontier.",h="A newly arrived traveler from the elemental plane is sent to the Crossroads in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Call to the Frontier",b="You have come to Azeroth from the elemental plane. Mortal conflicts may seem small beside what you have known, but the Horde faces dangers of its own. Service on the frontier gives you a chance to grow formidable while aiding the realm.",sp=0},{t="The Crossroads of Kalimdor",b="The Barrens lie southwest, and the Crossroads stands among its broad, sun-baked plains. This Horde outpost is a vital junction, though dangers press its defenders from every side. Report to Thork and join the settlement's defense.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thork?",a="Thork is a Horde authority stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He oversees the local defense and directs newcomers to help against threats to the settlement and nearby lands.",al={"who is thork","crossroads leader","where is thork"}},{q="What is the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads is a Horde outpost and trading hub where major trails meet in the Barrens. Hostile wildlife, centaur tribes, and quilboar raiders threaten the settlement, so its defenders need help keeping supply lines secure.",al={"what is the crossroads","crossroads barrens","why go to crossroads"}},{q="Where are the Barrens located?",a="The Barrens is a vast, arid savannah in central Kalimdor, southwest of Durotar. It connects Horde territories across the continent.",al={"where are the barrens","barrens location"}},{q="Why does the quest mention the elemental plane?",a="The traveler has recently arrived in Azeroth from the elemental plane. Conflicts there may seem vast, but dangers to the mortal realm and the Horde are immediate and severe.",al={"elemental plane arrival","why elemental plane","journey from elemental plane"}},{q="What is the purpose of Journey to the Crossroads?",a="You are sent to report to Thork at the Crossroads. There, you can join the Horde's frontline efforts and grow formidable through honorable service.",al={"crossroads quest purpose","why send to crossroads"}},{q="What dangers do the citizens of the Crossroads face?",a="The Barrens faces continual aggression from native predators, roaming centaur, quilboar warbands, and Alliance encroachment. Its outposts need capable defenders to hold their ground.",al={"what dangers in barrens","barrens threats"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Your journey brings you to the Horde's rugged frontier in Kalimdor, where you are called to prove yourself in its service.",["race:Skyborne"]="You have arrived in Azeroth from the elemental plane. Mortal conflicts may seem small beside what you have known, but the Horde's dangers are real, and you are urged to prove your mettle in its service."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","elemental plane","horde","journey to the crossroads","the barrens","thork"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","npc:thork","zone:barrens","topic:horde","topic:elemental-plane"},m={id=98024},src={"In-game quest text: Journey to the Crossroads"},fv=true}
E["quest:98025"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Jai'vhanel",z="general",s="Near Auberdine, Jai'vhanel ambushes travelers on the coastal roads. The Auberdine Village Council has set a bounty for her death near the ruins of Ameth'Aran, with proof to be brought to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",h="Near Auberdine, Jai'vhanel ambushes travelers on the coastal roads.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Road",b="On Darkshore's coastal roads near Auberdine, travelers face danger from a mad owl. Jai'vhanel, known locally as Swordfeather, has turned on those who pass. She ambushes travelers and couriers near the settlement, leaving the roads unsafe.",sp=0},{t="The Council's Bounty",b="The Auberdine Village Council offers a bounty to make the roads safer. Jai'vhanel hunts north of the ruins of Ameth'Aran, along the mountain base. Bring one of her black feathers to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine as proof of the kill and to claim the reward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jai'vhanel?",a="Jai'vhanel, called Swordfeather, is a large owl with black feathers. Native to Darkshore's forests, she has grown hostile to travelers through madness.",al={"who is jaivhanel","what is jaivhanel","who is swordfeather"}},{q="Why is there a bounty on Jai'vhanel?",a="The Auberdine Village Council posted a bounty because Jai'vhanel has gone mad and attacks travelers on the main road near Auberdine, putting them in danger.",al={"why kill jaivhanel","why is there a bounty on jaivhanel","why is the owl attacked"}},{q="Where can Jai'vhanel be found?",a="Jai'vhanel prowls north of the ruins of Ameth'Aran in Darkshore, near the base of the eastern mountains.",al={"where is jaivhanel","jaivhanel location","where to find swordfeather"}},{q="Who posted the bounty on Jai'vhanel?",a="The Auberdine Village Council posted the bounty. It oversees Auberdine's safety and welfare, along with that of the surrounding roads.",al={"who posted the bounty","who wants jaivhanel dead"}},{q="Who collects the reward for Jai'vhanel?",a="Bring one of Jai'vhanel's black feathers to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine as proof of the kill.",al={"who takes proof of death","where to turn in jaivhanel feather","glynda nalshea bounty"}},{q="What proof is needed to claim the bounty?",a="One of Jai'vhanel's black feathers proves she has been slain.",al={"what is proof of death for jaivhanel","what item proves jaivhanel died"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you help the Auberdine Village Council and night elf sentinels guard Darkshore's coastal roads from mad predators.",["class:Druid"]="As a night elf druid, you watch Darkshore's wildlife closely. Jai'vhanel's sudden madness and aggression alarm anyone who cares for the forests.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know Swordfeather as a fierce black owl near Darkshore's mountains. Her hunting has turned dangerously erratic."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","black owl","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","jai'vhanel","swordfeather","wanted: jai'vhanel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:ameth-aran"},m={id=98025},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Jai'vhanel"},fv=true}
E["quest:98027"] = {t="quest",n="Gleaming Crescent Necklace",z="general",s="A gleaming crescent necklace bears an inscription linking it to Maliynn in Astranaar. You can return the keepsake to its owner.",h="A gleaming crescent necklace bears an inscription linking it to Maliynn in Astranaar.",sec={{t="The Inscription",b="You examine a silver necklace shaped like a crescent moon. Its form recalls other night elf symbols you have seen, and an inscription on its reverse reads, “Alor'lormah, Maliynn.” The name points to Maliynn in Astranaar, where the necklace may find its owner.",sp=0},{t="Maliynn's Keepsake",b="Maliynn in Astranaar recognizes the necklace as hers. She lost it while carrying supplies to an outpost, then searched along the road before giving up. Her late parents gave it to her, and its return means much to her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who does the necklace belong to?",a="The inscription bears Maliynn's name, and she recognizes the necklace as hers in Astranaar.",al={"who owns it","necklace owner","Maliynn necklace"}},{q="What does the necklace look like?",a="It is a silver necklace shaped like a small crescent moon.",al={"crescent necklace","what shape is it","silver necklace"}},{q="What is written on the necklace?",a="The inscription reads “Alor'lormah, Maliynn.”",al={"necklace inscription","what does it say","Alor'lormah"}},{q="Where can I bring the necklace?",a="Bring the Crescent Necklace to Maliynn in Astranaar.",al={"where to take it","Maliynn location","Astranaar necklace"}},{q="Why does the necklace matter to Maliynn?",a="It was a gift from her late parents.",al={"why is it important","Maliynn keepsake","parents gift"}},{q="How did Maliynn lose it?",a="Maliynn lost it while delivering supplies to one of her outposts. She searched along the road before giving up.",al={"how necklace lost","where did she lose it","lost necklace"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may recognize the crescent shape among the symbols you have seen."},kw={"alor'lormah","astranaar","crescent necklace","gleaming crescent necklace","maliynn","night elf symbol","silver necklace"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","topic:night-elf"},m={id=98027},src={"In-game quest text: Gleaming Crescent Necklace"},fv=true}
E["quest:98028"] = {t="quest",n="Baron Marinous",z="general",s="Onu seeks to learn what happened to a water globe left by an elemental guardian. You bring it to him at the Grove of the Ancients, where he recognizes a troubling sign.",h="Onu seeks to learn what happened to a water globe left by an elemental guardian.",sec={{t="Onu's Counsel",b="Onu at the Grove of the Ancients needs the Clouded Water Globe. The elemental guardian is defeated, but the globe remains clouded and whatever happened to the guardian and the ruins it guarded may still be active. You bring it to Onu, the one most likely to know more.",sp=0},{t="Onu's Concern",b="At the Grove of the Ancients, Onu reacts with surprise to the globe and wonders whether there are stairs descending in Mathystra. He says he must confer with the others. He is glad you uncovered this before the naga or their cult allies, and notes that defeating the elemental guardian was no small feat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is the Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.",al={"onu","onu lore","ancient of lore"}},{q="What is the Clouded Water Globe?",a="It is all that remains of a powerful elemental, a globe of water clouded by an unknown substance.",al={"clouded globe","water globe","globe from elemental"}},{q="Why does the globe look clouded?",a="An unknown substance clouds the globe and seems to prevent anyone from seeing inside.",al={"what's in the globe","clouded water","why can't see inside"}},{q="Where do I take the globe?",a="Bring the Clouded Water Globe to Onu at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.",al={"where is onu","grove location","take globe"}},{q="What happened to the elemental guardian?",a="The elemental guardian has been defeated, and the globe is all that remains of it.",al={"elemental fate","guardian dead","what happened to guardian"}},{q="What does Onu say about the naga?",a="Onu says it is good the globe was uncovered before the naga or their cult allies.",al={"naga and globe","cult allies","why before naga"}}},kw={"baron marinous","clouded water globe","darkshore","elemental guardian","grove of the ancients","mathystra","naga","onu"},rel={"quest:952","zone:darkshore","topic:naga"},m={id=98028},src={"In-game quest text: Baron Marinous"},fv=true}
E["quest:98042"] = {t="quest",n="It's All Fun and Games Until...",z="general",s="Thundris hears a troubled report and examines the discovery brought before him. Its mark sends the relic to Darnassus for study.",h="Thundris hears a troubled report and examines the discovery brought before him.",sec={{t="A Troubling Report",b="You bring a troubling discovery to Thundris and seek his counsel. He listens to your report and examines what you have brought. Then he falls quiet, for the signs before him are too dark to dismiss.",sp=0},{t="The Mark of Ancient Evil",b="Thundris sees the mark of an ancient evil on the discovery. He knows the danger reaches beyond a local mishap, so he sends the relic at once to Darnassus. The capital's scholars and priests will study it and keep it contained.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is involved in completing this quest?",a="Thundris hears the adventurer's troubling report and examines the item or evidence presented. He prepares it for transport.",al={"who gives its all fun and games until","thundris quest","who turns in its all fun and games until"}},{q="Why is the object being sent to Darnassus?",a="Thundris sees the mark of an ancient evil and says the finding will be taken to Darnassus at once for study.",al={"why send to darnassus","darnassus study","ancient evil darnassus"}},{q="What is the ancient evil referenced by Thundris?",a="Thundris names the mark of an ancient evil, but gives no details about its origins before closer study in the night elven capital.",al={"what is the ancient evil","mark of ancient evil meaning"}},{q="What does 'Ande'thoras-ethil' mean?",a="“Ande'thoras-ethil” is a Darnassian phrase Thundris speaks as he finishes talking with you, after saying the find will be taken to Darnassus.",al={"meaning of ande'thoras-ethil","andethoras ethil night elf phrase","darnassian farewell thundris"}},{q="What happens after completing the quest?",a="After recognizing the mark of ancient corruption, Thundris prepares the relic for immediate transport to Darnassus, where scholars can examine it.",al={"what happens after its all fun and games until","next quest after fun and games","to darnassus followup"}},{q="Which faction handles this investigation?",a="Darnassian leadership and night elf figures like Thundris handle the matter, bringing threats before the night elven authorities.",al={"is its all fun and games alliance only","who can do its all fun and games until"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Darnassus respond at once to a discovery marked by ancient corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can bring troubling discoveries to night elf authorities so Darnassian scholars can examine and contain dangerous relics."},kw={"ancient evil","ande'thoras-ethil","darnassus","mark of an ancient evil","night elf","thundris"},rel={"zone:darnassus"},m={id=98042},src={"In-game quest text: It's All Fun and Games Until..."},fv=true}
E["quest:98046"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="general",s="In Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm turns from a failed rite and sends its vessel away. He asks you to carry it to Priestess Lariia at the Temple of the Moon for disposal.",h="In Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm turns from a failed rite and sends its vessel away.",sec={{t="Fandral's Frustration",b="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm guides the night elves while Malfurion Stormrage is absent. Seeking answers, he performs an incantation with sacred water held in a phial. The rite brings no answer, and Fandral's temper rises. Certain the water is useless, he dismisses you with sharp words and sends you south to the Temple of the Moon, where the priestesses can dispose of the vessel.",sp=0},{t="The Remaining Drops",b="Priestess Lariia asks you to make allowance for Fandral's harsh manner and the burden he bears. As she examines the phial, she finds several drops of water still inside. Perhaps Fandral's magic did not fail; perhaps the vessel was never emptied.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Crown of the Earth?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm gives you the task in Darnassus. With Malfurion Stormrage absent, Fandral oversees the Cenarion Circle. After an incantation with sacred water brings no answers, he sends you away in frustration.",al={"who starts crown of the earth","crown of the earth quest giver","fandral quest"}},{q="Where do you take the Drained Vessel?",a="You take the Drained Vessel to Priestess Lariia at the Temple of the Moon in southern Darnassus. Fandral expects the priestesses of Elune to dispose of the vessel, which he believes has no use left.",al={"where to take drained vessel","drained vessel turn in","where is lariia"}},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so frustrated?",a="Fandral Staghelm bears the burden of guiding the night elves and leading the Cenarion Circle while Malfurion Stormrage is away. When his incantation yields nothing, frustration and pride make him lash out and dismiss you before examining the failure more closely.",al={"why is fandral mad","fandral attitude","why is fandral impatient"}},{q="Why did Fandral's incantation fail?",a="Fandral believes the water had no useful power, but Priestess Lariia finds several drops still clinging inside the vessel. The rite may have failed because the vessel was not fully emptied.",al={"why did the incantation fail","did fandral ritual work","failed incantation"}},{q="Where is Malfurion during this quest?",a="Malfurion Stormrage is absent from Darnassus. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm guides the night elves and leads the Cenarion Circle in his absence, a heavy burden that feeds Fandral's temper and impatience with setbacks.",al={"where is malfurion","why is malfurion absent","malfurion status"}},{q="Who is Priestess Lariia?",a="Priestess Lariia serves Elune at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She receives the vessel with compassion for Fandral's burdens and notices that water remains inside.",al={"who is lariia","priestess lariia lore","lariia temple of the moon"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Fandral addresses you as a fellow druid. He meets the ritual's failure with curt impatience, then dismisses you.",["race:NightElf"]="In Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm's prickly authority meets the patient devotion of the Sisterhood of Elune at the Temple of the Moon.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darnassus is the Alliance's chief city on Kalimdor. With Malfurion Stormrage absent, quiet tensions mark the city's leadership."},kw={"cenarion circle","crown of the earth","darnassus","drained vessel","elune","fandral staghelm","lariia","malfurion","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:fandral-staghelm","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:druid","quest:2519"},m={id=98046},src={"In-game quest text: Crown of the Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:98065"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="general",s="Within Darnassus, purified Moonwell Remnants are brought to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. The meeting takes place in the Temple of the Moon, where the waters’ sacred meaning meets the strain between Tyrande and Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",h="Within Darnassus, purified Moonwell Remnants are brought to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",sec={{t="Audience with the High Priestess",b="Once the sacred Moonwell Remnants are collected, you pour the blessed water into a ceremonial vessel and carry it to Tyrande Whisperwind. The High Priestess of Elune keeps audience high within the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She watches over the city and offers her goddess’s light to all who enter. To place sacred water in her care is an honor and an act of devotion to Elune.",sp=0},{t="Tensions in Leadership",b="Tyrande gives deep thanks for saving the blessed water. Then her thoughts turn to the strains gripping Darnassus. With Malfurion Stormrage absent, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm has taken charge of druidic affairs. Yet Tyrande makes clear that governing the kaldorei is her burden alone. She urges respect for Staghelm’s station, but the exchange shows sharp friction between the Sisterhood of Elune and the Cenarion Circle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Crown of the Earth?",a="In Darnassus, you carry Moonwell Remnants in a ceremonial vessel to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind inside the Temple of the Moon. The meeting brings you before the night elves’ supreme leader.",al={"what is crown of the earth","crown of the earth quest","quest crown of the earth"}},{q="Who is Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="Tyrande Whisperwind is the High Priestess of Elune and the night elves’ political leader. From the upper tier of the Temple of the Moon, she oversees Darnassus and bears the burden of guiding her people through troubled times.",al={"who is tyrande whisperwind","where is tyrande","high priestess tyrande"}},{q="Why are the Moonwell Remnants brought to Tyrande?",a="The Moonwell Remnants are sacred water blessed by Elune. You place them in a ceremonial vessel and bring them to Tyrande, who receives and safeguards them on the goddess’s behalf.",al={"why bring moonwell remnants to tyrande","what are moonwell remnants","sacred water darnassus"}},{q="What is the dispute between Tyrande and Fandral Staghelm?",a="With Malfurion Stormrage absent, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids. Tyrande maintains that governing Darnassus and leading the kaldorei remain her responsibility alone, and will not let druidic authority eclipse Elune’s priesthood.",al={"tyrande fandral tension","why does tyrande dislike staghelm","fandral vs tyrande"}},{q="Where is Malfurion during this quest?",a="Malfurion Stormrage is absent from Darnassus, leaving a leadership vacuum among the druids. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm has stepped in to fill it, heightening the political strain with Tyrande.",al={"where is malfurion","what happened to malfurion","malfurion absence"}},{q="Where is the Temple of the Moon?",a="The Temple of the Moon stands in the heart of Darnassus. It is the Sisterhood of Elune’s chief sanctuary, and Tyrande holds audience on the upper level above the main sanctuary floor.",al={"temple of the moon location","where is temple of the moon","where to find tyrande"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you carry sacred moonwell water into a meeting that shows the kaldorei’s divided leadership between Tyrande’s priesthood and Fandral’s druids.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you serve High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, whose clergy helps guide and govern night elf society.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hear Tyrande’s sharp words about Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, which show the growing friction within the Cenarion Circle in Malfurion’s absence.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally, you meet the leader of Darnassus and glimpse the political strains within one of the Alliance’s key capitals."},kw={"crown of the earth","darnassus","elune","fandral staghelm","malfurion","moonwell remnants","temple of the moon","tyrande whisperwind"},rel={"npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","topic:druid","quest:2519"},m={id=98065},src={"In-game quest text: Crown of the Earth"},fv=true}
E["quest:98067"] = {t="quest",n="Eyes of the Sentinels",z="general",s="In Darnassus, Sentinel Dalia Sunblade sets owls to watch as unease grows across Teldrassil. Their posts guard the city and leave the Sentinels time to pray to Elune.",h="In Darnassus, Sentinel Dalia Sunblade sets owls to watch as unease grows across Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Devotion and Defense",b="At the Temple of the Moon, Sentinel Dalia Sunblade watches over Darnassus. General Shandris Feathermoon has decreed that every warrior must balance skill in battle with devotion to Elune. So Dalia arranges for sentinel owls to watch key places in the city. Their daily duties leave the Sentinels time for prayer and reflection before the Moon Goddess, while Darnassus remains guarded.",sp=0},{t="Watch Over Darnassus",b="Unease spreads across Teldrassil, and the Sentinels grow more watchful. Sentinel owls take posts at the northern entrance to the depths beneath Cenarion Hold, the bank in the town square, the inn in Craftsman's Terrace, and the main city gates. Local city guards help place them. From these posts, the owls watch over those who walk the streets of the Great Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Eyes of the Sentinels?",a="Sentinel Dalia Sunblade directs the placing of sentinel owls at key points around Darnassus. Their watch helps the Sentinels guard the city against looming threats.",al={"eyes of the sentinels quest","what is eyes of the sentinels","eyes of the sentinels overview"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Dalia Sunblade?",a="Sentinel Dalia Sunblade is a kaldorei guardian at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She oversees local defenses and sees that watchful owls guard key thoroughfares.",al={"who is dalia sunblade","dalia sunblade lore","sentinel dalia sunblade"}},{q="Why are Sentinel Owls being placed around Darnassus?",a="The sentinel owls watch over Darnassus as aerial lookouts and divine scouts granted by Elune. They survey key gathering places and transit chokepoints.",al={"why place sentinel owls","what do sentinel owls do","sentinel owl purpose"}},{q="Where are the Sentinel Owls placed?",a="The sentinel owls are posted at the northern entrance to the depths beneath Cenarion Hold, the Darnassus Bank in the town center, the inn at Craftsman's Terrace, and the city gates.",al={"owl placement spots","where do owls go","eyes of the sentinels locations"}},{q="Why are the Sentinels on high alert in Teldrassil?",a="Sentinel Dalia Sunblade says something feels amiss across Teldrassil, the World Tree. So the Sentinels increase their watch and stay ready for unseen dangers.",al={"why are sentinels worried","what is wrong with teldrassil","teldrassil amiss"}},{q="What role does General Feathermoon have in the Sentinels' daily duties?",a="General Shandris Feathermoon commands the Sentinels and sees that her huntresses balance martial duties with daily devotion and prayer to Elune.",al={"general feathermoon role","shandris feathermoon sentinels","feathermoon prayer rule"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Sentinels are the night elves' traditional standing army and guardians. They join martial skill with Elune's blessings and watchful eyes.",["faction:Alliance"]="Guarding Darnassus protects the night elves' capital and strengthens the Alliance's main stronghold in northern Kalimdor.",["class:Hunter"]="Scout owls reflect the night elves' traditional skill at reconnaissance. Trained beasts and celestial avian watchers extend a huntress's senses.",["class:Priest"]="Weapons alone cannot protect the kaldorei. Regular prayer and Elune's spiritual gifts are vital to the Sentinels' guardianship."},kw={"cenarion hold","craftsman terrace","dalia sunblade","darnassus","elune","eyes of the sentinels","feathermoon","sentinel owls","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:sentinels","topic:elune","quest:940","subzone:cenarion-hold"},m={id=98067},src={"In-game quest text: Eyes of the Sentinels"},fv=true}
E["quest:98069"] = {t="quest",n="Stolen Freewind Supplies",z="general",s="At Freewind Post, Jandia needs the harpies' stolen supplies back. The post has enough for now, but it will soon run short without another shipment.",h="At Freewind Post, Jandia needs the harpies' stolen supplies back.",sec={{t="The Missing Shipment",b="The harpies struck the last caravan bound for Freewind Post. Jandia says the post can manage for now, though its stores will not last without more supplies. The harpies' lair lies west of the post, along the cliff base and in a cave above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who needs the supplies?",a="Jandia in Freewind Post needs the stolen supplies recovered.",al={"who asked for supplies","Jandia supplies","freewind supplies"}},{q="Who took the caravan's supplies?",a="Harpies attacked the last caravan carrying supplies to Freewind Post.",al={"who stole them","harpy supplies","harpies stole what"}},{q="Where is the harpy lair?",a="The harpies' lair lies west of Freewind Post, along the cliff base and in a cave above.",al={"where are harpies","harpy cave","harpies west"}},{q="Why does Jandia need them back?",a="Freewind Post has enough supplies for now, but it will soon run short without another shipment.",al={"why recover supplies","freewind running short","why supplies matter"}},{q="What does Jandia ask you to recover?",a="Jandia asks you to recover eight stolen supplies for Freewind Post.",al={"how many supplies","stolen goods","what do i bring"}}},kw={"caravan","cave","cliff","freewind post","harpies","jandia","stolen freewind supplies","supplies"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","topic:harpy"},m={id=98069},src={"In-game quest text: Stolen Freewind Supplies"},fv=true}
E["quest:98070"] = {t="quest",n="Stop the Screeching",z="general",s="In Screeching Canyon, harpies ambush supply caravans bound for Freewind Post. Their attacks may keep those caravans from traveling there.",h="In Screeching Canyon, harpies ambush supply caravans bound for Freewind Post.",sec={{t="Caravans at Risk",b="A supplier fears the harpy attacks will stop caravans from traveling to Freewind Post. You are asked to slay Screeching Harpies, Screeching Roguefeather Harpies, and Screeching Windcallers. Until then, caravans that brave the canyon remain in danger.",sp=0},{t="Word to Suppliers",b="After the harpies are dealt with, the supplier will notify those who provide goods to Freewind Post. Then the caravans will face one less threat on their journeys.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the caravans being attacked?",a="Harpies in Screeching Canyon ambushed the last few supply caravans that traveled through.",al={"harpies attacking caravans","why harpies attack","caravan trouble"}},{q="What is at risk if the attacks continue?",a="The supplier fears no caravans will dare travel to Freewind Post if the attacks continue.",al={"why protect caravans","freewind post supplies","caravans stop"}},{q="Which harpies are involved?",a="The harpies are Screeching Harpies, Screeching Roguefeather Harpies, and Screeching Windcallers.",al={"harpy types","screeching harpies","roguefeather windcaller"}},{q="Where are the harpies?",a="The harpies live in Screeching Canyon.",al={"harpy location","screeching canyon harpies","where is screeching canyon"}}},kw={"caravan","freewind post","harpy","roguefeather","screeching canyon","screeching harpy","stop the screeching","supplies","windcaller"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","topic:harpy"},m={id=98070},src={"In-game quest text: Stop the Screeching"},fv=true}
E["quest:98072"] = {t="quest",n="Crocs of the Sky",z="general",s="James asks if you have the scales, then praises your skill. He offers you work if you leave adventuring behind.",h="James asks if you have the scales, then praises your skill.",sec={{t="James's Offer",b="James calls you a natural talent and invites you back if you take a break from adventuring. He jokes that you may be older by then.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking about the scales?",a="James asks whether you have the scales.",al={"who wants the scales","scales for james"}},{q="What does James think of me?",a="James thinks you are a natural talent.",al={"does james like me","james opinion"}},{q="What does James offer?",a="James offers you work if you take a break from adventuring.",al={"james job","work offer"}}},kw={"adventuring","crocs of the sky","james","scales","work"},m={id=98072},src={"In-game quest text: Crocs of the Sky"},fv=true}
E["quest:98094"] = {t="quest",n="Scout Support",z="general",s="South of Tarren Mill, you carry new orders from High Executor Darthalia to Deathstalker Masoj. The Forsaken press on with their plan to take control of these lands.",h="South of Tarren Mill, you carry new orders from High Executor Darthalia to Deathstalker Masoj.",sec={{t="Orders for Masoj",b="High Executor Darthalia trusts you with word for the forward spies. She gives you updated orders for Deathstalker Masoj, who waits on high ground north of Nethander Stead and outside Dun Garok. The Forsaken plan to take control of these lands continues, and Masoj is waiting for your delivery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gave me the orders?",a="High Executor Darthalia gave you updated orders for Deathstalker Masoj.",al={"who sent me","Darthalia orders","giver"}},{q="Who is Deathstalker Masoj?",a="Deathstalker Masoj is a forward spy posted outside Dun Garok, north of Nethander Stead.",al={"Masoj who","who's Masoj","Masoj"}},{q="Where do I find Masoj?",a="Masoj waits south of Tarren Mill, on high ground north of Nethander Stead and outside Dun Garok.",al={"Masoj location","where is Masoj","south of Tarren Mill"}},{q="What am I carrying to Masoj?",a="You carry updated orders for Deathstalker Masoj.",al={"what to deliver","orders for Masoj","the package"}},{q="Why am I delivering orders?",a="Your delivery supports the Forsaken plan to take control of these lands.",al={"why Masoj","what is the plan","Forsaken plan"}}},kw={"deathstalker masoj","dun garok","forsaken","forward spies","high executor darthalia","nethander stead","scout support","tarren mill","updated orders"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:nethander-stead","subzone:dun-garok"},m={id=98094},src={"In-game quest text: Scout Support"},fv=true}
E["quest:98095"] = {t="quest",n="Valuable Vantages",z="general",s="Around Hillsbrad Foothills, Deathstalker Masoj needs you to restore three signaling marks. Bat riders use those points to guide strategic troops to their drop-off sites.",h="Around Hillsbrad Foothills, Deathstalker Masoj needs you to restore three signaling marks.",sec={{t="Three Peaks",b="You carry Apothecary Vials to three high places: the hills beside Dun Garok, the plateau above Dunholde Keep, and the Headland ridge above Hillsbrad. Their vapors draw bats back to the marks. Then Masoj's high command can guide its troops through the foothills.",sp=0},{t="Masoj's Orders",b="Masoj asks you to search for crushed, empty vials and renew the marks at all three places. He says this work serves plans advancing under the Deathstalkers' banner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking me to place the vials?",a="Deathstalker Masoj asks you to restore the signaling marks around Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who gave valuable vantages","masoj vials","who is Masoj"}},{q="Why are the signaling marks needed?",a="Bat riders use the signaling points to guide strategic troops to drop-off sites.",al={"why bats need marks","bat signals","what are the beacons for"}},{q="Where do I place the vials?",a="Place the vials on the hills beside Dun Garok, the plateau above Dunholde Keep, and the Headland ridge above Hillsbrad.",al={"vial locations","where are the peaks","three vial spots"}},{q="What do the vial vapors do?",a="The vapors draw bats back to the desired drop-off points.",al={"what do vials do","bat scent","vial purpose"}}},kw={"apothecary vials","bat riders","deathstalker masoj","dun garok","dunholde keep","headland","hillsbrad foothills","signaling beacons","valuable vantages"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:dun-garok"},m={id=98095},src={"In-game quest text: Valuable Vantages"},fv=true}
E["quest:98155"] = {t="quest",n="Pristine Pesterhide Pelts",z="general",s="In Thousand Needles, Kristy Grant hopes to send Pesterhide pelts to her sisters in Stormwind. They can make the hides into garments and goods, while Kristy relies on travelers to gather them.",h="In Thousand Needles, Kristy Grant hopes to send Pesterhide pelts to her sisters in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Sisterly Ambition",b="As Kristy Grant crosses the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, the Pesterhide hyenas catch her eye. Their pelts are little known in the Eastern Kingdoms, and she hopes to send some home to her sisters in Stormwind. Skilled hands in her family can turn the hides into fine garments and goods.",sp=0},{t="Hunters of the Salt Flats and Canyons",b="Kristy Grant knows craft and trade, but she has no combat experience. Pesterhide hyenas roam beneath the mesas in vicious packs, so gathering their hides alone is dangerous. She relies on seasoned travelers to bring her five undamaged pelts for her sisters to work with back home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kristy Grant?",a="Kristy Grant is a traveler from Stormwind journeying through Kalimdor. She has no fighting experience, but a keen eye for valuable materials, and asks capable travelers to gather goods such as hyena pelts for her.",al={"kristy grant lore","who gives pristine pesterhide pelts","who is kristy grant"}},{q="What are Pesterhide hyenas?",a="Pesterhide hyenas are wild predators native to Thousand Needles. They hunt and scavenge in packs across the canyon floor and dusty expanses, and their striking coats catch the eye of travelers who work with hides and fur.",al={"pesterhide hyena","thousand needles hyenas","what are pesterhides"}},{q="Why does Kristy Grant want the pelts?",a="Kristy Grant wants pristine Pesterhide hyena pelts to send across the sea to her sisters in Stormwind. She admires their color and trusts her sisters to make the furs into fine goods.",al={"why collect pesterhide pelts","pesterhide pelt purpose","what does kristy do with the pelts"}},{q="Where do the pelts end up?",a="The pelts are bound for Stormwind in the Eastern Kingdoms. Kristy plans to send them across the Great Sea to her sisters, who can work with materials rarely found in Elwynn or Redridge.",al={"where are the pelts sent","pelts stormwind","who gets the hyena pelts"}},{q="Why can't Kristy hunt the hyenas herself?",a="Kristy Grant has no fighting experience, and the wild beasts of Thousand Needles are dangerous. She relies on skilled travelers to hunt the hyenas rather than risk injury or death among their packs.",al={"why can't kristy fight","kristy grant combat","why does kristy need help"}},{q="What makes these pelts pristine?",a="The pelts must be undamaged so Kristy's sisters can use their color and texture in fine garments. Careful hunting preserves the best hides.",al={"pristine pelts meaning","why pristine hides","pristine pesterhide pelt quality"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Kristy's effort to supply her artisan family in Stormwind shows Alliance subjects traveling deep into Kalimdor for rare materials.",["race:Human"]="Kristy Grant shows the enterprising spirit of Stormwind humans who cross the sea while keeping close ties with kin at home.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Crafters who work with cloth and decorative furs can appreciate Kristy's sisters' plan to turn wild Kalimdor hides into fine garments."},kw={"fur","hunting","hyena","kristy grant","pelts","pesterhide","stormwind","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={id=98155},src={"In-game quest text: Pristine Pesterhide Pelts"},fv=true}
E["quest:98189"] = {t="quest",n="Return the Statuette",z="general",s="A statuette's delivery to Menethil Harbor was interrupted by tragedy. You are asked to bring it to Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Keep.",h="A statuette's delivery to Menethil Harbor was interrupted by tragedy.",sec={{t="An Unfinished Delivery",b="The statuette was meant for Menethil Harbor, where Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Keep was expected to sign for it. Now you are asked to finish the delivery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is meant to receive the statuette?",a="Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Keep is expected to sign for the Menethil Statuette.",al={"who gets the statuette","statuette recipient","captain stoutfist delivery"}},{q="Where was the statuette supposed to go?",a="The statuette was meant to be delivered to Menethil Harbor.",al={"where does it go","statuette destination","menethil statuette"}},{q="Who was carrying it before?",a="The Blind Princess was supposed to deliver the statuette before tragedy struck.",al={"who had the statuette","blind princess statuette","statuette delivery"}},{q="What is being asked of me?",a="You are asked to bring the Menethil Statuette to Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Keep.",al={"what do i do","return statuette","statuette quest"}}},kw={"blind princess","captain stoutfist","menethil harbor","menethil keep","menethil statuette","statuette"},rel={"item:menethil-statuette","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={id=98189},src={"In-game quest text: Return the Statuette"},fv=true}
E["quest:98223"] = {t="quest",n="Old Habits",z="general",s="A burned Dragonmaw book reaches Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor. Its damaged pages mention dragon-binding rituals and the Shadow Council.",h="A burned Dragonmaw book reaches Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Damaged Book",b="You bring Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor a badly burned book that may have survived the dragonfire that ravaged the Dragonmaw clan. Its few legible pages describe rituals involving the Demon Soul, which the clan used to control dragons. The book is incomplete, though Nek’rosh seems to have tried to save it with pages of animal hide and fresh ink naming the Shadow Council.",sp=0},{t="Stoutfist’s Answer",b="Captain Stoutfist says the book should be destroyed, for he will not risk the orcs using it. He fears dragonriders at Menethil Harbor, and the mention of the Shadow Council troubles him. He plans to send word to his superiors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is in the tattered spellbook?",a="Its surviving pages describe rituals involving the Demon Soul, which the Dragonmaw clan used to control dragons. Fresh ink also names the Shadow Council.",al={"spellbook contents","what book","burned book"}},{q="Who tried to save the book?",a="Nek’rosh seems to have tried to salvage the book by inserting pages made of animal hide.",al={"who saved it","Nek'rosh book","Nekrosh"}},{q="Who wants the book brought to them?",a="Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor wants to hear about the book.",al={"where take spellbook","Stoutfist book","captain wants what"}},{q="Why is the book hard to read?",a="The book is badly burned, and little of it remains legible.",al={"why burned book","book damaged","can't read spellbook"}}},kw={"captain stoutfist","demon soul","dragonmaw clan","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","old habits","shadow council","tattered spellbook"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","npc:captain-stoutfist","topic:dragonmaw-clan","topic:shadow-council"},m={id=98223},src={"In-game quest text: Old Habits"},fv=true}
E["quest:98230"] = {t="quest",n="This Land Was Their Land",z="general",s="Howin Kindfeather has returned to the Wetlands, where the Wildhammers once founded Grim Batol. Find him east of Menethil Harbor; he welcomes a helping hand.",h="Howin Kindfeather has returned to the Wetlands, where the Wildhammers once founded Grim Batol.",sec={{t="The Road East",b="The Wildhammer dwarf Howin Kindfeather is waiting for help east of Menethil Harbor, along the road. You seek him out as one of the first Wildhammers to return in ages. He keeps apart from town, and help is hard to come by.",sp=0},{t="A Wildhammer Home",b="After the War of the Three Hammers, the Wildhammers settled in the Wetlands and founded Grim Batol. Gryphons once flew above the mountain fortress and dived into the wetlands for fish. That life did not last long; now Howin has returned, far from town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Howin Kindfeather?",a="Howin Kindfeather is a Wildhammer dwarf and one of the first of his people to return in ages.",al={"howin","who is howin","kindfeather"}},{q="Where can I find Howin?",a="Howin is east of Menethil Harbor, along the road, far outside town.",al={"where howin","find kindfeather","howin location"}},{q="Why is Howin out here?",a="Howin is one of the first Wildhammers to return in ages, and he keeps to himself outside town.",al={"why is howin here","howin back","wildhammer return"}},{q="What was Grim Batol?",a="The Wildhammers founded Grim Batol in the Wetlands after the War of the Three Hammers.",al={"grim batol history","wildhammer fortress","what is grim batol"}},{q="What happened to the Wildhammers' home?",a="Grim Batol was once a wondrous place, where gryphons flew over the wetlands to catch fish, but that life did not last long.",al={"wildhammer home","what happened grim batol","gryphons wetlands"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you meet Howin Kindfeather, a Wildhammer returning to the Wetlands after the War of the Three Hammers."},kw={"grim batol","gryphons","howin kindfeather","menethil harbor","this land was their land","war of the three hammers","wetlands","wildhammer"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={id=98230},src={"In-game quest text: This Land Was Their Land"},fv=true}
E["quest:98248"] = {t="quest",n="Shipping Label",z="general",s="A torn manifest points couriers toward Durotar Supply and Logistics in the Barrens. The company depends on travelers to recover lost crates and return paperwork to its post west of the Crossroads, keeping supplies and trade moving across central Kalimdor.",h="A torn manifest points couriers toward Durotar Supply and Logistics in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Wayward Manifest",b="A torn manifest is fixed to a freshly restocked cargo crate. Its recipient's name has worn away, but the heading names Durotar Supply and Logistics, a freight company in Horde territory. Beside the writing, a rough map points couriers toward the company's staging grounds in the central plains.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Commerce",b="The notice welcomes travelers bringing stray containers, damaged goods, or proof of salvage to the trade outpost west of the Crossroads. Durotar Supply and Logistics depends on independent haulers to recover scattered freight across the Barrens. Those who help keep regional supplies moving receive compensation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shipping Label?",a="The Shipping Label is a torn document fixed to a freshly restocked crate, with return instructions for Durotar Supply and Logistics and directions back to its post near the Crossroads.",al={"what is the shipping label","shipping label quest","torn shipping label"}},{q="Where should the label be delivered?",a="The label directs couriers to the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade hub west of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"where do i take the shipping label","who wants the shipping label","shipping label turn in"}},{q="What is Durotar Supply and Logistics?",a="Durotar Supply and Logistics is a freight company in Horde territory. It handles cargo transport, crate collection, and logistical support across Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"what is durotar supply and logistics","durotar supply outpost"}},{q="Who was the shipment originally intended for?",a="The recipient's name has been torn away, leaving the return instructions and the company's origin information on the crate.",al={"who was the crate meant for","crate recipient"}},{q="Where is the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade outpost located?",a="The label's directions and rough map place the outpost west of the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"where is the trade outpost","durotar supply location crossroads"}},{q="Does Durotar Supply and Logistics compensate travelers for returning crates?",a="Yes. The notice promises compensation for travelers who bring damaged shipments, labels, or empty crates to the hub.",al={"do they pay for returned crates","durotar supply compensation"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may encounter Durotar Supply and Logistics while traveling through the Barrens. Its work helps keep trade and supplies moving between Durotar and central Kalimdor."},kw={"crate","crossroads","durotar supply and logistics","shipping label","the barrens","trade outpost"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","quest:98247"},m={id=98248},src={"In-game quest text: Shipping Label"},fv=true}
E["quest:98251"] = {t="quest",n="Never Coming Back",z="general",s="Va'xug Firefure is trapped in an Ashenvale ravine and asks you to thin the nearby wildlife. The forest's confusing paths and the volatility of Va'xug's spells have left them angry.",h="Va'xug Firefure is trapped in an Ashenvale ravine and asks you to thin the nearby wildlife.",sec={{t="A Forest Snare",b="Va'xug Firefure is gathering herbs in Ashenvale when the forest's paths leave them trapped in a ravine. They say their spells grow volatile when they are angry, and the nearby beasts only worsen their temper. Va'xug asks you to thin the wildlife around them.",sp=0},{t="A Calmer Mood",b="Va'xug Firefure thanks you after the nearby wildlife has been thinned. They say it seems to have helped, though their anger at the forest remains plain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Va'xug Firefure?",a="Va'xug Firefure is gathering herbs in Ashenvale when they become trapped in a ravine.",al={"va'xug","firefure","who is va'xug"}},{q="Why is Va'xug angry?",a="Va'xug is angry because Ashenvale's paths have left them trapped in a ravine, and the nearby beasts grate on them.",al={"why mad","va'xug angry","hates ashenvale"}},{q="What does Va'xug ask me to do?",a="Va'xug asks you to thin the nearby wildlife.",al={"what do i do","thin wildlife","kill beasts"}},{q="Why are Va'xug's spells volatile?",a="Va'xug says their spells grow volatile and behave differently when they are angry.",al={"volatile spells","magic acting weird","spells different"}}},kw={"ashenvale","ashenvale bear","herbs","never coming back","ravine","shadowhorn stag","va'xug firefure","volatile spells"},rel={"quest:1035","zone:ashenvale"},m={id=98251},src={"In-game quest text: Never Coming Back"},fv=true}
E["quest:98284"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a camping item for your profession. Enchanters can learn to make an Enchanted Lute for entertainment on the trail.",h="Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft a camping item for your profession.",sec={{t="A Lute for Camp",b="An enchanter can improve a camp in the wilds, and you are directed to Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village. Once you have shown proficiency in your skill, Nasalanna can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute. The enchanted instrument offers entertainment during downtime before you return to the trail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who teaches me to make an Enchanted Lute?",a="Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village can teach you to craft an Enchanted Lute once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",al={"enchanted lute trainer","who teaches lute","Nasalanna camping"}},{q="What is the Enchanted Lute for?",a="The Enchanted Lute provides entertainment during downtime at a camp.",al={"lute use","camping lute","why enchanted lute"}},{q="Why are enchanters welcome at camps?",a="Enchanters can make things better at camps in the wilds, including an Enchanted Lute for entertainment.",al={"enchanter camping","why enchanters welcome","camping enchanting"}},{q="When can I learn the camping craft?",a="You can learn from Nasalanna Windsinger after you have shown proficiency in your skill.",al={"learn lute when","skill proficiency","camping craft requirement"}}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As an enchanter, you can learn to craft an Enchanted Lute for entertainment at camp."},kw={"camping 101","camping item","enchanted lute","enchanter","enchanting","nasalanna windsinger","shen'dar village"},m={id=98284},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:98285"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Engineering",z="general",s="The Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest teaches you to craft a camping item after you show skill as an engineer. The Reagent Bot is meant for use in a wilderness camp.",h="The Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest teaches you to craft a camping item after you show skill as an...",sec={{t="A Wilderness Camp",b="The Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest asks you to show proficiency in engineering before teaching you a camping craft. Engineers can put their trade to use while alone in the wilds, where helpful constructs can make a camp complete.",sp=0},{t="Setting Up Camp",b="The Strange Hermit teaches you to craft a Reagent Bot. To start a camp, you also need a campfire, which most cooks can teach you to make. The Hermit warns that townsfolk do not care for camps set up in the middle of town.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who teaches me the camping craft?",a="The Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest teaches you the camping craft after you show proficiency in engineering.",al={"who is the hermit","camping teacher","where learn camping engineering"}},{q="What does engineering have to do with camping?",a="The Hermit says engineers can use their trade in the wilds and craft helpful constructs for a camp.",al={"engineering camp item","why engineer camping","camping 101 eng"}},{q="What can I craft?",a="The Hermit teaches you to craft a Reagent Bot.",al={"what is the camping item","reagent bot","camp item engineering"}},{q="Do I need anything else for a camp?",a="You need a campfire to start your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make one.",al={"need campfire","how start camp","camping fire"}},{q="Where should I set up camp?",a="The Hermit says townsfolk do not care for camps set up in the center of town, so head into the wilderness to test your camp.",al={"camp location","where test reagent bot","can i camp in town"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn to craft a Reagent Bot for a wilderness camp after showing the Strange Hermit your proficiency.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can teach others to make the campfire needed to start a camp."},kw={"campfire","camping 101","cooking","engineering","reagent bot","shadowgale forest","strange hermit","wilderness camp"},rel={"quest:93159"},m={id=98285},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Engineering"},fv=true}
E["quest:98286"] = {t="quest",n="Camping 101: Enchanting",z="general",s="At Shen'dar Village, skilled enchanters can learn to make an Enchanted Lute for the campfire. Nasalanna Windsinger teaches them how it entertains and bolsters companions.",h="At Shen'dar Village, skilled enchanters can learn to make an Enchanted Lute for the campfire.",sec={{t="Comforts of the Hearth",b="On the open road, sharpened blades and rations are not enough. Travelers need rest and good spirits to endure long expeditions. Enchanters bring magical comforts to camps across Azeroth, helping weary travelers recover their strength and spirits before they return to perilous trails.",sp=0},{t="The Song of Shen'dar",b="Aspiring enchanters seeking to learn campsite magic travel to Shen'dar Village. There, Nasalanna Windsinger teaches capable spell-weavers to make an Enchanted Lute. First, they must prove their dedication and skill in enchanting. Then Nasalanna shares how to fashion an instrument whose melodies restore spirits beneath the stars.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nasalanna Windsinger?",a="Nasalanna Windsinger lives in Shen'dar Village and teaches skilled enchanters to craft special items for wilderness camps. She teaches those who prove their skill to make the Enchanted Lute.",al={"who teaches enchanted lute","who is nasalanna windsinger","where is nasalanna windsinger"}},{q="Where is Shen'dar Village?",a="Shen'dar Village is where Nasalanna Windsinger lives. Enchanters travel there for instruction in making campsite gear like the Enchanted Lute once they have developed their core skills.",al={"where is shendar village","how to find shendar village"}},{q="What is an Enchanted Lute?",a="Enchanters make the Enchanted Lute as a magical instrument for camps. It entertains companions around the campfire and restores their morale, helping travelers steel themselves for the wilderness ahead.",al={"what does enchanted lute do","why craft enchanted lute","camping lute"}},{q="What are the requirements to learn the recipe?",a="To learn how to make an Enchanted Lute, you must first prove your skill in enchanting to Nasalanna Windsinger. She trusts seasoned practitioners with this camp enchantment.",al={"requirements for camping 101 enchanting","when can i learn enchanted lute"}},{q="Why are enchanters valuable at wilderness campsites?",a="At wilderness camps, enchanters bring magical comforts when ordinary supplies fall short. Their enchantments help travelers recover, stay entertained, and prepare for hazards on the trail.",al={"why do campers want enchanters","enchanters camping benefits"}},{q="Can other professions craft camping items?",a="Yes. Craftsmen and gatherers in different disciplines learn to make tools for campsites. Enchanters learn to make the Enchanted Lute from Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village.",al={"are there other camping items","other profession camp crafts"}}},kw={"campfire","camping","camping 101","enchanted lute","enchanting","lute","nasalanna windsinger","shen'dar village"},m={id=98286},src={"In-game quest text: Camping 101: Enchanting"},fv=true}
E["quest:98293"] = {t="quest",n="Forced Disarmament",z="general",s="At Dragonmaw Retreat, you seize thirty bundles of weapons from hostile orcs for Captain Stoutfist. Their loss keeps the clan from arming more soldiers for future raids. You carry the gear to Captain Stoutfist at Menethil Keep, helping protect the region’s vital harbor.",h="At Dragonmaw Retreat, you seize thirty bundles of weapons from hostile orcs for Captain Stoutfist.",sec={{t="An Armory in the Marshes",b="In the Wetlands, the Dragonmaw clan has stored a troubling number of weapons at Dragonmaw Retreat. Left there, they could arm fresh bands of warriors for raids on nearby settlements. Taking the weapons weakens the orcs’ preparations before their warbands can take the field.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Coastal Port",b="Menethil Harbor links Khaz Modan and Stormwind to the sea, making it a vital port. Nearby military buildup puts it in danger. Captain Stoutfist directs the harbor’s defenses from Menethil Keep and watches hostile clans and beasts draw near. Recovering thirty sets of Dragonmaw armaments deprives the orcs of weapons and gives the dwarven garrison a measure of their readiness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist is a dwarven military officer at Menethil Keep. He is responsible for defending Menethil Harbor and the surrounding Wetlands. With hostile beasts, Dark Iron saboteurs, and the Dragonmaw clan pressing nearby, he directs soldiers and adventurers to suppress threats before the port’s supply lines and harbor facilities are overrun.",al={"stoutfist","who is stoutfist","menethil keep captain"}},{q="Why do the Dragonmaw need to be disarmed?",a="The Dragonmaw clan is gathering weapons at its retreat to arm new fighters. Left unchecked, its warbands could overwhelm local Alliance defenses and endanger Menethil Harbor. Taking thirty bundles hinders their preparations and keeps more orc soldiers from taking the field.",al={"why take dragonmaw weapons","dragonmaw armaments purpose","disarming dragonmaw"}},{q="Where is Dragonmaw Retreat located?",a="Dragonmaw Retreat is a Dragonmaw orc encampment in the Wetlands, eastward toward the mountains beyond Menethil Harbor. The clan stores weapons and gathers forces there, and stages attacks on travelers in the marshes. You venture into the heart of the camp to recover the stockpiled weapons.",al={"dragonmaw retreat location","where is dragonmaw retreat","dragonmaw retreat wetlands"}},{q="What are Dragonmaw Armaments?",a="Dragonmaw Armaments are bundles of martial gear, blades, and equipment the Dragonmaw clan forged or stole for its warriors. They represent the clan’s immediate military strength in the region. Captain Stoutfist asks you to confiscate thirty bundles and bring them to Menethil Keep for evaluation and disposal.",al={"dragonmaw weapons","what are armaments","dragonmaw gear"}},{q="Is the Dragonmaw clan part of the Horde in 25 ADP?",a="No. The Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands is an independent, hostile faction that does not answer to Warchief Thrall. Still loyal to its old ways after the Second War, the clan deeply hates the Alliance and refuses peaceful overtures. Alliance defenders and independent travelers alike treat the Dragonmaw as lethal adversaries.",al={"are dragonmaw horde","dragonmaw clan faction","dragonmaw thrall"}},{q="Why is Menethil Keep concerned with the Dragonmaw?",a="Menethil Keep is the administrative and military fortress that safeguards Menethil Harbor, the Alliance’s principal maritime hub in Khaz Modan. Marsh beasts and aggressive orcs plague the wetlands around the harbor. Captain Stoutfist cannot let a heavily armed camp like Dragonmaw Retreat thrive near the kingdom’s docks and trade routes.",al={"menethil keep dragonmaw threat","why stoutfist cares","menethil harbor defense"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on Menethil Harbor as a vital lifeline across the Great Sea. Disarming hostile clans nearby is an urgent concern.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Ironforge defenders garrison Menethil Keep. They work to secure Khaz Modan’s perimeter from old enemies entrenched in the marshes.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Dragonmaw are a splintered, unrepentant remnant of the Old Horde. Their violent warmongering sets them apart from the new Horde leadership in Kalimdor."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw armaments","dragonmaw clan","dragonmaw retreat","forced disarmament","menethil harbor","menethil keep","wetlands"},rel={"npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:menethil-keep"},m={id=98293},src={"In-game quest text: Forced Disarmament"},fv=true}
E["quest:98297"] = {t="quest",n="Stopping the Cycle",z="general",s="At the Dragonmaw Gates, warlocks are trying to enslave a red dragonspawn. Howin Kindfeather returns from a test flight with troubling news, and the Wildhammer will not let it happen again.",h="At the Dragonmaw Gates, warlocks are trying to enslave a red dragonspawn.",sec={{t="At the Gates",b="Howin Kindfeather asks you to face the subdued dragonspawn at the Dragonmaw Gates. First, kill the warlocks holding it down. That should free it. Then put the dragonspawn out of its misery. Howin expects you to bring friends, for the Wildhammer will not let the Dragonmaw stand in their way.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Howin Kindfeather asks you to stop the Dragonmaw from enslaving a red dragonspawn.",al={"who wants this","howin task"}},{q="What are the Dragonmaw doing?",a="A group of Dragonmaw warlocks is holding down a red dragonspawn and trying to enslave it.",al={"dragonmaw doing what","why dragonspawn subdued"}},{q="Where is the dragonspawn?",a="The subdued dragonspawn is at the Dragonmaw Gates.",al={"dragonspawn location","where subdued dragonspawn"}},{q="What does Howin ask me to do?",a="Howin asks you to kill the warlocks holding the dragonspawn down, then put it out of its misery.",al={"what do i do","stop the cycle"}},{q="Why does Howin say the Wildhammer cannot allow this?",a="Howin says the Dragonmaw are enslaving a red dragonspawn, and insists the Wildhammer will not let them stand in their way.",al={"why not again","wildhammer reason"}}},kw={"dragonmaw","dragonmaw gates","howin kindfeather","red dragonspawn","stopping the cycle","subdued dragonspawn","warlocks","wildhammer"},rel={"subzone:dragonmaw-gates","topic:warlock"},m={id=98297},src={"In-game quest text: Stopping the Cycle"},fv=true}
E["quest:98298"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="general",s="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks the truth behind the worgen near the Greymane Wall. He hopes their remains will prove that Archmage Arugal bound the beasts but did not bring their curse into being.",h="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks the truth behind the worgen near the Greymane Wall.",sec={{t="Exposing the Archmage",b="At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Forsaken mage Dalar Dawnweaver means to strip away the mystery around his rival, Archmage Arugal. Enchanted shackles show that Arugal lacked the power to summon or create the worgen packs terrorizing the region. His magic could only hold the beasts for a time. How the affliction began remains unknown.",sp=0},{t="The Beastly Incursion",b="Dalar sends you south to the Greymane Wall for proof. Feral worgen attack and infect nearby human populations in the wilderness around its imposing fortifications. You can bring Dalar physical evidence by killing the beasts and gathering pieces of their bodies. He needs those samples to study the affliction's nature.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Vindication",b="Dalar Dawnweaver inspects the worgen remains and claims victory over Arugal's reputation. The archmage had no part in the affliction's origin. Yet this finding brings grim news to the Forsaken. If Arugal did not create the curse, then his supposed remedies and countermeasures are worthless. The worgen outbreak remains unexplained.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Arugal's Folly?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver gives and receives the work at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He is a Forsaken mage who studies the arcane.",al={"who gives arugals folly","where do i turn in arugals folly","quest giver arugals folly"}},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver consider Arugal a fraud?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver believes Archmage Arugal lacked the power to create the worgen. He says Arugal could only bind them briefly, not bring them or their affliction into being.",al={"what does dalar think of arugal","did arugal make worgen","arugal fraud"}},{q="Where do you find the worgen bits for Dalar?",a="You find the worgen south of the Sepulcher near the Greymane Wall. They prowl by nearby human settlements, and their remains provide samples for Dalar's study.",al={"where are the worgen bits","greymane wall worgen","where to go arugals folly"}},{q="Does Dalar find a cure for the worgen curse?",a="Dalar discovers no cure for the worgen affliction. Since Arugal did not create it, his remedies and counter-spells cannot help, and the Forsaken must seek a true solution elsewhere.",al={"can worgen curse be cured","does arugal remedy work","is there a cure for worgen"}},{q="How is the worgen affliction spreading near the Greymane Wall?",a="Near the Greymane Wall, the affliction appears to spread to nearby humans through physical encounters and bites. Dalar finds no sign of an overarching ritual or spell cast by Arugal.",al={"how does the curse spread","worgen spreading to humans","who is getting infected"}},{q="What does Dalar conclude after inspecting the worgen bits?",a="The worgen remains convince Dalar Dawnweaver that Arugal's sorcery did not cause their curse. They confirm Arugal's limited magic, while the affliction remains active and unexplained, with no working antidote.",al={"what does dalar learn from the bits","conclusion arugals folly","arugals folly lore reveal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken of the Sepulcher, you help uncover the worgen outbreak's true nature in Silverpine. That knowledge matters as Lordaeron faces feral threats it cannot control.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you help Dalar Dawnweaver protect Silverpine Forest from feral predators and nearby human settlements suffering the affliction.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see the difference between Dalar's binding enchantments and the affliction spreading among the worgen."},kw={"arugal","arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","greymane wall","silverpine forest","the sepulcher","worgen bits","worgen curse"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:sepulcher","topic:worgen","topic:human"},m={id=98298},src={"In-game quest text: Arugal's Folly"},fv=true}
E["quest:98299"] = {t="quest",n="Stop the Spread",z="general",s="At Silverpine Forest's southern border, refugees gather by the Greymane Wall as Arugal's worgen spread. Researchers seek a way to halt the affliction, while orders aim to keep the living refugees from becoming his servants.",h="At Silverpine Forest's southern border, refugees gather by the Greymane Wall as Arugal's worgen spread.",sec={{t="The Silverpine Affliction",b="In Silverpine Forest, worgen spread under renegade Archmage Arugal's hand. Researchers do not yet know exactly how the feral affliction passes from one victim to another. Its danger to the territory is plain. They study the magic while trying to keep Arugal from gathering an overwhelming host of savage followers.",sp=0},{t="Containment at the Wall",b="Forsaken investigators have found that their undead bodies resist worgen infection. Living humans have no such defense. At Silverpine Forest's southern border, human refugees gather in desperation beside the locked gates of the Greymane Wall. The Forsaken fear the refugees will be bitten and made Arugal's loyal servants. So ruthless orders call for their removal before the affliction can claim them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Stop the Spread about?",a="Stop the Spread concerns containing the worgen curse in Silverpine Forest. Forces target human refugees near the Greymane Wall to keep Archmage Arugal from gaining more servants.",al={"what is stop the spread","stop the spread quest lore"}},{q="Who is responsible for the worgen in Silverpine?",a="Archmage Arugal is blamed for the worgen in Silverpine Forest, whether through deliberate acts or unforeseen effects of his magic. His growing pack threatens the region.",al={"who spreads worgen curse","arugal worgen connection"}},{q="Can the Forsaken catch the worgen curse?",a="Forsaken research indicates that the worgen curse cannot infect the undead. Forsaken forces can face the danger without becoming Arugal's beastly servants.",al={"can forsaken become worgen","are undead immune to worgen"}},{q="Why are human refugees being targeted at the Greymane Wall?",a="Many human refugees have gathered outside the sealed Greymane Wall. Since living humans can catch Arugal's curse, the Forsaken fear they may swell the worgen's ranks.",al={"why kill refugees","greymane wall refugees"}},{q="How does the worgen affliction spread?",a="Researchers in Silverpine Forest know that worgen infection can pass through bites. The exact workings of the magic and the body remain unclear.",al={"how do worgen spread","worgen curse transmission"}},{q="Is there a way to stop or cure the worgen curse?",a="No cure for the worgen affliction is known. Researchers seek a way to halt it, while containment remains their immediate concern.",al={"can the worgen curse be cured","cure for worgen"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne adventurer, you are warned to avoid bites while carrying out the grim orders near the Greymane Wall.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you are immune to the worgen affliction. You can take part in containment without risk of infection.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may be among the uninfected refugees at the sealed Greymane Wall. Forsaken researchers see them as possible carriers of Arugal's curse."},kw={"arugal","curse","forsaken","greymane wall","refugees","silverpine","skyborne","stop the spread","worgen"},rel={"subzone:greymane-wall","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","topic:forsaken","topic:skyborne","topic:human","topic:refugee"},m={id=98299},src={"In-game quest text: Stop the Spread"},fv=true}
E["quest:98313"] = {t="quest",n="For Further Study",z="general",s="Historian Karnik awaits a package in Ironforge, tied to something epic. What has been seen so far makes further study worthwhile.",h="Historian Karnik awaits a package in Ironforge, tied to something epic.",sec={{t="Karnik's Library",b="You are carrying the Whelgar Relic Package to Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers. He is usually in the library, reading at the back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is waiting for the package?",a="Historian Karnik awaits the Whelgar Relic Package in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"who gets it","package for who"}},{q="Where can I find Karnik?",a="Historian Karnik is usually reading at the back of the library in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"where's karnik","karnik location"}},{q="What package am I carrying?",a="You are carrying the Whelgar Relic Package for Historian Karnik.",al={"what package","relic package"}},{q="Why does this need further study?",a="The matter is called epic, and what has been seen so far makes further study seem worthwhile. No further details are given.",al={"why study it","what's the big deal"}}},kw={"for further study","hall of explorers","historian karnik","ironforge","library","whelgar relic package"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-explorers","subzone:library-ironforge","zone:ironforge"},m={id=98313},src={"In-game quest text: For Further Study"},fv=true}
E["quest:98319"] = {t="quest",n="Secure the Mountain",z="general",s="You face a growing danger in Dun Morogh: wendigos have overrun the Grizzled Den, and Whitebeard's report is missing. Cornelius entered the cavern while his partner waited outside.",h="You face a growing danger in Dun Morogh: wendigos have overrun the Grizzled Den, and Whitebeard's report is...",sec={{t="A Den Overrun",b="Wendigos are multiplying across the cold mountain slopes and crowding into the Grizzled Den to the north. Dwarven scouts already contend with Frostmane trolls. Now savage beasts make the crags perilous for patrols and couriers.",sp=0},{t="Reckless Valor",b="Cornelius charged into the Grizzled Den to secure Whitebeard's vital report. His partner waits outside, seeking help to find the scout and thin the ferocious wendigos in the cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cornelius?",a="Cornelius is a scout whose partner waits outside the Grizzled Den. He charged into the wendigo-filled cavern to secure Whitebeard's report, and his partner needs help finding him.",al={"who is cornelius","cornelius dwarf","where is cornelius"}},{q="What is the Grizzled Den?",a="The Grizzled Den is a cavern north of the mountaineers' post. Wendigos that usually keep to deep mountain hollows have overrun it in large numbers.",al={"what is grizzled den","where are wendigos","wendigo cave dun morogh"}},{q="Why are the wendigos spreading?",a="Wendigos have begun multiplying and spreading rapidly across the snowy mountain crags. Their numbers add to the danger scouts already face from local Frostmane trolls.",al={"why wendigos spreading","wendigo problem dun morogh","wendigos like bunnies"}},{q="Who is Whitebeard and what is his report?",a="Whitebeard awaits an essential report on mountain conditions. Cornelius went into the Grizzled Den to secure it.",al={"who is whitebeard","whitebeard report","senir whitebeard"}},{q="What is the goal of Secure the Mountain?",a="You enter the Grizzled Den to find Cornelius and thin out the wendigos overrunning the cave.",al={"what is secure the mountain","secure the mountain objective"}},{q="How do the trolls factor into the mountain's troubles?",a="Frostmane trolls already threaten scouts in the peaks. The sudden surge in wendigos adds another danger for patrols on the mountain passes.",al={"trolls dun morogh","troll threat"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, reclaiming the Grizzled Den helps protect mountaineers and travelers from wendigos encroaching on Dun Morogh's paths.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help get Whitebeard the intelligence he needs to maintain border security against threats in the mountains."},kw={"cornelius","dun morogh","grizzled den","mountaineer","secure the mountain","troll","wendigo","whitebeard"},rel={"subzone:grizzled-den","quest:313","topic:troll"},m={id=98319},src={"In-game quest text: Secure the Mountain"},fv=true}
E["quest:98321"] = {t="quest",n="Flintfire's Shipment",z="general",s="Kharanos forges need ore from the Grizzled Den, where savage wendigos have driven miners out. The miners left crates behind, and Tognus Flintfire needs the ore to keep local forges supplied.",h="Kharanos forges need ore from the Grizzled Den, where savage wendigos have driven miners out.",sec={{t="A Supply Crisis in Kharanos",b="Tognus Flintfire's forge in Kharanos is short of ore. Savage wendigos invaded the Grizzled Den, the region's most productive and dependable source. The miners fled for their lives, leaving their posts and freshly packed crates scattered across the cavern floor.",sp=0},{t="Venturing into the Grizzled Den",b="The Grizzled Den lies west of Kharanos. Tognus is grateful that every miner escaped the wendigos in one piece, yet the work stoppage threatens to halt local blacksmithing. Rather than wait for an armed expedition to clear the cave, he seeks daring travelers to slip into the wendigo lair, gather the stranded crates, and bring the ore back to his forge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tognus Flintfire?",a="Tognus Flintfire is a dwarf in Kharanos whose forge depends on steady ore shipments. Wendigos overran his primary mining cave, leaving a severe shortage, so he asks travelers to retrieve the abandoned crates.",al={"who is tongus flintfire","tongus flintfire","quest giver"}},{q="Where is the Grizzled Den located?",a="The Grizzled Den lies west of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. It was a reliable mining site, but savage wendigos now make it their den, and the lost ore remains inside.",al={"where is grizzled den","grizzled den location","where to find shipments"}},{q="Why was the mining cave abandoned?",a="Hostile wendigos invaded and overran the miners' most reliable source of ore. The workers fled in a desperate scramble, leaving equipment and packed shipments behind, but all made it out alive.",al={"why miners flee","what happened to the mine","wendigo attack"}},{q="What is inside the missing shipments?",a="The missing shipments are crates of ore packed before the wendigos drove the miners out. Without it, local metalworking and forge work in Kharanos are threatened with a halt.",al={"what are flintfire shipments","what is in the crates","shipment contents"}},{q="Did any miners get hurt during the attack?",a="Tognus says all the miners escaped the Grizzled Den in one piece despite the wendigos' ferocity. They left their supplies and ore behind.",al={"did miners survive","miner casualties","wendigo victims"}},{q="What happens once the shipments are recovered?",a="The recovered shipments give Tognus Flintfire the raw metal stock to get the local forge working again. That can happen without clearing the entire infested cavern first.",al={"why need ore","what happens after recovery","forge running"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you are welcome to take on hard physical work in Dun Morogh. Tognus Flintfire appreciates your grit.",["profession:Mining"]="The lost shipments are ore the miners left behind when they evacuated their main dig site after the wendigos attacked.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Flintfire's shipments supply Kharanos's local forges with workable metal."},kw={"dun morogh","flintfire","forge","grizzled den","kharanos","miners","ore","shipments","tongus flintfire","wendigo"},rel={"subzone:kharanos","subzone:grizzled-den","quest:313","topic:gnome"},m={id=98321},src={"In-game quest text: Flintfire's Shipment"},fv=true}
E["quest:98322"] = {t="quest",n="Secure the Mountain",z="general",s="Senir Whitebeard needs news from Mountaineer Gretchen, west of Kharanos. The scouts he sent to investigate aggressive wendigos have not reported back.",h="Senir Whitebeard needs news from Mountaineer Gretchen, west of Kharanos.",sec={{t="An Overdue Report",b="Senir Whitebeard gathers military reports for Ironforge. A team of mountaineers went to study the wendigos nearby, but they have not returned with news. Whitebeard will not enter the icy caves himself. So he asks you to travel just west of town and learn what became of the scouts.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Western Ridge",b="West of Kharanos, Mountaineer Gretchen has received Senir Whitebeard's inquiries. She says the wendigos in the mountain crags are more volatile than the first reports claimed. The danger now calls for closer scouting in the nearby wilds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Secure the Mountain?",a="Senir Whitebeard gives the request in Kharanos. Mountaineer Gretchen calls him 'Ol' Whitebeard.' He gathers reports on wilderness threats and sends them to Ironforge's dwarven leaders.",al={"who gives secure the mountain","secure the mountain questgiver","who starts secure the mountain"}},{q="Where can Mountaineer Gretchen be found?",a="Mountaineer Gretchen is just west of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. She is near the mountainsides and caves where wendigos threaten the area.",al={"where is gretchen","mountaineer gretchen location","find mountaineer gretchen"}},{q="Why is the questgiver looking for Mountaineer Gretchen?",a="Senir Whitebeard sends intelligence to Ironforge, but a scout investigating the wendigos has not reported back on time. He is behind schedule and will not enter dangerous caves, so he asks you to check on Mountaineer Gretchen.",al={"why send adventurer","why does whitebeard need help","why check on gretchen"}},{q="What wendigo problem is threatening the area?",a="Wendigos live in the rocky foothills and dark caves around Kharanos. Their aggression threatens travelers and local outposts, so Ironforge scouts watch their movements closely.",al={"wendigo threat kharanos","what are wendigos doing","why wendigo problem"}},{q="What does Mountaineer Gretchen report upon arrival?",a="West of town, Mountaineer Gretchen confirms she received Whitebeard's inquiries. She says the nearby wendigos have made a serious mess of things.",al={"what does gretchen say","secure the mountain turn in","gretchen report status"}},{q="What role do mountaineers play around Kharanos?",a="Mountaineers guard borders, track threats, and scout for the Ironforge dwarves. They survey remote passes, dark caves, and snowy trails across Dun Morogh to protect towns like Kharanos.",al={"who are mountaineers","ironforge mountaineer patrol","what do mountaineers do"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you rely on Dun Morogh's mountaineers to patrol snowy ridges and perilous caves. Their reports help keep dwarven settlements safe.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help local dwarven patrols around Kharanos coordinate defenses across the snowy heart of Khaz Modan."},kw={"dun morogh","dwarf","ironforge","kharanos","mountaineer gretchen","secure the mountain","wendigo","whitebeard"},rel={"subzone:kharanos","zone:ironforge"},m={id=98322},src={"In-game quest text: Secure the Mountain"},fv=true}
E["quest:98323"] = {t="quest",n="Secure the Mountain",z="general",s="Mountaineer Gretchen sends a grim report from Dun Morogh to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos. Scouts have found a nearby cave overrun, and she will risk no more lives in its tunnels. Ironforge must still guard the mountain frontier from rising threats.",h="Mountaineer Gretchen sends a grim report from Dun Morogh to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.",sec={{t="A Grim Report",b="Mountaineer Gretchen watches Dun Morogh's high passes from her post in the freezing peaks. A recent venture into a nearby cavern showed her how dangerous the wilderness remains. Hostile mongrels overrun its tunnels, and she judges the cave a death trap. Gretchen will risk no more lives there. She holds the line on the slopes and sends an emissary with her written assessment.",sp=0},{t="Losses in the Depths",b="Cornelius was among those lost in the failed scouting effort, and his death weighs heavily on Mountaineer Gretchen. She admits the cavern cannot be reclaimed under current conditions, so she halts further exploration of its tunnels. Her concern now is holding the threat back. She will sacrifice no more scouts to the creatures beneath the snowy crags.",sp=1},{t="Senir Whitebeard's Dossier",b="From Kharanos, Senir Whitebeard tracks dangers to the dwarven heartland. Gretchen's report brings little surprise: the cavern is overrun. He adds her letter to his growing stack of field reports. Each account helps Ironforge record and manage the dangers along its frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mountaineer Gretchen?",a="Mountaineer Gretchen is an Ironforge sentry in Dun Morogh's snowy wilderness. After a deadly scouting effort in a nearby cave, she writes a field report on the hostile creatures and sends it to Kharanos. She remains at her post until the surrounding territory is secure.",al={"gretchen","mountaineer gretchen lore","who is gretchen"}},{q="Who is Senir Whitebeard?",a="Senir Whitebeard is a dwarven authority in Kharanos. He coordinates local security across Dun Morogh and receives dispatches and scouting assessments from mountaineers in the field. He catalogs the reports to assess threats across the region.",al={"senir whitebeard","whitebeard kharanos","who is senir"}},{q="Who was Cornelius?",a="Cornelius was a fellow scout who explored the infested cavern. He died in the failed scouting effort, and Mountaineer Gretchen speaks of his loss with regret. His death helped convince her the cave was a deadly trap and no more scouts should enter.",al={"cornelius","who is cornelius","what happened to cornelius","cornelius secure the mountain"}},{q="What happened in the mountain cave?",a="Scouts found the mountain cavern overrun by hostile mongrels, and Cornelius died in the effort. Mountaineer Gretchen judged the tunnels a lost cause and refused to risk more scouts there. She chose to avoid the area.",al={"what is in the cave","why is the cave a death trap","cave lost cause"}},{q="Why does Gretchen refuse to leave her post?",a="Mountaineer Gretchen says she will not abandon her post until the mountain is secure. Though the nearby cavern is too dangerous to retake, she stays on the snowy heights to watch the approach and sends word of the threat to Kharanos.",al={"why is gretchen staying","gretchen post","why stay on the mountain"}},{q="How does Senir Whitebeard react to Gretchen's report?",a="Senir Whitebeard is hardly surprised to hear the cavern is overrun. He accepts the news and adds Gretchen's dispatch to his growing stack of notes, keeping a careful record of the dangers facing the realm.",al={"senir reaction","whitebeard report reaction","what does senir do"}},{q="What role do the Mountaineers play in Dun Morogh?",a="Mountaineers are Ironforge's frontier scouts and border guards in Dun Morogh. These hardy dwarves patrol snowy peaks, high trails and passes, watch for hostile beasts, explore caverns, and report dangers to places like Kharanos. Their work protects travelers and settlements.",al={"ironforge mountaineers","what are mountaineers","dwarf mountaineers lore"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Morogh is the ancestral mountain home of the Bronzebeard dwarves. Mountaineer Gretchen's stubborn vigil helps protect her kin from the dangers around them.",["faction:Alliance"]="Safe high passes around Ironforge matter to travel and defense across the Alliance's snowy stronghold in Khaz Modan."},kw={"cave","cornelius","dun morogh","kharanos","mountaineer gretchen","mountaineer's report","secure the mountain","senir whitebeard"},rel={"npc:senir-whitebeard","subzone:kharanos"},m={id=98323},src={"In-game quest text: Secure the Mountain"},fv=true}
E["quest:98326"] = {t="quest",n="Frosthowl",z="general",s="In Dun Morogh, Frosthowl's attack leaves a dwarven fisher without her catch. The wendigo fled into the Grizzled Den with the sack of fish.",h="In Dun Morogh, Frosthowl's attack leaves a dwarven fisher without her catch.",sec={{t="A Stolen Haul",b="A dwarven fisher and her husband, Paxton, spent days fishing on Dun Morogh’s frozen lake. Through biting winds, they gathered a single sack of fish to bring home. Then Frosthowl ambushed their camp and carried off the catch into the snowy wilderness.",sp=0},{t="The Loudmouth of the Grizzled Den",b="Frosthowl’s booming roars rattle the ice and frighten the lake’s sparse fish. After stealing the fisher’s sack, the beast fled deep into the Grizzled Den, southeast of the lake. Now the fishers are stranded without their catch. They need someone to confront Frosthowl and recover the stolen fish.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Frosthowl?",a="Frosthowl is an aggressive wendigo in Dun Morogh. Its roars frighten fish on the frozen lake. The beast recently attacked a dwarven fisher and stole the catch she and her husband had spent days gathering.",al={"who is frosthowl","what is frosthowl","frosthowl wendigo"}},{q="Where can Frosthowl be found?",a="Frosthowl hides deep within the Grizzled Den, southeast of the frozen lake where Paxton fishes.",al={"where is frosthowl","frosthowl location","where is the wendigo hiding"}},{q="What did Frosthowl steal?",a="Frosthowl stole a sack of fish that Paxton and his wife spent days catching on the frozen lake. The fisher asks travelers to confront the beast and recover their catch.",al={"what did frosthowl steal","why kill frosthowl","what did the wendigo take"}},{q="Who is Paxton?",a="Paxton is a dwarven fisherman who spent days fishing on the frozen lake. His wife asks passing travelers to track Frosthowl after it stole their sack of fish.",al={"who is paxton","paxton dun morogh","paxton fisher"}},{q="What is the Grizzled Den?",a="The Grizzled Den is a wendigo lair southeast of the frozen lake in Dun Morogh. Frosthowl fled into its tunnels after stealing the fishers’ catch.",al={"what is the grizzled den","grizzled den wendigo cave","where do wendigos live in dun morogh"}},{q="Why is the beast named Frosthowl?",a="Frosthowl is called a loudmouth for its thunderous roars and howls across the snowy plains. The noise threatens to frighten fish away and troubles those working on the frozen lakes.",al={"how did frosthowl get its name","why called frosthowl","loudmouth wendigo"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know how hard it is to fish Dun Morogh’s frozen lakes through biting cold. Wendigo attacks threaten local fishers and their livelihoods.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you help keep the icy paths and fishing spots near Brewnall and Kharanos safe from aggressive predators."},kw={"dun morogh","frosthowl","frozen lake","grizzled den","ice fishing","paxton","stolen fish","wendigo"},rel={"subzone:grizzled-den","quest:313"},m={id=98326},src={"In-game quest text: Frosthowl"},fv=true}
E["quest:98340"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Cat Spirit",z="general",s="Dendrite Starblaze calls you to Moonglade for the next step in your druidic training. He sets you on the path to learn nature’s cat perspective.",h="Dendrite Starblaze calls you to Moonglade for the next step in your druidic training.",sec={{t="A Call to Moonglade",b="Dendrite Starblaze seeks you in Nighthaven, the village in Moonglade. You have already learned the magic that brings you there, and your druidic training can continue when you meet him.",sp=0},{t="The Cat’s Perspective",b="Dendrite welcomes you back and turns your training toward the cat, another perspective of nature. As with the bear, understanding this aspect rests with you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent for me?",a="Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",al={"who wants me in moonglade","dendrite call","who sent for druid"}},{q="What does Dendrite want to teach me?",a="Dendrite will set you on the path to understanding the cat as a perspective of nature.",al={"cat training","learn cat","what is next"}},{q="Where do I meet Dendrite?",a="Dendrite is in the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade.",al={"where is dendrite","meet dendrite","nighthaven where"}},{q="How can I reach Moonglade?",a="You have already learned the magic that takes you to Moonglade.",al={"get to moonglade","moonglade travel","how go there"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="You have already learned the magic to travel to Moonglade, and Dendrite compares this learning to the bear aspect.",al={"what did i learn before","bear training before","previous druid step"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Dendrite’s teaching opens the next part of your training: understanding nature through the cat."},kw={"bear","cat","dendrite starblaze","druid training","great cat spirit","moonglade","nature","nighthaven"},rel={"quest:5921","quest:92472","subzone:nighthaven","npc:dendrite-starblaze","topic:cenarius"},m={id=98340},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98341"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",z="general",s="In Moonglade, the Avatar of Saeyleenan guides young shen'dorei druids through a spiritual trial. The spirit comes from Zephras and helps them embody the windborne feline form of their homeland.",h="In Moonglade, the Avatar of Saeyleenan guides young shen'dorei druids through a spiritual trial.",sec={{t="A Visitor from Zephras",b="South of Moonglade's twin bridges, a spirit from distant Zephras has appeared in the sacred sanctuary. Calling itself the Avatar of Saeyleenan, this windborne cat spirit has crossed into Azeroth to guide young shen'dorei druids ready to unlock their feline form.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of the Windborne Form",b="Druids seek wisdom in the feline form, but those from Zephras follow a different tradition from Azeroth's native peoples. The shen'dorei embody the windborne predator of their homeland instead of an Azerothian wildcat. So Saeyleenan oversees their trial in Moonglade, to teach them the spirit's nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Great Windborne Cat Spirit?",a="The windborne cat spirit appears as the Avatar of Saeyleenan, from distant Zephras. It has come to Moonglade to mentor and test young shen'dorei druids seeking its feline shape.",al={"who is the windborne cat spirit","what is avatar of saeyleenan","saeyleenan lore"}},{q="Where can the Avatar of Saeyleenan be found?",a="The Avatar of Saeyleenan appears in southern Moonglade, just south of the twin bridges.",al={"where to find cat spirit moonglade","avatar of saeyleenan location","windborne cat location"}},{q="Why do Zephras druids commune with a different cat spirit?",a="Shen'dorei druids come from Zephras, so their feline shape reflects the windborne spirits of their homeland rather than Azeroth's native big cats. The spirit oversees their trial to ensure they embody its essence.",al={"why does cat form look different","zephras cat form difference","why not azeroth cat spirit"}},{q="What does the trial of the windborne cat entail?",a="The Avatar of Saeyleenan has the initiate undertake the trial of Azeroth's Great Cat Spirit. The Avatar supervises and confirms that the druid understands the windborne spirit's unique nature.",al={"what trial does the cat spirit give","cat spirit trial zephras","how to get windborne cat form"}},{q="What does shen'dorei refer to?",a="The Avatar of Saeyleenan calls the initiate shen'dorei, marking their origin in Zephras and distinguishing their heritage and spiritual practices from Azeroth's native peoples.",al={"who are shendorei","shen dorei druids","what does shendorei mean"}},{q="What is Zephras?",a="Zephras is the distant homeland of the shen'dorei. Its native flora, fauna, and spirits differ from Azeroth's, giving rise to unique shapeshifting forms among its druids.",al={"what is zephras","where is zephras located","zephras homeland"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid from Zephras, you commune with the windborne cat spirit to master your feline form. The rite follows your heritage rather than Azeroth's traditional path.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you are called shen'dorei. The spirits of your homeland, Zephras, guide your druidic path."},kw={"cat form","cat spirit","druid trial","moonglade","saeyleenan","shen'dorei","windborne cat","zephras"},rel={"quest:98393","quest:5921"},m={id=98341},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Windborne Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98372"] = {t="quest",n="An Unfortunate End",z="general",s="In Duskwood, a Night Watchman lies dead in the gloom. A beast mauled him, and the unlit brand in his hand may help you see what the darkness hides.",h="In Duskwood, a Night Watchman lies dead in the gloom.",sec={{t="A Grim Discovery",b="A Night Watch patrolman lies dead on Duskwood's dark soil. Deep gashes and cuts mark his body. A great beast caught him before he could escape.",sp=0},{t="Light in the Darkness",b="An unlit torch remains in the fallen guard's rigid hand. Take it, and its light can reveal what hides in Duskwood's gloom and along other dark paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Whose body is this?",a="The fallen body belongs to a Night Watch guard, who patrols Duskwood's dark roads and borders. He died alone in the shadows.",al={"who is the dead body","who died here","who is the dead night watchman"}},{q="What killed the watchman?",a="A large beast mauled the watchman, leaving deep gashes and savage cuts. It caught him before he could defend himself or light his way.",al={"what killed the night watchman","how did the watchman die","what attacked him"}},{q="Why is the torch important?",a="The unlit torch from the guard's hand can light the gloom. Its glow may reveal what the darkness hides in Duskwood and beyond.",al={"what is the torch for","what do i do with the torch","torch uses duskwood"}}},kw={"an unfortunate end","beast","duskwood","mauled","night watchman","torch"},rel={"zone:duskwood"},m={id=98372},src={"In-game quest text: An Unfortunate End"},fv=true}
E["quest:98391"] = {t="quest",n="The Sisterhood of Elune",z="general",s="In Darnassus, the Sisterhood of Elune needs help with urgent troubles in night elf lands. Sister Aquinne receives those who come to aid the priestesses.",h="In Darnassus, the Sisterhood of Elune needs help with urgent troubles in night elf lands.",sec={{t="A Call to the Capital",b="You are sent to Darnassus to meet Sister Aquinne. When urgent matters threaten their people and sacred lands, the priestesses of Elune call on trusted champions for aid.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Sister Aquinne",b="Sister Aquinne welcomes you in Darnassus, relieved by your prompt arrival. The priestesses face growing demands, so they seek help beyond their cloistered ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sister Aquinne?",a="Sister Aquinne is a priestess and emissary of the Sisterhood of Elune in Darnassus. She receives travelers who come to help with urgent matters facing the night elves.",al={"who is sister aquinne","aquinne darnassus","where is aquinne"}},{q="What is the Sisterhood of Elune?",a="The Sisterhood of Elune is an ancient order of night elf priestesses devoted to Elune, the moon goddess. Its members guide and heal their people, lead kaldorei culture, and oversee their spiritual welfare and defense.",al={"what is sisterhood of elune","who are the sisters of elune","night elf priestesses"}},{q="Where do I need to go to complete this quest?",a="Travel to Darnassus, the night elf capital atop Teldrassil. Sister Aquinne awaits you there with word from the Sisterhood.",al={"where to turn in sisterhood of elune","sisterhood quest location","where do i go for sisterhood of elune"}},{q="Why does the Sisterhood require aid?",a="Sister Aquinne says the Sisterhood needs prompt help with pressing troubles in Darnassus and the surrounding night elf lands. Speak with her to learn what duties await.",al={"why does the sisterhood need help","sisterhood trouble","what aid does sisterhood require"}},{q="Can Horde characters undertake this quest?",a="No. The Sisterhood of Elune is part of night elf leadership and aligned with the Alliance. Darnassus is an Alliance capital, so only Alliance adventurers can answer this call.",al={"do horde get this quest","can horde do sisterhood of elune"}},{q="Who leads the Sisterhood of Elune?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads the Sisterhood of Elune and the kaldorei nation. She guides her sisters from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who leads the sisterhood of elune","sisterhood leader","tyrande sisterhood"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, answering the Sisterhood of Elune's summons is a sacred duty tied to your people's spiritual life and leadership.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, your devotion to Elune links you to the old traditions of the kaldorei temple. Answering Sister Aquinne's call follows those traditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Kalimdor, helping the Sisterhood supports night elf spiritual and civic leadership in Darnassus."},kw={"aquinne","darnassus","elune","priestess","sister aquinne","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil","the sisterhood of elune"},rel={"npc:sister-aquinne","zone:darnassus"},m={id=98391},src={"In-game quest text: The Sisterhood of Elune"},fv=true}
E["quest:98392"] = {t="quest",n="Darkness in the Glade",z="general",s="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak investigates tainted harpy belts in the Oracle Glade. Their amulets may show what is spreading through Teldrassil.",h="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak investigates tainted harpy belts in the Oracle Glade.",sec={{t="Tainted Fibers",b="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak finds something wrong among the harpies of the Oracle Glade. Their leather belts carry an unnatural taint woven through the fibers. She suspects demonic corruption, not ordinary aggression. Before she warns Darnassus, she needs proof.",sp=0},{t="A Blight Confirmed",b="Arynia sends you to the western nests to face three harpy matriarchs: Hatescreech, Windmistress Gaedress, and Witchmother Arysa. Each carries an amulet marked by her power. The gems hold foul green swirls. They confirm fel moss is warping the harpies and seeping into Teldrassil's sacred boughs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Darkness in the Glade?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak investigates strange taint in harpy belts in the Oracle Glade. She sends you to recover amulets from the harpy leaders and learn what is behind the affliction.",al={"what is darkness in the glade","darkness in the glade quest"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak asks for your help. She watches over Teldrassil's boughs from the Oracle Glade and investigates strange changes among its harpies.",al={"who gives darkness in the glade","quest giver oracle glade"}},{q="Why does Arynia want amulets from the harpy leaders?",a="Arynia found tainted fibers in belts taken from common harpies and needs more proof. She suspects the leaders' amulets may reveal the blight's nature and origin.",al={"why kill harpy leaders","why get amulets","harpy amulets reason"}},{q="Which harpy leaders hold the amulets?",a="The amulets belong to three leaders in western nests: Hatescreech, Windmistress Gaedress, and Witchmother Arysa.",al={"which harpies have amulets","harpy leaders oracle glade"}},{q="What is causing the corruption in the glade?",a="Fel moss is causing the corruption. Arynia finds foul green swirls in the recovered amulets' gemstones, proof that fel moss is tainting the region.",al={"what is corrupting the harpies","what is the green swirl","origin of glade darkness"}},{q="Has this corruption appeared anywhere else?",a="Yes. Arynia has heard reports of fel moss turning the land against the night elves in Shadowglen and other boughs across the world tree.",al={"fel moss elsewhere","is shadowglen corrupted"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Fel corruption in sacred boughs like the Oracle Glade threatens the kaldorei effort to nurture and protect Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="Sentinel Cloudsbreak serves Darnassus through its vigilance against demonic corruption threatening Alliance lands.",["class:Druid"]="Fel moss among wildlife and leather fibers points to an unnatural blight upsetting the World Tree's natural balance."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","arysa","darkness in the glade","fel moss","gaedress","harpies","hatescreech","oracle glade","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","subzone:oracle-glade","item:fel-moss","topic:harpy","subzone:shadowglen"},m={id=98392},src={"In-game quest text: Darkness in the Glade"},fv=true}
E["quest:98393"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Cat Spirit",z="general",s="In Nighthaven, druids gather at Dendrite Starblaze's call to learn the cat's ways. They have mastered the bear and now turn to another aspect of the wild under Father Cenarius's blessing.",h="In Nighthaven, druids gather at Dendrite Starblaze's call to learn the cat's ways.",sec={{t="The Summons to Moonglade",b="Druids who have mastered the enduring bear are summoned to Moonglade again. Elder Dendrite Starblaze calls them to Nighthaven, where they can deepen their communion with nature. Their spiritual gifts carry them across the distance to this haven of Cenarion wisdom.",sp=0},{t="The Perspective of the Cat",b="When you reach Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze invokes Father Cenarius and greets you with a faint aura of power. He says it is time to embrace the cat's perspective: swift, agile, and predatory. As before, Dendrite opens the path to understanding, while the work of embodying and spreading the feline spirit rests with you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends for you in The Great Cat Spirit?",a="Your druid trainers send you on behalf of Dendrite Starblaze, an elder mentor in Nighthaven, Moonglade's secluded haven.",al={"who gives the great cat spirit quest","dendrite starblaze summons"}},{q="Where can Dendrite Starblaze be found?",a="Dendrite Starblaze lives in Nighthaven, Moonglade's central settlement. Druids can reach it by teleportation.",al={"where is dendrite starblaze","dendrite starblaze location"}},{q="What is the purpose of meeting Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite prepares you to understand and commune with nature's feline aspect, after you have learned the bear's ways.",al={"what does dendrite teach","cat form training quest"}},{q="Why does Dendrite invoke Father Cenarius?",a="Dendrite invokes Father Cenarius to honor the demigod and patron of druidism, who taught mortals the secrets of nature and shapeshifting.",al={"why father cenarius","cenarius mention dendrite"}},{q="How do druids travel to Moonglade for this summons?",a="Druids use their spiritual bond with nature to teleport to Moonglade when their mentors call.",al={"how to get to moonglade","teleport to moonglade druid"}},{q="How does this aspect relate to the bear aspect?",a="Druidic teaching approaches nature through different aspects. You first master the bear's enduring strength, then advance to the cat's swift predator's instincts.",al={"cat form vs bear form lore","bear form first"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you take this rite of passage to extend your mastery of the wild beyond the bear.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you answer Cenarius's ancient teachings on Moonglade, ancestral ground for kaldorei druids.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you travel freely to Nighthaven with your night elf brethren under the Cenarion Circle's shared guidance."},kw={"cat aspect","cenarius","dendrite starblaze","druid training","moonglade","nighthaven","the great cat spirit"},rel={"npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:nighthaven","quest:5921","topic:druid","topic:cenarius"},m={id=98393},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98394"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Cat Spirit",z="general",s="A wise spirit in southern Moonglade teaches druids about the cat’s nature. Its wisdom guides those who seek the feline shape.",h="A wise spirit in southern Moonglade teaches druids about the cat’s nature.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Moonglade",b="In southern Moonglade, the Great Cat Spirit waits on a hill above the bridge. Druids who seek the feline shape come to it for guidance. You are here to learn what it can teach about the nature of the cat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Great Cat Spirit?",a="The Great Cat Spirit resides on a hill in southern Moonglade, overlooking the bridge.",al={"cat spirit location","where find cat spirit"}},{q="What does the Great Cat Spirit teach?",a="The Great Cat Spirit teaches druids about the nature of the cat and the feline shape.",al={"cat spirit teaches what","learn cat shape"}},{q="Why do druids seek the Great Cat Spirit?",a="Druids seeking the feline shape come to the Great Cat Spirit for wisdom and guidance.",al={"why see cat spirit","druid cat spirit"}},{q="Who is the Great Cat Spirit?",a="The Great Cat Spirit is a wise, cunning being in southern Moonglade who tutors druids seeking the feline shape.",al={"great cat spirit who","cat spirit"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid seeking the feline shape, you come to the Great Cat Spirit in Moonglade for wisdom about the cat."},kw={"cat nature","cat spirit","druid","feline shape","great cat spirit","moonglade"},rel={"quest:5921","topic:druid","quest:5929"},m={id=98394},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98398"] = {t="quest",n="The Oracle Tree",z="general",s="A fallen piece of bark draws travelers to the Oracle Tree, where an ancient voice reaches the mind. Its message calls those who have finished their first duties toward greater work.",h="A fallen piece of bark draws travelers to the Oracle Tree, where an ancient voice reaches the mind.",sec={{t="A Call to Greater Duties",b="The Oracle Tree watches its surroundings and guides travelers who have proved their mettle. When it needs an agent in the world, it deliberately sheds a piece of bark nearby. Those who notice are called to step forward, for their first duties are finished and greater responsibilities await.",sp=0},{t="Communion Through the Bark",b="The Oracle Tree reaches the mind through its fallen bark rather than speaking aloud. Examine the piece, and its calm presence washes over you. Its thoughts and desires come like a soft breeze through a canopy of leaves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient, sentient tree that can communicate telepathically with those nearby. When it has a message or duty to give, it sheds a piece of bark to draw worthy travelers’ attention.",al={"what is oracle tree","oracle tree lore"}},{q="How does the Oracle Tree communicate?",a="The Oracle Tree sends its thoughts telepathically instead of speaking aloud. Inspect the fallen bark, and its calm voice enters your mind like a gentle breeze through leaves.",al={"how does oracle tree speak","oracle tree communication"}},{q="Why do you need to find the Oracle Tree's bark?",a="The Oracle Tree sheds bark when it has a duty that needs tending. Inspecting the piece lets the tree send its guidance directly to your mind.",al={"why find bark","fallen bark purpose"}},{q="Who directs you to the Oracle Tree?",a="A local overseer or caretaker directs you to the Oracle Tree. They have watched your accomplishments, see that greater duties await, and notice the freshly shed bark.",al={"who sends you to oracle tree","quest giver oracle tree"}},{q="What is the purpose of the quest The Oracle Tree?",a="You make contact with the Oracle Tree by seeking out its bark. Inspecting it opens your mind to the tree’s message and the greater duty it needs completed.",al={"oracle tree quest goal","what does oracle tree want"}},{q="Where is the Oracle Tree bark found?",a="The Oracle Tree’s shed bark lies on the ground nearby, waiting for someone attuned enough to hear its message.",al={"where find oracle bark","bark location"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are attuned to sentient plant life and the voices of ancient trees. Communion with the Oracle Tree extends your reverence for nature."},kw={"oracle tree","oracle tree bark","sentient tree","shed bark","telepathy","the oracle tree"},m={id=98398},src={"In-game quest text: The Oracle Tree"},fv=true}
E["quest:98403"] = {t="quest",n="Twisted Hatred",z="general",s="In Teldrassil, Xethorr the Wicked’s schemes draw you to the Cleft northwest of Dolanaar. There you face the satyr and cull his corrupted spiders before their venom serves his demonic plots.",h="In Teldrassil, Xethorr the Wicked’s schemes draw you to the Cleft northwest of Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Shadowed Handler",b="Lord Melenas had a master in Xethorr the Wicked. The satyr held an entrenched presence in Teldrassil’s wilderness, pulling strings from the forest shadows to trouble the World Tree’s quiet boughs.",sp=0},{t="The Befouled Brood of the Cleft",b="Northwest of Dolanaar, Xethorr turned Teldrassil’s native Webwood spiders into befouled beasts. From the secluded Cleft, the satyr meant to wield their venom in demonic plots. Tallonkai Swiftroot sent adventurers to cull the brood and seize Xethorr’s Mature Fel Moss before the corruption spread.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Xethorr the Wicked?",a="Xethorr the Wicked is a satyr who orchestrated corruption within Teldrassil. He directed Lord Melenas and made his lair in the Cleft, where he twisted native spiders and used Mature Fel Moss in his schemes.",al={"who is xethorr","xethorr the wicked","who is the satyr"}},{q="Where is the Cleft located?",a="The Cleft lies deep in Teldrassil’s forest, northwest of Dolanaar. Xethorr the Wicked and his befouled brood have taken residence there.",al={"where is the cleft","cleft location","where do i find xethorr"}},{q="Why are the spiders of Teldrassil befouled?",a="Xethorr the Wicked corrupted the Befouled Webwoods, native spiders of Teldrassil. He twisted their minds and bodies to harvest their venom for a demonic plan.",al={"why did spiders change","what are befouled webwoods","befouled webwood lore"}},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf guardian stationed in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He sends adventurers to root out demonic subversion in the surrounding woods.",al={"who gave this quest","where is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot role"}},{q="What is the Mature Fel Moss?",a="Mature Fel Moss is a corrupting botanical specimen carried by Xethorr the Wicked. Tallonkai Swiftroot seeks it to learn more about the satyr’s motives and work within Teldrassil.",al={"mature fel moss","why collect fel moss","what is fel moss"}},{q="How was Lord Melenas involved?",a="Lord Melenas acted at Xethorr the Wicked’s behest, not from isolated malice. His deeds revealed a coordinated satyr conspiracy within Teldrassil.",al={"melenas connection","who is lord melenas","melenas and xethorr"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Teldrassil as the new heart of Kaldorei resurgence. Demonic corruption among its native wildlife in the Cleft threatens your people.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that befouling Teldrassil’s natural spiders strikes at nature’s balance. Cenarion defenders must cleanse the brood.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Tallonkai Swiftroot protect Dolanaar from satyr schemes within Teldrassil, the Alliance’s primary sanctuary on Kalimdor."},kw={"befouled webwood","cleft","dolanaar","lord melenas","mature fel moss","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred","xethorr the wicked"},rel={"subzone:cleft","subzone:dolanaar","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","topic:satyr","item:fel-moss","quest:940"},m={id=98403},src={"In-game quest text: Twisted Hatred"},fv=true}
E["quest:98404"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit",z="general",s="At the Avatar of Saeyleenan, young druids face a trial of cunning and stealth. They enter the nearby Stormrage Barrow Den to recover three relics while avoiding enraged spirits. Passing the rite earns them the blessing to wield cat form.",h="At the Avatar of Saeyleenan, young druids face a trial of cunning and stealth.",sec={{t="The Trial of Cunning and Stealth",b="A seeker must show the nature of a predator before drawing upon the Great Windborne Cat Spirit. The cat calls for cunning and patience, then fierce action when cornered. The spirit tests those who seek its power, asking them to think, move, and strike like wild feline hunters. Only then may an initiate earn the right to take the cat's shape.",sp=0},{t="The Stormrage Barrow Den",b="The trial leads into the Stormrage Barrow Den, just east of the spirit's avatar. Three sacred tokens lie in its halls: the Relic of the Fang, the Relic of the Claw, and the Relic of the Silent Shadow.\n\nEnraged spirits have overrun the den and attack intruders on sight. A seeker cannot rely on brute force alone, but must tread carefully through the darkness to reach the relics.",sp=0},{t="The Avatar of Saeyleenan",b="The Avatar of Saeyleenan is the physical manifestation through which the Great Windborne Cat Spirit speaks to young initiates. Untutored seekers lack a seasoned predator's stealth, so a statue at the barrow den's entrance grants them temporary concealment.\n\nThose who slip past the frenzied spirits and return all three relics show they have learned the predator's ways. The Avatar recognizes their worthiness and grants the blessing to wield cat form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Great Windborne Cat Spirit?",a="The Great Windborne Cat Spirit guides young druids in mastering feline shapeshifting. Through the Avatar of Saeyleenan, it embodies cunning, stealth, and ferocity. It tests aspirants before granting its form, to ensure they respect the cat's instincts and nature.",al={"windborne cat spirit","who is saeyleenan","cat spirit lore"}},{q="What is the Avatar of Saeyleenan?",a="The Avatar of Saeyleenan speaks for the Great Windborne Cat Spirit and stands west of the Stormrage Barrow Den. It assigns seekers to recover the stolen or hidden relics, then evaluates whether each initiate has shown enough stealth and cunning to earn the feline blessing.",al={"avatar of saeyleenan","who is avatar saeyleenan","saeyleenan npc"}},{q="What relics are required for the trial?",a="The trial calls for the Relic of the Fang, the Relic of the Claw, and the Relic of the Silent Shadow, all found in the Stormrage Barrow Den. Together, they symbolize the cat's physical weapons and elusive stealth, and prove an initiate's reverence for every aspect of the predator.",al={"three relics","relic of the claw","stormrage barrow den relics"}},{q="Where is the Stormrage Barrow Den located?",a="The Stormrage Barrow Den lies just east of the Avatar of Saeyleenan. Its subterranean chambers hold the three sacred relics and test the druids. Initiates must avoid the enraged spirits wandering its dark tunnels.",al={"stormrage barrow den location","where is barrow den","where to find relics"}},{q="Why are enraged spirits guarding the barrow den?",a="The Stormrage Barrow Den is overrun by powerful enraged spirits that attack living intruders on sight. They are hostile threats, not willing guardians. Their presence forces aspiring druids to use cunning and stealth to recover the relics instead of fighting them directly.",al={"why are spirits enraged","enraged spirits barrow den","barrow den guardians"}},{q="How do seekers sneak past the enraged spirits?",a="A stone statue at the Stormrage Barrow Den's entrance grants seekers a temporary blessing of stealth. Young initiates have not yet earned their own cat form or prowling abilities, so the enchantment helps them pass the hostile spirits unseen and secure the relics.",al={"how to stealth barrow den","statue stealth buff","how to avoid enraged spirits"}},{q="What reward or blessing is granted upon completing the trial?",a="When the seeker returns the Relic of the Fang, the Relic of the Claw, and the Relic of the Silent Shadow, the Avatar of Saeyleenan deems them worthy of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit's blessing. The rite shows their understanding of the cat's nature and grants the spiritual approval needed to take the predator's shape.",al={"trial reward","what do you get from cat spirit","cat spirit blessing"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you must show cunning and ferocity before the spirit grants its shapeshifting blessing. The rite teaches you to channel the wild cat's agility, stealth, and predatory instinct.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can trace the Stormrage Barrow Den's name to one of the most prominent night elven druidic lineages. Its depths connect Kaldorei practitioners to their people's ancient barrow heritage and ancestral spirits."},kw={"avatar of saeyleenan","cat form","druid trial","enraged spirits","relic of the claw","relic of the fang","relic of the silent shadow","saeyleenan","stormrage barrow den","the great windborne cat spirit"},rel={"topic:druid"},m={id=98404},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Windborne Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98423"] = {t="quest",n="The Treaty of Understanding",z="general",s="After the War of the Three Hammers, The Treaty of Understanding marks a peace between two dwarf clans. Its ancient words record the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer agreement, while the Dark Iron clan remains apart.",h="After the War of the Three Hammers, The Treaty of Understanding marks a peace between two dwarf clans.",sec={{t="A Relic of Dwarven Reconciliation",b="You find a stone tablet deep in an ancient vault. Its words record a formal end to hostilities between dwarf clans. The treaty belongs to the troubled years after the War of the Three Hammers, when the Bronzebeards secured control of Ironforge mountain. Then came peace between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans.",sp=0},{t="The Unsigned Peace",b="King Magni Bronzebeard knows the tablet as the work of his ancestor, Madoran Bronzebeard, the first Bronzebeard king of Ironforge. The Bronzebeard and Wildhammer leaders signed the document. The Dark Iron clan left no mark, and their absence tells of the lasting rift between them and their mountain kin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Treaty of Understanding?",a="The Treaty of Understanding is an ancient stone tablet recovered from deep vaults. It records the formal peace made between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans just after the War of the Three Hammers ended.",al={"what is treaty of understanding","treaty tablet","what is this treaty"}},{q="Who created the treaty?",a="Madoran Bronzebeard drafted the treaty after the War of the Three Hammers, while he ruled as the first Bronzebeard king of Ironforge. The three clans had fought for control of the mountain.",al={"who wrote treaty of understanding","who made treaty of understanding","who drafted the treaty"}},{q="Why did the Dark Iron clan not sign the treaty?",a="The Dark Iron clan refused peace after the Bronzebeards took control of Ironforge. Only the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans signed the agreement, leaving the Dark Irons isolated and hostile.",al={"why didnt dark iron sign","did dark iron sign treaty","dark irons not on treaty"}},{q="Who is interested in the Treaty of Understanding?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard receives the tablet in the High Seat of Ironforge. He values it as a relic of his ancestor Madoran and of dwarven history.",al={"who wants the treaty","who do i give treaty of understanding to","where to turn in treaty"}},{q="What was the War of the Three Hammers?",a="The War of the Three Hammers was a bitter civil war between the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer, and Dark Iron dwarf clans for control of Ironforge mountain. The Bronzebeards won the mountain and drove out the other clans.",al={"what was the war of the three hammers","dwarf civil war","three hammers war"}},{q="Who was Madoran Bronzebeard?",a="Madoran Bronzebeard was King Magni Bronzebeard’s ancestor and the first Bronzebeard king to rule Ironforge after the civil war among the three dwarven clans.",al={"who is madoran bronzebeard","madoran bronzebeard","magni ancestor madoran"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can read this stone tablet as a record of reconciliation. Your ancestors set aside their feud after the mountain was contested.",["faction:Alliance"]="The historic peace between Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarves laid the foundation for their modern cooperation within the Grand Alliance."},kw={"dark iron","ironforge","madoran bronzebeard","magni bronzebeard","peace treaty","treaty of understanding","war of the three hammers","wildhammer"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf","topic:dark-iron-clan"},m={id=98423},src={"In-game quest text: The Treaty of Understanding"},fv=true}
E["quest:98424"] = {t="quest",n="Fizsprocket's Notes",z="general",s="In the Venture Co. mine, Morin Cloudstalker seeks the notebook pages still missing. They hold important information about the company's schemes in the region.",h="In the Venture Co.",sec={{t="The Missing Pages",b="Morin Cloudstalker waits at Bloodhoof Village for the pages still missing from Fizsprocket’s notebook. You have found folded pages in Fizsprocket’s pocket, and the remaining notes lie in the Venture Co. mine. Their information can guide what comes next.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What pages am I looking for?",a="You are looking for the remaining pages of Supervisor Fizsprocket’s notebook.",al={"fizsprocket notes","notebook pages","missing notes"}},{q="Where are the rest of the notes?",a="The remaining pages are in the Venture Co. mine.",al={"where pages","venture co mine","notebook location"}},{q="Who wants the pages?",a="Morin Cloudstalker is waiting for the pages at Bloodhoof Village.",al={"who needs notes","Morin request","bring pages to who"}},{q="What is in Fizsprocket’s notebook?",a="The notebook contains important information about the Venture Co. and its schemes in the region.",al={"what notes say","Fizsprocket notebook","venture co information"}}},kw={"bloodhoof village","fizsprocket","mine","morin cloudstalker","notebook","pages","venture co."},rel={"npc:morin-cloudstalker"},m={id=98424},src={"In-game quest text: Fizsprocket's Notes"},fv=true}
E["quest:98427"] = {t="quest",n="Ceasing Operations",z="general",s="Morin Cloudstalker calls on you to stop the shredder before it fells another tree. He asks you to gather allies, return to the mine in the northeast, and stop it from cutting more trees.",h="Morin Cloudstalker calls on you to stop the shredder before it fells another tree.",sec={{t="A Threat to Home",b="One of Fizsprocket's pages speaks of a shredder, and Morin has seen such machines on his travels. They can bring down a forest far faster than axes and muscle. Groves that sheltered the children of the Earth Mother for ages can vanish in days. Morin will not let that happen so close to where the young ones take their first steps. Bring the Clearcutter Key back to him outside Bloodhoof Village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Morin asking me to do?",a="Morin asks you to gather allies, return to the mine in the northeast, and stop the shredder from felling more trees.",al={"what does Morin want","Morin request","shredder task"}},{q="Why is the shredder a threat?",a="Morin says shredders can cut down a forest far faster than axes and muscle. They can destroy groves that sheltered the children of the Earth Mother.",al={"why stop shredder","shredder danger","what can it do"}},{q="Where does Morin want me to go?",a="Morin asks you to return to the mine in the northeast.",al={"where is the mine","northeast mine","where return"}},{q="What do I bring back to Morin?",a="Bring the Clearcutter Key to Morin Cloudstalker outside Bloodhoof Village.",al={"what item Morin","Clearcutter Key","key for Morin"}},{q="Who is Morin Cloudstalker?",a="Morin Cloudstalker asks you to stop the shredder from cutting trees near the tauren home.",al={"who is Morin","Morin Cloudstalker","Morin guy"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Morin's concern for the groves that sheltered the children of the Earth Mother and for the safety of the young near home."},kw={"bloodhoof village","children of the earth mother","clearcutter key","mine","morin cloudstalker","northeast","shredder","trees"},rel={"npc:morin-cloudstalker"},m={id=98427},src={"In-game quest text: Ceasing Operations"},fv=true}
E["quest:98430"] = {t="quest",n="The Longwalkers",z="general",s="At Palemane Rock, Perith Stormhoof is trapped after a peace effort with the gnolls turned violent. Cairne Bloodhoof sent the scout, and his safe return matters to the Tauren people.",h="At Palemane Rock, Perith Stormhoof is trapped after a peace effort with the gnolls turned violent.",sec={{t="A Scout in Danger",b="Cairne Bloodhoof sent Perith Stormhoof to meet the gnolls settled here. Perith is one of Cairne’s Longwalkers, so he cannot speak of the full mission. The attempt at peace turned violent, and he fears the gnolls will eat him if he stays through the night. You are asked to help him escape Palemane Rock and report his safety to Cairne in Thunder Bluff.",sp=0},{t="Cairne’s Thanks",b="Cairne is relieved that Perith is safe. He calls the scout his most trusted and says the mission is greatly important. Cairne thanks you for risking your life to save Perith. You have done the Tauren people a greater service than you know.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Perith Stormhoof?",a="Perith Stormhoof is one of Cairne Bloodhoof’s Longwalkers, the chieftain’s scouts.",al={"perith who","stormhoof scout","longwalker guy"}},{q="Why is Perith at Palemane Rock?",a="Cairne sent Perith to meet the gnolls settled there, though Perith cannot discuss the full mission.",al={"why perith there","palemane rock","perith mission"}},{q="What happened to the peace effort?",a="The gnolls answered the Longwalkers’ attempt at peace with violence, leaving Perith in danger.",al={"gnolls peace","why is perith trapped","peace with gnolls"}},{q="What does Cairne ask me to do?",a="You are asked to help Perith escape Palemane Rock and tell Cairne in Thunder Bluff that he is safe.",al={"help perith","stormhoof task","get him out"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you are helping Cairne Bloodhoof’s trusted scout. His mission matters to the Tauren people."},kw={"cairne bloodhoof","gnolls","longwalkers","palemane rock","peace effort","perith stormhoof","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=98430},src={"In-game quest text: The Longwalkers"},fv=true}
E["quest:98435"] = {t="quest",n="Thunderhorn's Report",z="general",s="Mull Thunderhorn sends you to carry his report to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. The elders need to hear what your help has accomplished.",h="Mull Thunderhorn sends you to carry his report to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="The Report",b="Mull Thunderhorn’s report concerns the springs of Mulgore. Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is on the Elder Rise in eastern Thunder Bluff, where those waters sustain the tauren and the animals they rely on for food, clothing, and companionship.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who needs Thunderhorn’s report?",a="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff needs Thunderhorn’s report.",al={"who gets the report","report for Hamuul","thunderhorn report"}},{q="Where is Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Hamuul is on the Elder Rise in eastern Thunder Bluff.",al={"where is Hamuul","Hamuul location","find Hamuul"}},{q="Why does the report matter?",a="Mulgore’s springs support the tauren and the animals they rely on for food, clothing, and companionship.",al={"why report matters","what are the springs for","Mulgore springs"}},{q="What does Hamuul say about the springs?",a="Hamuul says the springs sustain both the tauren and the animals they depend on.",al={"Hamuul says what","springs and animals","what did Hamuul say"}}},kw={"elder rise","hamuul runetotem","mulgore","report","springs","tauren","thunder bluff","thunderhorn"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={id=98435},src={"In-game quest text: Thunderhorn's Report"},fv=true}
E["quest:98459"] = {t="quest",n="A Lack of Virtue",z="general",s="Tom Half-fish sends a parcel across the sea to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor. Their old quarrel over cards and the Maiden's Virtue now reaches a traveler carrying it.",h="Tom Half-fish sends a parcel across the sea to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Bitter Grudge",b="Tom Half-fish asks you to carry a parcel across the water to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor. The delivery is meant to sting his former companion. Tom says Bart is no true sea dog, but an actor who cheated at cards to buy his command.",sp=0},{t="Cards on the Table",b="When Tom's Gift reaches Bart Tidewater on the docks of Menethil Harbor, Bart rages at the mention of his old associate. He says Tom cheated at cards, and that he bought the Maiden's Virtue only after their poker circle banished Half-fish. Soon Bart catches himself. He apologizes for snapping at the courier and welcomes you to the harbor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bart Tidewater?",a="Bart Tidewater calls himself captain of the Maiden's Virtue, docked in Menethil Harbor. Tom Half-fish says Bart was an actor who bought the ship with poker winnings, though each man accuses the other of cheating.",al={"who is bart tidewater","bart tidewater lore","who is captain of the maidens virtue"}},{q="Who is Tom Half-fish?",a="Tom Half-fish is an old acquaintance of Bart Tidewater who gives travelers a gift to carry across the sea to Bart. He bears a fierce grudge against the captain and calls him a fraud, a cheapskate, and a card cheat.",al={"who is half-fish","who is tom half-fish","who gives a lack of virtue"}},{q="What is the Maiden's Virtue?",a="The Maiden's Virtue is a vessel docked in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Bart calls it the finest ship in the Great Sea, while Tom claims it has sailed only as far as a rock in Tanaris.",al={"what is the maidens virtue","maidens virtue ship","where is the maidens virtue"}},{q="What is Tom's Gift?",a="Tom's Gift is a package Tom Half-fish sends to Bart Tidewater in Menethil Harbor. The courier does not know what's inside, but its arrival prompts Bart to angrily accuse Tom of cheating at poker.",al={"what is toms gift","what is inside toms gift","why does bart get mad at toms gift"}},{q="Who actually cheated at poker?",a="Both sailors accuse the other of cheating. Tom Half-fish says Bart was an actor who cheated at poker to win enough for his ship. Bart says he won it honestly after expelling Tom from their poker circle for cheating.",al={"who cheated at poker","did bart cheat at poker","did tom cheat at poker"}},{q="How do you deliver the gift to Menethil Harbor?",a="You can reach Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands by ship across the Great Sea. Tom says a direct boat service stops at the harbor on its second stop.",al={"how do i get to menethil harbor","boat to menethil harbor"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler passing through Menethil Harbor, you may find Bart Tidewater barking orders at his crew. The delivery makes a quick detour while you wait for transport across the Great Sea."},kw={"a lack of virtue","bart tidewater","maidens virtue","menethil harbor","poker","tanaris","tom half-fish","toms gift","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:tanaris"},m={id=98459},src={"In-game quest text: A Lack of Virtue"},fv=true}
E["quest:98461"] = {t="quest",n="Unrequited Love",z="general",s="In Auberdine, Hollee sends a personal note across the sea to Tarrel Rockweaver, the classmate she still loves.",h="In Auberdine, Hollee sends a personal note across the sea to Tarrel Rockweaver, the classmate she still loves.",sec={{t="A Message Across the Sea",b="Hollee watches travelers board ships in Auberdine, the port town on Darkshore’s coast. She hopes one bound for the Eastern Kingdoms will carry her message to Tarrel Rockweaver. They studied excavation together for years. Then graduation sent them to opposite continents.",sp=0},{t="Unspoken Feelings",b="Hollee recalls Tarrel’s sharp mind and skill with excavation, but falters when she speaks of his wife, Merrin. Though Tarrel is married and far away, Hollee entrusts you with a personal letter. She asks you to find him near Menethil Harbor and make sure he is safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Unrequited Love?",a="Hollee asks travelers in Auberdine, on Darkshore’s coast, to carry a personal note to Tarrel Rockweaver, her former schoolmate. A boat sails from there to Menethil Harbor.",al={"who gives unrequited love","quest giver auberdine"}},{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is an excavator and Hollee’s former schoolmate. After their studies, he was sent to the Wetlands, where he works near Menethil Harbor with his wife, Merrin.",al={"who is tarrel rockweaver","tarrel lore"}},{q="Who is Merrin?",a="Merrin is Tarrel Rockweaver’s wife. Hollee hesitates and furrows her brow when she mentions her, though Hollee still loves Tarrel.",al={"who is merrin","tarrels wife"}},{q="Why is the quest called Unrequited Love?",a="Hollee still loves Tarrel Rockweaver, though he married Merrin. Their years studying excavation together ended with Hollee pining for him in Auberdine, across the sea.",al={"what is unrequited love quest about","why is it called unrequited love"}},{q="Where is Tarrel Rockweaver located?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is near Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, across the Great Sea from Darkshore. A passenger boat carries you from Auberdine to the harbor docks.",al={"where to find tarrel rockweaver","tarrel location wetlands"}},{q="What item is delivered in this quest?",a="You carry Hollee’s Note to Tarrel Rockweaver in the Wetlands, to check on his well-being and deliver her personal message.",al={"what do you deliver","hollees letter"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can sail from Auberdine in Darkshore to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, crossing from Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know excavation connects Hollee and Tarrel to a trade central to dwarven tradition and study across Azeroth."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","excavation","hollee","hollee's note","menethil harbor","merrin","tarrel rockweaver","unrequited love","wetlands"},rel={"npc:tarrel-rockweaver","subzone:auberdine","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore","zone:wetlands"},m={id=98461},src={"In-game quest text: Unrequited Love"},fv=true}
E["quest:98512"] = {t="quest",n="Al'Aketh Assassins",z="general",s="A scout asks you to end the Al'Aketh Assassins' deadly threat. Your survival and aid will be recorded for Valanaar.",h="A scout asks you to end the Al'Aketh Assassins' deadly threat.",sec={{t="A Deadly Threat",b="Scouts in the field call the Al'Aketh assassins stone-cold killers. They move together with ruthless purpose, putting nearby scouts and travelers in grave danger. You face a perilous fight before they can strike their targets.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Valanaar",b="After the Al'Aketh force is defeated, the scout is relieved to find you alive. Your timely aid will go into an official report for Valanaar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Al'Aketh Assassins?",a="You are asked to eliminate a lethal force of Al'Aketh operatives. A scout will record your aid in a report for Valanaar.",al={"what is alaketh assassins","what is this quest","alaketh assassins quest"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh assassins?",a="Scouts call the Al'Aketh assassins stone-cold killers. They work together as a dangerous strike force.",al={"who are alaketh","who are the alaketh assassins","alaketh killers"}},{q="Who is Valanaar?",a="Valanaar is a settlement at the island's southeastern edge and a base for its peacekeepers. The scout plans to report your aid there.",al={"who is valanaar","what is valanaar","reporting to valanaar"}},{q="Why must the Al'Aketh assassins be dealt with?",a="The Al'Aketh assassins threaten scouts and travelers in the area. Defeating them protects allied forces from their lethal attacks.",al={"why fight alaketh","why kill alaketh assassins","alaketh threat"}},{q="What happens after dealing with the assassins?",a="After the fight, the scout prepares to report to Valanaar and record your aid.",al={"what happens after alaketh assassins","next quest alaketh","report to valanaar quest"}},{q="Who acknowledges your aid in defeating the assassins?",a="A scout in the field acknowledges your help against the Al'Aketh assassins and notes your contribution for command.",al={"who gives alaketh assassins","who is the scout","scout report valanaar"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know the focus and precision it takes to face lethal killers like the Al'Aketh."},kw={"al'aketh","assassins","killers","quest","report","valanaar"},rel={"quest:92880","quest:92579"},m={id=98512},src={"In-game quest text: Al'Aketh Assassins"},fv=true}
E["quest:98545"] = {t="quest",n="Leonid's Letter",z="general",s="In Undercity, a sealed message from Leonid's Letter awaits delivery to Glix Xizzix. Leonid keeps away because of his strained past with Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, and entrusts the message to a neutral traveler bound for his old goblin acquaintance in the Trade Quarter.",h="In Undercity, a sealed message from Leonid's Letter awaits delivery to Glix Xizzix.",sec={{t="An Outsider's Errand",b="Leonid asks you to carry a sealed letter to an acquaintance in Undercity. Past friction with Lady Sylvanas Windrunner keeps him from entering the Forsaken capital himself. So he trusts a neutral traveler to pass the city's guards without raising alarm.",sp=0},{t="Old Comrades in the Trade Quarter",b="Glix Xizzix does business in Undercity's Trade Quarter. The message recalls the time he and Leonid survived together beneath the Scourge citadel Naxxramas. Leonid promised compensation, to Glix's surprise and annoyance. So the goblin reluctantly pays with lost-and-found items left behind by careless undead customers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Leonid and why won't he enter Undercity?",a="Leonid is an experienced soldier with delicate ties to various factions. His complicated past with Lady Sylvanas Windrunner keeps him from entering Undercity, so he relies on wandering adventurers to carry messages to his acquaintances.",al={"who gives leonid letter","leonid barthalomew","leonid quest giver"}},{q="Who is Glix Xizzix?",a="Glix Xizzix is a goblin in Undercity's Trade Quarter. He appears to work near grooming services and keeps lost-and-found items left behind by absent-minded undead patrons.",al={"where is glix xizzix","who is glix xizzix","undercity goblin barber"}},{q="What is Leonid's history with the Dark Lady?",a="Leonid has what he calls a somewhat colorful history with Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen of the Forsaken. He uses neutral couriers for his business in Undercity to avoid provoking her or her guards.",al={"leonid dark lady history","leonid and sylvanas"}},{q="How do Leonid and Glix know each other?",a="Glix remembers Leonid from their military struggles against the Scourge. He recalls the dread citadel Naxxramas raining destruction upon them.",al={"glix xizzix leonid naxxramas","how do glix and leonid know each other"}},{q="Why does Glix reward you with lost-and-found items?",a="Leonid told the courier that Glix would gladly pay a tip, though Glix had made no such promise. The goblin grudgingly offers odd trinkets from the salon's lost and found, left by forgetful Forsaken customers.",al={"quest reward glix","why lost and found"}},{q="Where is the letter delivered?",a="The letter goes to Undercity, the Forsaken capital, and into its Trade Quarter. Merchants, artisans, and goblins do business there under the watchful eyes of the Royal Apothecary Society and the city guards.",al={"where to deliver leonid letter","trade quarter delivery"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you see how Leonid's history with the Dark Lady keeps him from entering Undercity himself, reflecting tensions between independent undead and Sylvanas's loyalists.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you can enter Undercity's Trade Quarter amenities while carrying a message for an outsider."},kw={"dark lady","glix xizzix","leonid","lost and found","naxxramas","sealed letter","sylvanas","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","topic:forsaken","topic:goblin"},m={id=98545},src={"In-game quest text: Leonid's Letter"},fv=true}
E["quest:98574"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Memorandum",z="general",s="At Anvilmar, young gnome priests are summoned to study the Holy Light through the Hallowed Memorandum. It sends them to Branstock Khalder in Coldridge Valley, where curiosity and intellect meet a faith to ponder.",h="At Anvilmar, young gnome priests are summoned to study the Holy Light through the Hallowed Memorandum.",sec={{t="A Summons to Anvilmar",b="While you aid allies in Coldridge Valley, promising gnome novices receive the Hallowed Memorandum. It directs them to Branstock Khalder inside Anvilmar, where their formal spiritual study begins in Dun Morogh.",sp=0},{t="Puzzles of the Faith",b="Branstock Khalder welcomes each novice who brings the memorandum. He teaches that the Holy Light is a deep riddle, not a rigid craft. It calls for curiosity, keen thought, and harmony between intellect and feeling. Through contemplation and practice, students learn to channel its mysteries into healing and holy retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent the Hallowed Memorandum?",a="A local ally passes the Hallowed Memorandum to you while you help in Coldridge Valley. Branstock Khalder, the priest trainer inside Anvilmar, sent it.",al={"who gave me the memorandum","who sent hallowed memorandum","where did note come from"}},{q="Who is Branstock Khalder?",a="Branstock Khalder is a dwarven priest trainer inside Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley. He teaches young priests to understand the Light and use holy power to heal wounds or smite evil.",al={"who is branstock","branstock khalder anvilmar"}},{q="How do gnomes approach the Holy Light?",a="Branstock says gnomes can draw on curiosity and intellect to understand the Light. He urges them to ponder it as a philosophical riddle that brings thought and feeling together.",al={"can gnomes be priests","gnome connection to the light","how do gnomes view the light"}},{q="What does Branstock teach about the Light?",a="Branstock teaches that the Light is a riddle, not a rigid technical discipline. Its blessings and lessons come through joining thought with inner feeling.",al={"what is the light according to branstock","light riddle branstock"}},{q="What abilities does Branstock offer to teach?",a="As a priest begins to understand the Light, Branstock teaches how to channel it into healing prayers and holy blows against the wicked, in exchange for modest donations.",al={"what does branstock teach","what can priest trainers teach"}},{q="Where can Branstock Khalder be found?",a="You can find Branstock Khalder inside Anvilmar, the central fortress and welcoming hall in the heart of Coldridge Valley, Dun Morogh. Trainers and refuge for dwarves and visiting gnomes are found there.",al={"where is anvilmar","branstock location"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you bring curiosity and sharp intellect to the study of the Light, pondering its holy mysteries alongside your faith.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you begin formal instruction in Coldridge Valley and learn the philosophy of the Holy Light as a healer."},kw={"anvilmar","branstock khalder","coldridge valley","dun morogh","gnome priest","hallowed memorandum","holy light"},rel={"npc:branstock-khalder","subzone:anvilmar","topic:light","topic:gnome","topic:priest"},m={id=98574},src={"In-game quest text: Hallowed Memorandum"},fv=true}
E["quest:98575"] = {t="quest",n="Tainted Tablet",z="general",s="In the Valley of Trials, Tainted Tablet calls new practitioners to Nartok inside the Den. He teaches warlocks to command the Nether and shape their own fate, though its powers must be kept guarded.",h="In the Valley of Trials, Tainted Tablet calls new practitioners to Nartok inside the Den.",sec={{t="A Dark Summons",b="A stone message passes through uneasy camp caretakers to newly arrived practitioners in the Valley of Trials. Nartok, a warlock trainer who makes his home inside the Den, calls them to him. He invites you to leave ordinary tribal duties and study deeper, forbidden magic.",sp=0},{t="Commanding the Nether",b="Nartok speaks plainly about the troubled history between orcs and the Nether. He says the strong should command these volatile powers instead of rejecting them from shame or fear. Where ordinary chieftains falter, he believes those who cunningly master Nether entities can rise to prominence. Yet fearful minds strike at what they cannot understand, so these powers must be guarded closely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Tablet?",a="Tainted Tablet is a written summons for an aspiring practitioner in the Valley of Trials. It directs you to Nartok, your trainer inside the Den.",al={"what is tainted tablet","tainted tablet quest","tablet purpose"}},{q="Who sent the Tainted Tablet?",a="Nartok sent Tainted Tablet. He is an orc warlock trainer inside the Den in the Valley of Trials, and calls newly arrived practitioners to instruction.",al={"who wrote the tablet","who is nartok","who sent the tablet"}},{q="Where can Nartok be found?",a="Nartok lives inside the Den, a cavern in the Valley of Trials where darker arts and specialized training take place out of sight.",al={"where is nartok","where is the den","how to find nartok"}},{q="Why does Nartok warn to guard your powers closely?",a="Nartok warns you to guard your powers because ordinary folk may lash out in fear at what they do not understand. Orcs also remember the deep harm demonic corruption caused in their past, so warlocks keep their arts guarded and tread carefully.",al={"why hide warlocks","why guard powers","why secrecy warlocks"}},{q="What is Nartok's view on practicing fel magic?",a="Nartok believes those who master Nether entities can forge their own path and shape their people's fate. Where conventional leaders falter, warlocks can seize power instead of being enslaved by it.",al={"what is nartoks goal","nartok philosophy","why use nether powers"}},{q="Who gives you the Tainted Tablet?",a="A local in the Valley of Trials passes you the tablet. They admit unease with fel spellcasters, but know Nartok's summons must be delivered.",al={"who delivered the tablet","who handed me the tablet"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you receive your first call to Nartok, your trainer in Durotar. He urges you to master the Nether instead of fearing it.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know demonic pacts brought catastrophe to Draenor. Fel magic remains controversial, so Durotar's warlocks counsel both secrecy and boldness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Thrall's new people are wary of demonic corruption. Warlocks in places like the Den say they can command Nether powers safely and secure their people's future."},kw={"durotar","nartok","nether","tainted tablet","the den","valley of trials","warlock"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={id=98575},src={"In-game quest text: Tainted Tablet"},fv=true}
E["quest:98581"] = {t="quest",n="Archaic Rune",z="general",s="In Coldridge Valley, young dwarf Shamans begin learning the elements through an ancient rune. It leads them to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar for instruction in earth, air, fire, and water.",h="In Coldridge Valley, young dwarf Shamans begin learning the elements through an ancient rune.",sec={{t="An Ancient Inscription",b="Near Anvilmar, you find the Archaic Rune after aiding local allies in Coldridge Valley. Its markings follow the Wildhammer style, and elemental power courses through the stone. The inscription tests whether you can sense the primordial spirits. Read it, and the rune directs you to proper instruction at the nearby dwarven outpost.",sp=0},{t="Wildhammer Wisdom in Dun Morogh",b="In Anvilmar’s great hall, Teo Hammerstorm receives the inscribed stone. For generations, the Wildhammer kept the spiritual arts of the elements largely within their clan among the windswept peaks. Now these traditions are taking root among the Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge and Dun Morogh. Teo bridges the two dwarven cultures, welcoming young initiates called to commune with the elements and teaching them earth, air, fire, and water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Archaic Rune?",a="The Archaic Rune is an ancient stone tablet marked with old Wildhammer script and elemental power. Promising newcomers in Coldridge Valley receive it as their first test of spiritual potential. Reading it confirms an initiate’s calling to the shamanic path and points them to the trainer in Anvilmar.",al={"archaic rune quest","what is this rune","archaic rune item"}},{q="Who carved the Archaic Rune?",a="The Archaic Rune bears inscriptions in the traditional style of the Wildhammer clan. Teo Hammerstorm, a Wildhammer shaman in Anvilmar, sent it to find new initiates with an innate connection to the elemental spirits.",al={"who made the archaic rune","rune origin","wildhammer rune maker"}},{q="Who is Teo Hammerstorm?",a="Teo Hammerstorm is a Wildhammer dwarf and shaman trainer in Anvilmar, in Coldridge Valley. He has traveled to Dun Morogh to share his clan’s ancestral shamanic teachings with the Bronzebeard dwarves, guiding new practitioners in earth, fire, water, and air.",al={"who is teo hammerstorm","teo hammerstorm anvilmar","shaman trainer anvilmar"}},{q="Why are Wildhammer teachings being shared with Bronzebeard dwarves?",a="The Wildhammer kept the shamanic arts largely within their clan for many years. Now Bronzebeard dwarves practice those elemental ways too. Mentors such as Teo Hammerstorm teach Ironforge dwarves to commune with and honor the elemental spirits.",al={"why are dwarves shamans","bronzebeard wildhammer shaman","dwarf shaman lore"}},{q="Where do I take the Archaic Rune?",a="Bring the rune to Teo Hammerstorm inside Anvilmar’s main lodge in Coldridge Valley. Presenting it shows you can channel the elements and opens further training in fundamental shamanic spells.",al={"where to turn in archaic rune","archaic rune turn in","find teo hammerstorm"}},{q="What does reading the rune signify?",a="The Archaic Rune holds elemental energy and bears ancient dwarven script. Only an initiate attuned to the elemental forces can read it. Success confirms an adventurer’s calling to the shamanic path and readiness to become a shaman.",al={"why can i read the rune","rune meaning","reading the archaic rune"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, the Archaic Rune marks the first step in your spiritual journey. It confirms your elemental attunement and introduces you to your primary mentor.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the Archaic Rune mark an exchange between clans. The Wildhammer share their ancient spiritual traditions with their Bronzebeard kin in Coldridge Valley.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Wildhammer mentors bring shamanic arts to Dun Morogh, adding elemental traditions alongside the Holy Light."},kw={"anvilmar","archaic rune","bronzebeard","coldridge valley","elements","shaman","teo hammerstorm","wildhammer clan"},rel={"topic:wildhammer-clan","subzone:anvilmar"},m={id=98581},src={"In-game quest text: Archaic Rune"},fv=true}
E["quest:98731"] = {t="quest",n="Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit",z="general",s="After the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing, you are told to return to Dendrite. He senses new cunning and ferocity in you, and says you can now learn to call upon the cat’s spirit.",h="After the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing, you are told to return to Dendrite.",sec={{t="Dendrite’s Reading",b="Dendrite greets you with a gesture in the air, and an aura of power comes over him. He senses the cat’s cunning and ferocity in you, along with a new understanding of stealth and speed. Now he can teach you to focus that nature and call upon the cat’s spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Dendrite want to see me?",a="After the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing, you are told to return to Dendrite, who will instruct you further.",al={"why return to Dendrite","Dendrite cat blessing","what does Dendrite want"}},{q="What does Dendrite sense in me?",a="He senses the cat’s cunning and ferocity, and believes you understand the stealth and speed needed to adopt its nature.",al={"what changed in me","cat spirit power","Dendrite senses what"}},{q="What can I learn from Dendrite now?",a="Dendrite says you can learn to focus your cunning and call upon the cat’s spirit.",al={"call cat spirit","learn cat nature","what next with Dendrite"}}},kw={"blessing","cat spirit","cunning","dendrite","ferocity","great cat spirit","speed","stealth"},rel={"quest:98393"},m={id=98731},src={"In-game quest text: Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98738"] = {t="quest",n="Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit",z="general",s="After meeting the Great Cat Spirit of Zephras, an initiate returns to Dendrite with a newly awakened aura. The blessing brings the wild cat's stealth, speed, and ferocity, and Dendrite prepares the initiate for further instruction.",h="After meeting the Great Cat Spirit of Zephras, an initiate returns to Dendrite with a newly awakened aura.",sec={{t="Communion with the Windborne Spirit",b="An initiate returns to Dendrite after seeking the Great Cat Spirit of Zephras and earning its favor. The communion has awakened the wild cat's cunning, predatory stealth, and ferocity within them.",sp=0},{t="Dendrite's Instruction",b="Dendrite reads the initiate's newly awakened aura with subtle gestures. Sensing feline instincts woven into their spirit, he sees that the initiate is ready to focus their mind and call upon the true aspect of the cat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit?",a="An initiate who has received the Great Cat Spirit's blessing returns to Dendrite to continue their spiritual communion.",al={"what is this quest","blessings of the cat quest","cat spirit quest"}},{q="Who is Dendrite?",a="Dendrite mentors initiates and sends them to commune with the Great Cat Spirit. When they return, his ritual gestures let him sense whether they have absorbed the stealth, speed, and cunning needed to channel feline nature.",al={"who is dendrite","dendrite lore"}},{q="Who is the Great Cat Spirit?",a="The Great Cat Spirit is an ancient patron in Zephras. It grants worthy initiates spiritual favor, the speed of the winds, and predatory stealth before they return to their instruction.",al={"what is the cat spirit","great windborne cat spirit"}},{q="Where is Zephras located?",a="Zephras is the Great Cat Spirit's home. Promising initiates travel there to seek its counsel, receive its blessings of wind and shadow, and learn the foundations of the feline form.",al={"where is zephras","cat spirit location"}},{q="Why does the spirit address the initiate as shen'dorei?",a="The Great Cat Spirit addresses the initiate as young shen'dorei, recognizing the practitioner's ancestral heritage as they seek communion with nature spirits and mastery of feral shapeshifting.",al={"who are shendorei","young shendorei"}},{q="What does the blessing of the cat spirit grant?",a="The blessing grants the cunning, speed, and stealth of the feline form. It also earns the initiate Dendrite's recognition, so they can focus their inner ferocity and call upon the true nature of the cat.",al={"what does the blessing give","cat spirit blessing effect"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, this rite marks a milestone in mastering feline predatory instinct. It grants the stealth, speed, and ferocity needed to commune with and assume the aspect of the cat.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, the Great Cat Spirit recognizes you as young shen'dorei. Its guidance from Zephras teaches you to harness feral power through wind and shadow."},kw={"blessings of the great windborne cat spirit","cat form","dendrite","druid","great cat spirit","shen'dorei","stealth","zephras"},rel={"quest:98393"},m={id=98738},src={"In-game quest text: Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98739"] = {t="quest",n="Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit",z="general",s="Dendrite asks you to return after receiving the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing. He senses a new cunning and ferocity in you, and says you can now learn to call upon the cat’s spirit.",h="Dendrite asks you to return after receiving the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing.",sec={{t="Return to Dendrite",b="After the Great Cat Spirit’s blessing, Dendrite asks you to return to him. When you arrive, he gestures above you and senses the cat’s cunning and ferocity in your eyes. He says you now understand the stealth and speed needed to take on this nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who do I speak to?",a="Return to Dendrite and speak with him.",al={"who do i talk to","speak to who"}},{q="What blessing did I receive?",a="You have received the blessing of the Great Cat Spirit.",al={"great cat blessing","cat spirit blessing"}},{q="What does Dendrite sense in me?",a="Dendrite senses the cat’s cunning and ferocity in you, along with an understanding of its stealth and speed.",al={"what does dendrite see","cat nature"}},{q="What can I learn now?",a="Dendrite says you can now learn to focus your cunning and call upon the cat’s spirit.",al={"call cat spirit","what now"}}},kw={"blessing","blessings of the great cat spirit","cunning","dendrite","ferocity","great cat spirit","speed","stealth"},rel={"quest:98393"},m={id=98739},src={"In-game quest text: Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit"},fv=true}
E["quest:98815"] = {t="quest",n="Highland Hides",z="general",s="In the Highlands, Thicket Raptors offer tough hides for James Halloran’s leatherwork. The tanner in Menethil Harbor trades crafted goods for their skins.",h="In the Highlands, Thicket Raptors offer tough hides for James Halloran’s leatherwork.",sec={{t="A Tanner's Opportunity",b="From his workshop in Menethil Harbor, James Halloran seeks rare materials for his craft. Word reaches him of an expedition exploring forgotten ruins in the Highlands. He turns his attention to the beasts roaming the mountain marshes. Their hides suit his work, so he hires travelers to bring back fine pelts from the misty peaks.",sp=0},{t="Beasts of the Highlands",b="Thicket Raptors prowl the rugged marshes of the Highlands. Their tough, textured skins suit specialized leatherwork. Halloran asks travelers to hunt these predators and return with four intact hides. He uses them for fine details and decorative trim in his workshop’s creations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a tanner and craftsman in Menethil Harbor. He works with leather and oils, seeking fine skins from exotic beasts across the Wetlands and surrounding highlands for trim and armor.",al={"who gives highland hides","who is james halloran","tanner in menethil"}},{q="Why does James Halloran need these hides?",a="Halloran wants Thicket Raptor hides for their durability and texture. He uses them to add fine details to leatherwork trim.",al={"what are highland hides for","why does james want raptor hides","purpose of raptor hides"}},{q="Where can Thicket Raptors be found?",a="Thicket Raptors live in the mountainous marshlands of the Highlands, near forgotten ruins an expedition is exploring.",al={"where are thicket raptors","thicket raptor location","where are the raptors"}},{q="What ruins is Halloran referring to?",a="An expedition team is investigating forgotten ruins in the Highlands. Halloran focuses on the wildlife while scholars and explorers investigate the area’s ancient secrets.",al={"what ruins in highlands","highlands expedition ruins","who is exploring highlands"}},{q="Is this hunt intended for a group?",a="Halloran recommends traveling with well-equipped companions. Fierce wildlife makes the mountain marshlands dangerous for anyone traveling alone.",al={"is highland hides dangerous","group needed highland hides","do i need friends for highland hides"}},{q="What does James Halloran offer in trade?",a="Halloran offers leatherwork from his workshop in exchange for four Thicket Raptor hides. Travelers can choose a piece suited to their journeys.",al={"what does halloran trade","highland hides reward lore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find tradesmen like James Halloran in Menethil Harbor, a key port in the Wetlands. They equip travelers heading into the dangerous marshlands nearby.",["class:Hunter"]="As a Hunter, you can track formidable beasts such as Thicket Raptors in the Highlands’ mountain marshes. Their tough hides call for precise tracking and a clean hunt."},kw={"highland hides","highlands","james halloran","menethil harbor","raptor hides","tanner","thicket raptor","wetlands"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={id=98815},src={"In-game quest text: Highland Hides"},fv=true}
E["quest:98823"] = {t="quest",n="Earthen Echo",z="general",s="The Earthen Ring asks you to bring a strange Titan Relic to Muln Earthfury in northwest Mulgore. Its carvings may hold wisdom about buried ruins and forgotten lands.",h="The Earthen Ring asks you to bring a strange Titan Relic to Muln Earthfury in northwest Mulgore.",sec={{t="A Relic for the Elders",b="An unnamed observer sees the Titan Relic as more than a carving and urges you to take it to Muln Earthfury. You can find him with the Earthen Ring council at Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore. The elders may study it, for its meaning could touch buried ruins and forgotten lands.",sp=0},{t="The Shard's Memory",b="At Skywatcher Plateau, Muln Earthfury finds that the shard carries a voice like the world's own. Light within it holds memories and flashes of history. The Earthen Ring will guard and study the titan machine, then share what it reveals when they can understand its messages.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who should I bring the Titan Relic to?",a="Bring the Titan Relic to Muln Earthfury, who is with the Earthen Ring council at Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore.",al={"who gets the relic","Muln Earthfury relic","where to take titan relic"}},{q="Why does the relic matter?",a="It appears to be more than a carving, and the Earthen Ring may find wisdom in it about buried ruins and forgotten lands.",al={"what is this relic","titan relic meaning","weird carving"}},{q="Where is Muln Earthfury?",a="Muln Earthfury and the other Earthen Ring elders are at Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore.",al={"Muln location","skywatcher plateau","where is earthen ring"}},{q="What will the Earthen Ring do with the relic?",a="The Earthen Ring will safeguard and study the relic, and share its messages when they are able to understand them.",al={"what happens to shard","earthen ring study","relic after delivery"}}},kw={"earthen echo","earthen ring","mulgore","muln earthfury","shard","skywatcher plateau","titan machine","titan relic"},rel={"quest:95349","zone:mulgore","topic:titan"},m={id=98823},src={"In-game quest text: Earthen Echo"},fv=true}
E["quest:98895"] = {t="quest",n="Darkspear Islands Clash",z="general",s="Across the Darkspear Islands, Alliance forces are hard pressed. Without help at the front, they risk losing the whole archipelago to the fierce Darkspear Raiders.",h="Across the Darkspear Islands, Alliance forces are hard pressed.",sec={{t="A Contested Front",b="Open war now rages across the Darkspear Islands between the Alliance and the aggressive Darkspear Raiders. Alliance commanders fear their foothold in the archipelago will be overwhelmed without urgent reinforcements. So they call capable champions to the front to stem the attack.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Valor",b="Alliance commanders need proven fighters willing to serve on the front lines. Warriors bring back Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor as proof of their service. The marks uphold discipline and honor those whose courage turns the battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkspear Islands Clash?",a="Alliance officers overseeing the fighting call champions to face the Darkspear Raiders. Warriors prove their service by recovering marks of honor from the battle.",al={"what is darkspear islands clash","clash quest","darkspear islands battle"}},{q="Who are the Darkspear Raiders?",a="The Darkspear Raiders are troll warbands fighting for control of the Darkspear Islands. Their fierce attacks threaten Alliance footholds and prompt urgent calls for reinforcements.",al={"who are darkspear raiders","darkspear raider enemy","who are we fighting in darkspear islands"}},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting on the Darkspear Islands?",a="The Alliance fights to hold strategic ground in the Darkspear Islands and keep the region from falling under troll control. Losing ground would weaken Alliance influence and security across the contested coastal waters.",al={"why alliance fighting darkspear islands","why fight here","alliance darkspear war"}},{q="Who issues and completes this mission?",a="An Alliance Brigadier General stationed outside the battlegrounds oversees troop mobilization and receives returning champions' proof of battlefield service.",al={"who gives darkspear islands clash","who takes darkspear marks of honor","alliance brigadier general location"}},{q="What are Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor?",a="Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor are military tokens for valor and active service on the front line. Warriors present three marks to an Alliance Brigadier General as proof of their service in battle.",al={"what are marks of honor","darkspear islands mark of honor","how to prove front line service"}},{q="What is at stake if the Alliance fails?",a="Without rapid reinforcements, relentless Darkspear Raider attacks could bring Alliance positions on the Darkspear Islands to complete collapse. Holding the islands keeps hostile forces from claiming unchallenged dominance over the archipelago.",al={"what happens if alliance loses darkspear islands","why urgent aid needed","losing darkspear islands"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance high command calls champion volunteers to reinforce the front against the Darkspear Raiders and protect strategic positions in the islands.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you bear the brunt of the assault against fierce troll raiders. Your discipline and valor can turn the tide of battle.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you bring resolve to the violent clashes, answering the Alliance call to protect its people and repel hostile forces."},kw={"alliance","battleground","brigadier general","darkspear islands","darkspear islands clash","darkspear raiders","marks of honor"},rel={"zone:darkspearislands","topic:alliance"},m={id=98895},src={"In-game quest text: Darkspear Islands Clash"},fv=true}
E["quest:98896"] = {t="quest",n="Darkspear Islands Clash",z="general",s="Fighting rages across the Darkspear Islands Clash as Darkspear Raiders contest the archipelago. Fighters are called to rally their companions and stop enemy incursions across the islands.",h="Fighting rages across the Darkspear Islands Clash as Darkspear Raiders contest the archipelago.",sec={{t="The Archipelago at War",b="Darkspear Raiders skirmish across the beaches and interior of the islands. Forces sent there are urged to hold their ground as the campaign to secure a foothold in the archipelago continues.",sp=0},{t="Rallying the Front Line",b="Commanders on the front line call for fighters to gather against the resilient raiders. Survival and victory depend on rallying nearby allies into a force that can withstand counterattacks. Together, they can rout fortified raiding bands and break their hold on the disputed island strongholds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Darkspear Islands Clash?",a="Fighters are called to rally their allies and attack the Darkspear Raiders amid ongoing fighting across the Darkspear Islands.",al={"what is this quest","darkspear islands clash summary","clash quest info"}},{q="Where does this fight take place?",a="The fighting takes place across the Darkspear Islands, an archipelago marked by territorial struggles and clashes at sea.",al={"where does this happen","where are darkspear islands","clash location"}},{q="Who are the Darkspear Raiders?",a="The Darkspear Raiders are the Horde's troll defenders of the Darkspear Islands, the sacred isles of Vol'jin's tribe. Combatants are ordered to defeat them as they contest territory across the islands.",al={"who are the enemies","who do we fight","darkspear raiders target"}},{q="Why must forces be rallied for this clash?",a="Allied forces must gather to withstand sustained counterattacks and break the raiders' lines.",al={"why rally forces","what is the goal","how to complete clash"}},{q="Why does the fight in the Darkspear Islands continue?",a="The Horde and Alliance continue to struggle for the islands' strongpoints. The Horde guards them as sacred troll ground, while the Alliance seeks a foothold off Kalimdor's shore.",al={"why is there fighting","why conflict in islands","island battle cause"}},{q="Who directs the forces in this engagement?",a="The Alliance Brigadier General in the Alterac Mountains directs the forces. He urges soldiers on the ground to push forward without wavering.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver clash","clash commander"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you know the Darkspear Raiders targeted by this Alliance order are Vol'jin's own people. They defend their tribe's sacred isles.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the Alliance side of the fight for the Darkspear Islands. The Horde holds these sacred troll isles off Kalimdor's coast against outsiders."},kw={"clash","darkspear islands","darkspear raiders","islands conflict","rally","skirmish","troll raiders"},rel={"zone:darkspearislands"},m={id=98896},src={"In-game quest text: Darkspear Islands Clash"},fv=true}
E["quest:99046"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Runner",z="general",s="In Teldrassil, a courier from the Oracle Tree is overdue on the road to Darnassus. The elders rely on its messages for guidance.",h="In Teldrassil, a courier from the Oracle Tree is overdue on the road to Darnassus.",sec={{t="Messengers of the Oracle",b="The Council of the Forest keeps Sentinels at the Oracle Tree in Teldrassil. The ancient tree sends sacred messages to the night elf elders, and runners carry them along the forest roads to Darnassus. Their safe arrival guides the kaldorei and helps govern them.",sp=0},{t="An Overdue Courier",b="Silence from the Oracle Tree has lasted unusually long, and a courier has not arrived. Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow, an initiate still in training, was the latest runner sent out. Her superiors fear she has met misfortune on the trail, so they direct travelers west toward the Oracle Glade to search for her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the lost runner?",a="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow is the missing runner, a night elf sentinel still in training. She was sent to carry a message from the Oracle Tree to Darnassus.",al={"who is the lost runner","missing sentinel","who is eralya"}},{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient tree in the Oracle Glade that periodically sends messages to the night elf elders in Darnassus. Sentinels stationed there carry those messages safely.",al={"what is the oracle tree","oracle glade purpose","why messages from oracle tree"}},{q="Where was Eralya Leafshadow heading?",a="Eralya was expected on the westward road between Darnassus and the Oracle Glade. Runners use that road to carry messages from the tree.",al={"where was eralya going","eralya route","lost runner location"}},{q="Who stationed the Sentinels at the Oracle Tree?",a="The Council of the Forest stationed a detachment of Sentinels at the Oracle Tree. They carry its messages safely and swiftly to the elders in Darnassus.",al={"who sent sentinels to oracle tree","what is council of the forest"}},{q="Why is her absence a concern?",a="Messages from the Oracle Tree arrive at irregular intervals, but Eralya's absence has lasted unusually long. Her superiors are concerned because she is still a trainee.",al={"why is her delay unusual","how often does oracle send messages"}},{q="What is the objective of this search?",a="You are asked to search west along the road toward the Oracle Glade for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow and learn what delayed her.",al={"what do you do in the lost runner","lost runner quest goal"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know safe messages from the ancient Oracle Tree guide the kaldorei leadership in Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know safe roads and clear communication across Teldrassil help keep Darnassus and Alliance territory stable."},kw={"council of the forest","darnassus","eralya leafshadow","oracle glade","oracle tree","sentinels","the lost runner"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:oracle-glade","topic:sentinels","topic:elune","quest:98397"},m={id=99046},src={"In-game quest text: The Lost Runner"},fv=true}
E["quest:99047"] = {t="quest",n="Not Dead Yet",z="general",s="In Teldrassil, Eralya needs word carried to Dolanaar. Mortally wounded after a patrol toward the Oracle Tree was overwhelmed by harpies, she asks travelers to tell Byancie what became of her sisters.",h="In Teldrassil, Eralya needs word carried to Dolanaar.",sec={{t="An Ambushed Patrol",b="Eralya lies wounded in the wilderness of Teldrassil. Her patrol was ambushed while she and her sisters traveled toward the Oracle Tree. Harpies attacked and cut down the patrol. With her strength fading and no help coming, she entrusts passing travelers with carrying word back to safety.",sp=0},{t="A Cry for Dolanaar",b="Eralya asks you to bring her report to Byancie in Dolanaar. Harpies in Teldrassil's great boughs have grown bolder and more aggressive. They threaten lone messengers and sentinels on the forest paths. Byancie's village needs to hear of the ambush at the Oracle Tree before more lives are lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eralya?",a="Eralya is a night elf messenger ambushed while carrying out a mission toward the Oracle Tree. Mortally wounded and coughing blood, she asks travelers to carry word of her unit's fate.",al={"who is eralya","eralya quest","dying night elf"}},{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient landmark in Teldrassil's Oracle Glade. Eralya and her sisters were sent there with an urgent message, but harpies overwhelmed them along the way.",al={"what is oracle tree","oracle glade tree","where was eralya going"}},{q="What happened to Eralya and her patrol?",a="Harpies ambushed Eralya and her sisters in Teldrassil's boughs. The creatures overran the patrol and left Eralya mortally wounded.",al={"who attacked eralya","who ambushed her","why is eralya bleeding"}},{q="Who is Byancie?",a="Byancie is a contact in the night elf village of Dolanaar. Eralya asks you to bring her word of the harpy ambush and her patrol's plight.",al={"who is byancie","where is byancie","byancie dolanaar"}},{q="Where must Eralya's message be delivered?",a="Eralya's message is meant for Byancie in Dolanaar. The village is the primary night elf settlement on the road south of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Byancie lives there and receives reports and coordinates local defense efforts.",al={"where to bring message","eralya delivery","where is dolanaar"}},{q="What happened to the other sisters on the mission?",a="Harpies separated or killed Eralya's fellow night elf sentinels during the attack. With no reinforcements in sight, Eralya feared none of her sisters had escaped.",al={"what happened to eralyas sisters","sentinel patrol sisters"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Eralya and her sisters are Sentinels serving in Teldrassil. Harpies ambushed them near the Oracle Tree, showing the danger facing the bough.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer in Teldrassil, you may need to carry urgent word to settlements like Dolanaar when field scouts are cut off and overwhelmed."},kw={"byancie","dolanaar","eralya","harpies","not dead yet","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar"},m={id=99047},src={"In-game quest text: Not Dead Yet"},fv=true}
E["quest:99048"] = {t="quest",n="A Missing Hand",z="general",s="In Durotar, reports from Tiragarde Keep have fallen silent around Heglan Shadeeye. The Shattered Hand scout watched the human garrison occupying the keep, and now an investigator seeks her post.",h="In Durotar, reports from Tiragarde Keep have fallen silent around Heglan Shadeeye.",sec={{t="Silent Reports",b="Heglan Shadeeye's reports from Tiragarde Keep have stopped. A Shattered Hand scout, she watched the hostile human garrison occupying the keep from a post in Durotar. Her superiors doubt the soldiers detected and captured her. They fear something more dangerous may have intervened, and send you north of the keep to find her post and learn what happened.",sp=0},{t="The Cold Hut",b="At her observation post north of Tiragarde Keep, Heglan Shadeeye lies dead in the wreckage of a ruined hut. The evidence shows her attacker was not human. What creature or force struck down a trained operative so close to Horde lands?",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest A Missing Hand?",a="In Durotar, Heglan Shadeeye's sudden silence has prompted an investigation. The Shattered Hand scout's regular reports from her post north of Tiragarde Keep stopped without explanation.",al={"what is a missing hand","missing hand quest overview"}},{q="Who is Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye is a Shattered Hand operative who covertly watches Tiragarde Keep from a nearby post. Her reports have stopped, prompting an investigation into her whereabouts.",al={"who is heglan","where is heglan shadeeye","missing scout"}},{q="What happened to Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye's reports from a post north of Tiragarde Keep stopped without warning. Her superior doubts the humans caught her and fears something more dangerous may have intervened.",al={"what happened to heglan shadeeye","is heglan dead","heglan fate"}},{q="What is the Shattered Hand?",a="The Shattered Hand is the Horde's organization of subtle operatives, assassins, and spies. Its members carry out covert surveillance and intelligence work to protect Horde territories.",al={"what is shattered hand","who are the shattered hand"}},{q="Did the humans at Tiragarde Keep kill Heglan?",a="Heglan's superior doubts the humans caught her. She watched the hostile Kul Tiras humans at Tiragarde Keep, but the one who sends you fears something more dangerous may have intervened.",al={"did humans kill heglan","did tiragarde soldiers kill her"}},{q="Why was Tiragarde Keep being watched?",a="Heglan watched Tiragarde Keep, an outpost of hostile Kul Tiras sailors and soldiers threatening Durotar's coast. She kept watch nearby and relayed intelligence to the Horde.",al={"why was heglan watching tiragarde keep","tiragarde keep surveillance"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know the Shattered Hand as the Horde's covert backbone and intelligence guild. A vanished operative shows the danger of field surveillance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that watching the Kul Tiras remnants at Tiragarde Keep matters to Durotar's security. A scout's unexplained silence signals a possible threat near Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know Durotar as newly secured orcish territory. A scout going silent within sight of nearby human squatters raises alarm for the realm's safety."},kw={"a missing hand","durotar","heglan shadeeye","rogue","scout","shattered hand","tiragarde keep"},rel={"quest:1858","subzone:tiragarde-keep","topic:human"},m={id=99048},src={"In-game quest text: A Missing Hand"},fv=true}
E["quest:99049"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="general",s="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, Threat from Below begins with an ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye. The Horde searches her ruined post for clues to the attackers and what they find puts Razor Hill’s defenses at risk.",h="Along Durotar’s eastern shore, Threat from Below begins with an ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye.",sec={{t="Ambush on the Durotar Coast",b="Heglan Shadeeye’s post on the Durotar coast lies shattered after a fierce skirmish. A Shattered Hand scout, she was keeping watch when an unseen enemy ambushed her. The wreckage shows she fought back and wounded her attackers. With hostile forces moving along the eastern shore, the Horde needs to learn who struck her. You search the campsite and nearby ground for clues.",sp=0},{t="The Serpent Threat",b="The wreckage holds a torn banner and a broken piece of an exotic blade, both belonging to the naga. These serpent-like creatures seem to have moved south along the Durotar coast from Azshara. Razor Hill already faces human invaders from Tiragarde Keep to the south and quilboar in the western canyons. A new attack from the north could overwhelm the settlement’s defenses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Threat from Below?",a="The Horde investigates the ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye along Durotar’s coast. You search the damaged site for clues to the unknown attackers, then bring what you find to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill so he can judge the danger to the region.",al={"threat from below quest","what is threat from below","threat from below overview"}},{q="Who is Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Heglan Shadeeye is a Shattered Hand scout who watched Tiragarde Keep from a hut north of it. An enemy ambushed her at her coastal post while she kept watch, and the wreckage shows she fought fiercely. Razor Hill’s leaders need to know who attacked her.",al={"heglan shadeeye","who is heglan","heglan shadeeye lore"}},{q="Who attacked Heglan Shadeeye?",a="Naga attacked Heglan Shadeeye along Durotar’s shore. A torn banner and a broken blade fragment found at the site identify the serpent-like attackers, and the fierce fight left them wounded.",al={"who ambushed heglan","heglan attackers","what attacked heglan shadeeye"}},{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc authority stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar. He organizes the region’s defense and coordinates Horde scouts. When Heglan Shadeeye fails to report, he relies on returning scouts and travelers to identify the attackers and protect the settlement.",al={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar","orgnil in razor hill"}},{q="Why are the naga a danger to Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill faces human marines from Kul Tiras to the south and hostile quilboar to the west. If naga establish a permanent foothold on the northern coast, the outpost could be caught between its enemies, its small garrison stretched thin, and Durotar’s reinforcement routes cut off.",al={"why are naga dangerous here","naga threat razor hill","razor hill naga danger"}},{q="Where did the attacking naga come from?",a="The recovered remnants suggest the naga came south along the coast from northern waters, perhaps from Azshara or the Great Sea shelf. They used the waterways to evade inland patrols and strike isolated coastal posts before Durotar’s defenders could organize a perimeter.",al={"where did naga come from","naga origin durotar","how did naga get to durotar"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Searching the coast helps defend Durotar and keep the young Horde from being flanked along its shores.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you see the ambush on scout Heglan Shadeeye as an intolerable intrusion into your settled homeland. It calls for an immediate investigation and retaliation.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you know the naga’s treachery well. Your people have faced sea witches and horrors of the Great Sea."},kw={"durotar","heglan shadeeye","horde","naga","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","scout","threat from below"},rel={"topic:naga","subzone:razor-hill","npc:orgnil-soulscar"},m={id=99049},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99050"] = {t="quest",n="The Great Tree Provides",z="general",s="Byancie works in Dolanaar to save Eralya from a dangerous affliction. Dewy lasher fronds from Teldrassil's lakes and a few simple supplies can make a salve to keep the illness at bay.",h="Byancie works in Dolanaar to save Eralya from a dangerous affliction.",sec={{t="A Race Against Time",b="Byancie tends to the night elves of Dolanaar. When she learns that Eralya has fallen ill in the wilds of Teldrassil, she begins preparing an urgent treatment. Without a salve to slow the affliction, Eralya may not survive the journey back to Dolanaar for proper care.",sp=0},{t="The Bountiful World Tree",b="Byancie seeks a remedy in Teldrassil's living bounty. Dewy lasher fronds grow near Lake Al'Ameth to the south and Wellspring Lake to the northwest. Blended with clean spring water in a glass vial, the leaves make medicine that can hold the affliction at bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Great Tree Provides?",a="Byancie asks for help in Dolanaar because Eralya suffers from an affliction. A restorative salve can keep it at bay until further treatment is possible.",al={"what is the great tree provides","great tree provides quest","byancie quest"}},{q="Who is Byancie?",a="Byancie is a night elf healer or apothecary in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. She tends the sick and prepares natural remedies from local plants.",al={"who is byancie","byancie dolanaar","quest giver byancie"}},{q="Who is Eralya and what happened to her?",a="Eralya is afflicted and outside Dolanaar. Her condition is worsening, so Byancie needs a salve to stabilize her for the journey into town and full treatment.",al={"who is eralya","what happened to eralya","eralya affliction"}},{q="Where are dewy lasher fronds found?",a="Dewy lasher fronds grow on plant lashers around Lake Al'Ameth, south of Dolanaar, and along Wellspring Lake and its river to the northwest.",al={"where to find dewy lasher fronds","dewy lasher fronds location","lasher fronds teldrassil"}},{q="What ingredients are required to prepare the salve?",a="Byancie needs six dewy lasher fronds, an empty vial, and refreshing spring water to prepare the salve.",al={"what ingredients does byancie need","salve ingredients dolanaar","great tree provides items"}},{q="Where can you obtain an empty vial and refreshing spring water?",a="General or trade supplies vendors in Dolanaar sell empty vials and refreshing spring water.",al={"where do you get vial and spring water","empty vial dolanaar","refreshing spring water dolanaar"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Teldrassil's herbal remedies reflect the kaldorei belief that their world tree sustains and protects them. Its living plants can help against sudden afflictions.",["class:Druid"]="Druids value the restorative properties of Teldrassil's plants. They use native growth such as lasher fronds rather than artificial concoctions.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Practiced herbalists know how to gather native plants like dewy lasher fronds and brew them into healing salves."},kw={"affliction","byancie","dewy lasher fronds","dolanaar","eralya","healing salve","lake al'ameth","teldrassil","the great tree provides","wellspring lake"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:wellspring-lake"},m={id=99050},src={"In-game quest text: The Great Tree Provides"},fv=true}
E["quest:99051"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="general",s="Naga scouts are raising camps nearby, and Threat from Below sends you against them. Horde defenders hope to drive the invaders north and keep the area safe.",h="Naga scouts are raising camps nearby, and Threat from Below sends you against them.",sec={{t="Serpentine Incursion",b="Naga raiders have begun raising camps nearby. Local defenders send you to strike before the intruders gain a foothold. You are to slay the scouts and bring back naga spinefins as proof that their camp has been crushed.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borders",b="The serpentfolk have troubled the area before, and local command will not abide their presence. After you strike the scout camps, surviving naga are expected to flee north. Horde grunts will watch for stragglers and sudden ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Threat from Below?",a="You are sent to slay naga scouts who have begun raising camps nearby. Bring back naga spinefins as proof that you struck the encroaching serpentfolk.",al={"what is threat from below","threat from below quest"}},{q="Who are the snakes mentioned in the orders?",a="The snakes, or snake scum, are naga: amphibious serpentine humanoids who have emerged from coastal or aquatic depths to scout local positions.",al={"who are the snakes","snakes in threat from below"}},{q="Why must the naga scouts be eliminated?",a="Their camps point to an organized scouting effort, not wandering creatures. The local commander wants swift retaliation before the naga can mount a larger assault or strengthen their position.",al={"why kill naga scouts","naga motive"}},{q="Why are naga spinefins collected?",a="Naga spinefins provide physical proof that the scout camps were found and broken. They confirm that the immediate pressure along the border has eased.",al={"why spinefins","naga proof"}},{q="Where are the naga expected to retreat?",a="The commander hopes the strike will send surviving naga north. Grunts will watch for stragglers and suspicious movements.",al={"where do naga go","naga north"}},{q="Who keeps watch after the scouts are slain?",a="Horde grunts are ordered to watch the area for stragglers and further naga incursions.",al={"who watches for naga","grunts naga watch"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help defend Horde-held territory from encroaching naga scouts. Horde grunts will watch for stragglers."},kw={"grunts","naga","naga spinefins","scouts","snake scum","spinefins","threat from below"},rel={"topic:naga"},m={id=99051},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99052"] = {t="quest",n="Threat from Below",z="general",s="Along Durotar's northern coast, Threat from Below puts travelers and the nearby waters in danger. A sea giant prowls the shore, and defeating it earns the respect of Durotar's warriors.",h="Along Durotar's northern coast, Threat from Below puts travelers and the nearby waters in danger.",sec={{t="The Northern Coastline",b="A sea giant prowls Durotar's northern coast, where the Great Sea meets jagged sand and rocky shores. Scavengers and crabs usually roam there. Now the giant moves through the shallows, threatening coastal travelers and those who secure the waters beside the Horde's new homeland.",sp=0},{t="A Titan of the Waves",b="Sea giants can shatter longboats and crush warriors beneath their fists. Bringing one down is a hard fight for young adventurers. Those who succeed earn deep respect among the orcs. Their cry of “blood and thunder” rings across Durotar's dry red bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Threat from Below?",a="Horde warriors are called to hunt a dangerous sea giant along Durotar's northern coast and bring back proof of the deed.",al={"what is threat from below","threat from below quest","sea giant quest durotar"}},{q="Where is the sea giant found?",a="The sea giant roams the waters and shores along Durotar's north coast.",al={"where is sea giant","durotar sea giant location","threat from below location"}},{q="What kind of creature is a sea giant?",a="Sea giants are massive, ancient coastal behemoths created to dredge the oceans and shape Azeroth's coastlines. Few wanderers survive facing one directly.",al={"what is a sea giant","sea giant lore","who are sea giants"}},{q="Why does the sea giant need to be eliminated?",a="A huge creature prowling so close to Durotar endangers coastal travelers, fishermen, and Horde encampments along the shore.",al={"why kill sea giant","is sea giant dangerous","threat to durotar"}},{q="What does the quest giver mean by 'blood and thunder'?",a="“Blood and thunder” is a traditional orcish battle cry honoring martial strength, ferocity, and glory in victory against dangerous foes.",al={"blood and thunder meaning","orc greeting blood and thunder"}},{q="What proof is required to complete the task?",a="Proof of the sea giant's fall must be brought back from Durotar's north coast to verify that the beast has been slain.",al={"threat from below proof","proof of accomplishment"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defeating the sea giant removes a dangerous colossus from the shore beside the Horde's heartland.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know honor means facing titanic foes and answering “blood and thunder” against overwhelming might.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face a test of endurance in direct combat with one of the coast's heaviest brutes."},kw={"blood and thunder","coastal monster","durotar","horde quest","north coast","sea giant","threat from below"},rel={"zone:durotar"},m={id=99052},src={"In-game quest text: Threat from Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99053"] = {t="quest",n="Escaping Ban'ethil",z="general",s="Beneath Teldrassil, Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is trapped in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Gnarlpine furbolg seized her while she carried a message to the slumbering druids. She needs to reach the surface so Dolanaar can hear she is safe.",h="Beneath Teldrassil, Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is trapped in Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",sec={{t="Ambushed Beneath the Roots",b="Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom entered Ban'ethil Barrow Den on the Oracle Tree's orders. She carried a message to the druids resting there. But aggressive Gnarlpine furbolg had overrun the tunnels and ambushed her before she could retreat. They took her prisoner, and Lynessa feared the tribe would kill her. Now you can fight your way with her back to the surface.",sp=0},{t="Safe Return to Dolanaar",b="For the kaldorei Sentinels, the gloom of a barrow den is hard to endure. It leaves them far from Elune's starlight and Teldrassil's open air. After her rescue, Lynessa makes her way back toward civilization, while word of her survival reaches Dolanaar. Sentinel Kyra Starsong, Lynessa's friend, receives the news with relief. Those who help Lynessa defend the kaldorei people earn Kyra's thanks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom?",a="Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is a night elf sentinel on Teldrassil. The Oracle Tree sent her to carry a message to the druids resting in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where Gnarlpine furbolg captured her.",al={"who is lynessa duskblossom","lynessa duskblossom","who is trapped in the barrow den"}},{q="Why did Sentinel Lynessa enter Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Oracle Tree sent Lynessa to carry a message to the druids sleeping in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. But hostile furbolg had overrun the underground den, and she could not deliver it.",al={"why did lynessa go to banethil","what was lynessa's mission","oracle tree message"}},{q="Who captured Sentinel Lynessa?",a="Gnarlpine furbolg captured Lynessa in the barrow den. They ambushed her before she could escape and dragged her into the depths. There, she feared they would make her their next meal.",al={"who captured lynessa","what furbolg are in banethil","gnarlpine furbolg"}},{q="What is Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den lies underground on Teldrassil, west of Dolanaar. Night elf druids traditionally rest there in deep communion, but corrupt Gnarlpine furbolg have overrun it.",al={"where is banethil barrow den","what is banethil barrow den","barrow den teldrassil"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Kyra Starsong?",a="Sentinel Kyra Starsong is a night elf sentinel posted in Dolanaar. A close friend of Lynessa Duskblossom, she awaits news that Lynessa has escaped and reached safety.",al={"who is kyra starsong","where do i turn in escaping banethil","dolanaar sentinel"}},{q="Why does Lynessa loathe being underground?",a="Many night elf Sentinels and warriors dislike being trapped underground, though druids use barrow dens for sacred slumber. Kaldorei culture cherishes the open night sky, Elune's starlight, and the forest canopy above subterranean tunnels.",al={"why do night elves dislike barrow dens","under the earth is no place for kaldorei"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom is a sister-in-arms. Her capture beneath the roots cuts against the night elves' sacred bond with Teldrassil's open stars and canopy.",["class:Druid"]="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is meant as a sanctuary where druids sleep and commune with the Emerald Dream. Its fall to feral furbolg makes this an urgent crisis for Cenarion protectors.",["faction:Alliance"]="To safeguard Darnassus and Teldrassil, you aid the Sentinels against growing hostility from corrupted native wildlife and tribes."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","escaping ban'ethil","furbolg","gnarlpine","kaldorei","kyra starsong","lynessa duskblossom","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:elune"},m={id=99053},src={"In-game quest text: Escaping Ban'ethil"},fv=true}
E["quest:99073"] = {t="quest",n="Easing Suffering",z="general",s="Near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow lies stricken by a spreading rot. You carry Lashwater Salve to ease her pain and calm her failing breath.",h="Near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow lies stricken by a spreading rot.",sec={{t="A Race Against the Rot",b="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow lies on the road to the Oracle Tree, stricken by a rot spreading fast. To ease her agony, you bring her freshly made Lashwater Salve before the affliction takes firmer hold.",sp=0},{t="Peace in the Shadows",b="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow receives the salve, though her healers doubt it can drive out the blight. It quickly calms her labored breath. Whether she will survive remains uncertain, but she finds peace in her darkest hour.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow?",a="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow is a night elf guardian found ailing on the road to the Oracle Tree. A fast spreading rot has left her helpless and near death.",al={"who is eralya","eralya leafshadow","who is sentinel eralya"}},{q="What is Lashwater Salve?",a="Lashwater Salve is a prepared remedy brought to ease the pain of Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow's virulent rot. It may not cure her, but it soothes her distress.",al={"what is lashwater salve","lashwater salve","salve cure rot"}},{q="Does Sentinel Eralya survive the affliction?",a="The salve eases Sentinel Eralya's breathing and brings her peace, but whether she will recover or succumb to the rot remains uncertain.",al={"does eralya survive","is eralya cured","did eralya die"}},{q="Where can Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow be found?",a="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow lies on the road leading toward the Oracle Tree in Teldrassil.",al={"where is oracle tree","road to oracle tree","eralya location"}},{q="What affliction struck Sentinel Eralya?",a="Eralya suffers from a fast spreading rot that festers through her body. Its source is unknown, but the affliction grows more virulent with time.",al={"what caused eralyas sickness","what is the rot","eralya affliction"}},{q="Why is haste required to deliver the salve?",a="The rot spreads and strengthens quickly through Eralya's body. Haste matters because each passing moment brings her closer to succumbing to its agony and corruption.",al={"why rush salve","why haste eralya"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow is one of your own, stricken by a virulent corruption in Teldrassil near the Oracle Tree. Bringing her comfort honors the duty Sentinels bear toward their kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding fallen night elf Sentinels on the roads of Darnassus's homeland helps preserve the fragile frontline against growing corruption in Teldrassil's boughs."},kw={"easing suffering","eralya leafshadow","lashwater salve","oracle tree","rot","sentinel eralya","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:98398"},m={id=99073},src={"In-game quest text: Easing Suffering"},fv=true}
E["quest:99079"] = {t="quest",n="Longwalker Malah",z="general",s="In Mulgore, Bloodhoof Village awaits Longwalker Malah’s return from the eastern borderlands. Sent to survey the frontier, she has been missing for three days, and the village needs to know she is safe.",h="In Mulgore, Bloodhoof Village awaits Longwalker Malah’s return from the eastern borderlands.",sec={{t="The High Chieftain's Eyes",b="Across the plains, the Longwalkers serve as the shu'halo's eyes and ears. Pledged to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, these elite scouts travel vast territories to gather intelligence and carry vital messages. Their loyalty belongs to the High Chieftain alone. Young Baine Bloodhoof sometimes asks for their help protecting Bloodhoof Village and its surrounding pastures.",sp=0},{t="Vanished on the Borderlands",b="Longwalker Malah Longwind was sent to watch Mulgore's eastern border on a three-day reconnaissance. She has not returned to Bloodhoof Village on schedule, and the village leadership is concerned. Longwalkers carry vital intelligence, while dangers line Mulgore's frontier cliffs. Scouts and willing travelers are called to follow Malah's trail and make sure she is safe. Her ceremonial headband and feathered staff mark her as one of the Longwalkers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Longwalker Malah?",a="Longwalker Malah Longwind is a tauren scout serving the High Chieftain. She was sent to survey Mulgore's eastern border, wearing her order's traditional headband and carrying a feathered staff.",al={"who is malah","malah lore","longwalker malah identity"}},{q="What are the Longwalkers?",a="The Longwalkers are the tauren people's elite scouts and messengers. They answer directly to the High Chieftain, though young Baine Bloodhoof sometimes asks for their help with border intelligence.",al={"what are longwalkers","who are longwalkers","tauren scouts"}},{q="Why is Longwalker Malah being searched for?",a="Malah was sent to survey Mulgore's eastern border and was expected back within three days. Her absence has raised concern in Bloodhoof Village that she may have met trouble on the frontier.",al={"why is malah missing","malah quest why","where did malah go"}},{q="Where can Malah be found?",a="Longwalker Malah was sent toward Mulgore's eastern frontier, past Bloodhoof Village toward the boundary ridge. Search the borderlands east of the village.",al={"where is malah","malah location","find malah"}},{q="How do you recognize Longwalker Malah?",a="Malah wears a ceremonial headband and carries a feathered staff, the traditional marks of the Longwalkers.",al={"malah appearance","how to recognize malah","longwalker gear"}},{q="Why is Baine Bloodhoof involved with the Longwalkers?",a="The Longwalkers answer to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, but his son Baine Bloodhoof sometimes asks for their tracking skills. He oversees local matters in Bloodhoof Village and uses their help to watch border activity and protect the valley.",al={"baine role","why baine involved","baine bloodhoof scout"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Longwalkers answer directly to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Their safety matters to your people and to Mulgore's defense.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help Bloodhoof Village find missing border scouts and guard Mulgore against threats encroaching on Horde lands.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you respect the tracking skill and endurance it takes to patrol Mulgore's far edges on foot."},kw={"baine bloodhoof","bloodhoof village","feathered staff","longwalker malah","longwalkers","malah longwind","mulgore","tauren scout"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore"},m={id=99079},src={"In-game quest text: Longwalker Malah"},fv=true}
E["quest:99080"] = {t="quest",n="Drive Them Out",z="general",s="Baine Bloodhoof asks you to clear the Galak centaurs from the village’s path. Their defeat could give the children a measure of safety.",h="Baine Bloodhoof asks you to clear the Galak centaurs from the village’s path.",sec={{t="The Galak",b="Six Galak centaurs and four Galak outrunners must fall, and Herak the Pillager’s head must come back to Baine. The village’s safety is at stake.",sp=0},{t="A Village’s Relief",b="Baine hears the last centaur fall and the stampede cease. He calls it a great victory for the village. Its children need that feeling of safety more than ever.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks me to drive off the Galak?",a="Baine Bloodhoof asks you to confront the Galak centaurs and outrunners. He also asks you to bring him Herak the Pillager’s head.",al={"who gave this","Baine task"}},{q="What does Baine want from me?",a="Kill six Galak centaurs and four Galak outrunners for Baine, then bring him Herak the Pillager’s head.",al={"what do I do","Galak job"}},{q="Who is Herak the Pillager?",a="Herak the Pillager is a Galak whose head Baine asks you to bring.",al={"Herak who","pillager head"}},{q="Why does this matter to the village?",a="Baine says victory gives the village’s children a feeling of safety they need more than ever.",al={"why help village","kids safe"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Baine calls the bloodshed a unique honor among your people."},kw={"baine bloodhoof","centaurs","children","galak","herak the pillager","outrunners","village"},rel={"npc:baine-bloodhoof"},m={id=99080},src={"In-game quest text: Drive Them Out"},fv=true}
E["quest:99081"] = {t="quest",n="Grim Tidings",z="general",s="Malah’s report carries word of a new centaur camp in Mulgore. Brave Wildrunner needs to know what happened to her, who killed her, and why the camp points to a small raiding party entering the land.",h="Malah’s report carries word of a new centaur camp in Mulgore.",sec={{t="Malah's Report",b="You bring Malah’s report to Brave Wildrunner in Bloodhoof Village. He needs to know what happened to Malah and who killed her. Her report brings troubling news, and Baine must hear it at once.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Malah's report?",a="Brave Wildrunner in Bloodhoof Village wants Malah’s report.",al={"who needs the report","wildrunner report","who do i take it to"}},{q="What does the report concern?",a="The report concerns what happened to Malah and who killed her.",al={"what happened to malah","malah report","why is malah dead"}},{q="What is near the arrows' direction?",a="A new centaur camp lies in the direction from which the arrows that struck Malah seem to have come.",al={"new centaur camp","centaur camp","where did the raiders come from"}},{q="What does the camp suggest?",a="Activity at the camp suggests a small raiding party has entered Mulgore.",al={"centaur raid","raiders in mulgore","what does the camp mean"}},{q="Who needs to hear the news?",a="Brave Wildrunner says Baine must hear the news at once.",al={"tell baine","wildrunner tells baine","who gets informed"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you carry news of a centaur raiding party in Mulgore to Brave Wildrunner."},kw={"baine","bloodhoof village","centaur camp","brave wildrunner","malah longwind","malah","mulgore","grim tidings"},rel={"zone:mulgore"},m={id=99081},src={"In-game quest text: Grim Tidings"},fv=true}
E["quest:99082"] = {t="quest",n="The High Chieftain",z="general",s="Cairne Bloodhoof’s son sends you to Thunder Bluff to seek his father’s audience. Your defense of your people has earned recognition.",h="Cairne Bloodhoof’s son sends you to Thunder Bluff to seek his father’s audience.",sec={{t="A Chieftain’s Deed",b="Cairne Bloodhoof and the young Warchief Thrall led the effort to reclaim these plains from the centaurs. As High Chieftain, Cairne can recognize your part in defending your people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who am I being sent to see?",a="You are being sent to seek an audience with Cairne Bloodhoof, the High Chieftain of Thunder Bluff.",al={"who is the high chieftain","cairne audience","meet cairne"}},{q="Why am I going to Thunder Bluff?",a="Your courage in defending your people has earned recognition. So you are asked to seek an audience with Cairne Bloodhoof.",al={"why thunder bluff","what does cairne want","cairne meeting"}},{q="Who helped reclaim the plains?",a="Cairne Bloodhoof and the young Warchief Thrall led the effort to reclaim the plains from the centaurs.",al={"who fought centaurs","thrall and cairne","reclaim plains"}},{q="Where is Cairne?",a="Cairne Bloodhoof is on Thunder Bluff’s central rise.",al={"where is high chieftain","cairne location","find cairne"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you are sent to Cairne Bloodhoof after defending your people. He and Thrall led the effort to reclaim the plains."},kw={"audience","cairne bloodhoof","centaurs","high chieftain","tauren","thrall","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","npc:thrall"},m={id=99082},src={"In-game quest text: The High Chieftain"},fv=true}
E["quest:99101"] = {t="quest",n="Our Ancient Enemy",z="general",s="Malah's report has reached Baine Bloodhoof, and his answer is grim. The matter will not go unanswered.",h="Malah's report has reached Baine Bloodhoof, and his answer is grim.",sec={},faq={{q="Who receives Malah's report?",a="Baine Bloodhoof receives Malah's report.",al={"who gets the report","Baine report","Malah's report"}},{q="What does Baine say about the report?",a="After reading Malah's report, Baine says the matter will not go unanswered.",al={"Baine reaction","what does Baine say","report response"}},{q="Who brought the report to Baine?",a="You bring Malah's report to Baine Bloodhoof.",al={"bring Malah report","who delivers it","report to Baine"}}},kw={"ancient enemy","baine bloodhoof","malah","our ancient enemy","report"},rel={"npc:baine-bloodhoof"},m={id=99101},src={"In-game quest text: Our Ancient Enemy"},fv=true}
E["quest:99108"] = {t="quest",n="Sparring Match",z="general",s="At Tang Stonehoof's arena, newcomers face a trial of strength. Whatever their class or background, they can meet three novices or willing duelists and show their skill in combat.",h="At Tang Stonehoof's arena, newcomers face a trial of strength.",sec={{t="The Sparring Grounds",b="Tang Stonehoof welcomes travelers of every path into his sparring ring. He takes special notice of those who follow a tradition beyond the warrior's, yet believes martial discipline and direct combat teach lessons to all who travel through a dangerous world.",sp=0},{t="Sharpening the Horns",b="In Tang Stonehoof's arena, lineage and weapon matter little. You may wield a sword, bow, or magic, but you must defeat three willing opponents. They may be Novice Warriors in training or fellow adventurers who agree to duel. Victory earns Tang's respect and bandages for wounds suffered in honest combat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tang Stonehoof?",a="Tang Stonehoof oversees the local sparring arena as its combat instructor. He teaches those who follow paths beyond the warrior's and invites promising adventurers to face novices or willing peers.",al={"who is tang stonehoof","tang stonehoof lore","quest giver"}},{q="What does Tang Stonehoof require for the sparring match?",a="Tang Stonehoof asks you to defeat three opponents in the arena. They may be willing adventurers who duel you or Novice Warriors training under his guidance. The trial tests your readiness and skill in direct combat.",al={"sparring match goal","what to do sparring match","who to fight"}},{q="Why does a warrior instructor train other classes?",a="Tang Stonehoof believes direct combat benefits every adventurer, whether they wield a blade, bow, or magic. In his arena, lineage and class discipline matter less than the will to test yourself and strengthen your resolve.",al={"can non warriors do this","why sparring for other classes","not a warrior"}},{q="Where does the sparring match take place?",a="The contest takes place in the open sparring arena before Tang Stonehoof. Novice combatants train there, and willing challengers can face one another on equal footing.",al={"where fight novices","arena location","where is the ring"}},{q="Can you duel other players instead of the novice warriors?",a="Yes. Tang Stonehoof accepts victories over Novice Warriors training in the arena or other adventurers defeated in formal duels. He asks only that you test your abilities against willing opponents.",al={"can i fight players","duel players for quest","novice warriors or players"}},{q="What does Tang Stonehoof say when you complete the match?",a="After you prove yourself against three adversaries, Tang acknowledges your skill and places his hope in the new generation. He offers medical supplies for your wounds before the harsh road ahead.",al={"sparring match reward","what does tang give you"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know Tang Stonehoof's sparring ring teaches more than one discipline. He believes combat fundamentals, courage, and resolve help every adventurer.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may hear Tang Stonehoof use traditional turns of phrase such as “sharpen their horns” when speaking of testing one's mettle. He welcomes any willing adversary to the sparring arena, whatever their origins."},kw={"arena","combat training","duel","novice warrior","sparring","sparring match","tang stonehoof"},rel={"topic:warrior"},m={id=99108},src={"In-game quest text: Sparring Match"},fv=true}
E["quest:99123"] = {t="quest",n="Lost in the Shadows",z="general",s="Pal'juh is lost in dangerous country after setting out alone. Her rescue shows why a hunter needs courage and patience.",h="Pal'juh is lost in dangerous country after setting out alone.",sec={{t="A Reckless Scout",b="Pal'juh went into hostile territory alone because she would not wait for help. A talented hunter, she soon found herself in over her head. Someone had to bring her safely back.",sp=0},{t="Patience of the Hunt",b="After Pal'juh is rescued, her overseers see promise in her as a scout and tracker. Yet she charges like a raptor instead of stalking with a tiger's patience. The wilderness offers little mercy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pal'juh?",a="Pal'juh is a promising young hunter who heads into danger alone. She has talent, but acts rashly and can be overwhelmed by beasts and the wilds.",al={"who is paljuh","paljuh lore","pal'juh"}},{q="What happens during the quest 'Lost in the Shadows'?",a="Pal'juh went out alone and got into trouble again. Someone had to track her down and help her before she came to serious harm.",al={"what happened in lost in the shadows","lost in the shadows quest lore","lost in the shadows story"}},{q="Why does the quest giver say Pal'juh acts more like a raptor than a tiger?",a="A raptor lunges without caution, while a tiger waits, stalks, and strikes with precision. The comparison warns that Pal'juh needs patience and discipline as a hunter.",al={"why raptor tiger","raptor than a tiger meaning","hunter raptor tiger"}},{q="Who receives the report for Lost in the Shadows?",a="Someone who knows Pal'juh and expects her recklessness receives the report. They are relieved that help came to the headstrong tracker.",al={"who turns in lost in the shadows","lost in the shadows questgiver"}},{q="Does Pal'juh learn her lesson from this misadventure?",a="Pal'juh survived because someone intervened. Her overseers remain watchful to see whether she learns the danger of wandering off alone.",al={"did paljuh learn her lesson","is paljuh okay"}},{q="Is Pal'juh considered a skilled hunter?",a="Pal'juh has raw talent and courage as a hunter. Her mentors warn that instinct cannot replace patience when tracking dangerous prey.",al={"is paljuh a good hunter","paljuh skill"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need patience and careful stalking, not a reckless charge like a hungry raptor.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you may recognize Pal'juh's eagerness to prove herself in the wilderness before she has mastered restraint."},kw={"hunter","lost in the shadows","pal'juh","paljuh","raptor","tiger"},rel={"topic:hunter"},m={id=99123},src={"In-game quest text: Lost in the Shadows"},fv=true}
E["quest:99127"] = {t="quest",n="A Net Disaster",z="general",s="At Crystal Lake, A Net Disaster starts with fishermen finding no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the shallows. They set traps overnight to protect their stock.",h="At Crystal Lake, A Net Disaster starts with fishermen finding no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the...",sec={{t="Troubled Waters at Crystal Lake",b="Fishermen at Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest come up empty. Hooks bring in no fish, and even the minnows have vanished from the shallows. So they set traps overnight, hoping to catch enough to keep their stock.",sp=0},{t="Wrecked Traps and Neighboring Nuisances",b="Lee's traps beneath Crystal Lake lie ruined. Hostile neighbors along the shore have wrecked the fishing gear. If the damage continues, local fishermen risk losing their livelihoods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is A Net Disaster?",a="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, fishermen find no fish on their hooks and no minnows in the shallows. They set traps overnight to protect their stock.",al={"what is a net disaster","net disaster quest","crystal lake net disaster"}},{q="Where do you inspect the fishing traps?",a="Lee's overnight fishing traps lie beneath the waters of Crystal Lake. Lee set them to preserve the fish stock after hook-and-line fishing failed.",al={"where are the traps","net disaster location","crystal lake traps"}},{q="Who is Lee?",a="Lee is a fisherman at Crystal Lake. After hook-and-line fishing brought in nothing, Lee set traps overnight to secure the fish stock.",al={"who is lee","lee fisherman"}},{q="What happened to the fish in Crystal Lake?",a="No fish are biting, and not even minnows appear in Crystal Lake's shallows. Hostile neighbors have ruined the overnight traps.",al={"what happened to crystal lake fish","why no fish crystal lake","crystal lake empty"}},{q="Who are the neighboring nuisances mentioned at the end?",a="The neighboring nuisances are aggressive murlocs. They have made camps in Crystal Lake's waters and along its shores, disrupting local wildlife and fishing gear.",al={"who are the neighboring nuisances","net disaster nuisances","who broke the traps"}},{q="Why is the lack of fish such a big problem for the fishermen?",a="The fishermen rely on Crystal Lake's fish for their livelihoods. With the catch gone and the traps ruined, their work and income are at risk.",al={"why does the quest giver care","crystal lake fishing business"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest. Disruptions there threaten local livelihoods and the supplies that support Alliance territory."},kw={"a net disaster","crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish stock","fishing traps","lee","murlocs","nuisances"},rel={"subzone:crystal-lake"},m={id=99127},src={"In-game quest text: A Net Disaster"},fv=true}
E["quest:99128"] = {t="quest",n="Slimy Menace",z="general",s="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, murlocs threaten the fish and people along the shore. Their growing numbers endanger the lake's supply and nearby locals.",h="At Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, murlocs threaten the fish and people along the shore.",sec={{t="Trouble at Crystal Lake",b="Aggressive murlocs have settled along Crystal Lake's eastern shore. Sharp teeth and fierce tempers make the water dangerous for anyone who fishes or comes near. Local residents depend on the lake for their livelihoods, and the murlocs threaten them at the water's edge.",sp=0},{t="An Endless Infestation",b="If their numbers grow unchecked, murlocs may devour every fish in the lake. Thinning them gives the waters respite, though their eerie, echoing warbles warn that they persist. Even when scattered, they replenish their ranks swiftly, so the shoreline needs constant watch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Slimy Menace about?",a="Murlocs along Crystal Lake's far shores threaten the fish and anyone working or traveling nearby. Left unchecked, they can devour the local fish supply.",al={"what is slimy menace","slimy menace quest info","slimy menace summary"}},{q="Where do the events of this quest take place?",a="The disturbance is at Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, where murlocs have gathered on the opposite shoreline. They disrupt the lake's wildlife and endanger local residents.",al={"where are murlocs crystal lake","crystal lake location","where does this happen"}},{q="Why must the murlocs at Crystal Lake be culled?",a="Murlocs rapidly deplete the lake's fish and terrorize the surrounding area with fierce tempers and sharp teeth. Thinning their ranks helps protect the fishery and slows their aggressive expansion for a time.",al={"why kill crystal lake murlocs","murlocs eating fish","what is the problem with murlocs"}},{q="Does clearing the murlocs permanently resolve the problem?",a="No. Thinning the murlocs offers only a temporary reprieve. They reproduce and regroup swiftly, so their numbers recover despite initial losses.",al={"are murlocs gone forever","did we wipe out murlocs","will crystal lake murlocs return"}},{q="Who asks for help with the slimy menace?",a="An Elwynn local concerned about Crystal Lake asks for help. Distressed by the murlocs' unsettling warbling and voracious appetite, they want the murlocs thinned to protect the fishery.",al={"who gives slimy menace","slimy menace quest giver"}},{q="What makes the murlocs such a threat?",a="Murlocs are vicious, temperamental amphibious creatures with sharp teeth and a guttural warble. They gather along shores, aggressively defend their territory, and attack anything that ventures too close to their feeding grounds.",al={"what are murlocs like","murloc behavior crystal lake"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting Crystal Lake's shores helps keep local Elwynn fishermen and travelers near Goldshire safe from aggressive murloc raids.",["race:Human"]="As a human, your people in Elwynn Forest face murloc encroachment that threatens their waterways, food supply, and nearby settlements."},kw={"crystal lake","elwynn forest","fish","goldshire","murloc","murlocs","slimy menace"},rel={"subzone:crystal-lake","topic:murloc"},m={id=99128},src={"In-game quest text: Slimy Menace"},fv=true}
E["quest:99129"] = {t="quest",n="A Man About a Murloc",z="general",s="Jason's fishing is in danger, and he turns to Remy \"Two Times\" for help. Remy shares his hatred of murlocs and has plans of his own.",h="Jason's fishing is in danger, and he turns to Remy \"Two Times\" for help.",sec={{t="Trouble on the Water",b="Jason is a local fisherman, and murlocs keep raiding his catches. He knows Remy \"Two Times\" hates them as much as he does. So Jason sends you to ask whether Remy has found a way to drive the creatures from the waters.",sp=0},{t="Remy's Retaliation",b="Remy says the local guards have ignored his repeated warnings about the murloc threat. He will not wait for their help. Instead, he prepares to strike back and asks you to aid his plans.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Man About a Murloc?",a="Jason, a local fisherman, asks how to stop murlocs from raiding his catches.",al={"who gives a man about a murloc","who starts a man about a murloc","jason murloc quest"}},{q="Who is Remy \"Two Times\"?",a="Remy \"Two Times\" is a local resident who has repeatedly warned the guards about murlocs. Jason hopes Remy can find a way to drive them away.",al={"who is remy two times","remy two times elwynn","where is remy"}},{q="Why does Jason want to consult Remy?",a="Murlocs raid Jason's catches, so he turns to Remy for help protecting his fishing.",al={"why does jason need help","jason fish murlocs","murloc problem jason"}},{q="What does Remy plan to do about the murlocs?",a="Remy says the town guards ignore his warnings. He plans to strike back at the murlocs and asks you to gather materials.",al={"remy two times ideas","what is remy plan","remy murlocs plan"}},{q="Why haven't the guards dealt with the murlocs?",a="Remy says he has repeatedly warned the local guards about the murlocs, but they have not heeded him.",al={"guards murlocs elwynn","why dont guards help remy","remy guards warning"}},{q="What happens after speaking to Remy?",a="After you speak with Remy, he shares his plans to strike back at the local murlocs and sets you to further work for him.",al={"where does a man about a murloc lead","after a man about a murloc","next quest after remy"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you may find murlocs troubling settlements along lakeshores and docks. Their incursions strain residents and guards across Elwynn and nearby Alliance territories."},kw={"a man about a murloc","elwynn","fish","jason","murloc","remy two times"},rel={"npc:remy-two-times","topic:murloc"},m={id=99129},src={"In-game quest text: A Man About a Murloc"},fv=true}
E["quest:99130"] = {t="quest",n="An Enticing Offer",z="general",s="Remy asks you to gather duskweed for bait against nearby murlocs. Clearing it may also help local farmers.",h="Remy asks you to gather duskweed for bait against nearby murlocs.",sec={{t="A Twofold Solution",b="Remy has a plan for two local troubles. You gather duskweed from nearby fields, where it troubles the growers, then use it to make bait meant to keep murlocs from settled lands. The plan is to teach the murlocs to avoid the weed.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of Duskweed",b="Duskweed is both the heart of the bait and a persistent weed in nearby farm plots. Its petals harm most beasts when gathered in substantial quantities. Gathering it from troubled farmers clears an aggressive plant from their fields and supplies the base for bait meant to steer murloc packs away.",sp=0},{t="Baiting the Waters",b="Duskweed makes the bait hazardous to handle because its toxins harm other creatures too. Keep domestic animals and pets away from the mixture. Remy also warns you to make sure Jason does not mistake the pungent bait for a meal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest An Enticing Offer?",a="Remy asks you to gather duskweed and make toxic bait to deter nearby murlocs. The gathering also helps farmers clear the weed from their fields.",al={"what is an enticing offer","what is this quest"}},{q="What is duskweed?",a="Duskweed is a persistent weed in local farm fields. Its petals are toxic to most beasts in substantial quantities, making them useful in bait meant to deter murlocs.",al={"what is duskweed","duskweed plant","duskweed effects"}},{q="How is the murloc bait intended to work?",a="The plan uses bait made with toxic duskweed petals to teach local murlocs to avoid the area instead of trying to exterminate them.",al={"how does the bait work","murloc poison bait","why make bait"}},{q="Who is Jason?",a="Jason is the fisherman who sent you to Remy about his murloc trouble. Remy says to warn Jason not to eat the duskweed bait.",al={"who is jason","dont let jason eat it","jason bait warning"}},{q="Is the murloc bait dangerous to other creatures?",a="Yes. Duskweed petals are toxic to most animals in substantial quantities. Keep domestic animals and pets away from the mixture.",al={"is duskweed bait dangerous","pet poison bait"}},{q="Why is gathering duskweed considered a win-win?",a="Duskweed aggressively invades cultivated fields and troubles local growers. Gathering it clears the fields and provides the ingredient for bait against murlocs.",al={"why help farmers","win win situation"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you know duskweed as a troublesome local plant with toxic petals. Handle it carefully when gathering it for bait.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the bait can harm domestic beasts and hunting companions if they eat it."},kw={"an enticing offer","duskweed","jason","murloc bait","murlocs","toxic bait"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={id=99130},src={"In-game quest text: An Enticing Offer"},fv=true}
E["quest:99131"] = {t="quest",n="Baited for Success",z="general",s="Jason Mathers asks Remy for help as murlocs disrupt his fishing waters. He hopes poisoned bait will drive them off without harming the fish he sells.",h="Jason Mathers asks Remy for help as murlocs disrupt his fishing waters.",sec={{t="A Fisherman's Dilemma",b="Aggressive murlocs disrupt the waters where Jason Mathers fishes. He asks how to clear them so he can sell his catch again. Remy prepares poisoned bait meant to target the murlocs and let ordinary fishing resume.",sp=0},{t="A Targeted Solution",b="Remy prepares poison and promises to explain how to use it against murlocs without contaminating the fish. Mathers plans to collect it from Remy later that day. He hopes the waters will be clear and his livelihood restored.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who prepared the bait for Jason Mathers?",a="Remy prepares poisoned bait for Jason Mathers and promises to explain how to use it when Mathers comes by later that day.",al={"who gives baited for success","remy bait quest","who made the bait"}},{q="Why does Jason Mathers need this bait?",a="Local murlocs disrupt Jason Mathers's fishing, making it hard to sell his catch. The bait is meant to reduce their numbers without harming the fish he hopes to catch and sell.",al={"why does jason mathers need bait","mathers fish business","why poisoned bait"}},{q="Will the poisoned bait harm the fish?",a="Mathers worries that fish might consume the poison. Remy plans for it to target murlocs while leaving the fish unharmed, so Mathers can return to fishing.",al={"is the bait safe for fish","does poisoned bait kill fish"}},{q="Where is this task completed?",a="You report directly to Jason Mathers that Remy is preparing the bait.",al={"where do i turn in baited for success","baited for success quest end"}},{q="What threat do the murlocs pose to Mathers?",a="Murlocs disrupt the fishing waters, making it dangerous or impossible for Mathers and other fishermen to earn a living until their numbers fall.",al={"why kill murlocs here","murloc problem mathers"}},{q="What are Mathers's plans once he hears from Remy?",a="After hearing from Remy, Mathers plans to collect the poisoned bait from him later that day and learn how to use it safely.",al={"what happens after delivering the message","does mathers get the bait"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure the waters for local fishing and reduce the aggressive murloc population.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can appreciate poison tailored to control troublesome murlocs."},kw={"baited for success","fishing","jason mathers","murloc","poisoned bait","remy"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={id=99131},src={"In-game quest text: Baited for Success"},fv=true}
E["quest:99143"] = {t="quest",n="Bottles and Baubles",z="general",s="An angler wants to try a curious theory with murloc trinkets. Their shine may draw fish to the hook.",h="An angler wants to try a curious theory with murloc trinkets.",sec={{t="Fish Logic and Shoreline Scavenging",b="An eccentric angler has a theory about murlocs and fish. Murlocs look like fish, so the angler reasons that their minds work alike. Whatever catches a murloc's eye may tempt a hungry fish on a hook. You search a nearby murloc camp, sifting through its hoards for shiny discarded junk to test the idea.",sp=0},{t="Gleaming Baubles as Bait",b="Along coasts and riverbanks, murlocs gather bright stones, shells, polished glass, and metal scraps in messy piles around their huts. Sifting through the muddy heaps turns up glittering refuse that an angler can shape into crude lures and flashers. The finds satisfy the angler enough to earn you starter fishing supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do you need to collect junk from murlocs?",a="The angler believes that whatever attracts a murloc may also attract fish beneath the water. Since murlocs look like fish, the angler reasons that their minds work alike, and shiny trinkets from their camps could make bait.",al={"why collect junk","what are bottles and baubles for","shiny junk murloc"}},{q="Where is the shiny junk found?",a="The shiny junk lies in a nearby murloc camp. Murlocs hoard glittering debris, discarded trinkets, and glass along shorelines and waterways.",al={"where find junk","murloc camp location","how to get shiny junk"}},{q="Who gives this task and what do they want?",a="A local angler asks for the work, hoping to stock up on lures and bait. The angler offers surplus fishing gear to helpful scavengers and beginners.",al={"who gives bottles and baubles","who is the questgiver","quest turn in"}},{q="Do murlocs actually think like fish?",a="The angler believes murlocs think like fish, but murlocs are amphibious tribal humanoids. They are drawn to gleaming items, polished shells, and bright trinkets, while their hoard piles happen to hold glittering materials.",al={"do murlocs think like fish","murloc intellect","are murlocs actually fish"}},{q="How will the murloc junk be used as bait?",a="The angler plans to fashion reflective glass, metal bits, and polished odds and ends into lures and improvised bait. Their sheen may mimic small minnows or catch the curiosity of feeding fish.",al={"what is shiny junk used for","is shiny junk bait","does murloc junk work as bait"}},{q="What does the questgiver offer as a reward?",a="After you bring back enough suitable shiny scraps, the angler gives you older personal angling supplies. The basic tools and provisions help aspiring fishermen try their hand at the waters.",al={"what reward bottles and baubles","what do you get","fishing supplies reward"}}},kw={"bait","bottles and baubles","fishing","lures","murloc","murloc camp","shiny junk"},rel={"topic:murloc"},m={id=99143},src={"In-game quest text: Bottles and Baubles"},fv=true}
E["quest:99144"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking Refuge",z="general",s="At Crusader's Outpost, Bareth Dawnstone waits far from the meeting in Brill he was sent to reach. His safe return matters to the young order at Bandarion Keep, where followers of the Holy Light face prejudice from local zealots.",h="At Crusader's Outpost, Bareth Dawnstone waits far from the meeting in Brill he was sent to reach.",sec={{t="A Perilous Journey",b="Bareth Dawnstone left Bandarion Keep to speak with Shari Stilwell in Brill. Zealous warriors seized him at Crusader's Outpost before he could reach her. They despise him for being undead, yet Bareth remains devoted to the Light. He seeks a way out of their hands and a chance to deliver his message.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Versus Devotion",b="At Crusader's Outpost, zealots wield the Holy Light with rigid conviction and vengeance. They see Bareth's existence as an offense. He meditates on the Light as a source of protection and inner purity. His captors' cruelty grieves him, for it twists the sacred teachings he cherishes.",sp=0},{t="Sanctuary on the Bluffs",b="In Brill, Shari Stilwell learns that Bareth has escaped and is safe. Their monastic order is still taking root on the bluffs northwest of Solliden Farmstead. Losing a promising practitioner like Bareth would have hurt the young fellowship. Its doors are open to travelers seeking sincere guidance in the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bareth Dawnstone?",a="Bareth Dawnstone is a devotee of the Holy Light at Bandarion Keep. He was on his way to Brill with a message when zealots ambushed and imprisoned him because he is undead. He meditates on the Light and seeks to use it for protection.",al={"who is bareth dawnstone","bareth dawnstone lore","dawnstone"}},{q="Who captured Bareth Dawnstone, and why?",a="Zealots at Crusader's Outpost ambushed Bareth Dawnstone on the road from Bandarion Keep. He laments that they wield the Holy Light with hatred, twisting the benevolence he meditates upon as they persecute those they judge to be abominations.",al={"who captured bareth dawnstone","crusaders outpost captors","why was he captured"}},{q="Who is Shari Stilwell?",a="Shari Stilwell represents the monastery's order in the Forsaken town of Brill. She receives travelers and coordinates with emissaries from Bandarion Keep. She welcomes anyone seeking guidance in the Light.",al={"who is shari stilwell","stilwell brill","shari brill"}},{q="What is Bandarion Keep?",a="Bandarion Keep is a secluded monastery on the bluffs northwest of Solliden Farmstead in Tirisfal Glades. It is a sanctuary and training ground for a growing religious order devoted to meditation and study of the Holy Light.",al={"what is bandarion keep","where is bandarion keep","monastery northwest solliden"}},{q="Why do Bareth's captors take issue with his kind?",a="Bareth Dawnstone speaks of what remains of his blood and acknowledges prejudice against his kind. He is an undead practitioner of the Holy Light. Tirisfal's fanatical crusaders despise all undead and refuse to believe their intentions or devotion can be pure.",al={"why do they hate his kind","undead using light","bareth what is left of my blood"}},{q="What kind of order is based at Bandarion Keep?",a="Bandarion Keep is home to a young monastic brotherhood taking root on the bluffs of Tirisfal. The order teaches peaceful meditation and protection. It welcomes anyone seeking true guidance in the Light.",al={"what is the order at bandarion keep","bandarion keep monks","bandarion faith"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find Bandarion Keep's way compelling. Its members pursue meditation and guidance in the Holy Light despite prejudice against undead wielders.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see the divide between the hateful zealots at Crusader's Outpost and Bareth Dawnstone's pursuit of benevolence and protection through the Light.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may face hostility from living zealots and skeptical kin if you revere the Holy Light. The growing brotherhood at Bandarion Keep offers a rare sanctuary.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help keep couriers moving between Bandarion Keep and Brill. Emerging neutral or allied orders gain a foothold in Tirisfal Glades against hostile crusaders."},kw={"bandarion keep","bareth dawnstone","brill","crusader's outpost","crusaders","holy light","seeking refuge","shari stilwell","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:shari-stilwell","subzone:bandarion-keep","subzone:crusader-s-outpost","subzone:brill","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:light"},m={id=99144},src={"In-game quest text: Seeking Refuge"},fv=true}
E["quest:99152"] = {t="quest",n="As Above, So Below",z="general",s="At Bandarion Keep, Hilda the Breaker sends you to investigate the hidden Scourge beneath Shadowvale. Bones still humming with reanimation magic may reveal how the undead gathered beneath the town unseen.",h="At Bandarion Keep, Hilda the Breaker sends you to investigate the hidden Scourge beneath Shadowvale.",sec={{t="The Hidden Threat",b="Hilda the Breaker prepares defenders at Bandarion Keep for the dangers around them. To the southwest, Shadowvale faces regular unrest from the Tarnished, a hostile faction. Yet beneath the town, the Scourge gathers strength in hidden cellars. If left unchecked, it may erupt in a sudden assault on the keep.",sp=0},{t="Magic in the Cellars",b="Hilda sends seasoned adventurers into the cellars beneath Shadowvale for a direct lesson in the danger below. She will not send green trainees blindly into subterranean crypts. The aim is to gather intelligence by recovering skeletal remains that still hold reanimation magic. Those bones may show defenders how dark necromancy worked beneath their feet without being noticed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is As Above, So Below?",a="Hilda the Breaker sends an adventurer from Bandarion Keep into Shadowvale's cellars to investigate a hidden Scourge presence. The adventurer collects reanimated bone samples while trainees are drilled at the keep.",al={"what is as above so below","as above so below quest"}},{q="Who gives the quest As Above, So Below?",a="Hilda the Breaker instructs and prepares recruits at Bandarion Keep. She is tough and uncompromising, and demands results from those under her command. She would rather a recruit return on a stretcher than come back empty-handed.",al={"who gives as above so below","who is hilda the breaker","quest giver hilda"}},{q="Where is Shadowvale located?",a="Shadowvale lies southwest of Bandarion Keep. The Tarnished cause trouble on the surface, while the town's cellars hold a greater danger.",al={"where is shadowvale","shadowvale location"}},{q="What threat lurks beneath Shadowvale?",a="Reanimated undead gather in Shadowvale's cellars. If left unchecked, the hidden Scourge presence threatens Bandarion Keep with an uprising.",al={"what are the cellars below shadowvale","scourge in shadowvale cellars","threat beneath shadowvale"}},{q="Why does Hilda need faintly glowing bones?",a="Hilda needs bones that retain the magic of their reanimation. By studying them, defenders hope to learn how the necromancy went unnoticed beneath the town.",al={"why collect glowing bones","faintly glowing bones purpose","reanimation magic bones"}},{q="Who are the Tarnished in Shadowvale?",a="The Tarnished are a hostile faction active on Shadowvale's surface. Hilda sees the hidden Scourge beneath the town as the greater danger.",al={"who are the tarnished","tarnished shadowvale"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see any hidden Scourge presence as an immediate peril. Investigating the reanimation magic beneath Shadowvale is a pressing duty.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest trained against the unholy, you have reason to fear dark reanimation arts beneath an inhabited settlement.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can study the reanimation magic clinging to the glowing bones. It may reveal the necromantic methods used beneath the town."},kw={"as above so below","bandarion keep","glowing bones","hilda the breaker","reanimation magic","scourge","shadowvale","tarnished"},rel={"subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:scourge"},m={id=99152},src={"In-game quest text: As Above, So Below"},fv=true}
E["quest:99153"] = {t="quest",n="The One That Got Away",z="general",s="Near Naxxramas's remnants, Ephram Barbaro seeks the cultist who escaped with a dangerous crystal fragment. The fugitive fled beneath Shadowvale, and its power may raise or strengthen the dead.",h="Near Naxxramas's remnants, Ephram Barbaro seeks the cultist who escaped with a dangerous crystal fragment.",sec={{t="A Fugitive in the Shadows",b="After the clash with cultists near the Naxxramas battle remnants, word spreads among the ranks. Ephram Barbaro hears that one cultist slipped past the perimeter with an active piece of a Scourge focusing crystal. He seeks capable adventurers to find the fugitive.",sp=0},{t="The Threat Beneath Shadowvale",b="The escaped cultist fled into passages beneath Shadowvale. The fragment still holds necromantic power, and may raise the dead or strengthen hostile forces underground. Ephram Barbaro sends you to track it down and secure it before that power brings greater harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The One That Got Away?",a="Ephram Barbaro gives the request after hearing of your earlier efforts against cultists near the Naxxramas battle remnants.",al={"who gives the one that got away","who starts this quest","quest giver the one that got away"}},{q="What is the focusing crystal fragment?",a="The fragment is a piece of a Scourge focusing crystal carried off by an escaped cultist. Ephram Barbaro says it still holds power that may raise the dead or strengthen them beneath Shadowvale.",al={"what is the crystal fragment","what does the crystal do","why is the crystal dangerous"}},{q="Where is the crystal fragment located?",a="Ephram Barbaro's intelligence places the fragment beneath Shadowvale, where the fugitive hid it underground.",al={"where is the crystal hidden","crystal location shadowvale","where to find crystal fragment"}},{q="Who is 'the one that got away'?",a="The title refers to the cultist who escaped the clash near the Naxxramas battle remnants with an active shard of a focusing crystal.",al={"who escaped with the crystal","cultist with crystal","the one that got away meaning"}},{q="What happens when you return the crystal to Ephram Barbaro?",a="When you return the fragment, Ephram Barbaro commends your speed and says it is time for his favorite part of handling the situation.",al={"what happens when you return the crystal","turn in the one that got away","ephram barbaro favorite part"}},{q="How does Ephram Barbaro know about you?",a="Ephram Barbaro says word travels quickly among the ranks. He has heard of your earlier work against cultists near the Naxxramas battle remnants.",al={"naxxramas battle remnants cultists","how does ephram know you","prerequisites the one that got away"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you know the danger of an active Scourge focusing crystal that can animate or strengthen the dead beneath the ground.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know unholy relics can corrupt the land around them if they are not recovered and cleansed promptly."},kw={"crystal fragment","cultist","ephram barbaro","focusing crystal","naxxramas","shadowvale","the one that got away"},m={id=99153},src={"In-game quest text: The One That Got Away"},fv=true}
E["quest:99158"] = {t="quest",n="Dawn in the Mountains",z="general",s="At Misty Pine Refuge, Father Gavin tends travelers with the Light's healing and comfort. He needs holy candles to keep his mountain sanctuary supplied.",h="At Misty Pine Refuge, Father Gavin tends travelers with the Light's healing and comfort.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary in the Peaks",b="Father Gavin follows the Light's gentler calling within the Argent Dawn. Many in the order take up arms against unholy horrors across Azeroth, but he heals the afflicted and tends the weary. He restored an abandoned structure in the rugged mountain wilderness and made it Misty Pine Refuge, a safe stop for travelers facing the high passes.",sp=0},{t="Candles for the Light",b="An isolated mountain refuge needs steady care. Father Gavin depends on charity from distant allies to sustain his ministry and keep the lamps and altars burning. A delivery of consecrated candles replenishes the sanctuary's supply, keeping it a beacon of light, warmth, and hope in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Father Gavin?",a="Father Gavin is an Argent Dawn priest who tends Misty Pine Refuge in the mountains. Many in his order take up arms against the unholy, while he heals and comforts travelers and gives them shelter.",al={"who is father gavin","father gavin lore","who is the priest at misty pine"}},{q="What is Misty Pine Refuge?",a="Misty Pine Refuge is a peaceful rest stop for mountain travelers. Father Gavin restored an old building in the wilderness for wanderers to recover, rest, and receive healing.",al={"what is misty pine refuge","where is misty pine refuge","misty pine refuge lore"}},{q="What is the Argent Dawn?",a="The Argent Dawn is a holy order that seeks out and destroys unholy and unnatural threats across Azeroth. It also aids those struggling to survive in troubled lands.",al={"what is the argent dawn","argent dawn purpose","who are argent dawn"}},{q="Why does Father Gavin need a shipment of holy candles?",a="Holy candles replenish Father Gavin's supplies at Misty Pine Refuge. They serve religious rites and prayer, and light the refuge for weary travelers.",al={"why candles","holy candles purpose","crate of candles delivery"}},{q="Does Father Gavin take up arms like other Argent Dawn members?",a="Father Gavin chooses to heal and shelter travelers instead of taking up a weapon. The Argent Dawn fights darkness, while he serves through compassion, hospitality, and spiritual care.",al={"does father gavin fight","is father gavin a fighter"}},{q="What is the purpose of the quest Dawn in the Mountains?",a="You carry a crate of holy candles through the mountains to Father Gavin at Misty Pine Refuge, helping sustain his mountain sanctuary.",al={"who gave this quest","where does dawn in the mountains lead"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can follow Father Gavin's gentler path. He ministers to travelers and tends wounds instead of wielding a weapon on the Argent Dawn's front lines.",["faction:Alliance"]="You can aid neutral humanitarian work in dangerous mountain country by supporting an Argent Dawn shelter like Misty Pine Refuge.",["faction:Horde"]="The Argent Dawn accepts aid and offers sanctuary regardless of allegiance. Outposts like Father Gavin's are rare safe havens in the wilderness."},kw={"argent dawn","dawn in the mountains","father gavin","holy candles","misty pine refuge","priest","refuge"},rel={"subzone:misty-pine-refuge","topic:argent-dawn","topic:priest"},m={id=99158},src={"In-game quest text: Dawn in the Mountains"},fv=true}
E["quest:99159"] = {t="quest",n="Finding Warmth",z="general",s="A hearth waits for firewood, while its keeper tends to other duties. Gathered logs keep the fire ready to warm anyone who seeks comfort.",h="A hearth waits for firewood, while its keeper tends to other duties.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Hearth",b="The hearth welcomes travelers who seek warmth. Its keeper has other duties and cannot gather fuel. Bring firewood to keep the flames alive for those who need shelter and comfort.",sp=0},{t="Tending the Fire",b="Some gathered wood is too damp to burn at once. The keeper sets wet pieces aside to dry and feeds seasoned wood to the fire. With the hearth tended, the keeper turns to other pressing matters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the quest Finding Warmth about?",a="You gather firewood to keep a welcoming hearth burning. Its keeper has other duties and asks for help collecting fuel.",al={"finding warmth quest","what is finding warmth","finding warmth firewood"}},{q="Why is the firewood needed?",a="The hearth offers warmth to passing travelers and locals. Firewood keeps it burning while its keeper is busy with other duties.",al={"why need wood","firewood finding warmth","hearth firewood"}},{q="What happens to wet firewood brought in?",a="Wet logs are set aside to dry. The keeper burns seasoned wood right away.",al={"finding warmth wet wood","damp firewood"}},{q="What kind of person offers this task?",a="The host's identity is not given. Their blessing, “Light guide you on your tasks,” suggests reverence for the Holy Light. The host offers an open hearth to warm anyone.",al={"who gives finding warmth","finding warmth light guide you"}},{q="Are there more tasks after completing Finding Warmth?",a="Yes. After you deliver the firewood, the host says other tasks need an able pair of hands.",al={"more quests after finding warmth","finding warmth followup"}},{q="Who is welcome at this hearth?",a="Anyone passing through who needs warmth, shelter, or comfort is welcome at the hearth.",al={"hearth open soul","open hearth finding warmth"}}},kw={"finding warmth","firewood","hearth","light","warmth","wood"},rel={"topic:light"},m={id=99159},src={"In-game quest text: Finding Warmth"},fv=true}
E["quest:99160"] = {t="quest",n="Rime's Wrath",z="general",s="Minor ice elementals roam the area, and no peaceful way to calm them is known. You are asked to destroy them before they can harm anyone.",h="Minor ice elementals roam the area, and no peaceful way to calm them is known.",sec={{t="A Bitter Manifestation",b="Minor ice elementals have gathered nearby, and their biting cold puts passersby at risk. You are asked to contain the danger before the spirits can harm anyone.",sp=0},{t="Beyond Placation",b="Those who hoped to calm the frost spirits do not know how. As the elementals grow more dangerous, you are asked to destroy them and protect the surrounding territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rime's Wrath?",a="You are asked to destroy minor ice elementals that threaten the area. No peaceful way to calm them is known, so force is needed to keep others safe.",al={"what is rimes wrath","quest rimes wrath","rimes wrath overview"}},{q="Why do the minor ice elementals need to be destroyed?",a="The minor ice elementals have grown too dangerous to leave unchecked. With no known way to calm them, you are asked to destroy them to protect the area.",al={"why kill ice elementals","why fight them","cant we calm the elementals"}},{q="Who requests the destruction of the elementals?",a="Someone concerned for the area's safety hoped to calm the spirits but did not know how. You are asked to destroy the elementals before they can harm anyone.",al={"who gives rimes wrath","who wants the elementals dead","who is the questgiver"}},{q="Could the elementals have been dealt with peacefully?",a="Those who sent you do not know how to calm the elementals. Without a way to soothe their aggression, you are asked to destroy them.",al={"can ice elementals be calmed","placate ice elementals","why not soothe elementals"}},{q="What kind of creatures are minor ice elementals?",a="Minor ice elementals are spirits of elemental frost. Their cold and aggression make them dangerous to travelers and local inhabitants if left roaming freely.",al={"what are minor ice elementals","ice elementals danger","how strong are minor ice elementals"}},{q="What is the outcome of dealing with the elementals?",a="After you defeat ten minor ice elementals, the immediate danger is quelled. Those who sent you regret that violence was needed, but leaving the spirits unchecked was too risky.",al={"what happens after rimes wrath","rimes wrath conclusion"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you study the shaping of ice magic, and wild minor ice elementals show elemental forces in an unruly form.",["class:Shaman"]="As a Shaman, you seek to understand and commune with elemental spirits. These hostile ice spirits cannot be calmed, so you must quell them by force."},kw={"elementals","frost","ice elementals","minor ice elementals","placate","rime's wrath","rimes wrath"},m={id=99160},src={"In-game quest text: Rime's Wrath"},fv=true}
E["quest:99161"] = {t="quest",n="Rime's Wrath",z="general",s="After a rockslide, Avala makes the mountain pass dangerous. An observer asks you to hunt the great elemental and bring back its core, so the slopes may grow safer for travelers.",h="After a rockslide, Avala makes the mountain pass dangerous.",sec={{t="The Wake of the Rockslide",b="A rockslide has unsettled the mountain pass, and elementals have appeared. One is far larger and stronger than the others. The observer watching the pass named it Avala. Its power brings sudden weather shifts and shakes the cliffs. Loose stone and bitter winter chills now make the pass perilous for travelers.",sp=0},{t="Quelling Avala",b="Avala's influence makes the pass more dangerous. The observer calls on you to stop it before more collapses claim lives. You face the elemental amid the harsh conditions it stirs, then bring back its core as proof of its death. With Avala gone, the violent weather shifts ease, and the mountain passes grow safer for travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rime's Wrath?",a="An observer asks you to hunt Avala, a great elemental that appeared after a rockslide, and bring back its core. Avala brings erratic weather and more slides to the mountain pass.",al={"rimes wrath","what is rimes wrath","rime's wrath quest"}},{q="Who or what is Avala?",a="Avala is a particularly large elemental that appeared after a major rockslide. It brings sudden weather changes, freezing chills, and dangerous tremors to the area. The observer watching the pass gave Avala its name.",al={"what is avala","who is avala","avala elemental"}},{q="Why does Avala need to be destroyed?",a="Avala brings unpredictable weather and rockslides to the nearby slopes. If it remains, its influence over winter weather and the land could cause further collapses and kill travelers crossing the pass.",al={"why kill avala","reason to kill avala","why destroy avala"}},{q="What proof is needed to complete Rime's Wrath?",a="The observer asks you to bring back Avala's core after defeating it. The core proves the elemental is dead and the threat has ended.",al={"avala proof","what item drops","avala core proof"}},{q="How did Avala first appear?",a="Avala appeared after an initial rockslide disrupted the region. Other elementals surfaced too, but Avala was the largest and most dangerous among them.",al={"where did avala come from","avala origin","how did avala spawn"}},{q="Who offers the quest Rime's Wrath?",a="A local observer near the dangerous mountain pass calls on capable champions to stop Avala. After watching the rockslide and the elementals appear, the observer seeks to prevent needless deaths. When the work is done, the observer invokes the Holy Light's blessing.",al={"who gives rimes wrath","quest giver rimes wrath","rimes wrath questgiver"}},{q="What happens after Avala is defeated?",a="After Avala dies and you return its core, the severe weather swings and tremors ease. The observer blesses you in the Light and gives you a reward, saying the pass is safer for travelers.",al={"what happens after avala dies","rimes wrath completion","after rimes wrath"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know how dangerous an unbridled elemental like Avala can be. Its turmoil changes the weather and shakes the stone. Calming such beings helps restore harmony among the elements.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you protect travelers and common folk from sudden calamity. The observer invokes the Light's blessing in gratitude for the deaths you helped prevent."},kw={"avala","avala core","elemental","elemental core","rime's wrath","rockslide","weather","winter"},rel={"topic:light"},m={id=99161},src={"In-game quest text: Rime's Wrath"},fv=true}
E["quest:99162"] = {t="quest",n="Treacherous Cold",z="general",s="In Dun Morogh, snow and ice slides bury Ironforge mountaineers in the high passes. You search for their inscribed rifles so their families can learn who fell.",h="In Dun Morogh, snow and ice slides bury Ironforge mountaineers in the high passes.",sec={{t="Perils of the Peaks",b="In Dun Morogh, sudden avalanches and falling ice threaten travelers and soldiers. Even Ironforge's hardened mountaineers can be overwhelmed. When winter strikes without warning, novice recruits may pay with their lives.",sp=0},{t="Grim Recovery",b="Mountain slides can bury patrols, and each search through the hazardous terrain races against time. Elemental activity across the region has grown more intense, making rescue parties perilous to send out. Scouts ask you to search the drifts for fallen mountaineers and recover their inscribed rifles before snow hides them forever.",sp=0},{t="Inscribed Stocks",b="Ironforge mountaineers carve their names into their rifle stocks. Recovering those weapons from the drifts helps identify the fallen, so their families in Ironforge can learn of their service.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Treacherous Cold?",a="You search Dun Morogh's snow-choked passes for mountaineers caught in sudden slides and recover their service rifles.",al={"what is treacherous cold","treacherous cold quest"}},{q="Why are the mountaineers' rifles collected?",a="Mountaineers engrave their names on their rifle stocks. If snow buries their bodies or makes them impossible to recover, their weapons can identify them so Ironforge can notify their families.",al={"why collect rifles","mountaineer rifles","why do we need their guns"}},{q="Who is being lost in the snow?",a="Novice mountaineers on patrol in Dun Morogh face particular danger from sudden avalanches, falling ice, and harsh weather in the high peaks.",al={"who are the victims","who gets lost in dun morogh"}},{q="Why hasn't the search been conducted already?",a="The scout who asks for help usually searches for survivors and gathers the fallen after a slide. Recent elemental disturbances in Dun Morogh have made the deep passes too dangerous to search alone.",al={"why cant the questgiver look","why need an adventurer"}},{q="What happens to the rifles once recovered?",a="The recovered rifles go back to Ironforge, where authorities make sure the fallen mountaineers' families receive their personal weapons.",al={"where do rifles go","what happens to recovered rifles"}},{q="What makes the high passes of Dun Morogh so dangerous?",a="Dun Morogh's heights bring severe cold, blinding slides, and unstable cliffs. Restless elemental activity adds to the danger, and even trained dwarven patrols can quickly succumb.",al={"how dangerous is dun morogh","dun morogh hazards"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Dun Morogh's peaks as your homeland. Yet sudden avalanches and hostile elements can claim even seasoned mountaineers in the high passes.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know mountaineers depend on their rifles in the frozen wilds. They carve their names into the stocks so their identities and deeds will be remembered.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help recover fallen mountaineers' gear. Then Ironforge can bring word to the families whose loved ones guard the high roads."},kw={"avalanche","dun morogh","ironforge","mountaineers","rifles","snow slide","treacherous cold"},rel={"zone:dunmorogh","zone:ironforge","topic:light"},m={id=99162},src={"In-game quest text: Treacherous Cold"},fv=true}
E["quest:99191"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="The High Order is taking wool cloth from those who seek its full recognition. Sixty pieces meet its current need.",h="The High Order is taking wool cloth from those who seek its full recognition.",sec={{t="A Worthy Gift",b="The High Order is accepting wool cloth, and sixty pieces meet its current needs. The giver can take your donation now. In return, the order grants you full recognition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the High Order need?",a="The High Order needs wool cloth, and sixty pieces meet its current need.",al={"high order wool","what to donate","wool donation"}},{q="How much wool cloth should I give?",a="Give sixty pieces of wool cloth to earn full recognition from the High Order.",al={"how much wool","sixty wool","wool amount"}},{q="Who can take the donation?",a="The giver can accept your sixty pieces of wool cloth.",al={"who takes wool","donation giver","give wool"}},{q="What do I gain by donating?",a="Giving sixty pieces of wool cloth earns you full recognition from the High Order.",al={"wool recognition","high order standing","donation benefit"}}},kw={"donation","high order","recognition","sixty pieces","wool","wool cloth"},rel={"quest:92596"},m={id=99191},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:99196"] = {t="quest",n="A Donation of Wool",z="general",s="The Windshapers are taking wool cloth donations, and sixty pieces will earn their full recognition.",h="The Windshapers are taking wool cloth donations, and sixty pieces will earn their full recognition.",sec={{t="A Gift of Wool",b="The Windshapers accept wool cloth from you. When you are ready to give, their representative can take sixty pieces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do the Windshapers want?",a="The Windshapers are accepting wool cloth donations.",al={"windshapers donation","what wool do they take"}},{q="How much wool cloth should I give?",a="Give the Windshapers sixty pieces of wool cloth for full recognition.",al={"how much wool","sixty wool"}},{q="What do I get for donating the wool?",a="Sixty pieces of wool cloth earn the Windshapers’ full recognition for your generosity.",al={"wool donation result","windshapers recognition"}},{q="Can their representative take the wool now?",a="Their representative can take the sixty pieces when you have them with you and are ready to donate.",al={"give wool now","donate cloth"}}},kw={"donation","recognition","sixty pieces","windshapers","wool","wool cloth"},m={id=99196},src={"In-game quest text: A Donation of Wool"},fv=true}
E["quest:99260"] = {t="quest",n="Fillion's Mission",z="general",s="Fillion lies wounded after his survey at the Overlook Standing Stones. The readings meant to guide skycutters between Skywall and Azeroth are presumed lost.",h="Fillion lies wounded after his survey at the Overlook Standing Stones.",sec={{t="A Perilous Assignment",b="Fillion went to the Overlook Standing Stones to measure elemental currents. Those readings are needed to calculate safe courses for skycutter vessels between Skywall and Azeroth. After an ordeal that required his rescue, he is too wounded to finish the work. The vital data is presumed lost, so he sends his rescuer to report to the Supreme Magister.",sp=0},{t="Planar Strife in Valanaar",b="In Valanaar, Supreme Magister Elaadrin Evengale is relieved to hear that Fillion survived, though the research is lost. Without reliable readings, safe routes across the Elemental Plane will be hard to open. Reports say the rival Windshapers have found their own way through the planes. They refuse to share it, putting factional secrecy before the welfare of all.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fillion?",a="Fillion is an emissary or scout sent by the Supreme Magister to measure elemental currents at the Overlook Standing Stones. After an adventurer rescues him, he is too weak to finish the work.",al={"who is fillion","fillion backstory","fillion wow"}},{q="Who is Supreme Magister Elaadrin Evengale?",a="Elaadrin Evengale is the Supreme Magister in Valanaar. He directs efforts to navigate the elemental plane safely and recover planar data for travel between Skywall and Azeroth.",al={"who is supreme magister","elaadrin evengale","who is elaadrin"}},{q="Why was Fillion's data so important?",a="The readings track elemental currents at the Overlook Standing Stones. They are needed to calculate safe courses for skycutters through the elemental plane to Azeroth.",al={"why is data important","what data fillion lost","elemental data skywall"}},{q="Who are the Windshapers?",a="The Windshapers are a faction reported to have found their own way through the planes. Supreme Magister Evengale says they guard it out of dogmatic hubris instead of sharing it for the wider good of their people.",al={"who are windshapers","windshapers lore","windshaper rivals"}},{q="What are skycutters?",a="Skycutters are vessels made to fly through the elemental planes. They need precise readings of elemental currents to travel between Skywall and Azeroth safely.",al={"what are skycutters","skycutter ship","sky cutter"}},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are a faction Supreme Magister Evengale regards with disdain. He compares the Windshapers' selfish, dogmatic conduct to theirs.",al={"who are alaketh","al'aketh","alaketh lore"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can appreciate the delicate magical calculations needed to guide skycutter vessels through planar turbulence.",["race:Skyborne"]="As one of the Skyborne, you know the struggle to establish safe routes between Skywall and Azeroth amid factional discord."},kw={"elaadrin evengale","elemental plane","fillion","overlook standing stones","skycutter","skywall","valanaar","windshapers"},rel={"quest:92699","topic:skywall","topic:elemental-plane","quest:92595"},m={id=99260},src={"In-game quest text: Fillion's Mission"},fv=true}
E["quest:99411"] = {t="quest",n="Kyle's Gone Missing!",z="general",s="In Bloodhoof Village, Ahab Wheathoof asks you to find his missing dog, Kyle the Frenzied. A cut of tender strider meat calms the hungry pup and guides him safely home.",h="In Bloodhoof Village, Ahab Wheathoof asks you to find his missing dog, Kyle the Frenzied.",sec={{t="A Missing Hound",b="Ahab Wheathoof is an elder in Bloodhoof Village, and he worries over his wayward pet, Kyle the Frenzied. To outsiders, Kyle's name sounds alarming, but to Ahab he is a prized puppy. He has slipped away onto Mulgore's grassy plains.\n\nAhab asks travelers passing through the settlement to track down his unruly companion. A hearty meal may calm Kyle's wild spirits.",sp=0},{t="A Simple Remedy",b="Kyle needs a cut of tender strider meat from the swift plainstriders roaming Mulgore. The treat satisfies the hungry pup and soothes his frenzied mood. Then it nudges him back toward Bloodhoof Village and his grateful owner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ahab Wheathoof?",a="Ahab Wheathoof is an elder tauren who lives in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. He cares deeply for his prized dog, Kyle, and asks traveling adventurers to find and feed him when he wanders too far from home.",al={"who is ahab wheathoof","ahab mulgore","quest giver kyle"}},{q="Who is Kyle the Frenzied?",a="Kyle the Frenzied is Ahab Wheathoof's beloved dog and prized companion. Tender strider meat can calm him and lure him back.",al={"who is kyle","kyle dog","kyle the frenzied"}},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="Bloodhoof Village lies in central Mulgore, south of Thunder Bluff. Local tribes, traders, and herders gather there.",al={"where is bloodhoof village","bloodhoof location"}},{q="Why does Kyle need tender strider meat?",a="Kyle has a particular appetite for fresh meat from the plainstriders that wander Mulgore. Tender strider meat pacifies the hungry hound and convinces him to return safely to Ahab.",al={"why tender strider meat","strider meat kyle","how to calm kyle"}},{q="Why is Kyle considered frenzied?",a="Locals know Kyle as the Frenzied because he roams the plains when lost or famished. His frenzy subsides once a patient traveler properly feeds him.",al={"why is kyle frenzied","kyle angry"}},{q="Where can Kyle be found?",a="Kyle wanders the open plains around Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. Travelers search the nearby prairies until they find him and can offer him a meal.",al={"kyle location","where is kyle"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Ahab Wheathoof as a Bloodhoof Village resident. Helping him is a familiar gesture of community support across Mulgore's pastures.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strengthen ties with the Shu'halo by helping Bloodhoof's villagers with everyday matters as they settle and defend their homeland."},kw={"ahab wheathoof","bloodhoof village","kyle","kyle the frenzied","kyle's gone missing!","mulgore","plainstrider","tender strider meat"},rel={"subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore"},m={id=99411},src={"In-game quest text: Kyle's Gone Missing!"},fv=true}
E["topic:agamaggan"] = {t="topic",n="Agamaggan",z="general",s="In the War of the Ancients, Agamaggan gave his life against the Burning Legion. His blood and fallen body gave rise to the Razorfen, now home to the quilboar.",h="In the War of the Ancients, Agamaggan gave his life against the Burning Legion.",sec={{t="The War of the Ancients",b="Ten thousand years ago, Agamaggan joined the fight against the Burning Legion. The mighty demigod charged with terrifying force, yet fell in the War of the Ancients. His sacrifice helped save Azeroth from ruin.",sp=0},{t="The Razorfen and Blood Shards",b="Agamaggan fell in the southern Barrens, and his body changed the land. His blood soaked the soil, and thorny vines rose from the dry earth to form the Razorfen. The quilboar hold this ground sacred. They see Razorfen Kraul as his resting body and Razorfen Downs as his gaping skull.\n\nAcross the Barrens, crystallized Blood Shards are believed to be remnants of his spilled blood. Quilboar geomancers and shamans draw power from the lingering primal energy within them.",sp=0},{t="Father of the Quilboar",b="The quilboar revere Agamaggan as their divine forefather. To them, the surrounding brambles are the living armor their creator left to shelter them from hostile neighbors. They believe his spirit watches over them, lending vigor to their warriors and earth magic to their geomancers.\n\nThey defend the thorns against tauren, orcs, and centaur. They believe it is their sacred duty to guard the fallen body of the boar god who birthed them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan was a colossal boar wild god and one of the Ancient Guardians from Azeroth's earliest days. He fought the Burning Legion in the War of the Ancients and gave his life to help save the world.",al={"agamaggan lore","who is the great boar","agamaggan background"},it="identity"},{q="How did the Razorfen form?",a="Agamaggan's blood soaked into the earth where he fell in the southern Barrens. Thorny vines rose from the soil and formed the Razorfen, including Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs.",al={"how did razorfen get there","why are there huge thorns in the barrens","razorfen origin"},it="origin"},{q="What is the connection between Agamaggan and the quilboar?",a="The quilboar are Agamaggan's descendants and revere him as their creator and god. They build their settlements among the thorns and devote their shamanic rites to his memory.",al={"are quilboar related to agamaggan","quilboar god","who made the quilboar"},it="ties"},{q="What are Blood Shards?",a="Blood Shards are crystallized remnants of Agamaggan's spilled blood, found across the Barrens. Their lingering primal energy gives quilboar geomancers and shamans power.",al={"what do blood shards do","blood shards lore","blood of agamaggan"},it="item"},{q="Did night elves worship Agamaggan?",a="Yes. Night elves revere Agamaggan as one of the noble Ancients who gave his life fighting the Burning Legion.",al={"night elves agamaggan"}},{q="Is Agamaggan's skull visible in the world?",a="Quilboar tradition holds that the gaping entrance to Razorfen Downs is Agamaggan's hollowed skull and jaw. They believe its maw will consume trespassers who are not loyal to their god.",al={"razorfen downs skull","where is agamaggan head","agamaggan entrance"},it="place"},{q="What is the history of Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan was one of the primeval Ancient Guardians, revered as the Great Boar. Ten thousand years ago, during the War of the Ancients, he came forth to battle the Burning Legion. Though the colossal boar fell in combat, his actions helped save Azeroth from ruin, and where his blood soaked the earth, the great thorny vines of the Razorfen arose.",al={"agamaggan lore","story of agamaggan","how did agamaggan die","agamaggan war of the ancients"},it="history",add="f6e0fe38"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids honor Agamaggan as an Ancient Guardian who fought alongside Cenarius and gave his life in the War of the Ancients.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman in the Barrens, you can sense potent earth and spirit energies lingering in Agamaggan's blood and the Razorfen thorns.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you remember Agamaggan as the fierce demigod who gave his life against the Burning Legion in the War of the Ancients.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Agamaggan's quilboar children, whose devotion to their fallen god drives relentless attacks across the Barrens."},kw={"agamaggan","ancient guardian","barrens","blood shards","cenarius","great boar","quilboar","razorfen","war of the ancients"},rel={"topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:cenarius","quest:5052","quest:5044"},src={"Agamaggan"}}
E["topic:alliance"] = {t="topic",n="Alliance",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Alliance now gathers its peoples around Stormwind. Its roots lie in Lordaeron's ruin, and its heart is Stormwind City, beside Ironforge's dwarves, the exiled gnomes, and Kalimdor's night elves.",h="Across Azeroth, the Alliance now gathers its peoples around Stormwind.",sec={{t="From Lordaeron to Stormwind",b="The modern Alliance descends from the Alliance of Lordaeron. During the Second War, Sir Anduin Lothar led Stormwind refugees north and united the Seven Kingdoms, dwarves, and high elves against the Old Horde.\n\nThe Scourge and the Third War ravaged the north. Lordaeron lay in ruins, and survivors were driven into scattered resistance. The restored Kingdom of Stormwind filled the void. Today it is the foremost seat of human leadership, carrying honor and faith into a fractured world.",sp=0},{t="A Coalition of Necessity and Kinship",b="In the Eastern Kingdoms, the Alliance rests on the steadfast bond between humans and the dwarves of Ironforge, ruled by King Magni Bronzebeard. Gnomes also live among the dwarves, driven from Gnomeregan by a devastating trogg uprising.\n\nHigh Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque guides the exiled gnomes. They bring their brilliant engineering to the Alliance war effort, believing the coalition must survive if they are ever to reclaim their irradiated home.",sp=0},{t="The Kalimdor Front",b="Across the Great Sea, the reclusive night elves left millennia of isolation after the Battle of Mount Hyjal. They lost their immortality and now clash bitterly with the Horde over logging in Ashenvale. So the kaldorei allied with their newfound mortal companions.\n\nCultural friction remains. Some traditionalists condemn the presence of humans and dwarves in ancient forests. The Alliance offers vital military and diplomatic help to guard Kalimdor from demonic remnants and Horde expansion.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Shadows",b="The Alliance faces strains within its own ranks. King Varian Wrynn vanished under mysterious circumstances while traveling to a diplomatic summit. His young son Anduin took the throne under Highlord Bolvar Fordragon's regency.\n\nRelations with former human allies have also frayed. The maritime kingdom of Kul Tiras keeps its distance, while Sylvanas Windrunner's undead Forsaken hold the ruins of Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What races make up the Alliance?",a="The Alliance's core peoples are the humans of Stormwind, the mountain dwarves of Ironforge, the exiled gnomes of Gnomeregan, and the night elves of Kalimdor.",al={"alliance races","who is in the alliance","playable alliance races"},it="people"},{q="Who leads the Alliance right now?",a="No single absolute monarch rules the whole Alliance. Stormwind is ruled by the boy king anduin wrynn under highlord bolvar fordragon, his regent, after King Varian Wrynn disappeared. The other member nations follow King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque of the gnomes, and the night elf leadership on Kalimdor.",al={"alliance leader","who is high king","who runs stormwind"},it="leader"},{q="How did the Alliance of Lordaeron become the modern Alliance?",a="King Terenas Menethil II and Anduin Lothar established the original Alliance to repel the Old Horde during the Second War. After the Scourge destroyed Lordaeron in the Third War, leadership shifted south to the rebuilt Kingdom of Stormwind, which forged new covenants with the dwarves, gnomes, and night elves.",al={"alliance of lordaeron vs alliance","what happened to lordaeron","alliance origin"},it="history"},{q="Why did the night elves join the Alliance?",a="After the Third War and the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the night elves lost their immortality and could no longer remain secluded. The Orcish Horde was actively deforesting Warsong Gulch in Ashenvale, so the kaldorei made a military pact with the humans and dwarves to defend their ancestral lands.",al={"why are night elves alliance","night elf alliance lore","kaldorei alliance"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Kul Tiras not part of the Alliance right now?",a="Kul Tiras was a pillar of the old Alliance of Lordaeron, but it has kept to itself since that alliance splintered. Its Grand Admiral, Daelin Proudmoore, invaded Durotar and was slain by the Horde. The island kingdom has not joined the new Alliance led from Stormwind.",al={"where is kul tiras","is kul tiras alliance","daelin proudmoore kul tiras"}},{q="Why didn't the gnomes help during the Third War?",a="During the Third War, a subterranean trogg invasion struck Gnomeregan. Believing the Scourge threat to the surface was greater, the gnomes concealed their crisis from their allies and fought alone. Radiation and invasion brought down the city, forcing survivors into Ironforge.",al={"where were gnomes in warcraft 3","gnomes third war","gnomeregan fall"},it="history"},{q="What is the Alliance's stance toward the Forsaken?",a="Many in the Alliance regard the undead as abominations and tools of the Scourge that destroyed Lordaeron. The Alliance remains openly hostile toward the undead who are reclaiming the northern kingdom.",al={"alliance view of forsaken","why hate undead","forsaken alliance relations"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the Alliance?",a="The Alliance is a grand coalition of mortal races dedicated to nobility, honor, justice, and preserving order across Azeroth. Evolved from the remnants of the fallen Alliance of Lordaeron, it unites humans, Ironforge dwarves, gnomes, and night elves under a shared purpose. Rather than being bound purely by desperation, its members are tied together by common traditions, faith, and an abiding loathing of demonic corruption. Together, they pool their military might, technical skill, and ancient wisdom to protect their people and bring light to a war-torn world.",al={"what is the alliance","who are the alliance","grand alliance"},it="identity",add="90827062"},{q="Why does the Alliance fight the Horde?",a="The conflict runs deep, born from generations of bloodshed. The Alliance remembers the brutality of the First and Second Wars, when the original Horde destroyed the kingdom of Stormwind and devastated the Eastern Kingdoms. Even after uniting temporarily at Mount Hyjal, peace remains fragile and bitter. Ongoing resource skirmishes, such as the Warsong Clan's continued logging in the ancestral forests of Ashenvale, keep animosity boiling. To many across the Alliance, the Horde represents an untamed and dangerous threat that must constantly be guarded against.",al={"why fight horde","why hate horde","alliance horde conflict","why war with horde"},it="conflict",add="76fd3754"},{q="What does it mean to serve the Alliance?",a="To champion the Alliance is to stand as a bulwark of duty, justice, and order against the encroaching darkness. Whether you hail from the halls of Ironforge, the towers of Stormwind, the refugee workshops of Tinker Town, or the sacred boughs of Teldrassil, you are sworn to protect allied lands from monsters, invaders, and the savage reach of enemies. Serving means putting the greater good and noble ideals above individual gain, upholding sacred traditions, and ensuring the survival of free peoples across Azeroth.",al={"serving the alliance","alliance duty","what does alliance expect"},it="for_you",add="760e04fc"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As the chief architects of the faction's recovery, humans see the Alliance as civilization's rightful defender and a guardian of the Church of the Holy Light against wild and demonic forces.",["race:Dwarf"]="The dwarves of Ironforge are humanity's most steadfast and loyal allies. They lend the Alliance their formidable iron, mountain infantry, and deep friendship.",["race:Gnome"]="As refugees in Ironforge, gnomes bring their scientific ingenuity to Alliance armadas. They trust that loyalty between allies will one day provide the strength to liberate Gnomeregan.",["race:NightElf"]="Driven from isolation by the Third War, night elves must find a necessary kinship with the younger races to check Horde aggression in Ashenvale.",["faction:Alliance"]="Your sworn faction fights across two continents to preserve law, tradition, and mortal sovereignty against the Scourge, wild beasts, and the advancing Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde sees the Alliance as an entrenched, expansionist power whose self-righteous ideals threaten its members' sovereignty and survival on their lands."},kw={"alliance","alliance of lordaeron","anduin wrynn","bolvar fordragon","darnassus","gnomeregan","grand alliance","ironforge","magni bronzebeard","mekkatorque","stormwind"},rel={"topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:horde","zone:stormwind","zone:ironforge","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:second-war"},src={"Alliance"}}
E["topic:alliance-of-lordaeron"] = {t="topic",n="Alliance of Lordaeron",z="general",s="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, the Alliance of Lordaeron once held the Old Horde at bay. Seven human kingdoms joined with Khaz Modan dwarves, Wildhammer gryphon riders, gnomes, and high elves in the Second War, under Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar and King Terenas Menethil II. Political fractures and the Scourge broke the coalition during the Third War, yet its legacy endures in today’s Alliance.",h="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, the Alliance of Lordaeron once held the Old Horde at bay.",sec={{t="A Coalition Born in Ashes",b="After Stormwind fell in the First War, Regent Lord Anduin Lothar led its battered refugees across the Great Sea to Capital City. There he pleaded their cause before King Terenas Menethil II. The king called the human rulers to council, though old rivalries and border tensions divided them. The Horde’s threat outweighed those disputes. The seven human nations chose Lothar as Supreme Commander and bound themselves in a desperate pact.",sp=0},{t="The Second War and the New Vanguard",b="The Alliance faced brutal orcish warriors, dark warlocks, and monstrous red dragons. Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Lothar formed the Knights of the Silver Hand, raising holy paladins such as Uther the Lightbringer to counter the Horde’s dark magic. Fighting spread across the Hinterlands, and the siege of Aerie Peak was broken. Then Kurdran Wildhammer pledged his gryphon riders to the skies.\n\nSoon after, the Bronzebeard dwarves and Gnomeregan gnomes were freed. They joined the high elven rangers under Alleria Windrunner. King Perenolde of Alterac betrayed the coalition, but the Alliance drove the Horde back to Blackrock Spire and broke its dominion.",sp=0},{t="Fracture and Ruin",b="Victory left bitterness in place of lasting peace. Disputes flared over the taxes needed to keep the orc internment camps and rebuild Stormwind. Gilneas saw little gain in remaining, built the Greymane Wall, and cut ties. Stromgarde departed over disputes about territory and prisoners, while Quel'Thalas withdrew behind its enchanted runestones. King Terenas tried to hold together the coalition that remained.\n\nDuring the Third War, the Cult of the Damned and the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron and dismantled it. Arthas Menethil’s betrayal tore out the kingdom’s heart and ended the golden age of the northern realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Alliance of Lordaeron?",a="The Alliance of Lordaeron united the Seven Kingdoms of humanity, the dwarves of Ironforge and Aerie Peak, the gnomes of Gnomeregan, and the high elves of Quel'Thalas against Orgrim Doomhammer’s Horde in the Second War.",al={"what is lordaeron alliance","who was in the first alliance","grand alliance history"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the Alliance formed in Capital City instead of Stormwind?",a="Stormwind had been conquered and destroyed in the First War. Regent Lord Anduin Lothar led the surviving people north by ship to Lordaeron, where he warned King Terenas Menethil II of the alien threat.",al={"why lordaeron","stormwind in second war","why did lothar go north"},it="origin"},{q="Who led the Alliance of Lordaeron?",a="King Terenas Menethil II hosted the coalition and guided its diplomacy. Sir Anduin Lothar became Supreme Commander of its armed forces, and Daelin Proudmoore served as Grand Admiral of the fleets.",al={"leader of lordaeron alliance","supreme commander","who was in charge"},it="leader"},{q="Why did Alterac betray the Alliance?",a="King Aiden Perenolde feared the Orcish Horde could not be stopped, so he secretly made a deal with Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Alterac offered safe passage through its mountain passes in return for being spared from slaughter.",al={"perenolde betrayal","what did alterac do","alterac second war"},it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Alliance of Lordaeron fall apart?",a="After the Second War, disputes over the cost of internment camps and rebuilding Stormwind led Gilneas, Stromgarde, and Quel'Thalas to secede. The remaining coalition was later destroyed in the Third War, when Prince Arthas and the Scourge annihilated Lordaeron.",al={"why did alliance collapse","what happened to the old alliance","why did gilneas leave"},it="ruin"},{q="How is this different from the Alliance of today?",a="The Alliance of Lordaeron centered on the northern kingdoms around Capital City and Dalaran. Today’s Alliance centers on the rebuilt southern kingdom of Stormwind and includes the night elves of Kalimdor, while drawing inspiration from Lothar’s coalition.",al={"old alliance vs new alliance","difference between alliances","is this the current alliance"},it="today"},{q="Who was part of the Alliance of Lordaeron?",a="The coalition united all seven human kingdoms: Lordaeron, Stormwind, Stromgarde, Kul Tiras, Dalaran, Gilneas, and Alterac. As the Second War escalated, they were joined by the Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge, the Wildhammer dwarves of Aerie Peak, the gnomes of Gnomeregan, and the high elves of Quel'Thalas, alongside the paladins of the Silver Hand and the Church of the Holy Light.",al={"alliance of lordaeron members","who joined alliance of lordaeron","alliance of lordaeron nations"},it="allies",add="dd426ccb"},{q="How was the Alliance of Lordaeron formed?",a="After the Orcish Horde destroyed Stormwind in the First War, Regent Lord Anduin Lothar fled north with the survivors to seek aid from King Terenas Menethil II. Terenas gathered the rulers of the human nations in Capital City to confront the threat. Setting aside their rivalries, the kingdoms united under Lothar's supreme command.",al={"alliance of lordaeron history","how did alliance of lordaeron start","creation of alliance of lordaeron"},it="history",add="62444fc6"},{q="Why was it called the Alliance of Lordaeron?",a="It earned the name because the northern kingdom of Lordaeron served as the heart and rallying ground of the union. King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron called the Seven Kingdoms together in Capital City to answer the fall of Stormwind, and Lordaeron stood as the political anchor and primary military supplier through the Second War.",al={"why alliance of lordaeron","alliance of lordaeron name meaning","why called alliance of lordaeron"},it="name",add="913db280"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The memory of the Alliance of Lordaeron gives the modern Alliance, centered in Stormwind, its ideals and sense of purpose.",["class:Paladin"]="Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Anduin Lothar created the Knights of the Silver Hand as the Alliance of Lordaeron’s holy shock troops.",["race:Human"]="The Alliance brought all Seven Kingdoms under one banner for the only time since the ancient Empire of Arathor. Regional rivalries and the Scourge later scattered them.",["race:Dwarf"]="The Ironforge Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers of Aerie Peak forged their modern ties to human civilization in the battles of the Second War."},kw={"alliance of lordaeron","anduin lothar","capital city","grand alliance","second war","seven kingdoms","silver hand","terenas menethil"},rel={"topic:anduin-lothar","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:second-war","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Alliance of Lordaeron"}}
E["topic:alterac-kingdom"] = {t="topic",n="Alterac (kingdom)",z="general",s="In the years after the Second War, Alterac lies broken and its capital stands abandoned in the snow. Once one of seven human kingdoms in the Alterac Mountains, it fell when King Aiden Perenolde secretly aided the Old Horde. Now dispossessed nobles and outlaws fight beneath the Syndicate's banner.",h="In the years after the Second War, Alterac lies broken and its capital stands abandoned in the snow.",sec={{t="A Nation in the Crags",b="Alterac began as an Arathorian city-state after the Troll Wars, thousands of years ago. Its settlers held mountain passes and trading outposts. When the empire fractured, they formed an independent realm. Rugged Alterac bordered the prosperous lands of Lordaeron and Stromgarde. Its mountain fighters were tough, yet friction along the border with Thoras Trollbane's Stromgarde left the kingdom isolated long before the Dark Portal opened.",sp=0},{t="The Great Betrayal",b="Sir Anduin Lothar forged the Alliance of Lordaeron, and King Aiden Perenolde joined with deep reluctance. As Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde swept north, Perenolde believed humanity was doomed. So he secretly made a pact with the Warchief.\n\nIn return for Alterac's safety, Perenolde opened fortified mountain passes, plotted against Alliance forces, and sent soldiers and sailors to help the Horde besiege Lordaeron. The betrayal let the orcs reach Capital City far ahead of schedule. When the truth came to light, it shook the Alliance to its core.",sp=0},{t="Ruin and the Syndicate",b="Stromgarde's forces marched into the mountains, exposed Perenolde's treason, and broke Alterac's military. King Terenas Menethil II placed the fallen nation under martial law. For years, Alliance diplomats argued over who should inherit the throne. After the kingdom collapsed, King Perenolde died in disgrace.\n\nHis son, Lord Aliden Perenolde, gathered the bitter, displaced nobles and formed the Syndicate. In orange cloth from their fallen homeland, its bandits and mercenaries now fight ruthlessly to reclaim their ancestral holdings across Hillsbrad and Alterac.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the Kingdom of Alterac?",a="Alterac collapsed during the Second War after King Aiden Perenolde betrayed humanity and sided with the Old Horde. Stromgarde's forces broke the kingdom's military. The crown was dissolved, martial law followed, and Alterac's people were scattered among its ruins.",al={"alterac downfall","why is alterac destroyed","fate of alterac","who destroyed alterac"},it="ruin"},{q="Why did King Perenolde betray the Alliance?",a="Aiden Perenolde believed the Alliance could not defeat the invading Horde. Fearing the destruction of his mountain realm, he secretly allied with Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Doomhammer promised to spare Alterac and grant it sovereign protection after Lordaeron fell, in return for passage through the mountains.",al={"why did perenolde betray","perenolde motive","alterac betrayal reason"},it="motive"},{q="How does the Syndicate relate to Alterac?",a="The Syndicate grew from Alterac's nobility under Lord Aliden Perenolde, son of King Perenolde. It seeks to take back family estates and land across Hillsbrad and Alterac by force. Its orange masks recall Alterac's historic national color.",al={"syndicate connection alterac","who leads the syndicate","why orange masks"},it="ties"},{q="What are Alterac's traditional colors and symbols?",a="Alterac's national color is orange. Its royal military wore that color scheme during the Second War. The Syndicate preserves it today with orange masks and hoods.",al={"alterac flag","alterac color"},it="identity"},{q="Who controls Alterac City right now?",a="Alterac City has no recognized monarch or lawful government. Syndicate outlaws, ogres, and wild mountain beasts overrun much of the ruined capital. No formal Alliance garrison can hold the high passes.",al={"who rules alterac now","alterac city ruins","who lives in alterac city"},it="in_charge"},{q="What was the Kingdom of Alterac?",a="Alterac was one of the seven historic human nations, settled in the high, rugged peaks of the Alterac Mountains. Originating as a fortified city-state of the ancient empire of Arathor, it grew into an independent kingdom commanding strategic mountain passes and trading routes. Though smaller and militarily weaker than neighbors like Lordaeron and Stromgarde, Alterac held vital territory between the northern kingdoms until its catastrophic treason during the Second War shattered its standing forever.",al={"what is alterac","alterac kingdom overview","who are alterac"},it="identity",add="a8320e62"},{q="Where did the Kingdom of Alterac come from?",a="Alterac began as one of the city-states founded by the ancient human empire of Arathor. When Arathor fractured, Alterac became an independent kingdom, often clashing with neighboring Stromgarde, before joining the Alliance of Lordaeron against the Orcish Horde.",al={"alterac history","origin of alterac","how was alterac founded"},it="history",add="c0d5a913"},{q="Who leads the people of Alterac now?",a="The kingdom itself has no recognized sovereign or unified government following the imprisonment and death of King Aiden Perenolde. Its remnants are fractured: many dispossessed nobles and citizens rally under Aiden's son, Lord Aliden Perenolde, who commands the Syndicate in a lawless campaign to reclaim their ancestral lands. Meanwhile, their devastated capital remains contested by wild beasts and rival factions.",al={"who leads alterac","king of alterac","alterac leader"},it="leader",add="6b4d83cf"},{q="Who is Alterac allied with?",a="As a recognized nation, Alterac has no allies left. It broke its original pact with the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War to aid Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde, earning the lasting enmity of the other human realms. Today, its noble remnants within the Syndicate operate as outlaws, working with hired cutthroats and rogues while fighting both the Alliance and the new Horde for survival.",al={"alterac allies","who does alterac fight for","who supports alterac"},it="allies",add="080e3676"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, Alterac's fall recalls the treason that nearly cost humanity everything during the Second War. That memory feeds hostility toward Syndicate bandits trying to reclaim their ancestral estates.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the northern kingdoms, you know Alterac's fall as a tragic lesson in cowardice and division. Fear can shatter the unity forged against foreign invaders.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find the mountain valleys of former Alterac claimed by covert operatives. The highborn thugs of the Syndicate share the region with the secretive assassins of Ravenholdt Manor."},kw={"aiden","aliden","alterac","betrayal","horde","orgrim doomhammer","perenolde","second war","seven kingdoms","syndicate","treason"},rel={"topic:syndicate","topic:second-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","subzone:ravenholdt-manor"},src={"Alterac (kingdom)"}}
E["topic:anduin-lothar"] = {t="topic",n="Anduin Lothar",z="general",s="In Stormwind's royal court, Anduin Lothar grew up beside Prince Llane Wrynn and Medivh. Last of the ancient Arathi bloodline, he led humanity through the First War and united the northern nations in the Second War as Supreme Commander of the Alliance of Lordaeron. His campaign ended at Blackrock Mountain.",h="In Stormwind's royal court, Anduin Lothar grew up beside Prince Llane Wrynn and Medivh.",sec={{t="The Lion's Youth",b="Anduin Lothar grew up in Stormwind's royal court, heir to the bloodline of the Arathi kings. He shared his youth with Prince Llane Wrynn and Medivh. Together, the three ventured recklessly into the wilderness and skirmished with Gurubashi trolls in Stranglethorn Vale. Lothar rose through Stormwind's martial ranks and joined the King's Honor Guard. He also earned renown as an Armsman of the Brotherhood of the Horse.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Stormwind",b="When green-skinned invaders poured from the Black Morass, King Llane named Lothar the King's Champion and charged him with defending the kingdom. Lothar ambushed orcish raiding parties in Westfall, the Redridge Mountains, and Elwynn Forest. He outmaneuvered Warchief Blackhand and broke the first siege of Stormwind City.\n\nThen Medivh was revealed as the one who had opened the Dark Portal. Lothar and the apprentice Khadgar stormed Karazhan and executed the corrupted Guardian. They returned to find King Llane assassinated and Stormwind burning. Lothar gathered the survivors, including young Prince Varian, and led them north across the Great Sea.",sp=1},{t="Supreme Commander and Blackrock Mountain",b="On Lordaeron's shores, Lothar brought King Terenas Menethil II grim news of the Horde. His Arathi lineage and standing as a diplomat helped unite the human realms, Ironforge dwarves, and high elves as the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron. Named Supreme Commander, he led the campaign that drove the Horde south to the foot of Blackrock Mountain.\n\nNear the end of the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer slew Lothar in a clash there. His death did not break the Alliance. His lieutenant Turalyon took command and led the charge that broke the Horde forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Anduin Lothar?",a="Anduin Lothar was a Stormwind knight and the last descendant of the Arathi bloodline. He served as King's Champion during the First War and became Supreme Commander of the Alliance of Lordaeron in the Second War. Humanity remembers him among its great heroes and tacticians.",al={"who is lothar","who was lothar","lion of stormwind lore"},it="identity"},{q="How did Lothar die?",a="Near the end of the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer slew Lothar at the foot of Blackrock Mountain. Afterward, Alliance forces under Turalyon routed the Horde and pursued them to the Dark Portal.",al={"lothar death","how lothar died","who killed lothar"},it="history"},{q="Why is the current prince named Anduin?",a="King Varian Wrynn named his young son, Prince Anduin Wrynn, to honor Sir Anduin Lothar. Lothar rescued Varian from Stormwind's ruins, protected him in exile, and gave his life in the Second War as their homeland was reclaimed.",al={"why is anduin named anduin","anduin wrynn name origin"}},{q="What was Lothar's connection to Medivh and King Llane?",a="Lothar, Prince Llane Wrynn, and the young mage Medivh were childhood friends in Stormwind's royal court. They explored Azeroth and fought trolls and beasts together. Later, Lothar led the strike at Karazhan after Medivh was revealed as the one who opened the Dark Portal and betrayed the realm.",al={"lothar medivh llane","lothar childhood friends"},it="allies"},{q="Why is Lothar called the 'Last of the Arathi'?",a="Lothar was the last direct descendant of the ancient Arathi line, the dynasty that united humanity and founded the empire of Arathor millennia ago. That heritage gave him standing with the northern kings when he united them under the Alliance banner in Lordaeron.",al={"lothar arathi bloodline","arathi descendant"},it="name"},{q="What was Lothar's role in the Brotherhood of the Horse?",a="Lothar joined the Brotherhood of the Horse and earned renown as an Armsman. During the First War, he used the order's disciplined cavalry charges to outflank and disrupt Horde formations.",al={"brotherhood of the horse lothar","knights of stormwind lothar"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="To humanity, Lothar is a model of sacrifice and honor. His Arathi blood helped unite the human kingdoms, and he died at Blackrock Mountain as the kingdom was liberated.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lothar united elves, dwarves, and humans as the Alliance's first Supreme Commander. He led them against the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Warrior"]="Lothar was renowned as an armsman and battlefield commander. His mounted tactics and martial resolve inspire warriors across Azeroth.",["class:Paladin"]="Lothar trusted the paladins of the Knights of the Silver Hand, including Turalyon. After Lothar fell, Turalyon took up his shattered sword and led the Alliance to victory."},kw={"anduin lothar","arathi","blackrock mountain","brotherhood of the horse","lion of stormwind","llane wrynn","lothar","supreme commander"},rel={"topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:medivh","topic:varian-wrynn","subzone:blackrock-mountain","quest:2997","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Anduin Lothar"}}
E["topic:argent-dawn"] = {t="topic",n="Argent Dawn",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Argent Dawn holds its ground against the Scourge and the Burning Legion. Survivors of the Silver Hand formed the order after rejecting the Scarlet Crusade's zealotry. They welcome champions of any race or faction who honor the Light, from Light's Hope Chapel to outposts across Kalimdor.",h="Across Azeroth, the Argent Dawn holds its ground against the Scourge and the Burning Legion.",sec={{t="A Schism of Faith",b="After Highlord Alexandros Mograine fell and Lordaeron collapsed, the Knights of the Silver Hand split over what to do. Grief and paranoia drove many survivors into the xenophobic Scarlet Crusade.\n\nLord Maxwell Tyrosus and other veterans saw that their former comrades had forsaken the true tenets of the Holy Light. They would neither yield to madness nor abandon the dead kingdom. So they formed the Argent Dawn, ready to defend Azeroth beside any fighter from the Alliance or the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Front Lines of the Plaguelands",b="Light's Hope Chapel, in the blighted Eastern Plaguelands, is the Argent Dawn's chief stronghold. From there, the order directs its war against Kel'Thuzad's necromancers and skeletal legions. Its forward camps include Chillwind Camp and a camp outside the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.\n\nArgent officers give adventurers enchanted commissions and pay bounties for Scourgestones taken from fallen undead. The Dawn has fewer fighters than the Scarlet Crusade, yet perseverance, unity, and discipline keep it holding the line.",sp=0},{t="Vigilance Across Azeroth",b="Lordaeron remains the Argent Dawn's main battleground, but its watch reaches across Kalimdor and the world's capitals. The order keeps diplomatic presences in Stormwind City, Darnassus, and the goblin trade town of Everlook. In Darkshore and Ashenvale, operatives such as Delgren the Purifier contest demonic cults. Scouts in Desolace and the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps investigate threats involving the Shadow Council and the Twilight's Hammer cult.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Truces and Hidden Foes",b="The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge while the Brotherhood of the Light, a pragmatic sect, tries to keep a cold truce with the Scarlet Crusade. Relations remain strained. Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff and other high-ranking officers sanction covert strikes against Scarlet leaders in Stratholme. They seek to purge what they see as heretical madness.\n\nThe Dawn also faces attempts to infiltrate its ranks. Secret agents siphon necromantic secrets from the front lines for treacherous masters elsewhere.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the difference between the Argent Dawn and the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Both orders arose from the Silver Hand's remnants after Lordaeron fell. The Scarlet Crusade became fanatical and xenophobic, seeing outsiders and non-humans as possible carriers of the plague. The Argent Dawn kept to the Holy Light's true tenets and welcomes Alliance and Horde races to fight evil together.",al={"argent dawn vs scarlet crusade","why did argent dawn split","difference between dawn and crusade"},it="conflict"},{q="What do I do with Scourgestones?",a="Argent Dawn officers accept Scourgestones as proof of service against the undead. The tokens mark victories over the Scourge and help the order recognize its allies.",al={"what are scourgestones for","argent dawn scourgestones","scourgestone turn in"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Can Horde players join or work with the Argent Dawn?",a="Yes. The Argent Dawn is neutral and stands apart from political allegiances. It welcomes orcs, trolls, tauren, and even Forsaken who fight the Scourge and the Burning Legion. Its recruitment stations include the Bulwark on the Tirisfal border.",al={"can horde join argent dawn","is argent dawn alliance only","argent dawn horde friendly"},it="side"},{q="What are they doing in Kalimdor?",a="The Argent Dawn seeks to protect all Azeroth, not only Lordaeron. Its agents have gone to Darkshore, Ashenvale, and Desolace to fight Shadow Council cults, confront Twilight's Hammer conspirators, and guard against demonic incursions.",al={"argent dawn in kalimdor","argent dawn ashenvale","why is argent dawn in darkshore"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Brotherhood of the Light?",a="The Brotherhood of the Light is a militant faction within the Argent Dawn, led by Commander Eligor Dawnbringer. Its members try to keep a working, if tense, relationship with the Scarlet Crusade so both can turn their fury on Kel'Thuzad instead of each other.",al={"brotherhood of the light","brotherhood of light argent dawn","eligor dawnbringer faction"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Argent Dawn?",a="The Argent Dawn is a neutral, knightly order dedicated to defending Azeroth from destructive evils, chief among them the Scourge and the Burning Legion. Unlike political factions or insular sects, the Dawn welcomes members and champions from any race without distinction, united solely by their devotion to the Light and their refusal to let the world fall to darkness.",al={"who are argent dawn","argent dawn order","what does argent dawn do"},it="identity",add="a2a95d31"},{q="Who leads the Argent Dawn?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus leads the Argent Dawn, directing their crusade against the undead from their primary sanctuary at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"argent dawn leader","who is in charge of argent dawn","lord tyrosus argent dawn"},it="leader",add="fb8338d1"},{q="Who are the Argent Dawn allied with?",a="The Argent Dawn maintains strict political neutrality, counting both the Alliance and the Horde as allies in the greater struggle against evil. Their officers recruit heroes from Stormwind to Orgrimmar alike. While they share common undead foes with the Scarlet Crusade and occasionally hold an uneasy truce through the Brotherhood of the Light, they view the Crusade's zealous fanaticism as dangerous heresy.",al={"argent dawn allies","does argent dawn work with horde","who works with argent dawn"},it="allies",add="7fcb74f5"},{q="How was the Argent Dawn founded?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron and the murder of Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the remnants of the Silver Hand fractured. While many knights succumbed to zealous paranoia and formed the Scarlet Crusade, those disgusted by this rising extremism broke away. Determined to uphold the true tenets of the Light without prejudice, they formed the Argent Dawn to fight the Scourge with honor.",al={"argent dawn history","origin of argent dawn","how did argent dawn start"},it="history",add="7042b727"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, the Argent Dawn carries on the Silver Hand's uncorrupted legacy. It holds to compassion, sacrifice, and duty after the Scarlet Crusade gave in to madness.",["faction:Horde"]="Though former knights of Lordaeron founded the Argent Dawn, it welcomes Horde champions without prejudice. Its camps give Horde heroes one of the few ways to fight directly in the Plaguelands.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken who despises the Scourge, you can find a rare, practical refuge in the Argent Dawn's camps. Your actions against Kel'Thuzad matter more to the order than your rotting flesh.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Argent Dawn keeps official embassies in Stormwind and Darnassus. As an Alliance soldier, you can join its fight to reclaim Lordaeron from the Lich King's grasp."},kw={"argent dawn","bulwark","chillwind camp","commission","light's hope chapel","maxwell tyrosus","plaguelands","scarlet crusade","scourge","scourgestone","silver hand"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:scourge","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:chillwind-camp","subzone:bulwark"},src={"Argent Dawn"}}
E["topic:black-dragonflight"] = {t="topic",n="Black dragonflight",z="general",s="From the shadows, the Black dragonflight wages war. The titans charged its dragons to guard Azeroth's deep places, but madness and treachery turned them from that duty. Neltharion became Deathwing, and his surviving brood plots against mortal kingdoms.",h="From the shadows, the Black dragonflight wages war.",sec={{t="The Fallen Protectors",b="The titans charged Neltharion and the Black dragonflight with guarding Azeroth's deep caverns and raising its mountains. For ages, they guarded the earth beside the other flights. Their duty brought them near the Old Gods' sunken prisons. Over centuries, dark whispers from those prisons broke Neltharion's mind and turned his brood toward ruin.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and Fire",b="In the ancient War of the Ancients, Neltharion betrayed the other dragons and became Deathwing the Destroyer. Since then, the Black flight has warred against the red, blue, green, and bronze flights. The other dragons see its cruelty as a profanation of life. Now Black dragons wield magma, black magic, and brimstone to scorch the lands they once tended. Misery and strife spread across mortal realms.",sp=0},{t="Human Guises and Mortal Intrigues",b="Black dragons take humanoid forms to enter royal courts and council chambers. They commonly appear as dark-haired humans with piercing eyes. From within, they steer leaders toward arrogance, divide noble houses, and whisper poisonous counsel to the vulnerable. Kingdoms may fall to their own divisions before Black drakes arrive to burn what remains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are black dragons evil?",a="The Old Gods' whispers corrupted Neltharion and his brood. Their ancient duty brought them near the subterranean prisons where the Old Gods were sealed. Over time, those whispers turned Neltharion's protective instincts to paranoia and malice. His brood followed him into corruption.",al={"why did black dragons turn bad","who corrupted deathwing","black dragon madness"},it="hostile"},{q="What powers do black dragons wield?",a="Black dragons command stone, magma, and subterranean forces. The titan Khaz'goroth gave them power over the earth. Corrupted, they wield black magic, breathe searing fire and molten rock, and radiate heat through their scales.",al={"black dragon magic","black dragon flight abilities","what can black dragons do"},it="power"},{q="Do black dragons use disguises?",a="Yes. Black dragons use humanoid disguises to enter courts and manipulate rulers. They often appear as noble humans with dark hair and dark eyes, stirring conflict without revealing their draconic nature.",al={"do dragons take human form","black dragon mortal guises","black dragons disguised as humans"}},{q="How can you tell a black dragon's name?",a="Black dragon names often have distinct endings. Male names frequently end in '-ion', as in Neltharion, while female names often end in '-ia', as in Onyxia. Many names evoke ash, shadow, stone, or ruin.",al={"black dragon naming conventions","black dragon names","how do black dragons get named"},it="name"},{q="Why do the other dragonflights hate them?",a="The Earth-Warder betrayed the other flights during the War of the Ancients and killed thousands of his kin. The red flight especially despises Black dragons. It sees their fiery malice and corrupting influence as a blasphemy against life.",al={"red dragonflight vs black dragonflight","why do dragons fight each other","dragonflight civil war"},it="conflict"},{q="Who leads the black dragonflight now?",a="Deathwing, the ancient Aspect, has vanished from public view after past defeats. His brood is scattered among splintered cabals. Offspring such as Nefarian and Onyxia pursue their own ambitions: to enslave rivals, subvert kingdoms, and breed dark creations.",al={"who is the black dragon leader","where is deathwing","who rules the black dragons"},it="leader"},{q="What is the black dragonflight?",a="The black dragonflight is a brood of dragons, drakonid, and dragonspawn originally blessed by the titan Khaz'goroth to serve as the steadfast warders of the earth. Once revered as the noble defenders of Azeroth's deepest realms, mountains, and subterranean caverns, the entire flight fell into madness when their ancient leader succumbed to the dark whispers of the Old Gods.",al={"who are the black dragons","what are black dragons","what is black dragonflight"},it="identity",add="0af770e1"},{q="Where did the black dragonflight come from?",a="Countless millennia ago, the titans empowered the Great Aspect Neltharion the Earth-Warder and his black brood with dominion over stone and magma. For ages, they shaped mountains and valleys in harmony with the other flights. However, their intimate bond with the deep places of the earth left them exposed to the whispers of the imprisoned Old Gods. Driven utterly mad, Neltharion and his children betrayed their sacred charge, turning their elemental might toward ruin and terror.",al={"black dragonflight history","black dragon origin","history of black dragons"},it="history",add="146344cc"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you must guard against political subversion. The Black dragonflight has repeatedly sought to corrupt human nobility and exploit aristocratic ambition in human courts.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you bear an enduring grudge against the Black flight's schemes. You have suffered its meddling in past wars and face its subterranean broods in the crags of Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may feel sorrow and revulsion toward Black dragons. They twist the sacred power of earth, turning stone and magma into instruments of torment instead of keeping harmony."},kw={"black dragonkin","black dragons","deathwing","dragonflight","earth-warder","khaz'goroth","nefarian","neltharion","onyxia"},rel={"npc:deathwing","topic:titan","topic:old-god","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:dragonmaw-clan"},src={"Black dragonflight"}}
E["topic:blackrock-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Blackrock clan",z="general",s="In Blackrock Mountain, veterans of the Blackrock clan now stand divided between Thrall's New Horde and the Dark Horde. Strict ranks, heavy armor, and skill at the forge once made the clan a force in the First and Second Wars.",h="In Blackrock Mountain, veterans of the Blackrock clan now stand divided between Thrall's New Horde and the...",sec={{t="The Anvil of the Old Horde",b="From Draenor came the Blackrock orcs, whose strength lay in strict ranks, heavy armor, and skill at the forge. Under Chieftain Blackhand, they formed the brutal core of the Old Horde's invasion of Azeroth and laid siege to Stormwind.\n\nOrgrim Doomhammer killed Blackhand to free the Horde from Gul'dan's direct control. Blackrock leaders then commanded both the clan and the Horde through the hard campaigns of the Second War.",sp=0},{t="A Fractured Legacy",b="After the Horde's defeat at Blackrock Mountain, the clan broke apart. Many warriors went to Alliance internment camps, then Thrall freed them and welcomed them into his reformed New Horde.\n\nOthers would not yield. They gathered behind Blackhand's sons, Rend and Maim, and withdrew to the heights of Blackrock Spire. There they formed the hostile Dark Horde with remnants of the Dragonmaw and other rogue clans.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Spire",b="From his throne in Blackrock Spire, Rend Blackhand claims the title of true Warchief. The Dark Horde keeps a tense truce with the Dark Iron dwarves in the molten depths below, even as it fights both the Alliance and Thrall's Horde.\n\nClan remnants tainted by demons have also been seen in Lordaeron. There they seek to revive dark sacrificial rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Are the Blackrock orcs part of Thrall's Horde?",a="Some Blackrock orcs serve Thrall, but most found in the Eastern Kingdoms do not. Veteran Eitrigg and others serve Thrall in Kalimdor. At Blackrock Mountain, most follow Rend Blackhand and regard Thrall's New Horde as weak traitors.",al={"is blackrock clan horde","are blackrocks friendly","thrall blackrock clan"},it="side"},{q="Who is currently leading the Blackrock clan?",a="Rend Blackhand leads the Dark Horde splinter faction in Blackrock Mountain and claims command of the clan his father led. Blackrock orcs who joined the New Horde answer to Warchief Thrall.",al={"blackrock clan leader","who leads blackrock","rend blackhand leader"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Dark Horde?",a="The Dark Horde is a rogue force in Upper Blackrock Spire, made up of unrepentant Blackrock orcs, Black Tooth Grin veterans, and allied Dragonmaw orcs. Led by Rend Blackhand, they reject Thrall's authority and seek to conquer Azeroth under the Old Horde's banner.",al={"what is dark horde","rend's horde","blackrock dark horde"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Blackhand?",a="Orgrim Doomhammer killed Warchief Blackhand during the First War to strip the Shadow Council of its puppet ruler. In a mak'gora duel, Orgrim crushed Blackhand's skull with the Doomhammer, then took the titles of Warchief and Blackrock clan leader.",al={"how did blackhand die","who killed blackhand","orgrim kills blackhand"},it="history"},{q="Why are there Blackrock orcs in Lordaeron?",a="Some Blackrock warbands fled north or hid in Lordaeron after the Second War. Some returned to demon worship and dark sacrifices, drawing the ire of the Alliance and, during the Third War, the Scourge.",al={"blackrock orcs alterac","blackrocks in lordaeron","demon worshipping blackrocks"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Blackrock clan?",a="The Blackrock clan is one of the most renowned and militarily disciplined orcish clans from Draenor. Famed for their master blacksmithing and iron will, they formed the central backbone of the Old Horde during the First and Second Wars under Warchiefs Blackhand and Orgrim Doomhammer. While some members eventually followed Thrall into his new Horde, the majority remain rogue traditionalists entrenched in Blackrock Mountain.",al={"who are blackrock orcs","blackrock clan lore","what is blackrock clan"},it="identity",add="2b76c337"},{q="Why are the Blackrock orcs hostile to travelers?",a="The free Blackrock orcs still cling to the bloody conquests of the Old Horde and reject Thrall's peaceful ideals. Driven by martial pride and deep hatred for both the Alliance and Thrall's Horde, they treat any trespassers into their lands—particularly around Blackrock Mountain and Redridge—as invaders to be slaughtered or enslaved.",al={"why do blackrock orcs attack","blackrock clan hostile","why are blackrocks evil"},it="hostile",add="77427c0a"},{q="Who are the Blackrock clan allied with?",a="The Blackrocks who follow Rend Blackhand lead the Dark Horde from Blackrock Spire. To bolster their numbers against the Dark Iron dwarves and the Alliance, they have allied with remnants of the Dragonmaw clan, local forest trolls, ogres, and the black dragonflight.",al={"blackrock clan allies","who do blackrock orcs work with","dark horde allies"},it="allies",add="2a83fd4b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Blackrocks gave the Horde two of its greatest Warchiefs. Their surviving remnants in the Eastern Kingdoms recall the Old Horde's bloodshed.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can trace orcish siegecraft and heavy plate armor to the Blackrock clan's famed metalworking. They forged for centuries in elemental-powered furnaces using unique ores.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you have faced the Blackrock clan in three wars, from Stormwind's burning to the bloody sieges of Blackrock Mountain and Khaz Modan.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde loyalist, you know Thrall sees Rend's Blackrock extremists as a grave threat to the New Horde's peace and honor. He calls them renegades who cling to demonic servitude."},kw={"blackhand","blackrock","dark horde","doomhammer","eitrigg","rend","spire"},rel={"subzone:blackrock-mountain","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","npc:eitrigg","topic:old-horde","topic:new-horde","topic:dragonmaw-clan","topic:second-war"},src={"Blackrock clan"}}
E["topic:bronzebeard-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Bronzebeard clan",z="general",s="In Ironforge, King Magni Bronzebeard leads his clan and its kingdom. The Bronzebeards won the War of the Three Hammers, then forged close ties with humanity and the gnomes. Now they anchor the Alliance.",h="In Ironforge, King Magni Bronzebeard leads his clan and its kingdom.",sec={{t="The War of the Three Hammers",b="High King Modimus Anvilmar’s death opened old rivalries within Ironforge. For years, dwarven society had flourished under his rule, but when he died of old age about two hundred and thirty years ago, those rivalries became civil war. Thane Madoran Bronzebeard commanded Ironforge’s traditional garrison and largest standing army. He drove the Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans from beneath the mountain.\n\nSorcerer-Thane Thaurissan attacked to reclaim Khaz Modan, and Madoran led his clan and army in a decisive campaign. The Bronzebeards shattered the Dark Iron host and secured their supremacy over Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="A Pillar of the Alliance",b="The Bronzebeards and human kingdoms first met nearly two thousand years ago. Their shared skill in metalcraft, trade, and battle built mutual respect. Then the Orcish Horde swept across the continent in the Second War, and King Magni Bronzebeard brought his realm into the Alliance of Lordaeron.\n\nThe Bronzebeards withstood brutal sieges inside their subterranean fortress. Their engineers, gunners, and demolitionists supplied vital firepower and arms, helping turn the tide of war.",sp=0},{t="Grief at the High Seat",b="King Magni Bronzebeard governs from the High Seat in the Great Forge. His younger brother, Muradin Bronzebeard, served as an Alliance emissary in Lordaeron before vanishing in Northrend’s frozen wastes alongside Prince Arthas Menethil. Muradin was presumed dead when the prince claimed Frostmourne, the cursed blade.\n\nMagni’s daughter, Princess Moira, has also gone missing. With the succession uncertain, the clan searches ancient Titan excavation sites to divine its origins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Bronzebeard clan?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules the clan from the High Seat in the Great Forge. A veteran of the Second War and a master smith, he leads his clan and the allied dwarves of Khaz Modan.",al={"bronzebeard leader","who is king of ironforge","current bronzebeard king"},it="leader"},{q="How did the Bronzebeard clan win control of Ironforge?",a="The Bronzebeards won control of Ironforge in the civil war that followed High King Modimus Anvilmar’s death about two hundred and thirty years ago. Thane Madoran Bronzebeard commanded Ironforge’s central standing army and drove the Wildhammers and Dark Irons from the mountain. Then he led his clan and army to crush Thaurissan’s invading Dark Iron force.",al={"war of the three hammers","dwarf civil war","why bronzebeards rule"},it="history"},{q="What is the difference between Bronzebeard and other dwarven clans?",a="The Bronzebeards inhabit Ironforge and represent the traditional mountain dwarves, known for heavy plate, firearms, and subterranean architecture. The Wildhammers dwell among the crags and skies as gryphon riders, while the hostile Dark Irons master dark sorcery and pyromancy beneath Blackrock Mountain.",al={"dwarf clans difference","ironforge vs wildhammer","types of dwarves"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Muradin Bronzebeard?",a="Muradin Bronzebeard traveled to Northrend as an Alliance emissary and explorer. He guided Prince Arthas Menethil in the hunt for Frostmourne, a runeblade, and was reported dead when the prince freed the cursed weapon from its pedestal.",al={"where is muradin","is muradin alive","muradin fate"}},{q="Why are the Bronzebeards so devoted to archaeological digs?",a="Bronzebeard scholars have found relics linking their ancestry to the ancient, stone-hewn earthen. Driven to discover their race’s roots, the clan funds digs and expeditions across Azeroth.",al={"why dwarves dig","dwarven excavations","earthen origins"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Bronzebeard royal family's seat of power?",a="The Bronzebeard royal family’s seat of power is the High Seat, situated in the heart of Ironforge along the Great Forge. King Magni conducts state affairs there, surrounded by councilors and royal guards.",al={"where is the throne room","high seat location","bronzebeard throne"},it="place"},{q="Who are the Bronzebeard clan's allies?",a="The Bronzebeards are staunch, founding pillars of the Grand Alliance. Their closest bond lies with humanity, dating back roughly eighteen centuries when human explorers from Arathor first journeyed south into Khaz Modan and discovered Ironforge. The two races forged an enduring partnership over shared smithing, engineering, and storytelling. They also share strong ties with the gnomes of nearby Gnomeregan and have long reestablished friendly relations with their Wildhammer cousins in the Aerie Peak, despite past civil conflicts.",al={"bronzebeard allies","who do bronzebeards ally with","ironforge allies"},it="allies",add="177e0e99"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hail from or answer to the Bronzebeard kingdom. You serve King Magni as a steadfast defender of Khaz Modan.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can remember that the Bronzebeards offered refuge in Ironforge’s Tinkertown when Gnomeregan fell to the trogg invasion.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share longstanding ties with the Bronzebeards, built through trade and shared martial traditions.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can look to the Bronzebeards, renowned across Azeroth for their mastery of smelting, weapon crafting, and heavy armors."},kw={"bronzebeard","high seat","ironforge","khaz modan","madoran","magni","muradin","three hammers"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","topic:dwarf","zone:ironforge","topic:muradin-bronzebeard","subzone:high-seat","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:wildhammer-clan","topic:alliance"},src={"Bronzebeard clan"}}
E["topic:brotherhood-of-northshire"] = {t="topic",n="Brotherhood of Northshire",z="general",s="At Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest, the Brotherhood of Northshire guides the faithful and trains new defenders. Once called the Clerics of Northshire, the order was rebuilt after its losses in the First War.",h="At Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest, the Brotherhood of Northshire guides the faithful and trains new...",sec={{t="The Clerics of the First War",b="Centuries ago, missionaries from Lordaeron traveled south and founded Northshire Abbey in Stormwind. They served its people through the Holy Light and sought to soothe the realm. First called the Holy Order of Northshire Clerics, they showed compassion even to injured gnolls and jungle trolls during past border wars.\n\nWhen the Orcish Horde crossed the Dark Portal, the clerics went unarmed and without armor to heal fallen soldiers. Their healing sustained the Stormwind Army, so the orcs made them targets. The order was decimated, and the abbey was ransacked and burned. The surviving clerics fled north across the sea to Southshore with Sir Anduin Lothar.",sp=0},{t="The Spark of the Paladins",b="The slaughter of Northshire’s clerics shook the human kingdoms. Archbishop Alonsus Faol saw that faith alone could not withstand an axe without armor and martial discipline. He joined surviving clerics with devout knights to form the Knights of the Silver Hand. These warriors bore the Light’s sacred power and a knight’s skill in battle. Northshire’s fallen healers laid the foundation for the holy warriors who broke the Horde in the Second War.",sp=0},{t="Rebuilding and Present Duty",b="After Stormwind was reclaimed and the Dark Portal destroyed, Archbishop Faol rebuilt Northshire Abbey and reorganized the order as the Brotherhood of Northshire. Today, the abbey is a quiet place where new recruits begin their service to the realm. Priestess Anetta, Brother Sammuel, and Brother Paxton help tend the valley’s spiritual needs, preserve ancient texts in the library, and train defenders against brigands, wolves, and the gathering shadows across Elwynn Forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brotherhood of Northshire?",a="The Brotherhood of Northshire is a monastic order of the Church of the Holy Light based at Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. Once called the Clerics of Northshire, its members offer spiritual guidance, heal the wounded, and train new Alliance defenders.",al={"who are the brotherhood of northshire","brotherhood of northshire lore","clerics of northshire"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the original clerics during the First War?",a="The clerics entered the First War as unarmored battlefield healers, and their healing sustained the Stormwind Army. The orcs targeted them, and the abbey was overrun and ruined. Only a remnant escaped across the Great Sea to Lordaeron.",al={"northshire clerics first war","what happened to the abbey","destruction of northshire abbey"},it="history"},{q="How did the Northshire Clerics inspire the paladins?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol saw that unarmored clerics could not survive brutal combat. He joined their devotion to the Light with the martial skill of knights and formed the Knights of the Silver Hand.",al={"creation of paladins","silver hand origin","alonsus faol paladins"},it="origin"},{q="Who leads or trains people at Northshire Abbey today?",a="Brother Paxton manages provisions and copies texts for the library. Priestess Anetta instructs aspiring priests, and Brother Sammuel guides novice paladins at the abbey.",al={"who is at northshire abbey","northshire abbey trainers","brother paxton"},it="leader"},{q="What was the expedition to the Deadmines during the First War?",a="An ogre chieftain named Turok stole Northshire’s sacred Tome of Divinity. Sir Anduin Lothar led an expedition into the Deadmines of Westfall to retrieve it, but became trapped until Stormwind forces rescued him and returned the book to the abbey.",al={"tome of divinity deadmines","anduin lothar deadmines","turok deadmines"},it="history"},{q="Are they connected to the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. Though both groups share the word “brotherhood,” the Brotherhood of Northshire is a holy order loyal to Stormwind. The Defias Brotherhood is a criminal band of outlaws and bandits who plague the countryside.",al={"brotherhood of northshire defias","are they defias","northshire defias"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Brotherhood based in Northshire Valley?",a="Centuries ago, clerics from the Church of the Holy Light traveled south from Lordaeron and established Northshire Abbey as their spiritual home in Stormwind. Though the original abbey was razed by the Orcish Horde during the First War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol oversaw its reconstruction after the war ended. The valley remains their ancestral sanctuary, now serving as a training and recruitment ground to prepare new defenders for the kingdom.",al={"why are they in northshire","why northshire valley","brotherhood of northshire location"},it="why_here",add="5eaf3832"},{q="Who is the Brotherhood of Northshire allied with?",a="The Brotherhood of Northshire is an order within the Church of the Holy Light and operates directly in service to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Grand Alliance. Historically, its clerics tended to Stormwind's armies during major conflicts like the Gnoll War and the Gurubashi War, and their restored order now directly recruits and trains fledgling champions to safeguard the realm.",al={"brotherhood of northshire allies","who does the brotherhood work for","brotherhood allegiance"},it="allies",add="24abd8af"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you find Northshire Abbey at the heart of Stormwind’s clerical tradition. Its people cultivated healing, confession, and the Holy Light long before the First War.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you carry a legacy born from the butchery of Northshire’s unarmored clerics. Their deaths drove Archbishop Faol to create the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you inherit a tradition that has brought spiritual comfort to generations of Stormwind citizens. Northshire Abbey is also the humble beginning of the kingdom’s greatest champions."},kw={"alonsus faol","brother paxton","brotherhood of northshire","church of the holy light","clerics of northshire","elwynn forest","northshire abbey","priestess anetta"},rel={"subzone:northshire-abbey","subzone:northshire-valley","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:anduin-lothar","zone:elwynn","quest:1641"},src={"Brotherhood of Northshire"}}
E["topic:burning-blade-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Burning Blade clan",z="general",s="Across Durotar and the Barrens, the Burning Blade threatens the young Horde from within. Once renowned for its blademasters, the clan broke under demonic corruption. Now most of its scattered members serve the Shadow Council, while a few honorable blademasters stand with Warchief Thrall.",h="Across Durotar and the Barrens, the Burning Blade threatens the young Horde from within.",sec={{t="From Clan to Elemental Fury",b="The Burning Blade once fought beside clans such as the Warsong on Draenor. Its blademasters were famed for deadly skill. After drinking Mannoroth’s blood and crossing the Dark Portal into Azeroth during the First War, the clan’s minds broke into chaos.\n\nBy the Second War, it had lost all order and raged like a force of nature. These nomadic fighters charged without regard for survival, so ogres held them back until battle called. Near the Dark Portal, the Alliance battered and routed them.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Durotar",b="Across Kalimdor, Burning Blade covens trouble newly arrived orcs and Darkspear trolls from their first days in the Valley of Trials. Warlocks dwell in Thunder Ridge and keep a major hideout in Skull Rock, near Orgrimmar’s eastern gates. The cultists gather around dark relics such as the Demon Seed and harvest souls for demonic rites. In Durotar and the Barrens, they threaten the young Horde from within.",sp=0},{t="The Traitor in the Cleft",b="Neeru Fireblade lives in the Cleft of Shadow as a Horde warlock, yet secretly leads the Burning Blade for the Shadow Council. He uses pawns such as the expendable Searing Blade of Ragefire Chasm to preserve the guise of a harmless researcher aiding the Warchief. Thrall has already deduced Neeru’s treachery and watches him closely.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.2","q5726.3"}},{t="A Split Legacy",b="After the Second War, surviving members of the Burning Blade split apart. A disciplined band of blademasters vowed to free their people from demonic enslavement and pledged their swords to Warchief Thrall as his personal honor guard. Many others fell under the Burning Legion and the Shadow Council. Across Kalimdor, they became a hidden cult of warlocks, fel acolytes, and conspirators.",sp=1,bt={"q5726.3"}}},faq={{q="What is the Burning Blade clan?",a="The Burning Blade began as an orcish clan from Draenor, renowned for its blademasters. Bloodlust consumed the clan during the First and Second Wars. Now most who bear its name belong to a demon-worshiping cult serving the Shadow Council across Kalimdor, though a few reformed blademasters serve Thrall’s Horde.",al={"burning blade lore","who are burning blade","burning blade background"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="Who actually leads the Burning Blade?",a="The Shadow Council directs the Burning Blade, whose covens in Durotar and the Barrens are led by warlocks and demon-summoners. Their true master remains hidden, though the trail leads close to Orgrimmar.",al={"burning blade leader","who is the leader of burning blade"},sp=1,it="leader",bt={"q5726.3"}},{q="Why are they attacking new orcs in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Burning Blade keeps a coven in the northern caves of the Valley of Trials to disrupt young orcs and trolls as they undergo their rites of passage. Its familiars and dark medallions spread fel corruption in the heart of Horde lands.",al={"valley of trials burning blade","why are cultists in valley of trials"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the difference between the Burning Blade and Searing Blade?",a="The Searing Blade is a smaller sect deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. The Burning Blade is the broader cult across Durotar and the Barrens. The chasm holds clues to who directs the sect.",al={"searing blade vs burning blade","difference between burning and searing blade"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Are all Burning Blade members demon-worshiping cultists?",a="No. Though the cult holds most of the clan’s scattered members, proud blademasters broke away by the Third War. They vowed to free their people from demonic enslavement and now serve in the New Horde as Thrall’s personal honor guard.",al={"are all burning blade bad","burning blade blademasters good"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the Burning Blade hostile to travelers?",a="The Burning Blade serves the demonic will of the Burning Legion and the Shadow Council. Ever since their clan was consumed by demonic bloodlust during the early wars, they have abandoned any true allegiance or honor. Now reorganized as a secretive apocalyptic cult, they view outsiders, loyal Horde subjects, and curious travelers as direct threats to their covens or as fuel for demonic blood sacrifices.",al={"why do burning blade attack","burning blade hostile","why does the burning blade fight"},it="hostile",add="59650569"},{q="Who are the Burning Blade allied with?",a="The cult acts as a direct arm of the sinister Shadow Council, carrying out their dark designs across Kalimdor. They frequently cooperate with allied demon-worshiping splinter factions like the Searing Blade hiding beneath Orgrimmar and the Argus Wake in the Eastern Kingdoms. Above all, they are sworn in servitude to the Burning Legion, summoning demons and gathering corrupt artifacts to hasten their masters' designs.",al={"burning blade allies","who does the burning blade work for","burning blade shadow council"},it="allies",add="d02d80de"},{q="Where did the Burning Blade come from?",a="Originally an ancient orcish clan from Draenor known for their fearsome blademasters, the Burning Blade joined the Old Horde and crossed into Azeroth during the First War. Demonic corruption eroded their minds until they became a reckless, mad frenzy during the Second War, eventually breaking apart entirely. While honorable blademasters later swore fealty to Thrall's New Horde, the remaining remnants transformed into the shadowy demonic cult threatening Kalimdor today.",al={"burning blade origin","burning blade lore","history of burning blade clan"},it="history",add="7b15f473"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Burning Blade is a lingering sign of the Horde’s corrupt demonic past, threatening Durotar and the Barrens from within.",["class:Warlock"]="The Burning Blade shows the danger of demonic enslavement, which drives Horde warlocks to conceal their studies and endure suspicion.",["race:Orc"]="The clan’s fall recalls the blood curse, while its honor-bound blademasters seek atonement in service to Thrall."},kw={"blademaster","burning blade","cleft of shadow","durotar","searing blade","shadow council","skull rock","zmodlor"},rel={"npc:thrall","quest:5726","quest:829","zone:durotar","zone:ragefire","topic:shadow-council","quest:827","npc:orgnil-soulscar"},src={"Burning Blade clan"}}
E["topic:burning-legion"] = {t="topic",n="Burning Legion",z="general",s="Across creation, the Burning Legion remains an infinite host bent on scouring all life. Led by the fallen titan Sargeras, its demons shattered ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, corrupted the orcs, and brought the horrors of the Third War to Azeroth.",h="Across creation, the Burning Legion remains an infinite host bent on scouring all life.",sec={{t="Genesis of the Host",b="Sargeras once served the titans, hunting demons across the cosmos and locking them away. Ages of battle convinced him that creation was flawed beyond repair and must burn. He freed the demons he had imprisoned and bent them to his will with fel magic. The corrupted eredar brought intellect to their chaos, and Archimonde and Kil'jaeden became his chief lieutenants. Together they formed an unstoppable engine of cosmic annihilation.",sp=0},{t="The War of the Ancients",b="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne's reckless sorceries drew the Burning Legion's gaze to Azeroth. Through the Well of Eternity, Sargeras whispered to Queen Azshara and her councilor Xavius, promising them a chance to reshape the world as a paradise.\n\nThe portal unleashed Mannoroth and Archimonde, with swarms of doomguard, felhounds, and flaming infernals. Their war ruined Kalimdor's civilization before night elves, dragonflights, and demigods brought down the gateway. Its catastrophic implosion tore the supercontinent apart in the Great Sundering, scattering ruined lands across vast new seas.",sp=0},{t="Shadows over Azeroth",b="The Legion was cast back into the Twisting Nether, yet Azeroth remained in its sights. Kil'jaeden arranged proxy cataclysms from afar. The deceiver bound the orcs of Draenor through demonic blood pacts, and the Horde charged through the Dark Portal to weaken mortal defenses.\n\nWhen that failed, the Legion forged the Lich King and unleashed the undead Scourge across Lordaeron, paving the way for Archimonde's return in the Third War. Archimonde fell at Mount Hyjal, but Legion remnants still linger across Felwood, the Blasted Lands, and hidden cults throughout the world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Burning Legion?",a="The Burning Legion is an infinite host of demons, corrupted races, and destructive horrors forged by the fallen titan Sargeras. It is bent on scouring all life and ordered existence from the cosmos.",al={"who are the legion","what is the burning legion","legion demons","what are demons"},it="identity"},{q="Who leads the Burning Legion?",a="The fallen titan Sargeras is the Legion's ultimate master. Beneath him serve the eredar demon lords Archimonde the Defiler, who led military assaults until his death at Mount Hyjal, and Kil'jaeden the Deceiver, who orchestrates insidious plots across worlds.",al={"who rules the legion","legion leader","who is the demon king","archimonde boss"},it="leader"},{q="Why does the Legion want to destroy Azeroth?",a="Azeroth has repeatedly defied the Legion and is the only world known to have repelled its assaults.",al={"why do demons attack","legion motive","why invade azeroth","sargeras goal"},it="purpose"},{q="How did the demons first arrive on Azeroth?",a="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara and her Highborne channeled the Well of Eternity's vast energies, drawing Sargeras to Azeroth. Deceived by promises of limitless power, they opened a massive portal beneath the palace, allowing the Legion to invade Kalimdor.",al={"first demon invasion","how did legion get here","well of eternity portal","queen azshara demons"},it="history"},{q="What happened to the Legion during the Third War?",a="Summoned back to Azeroth with the book of Medivh, Archimonde marched across Lordaeron and sailed west to devour the World Tree, Nordrassil. At Mount Hyjal, mortal races held his assault long enough for Malfurion Stormrage to call upon the ancestral spirits and detonate the tree's power, obliterating Archimonde.",al={"third war demons","mount hyjal invasion","did legion lose third war","what happened to archimonde"},it="history"},{q="Are demons still a threat right now?",a="Yes. Though Archimonde's fall fractured the main host, dangerous remnants remain entrenched across corrupted zones in Azeroth. Dreadlords, infernals, and lingering fiends occupy Felwood and the Blasted Lands, while mortal cultists such as the Shadow Council work in secret.",al={"are demons still around","legion remnants","demons in classic","where are demons now"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the Burning Legion hostile to everyone?",a="The Burning Legion's ultimate purpose is nothing less than the absolute annihilation of all mortal life and creation across the cosmos. Under the command of the fallen titan Sargeras, demons do not seek conquest, coexistence, or surrender; they view mortal worlds as flawed remnants to be purged in fel fire. Any traveler or soul they encounter on Azeroth is merely fuel for their magic or prey to be wiped out.",al={"why is the legion hostile","why does the burning legion attack","burning legion hostile reasons"},it="hostile",add="5561206b"},{q="Who serves alongside or works for the Burning Legion?",a="The Legion relies on an endless tide of demonic races, including monstrous pit lords, cunning dreadlords, ravenous felhounds, and towering infernals. Beyond pure demons, they corrupt mortal races to act as pawns and vanguards. In the past, they swayed Queen Azshara's Highborne sorcerers, corrupted the orcs of Draenor through demonic blood, and forged the Scourge to soften mortal resistance before invasions.",al={"burning legion allies","who works for the legion","who serves the burning legion"},it="allies",add="c3b2191d"},{q="Why are demonic remnants still found across Azeroth?",a="Following Archimonde's defeat at the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the centralized demonic assault shattered, scattering surviving fiends into hiding. Today, lingering demons and renegade dreadlords lurk in desolate reaches like Desolace, Felwood, and the Blasted Lands. Additionally, corrupt mortal cabals, such as the warlocks of the Shadow Council, secretly summon fresh reinforcements through hidden dark portals to carry on the Legion's work.",al={"why are demons still on azeroth","why are legion demons here","burning legion locations azeroth"},it="why_here",add="9252264e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, your people bear the deepest scars of the Legion's invasions. The Sundering shattered your ancient empire, and the recent sacrifice of your World Tree at Mount Hyjal cost you your immortality.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you carry a bitter legacy with the Legion. The demonic blood pact of Mannoroth enslaved orcs until Grom Hellscream sacrificed himself to break the curse once and for all.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you bend raw fel magic and the Legion's subservient demons to your mortal will, despite constant suspicion and the ever-present threat of corruption.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see the Burning Legion as the antithesis of the Holy Light. Your martial vows and righteous power are devoted to purging demonic filth wherever it festers."},kw={"archimonde","burning legion","demons","eredar","fel","hyjal","kil'jaeden","mannoroth","sargeras","sundering","twisting nether","well of eternity"},rel={"topic:sargeras","topic:third-war","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf","topic:titan","topic:old-god","topic:lich-king","npc:malfurion-stormrage"},src={"Burning Legion"}}
E["topic:cenarion-circle"] = {t="topic",n="Cenarion Circle",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Cenarion Circle guards nature’s balance. Founded by Malfurion Stormrage under Cenarius, it keeps its sacred haven in Moonglade and tends the Emerald Dream and blighted lands. Once made up of night elves, it now welcomes tauren druids to defend the living world.",h="Across Azeroth, the Cenarion Circle guards nature’s balance.",sec={{t="Origins of the Circle",b="Thousands of years ago, Cenarius taught Malfurion Stormrage, the first mortal druid. After the Great Sundering, Malfurion gathered those who wished to learn nature’s ways. The order made its home in Moonglade’s sacred vale. Ever since, the Circle has watched over Azeroth’s wild places.",sp=0},{t="A Sacred Neutrality",b="The Cenarion Circle is rooted in night elf history, yet answers neither to Darnassus nor to the Sisterhood of Elune. Its heart is Moonglade, where the peaceful town of Nighthaven keeps an ancient truce. Weapons stay sheathed there, beyond the reach of mortal wars.\n\nAfter the Third War, Malfurion and Hamuul Runetotem, a tauren elder, became friends and came to respect one another. The Circle honored the tauren’s reverence for the Earth Mother and welcomed Hamuul into its ranks. Through him, druidism returned to his people after thousands of years.",sp=0},{t="Tension and the Absent Archdruid",b="After the devastation at Mount Hyjal, Malfurion fell into an unnatural, impenetrable coma in his barrow den. With no leader, the druids left Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in practical command of the Circle. Fandral used Malfurion’s silence to rally support for growing Teldrassil, hoping to restore the kaldorei’s lost immortality.\n\nThe Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, and strange corruption has taken root in its branches. Division stirs within the order as Fandral rules with a stern hand. Ancient guardians sense darkness spreading from Silithus and the Emerald Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle is an ancient order of druids devoted to nature’s balance, the wild, and the Emerald Dream. Malfurion Stormrage founded it under Cenarius’s guidance, and its sanctuary lies in Moonglade.",al={"cenarion circle lore","who are the cenarion circle","what is the circle"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the headquarters of the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle is based in Moonglade, around Nighthaven and the shores of Lake Elune'ara. Its outposts and barrow dens reach across Kalimdor, including Cenarion Hold in Silithus, where the order keeps watch.",al={"cenarion circle base","where are cenarion druids based","nighthaven cenarion"},it="place"},{q="Why are tauren in the Cenarion Circle?",a="Hamuul Runetotem joined the Cenarion Circle after he and Malfurion Stormrage fought together at Mount Hyjal during the Third War. They came to respect one another, and Malfurion shared druidic teachings with Hamuul. Hamuul became the first tauren druid in millennia, bringing tauren and night elf druids into partnership.",al={"why are tauren druids","hamuul cenarion circle","tauren night elf druids"},it="people"},{q="Who leads the Cenarion Circle?",a="Malfurion Stormrage led the Cenarion Circle with elder archdruids. While Malfurion lies in an unexplained coma in his barrow, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads in practice from Darnassus. Hamuul Runetotem and the keepers in Moonglade guide their own factions.",al={"leader of cenarion circle","who is the archdruid","archdruid leader"},it="leader"},{q="Is the Cenarion Circle part of the Alliance?",a="No. The Cenarion Circle is neutral, and its members swear themselves to nature rather than mortal rulers. Alliance and Horde druids walk side by side in Moonglade and other Cenarion encampments.",al={"is cenarion circle alliance","cenarion circle faction","are cenarion druids neutral"},it="side"},{q="What happened at the Scarab Wall in Silithus?",a="During the War of the Shifting Sands a thousand years ago, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm led the night elves and the Cenarion Circle against the qiraji swarm, aided by the dragonflights. The bronze dragon Anachronos and his allies raised the Scarab Wall to seal away the hive. The Circle built Cenarion Hold to watch over the seal.",al={"cenarion hold silithus","war of the shifting sands","druids scarab wall"},it="conflict"},{q="Why is it called the Cenarion Circle?",a="The order was named after and blessed by Cenarius, the demigod Lord of the Forest. Cenarius was the patron of the wild who originally tutored Malfurion Stormrage, the first mortal druid of Azeroth. When Malfurion and his fellow practitioners gathered to organize their traditions and safeguard the balance of nature, they took the demigod's name to honor their divine teacher.",al={"cenarion circle name origin","why cenarion","who is cenarion circle named after"},it="name",add="93dd49b8"},{q="Where did the Cenarion Circle come from?",a="The Circle was founded in Moonglade by Malfurion Stormrage following the Great Sundering, when he brought the early night elf druids together to establish their guidelines and traditions. For thousands of years during the Long Vigil, the Circle maintained balance and healed demonic scars across Azeroth while walking the Emerald Dream alongside the green dragonflight.",al={"cenarion circle history","origin of the cenarion circle","how was cenarion circle founded"},it="history",add="975f0135"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you belong to the Cenarion Circle, your spiritual authority. Whether your tutelage comes from Darnassus or the plains of Mulgore, the Circle’s rites in Moonglade guide your power, trials, and callings.",["race:NightElf"]="For ten thousand years, your people’s men chiefly slept in barrows in service to the Cenarion Circle while Sentinels guarded your borders. The Circle’s bond with the wild shaped every part of kaldorei culture.",["race:Tauren"]="Through Hamuul Runetotem’s friendship with Malfurion Stormrage, your people reclaimed ancient traditions tied to the Earth Mother and earned an honored place in the Cenarion Circle.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The Cenarion Circle’s druids understand Azeroth’s plant life and the delicate ecosystems that sustain rare and magical flora."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarion hold","cenarius","druid","emerald dream","fandral staghelm","hamuul runetotem","malfurion","moonglade","nighthaven"},rel={"quest:5921","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:cenarius","quest:1489","npc:fandral-staghelm","subzone:nighthaven","subzone:cenarion-hold","topic:druid"},src={"Cenarion Circle"}}
E["topic:centaur"] = {t="topic",n="Centaur",z="general",s="Centaur clans still roam central Kalimdor, where they once drove the tauren close to extinction. Their line began with Zaetar and Theradras, and the Horde's arrival changed the course of their war with the tauren.",h="Centaur clans still roam central Kalimdor, where they once drove the tauren close to extinction.",sec={{t="A Cursed Lineage",b="Centaur legend begins in Maraudon, beneath Desolace. Zaetar was an immortal son of the demigod Cenarius. Princess Theradras was daughter of Therazane, the elemental lord. Together they sired the first centaur. Soon after they emerged, the barbaric offspring turned on Zaetar and killed him. Grief-stricken, Theradras trapped his spirit in Maraudon's winding caverns. She shielded her vicious children as they multiplied across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Centuries of Slaughter",b="From Desolace, centaur spread across Kalimdor and waged brutal war against its native peoples. The nomadic tauren suffered most. Driven from their fertile ancestral home in Mulgore, they fled across the Barrens as centaur warbands burned their settlements and hunted them for sport. By the Third War, centuries of pursuit had brought the tauren near extinction. They fled the endless marauders across the savannah.",sp=0},{t="The Tide Turns",b="The balance shifted when Warchief Thrall and the newly arrived orcish Horde landed on Kalimdor. Thrall made a pact with Cairne Bloodhoof. Orcish steel joined with tauren might, and together they crushed the aggressive Kolkar warbands and broke their hold on the plains. The tauren could safely establish Thunder Bluff and reclaim Mulgore. Their exile ended, and a debt of blood and honor bound them to the Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Fractured Menace",b="Centaur remain a threat across central Kalimdor despite their defeats. Their society is divided among warring clans, chiefly the Kolkar, Gelkis, Magram, and Maraudine. Each follows a khan, and the clans feud over territory and water. Their infighting keeps them from uniting. Yet raiding parties still strike trade caravans and settlements across Durotar, the Barrens, Thousand Needles, and the borders of Mulgore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did centaur come from?",a="Centaur legend traces their birth to Zaetar, son of Cenarius, and Princess Theradras, daughter of Therazane, the elemental lord. The first centaur killed Zaetar, and Theradras trapped his spirit in Maraudon's caverns.",al={"centaur origin","who created the centaur","centaur creation lore"},it="origin"},{q="Why do centaur hate the tauren so much?",a="Centaur spread from Desolace and raided the plains' native peoples for generations. They hunted the tauren for sport and drove them from Mulgore into exile across the Barrens. Before the orcs intervened, the tauren stood near extinction.",al={"tauren centaur feud","why do centaur hunt tauren","centaur tauren war"},it="conflict"},{q="What clans do the centaur belong to?",a="The main centaur clans on Kalimdor are the Kolkar, Gelkis, Magram, Maraudine, and Galak. Each traces its leadership to its founding khan, and the clans often fight bloody feuds.",al={"centaur tribes","names of centaur clans","centaur factions"},it="people"},{q="Where are centaur encountered today?",a="Centaur territory centers on Desolace, where Maraudon lies. Warbands and outposts also roam the Barrens, Durotar, and Thousand Needles.",al={"where are centaur found","centaur locations","centaur zones"},it="place"},{q="Can centaur be reasoned or allied with?",a="Centaur generally see other races as prey to enslave or destroy. Rivalries between clans can be turned against them. In Desolace, the Magram or Gelkis have sometimes accepted outsider help to destroy their hated kin.",al={"are centaur friendly","can you ally with centaur","friendly centaur"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Princess Theradras to the centaur?",a="Princess Theradras is the centaur's mother and revered patron. In Maraudon, she protects the spirit of Zaetar, their murdered father. At times she has infused her descendants with elemental fury to spur them to conquer more territory across Kalimdor.",al={"centaur mother","theradras and centaur","princess theradras lore"},it="ties"},{q="What are centaur?",a="Centaur are a warlike, primitive race possessing the torso and arms of a human joined to the lower body and four legs of a horse. Savage and nomadic by nature, they roam the arid plains and valleys of central Kalimdor. They are organized into fiercely territorial clans that value brute strength, raiding neighboring settlements, and driving off any outsiders who tread near their hunting grounds and watering holes.",al={"what is centaur","who are the centaur","centaur race"},it="identity",add="f5a4aa83"},{q="Why are centaur so hostile to travelers?",a="Hostility is deeply woven into centaur nature. Born cursed and filled with self-loathing and fury, they murdered their own father shortly after their creation. Ever since, they have viewed the world through violence and conquest. They see central Kalimdor as their rightful territory, treating any passing caravan, traveler, or settlement as trespassers to be slaughtered, enslaved, or driven out.",al={"why do centaur attack","why are centaur aggressive","centaur hostile"},it="hostile",add="5b0a3e11"},{q="Who leads the centaur?",a="The centaur have no single ruler. Instead, they are divided into independent, feuding clans—such as the Kolkar, Gelkis, Magram, Maraudine, and Galak—each governed by its own khan. These khans rule through ruthless physical dominance and cunning, and the clans spend nearly as much effort waging bloody territorial wars against one another as they do raiding foreign enemies.",al={"centaur leader","who rules the centaur","centaur khan"},it="leader",add="9cda8173"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know centaur as the ancient tormentors who nearly wiped out your ancestors and drove them across the Barrens for centuries. The Horde offered salvation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, defending against centaur incursions in the Barrens and Durotar means survival. It also honors the pact Thrall made with Cairne Bloodhoof.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see centaur as a tragic perversion of nature's balance. They share blood with Cenarius through his fallen son Zaetar, yet bring desolation and slaughter."},kw={"barrens","centaur","desolace","khan","kolkar","maraudon","theradras","zaetar"},rel={"topic:tauren","zone:desolace","zone:barrens","topic:kolkar-clan","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","npc:thrall","topic:cenarius","quest:850"},src={"Centaur"}}
E["topic:church-of-the-holy-light"] = {t="topic",n="Church of the Holy Light",z="general",s="After Lordaeron's fall, the Church of the Holy Light gathers in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light. Its clergy guide human souls through compassion, justice, and devotion.",h="After Lordaeron's fall, the Church of the Holy Light gathers in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light.",sec={{t="Origins and the Light's Creed",b="Among the humans of Arathor, faith in the Holy Light took root more than a thousand years ago. The faithful learned to channel it to heal injuries and purge affliction. They were taught to give charity and seek righteousness, believing the Light dwells within all thinking beings. In time, these beliefs became an organized faith. Lordaeron became its heartland, with revered sanctuaries in Stratholme, Andorhal, Tyr's Hand, and Light's Hope Chapel.",sp=0},{t="A Shield in the Great Wars",b="In the First War, the Brotherhood of Northshire went to battle, healing defenders who fell against the invading Orcish Horde. The clerics had no weapons or heavy armor, and suffered terrible losses to the orcs. During the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol met with Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar.\n\nTogether they formed the Knights of the Silver Hand, holy warriors who could wield holy wrath and endure physical combat. Paladins and priests became the Alliance of Lordaeron's moral and martial bulwark, preserving humanity from annihilation.",sp=0},{t="Fall of the North and the Southern Haven",b="The Third War brought sorrow to the faithful. As the Plague of Undeath spread across Lordaeron, the Church aided the sick and tried to contain the contamination. But the kingdom collapsed from within, and the clergy could not stem the disaster.\n\nLordaeron is now a wilderness haunted by the Scourge, so the Church moved its seat south. Under Archbishop Benedictus, its clergy rebuilt their hierarchy in Stormwind's newly constructed Cathedral of Light. There they offer solace, spiritual guidance, and military purpose to the battered survivors of the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the core philosophy of the Church of the Holy Light?",a="The Church teaches that one holy energy connects all living things. Its followers seek righteousness, altruism, and compassion to improve themselves and the world around them. They believe virtue, justice, and self-sacrifice let a person reflect the Light's purest essence.",al={"holy light beliefs","what does the church believe","tenets of the light","church philosophy"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the Church today?",a="Archbishop Benedictus leads the Church of the Holy Light. After Archbishop Alonsus Faol's passing and Lordaeron's fall, Benedictus organized the priesthood from the Cathedral of Light in the heart of Stormwind City.",al={"church leader","who is the archbishop","head of the church"},it="leader"},{q="How was the order of Paladins formed?",a="During the First War, the Horde targeted and massacred unarmored Northshire clerics. Before the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the Knights of the Silver Hand so holy spellcasters could survive at the front, joining knightly combat with divine spellcasting.",al={"origin of paladins","how were paladins created","alonsus faol paladins","formation of silver hand"}},{q="Where are the Church's most sacred places?",a="The Church's oldest holy sites stood in Lordaeron's Eastweald: Andorhal, Stratholme, Tyr's Hand, and Light's Hope Chapel. After the Scourge destroyed the north, Stormwind's Cathedral of Light became the faith's foremost sanctuary and seat of authority.",al={"holy sites","sacred places","important shrines"},it="place"},{q="What role did the Church play against the Plague of Undeath?",a="During the Third War, priests and clerics worked in field hospices across Lordaeron, trying to cleanse the afflicted and halt the plague. Holy magic could not fully reverse the supernatural corruption, and many clergy fell when their patients succumbed and rose as Scourge monstrosities.",al={"church role in plague","holy light curing the plague","scourge and church"},it="conflict"},{q="Do races other than humans follow the Church?",a="Yes. Ironforge dwarves embraced the Church's teachings centuries ago and formed their own orders of priests and paladins. The high elves of Quel'Thalas also adopted its philosophy, mastering restorative healing magic that they later shared with human clerics.",al={"non human light worshipers","do dwarves follow the light","high elf priests"},it="people"},{q="What is the Church of the Holy Light?",a="The Church of the Holy Light is the central religious institution of humanity. Its clergy preach that a benevolent Holy Light dwells within all living beings, urging followers to practice compassion, honor, and justice to bring out the best in themselves and the world. Through their devotion, its priests heal the sick and wounded, while the paladins of the Silver Hand serve as the Church's martial arm to protect the weak and vanquish evil.",al={"what is the church of light","who are the church of holy light","church of holy light"},it="identity",add="1109d54d"},{q="Where did the Church of the Holy Light come from?",a="The Church traces its roots to the faith in the Holy Light that spread among the humans of Arathor. Centuries later, migrants founded the kingdom of Lordaeron, which became a heartland for holy ascetics and pilgrims. Lordaeron's leaders eventually organized these beliefs into a unified church hierarchy, establishing shrines, monasteries, and chapels across the human kingdoms.",al={"origins of the church of light","history of church of holy light","how was the church founded"},it="history",add="e7672a04"},{q="Who is the Church of the Holy Light allied with?",a="The Church is deeply intertwined with the Grand Alliance. During the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol pledged the Church's spiritual and martial support to repel the Horde, establishing the Knights of the Silver Hand to fight on the front lines. Following the fall of Lordaeron, the Church reconstituted its seat at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, working directly alongside the Kingdom of Stormwind and its allies.",al={"church of light faction","who does the church of light support","church of light alliance"},it="allies",add="12379874"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Your holy vows trace to Archbishop Faol's covenant during the Second War. It joined knightly chivalry with the Light's restorative and retributive grace.",["class:Priest"]="Your calling belongs to thousands of years of human devotion. You may comfort the wounded or study the difficult balance between luminescence and shadow.",["race:Human"]="For generations, the Church has blessed human kingdoms through crisis and plague. Its presence in Stormwind remains the spiritual backbone of your civilization.",["race:Dwarf"]="Long allied with the human realms, many Ironforge dwarves share the Holy Light's virtues. They find common ground in its sermons and sanctified halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Church of the Holy Light gives the Alliance moral unity and battlefield hospice care. It remains a symbol of hope against darkness."},kw={"alonsus faol","benedictus","cathedral of light","church","holy light","lordaeron","northshire","paladin","priest","silver hand","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","npc:archbishop-benedictus","topic:light","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:brotherhood-of-northshire","topic:lordaeron","zone:stormwind","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Church of the Holy Light"}}
E["topic:cult-of-the-damned"] = {t="topic",n="Cult of the Damned",z="general",s="Across Lordaeron, the Cult of the Damned still serves the Lich King. Before the Third War, its poisoned grain spread the Scourge and helped bring down humanity's greatest kingdom. Now cultists tend plague cauldrons and necromantic academies in the Plaguelands, while living agents infiltrate the cities of the living.",h="Across Lordaeron, the Cult of the Damned still serves the Lich King.",sec={{t="A Sickness in the Soul",b="Kel'Thuzad founded the cult after hearing the Lich King's whispers from the Frozen Throne. Exiled from the Kirin Tor, the archmage returned to Lordaeron with great wealth and forbidden arts. To the desperate poor, he promised equality and freedom from misery. To wealthy landowners such as House of Barov, he promised eternal life and lasting power over their domains. Both were drawn into a death cult meant to betray their homeland from within.",sp=0},{t="The Poisoned Harvest",b="Beneath Caer Darrow, cultists practiced necromancy in secret. They built abominations and perfected the Plague of Undeath brought from Northrend. Then they contaminated grain stores in Andorhal, Lordaeron's breadbasket.\n\nFlour traveled along merchant routes to homes across the Eastweald. Within days, commoners sickened and died, then rose as thralls under the Lich King's command. When Prince Arthas killed Kel'Thuzad in Andorhal, the cult had already spread too far to stop the kingdom's fall.",sp=0},{t="The Present Threat",b="The Cult of the Damned still threatens northern Lordaeron under the resurrected archlich Kel'Thuzad. Living cultists operate from the ruins of Stratholme and Scholomance. They perform dark rites, tend plague cauldrons among ruined farms, and try to kill Scarlet Crusaders and Forsaken. Their agents pass unnoticed through settlements, poison wells, disrupt supplies, and recruit others for the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why would living mortals join a cult that turns people undead?",a="Kel'Thuzad preyed on mortal weakness. He promised the poor equality and relief from hardship, while offering nobles such as Baron Rivendare and the Barov family immortality and lasting power. Many initiates did not learn the plague's true nature until escape was no longer possible.",al={"why join cult of the damned","cultist motives","why serve scourge"},it="motive"},{q="Why are cultists allowed to stay alive instead of being killed and raised?",a="Living agents can pass unnoticed through human settlements, trade along merchant routes, buy supplies, and undermine kingdoms from within. Cult doctrine treats undeath as a reward earned through devoted service.",al={"why are cultists human","why aren't they undead","living cultists"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Cult of the Damned based?",a="The cult's chief spiritual and scholastic refuge is Scholomance, in the catacombs beneath Caer Darrow. Cultists also gather in Stratholme's ruins, around plague cauldrons in both Plaguelands, and in secret cells within living settlements.",al={"cult headquarters","where is the cult","cult main base"},it="place"},{q="Who founded the Cult of the Damned?",a="Archmage Kel'Thuzad founded the cult after leaving the Kirin Tor in disgrace for forbidden necromancy. He traveled north, communed with the Lich King, gained great power, and returned to Lordaeron to organize the Scourge's mortal vanguard.",al={"who made cult of damned","cult founder","kel'thuzad cult"},it="origin"},{q="How does the Cult of the Damned spread the plague today?",a="Cultists first spread the plague through tainted grain from Andorhal. Now they use great cauldrons across Plaguelands farms, where cauldron lords brew reagents that release blight and raise fallen corpses.",al={"how plague spreads","plague cauldrons","how does cult attack"},it="threat"},{q="What is the cult's relationship to the Forsaken?",a="The Forsaken and the cult are bitter enemies. The Forsaken broke free of the Lich King's command and seek vengeance on the Scourge. Cultists call them stolen property and heretics, and seek to destroy them or reclaim Lordaeron's ruins for the Frozen Throne.",al={"cult vs forsaken","forsaken cult of the damned"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Cult of the Damned?",a="The Cult of the Damned is a clandestine network of living mortals who serve the Lich King and act as the mortal foundation of the Scourge. Composed primarily of fanatical humans alongside members of other races, they infiltrate settlements, study dark necromancy, and work tirelessly to bring death and plague to the living kingdoms in exchange for promises of immortality and power.",al={"what is cult of the damned","who are the cult of the damned","cult of the damned identity"},it="identity",add="13254224"},{q="Who leads the Cult of the Damned?",a="The cult is commanded on Azeroth by the archlich Kel'Thuzad, the former Dalaran archmage who founded the order. Above him reigns the Lich King himself, bound to the Frozen Throne in Northrend, whom all cultists revere as their dark lord and god.",al={"who leads cult of the damned","cult of the damned leader","who is the leader of the cult"},it="leader",add="3f52b63c"},{q="Who are the Cult of the Damned allied with?",a="The cult works directly for the Lich King and serves alongside the legions of the undead Scourge. While they once facilitated the arrival of the Burning Legion during the Third War, their absolute devotion belongs to the throne of Northrend and its lich commander, Kel'Thuzad.",al={"cult of the damned allies","who does the cult work for","who is cult of the damned allied with"},it="allies",add="3a452ce2"},{q="Where did the Cult of the Damned come from?",a="Years before the Third War, the Lich King telepathically reached out from Northrend to Archmage Kel'Thuzad, tempting him with necromantic power. Kel'Thuzad returned to Lordaeron, using his fortune and demagoguery to recruit disillusioned commoners and power-hungry nobles alike. Operating in secret out of Caer Darrow's catacombs, the cult developed the plague of undeath, distributed tainted grain throughout Andorhal and northern Lordaeron, and paved the way for the kingdom's catastrophic downfall.",al={"cult of the damned history","history of cult of the damned","how did the cult start"},it="history",add="3250aa21"},{q="Why are the Cult of the Damned hostile to travelers?",a="The cultists view all living people outside their ranks as raw materials for their necromantic experiments or future soldiers for the Scourge. They attack outsiders on sight to guard their clandestine laboratories, protect their plague cauldrons, and eliminate anyone who could disrupt their dark rituals.",al={"why are cultists hostile","why does the cult attack you","cult of the damned hostile"},it="hostile",add="af150ded"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you remember Lordaeron's fall. The Cult of the Damned recalls how traitors within human cities and estates helped bring humanity down alongside demons.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know cultists as lapdogs who gave up their freedom to the master whose mental chains you fought to break.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a blasphemy against the Holy Light. Cultists use necromancy to corrupt the living and disturb the dead.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the cult stains the Kirin Tor's honor. Kel'Thuzad, one of Dalaran's esteemed archmages, founded it.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier or scout, you must watch for cult infiltrators seeking to spread plague and chaos in living cities such as Stormwind."},kw={"andorhal","caer darrow","cauldron lord","cult of the damned","kel'thuzad","lich king","plague of undeath","plaguelands","scholomance","scourge"},rel={"subzone:scholomance","subzone:andorhal","subzone:caer-darrow","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:forsaken"},src={"Cult of the Damned"}}
E["topic:dark-iron-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Dark Iron clan",z="general",s="In Blackrock Mountain, the Dark Iron clan serves Ragnaros under Emperor Dagran Thaurissan. Driven from Ironforge in the War of the Three Hammers, they called the Firelord from beneath the earth and fell beneath his rule.",h="In Blackrock Mountain, the Dark Iron clan serves Ragnaros under Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.",sec={{t="The War of the Three Hammers",b="The War of the Three Hammers began when High King Modimus Anvilmar died. Three dwarven factions had shared Ironforge, but the Bronzebeards defeated both rivals in the civil war. They drove out the Wildhammers and Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan's Dark Irons.\n\nThaurissan swore vengeance and founded a settlement in the Redridge Mountains. His sorceress wife, Modgud, led an army against Grim Batol. Both assaults failed, and the united Bronzebeard and Wildhammer armies marched on Thaurissan's stronghold. Desperate, he tried to free an apocalyptic being beneath the earth. His ritual broke through the world's core and released Ragnaros the Firelord.",sp=0},{t="Shattered Lands and Bondage",b="Ragnaros's return shattered the peaks around him and formed Blackrock Mountain's blazing caldera. The Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes lie beside it. The cataclysm killed Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan, and the surviving Dark Irons became the Firelord's servants.\n\nOver the centuries, they built Shadowforge City in the mountain's lower chambers. Their artisans and sorcerers mastered stone golems, dark sorceries, and steam-driven siege engines. Under the watch of flamewakers and elemental overlords, they made weapons from the molten elements around them.",sp=0},{t="Spreading Shadow",b="Emperor Dagran Thaurissan rules the clan from his Imperial Seat in Blackrock Depths. He follows Ragnaros's orders and prepares for total war, while secretly plotting to overthrow the Firelord with the strength of all dwarven lands.\n\nDark Iron infiltrators and raiding parties strike in Loch Modan, Dun Morogh, the Badlands, and the Wetlands. Dark Iron forces and an ambassador are also inside Gnomeregan, though their precise role in its fall is unclear.",sp=1},{t="The Stolen Princess",b="Princess Moira Bronzebeard, King Magni's daughter and sole heir, was taken by Dark Iron agents while traveling to Lakeshire. Magni believes she is an enchanted hostage held against her will in Blackrock Depths.\n\nRumors from Shadowforge City tell another tale. Moira has become Emperor Dagran Thaurissan's bride and embraced a place of power among the dwarves her father despises.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Dark Iron capital located?",a="The Dark Iron capital, Shadowforge City, lies deep in the caverns of Blackrock Depths beneath Blackrock Mountain. Its great stone halls hold Senate chambers, barracks, and the emperor's Imperial Seat.",al={"where do dark iron dwarves live","dark iron home","dark iron capital name","shadowforge city location"},it="place"},{q="Why do the Dark Iron dwarves have dark skin and glowing eyes?",a="Dark Iron dwarves have ash-gray or dark skin and glowing red eyes. They live beneath Blackrock Mountain, but the precise cause of their appearance is unknown.",al={"why do dark iron look different","dark iron dwarf appearance","why are they ashen"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Emperor Dagran Thaurissan?",a="The emperor descends directly from the sorcerer-thane who led the Dark Irons into exile. He rules the clan from his Imperial Seat in Blackrock Depths.",al={"dagran thaurissan","who leads dark iron clan","dark iron king"},it="leader"},{q="Why did the Dark Iron clan summon Ragnaros?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorcerer-thane faced defeat as the combined armies of Ironforge and Grim Batol marched on his city. Seeking a weapon to destroy his enemies, he performed an ancient ritual that shattered the mountains and enslaved his people.",al={"how was ragnaros summoned","thaurissan ragnaros summon","why summoned firelord"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Thorium Brotherhood?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood is a splinter faction of Dark Iron craftsmen who broke away from the clan. Based at Thorium Point in Searing Gorge, they trade with outsiders and seek their own fortunes, earning the lasting enmity of their former kin.",al={"thorium brotherhood dark iron","are thorium brotherhood dark irons","friendly dark iron dwarves"}},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves fighting in Gnomeregan?",a="Dark Iron forces, including the Dark Iron Ambassador, are inside fallen Gnomeregan. Their presence suggests involvement with Mekgineer Thermaplugg, but their precise role in the disaster is unclear.",al={"dark iron in gnomeregan","dark iron ambassador gnomeregan","why are dark irons with troggs"},it="why_here"},{q="Are the Dark Irons allied with the Blackrock orcs?",a="No. The Dark Irons once tolerated the Old Horde in the upper spire, but now fight a bitter turf war with the Blackrock orcs above. The Dark Irons hold the depths, while Rend Blackhand's orcs control the upper citadel.",al={"dark iron orc alliance","dark iron vs blackrock clan","who owns blackrock mountain"},it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Dark Irons attack Grim Batol?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, Sorceress Modgud led a Dark Iron army against the Wildhammer clan at Grim Batol. Khardros Wildhammer slew Modgud, but her foul sorceries cursed the fortress so deeply that the Wildhammers could never live there again.",al={"modgud grim batol","why grim batol abandoned","curse of grim batol"},it="history"},{q="What is the Dark Iron clan?",a="The Dark Iron clan is one of the three primary dwarven factions, alongside the Bronzebeards and Wildhammers. Renowned for their sorcery, ruthless ambition, and master stonework, they dwell deep within Blackrock Mountain under their capital of Shadowforge City. Bound in servitude to a fiery master, they wage war against both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"who are dark irons","dark iron dwarves","what are dark irons"},it="identity",add="95b345ff"},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves hostile to travelers?",a="Driven by centuries of bitter hatred toward Ironforge and ensnared by a fiery tyranny, the Dark Irons see all outsiders as enemies or tools. Under their emperor's commands, the clan is preparing for total conquest, launching aggressive raids into neighboring lands and slaughtering anyone who trespasses on their territory.",al={"why do dark irons attack","dark iron hostility","are dark irons evil"},it="hostile",add="eeaf4afe"},{q="Who are the Dark Iron clan allied with?",a="The Dark Iron clan serves a fiery master and his elemental armies, bound in harsh servitude ever since their sorcerers mistakenly summoned him. While they maintain a treacherous rivalry with the Blackrock orcs occupying the upper spire, their forces are also present inside fallen Gnomeregan, though their precise role there is unclear.",al={"dark iron allies","who do dark irons work for","dark iron masters"},it="allies",add="da520a46"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a Bronzebeard, you know the Dark Irons as ancestral traitors and sorcerers. Their old grudges still threaten Ironforge's borders from Loch Modan to Dun Morogh.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may wonder why a Dark Iron Ambassador is deep inside fallen Gnomeregan. The clan's role in its fall remains unclear.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know Dark Iron smiths as masters of fiery metalwork. Their specialized anvils and forges deep in Blackrock Depths are needed to craft legendary armaments.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face Dark Iron border raids and the threat posed by their capture of Ironforge's crown princess, Moira Bronzebeard.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you clash with Dark Iron armies across the Badlands and the Burning Steppes. Both sides seek supremacy over the ruins around Blackrock Spire."},kw={"blackrock","bronzebeard","dark iron","flamelash","modgud","moira","ragnaros","shadowforge","sorcerer-thane","thaurissan"},rel={"topic:dark-iron-dwarf","subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:bronzebeard-clan","topic:wildhammer-clan","zone:searinggorge","zone:burningsteppes","npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:dark-iron-ambassador"},src={"Dark Iron clan"}}
E["topic:dark-iron-dwarf"] = {t="topic",n="Dark Iron dwarf",z="general",s="Beneath Blackrock Mountain, Dark Iron dwarves live under Ragnaros's rule. Banished from Ironforge after the War of the Three Hammers, they have built a society shaped by fire and tyranny.",h="Beneath Blackrock Mountain, Dark Iron dwarves live under Ragnaros's rule.",sec={{t="Fiery Heritage and Exile",b="Dark Iron dwarves have dark gray or soot-black skin and eyes like glowing embers. Their Bronzebeard and Wildhammer cousins look different. Their people split during the War of the Three Hammers, when Sorcerer-thane Thaurissan tried to conquer Ironforge. Defeated, he led them south into the Redridge Mountains.\n\nThere, he sought dark powers to avenge his losses and released Ragnaros the Firelord from the Elemental Plane. The summoning shattered the surrounding peaks into the volcanic waste of Blackrock Mountain. It bound the Dark Iron to fiery servitude.",sp=0},{t="Under the Firelord's Shadow",b="Life in Shadowforge, deep beneath the mountain, is brutal. The Dark Irons were once ambitious and cunning, but generations beneath Ragnaros's oppressive aura have warped much of their culture. Cruelty, paranoia, and tyranny now shape it.\n\nDark Iron law gives one sentence for infractions: trial by combat in the Ring of the Law. Poisoning and political intrigue run so deep that Dark Iron travelers bring their own rations rather than trust food from strangers.",sp=0},{t="Splinters and Outcasts",b="Not all Dark Iron dwarves serve Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and the cult of Ragnaros. Dissident factions have broken away to follow their own ends. The best known is the Thorium Brotherhood, a guild of master smiths based at Thorium Point in Searing Gorge. They left the main clan and hire outsiders to fight their former masters.\n\nOther Dark Irons work as mercenaries, spies, or trade engineers alongside neutral groups such as the Venture Company.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do Dark Iron dwarves have gray skin and red eyes?",a="Dark gray skin and fiery red eyes are natural traits that distinguish Dark Iron dwarves from mountain and hill dwarves. Life deep underground near the mountain's elemental fires has further marked their volcanic nature.",al={"dark iron appearance","why do dark irons look like that","red eyes dark iron"},it="origin"},{q="Are all Dark Iron dwarves evil?",a="No. Imperial Dark Iron society is treacherous. The legendary architect Franclorn Forgewright and the rebel smiths who broke from the clan show honor, valor, and independence from its corruption.",al={"are all dark irons bad","good dark iron dwarves","can dark irons be good"},it="people"},{q="Where is the capital of the Dark Iron dwarves?",a="Dark Iron civilization centers on Shadowforge City, deep in the subterranean caverns of Blackrock Depths within Blackrock Mountain. Their emperor rules from there.",al={"dark iron capital","where do dark irons live","dark iron city"},it="place"},{q="What is the Ring of the Law?",a="The Ring of the Law is the arena where Dark Iron justice is carried out. Crimes against the clan carry the death penalty, and the accused must pay the blood price by fighting waves of vicious beasts and gladiators. Virtually no prisoner survives.",al={"ring of the law","dark iron arena","shadowforge trial"}},{q="What is the Thorium Brotherhood?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood is a rogue faction of Dark Iron craftsmen who broke away from the main clan. Based at Thorium Point in Searing Gorge, they trade their unmatched knowledge of fiery metallurgy and Dark Iron smithing secrets to outsiders willing to undermine the imperial clan.",al={"thorium brotherhood lore","who are the thorium brotherhood","thorium point dwarves"}},{q="What are Dark Iron dwarves?",a="The Dark Irons are a distinct breed of dwarves, predominantly hailing from the Dark Iron clan. Known for their ashen skin, fiery red eyes, and mastery over sorcery and craft, they possess fierce determination and notorious tempers. While most dwell in their subterranean domain beneath Blackrock Mountain, some belong to independent factions like the Thorium Brotherhood or mercenary outfits.",al={"who are dark irons","dark iron dwarves","what is dark iron dwarf"},it="identity",add="95842395"},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves hostile to travelers?",a="Centuries of isolation, internal treachery, and the corrupting presence of the Firelord, Ragnaros, have left the Dark Iron clan manipulative, cruel, and deeply suspicious of outsiders. They view transgressions against their clan with extreme severity, punishing trespassers and criminals with death or bloody combat in the Ring of the Law.",al={"why do dark irons attack","dark iron dwarves aggressive","why are dark irons hostile"},it="hostile",add="25c6bc58"},{q="Who leads the Dark Iron dwarves?",a="The Dark Iron clan is ruled by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan from his throne in Shadowforge City, deep within Blackrock Depths.",al={"dark iron dwarf leader","who is emperor of dark irons","dark iron ruler"},sp=1,it="leader",add="606deda9"},{q="Who are the Dark Iron dwarves allied with or serving?",a="Most of the Dark Iron clan is bound in servitude to the elemental Firelord, Ragnaros, whose fiery influence permeates their society. Many also operate alongside elemental forces and dark cults, while independent splinter groups like the Thorium Brotherhood work against the clan's leadership.",al={"who do dark irons work for","dark iron allies","dark irons ragnaros"},it="allies",add="d8b686f4"},{q="Where did the Dark Iron dwarves come from?",a="The Dark Irons were once one of the three ruling dwarven clans of Ironforge. Following the War of the Three Hammers, their sorcerer-thane Thaurissan fled south and inadvertently summoned Ragnaros the Firelord into Azeroth. The cataclysm shattered the Redridge Mountains, creating Blackrock Mountain and chaining the Dark Iron clan to the Firelord's will.",al={"dark iron dwarf origin","history of dark irons","war of the three hammers"},it="history",add="7edffefb"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge, the Dark Irons are a family feud turned existential threat, rooted in their bloody rebellion during the War of the Three Hammers.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Dark Iron artisans are renowned smiths with exclusive mastery of Dark Iron ore. It takes the searing heat of Blackrock Mountain's Black Forge to melt and shape it.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts watch the Dark Irons warily. Their imperial armies are an aggressive, expansionist menace pressing against Ironforge's southern borders.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde sees the Dark Irons as dangerous zealots occupying Blackrock Mountain and threatening Horde supply routes through the Badlands and nearby passes."},kw={"blackrock depths","dark iron","dwarf","ironfoe","ragnaros","shadowforge","thaurissan","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:dwarf","subzone:blackrock-mountain","subzone:thorium-point","zone:searinggorge","subzone:grim-batol","zone:ironforge","topic:venture-company"},src={"Dark Iron dwarf"}}
E["topic:darkspear-tribe"] = {t="topic",n="Darkspear tribe",z="multi",s="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, the Darkspear tribe follows Thrall’s Horde. Driven from Stranglethorn Vale and rescued from a sea witch in the Great Sea, the jungle trolls follow Shadow Hunter Vol’jin from Sen’jin Village. They now struggle to reclaim the Echo Isles from Zalazane.",h="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, the Darkspear tribe follows Thrall’s Horde.",sec={{t="Exile and Salvation",b="Once part of the broken Gurubashi Empire in Stranglethorn Vale, the Darkspear were smaller and less ruthless than their neighbors. For centuries, they endured famine and fought the brutal Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter tribes. Driven out to sea, they settled on remote islands, where murlocs, Kul Tiran sailors, and a naga sea witch threatened them.\n\nTheir elder chieftain, Sen’jin, was captured and slain in dark rites beneath the sea. Before he died, he foretold that the orc Warchief Thrall would lead the Darkspear to a new destiny. Thrall’s fleet rescued the survivors. They pledged loyalty to the new Horde and sailed west to Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Echo Isles",b="After reaching Durotar, the Darkspear made their home on the tropical Echo Isles, just off the mainland coast. Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet drove them into the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh for a time. Horde forces then destroyed the invaders.\n\nWitch doctor Zalazane embraced twisted voodoo and seized control of his kin’s minds. To preserve his free people, Vol’jin, Sen’jin’s son and successor, ordered another evacuation. The Darkspear now live in coastal Sen’jin Village. Champions cross the water to slay Zalazane and free their thrall-bound brothers.",sp=1},{t="Voodoo and the New Horde",b="The Darkspear have adapted quickly to the Horde’s values of honor, unlike their cannibalistic jungle kin. They have enclaves in Malaka’jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, Shadowprey Village in Desolace, and Zoram’gar Outpost in Ashenvale. In Orgrimmar, they make their spiritual home in the Valley of Spirits, where shadow hunters and witch doctors commune with the loa.\n\nTheir scouts, bat riders, and powerful hexes are respected. Yet old traditions run deep, and some ancient rites their allies frown upon are still practiced quietly in the dark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Darkspear trolls in the Horde?",a="During the Third War, Warchief Thrall’s fleet took shelter on the Darkspear islands during a violent storm. A naga sea witch and her murloc minions captured the trolls and orcs, but Thrall freed them. Chieftain Sen’jin died in the escape after foreseeing that Thrall would guide the Darkspear to safety. In gratitude, Sen’jin’s son Vol’jin swore the tribe’s allegiance to the Horde.",al={"why trolls horde","darkspear thrall origin","how did trolls join horde"},it="allies"},{q="Who leads the Darkspear tribe right now?",a="Vol’jin leads the Darkspear tribe. He is the son of the fallen chieftain Sen’jin, a cunning shadow hunter, and one of Warchief Thrall’s closest and most trusted confidants. Vol’jin advises the Horde from Orgrimmar’s Valley of Spirits and oversees the struggle to reclaim the Echo Isles.",al={"darkspear leader","who is troll leader","troll chieftain"},it="leader"},{q="Why do the Darkspear live in Sen'jin Village instead of the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear live in Sen’jin Village because witch doctor Zalazane betrayed them on the Echo Isles. He used dark magic to enslave the minds of his fellow trolls. Rather than slaughter their enchanted kin, Vol’jin ordered the free Darkspear to retreat to the mainland shore and founded Sen’jin Village as a base for their fight.",al={"why senjin village","what happened to echo isles","why are echo isles hostile"},it="why_here"},{q="Where did the Darkspear originally come from?",a="The Darkspear came from the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, where they belonged to the fractured Gurubashi Empire. Smaller and less merciless than rivals such as the Bloodscalp and Skullsplitter, they suffered constant warfare and starvation until they were driven out of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"darkspear original home","darkspear stranglethorn","where are darkspear from"},it="history"},{q="Do Darkspear trolls still practice cannibalism?",a="Officially, the Darkspear have renounced cannibalism and headhunting as tribal policy so they can live in harmony with Thrall’s Horde and honor their alliance. Centuries of jungle heritage run deep, and whispers persist that darker traditional rites are still observed in secret, far from prying eyes.",al={"are darkspear cannibals","troll cannibalism horde","do horde trolls eat people"}},{q="What deities do the Darkspear worship?",a="The Darkspear revere the loa, powerful primal spirits and animal gods. Their faith centers on a vast pantheon, honored through the voodoo rites of their witch doctors and shadow hunters.",al={"darkspear religion","darkspear gods","troll loa"}},{q="What is the Darkspear tribe?",a="The Darkspear are a tribe of jungle trolls who stand as core members of Thrall's Horde. Once driven out of their ancient lands in Stranglethorn Vale, they survived exile, a perilous sea voyage, and betrayal at home. Known for their adaptability and cunning, they have embraced the Horde's code of honor while maintaining their traditions of shadow magic, voodoo, and loa worship.",al={"who are darkspear trolls","what are the darkspear","darkspear tribe"},it="identity",add="f751a05c"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you carry the weight of an exiled people rebuilding on foreign shores. Every blow you strike against Zalazane on the Echo Isles or your brutal Gurubashi cousins in Stranglethorn Vale helps secure your tribe’s survival.",["race:Orc"]="The bond between orc and troll was forged in the blood of the Third War. Thrall considers Vol’jin his closest brother-in-arms, and Darkspear scouts and witch doctors serve faithfully beside Durotar’s warrior clans.",["faction:Horde"]="From bat riders defending the skies to herbalists brewing draughts in Stonetalon, the Darkspear bring mystical cunning and stealth to the Horde’s raw martial might.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how Darkspear shamans join the ancient worship of primal loa spirits with elemental teachings learned from their orc and tauren allies. Je’neu Sancrea represents the tribe within the Earthen Ring."},kw={"darkspear","echo isles","gurubashi","loa","malaka'jin","sen'jin","shadowprey","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","quest:826","subzone:valley-of-spirits","topic:troll","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Darkspear tribe"}}
E["topic:defias-brotherhood"] = {t="topic",n="Defias Brotherhood",z="general",s="Across Stormwind’s southern lands, the Defias Brotherhood wages war on the kingdom. Bandits, brigands, and assassins terrorize the farmlands. From a hidden redoubt, they seek to overthrow the corrupt House of Nobles and lay waste to Stormwind.",h="Across Stormwind’s southern lands, the Defias Brotherhood wages war on the kingdom.",sec={{t="A Web of Conspiracies",b="Far beyond a band of displaced laborers, the Defias Brotherhood has spread its reach. VanCleef hired mercenary goblins to oversee armaments, joined forces with Riverpaw gnolls and Elwynn kobolds, and traded with cutthroat pirates such as the Bloodsail Buccaneers.\n\nHighwaymen rob gold shipments across Elwynn Forest. Their agents gained a foothold in Duskwood, then uncovered a cursed artifact in Roland's Doom. Treacherous aristocrats in the House of Nobles secretly support them, and the Brotherhood arranges kidnappings aimed at the Alliance's highest offices.",sp=1,bt={"unsent.lescovar"}},{t="The Juggernaught in the Deadmines",b="Beneath Moonbrook, goblin engineers secretly build the Defias Juggernaught at Ironclad Cove. The iron-plated warship is a floating fortress, meant to sail through underground coastal waterways and bombard Stormwind City from the sea. Its guns would reduce the city's grand architecture to rubble.\n\nThe conspiracy reaches the royal court. Corrupt nobles such as Lord Gregor Lescovar act as eyes and ears for the uprising. Lady Katrana Prestor's court machinations keep the kingdom divided and blind to the fleet rising beneath Westfall.",sp=2,bt={"defias.juggernaut","unsent.lescovar","prestor.onyxia"}},{t="From Masons to Marauders",b="After the Second War, the Stonemasons Guild rebuilt Stormwind from smoldering ruins into a grand stone capital. When the work was done, the House of Nobles refused the promised payment, citing crushing wartime debt. Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef spoke for his workers and demanded fair restitution. The nobles ordered the guild disbanded. Riots followed, and the laborers were driven from Stormwind into exile.\n\nOutlawed and stripped of their livelihood, VanCleef and the desperate workers banded together. They bound red silk around their faces for the blood of the wronged. Then they turned to highway robbery to claim what they believed they were owed.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="The Shadow Over Westfall",b="With the royal army stretched thin, VanCleef made Westfall's neglected farmlands the Brotherhood's base. The bandits seized Moonbrook and took over the abandoned tunnels beneath the Deadmines. Defias agents took local mines and drove farmers from their homes with reprogrammed harvest golems. They also salted the earth to starve the region.\n\nThe Crown could not or would not send soldiers to protect rural citizens. From Sentinel Hill, local farmers formed The People's Militia. Now they wage a desperate war of attrition against an enemy that outnumbers and outguns them.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red bandanas?",a="Edwin VanCleef and the exiled stonemasons wore red silk bandanas as a sign of defiance. The color recalls the blood shed by the workers who rebuilt Stormwind, then faced broken promises, violence, and exile from the nobility.",al={"defias mask meaning","why red silk","red bandanas meaning"},sp=1,it="name",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Why is the Brotherhood attacking innocent farmers instead of nobles?",a="The Brotherhood began with real grievances against the nobility, but years of lawless exile turned it into a brutal criminal empire. Desperation, greed, and the arrival of ruthless cutthroats and goblins drove its members to pillage homesteads, burn crops, and seize mines to fund their war machine.",al={"why defias attack farmers","why hurt westfall","defias motive"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant guildmaster of the Stonemasons Guild, which rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. Skilled in stealth and subterfuge, he founded the Defias Brotherhood after the House of Nobles refused to pay the workers. He now directs its operations from deep within the Deadmines.",al={"who is vancleef","edwin vancleef lore","defias leader"},sp=1,it="leader",bt={"defias.masons","defias.hideout"}},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send the army to deal with the Defias?",a="The kingdom's coffers are drained, and the Stormwind Army is stretched thin guarding distant outposts such as those in Stranglethorn. Gridlock in the House of Nobles further paralyzes the throne, leaving rural Westfall and Duskwood to rely on volunteer militias.",al={"where is the stormwind army","why no guards in westfall","why people's militia"},sp=2,it="conflict"},{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer defense force organized by Gryan Stoutmantle and the beleaguered farmers of Sentinel Hill. Stormwind has sent almost no soldiers to drive the Defias from Westfall, so local citizens took up arms to defend their land.",al={"peoples militia westfall","gryan stoutmantle militia","sentinel hill army"},it="conflict"},{q="What are the Defias building inside the Deadmines?",a="Goblin engineers and rogue artisans are building the Defias Juggernaught in Ironclad Cove, a hidden cavern beneath the earth. The massive iron-plated war galley is meant to sail into Stormwind Harbor and destroy the capital.",al={"deadmines ship","what are they building deadmines","defias juggernaught"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"defias.juggernaut"}},{q="Did the Defias have something to do with the King's disappearance?",a="What became of King Varian Wrynn remains a mystery. He vanished while traveling to a peace summit in Theramore, leaving the child Anduin on the throne under a regent.",al={"did defias kidnap varian","missing king defias","missing diplomat defias"},sp=2,it="ties"},{q="What is the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is an extensive criminal syndicate and rebel order made up of former stonemasons, thieves, brigands, and mercenaries. Originally born out of a bitter dispute between the craftsmen who rebuilt Stormwind and the corrupt nobility who refused to pay them, the group has evolved into a violent underground army committed to overthrowing the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"what is the defias brotherhood","who are the defias","defias brotherhood overview"},it="identity",add="d3e0b685",nx={9}},{q="How did the Defias Brotherhood form?",a="After the Second War, the Stonemasons Guild restored Stormwind City from ruins. When the work was complete, the House of Nobles, burdened by military debt, refused to pay them. The guildmaster, Edwin VanCleef, led riots in protest, and the stonemasons were driven into exile. They took refuge in Westfall and turned to banditry to claim their promised wages, steadily swelling their ranks with criminals and outcasts.",al={"defias origin","history of defias","how did defias start","stonemasons guild defias"},it="history",add="5e60415a"},{q="Why are the Defias Brotherhood operating in Westfall and Elwynn?",a="The Defias base their primary operations beneath the town of Moonbrook in the Deadmines of Westfall, an impoverished region neglected by Stormwind's military. From there, they spread through Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and Duskwood to seize valuable mines, raid supply lines, and keep Stormwind's stretched defenses preoccupied while they secretly prepare a catastrophic strike against the capital.",al={"why are defias in westfall","why are defias in elwynn","where are defias located"},it="why_here",add="a3005855"},{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood allied with?",a="The Brotherhood has forged ties across the southern lands. In Elwynn Forest, they employ kobolds to secure captured mines, while coordinating with Riverpaw gnolls in Westfall. They have engaged goblin engineers to build deadly harvest golems, dealt with the Bloodsail Buccaneers for maritime expertise, and covertly collaborated with treacherous figures inside the capital.",al={"defias allies","who works with defias","defias brotherhood partners"},sp=1,it="allies",add="b1c3d7cc",bt={"q65.7"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, the Defias are a bitter reminder of rot within Stormwind. Aristocratic greed turned honest city builders into cutthroats.",["class:Paladin"]="The Knights of the Silver Hand and church leaders such as Duthorian Rall call on you to defend homesteaders like Daphne Stilwell from Defias brigands in Westfall.",["class:Rogue"]="Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7 watch the Defias closely. VanCleef's operatives rival royal scouts in lockpicking, stealth, and deadly ambushes beneath the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="The uprising threatens the kingdom's stability. It chokes Westfall's grain supplies, destabilizes gold mines, and shakes public faith in Stormwind's leadership."},kw={"bandanas","brotherhood","deadmines","defias","elwynn","juggernaught","moonbrook","stonemasons","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","zone:westfall","zone:deadmines","topic:stonemasons-guild","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:moonbrook","quest:65"},src={"Defias Brotherhood"}}
E["topic:dragonmaw-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Dragonmaw clan",z="general",s="Across Khaz Modan, Dragonmaw remnants still lurk in wetlands and mountains. During the Second War, they became infamous for subduing and riding red dragons. After Alexstrasza was freed, the scattered orcs remained hostile to both the Alliance and Thrall's New Horde.",h="Across Khaz Modan, Dragonmaw remnants still lurk in wetlands and mountains.",sec={{t="From Draenor to Azeroth",b="The Dragonmaw crossed the Dark Portal from Draenor with the Old Horde. On Azeroth, they turned their skill toward subduing its winged terrors.",sp=0},{t="The Demon Soul and Grim Batol",b="Black dragon Deathwing whispered to Zuluhed the Whacked, chieftain of the Dragonmaw, and led him to an ancient golden disk called the Dragon Soul. Zuluhed gave it to Nekros Skullcrusher, his greatest warlock. Nekros drew on its fel taint and named it the Demon Soul. With its agonizing power, he ensnared Alexstrasza the Life-Binder.\n\nThe Dragonmaw fortified Grim Batol, an abandoned dwarven bastion, and chained the Dragonqueen in darkness. During the Second War, they forced her red dragon brood to serve the Old Horde as aerial dreadnoughts.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Dragon Riders",b="The Dragonmaw reign ended when the Demon Soul was destroyed, freeing Alexstrasza and her flight from psychic torment. Alexstrasza devoured Nekros Skullcrusher, and her vengeful flight laid waste to Grim Batol. The clan's strength broke.\n\nRouted and terrified, survivors scattered into the Wetlands' marshy bogs and the jagged peaks around Grim Batol. The Dragonmaw who remain on Azeroth are desperate, feral renegades. They fiercely guard their dwindling camps against dwarven patrols and vengeful dragons, and remain hostile to both the Alliance and Thrall's New Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are they called the Dragonmaw if they are from Draenor?",a="The clan became infamous on Azeroth for enslaving and riding red dragons for the Old Horde during the Second War.",al={"dragonmaw name origin","orcish name"},it="name"},{q="How did the clan manage to control giant red dragons?",a="The Demon Soul gave Nekros Skullcrusher power over the dragons. The black Aspect Deathwing had passed the ancient artifact to the clan, and Nekros used it to inflict torturous agony on Alexstrasza. He forced her and her flight to obey under threat of her destruction.",al={"how did they control dragons","demon soul enslavement","how was alexstrasza captured"},it="power"},{q="Are the Dragonmaw part of Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Dragonmaw served the Old Horde of Blackhand and his sons. Thrall's New Horde rejected demon worship and the enslavement of dragons, leaving the Dragonmaw as renegade outcasts hostile to both Horde and Alliance.",al={"are dragonmaw in horde","dragonmaw new horde","thrall and dragonmaw"},it="side"},{q="What happened to the clan after the Second War?",a="When the Demon Soul was destroyed, the freed red dragons turned on the Dragonmaw and destroyed Grim Batol. Nekros was slain, and survivors fled into the Wetlands and neighboring mountains. They remain entrenched there as aggressive raiders.",al={"where are the dragonmaw now","dragonmaw after second war","what happened to grim batol"},it="history"},{q="Who is Zuluhed the Whacked?",a="Zuluhed the Whacked was the Dragonmaw clan's elder shaman and chieftain. Deathwing first gave him visions of dragon riding.",al={"zuluhed","chieftain of dragonmaw","who leads dragonmaw"},it="leader"},{q="Where can Dragonmaw orcs be found right now?",a="Dragonmaw orcs are found on Azeroth mainly in the Wetlands, around Angerfang Encampment and the grim approaches to Grim Batol. They constantly skirmish with the dwarves of Menethil Harbor and the Wildhammer clan.",al={"dragonmaw locations","where to find dragonmaw","dragonmaw wetlands"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Dragonmaw clan?",a="The Dragonmaw clan is an orcish clan from Draenor. They gained infamy during the Second War after using the Demon Soul to enslave the Dragonqueen Alexstrasza and force the red dragonflight to fight for the Old Horde. Broken after losing control of their dragons at Grim Batol, they remain a dangerous, renegade remnant in the eastern lands.",al={"who are dragonmaw","dragonmaw clan info","what are dragonmaw"},it="identity",add="27e0e992"},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw hostile to travelers?",a="The Dragonmaw are unrepentant remnants of the Old Horde who reject Thrall's peaceful new path. Embittered by the loss of their enslaved dragons and driven from Grim Batol, they survive through violent raiding, clashing fiercely with local Wildhammer dwarves, Alliance travelers, and anyone else who ventures near their fortified encampments in the marshlands.",al={"why dragonmaw attack","are dragonmaw evil","why are dragonmaw hostile"},it="hostile",add="ef3e041c"},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw clan allied with?",a="The Dragonmaw remnants in the Wetlands operate outside Thrall's New Horde. Under Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, they defend their camps against nearby enemies and seek revenge against the dragons that destroyed their power at Grim Batol.",al={"dragonmaw allies","who do dragonmaw work for","dragonmaw faction"},it="allies",add="2417d206"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance remembers the terrifying rain of fire the Dragonmaw brought upon its fleets and armies during the Second War. Any sighting in Khaz Modan brings an immediate military response.",["race:Dwarf"]="To dwarves, the Dragonmaw are a desecration. They fouled the ancient fortress of Grim Batol and still infest Khaz Modan's mountain passes.",["race:Orc"]="To the orcs of Thrall's New Horde, the Dragonmaw embody the cruelty and fel corruption of the Old Horde that brought ruin upon their people.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks study Nekros Skullcrusher's history. His mastery of the Demon Soul showed how fel energies could subjugate even Azeroth's grandest creatures."},kw={"alexstrasza","deathwing","demon soul","dragon soul","dragonmaw","grim batol","nekros skullcrusher","red dragonflight","wetlands","zuluhed the whacked"},rel={"subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands","topic:second-war","topic:old-horde","topic:new-horde","npc:deathwing","npc:orgrim-doomhammer"},src={"Dragonmaw clan"}}
E["topic:druid"] = {t="topic",n="Druid",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, Druid protect the wild and heal the wounded with nature’s power. They draw on wild spirits, the celestial bodies, and the Emerald Dream, and take beast forms to defend the land. Night elves have followed this path for ages, tauren have renewed it, and the Skyborne keep their own traditions.",h="Across Kalimdor, Druid protect the wild and heal the wounded with nature’s power.",sec={{t="Wardens of the Wilds",b="Druidism binds its followers to nature and to the demigod Cenarius. Druids call up roots to hold their foes, draw power from the moon and stars, and use healing plants to mend bone and flesh. Their charge is to preserve the world’s balance and guard the wild from corruption and exploitation.",sp=0},{t="The Gift of Shapeshifting",b="Shapeshifting is the druid’s mark. Through spiritual devotion, druids channel the primal nature of Azeroth’s beasts. They take a bear’s thick hide to endure attacks, become lithe feline hunters to strike from shadow, or assume aquatic and avian forms to cross sea and sky. In animal form, their mouths rarely shape mortal words, yet their strength rivals the wild’s fiercest predators.",sp=0},{t="The Cenarion Circle",b="Cenarius taught Malfurion Stormrage the druidic arts ten thousand years ago. Later, the Cenarion Circle gave mortal druidism its order. From sacred Moonglade, it watches over druids across Kalimdor, apart from mortal factions and political disputes. For ages, only night elf men belonged, spending centuries in the Emerald Dream. After the Third War, night elf women and tauren joined them.",sp=0},{t="Druids of the Skyborne",b="The Skyborne learned druidism long ago. When common folk joined the Shal'nan's rebellion against Prince Tortheldrin in Eldre'Thalas, they took up nature magic, influenced by the Cenarion Circle to the north. Tortheldrin scorned the practice as beneath the Highborne. Their descendants still follow that path: the Nightclaw Druids of Shadowgale Forest on Zephras Isle remain largely apart from other Skyborne factions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was the first mortal druid?",a="Malfurion Stormrage was the first mortal to master druidic arts. He learned directly from the demigod Cenarius about ten thousand years ago, before the War of the Ancients.",al={"first druid","who founded druidism","malfurion first druid"}},{q="How can tauren become druids?",a="Tauren learn the ways of the wild under Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem of Thunder Bluff. They now belong to the Cenarion Circle alongside the night elves.",al={"tauren druid lore","why are tauren druids","hamuul runetotem druid"}},{q="What is the Cenarion Circle?",a="The Cenarion Circle guides druids across Azeroth and protects nature. It stands apart from the Alliance and the Horde. Its members answer to the Circle’s archdruids and gather in sacred Moonglade.",al={"cenarion circle lore","what is moonglade order"}},{q="Can druids speak while in animal form?",a="Druids generally cannot speak normally in animal form because their voices reflect the beasts they have become. A few rare and exceptionally powerful druids have found magical ways around this limit.",al={"can druids talk in bear form","shapeshift talking lore"}},{q="What is the Emerald Dream?",a="The Emerald Dream mirrors Azeroth as it might be without civilization’s touch. Night elf druids have spent centuries asleep as they walk its paths and commune with nature’s spirits.",al={"emerald dream lore","where do druids sleep"}},{q="Why were druids originally sleeping for centuries?",a="After the World Tree Nordrassil blessed them, night elf druids entered the Barrow Dens to wander the Emerald Dream for centuries. They aided Ysera’s green dragonflight in nurturing Azeroth’s spiritual ecosystem, until the Third War called them awake.",al={"druid hibernation","barrow dens sleeping","long slumber"}},{q="Which races can be druids?",a="Night elves and tauren belong to the Cenarion Circle, while the Skyborne keep their own druidic traditions. The Nightclaw Druids live on Zephras Isle.",al={"who can be a druid","druid races","skyborne druid"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For ten thousand years, kaldorei druids have guarded Kalimdor in quiet slumber. They keep nature’s balance under Malfurion Stormrage and the demigod Cenarius.",["race:Tauren"]="Under Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, tauren have renewed an ancient bond with the wilds. They have joined the Cenarion Circle in sacred Moonglade and follow the path of the Earth Mother.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you guard the balance with animal strength, healing magic, and celestial power. You draw wisdom from Cenarius and the Emerald Dream.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne druid, you follow the path taken by Eldre'Thalas common folk during the Shal'nan's rebellion. The Nightclaw Druids of Shadowgale Forest still keep that tradition."},kw={"bear form","cat form","cenarion circle","cenarius","druid","emerald dream","hamuul","malfurion","moonglade","shapeshifter"},rel={"topic:cenarion-circle","topic:cenarius","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:emerald-dream","quest:5921","quest:1489","npc:remulos","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:skyborne"},src={"Druid"}}
E["topic:druids-of-the-fang"] = {t="topic",n="Druids of the Fang",z="general",s="In the Wailing Caverns, the Druids of the Fang pursue their design. These rogue night elves severed ties with the Cenarion Circle and took serpent forms under Lord Serpentis. Their true origin remains a mystery to outsiders. They seek to seize the underground waters and remake the Barrens as their own paradise.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, the Druids of the Fang pursue their design.",sec={{t="A Noble Vision Turned Poisonous",b="Naralex led young druids into the Wailing Caverns to restore the Barrens. The land had once been a lush sanctuary, and he hoped to bring it back. Beneath the caverns, they reached natural fissures and springs. Naralex entered an induced slumber to channel the living energies of the Emerald Dream into those waters. He hoped to revive the scorched savannah above.",sp=0},{t="Descent into Nightmare",b="Within Naralex's trance, a malevolent nightmare took hold where the Emerald Dream's serenity should have been. Its darkness spread through the caverns, warping the wildlife and poisoning the underground springs. Naralex's acolytes did not flee to seek help from the Cenarion Circle. The nightmare overwhelmed them, changing their minds and spirits along with the life beneath the earth.",sp=1,bt={"q886.5"}},{t="The Fang Ascendant",b="Naralex's prize pupil had once been a devoted student. He cast aside his master's teachings and embraced the corruption as Lord Serpentis. He gathered the fallen acolytes into the Druids of the Fang and took the venomous forms of vipers and serpents, rather than the bear and cat forms Cenarius sanctioned.\n\nThe Fang hold their sleeping master captive and seek to feed on his nightmare. They would remake the Barrens as a paradise ruled by serpents.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="The Druids of the Fang are night elf druids who entered the Wailing Caverns under Naralex. The nightmare in his trance drove the acolytes mad and transformed them into fanatical snake-worshiping renegades.",al={"druids of the fang lore","who are the fang druids","wailing caverns druids"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q886.5"}},{q="Why did they enter the Wailing Caverns originally?",a="Naralex and his acolytes entered the Wailing Caverns to reach its underground springs. They hoped to channel the Emerald Dream's vitality through the waters and turn the arid Barrens back into a thriving green forest.",al={"why are they in wailing caverns","naralex goal","why heal the barrens"},it="why_here"},{q="Who leads the Druids of the Fang?",a="Lord Serpentis leads the Druids of the Fang. Once the foremost and brightest of Naralex's students, he fell into madness when the nightmare struck and declared himself leader of the new order.",al={"leader of the fang","lord serpentis lore","who leads them"},sp=1,it="leader"},{q="What animal forms do they take?",a="The Druids of the Fang take the forms of venomous serpents and vipers. They embrace serpentine magic and vicious snake forms instead of the bears, cats, or stormcrows of traditional Cenarion Circle druids.",al={"snake form druids","fang druid shapeshift","serpent form"}},{q="How does the Cenarion Circle view them?",a="The Cenarion Circle sees the Druids of the Fang as a dangerous aberration and cult. Elders such as Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff and Naralex's loyalists work urgently to eliminate the Fang's leaders and cleanse the corruption before it destroys the land.",al={"cenarion circle opinion","are they part of the cenarion circle","hamuul on the fang"}},{q="What happened to Naralex?",a="Naralex lies trapped in a deep, agonizing slumber in the heart of the Wailing Caverns. His disciples keep him confined and use his ongoing nightmare to warp the caverns and their own magic.",al={"is naralex dead","naralex status","where is naralex"},sp=1},{q="Why are the Druids of the Fang hostile?",a="When Naralex tapped into the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens, his vision decayed into an encroaching nightmare. That nightmare warped the minds and spirits of his disciples, driving them mad. Now twisted into the Druids of the Fang, they violently attack any intruders to protect their corrupted domain and force the surrounding world to reflect their nightmarish visions.",al={"why do druids of the fang attack","why are druids of the fang aggressive","druids of the fang enemies"},it="hostile",add="f17ecb7b"},{q="How did the Druids of the Fang come to exist?",a="They were originally a noble order of night elf druids who followed Naralex into the subterranean springs of the Wailing Caverns. Their mission was benevolent: channel the Emerald Dream to restore lush life to the arid Barrens. However, the Dream twisted into madness around Naralex, corrupting his followers and turning his finest student, Lord Serpentis, toward dark fanatical devotion.",al={"druids of the fang origin","how did druids of the fang start","history of druids of the fang"},it="history",add="1c4e8a0d"},{q="Why are they called the Druids of the Fang?",a="Rather than embracing traditional druidic forms like bears or cats, these fallen druids embraced the aspect of the serpent. Under the guidance of Lord Serpentis and their serpentine leaders, they shapeshift into vipers, employ deadly venom, and keep lethal reptiles as companions, abandoning traditional Cenarion paths to embody the venomous fang.",al={"why druids of the fang","druids of the fang name meaning","why the fang name"},it="name",add="d5ccf0b1"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, the Druids of the Fang show the peril of corruption in the Emerald Dream. They show what follows when a druid abandons Cenarion harmony for twisted, unorthodox animal forms.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Nara Wildmane and Thunder Bluff's concern with ending the Fang's threat. Their defilement of the Barrens' water affronts the Earth Mother.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing kaldorei kin become a feral, nightmare-ridden snake cult in the heart of Kalimdor brings sorrow and shame to your traditions."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","emerald dream","nara wildmane","naralex","nightmare","serpentis","snake form","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lord-serpentis","npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","quest:1489","zone:barrens"},src={"Druids of the Fang"}}
E["topic:dwarf"] = {t="topic",n="Dwarf",z="general",s="In Khaz Modan, dwarves keep to the mountain homes they carved from stone. Once earthen, they changed under the Curse of Flesh and now live across Khaz Modan and beyond. King Magni Bronzebeard rules from Ironforge, beneath the peaks of Dun Morogh, a steadfast heart of the Alliance.",h="In Khaz Modan, dwarves keep to the mountain homes they carved from stone.",sec={{t="Sons of the Mountain",b="Dwarves began as earthen, beings forged by the titans who slept for ages in Uldaman's vaults. The Curse of Flesh changed them into creatures of blood and bone. They took the name dwarves and made their home in Khaz Modan, named for the titan Khaz'goroth. Beneath Dun Morogh's peaks, they carved the stronghold of Ironforge.\n\nTheir bodies endure hardship, and their keen eyes find stone and ore. They bring fierce resolve to the forge and to battle. Their halls ring with roaring hearths, and ale is a favored drink.",sp=0},{t="The War of the Three Hammers",b="After High King Modimus Anvilmar died, the dwarves fought over Ironforge. The Bronzebeard, Wildhammer, and Dark Iron clans each sought power, and their struggle became a civil war. The Bronzebeards took the mountain and drove the other clans out.\n\nSorcerer-Thane Thaurissan of the Dark Irons then waged war against both rivals. His forces were driven beneath the Redridge Mountains, where Thaurissan accidentally summoned Ragnaros the Firelord. Flames consumed the Dark Iron realm, leaving the volcanic wastes of Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes. The survivors became slaves beneath Blackrock Mountain. The Wildhammers, their home devastated, migrated north to Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.",sp=0},{t="Steadfast Shield of the Alliance",b="When the Horde swept across the continent in the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard shut Ironforge's gates against its sieges. Dwarven forces fought beside the Alliance of Lordaeron in heavy plate armor and with muskets, while gryphon riders took to the sky. Their courage helped break the Horde.\n\nIronforge remains one of the Alliance's steadfast defenders. The dwarves have also welcomed their displaced gnome cousins into their halls. Across Khaz Modan, they uncover titan ruins in search of answers about their ancient origins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did the dwarves come from originally?",a="Dwarves descend from the earthen, living stone beings made by the titan keepers. The earthen slept in Uldaman's vaults until the Curse of Flesh changed them into mortal dwarves. Then they settled the mountains of Khaz Modan.",al={"dwarf origin","dwarf lore","how were dwarves made","earthen"}},{q="Who rules the dwarves right now?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Bronzebeard clan from the Great Forge. He led his people through the Second and Third Wars and remains one of the founding pillars of the Grand Alliance.",al={"who is dwarf king","dwarf leader","king of ironforge","magni bronzebeard"}},{q="What are the three main dwarven clans?",a="The three major clans are the Bronzebeards, who rule Ironforge and Dun Morogh; the Wildhammers, who live in the open air of the Hinterlands and ride gryphons; and the Dark Irons, who live beneath Blackrock Mountain under Ragnaros's fiery dominion.",al={"dwarf clans","three hammers","bronzebeard wildhammer dark iron","clans of ironforge"}},{q="Why are the Dark Iron dwarves enemies?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Irons tried to destroy both the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans. Facing defeat, their sorcerer-thane summoned Ragnaros the Firelord. The flames shattered their homeland, and bound the clan to serve elemental fire and shadow beneath Blackrock Mountain.",al={"why are dark irons evil","dark iron clan lore","shadowforge city dwarves"}},{q="Why are gnomes living inside Ironforge?",a="Dwarves and gnomes have shared a close bond for centuries, trading stoneworking secrets for mechanical engineering. When Gnomeregan fell to a trogg invasion and toxic radiation, King Magni gave High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and the refugees shelter in Tinker Town.",al={"why are gnomes in ironforge","ironforge gnomes","what happened to gnomeregan"}},{q="Do dwarves worship the Holy Light?",a="Yes. Many Ironforge dwarves follow the Holy Light, which humans introduced to them. Dwarven priests keep their own teachings, and stout-hearted dwarves have recently joined the Order of the Silver Hand as paladins.",al={"dwarf religion","dwarves holy light","do dwarves believe in the light"}},{q="Which classes can dwarves be?",a="Dwarves train as warriors, paladins, hunters, rogues, priests and shaman.",al={"dwarf classes","what classes can dwarves be","can dwarves be shaman"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you carry a legacy of living stone. Your clans have old blood feuds, and you dig through titan ruins for answers about your origins.",["race:Gnome"]="The dwarves are your oldest and truest allies. They helped build Gnomeregan's first stonework and now shelter your people in Tinker Town.",["faction:Alliance"]="Ironforge's mineral wealth, siege craft and steadfast infantry help guard the Alliance's northern reaches.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you carry the Holy Light with the resolve of Khaz Modan, joining human teachings with dwarven martial discipline.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Dwarven smiths are renowned across Azeroth. The Great Forge's volcanic heat helps them temper arms and armor.",["profession:Mining"]="As a dwarf, you have a keen eye for ore and gemstones buried beneath the earth."},kw={"bronzebeard","dark iron","dun morogh","dwarf","dwarves","earthen","ironforge","khaz modan","magni","uldaman","wildhammer"},rel={"zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh","npc:magni-bronzebeard","topic:bronzebeard-clan","topic:wildhammer-clan","topic:dark-iron-clan","subzone:uldaman","topic:alliance"},src={"Dwarf"}}
E["topic:earth-mother"] = {t="topic",n="Earth Mother",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Earth Mother’s presence lives in the land and its elements. Tauren say she shaped the world, raised the sun and moon, and guides their lives and hopes for what follows death.",h="Across Azeroth, the Earth Mother’s presence lives in the land and its elements.",sec={{t="The Dawn of Creation",b="Tauren creation myths say the Earth Mother shaped Azeroth before day and night, making it a haven for her coming children. She scraped her nails across the new mountains, and the first fires sparked. Her hands carved rivers and ocean beds, while her laughter gave breath to the wind. Then she lifted the primordial fogs into the sky. The first rains coaxed grass, forests, and grain from the soil.",sp=0},{t="Sun, Moon, and the Shu'halo",b="With help from the friendly elements, the Earth Mother brought forth twins: An'she, the sun, and Mu'sha, the moon. She placed the radiant twins in her eyes, so she could rest while keeping them safe. As she opened and closed each lid, day, night, and the seasons began.\n\nLater, she pressed her heart against the fertile earth and breathed the song of life into the land. There she created the shu'halo, the first tauren. She charged the twins and the elements to teach these young mortals to hunt, build, dance, and live in harmony with the wilds.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Heavens",b="In time, the Earth Mother set An'she and Mu'sha in the sky to watch over the land by day and night. Tauren say her spirit now dwells in the world's rivers, trees, plains, and mountains. Every lesser nature spirit springs from her and returns to her in the end.",sp=0},{t="Living Legacy",b="Tauren believe the Earth Mother's spirit still cradles Azeroth. Her ear listens to the winds for her children's prayers, and her heart beats within the deep stone. Tauren hunters, shamans, and druids give thanks to her for every kill and harvest. They believe all life begins in her embrace, and every tauren spirit returns to her soil upon death.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Earth Mother?",a="Tauren worship the Earth Mother as the creator at the heart of their faith. Their myths say she shaped Azeroth's landscape, brought forth the sun and moon, and created the tauren from the soil.",al={"what is the earth mother","earthmother lore","tauren god"},it="identity"},{q="What are her eyes in the sky?",a="An'she, the sun, is the Earth Mother's right eye and brings light and warmth to the world. Mu'sha, the White Lady moon, is her left eye and brings peace and slumber. Tauren myth says she set them in the heavens to watch over the land.",al={"anshe and musha","tauren sun and moon","earth mother eyes"},it="power"},{q="Is the Earth Mother an actual living entity?",a="Tauren believe the Earth Mother is an active, loving spiritual presence throughout the natural world, stone, and winds. Shamans and druids channel nature and elemental spirits through her blessings. Whether she was a primordial giant, a world-soul, or an allegory remains a matter of faith.",al={"is earth mother real","does earth mother exist","who is the earthmother"}},{q="Do other races worship the Earth Mother?",a="The tauren are the Earth Mother's primary worshippers, and other peoples who commune with the land acknowledge her. Some orc shamans and centaur invoke her name respectfully, and her blessings are often exchanged throughout the Horde.",al={"orcs earth mother","who worships earth mother","do trolls believe in earth mother"},it="ties"},{q="What do tauren believe happens after death?",a="Tauren believe every soul returns to the Earth Mother after death, since all living things were born from her touch. Traditional rites commit the deceased to the land, trusting their spirits to rest in her eternal embrace.",al={"tauren afterlife","tauren burial beliefs","returning to the earth mother"},it="history"},{q="How did the Earth Mother create the world and the tauren?",a="According to tauren creation myths, the Earth Mother shaped the mountains, seas, and skies before the dawn of memory. After birthing her twin children, An'she and Mu'sha, the sun and moon, she gave life to the plains and fashioned the first tauren, whom she loved dearly. Tauren believe her spirit still dwells in every river, tree, plain, and mountain of the world.",al={"earth mother creation story","how did earth mother make world","earth mother history"},it="history",add="dbad9a55"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a shu'halo, your society's ways, from respect for prey to the council of chieftains, are rooted in the Earth Mother's law, sacrifice, and enduring love.",["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, your bond with nature is direct communion with the Earth Mother's living body, answering her ancient call to preserve the land's balance.",["class:Shaman"]="As a tauren shaman, you honor the Earth Mother alongside the elemental spirits, remembering that wind, water, fire, and stone were her first companions.",["faction:Horde"]="As an orc or jungle troll in the Horde, you know tauren reverence for the Earth Mother through your alliance with Mulgore. You may invoke her name as a respectful blessing."},kw={"an'she","creation","earth mother","earthmother","mu'sha","mulgore","shu'halo","tauren"},rel={"topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:centaur","zone:feralas","quest:860","quest:6381","topic:light"},src={"Earth Mother"}}
E["topic:elemental-plane"] = {t="topic",n="Elemental Plane",z="general",s="Across the Elemental Plane, its wards still hold the elementals—though cracks now let them reach Azeroth. The titans made this realm to imprison Azeroth’s chaotic elementals, dividing it into Skywall, Deepholm, the Abyssal Maw, and the Firelands. Breaches have brought violent incursions and catastrophic summonings into Azeroth.",h="Across the Elemental Plane, its wards still hold the elementals—though cracks now let them reach Azeroth.",sec={{t="A Prison for Primordial Chaos",b="Long ago, the elementals served as lieutenants to the Old Gods. The titans defeated the Old Gods, then banished the elemental lords and their many servants to the Elemental Plane. They divided the realm into four domains: Skywall for air, Deepholm for earth, the Abyssal Maw for water, and the Firelands for fire. With the elementals gone, nature calmed and peace returned to Azeroth’s surface.",sp=0},{t="Endless Strife",b="Captivity did not still the elementals’ fury. Across their divided domains, the primordial powers wage endless war against one another.",sp=0},{t="Breaching the Wards",b="Strong wards bar the way between Azeroth and the Elemental Plane, but they can break. Two centuries ago, near the desperate end of the War of the Three Hammers, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan pierced the veil and summoned Ragnaros the Firelord from the Firelands. His arrival ruptured the Redridge Mountains and forged Blackrock Mountain.\n\nNow, volatile cracks have opened across Kalimdor. Dimensional rifts keep appearing in Silithus, Un'Goro Crater, Azshara, and Winterspring. Hostile elementals pour through and test the mortal world's defenses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Elemental Plane?",a="The Elemental Plane is where the titans imprisoned Azeroth’s chaotic elementals. Its four domains are Skywall for air, Deepholm for earth, the Abyssal Maw for water, and the Firelands for fire.",al={"what is elemental plane","elemental plane explained","elemental realms"},it="identity"},{q="Who created the Elemental Plane and why?",a="The titans created the Elemental Plane after defeating the Old Gods, whom the elemental lords had served. They banished the elementals there, and nature calmed across Azeroth’s surface.",al={"who made elemental plane","why was elemental plane made","how was elemental plane made"},it="origin"},{q="What are the four realms within the plane?",a="The four domains are Skywall for air, Deepholm for earth, the Abyssal Maw for water, and the Firelands for fire. Each belongs to one of the four primary elements.",al={"four elemental planes","elemental domains","names of elemental realms"},it="place"},{q="Can creatures travel between Azeroth and the Elemental Plane?",a="Ancient wards bar travel between Azeroth and the Elemental Plane, but powerful sorcery or unstable barriers can breach them. Thaurissan summoned Ragnaros across the veil, and volatile rifts now open at times in remote parts of Kalimdor.",al={"portal to elemental plane","visiting elemental plane","how to get to elemental plane"},it="power"},{q="Why are elementals invading Kalimdor right now?",a="Rifts have opened across Silithus, Un'Goro Crater, Azshara, and Winterspring. They let waves of elementals from the Elemental Plane enter mortal lands, where defenders of the Horde and Alliance beat them back.",al={"elemental invasions","why are elementals attacking","elemental rifts kalimdor"},it="conflict"},{q="How was Blackrock Mountain created by the plane?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan tried to summon a fiery power to save his clan. He tore open a gateway to the Firelands and brought Ragnaros into Azeroth. The Firelord’s arrival shattered the surrounding mountains, carving out the Burning Steppes, Searing Gorge, and Blackrock Mountain.",al={"thaurissan ragnaros","creation of blackrock mountain","how did ragnaros get here"},it="history"},{q="Who rules the Elemental Plane?",a="The plane has no single ruler, as its four domains are governed independently by the four mighty Elemental Lords: Ragnaros the Firelord commands the Firelands, Therazane the Stonemother rules Deepholm, Al'Akir the Windlord holds Skywall, and Neptulon the Tidehunter oversees the Abyssal Maw. Rather than cooperating, these entities and their armies have spent millenia locked in endless war against one another across the boundaries of their respective realms.",al={"elemental plane leaders","who leads the elemental plane","elemental plane lords"},it="leader",add="4757a26f"},{q="Who are the elementals allied with?",a="In primordial times, the elementals were bound into service by the Old Gods, warring against the titans and their forged armies on their masters' behalf. In the current age, however, most elementals fight strictly for their respective Elemental Lords. They remain intensely hostile to nearly all mortals, though specific factions or summoners—such as the Dark Iron dwarves who accidentally bound themselves to Ragnaros—occasionally serve or bargain with them.",al={"elemental plane allies","who do elementals serve","elemental allegiances"},it="allies",add="a219565c"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you seek harmony with spirits whose ancient rulers remain imprisoned beyond the veil. Knowing how Azeroth and the Elemental Plane are divided helps explain why summoned elements lash out.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you draw on the distant realms’ fringe energies to conjure elemental familiars. Strict control keeps that magic from tearing wider breaches into the material world.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Dark Iron clan’s grim history warns what can happen when mortal ambition pierces the Elemental Plane to summon beings like Ragnaros.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne, you know Zephras Isle floats high within Skywall, a sanctuary in the Elemental Plane’s windy domain."},kw={"abyssal maw","deepholm","elemental plane","firelands","invasions","ragnaros","skywall"},rel={"topic:titan","topic:old-god","topic:skywall","topic:skyborne","subzone:blackrock-mountain","zone:burningsteppes","zone:searinggorge","npc:highlord-demitrian"},src={"Elemental Plane"}}
E["topic:elune"] = {t="topic",n="Elune",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Elune is chiefly worshipped by the night elves as their protector and mother of Cenarius. The larger moon, the White Lady, is hers, and her gifts reach from healing and peace to lunar fury. Tauren know her as Mu'sha, the gentle left eye of the Earth Mother.",h="Across Azeroth, Elune is chiefly worshipped by the night elves as their protector and mother of Cenarius.",sec={{t="The White Lady",b="Elune is one of the few true deities known across Azeroth, bound to the night sky and the larger moon, the White Lady. Though she has never appeared in bodily form, night elven artists portray her as a radiant kaldorei with alabaster skin, silver hair, and eyes of pure moonlight. Ancient kaldorei legends say she rested in the depths of the Well of Eternity by day, whispering wisdom to the first night elves.",sp=0},{t="The Sisters and the Forest",b="Night elven life, both sacred and civic, centers on devotion to Elune through the Sisterhood of Elune. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads this ancient order. The Sisters call on Elune to mend even lethal wounds, and turn her radiant wrath upon their foes with searing starlight.\n\nElune and the Great White Stag, Malorne, brought forth Cenarius. Through him, Elune's heavenly mysteries are bound to the druidic traditions that tend Kalimdor's wildlands.",sp=0},{t="Aspects and Names",b="Elune is known for peace, harmony, and restoration, yet battle has its place in her worship. As the Night Warrior, she is a fierce patron of battle. She gathers the spirits of fallen heroes and sets them in the heavens, where they ride as stars.\n\nThe nomadic tauren call Elune Mu'sha, the radiant left eye of the Earth Mother. She lights the night and guides wandering hunters beside her fiery twin, An'she the sun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elune?",a="Elune is the moon goddess chiefly worshipped by the night elves and one of Azeroth's few true deities. She is associated with healing, nature, peace, and the White Lady, the world's larger moon.",al={"what is elune","elune lore","who is the moon goddess"},it="identity"},{q="Has Elune ever appeared in person?",a="Elune has never appeared in physical form on Azeroth. Kaldorei artists depict her as a radiant night elf maiden crowned in platinum, with long silver hair and glowing moonlight eyes. Her true cosmic shape remains a mystery.",al={"has elune taken physical form","what does elune look like"}},{q="What is the Night Warrior?",a="The Night Warrior is Elune's fiercest aspect and her patronage of battle. In this form, her wrath rises in combat, and she lifts the spirits of courageous fallen warriors into the night sky to ride among the stars.",al={"elune night warrior","wrath of elune"},it="power"},{q="How is Elune related to Cenarius?",a="Elune and the wild stag demigod Malorne brought forth Cenarius. He inherited his mother's deep love for living creatures and his father's bond with the natural wild and the Emerald Dream.",al={"is elune cenarius mother","cenarius parents"},it="ties"},{q="Do the tauren worship Elune?",a="Yes. Tauren call Elune Mu'sha, the gentle left eye of the Earth Mother. In their myths, she watches over the world by night alongside her solar brother, An'she.",al={"musha","tauren moon goddess","who is musha"},it="people"},{q="Who leads the worship of Elune in Kalimdor?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind leads the Sisterhood of Elune in Kalimdor. The Sisterhood is the chief spiritual and civic authority among the night elves.",al={"priestesses of elune leader","sisters of elune"},it="leader"},{q="Where did Elune come from?",a="Elune's true origins remain shrouded in myth, as she is one of the few true deities worshipped across Azeroth. According to night elven belief, the early kaldorei first sensed her presence after being transformed by the Well of Eternity, where they believed she rested during the day. Ancient legends tell of her taking the Great White Stag, Malorne, as her consort to bring forth Cenarius.",al={"elune origins","where did elune come from","history of elune"},it="history",add="33d35cb4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, your civilization looks to the Mother Moon, from the ruling Sisterhood to the moonlight bathing your woodland settlements.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your ancestral myths praise Mu'sha, the left eye of the Earth Mother, for watching over the tribes and creatures of the dark.",["class:Priest"]="As a night elf priest, you draw divine spells and celestial fury from Elune's guidance. You wield radiant moonlight rather than the Holy Light worshipped in the eastern kingdoms.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are kin to the living wild, and Elune's celestial influence is woven into your astral powers as the divine mother of Lord Cenarius."},kw={"cenarius","elune","mother moon","mu'sha","night warrior","sisterhood of elune","tyrande","white lady"},rel={"npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:cenarius","topic:earth-mother","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:druid","topic:tauren","topic:emerald-dream"},src={"Elune"}}
E["topic:emerald-dream"] = {t="topic",n="Emerald Dream",z="general",s="Druids and green dragons keep watch over the Emerald Dream, where Azeroth’s wild nature runs free. Its lands shift with ancient rhythms, and druids enter to seek communion with the cycle of life.",h="Druids and green dragons keep watch over the Emerald Dream, where Azeroth’s wild nature runs free.",sec={{t="A Mirror of Primordial Azeroth",b="The Emerald Dream shows Azeroth as it might have been without intelligent beings clearing forests or raising cities. Though it lies beyond the physical world, it remains bound to Azeroth’s heartbeat. Shaped during the ancient ordering of the world, it holds forests, plains, and rivers in a wilderness that never rests in one form. Time and distance lose their usual meaning there. A day in the waking world can feel like decades, while landmarks shift before mortal eyes.",sp=0},{t="The Realm of the Dreamer",b="After the ordering of the world, the titans entrusted the Emerald Dream to Ysera the Dreamer, great Aspect of the green dragonflight. She guides Azeroth’s natural rhythms and evolution, dwelling in an unending trance. Through enchanted dreamsight, she perceives both the waking world and its spirit reflection. Green dragons guard the rare natural portals between the physical world and the Dream, watching the boundary between sleep and waking.",sp=0},{t="Druids and the Dreaming",b="For mortal druids, the Emerald Dream is the wellspring of their craft. Through nature magic, they send their spirits into the Dream while their bodies rest in barrow dens, sometimes for years or centuries. There they commune with ancient nature spirits and the Wild Gods, seeking insight into the Great Cycle of life and death. Skilled dreamwalkers move beyond physical laws in their dreamforms. They can cross vast distances or pass through solid barriers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Emerald Dream?",a="The Emerald Dream is a spirit reflection of Azeroth, preserving the world as it was before civilized races changed its landscape. Nature spirits and the green dragonflight dwell in its untamed wilderness.",al={"what is emerald dream","emerald dream lore","the dream explained"},it="identity"},{q="Who rules the Emerald Dream?",a="Ysera the Dreamer and the green dragonflight watch over the Emerald Dream. Ysera guides its natural rhythms, while the Dream’s wild structure follows its ancient course.",al={"who controls emerald dream","emerald dream ruler","ysera dream"},it="leader"},{q="How do mortals enter the Emerald Dream?",a="Most mortals enter the Emerald Dream through druidic slumber, sending their spirits into dreamforms while their bodies rest in barrows. Rare physical portals guarded by green dragons also link the Dream to Azeroth, and crossing them is perilous.",al={"visiting emerald dream","how to enter the dream","dreamform"}},{q="Can you change things inside the Dream?",a="Dreamers can briefly shape parts of the Emerald Dream with thought and magic, but those changes do not last. The Dream’s primordial pattern returns and erases any lasting mortal mark.",al={"changing emerald dream","can you alter the dream"}},{q="Why do druids sleep for centuries?",a="Druids sleep for years or centuries to wander the Emerald Dream, commune with nature spirits, and learn from the Wild Gods. Their long slumber also lets them help the green dragonflight keep Azeroth’s natural cycles in balance across generations.",al={"why druids hibernate","druid slumber","barrow dens sleeping"}},{q="Where do animal spirits go when they die?",a="No one knows for certain where animal spirits go after death. Druids honor beasts as part of life’s natural cycle, but what follows remains a mystery.",al={"animal afterlife","wild god spirits","beast spirits"}},{q="Where did the Emerald Dream come from?",a="Its origins are shrouded in mystery. The Dream is said to have been shaped during the titans' ordering of Azeroth as a living blueprint of the natural world, and it was entrusted to Ysera and her green dragonflight to watch over.",al={"emerald dream origin","who made emerald dream","how was emerald dream created"},it="history",add="8b438d74"},{q="Why is it called the Emerald Dream?",a="It is named for its lush, pristine verdure and its spiritual nature. Charged to Ysera and the green dragonflight, this verdant realm mirrors an untouched, flourishing Azeroth that mortals often enter through dreams and spirit forms, though physical portals also exist.",al={"why emerald dream","emerald dream name meaning"},it="name",add="68609b47"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you draw on the Emerald Dream, where your order communes with the Wild Gods and studies the delicate balance of the Great Cycle.",["race:NightElf"]="For ten thousand years, your male druids slept in sacred barrows and walked the Emerald Dream alongside Ysera. The Sentinels and Priestesses guarded the waking world.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you walk the land of dreams to commune with the spirits of the earth. You see it as the untamed cradle of the Earth Mother's creation."},kw={"cenarius","dreaming","druid slumber","emerald dream","green dragonflight","wild gods","ysera"},rel={"topic:druid","topic:titan","topic:night-elf","quest:1490","quest:480","quest:1599","quest:6381"},src={"Emerald Dream"}}
E["topic:explorers-league"] = {t="topic",n="Explorers' League",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Explorers' League seeks the lost beginnings of the dwarves. King Magni Bronzebeard helped found it, and his brother Brann now leads its work from Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. The League searches far beyond dwarven lands, where its digs often stir conflict.",h="Across Azeroth, the Explorers' League seeks the lost beginnings of the dwarves.",sec={{t="A Shift in Dwarven Purpose",b="Dwarves in Khaz Modan once devoted their strength to mining, stonework, and engineering. Ancient ruins then pointed to a forgotten bond between dwarves and the mythical titans who created them.\n\nKing Magni Bronzebeard wanted to learn his people's origins, so he turned much of dwarven industry toward archaeology. With his brother Brann, Magni founded the Explorers' Guild, now called the Explorers' League. Its members seek relics, lost cities, and signs of their ancient ancestry.",sp=0},{t="The Hall and the Digs",b="The League directs its work from Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. High Explorer Muninn Magellas handles daily affairs while Brann Bronzebeard explores distant lands. Prospectors oversee broad digsites across Khaz Modan and beyond. At Ironband's Excavation in Loch Modan and Whelgar's Excavation in the Wetlands, they uncover vast fossil beds and ancient buildings. Displaced wildlife, troggs, and rival factions seeking buried relics often besiege the prospectors.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Clashes",b="Beyond dwarven lands, the League's expeditions have met fierce resistance. In Kalimdor, blasting at the Bael Modan dig in the southern Barrens drove out the native Stonespire tauren. The work stirred their anger and roused local earth spirits. In the Badlands, League prospectors openly clash with the Dark Iron clan over the vast titan vaults of Uldaman.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Explorers' League?",a="The Explorers' League searches for relics and studies the origins of the dwarven race. Based in Ironforge, its members work at digsites across the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",al={"explorers guild","dwarf explorers","who are the explorers league","league of explorers"},it="identity"},{q="Who leads the Explorers' League?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard helped found the League, and his youngest brother, Brann Bronzebeard, leads it. When Brann explores distant lands, High Explorer Muninn Magellas oversees its affairs in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.",al={"leader of explorers league","brann bronzebeard role","muninn magellas"},it="leader"},{q="Why did King Magni start the League?",a="King Magni turned much of dwarven industry toward archaeology after underground ruins suggested a mythical heritage tied to the titans. He wanted to discover the beginnings of his people.",al={"why do dwarves dig","dwarven origins","why archaeology"},it="history"},{q="Can non-dwarves join the League?",a="Yes. Though most members and leaders are dwarves, other Alliance races join the League. They include adventurous gnomes such as Clopper Wizbang and trusted field assistants across the continents.",al={"gnomes in explorers league","other races in league","who can join"},it="people"},{q="Why are the tauren fighting the Explorers' League?",a="Dwarven prospectors at Bael Modan used heavy explosives and displaced the native Stonespire tauren. The blasts devastated their settlement and angered local earth spirits by destroying sacred ground.",al={"bael modan tauren","dwarves vs tauren","stonespire feud"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Uldaman and why does the League care about it?",a="Uldaman is a vast underground titan facility beneath the Badlands. The League sees it as the crown jewel of its research and believes its sealed chambers hold proof of the dwarves' transformation and ancient creation.",al={"uldaman excavation","league badlands","titan ruins uldaman"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are Explorers' League camps found across the world?",a="King Magni turned dwarven industry toward archaeology after discovering ancient ruins tied to their heritage. Since then, the League has dispatched prospectors and excavators to anywhere ancient titan relics, mysterious ruins, or historical secrets might lie buried. You will find their dig sites scattered across Khaz Modan, deep in Kalimdor's wilderness like Darkshore and the Barrens, and throughout ancient subterranean complexes like Uldaman.",al={"why is explorers league everywhere","explorers league dig sites locations","why is the league in kalimdor"},it="why_here",add="f9af476b"},{q="Who is the Explorers' League allied with?",a="The League is an official arm of the dwarven kingdom of Ironforge, placing them firmly within the Grand Alliance. Dwarven and Alliance troops guard their digs, and prospectors across Azeroth's remote frontiers rely on that protection against troggs, rival factions, and hostile locals.",al={"explorers league alliance ties","who does the explorers league work for","explorers league si7"},it="allies",add="5a1072b2"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Each digsite and titan artifact brings dwarves closer to understanding their ancient creators and their departure from stone.",["race:Tauren"]="The League's careless use of dynamite in Kalimdor desecrated Stonespire ancestral lands. Its relentless digging often comes at the earth's expense.",["faction:Alliance"]="The League carries the Alliance banner into remote territories. Its prospectors often need protection from troggs, rival factions, and angry locals.",["profession:Mining"]="Dwarven prospectors draw on mining traditions to shore up tunnels, survey strata, and free delicate titan machinery from solid rock."},kw={"archaeology","brann bronzebeard","excavation","explorers guild","explorers' league","hall of explorers","magni bronzebeard","muninn magellas","prospector","uldaman"},rel={"subzone:hall-of-explorers","npc:brann-bronzebeard","npc:magni-bronzebeard","subzone:uldaman","subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","subzone:bael-modan","quest:2300"},src={"Explorers' League"}}
E["topic:first-war"] = {t="topic",n="First War",z="general",s="The First War drove Stormwind's survivors north after the kingdom fell. The five-year conflict began when the Orcish Horde crossed the Dark Portal and ended with King Llane Wrynn I dead and Stormwind in ruins.",h="The First War drove Stormwind's survivors north after the kingdom fell.",sec={{t="Opening of the Portal",b="For years after the Gnoll War, the Knights of Stormwind and the Clerics of Northshire Abbey guarded a peaceful kingdom. Then Guardian Medivh, secretly possessed by the demon lord Sargeras, contacted the orc warlock Gul'dan on Draenor. Together, they forged the Dark Portal in the Black Morass.\n\nDriven by demon blood and the slow death of their homeworld, the Orcish Horde crossed into Azeroth in force. Some dismissed the first reports as vengeful spirits or strange offshoots of trolls. Sir Anduin Lothar's scouting patrols soon confirmed a disciplined, bloodthirsty army had arrived.",sp=0},{t="The War for Stormwind",b="Warchief Blackhand led the Horde openly, while Gul'dan's Shadow Council guided it from the shadows. The Horde overran the kingdom's southern reaches. An attempt to push into Stranglethorn Vale against the Gurubashi trolls failed, yet the campaign across human lands brought ruin.\n\nThe Horde conquered until only Elwynn Forest remained under human control. Blackhand then launched a direct assault on Stormwind City. Sir Anduin Lothar repelled it with a surprise flanking attack by sea, saving the capital from destruction for a time.",sp=0},{t="Treachery and the Fall",b="Sir Anduin Lothar and the young mage Khadgar uncovered Medivh's betrayal. They invaded Karazhan and slew the Guardian. Medivh's death left Gul'dan in a coma, giving Orgrim Doomhammer the chance to challenge and kill Blackhand in a mak'gora duel. Doomhammer took absolute command, crushed the Shadow Council, and began a second siege of Stormwind.\n\nDuring the attack, the half-orc assassin Garona murdered King Llane Wrynn I inside his keep. The Horde sacked and burned Stormwind to ash. Lothar gathered the survivors and fled north across the Great Sea to Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How did the orcs get to Azeroth in the first place?",a="The orc warlock Gul'dan on Draenor and Guardian Medivh on Azeroth joined forces to open the Dark Portal in the Black Morass with dark fel magic.",al={"how did orcs get here","dark portal origin","first war start"},it="origin"},{q="Why didn't the other human kingdoms help Stormwind?",a="Stormwind stood alone because the distant northern kingdoms dismissed reports of green-skinned invaders as wild exaggerations or local disputes. The northern kings united only after Stormwind fell and Lothar reached Lordaeron with boats full of refugees.",al={"why no alliance","did lordaeron help","reinforcements for stormwind"},it="conflict"},{q="Who killed King Llane?",a="Garona Halforcen, an emissary trusted by King Llane Wrynn I, assassinated him inside his own keep during the final siege, dealing a severe blow to human morale.",al={"who murdered llane","king llane death","garona killed king"},it="history"},{q="Did the orcs fight anyone besides humans in the First War?",a="Yes. The Horde pushed south into Stranglethorn Vale early in the war, but the Gurubashi jungle trolls repelled them in a fierce clash.",al={"did orcs fight trolls","gurubashi in first war","other races first war"},it="history"},{q="Who won the First War?",a="The Orcish Horde won the First War. Stormwind was razed, King Llane was slain, and the surviving humans fled by sea to Lordaeron.",al={"first war victor","who won wc1","outcome of first war"},it="history"},{q="What happened to Warchief Blackhand?",a="After Medivh's death left Gul'dan incapacitated, Orgrim Doomhammer challenged Blackhand to mak'gora, slew him, and took command of the Horde.",al={"how did blackhand die","orgrim doomhammer challenge","warchief killed"},it="leader"},{q="What was the First War?",a="The First War, also known as the first Great War, was the devastating five-year conflict fought between the Orcish Horde and the human Kingdom of Stormwind. Orchestrated in secret by the warlock Gul'dan and the corrupted Guardian Medivh, the orcs crossed from their dying homeworld of Draenor through the Dark Portal into the Black Morass. What began as scattered frontier clashes escalated into an all-out invasion that destroyed the kingdom's towns, culminated in the assassination of King Llane Wrynn, and ended with the total sack of Stormwind City.",al={"what is first war","first war summary","the first great war"},it="identity",add="a8364e3f"},{q="Why is it called the First War?",a="It is named the First War because it marked the very first clash between humanity and the Orcish Horde on Azeroth. Before the Dark Portal opened, humans had never seen orcs and had enjoyed generations of relative peace following the Gnoll War. The conflict shattered that isolation, and because a second grand confrontation soon followed when the Horde invaded the northern human nations, historians and survivors refer to this initial struggle for Stormwind as the First War.",al={"why first war","first war name meaning","why is it called the first war"},it="name",add="bf3015cc"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans, the First War brought Stormwind to its darkest hour. The kingdom fell, its king was murdered, and its survivors fled across the sea as penniless refugees.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, the First War began their bloody conquest of Azeroth, tainted by Mannoroth's blood-curse and Gul'dan's Shadow Council working in secret.",["class:Paladin"]="The slaughter of the Clerics of Northshire Abbey showed that holy faith alone could not withstand brutal melee combat. It inspired the founding of the Knights of the Silver Hand.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's destruction warned the northern nations to abandon their isolation and unite as the Alliance of Lordaeron.",["class:Warlock"]="Gul'dan and his Shadow Council guided the Horde's conquests with fel sorceries, showing the devastation demonic pacts can unleash upon the world."},kw={"anduin lothar","black morass","blackhand","dark portal","first war","gul'dan","llane wrynn","medivh","northshire abbey","orgrim doomhammer"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:llane-wrynn-i","topic:medivh","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:dark-portal","topic:second-war","subzone:northshire-abbey"},src={"First War"}}
E["topic:forsaken"] = {t="topic",n="Forsaken",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, intelligent undead called the Forsaken live beneath Lordaeron's ruined capital in the Undercity. They broke from the Scourge after the Third War under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Though mistrusted, they hold a wary alliance with the Horde.",h="Across Azeroth, intelligent undead called the Forsaken live beneath Lordaeron's ruined capital in the...",sec={{t="Broken Shackles",b="After the Third War, the Lich King's hold weakened. Thousands of undead in Lordaeron's blighted ruins regained their minds and memories, and recalled the slaughter they had been forced to commit. The living hunted them, though they had once been citizens of Lordaeron.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner, Quel'Thalas's fallen ranger-general, had become an unholy banshee. She gathered the wandering undead and claimed the catacombs beneath Capital City. There she named their new nation the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="An Alliance of Convenience",b="Enemies surrounded the Forsaken, above all the Scarlet Crusade and the Scourge. Lady Sylvanas sent emissaries in search of allies. Across the Great Sea, tauren elders urged compassion, believing the cursed people might find redemption or a cure through the earth.\n\nWarchief Thrall had misgivings, but the Horde accepted the Forsaken. In return, the Horde gained a vital foothold in the north of the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="Dark Laboratories",b="The Forsaken seek their own survival while presenting a cooperative face to their allies in Kalimdor. Beneath the Undercity, the Royal Apothecary Society works in the Apothecarium to create a New Plague potent enough to destroy both the Scourge and living threats.\n\nForsaken champions such as Nathanos Blightcaller wage bitter wars across the Plaguelands, Hillsbrad Foothills, and the Scarlet Monastery. They fight to secure their sovereign borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Are the Forsaken part of the Scourge?",a="No. The Forsaken broke free from the Lich King's mental domination after the Third War. They loathe the Scourge, regard Arthas as their absolute mortal enemy, and bitterly fight his minions throughout the Plaguelands.",al={"scourge difference","are forsaken scourge","are undead evil"}},{q="Where is the Forsaken capital?",a="The Forsaken capital is the Undercity, a vast sprawl beneath the ruins of Capital City in Tirisfal Glades. Sylvanas's forces expanded the royal crypts and sewers into a fortified sanctuary safe from the light and outdoor threats.",al={"undead capital","forsaken city","where do undead live"}},{q="Why did the Horde let the Forsaken join?",a="The tauren urged the Horde to accept the Forsaken, seeing a chance for redemption and hoping the earth's powers might cure their affliction. Magatha Grimtotem also supported the pact. Warchief Thrall agreed because the Horde urgently needed a military foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why are undead horde","how did forsaken join horde","thrall forsaken alliance"}},{q="Who rules the Forsaken?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen, rules the Forsaken. Once a high elven ranger-general, she fell defending Silvermoon and freed the undead who had regained their own will. She rules from the Undercity with her dreadlord advisor, Varimathras.",al={"undead leader","forsaken queen","who leads forsaken"}},{q="Are the Forsaken all former humans?",a="Most Forsaken were once humans of Lordaeron, slain and raised during the Scourge invasion. Their leaders include former elves such as Sylvanas. Anyone who bends the knee to the Dark Lady is welcomed into their ranks.",al={"undead races","are forsaken only humans","what race are forsaken"}},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade hate the Forsaken so much?",a="The Scarlet Crusade makes no distinction between mindful Forsaken and mindless Scourge. Its zealots see all undead as abominations to be purged with fire and holy wrath, whatever their will or allegiance.",al={"scarlet crusade undead","crusade vs forsaken","why scarlet crusade attacks"}},{q="Which classes can the Forsaken be?",a="The Forsaken train as warriors, paladins, rogues, priests, mages, and warlocks. Their paladins still wield the Holy Light, though it burns their dead flesh.",al={"undead classes","forsaken classes","what classes can undead be","can undead be paladins","undead paladin"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you walk the earth in rotting flesh, cursed and spurned by former kin. Your people are bound together under the Dark Lady as they carve out an empire of their own.",["race:Tauren"]="Your elders championed the Forsaken's place in the Horde out of sympathy. They hoped your shamanic and druidic rites might soothe or heal the Forsaken's tragic condition.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, the Forsaken are nightmarish parodies of fallen friends and family from Lordaeron. They hold former imperial lands and answer overtures with poison and steel.",["faction:Horde"]="Thrall forged an alliance of convenience with the Undercity to secure territory in the East. Many orcs and trolls view the Forsaken's grim apothecary experiments and necromantic culture with deep suspicion."},kw={"apothecary","forsaken","lordaeron","plaguelands","sylvanas","tirisfal","undead","undercity"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:undercity","topic:scourge","topic:horde","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:1489","npc:varimathras","npc:nathanos-blightcaller"},src={"Forsaken"}}
E["topic:furbolg"] = {t="topic",n="Furbolg",z="general",s="Across northern Kalimdor, Furbolg tribes turn on their old allies as madness takes hold. For millennia, they lived in harmony with nature and the night elves. Now demonic corruption and lingering fel magic leave only a few tribes sane.",h="Across northern Kalimdor, Furbolg tribes turn on their old allies as madness takes hold.",sec={{t="Ancient Kinship",b="Furbolg packs once fought beside night elves and tauren against the Burning Legion. During the War of the Ancients, ten thousand years ago, chieftain Unng Ak united the tribes. They had long revered the wild god Ursoc. After the Great Sundering, they withdrew into the northern woodlands. There, they kept peaceful ties with night elf druids and forest wardens, living simply among the wild.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Madness",b="The Third War shattered the furbolgs’ quiet life. As the Burning Legion crossed Kalimdor, fel taint spread through the soil and canopy of Ashenvale and Felwood. Deeply attuned to the land, the bear-men took the corruption into themselves, and madness seized their tribes.\n\nWizened shamans were overthrown or silenced by bloodthirsty firebrands. These new leaders channeled fel moss, dark talismans, and corrupt alchemy. Peaceful gatherers became raiders who attack travelers and night elf settlements on sight.",sp=0},{t="The Unbroken Line",b="Across northern Kalimdor, nearly every major tribe has fallen. The Gnarlpine dwell across Teldrassil, the Blackwood in Darkshore, and the Thistlefur and Foulweald in Ashenvale. The Deadwood and Winterfall live in the northern highlands. Yet a few still hold to their old ways.\n\nDeep in fortified tunnels linking Felwood, Winterspring, and Moonglade, the Timbermaw guard their sanity. Wary and isolated, they defend their hold against their crazed northern kin. They fight to preserve what remains of their uncorrupted culture.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the furbolgs attacking everyone?",a="Since the Third War, lingering demonic corruption has spread through Kalimdor’s northern forests. Furbolgs are deeply attuned to nature, and the taint seeped into their minds. It drove their tribes into a paranoid, violent frenzy and displaced peaceful elders with aggressive chieftains.",al={"why are furbolgs hostile","furbolg madness","why furbolgs went crazy"},it="hostile"},{q="Were furbolgs always enemies of the night elves?",a="No. For thousands of years, furbolgs and night elves were peaceful neighbors and close allies. They fought together against the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. Night elf druids kept gentle ties with tribal settlements until the recent madness took hold.",al={"furbolg night elf history","did furbolgs like night elves"},it="ties"},{q="Are there any furbolgs who are still friendly?",a="Yes. The Timbermaw keep an uncorrupted enclave in Timbermaw Hold, the crossroads tunnel system between Felwood, Moonglade, and Winterspring. Deeply suspicious of outsiders, they tolerate travelers who prove their enmity toward the tainted Deadwood and Winterfall tribes.",al={"friendly furbolgs","good furbolg tribe","uncorrupted furbolgs"},it="residents"},{q="What is wrong with the furbolgs on Teldrassil?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe on Teldrassil has fallen to fel moss, a corruption spreading through the world tree’s boughs. Under Chieftain Ursal the Mauler, the Gnarlpine abandoned their traditional villages and overran sacred places such as the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and Starbreeze Village.",al={"teldrassil furbolgs","gnarlpine corruption"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is behind the corruption of the Winterfall in Winterspring?",a="A satyr named Xandivious secretly manipulates the Winterfall from within their chieftain’s den. Their frenzy is sustained by Winterfall Firewater, brewed from tainted materials inside Felwood’s Deadwood Cauldron and carried north through the mountain passes.",al={"winterfall tribe lore","who corrupted winterfall","winterfall firewater origin"},sp=1},{q="Can corrupted furbolgs ever be cured?",a="Night elf sentinels and druids have tried to cleanse individual tribes with moonwell waters and sacred relics. Broad recovery has proven nearly impossible. Satyrs and dark relics deepen the corruption, leaving defenders often with no choice but to cull hostile packs to protect settlements.",al={"cure furbolgs","can furbolgs be saved"},it="threat"},{q="What are furbolgs?",a="Furbolgs are a race of hulking, bear-like humanoids native to the ancient forests of northern Kalimdor. Traditionally simple-minded, deeply spiritual, and reclusive, they lived peacefully alongside nature for millennia. Though powerful in stature and capable of fierce combat, they possessed no natural appetite for war or cruelty until recent tragedies twisted their minds.",al={"what is a furbolg","who are furbolgs","furbolg race"},it="identity",add="ec2e8979"},{q="Where did the furbolgs come from?",a="Furbolgs are an ancient people of Kalimdor. During the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago, furbolg packs led by Unng Ak stood shoulder to shoulder with night elves, tauren, and earthen against the Burning Legion, cementing an alliance that lasted peacefully for generations.",al={"furbolg origin","history of furbolgs","where do furbolgs come from"},it="history",add="195c4c39"},{q="Who leads the furbolgs?",a="Furbolgs do not have a single overarching leader or ruler. Instead, they are divided into independent tribes, each led by its own chieftains, shamans, and elders. In recent times, many of these tribes' wise elders have been overthrown, slain, or replaced by aggressive firebrands and corrupt chieftains who lead their crazed kin into violence.",al={"furbolg leader","who rules the furbolgs","furbolg king"},it="leader",add="11e5052c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the furbolgs’ fall is a bitter tragedy. Tribes trusted as woodland allies for ten thousand years have become feral predators threatening Astranaar and Teldrassil’s sacred barrows.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mourn the bear-men as kindred spirits of Ursoc. Fel taint has turned their bond with nature into a weapon, and their unrest reflects the land’s wider sickness.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde sees Ashenvale’s hostile tribes as barriers to its advance. It clears aggressive packs such as the Foulweald and Thistlefur to secure supply routes and outposts along the forest fringe."},kw={"ashenvale","corruption","deadwood","foulweald","furbolg","gnarlpine","thistlefur","timbermaw","ursoc","winterfall"},rel={"subzone:timbermaw-hold","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood","zone:winterspring","topic:night-elf","topic:war-of-the-ancients","quest:486","quest:991"},src={"Furbolg"}}
E["topic:gnoll"] = {t="topic",n="Gnoll",z="general",s="Across the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor, gnoll packs prey on settlements and travelers. Hyena-like scavengers, they are known for vicious infighting, brutal strength, and animal cunning. Their warlords lead raids, butcher wildlife, and threaten frontier hamlets and trade roads.",h="Across the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor, gnoll packs prey on settlements and travelers.",sec={{t="Hyenas of the Wilds",b="Gnolls roam the wilds on two legs or all fours. Slightly shorter than an average human, these hyena-kin have thick pelts, spiky teeth, and a barking laugh. They lope swiftly through brush and track prey by scent.\n\nAmong gnolls, raw strength rules. Fractious packs follow the strongest and cruelest alpha. They yield only when a superior force batters them into submission.",sp=0},{t="The Gnoll War",b="United gnolls once brought open war to the kingdom of Stormwind. Stormwind's armies defeated them, and the kingdom knew lasting peace until the orcs came through the Dark Portal.",sp=0},{t="Raiders of the Southern Kingdoms",b="With Stormwind's full military might absent from the south, gnoll packs run rampant. In Elwynn Forest and Westfall, the Riverpaw pack follows the notorious Hogger. They raid homesteads and force subjugated kobolds to dig for gold. The pack secretly colludes with the Defias Brotherhood.\n\nFarther east, the Redridge pack snatches horses outside Lakeshire and sabotages bridge repairs. In Galardell Valley, the Shadowhide clan serves the dark will of the rogue wizard Morganth.",sp=1},{t="Pestilence and Territory",b="Gnolls threaten lands beyond the human south. In northern Lordaeron, the Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw raises undead Rot Hide gnolls to dig up corpses across Tirisfal and Silverpine. Near Hillsbrad, the Mudsnout harvest foul, toxic blossoms among ruined farmsteads.\n\nAcross the Great Sea in Kalimdor, the Palemane pack butchers game across Mulgore despite tauren efforts to make peace. In Feralas, the Woodpaw wage a desperate, frenzied war against encroaching silithid swarms.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What exactly is a gnoll?",a="Gnolls are hyena-like humanoid carnivores, feared for their violence, endurance, and low cunning. They roam in nomadic or semi-permanent camps, living mostly on plunder, hunting, and carrion.",al={"what are gnolls","gnoll race","are gnolls hyenas"},it="identity"},{q="Why don't gnolls form a proper kingdom?",a="Gnolls follow fierce, immediate hierarchies. Without an exceptional, tyrannical warlord to beat them into line, packs splinter into bloody territorial feuds. Long-term organization and civil progress cannot take hold.",al={"why are gnolls scattered","gnoll empire","gnoll unity"},it="conflict"},{q="What was the Gnoll War?",a="Long before the First War, united gnoll packs waged war on the kingdom of Stormwind. Stormwind's armies prevailed, and the kingdom knew lasting peace until the orcs came through the Dark Portal.",al={"stormwind gnoll war"},it="history"},{q="Why are gnolls working with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Riverpaw pack in Westfall and Elwynn colludes with the Defias Brotherhood for arms, coordination, and shared spoils. The bandits use the gnolls as brute muscle to overrun farmlands and distract Stormwind's dwindling garrisons.",al={"defias gnoll alliance","riverpaw defias","hogger defias"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Are the Rot Hide gnolls alive?",a="No. The Rot Hide gnolls in Tirisfal Glades and Silverpine Forest are undead thralls. They answer to Thule Ravenclaw, an exiled human necromancer who uses Fenris Isle as a redoubt to gather corpses for the Scourge.",al={"rot hide undead","silverpine gnolls","fenris isle gnolls"},sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Why do tauren fight the Palemane gnolls?",a="When the tauren settled Mulgore, they tried to coexist and communicate with the indigenous Palemane pack. The gnolls rebuffed every peaceful gesture, slaughtered plains wildlife without restraint, and threatened tauren villages.",al={"palemane mulgore","tauren and gnolls","why kill palemane"},it="motive"},{q="Why are gnolls hostile to travelers?",a="Gnolls are brutish, predatory scavengers who view other races primarily as prey, trespassers, or sources of plunder. Belligerent and driven by basic animal cunning, they value physical strength above all else and respect little else. Because they rely heavily on raiding, kidnapping, and stealing livestock from nearby settlements, gnoll packs reflexively attack anyone who wanders into their territory or crosses their hunting grounds.",al={"why do gnolls attack","are gnolls hostile","gnolls attack on sight"},it="hostile",add="06f85769"},{q="Who leads the gnolls?",a="Gnolls have no unified leader or central king. Instead, they are splintered into scattered, squabbling packs and tribes across both continents. In each clan, leadership falls to the alpha or packlord—the largest, most brutal brute capable of beating rivals into submission. Notable warlords include Hogger of the Riverpaw in Elwynn Forest, Packlord Yowler in Redridge, and Lieutenant Fangore among the Shadowhide.",al={"who is gnoll leader","gnoll king","gnoll pack leader"},it="leader",add="15503234"},{q="Where did gnolls come from?",a="Gnolls are an ancient race of hyena-like humanoids whose origins are lost to history. They have inhabited both Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms for millennia, long before the rise of modern nations. Early human settlers encountered vicious gnoll packs in Tirisfal Glades thousands of years ago, and troll tribes fought them in southern forests. Wherever wild lands exist, gnolls have carved out a savage existence.",al={"gnoll origin","where do gnolls come from","history of gnolls"},it="origin",add="1c9639a8"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, gnolls are an ancient enemy who once burned the kingdom's heartlands. Today, packs like the Riverpaw and Shadowhide threaten the kingdom's vulnerable frontier roads.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Palemane tribe treats Mulgore with careless cruelty. Young tauren braves must drive them back to preserve the balance of the plains.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance marshals across Elwynn, Westfall, Redridge, and the Wetlands rely heavily on freelance champions to thin the encroaching gnoll populations.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken see gnolls as either an annoyance or a resource. In Hillsbrad, the Mudsnout cultivate restorative fungi, while Sylvanas previously enslaved northern packs through banshee possession."},kw={"gnoll","hogger","mosshide","mudsnout","palemane","riverpaw","rot hide","shadowhide","woodpaw"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:elwynn","zone:redridge","zone:westfall","zone:silverpine","zone:mulgore","quest:124"},src={"Gnoll"}}
E["topic:gnome"] = {t="topic",n="Gnome",z="general",s="Gnomes in Ironforge fight to reclaim Gnomeregan, their poisoned home. Across Azeroth, they are renowned for engineering and arcane mastery, and remain staunch allies even in exile.",h="Gnomes in Ironforge fight to reclaim Gnomeregan, their poisoned home.",sec={{t="Ingenuity and Optimism",b="Gnomes are small in stature and vast in intellect. Curiosity drives them to study machines and magic, and to invent what no one has built before. Clockwork devices, flying machines, and subterranean trains are among their works. Hardship has not dimmed their cheer; they still mean to rebuild and solve what seems impossible.",sp=0},{t="Forged in the Mountains",b="The gnomes made their home in the frozen crags of Dun Morogh. There, they found kinship with the dwarves of Ironforge. Together, dwarven strength and gnomish ingenuity carved Gnomeregan, a remarkable city beneath western Dun Morogh. Visionary leaders called High Tinkers lead the gnomes.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Gnomeregan",b="During the Third War, gnomes sent armaments to Lordaeron but held back their troops, leaving their allies confused. Savage troggs, stirred by excavations near Uldaman, had surged into Gnomeregan's lower sectors.\n\nHoping to drive them out without burdening an embattled Alliance, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque followed his chief advisor's counsel and vented radioactive waste into the lower city. The plan failed. The troggs survived, mutated and frenzied, while nearly eighty percent of the gnomish people perished.",sp=1},{t="Exile in Tinker Town",b="The surviving gnomes fled their poisoned home and found sanctuary with their dwarven cousins in Ironforge. High Tinker Mekkatorque and his people made their home in Ironforge's Tinker Town. There, they continue to support the Alliance and oversee the Deeprun Tram to Stormwind.\n\nFrom this adopted quarter, gnomish commandos and volunteers make repeated expeditions into Gnomeregan's irradiated depths. They seek to clear the troggs and mechanical abominations from their grand city and reclaim it someday.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are gnomes living in Ironforge instead of their own city?",a="Gnomes live in Ironforge as refugees because subterranean troggs overran their ancestral home, Gnomeregan. A desperate plan to irradiate the troggs failed, filling the city with lethal fallout and killing most of its inhabitants. King Magni Bronzebeard offered the survivors shelter in the dwarven capital.",al={"why in ironforge","where do gnomes live","gnome refugee city"}},{q="Who leads the gnomes?",a="High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque leads the gnomes. They choose leaders for merit, engineering skill, and visionary thinking rather than a hereditary royal line. Mekkatorque ordered Gnomeregan irradiated to stop the troggs, and now directs the effort to reclaim their home.",al={"gnome leader","gnome king","who rules gnomes","high tinker"}},{q="Why didn't the gnomes help fight the Scourge in Lordaeron?",a="The gnomes sent siege weapons and technology to the Alliance of Lordaeron, but Gnomeregan was fighting for survival against troggs, so they could not spare soldiers. They did not ask their allies for help, believing the Alliance had enough to face the undead Scourge.",al={"gnomes in third war","why gnomes skipped third war","gnomes third war help"}},{q="What is the Deeprun Tram?",a="The Deeprun Tram is a subterranean railway designed by High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and built by gnomish engineers. It links Tinker Town in Ironforge directly to the dwarven district of Stormwind City, letting troops, supplies, and travelers move rapidly between the allied capitals.",al={"who built the tram","stormwind ironforge train","deeprun tram origin"}},{q="What is the rivalry between gnomes and goblins?",a="Gnomes and goblins have an intense cultural and technological rivalry that flared during the Second War. Gnomish engineering favors precision, stability, and intricate, safe mechanisms. Goblin engineering favors raw explosive power, cheap production, and swift results despite volatility. Both peoples try to out-invent and mock one another.",al={"gnomes vs goblins","gnome goblin engineering","why do gnomes hate goblins"}},{q="Which classes can gnomes be?",a="Gnomes train as warriors, rogues, priests, mages, and warlocks.",al={"gnome classes","what classes can gnomes be","can gnomes be priests"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you carry the loss of Gnomeregan with quiet resolve. From exile in Tinker Town, your brilliance, optimism, and explosive firepower help you fight for your stolen home.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you have shared the mountains with the gnomes for generations; they are your oldest and dearest neighbors. Giving their survivors a home in Tinker Town was an easy choice for your people, bound to them by generations of brotherhood.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know gnomish engineering across the world for its sophisticated contraptions, ray devices, and mind-boggling precision. Its meticulous designs differ from volatile goblin detonations.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you share your people's gift for the arcane. Gnomes are exceptionally gifted arcanists despite their small stature.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on gnomes for strategic mobility and siege technology. They faithfully supply machines and maintain the Deeprun Tram, even while displaced from their home."},kw={"deeprun tram","gnomanity","gnome","gnomeregan","gnomes","high tinker","mekkatorque","tinker town","trogg"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","subzone:deeprun-tram","topic:trogg","topic:goblin","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Gnome"}}
E["topic:goblin"] = {t="topic",n="Goblin",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, goblins bargain, build, and trade for profit. Their cartels began on the Isle of Kezan, and their craft and hunger for gain now reach far beyond it. Most keep neutral so they can trade with both Alliance and Horde, while the Venture Company and Steamwheedle Cartel leave their mark across the world.",h="Across Azeroth, goblins bargain, build, and trade for profit.",sec={{t="Cartels of Kezan",b="Goblins come from the Isle of Kezan in the South Seas. Long ago, rival economic cartels divided their society. Their leaders sought profit through hard bargaining, volatile engineering, and industry. They built neither kingdoms nor armies, and their ventures now reach across the world.",sp=0},{t="Mercenaries and Mercantilism",b="During the Second War, Trade Prince Steamwheedle joined his cartel to Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde. Goblins supplied maps, siege craft, and knowledge of fleet-building in return for plunder taken from Stormwind. After the Horde fell, the cartels learned that open allegiance cost them profitable markets.\n\nToday, the major cartels claim neutrality and keep trade havens such as Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale and Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert. Alliance and Horde travelers meet there without drawn blades, while port bruisers keep the peace.",sp=0},{t="Hired Hands and Industry",b="For many goblins, gold comes before every other loyalty. Some serve beyond the neutral cartels as hired specialists or ruthless industrial barons. The Venture Company cuts forests and strips resources across continents, heedless of local people.\n\nIn the Deadmines, goblin engineers Sneed, Gilnid, and Captain Greenskin serve criminal enterprises. They oversee smelters and shipwrights building a massive ironclad juggernaut for the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="Are goblins aligned with the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither. The major trade cartels, including the Steamwheedle Cartel, claim neutrality so they can trade with both sides. Individual goblins and private firms sell their services to the Horde, Alliance, or groups such as the Defias Brotherhood for the right price.",al={"are goblins horde","goblin faction","who do goblins fight for"},it="side"},{q="Why are goblin inventions so prone to exploding?",a="Goblin engineers favor raw power, speed, cheap production, and strong explosive force over structural safety. Their devices can bring spectacular results and blasts in equal measure.",al={"goblin engineering dangerous","why do goblin machines blow up","goblin vs gnome tech"}},{q="What is the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel is the mainland's most influential trading cartel. It runs important neutral ports and routes between continents, including Booty Bay in southern Stranglethorn and Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert.",al={"steamwheedle cartel","who rules booty bay","goblin ports"}},{q="What is the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is a ruthless goblin-run industrial power known for cutting forests, strip-mining, and extracting oil. It pays little heed to local law or the land's balance, and often clashes violently with native peoples.",al={"venture co","who are venture company","what is venture co"}},{q="Why are there goblins working with the Defias in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood had plenty of plundered coin and raw ore from the Moonbrook mines, so it could hire skilled goblin specialists. Sneed, Gilnid, and Captain Greenskin took contracts to oversee heavy smelting and build Edwin VanCleef's ironclad juggernaut.",al={"deadmines goblins","why are goblins in deadmines","gilnid sneed deadmines"},sp=1,it="why_here",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="Where is the goblin homeland?",a="Goblins come from the Isle of Kezan in the South Seas. Their great trading cartels first rose there, building an empire of commerce and industrial smog.",al={"where do goblins come from","goblin home island","kezan"},it="origin"},{q="What are goblins?",a="Goblins are small, green-skinned humanoids renowned across Azeroth for their shrewd mercantile cunning, mastery of volatile technology, and love of explosives. Driven by an insatiable appetite for profit, they view almost every endeavor through the lens of trade, mining, and industry. While physically small, their ingenuity and willingness to weaponize raw engineering make them both formidable and unpredictable.",al={"what is a goblin","who are goblins","goblin race"},it="identity",add="d8aa07c2"},{q="Who leads the goblins?",a="Goblins have no single ruler. Instead, their society is divided into competing commercial cartels and syndicates, each commanded by a wealthy Trade Prince or executive mogul. Prominent figures like Trade Prince Steamwheedle lead massive trading syndicates, while local barons and overseers—such as Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay—direct operations and enforce order across individual ports and settlements.",al={"goblin leader","who is in charge of goblins","goblin ruler"},it="leader",add="d5109913"},{q="Why are some goblins hostile to travelers?",a="While major ports like Booty Bay and Gadgetzan maintain strict armed neutrality to protect trade, many goblins belong to cutthroat organizations that view travelers as obstacles or competition. Entities like the Venture Company aggressively defend their illicit logging and mining claims with brute force, while other goblins readily hire themselves out as mercenaries, technicians, or pirates to criminal factions.",al={"hostile goblins","why do goblins attack","are goblins enemies"},it="hostile",add="68045a57"},{q="Where did the goblins come from, and what is their history?",a="Goblins hail from the Isle of Kezan in the South Seas, where their society divided into rival trading cartels. Rather than building kingdoms or armies of their own, the cartels turned their energy toward economic warfare, trade, and worldwide technological enterprise.",al={"goblin history","origin of goblins","where did goblins come from"},it="history",add="a6996125"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can favor explosive force, offensive gadgets, and risky mechanical devices. Gnomes favor precise, defensive designs.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you help fuel goblin industry and trade. Goblin cartels fiercely guard valuable mineral claims across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you may distrust goblin neutrality. The cartels once served the Old Horde as mercenaries, supplying warships and sappers during the Second War.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of Thrall's Horde, you can use goblin mechanics and trade through neutral hubs. The mercenary contracts between Orgrim Doomhammer and Trade Prince Steamwheedle remain fresh in memory."},kw={"booty bay","cartel","deadmines","engineering","gadgetzan","goblin","kezan","steamwheedle","venture company"},rel={"topic:steamwheedle-cartel","topic:venture-company","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:gadgetzan","npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:captain-greenskin","topic:second-war","zone:deadmines"},src={"Goblin"}}
E["topic:grimtotem-tribe"] = {t="topic",n="Grimtotem tribe",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, the Grimtotem tribe raids settlements and keeps apart from Thrall's Horde. Dark hides and fierce warpaint mark them, and they seek to drive foreign races from Kalimdor and reclaim ancestral lands by any means. Their matriarch, Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem, resides atop Thunder Bluff while her kin raid across the continent.",h="Across Kalimdor, the Grimtotem tribe raids settlements and keeps apart from Thrall's Horde.",sec={{t="A Tribe Apart",b="Grimtotem warriors train for ruthless combat rather than the patient harmony of the Great Hunt. They believe Kalimdor belongs only to the tauren. Their peaceful cousins honor the Earth Mother with reverence, but the Grimtotem disdain the other races settled on their ancient lands.\n\nCairne Bloodhoof welcomed them into Thunder Bluff, hoping to unite all tauren. Yet the Grimtotem remain the only major tribe never to formally join Thrall's Horde. They keep apart and pursue a violent cause.",sp=0},{t="Wildland Aggressors",b="Beyond Thunder Bluff's watch, Grimtotem hostility turns to violence. In Stonetalon Mountains, they butcher local settlements and threaten Horde supply outposts. Across the mesas of Thousand Needles, they gather around Darkcloud Pinnacle, menace Freewind Post, and plot to seize the canyon.\n\nFeralas is no safer. They attack Horde travelers, Alliance caravans, and fellow tauren without hesitation. Horde garrisons at Sun Rock Retreat and Camp Mojache regularly post bounties and send warriors to cut down these violent outcasts.",sp=0},{t="Shadows and Apothecaries",b="Magatha Grimtotem's spiritual counsel conceals a web of intrigue. The Elder Crone ardently supports the tauren's controversial ties with the Forsaken. In public, she says she wants to heal the undead. In secret, she seeks toxic plagues and Highborne artifacts. In Thousand Needles, scouts from Freewind Post intercept guarded letters between cloaked couriers and Grimtotem chieftains in Darkcloud Pinnacle.",sp=1,bt={"q4542.4"}}},faq={{q="Why are the Grimtotem hostile if their leader lives in Thunder Bluff?",a="The Grimtotem never formally joined the Horde. Cairne Bloodhoof tolerates Magatha Grimtotem on Thunder Bluff's high mesas, hoping to keep peace among the tauren. Yet the tribe's roaming warriors reject outside diplomacy. In Stonetalon, Thousand Needles, and Feralas, they attack anyone who trespasses on ancestral territory, including other tauren.",al={"why grimtotem red","why do grimtotem attack horde","are grimtotem friendly"},it="hostile"},{q="How can you tell a Grimtotem apart from other tauren?",a="Grimtotem tauren almost always have pitch-black fur. They paint sharp patterns in stark white, deep red, or blue across their bodies and faces.",al={"grimtotem appearance","grimtotem fur color"}},{q="Who leads the Grimtotem?",a="Magatha Grimtotem, the Elder Crone, rules the tribe as a powerful shaman on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She took power after marrying the previous chieftain. He died shortly afterward in an unexplained climbing mishap.",al={"grimtotem leader","elder crone"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Grimtotem goal?",a="The Grimtotem seek to purge Kalimdor of foreign races they consider lesser, including orcs, humans, and night elves. They also seek to reclaim all ancestral tauren lands. Unlike Cairne's people, they believe these lands should be taken through force, deception, and elemental dominion.",al={"what do grimtotem want","grimtotem motive"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Magatha Grimtotem work with the Forsaken?",a="Magatha publicly says she champions the Forsaken because tauren shamanism and earth wisdom may cure their affliction and restore their humanity.",al={"magatha and undead","grimtotem forsaken"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="What is the Grimtotem tribe?",a="The Grimtotem are one of the most powerful and aggressive tauren tribes in Kalimdor. Unlike the generally peaceful and spiritual clans united under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, the Grimtotem are militaristic extremists. From childhood, their warriors are trained in ruthless combat, eschewing traditional honorable hunting rites in favor of learning to kill swiftly with any weapon at hand.",al={"who are the grimtotem","grimtotem clan","what is grimtotem"},it="identity",add="855936f4"},{q="Why are the Grimtotem found throughout Kalimdor?",a="You will encounter Grimtotem outposts and warbands across the Stonetalon Mountains, Thousand Needles, and Feralas. They have established fortified positions in these regions to assert dominance over ancestral lands, actively raiding rival settlements and encroaching on both Horde and Alliance territories.",al={"where are grimtotem found","why are grimtotem in stonetalon","grimtotem locations"},it="why_here",add="04251e4b"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem bring open shame to the Bloodhoof and other tribes. Cairne gives them shelter in Thunder Bluff for tauren unity, but their warmongering threatens to tear that unity apart.",["faction:Horde"]="Their black hides do not make the Grimtotem allies. Across Kalimdor's barrens, mountains, and marshes, their warriors ambush Horde scouts on sight.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Grimtotem despise all who cross into Kalimdor. They attack Alliance traders and night elf enclaves without distinction.",["race:Undead"]="Magatha Grimtotem is one of the few tauren leaders in Thunder Bluff who openly courts the Forsaken. She arranges research into exotic plagues with Royal Apothecary Society specialists."},kw={"darkcloud pinnacle","elder crone","freewind post","grimtotem","magatha","tauren tribe","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","zone:thousandneedles","zone:stonetalon","quest:5064","quest:6548"},src={"Grimtotem tribe"}}
E["topic:harpy"] = {t="topic",n="Harpy",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor and Alterac's high passes, Harpies foul their roosts and hunt travelers. Their shrieks and storm magic are feared, while night elf tales link them to Azshara's cursed betrayers. Their true origins remain uncertain.",h="Across Kalimdor and Alterac's high passes, Harpies foul their roosts and hunt travelers.",sec={{t="Winged Scourge of Kalimdor",b="Harpies spread from the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains across Kalimdor. Their heads and upper bodies resemble night elf women, with broad feathered wings and wicked talons. Age makes their elven faces more striking, but their nature is savage. They terrorize Durotar's arid canyons, Teldrassil's sacred boughs, and the heights of Mulgore. Around their roosts, they despoil plant and animal life, leaving the picked-clean bones of their prey.",sp=0},{t="Avian Lineage and Dark Nature",b="Night elf tales say harpies began as handmaidens who betrayed Queen Azshara and were cursed before the Great Sundering. Their true origins remain uncertain. Today, ruthless matriarchies rule the harpies. Those who seek command betray, slaughter, and torment their rivals to hold it.",sp=0},{t="Tempest Magic and Wicked Habits",b="Harpies tear flesh with razor-sharp claws and wield dangerous wind and lightning magic. From above, their shrieking gales batter their foes. Cunning hunters, they can speak and sometimes trade scavenged oddities with subterranean creatures such as kobolds for bright gems and shiny trinkets. Their elven forms can beguile unwary explorers, but their kiss is venomous and swiftly brings a violent, wasting fever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do harpies originally come from?",a="Harpies first roosted among the jagged peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains in central Kalimdor. From there, they spread to Teldrassil, the Barrens, Durotar, Mulgore, Feralas, and the Thousand Needles. They also crossed the Great Sea to Alterac Valley's snowy crags.",al={"harpy origins","harpy homeland","where do harpies live"},it="origin"},{q="Are harpies actually related to night elves?",a="Kalimdor folklore says harpies were night elf women cursed for betraying Queen Azshara. Their elven features fit the tale, but no one knows whether it is true.",al={"are harpies night elves","harpy night elf connection","curse of azshara"},it="ties"},{q="Why are harpy nests so infamous?",a="Harpies foul the land around their nests, leaving stench-ridden middens of trampled foliage and noxious waste. They also leave butchered bones and remnants of travelers and beasts dragged from nearby trails.",al={"harpy smell","what are harpy nests like","harpy roosts"},it="danger"},{q="How do harpy covens choose their leaders?",a="Harpies fiercely contest leadership. To claim and hold command as queen or matriarch, one must prove more ruthless than her roost-mates through betrayal, murder, and relentless cruelty toward enemies and rivals.",al={"harpy matriarch","harpy queen","who leads harpies"},it="leader"},{q="What powers and combat tactics do harpies use?",a="Harpies attack with crude weapons or razor-sharp talons, often diving from above. Their spellcasters wield storm magic, striking with crackling lightning, swirling gusts of wind, and shrill, disorienting shrieks.",al={"harpy abilities","harpy magic","how do harpies fight"},it="power"},{q="Is it true that a harpy's kiss is dangerous?",a="Yes. A harpy's kiss is toxic. Travelers beguiled by her elven features risk potent poison if they let her close, and it swiftly brings a sudden, debilitating fever.",al={"harpy kiss","harpy poison","harpy fever"},it="threat"},{q="What are harpies?",a="Harpies are vicious, intelligent avian creatures resembling a hybrid of a female night elf and a predatory bird, possessing graceful wings for arms and wicked talons for feet. Rather than harmonizing with the wilderness, they actively despoil their surroundings, slaughtering local wildlife and building foul, noxious nests. They wield primal storm magic alongside their talons and crude weaponry, causing misery wherever they roost.",al={"what is a harpy","who are harpies","harpy lore"},it="identity",add="fb0f8e51"},{q="Why are harpies hostile to travelers?",a="Harpies attack on sight because they are territorial, predatory, and thrive on causing havoc and sorrow. They expand aggressively from their roosts, ambushing travelers, raiding supply caravans, and killing nearly every creature that wanders into their lands to litter their nests with the grisly remains of their victims.",al={"why do harpies attack","are harpies friendly","why are harpies aggressive"},it="hostile",add="6541e8e0"},{q="Do harpies have any allies?",a="Harpies rarely tolerate outsiders, but they are known to maintain loose ties with kobolds. Because harpies covet shiny gems and ores, kobolds trade these scavenged treasures in exchange for items like harpy earwax, and in some regions, kobolds offer tribute to harpies in exchange for protection.",al={"who do harpies work with","harpy allies","who aligns with harpies"},it="allies",add="b7cf3fa6"},{q="Why are harpies found all across Kalimdor?",a="Harpies were once confined to their ancestral roosts in the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. Over time, their growing numbers and aggressive nature drove covens to migrate outward across the continent. You can now encounter their foul roosts anywhere from the forests of Teldrassil to the mesas of Mulgore, Durotar, and the Barrens.",al={"where do harpies live","why are harpies in kalimdor","harpy territory"},it="why_here",add="518dbd10"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Harpies resemble night elf women, yet they despoil the sacred boughs around Teldrassil's Oracle Glade.",["race:Tauren"]="The Windfury harpies of Mulgore and the Screeching brood of Thousand Needles have plagued tauren caravans and blighted the plains for generations. The tribes revile them as enemies.",["race:Orc"]="Dustwind harpies roost in Drygulch Ravine and Razorwind Canyon, where they menace supply routes between Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar. Constant armed patrols are needed.",["class:Druid"]="Harpies scorn nature's balance and foul the wilderness with tempest magic and filthy nests."},kw={"bloodfeather","dustwind","harpy","kalimdor","stonetalon","talons","windfury","witchwing"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","quest:876","zone:durotar","zone:mulgore","zone:barrens","subzone:oracle-glade","topic:night-elf","topic:tauren"},src={"Harpy"}}
E["topic:highborne"] = {t="topic",n="Highborne",z="general",s="Across the ancient Kaldorei Empire, the Highborne wielded the Well of Eternity for Queen Azshara. Their sorcery drew the Burning Legion to Azeroth, unleashing the War of the Ancients and the Great Sundering.",h="Across the ancient Kaldorei Empire, the Highborne wielded the Well of Eternity for Queen Azshara.",sec={{t="Aristocrats of the Well",b="Before the Sundering, the Highborne rose around Queen Azshara as the favored upper class. They claimed superiority over common kaldorei through selective bloodlines and intelligence. Opulent privilege set them apart, and they kept tight control of the Well of Eternity.\n\nThere they learned to shape its primal arcane power. Across ancient Kalimdor, they raised magnificent cities. Their hunger for sorcery drove them to draw ever more deeply from the Well, until its calm waters grew turbulent and dark.",sp=0},{t="The Betrayal and the Sundering",b="The Highborne’s spellcraft drew the attention of the dark titan Sargeras and the Burning Legion. Azshara and her counselor Xavius persuaded the Highborne that demons would remake the world as an untainted paradise.\n\nThe Highborne opened a massive gateway inside the Well of Eternity, unleashing the War of the Ancients. Demonic hordes slaughtered the populace, while rebels rallied by Malfurion Stormrage fought to close the portal. Then the Well imploded and tore the supercontinent apart.",sp=0},{t="Scattered Heirs and Remnants",b="After the Sundering, the Highborne met different fates. Those dragged beneath the waves with Azshara were twisted into serpentine naga. Others fell to demonic curses and became satyrs. Dath'Remar Sunstrider led a faction that aided the resistance but refused to give up arcane magic.\n\nExiled across the sea, they founded the high elven kingdom of Quel'Thalas. Today, isolated enclaves such as the Shen'dralar remain cloistered in Eldre'Thalas, shunned remnants of an empire that nearly destroyed Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does 'Highborne' mean?",a="In Darnassian, the Highborne were called the quel'dorei, meaning “children of noble birth.” They chose that name for their aristocratic bloodlines and magical aptitude, setting themselves apart from the rest of kaldorei society.",al={"queldorei meaning","what does queldorei mean","highborne translation"},it="name"},{q="Are modern night elves related to the Highborne?",a="Yes. The Highborne were the noble, magic-wielding ruling caste of the ancient night elves. They were physically the same race, though slightly paler and prone to flamboyant dress. After the Sundering, night elf society banned arcane magic and abolished the caste.",al={"are night elves highborne","difference between night elves and highborne","highborne night elf connection"},it="people"},{q="How did the Highborne cause the War of the Ancients?",a="The Highborne’s unchecked use of the Well of Eternity sent magical ripples across the cosmos and attracted the Burning Legion. Enticed by Sargeras’s promises of unmatched power and an idealized world, Azshara and her nobles channeled the Well to open a portal. The demon army then entered Kalimdor.",al={"why did burning legion come","how did highborne summon demons","highborne war of ancients role"},it="history"},{q="Did all Highborne side with Queen Azshara?",a="No. Several factions broke away when they saw the demonic devastation. Sorcerers led by Dath'Remar Sunstrider joined Malfurion's Kaldorei Resistance. Groups such as the Shen'dralar in Eldre'Thalas focused on surviving and defending their regional holdings.",al={"good highborne","did any highborne fight azshara","highborne resistance"},it="side"},{q="What happened to the surviving Highborne after the war?",a="The Highborne lineage scattered into several fates. Many who sank with Zin-Azshari became naga, while others were twisted into satyrs. Those who followed Dath'Remar were exiled to the Eastern Kingdoms and became high elves. A few, including the Shen'dralar in Dire Maul, remained cloistered in ancient ruins.",al={"what became of the highborne","where are the highborne now","highborne descendants"},it="origin"},{q="Who are the Shen'dralar?",a="The Shen'dralar are an ancient sect of Highborne scholars and arcanists who defended Eldre'Thalas, the southern city, during the Great Sundering. Cut off from Queen Azshara and mainstream kaldorei society, they retreated into the city, now called Dire Maul. There they relied on dark sorceries to preserve their immortality.",al={"dire maul highborne","eldre thalas elves","who lives in dire maul"},it="residents"},{q="Who were the Highborne?",a="The Highborne—or quel'dorei—were the wealthy aristocratic caste of the ancient night elven empire, serving as the favored courtiers and sorcerers of Queen Azshara. Distinguishing themselves through hereditary privilege and relentless study of arcane magic from the Well of Eternity, they grew arrogant and detached from ordinary kaldorei. Their reckless magical experimentation and pact with Sargeras brought about the Burning Legion's first invasion ten thousand years ago.",al={"what are highborne","who are the highborne","quel'dorei night elves"},it="identity",add="798aa346"},{q="Who leads the Highborne?",a="In ancient times, the Highborne answered directly to Queen Azshara, their beloved and tyrannical monarch. Following the Great Sundering and the collapse of the Kaldorei Empire, the caste fragmented into scattered remnants. Surviving enclaves like the Shen'dralar in Dire Maul follow their own local rulers, while the Highborne who fled across the sea formed new lineages, leaving no single leader over the ancient caste today.",al={"highborne leader","who rules the highborne","queen azshara highborne"},it="leader",add="de607c9c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Highborne caste remains a deep scar in night elven memory. After the Sundering, arcane magic was outlawed across Kalimdor under pain of exile or death.",["class:Mage"]="The Highborne were the first mortal practitioners of arcane magic on Azeroth. Their breathtaking achievements and catastrophic mistakes shaped the dangerous rules of modern spellcasting.",["class:Druid"]="Druidism arose as a natural philosophy against the Highborne’s reckless exploitation of the Well of Eternity. It laid the foundation for healing Kalimdor after the empire fell.",["class:Warlock"]="The Highborne were the first mortals on Azeroth to treat with the Burning Legion. They bartered cosmic secrets and made demonic pacts that paved the way for modern fel studies."},kw={"azshara","dath'remar","dire maul","eldre'thalas","highborne","quel'dorei","sargeras","shen'dralar","well of eternity","zin-azshari"},rel={"topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf","subzone:dire-maul","topic:burning-legion","topic:naga","topic:satyr","npc:malfurion-stormrage","zone:azshara"},src={"Highborne"}}
E["topic:horde"] = {t="topic",n="Horde",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, the Horde seeks survival and freedom under warchief thrall. Orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren share shamanic bonds, while the Forsaken keep an uneasy place among them. Old grievances and hostile neighbors test a people who prize strength, action, and honor over political maneuvering.",h="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, the Horde seeks survival and freedom under warchief thrall.",sec={{t="A Reborn Union",b="The Horde that stands now has left behind the demonic army that crossed the Dark Portal in the First and Second Wars. After freeing his people from the Burning Legion, warchief thrall led the orcs across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.\n\nThere they sought a spiritual homeland shaped by ancestral traditions and honor. Along the way, Thrall formed lasting ties with Vol'jin's displaced Darkspear trolls and Cairne Bloodhoof's tauren. Together, they fought centaur and demonic incursions during the Third War.",sp=0},{t="The Kalimdor Core",b="In Kalimdor, the orcs founded Durotar and raised Orgrimmar as its fortress capital. They gave the Darkspear refuge on the nearby Echo Isles. Farther south, the nomadic tauren gathered across Mulgore's plains around Thunder Bluff under high chieftain cairne bloodhoof. These three peoples share shamanic reverence, a deep bond with nature, and the need to survive. Bloodshed and spiritual respect have bound them as family, not merely allies of convenience.",sp=0},{t="An Alliance of Convenience",b="Across the sea, in Lordaeron's ruined lands, lady sylvanas windrunner led the free-willed Forsaken out of the Scourge's grasp. Human factions and Scourge remnants still opposed them, so Sylvanas sought a place in the Horde. Tauren elders argued that the undead might yet be redeemed. Thrall accepted the Forsaken, giving the Horde a vital military outpost in the Eastern Kingdoms, though many in Kalimdor had misgivings.",sp=0},{t="A Cold War",b="Thrall hopes to preserve peace with the Alliance, but the Old Horde's legacy still casts a shadow. To humans and dwarves, orcs remain bloodthirsty invaders, and the undead cannot be trusted.\n\nClashes over Ashenvale's vital lumber and skirmishes along territorial borders have left both factions in a tense, fragile cold war. Thrall directs campaigns against demon cults such as the Burning Blade to prove the Horde has broken with the Legion. Deep hatred still threatens to ignite all-out war at any spark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between the Old Horde and the New Horde?",a="The Old Horde was a blood-crazed conquering host manipulated by the Burning Legion into invading Azeroth during the First and Second Wars. Founded by Warchief Thrall, the New Horde rejected demonic corruption and returned to ancestral shamanism. It became a defensive alliance of outcasts seeking survival, land, and spiritual renewal.",al={"old horde vs new horde","how is this horde different","is this the same horde"},it="history"},{q="Who leads the Horde?",a="Warchief Thrall leads the Horde from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar. He directs its military and diplomacy, with counsel and leadership from High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof of the tauren, Shadow Hunter Vol'jin of the Darkspear, and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner of the Forsaken.",al={"who is the horde leader","horde warchief","who rules the horde"},it="leader"},{q="Why are the Forsaken part of the Horde?",a="With hostile Alliance remnants and the Scourge surrounding them in Lordaeron, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner sought allies for survival. Tauren elders argued that the Forsaken might yet be redeemed, and Thrall accepted them despite his reluctance. In return, the Horde gained a critical defensive foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why are undead in horde","how did forsaken join horde","tauren helped undead join"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the capital of the Horde?",a="Orgrimmar is the Horde's fortified capital and its center of government and war. Built into the crags of northern Durotar in Kalimdor, it holds Thrall's throne and enclaves for troll, tauren, and Forsaken delegates.",al={"horde capital","what is the horde main city","where does thrall rule"},it="place"},{q="Are the Horde and Alliance actively at war right now?",a="The Horde and Alliance live under an uneasy truce made after the Battle of Mount Hyjal. Fights over lumber in Ashenvale, territorial friction in the Alterac Mountains, and old hatred keep both sides in a simmering cold war of local skirmishes.",al={"are we at war with alliance","horde alliance war classic","is it peace or war"}},{q="Do all trolls belong to the Horde?",a="No. The Darkspear tribe is the Horde's main troll member, having sailed to Kalimdor with Thrall. Most other troll tribes across Azeroth are hostile, though groups such as the Revantusk tribe of the Hinterlands keep separate pacts of friendship and mutual defense without formally joining.",al={"which trolls are horde","are forest trolls horde","trolls in horde"},it="people"},{q="What is the Horde?",a="The Horde is a coalition of four disparate races—orcs, tauren, Darkspear trolls, and the Forsaken—banded together for mutual survival in an unforgiving world that would see them destroyed. Reborn under Warchief Thrall after breaking free from demonic corruption, this New Horde values strength, honor, and freedom. Rather than conquering, these outcasts and spiritual allies stand united to protect their newfound homes in Kalimdor and Lordaeron from enemies on all sides.",al={"what is horde","who are the horde","horde faction explained"},it="identity",add="34e0453c"},{q="Why does the Horde fight the Alliance?",a="Deep-seated mistrust and painful history keep both sides locked in a tense cold war. The Alliance remembers the brutality of the demonic Old Horde and struggles to believe the orcs have genuinely changed, while also viewing the undead Forsaken as monstrous abominations. Territorial skirmishes, scarce resources, and old grudges flare up constantly across the world. Even though leaders like Thrall seek peace and distance from the past, the Alliance's lingering suspicion makes open conflict an ever-present reality.",al={"why hate alliance","horde alliance war reason","why fight the alliance"},it="conflict",add="b47060cc"},{q="What does it mean to serve the Horde?",a="Serving the Horde means fighting for the survival, freedom, and honor of peoples cast aside by the rest of Azeroth. You are expected to stand beside your comrades as family and answer threats with action and strength rather than empty diplomacy. Whether securing vital timber in contested forests, hunting alongside tauren braves, or defending new settlements from hostile neighbors, your blade protects an alliance of outcasts striving to carve out a permanent place in the world.",al={"serving the horde","horde duty","what does the horde expect"},it="for_you",add="93715b4a"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The New Horde offers your people a path to redemption. Under Thrall's banner, you cast off the legacy of demon blood and reclaim ancestral shamanic honor.",["race:Tauren"]="You stood shoulder to shoulder with the orcs in the centaur wars. Together, you preserved your sacred lands in Mulgore and found steadfast spiritual brothers.",["race:Troll"]="Thrall's fleet rescued your Darkspear tribe from destruction on its island home. Your people pledged their spears and shadows to the Horde's survival.",["race:Undead"]="Your place in the Horde shields the Forsaken from the Living who would purge Lordaeron. Many in Kalimdor regard your ways with quiet caution.",["faction:Alliance"]="To human, dwarven, and elven eyes, the Horde remains a gathering of monstrous savages and treacherous corpses. They believe it cannot keep the peace."},kw={"cairne bloodhoof","darkspear","durotar","forsaken","horde","kalimdor","new horde","orgrimmar","tauren","thrall","vol'jin","warchief"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:orgrimmar","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","npc:vol-jin","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:old-horde","topic:alliance","quest:787"},src={"Horde"}}
E["topic:house-of-nobles"] = {t="topic",n="House of Nobles",z="general",s="In Stormwind Keep, the House of Nobles holds the kingdom’s lands, taxes, and trade. Their refusal to pay the laborers who rebuilt the city set off bloody riots that shook the realm.",h="In Stormwind Keep, the House of Nobles holds the kingdom’s lands, taxes, and trade.",sec={{t="Aristocrats of the Realm",b="Stormwind’s greatest patrician families form the House of Nobles, the Crown’s chief council. They own most arable land in Elwynn, Westfall, and Duskwood, and so hold great sway over trade, regional magistrates, and royal decrees. Boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon rule Stormwind in name. Yet the council can bind the throne in red tape, stall trials, block executions, and meddle in provincial affairs.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucratic Paralysis",b="With King Varian missing, the nobles leave outlying territories to fend for themselves, yet wield royal authority in petty disputes. Darkshire’s officials seethe after the House overturned their death sentence for grave robber Dextren Ward.\n\nThe nobles ordered him spared and sent to the Stormwind Stockade instead. The execution of Blackrock Orc chieftain Targorr the Dread has also been delayed indefinitely. A scheming noble would use him as a political pawn, while local sentries watch Stormwind rot from within.",sp=1},{t="Whispers of Treason",b="The House of Nobles’ stubbornness reaches beyond greed. Lady Katrana Prestor, secretly the black dragon Onyxia, has manipulated the council and paralyzed the kingdom. During talks with the stonemasons, she fed the aristocracy’s arrogance and urged them to hoard royal funds. Lord Gregor Lescovar and other high-ranking nobles conspire with the Defias Brotherhood in the throne’s shadow. No imperial troops march to aid the outlying towns.",sp=1,bt={"q65.7"}},{t="The Labor Revolt",b="After the Second War, the House of Nobles hired Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef and the Stonemasons Guild to rebuild Stormwind City from its ashes. At the same time, the nobles ran up great debts while pushing the kingdom’s military frontier south into Stranglethorn. Once the gleaming capital was finished, they balked at the bill and withheld the workers’ full wages.\n\nBetrayed, the masons rioted in the streets. The nobles banished the guild, driving the ruined workers into Westfall, where they formed the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="What is the House of Nobles?",a="The House of Nobles is Stormwind’s ruling assembly of aristocratic families, whose titles and seats pass through inheritance. Its members advise the monarch and control much of the kingdom’s domestic policy, taxes, and labor laws.",al={"what is the house of nobles","who are the nobles in stormwind","house of nobles lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the House of Nobles refuse to pay the Stonemasons?",a="Stormwind’s nobles overextended the treasury with costly military expeditions southward into Elwynn and Stranglethorn. When Edwin VanCleef presented the bill for rebuilding Stormwind City, they could not pay. They offered only a fraction of the promised sum, then ordered the guild disbanded.",al={"why didn't stonemasons get paid","why did nobles stiff vancleef","defias unpaid"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened when the Stonemasons rioted?",a="When the House of Nobles refused payment, the stonemasons rioted in Stormwind’s streets. The nobles banished the guild, and the ruined workers fled to Westfall, where they became the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"stonemason riots","what happened in the riots","why were the stonemasons banished"},sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Why won't Stormwind send troops to help Westfall or Duskwood?",a="The House of Nobles controls the realm’s purse strings and administrative approvals. Its members repeatedly block funding, troop deployments, and municipal aid to outlying territories, leaving local forces such as the People’s Militia and the Night Watch isolated.",al={"why no help for duskwood","why does stormwind ignore westfall","why won't stormwind send army"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Who was Lord Baurles K. Wishock?",a="Lord Baurles K. Wishock is an influential noble pressing for an investigation of the warlocks beneath The Slaughtered Lamb. The consequences of his inquiry unfold in the warlock storyline.",al={"lord wishock","baurles wishock","noble murdered by warlocks"},sp=1},{q="Did all the nobles turn against the Stonemasons?",a="No. Count S. J. Erlgadin supported the masons and fought to improve their wages and working conditions. Disgusted by his peers’ betrayal, he gave up his title and seat, left society, and joined Hemet Nesingwary’s expedition in Stranglethorn.",al={"did any nobles help stonemasons","count erlgadin","nobles who supported masons"}},{q="What is the history of the House of Nobles?",a="The House of Nobles predates the First War, representing the kingdom's wealthiest aristocratic landholders. Most of its bloodlines were nearly wiped out when the Old Horde sacked Stormwind City. After the Second War, Prince Varian Wrynn restored the assembly with ministers and advisors to oversee domestic recovery. The House oversaw the rebuilding of Stormwind by hiring the Stonemasons' Guild, but ran up heavy debts through military ventures, sparking bitter disputes, riots, and years of political paralysis.",al={"history of house of nobles","house of nobles origins","where did the nobles come from"},it="history",add="7a9e9579"},{q="Who leads the House of Nobles?",a="The House of Nobles has no single presiding ruler; it is a hereditary council of powerful aristocrats that advises the throne. With King Varian missing, the boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon hold formal executive authority, but court counselor Lady Katrana Prestor commands immense sway over the nobility. Her whispers guide much of their policy, keeping the assembly divided, fearful, and hesitant to commit royal troops to the outlying frontiers.",al={"leader of house of nobles","who controls the house of nobles","who is in charge of the nobles"},it="leader",add="f6b9ddca"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Westfall and Duskwood, the House of Nobles means arrogant highborn in a marble palace, while common folk bleed defending their homesteads from bandits and monsters.",["class:Rogue"]="The nobles’ bitter quarrels, corrupt dealings, and dirty secrets offer work for fixers, cutpurses, and master cheesemonger Elling Trias.",["class:Warlock"]="Influential nobles are turning their attention to Stormwind’s practitioners of the dark arts beneath The Slaughtered Lamb.",["faction:Alliance"]="The House of Nobles holds power in Stormwind City’s court but little sway over the wider Grand Alliance. Its stinginess keeps threatening the southern human territories’ stability."},kw={"baurles wishock","defias","erlgadin","gregor lescovar","house of nobles","katrana prestor","nobles","stonemasons guild","vancleef"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stonemasons-guild","topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:stormwind-keep","npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:onyxia","npc:lord-baurles-k-wishock","quest:434"},src={"House of Nobles"}}
E["topic:human"] = {t="topic",n="Human",z="general",s="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, humans still defend their place among the mortal realms. Their old empire broke into seven kingdoms. Now Stormwind is their strongest realm and the Alliance’s chief human power.",h="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, humans still defend their place among the mortal realms.",sec={{t="The Empire of Arathor",b="Long ago, human tribes wandered apart beneath the threat of the Amani forest trolls. Warlord Thoradin of the Arathi saw that division would bring their end. Through diplomacy and conquest, he united the clans and founded the Empire of Arathor, with its fortress capital at Strom.\n\nDuring the Troll Wars, the beleaguered high elves of Quel'Thalas allied with Arathor. They taught one hundred humans the arts of arcane magic. Together, humans and high elves broke the troll armies. Arathor secured human rule over the central continents, and the alliance laid the ground for future ties among mortal peoples.",sp=0},{t="Fracture into Seven Kingdoms",b="As Arathor grew secure and prosperous, its distant settlements became powerful city-states, able to stand alone. In time, the empire split into seven realms: Gilneas, Alterac, Dalaran, Lordaeron, Kul Tiras, Stormwind, and Stromgarde, whose first home was Strom.\n\nThese kingdoms traded with dwarves, gnomes, and elves, yet peace remained fragile. Border clashes and claims over land stirred rivalries, including old mountain feuds between Alterac and Stromgarde. Court intrigue added to the strain. The kingdoms stayed divided until disasters beyond their borders forced them to act together.",sp=0},{t="Invasion and Ruin",b="The orcish Horde came through the Dark Portal, forcing humanity’s kingdoms to face a common enemy. Stormwind fell in the First War, and its refugees fled north to warn the other realms. King Terenas Menethil II helped forge the Alliance of Lordaeron, joining humans, dwarves, gnomes, and high elves against the Horde in the Second War.\n\nStormwind was rebuilt with great effort. Then the Scourge plague ravaged Lordaeron, and Dalaran fell during the Third War. The northern human realms lay in smoking ruin.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Present",b="Stormwind is the strongest human kingdom left and the heart of the grand Alliance. King Varian Wrynn vanished while traveling to a diplomatic summit. His ten-year-old son, Anduin Wrynn, was crowned king, with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon as regent.\n\nNorthward, Lordaeron’s survivors are scattered or dead. Gilneas remains behind its colossal Greymane Wall, leaving Stormwind to carry the burden of humanity’s defense.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Seven Kingdoms of humanity?",a="The Seven Kingdoms were Lordaeron, Stormwind, Stromgarde, Dalaran, Kul Tiras, Gilneas, and Alterac. They arose when the Empire of Arathor fractured into independent city-states, each with its own ways and strengths.",al={"seven human kingdoms","human nations","arathor kingdoms"}},{q="Where did humans originally come from?",a="Humans began as nomadic tribes roaming the forests and highlands of the northern Eastern Kingdoms, especially around Tirisfal Glades. They later united under Warlord Thoradin as the first human nation.",al={"human origin","ancient humans","human ancestors"}},{q="What happened to the kingdom of Lordaeron?",a="Lordaeron was devastated by the Scourge’s plague of undeath during the Third War, and its prince, Arthas Menethil, betrayed it. Its ruined capital and nearby lands are now contested by the undead Forsaken, the Scourge, and remnants such as the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why is lordaeron destroyed","fall of lordaeron","fate of lordaeron"}},{q="Who currently rules humanity and Stormwind?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing under suspicious circumstances, his young son Anduin Wrynn holds the throne as a figurehead. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon rules as Regent alongside royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor.",al={"who leads stormwind","king of stormwind","stormwind ruler"}},{q="Why did the high elves teach humans magic?",a="During the Troll Wars, the high elves of Quel'Thalas faced annihilation by the Amani trolls. They made a treaty with Thoradin, ruler of Arathor, trading lessons in arcane magic for one hundred human soldiers.",al={"elves taught humans magic","first human mages","troll wars magic"}},{q="What role did humans play in forming the Alliance?",a="After Stormwind fell to the orcs in the First War, human refugees rallied the northern kingdoms. Under King Terenas of Lordaeron and Lord Lothar of Stormwind, human realms joined Ironforge dwarves, gnomes, and high elves to form the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"formation of alliance","alliance of lordaeron origin","how did alliance start"}},{q="Which classes can humans be?",a="Humans train as warriors, paladins, hunters, rogues, priests, mages, and warlocks.",al={"human classes","what classes can humans be","can humans be hunters"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you inherit the legacy of fallen Arathor and ruined Lordaeron. Stormwind now bears the defense and survival of the mortal realms.",["faction:Alliance"]="Human diplomacy and resolve forged the Alliance of Lordaeron. Stormwind remains the faction’s political and military heart.",["class:Mage"]="Human wizardry began in the Troll Wars, when the high elves taught the first one hundred human mages. Their teaching led in time to the founding of Dalaran.",["class:Paladin"]="Human holy men and knights founded the Knights of the Silver Hand in Lordaeron to fight the horrors of the Second War.",["faction:Horde"]="Humans were the first enemies the orcs met after crossing the Dark Portal. Their meeting began three brutal wars for survival on Azeroth."},kw={"alliance","arathor","human","lordaeron","mankind","stormwind","thoradin","troll wars","wrynn"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:lordaeron","zone:stormwind"},src={"Human"}}
E["topic:hunter"] = {t="topic",n="Hunter",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, hunters follow wild trails with loyal beasts at their sides. Bows, rifles, and crossbows let them strike from afar, while traps and primal aspects help control a fight. They track quarry through forests and over snowbound peaks, relying on their wits and bond with nature.",h="Across Azeroth, hunters follow wild trails with loyal beasts at their sides.",sec={{t="Kinship with the Wild",b="Hunters make their lives among Azeroth’s wild places. They study how beasts move, hunt, and defend themselves, earning respect instead of breaking spirits. With patience, they can tame dangerous creatures, from prowling cats to mountain bears and sharp-eyed raptors. These animals become steadfast allies, ready to defend their companions to the death.",sp=0},{t="Master Marksmen and Trackers",b="Hunters fight from a distance with bows, heavy crossbows, and rifles. Their volleys can pierce heavy armor before an attacker draws near. Keen senses lead them along faint footsteps, scents, and other signs left by their quarry. When enemies close in, frost and flame traps, disorienting ambushes, and quick evasive movements keep foes at bay.",sp=0},{t="Traditions Across Cultures",b="The hunter’s path takes many forms across Azeroth. Night elf Sentinels use bows and shadowcraft beneath Ashenvale’s canopy, moving in quiet accord with the wilderness. Dwarven riflemen brave Dun Morogh’s freezing crags with hardy bears and master the craft of gunpowder. Across Kalimdor, Tauren and Orc trackers follow ancient nomadic customs. They pursue prey with sacred respect and call on bestial spirits to guide their shots.\n\nIn Elwynn Forest, young humans learn from seasoned trackers such as the dwarf Tordrin Sternblade in Northshire Valley and Josephine Carson in Goldshire. The Skyborne learn to track and tame the beasts of Zephras Isle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What weapons do hunters use?",a="Hunters fight with ranged weapons such as bows, crossbows, and rifles. At close quarters, they also wield polearms, staves, axes, and daggers. Traps make room for them to shoot again.",al={"hunter weapons","what do hunters equip","hunter bows rifles"},gp=true},{q="How do hunters tame beasts?",a="Hunters study wild creatures and approach them without malice. By showing strength and respect, they can soothe dangerous predators and form a lasting bond, training a beast to fight at their side.",al={"how to tame pets","beast taming","tame animal"},gp=true},{q="What armor do hunters wear?",a="Hunters begin in light leather armor, which lets them move freely over rugged ground. With experience, they learn to wear sturdy mail for greater protection without greatly hindering their movement.",al={"hunter armor type","can hunters wear mail","hunter gear"},gp=true},{q="What are hunter aspects?",a="A hunter’s aspects attune the senses and body to strengths found in wild creatures. One can bring the fleetness of a cheetah, the keen focus of a hawk, or the resilience of a monkey.",al={"hunter aspects","aspect of the cheetah","hunter animal aspects"},gp=true},{q="What happens if an enemy gets too close to a hunter?",a="At close range, hunters struggle to fire their ranged weapons. Frost and immolation traps, concussive tools, and melee strikes can slow, wound, or disorient an attacker while the hunter or their beast retreats to regain distance.",al={"hunter deadzone","close combat hunter","hunter melee"},gp=true},{q="Which races practice the ways of the hunter?",a="Many peoples practice the hunt in their own ways. Night elves, dwarves, and humans in the Alliance favor bows and rifles; orcs, tauren, and trolls in the Horde honor tracking and beast mastery as ancestral ways of survival. The Skyborne train hunters on both sides, while gnomes and the Forsaken do not follow the hunter’s path.",al={"who can be a hunter","hunter races","playable hunter races","can humans be hunters","human hunter"},gp=true},{q="What is a Hunter in the lore?",a="Hunters are masters of the wilderness, expert marksmen, and rugged trackers who heed the call of the wild. Uniquely attuned to nature, they survive in uncharted territories by their wits and knowledge of the creatures they pursue. While deadly with bows, crossbows, rifles, and traps, a hunter is defined by a deep empathy for beasts, forging lifelong bonds with feral companions who fight and scout alongside them against the encroaching threats of the world.",al={"what is a hunter","hunter lore","hunter class lore"},it="identity",add="b60a9390"},{q="Where does a Hunter's power come from?",a="A hunter's prowess comes from an intimate connection to the natural world, rigorous martial training, and keen observation of wild quarry. Rather than drawing upon arcane study or divine worship, they channel strength through attuning themselves to the primal aspects of wild beasts. Combined with unmatched marksmanship, herbal venoms, and an innate kinship that commands loyalty from ferocious predators, their power lies in complete harmony with the wilderness.",al={"where do hunters get their power","hunter source of power","hunter magic source"},it="power",add="49aa042d"},{q="What does it mean for a new adventurer to become a Hunter?",a="Stepping out as a hunter means answering an inner call to leave civilized comforts behind for the untamed wilds. You rely entirely on your cunning, your keen senses, and your ranged weapons to survive alone in hostile lands. As you learn to read trails and set ambushes, you will earn the respect of a wild beast, gaining a loyal partner to guard your back as you defend the wilderness from corruption and exploitation.",al={"becoming a hunter","what does it mean to be a hunter","starting as a hunter"},it="for_you",add="fa19871b"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Your bond with the wild and your companion beast are your strengths. Master your ranged weapons, keep your distance, and let your beast hold the enemy’s attention.",["race:NightElf"]="For millennia, Kaldorei Sentinels have patrolled ancient forests with bows and trusted sabers, guarding sacred groves from outside corruption.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven marksmen are known for their skill with heavy rifles. They brave Khaz Modan’s treacherous mountain passes alongside fierce polar bears.",["race:Tauren"]="To the Tauren, the hunt is a sacred trial of endurance and reverence. They honor the Earth Mother by respecting every beast that feeds and clothes the tribe.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish beastmasters keep ancestral survival traditions forged on harsh worlds. They form strong combat bonds with loyal wolves and boars.",["race:Human"]="In Elwynn Forest, human hunters learn from seasoned trackers such as the dwarf Tordrin Sternblade in Northshire Valley and Josephine Carson in Goldshire.",["race:Skyborne"]="Skyborne hunters learn to track and tame the beasts of Zephras Isle, a floating land adrift in Skywall."},kw={"archery","aspects","beasts","hunter","marksmanship","pet","rifle","survival","tracking","traps"},rel={"topic:sentinels","topic:tauren","topic:dwarf","topic:night-elf","topic:horde","topic:alliance","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:gnome","topic:human","topic:skyborne"},src={"Hunter"}}
E["topic:juggernaught"] = {t="topic",n="Juggernaught",z="general",s="During the Second War, ogres forged the Horde's answer to the Alliance fleet: the juggernaught. Its iron hull and heavy guns made it a floating fortress built to batter ships and coastal strongholds.",h="During the Second War, ogres forged the Horde's answer to the Alliance fleet: the juggernaught.",sec={{t="Terror of the Second War",b="During the Second War, the Horde needed ships to cross the Great Sea and meet the Alliance fleet. Orcs had little seafaring tradition, so they turned to ogre ingenuity. The ogre juggernaught became the backbone of the Horde armada. Slower and less nimble than troll destroyers, these great ships bore heavy plating and broadside guns. Their volleys broke Alliance hulls and reduced shore fortifications to rubble.",sp=0},{t="Ironclad Cove",b="Beneath Westfall's hills, caverns in the Deadmines hide Ironclad Cove. Away from prying eyes and royal inspectors, Edwin VanCleef's craftsmen secretly built a fully armed juggernaught there. The cavern opens directly to the sea. From it, the Defias could bypass Stormwind's overland defenses and launch a surprise naval strike at the heart of the kingdom.",sp=1,bt={"defias.hideout"}}},faq={{q="What is a juggernaught?",a="A juggernaught is an enormous, heavily armored battleship armed with heavy naval cannons. Ogres helped the Old Horde build these floating fortresses during the Second War to overpower enemy fleets and coastal defenses.",al={"juggernaut warcraft","orc battleship","ogre juggernaut"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a huge ship inside the Deadmines?",a="Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood built a juggernaught in Ironclad Cove, a secluded cavern inside the Deadmines. The underground shipyard hid their work from prying eyes and royal inspectors.",al={"ship in deadmines","why boat in mines","deadmines ship"},sp=1,it="why_here",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="What did Edwin VanCleef intend to do with the ship?",a="The ship is part of VanCleef's activities beneath Westfall. Investigating the Defias Brotherhood reveals what he intended for it.",al={"vancleef boat plan","why did defias build a ship","defias juggernaught purpose"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Who originally invented the juggernaught?",a="The Old Horde built juggernaughts with ogre ingenuity during the Second War. Orcs had little seafaring tradition, and these warships became the backbone of the Horde fleet.",al={"who made juggernauts","ogre ships lore","horde navy origin"},it="origin"},{q="How does the ship get out of the Deadmines cavern?",a="Ironclad Cove opens directly to the sea, allowing a juggernaught built there to reach open waters.",al={"how does deadmines ship leave","ironclad cove exit","deadmines water exit"},sp=1},{q="Does the Horde still use juggernaughts?",a="Orcish battleships were still called juggernaughts during the Third War. They brought heavy firepower to the Horde fleet, though the current deployment of such ships is uncertain.",al={"modern horde juggernauts","horde battleships"},it="today"},{q="What is the history of the juggernaught?",a="Juggernaughts were first constructed during the Second War to serve as the iron core of the Old Horde's naval armada. Because the orcs possessed little naval tradition, they relied heavily on ogre craftsmanship and brute force to fashion these gargantuan floating fortresses. Bristling with heavy cannons and thick armor, they terrorized the seas of Azeroth and inflicted devastating losses upon the Alliance fleet. Though many were sunk or abandoned following the Horde's ultimate defeat, surviving vessels and salvageable designs continue to be prized by outlaws and warlords alike.",al={"juggernaught history","where did juggernaughts come from","second war juggernaughts"},it="history",add="f4436d36"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, a juggernaught under construction beneath Westfall threatens Stormwind and King Anduin's court.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, juggernaughts recall its naval heritage from the Second War, when ogre ingenuity helped challenge Alliance mastery of the seas.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know Stormwind's rebuilders were betrayed and driven to outlawry under VanCleef. They brought their architectural and stonework skills to a warship hidden beneath Westfall's hills.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you see the audacity in Edwin VanCleef's plan to build a capital battleship beneath the noses of SI:7 and the Stormwind guard."},kw={"battleship","deadmines","defias","ironclad cove","juggernaught","juggernaut","ogre juggernaught","ship","stormwind","vancleef"},rel={"subzone:ironclad-cove","zone:deadmines","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","topic:second-war","topic:horde","quest:65"},src={"Juggernaught"}}
E["topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"] = {t="topic",n="Knights of the Silver Hand",z="general",s="Across Stormwind, Ironforge, and the Plaguelands, the Knights of the Silver Hand still keep their vows. Founded after the First War, the order joined martial skill with the healing and smiting power of the Holy Light. Its northern chapter fell with Lordaeron, but knights still serve in the south and fight the undead in the north.",h="Across Stormwind, Ironforge, and the Plaguelands, the Knights of the Silver Hand still keep their vows.",sec={{t="Creation of the Paladins",b="After Stormwind fell in the First War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol saw that the Alliance needed holy warriors fit for battle. The clerics of Northshire could heal, but lacked the martial training to hold the front lines.\n\nSo Faol and his foremost student, Uther the Lightbringer, founded the Knights of the Silver Hand, training holy warriors to endure the Second War. They joined battle-hardened knights ready to learn devotion to the Light with devout clerics willing to wear plate armor and wield warhammers.",sp=0},{t="Glory in the Second War",b="Under Uther the Lightbringer, the first paladins became vital to the Alliance of Lordaeron. They rode into battle, lifted the spirits of weary soldiers, and faced the Horde's death knights and their sinister necromancy.\n\nDuring the war, the Silver Hand put down peasant rebellions, reclaimed Caer Darrow, and helped defend Capital City from the orc siege. In the peace that followed, paladins guarded Lordaeron's borders, settled civil disputes, and upheld honor, humility, and justice.",sp=0},{t="The Fall and Fractured Remnants",b="The Third War fractured the order. Outside Stratholme, Prince Arthas Menethil, a decorated Silver Hand knight, clashed with his mentor Uther. Uther refused to butcher the infected citizens, so Arthas unlawfully suspended the paladins. Later, Arthas fell to corruption and led the Scourge against Lordaeron. Uther was slain, and the order lost its central leadership.\n\nThe surviving northern knights split over doctrine, giving rise to the zealous Scarlet Crusade and the vigilant Argent Dawn. In Stormwind and Ironforge, surviving chapters still train paladins under the Silver Hand's banner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who founded the Knights of the Silver Hand?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the Knights of the Silver Hand after the First War and chose Uther the Lightbringer as its first knight.",al={"who made the silver hand","founder of paladins","who created paladins"},it="origin"},{q="Does the Silver Hand still exist?",a="Yes. Though the Scourge's destruction of Lordaeron shattered its northern high command, active chapters still serve the Alliance from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light and Ironforge's halls.",al={"is silver hand alive","silver hand today","are paladins still around"},it="today"},{q="How are the Scarlet Crusade and Argent Dawn related to the Silver Hand?",a="After Uther and Highlord Alexandros Mograine died, the surviving paladins in Lordaeron split over their beliefs. Hardline fanatics formed the Scarlet Crusade to eliminate outsiders, while more moderate veterans founded the Argent Dawn.",al={"scarlet crusade silver hand","argent dawn silver hand","how did the silver hand split"},it="ties"},{q="Can non-humans join the Knights of the Silver Hand?",a="Yes. The order began with human knights and clerics from Lordaeron, then welcomed dwarven priests and warriors of Ironforge during and after the Second War. They bore the Silver Hand's insignia and followed its rites.",al={"dwarf paladins silver hand","who can be a silver hand paladin","can dwarves be silver hand"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Order of the Silver Hand?",a="The Knights of the Silver Hand are an order of holy warriors, commonly known as paladins. Formed as the martial branch of the Church of the Holy Light, they blend martial prowess with divine power. Armed with heavy plate, warhammers, and sacred incantations, they serve as paragons of virtue, dedicated to protecting the innocent, healing the wounded, and vanquishing evil.",al={"what are the knights of the silver hand","who are the silver hand","paladins of the silver hand"},it="identity",add="f98dc644"},{q="What is the history of the Knights of the Silver Hand?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol established the order during the Second War after the clergy suffered heavy losses in the First War. He sought to create champions who could fight on the front lines while channeling the Light. Under Uther the Lightbringer, the paladins turned the tide against the Horde. For decades, they defended Lordaeron until Prince Arthas shattered their ranks during the Third War.",al={"history of silver hand","how did the silver hand start","silver hand origin story"},it="history",add="a6d23619"},{q="Who leads the Knights of the Silver Hand?",a="The order lacks a single supreme leader. Lord Uther the Lightbringer originally commanded the knights until his tragic demise at the hands of Arthas. Highlord Alexandros Mograine briefly rallied the survivors in Lordaeron until his assassination. Today, the remnants in Lordaeron have splintered, while paladin leaders in Stormwind and Ironforge guide the brothers fighting under the Alliance banner.",al={"silver hand leader","who commands the silver hand","leader of paladins"},it="leader",add="1db4f553"},{q="Who are the Knights of the Silver Hand allied with?",a="The Silver Hand was established to defend humanity and fight for the Grand Alliance. While its original northern chapter fell into ruin during the Third War, active chapters in Stormwind and Ironforge remain staunch champions of the Alliance of Lordaeron's successor nations, fighting alongside humans, dwarves, and high elves against threats across Azeroth.",al={"who does the silver hand fight for","silver hand factions","silver hand alliance"},it="allies",add="0d7dcf69"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a human or dwarf serving the Alliance, your paladin's oaths, librams, and martial ways trace back to the laws laid down by Archbishop Faol and Uther the Lightbringer.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, your calling helped shape the Silver Hand. The order arose because the priesthood was vulnerable in the First War, joining divine ministry with heavy warfare.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you inherit the Silver Hand's ideals. They inspired soldiers across every human realm to stand firm against darkness.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can honor the Silver Hand as the height of virtue, honor, and courage. Its great northern masters have fallen, but Stormwind keeps their memory alive."},kw={"alonsus faol","arthas","holy light","paladin","silver hand","stratholme","tirion fordring","turalyon","uther"},rel={"topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:light","npc:tirion-fordring","subzone:stratholme","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:second-war","topic:argent-dawn","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Knights of the Silver Hand"}}
E["topic:kobold"] = {t="topic",n="Kobold",z="general",s="In Azeroth's mines and caverns, kobolds guard the candles fixed to their heads. Small and rat-like, they dig in the dark and defend their tunnels in numbers.",h="In Azeroth's mines and caverns, kobolds guard the candles fixed to their heads.",sec={{t="Miners of the Dark",b="Kobolds stand barely four feet tall. Filthy scavengers, they spend their lives delving underground. Their low-light vision fails in the deepest shafts, so each kobold fixes a crude candle to its head. Alone, one is cowardly when cornered. Yet kobolds breed in massive numbers and work with relentless energy. When agitated, their rat-like tails whip as they rush intruders in frantic swarms. They wield heavy iron mining picks and beat foes to death with them.",sp=0},{t="You No Take Candle!",b="Kobolds fear pitch-black tunnels with a deep, primal terror. To them, a candle is more than light. Its flame shields them from a darkness they believe will consume them.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Pests of the Kingdoms",b="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, kobolds often overrun working mines. In Elwynn Forest, a clan displaced from the Redridge Mountains seized the Echo Ridge, Fargodeep, and Jasperlode mines. Riverpaw gnolls and the Defias Brotherhood helped drive them there. In Loch Modan, the Tunnel Rat clan seized the Silver Stream Mine from the dwarven Miners' League.\n\nKobolds also plague industrial digs in Kalimdor. They labor for the Venture Company in Stonetalon and uncover strange minerals in Thousand Needles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do kobolds care so much about their candles?",a="Kobolds feel deep, paralyzing terror at complete darkness. Their folklore treats it as a predator that snuffs out life and swallows miners whole. They guard their candles as their only defense.",al={"why candles","kobold candles","you no take candle meaning"},it="motive"},{q="Where do kobolds come from?",a="Kobolds' true origins are unknown. They have dwelt in tunnels and caverns beneath Azeroth for as long as anyone remembers, wherever earth can be dug.",al={"kobold origins","where do kobolds come from","kobold evolution"},it="origin"},{q="Are kobolds allied with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Kobolds were not willing partners of the Defias Brotherhood. In Elwynn Forest and Westfall, Riverpaw gnolls largely bullied and enslaved them. The Defias hired those gnolls to disrupt mining and secure mineral wealth.",al={"kobold defias","are kobolds working for defias","fargodeep defias"},it="allies"},{q="How do kobolds choose their leaders?",a="Kobolds have no single ruler. Each clan answers to its own bosses, including taskmasters who drive the diggers to work in the mines they claim.",al={"kobold leader","kobold boss","how do kobolds pick chiefs"},it="leader"},{q="Are kobolds found in Kalimdor as well as the Eastern Kingdoms?",a="Yes. Kobolds infested the underground caverns beneath Orgrimmar during the city's founding. They also work in the Venture Company's Windshear Mine in the Stonetalon Mountains and burrow throughout Thousand Needles.",al={"kobolds in kalimdor","stonetalon kobolds","orgrimmar kobolds"},it="place"},{q="What do kobolds eat?",a="Little is recorded about kobold diets. They are filthy scavengers who live on whatever they find in and around their tunnels.",al={"kobold diet","what do kobolds eat"}},{q="What are kobolds?",a="Kobolds are diminutive, rat-like subterranean humanoids standing barely four feet tall. Infamous for their cowardice and foul odor, they make their homes tunneling through caverns and abandoned mines. While individually weak and fearful of larger races, they reproduce rapidly and rely on overwhelming numbers when forced into a fight, swarming intruders with crude mining picks.",al={"what is a kobold","who are the kobolds","kobold info"},it="identity",add="31a27fce"},{q="Why are kobolds found infesting so many mines?",a="Kobolds are natural diggers and miners who prefer subterranean dens far from populated surface settlements. They naturally flock to pre-existing caves, quarries, and rich mineral seams. When humanoid settlements leave excavations unattended or lightly defended—such as the mines across Elwynn, Loch Modan, and Stonetalon—opportunistic kobolds quickly burrow in, expand the tunnels, and claim the veins for themselves.",al={"why are kobolds in mines","kobold mines why","where do kobolds live"},it="why_here",add="427afc17"},{q="Why are kobolds hostile to travelers?",a="Kobolds are skittish, paranoid, and distrustful of anything larger than themselves. Deep underground, they constantly fear cave-ins, starvation, and the absolute dark. When outsiders enter their territory, kobolds perceive them as an immediate threat come to rob their claims or snuff out their precious head-candles, driving them to attack in frantic, desperate mobs.",al={"why do kobolds attack","are kobolds always hostile","why do kobolds fight"},it="hostile",add="840836f4"},{q="What is known about the history of kobolds?",a="Kobolds have inhabited the tunnels beneath Azeroth for as long as anyone remembers, though their true origins are unknown. Largely splintered into local clans, they regularly collide with other races, such as when goblin workers digging beneath Orgrimmar during its construction accidentally broke into a kobold den.",al={"kobold history","how long have kobolds existed","where did kobolds come from history"},it="history",add="d2531c8b"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner in human or dwarven lands, you will inevitably encounter kobold infestations. Kobolds gravitate toward rich veins of copper, tin, and silver.",["race:Human"]="For the Kingdom of Stormwind, kobolds are a constant economic headache. They have overrun vital local operations at Fargodeep, Jasperlode, and Echo Ridge.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Miners' League regularly employs adventurers to clear Tunnel Rat kobolds from mountain digs like the Silver Stream Mine in Loch Modan.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know kobold warrens beneath the dry earth caused chaos during Orgrimmar's founding. Clans like the Gravelsnouts still harass frontier outposts in Kalimdor."},kw={"candle","echo ridge","fargodeep","jasperlode","kobold","silver stream","trogg","tunnel rat","windshear"},rel={"quest:60","subzone:fargodeep-mine","subzone:jasperlode-mine","subzone:silver-stream-mine","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:trogg","quest:21"},src={"Kobold"}}
E["topic:kolkar-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Kolkar clan",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, the Kolkar clan raids settlements and turns on all who cross its path. The red-marked centaur claim descent from the first Khan, Kolk, and hold strongholds in Desolace and the Barrens.",h="Across Kalimdor, the Kolkar clan raids settlements and turns on all who cross its path.",sec={{t="Sons of Kolk",b="The Kolkar take their name from Khan Kolk, the first centaur khan. He was born from the union of Zaetar and Theradras. The clan hates other races and its fellow centaur clans, and its red markings set it apart. The Kolkar refuse all alliances. Their ancient village stood in eastern Desolace, where Khan Kolk's restless spirit still wanders beneath their ancestral lands.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of the Barrens",b="For generations, Kolkar raids harried the nomadic tauren crossing the arid Barrens. During the Third War, the orcs came to Kalimdor. Thrall joined Cairne Bloodhoof to drive the marauding centaur back and escort the tauren to safety in Mulgore. Defeat only deepened the feud. The Kolkar entrenched themselves around the Barrens' three vital water sources: the Forgotten Pools, the Lushwater Oasis, and the Stagnant Oasis.",sp=0},{t="Encroachment on Durotar",b="From fortified positions across the savanna, the Kolkar have pushed east past the Southfury River into Durotar. At Kolkar Crag in the south, raiding parties plot assaults on Sen'jin Village, the Valley of Trials, and the paths toward Orgrimmar. Senior Horde leaders face larger regional threats, so young recruits are sent to curb the centaur advance before its raiders strike the young orc capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the Kolkar centaur?",a="The Kolkar are one of Kalimdor's five major centaur clans. Named for their first leader, Khan Kolk, they are fierce and xenophobic, marked by red armor. They keep settlements in Desolace, control the Barrens' main water oases, and maintain raiding camps in southern Durotar.",al={"kolkar clan","who are kolkar","kolkar lore","centaur in barrens"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Kolkar hate the Horde so much?",a="For generations, the Kolkar hunted and harried the tauren across the Barrens. When Thrall's Horde arrived, the orcs joined Cairne Bloodhoof to drive the centaur back and help the tauren settle in Mulgore. The Kolkar Khans were humiliated, and their long hunt became a bitter war against both orcs and tauren.",al={"why do kolkar attack orcs","kolkar tauren feud","centaur vs horde"},it="hostile"},{q="Why are the Kolkar occupying the Barrens oases?",a="The Kolkar hold the Barrens' oases because water means survival in that arid land. Command tents, tribal totems, and hyena packs guard the Forgotten Pools, Lushwater Oasis, and Stagnant Oasis, keeping travelers, merchants, and the Horde from these watering holes.",al={"kolkar at oases","forgotten pools centaur","lushwater oasis centaur"},it="why_here"},{q="Who leads the Kolkar clan?",a="Khan Kolk was the clan's first ruler, and his spirit lingers in Maraudon. In recent times, Khan Dez'hepah and his officers led the clan from the ancient Kolkar Village in Desolace, while Barrens camps answered to leaders such as Hezrul Bloodmark. Other khans, including the fallen Khan Gragtor, led warbands farther afield.",al={"kolkar leader","kolkar khan","who is the kolkar boss"},it="leader"},{q="What is Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar Crag is a rocky canyon outpost in southern Durotar. Centaur warbands use it as a forward staging ground to harass Horde initiates in the Valley of Trials, menace Sen'jin Village, and test Orgrimmar's defenses.",al={"where is kolkar crag","durotar centaur camp","kolkar in durotar"},it="place"},{q="Do the Kolkar work with other centaur clans?",a="No. The Kolkar have no kinship or treaties with the other four centaur clans native to Desolace. Centaur society is violently divided, and the Kolkar fight other clans as readily as they fight the Horde and Alliance.",al={"centaur clans alliance","kolkar allies","do centaur cooperate"},it="allies"},{q="Where did the Kolkar clan come from?",a="The Kolkar are one of the original centaur clans born in Desolace, tracing their bloodline to Khan Kolk, the son of Zaetar and Princess Theradras. Long before the Third War, their roaming warbands pushed east into the Barrens, violently driving the nomadic tauren away from their sacred hunting grounds. When Thrall's newly arrived orcs allied with Cairne Bloodhoof, the united Horde shattered the centaur army and opened the way for the tauren to settle Mulgore. Now fractured across Desolace, Durotar, and the Barrens, the Kolkar nurse a bitter grudge and wage constant territorial wars to reclaim their lost dominance.",al={"kolkar history","origin of kolkar","kolkar clan origins"},it="history",add="0aa5759f"},{q="How did the Kolkar clan get their name?",a="The clan takes its name from its founding father, Khan Kolk. As the legendary eldest son of the demigod Zaetar and the earth elemental Princess Theradras, Kolk stood as the first of the great centaur khans who led their brutish descendants out of Maraudon and claimed the barren reaches of central Kalimdor.",al={"why are they called kolkar","kolkar name origin","who is kolk"},it="name",add="a5b3ba08"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Across the Barrens, the Kolkar hunted your people nearly to extinction before the orcs intervened. Each encounter with them touches the survival of your ancestors.",["race:Orc"]="Your first pact with the tauren was forged in blood against Kolkar marauders. Their scouts at Kolkar Crag now threaten the Valley of Trials, where young orcs come of age.",["faction:Horde"]="Kolkar control of the three Barrens oases cuts off vital trade and water supplies between Durotar, Mulgore, and the Crossroads.",["class:Hunter"]="Kolkar raiding parties rely on trained, partly domesticated hyenas to track intruders and guard the edges of their watering holes."},kw={"barrens","centaur","desolace","dezhepah","durotar","khan","kolk","kolkar","kolkar crag","maraudon","oasis"},rel={"topic:centaur","zone:barrens","zone:desolace","subzone:kolkar-crag","topic:tauren","topic:horde","quest:1362","subzone:lushwater-oasis"},src={"Kolkar clan"}}
E["topic:kul-tiras"] = {t="topic",n="Kul Tiras",z="general",s="Across the Great Sea, Kul Tiras keeps to its island waters west of Dun Morogh and Baradin Bay. Its navy once anchored the Alliance of Lordaeron. Since that alliance fractured and losses came in Kalimdor, the kingdom has drawn back.",h="Across the Great Sea, Kul Tiras keeps to its island waters west of Dun Morogh and Baradin Bay.",sec={{t="A Nation Born of the Sea",b="Kul Tiras rose to power on the work of its merchant marine and the wealth of its fishing grounds. Its naval armada had no equal in human history.",sp=0},{t="The Second War and Isolation",b="When the Orcish Horde swept through the Eastern Kingdoms, Kul Tiras answered King Terenas Menethil II and joined the Alliance of Lordaeron. Lord Admiral Daelin Proudmoore commanded humanity's naval forces. They fought across the open ocean to cut the Horde's sea lanes and guard the coasts.\n\nAfter the war, the northern kingdoms eventually split. Kul Tiras drew back its fleets, strengthened its coastal defenses, and kept to itself.",sp=0},{t="Shadows over the Proudmoores",b="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore sailed to Kalimdor in search of Lady Jaina Proudmoore. She had led refugees across the ocean to build Theramore. Daelin then began a campaign against the Horde. The crusade brought ruin, and Daelin died at Theramore.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Kul Tiras located?",a="Kul Tiras lies in the Great Sea, west of Baradin Bay and the coast of Dun Morogh. Its rugged, cold, mountainous islands are guarded by massive seawalls and heavy coastal garrisons.",al={"where is kul tiras","kul tiras map","kul tiras location"},it="place"},{q="Is Kul Tiras still part of the Alliance?",a="Kul Tiras helped found the Alliance of Lordaeron. Since the old Alliance splintered, the kingdom has largely withdrawn from continental affairs and keeps itself apart.",al={"is kul tiras alliance","kul tiras alliance member"},it="allies"},{q="Who rules Kul Tiras?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore led Kul Tiras for decades. His campaign in Kalimdor ended with his death at Theramore.",al={"kul tiras leader","who leads kul tiras","king of kul tiras"},it="leader"},{q="Why is Kul Tiras famous across Azeroth?",a="Kul Tiras is famed for its maritime fleet, shipwrights, and sailors, the greatest in the known world. Its warships and vast merchant convoys dominated the sea lanes for centuries. Its navy helped hold off the Horde in the Second War.",al={"what is kul tiras known for","why is kul tiras famous"},it="fame"},{q="How is Kul Tiras connected to Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is Kul Tiran and the daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. Born to the ruling family, she studied in Dalaran, then established the independent port of Theramore Isle on Kalimdor. In doing so, she distanced herself from her homeland's leadership.",al={"jaina kul tiras","is jaina from kul tiras"},it="ties"},{q="What threats face Kul Tiras?",a="Beyond their deep enmity with the Horde, Kul Tiras faces renegade pirate crews and hostile coastal beasts in its waters. Constant watch and fortified seagates protect the shipping lanes.",al={"kul tiras enemies","threats to kul tiras"},it="threat"},{q="What is Kul Tiras?",a="Kul Tiras is an island nation and archipelago situated in the Great Sea west of the Eastern Kingdoms. Renowned for their peerless maritime mastery and trading vessels, the people of Kul Tiras built one of the seven historic human kingdoms. They command the mightiest naval fleet in the world, built on a long tradition of shipwrighting, fishing, and open-ocean exploration.",al={"what is kul tiras","kul tiras kingdom","kul tiras nation"},it="identity",add="31ee9d0a"},{q="What is the history of Kul Tiras?",a="Kul Tiras grew into a powerful maritime nation whose merchant lanes reached across the world. It provided the core naval strength of the Alliance during the Second War under Daelin Proudmoore.",al={"history of kul tiras","how was kul tiras founded","kul tiras origin"},it="history",add="db90478b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="At sea, the Alliance of Lordaeron relied on the Kul Tiran armada to survive. After the losses of the Third War, the island nation keeps its distance and remains guarded.",["faction:Horde"]="Kul Tiran sailors under Admiral Proudmoore fought bitterly against the Horde in the Second War. Later, they attacked Thrall's new homeland in Durotar, deepening an enduring blood feud.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can trace Kul Tiras's hardy island culture to its shipbuilding, trade, and resilience against the open ocean.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know Kul Tiras's shipyards use great quantities of metal to build the armored warships of Azeroth's mightiest navy."},kw={"alliance of lordaeron","daelin proudmoore","great sea","jaina proudmoore","kul tiras","tiragarde"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:second-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:alliance","topic:horde","subzone:baradin-bay","zone:dunmorogh","topic:pirate"},src={"Kul Tiras"}}
E["topic:leper-gnome"] = {t="topic",n="Leper gnome",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, leper gnomes endure the ruin of Gnomeregan. Most still dwell in the city, changed by its toxic fallout and loyal to Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",h="Across Azeroth, leper gnomes endure the ruin of Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="The Fall of the Great City",b="Troggs broke into Gnomeregan during the Third War. Mekgineer Thermaplugg urged High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque to flood the city with radioactive toxins. He claimed they would kill the troggs and spare the gnomes. Instead, eighty percent of the city's inhabitants died. Survivors sealed in the lower levels were warped in mind and body by the fallout. Their pale, pustulant forms became known as leper gnomes.",sp=0},{t="Thermaplugg's Enclave",b="Mekgineer Thermaplugg also succumbed to the poisonous fallout. His complexion changed, and his sanity failed. He named himself techno-overlord and King of Gnomeregan, then gathered the crazed survivors in the Tinkers' Court. Many now mistake surface dwellers for trogg intruders. They attack returning rescue parties with frantic savagery.\n\nThe survivors pilot salvaged mechanical constructs and build volatile ordnance. With fanatical devotion, they guard Thermaplugg's kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Scattered Across Azeroth",b="Most leper gnomes remain trapped in Gnomeregan's contaminated corridors, though a handful have reached the wider world. Some, driven by desperation or dark ambition, have joined the Dark Iron dwarves in Blackrock Depths. Others operate machinery for the Venture Company in Stonetalon. A few serve as lab assistants to the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society in the depths of the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="The Search for a Cure",b="Gnome scholars exiled in Ironforge still seek ways to help their irradiated kin. In Dun Morogh, engineers and tinkers Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle Sprysprocket work on Operation Recombobulation. They hope to reverse the mutation through alchemy or machinery. Whether toxic fallout can break a mind beyond repair remains unanswered.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What turned the gnomes into leper gnomes?",a="During the trogg invasion of Gnomeregan, Mekgineer Thermaplugg urged High Tinker Mekkatorque to release radioactive vents and purge the caverns. The toxins failed to kill the troggs. Instead, they irradiated trapped gnomish citizens, changing their bodies and destroying their sanity.",al={"why are leper gnomes green","how did they become leper gnomes","gnome radiation cause"},it="origin"},{q="Are leper gnomes undead?",a="No. Leper gnomes are living gnomes, changed in body by severe radiation poisoning. Some serve alongside the Forsaken in Lordaeron because of their affinity for blight and toxins. Radiation from gnomish engineering caused their affliction, not necromancy.",al={"are leper gnomes zombies","are they undead","leper gnome scourge"}},{q="Can leper gnomes be cured?",a="Gnome inventors Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle Sprysprocket are testing recombobulation devices and alchemical washes. Some experiments show minor promise, but no reliable cure can reverse both the physical rot and deep mental decline.",al={"can leper gnomes be saved","leper gnome cure","operation recombobulation"}},{q="Who leads the leper gnomes?",a="Mekgineer Thermaplugg leads the leper gnomes as their despotic techno-overlord. Mutated by the radiation he insisted on releasing, he rules from the Tinkers' Court in Gnomeregan. He uses the survivors' fractured minds to keep control of the ruins.",al={"leper gnome leader","king of gnomeregan","thermaplugg boss"},it="leader"},{q="Why do leper gnomes attack anyone who enters Gnomeregan?",a="Prolonged exposure to radioactive gasses shattered their minds. In paranoia and delirium, most leper gnomes see any outsider, even an uncorrupted surface gnome, as a trogg invader bent on their destruction.",al={"why are leper gnomes hostile","why do they fight us"},it="hostile"},{q="Why are some leper gnomes working with the Forsaken?",a="Some leper gnomes, including Ganoosh in the Undercity's Apothecarium, have joined the Forsaken. The Royal Apothecary Society employs them as research assistants, valuing their affinity for plague and blighted alchemy. They also value the gnomes' survival despite severe bodily decline.",al={"leper gnomes in undercity","forsaken leper gnomes"},it="allies"},{q="What are leper gnomes?",a="Leper gnomes are gnomes who were twisted, diseased, and driven mad by the toxic radiation released within Gnomeregan. Marked by pale, greenish, lesion-covered skin and violent instability, most have devolved into deranged wretches who wander the ruined halls of their former capital, completely severed from civilized gnome society.",al={"what is a leper gnome","who are leper gnomes","leper gnome info"},it="identity",add="e1b9c7cf"},{q="Where did the leper gnomes come from?",a="During the Third War, troggs invaded Gnomeregan from subterranean depths. To repel them, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque—advised by Mekgineer Thermaplugg—opened the city's radioactive waste tanks. The plan proved disastrous: toxic radiation blanketed the underground metropolis, slaughtering eighty percent of the gnome population and horrifically mutating the survivors into the maddened leper gnomes seen today.",al={"leper gnome history","origin of leper gnomes","how did leper gnomes happen"},it="history",add="acba60f9"},{q="Why are they called leper gnomes?",a="They earn their name from their sickly, rotting appearance. Heavy exposure to irradiated waste left their flesh discolored, peeling, and pocked with vile sores and lesions, resembling the afflictions of classic leprosy. Combined with their slow physical and mental degradation, the title reflects their tragically diseased state.",al={"why leper gnomes","leper gnome name meaning","why are they named leper gnomes"},it="name",add="7550d48d"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may see leper gnomes as a reminder of Gnomeregan's fall and the cost of Mekkatorque's trust in Thermaplugg. Exiled gnomes in Tinker Town grieve for them and remain determined to find a cure.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may find common ground with these irradiated outcasts. Forsaken apothecaries look past their diseased forms and put their mechanical skills to work in Undercity labs.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may recognize that leper gnomes retain an uncanny skill for assembly lines, automated defense turrets, and high-voltage devices, even in their madness."},kw={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","leper gnome","mekkatorque","radiation","recombobulation","thermaplugg","toxic"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","topic:gnome","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","quest:412","subzone:tinkers-court","topic:trogg","zone:undercity"},src={"Leper gnome"}}
E["topic:lich-king"] = {t="topic",n="Lich King",z="general",s="In Icecrown, the Lich King commands the undead Scourge from the frozen throne. Kil'jaeden made him from the spirit of the orc shaman ner'zhul. His power drew Prince Arthas Menethil toward corruption, until the two joined atop Northrend's icy peaks.",h="In Icecrown, the Lich King commands the undead Scourge from the frozen throne.",sec={{t="Birth of the Frozen God",b="Ner'zhul fled dying Draenor, but Kil'jaeden seized him. The demon lord tore away his body and bound his tormented soul in diamond-hard ice from the Twisting Nether. That glacial prison struck Northrend's northern wastes and formed the frozen throne.\n\nKil'jaeden meant the Lich King to forge an unstoppable undead vanguard. It would break the mortal kingdoms without the infighting that had ruined the Orcish Horde. Yet Ner'zhul wielded immense telepathic power, and began at once to plot his freedom.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Lordaeron",b="Watching dreadlords guarded Ner'zhul closely, so he acted in secret. Through his mind, he ensnared Kel'Thuzad, an exiled Kirin Tor archmage. Kel'Thuzad founded the Cult of the Damned in Lordaeron, where cauldrons of tainted grain spread the Plague of Undeath through the northern kingdoms.\n\nPrince Arthas Menethil rushed to save his people, but desperation drove him to ruthless acts, including the infamous slaughter of Stratholme. Seeking vengeance against the dreadlord Mal'Ganis, Arthas pursued him to Northrend. There Frostmourne waited to steal his soul and make him the Scourge's foremost death knight.",sp=0},{t="Treachery and Ascendance",b="For a time, the Lich King summoned Archimonde and yielded command to the Burning Legion. He expected the demons' hubris. Arthas turned the demon hunter Illidan Stormrage toward the Skull of Gul'dan and Tichondrius's death. That helped bring about Archimonde's ruin at Mount Hyjal.\n\nAfterward, a desperate Kil'jaeden ordered Illidan to destroy the frozen throne. Cracks in the icy spire weakened Ner'zhul's power, and Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken broke free. The Lich King summoned his champion back. Arthas returned to Northrend, defeated Illidan at icecrown's foot, climbed the spire, and shattered the ice. He joined with Ner'zhul as one terrible consciousness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Lich King right now?",a="The Lich King is Prince Arthas Menethil joined with the orc shaman Ner'zhul. Arthas shattered the glacial prison atop the frozen throne in Icecrown and donned the Helm of Domination. His mortal form and dark soul joined with Ner'zhul's spirit, and he rules the Scourge.",al={"current lich king","who rules the scourge","is arthas the lich king"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the Burning Legion create him?",a="Kil'jaeden made the Lich King to weaken Azeroth's defenders before a full demonic invasion. The previous invasion had failed amid the mortal Orcish Horde's internal quarrels. So Kil'jaeden sought an army of the dead under telepathic control, one that would obey and exhaust mortal armies.",al={"why make lich king","kiljaeden purpose","legion scourge origin"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Lich King located?",a="The Lich King sits on the frozen throne atop Icecrown's glacier, in remote, frozen Northrend. The continent lies far across the Great Sea, north of Lordaeron.",al={"where is frozen throne","lich king location","where does he live"},it="place"},{q="How did Sylvanas break free from his control?",a="Illidan Stormrage struck the frozen throne with powerful sorcery, fracturing its ice and weakening the Lich King's power. Some undead regained their free will, rallied under Sylvanas Windrunner, and founded the Forsaken.",al={"how did forsaken break free","why sylvanas free","scourge loss of control"},it="history"},{q="What is Frostmourne?",a="Frostmourne is a cursed runeblade that steals souls. It was sent from the frozen throne to draw in a mortal champion. In Northrend, it lured Prince Arthas Menethil to claim it, devoured his soul, and made him the Scourge's foremost death knight.",al={"what sword did arthas use","frostmourne lore","runeblade"},it="item"},{q="Who was Ner'zhul?",a="Ner'zhul was an elder orc shaman of Draenor. As he fled his dying homeworld through dimensional rifts, Kil'jaeden captured him, tore away his flesh, and warped his spirit into the all-seeing mind that became the Lich King.",al={"nerzhul lore","who was nerzhul","original lich king"},it="history"},{q="Why are the Lich King and his Scourge hostile to all living travelers?",a="The Lich King seeks the utter extinction and subjugation of mortal life. Every living creature slain by his plague or his unholy legions can be reanimated under his absolute mental command, expanding his power exponentially. He sees mortal races not as neighbors, but as raw material to swell his eternal Scourge.",al={"why is lich king hostile","scourge hostility","why does the lich king attack the living"},it="hostile",add="66564786"},{q="Who is allied with the Lich King?",a="The Lich King works with no living nations. He commands the Undead Scourge directly through psychic domination, supported by mortal necromancers and zealots in the Cult of the Damned like Kel'Thuzad. Though created by the demon lord Kil'jaeden, he secretly betrayed the Burning Legion to pursue his own supreme dominion over Azeroth.",al={"lich king allies","who works for lich king","who does the lich king serve"},it="allies",add="b2423b94"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken began when the Lich King's telepathic grip faltered. Queen Sylvanas leads her people with burning hatred for their former master in the frozen north.",["race:Human"]="For humans, the Lich King is bound to a terrible tragedy. Prince Arthas, heir to Lordaeron's throne and a paladin of the Silver Hand, murdered his father and destroyed his kingdom in the entity's name.",["class:Paladin"]="The Order of the Silver Hand was shattered by the Lich King's corrupting power. That power made their greatest champion a death knight, and he struck down Uther the Lightbringer.",["class:Priest"]="The Scourge twists the Light's sanctity into something grim. It reminds holy practitioners of the terrible cost paid across Lordaeron's fallen parishes."},kw={"arthas","cult of the damned","frostmourne","frozen throne","helm of domination","icecrown","kiljaeden","lich king","nerzhul","scourge"},rel={"topic:arthas-menethil","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:cult-of-the-damned","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:lordaeron","topic:burning-legion","subzone:stratholme"},src={"Lich King"}}
E["topic:light"] = {t="topic",n="Light",z="general",s="Across creation, Light flows through living things, and its power is called upon in Azeroth as Holy magic. Faith and will can turn it to healing, shelter, or a strike against darkness.",h="Across creation, Light flows through living things, and its power is called upon in Azeroth as Holy magic.",sec={{t="A Primal Force",b="Across creation, Light flows as living energy. In Azeroth, it takes the form of Holy magic, moving through living souls and binding mortal hearts. Mortals may picture it as a conscious protector. Yet Light answers the absolute conviction of the soul that calls upon it.",sp=0},{t="Instruments of Faith",b="Channeling Light calls for self-abnegation, disciplined meditation, and unshakable will. Priests of the Church of the Holy Light and holy paladins train for years to become clear vessels for its radiance. Through devotion, Light can mend wounds with restorative warmth and shelter the innocent with brilliant wards. It can also strike demons and the risen undead with searing fire.",sp=0},{t="Many Faces of Radiance",b="Humans and dwarves revere Light through formal scripture, while other peoples follow their own spiritual traditions. Night elves devote themselves to Elune and channel sacred moonlight, weaving holy magic to cleanse and protect. Tauren honor the sun deity An'she through their own spiritual traditions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Light?",a="Light is a fundamental cosmic energy found across creation. As a primal source of life and positive energy, it binds sentient souls together. Mortals call upon it for Holy magic that heals, protects, and aids them in warfare.",al={"holy light lore","what is the holy light","the light explained"},it="identity"},{q="Does the Light have a conscious will or mind?",a="Light is a primal cosmic force rather than a god. Mortals may speak of its will and treat it as a guiding patron, but it does not share mortal morality. It answers the caster's certainty, willpower, and faith.",al={"is the light alive","does light have a mind","is the light a god"}},{q="Why can evil zealots still use the Light?",a="Light answers conviction, not abstract righteousness. If a caster has absolute faith that their cause is just and an undivided spirit, Light can flow through them, even when their deeds are ruthless or misguided.",al={"why do scarlet crusade have light","can bad guys use the light","evil paladins light"}},{q="How does the Light affect the undead?",a="Holy magic is a powerful weapon against the Scourge, yet it can also heal undead bodies. Channeling Light or receiving its healing brings intense pain to the undead, but does not automatically burn away their flesh.",al={"light vs undead","why does light hurt scourge","can undead use light"}},{q="How do priests and paladins learn to wield it?",a="Wielding Light takes rigorous mental discipline, emotional clarity, and years of meditation. A caster must quiet personal ego and focus their spirit entirely, becoming a clear conduit through which Holy magic pours into the world.",al={"how to use holy magic","paladin magic source","priest light training"}},{q="Is Elune's magic connected to the Light?",a="Yes. The moonlight channeled by Elune's priestesses appears as holy magic. It can restore, protect, and purify, like the spells wielded by paladins and church priests.",al={"is elune holy magic","elune and the light","moonlight holy light"}},{q="Where did the Light come from?",a="Its true origins are unknown. Priests of the Church of the Holy Light teach that the Light dwells within all living beings, but where the Light itself comes from remains a mystery.",al={"origin of the light","where did light come from","how was the light created","history of the holy light"},it="history",add="73e6193d"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you join martial discipline and your mortal body with Light. You wield its incandescent fury against the Scourge and demonic evil.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you serve as a spiritual shepherd and conduit. Through deep meditation and prayer, you mend flesh, steady broken spirits, and shield allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find Stormwind and Ironforge's spiritual bedrock in the Church of the Holy Light. It offers hope in an era darkened by Lordaeron's fall.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, channeling Light or receiving its healing brings you intense pain, even when the spell mends your body.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you channel holy energy through reverence for the moon goddess Elune and her silver light, rather than church doctrine.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you revere An'she, the golden right eye of the Earth Mother, through traditional sun worship."},kw={"an'she","church","elune","faith","healing","holy light","holy magic","light","paladin","priest","scourge"},rel={"topic:church-of-the-holy-light","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:elune","topic:lordaeron","topic:tauren","topic:alliance","quest:99134","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Light"}}
E["topic:llane-wrynn-i"] = {t="topic",n="Llane Wrynn I",z="general",s="Stormwind's defense falters as the First War turns against King Llane Wrynn I and his kingdom. Beloved and proud, Llane cannot accept that his friend Medivh has betrayed humanity, and that refusal dooms the capital.",h="Stormwind's defense falters as the First War turns against King Llane Wrynn I and his kingdom.",sec={{t="A Prince of Reckless Valor",b="Born to King Barathen Wrynn, Prince Llane grew up with Anduin Lothar and Medivh. As youths, the three friends ventured into Stranglethorn Vale's jungles and clashed with the Gurubashi trolls. In time, Llane took the throne as Stormwind's king.",sp=0},{t="The First War",b="When green-skinned strangers came from the southern swamps, King Llane sent Lothar to investigate the Black Morass. Minor skirmishes became the First War as the Horde overran the forests of Duskwood, Westfall, and Redridge. Messengers seeking aid from Lordaeron and the northern human kingdoms were turned away. Stormwind's long isolation and aristocratic intrigue weakened their pleas.\n\nEven so, Llane and Lothar led a daring counterattack. They broke the Horde's first siege of Stormwind and dealt the invaders their first major defeat.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal in the Keep",b="King Llane's steadfastness left him blind to danger in his own circle. Medivh's apprentice Khadgar and the emissary Garona told Llane that the Guardian had opened the Dark Portal. He refused to believe his childhood friend had betrayed him.\n\nSoon after, Orgrim Doomhammer united the Horde and breached Stormwind's outer defenses. Llane directed the defense from Stormwind Keep. Under the Shadow Council's magical influence, Garona murdered the King in his throne room, carved out his heart, and sealed the city's doom.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who was King Llane Wrynn I?",a="King Llane Wrynn I ruled the Kingdom of Stormwind during the First War. He was the father of King Varian Wrynn and grandfather of young Prince Anduin Llane Wrynn. He died defending his people during Stormwind's first fall.",al={"who is llane","llane wrynn lore","king llane"},it="identity"},{q="How did King Llane die?",a="Llane was assassinated in Stormwind Keep during the First War's final siege. Garona Halforcen, a half-orc emissary he trusted as a friend and confidante, killed him under the Shadow Council's mind control.",al={"who killed king llane","llane death","how did llane die"},it="conflict"},{q="What was Llane's relationship to Medivh and Lothar?",a="Llane, Medivh, and Anduin Lothar were childhood companions who adventured across southern Azeroth. Lothar became Llane's greatest champion. Llane's refusal to believe Medivh could betray him led to his downfall.",al={"llane medivh lothar","llane childhood friends"},it="allies"},{q="Why didn't the other human kingdoms help Llane during the First War?",a="Stormwind had long followed an isolationist foreign policy that northern nations saw as arrogant. When Llane warned of the green-skinned invaders, Lordaeron's leaders dismissed the reports as an exaggerated civil rebellion. Stormwind was left to fight alone.",al={"why didn't lordaeron help llane","alliance during first war"}},{q="How did Varian escape the fall of Stormwind?",a="After King Llane's murder and Stormwind Keep's fall, Champion Anduin Lothar gathered the surviving citizens and Llane's young son, Prince Varian Wrynn. Lothar led them to the harbor, then fled north across the Great Sea to Lordaeron.",al={"what happened to varian after llane died","varian escape stormwind"},it="history"},{q="What did Medivh give Llane at his ascension?",a="When Llane came of age as Prince of Stormwind, Medivh emerged from a long coma and gave him an enchanted obsidian hourglass. Its sand trickled endlessly, and its upper chamber never emptied, symbolizing Stormwind's eternal prosperity.",al={"medivh gift to llane","llane hourglass"},it="item"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="King Llane's murder and Stormwind's fall drove the survivors north. This directly prompted the creation of the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron to oppose the Horde.",["race:Human"]="For Stormwind's people, King Llane remains a tragic hero. His sacrifice is honored across the restored city, including in the name of King Varian's son, Anduin Llane Wrynn.",["class:Warrior"]="King Llane fought beside his Champion, Anduin Lothar, and directed Stormwind's martial defense from the front lines of the Keep.",["class:Rogue"]="Garona's assassination of King Llane remains one of Azeroth's most famous and devastating blade strikes."},kw={"barathen","first war","garona","gurubashi","kingslayers","llane","lothar","medivh","shadow council","stormwind","wrynn"},rel={"topic:varian-wrynn","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:first-war","topic:medivh","topic:stormwind-kingdom","subzone:stormwind-keep","topic:shadow-council","npc:orgrim-doomhammer"},src={"Llane Wrynn I"}}
E["topic:lordaeron"] = {t="topic",n="Lordaeron",z="general",s="Across Lordaeron, the Scourge, Sylvanas Windrunner’s Forsaken, and desperate survivors contest the ruined kingdoms. Once the heart of human civilization and the Alliance, the northern subcontinent was laid waste in the Third War.",h="Across Lordaeron, the Scourge, Sylvanas Windrunner’s Forsaken, and desperate survivors contest the ruined...",sec={{t="Cradle of Northern Humanity",b="Lordaeron takes its name from the human city-state that rose in the north after the ancient Empire of Arathor. In time, it became the most powerful of the human kingdoms. The region runs from the rugged Arathi Highlands in the south, across forests and waterways, toward Quel'Thalas.\n\nIt nurtured kingdoms such as Lordaeron, Dalaran, Gilneas, and Alterac. Tirisfal and Hillsbrad were known for fertile farmland, while mountains held strongholds. The land was also a sacred cradle of the Holy Light.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge and the Fall",b="During the Third War, the Lich King's invasion struck Lordaeron first. The Cult of the Damned used tainted grain to turn countless northern citizens into mindless undead. Prince Arthas Menethil fell to darkness, then returned from Northrend and killed his father, King Terenas Menethil II. He orchestrated the slaughter of the Capital City. The thriving heartland soon rotted into the blighted Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Wasteland",b="Lordaeron is now a brutal battleground of fractured loyalties. Beneath the Capital City's ruins, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken have made the Undercity, a sovereign realm of free-willed undead aligned with the Horde. In the east, the Lich King's mindless Scourge hold corrupted keeps and strongholds. Human zealots of the Scarlet Crusade, surviving Alliance settlements in Hillsbrad, and wild forest trolls clash over what remains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What exactly is Lordaeron?",a="Lordaeron names both the northern subcontinent of the Eastern Kingdoms and the former human kingdom that ruled its central lands. The region stretches from the Thandol Span at the Arathi border north toward Quel'Thalas, across mountains, forests, and inland lakes.",al={"is lordaeron a continent","what does lordaeron mean","lordaeron geography"},it="identity"},{q="Who controls Lordaeron right now?",a="No single power controls all of Lordaeron. Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken hold Tirisfal Glades and Silverpine from their subterranean Undercity. The Scourge, under Kel'Thuzad, remains powerful in the Plaguelands, while the Scarlet Crusade, the Kingdom of Stormwind's allies in Hillsbrad, and troll tribes hold isolated frontiers.",al={"who rules lordaeron","who owns lordaeron now","current ruler of lordaeron"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to the original living humans of Lordaeron?",a="Most of Lordaeron's people died during the Third War, struck down by the plague of undeath or Arthas's Scourge army. Many dead were raised into mindless servitude, then later regained their minds and became the Forsaken. The living who survived fled south to Stormwind, sailed to Kalimdor with Jaina Proudmoore, or joined militant enclaves such as the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"where did the people of lordaeron go","did lordaeron humans die","what happened to lordaeron"},it="people"},{q="Why was the subcontinent named Lordaeron?",a="The northern land took its name from the city-state of Lordaeron, which rose after the ancient Empire of Arathor and became one of humanity's most powerful kingdoms. Its name eventually spread across the whole subcontinent.",al={"origin of name lordaeron","who is lordaeron named after","lordain name"},it="name"},{q="Where is the Capital City of Lordaeron?",a="The Capital City of Lordaeron stands on the northern shore of Lordamere Lake in Tirisfal Glades. Its surface streets and palace courtyards lie in silent ruins, while Sylvanas Windrunner has turned the catacombs below into the Undercity, capital of the Forsaken.",al={"where was lordaeron city","capital of lordaeron","ruins of lordaeron location"},it="place"},{q="Is Lordaeron part of the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Lordaeron is bitterly contested. Its kingdom founded and led the original Alliance of Lordaeron. Now the Undercity is an official Horde capital and western Lordaeron is a Horde stronghold, while Alliance forces struggle to hold their few outposts in Hillsbrad and Arathi.",al={"is lordaeron alliance or horde","who claims lordaeron"},it="side"},{q="What is the history of Lordaeron?",a="Originally settled by human tribes following the era of the Empire of Arathor, Lordaeron grew into one of humanity's most powerful kingdoms and gave its name to the entire northern continent. For generations, its realm encompassed rich farmlands and strong cities, standing as the bulwark of the Alliance during the Second War. That glory crumbled in the Third War, when the Scourge unleashed the plague of undeath upon its lands, tearing the kingdom apart and reducing its once-thriving territories to the blighted Plaguelands and contested ruins you see today.",al={"history of lordaeron","lordaeron lore","where did lordaeron come from"},it="history",add="ca72f255"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Lordaeron was your homeland in life. You walk the Capital City's ruined courtyards as an heir claiming what is yours under Lady Sylvanas.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, Lordaeron is a sacred tragedy. It was the cradle of the Holy Light and leader of the original Alliance. Seeing undead overrun its halls brings grief and fury.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance once took its name from Lordaeron. Now its footholds in Hillsbrad and its fight against the Scourge in the Plaguelands mark a painful struggle to recover human heritage.",["faction:Horde"]="Through their Forsaken allies, the Horde holds a vital, contested foothold in the northern Eastern Kingdoms. It surrounds Alliance outposts and confronts the Scourge's remnants.",["class:Paladin"]="The Order of the Silver Hand began in Lordaeron at the Chapel of Alonsus Faol. These northern roads and ruins hold the history of the earliest paladins."},kw={"hillsbrad","lordaeron","menethil","plaguelands","scourge","silverpine","terenas","tirisfal","undercity"},rel={"topic:third-war","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal","zone:westernplaguelands","zone:easternplaguelands","zone:hillsbrad","zone:silverpine","zone:arathi"},src={"Lordaeron"}}
E["topic:mage"] = {t="topic",n="Mage",z="general",s="For a mage, arcane power answers to study, while the body remains frail beneath cloth armor. Fire, frost, and raw arcane force make mages formidable allies and dangerous foes. They conjure, teleport, and control the field of battle, but their discipline demands deep focus. Misused arcane power has left a perilous legacy.",h="For a mage, arcane power answers to study, while the body remains frail beneath cloth armor.",sec={{t="Scholars of the Arcane",b="A mage’s path asks for intellect, focus, and years of study. Magi neither commune with spirits nor rely on divine faith; they approach magic as a precise cosmic science. Drawing on arcane energies, they unleash raw destruction, summon searing flame, or chill air into solid ice and howling blizzards. Heavy armor hinders the delicate gestures and concentration their incantations require, so they wear light cloth. Wards, mana barriers, and evasive spells help keep them safe.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Dalaran and Arathor",b="Human magical tradition began nearly three millennia ago during the Troll Wars. High elven sorcerers taught one hundred humans of the Empire of Arathor to help turn the tide against the Amani. As more humans took up magic, citizens without such skill grew fearful, driving many magi to found the magocracy of Dalaran.\n\nGoverned by the Kirin Tor, Dalaran became the northern kingdoms’ central archive of magical study. There, combat magic took shape in traditions that served the Alliance of Lordaeron through the First and Second Wars.",sp=0},{t="Suspicion and Necessity",b="Arcane practitioners have never won easy trust. The ancient cataclysm wrought by the Highborne and Dalaran’s fall during the Third War left many wary of magic’s volatile nature. The Church of the Holy Light has long viewed wizardry with suspicion.\n\nConservative knights have regarded arcane spellcasters as damned souls or a necessary evil in battle. Yet civil and military leaders know a capable magus can bring battlefield supremacy, swift mass transport, and vital defenses against supernatural threats.",sp=0},{t="Mages of the Horde and the High Order",b="The arcane belongs to more than the Alliance. Troll and Forsaken mages serve the Horde, and orcs who study the art begin under Mai'ah, a Darkspear mage in the Valley of Trials. Mai'ah teaches that patience and careful judgment matter more than raw power.\n\nAmong the Skyborne, the High Order descends from the Highborne of Eldre'Thalas. Their time in Skywall cost them much of their ancestors’ arcane knowledge. With the wind spirits gone from Zephras Isle, they seek to recover it. Skyborne mages fight for the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What schools of magic do mages specialize in?",a="Mages study three core schools: Arcane, Fire, and Frost. Arcane alters time, space, and reality, allowing polymorphing, teleportation, and focused bursts of power. Fire brings swift, overwhelming combustion, while Frost slows, snares, and shatters foes before they can close to melee range.",al={"mage specs","mage magic types","arcane fire frost"}},{q="Why do mages only wear cloth armor?",a="Complex spells require free movement, precise hand gestures, and steady mental focus. Heavy materials such as leather, chainmail, or plate interfere with the gestures and concentration needed for incantations. Mages guard their physical vulnerability with magical barriers and spells that keep enemies at bay.",al={"why cloth","mage armor type","can mages wear leather"}},{q="How did humans first learn to cast arcane magic?",a="During the ancient Troll Wars, roughly two thousand eight hundred years ago, the human Empire of Arathor allied with the high elves of Quel'Thalas against the Amani trolls. In return for military aid, elven magi taught one hundred humans the fundamentals of arcane magic. These pioneers proved devastating in battle and began the human magical lineage that eventually founded Dalaran.",al={"first human mages","troll wars mages","human magic origin"}},{q="What is the relationship between mages and the Church of the Holy Light?",a="The Church of the Holy Light and mages have a tense relationship. For centuries, orthodox members of the Church viewed arcane studies and the Kirin Tor with suspicion, sometimes treating them as heretical. Paladins and devout priests often see wizardry as unpredictable and morally dubious, though its strength in war makes it necessary.",al={"church views on mages","paladins and mages","holy light arcane heresy"}},{q="Are Stormwind's mages part of Dalaran's Kirin Tor?",a="Stormwind’s mages historically followed their own traditions, first led by court conjurers who worked largely apart from Dalaran. The Kirin Tor remained the northern center of magical learning, while southern wizards built their own enclaves and royal advisory roles. Communication and common ties between both realms endured.",al={"stormwind mages dalaran","conjurers of azeroth","stormwind wizards"}},{q="Can mages create food and transport people instantly?",a="Yes. Mages conjure fresh food and water from thin air, enchant allies’ intellects, and bend space to open portals that instantly connect major cities across the world.",al={"mage utility","mage portals","conjure water food"}},{q="Which races can be mages?",a="Humans, gnomes, and the Skyborne train as Alliance mages; trolls, the Forsaken, and orcs serve as Horde mages. Dwarves, night elves, and tauren do not. Night elves shun the arcane after Queen Azshara’s Highborne brought ruin to ancient Kalimdor.",al={"who can be a mage","mage races","can orcs be mages","orc mage","skyborne mage"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you need meticulous intellectual discipline. You master fire, frost, and arcane force while guarding the fragile balance of reality.",["race:Human"]="Your people’s arcane legacy reaches back to the hundred original magi taught during the Troll Wars. Their descendants built Dalaran into a great center of magical study.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you belong to a society that strictly shuns arcane magic, remembering the ruin Queen Azshara and her Highborne magi brought upon ancient Kalimdor.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you fight beside magi, though the Knights of the Silver Hand have long regarded their worldly arcane methods with deep caution.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you share a path many began as mages, before they abandoned academic restraint and strict Dalaran edicts to pursue demonic power.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc mage, you begin your studies under Mai'ah, a Darkspear mage in the Valley of Trials. Mai'ah teaches patience and careful judgment before power.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne mage of the High Order, you seek to recover the Highborne spellcraft your ancestors carried out of Eldre'Thalas, hoping it can save your failing island."},kw={"arcane","conjuration","dalaran","fire","frost","kirin tor","mage","magus","mana","spellcaster","teleport","wizard"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","topic:highborne","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:medivh","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:stormwind","topic:skyborne","npc:mai-ah"},src={"Mage"}}
E["topic:medivh"] = {t="topic",n="Medivh",z="general",s="The Dark Portal stands open, and Medivh's hand has begun the First War. He was the last Guardian of Tirisfal, an ancient order sworn to defend Azeroth from demonic corruption. Yet Sargeras's spirit had bound itself to Medivh before his birth.",h="The Dark Portal stands open, and Medivh's hand has begun the First War.",sec={{t="A Cursed Heritage",b="Born to Aegwynn, a powerful Guardian, and Nielas Aran, a court conjurer, Medivh inherited a cursed legacy. Centuries earlier, Aegwynn fought the fallen Titan Sargeras in Northrend, unaware that his dark essence had slipped into her body to await an heir. On Medivh's fourteenth birthday, the vast magic he inherited from his mother burst forth in a terrifying display. The boy fell into a coma that lasted a decade, watched over by clerics at Northshire Abbey.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Karazhan",b="When Medivh awoke, he took up residence in the remote tower of Karazhan. He served as court magus to his childhood friend, King Llane Wrynn of Stormwind. The dark spirit within him slowly wore away his sanity. Seeking to unleash devastation, Medivh reached across the stars to Gul'dan, an orc warlock, and the Shadow Council.\n\nTogether they wielded tremendous magic to tear open the Dark Portal. The Horde poured into the Eastern Kingdoms, beginning the First War. Medivh died in his tower at the hands of his closest friend, Anduin Lothar, and his apprentice, Khadgar.",sp=0},{t="The Prophet's Redemption",b="Medivh returned from beyond death, free of Sargeras and seeking to atone for his crimes. During the Third War, he wore a raven cloak and the guise of an enigmatic Prophet. He warned King Terenas Menethil and Warchief Thrall that the Burning Legion was returning.\n\nLordaeron ignored his pleas, but Medivh guided Thrall's Horde and Jaina Proudmoore's refugees across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. There, orcs, humans, and night elves united for the decisive stand at Mount Hyjal. Medivh then faded into myth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Medivh?",a="Medivh was the last human Guardian of Tirisfal, gifted with immense arcane power to defend Azeroth. Magna Aegwynn was his mother, and he opened the Dark Portal.",al={"who is medivh","medivh lore","the last guardian"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Medivh open the Dark Portal?",a="Sargeras's spirit possessed Medivh before he was born. Under its influence, Medivh bargained with the warlock Gul'dan, trading the location of the Tomb of Sargeras for the Horde's invasion of Azeroth and the ruin of the mortal kingdoms.",al={"why did medivh betray stormwind","medivh dark portal","why bring orcs"},it="motive"},{q="Who killed Medivh?",a="During the First War, Medivh faced his close friend Anduin Lothar, his apprentice Khadgar, and the half-orc assassin Garona in Karazhan. Khadgar pierced Medivh's heart, and Lothar severed his head, ending his life and casting Sargeras's spirit back into the Nether.",al={"how did medivh die","who killed the guardian","medivh death"},it="conflict"},{q="What was Medivh's relationship with Stormwind's royalty?",a="Medivh grew up at Stormwind's royal court alongside Prince Llane Wrynn and Anduin Lothar. The three fought Gurubashi trolls together in their youth, and King Llane trusted Medivh completely. Medivh's betrayal brought devastating grief to the kingdom.",al={"medivh and llane","was medivh friends with lothar"},it="ties"},{q="Is Medivh still alive?",a="After guiding the mortal races to victory over Archimonde at the Battle of Mount Hyjal, Medivh left for the legends of the past. His whereabouts since are unknown.",al={"where is medivh now","is the prophet medivh","medivh status"},sp=1,it="today"},{q="What is Karazhan?",a="Karazhan is a spire atop a potent meeting of ley lines in Deadwind Pass. Aegwynn established the tower, and Medivh later inherited it. Arcane and demonic energies warped it after the Guardian fell, and it remains a haunted ruin.",al={"medivh tower","what happened to karazhan"},it="place"},{q="Where did Medivh come from?",a="Medivh was born to Magna Aegwynn, the Guardian of Tirisfal, and Nielas Aran, a mage of the Kirin Tor. Unknown to his parents, the dark titan Sargeras possessed Medivh in his mother's womb. Raised among the court of Stormwind as a close childhood friend to Prince Llane Wrynn and Anduin Lothar, his inherited magical powers violently manifested on the eve of his fourteenth birthday, casting Medivh into a decade-long coma.",al={"medivh history","medivh origin","medivh past"},it="history",add="121458c2"},{q="What does the name Medivh mean?",a="Medivh means \"keeper of secrets\" in Thalassian, the tongue of the high elves. Given to him at birth by his mother, Aegwynn, the name proved chillingly fitting for a Guardian who concealed both the boundless power of Tirisfal and the insidious corruption of Sargeras within his soul.",al={"what does medivh mean","medivh name meaning","meaning of medivh"},it="name",add="2cdc20e2"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see Medivh as both the height of arcane mastery and its peril. Kirin Tor scholars study his fall as a warning against unchecked power.",["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you know Medivh's communion with Gul'dan and his place as Sargeras's mortal conduit. His story remains a legendary display of fel summoning and interplanar manipulation.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you may remember Medivh with bitter sorrow. Stormwind loved him as a companion to the royal family, yet he brought the ruinous Horde into its lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Medivh as the human sorcerer whose bargain with Gul'dan opened the Dark Portal and first brought the orcs into this world."},kw={"aegwynn","atiesh","dark portal","guardian","karazhan","khadgar","lothar","medivh","sargeras","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","subzone:dark-portal","topic:sargeras","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:first-war","topic:third-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Medivh"}}
E["topic:muradin-bronzebeard"] = {t="topic",n="Muradin Bronzebeard",z="multi",s="Across Khaz Modan and Lordaeron, Muradin Bronzebeard is honored for his skill in war and diplomacy. Brother to King Magni Bronzebeard and Brann Bronzebeard, he helped found the Explorers' League. In Northrend, he is believed to have died when Prince Arthas Menethil claimed Frostmourne.",h="Across Khaz Modan and Lordaeron, Muradin Bronzebeard is honored for his skill in war and diplomacy.",sec={{t="A Brother and Ambassador",b="In the Second War, Muradin carried messages between Khaz Modan's mountain halls and the Alliance of Lordaeron. He helped defend Ironforge during the Horde's siege, then marched with Alliance forces through Blackrock Spire to the Dark Portal.\n\nAfter peace came, Muradin settled in Capital City as Ironforge's official ambassador. Jovial yet formidable, he became a familiar face in the palace and grew close to King Terenas Menethil. He also taught young Prince Arthas the arts of swordplay and combat.",sp=0},{t="The Explorers' League and Northrend",b="Muradin's curiosity ranged beyond politics and war. With his brothers, he helped found the dwarven Explorers' League, devoted to finding lost titan relics and recording the world's farthest corners. He loved Northrend and often traveled north to sketch ancient buildings and document its fierce inhabitants.\n\nThe continent's rugged mysteries drew Muradin on his final expedition. He sought lore and relics there, and followed whispers of a forgotten runeblade.",sp=0},{t="The Claiming of Frostmourne",b="Prince Arthas came to Northrend to hunt the dreadlord Mal'Ganis. There he met Muradin again and enlisted the dwarven expedition. Arthas sought Frostmourne's power to turn the tide, while Muradin grew alarmed as the prince betrayed his mercenaries and cast honor aside.\n\nAt the blade's altar, Muradin read the warning carved into its icy pedestal. He pleaded with his former pupil to turn back, but Arthas refused. When the prince seized Frostmourne, unholy ice burst outward and struck Muradin down. He lay apparently dead on the cavern floor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Muradin Bronzebeard?",a="Muradin Bronzebeard was the middle brother of King Magni Bronzebeard and the explorer Brann. A veteran of the Second War, he served as Ironforge's ambassador to Lordaeron and helped found the Explorers' League.",al={"who is muradin","muradin lore","magni brother muradin"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Muradin in Northrend?",a="Muradin accompanied Prince Arthas to the cavern where Frostmourne lay. Arthas ignored his warnings and shattered the icy prison around the runeblade. An enchanted shard struck Muradin, seemingly killing him on the spot. Arthas left his body and took the blade.",al={"how did muradin die","muradin death","did arthas kill muradin"},it="history"},{q="What was Muradin's relationship with Prince Arthas?",a="As Ironforge's ambassador in Capital City, Muradin took Arthas under his wing. He taught the young prince bladed combat and shared many adventures with him. Muradin saw Arthas almost as a surrogate son or beloved nephew, until Arthas's dark descent in Northrend.",al={"did muradin know arthas","muradin arthas teacher","muradin and arthas"},it="ties"},{q="What was Muradin's role in the Second War?",a="Muradin served as the Alliance liaison between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan. He defended Ironforge during the Horde's siege, then marched south with the united Alliance army to fight at Blackrock Spire and the Dark Portal.",al={"muradin second war","muradin battles","did muradin fight the horde"},it="history"},{q="Why did Muradin go to Northrend in the first place?",a="As a founder of the Explorers' League, Muradin was fascinated by Northrend's archaeology and ancient ruins. He returned on an expedition to uncover forgotten history and seek relics, and his search led him onto Frostmourne's trail.",al={"why was muradin in northrend","muradin expedition","what was muradin looking for"},it="motive"},{q="How did King Magni react to Muradin's death?",a="King Magni and the entire Bronzebeard clan were devastated by Muradin's loss. His apparent death severed Ironforge's once-warm bond with Prince Arthas, turning grief to bitter fury toward the Scourge.",al={"magni muradin reaction","ironforge muradin grief"}},{q="Who was Muradin Bronzebeard allied with?",a="Muradin was fiercely loyal to the Alliance of Lordaeron and his own people of Khaz Modan. As a prince of the Bronzebeard clan, he answered directly to his brother, King Magni Bronzebeard, while serving as Ironforge's official ambassador to the royal court of Lordaeron. There, he developed strong ties with King Terenas Menethil II and Prince Arthas. Muradin also helped found the dwarven Explorers' League, leading intrepid teams of dwarven archaeologists and adventurers into the world's most remote corners under Ironforge's banner.",al={"muradin bronzebeard allies","who did muradin work for","muradin factions"},it="allies",add="3bcb591a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can remember Muradin as a paragon of your people: brave, fiercely loyal, and driven by curiosity about the history of your makers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of Ironforge, you can remember how Muradin forged bonds of camaraderie between the dwarves and the northern human kingdoms. He was one of the Alliance's founding heroes.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can look to Muradin, one of the finest dwarven duelists and weapon masters of his age. He taught Prince Arthas Menethil the art of the blade."},kw={"arthas","bronzebeard","explorers league","frostmourne","ironforge","magni","muradin","northrend"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:brann-bronzebeard","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:bronzebeard-clan","topic:explorers-league","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war"},src={"Muradin Bronzebeard"}}
E["topic:murloc"] = {t="topic",n="Murloc",z="general",s="Along Azeroth's shores, lakes, and rivers, Murloc tribes gather and press inland from the deep ocean. Their cries and sudden swarms make them a threat, yet their deeds hint at minds sharper than their looks suggest.",h="Along Azeroth's shores, lakes, and rivers, Murloc tribes gather and press inland from the deep ocean.",sec={{t="Creatures of the Shallows",b="Murlocs gather along coasts, riverbanks, and freshwater lakes. They stand about four feet tall, with bulbous bodies coated in slime and wide mouths full of sharp fangs. Their keen sight pierces pitch-black water, and few stray far from their kin. Where one appears, a dozen more may wait below the surface. Together, they overwhelm foes with numbers and crude, sharp weapons.",sp=0},{t="The Inland March",b="Ancient lineages say Murlocs lived beneath the waves before recorded history. Their spread onto Lordaeron and Kalimdor is recent, and began suspiciously alongside the naga's return from the ocean depths. Some tribes appear to worship monstrous beings in the deepest reaches. They may be fleeing darker terrors, or preparing the world for their masters' awakening. Their movement into freshwaters grows more coordinated, and more dangerous.",sp=0},{t="A Hidden Intellect",b="Outsiders hear bubbling Murloc speech and mistake it for nonsense, dismissing them as feral pests. Yet their ambushes are coordinated, and they practice earth and water magic and live in communities. Explorer Brann Bronzebeard has suggested they hide their cunning and are far smarter than civilized races realize.\n\nMurlocs have shaped history, too. Their raid on the Darkspear tribe brought Thrall to intervene. That intervention forged the bond between orcs and trolls that built the modern Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do murlocs attack all at once?",a="Murlocs rarely fight alone. Their crowded settlements answer intruders together, swarming them with overwhelming numbers.",al={"murloc swarming","why do murlocs group up","murloc aggro"},it="danger"},{q="Are murlocs actually intelligent?",a="Yes. Murlocs are far more intelligent than their comical appearance suggests. Most outsiders cannot understand their guttural, gurgling speech, but Murlocs make weapons, plan ambushes, and wield water and earth magic. Brann Bronzebeard believes they let others underestimate their minds.",al={"are murlocs smart","murloc intelligence","can murlocs think"},it="power"},{q="Why are murlocs moving inland from the sea?",a="Murlocs once lived on the ocean floor and have steadily spread into freshwater lakes and riverbeds. Historians suspect the naga's return or deep-sea beings sleeping in the abyss may have driven them inland. Those entities' awakening commands the Murlocs to secure the land.",al={"why are murlocs on land","murloc migration","why are murlocs everywhere"},it="why_here"},{q="How did murlocs help form the Horde?",a="During the Third War, Murlocs serving the sea witch Zar'jira ambushed the Darkspear trolls on their island home. Warchief Thrall and his orc warriors joined Sen'jin to defend them. The battle forged a lasting bond between orcs and the Darkspear tribe, laying the foundation of the modern Horde.",al={"murloc horde origin","murlocs and darkspear","thrall murloc island"},it="conflict"},{q="What are mur'gul?",a="Mur'gul are Murlocs encountered during the Third War. Despite their strange appearance and name, they are living creatures.",al={"mur'gul","warcraft iii murlocs","murgul identity"}},{q="What is that iconic sound murlocs make?",a="When hunting or sounding an alarm, Murlocs make a loud, wet, wavering gargle, often rendered as “Aaaaaughibbrgubugbugrguburgle” or “RwlRwlRwlRwl.” The sound can unsettle foes and call their pack to gather.",al={"murloc noise","murloc battle cry","rwlrwlrwl"}},{q="What are murlocs?",a="Murlocs are a bipedal, amphibious race found clustering along shores, lakes, and rivers across Azeroth. Averaging around four feet in height, they possess bulbous bodies, slimy skin, clawed digits, and mouths lined with razor-sharp fangs. While often dismissed as primitive fish-beasts due to their gurgling tongue, they construct communal settlements, wield handcrafted weaponry, and channel earth and water magic.",al={"what is a murloc","murloc race","who are the murlocs"},it="identity",add="87c77fd7"},{q="Why are murlocs hostile to travelers?",a="Murlocs are deeply insular creatures that shun dry-land mortals and hold almost no tolerance for other races. They fiercely protect their nesting grounds, egg caches, and food stores from outsiders. Combined with their habit of living in tightly packed encampments, any trespasser venturing near their shoreline settlements is quickly swarmed and driven off by the entire tribe.",al={"why do murlocs attack","murloc aggression","why are murlocs aggressive"},it="hostile",add="033f2da0"},{q="Where did murlocs come from?",a="Though they only recently invaded Azeroth's inland shores, murlocs are an ancient people. Their early forebears inhabited the abyssal depths of the world's oceans long before surface-dwellers ever knew of them, possibly predating even the trolls. In recent years, they have migrated steadily out of the oceanic abyss and adapted to freshwater waterways across the continents.",al={"murloc origin","history of murlocs","where do murlocs come from"},it="history",add="630a3c8a"},{q="Who are murlocs allied with?",a="Murlocs generally isolate themselves, but scholars suspect their emergence is tied to darker ocean powers. Some tribes revere sea witches or possibly slumbering deep-sea monstrosities waiting in the oceanic fathoms, carrying out rituals in their name.",al={"who do murlocs work for","murloc masters","murloc allies"},it="allies",add="b6922777"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear tribe has a bitter history with Murlocs. Coastal tribes captured Darkspear trolls for ritual sacrifice before the tribe joined Warchief Thrall.",["race:Orc"]="Thrall's warriors fought Murlocs while rescuing the Darkspear trolls at sea. They learned early that a comical appearance can hide savage brutality.",["faction:Alliance"]="Settlers across Westfall, Darkshore, and Lakeshire often find Murloc tribes besieging their shipping, farms, and docks.",["class:Shaman"]="Murloc mystics have a crude, innate bond with water and earth elementals. They bend local spirits to strengthen their shoreline villages."},kw={"brann bronzebeard","coastal","fin","mur'gul","murloc","rwlrwlrwl","shoreline","tadpole"},rel={"topic:naga","topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:thrall","zone:westfall","subzone:westfall-lighthouse","npc:brann-bronzebeard","topic:scourge","topic:gnoll"},src={"Murloc"}}
E["topic:naga"] = {t="topic",n="Naga",z="general",s="Along shores across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Naga press toward the surface. Once the Highborne elite of the Kaldorei Empire, they were changed in the Great Sundering and now serve their ancient empress, Queen Azshara, beneath the sea.",h="Along shores across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Naga press toward the surface.",sec={{t="Fall of the Highborne",b="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne ruled the Kaldorei Empire from Zin-Azshari. Queen Azshara and her inner court drew on the Well of Eternity, consumed by arcane power, to summon the Dark Titan Sargeras. Their act brought the invasion called the War of the Ancients. Then the Well collapsed and the Great Sundering began. The palace sank into the crushing abyss.\n\nFacing annihilation, Azshara bargained with the Old Gods below. They spared her and her followers, changing them into cold, scaly serpentine beings bound to the deep.",sp=0},{t="Depths of Nazjatar",b="Beneath the Maelstrom, the survivors built the underwater empire of Nazjatar. For ten thousand years, the naga kept their Highborne arrogance and their grudge against the surface world. They became distinct casts: hulking warriors and sea witches with many arms, who weave spells. Under Azshara's gaze, they mastered sea creatures, storm magic, and frost sorcery. Their strength grew as they waited for a chance to strike at those who lived on land.",sp=0},{t="The Resurfacing",b="The naga broke their silence during the Third War. Thrall's Horde first met the sea witch Zar'jira in the Great Sea. Lady Vashj answered Illidan Stormrage's summons and led naga forces through Dalaran's ruins.\n\nNow naga camps press against coasts in Azshara, Darkshore, Ashenvale, Desolace, Feralas, Dustwallow Marsh, Hillsbrad, Arathi, and Stranglethorn. Ancient contempt and whispers of the Old Gods drive them to forge quiet alliances with the Twilight's Hammer and savage satyrs. They seek to claim what was once theirs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the naga before they were transformed?",a="The naga were once the Highborne, the aristocratic upper class of the ancient night elven empire. During the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the Well of Eternity collapsed and Queen Azshara and her courtiers drowned in the sea. The Old Gods offered salvation and changed them into serpentine aquatic beings.",al={"what are naga","naga origin","who were the naga"},it="origin"},{q="Who rules the naga?",a="Queen Azshara, the former empress of the Kaldorei, rules the naga. From Nazjatar beneath the Maelstrom, she directs her sea witches and warriors. The naga venerate her with fanatical devotion, even after thousands of years in monstrous forms.",al={"naga leader","naga queen","who leads the naga"},it="leader"},{q="Why are naga attacking the beaches and coasts now?",a="The naga resurfaced during the Third War after hiding beneath the waves for ten thousand years. They believe ancient Kalimdor belongs to them as heirs of the Kaldorei Empire. Guided by Queen Azshara and the Old Gods, they seek to subjugate coastal lands and conquer the surface races.",al={"why are naga on land","naga invasion","why did naga return"},it="why_here"},{q="Why do male and female naga look so different?",a="Naga females retain the intellectual and magical cunning of their Highborne ancestors. Many have four arms and great skill with arcane, frost, and storm magic. Males are larger, hulking brutes with heavy scales and fins, shaped for physical warfare and violence.",al={"male vs female naga","naga differences","naga sea witches"}},{q="What is the relationship between the naga and Illidan Stormrage?",a="After the Third War, Illidan summoned allies from the deep sea with powerful magic. Lady Vashj answered with an army of naga, honoring ancient Highborne ties. Naga forces aided Illidan in the Broken Isles, Lordaeron, and beyond.",al={"why did naga help illidan","illidan naga","lady vashj illidan"},it="allies"},{q="Where can naga be encountered right now?",a="Naga hold beachheads along many coasts. In Kalimdor, they are numerous in Azshara, Darkshore, Ashenvale, Desolace, Feralas, and Dustwallow Marsh. In the Eastern Kingdoms, their raiding parties and altars can be found along the shores of Hillsbrad Foothills, Arathi Highlands, and Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"naga locations","where to find naga","naga zones"},it="place"},{q="What are the naga?",a="The naga are a cruel, serpentine race of aquatic beings who dwell in the ocean depths and have recently invaded the coasts of Azeroth. Once the aristocratic Highborne of the ancient night elf empire, they were transformed ten thousand years ago after the Great Sundering drowned their civilization. They possess formidable mastery over water, frost, and arcane sorcery, wielding heavy tridents and slithering upon muscular, scaled tails.",al={"who are the naga","what is a naga","naga race"},it="identity",add="443d0bbf"},{q="Why are naga hostile to land dwellers?",a="The naga harbor bitter resentment over their ancient banishment beneath the waves. Having lost the empire they once ruled as Highborne nobility, their minds and hearts were warped with hatred toward the surface world. They view air-breathing races as inferior usurpers of their rightful lands. Now driven to reclaim their place and serve their dark masters, they show no mercy to anyone trespassing upon the shores they claim.",al={"why do naga attack","why are naga aggressive","why do naga hate us"},it="hostile",add="b021c83f"},{q="What is the history of the naga?",a="Over ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara's Highborne courtiers brought about the War of the Ancients by reckless use of the Well of Eternity. When the Well collapsed during the Great Sundering, their capital sank into the ocean depths. Facing drowning, Azshara struck a pact with the Old Gods, who twisted the survivors into serpentine horrors. From the underwater city of Nazjatar beneath the Maelstrom, they spent millennia plotting their return.",al={"where did naga come from","naga history","history of naga"},it="history",add="14259e40"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="To the night elves, the naga are a painful reminder of the Highborne pride that shattered Ancient Kalimdor. Seeing Azshara's former court on the shores of Darkshore and Ashenvale makes them want to purge their ancient kin.",["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear trolls hate the naga because the sea witch Zar'jira drove them from their island home during their voyage across the Great Sea. The attack claimed the life of their elder leader, Sen'jin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance remembers the naga in Dalaran's ruins, where Lady Vashj's creatures captured survivors and stirred division between the blood elves and Grand Marshal Garithos's forces.",["faction:Horde"]="Thrall and the Horde fought naga raiders from the Darkspear Isles to Dustwallow Marsh. There, Lady Darkscale butchered human settlements and attacked the outskirts of Durotar."},kw={"azshara","highborne","naga","nazjatar","old gods","sea witch","sundering","vashj"},rel={"topic:highborne","topic:night-elf","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:old-god","zone:azshara","zone:darkshore","zone:dustwallow","topic:third-war"},src={"Naga"}}
E["topic:new-horde"] = {t="topic",n="New Horde",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, the New Horde seeks a home and allies under warchief thrall. Orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren join in shamanic tradition, honor, and mutual survival, while a wary pact binds them to the Forsaken.",h="Across Kalimdor and Lordaeron, the New Horde seeks a home and allies under warchief thrall.",sec={{t="A Legacy Reborn",b="The first Horde was forged by the Burning Legion and the Shadow Council as a weapon. Demonic bloodlust drove the orcs through the Dark Portal. After the Second War ended in ruin, the Alliance confined surviving orcs in internment camps, where they sank into soul-draining lethargy. Orgrim Doomhammer, Grommash Hellscream, and the young shaman Thrall helped the orcs break their demonic shackles. They reclaimed their ancestral shamanism and fought their way to freedom.",sp=0},{t="Crossing the Great Sea",b="Guided by visions from the mysterious Prophet, Thrall led his people across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. Along the way, they welcomed the displaced Darkspear trolls of Sen'jin. On Kalimdor, Thrall joined Cairne Bloodhoof and the nomadic tauren to drive back hostile centaur tribes. Together with humans and night elves, they fought at Mount Hyjal and broke the Burning Legion's invasion. Then they made their home in Durotar.",sp=0},{t="The Modern Coalition",b="From their fortified capital of Orgrimmar, the New Horde works to build a lasting society. Orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren share strong bonds, while the need to survive has drawn Thrall into uneasy alliances. One binds him to Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken in the ruins of Lordaeron. Thrall seeks peace with the Alliance, yet old enmities, scarce resources, and hawkish voices on both sides keep the borders close to war.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes the New Horde different from the Old Horde?",a="The Old Horde served demonic corruption, dark warlocks, and brutal conquest in the First and Second Wars. Thrall founded the New Horde in rejection of the Burning Legion. It restored the orcs' shamanic roots and embraced honor, cultural survival, and self-determination.",al={"old horde vs new horde","how is this horde different","thrall horde difference"}},{q="Who leads the New Horde?",a="Thrall, son of Durotan, leads the New Horde as warchief. From the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, he works in close council with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof of the tauren and Shadow Hunter Vol'jin of the Darkspear trolls.",al={"warchief","who is the leader","thrall's role"},it="leader"},{q="Which races belong to the New Horde right now?",a="The New Horde's core is made up of orcs, the Darkspear tribe of trolls, and the tauren of Mulgore. In the Eastern Kingdoms, the undead Forsaken under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner belong through a pragmatic military alliance.",al={"horde races","who is in the horde","horde members"},it="allies"},{q="Why did the Forsaken join the New Horde?",a="Surrounded by the Scarlet Crusade, hostile humans, and Scourge remnants, Sylvanas Windrunner sought powerful allies to survive. The tauren, led by Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, spoke for the Forsaken in Orgrimmar because they believed the Forsaken could be redeemed. Their appeal convinced Thrall to accept a mutual pact of convenience.",al={"undead in the horde","why forsaken horde","why are undead with thrall"}},{q="Are the orcs still corrupted by demon blood?",a="No. Grommash Hellscream and Thrall faced the pit lord Mannoroth in Ashenvale. Grom struck the demon down at the cost of his own life, breaking the blood curse and freeing every orc from demonic enslavement.",al={"demon blood","blood curse","are orcs still evil"}},{q="Is the New Horde currently at war with the Alliance?",a="The uneasy truce between Thrall and Lady Jaina Proudmoore of Theramore keeps open war in check. Skirmishes still rage across Ashenvale, Alterac Valley, and the Arathi Basin. Mistrust and disputes over resources threaten to spark open conflict.",al={"are horde and alliance at war","peace with alliance","horde alliance conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the New Horde?",a="The New Horde is the coalition of races gathered under Warchief Thrall. Built upon the ideals of honor, shamanism, and mutual survival, it stands distinct from the bloodthirsty demonic puppet of the First and Second Wars. Today, its core consists of the free orcs who broke their demonic lethargy, the Darkspear trolls, the tauren of Kalimdor, and a tenuous pact with the Forsaken of Lordaeron.",al={"what is new horde","who are new horde","new horde faction"},it="identity",add="48a04cd3",nx={8}},{q="Where did the New Horde come from?",a="The seeds of the New Horde were sown when Thrall, Orgrim Doomhammer, and Grommash Hellscream liberated the lethargic orcs from human internment camps across Lordaeron. Guided by a prophetic vision, Thrall led his people across the Great Sea to the forgotten continent of Kalimdor. Along their journey, they allied with Sen'jin's Darkspear trolls and later Cairne Bloodhoof's tauren, establishing a permanent home in the harsh lands of Durotar.",al={"history of new horde","origin of new horde","how was new horde founded"},it="history",add="7f9c7de9"},{q="Why is it called the New Horde?",a="The name distinguishes Thrall's renewed alliance from the Old Horde that invaded Azeroth through the Dark Portal. While the Old Horde was bound to the Burning Legion's fel corruption and endless slaughter, the New Horde seeks redemption through ancient shamanic traditions, honor, and freedom from demonic dominion.",al={"why new horde","new horde name meaning"},it="name",add="a76f0096"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The New Horde offers outcasts sanctuary, mutual defense, and a chance to preserve their cultures. Its members share an oath of honor under Warchief Thrall.",["faction:Alliance"]="Many in the Alliance remember the bloodshed of the First and Second Wars. They still doubt that orcs can leave their violent past behind.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you find redemption and freedom from the lethargy of the internment camps in the New Horde. You can honor Grom Hellscream's sacrifice and live as a free shamanic warrior.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you follow the New Horde's spiritual backbone. Shamanism renews ancient traditions that connect mortals with the elements, traditions nearly lost to demonic corruption."},kw={"darkspear","doomhammer","durotar","new horde","orgrimmar","shamanism","tauren","thrall","warchief"},rel={"topic:horde","npc:thrall","topic:old-horde","topic:tauren","topic:troll","topic:grommash-hellscream","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","quest:787"},src={"New Horde"}}
E["topic:night-elf"] = {t="topic",n="Night elf",z="general",s="Night elves now defend their ancestral forests beside the Alliance. The kaldorei are an ancient, reclusive people of northern Kalimdor. Once rulers of a vast magical empire, they turned from arcane magic after the War of the Ancients and embraced Elune and druidism. In the Third War, they gave up immortality to stop the Burning Legion, then joined the Alliance as the Horde pressed into their lands.",h="Night elves now defend their ancestral forests beside the Alliance.",sec={{t="Children of the Stars",b="Beside the Well of Eternity, the kaldorei began as a curious nocturnal tribe. Over generations, its raw arcane power changed them into tall, violet-skinned, long-lived people. They called themselves kaldorei, meaning “children of the stars.” Elune, the moon goddess, and Cenarius, the forest demigod, guided their early society and bound them to Kalimdor’s living wilds.",sp=0},{t="The Empire and the Sundering",b="Queen Azshara led the Highborne, the ruling caste, in pursuit of the Well’s endless arcane secrets. Their sorcery raised breathtaking wonders, but its reckless use drew the Burning Legion to Azeroth. The invasion ended in the Great Sundering. The Well imploded, breaking ancient Kalimdor into separate continents and destroying Azshara’s realm. The surviving kaldorei outlawed arcane magic, on pain of death or exile.",sp=0},{t="The Long Vigil and the New Age",b="For ten thousand years, the night elves kept to themselves. Druids slept in the Emerald Dream to heal the world, while the Priestesses of Elune and Sentinels guarded Kalimdor’s forests beneath Nordrassil. Their seclusion ended when the Legion returned in the Third War and attacked Mount Hyjal. The kaldorei gave up immortality to defeat Archimonde.\n\nHigh Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm now lead their people from their young World Tree, Teldrassil. The night elves fight beside the Alliance to protect Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does 'kaldorei' mean?",a="In Darnassian, the night elves’ native language, kaldorei means “children of the stars.” The early night elves took that name after settling beside the Well of Eternity and devoting themselves to Elune.",al={"kaldorei meaning","what is kaldorei","night elf native name"}},{q="Where did the night elves originate?",a="The night elves began as a curious nocturnal tribe beside the Well of Eternity, long before the Sundering. Over generations, the Well’s raw magic changed their bodies and minds, making them the graceful, long-lived kaldorei.",al={"night elf origins","where do night elves come from","are elves evolved trolls"}},{q="Why don't night elves practice arcane magic?",a="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara and the Highborne drew the Burning Legion to Azeroth through their reckless use of the Well of Eternity. The war brought the Great Sundering and shattered the world. Afterward, the night elves outlawed arcane magic to keep demons from finding Azeroth again.",al={"why no night elf mages","night elf arcane ban","why did night elves ban magic"}},{q="Are night elves still immortal?",a="No. The Dragon Aspects blessed Nordrassil, the World Tree that gave the night elves immortality and agelessness. During the Third War’s Battle of Mount Hyjal, the kaldorei unleashed Nordrassil’s ancestral power to destroy Archimonde and lost their immortality.",al={"are night elves immortal","did night elves lose immortality","how long do night elves live"}},{q="Where is the night elf capital located?",a="Darnassus, the night elf capital, rests in the vast canopy of Teldrassil. The colossal World Tree was planted off Kalimdor’s northwest coast after the Third War.",al={"night elf capital","where do night elves live","darnassus location"}},{q="Why did the night elves join the Alliance?",a="The kaldorei ended their long isolation to fight beside humans and dwarves against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. After the war, the Horde began heavily logging Ashenvale’s sacred forests for lumber. The night elves then formalized an alliance with the Eastern Kingdoms to defend their borders.",al={"why are night elves alliance","night elf alliance allegiance","why join alliance"}},{q="Which classes can night elves be?",a="Night elves train as warriors, hunters, rogues, priests and druids. They shun arcane magic, so they have no mages or warlocks.",al={"night elf classes","what classes can night elves be"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you carry ten millennia of wisdom and burdens. Your people face a perilous new age: mortality is real, ancestral forests are under siege, and old traditions are tested.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you inherit a history that remembers the elves as ancient enemies, in a bitter rivalry lasting thousands of years.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the kaldorei’s fierce Sentinels and watchful druids, made relentless and deadly adversaries by the Horde’s aggressive logging in Ashenvale.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you follow a tradition shaped by Cenarius. Night elf guardians bind kaldorei druidism to the Emerald Dream and the defense of nature’s balance."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarius","darnassus","elune","kaldorei","night elf","nordrassil","sundering","teldrassil","well of eternity"},rel={"zone:darnassus","topic:elune","topic:cenarius","topic:nordrassil","topic:highborne","zone:ashenvale","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:malfurion-stormrage"},src={"Night elf"}}
E["topic:nordrassil"] = {t="topic",n="Nordrassil",z="general",s="Above Mount Hyjal, Nordrassil bears its wounds, and the night elves know age and sickness. Planted over the second Well of Eternity, the World Tree once sheltered its power and gave the kaldorei immortality for ten thousand years. Its sacrifice broke Archimonde’s assault during the Third War.",h="Above Mount Hyjal, Nordrassil bears its wounds, and the night elves know age and sickness.",sec={{t="Crown of the Heavens",b="Nordrassil rose from an acorn of G'Hanir above the new Well of Eternity. Ten thousand years ago, after the Great Sundering, Illidan Stormrage poured vials of the original Well into a lake atop Mount Hyjal. There he made a new font of arcane power.\n\nTo keep its magic from corrupting the world or drawing the Burning Legion back, Alexstrasza planted the acorn. Nordrassil’s roots reached deep beneath Azeroth, sealing the Well’s volatile energies and spreading gentle, life-giving vigor across the continents.",sp=0},{t="The Aspects' Gifts",b="Three Great Dragon Aspects blessed Nordrassil, and the tree became the spiritual and cultural heart of night elf civilization. Alexstrasza filled it with vigor that sustained the kaldorei. Ysera bound its roots to the Emerald Dream, so night elf druids could enter her sleeping realm with effortless clarity.\n\nNozdormu the Timeless One laid his blessing over its boughs. While the tree stood, the night elves would not age or succumb to natural disease. For ten thousand years, the kaldorei knew immortality.",sp=0},{t="The Fall at Mount Hyjal",b="During the Third War, Archimonde brought his war to Nordrassil. The demon lord marched on Mount Hyjal to tear apart the tree and seize the Well’s infinite power. As the mortal defenders neared defeat, Malfurion Stormrage sounded the Horn of Cenarius and called thousands of nature spirits. Then he unleashed the enchantments within Nordrassil. The blast destroyed Archimonde and shattered the Legion’s assault.\n\nNordrassil survived, but its enchantments broke. The night elves lost their immortality, and the wounded tree began a slow healing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does Nordrassil mean?",a="In Darnassian, Nordrassil means “Crown of the Heavens.” Its great height rises above sacred Mount Hyjal’s summit.",al={"nordrassil translation","what does nordrassil mean in darnassian","nordrassil name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where is Nordrassil located?",a="Nordrassil grows at Mount Hyjal’s summit in northern Kalimdor. Its roots reach into the waters of the second Well of Eternity, created by Illidan Stormrage.",al={"nordrassil location","where is the original world tree","where is nordrassil"},it="place"},{q="Why did the night elves lose their immortality?",a="The night elves lost their immortality when Malfurion Stormrage unleashed Nordrassil’s magic to defeat Archimonde at Mount Hyjal. The blast destroyed the demon lord and broke the Dragon Aspects’ blessings, ending Nozdormu’s spell of eternal life.",al={"why aren't night elves immortal anymore","night elf mortality","loss of immortality"},it="power"},{q="How is Nordrassil related to Teldrassil?",a="Nordrassil is the original World Tree atop Mount Hyjal. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm and the Circle of the Ancients grew the younger Teldrassil off Kalimdor’s coast in a desperate bid to replace Nordrassil and reclaim the lost immortality.",al={"nordrassil vs teldrassil","difference between teldrassil and nordrassil","is teldrassil nordrassil"},it="ties"},{q="Did Nordrassil die when Archimonde was defeated?",a="Nordrassil survived Archimonde’s defeat. The blast scorched and wounded the tree, but its roots endured. It remains atop Mount Hyjal, slowly mending, though its ancient dragon blessings are gone.",al={"is nordrassil dead","did nordrassil survive","nordrassil destroyed"},it="today"},{q="Which dragons blessed Nordrassil?",a="Three Dragon Aspects blessed Nordrassil. Alexstrasza the Life-Binder planted it and gave it vitality, Ysera the Dreamer bound it to the Emerald Dream, and Nozdormu the Timeless One granted the night elves eternal youth.",al={"who blessed nordrassil","dragon blessings world tree","which aspects blessed nordrassil"},it="allies"},{q="What is Nordrassil?",a="Nordrassil is the original World Tree of the night elves, standing atop Mount Hyjal above the second Well of Eternity. Grown to shield and contain the Well's raw arcane magic, its massive roots spread life-giving energy throughout Azeroth. For millennia, it served as the sacred heart of night elf civilization.",al={"what is nordrassil","who is nordrassil","nordrassil identity"},it="identity",add="1a91b9d6"},{q="What is the history of Nordrassil?",a="After the Great Sundering, the dragon Alexstrasza planted an acorn from the Mother Tree, G'Hanir, into the second Well of Eternity created atop Mount Hyjal. The Great Aspects Alexstrasza, Ysera, and Nozdormu blessed the growing tree, binding the night elves to nature, granting druids direct access to the Emerald Dream, and bestowing immortality upon the Kaldorei. Nordrassil stood unharmed for ten thousand years until the Third War, when Malfurion Stormrage detonated the tree's ancestral energies to obliterate the demon lord Archimonde.",al={"history of nordrassil","where did nordrassil come from","how was nordrassil created"},it="history",add="734b781a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Nordrassil cradled your civilization for ten thousand years. Its sacrifice saved the world from Archimonde, but now you face aging, sickness, and mortality for the first time.",["class:Druid"]="Nordrassil’s bond with Ysera let druids cross into the Emerald Dream with ease. Its wounds show the cost of defending nature.",["faction:Alliance"]="At Mount Hyjal, the Alliance joined a desperate coalition to shield Nordrassil from the Burning Legion and save Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Thrall led the Horde to Mount Hyjal’s slopes with humans and night elves. Their stand gave Malfurion time to spring the trap at Nordrassil’s base."},kw={"alexstrasza","archimonde","hyjal","immortality","malfurion","nordrassil","nozdormu","teldrassil","well of eternity","world tree","ysera"},rel={"quest:940","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:third-war","topic:emerald-dream","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:druid","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:cenarius"},src={"Nordrassil"}}
E["topic:old-god"] = {t="topic",n="Old God",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the Old Gods’ whispers still poison mortal minds and twist the world. Once they ruled the primordial world, until the Titans bound them beneath the earth. Their influence endures.",h="Across Azeroth, the Old Gods’ whispers still poison mortal minds and twist the world.",sec={{t="Masters of the Primordial World",b="In Azeroth’s first age, the Old Gods ruled through vast bodies of chaotic flesh, among them C'Thun. They took root in the planet’s crust and commanded elemental armies and insectoid swarms. When the Titans arrived, their armies waged an apocalyptic war against the Old Gods. Rather than destroy them, the Titans bound them in vast prisons beneath the earth.",sp=0},{t="Whispers from the Deep",b="The Old Gods have never truly slept beneath their chains, miles of stone and enchanted wards. Their psychic malice seeps into the world and corrupts the vulnerable. During the War of the Ancients, that malice slowly drove Neltharion the Earth-Warder mad and twisted the noble dragon into Deathwing.\n\nAs the Great Sundering’s raging waters swallowed Queen Azshara and her Highborne, an Old God answered their desperation. The Old God transformed them into the serpentine naga.",sp=0},{t="Stirrings in the Sands",b="Many mortal civilizations now treat the Old Gods as myth, though their prisons are fracturing. Nearly a millennium ago, insectoid qiraji swarmed from southern Silithus in the War of the Shifting Sands. They served C'Thun until the night elves and dragons sealed them behind the Scarab Wall.\n\nToday, cults such as the Twilight's Hammer gather in dark corners across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Their foul rites seek to break the Titans’ bindings and hasten the end of all mortal life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What exactly are the Old Gods?",a="The Old Gods are ancient, eldritch monstrosities of flesh and madness who ruled Azeroth in primordial times. They feed on chaos and seek to corrupt the world, driving mortals and elementals toward madness.",al={"what is an old god","old gods lore","who are the old gods"},it="identity"},{q="How many Old Gods were there on Azeroth?",a="No mortal knows for certain how many Old Gods there were. C'Thun, imprisoned beneath Ahn'Qiraj in Silithus, is best known. Others lie chained in subterranean vaults across the globe.",al={"how many old gods","list of old gods","names of old gods"}},{q="Why didn't the Titans just kill them all?",a="The Old Gods had burrowed so deeply into Azeroth’s bedrock that tearing them out risked destroying the world. So the Titans built prisons instead.",al={"why didn't titans kill old gods","why imprison old gods","why spare old gods"}},{q="Are the Old Gods connected to Deathwing and the naga?",a="Yes. The Old Gods whispered into Neltharion the Earth-Warder’s mind and slowly drove him mad, until he snapped and became Deathwing. As the Great Sundering’s waters raged, an Old God answered Queen Azshara and her Highborne’s cries. It remade them into the naga.",al={"did old gods make naga","old gods deathwing","who corrupted neltharion"},it="ties"},{q="Who are the Twilight's Hammer?",a="The Twilight's Hammer is an apocalyptic cult devoted to nihilism and the Old Gods. Its followers seek to unbind the imprisoned entities, unleash the elemental lords and plunge the world into total ruin.",al={"twilights hammer cult","who worships old gods","old god cultists"},it="allies"},{q="Where are the Old Gods imprisoned?",a="The Old Gods’ known prisons lie scattered across the world, deep beneath Titan ruins. C'Thun is trapped beneath Ahn'Qiraj in Silithus. Others were bound beneath the northern reaches and deep subterranean foundations.",al={"where are old gods","old god locations","c'thun location"},it="why_here"},{q="Why are the Old Gods hostile to mortals?",a="The Old Gods exist solely to corrupt reality. To these primordial horrors, mortal life is little more than insects to be twisted, driven mad, or utterly enslaved. They hold no concept of peaceful coexistence; their dark whispers seek only to undermine your sanity and bend every living soul to their will.",al={"why do old gods attack","old god hostility","why are old gods evil"},it="hostile",add="6f130189"},{q="Where did the Old Gods come from?",a="No mortal knows where the Old Gods came from. They were already entrenched deep within the planet's crust, ruling primordial Azeroth with elemental armies and insectoid swarms, when the Titans arrived to defeat and seal them beneath the earth.",al={"old god origins","origin of the old gods","how were the old gods created"},it="history",add="2cc577ae"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you fought the qiraji minion hordes in the War of the Shifting Sands and sealed Silithus behind the Scarab Wall.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest who delves into shadow magic, you walk a perilous path. Beware the maddening whispers said to rise from ancient horrors chained beneath the earth.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold a sacred duty to guard the Emerald Dream against the Emerald Nightmare. Its true source remains unknown.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you draw mainly on fel magic and demons of the Burning Legion. Some foolishly seek the forbidden curses and sacrificial rites left behind by the Old Gods’ servants."},kw={"ahn'qiraj","c'thun","old god","qiraji","silithus","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:scarab-wall","zone:silithus","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:titan","topic:emerald-dream","topic:naga","npc:deathwing","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},src={"Old God"}}
E["topic:old-horde"] = {t="topic",n="Old Horde",z="general",s="Across Draenor and Azeroth, the Old Horde left conquest in its wake. Demonic power drove the orc clans to conquer Draenor and invade Azeroth. Blackhand and then Orgrim Doomhammer led them through the First and Second Wars, until the Alliance of Lordaeron defeated them. Thrall's New Horde now seeks to overcome that legacy, while remnants such as the Dark Horde cling to the bloody past.",h="Across Draenor and Azeroth, the Old Horde left conquest in its wake.",sec={{t="Rise and Deception",b="Kil'jaeden turned the orc clans toward war before they crossed into Azeroth. Through the warlock Gul'dan and the elder shaman Ner'zhul, the demon lord corrupted the proud, spiritual orcs. As the clans fought, the elemental spirits abandoned them. The orcs cast aside shamanism for warlock magic. Then they drank Mannoroth's blood and gave themselves to bloodlust. They slaughtered the draenei and drained life from their homeland.",sp=0},{t="Invasion of Azeroth",b="Draenor's withering lands could no longer provide what the Horde needed. Gul'dan and Medivh, a human guardian possessed by demonic power, opened the Dark Portal into Azeroth. The Horde poured through and began the First War against the Kingdom of Stormwind. Warchief Blackhand led them, while Gul'dan's Shadow Council secretly directed events.\n\nNear the war's end, Orgrim Doomhammer slew Blackhand and purged the Shadow Council. He took command, then razed Stormwind to the ground.",sp=0},{t="Collapse and Demonic Hangover",b="Orgrim Doomhammer led the Horde north across the seas to fight the Second War. There, the Horde joined forces with forest trolls and goblin mercenaries. At the height of the siege of Lordaeron, Gul'dan and his loyalists abandoned the war to seek the Tomb of Sargeras. Betrayed and divided, the Horde was driven back to Blackrock Mountain and crushed by the Alliance of Lordaeron.\n\nThe Alliance destroyed the portal and herded surviving orcs into internment camps. As the demonic blood haze faded, lethargy settled over them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between the Old Horde and the New Horde?",a="The Old Horde pursued conquest under demonic corruption, warlock magic, and the influence of the Burning Legion and Gul'dan's Shadow Council. After escaping the internment camps, Thrall established the New Horde. It returned to shamanism and honor, uniting survivors instead of leading an invading army.",al={"old horde vs new horde","difference in hordes","thrall's horde vs old horde"},it="identity"},{q="Who led the Old Horde?",a="Blackhand led the Old Horde during the slaughter of the draenei and most of the First War, though Gul'dan used him as a figurehead. Orgrim Doomhammer slew Blackhand in a duel and took the title of Warchief. He led the Horde through the end of the First War and the Second War.",al={"who was warchief","old horde leader","who led the first horde"},it="leader"},{q="Why did the orcs drink demon blood?",a="Gul'dan offered the clan chieftains the blood of Mannoroth, a pit lord, and promised overwhelming power and victory. He concealed that drinking it bound their souls to the Burning Legion and filled them with reckless bloodlust.",al={"why did orcs drink fel blood","mannoroth blood","orc corruption reason"},it="motive"},{q="What was the Shadow Council?",a="Gul'dan founded the Shadow Council, a secret order of warlocks, necrolytes, and assassins. The order controlled Warchief Blackhand and secretly guided the Horde according to the Burning Legion's will, until Orgrim Doomhammer uncovered and purged it.",al={"who were the shadow council","gul'dan council","shadow council role"}},{q="How was the Old Horde defeated?",a="During the Second War, Gul'dan abandoned the Horde at the gates of Lordaeron to seek godhood at the Tomb of Sargeras. His departure fractured the army. The Alliance of Lordaeron rallied, drove Doomhammer back to Blackrock Mountain, captured him, and herded the demoralized survivors into internment camps.",al={"how did the old horde lose","second war ending","defeat of the orcs"},it="history"},{q="Do any remnants of the Old Horde still exist?",a="Yes. Splinter factions such as the Dark Horde, which holds Blackrock Spire under Rend Blackhand, reject Thrall's New Horde and cling to conquest and the old brutal ways. They ally with dragons and forest trolls.",al={"is the old horde still around","dark horde","remnants of old horde"},it="today"},{q="Why is it called the Old Horde?",a="During its existence, it was simply known as the Horde or the Orcish Horde. Historians and travelers now call it the Old Horde or the first Horde to distinguish it from the New Horde founded by Thrall. Thrall's Horde broke free from demonic corruption and returned to the spiritual ways of shamanism, leaving behind the dark legacy of the original faction.",al={"why old horde","old horde name meaning","why called old horde"},it="name",add="354eaa00"},{q="Who did the Old Horde ally with?",a="Originally, the Old Horde consisted solely of the orcish clans of Draenor, though they were soon joined by ogres from their homeworld. During the Second War on Azeroth, their ranks expanded further to include the forest trolls of the Amani Empire and mercenary goblins who provided engineering, Zeppelins, and munitions to bolster their conquest.",al={"old horde allies","who fought with the old horde","old horde races"},it="allies",add="b4ccff16"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you inherit the Old Horde's shameful history of demonic slavery and ruin. Thrall strives to overcome that legacy through honor and shamanism.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you live with the scars of the Old Horde's invasion. It leveled Stormwind City and ravaged the lands of Lordaeron during the First and Second Wars.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the Old Horde's rise drove Draenor's elemental spirits to turn from the orcs. Under Thrall's guidance, that spiritual breach has only recently begun to heal.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you know how Gul'dan and his Shadow Council spread warlock magic among the orc clans as they built the Old Horde. They drew on the Burning Legion's corrupting power.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you stand with a coalition formed to unite the mortal kingdoms against the threat of the Old Horde."},kw={"blackhand","dark portal","draenor","first war","gul'dan","mannoroth","old horde","orgrim doomhammer","second war","shadow council"},rel={"npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:shadow-council","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","subzone:dark-portal","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:new-horde"},src={"Old Horde"}}
E["topic:orc"] = {t="topic",n="Orc",z="general",s="In Durotar, orcs lead the Horde and seek honor after a long fall into demonic corruption. Once shamanistic clans on Draenor, they were deceived by the Burning Legion, invaded Azeroth, and were defeated and interned. Warchief Thrall led them back to their spiritual heritage and into a new home.",h="In Durotar, orcs lead the Horde and seek honor after a long fall into demonic corruption.",sec={{t="Children of Draenor",b="Across Draenor, orcs once roamed as nomadic hunter-gatherers in spiritual clans. They honored their ancestors and communed with elemental spirits, guided by revered shamans. Among their clans were the Frostwolves, Warsongs, and Shadowmoon. Orcs were physically formidable and proud, yet their society prized survival, honor, and harmony with the elements over conquest.",sp=0},{t="Corruption and the Great Wars",b="Kil'jaeden and the warlock Gul'dan changed the orcs' fate through corruption. Deceived into drinking the blood of the demon Mannoroth, they fell to supernatural bloodlust. The original Horde nearly wiped out Draenor's draenei, then crossed the Dark Portal into Azeroth.\n\nIn the First and Second Wars, human kingdoms fell and orcish armies reached Lordaeron's gates. Treachery within their ranks and the united Alliance of Lordaeron defeated them, and survivors were driven into internment camps.",sp=0},{t="A New Beginning in Kalimdor",b="As prisoners, the orcs lost their demonic frenzy and grew lethargic and broken. Thrall, raised in human captivity, escaped and returned to shamanism. He rallied the Frostwolf clan, freed his kin from the camps, and formed a renewed Horde. After receiving prophetic warnings, he led his people across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.\n\nGrom Hellscream's sacrifice finally broke Mannoroth's blood curse. The orcs now live in Durotar, where they built the fortress-city of Orgrimmar. They strive to keep their hard-won honor amid renewed tensions with the Alliance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are orcs green?",a="No tale in Azeroth explains for certain why orcs are green. They have been green-skinned for as long as this world has known them. Every orc who came through the Dark Portal was green, and Thrall's orcs are green today.",al={"why is orc skin green","orc green skin origin","brown orcs vs green orcs"}},{q="Where did the orcs come from?",a="The orcs came from Draenor, a world beyond Azeroth. They crossed through the Dark Portal after Gul'dan and the demon-possessed human sorcerer Medivh opened a rift between the worlds.",al={"orc homeworld","are orcs native to azeroth","where are orcs from"}},{q="Who is the leader of the orcs?",a="Warchief Thrall leads the orcs, and he is the son of Durotan. Humans raised him as a gladiator slave, but he rediscovered shamanism, freed the orc internment camps, and led the new Horde to Kalimdor.",al={"orc warchief","orc faction leader","who leads the orcs"}},{q="What is the blood curse?",a="The blood curse was the demonic enslavement that took hold when the orcs drank the blood of the annihilan Mannoroth. It filled them with uncontrollable bloodlust and drove their wars. Grom Hellscream gave his life to slay Mannoroth and finally break the curse.",al={"blood of mannoroth","orc bloodlust curse","mannoroth blood"}},{q="Why do the orcs live in Durotar?",a="After the Third War, Thrall settled the orcs in a harsh, dry coastal realm and named it Durotar for his father, Durotan. Its punishing terrain is penance for past sins and a trial that keeps his people strong and resilient.",al={"why is durotar a desert","why orgrimmar","why durotar"}},{q="Are all orcs part of Thrall's Horde?",a="No. Thrall leads the New Horde, but rogue clans remain. The Dragonmaw clan still follows its enslaver traditions in the Wetlands, while the Blackrock clan under Rend Blackhand wages war from Blackrock Mountain and rejects Thrall's peace.",al={"evil orcs","hostile orcs","are all orcs friendly to horde"}},{q="Which classes can orcs be?",a="Orcs can train as warriors, hunters, rogues, shaman, mages, and warlocks.",al={"orc classes","what classes can orcs be","can orcs be mages"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Orcs form the modern Horde's military and ideological backbone. They champion honor and survival alongside their troll, tauren, and Forsaken allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance races still regard orcs with deep suspicion and resentment. They remember the slaughter of the First and Second Wars and the destruction of Stormwind.",["class:Shaman"]="For orcs, shamanism is more than magic. It is their reclaimed cultural soul and a path to spiritual redemption after decades of demonic servitude.",["class:Warlock"]="Orc warlocks face deep distrust and revulsion from their kin. Fel magic is the force that corrupted and enslaved their race."},kw={"bloodlust","draenor","durotar","fel","koshharg","mannoroth","orc","orcs","orgrimmar","shamanism","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:new-horde","zone:orgrimmar","zone:durotar","topic:burning-legion","subzone:dark-portal","topic:warsong-clan","topic:dragonmaw-clan"},src={"Orc"}}
E["topic:paladin"] = {t="topic",n="Paladin",z="general",s="Paladins stand between the innocent and those who would harm them. They wear heavy plate, mend the wounded and strike down the wicked with arms and the Holy Light. Humans and dwarves bear the Silver Hand's legacy in the Alliance. In the Horde, Forsaken who served the Light in life still answer its call, though it burns them.",h="Paladins stand between the innocent and those who would harm them.",sec={{t="Origins in Lordaeron",b="Archbishop Alonsus Faol formed the paladins during the Second War. After the First War left the pious Clerics of Northshire devastated, he saw that healers alone could not stand against orcish warfare. He gathered virtuous knights of Lordaeron and taught surviving clerics to fight with weapons and divine magic. Under Uther the Lightbringer, the Knights of the Silver Hand defended bodies and renewed spirits across humanity's kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="Champions of the Holy Light",b="Priests speak for the Holy Light, preaching faith and tending to common folk's spirits. Paladins take up arms in its name. Their conviction lets them strengthen allies with auras, seal blessings upon them and mend fatal wounds. Against unholy horrors, the Light courses through their blows and burns undead and demonic foes with righteous fury.",sp=0},{t="Heirs of the Silver Hand",b="The fall of Lordaeron in the Third War scattered the original order, but its ideals endure. Humans in the south and dwarves of Ironforge have taken up its mantle. In sanctuaries such as the Cathedral of Light and the Hall of Mysteries, they train and pledge sword and shield to justice. They defend the Alliance against gathering shadows.",sp=0},{t="Paladins of the Forsaken",b="Some knights of Lordaeron returned from the grave as Forsaken. Those who served the Light in life still keep their vows, and it still answers them, though each prayer sears their dead flesh. Aramis Hammerhand trains the risen paladins in the chapel at Deathknell, while Shari Stilwell continues their instruction in Brill.\n\nTyr's Watch, an order of Forsaken paladins, holds Bandarion Keep in western Tirisfal. Their path is lonely. They wield the power that burned their people, and Sylvanas Windrunner tolerates the order while watching it closely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between a priest and a paladin?",a="Priests speak for the Light and guide the faithful through prayer and ritual. Paladins wear heavy plate and wield weapons in its name, defending the weak and enforcing divine justice in battle.",al={"paladin vs priest","difference between priest and paladin","how are paladins different from priests"}},{q="Who created the first paladins?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol created the order during the Second War. After the Clerics of Northshire were slain in the First War, he gathered devout knights and trained surviving clerics to join martial discipline with holy magic as the Knights of the Silver Hand.",al={"who made paladins","founder of paladins","origin of the silver hand"}},{q="Which races can be paladins?",a="Humans and dwarves serve as paladins in the Alliance, while Forsaken do so in the Horde. The order began among humans, Ironforge's dwarves embraced the Holy Light, and some Forsaken who were knights or clerics in life still wield it after death, though it brings constant pain.",al={"can horde be paladins","who can be a paladin","paladin races","can undead be paladins","undead paladin","forsaken paladin"}},{q="Why are paladins effective against the undead?",a="The Holy Light opposes necrotic corruption and demonic energy. Paladins channel it to purge blight and burn unholy creatures, making them foremost champions against the Scourge and other foul beings.",al={"paladins vs undead","why does holy magic hurt undead","paladin scourge counter"}},{q="What happened to the original Knights of the Silver Hand?",a="The plague devastated Lordaeron during the Third War, and the original order suffered grievous losses. Betrayal and political strife fractured the brotherhood, but surviving members and new initiates in Stormwind and Ironforge carry its title and ideals forward. Some fallen knights rose again as Forsaken and still keep their oaths.",al={"what happened to silver hand","is silver hand gone","fall of the silver hand"}},{q="Can members of the Horde become paladins?",a="Only Forsaken become paladins within the Horde. Many were knights or clerics of Lordaeron before the plague, and some still keep their vows; the Light answers them, though it burns their dead flesh. Orcs, tauren and trolls follow shamans, druids and witch doctors rather than the knightly way of the Holy Light.",al={"horde paladins","can orcs be paladins","why no horde paladin","can forsaken be paladins","horde paladin races"}},{q="Why does the Light hurt Forsaken paladins?",a="The Holy Light opposes the dark energy that sustains the undead. A Forsaken paladin's faith and will let them channel it, but the Light burns dead flesh and reawakens deadened nerves. Each blessing and heal brings searing pain, which their trainers teach them to endure as proof that the Light still answers.",al={"does the light hurt undead paladins","undead paladin pain","forsaken paladin pain","can undead use the light"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a novice paladin, you follow Uther the Lightbringer and Alonsus Faol, joining readiness for battle to an oath of selfless duty.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you share a deep spiritual bond with paladins. You guide the faithful through sermons and faith, while they shield them with steel.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you have embraced the tenets of the Silver Hand, whose discipline of the Light fits your unyielding nature.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you carry the enduring soul of the Alliance as a paladin, keeping alive the sacred crusade forged in the horrors of the Second War.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance paladin, you rally troops with sacred auras and kindle hope across the battlefield.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you may be one of the rare risen paladins, a knight who kept your vows beyond death and still wields the Light, paying for every prayer in pain.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know that only the Forsaken raise paladins, and even among your own people the order meets suspicion."},kw={"alonsus faol","auras","blessings","cleric","crusader","holy light","paladin","plate","silver hand","uther","forsaken paladin","tyr's watch","undead paladin"},rel={"topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:light","topic:priest","topic:warrior","topic:alliance","topic:second-war","zone:stormwind","zone:ironforge","npc:aramis-hammerhand","subzone:bandarion-keep","topic:forsaken"},src={"Paladin"}}
E["topic:pirate"] = {t="topic",n="Pirate",z="general",s="Across Azeroth's seas, pirates prey on ships from every shore. Their crews strike Alliance, Horde, and neutral merchant vessels across the Great Sea and coastal waters. They gather under loose flags to seize wealth, cargo, and coves, sparking naval fights from Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms.",h="Across Azeroth's seas, pirates prey on ships from every shore.",sec={{t="Lords of the High Seas",b="Pirate crews roam Azeroth's seas, raiding ships and coastal settlements. They are called buccaneers, corsairs, or freebooters, and nearly every race joins their ranks. Their work ranges from smuggling and kidnappings to mercenary contracts for anyone with coin. After the Third War and the collapse of northern kingdoms, naval enforcement fractured. Pirates seized the chance to build fortified footholds on neglected islands and in coastal coves.",sp=0},{t="A Ruthless Life",b="Life aboard a buccaneer vessel is brutal and often short. Crews endure squalid, rat-infested holds and harsh discipline, while supplies of limes hold scurvy at bay. Betrayal is common, and captains keep command through strength and fear of punishment. A sailor might face execution, marooning, or be fed to sharks. After battle, buccaneers celebrate with dice, song, and heavy rum.",sp=0},{t="Factions and Havens",b="Independent crews roam every sea lane, while larger organizations command enough ships to challenge sovereign navies. The Southsea Freebooters harass shipping in the waters around Kalimdor. The Bloodsail Buccaneers menace the southern seas and wage open war against the Steamwheedle Cartel in Booty Bay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between a pirate, buccaneer, and freebooter?",a="Along Azeroth's sea lanes, pirate, buccaneer, and freebooter are largely interchangeable names. Some crews favor particular banners, such as the Southsea Freebooters or Bloodsail Buccaneers. All raid at sea, smuggle, rob, and plunder the coast.",al={"buccaneer vs pirate","freebooter difference","pirate titles"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the main pirate bases located?",a="Pirate crews gather in lawless anchorages and hidden harbors around the world. Their main havens include Plunder Isle and coastal camps along Tanaris, the Barrens, and Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"pirate towns","where do pirates live","pirate ports"},it="place"},{q="Who do pirates attack?",a="Most pirate crews prey on almost anyone. They hunt merchant vessels, civilian transports, and military supply craft belonging to the Alliance, Horde, and neutral Steamwheedle Cartel. Any ship carrying gold, timber, or trade goods may draw their attack.",al={"who do pirates target","are pirates alliance or horde"},it="target"},{q="How do pirate crews recruit new members?",a="Pirate crews hire desperate cutthroats and mercenaries in port towns, and they also press people into service. Captured sailors and travelers are often forced to choose between swearing fealty to the crew and being cast into the sea.",al={"joining pirates","how do they get crew"}},{q="How does Kul Tiras deal with pirates?",a="Since the Second War, Kul Tiran fleets have patrolled trade lanes, hunting pirates and marauders on the high seas.",al={"kul tiras piracy","kul tiran pirate law"}},{q="Are there non-human pirates?",a="Yes. Human crews are common, but buccaneers accept anyone willing to raid and follow orders. Their crews include orcs, goblins, trolls, and dwarves.",al={"orc pirates","goblin pirates"},it="people"},{q="What is a pirate?",a="Pirates are cutthroat seafaring raiders who plunder ships along the high seas and coastlines of Azeroth. Rather than flying national banners, they operate independently for personal gain through looting, smuggling, kidnapping, and mercenary work. Crews consist of ruthless renegades from across the mortal races, feared by merchants and hunted as criminals by both the Alliance and Horde navies.",al={"what is a pirate","who are pirates","define pirate"},it="identity",add="d5e8dad6"},{q="Why are pirates hostile to travelers?",a="Pirates view anyone crossing their territory or sea lanes as fresh prey. They take what they want through bloodshed and intimidation, caring little for the lives or allegiances of those they ambush. Any passing adventurer or merchant vessel represents plunder, hostage ransoms, or cargo to strip and sell.",al={"why do pirates attack","why are pirates hostile","are pirates dangerous"},it="hostile",add="433b56ef"},{q="Where do pirates come from?",a="Piracy has troubled the Great Sea for generations, thriving wherever kingdoms falter or fail to patrol the waters. In the aftermath of the Second and Third Wars, the destruction of coastal kingdoms and the breakdown of naval enforcement allowed lawless outcasts, deserters, and opportunists to seize abandoned outposts and terrorize maritime trade routes.",al={"pirate history","origin of pirates","where did pirates come from"},it="history",add="41dff7f7"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Pirate crews use cutthroat tactics, blinding powder, and swift blade work, much like the practical and lethal methods favored by roguish mercenaries.",["faction:Alliance"]="Buccaneers prowl coastal trade routes, putting Alliance transports between Stormwind, Ironforge, and Theramore under constant threat.",["faction:Horde"]="The Southsea Freebooters keep aggressive camps along the Durotar and Barrens coasts, raiding Horde caravans and landing parties.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren traditionally dwell on the plains, but some traveling along Kalimdor's shores have ended up aboard pirate vessels, pressed into crews or seeking fortune."},kw={"bloodsail","booty bay","buccaneer","corsair","freebooter","great sea","pirate","plunder","southsea"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","subzone:baradin-bay","quest:887","topic:kul-tiras","topic:goblin","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Pirate"}}
E["topic:plague-of-undeath"] = {t="topic",n="Plague of Undeath",z="general",s="Across the northern Eastern Kingdoms, the Plague of Undeath spreads at the Burning Legion's command. The Lich King fashioned it to scour the region, and tainted grain, airborne cauldrons, and poisoned waterways carry it to the living. The sickness kills mortals swiftly and raises them as thralls bound to the Scourge.",h="Across the northern Eastern Kingdoms, the Plague of Undeath spreads at the Burning Legion's command.",sec={{t="Origins in the Ice",b="After Kil'jaeden transformed the fallen shaman Ner'zhul into the Lich King, Ner'zhul devised the plague. From the Frozen Throne in Northrend, he perfected it as a weapon for the Burning Legion's invasion. He tested it on isolated human villages across Northrend, learning how to extinguish life and command the corpses that soon rose.\n\nHis summons crossed the Great Sea and reached Kel'Thuzad, a Kirin Tor mage who left Dalaran to serve him. Kel'Thuzad formed the secretive Cult of the Damned. Its mortal members infiltrated Lordaeron and prepared to poison the kingdom from within.",sp=0},{t="The Grain of Andorhal",b="Kel'Thuzad and the dreadlord Mal'Ganis chose Lordaeron's farmland for the contagion. The Cult secured distribution centers around Andorhal, then packed plague into grain crates bound for northern population centers, including Brill and Stratholme. Villagers baked bread from the tainted grain and fell ill. Their joints burned, sores oozed, and their eyes turned milky.\n\nWithin three days, whole communities died and rose as flesh-eating zombies, bound to the Lich King's psychic call. Prince Arthas Menethil raced to stop the shipments. In Stratholme, he culled the citizens before infected bread could turn them into Mal'Ganis's army.",sp=1},{t="A Land Corrupted",b="The blight reaches beyond humanity, and the land bears its demonic and necromantic decay. Non-human wildlife usually suffers fever or rot instead of rising as undead thralls. Across the Plaguelands, massive plague cauldrons send alchemical and magical vapors into the air, corrupting the land around them. Carrion grubs and colossal mushrooms choked with spores thrive there.\n\nThe Argent Dawn sabotages the cauldrons, reversing their mixtures so they burn the Scourge instead of feeding it. In the Undercity, the Royal Apothecary Society keeps experimenting to refine a New Plague meant to kill both the living and the undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How was the plague originally spread across Lordaeron?",a="The Cult of the Damned infiltrated Andorhal's grain distribution centers. Its members tainted supplies and sent crates to towns across Lordaeron, including Stratholme and Brill. Those who ate bread made from the grain fell sick and rose as undead.",al={"how did plague spread","infected grain","plagued grain distribution","grain of andorhal"},it="history"},{q="What happens to someone infected by the plague?",a="The plague swiftly brings weakness, nausea, aching joints, and fever. Boils and leaking yellow-green lesions break out on the skin, and the eyes turn milky. Severe bleeding from the ears and eyes follows. Most mortals die within three days, then rise as servants awaiting the Lich King's commands.",al={"plague symptoms","what does the plague do","how fast does plague kill"},it="threat"},{q="Why does the plague affect humans differently than other races?",a="The Lich King engineered the plague to target humanity and destroy Lordaeron. Non-human wildlife and races exposed to it often suffer rot, delirium, and fever, but rarely rise as Scourge thralls without direct necromantic spells.",al={"why humans","does plague affect elves","are orcs immune to plague"},it="target"},{q="Can the Plague of Undeath be cured?",a="No established cure is known in this age. Natural medicines cannot reverse the plague, and those who have died and risen cannot be restored.",al={"is plague curable","cure for the plague","healing the plague"},it="power"},{q="What are the giant cauldrons in the Plaguelands for?",a="The Scourge built massive cauldrons across the former farmlands to send vaporized plague into the air. The vapors corrupt the soil, cloud the sky, and sicken passing beasts. The Argent Dawn counters them by turning their reagents into holy or toxic weapons against the Scourge.",al={"plague cauldrons","what are cauldrons doing","why are cauldrons in fields"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Forsaken's New Plague?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society developed the New Plague in the Undercity. This chemical and magical pathogen is designed to kill both living mortals and the Lich King's undead thralls.",al={"forsaken plague","royal apothecary society plague","new plague undercity"}},{q="What is the Plague of Undeath?",a="It is a potent magical disease conjured by Ner'zhul, the Lich King, under the direction of the demon lord Kil'jaeden. Engineered to drain life and spread undeath, the affliction was designed as a weapon to destroy mortal civilizations and reanimate their dead as mindless thralls under the Lich King's psychic dominion.",al={"what is the plague","plague of undeath explained","scourge plague"},it="identity",add="e29c4cee"},{q="Why is it called the Plague of Undeath?",a="It earned the name because death is not its conclusion. While natural diseases merely kill their hosts, this affliction reanimates those who succumb to it. Victims perish rapidly from agonizing symptoms only to rise again as mindless, walking undead bound to the will of the Lich King.",al={"why plague of undeath","origin of plague name","why is it called undeath"},it="name",add="8d7ecba0"}},ang={["race:Human"]="The Plague of Undeath destroyed the Kingdom of Lordaeron and tore families apart. Its devastation became humanity's greatest historical catastrophe.",["race:Undead"]="Many Forsaken bear the plague's physical scars. They endured its agony, died, and later broke free of the Lich King's psychic grip.",["class:Paladin"]="The Order of the Silver Hand shattered while trying to contain the contagion. Paladins now rely on the Holy Light to purge its foul residue.",["class:Priest"]="Priests face the plague's corruption of body and spirit. Their faith drives them to burn away necrotic sickness before it festers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The loss of the northern kingdoms to the plague remains an unhealed wound for the Alliance. It drives the Alliance's ongoing crusade to cleanse the Plaguelands.",["faction:Horde"]="Orcs and tauren viewed the northern sickness as a human curse. The Royal Apothecary Society's research has since brought the horror of plague experimentation into the Horde."},kw={"andorhal","blight","cauldrons","grain","kel'thuzad","mal'ganis","ner'zhul","plague","scourge","stratholme","undeath"},rel={"topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:arthas-menethil","subzone:andorhal","subzone:stratholme","subzone:cauldron","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},src={"Plague of Undeath"}}
E["topic:priest"] = {t="topic",n="Priest",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Priest traditions shape belief, mend flesh, and guard souls. Some draw on the radiant power of faith, while others reach into the terrifying depths of the Void. Their paths range from the Church of the Holy Light to the Sisterhood of the Moon Goddess and shadowy Forsaken cults.",h="Across Azeroth, Priest traditions shape belief, mend flesh, and guard souls.",sec={{t="Vessels of Faith and Devotion",b="Priests guide the spiritual lives of their communities. While warriors test their strength with steel, priests draw power from conviction. Their divine connection can soothe grievous wounds, lift fallen companions from death's threshold, and weave mystic barriers against harm. On the field, their presence can mean the difference between survival and annihilation.",sp=0},{t="Light and Shadow",b="The priesthood does not serve only benevolent ends. Life holds both light and darkness, and priests walk a perilous line between healing and devastation of the mind. Those who master the holy arts call down searing righteous vengeance upon their enemies. Practitioners of Shadow magic delve into the Void to dominate minds, twist willpower, and inflict agonizing pain from afar.",sp=0},{t="Many Paths of Faith",b="No single faith guides every priest in Azeroth. Among humans, dwarves and gnomes, the Church of the Holy Light teaches a philosophy of virtue. After the First War, it shaped its fragile Clerics of Northshire into a hardened order.\n\nIn Kalimdor, the night elven Sisterhood of Elune honors the Mother Moon with starlight and grace, while troll witch doctors beseech the primal Loa. Among the newly risen Forsaken, many have turned from former dogmas to the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow. Its followers preach that darkness and light must exist in delicate equilibrium.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between a priest and a paladin?",a="During the First War, human clerics suffered immense slaughter on the battlefield because they lacked martial defense. In response, Archbishop Alonsus Faol and the Church formed the Knights of the Silver Hand, training armored holy warriors called paladins. Priests remain robed casters devoted to spiritual ministry, prayer, and deeper mastery of the mind and shadow.",al={"priest vs paladin","why play priest not paladin","paladin or priest lore"}},{q="Can priests use Shadow magic without losing their faith?",a="Yes. Spiritual balance holds that light cannot exist without darkness. Many priests study shadow to understand the perils threatening their flock, while others, like the Forsaken Cult of the Forgotten Shadow, embrace dark energies as necessary to existence. They argue that understanding both forces is the way to master the self.",al={"why do priests use shadow","shadow priest lore","shadow and holy balance"}},{q="Do all playable races worship the same thing as priests?",a="No. Humans, dwarves and gnomes primarily follow the Church of the Holy Light, a philosophy of virtue rather than worship of a deity. Night elves revere Elune through her Sisterhood, and trolls beseech spirits and Loa. Undead Forsaken practitioners follow the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow or struggle with their fractured bond to their former human faith.",al={"priest religions","what gods do priests worship","elune vs holy light priest"}},{q="Who leads the human priesthood in Stormwind?",a="After the fall of Lordaeron, the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind became the primary seat of the human church. Its clergy and surviving clerics from Northshire oversee humanity's spiritual recovery and guide the souls of the Alliance in these unsettled times.",al={"who leads church of holy light","stormwind cathedral leader","priest leader stormwind"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken still have priests?",a="Many undead retained memories and techniques from their living devotions in Lordaeron. After facing death's abandonment, some embraced the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow and wield dark energies while studying the balance between darkness and light. Others still call upon the Holy Light they served in life.",al={"undead priests lore","can undead use the light","forsaken shadow priests"}},{q="What is the Sisterhood of Elune?",a="The Sisterhood of Elune is an ancient order of night elf priestesses, established long before the War of the Ancients. Led by High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, they revere the moon goddess Elune. They serve as healers and spiritual guides, and as fiercely capable leaders within night elf society.",al={"night elf priests","priestesses of the moon","sisterhood of elune"}},{q="Which races can be priests?",a="Humans, dwarves, gnomes and night elves train as priests in the Alliance. Trolls and the Forsaken do so in the Horde. Orcs, tauren and the Skyborne do not walk the priest's path.",al={"who can be a priest","priest races","can gnomes be priests","gnome priest"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you walk between pure radiance and devastation of the mind. You command the healing mercy of prayer and the punishing horrors of the Void.",["race:Human"]="As a human priest, you inherit the resilient tradition of the Northshire Clerics. Through the Church of the Holy Light, you help form the spiritual bedrock of the Alliance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf priestess, you honor the Sisterhood of Elune and channel starlight and lunar grace under High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind's guidance.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken priest, you reshape your shattered faith through the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow. You embrace the balance of dark energies after former vows brought only ruin.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you share holy teachings with the priesthood. The paladins arose from the Church's need to protect robed clerics after the bloody lessons of the First War.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome priest, you serve the Holy Light alongside the dwarven clergy of Ironforge's Hall of Mysteries. You tend a people still scattered by Gnomeregan's fall."},kw={"cathedral","cleric","cult","elune","healing","holy light","priest","shadow","sisterhood","void"},rel={"topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:light","topic:elune","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:forsaken","topic:paladin","quest:5650","topic:gnome"},src={"Priest"}}
E["topic:quilboar"] = {t="topic",n="Quilboar",z="general",s="Across central Kalimdor, Quilboar defend their lands with sharp quills and fierce resolve. They claim descent from Agamaggan and dwell in thorn mazes across Durotar, Mulgore, and the Barrens. Their struggles over water, soil, and sacred ground threaten travelers and Horde settlements.",h="Across central Kalimdor, Quilboar defend their lands with sharp quills and fierce resolve.",sec={{t="Children of the Great Boar",b="Quilboar honor Agamaggan, the colossal boar Ancient who died fighting the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago. Their sacred traditions call them his mortal offspring.\n\nWhere Agamaggan bled and died across central Kalimdor, enormous thorny vines burst from scorched earth and formed sprawling root mazes. Quilboar hold these places sacred. Across the Barrens, his crystallized blood remains as crimson Blood Shards. Quilboar geomancers dig them up and honor them as powerful talismans.",sp=0},{t="Bramble Harrows and Geomancy",b="Quilboar build no towns of stone or timber. Instead, they grow colossal briars that choke nearby plants and leave the ground barren. Each tribe is usually guided by powerful geomancers. These practitioners follow a crude, earthbound shamanism, consulting stones and crystals to guide their clan. They call on Agamaggan's spirit to send spectral boars into battle.\n\nThe arid central plains have few oases, so quilboar prize water above all. When rare rains come, they hold lavish feasts. They defend their water holes fiercely.",sp=0},{t="The War for the Barrens",b="For generations, quilboar have clashed with nomadic tauren and roaming centaur packs. When Thrall led the Orcish Horde into Kalimdor, orcs quickly settled Durotar and opened trade routes through the Barrens. Displaced quilboar tribes rose in revolt.\n\nTheir war parties ambush supply wagons, are suspected of driving tallstriders into wagon trains, and raid outposts such as Crossroads and Camp Taurajo. Two tribes dominate the open plains: the Razormane and the Bristleback. Both fight the Horde and each other.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow over Razorfen",b="Razorfen Kraul and nearby Razorfen Downs lie on the Barrens' southern edge, at the spiritual heart of quilboar civilization. Agamaggan's gargantuan remains formed these tangled mazes. An ambitious crone named Charlga Razorflank seized the Kraul and directed attacks on rival clans and Horde territories.\n\nRazorfen Downs, the traditional quilboar capital, has fallen to the Scourge. The corrupted Death's Head quilboar joined the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer and succumbed to undeath. Now the ancestral tomb is a plague-ridden stronghold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do quilboar hate the Horde so much?",a="The Horde displaced quilboar when Thrall's people landed and claimed land for Orgrimmar. Quilboar had occupied Durotar and the Barrens' fertile oases and thorned ravines long before the Horde arrived. Now the tribes see every caravan, outpost, and water well as stolen ancestral ground.",al={"why do quilboar attack orcs","quilboar horde conflict","why are quilboar hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the relationship between quilboar and Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan is a colossal boar Ancient who fought the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago. Quilboar claim descent from him. The great briars they inhabit sprang up where his blood soaked the earth, and the sacred tunnels of Razorfen Downs are said to be carved from his remains.",al={"agamaggan quilboar god","who is agamaggan","quilboar demigod"},it="ties"},{q="What are the red stones quilboar carry?",a="The red crystals are Blood Shards, formed from Agamaggan's petrified blood. Quilboar dig them up across the Barrens, believing they hold the vitality and strength of their fallen ancestor. Geomancers use them to fuel earth rituals and battle enchantments.",al={"blood shards","red rocks quilboar","blood of agamaggan"},it="item"},{q="What kind of magic do quilboar use?",a="Quilboar practice geomancy, an elemental craft like crude shamanism, centered on stone, earth, and thorns. They prize the reading of stones and gems above other mystical arts. Tribal geomancers call on earth spirits, summon brambles to snare foes, and conjure boar spirits in Agamaggan's image.",al={"quilboar magic","quilboar geomancers","what is geomancy"},it="power"},{q="Why are quilboar so protective of water?",a="The Barrens is arid, with very few natural springs and oases. Quilboar regard water as survival, wealth, and spiritual blessing. They feast even when light desert rains fall and fiercely guard springs from approaching caravans and herds.",al={"quilboar water","why quilboar hoard water","quilboar oases"},it="motive"},{q="What is the difference between Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs are vast briar mazes in southern Kalimdor, grown from Agamaggan's carcass. Razorfen Kraul is the stronghold of the crone Charlga Razorflank, who rallies living quilboar against outsiders. Razorfen Downs was the quilboar ancestral capital. Now the Scourge lich Amnennar the Coldbringer rules there and raises dead quilboar as undead minions.",al={"kraul vs downs","razorfen dungeons","where do quilboar live"},sp=1,it="place"},{q="What are quilboar?",a="Quilboar are a primitive, aggressive race of boar-like humanoids native to Kalimdor. Short, hunched, and muscular, their most striking feature is the array of razor-sharp spines that protrudes from their backs and heads. Believed to be the mortal descendants of the demigod Agamaggan, they revere massive bramble thorns and live in fiercely protective tribal societies governed largely by powerful geomancer shamans.",al={"what is quilboar","who are quilboars","quilboar race"},it="identity",add="606f2b6f"},{q="Why are quilboar found in the Barrens and Durotar?",a="Quilboar flock to areas dominated by colossal, thorn-covered roots, believing them to be sacred ground grown from the blood of their fallen god, Agamaggan. Central Kalimdor—spanning the Barrens, Durotar, and Mulgore—contains the heart of these brambles, culminating in the massive colonies of Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs. Their shaman intentionally cultivate and spread these choking thorns wherever they settle.",al={"why are quilboar here","quilboar locations","why do quilboar live in the barrens"},it="why_here",add="d22ef352"},{q="Who leads the quilboar?",a="Quilboar are divided into distinct tribes like the Bristleback, Razormane, and Death's Head, each led by its own chiefs and shamans. However, the crone Charlga Razorflank holds dominion over Razorfen Kraul and commands her followers. Under her tyrannical rule, quilboar stage aggressive strikes against rival tribes, the Horde, and travelers throughout the Barrens.",al={"quilboar leader","who is in charge of quilboar","quilboar crone"},it="leader",add="361cc79b"},{q="Who are the quilboar allied with?",a="Most quilboar tribes are fiercely independent and despise outsiders, fighting anyone who enters their territory. However, Charlga Razorflank and her Death's Head tribe forged a dark alliance with the Scourge. This pact allowed the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer into Razorfen Downs, converting the traditional capital of the quilboar into an undead stronghold bolstered by reanimated boar-folk.",al={"quilboar allies","do quilboar have allies","who do quilboar work for"},it="allies",add="b83eba15"},{q="Where did the quilboar come from?",a="Quilboar believe themselves to be the mortal offspring of Agamaggan, the colossal boar demigod who fought the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. They were already abundant before the Great Sundering. When Agamaggan fell, massive thorn-ridden vines sprouted where his blood seeped into the earth, and the quilboar came to occupy these sacred brambles.",al={"quilboar origin","quilboar history","how were quilboar created"},it="history",add="5fc285c1"},{q="Why are they called quilboar?",a="Their name comes from their distinct appearance: boar-like humanoids bristling with sharp, defensive quills along their spines and skulls. These spines are central to their physiology and identity, used both defensively and launched in battle, with tribal names like Bristleback and Razormane reflecting their formidable quilled backs.",al={"quilboar name meaning","why the name quilboar","why are they called quillboar"},it="name",add="dac333bc"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your ancestors fought quilboar for watering holes and grazing land long before the orcs sailed west. Their spreading briars choke the natural earth sustained by the Earth Mother.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, securing Durotar and the Barrens means breaking quilboar war bands. Their raids keep harassing Horde trade wagons and outlying farmsteads.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see quilboar geomancy as an earthy, ancient branch of shamanic tradition, turned toward territorial brutality and the summoning of savage boar spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face quilboar ambushes along vital caravans between Orgrimmar, the Crossroads, and Thunder Bluff. Their presence threatens supply routes across central Kalimdor."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","blood shards","brambles","bristleback","charlga razorflank","geomancer","quilboar","quillboar","razorfen","razormane"},rel={"topic:agamaggan","zone:barrens","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","npc:charlga-razorflank","topic:tauren","quest:5052","quest:899"},src={"Quilboar"}}
E["topic:ravenholdt"] = {t="topic",n="Ravenholdt",z="general",s="In the mountains above the Hillsbrad Foothills, Ravenholdt wages a shadow war against the Syndicate. Lord Jorach Ravenholdt leads the Assassin's League, a company of rogues, thieves, and killers that keeps clear of faction politics. It recruits the most cunning operatives across Azeroth, prized for discipline, stealth, and lethal efficiency.",h="In the mountains above the Hillsbrad Foothills, Ravenholdt wages a shadow war against the Syndicate.",sec={{t="The Hidden League",b="Ravenholdt Manor gathers Azeroth's foremost brotherhood of assassins in the mountains between Hillsbrad and Alterac. Lord Jorach Ravenholdt leads the League beyond the reach of kings and warchiefs.\n\nMaster Kang teaches close combat and assassination, while the Thunderwood brothers brew rare, deadly poisons. Gnome craftsmen build intricate locks to test new disciples. For anyone who is not a rogue, entering the estate courts death; one careless step can bring a poisoned dagger to the ribs.",sp=0},{t="Shadow War with the Syndicate",b="For years, Ravenholdt has waged an escalating feud against the Syndicate, an aristocratic criminal cartel that infests Alterac and Arathi. The League sees its rivals as clumsy, arrogant amateurs, yet their numbers make them impossible to wipe out through slaughter alone. So contracted rogues pickpocket the signet emblems worn by Syndicate ringleaders. Ravenholdt counts on the Syndicate's paranoia and ruthless hierarchy to execute its disgraced members from within.",sp=0},{t="An Independent Guild of Shadows",b="Ravenholdt sometimes works with other intelligence groups, including Stormwind's SI:7, but answers to no crown. Master Mathias Shaw can find an ally in Jorach Ravenholdt against the Syndicate, yet Jorach guards his independence fiercely.\n\nWhen SI:7 suffered heavy losses investigating the fallen ranger Nathanos Marris in the Plaguelands, Ravenholdt flatly refused Shaw's plea for help. The League chooses its own battles, pursuing ancient relics, perfecting deadly arts, and keeping its blade at the throat of anyone foolish enough to cross it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ravenholdt?",a="Ravenholdt is an ancient, hidden guild of thieves, assassins, and shadow-dancers led by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt. Also called the Assassin's League, it works from a secret mountain estate above the Hillsbrad Foothills, trains promising rogues, and offers deadly contracts.",al={"who are ravenholdt","what is the assassin's league","ravenholdt faction"},it="identity"},{q="Why are they fighting the Syndicate?",a="Ravenholdt and the Syndicate vie for dominance across the ruins of Alterac and the surrounding highlands. The League sees the Syndicate as undisciplined, dishonorable brigands whose messy crimes threaten the region's subtle balance of power. Rather than destroy them through attrition, Ravenholdt undermines their leadership by stealing their rank emblems.",al={"why syndicate vs ravenholdt","ravenholdt syndicate war","why do they hate the syndicate"},it="conflict"},{q="Can non-rogues visit Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Non-rogues can reach Ravenholdt Manor, but entering the estate courts death. Its residents hint at poisoned drinks and daggers in the back for anyone who arrives without shadowcraft credentials or business with Lord Ravenholdt.",al={"can other classes go to ravenholdt","warrior at ravenholdt manor","is ravenholdt rogues only"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Jorach Ravenholdt?",a="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt is the elusive master of the Assassin's League. From his mountain estate, he directs rogue trainers and informants across the continents, sending trusted disciples to recover powerful artifacts and neutralize rival threats.",al={"who leads ravenholdt","jorach ravenholdt","ravenholdt leader"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Rite of Cunning?",a="The Rite of Cunning is an introductory test for those seeking entry to Ravenholdt Manor. An initiate must use trap-detection skills to pass through the mountain tunnel to the grounds, where the rite's danger becomes clear.",al={"rite of cunning","ravenholdt rogue trial","ravenholdt tunnel test"}},{q="How does Ravenholdt view the Alliance and the Horde?",a="Ravenholdt keeps entirely apart from Alliance and Horde politics, accepting skilled cutthroats from Orgrimmar or Ironforge alike. It maintains cordial ties with groups such as Stormwind's SI:7, but refuses to serve any kingdom's war effort.",al={"is ravenholdt alliance or horde","ravenholdt alignment","who does ravenholdt work for"},it="side"},{q="Why is Ravenholdt Manor hidden in the Alterac Mountains?",a="Ravenholdt operates from a secluded manor concealed high in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills to guard its secrets and protect its members from outside scrutiny. Tucked away behind an easily overlooked mountain path, the estate provides an ideal stronghold for an elite assassin's guild, offering security against unwanted intrusions and placing them directly adjacent to the Syndicate forces they actively undermine across the region.",al={"why are they in alterac","ravenholdt manor location why","why hide in hillsbrad mountains"},it="why_here",add="d3774f53"},{q="Who are Ravenholdt allied with?",a="Ravenholdt operates independently as an autonomous league of assassins and thieves, strictly bound to its own interests and code. However, they maintain selective professional contacts with other clandestine circles. They have accepted cooperative aid from Stormwind's intelligence service, SI:7, specifically to root out the Syndicate affliction in the northern kingdoms, though they remain purely mercenary and will refuse requests that do not serve their guild's priorities.",al={"who does ravenholdt work for","ravenholdt allies","ravenholdt connections"},it="allies",add="eb92cd94"},{q="What is the history of Ravenholdt?",a="Formed as the Assassin's League under the leadership of Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, the guild has long gathered the world's finest practitioners of stealth, poison, and theft. Years ago, their treasured artifact, the Horns of Nez'ra, was stolen by the Blackrock clan, sparking a relentless hunt across continents. In recent times, their primary focus has been a bitter, protracted shadow war against the noble-led Syndicate across Alterac and Arathi.",al={"history of ravenholdt","where did ravenholdt come from","origins of ravenholdt"},it="history",add="77e129fe"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Ravenholdt is your far-reaching fraternity and proving ground. Its trainers, poison-brewers, and shadowmasters offer trials, rare weapon schematics, and recognition found nowhere else in Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mathias Shaw and SI:7 sometimes work with Ravenholdt against the Syndicate, but Lord Ravenholdt owes Stormwind no allegiance and may casually rebuff high-stakes Alliance requests.",["faction:Horde"]="Though Ravenholdt has a noble human exterior and lies in the northern highlands, it judges operatives by prowess alone. Horde stalkers are welcome if they prove their mettle."},kw={"alterac","assassin","fahrad","hillsbrad","jorach","lockpicking","manor","poisons","ravenholdt","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:ravenholdt-manor","npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","quest:8249","npc:mathias-shaw","quest:2300"},src={"Ravenholdt"}}
E["topic:razorfen"] = {t="topic",n="Razorfen",z="general",s="Across southern Kalimdor, Razorfen's quilboar defend their thorn-walled homes. Their strongholds span the southern Barrens and the edge of Thousand Needles, where their faith and power run deep.",h="Across southern Kalimdor, Razorfen's quilboar defend their thorn-walled homes.",sec={{t="The Thorns of Agamaggan",b="Razorfen's thorned brambles reach back to the War of the Ancients. Legend says they rose where Agamaggan, the giant boar Ancient, fell fighting the Burning Legion ten thousand years ago. His blood entered the earth, and vast vines of petrified bramble and iron-hard thorns grew there. The quilboar, his descendants, have lived among these defenses ever since.",sp=0},{t="The Razorfen Tribe",b="Razorfen's quilboar are among the most aggressive and firmly rooted of their kind. They build their communities among the vast briars instead of scattering into open warrens. From these strongholds, they defend their ancestral land against neighboring tauren tribes, Horde settlements in the Barrens, and any outsider who enters their holy grounds.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Citadel",b="Razorfen's two bastions hold different places in quilboar life. Razorfen Kraul is the tribe's main stronghold and military camp, guarded by shamans and huntresses. Farther south at the edge of Thousand Needles, Razorfen Downs is their traditional capital, sacred ancestral city, and burial ground of quilboar elders. A deeper necromantic corruption now shadows the city and threatens the surrounding lands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen?",a="Razorfen names a prominent quilboar tribe of the southern Barrens and its settlements, woven through massive briar labyrinths. They include Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs.",al={"what is razorfen","razorfen meaning","razorfen lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the giant thorns come from?",a="Legend says the giant thorns grew from the blood and remains of Agamaggan, the Great Boar. He fell fighting the Burning Legion during the ancient War of the Ancients, and thorned tendrils rose where his blood struck the earth.",al={"giant briars barrens","agamaggan thorns","why giant thorns"},it="origin"},{q="What is the difference between Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Kraul is the tribe's living city and main stronghold, filled with warriors and geomancers. Farther south toward Thousand Needles, Razorfen Downs is the ancestral burial ground and sacred resting place of quilboar elders.",al={"kraul vs downs","difference between razorfen dungeons"}},{q="Why are the quilboar hostile to everyone?",a="The quilboar see the Barrens and its great briars as a divine birthright from Agamaggan. They regard outside races, especially the expanding Horde, as thieves invading their holy ground.",al={"why do quilboar attack","quilboar lore"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is Razorfen located?",a="Razorfen's vast thorn networks lie in the far south of the Barrens, along the high cliffs descending into the salt flats and river canyon of Thousand Needles.",al={"razorfen map location","where is razorfen"},it="place"},{q="What kind of magic do the Razorfen quilboar use?",a="Razorfen quilboar traditionally practice geomancy, an earth and nature magic that calls on stone and thorn. Recent developments within Razorfen Downs reveal alarming incursions of dark necromantic arts.",al={"quilboar magic","razorfen shamans"},it="power"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Razorfen quilboar have fought tauren hunting bands and settlements across the Barrens for generations. Their eradication is a matter of homeland security.",["faction:Horde"]="Control of the southern Barrens is critical to Horde logistics. Razorfen raiders repeatedly harass caravans traveling between Mulgore, Crossroads, and the southern frontier.",["class:Druid"]="The briars of Razorfen grew from the sacrifice of the Ancient Agamaggan. As a druid, you have reason for deep concern when such a sacred site is desecrated and corrupted.",["class:Shaman"]="Razorfen geomancers use crude elemental rites to shape the spirits of earth and stone. As a shaman, you must attend to their work in seeking balance."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","brambles","downs","kraul","quilboar","razorfen","thorns"},rel={"topic:quilboar","subzone:razorfen-kraul-classic","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Razorfen"}}
E["topic:refugee"] = {t="topic",n="Refugee",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Refugees flee as invasion and betrayal bring war to their homes. From Stormwind's fall in the First War to Lordaeron's ruin in the Third, civilians lose their homes and face plague and worse.",h="Across Azeroth, Refugees flee as invasion and betrayal bring war to their homes.",sec={{t="The Exodus of Stormwind",b="The Orcish Horde swept through Stormwind in the First War, burning Goldshire, Moonbrook, and Grand Hamlet. After King Llane Wrynn was assassinated, Sir Anduin Lothar took command of the kingdom's remnants. He gathered surviving soldiers and desperate civilians, then led them to the harbor as the city burned.\n\nLothar guided a massive fleet across the Great Sea to Lordaeron's northern shores. Near Southshore, King Terenas Menethil II granted sanctuary to the exiles, among them the young Prince Varian Wrynn.",sp=0},{t="Flight from the Scourge",b="A generation after Stormwind's exiles found welcome, the Scourge plague and undead legions brought ruin to Lordaeron in the Third War. Prince Arthas Menethil slaughtered his own subjects as he swept across the realm, scattering survivors in terror. Lady Jaina Proudmoore led an expedition of refugees across the sea to Kalimdor, where they eventually established a settlement at Theramore.\n\nCountless others remained in the Eastern Kingdoms. The Scourge, the Forsaken, and monstrous horrors risen from the ruins hunted them.",sp=0},{t="Turned Away at the Gate",b="Many who could not flee Lordaeron across the sea sought shelter behind whatever walls still stood. Desperate refugees traveled south to the massive Greymane Wall and begged to enter Gilneas, a kingdom sealed off from the world. The gates stayed shut.\n\nDestitute on the borders of Silverpine Forest, the survivors huddled in makeshift camps. Selfless caretakers like Dalin Forgewright supported them as they faced starvation, undead raiders, and predatory worgen roaming near Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the people who fled Stormwind during the First War?",a="Sir Anduin Lothar led thousands of Stormwind survivors across the Great Sea to Lordaeron. They landed at Southshore, where King Terenas Menethil II granted them refuge until Stormwind was reclaimed and rebuilt.",al={"stormwind refugees first war","where did stormwind flee","exodus of stormwind"},it="history"},{q="Did all of Stormwind's citizens escape the First War?",a="No. Many died in the streets as Stormwind fell. Countless survivors who never reached the ships wandered Azeroth's wilderness alone.",al={"stormwind survivors","who stayed in stormwind","cathedral of light refugees"},it="history"},{q="Where did the survivors of Lordaeron go?",a="Many refugees sailed west to Kalimdor with Lady Jaina Proudmoore and eventually settled at Theramore. Others scattered across the Eastern Kingdoms, seeking haven in places like Southshore and the Hinterlands, or pleading in vain at the sealed Greymane Wall.",al={"lordaeron refugees","where did lordaeron people go","survivors of the plague"},it="history"},{q="Why didn't Gilneas let the refugees from Lordaeron in?",a="Gilneas chose isolation and closed the Greymane Wall to cut itself off from the world and avoid external wars. When desperate, sick victims of the Scourge reached the gates, Gilneas turned them away, leaving them exposed in Silverpine Forest.",al={"greymane wall refugees","gilneas closed gates","why did greymane lock out survivors"},it="history"},{q="Who helped the refugees stranded outside the Greymane Wall?",a="Dalin Forgewright cared for the haggard, sick refugees stranded outside Gilneas's gates. He tended to their ailments and offered what solace he could in the perilous wilderness.",al={"dalin forgewright","who helped silverpine refugees"},it="people"},{q="Who took in the Stormwind exiles when they reached Lordaeron?",a="King Terenas Menethil II welcomed the Stormwind exiles when their fleet reached Lordaeron's shores near Southshore. He granted them sanctuary in his kingdom.",al={"southshore landing","marcus redpath refugees","who greeted stormwind"},it="allies"},{q="What is a refugee in Azeroth?",a="Refugees are survivors forced from their homes by the unending wars, plagues, and cataclysms that ravage Azeroth. Across the world, whole populations have been displaced when their kingdoms fell—from the citizens of Stormwind driven north across the Great Sea during the First War, to the survivors of Lordaeron fleeing the Scourge in the Third War. Stripped of shelter and safety, they wander in search of sanctuary.",al={"what is a refugee","who are refugees","refugee meaning"},it="identity",add="6f7a70cf"},{q="Why are there so many refugees across Azeroth?",a="You find displaced folk scattered across the world because successive conflicts have shattered entire nations in recent decades. The sacking of Stormwind by the Horde scattered survivors throughout the Eastern Kingdoms, while the Scourge's destruction of Lordaeron sent desperate remnants wandering toward places like the barricaded Greymane Wall or following Jaina Proudmoore overseas to Kalimdor.",al={"why are there refugees","where do refugees come from","refugees reason"},it="why_here",add="8e410108"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you share a history of displacement, from the flight from burning Stormwind to Southshore a generation ago to the escape from Arthas's slaughter in Lordaeron.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance of Lordaeron began with a plea from homeless Stormwind refugees. Shared survival and sanctuary remain its foundations.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you follow the Holy Light's call to aid the dispossessed, as caretakers did when they sheltered the wounded in ruined sanctuaries.",["race:Undead"]="Many Forsaken were once Lordaeron refugees who failed to outrun the plague and the Scourge. They now inhabit the ruined kingdom they died trying to flee."},kw={"exodus","greymane wall","jaina proudmoore","lordaeron","lothar","refugee","silverpine","southshore","stormwind"},rel={"topic:first-war","topic:third-war","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:lordaeron","subzone:southshore","subzone:greymane-wall","npc:jaina-proudmoore","quest:1476"},src={"Refugee"}}
E["topic:riverpaw-pack"] = {t="topic",n="Riverpaw pack",z="multi",s="In Elwynn and Westfall, the Riverpaw pack raids farms and roads and rules local kobolds. Since the Third War, its attacks have grown bolder and better organized as Stormwind's forces are stretched thin.",h="In Elwynn and Westfall, the Riverpaw pack raids farms and roads and rules local kobolds.",sec={{t="A Plague on the Heartland",b="For decades, Riverpaw gnolls stayed near the edges of human lands. In recent years, their raids have grown bolder. In Elwynn Forest, packs led by the infamous brute Hogger prowl the southern woods around Forest's Edge and the shores of Stone Cairn Lake. In Westfall, they cross the Dust Plains and coast, ambushing lone travelers and raiding homesteads.\n\nDeputy Rainer at Westbrook Garrison and Captain Danuvin at Sentinel Hill rely on mercenaries to thin their ranks. They offer standing bounties for painted armbands and severed paws.",sp=0},{t="Merciless Taskmasters",b="The Riverpaws seek more than easy prey. They drove a clan of kobolds from the Redridge Mountains and forced them to work in gold mines across Elwynn Forest and Westfall. There, the kobolds labor for ore until exhaustion.\n\nTheir hold over the kobolds and the mines shows a clan gathering wealth and pressing into strategic ground. Stormwind's attention is elsewhere.",sp=0},{t="Shadows and Gold",b="Ledgers and documents recovered from the Riverpaw pack point to dealings with the Defias Brotherhood. The Stormwind Army first dismissed the gnolls as an animal nuisance. Now Wiley the Black and Captain Danuvin know the pack receives money and direction as part of an effort to destabilize the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who leads the Riverpaw gnolls?",a="Hogger, a massive and ferocious gnoll, is the Riverpaw pack's most infamous leader. He stalks the southwestern woods of Elwynn Forest near Forest's Edge, and Stormwind authorities offer a great bounty for his head.",al={"riverpaw leader","who leads the riverpaw","hogger riverpaw"},it="leader"},{q="Where are Riverpaw gnolls found?",a="Riverpaw gnolls roam southwestern Elwynn Forest around Forest's Edge and Stone Cairn Lake. They also cross Westfall's Dust Plains and coastline.",al={"riverpaw locations","where to find riverpaws","riverpaw gnoll spawn"},it="why_here"},{q="Why are the Riverpaw gnolls working with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Recovered documents show payments passing between the Riverpaw clan and the Defias Brotherhood. The Defias fund and equip the gnolls to spread chaos, plunder resources, and keep local militias occupied across Westfall and Elwynn. This weakens Stormwind's defenses.",al={"riverpaw defias connection","defias paying gnolls","gnoll brotherhood connection"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Why are kobolds working in the gold mines near the Riverpaw?",a="The Riverpaw gnolls drove a clan of Redridge kobolds from their home and enslaved them in mines across Elwynn Forest and Westfall. The gnolls force them to dig for gold to fuel their war efforts.",al={"gnolls and kobolds","why do gnolls have kobold slaves","riverpaw kobolds"}},{q="Why hasn't the Stormwind Army wiped out the Riverpaw pack?",a="Stormwind's military is stretched thin, and rural garrisons such as Sentinel Hill and Westbrook receive few reinforcements. Local marshals rely on passing adventurers and militia bounties to keep Riverpaw numbers in check.",al={"why aren't guards fighting gnolls","stormwind gnoll response"},it="danger"},{q="What is the historical relationship between the Riverpaws and Stormwind?",a="The Riverpaws have clashed with Stormwind for generations. Since the Third War, they have grown bolder and more organized, raiding farms and roads in Elwynn and Westfall while the kingdom's soldiers are stretched thin.",al={"riverpaw history","prince llane gnolls"},it="history"},{q="What is the Riverpaw pack?",a="The Riverpaw pack is an aggressive clan of gnolls indigenous to Elwynn Forest and Westfall. Ferocious, hyena-like scavengers and brigands, they roam the countryside raiding farms, plundering travelers, and clashing with local garrisons. Recently, they have demonstrated an alarming degree of organization, enslaving kobolds to mine gold and aligning themselves with human outlaws to destabilize Stormwind's territories.",al={"riverpaw gnolls identity","who are the riverpaw","what are riverpaws"},it="identity",add="dbbc58c8"},{q="Why are the Riverpaw gnolls hostile to travelers?",a="Like all gnolls, the Riverpaws are vicious, territorial scavengers driven by bloodlust and greed. They view any traveler through Elwynn or Westfall as prey, food, or plunder. Their hostility has only grown bolder and more coordinated as shadowy backers supply them with weapons, magic, and tactical direction to terrorize settlements and drive human defenders out of the countryside.",al={"why do riverpaw attack","riverpaw gnoll hostility","why are gnolls hostile"},it="hostile",add="b2a04ab0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Riverpaws threaten the Alliance heartland and disrupt trade between Goldshire, Westfall, and Redridge. Stormwind's armies are absent.",["race:Human"]="For farmers and homesteaders in Westfall and Elwynn, the Riverpaws threaten their homes. They slaughter families, steal livestock, and seize local mines.",["class:Warrior"]="Town marshals offer warriors coin and prestige to hunt Riverpaw brutes in the brush and challenge their warlords, including Hogger.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues can intercept Riverpaw messengers to learn how criminal syndicates direct the gnolls' violence and uncover intelligence on the Defias network."},kw={"defias","dust plains","elwynn","forest's edge","gnolls","hogger","kobold slaves","riverpaw","westfall"},rel={"npc:hogger","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:176","quest:11","quest:102","subzone:westbrook-garrison"},src={"Riverpaw pack"}}
E["topic:rogue"] = {t="topic",n="Rogue",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Rogues choose when to face danger and when to slip away unseen. Light leather, paired blades, and brewed toxins let them strike before foes can react. They serve as scouts, assassins, pickpockets, and agents of factions and hidden syndicates.",h="Across Azeroth, Rogues choose when to face danger and when to slip away unseen.",sec={{t="Strike from the Shadows",b="Rogues favor quiet, quick attacks over the open clashes of frontline warriors. In light leather, they stalk their quarry unseen. When an opening comes, they strike with precision at vital organs or exposed joints. A swift chain of blows weakens an enemy, and a finishing strike can end the fight.",sp=0},{t="Poisons and Street Smarts",b="A blade alone rarely serves a cutpurse or killer. Rogues brew venoms to numb limbs, slow an escape, or drain a target's strength. Lockpicks, thrown weapons, and tricks that draw attention elsewhere help them slip past guarded walls, disarm traps, and enter vaults that would confound a company of soldiers.",sp=0},{t="Guilds, Crowns, and Syndicates",b="Many rogues work alone as highwaymen or street thugs. The finest join intelligence networks and assassin guilds. Stormwind relies on SI:7, while the Forsaken rely on the relentless Deathstalkers. In Orgrimmar, remnants of the Shattered Hand serve the Warchief. The neutral League of Assassins answers to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What armor and weapons do rogues use?",a="Rogues wear leather armor and favor one-handed weapons, often wielding a blade in each hand. They use daggers, swords, maces, and fist weapons. For ranged attacks, they carry throwing knives, bows, or crossbows.",al={"rogue gear","what can rogues equip","rogue armor type"}},{q="How does stealth work for a rogue?",a="A rogue uses quiet steps and shadow to pass unseen from a distance. An alert guard or enemy may spot one who moves too close. From stealth, rogues can get behind a foe and strike with ambushes, garrotes, or blows that disable.",al={"how does rogue stealth work","can rogues turn invisible","stealth lore"}},{q="What is the Ravenholdt League?",a="The League of Assassins is an ancient, secretive brotherhood based at Ravenholdt Manor in the Alterac Mountains and led by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt. Free of faction ties, the guild devotes itself to the discipline, honor, and business of assassination. It takes contracts without regard to political allegiance.",al={"who are ravenholdt","assassins league","lord jorach ravenholdt"}},{q="What is SI:7?",a="SI:7 is Stormwind's chief covert intelligence and reconnaissance wing, based in Stormwind City. Its field agents, snipers, and thieves carry out espionage, high-profile assassinations, and border reconnaissance to protect Alliance interests across Azeroth.",al={"stormwind si7","si7","stormwind intelligence"}},{q="How do rogues fight in prolonged combat?",a="When a first strike fails to end a fight, rogues use agility and footwork to avoid counterblows. They attack in quick succession with paired weapons, find openings, then finish with lethal moves such as ruptures or eviscerations.",al={"rogue combat style","combo points lore","how do rogues fight"}},{q="Do rogues use magic?",a="Most rogues depend on physical conditioning, martial training, alchemy, and ordinary stealth. Skilled practitioners may also use minor mysticism or shadow magic to conceal themselves, slip into shadows in daylight, or vanish from sight.",al={"is rogue stealth magic","do rogues cast spells"}},{q="Which races can be rogues?",a="All races except the tauren can be rogues: humans, dwarves, gnomes, and night elves in the Alliance; orcs, trolls, and the Forsaken in the Horde; and the Skyborne on either side.",al={"who can be a rogue","rogue races","can tauren be rogues"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you rely on patience and precision, whether you serve high command or pick pockets in city alleys.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance's covert strength includes Stormwind's SI:7, which handles threats within its borders and beyond them.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on the Shattered Hand in Orgrimmar and Sylvanas Windrunner's feared Deathstalkers in the Undercity to scout enemy territory and quietly eliminate threats."},kw={"assassin","deathstalker","eviscerate","lockpicking","poisons","ravenholdt","rogue","shattered hand","si:7","stealth"},rel={"topic:ravenholdt","npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt","quest:2300","quest:1858","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:forsaken","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:forlorn-cavern"},src={"Rogue"}}
E["topic:royal-apothecary-society"] = {t="topic",n="Royal Apothecary Society",z="general",s="Beneath the Undercity, the Royal Apothecary Society works under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Its Forsaken researchers seek a New Plague to destroy the Scourge and avenge themselves on the living. They tell Horde allies they seek a cure for undeath, while agents gather venoms, slimes, and toxic reagents across Azeroth.",h="Beneath the Undercity, the Royal Apothecary Society works under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",sec={{t="Vengeance Through Alchemy",b="After the Forsaken won their freedom, the Royal Apothecary Society became the scientific and alchemical arm of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's kingdom. In the Apothecarium's vats and underground laboratories, researchers try to turn the force that damned them into a weapon. Their chief work is a New Plague meant to eradicate the Scourge and destroy the Lich King.\n\nHuman alchemists often pursue healing draughts or transmutation. The Society experiments with pathogens, caustic acids, and necromantic mixtures. Its alchemists also raise fallen warhorses as skeletal steeds and brew ever deadlier strains of toxic blight.",sp=0},{t="A Calculated Deception",b="The Royal Apothecary Society tells its allies in Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff that its alchemists seek a remedy for undeath. The claim makes its members seem like misunderstood scholars laboring for their people. Master Apothecary Faranell and the dark council have little interest in curing the affliction.\n\nIn secret, the Society refines toxins that spare no one. Its researchers test them on living and undead subjects to ensure their enemies can be annihilated.",sp=1},{t="Outposts Across Azeroth",b="The Apothecary Society sends its work far beyond the Undercity's canals. Field apothecaries serve at remote outposts across Lordaeron and Kalimdor. In Silverpine and Hillsbrad, Apothecaries Renferrel and Lydon gather local plants and distill venoms. In the arid Barrens, Apothecary Helbrim catalogs strange desert plants and creatures.\n\nApothecary Zamah works beneath Thunder Bluff in the Pools of Vision. The Society sends acolytes wherever natural toxins, shifting oozes, or virulent organisms can be found. They collect samples for the Apothecarium's cauldrons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is the Forsaken alchemical order based in the Apothecarium beneath the Undercity. Founded under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, its members study pathogens, necromancy, and toxic reagents to make weapons for the Forsaken.",al={"what is the ras","who are the apothecaries","forsaken alchemy guild"},it="identity"},{q="What is the New Plague they are working on?",a="The New Plague is an alchemical pathogen the Society develops under Sylvanas's direct orders. It is meant to destroy the Scourge and the Lich King, while remaining lethal to living beings who threaten the Forsaken.",al={"new plague explained","what is the forsaken plague","why make a new plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Does the Horde know what the Society is really brewing?",a="No. The Forsaken tell their Horde allies they seek a remedy for undeath and a peaceful place for their people. Tauren and Orcs believe the apothecaries pursue a cure, unaware that the Society is making a weapon of annihilation.",al={"does thrall know about the plague","horde stance on apothecaries","do orcs know about the plague"},it="ties"},{q="Who leads the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="Queen Sylvanas Windrunner holds authority over the Royal Apothecary Society. Master Apothecary Faranell and other senior overseers direct its daily scientific work and research in the Undercity.",al={"leader of the apothecaries","ras leader","who runs the apothecarium"},it="leader"},{q="Why are apothecaries stationed in places like the Barrens or Thunder Bluff?",a="Field apothecaries seek biological agents, exotic venom, fungi, and mutagenic oozes that Lordaeron lacks. Helbrim in the Crossroads and Zamah in Thunder Bluff study local life and send dangerous samples to the Undercity laboratories.",al={"why are apothecaries in kalimdor","apothecaries outside tirisfal","apothecary zamah pools of vision"},it="why_here"},{q="How does the Society create Forsaken mounts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society uses dark alchemy and necromancy to raise fallen warhorses as skeletal mounts for Forsaken riders in battle.",al={"where do undead horses come from","forsaken mount lore","skeletal horse origin"}},{q="Who is the Royal Apothecary Society allied with?",a="The Society serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner directly as an organ of the Forsaken state, working in close cooperation with her dreadlord enforcer Varimathras for supplies and subjects. Through the Forsaken, they are nominally part of the Horde, though their relationship with the rest of the faction is built on deceit: while the orcs and tauren believe the Society seeks a cure for undeath, the apothecaries operate purely in service to Sylvanas's vengeance.",al={"apothecary society allies","who do the apothecaries work for","who controls royal apothecary society"},it="allies",add="da4c33fe"},{q="How was the Royal Apothecary Society formed?",a="The Society was founded after Sylvanas established the Forsaken realm in the Undercity, to turn the plague that created the Forsaken into a weapon against their enemies. Today Master Apothecary Faranell directs its research from the Apothecarium beneath the capital.",al={"origin of the royal apothecary society","how did the apothecary society start","history of royal apothecary society"},it="history",add="ac67cb21"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, your people turn the plague that butchered Lordaeron into an instrument of vengeance against the Scourge and all who oppose you.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear Forsaken representatives say their alchemical work seeks a cure for undeath. Their cauldrons in the Apothecarium hide more deadly aims.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know the Society prizes deadly plants, gathering toxic fungi, stranglekelp, and grave moss across Azeroth for its cauldrons.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know your elders allowed Apothecary Zamah into the Pools of Vision out of pity for the cursed dead. They believed the Forsaken sought a cure for their affliction."},kw={"alchemy","apothecarium","faranell","helbrim","lydon","new plague","royal apothecary society","sylvanas windrunner","undercity","zamah"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","quest:367","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge"},src={"Royal Apothecary Society"}}
E["topic:ruins-of-gilneas"] = {t="topic",n="Gilneas",z="general",s="Beyond the Greymane Wall, Gilneas keeps the world at a distance. The human kingdom lies on a rugged peninsula south of Silverpine Forest, sealed away after the Second War by King Genn Greymane.",h="Beyond the Greymane Wall, Gilneas keeps the world at a distance.",sec={{t="A Nation Withdrawn",b="Gilneas once ruled the waves among the human kingdoms and traced its line to Arathor, the ancient human empire. King Genn Greymane entered the Second War reluctantly. He believed his realm could defend itself without ties to foreign powers.\n\nBitter over Gilnean deaths and unwilling to help pay for internment camps holding captured orcs, he broke with the Alliance of Lordaeron. Then he ordered a great stone wall along Gilneas's northern frontier to shield the kingdom from calamity beyond its borders.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Frontier",b="The Greymane Wall left two villages exposed. Its builders anchored the ramparts to natural mountain passes, leaving Ambermill and Pyrewood Village beyond the gate on the northern side. When the Scourge crossed Lordaeron during the Third War, King Greymane refused pleas for aid. He barred human refugees from entering, and the villages beyond the wall faced plague and undead alone.",sp=0},{t="A Looming Shadow",b="During the Third War, Dalaran archmage Arugal summoned feral worgen to aid the Kirin Tor against the Scourge. The beasts slew the undead, then turned on the wizards and besieged Baron Silverlaine's keep. They spread through the shadows of Silverpine. Gilneas remains sealed behind its gates and treacherous sea reefs, while eerie rumors and silence shroud the kingdom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Can players enter Gilneas?",a="No. Gilneas lies behind the Greymane Wall at Silverpine Forest's southern border. Its iron gate is barred, and sheer sea cliffs and treacherous reefs guard the peninsula's coast.",al={"can you go past greymane wall","is gilneas open","get into gilneas"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why was the Greymane Wall built?",a="King Genn Greymane believed Gilneas could stand on its own and resented spending lives and resources to aid other human nations. After the Second War, bitter over debts, internment camps and foreign conflicts, he built the wall to isolate Gilneas from the rest of Lordaeron.",al={"why did gilneas isolate","greymane wall purpose","why closed off"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to Pyrewood Village and Ambermill?",a="The Greymane Wall followed defensible mountain ridges, leaving Pyrewood Village and Ambermill on its northern side, outside the kingdom. Once the gates were sealed, the villages were cut off from Gilneas.",al={"why is pyrewood outside wall","ambermill gilneas connection"},it="ruin"},{q="Is Gilneas part of the Alliance?",a="No. Genn Greymane withdrew Gilneas from the Alliance of Lordaeron. The kingdom has no diplomatic ties, military treaties or trade with Stormwind, Ironforge or any other Alliance power.",al={"gilneas faction","are gilneans in the alliance","gilneas alliance"},it="allies"},{q="What connection does Arugal have to Gilneas?",a="During the Third War, Dalaran archmage Arugal summoned feral worgen to aid the Kirin Tor against the Scourge. They slew the undead, then turned on the wizards, overran Shadowfang Keep and spread through Silverpine, driving Arugal mad.",al={"arugal gilneas","how did arugal get worgen"},it="ties"},{q="Who rules Gilneas?",a="King Genn Greymane rules Gilneas. He fiercely guards the kingdom's independence, leaving the world beyond its gates to fend for itself.",al={"gilneas leader","king of gilneas"},it="leader"},{q="What is Gilneas?",a="Gilneas is an ancient human kingdom situated on a rugged peninsula southwest of Silverpine Forest. Once an influential member of the original Alliance of Lordaeron, its rulers chose a path of fierce isolationism after the Second War. Today, the entire kingdom remains sealed away behind the towering Greymane Wall, cut off from the rest of Azeroth by land and guarded by stormy seas and jagged reefs.",al={"what is gilneas","ruins of gilneas","gilneas kingdom"},it="identity",add="54d2a8c9"},{q="What is the history of Gilneas?",a="Gilneas arose over two thousand years ago as an independent city-state during the expansion of the human empire of Arathor. Known for its self-reliance, the kingdom joined the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. Disillusioned with the costs of the conflict and unwilling to help pay for orcish internment camps, King Genn Greymane severed ties with his allies and constructed the Greymane Wall to shut out foreign troubles.",al={"gilneas history","origin of gilneas","how was gilneas founded"},it="history",add="8a1cf72e"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Lordaeron or Stormwind, you may see Gilneas as a bitter reminder of how pride and isolation broke the unity of the Seven Kingdoms before the Third War.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you patrol southern Silverpine and watch the great gate. A whole human kingdom remains alive and hostile just across your border.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Archmage Arugal's summoning beneath the Greymane Wall as a grim warning of magic turned to war without restraint."},kw={"ambermill","arugal","genn","gilneas","greymane","greymane wall","pyrewood","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","npc:arugal","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","topic:worgen","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron"},src={"Ruins of Gilneas"}}
E["topic:sargeras"] = {t="topic",n="Sargeras",z="general",s="Once the Pantheon’s greatest warrior, Sargeras now leads the Burning Legion against all life. Despair turned him against his kind, and his designs brought the Sundering and later demonic catastrophes.",h="Once the Pantheon’s greatest warrior, Sargeras now leads the Burning Legion against all life.",sec={{t="Champion of the Pantheon",b="Sargeras once guarded the Pantheon’s creations across the Great Dark Beyond. The Pantheon of Order had charged their greatest warrior with that duty. There he fought demons born in the Twisting Nether. Unable to imagine pure evil, he trapped countless fiends in a great prison. Yet eons of battle against cosmic horrors slowly wore down his altruistic spirit.",sp=0},{t="Despair and the Burning Crusade",b="Across eons of battle, Sargeras lost faith in the titans’ work. Despair at the evil he faced led him to believe creation was flawed and order could never prevail. He turned from the Pantheon and shattered the demons’ prison. Then he took up the chaotic fel fire he had once fought. Sargeras gathered the freed demons into the Burning Legion, an army bent on scouring life from the cosmos.",sp=0},{t="Obsession with Azeroth",b="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara and her Highborne wielded reckless magic that reached across the stars. That magic revealed Azeroth to Sargeras. From the depths of the Well of Eternity, the Dark Titan whispered to Azshara and seduced her into opening a portal for his vanguard.\n\nThe invasion ended in the catastrophic Sundering. Yet Sargeras kept plotting to consume Azeroth. He orchestrated the opening of the Dark Portal and guided the demonic corruption of the orcish Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sargeras?",a="Sargeras is a fallen titan who once served as the Pantheon’s greatest warrior. Despair over cosmic evil turned him against his kind. He forged the Burning Legion to purge life from the universe.",al={"sargeras backstory","who is the dark titan","creator of the burning legion"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sargeras want to destroy the universe?",a="Eons of battle with demons and corruption drove Sargeras to despair. He came to believe creation was flawed and order could never prevail. So he chose to burn away all life.",al={"sargeras motive","why burning crusade","why does sargeras want to destroy everything"},it="motive"},{q="What is Sargeras's connection to Queen Azshara?",a="Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara’s reckless use of the Well of Eternity drew Sargeras’s attention. She and her Highborne saw him as a god and tried to summon the Dark Titan through the Well. Their attempt brought the War of the Ancients and the Great Sundering.",al={"sargeras and azshara","well of eternity sargeras","ancient invasion azshara"},it="ties"},{q="Did Sargeras create the demons?",a="No. Demons arose naturally in the chaotic Twisting Nether. Sargeras fought and imprisoned them for ages, then broke their prison and united them under his command as the Burning Legion.",al={"did sargeras make demons","where did the burning legion come from"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the other titans?",a="Mortal scholars do not know what became of the other titans. They left Azeroth long ago after shaping it. Nothing known on Azeroth tells what became of them after Sargeras turned against his kin.",al={"where are the other titans","pantheon fate","did sargeras kill the pantheon"},it="history"},{q="How was Sargeras connected to the opening of the Dark Portal?",a="Long after the Sundering, Sargeras pursued his designs on Azeroth from afar. He arranged the corruption of the orcs of Draenor and used the guardian Medivh to tear open the Dark Portal. Invasion came to mortal shores again.",al={"sargeras orcs","sargeras dark portal","did sargeras bring orcs"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are Sargeras's allies in the cosmos?",a="Sargeras commands the Burning Legion, a vast and terrifying horde of demonic entities he bound to his will. Rather than fighting alongside equal allies, he rules over corrupted races such as the eredar lords Archimonde and Kil'jaeden, dreadful pit lords like Mannoroth, cunning nathrezim dreadlords, and endless ranks of lesser demons. All in the Legion exist solely to serve his apocalyptic crusade.",al={"sargeras allies","who serves sargeras","sargeras burning legion"},it="allies",add="f96cad47"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Sargeras is the architect of the Great Sundering. His whispers corrupted Queen Azshara and shattered ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you draw on fel power and demon servants bound together by the Dark Titan. You wield the ruinous sorceries that formed the Legion.",["race:Orc"]="The tragic history of the orcish clans traces back to Sargeras and his demonic lieutenants. Their blood-curse and madness led to the invasion of Azeroth.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you remember Sargeras as a terror. Unchecked arcane ambition drew the Burning Legion’s gaze across the stars."},kw={"aggramar","azshara","burning legion","dark titan","fel","pantheon","sargeras","sundering"},rel={"topic:burning-legion","topic:titan","topic:old-god","topic:highborne","zone:azshara","subzone:dark-portal","topic:horde"},src={"Sargeras"}}
E["topic:satyr"] = {t="topic",n="Satyr",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, satyr sects foul woodlands and moonwells. They began as Highborne night elves, transformed by Sargeras during the War of the Ancients. Now they torment their kaldorei kin and spread fel corruption in the Burning Legion’s name.",h="Across Kalimdor, satyr sects foul woodlands and moonwells.",sec={{t="Origins of the Curse",b="During the War of the Ancients, Xavius failed to hold the Burning Legion’s first gateway against Malfurion Stormrage. Sargeras tore apart the Highborne councilor’s spirit, then remade him as punishment and a tool. Xavius kept an elven torso but gained horns, taloned claws, a leonine tail, and a goat’s cloven lower body.\n\nSent back to Zin-Azshari, Xavius eagerly spread his fel affliction among other power-hungry Highborne. Xavius was struck down, but his demonic descendants survived. They still seek to make more of their kind by corrupting others.",sp=0},{t="After the Sundering",b="After the Great Sundering, surviving satyrs continued to threaten the shattered night elf civilization. Over the ages, they were broken and driven away. Their remnants split into scattered sects that linger in dark forests and ancient ruins, still hating their kaldorei cousins.",sp=0},{t="Corrupters of Kalimdor",b="Satyr clans now dwell in deep woodland enclaves across Kalimdor, from Darkshore and Ashenvale to Felwood, Azshara, and Feralas. They feed on the land’s pure magic, leeching and spoiling nature until their hooves swell with drained arcane energy.\n\nSatyrs turn peaceful furbolg tribes violent, taint ancient moonwells, and work as covert liaisons for the Shadow Council and the Burning Blade. Some join Twilight’s Hammer cultists or hide in ancient ruins such as Dire Maul. All remain bound to the Burning Legion’s shadow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What exactly is a satyr?",a="A satyr is a demon made from a night elf by an ancient fel curse. Satyrs have cloven hooves, horns, sharp claws, and a tail. Their elven torsos bear mastery of dark fel sorcery and physical savagery.",al={"what are satyrs","satyr race","satyr lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who was the first satyr?",a="Lord Xavius, Highborne sorcerer and chief advisor to Queen Azshara, was the first satyr. He failed to defend the Burning Legion’s portal during the War of the Ancients. Sargeras then remade his body into a horned demon as punishment and a dark gift.",al={"first satyr","who created satyrs","xavius satyr"},it="origin"},{q="Can satyrs make new satyrs?",a="Yes. Satyrs can pass their transformative curse to other beings, chiefly night elves. The magic has weakened over the millennia, so successful transformations are far rarer now. Scattered cultists sometimes revere Xavius in hope of gaining the transformation.",al={"how are satyrs made","satyr curse spread","becoming a satyr"},it="power"},{q="Are there female satyrs?",a="Scattered reports speak of female satyrs, but no irrefutable proof of their existence has been secured.",al={"female satyrs","are all satyrs male","girl satyr"},it="people"},{q="Why do satyrs target moonwells and forests?",a="Satyrs feed on purity and natural arcane magic, drawing it from pristine lands and night elf moonwells. The stolen energy gathers in their hooves, which swell and lose their cloven shape as they absorb immense magical power.",al={"why do satyrs corrupt moonwells","satyr hooves lore","satyr magic"},it="motive"},{q="Where are satyrs found right now?",a="Satyrs are scattered through ruined and corrupted reaches of Kalimdor: Satyrnaar and Xavian in Ashenvale, Bashal'Aran in Darkshore, Jadefire Run in Felwood, Sargeron in Desolace, the Haldarr and Legash encampments in Azshara, and Dire Maul in Feralas.",al={"satyr locations","where do satyrs live","satyr zones"},it="why_here"},{q="Why are satyrs hostile to travelers?",a="Satyrs are thoroughly demonic beings consumed by cruelty and spite. They delight in inflicting physical and emotional pain upon mortals, harboring a deep, ancient hatred particularly for night elves. As servants of demonic corruption, they see any uncorrupted travelers as trespassers and prey, actively striving to taint the land and butcher anyone who stands in the way of spreading their fel corruption.",al={"why do satyrs attack","are satyrs hostile","why satyrs fight"},it="hostile",add="5dcac0d4"},{q="Who leads the satyrs?",a="They have no single overall ruler. In the ages after the War of the Ancients, their centralized hierarchy shattered completely, forcing them into fractured sects and cults. Each local band answers to its own warlord or sorcerer—such as Prince Xavalis in Felwood. Many continue to revere the memory of Xavius, the first satyr, hoping he will return to command them.",al={"satyr leader","who is the satyr king","satyr leadership"},it="leader",add="bac5d43e"},{q="Who are satyrs allied with?",a="Most satyrs remain bound to the will of the Burning Legion, operating alongside demonic remnants and demonic cults like the Shadow Council and the Burning Blade. While some isolated sects act on their own or ally with other dark forces such as the Twilight's Hammer, they ultimately remain demonic thralls who will answer the call whenever the Legion commands them.",al={"satyr allies","who do satyrs serve","satyr factions"},it="allies",add="6fc26cea"},{q="What is the history of the satyrs?",a="Satyrs arose during the War of the Ancients when Sargeras punished the Highborne sorcerer Xavius by reshaping his soul and body into the first horned, cloven-hoofed demon. Xavius passed this demonic curse to other ambitious Highborne. After the Legion fell, the satyrs waged a desperate war against the night elves until they were broken and scattered, lingering in ruined forests as bitter, fragmented remnants.",al={"satyr history","how were satyrs created","where did satyrs come from"},it="history",add="5221b631"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see satyrs as the ultimate betrayal of kaldorei heritage. They are a bitter reminder of the Highborne’s arrogance during the War of the Ancients.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know satyrs poison the wilds, corrupt furbolgs, and defile sacred groves. The Cenarion Circle sees their destruction as urgent.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see the corruptive power of the Burning Legion’s ancient curses in satyrs. Their malice is demonic.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you fight alongside Sentinels to clear satyr camps encroaching on night elven settlements in Ashenvale and Darkshore.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you clash with satyr sects in Ashenvale and Desolace. You root out their secret alliances with the Burning Blade."},kw={"corrupter","demon","fel","highborne","jadefire","sargeron","satyr","satyrnaar","xavian","xavius"},rel={"topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf","topic:burning-legion","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood","subzone:satyrnaar","quest:1842"},src={"Satyr"}}
E["topic:scarlet-crusade"] = {t="topic",n="Scarlet Crusade",z="general",s="Across Tirisfal Glades and the Plaguelands, crimson banners mark the Scarlet Crusade's war on the undead. The crusaders rose from the broken Knights of the Silver Hand to reclaim Lordaeron. Paranoia blinds them to anyone beyond their ranks, whom they brand plague carriers and shoot on sight.",h="Across Tirisfal Glades and the Plaguelands, crimson banners mark the Scarlet Crusade's war on the undead.",sec={{t="Rise from the Ashes",b="After Prince Arthas betrayed Lordaeron and murdered King Terenas Menethil II, the Order of the Silver Hand broke apart. Surviving paladins and priests rallied around leaders such as Alexandros Mograine, saidan dathrohan, and General Abbendis.\n\nThey gathered at Hearthglen and Tyr's Hand to reclaim their ruined homeland, then swore to burn away the undead scourge with holy fire. As the war dragged on, tragedy and suspicion took hold. Their desperate resistance hardened into an unyielding, xenophobic crusade.",sp=0},{t="The Great Schism",b="As the Crusade's teachings hardened into madness, moderate commanders recoiled. Lord Maxwell Tyrosus and his followers argued that reclaiming the north required allies across Azeroth, and sought aid from dwarves, gnomes, and night elves. The zealots refused, so Tyrosus and other disillusioned knights left to form the Argent Dawn, devoted to the Holy Light's pure and inclusive tenets.\n\nThe Scarlet Crusade made the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades its center of power. There, they slaughter travelers and refugees, convinced that all who walk the Plaguelands carry the Scourge's contagion.",sp=0},{t="A Puppet in Crimson",b="The Scarlet Crusade's descent into butchery was not entirely its own. During an assault on Stratholme, Grand Crusader saidan dathrohan became separated from his men. The dreadlord Balnazzar quietly murdered him, took possession of his corpse, and seized direct control of the Scarlet ranks.\n\nBalnazzar fed their paranoia and arranged for Highlord alexandros mograine to be murdered through the jealousy of his son renault. Beneath speeches of purity and righteous fury, the crusaders unknowingly serve the demonic darkness they believe the Light commands them to destroy.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile to everyone?",a="The Scarlet Crusade's paranoia grew after Lordaeron fell. They believe anyone who has spent time in northern Lordaeron without their order's cleansing carries the plague of undeath, whether openly or in wait. To preserve their vision of pure humanity, they execute outsiders on sight.",al={"why are scarlets hostile","are scarlets bad guys","why does scarlet crusade attack me"},it="hostile"},{q="Where did the Scarlet Crusade come from?",a="The Scarlet Crusade arose from surviving knights and priests of the Knights of the Silver Hand after Lordaeron fell during the Third War. They regrouped at Hearthglen and the Scarlet Monastery under leaders such as Saidan Dathrohan and Alexandros Mograine. They pledged to eradicate the Scourge by any means.",al={"scarlet crusade origin","who founded scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade history"},it="history"},{q="How is the Scarlet Crusade different from the Argent Dawn?",a="Both orders broke from the original Silver Hand. The Argent Dawn welcomes all races and follows the Light's compassionate virtues. The Scarlet Crusade became a fanatical, human-supremacist cult that massacres refugees and travelers in the name of holy cleansing.",al={"argent dawn vs scarlet crusade","difference between scarlet and argent dawn"},it="conflict"},{q="Where are the Scarlet Crusade's main bases located?",a="The Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades is the Crusade's chief stronghold. They also control Hearthglen in the Western Plaguelands, Tyr's Hand in the east, and the Scarlet Bastion in Stratholme's ruins. Scout towers stand across the region.",al={"scarlet crusade bases","scarlet locations","where are scarlet crusaders"},it="why_here"},{q="Who actually leads the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Grand Crusader Saidan Dathrohan appears to command the Crusade from Stratholme. High Inquisitor Whitemane and Scarlet Commander Mograine support him at the Monastery.",al={"who is leader of scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade grand crusader"},sp=2,it="leader"},{q="Can the Scarlet Crusaders still use the Holy Light if they are evil?",a="Yes. The Light answers absolute conviction and faith, not moral goodness. The crusaders believe their brutal cause is pure and just, and that belief lets them wield holy wrath despite their cruelty.",al={"why can scarlets use the light","scarlet crusade paladins light","do scarlets have the light"},it="power"},{q="What is the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical religious order of human zealots dedicated to wiping out all undead from the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. Originally formed from surviving paladins and priests of the Knights of the Silver Hand after the Third War, their righteous cause quickly devolved into paranoid extremism. Convinced that anyone outside their ranks could carry the plague, they violently purge any outsider they encounter.",al={"who are scarlet crusade","scarlet crusaders who are they","what are the scarlets"},it="identity",add="7fbcc7ca"},{q="Who is the Scarlet Crusade allied with?",a="They have no true allies. While born from the ruins of the human Alliance of Lordaeron, the Scarlet Crusade views all outsiders as potential carriers of the Scourge plague or traitors to humanity. They reject the Alliance of Stormwind, murder night elves, dwarves, and gnomes on sight, and wage relentless war against both the Scourge and the Forsaken.",al={"scarlet crusade allies","who supports scarlet crusade","are scarlets part of the alliance"},it="allies",add="6a9b40aa"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see how the Scarlet Crusade twists the Silver Hand's teachings. Righteous conviction without humility or compassion can become tyranny.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you face the Scarlet Crusade as the Forsaken's nearest living enemy. They contest Tirisfal Glades' borders and hunt undead who have escaped the Lich King's grasp.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you may wear Lordaeron's armor and speak its tongue, but the Scarlet Crusade considers the modern Alliance compromised. They execute Alliance emissaries without hesitation.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see how faith loses its bounds without moral restraint. The Crusade's followers use holy scripture to justify ruthless inquisitions and village purges."},kw={"argent dawn","ashbringer","hearthglen","saidan dathrohan","sally whitemane","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","silver hand","tyr's hand"},rel={"zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:argent-dawn","npc:sally-whitemane","subzone:stratholme","subzone:hearthglen","subzone:tyr-s-hand"},src={"Scarlet Crusade"}}
E["topic:scourge"] = {t="topic",n="Scourge",z="general",s="Across Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas, the Scourge leaves kingdoms in ruin. The Burning Legion made it to weaken Azeroth before the Third War. Its undead, necromancers, and enslaved spirits broke free of demonic control. Now it wages war from Northrend and the corrupted Plaguelands.",h="Across Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas, the Scourge leaves kingdoms in ruin.",sec={{t="A Plague of Demonic Design",b="The Burning Legion made the Scourge to destroy Azeroth. The demon lords bound the spirit of fallen orc shaman Ner'zhul to the Frozen Throne in Northrend and made him the Lich King. His terrifying telepathic power was meant to prepare the world for conquest. He sent the Plague of Undeath south into Lordaeron, where mortal traitors in the Cult of the Damned poisoned the grain. Those who died rose again as twisted thralls bound to his will.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the North",b="Prince Arthas Menethil heeded the Lich King's whispers, and the Scourge brought ruin to the north. Seeking vengeance in Northrend, Arthas claimed Frostmourne and lost his soul. He became the Scourge's foremost death knight. Returning home, he slew his father, King Terenas, butchered Capital City, and sent the undead across Lordaeron.\n\nThey swept through Darrowshire and Andorhal, slaughtered the Silver Hand paladins, and destroyed Dalaran to summon Archimonde. Across Quel'Thalas, they cut a dead scar to raise Kel'Thuzad as a lich.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and the Schism",b="Ner'zhul never meant to serve the Burning Legion forever. Through Arthas, he secretly brought about the Legion's defeat by urging Illidan Stormrage to kill the dreadlord Tichondrius in Felwood. Enraged, Kil'jaeden later ordered Illidan to destroy the Frozen Throne. Illidan's attack cracked the icy prison and weakened the Lich King's hold over his minions.\n\nLed by the resurrected banshee Sylvanas Windrunner, a faction of free-willed undead broke away and took the name Forsaken. They seized the ruins of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="The Present Threat",b="Even after the Frozen Throne was damaged and the Forsaken rebelled, the Scourge remains the deadliest force in the northern world. The lich Kel'Thuzad leads its forces in the field. Abominations, crypt fiends, and necromancers rule the corrupted Eastweald and Westweald, now called the Plaguelands.\n\nFrom grim strongholds and blighted fields, the Scourge wages war against the Forsaken of the Undercity, the fanatics of the Scarlet Crusade, and the Alliance's remaining enclaves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scourge?",a="The Scourge is a vast host of undead thralls, necromancers, and warped beasts bound to the Lich King's mind. It seeks to destroy the living and make the fallen its servants.",al={"what is the scourge","undead scourge","who are the scourge"},it="identity"},{q="Who leads the Scourge?",a="The Lich King commands the Scourge from his Frozen Throne in Northrend. In Lordaeron's ruins, lieutenants such as the lich Kel'Thuzad direct its armies.",al={"who is the scourge leader","scourge master","who controls the scourge"},it="leader"},{q="How does the Scourge differ from the Forsaken?",a="The Scourge are undead dominated by the Lich King's will. The Forsaken were Scourge victims who regained their freedom when his power weakened. Led by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, they hate the Scourge and fight to destroy it.",al={"scourge vs forsaken","are forsaken scourge","why are undead fighting each other"},it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Scourge attack Lordaeron?",a="The Burning Legion ordered the Lich King to spread the Plague of Undeath across Lordaeron. It was meant to slaughter the people, weaken the Alliance, and clear resistance before the demons invaded Azeroth during the Third War.",al={"why destroy lordaeron","scourging of lordaeron","why did scourge invade"},it="history"},{q="Who is the Cult of the Damned?",a="The Cult of the Damned is a mortal group founded by the archmage Kel'Thuzad. Its living human members chose to serve the Lich King for promises of dark magic and eternal life through undeath. They spread the tainted grain that began the plague.",al={"cult of the damned","scourge cultists","why do humans join scourge"},it="allies"},{q="How was Prince Arthas corrupted by the Scourge?",a="Prince Arthas pursued the dreadlord Mal'Ganis to Northrend, obsessed with saving his kingdom from the plague. In desperation, he took Frostmourne, a cursed runeblade that stole his soul. The Lich King's whispers twisted him into the Scourge's foremost champion, and Arthas butchered his homeland.",al={"how did arthas turn","arthas scourge","why did arthas betray his people"},it="history"},{q="Why is the undead army called the Scourge?",a="The necromancer Kel'Thuzad bestowed the name upon the army as he watched its ranks swell with freshly infected victims in northern Lordaeron. Beholding the monstrous host of mindless undead and devoted cultists rising under the Lich King's dark will, he proclaimed that the army would act as a scourge to sweep down upon the living and scour humanity from the face of the world.",al={"why called scourge","scourge name origin","how did scourge get its name"},it="name",add="8fc504d6"},{q="Why are the Scourge hostile to everyone?",a="The Scourge exists for a single horrific purpose: the eradication of all mortal life. Bound telepathically to the absolute will of the Lich King, its legions of rotting corpses, banshees, and monstrosities feel no mercy, exhaustion, or doubt. They view any living traveler as both an enemy to slaughter and fresh material to raise into their ever-expanding army of the dead.",al={"why does the scourge attack","why is scourge hostile","scourge aggressive why"},it="hostile",add="4bf4ad75"},{q="Where did the Scourge come from?",a="The Scourge was originally created by the demonic Burning Legion to soften Azeroth's defenses ahead of their invasion. The Legion took the spirit of the orc shaman Ner'zhul, bound him as the Lich King within the Frozen Throne in distant Northrend, and granted him dominion over necromancy. From his icy seat, he unleashed the Plague of Undeath southward into Lordaeron, subverting mortals into an unstoppable legion of undead servants.",al={"where did scourge come from","scourge origin","how was scourge created"},it="origin",add="03d58107"},{q="Why are the Scourge found throughout Lordaeron?",a="Lordaeron was ground zero for the Scourge's devastation of humanity. The Cult of the Damned contaminated the northern grain supplies with the Plague of Undeath, killing vast populations and raising them as mindless thralls. After Prince Arthas returned from Northrend as the Lich King's champion and murdered King Terenas, the Scourge swept across the kingdom, claiming its towns and transforming the Eastweald into the blighted Plaguelands you see today.",al={"why is scourge in plaguelands","scourge lordaeron why","why are undead in lordaeron"},it="why_here",add="51cb9edc"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken was once enslaved by the Scourge and forced to butcher friends and kin until the Lich King's grip weakened. Destroying the Scourge is a fight for survival and deeply personal vengeance.",["race:Human"]="The Scourge destroyed humanity's greatest kingdom, slaughtered the Menethil line, and turned Lordaeron's heartland into a blighted wasteland.",["class:Paladin"]="The Scourge shattered the Knights of the Silver Hand when Prince Arthas turned on his mentors and murdered Uther the Lightbringer. For a paladin, cleansing the Scourge with the Holy Light is sacred duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lordaeron's fall remains an open wound for the Alliance, driving its efforts to reclaim the Plaguelands and avenge the fallen.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken have been accepted into the Horde, drawing the whole coalition into the ongoing war against the Lich King's remaining armies in the north."},kw={"arthas","cult of the damned","frostmourne","frozen throne","kel'thuzad","lich king","lordaeron","plague","plaguelands","scourge","undead"},rel={"topic:lich-king","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Scourge"}}
E["topic:second-war"] = {t="topic",n="Second War",z="general",s="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, the Second War rages between the Orcish Horde and the newly forged Alliance of Lordaeron. After Stormwind falls, battle sweeps through Khaz Modan and the northern human realms, then reaches the gates of Capital City. The war ends when the Dark Portal is destroyed and the old Horde is scattered.",h="Across the Eastern Kingdoms, the Second War rages between the Orcish Horde and the newly forged Alliance of...",sec={{t="A Continent at War",b="After Stormwind fell in the First War, Regent Anduin Lothar led human refugees north across the Great Sea to Lordaeron. King Terenas Menethil II called the Council of Seven Nations and forged the Alliance of Lordaeron. The high elves of Quel'Thalas, the Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge, and the gnomes of Gnomeregan joined it.\n\nAcross the sea, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer gathered the Horde. He allied with forest troll tribes and the Steamwheedle Cartel. The Dragonmaw clan brought red dragons under Horde control for the invasion of the northern continents.",sp=0},{t="The Invasion of the North",b="The Horde struck by land and sea, swiftly overrunning Khaz Modan. Dwarves and gnomes fell back behind the sealed gates of Ironforge and Gnomeregan. Horde forces crossed the Thandol Span and the seas, burning through Hillsbrad and the Hinterlands before laying siege to Capital City.\n\nAlterac betrayed the Alliance and guided orc divisions through mountain passes. Dragon attacks battered the defenders, but the Alliance rallied around the newly formed Knights of the Silver Hand. Their paladins wielded the Holy Light against orcish warlocks and death knights.",sp=0},{t="The Turning Tide and the Dark Portal",b="The war turned when the warlock Gul'dan left the Horde with his followers to seek personal power. Doomhammer had to draw vital forces away from the front lines. The Alliance counterattacked, broke the siege of Lordaeron, and drove the Horde south across the Thandol Span, freeing Khaz Modan along the way.\n\nIn the final mountain passes of the Burning Steppes, Anduin Lothar fell in single combat against Doomhammer. Lothar's lieutenant Turalyon rallied the troops and routed the orcs. The Alliance pursued the survivors to the Black Morass, shattered the remnants, and demolished the Dark Portal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How did the Second War begin?",a="After the Horde razed Stormwind in the First War, Orgrim Doomhammer saw that the northern human realms would eventually strike back. He chose to attack before humanity could organize. At the same time, Stormwind refugees led by Anduin Lothar warned King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, prompting the creation of the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"why did the second war start","how did it start","second war cause"},it="origin"},{q="Who won the Second War?",a="The Alliance of Lordaeron won a decisive victory. Its forces drove the Horde from Capital City and south through Khaz Modan, then defeated Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer at the foot of Blackrock Mountain. They dismantled the Dark Portal in the Black Morass.",al={"who won","alliance or horde win","second war victor"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to Khaz Modan during the fighting?",a="The Horde overran Khaz Modan's surface lands to seize its rich mineral deposits and forges. The Bronzebeard dwarves and their gnomish allies destroyed mountain passes and tunnels to slow the advance, then retreated behind the sealed gates of Ironforge and Gnomeregan. The Horde besieged Ironforge but could not breach its gates before the Alliance pushed south and freed the realm.",al={"khaz modan second war","ironforge siege second war","what happened to the dwarves"},it="ruin"},{q="Why did the Horde lose when they reached Capital City?",a="At the height of the siege of Lordaeron's capital, the warlock Gul'dan abandoned the front line with the Stormreaver and Twilight's Hammer clans to hunt for ancient demonic power. Doomhammer split his army to punish the deserters, fatally weakening the siege lines just as the Alliance counterattack struck.",al={"why did the horde lose","gul'dan betrayal second war","why did doomhammer fail"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Anduin Lothar?",a="Sir Anduin Lothar was the Lion of Azeroth and Regent of Stormwind after King Llane's assassination. He led the survivors north and became Supreme Commander of the Alliance armies. Near the war's end, Lothar died in single combat against Orgrim Doomhammer in the Burning Steppes, inspiring Turalyon to lead the Alliance to victory.",al={"who is lothar","anduin lothar death","supreme commander lothar"},it="leader"},{q="Where did the final battle take place?",a="The decisive battle between the armies took place around Blackrock Mountain in the Burning Steppes, where Doomhammer was defeated. The surviving orcs fled to the Black Morass, where the Alliance fought a final engagement at the Dark Portal. They demolished its stone framework and imprisoned or scattered the remaining Horde clans.",al={"last battle second war","dark portal battle","burning steppes second war"},it="place"},{q="What was the Second War?",a="The Second War was a massive, continent-spanning conflict fought across the Eastern Kingdoms between the Orcish Horde and the original Alliance of Lordaeron. Beginning shortly after the fall of Stormwind, it pitted humanity and their newfound allies—the dwarves of Khaz Modan, the gnomes of Gnomeregan, and the high elves of Quel'Thalas—against Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde, bolstered by forest trolls, goblins, and enslaved red dragons.",al={"what is second war","second great war","who fought second war"},it="identity",add="1c320fa5"},{q="Who were the factions and allies in the Second War?",a="The war united races on both sides into vast coalitions. The Alliance of Lordaeron brought together the seven human kingdoms alongside Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarves, Gnomeregan's gnomes, and high elves. Opposing them was the Orcish Horde, joined by the Amani forest trolls, the goblins of the Steamwheedle Cartel, and red dragons forced into servitude by the Dragonmaw clan using the Demon Soul.",al={"second war alliances","who fought with who second war","second war factions"},it="allies",add="b89daeed"},{q="Why is it called the Second War?",a="It is named the Second War because it immediately followed the First War, the initial conflict triggered when orcs first surged through the Dark Portal and razed the Kingdom of Stormwind. When the survivors fled north and Orgrim Doomhammer pushed across the continent to eradicate the remaining human kingdoms, the renewed clash became the second Great War between the two mortal factions.",al={"why called second war","second great war name","name second war"},it="name",add="5ecc4b82"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you stand with the union of humans, dwarves, gnomes, and elves forged in the Second War against an existential threat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you inherit a people marked by the collapse of the old blood-cursed Horde. That collapse led directly to the internment camps and the eventual rebirth of the new Horde under Thrall.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you follow the path of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Uther the Lightbringer founded them during this conflict to oppose the fel magic and death knights of the Horde.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you come from Khaz Modan, which suffered widespread devastation during the war. It endured a long Horde siege behind Ironforge's sealed mountain gates until Alliance armies lifted it."},kw={"alliance of lordaeron","blackrock mountain","dark portal","doomhammer","guldan","lothar","second war","silver hand","thandol span"},rel={"topic:first-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:anduin-lothar","subzone:dark-portal","topic:dragonmaw-clan","zone:ironforge","zone:burningsteppes"},src={"Second War"}}
E["topic:sentinels"] = {t="topic",n="Sentinels",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, the Sentinels defend night elf lands and meet the Horde in battle. Formed after the War of the Ancients, this elite force is guided by the Sisterhood of Elune and led by General Shandris Feathermoon. Its mostly female ranks guard settlements and sacred ground from Ashenvale to Feralas, and watch over the night elves’ new home on Teldrassil.",h="Across Kalimdor, the Sentinels defend night elf lands and meet the Horde in battle.",sec={{t="Born from the Sundering",b="The Sentinels took shape after the War of the Ancients laid bare the failures of the old Kaldorei military. Before the Great Sundering, noble birth decided rank in the ancient Kaldorei Empire, while skill in battle counted for little. That order could not shield Azeroth from the war’s devastation.\n\nAfterward, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind remade night elf society. She looked to the Sisterhood of Elune, an order that had survived intact and knew tactics, combat, and healing. From its devoted ranks, Tyrande formed a standing army to guard the growing society, whatever a Sentinel’s heritage.",sp=0},{t="Structure and Warfare",b="Tyrande Whisperwind remains the Sentinels’ spiritual supreme commander. Her lieutenant, General Shandris Feathermoon, directs their active military from Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas. Sentinel discipline is known in the bow and the deadly moonglaive, and in their specialized forces.\n\nElite archers fight beside huntresses riding nightsabers. Scouts mounted on hippogryphs command the skies. Centuries before the Third War, the Sentinels fought under Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in the brutal War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus, where they halted the qiraji swarm. From Astranaar to Darnassus’s spreading branches, night elf settlements rely on Sentinel garrisons for protection.",sp=0},{t="Defending Sacred Soil",b="During the Third War, the Sentinels faced demons and early Horde incursions in desperate battles. They suffered immense losses when Cenarius fell in Ashenvale. They survived the Battle of Mount Hyjal and pursued Illidan across Lordaeron, then returned to a changed Kalimdor.\n\nNow danger presses from several fronts. On Teldrassil, garrisons face corrupted wildlife and enraged furbolgs. Farther south in Warsong Gulch, the Silverwing Sentinels fight the Warsong Outriders. They are determined to drive the Horde from Ashenvale and protect the ancient forests from further exploitation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the Sentinels?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind guides the Sentinels politically and spiritually, and founded them from the Sisterhood of Elune. General Shandris Feathermoon commands the army day to day from Feathermoon Stronghold and directs its operations across Kalimdor.",al={"sentinel leader","who is in charge of sentinels","shandris or tyrande"},it="leader"},{q="Why are most Sentinels female?",a="Most Sentinels are female because night elf society traditionally divided spiritual and martial duties by gender. Women dominated Elune’s priesthood and formed the Sentinels, while men overwhelmingly joined the Cenarion Circle as druids. That division shaped the army for millennia, though society has slowly begun to shift since the Third War.",al={"why only female sentinels","women army night elf","can men be sentinels"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Sentinels' main base of operations?",a="The Sentinels’ primary fortress outside Darnassus is Feathermoon Stronghold, on an island off the coast of Feralas. They also keep prominent garrisons across Ashenvale, including Astranaar and Silverwing Outpost.",al={"sentinel base","sentinel headquarters","feathermoon stronghold"},it="place"},{q="What weapons do the Sentinels specialize in?",a="Sentinels are celebrated archers who use recurve bows, and the three-bladed moonglaive is their cultural hallmark. Huntresses wield glaives from nightsaber panthers, while riders strike from armored hippogryphs.",al={"sentinel weapons","moonglaive","what do sentinels use"}},{q="Why are the Sentinels fighting in Warsong Gulch?",a="The Silverwing Sentinels fight the Horde’s Warsong Outriders over Ashenvale. The orcs have cut heavily into the forest for lumber, violating woods the night elves hold sacred. The Sentinels are determined to drive out every invader.",al={"warsong gulch sentinels","silverwing sentinels","why ashenvale war"},it="conflict"},{q="Did the Sentinels fight in the Third War?",a="Yes. The Sentinels formed the main front-line defense when the Burning Legion and the Scourge marched on Kalimdor. Led by Tyrande, they held the line until they joined forces with human and orc refugees. The fighting ended in victory at the Battle of Mount Hyjal.",al={"sentinels third war","sentinels hyjal","sentinels wc3"}},{q="What are the Sentinels?",a="The Sentinels, or the Sentinel Army, are the standing military force and primary guardians of the night elf race. Deeply entwined with the Sisterhood of Elune, their ranks consist of devout, elite warriors—chiefly deadly archers, saber-mounted huntresses, and aerial hippogryph riders. They patrol ancient woodlands, guard night elven settlements, and defend kaldorei territories against all outside threats.",al={"who are sentinels","sentinel army","night elf sentinels"},it="identity",add="b427a0e4"},{q="Where are the Sentinels found across Kalimdor?",a="You will encounter Sentinels stationed in nearly every night elf settlement and wilderness outpost across northern and central Kalimdor. They maintain a heavy garrison guarding their new home in Teldrassil and their capital of Darnassus. Across Ashenvale, Darkshore, and Stonetalon, they actively repel invading Horde lumber expeditions, corrupted furbolgs, and demonic remnants, while maintaining their southern fortress of Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.",al={"sentinel locations","where do sentinels patrol","why sentinels here"},it="why_here",add="3421f1ac"},{q="Why are the Sentinels hostile to the Horde?",a="If you march under the Horde banner, the Sentinels view you as an invading trespasser. Bitter hostility began during the Third War when the Warsong clan slew their revered demigod Cenarius. Today, the Horde continues to harvest timber from the sacred groves of Ashenvale, driving the Sentinels to violently defend their ancestral borders from all encroaching orcs and their allies.",al={"why sentinels attack me","sentinels kos horde","are sentinels hostile"},it="hostile",add="da0cb30d"},{q="Who are the Sentinels allied with?",a="The Sentinels serve Darnassus and answer directly to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and the Sisterhood of Elune. As the night elves joined the Grand Alliance, the Sentinels fight alongside humans, dwarves, and gnomes, deploying troops to assist allied campaigns and standing guard at joint outposts across the world.",al={"sentinel allies","who do sentinels fight for","are sentinels alliance"},it="allies",add="37da9748"},{q="How was the Sentinel Army formed?",a="The Sentinels were forged in the aftermath of the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago. Following the collapse of the old empire—where military leadership had decayed into idle noble status—High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind reformed their martial forces. Drawing upon the battle-tested, disciplined ranks of the Sisterhood of Elune, she created a vigilant, standing army to ensure the night elves would never again fall unprepared to demonic invasion.",al={"sentinel origin","origin of sentinels","history of sentinels"},it="history",add="fe6bc7d9"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, your hamlet relies on the Sentinels’ watch. Many young women aspire to join the army of Shandris and Tyrande.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face lethal woodland skirmishers who strike from Ashenvale’s shadows and fight your logging efforts.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see Sentinel archers and nightsaber-riding huntresses as masters of marksmanship and animal companionship on Kalimdor.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you share a bond between military duty and devotion to the Moon Goddess. The Sentinels were formed from the Sisterhood of Elune."},kw={"ashenvale","feathermoon","huntress","kaldorei","moonglaive","nightsaber","sentinels","shandris","silverwing","tyrande"},rel={"npc:shandris-feathermoon","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:night-elf","topic:elune","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","zone:ashenvale","topic:war-of-the-ancients","npc:warsong-outrider"},src={"Sentinels"}}
E["topic:shadow-council"] = {t="topic",n="Shadow Council",z="general",s="Across Draenor and Azeroth, the Shadow Council served Gul'dan's designs. At the Burning Legion's direction, the secret cabal of warlocks and necrolytes manipulated the clans and drove the Old Horde's invasion. Orgrim Doomhammer later purged its stronghold in Blackrock Mountain.",h="Across Draenor and Azeroth, the Shadow Council served Gul'dan's designs.",sec={{t="Architects of the Blood Curse",b="Before the Horde crossed into Azeroth, Gul'dan gathered warlocks, necrolytes, and chieftains who sought their own advantage. The Shadow Council ruled the orcish clans from the shadows and raised Blackhand the Destroyer as a figurehead. Across Draenor, its members spread fel magic. They gave the clans the blood of the demon Mannoroth and bound the orcs to the Burning Legion.",sp=0},{t="The Crossing and Blackrock Mountain",b="The Shadow Council struck a pact with Medivh, the Guardian possessed by Sargeras, to break the barrier between worlds. Through the Dark Portal, its members guided the Horde into the Kingdom of Stormwind. The warlocks watched over the war from their sanctum in Blackrock Spire.",sp=0},{t="Doomhammer's Purge and Death Knights",b="After Medivh died, Gul'dan fell into a comatose trance. Orgrim Doomhammer seized the moment, killed Blackhand, and questioned Garona until he learned where the Council's inner sanctum lay. His assault destroyed most of its warlocks.\n\nWhen Gul'dan awoke to find his cult shattered, he offered Doomhammer a weapon against human magic in exchange for his life. Gul'dan placed the spirits of slain Shadow Council warlocks in the corpses of fallen human knights. Thus he created the first death knights.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who founded the Shadow Council?",a="Gul'dan, an orc warlock, founded the Shadow Council on Draenor. Serving the demon lord Kil'jaeden, he gathered practitioners of fel magic to manipulate the clans. Warchief Blackhand was their unwitting puppet.",al={"who made shadow council","shadow council founder","guldan council"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the Shadow Council during the First War?",a="After Medivh died and Gul'dan fell into a trance, Orgrim Doomhammer killed Blackhand and took command of the Horde. He tortured Garona to find the Council's hidden sanctuary in Blackrock Spire. Then he led a purge that killed nearly all its warlocks.",al={"how did shadow council fall","doomhammer shadow council","purge of the shadow council"},it="history"},{q="How did the first death knights come from the Shadow Council?",a="After Doomhammer destroyed the Council, Gul'dan offered a weapon against human sorcerers in exchange for his life. He infused the lingering souls of slain warlocks, including Teron Gorefiend, into the preserved bodies of fallen Stormwind knights. Thus he created the first death knights.",al={"shadow council death knights","who became death knights","teron gorefiend council"}},{q="Did all orc warlocks belong to the Shadow Council?",a="No. The Shadow Council was a secret inner circle of Gul'dan's trusted warlocks, necrolytes, and chieftains. It ruled the Horde from behind the scenes, while fel magic spread much more widely among the orcish clans.",al={"were all warlocks shadow council","drekthar shadow council","nekros shadow council"}},{q="What was Cho'gall's role in the Council?",a="Cho'gall was Gul'dan's foremost apprentice and chief lieutenant. He led the Twilight's Hammer clan within the Council's orbit.",al={"chogall shadow council","chogall role","twilight hammer shadow council"}},{q="Does the Shadow Council still exist?",a="Doomhammer shattered the original Council, and its remnants fractured further after Gul'dan died at the Tomb of Sargeras. Across Azeroth and the ruins of Draenor, splintered cultists, surviving warlocks, and demonic agents still carry on the Legion's work. They trace their lineage to Gul'dan's organization.",al={"is shadow council around","shadow council today","shadow council present"},it="today"},{q="What is the Shadow Council?",a="The Shadow Council is a clandestine cult of mortal warlocks dedicated to serving the demonic Burning Legion. Founded on Draenor by the orc warlock Gul'dan, the Council worked from the shadows to manipulate the Orcish Horde, corrupt its clans with fel magic, and coordinate the genocide of the draenei before steering the orcs through the Dark Portal into Azeroth.",al={"what is shadow council","who are the shadow council","shadow council meaning"},it="identity",add="5ec0e415"},{q="Who do the Shadow Council serve?",a="The Shadow Council serves the Burning Legion and its demon lords, notably Kil'jaeden. While mortal leaders like Gul'dan have directed its day-to-day machinations, the cult's ultimate purpose has always been carrying out the Legion's dark designs across both Draenor and Azeroth.",al={"who do shadow council serve","shadow council allies","who leads shadow council","shadow council demon masters"},it="allies",add="5b2501ce"},{q="Why are the Shadow Council hostile to travelers?",a="The Shadow Council operates entirely in secrecy to further the Burning Legion's schemes of destruction and demonic corruption. Anyone outside their demonic fold—whether Alliance or the new Horde—is an obstacle, an enemy, or fuel for their dark soul-draining rituals.",al={"why does shadow council attack","shadow council hostile why","why is shadow council evil"},it="hostile",add="26726978"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Shadow Council formalized fel sorcery and demonic pacts among mortals. Modern warlocks draw on the summoning rites and soul-harvesting techniques its members pioneered.",["race:Orc"]="The Shadow Council brought ruin to Draenor and bound the orcish race through a blood pact. That legacy brings deep shame across generations, and Thrall's new Horde strives to cast it off.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer's slaughter of the Shadow Council marked the Horde's first attempt to break free of demonic puppet masters.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Shadow Council's covert operations helped bring down the kingdom of Stormwind. They began with the opening of the Dark Portal and reached the assassination of King Llane Wrynn."},kw={"blackhand","blackrock mountain","burning legion","cho'gall","dark portal","death knight","fel magic","gul'dan","mannoroth","shadow council","teron gorefiend"},rel={"npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:old-horde","subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:burning-legion","subzone:dark-portal","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:medivh","topic:first-war"},src={"Shadow Council"}}
E["topic:shaman"] = {t="topic",n="Shaman",z="general",s="Among the Horde and the dwarves, Shaman seek aid from earth, air, fire and water. Totems help them wield lightning and ancestral healing as they guide their people. Dwarves follow the path too, as the Wildhammer have long done, and the Skyborne Windshapers seek to restore their people's bond with the winds.",h="Among the Horde and the dwarves, Shaman seek aid from earth, air, fire and water.",sec={{t="Mediators of the Elements",b="Shaman petition the primal forces of nature. Earth, air, fire and water are chaotic, locked in constant conflict. Shaman do not enslave them; they ask for aid and try to keep the elements' fury in balance with the mortal world. Wooden and stone totems planted in the soil help them channel these bargains. Through the totems, shaman protect allies, hinder foes and use cleansing water to mend the wounded.",sp=0},{t="Loss and Rebirth Among Orcs",b="Shamanism once formed the ancient foundation of orcish clan life on Draenor. Kil'jaeden and the Shadow Council deceived the shamans into war against the draenei, and the elemental spirits withdrew their favor. Stripped of their gifts, many shamans fell to demonic corruption and became warlocks. The tradition came close to extinction.\n\nAfter the Second War, Thrall rediscovered the ancient rites under the guidance of Drek'Thar of the Frostwolf clan. As Warchief, Thrall revived shamanism and made it the moral compass of the New Horde.",sp=0},{t="Traditions of the Horde",b="Across Kalimdor, the Horde's allied peoples keep different shamanic traditions. Tauren mystics hold communion with the earth and spirits, a sacred anchor of their culture. Darkspear trolls honor the loa and ancestral wild spirits, blending voodoo with nature rites. Across tribal lines, shaman serve as community elders and advisers. They also defend their people on the front lines.",sp=0},{t="Beyond the Horde",b="The shaman's path reaches beyond the Horde. Wildhammer dwarves of Aerie Peak have long called on storm and stone. Earthseer Farsen brings their far-seeing craft to Dun Morogh, while dwarves of Ironforge also take up the totem and fight for the Alliance.\n\nHigh above the world, the Windshapers lead the Skyborne in spiritual matters. The wind spirits of Zephras Isle have fallen silent, so the Windshapers train new shaman in hope of restoring that lost bond. Skyborne who join the Horde follow their path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Which races can become shaman?",a="Orcs, tauren and trolls of the Horde can become shaman, drawing on elemental spirits, ancestors and, among trolls, the loa. Dwarves follow the path for the Alliance, while Skyborne who join the Horde train with the Windshapers.",al={"who can be shaman","shaman races","can alliance be shaman","can dwarves be shaman","dwarf shaman","alliance shaman","skyborne shaman"},it="people"},{q="How do shaman get their magic?",a="Shaman gain power through communion with the elemental spirits of earth, air, fire and water, and with ancestral spirits. They petition these spirits for aid instead of forcing them to obey, seeking balance and anchoring their bonds with ritual totems.",al={"how does shaman magic work","shaman source of power","where do totems come from"},it="power"},{q="Why did the orcs lose their shaman powers before the First War?",a="Kil'jaeden deceived the orc shamans into attacking the peaceful draenei. Offended by the slaughter, Draenor's elemental spirits severed their ties and stopped answering the shamans. Many, left without their gifts, turned to fel magic and became warlocks.",al={"why did orc shaman become warlocks","draenor shaman fall","kiljaeden trick shaman"},it="history"},{q="Who brought shamanism back to the orcs?",a="Thrall brought shamanism back to the orcs. The son of Durotan sought out the Frostwolf clan in the Alterac Mountains and learned the ancient spiritual bonds from the elder shaman Drek'Thar. Thrall broke the demonic lethargy that plagued his people and restored shamanism as the heart of the New Horde.",al={"who revived shamanism","thrall and drek'thar shaman","shaman return"},it="history"},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an order of shaman with elders among the tauren of Thunder Bluff. Its members seek harmony among the volatile elemental spirits and heal regions afflicted by spiritual unrest.",al={"earthen ring lore","who are earthen ring","shaman faction"},it="allies"},{q="How does a shaman differ from a druid?",a="Druids commune with the Emerald Dream, plant life and animal spirits to protect nature's living cycle. Shaman work with the physical world's primordial elements—earth, fire, water and wind—and with the spirits of the dead.",al={"druid vs shaman","difference between druid and shaman","shaman or druid"},it="identity"},{q="What is a shaman in lore?",a="Shaman are spiritual guides and mortal mediators who commune directly with the natural elements: earth, air, fire, and water. Rather than serving as masters of the divine, they act as moderators between primal, chaotic elemental forces that are in unending conflict. In tribal societies like those of the orcs, tauren, and trolls, shaman serve as revered advisors, seers, and protectors. In battle, they call upon these elemental energies to unleash lightning, mend wounds with cleansing water, or empower allies through carved totems.",al={"what is a shaman","shaman lore","who are shamans"},it="identity",add="82a70d6c"},{q="What does it mean to become a shaman?",a="Walking the path of the shaman means learning to listen to the living world and earning the respect of its spirits. You do not command elemental forces through arcane mastery or sheer will; you commune with them, bringing balance to their volatile fury. As an initiate, you craft and carry totems that focus the elements of earth, fire, water, and air. Whether fighting on the front lines with weapon-imbued elemental force, healing allies through ancestral guidance, or calling down storms, your strength relies entirely upon keeping harmony with the primal spirits.",al={"becoming a shaman","why become a shaman","path of the shaman"},it="for_you",add="8fa4f120"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, your powers come through mutual respect with fickle elemental spirits and ancestors. Keeping balance is your duty in battle and your spiritual burden.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you inherit a spiritual renewal through shamanism, a path of honor and nature worship that replaced demonic corruption.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you inherit generations of shamanic practice and serve as a patient spiritual anchor for the Horde's younger cultures.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you reclaim ancestral heritage through shamanism, which helped your people overcome the lethargy of the internment camps.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you channel the primal elements through tribal traditions, joining reverence for nature spirits with honor for the ancient loa.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you may see shaman as foes whose totems call lightning and tremors. Dwarven shaman bring those same storm-born gifts to Ironforge's defense.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you answer the stone and storm, following a path shared with the Wildhammer earthseers of Aerie Peak, who have long heard the elements' voices.",["race:Skyborne"]="As a Skyborne shaman, you train with the Windshapers, who hope to bring the vanished wind spirits back to Zephras Isle."},kw={"air","ancestors","drek'thar","earth","earthen ring","elements","fire","primal","shaman","thrall","totem","water","wildhammer","windshapers","earthseer"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:tauren","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:new-horde","topic:horde","topic:burning-legion","zone:durotar","topic:wildhammer-clan","topic:skyborne"},src={"Shaman"}}
E["topic:shan-do"] = {t="topic",n="Shan'do",z="general",s="Among the night elves, Shan'do is spoken with deep respect for a mentor and guide. The Darnassian title means “honored teacher” or “honored instructor,” while thero'shan honors a student.",h="Among the night elves, Shan'do is spoken with deep respect for a mentor and guide.",sec={{t="A Title of Deep Reverence",b="In Darnassian, shan'do means “honored teacher” or “honored instructor.” Calling an elder or mentor shan'do shows humility, filial devotion, and lasting respect for their guidance.",sp=0},{t="The Lineage of the Druids",b="The Cenarion Circle's history is bound to the title. Before the War of the Ancients, the demigod Cenarius taught Malfurion Stormrage the ways of nature as his shan'do. Malfurion then guided generations of mortal druids. Across Kalimdor, night elves, forest keepers, and reverent allies commonly address him as Shan'do Stormrage.",sp=0},{t="Mentors Beyond the Circle",b="Cenarion druids often use the title for mentors such as Naralex or the slumbering Malfurion. Yet shan'do belongs to the Darnassian language and reaches beyond religious life. It marks the bond between master and pupil, whatever their school of thought.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the word shan'do actually mean?",a="In Darnassian, shan'do means “honored teacher” or “honored instructor.” The title shows deep respect and gratitude toward a mentor.",al={"shando meaning","what does shando translate to","shando translation","darnassian shando"},it="name"},{q="What is the opposite or student version of shan'do?",a="The complementary honorific is thero'shan, meaning “honored student.” Mentors use it for apprentices to recognize their devotion and discipline.",al={"opposite of shando","student word in darnassian","theroshan meaning","what is thero'shan"}},{q="Who is most commonly called Shan'do?",a="Night elves and the Cenarion Circle most commonly hail Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage as Shan'do. Cenarius was called shan'do by his first pupils, and followers also use the title for prominent leaders such as Naralex.",al={"who is shando","shando stormrage","who has the title shando"},it="fame"},{q="Is the title shan'do only used by druids?",a="No. Shan'do comes from Cenarion druidic tradition, but it is a Darnassian courtesy. A student can use it for a master of craft, magic, or wisdom.",al={"can non druids be shando","is shando only for druids","shando outside druidism"}},{q="What is the meaning and role of a Shan'do?",a="Shan'do is an esteemed Darnassian courtesy title translating to \"honored teacher\" or \"honored instructor.\" It is bestowed upon revered mentors within night elven culture, most notably among druids who guide apprentices in the ways of nature. The title conveys deep reverence, placing the teacher in a position of sacred guidance and elder authority over their thero'shan, or honored student.",al={"what is shando","who is shando","shan'do meaning"},it="identity",add="9fa21e25"},{q="What is the history of the title Shan'do?",a="The honorific dates back millennia to the earliest teachings of nature and arcane magic. During the ancient era before the Great Sundering, the demigod Cenarius served as shan'do to Malfurion Stormrage, instructing him as the first mortal druid. Over the ages, it has endured as the quintessential Darnassian honorific for masters of profound spiritual and magical disciplines.",al={"history of shando","where did shando come from","origin of shando"},it="history",add="01c1f540"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know shan'do as a solemn courtesy for an elder or teacher, carrying millennia of cultural weight.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you trace your teachings through mentors back to Shan'do Stormrage and Cenarius. Speaking the title honors that chain.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren druid studying alongside the night elves in Moonglade, you recognize shan'do and use it respectfully for mentors such as Malfurion Stormrage."},kw={"cenarius","darnassian","druid","honored teacher","malfurion","shan'do","shando","thero'shan"},rel={"npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:cenarius","topic:druid","npc:naralex","topic:war-of-the-ancients","npc:remulos","quest:952","quest:963"},src={"Shan'do"}}
E["topic:skyborne"] = {t="topic",n="Skyborne",z="general",s="In Skywall, the Skyborne face a failing refuge and the loss of those who once guarded it. Their ancestors, high elves descended from night elves, fled Eldre'Thalas after resisting Prince Tortheldrin's demonic pacts. A bargain with wind spirits carried them to Zephras Isle, but now the spirits are gone and the island is breaking apart.",h="In Skywall, the Skyborne face a failing refuge and the loss of those who once guarded it.",sec={{t="Flight from Eldre'Thalas",b="After the Sundering, the Shen'dralar of Eldre'Thalas struggled without the Well of Eternity. Prince Tortheldrin sought salvation by summoning the demon Immol'thar and draining its power. Nobles and citizens feared another Legion invasion, so they resisted. Tortheldrin answered with a purge that killed dozens of houses.\n\nSurvivors rallied behind a masked figure called the Shal'nan, or the Veiled One. A desperate raid on Tortheldrin's ritual sanctum unleashed chaotic magic. The Shal'nan gathered the survivors and led them west to the port of Eldre'narr. They took to the sea as the Prince's fleet pursued them.",sp=0},{t="Sanctuary in the Sky",b="At sea, the exiles found themselves cornered, so they made a pact with primordial wind spirits. The spirits lifted Zephras Isle into the sky and anchored it in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air. During the Shrine of the Four Winds' consecration, the Shal'nan gave up absolute rule and entrusted governance to an elected council.\n\nOver millennia in this strange realm, the night elf exiles became fair, slender high elves. In recent generations, more children have been born with pale blue skin through the Sky-Touched Blessing.",sp=0},{t="A Shattering Calm",b="For centuries, the Skyborne lived in isolation. The wind spirits forbade them to speak of the Windlord, Al'Akir, and questions about him met only eerie unease. Then, a few centuries ago, the spirits vanished without explanation, and the Shal'nan disappeared with them.\n\nWithout their caretakers, the arcane pylons holding Zephras Isle aloft began to fail. Outlying landmasses broke away, refugees crowded the remaining isle, and desperation gave rise to bandits and the Al'Aketh, a fanatical cult devoted to Al'Akir. Now the High Order seeks salvation by reclaiming ancestral arcane magic, while the Windshapers hold to elemental rites.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Skyborne?",a="The skyborne, or shen'dorei, are high elves descended from ancient night elves who rebelled against Prince Tortheldrin in Eldre'Thalas. Their name means the hidden people. To escape his vengeful fleet, they struck a pact with wind spirits, who carried their island, Zephras Isle, into Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air.",al={"what are skyborne","who are shen'dorei","shendorei","skyborne lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why do some Skyborne have blue skin?",a="Millennia in the Elemental Plane of Air changed the Skyborne. Through the Sky-Touched Blessing, roughly three out of ten children are now born with blue skin. Scholars predict their ancestral night elf traits will soon be entirely supplanted.",al={"sky-touched blessing","why are they blue","blue elves","sky touched"},it="origin"},{q="Who was the Shal'nan?",a="The Shal'nan, or the Veiled One, was the masked leader of the resistance against Prince Tortheldrin's demon summoning in Eldre'Thalas. After leading survivors to safety in Skywall, the Shal'nan surrendered absolute rule for an elected council and served the Skyborne until disappearing centuries ago with their elemental benefactors.",al={"who is the veiled one","shalnan","the masked rebel","leader of skyborne"},it="leader"},{q="What is happening to Zephras Isle?",a="Zephras Isle remains aloft in Skywall on magical pylons attuned to elemental power. After the wind spirits who maintained them vanished centuries ago, the pylons began to fail. Parts of the isle broke away into the void, stranding survivors and driving displaced elves to banditry.",al={"why is zephras isle crumbling","zephras falling","what happened to skywall island"},it="ruin"},{q="What are the High Order and the Windshapers?",a="The High Order and the Windshapers are the Skyborne's two main cultural factions. The High Order descends from Highborne magisters and seeks to rebuild society through disciplined arcane mastery. The Windshapers trace their roots to ordinary night elf citizens and honor the elemental and spiritual customs they developed in Skywall.",al={"skyborne factions","high order vs windshapers","windshaper lore"},it="people"},{q="Who are the Al'Aketh?",a="The Al'Aketh are Skyborne who worship Al'Akir the Windlord. Their ancestors' elemental benefactors feared and avoided speaking of Al'Akir. After Zephras Isle began to collapse, homeless and disenfranchised refugees turned to him for salvation and power.",al={"alaketh cult","cult of al'akir","skyborne cult"},it="threat"},{q="Where do the Skyborne stand in the world today?",a="Their civilization faces slow collapse. Centuries ago, the wind spirits and the Shal'nan vanished, destabilizing the ancient pylons holding Zephras Isle together. With parts of their realm crumbling into ruin, communication cut off from other settled islands, and refugees flooding the isle, surviving Skyborne have fractured. The High Order and Windshapers vie over whether arcane heritage or elemental traditions will save them, while desperate exiles turn to banditry or join the Al'Akir-worshipping Al'Aketh cult.",al={"skyborne current situation","state of the skyborne","where are the skyborne now"},it="today",add="10ab7a6f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share bloodlines with the ancient Shen'dralar and northern night elves. Millennia in Skywall changed the Skyborne into high elves, and more of their children are now born with elemental blue skin.",["class:Mage"]="Among the Skyborne, the High Order preserves ancient Highborne spellcraft carried out of Eldre'Thalas. Its members seek to save their crumbling island through rigorous arcane mastery.",["class:Shaman"]="Among the Skyborne, the Windshapers follow an elven lineage closely tied to Skywall's wind spirits. They rely on communion with the elements rather than the arcane traditions of their Highborne forebears."},kw={"al'aketh","eldre'thalas","high order","shal'nan","shen'dorei","sky-touched","skyborne","skywall","windshapers","zephras isle"},rel={"zone:zephras","subzone:dire-maul","topic:highborne","topic:skywall","topic:elemental-plane","npc:ventaari-brightwish","quest:93552","zone:feralas"},src={"Skyborne"}}
E["topic:skywall"] = {t="topic",n="Skywall",z="general",s="Within the Elemental Plane, Al'Akir rules Skywall and its air elementals. The titans banished them there long ago, to a realm of wind, cloud, and lightning.",h="Within the Elemental Plane, Al'Akir rules Skywall and its air elementals.",sec={{t="A Prison in the Heavens",b="The titans made the Elemental Plane a prison for Azeroth's unruly elemental spirits. After overthrowing the Old Gods, they sealed the spirits away from the surface world. The elemental lords fought among themselves and carved out separate dominions. Al'Akir the Windlord rules Skywall, where tempests still swirl in isolation.",sp=0},{t="The War of Elements",b="Old feuds followed the elemental lords into exile. Skywall has long fought over its borders with nearby realms, including the Firelands. During the Elemental Sundering, Garr and Baron Geddon, chief lieutenants of Ragnaros the Firelord, ambushed and betrayed Prince Thunderaan the Windseeker. Ragnaros devoured the prince's essence and bound its fragments in a shattered talisman.",sp=0},{t="Isles of the Mist",b="Beyond gales and djinn citadels, Zephras Isle drifts among Skywall's cloudbanks. The isle is a sanctuary inhabited by the Shen'dorei. Mortals on Azeroth rarely pierce the veil into the air realm. Across history, reckless spellcasters and weapon-crafters have risked disaster to siphon the Windlord's living storms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skywall?",a="Within the Elemental Plane, Skywall is the air elementals' dominion. The titans made that prison for the servants of the Old Gods, and its skies hold storms, clouds, and lightning.",al={"what is skywall","skywall lore","domain of air"},it="identity"},{q="Who rules Skywall?",a="Al'Akir the Windlord rules Skywall as the supreme Elemental Lord of air. Djinn, cyclones, and living storms fall within his dominion.",al={"who leads skywall","skywall boss","ruler of air"},it="leader"},{q="How was Skywall created?",a="After defeating the Old Gods, the titans fashioned the Elemental Plane to imprison the chaotic elementals. The air elementals claimed a vast territory there, which became Skywall.",al={"origin of skywall","how was skywall made"},it="history"},{q="What happened to Prince Thunderaan?",a="During the Elemental Sundering, Garr and Baron Geddon, Ragnaros the Firelord's lieutenants, ambushed Prince Thunderaan. Ragnaros consumed the air prince's essence and bound its remains in a shattered talisman of elemental binding.",al={"thunderaan lore","what happened to thunderaan","windseeker fate"}},{q="Who lives in Skywall?",a="Air elementals, powerful djinn lords, lightning revenants, and elemental storm drakes live in Skywall. The Shen'dorei dwell in a sanctuary on Zephras Isle.",al={"skywall inhabitants","skywall denizens","who is in skywall"},it="residents"},{q="Can mortals reach Skywall?",a="Skywall lies within a separate dimensional prison, and mortals rarely reach it. Powerful sorcerers have manipulated elemental rifts to enter, while others have sought the isolated Shen'dorei on Zephras Isle.",al={"how to get to skywall","travel to skywall","skywall portal"},it="arrival"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you revere Skywall's raw winds and lightning, and beseech them when you commune with the spirits of air.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you follow the long history of arcanists seeking Skywall's boundless atmospheric power. Attempts to siphon Al'Akir's tempests often end in ruin."},kw={"air elemental","al'akir","elemental plane","shen'dorei","skywall","stormwall","thunderaan","windlord","zephras isle"},rel={"topic:elemental-plane","npc:thunderaan","zone:zephras","npc:highlord-demitrian","topic:titan","topic:old-god","subzone:uldum"},src={"Skywall"}}
E["topic:steamwheedle-cartel"] = {t="topic",n="Steamwheedle Cartel",z="general",s="In its ports, the Steamwheedle Cartel welcomes Alliance and Horde alike, so long as their coin is genuine. This powerful goblin enterprise has hubs in Booty Bay, Ratchet, and Gadgetzan. Its trade reaches shipping, alchemy, salvaging, and mercenary contracts.",h="In its ports, the Steamwheedle Cartel welcomes Alliance and Horde alike, so long as their coin is genuine.",sec={{t="A Profitable Neutrality",b="The Steamwheedle Cartel began beneath the earth in Undermine, the goblin capital. During the Second War, it backed the Old Horde with war machines, sappers, and naval engineering. When the war ended, its leaders judged that choosing sides cost more than it earned.\n\nSo the cartel turned to neutrality and spread across both continents, opening trade to Alliance and Horde alike. As tensions rise, its ports remain common ground. Anyone with gold can buy passage, store goods, or hire local specialists.",sp=0},{t="Ports and Outposts",b="The Steamwheedle Cartel builds its influence around ports and frontier towns. In Stranglethorn Vale, Baron Revilgaz rules Booty Bay, a harbor fortified in the cliffs beside the Blackwater Raiders. Across the Great Sea, Chief Engineer Gazlowe directs Ratchet on the Barrens coast.\n\nA deep-water ferry runs straight from Ratchet to Booty Bay. Gadgetzan lies deep in Tanaris, while Steamwheedle Port and outposts in Desolace, Azshara, and Stonetalon Mountains secure resources across the region.",sp=0},{t="Rivals and Reavers",b="Cutthroats threaten Steamwheedle trade at sea and on land. The Bloodsail Buccaneers menace Booty Bay's sea lanes, while Southsea Freebooters raid the coast near Ratchet. On land, the cartel fights its corporate rival, the Venture Company, over timber rights, oil fields, and shredder technology in Stonetalon and the Barrens. To keep order and enforce trade contracts, cartel barons hire passing mercenaries to settle disputes with extreme force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel is a neutral goblin trading enterprise based in Undermine. Its towns include Booty Bay, Ratchet, and Gadgetzan, where it offers banking, engineering, transport, and auction houses to every faction.",al={"who are steamwheedle","steamwheedle goblins","what is steamwheedle"},it="identity"},{q="Are the Steamwheedle goblins part of the Horde or Alliance?",a="Neither. The cartel keeps political neutrality and trades with both the Alliance and the Horde. It backed the Old Horde during the Second War, then ended its faction ties to pursue profit. Armed bruisers keep order in its towns.",al={"is steamwheedle horde","is steamwheedle cartel neutral","steamwheedle faction"},it="side"},{q="Which major cities belong to the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="The cartel's principal towns are Booty Bay in southern Stranglethorn Vale, Ratchet on the eastern shore of the Barrens, Gadgetzan in Tanaris, and Everlook in Winterspring. It also keeps smaller hubs, including Steamwheedle Port, and isolated trading outposts.",al={"steamwheedle towns","cartel cities","goblin towns list"},it="place"},{q="Who leads the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="The cartel is run from Undermine. Its towns answer to local bosses, including Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay and Chief Engineer Gazlowe in Ratchet.",al={"steamwheedle leader","trade prince steamwheedle","who runs steamwheedle"},it="leader"},{q="Why are the Steamwheedle goblins enemies with the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is a rival goblin enterprise known for strip-mining and deforestation. The two groups fight over territorial concessions, industrial blueprints, and natural resources across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"venture co vs steamwheedle","why hate venture co","venture company rivalry"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens if you fight inside a Steamwheedle port?",a="Armed goblin bruisers keep order in Steamwheedle towns. If you attack other travelers, guards may come after you; killing cartel guards or citizens harms your standing with the cartel.",al={"guards in booty bay","pvp in ratchet","ratchet bruisers"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Where did the Steamwheedle Cartel come from?",a="Originating from the subterranean metropolis of Undermine on Kezan, the Steamwheedle Cartel is the oldest and largest merchant syndicate in goblin society. They seized control of Blackwater Cove in Stranglethorn Vale, transforming it into the bustling haven of Booty Bay. During the Second War, the cartel sold its services to Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde, providing zeppelins, alchemists, and engineers for profit. When that conflict ended, the cartel recognized that strict neutrality across Azeroth offered vastly superior trade opportunities, prompting them to open neutral ports and trading outposts spanning both continents.",al={"steamwheedle history","origin of steamwheedle cartel","steamwheedle background"},it="history",add="ae8eebbb"},{q="Why are the Steamwheedle Cartel found in so many distant lands?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel pursues profit wherever trade routes, rare resources, or regional turmoil emerge. Establishing settlements like Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale, Ratchet along the Barrens coast, and Gadgetzan in Tanaris grants them dominion over maritime passage and frontier commerce between the continents. Their independent outposts and ventures allow them to trade openly with both the Alliance and the Horde while harvesting minerals, brokering salvage, and bankrolling lucrative contracts regardless of local peril.",al={"why is steamwheedle everywhere","why are goblins in ratchet and booty bay","steamwheedle locations why"},it="why_here",add="02088509"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Ratchet and Gadgetzan are key places to find Goblin Engineering schematics, shredder parts, and experimental mechanical components.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can use Steamwheedle ferries and desert outposts as waystations and flight paths through remote wilderness where the Horde is strong.",["faction:Horde"]="Gazlowe and his crew have long worked with the orcs of Durotar, but the cartel still expects payment for its services and keeps to neutrality.",["class:Rogue"]="Booty Bay and Ratchet's lawless fringes offer work for thieves, lockpicks, and covert contractors willing to fleece pirates and rivals."},kw={"booty bay","bruisers","cartel","gadgetzan","gazlowe","goblins","ratchet","revilgaz","steamwheedle","undermine"},rel={"subzone:ratchet","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:gadgetzan","subzone:steamwheedle-port","quest:1040","quest:887","quest:764","zone:barrens"},src={"Steamwheedle Cartel"}}
E["topic:stonefield-family"] = {t="topic",n="Stonefield family",z="general",s="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, the Stonefield family works its land while the Maclure feud endures. Young Tommy Joe is caught across the family divide.",h="At Stonefield Farm in western Elwynn, the Stonefield family works its land while the Maclure feud endures.",sec={{t="Life on the Homestead",b="South of the road to Westfall, the Stonefields work their farm in western Elwynn. Gramma Mildred Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield make their home there. They tend crops and livestock, while pests and kobolds from nearby mines and borders trouble the region.",sp=0},{t="The Maclure Feud",b="Woodland and pasture lie between the Stonefield and Maclure farms. The older generations keep a bitter, long-running grudge, and petty squabbles and claims over territory shape their dealings. Yet young Tommy Joe Stonefield and Maybell Maclure have fallen in love. With their families hostile, they depend on discreet travelers to carry messages between them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Stonefield family live?",a="The Stonefields live at Stonefield Farm in southwestern Elwynn Forest, just south of the main road toward the Westfall border.",al={"stonefield farm location","where are the stonefields","stonefield family location"},it="place"},{q="Who are the known members of the Stonefield family?",a="The known members of the Stonefield household are Gramma Mildred Stonefield, Ma Stonefield, and young Tommy Joe Stonefield.",al={"who is in the stonefield family","stonefield members","stonefield family tree"},it="people"},{q="Why do the Stonefields hate the Maclures?",a="The Stonefields and Maclures hold old territorial grudges and remain unwilling to reconcile.",al={"stonefield maclure feud","why are stonefields fighting maclures","maclure rivalry"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the feud affect Tommy Joe Stonefield?",a="Tommy Joe Stonefield is in love with Maybell Maclure, whose family is the Stonefields’ rival. They rely on discreet intermediaries to exchange letters and tokens of affection.",al={"tommy joe maclure","tommy joe romance","who is tommy joe in love with"},it="ties"},{q="Is the family aligned with Stormwind?",a="Yes. As humans in Elwynn Forest, the Stonefields fall under the protection of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Their attention stays on the farm and threats in the region.",al={"are stonefields alliance","stonefield loyalty"},it="side"},{q="What threats does the Stonefield family face?",a="The Stonefields face kobolds, roaming wildlife, too few Stormwind guards in the rural farmlands, and friction with the Maclures.",al={"stonefield dangers","problems at stonefield farm"},it="threat"},{q="Who are the Stonefields?",a="The Stonefields are an established human farming family residing in Elwynn Forest. Operating out of the Stonefield Farm southwest of Goldshire, they work the land while contending with surrounding wilderness threats and an ongoing, bitter feud with their neighbors, the Maclures.",al={"stonefield family lore","who are stonefield","stonefields"},it="identity",add="e2a78cbe"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you can see the Stonefields as part of the working backbone that provides grain and produce for the kingdom.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer traveling toward Westfall, you may find yourself helping the Stonefields with farm chores and family disputes in Elwynn."},kw={"elwynn forest","gramma stonefield","maclure","mildred stonefield","stonefield","stonefield family","stonefield farm","stonefields","tommy joe"},rel={"subzone:stonefield-farm","npc:tommy-joe-stonefield","npc:gramma-stonefield","npc:ma-stonefield","npc:maybell-maclure","zone:elwynn","topic:human","topic:alliance"},src={"Stonefield family"}}
E["topic:stonemasons-guild"] = {t="topic",n="Stonemasons Guild",z="general",s="Stormwind's rebuilding ended in a bitter dispute between the Stonemasons Guild and the House of Nobles. Deadly riots followed, and the guild was dissolved. Its members went into exile, and the scattered artisans' fate remains a mystery.",h="Stormwind's rebuilding ended in a bitter dispute between the Stonemasons Guild and the House of Nobles.",sec={{t="Architects of the Realm",b="Edwin VanCleef led the Stonemasons Guild as its elected Guildmaster. Its masons matched the skill of the dwarven Royal Stonecutters Union. After the First and Second Wars left Stormwind in ruins, the House of Nobles hired them to rebuild the city and restore the capital to its ancient grandeur.",sp=0},{t="Toil and Betrayal",b="For years, VanCleef and his craftsmen worked across Elwynn. They raised Stormwind Keep's soaring spires and the Cathedral of Light's great arches. Then royal finances collapsed under debts from military campaigns in the south. Guided by aristocratic politics, the House of Nobles refused to pay the agreed salaries and fees. When VanCleef sought restitution, the nobles disbanded the guild without its consent. Fury spread among the laborers who had bled to rebuild the city.",sp=0},{t="Blood in the Streets",b="The wage dispute became violent unrest throughout Stormwind. The Crown cracked down, capturing key conspirators, including VanCleef's lieutenant, Bazil Thredd. VanCleef and hundreds of ruined stonemasons fled into the Westfall countryside. Branded traitors and forced into exile, the desperate artisans turned their trade union into the militant Defias Brotherhood.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{t="The Hidden Hand",b="Lady Katrana Prestor, an advisor to the royal court, fed discord between the nobility and the builders. She persuaded the aristocracy that the Stonemasons' bills were extortionate and their work shoddy. At the same time, she provoked the craftsmen into open rebellion. By paralyzing Stormwind with strife and cutting off supplies to Westfall, the black dragon Onyxia fractured the kingdom from within.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What was the Stonemasons Guild?",a="The Stonemasons Guild was an association of human artisans, architects, and stonecutters led by elected Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef. Its members earned renown rebuilding Stormwind City after the Second War.",al={"who were the stonemasons","stonemasons guild lore","what did the stonemasons do"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the Stonemasons Guild become the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The House of Nobles refused to pay the guild's wages after Stormwind's rebuilding, amid crippling debt and court intrigue. Deadly protests drove the workers into exile, where they formed the Defias Brotherhood to claim their stolen wealth by force.",al={"why defias mad","why did stonemasons turn evil","origin of defias brotherhood"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Who was the leader of the Stonemasons Guild?",a="Edwin VanCleef was the guild's elected Guildmaster. Under his leadership, the masons became known for their stonework before he was exiled and founded the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"stonemasons guildmaster","vancleef guild","who led the stonemasons"},sp=1,it="leader",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What notable structures did the Stonemasons build?",a="The guild rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War, including the Cathedral of Light and Stormwind Keep.",al={"what did stonemasons build","did stonemasons build stormwind"},it="fame"},{q="Did all the Stonemasons join the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Some stonemasons did not join the rebellion. Master craftsman Baros Alexston broke with Edwin VanCleef, remained in Stormwind, and became City Architect. His former guildmates hated him for it.",al={"did all stonemasons become bandits","baros alexston stonemason","did any stonemasons stay in stormwind"},sp=1,it="people",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What happened during the Stonemason riots?",a="When the nobles disbanded the guild instead of paying it, stonemasons rioted in Stormwind's streets. The Crown captured VanCleef's lieutenant Bazil Thredd, while VanCleef and the other masons fled to Westfall.",al={"stonemason riots","what happened in the riots","stonemasons riot stormwind"}},{q="Who was Bazil Thredd in the Stonemasons Guild?",a="Bazil Thredd was Edwin VanCleef's trusted assistant and chief lieutenant in the guild. The Crown captured him after the riots, and he remains locked inside the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"bazil thredd backstory","thredd stonemason","vancleef lieutenant"},it="people"},{q="What is the history of the Stonemasons Guild?",a="Following the Second War, the Stonemasons Guild was commissioned by the House of Nobles to rebuild Stormwind City from the ruins left by the Orcish Horde. Composed of skilled engineers and artisans, they spent years restoring the kingdom to glory, shaping landmarks like the Cathedral of Light and Stormwind Keep. However, rising royal debts and political maneuvering led the nobility to refuse payment, culminating in riots and the guild's exile into Westfall.",al={"stonemasons history","stonemasons background","origin of stonemasons"},it="history",add="1a605800"},{q="Why are the Stonemasons called that?",a="They were named for their craft as professional stonecarvers, builders, and architects. Functioning as a chartered trade union akin to Ironforge's Royal Stonecutters Union, the guild brought together masons and artisans whose masterwork masonry was capable of constructing massive stone fortresses, cathedrals, and city ramparts.",al={"why called stonemasons","stonemasons guild name meaning"},it="name",add="f8ddb796"}},ang={["race:Human"]="Stormwind's beautiful white stone recalls a bitter tragedy within the kingdom and the cost of aristocratic pride for human travelers.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven masons respected the Stonemasons Guild. Its precision and towering ramparts rivaled those of Ironforge's Royal Stonecutters Union.",["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef's cunning reached far: master tradesmen became deadly highwaymen, lockpicks, and assassins.",["faction:Alliance"]="The guild's collapse left Westfall's breadbasket defenseless and overrun by outlaws. The Alliance's supply lines were strained just outside the capital."},kw={"alexston","defias","nethergarde","nobles","stonemasons","stormwind","thredd","vancleef"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:house-of-nobles","zone:stormwind","npc:baros-alexston","subzone:nethergarde-keep","npc:onyxia","quest:389"},src={"Stonemasons Guild"}}
E["topic:stormwind-army"] = {t="topic",n="Stormwind Army",z="general",s="Across the southern kingdom, the Stormwind Army struggles to guard its lands and the Grand Alliance. Its knights and marshals are famed for resilience, yet the king is missing, nobles quarrel, and too few soldiers hold the provinces.",h="Across the southern kingdom, the Stormwind Army struggles to guard its lands and the Grand Alliance.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Iron and Blood",b="For centuries, Stormwind's army has fought gnolls on the frontier and Gurubashi trolls in desperate battles. In the First War, King Llane Wrynn I and Sir Anduin Lothar led the Knights of Stormwind in famed ambushes against the Orcish Horde. Yet fire took the capital. Survivors fled to Lordaeron, helped form the Alliance of Lordaeron, and fought through the Second War. After the Dark Portal fell, the restored kingdom raised its military anew.",sp=0},{t="Structure and Ranks",b="Stormwind Keep holds the army's command, and regional garrisons answer to the Stormwind Marshals. Within the capital, the Stormwind City Guard keeps civil order. The elite Royal Guard protects the boy-king Anduin Wrynn and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Beyond the gates, outposts patrol Elwynn Forest, watch the trade roads, and man ramparts as far as the Redridge Mountains. On the water, the Stormwind Fleet supports the army.",sp=0},{t="A Thin Blue Line",b="The Stormwind Army is stretched thin, despite its proud traditions. The House of Nobles took on debts to extend its reach into Stranglethorn. Those debts deepened a bitter rift with the Stonemasons Guild. Civil riots followed, and the Defias Brotherhood was born.\n\nWith King Varian missing, the House of Nobles has often withheld troops, funds, and supplies from settlements such as Westfall, Lakeshire, and Duskwood. Local marshals turn to wandering adventurers to shoulder the realm's burdens.",sp=1,bt={"q123.3"}}},faq={{q="Why aren't more troops sent to Lakeshire and Sentinel Hill?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin, and provincial pleas for reinforcements go unanswered. Westfall depends on the People's Militia, while royal soldiers in Lakeshire survived the loss of Stonewatch Keep. With few defenders and supplies running low, officers ask traveling adventurers for help.",al={"where is the stormwind army","why no soldiers in westfall","why won't stormwind help"},it="motive"},{q="What is the difference between the Stormwind Army and the Stormwind Guard?",a="The Stormwind Army is the kingdom's wider military, with frontier marshals, garrisons, and knights serving across its lands. The Stormwind Guard enforces the law, patrols streets, and defends gates in Stormwind City and nearby rural hubs.",al={"guard vs army","who are stormwind guards","stormwind military branches"}},{q="Who commands the Stormwind Army right now?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the boy-king Anduin Wrynn holds official military authority, guided by Regent Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. The House of Nobles often contests and undermines their strategic choices.",al={"who leads stormwind army","stormwind army commander","supreme commander stormwind"},it="leader"},{q="Why do marshals give out deputy badges to adventurers?",a="Stormwind's army lacks soldiers, and the capital denies regional marshals reinforcements. McBride in Northshire and Dughan in Goldshire grant competent outsiders acting deputy status, so they can lawfully fight outlaws and defend the borders.",al={"deputy status","why deputize players","deputy stormwind"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the army during the First War?",a="Sir Anduin Lothar led the army in disciplined cavalry strikes that held the Orcish Horde at bay. But after King Llane was assassinated, the army was overwhelmed. Lothar led surviving soldiers and civilians across the Great Sea to Lordaeron, where the veterans formed the heart of the original Alliance forces.",al={"first war stormwind army","did stormwind army lose","lothar stormwind army"},it="history"},{q="Where does the army currently maintain active garrisons?",a="The army keeps formal garrisons across Elwynn Forest, including Northshire, Goldshire, and Westbrook Garrison. Westfall and Duskwood depend on local militias. Soldiers remain in Lakeshire after the loss of Stonewatch Keep, waiting for reinforcements.",al={"stormwind garrisons","where is army stationed","stormwind troop locations"},it="place"},{q="What is the Stormwind Army?",a="The Stormwind Army is the primary military force of the human Kingdom of Stormwind and a core pillar of the Grand Alliance. Based in Stormwind City, the army includes foot soldiers, heavily armored knights, and officers known as marshals. In addition to defending the realm's core territories across southern Azeroth, its commanders oversee provincial garrisons and commission local militias and adventuring deputies to maintain order.",al={"what is stormwind army","who are stormwind army","stormwind military"},it="identity",add="bbf0b2a6"},{q="Who is the Stormwind Army allied with?",a="The army serves the Crown of Stormwind, upholding the authority of the House of Wrynn and the ruling council. Beyond the kingdom's borders, it is formally bound to the Grand Alliance, standing in common defense alongside Ironforge, the gnomes of Gnomeregan, and the night elves of Kalimdor. Domestically, it collaborates with the Stormwind Fleet and the capital's City Guard.",al={"stormwind army allies","who does the army serve","who do they work for"},it="allies",add="b7687992"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a human warrior, you can look to the Knights of Stormwind and Lothar's infantry as models of disciplined service. Many soldiers still struggle with the nobility's abandonment of the frontier.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see the army's heavy cavalry and leaders work alongside the Order of the Silver Hand and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon to bring the Light's justice to lawless lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Lordaeron shattered by the Scourge, Stormwind's army forms the Grand Alliance's main defense in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you know the royal army as a lasting sign of survival against impossible odds, and as a reminder of neglect in distant hamlets."},kw={"anduin lothar","bolvar fordragon","defias","deputy","garrison","knights of stormwind","marshals","stormwind army","stormwind guard"},rel={"topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:varian-wrynn","zone:elwynn","npc:marshal-mcbride","quest:18"},src={"Stormwind Army"}}
E["topic:stormwind-guard"] = {t="topic",n="Stormwind Guard",z="general",s="Across Elwynn and Redridge, the Stormwind Guard struggles to hold its ground. Political gridlock and distant campaigns leave scattered marshals short of aid as gnolls, orcs, and bandits press the kingdom's borders.",h="Across Elwynn and Redridge, the Stormwind Guard struggles to hold its ground.",sec={{t="Shield of the Crown",b="The Stormwind Guard patrols the roads and watchtowers that bind the kingdom together. Appointed marshals defend the outlying settlements: Marshal McBride in Northshire Valley, Marshal Dughan in Goldshire, and Marshal Marris in Lakeshire. They gather recruits and keep order. Between posts such as Westbrook Garrison, they ride brown horses prized for their stamina.",sp=0},{t="A Border Stretched Thin",b="Since the Third War, the Guard has kept Elwynn Forest safe and quiet. In recent years, though, crisis has come. King Varian Wrynn has vanished, and the kingdom's standing army is tied down abroad, leaving regional garrisons with little aid. At Westbrook Garrison, Deputy Rainer struggles to hold the western border against Riverpaw gnolls and Defias thieves. Local commanders now depend on visiting adventurers for crucial security work and bounties.",sp=0},{t="The Abandoned Territories",b="Royal court decisions have deepened the Guard's crisis. Under Lady Katrana Prestor's influence, the kingdom judged Westfall too costly to garrison and withdrew its troops. Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood then seized the region. Duskwood met the same fate. Soldiers were withdrawn, to Darkshire's despair, and abandoned locals formed the ragtag Night Watch to defend themselves.",sp=1},{t="The Siege in the East",b="The crown kept a tenuous military presence in the Redridge Mountains, even as Duskwood and Westfall were abandoned. The Guard's position there is desperate. Shadowhide gnolls and Blackrock orcs from the Burning Steppes overwhelmed the soldiers and drove them from Stonewatch Keep. In Lakeshire, blacksmith Verner Osgood uses iron to keep guards equipped. Exhausted sentries watch the road for the 2nd Battalion, which never arrives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between the Stormwind Guard and the City Guard?",a="The Stormwind City Guard polices the capital within its walls. The Stormwind Guard defends the crown's outer territories, with regional garrisons patrolling roads and holding watchtowers across Elwynn Forest and Redridge.",al={"stormwind guard vs city guard","are they the same guards","city guard"}},{q="Why aren't there any Stormwind Guards in Westfall?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor's counsel on state expenses influenced the royal court to judge Westfall too costly to garrison, so all official troops withdrew. Without military protection, Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood quickly overran the territory's farms and roads.",al={"why did guards leave westfall","westfall army","where are westfall guards"}},{q="Why did the guard leave Duskwood?",a="Royal garrisons left Duskwood as resources dwindled. With crown protection gone amid rising dark magic and horrors, Darkshire's townsfolk formed the Night Watch to survive.",al={"duskwood guards","why did stormwind abandon darkshire","darkshire garrison"}},{q="Who leads the local garrisons?",a="Appointed regional marshals lead local defense. Marshal McBride oversees Northshire Valley, Marshal Dughan commands the forces centered in Goldshire, and Marshal Marris directs Lakeshire's desperate defense in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"who is in charge","guard leaders","marshals"},it="leader"},{q="Why are the guards in Lakeshire in such bad shape?",a="Blackrock orcs and local gnolls drove the Redridge garrison from Stonewatch Keep. Trapped in Lakeshire, the guards lack equipment, and blacksmith Verner Osgood uses nearly all available iron to rearm sentries. They wait for reinforcements promised by royal leaders, but those reinforcements are delayed.",al={"redridge guards losing","what happened at stonewatch","lakeshire garrison trouble"}},{q="Who is Marshal Haggard?",a="Marshal Haggard is a retired commander who once led the Stormwind Guard in calmer days. Back then, off-duty soldiers could travel south to drink together at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire.",al={"marshal haggard lore","retired marshal","old guard marshal"}},{q="What is the Stormwind Guard?",a="The Stormwind Guard, often known as the Stormwind Garrisons, is the territorial military branch of the Stormwind Army. Unlike the Stormwind City Guard who protect the capital's streets, these guards patrol the kingdom's outer territories—manning watchtowers, keeping roads secure, and enforcing royal law across Elwynn Forest and the Redridge Mountains.",al={"who are stormwind guards","stormwind garrison","what are stormwind guards"},it="identity",add="8131ff5c"},{q="Why are the Stormwind Guard stationed where they are?",a="They are stationed at outposts and scout towers every few miles along main roads to protect settlements and travelers from threats like gnolls, kobolds, and bandits. While they once maintained order across Westfall and Duskwood, court politics and resource shortages forced them to pull back, leaving active garrisons mainly in Elwynn Forest and Redridge.",al={"where are stormwind guards","guard locations","why guard towers"},it="why_here",add="fe3d1e2d"},{q="Who do the Stormwind Guard fight for?",a="They serve the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance under the authority of the crown and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Locally, they answer to appointed marshals and cooperate closely with town magistrates, local militia, and Alliance adventurers willing to reinforce their hard-pressed outposts.",al={"stormwind guard allegiances","who do guards serve","stormwind army faction"},it="allies",add="b4df286f"},{q="What is the history of the Stormwind Guard?",a="Following the Third War, the Guard maintained widespread stability, keeping watchtowers manned to protect Elwynn, Duskwood, and Westfall. However, recent political intrigue and royal court maneuvering led by Lady Katrana Prestor caused funding and troops to be withdrawn from outlying regions. With much of the army abroad or held back, the remaining garrisons now struggle to hold basic border posts like Westbrook and Lakeshire.",al={"stormwind guard history","origins of the guard","history of stormwind garrison"},sp=1,it="history",add="7b82470a",bt={"prestor.onyxia"}},{q="Why are they called the Stormwind Guard?",a="They bear the name of the Kingdom of Stormwind, representing royal authority and military law beyond the capital's walls. They are also known as the Stormwind Garrisons because their ranks are split into regional outposts stationed in fortified towers and towns across the realm.",al={"why stormwind guard","stormwind guard name meaning","why the garrison name"},it="name",add="8669b7db"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Stormwind Guard is the kingdom's front line. Its abandoned sister settlements reveal deep political cracks threatening the heart of the Alliance.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the southern farmlands, you may know the guard's blue tabards as a sign of safety. Their sudden absence in Westfall and Duskwood can feel like a bitter betrayal.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you may begin as a Northshire recruit and become a hardened veteran at Westbrook Garrison, marching with regional marshals against gnolls and bandits.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know a garrison depends on its armor. In places like Lakeshire, local smiths use entire iron reserves just to keep blades and shields serviceable."},kw={"garrison","goldshire","lakeshire","marshal dughan","marshal marris","marshal mcbride","stonewatch","stormwind guard","westbrook garrison"},rel={"topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom","npc:marshal-dughan","npc:marshal-marris","zone:elwynn","zone:redridge","topic:night-watch","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Stormwind Guard"}}
E["topic:stormwind-kingdom"] = {t="topic",n="Stormwind (kingdom)",z="general",s="In the years after Lordaeron fell, Stormwind is the Alliance's foremost power and humanity's greatest remaining bastion. Its southern lands include Elwynn Forest, Westfall, Duskwood, and the Redridge Mountains. Sacked in the First War and rebuilt after the Second, the kingdom now has a ten-year-old king, Anduin Wrynn, while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon guides its affairs amid troubles at home and beyond its borders.",h="In the years after Lordaeron fell, Stormwind is the Alliance's foremost power and humanity's greatest...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Defiance",b="Stormwind began more than a thousand years ago, founded by descendants of the ancient Arathi empire. They traveled south beyond the crags of Khaz Modan into fertile, forested valleys. Far from the northern kingdoms, Stormwind grew proud of its self-reliance and its faith in the Light.",sp=0},{t="Ashes and Restoration",b="The Orcish Horde came through the Dark Portal, and Stormwind's independence neared its end. In the First War, Stormwind City burned to ash and King Llane was slain. Sir Anduin Lothar led the survivors north across the Great Sea, where he rallied the northern realms into the Alliance of Lordaeron.\n\nAfter the Orcish threat was crushed in the Second War, refugees returned. They hired the Stonemasons Guild to rebuild their capital with white stone and blue banners. Then the Scourge wiped out Lordaeron during the Third War, leaving Stormwind humanity's greatest remaining bastion.",sp=0},{t="A Fractured Realm",b="Stormwind struggles to govern its vast southern holdings. Elwynn Forest remains relatively secure, but outlaws swarm through Westfall, while orcs and gnolls repeatedly enter Redridge. Duskwood's darkened woods have slipped from the kingdom's control.\n\nA bitter dispute between the House of Nobles and the Stonemasons erupted into violent riots in the capital. Displaced workers took up open rebellion across the provinces.",sp=1},{t="The Hollow Throne",b="King Varian Wrynn disappeared while sailing to a diplomatic summit with the Horde at Theramore. His ten-year-old son, Anduin Wrynn, inherited the crown, and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon became Lord Regent to preserve fragile public order.\n\nRoyal authority remains divided and stalled. Guided closely by the enigmatic Lady Katrana Prestor, the House of Nobles repeatedly vetoes military deployments. Local towns must defend themselves as dangerous secrets fester within Stormwind Keep.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is currently ruling Stormwind?",a="King Anduin Wrynn holds Stormwind's crown, while Highlord Bolvar Fordragon governs as Lord Regent because the king is a child. Lady Katrana Prestor and the House of Nobles provide heavy counsel and oversight.",al={"who is king of stormwind","current ruler","who runs stormwind","king of stormwind"},it="leader"},{q="What happened to King Varian Wrynn?",a="King Varian Wrynn left Stormwind on a confidential diplomatic voyage to Theramore to negotiate peaceful relations with the Horde. He vanished along the way, and his fate remains a guarded state secret, kept from the kingdom's people and external rivals to prevent chaos.",al={"where is varian","varian missing","what happened to the king","varian wrynn backstory"}},{q="Why was Stormwind destroyed in the past?",a="The Orcish Horde first encountered a human nation when it invaded Stormwind through the Dark Portal in the First War. King Llane and Sir Anduin Lothar led a stubborn defense, but the city was breached, sacked, and razed. The survivors fled north by sea to Lordaeron.",al={"first war stormwind","fall of stormwind","when did stormwind burn","stormwind destroyed"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood lacking royal soldiers?",a="Court politics and a stretched royal military leave Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood without royal soldiers. Lady Katrana Prestor and the House of Nobles often block requests for garrisons beyond Elwynn Forest, arguing that capital funds and forces cannot be spent policing peripheral lands. The People's Militia and the Night Watch are left to fight alone.",al={"why no soldiers","why no army help","abandoned towns","outlying towns undefended"},it="conflict"},{q="What territory does the Kingdom of Stormwind claim?",a="Stormwind claims Elwynn Forest, the Redridge Mountains, Westfall, and Duskwood on Azeroth's southern continent. It once maintained frontier posts reaching south into northern Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"stormwind borders","stormwind lands","what lands are stormwind"},it="place"},{q="Why did the Stonemasons turn against Stormwind?",a="After rebuilding Stormwind City in white stone, the Stonemasons Guild presented its invoice. Influenced by noble politics, the House of Nobles refused full payment, and the stonemasons would not compromise. Riots followed, driving the guild out to become the outlaw Defias Brotherhood.",al={"why defias mad","stonemasons riot","defias backstory","why did builders rebel"},sp=1,it="motive",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What is the Kingdom of Stormwind?",a="The Kingdom of Stormwind, also called the Kingdom of Azeroth, is the southernmost of humanity's Seven Kingdoms and the heart of the Grand Alliance. Settled by descendants of the ancient Arathor empire, it encompasses fertile territories stretching across Elwynn Forest, Westfall, the Redridge Mountains, and Duskwood. Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge in the north, Stormwind now stands as the strongest remaining bastion of human power and civilization in the world.",al={"what is stormwind","who is stormwind","stormwind kingdom"},it="identity",add="4ff36454"},{q="Who are the Kingdom of Stormwind allied with?",a="Stormwind is the pillar of the Grand Alliance, maintaining close ties with the Ironforge dwarves and Gnomeregan gnomes of Khaz Modan, as well as the night elves across the sea in Kalimdor. Its people also share profound spiritual and historical bonds with the Church of the Holy Light. While it once stood isolated from the northern human kingdoms, Stormwind now leads the unified factions striving to defend civilization across Azeroth.",al={"stormwind allies","who is stormwind allied with","alliance of stormwind"},it="allies",add="4fc8efc2"},{q="What is the history of Stormwind?",a="Founded roughly twelve hundred years ago by Arathi migrants who journeyed south past Khaz Modan, Stormwind prospered as an independent, agrarian realm. It was utterly sacked by the Orcish Horde in the First War. Led by Lord Anduin Lothar, the survivors fled north to Lordaeron, returning after the Second War to rebuild their gleaming capital. With Lordaeron's recent fall to the Scourge, Stormwind has become humanity's paramount stronghold.",al={"stormwind history","history of stormwind","where did stormwind come from"},it="history",add="bf266b42"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you stand with Stormwind, humanity's beating heart and last sovereign stronghold after Lordaeron, Alterac, and Dalaran fell in the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you look to Stormwind as the Alliance's main military and economic anchor. It offers shelter, leadership, and resources to its dwarven, gnomish, and night elven allies.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you follow the ancient holy traditions of the Church of the Holy Light and the legacy of the Silver Hand. The Cathedral of Light houses consecrated orders.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know Stormwind's bitter domestic strife and the Defias uprising have filled its back alleys, sewers, and countryside with opportunistic cutpurses and political spies."},kw={"anduin","azeroth","bolvar","elwynn","first war","house of nobles","prestor","stonemasons","stormwind","varian","wrynn"},rel={"zone:stormwind","zone:elwynn","zone:westfall","zone:redridge","zone:duskwood","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Stormwind (kingdom)"}}
E["topic:syndicate"] = {t="topic",n="Syndicate",z="general",s="Across northern Lordaeron, the Syndicate holds strongholds and fights to reclaim Alterac. Dispossessed nobles lead this human criminal organization against both the Alliance and the Horde, seeking to restore their lost aristocracy.",h="Across northern Lordaeron, the Syndicate holds strongholds and fights to reclaim Alterac.",sec={{t="Fallen Nobility",b="After King Aiden Perenolde's treachery during the Second War, the kingdom of Alterac collapsed in dishonor. Its aristocracy lost its lands and titles, but the surviving nobles refused to accept exile. They gathered under the late king's son, Prince Aliden Perenolde, and forged the Syndicate.\n\nThey marked themselves with orange bandanas and filled their ranks with hired thugs, highwaymen, and hedge wizards. To outsiders, they are brigands who raid caravans, ambush travelers, and extort people. Yet their crimes exist only to fund an organized bid to reclaim their ancestral lands and subjugate the surrounding regions.",sp=0},{t="Strongholds of the North",b="Across northern Lordaeron, the Syndicate holds fortified ground. In the snowy Alterac Mountains, they fortified the ruined town of Strahnbrad and set camps in the Uplands and Dandred's Fold. Farther south, they hold the crumbling Durnholde Keep in the Hillsbrad Foothills. From there, they harass Southshore and raid supply routes.\n\nFarther east, beyond Thoradin's Wall, Lord Falconcrest commands an occupying Syndicate army in the historic ruins of Stromgarde Keep. There, they battle the battered Stromgarde Militia for control of the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="Enemies on All Fronts",b="The Syndicate's ambitions reach beyond ordinary outlawry, earning them the hatred of nearly every regional faction. They call the Alliance their mortal enemy, believing it stole their rightful heritage. Their attacks often target Southshore officials such as Magistrate Henry Maleb.\n\nToward the Horde, their scorn is open. Following Aedelas Blackmoore's philosophy, they see orcs as beasts fit for slave labor and seek to restore the internment camps. Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken execute captured Syndicate members on sight. Ravenholdt's clandestine thieves' guild wages a shadow war against Syndicate operatives it considers sloppy and arrogant.",sp=0},{t="Puppets of the Shadow Council",b="The Syndicate's noble leaders believe they fight for human supremacy and their birthright. Yet cultists of the Argus Wake have infiltrated the upper ranks and steer men such as Lord Falconcrest toward seizing Stromgarde Keep.\n\nThe Argus Wake answers to the Shadow Council in Jaedenar, within Felwood. It uses the Syndicate's armies and stolen lands as a mortal vanguard, clearing the way for the Burning Legion.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who are the Syndicate?",a="The Syndicate is a criminal organization of dispossessed nobles, brigands, and mercenaries from fallen Alterac. Exiled aristocrats such as Prince Aliden Perenolde and Lord Falconcrest lead them. They use highway robbery, assassination, and military occupation to try to rebuild Alterac.",al={"what is the syndicate","syndicate background","who are these guys in orange"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Syndicate hate the Alliance?",a="Alterac betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War, and the Alliance dismantled the kingdom and stripped its nobles of their lands. Syndicate leaders consider the Alliance their mortal enemy and sabotage its towns, trade caravans, and garrisons such as Stromgarde Keep.",al={"why does syndicate attack alliance","syndicate alliance relationship","alterac vs alliance"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does the Syndicate capture and enslave orcs?",a="The Syndicate follows the harsh philosophy of former Durnholde commander Aedelas Blackmoore, who viewed orcs as savage beasts fit only for unpaid servitude. Prince Aliden Perenolde sought to restore the Alliance internment camps, using enslaved orcs captured in the Hillsbrad Foothills and Alterac as forced labor.",al={"syndicate orc slaves","why are orcs in cages in strahnbrad","syndicate slavery"},sp=1,it="motive",bt={"q533.4"}},{q="What is the Syndicate's relationship with Ravenholdt?",a="Ravenholdt is a prestigious guild of professional assassins and thieves in the Alterac Mountains. Its members consider the Syndicate amateurish and undisciplined, and contract rogues to steal Syndicate emblems. The Syndicate's leaders ruthlessly cull operatives who lose theirs.",al={"ravenholdt vs syndicate","why does ravenholdt hate syndicate","syndicate emblems"},it="ties"},{q="Who is really pulling the strings behind the Syndicate?",a="The Syndicate publicly answers to exiled Alteraci nobles such as Prince Aliden Perenolde and Lord Falconcrest. They believe they are fighting to reclaim their lost titles. Yet whispers in the Arathi Highlands hint at darker hands behind their hold on Stromgarde, and travelers can look into it at the Syndicate's strongholds there.",al={"who leads the syndicate","argus wake syndicate","shadow council syndicate"},sp=2,it="power"},{q="Where are the Syndicate's primary strongholds?",a="The Syndicate's main strongholds lie across the Alterac Mountains, the Hillsbrad Foothills, and the Arathi Highlands. They hold Strahnbrad and Dandred's Fold in Alterac, Durnholde Keep in Hillsbrad, and Northfold Manor in Arathi. Under Lord Falconcrest, they also occupy a large part of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"where are syndicate bases","syndicate locations","where to find syndicate"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Syndicate hostile to travelers?",a="The Syndicate views all outsiders as threats to their criminal plots and territorial ambitions. They despise the Alliance for dismantling Alterac after the Second War, regard the Horde merely as brutes fit only for forced labor, and brook no interference in their banditry, assassinations, and raids.",al={"why do syndicate attack","syndicate hostile","why syndicate attack players"},it="hostile",add="1053e6ff"},{q="Who leads the Syndicate?",a="The organization was founded and led in the Alterac Mountains by Prince Aliden Perenolde, the son of Alterac's traitorous late king. In the Arathi Highlands, operations are commanded by Lord Falconcrest from the ruins of Stromgarde Keep, supported by regional overseers like Baron Vardus and Master Ryson.",al={"syndicate leader","who is in charge of syndicate","syndicate boss"},it="leader",add="8dd05730"},{q="Who is the Syndicate allied with?",a="Openly, they rely on rogue mercenaries, bandits, and corrupt human nobility while fighting nearly every established faction. In secret, however, the Syndicate is manipulated by the Argus Wake, a sinister warlock coven serving the Shadow Council at Jaedenar, which promised to restore Alterac's rule in exchange for footholds across northern Lordaeron.",al={"syndicate allies","who works with syndicate","syndicate partners"},sp=1,it="allies",add="c949a5e9"},{q="Where did the Syndicate come from?",a="The Syndicate was born from the ruins of the Kingdom of Alterac. After King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance during the Second War, Alterac was stripped of sovereignty and fell into ruin. Deposed nobles and disgruntled aristocrats banded together under Prince Aliden Perenolde, turning to smuggling, banditry, and terrorism to reclaim their lost lands.",al={"syndicate origin","syndicate history","how was syndicate formed"},it="history",add="ff7f041a"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Ravenholdt pays thieves to slip behind enemy lines and steal emblems from Syndicate brigands, taking advantage of their fear of losing rank.",["race:Orc"]="The Syndicate sees your people as beasts destined for chains and internment. Freeing captured brethren in Strahnbrad and Durnholde is a matter of honor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Syndicate operatives murdered Southshore's former magistrate and keep pushing the beleaguered Stromgarde Militia toward extinction in the Arathi Highlands.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Thrall and Lady Sylvanas both maintain active bounties against the Syndicate. They send scouts to destroy its camps and recover stolen relics."},kw={"aliden perenolde","alterac","bandanas","durnholde keep","falconcrest","ravenholdt","strahnbrad","stromgarde","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:ravenholdt","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:dandred-s-fold","zone:alterac","quest:5726"},src={"Syndicate"}}
E["topic:tauren"] = {t="topic",n="Tauren",z="general",s="Across central Kalimdor, the tauren are building a home in Mulgore while keeping their old ways. They call themselves shu'halo and honor the Earth Mother, shamanism, and the natural world. Centaur clans nearly destroyed them before they joined Thrall's New Horde. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof now leads them from Mulgore and Thunder Bluff.",h="Across central Kalimdor, the tauren are building a home in Mulgore while keeping their old ways.",sec={{t="Nomads of the Barrens",b="For countless generations, the tauren roamed the arid Barrens with the seasons. They hunted the great kodo and listened for the Earth Mother's voice. Then the centaur tribes brought their peaceful wanderings to an end. Born from the tragic union of Zaetar and Princess Theradras, the fierce centaur waged a relentless war against them. Without a fortified homeland, and unwilling to fight without end, the tauren were driven near annihilation.",sp=0},{t="The New Horde and Thunder Bluff",b="An alliance from across the sea gave the tauren a chance to survive. During the Third War, Cairne Bloodhoof met Warchief Thrall and the orcs who had newly arrived. The leaders recognized a shared honor and longing for their shamanic heritage, and joined forces.\n\nWith the Horde's help, the tauren defeated the marauding centaur and claimed Mulgore's sheltered grasslands. Cairne founded Thunder Bluff on Mulgore's windswept mesas. In gratitude, the tauren marched with the Horde to Mount Hyjal and helped turn back the Burning Legion.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Guardians and Internal Tensions",b="The tauren bring a peaceful, steadying voice to the Horde. Their mastery of nature and the elements helped revive orcish shamanism. Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem also keeps rare diplomatic and spiritual ties with night elf druids as they investigate growing corruption within the Emerald Dream.\n\nYet unity among the tribes remains fragile. Most revere Cairne's wisdom, but the xenophobic and ruthless Grimtotem clan lives within Thunder Bluff. Its leader, the scheming elder crone Magatha, secretly plots to seize leadership and steer the shu'halo toward supremacy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why did the tauren join the Horde?",a="Ruthless centaur clans nearly wiped out the tauren in the Barrens. During the Third War, Warchief Thrall and his orcs fought beside Cairne Bloodhoof, drove the centaur back, and helped secure Mulgore. Bound by honor and shared spiritual values, Cairne pledged his people's loyalty to the New Horde in gratitude.",al={"why join horde","tauren horde alliance","why are tauren in horde"}},{q="Who leads the tauren?",a="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof leads the tauren and heads the Bloodhoof tribe. Respected for his strength and measured judgment, he unites the tribes from Thunder Bluff, with Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem assisting him.",al={"tauren leader","tauren chieftain","who rules thunder bluff"}},{q="What is the Earth Mother?",a="The Earth Mother is the central deity of tauren belief. The shu'halo believe she created the world, the sun, and the moon. They honor her through a life attuned to nature's balance, seasonal migration, hunting, and respect for the elements.",al={"earthmother","who is the earth mother","tauren religion"}},{q="Why do the tauren hate the centaur?",a="Centaur hunted the tauren for sport and warred with them for centuries across central Kalimdor. They saw the tauren's peaceful spirituality as weakness, drove them from place to place, and nearly wiped out the shu'halo before the orcs intervened.",al={"tauren centaur war","centaur feud"}},{q="Can tauren be druids?",a="Yes. Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem leads the tauren druids, who learn the ways of the wild alongside night elves. Tauren druids are a cornerstone of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"tauren druid lore","how did tauren become druids"}},{q="Are all tauren loyal to Cairne Bloodhoof?",a="Most tauren tribes revere Cairne, but the Grimtotem are a bitter exception. Led by Magatha Grimtotem, they believe tauren are superior to all other races and despise Cairne's alliance with the Horde. They quietly work to undermine his peaceful reign.",al={"grimtotem loyalty","tauren civil war"}},{q="Which classes can tauren be?",a="Tauren train as warriors, hunters, shaman and druids.",al={"tauren classes","what classes can tauren be"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As shu'halo, your people's ancient nomadic wanderings have given way to a homeland in Mulgore, secured through the brotherhood between Cairne and Thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="The tauren give the Horde moral guidance and deep spiritual roots, tempering the aggressive instincts of orcs and trolls with ancient wisdom and honor.",["class:Druid"]="Through Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, tauren druids work alongside the night elves of the Cenarion Circle to heal the land and protect the Emerald Dream.",["class:Shaman"]="Tauren shamanic traditions are among Azeroth's oldest. Their teachings helped the orcs rediscover their sacred elemental bonds after the demonic taint of past wars."},kw={"barrens","cairne bloodhoof","centaur","earth mother","hamuul runetotem","kodo","magatha grimtotem","mulgore","shu'halo","tauren","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","zone:barrens","topic:earth-mother","topic:centaur","npc:magatha-grimtotem","quest:1489"},src={"Tauren"}}
E["topic:third-war"] = {t="topic",n="Third War",z="general",s="Across Lordaeron and Kalimdor, the Third War ended only after mortals stood against the Burning Legion. The war began with the Lich King's Plague of Undeath and brought down Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas before the defense of Mount Hyjal.",h="Across Lordaeron and Kalimdor, the Third War ended only after mortals stood against the Burning Legion.",sec={{t="The Plague and the Prince",b="The Third War began with plague in northern Lordaeron. Infected grain from Andorhal carried a sickness that killed its victims and raised them as ghouls bound to the Lich King's will. Prince Arthas Menethil and Jaina Proudmoore, a sorceress of the Kirin Tor, tried to stop it.\n\nDreadlords turned Arthas's grief and fear toward Stratholme. He purged its infected people, then pursued his foe to Northrend. There Arthas took Frostmourne, the cursed runeblade, and cast aside his soul. He returned south and murdered his father, King Terenas. Lordaeron then fell into the Scourge's hands.",sp=0},{t="The Invasion of the Legion",b="Arthas used the dead to crush Quel'Thalas and raise the necromancer Kel'Thuzad at the Sunwell. The Scourge then besieged Dalaran and seized the spellbooks needed to summon Archimonde, the demon lord, into Azeroth. With Archimonde on mortal soil, Dalaran was leveled by arcane devastation. The Scourge had served as the Legion's advance guard. Now the Burning Legion turned toward the eternal power across the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="The Flight West and Mount Hyjal",b="The mysterious Prophet sent cryptic warnings to Warchief Thrall and Lady Jaina Proudmoore. Thrall led the New Horde across the Great Sea, while Jaina brought surviving Alliance refugees to safety. In ancient Kalimdor, the newcomers clashed with the reclusive night elves.\n\nThen the three factions recognized the threat before them. Atop Mount Hyjal, mortals joined forces beneath the World Tree Nordrassil. When Archimonde reached the tree, ancestral wisps destroyed him. The Legion's vanguard was broken, and the war ended.",sp=0},{t="A Scarred World",b="Archimonde's fall brought no lasting peace. Lordaeron's Alliance is gone. Stormwind and Ironforge now anchor the southern Alliance, while the old kingdom rots as the Plaguelands. In Kalimdor, Thrall's Horde has carved out Durotar, though tensions with the newly allied night elves remain volatile.\n\nThe Scourge still holds the northern ruins. The freed undead, called the Forsaken, hold the catacombs of Capital City. They fight to survive against their former masters and vengeful crusaders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="When did the Third War happen?",a="The Third War began when the Plague of Undeath broke out in Lordaeron and ended at the Battle of Mount Hyjal. The devastation is only four years past, so ruins are fresh and nearly every adult alive fought in the war or lost family to it.",al={"when was the third war","how long ago was the war","third war dates"},it="history"},{q="How was the Third War different from the First and Second Wars?",a="The First and Second Wars were chiefly struggles between the Old Horde and the Alliance kingdoms. The Third War brought a demonic invasion that shattered nations. Mortals fought the Burning Legion and its undead Scourge across three continents, forcing enemies into a desperate truce.",al={"difference between third war and second","why was third war different","horde vs alliance third war"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to the Kingdom of Lordaeron?",a="Lordaeron was destroyed from within. The Cult of the Damned tainted the regional grain with the Plague of Undeath, killing people and raising them as monsters. Prince Arthas fell to corruption, murdered his father King Terenas II, and delivered the broken kingdom to the Scourge.",al={"fate of lordaeron","why is lordaeron destroyed","what happened to terenas"},it="ruin"},{q="Who was the Prophet that warned everyone to go to Kalimdor?",a="The Prophet was Medivh, the Last Guardian of Tirisfal. Seeking atonement for opening the Dark Portal, he traveled as a raven-cloaked wanderer. He warned that Lordaeron was doomed and urged its leaders to unite in Kalimdor.",al={"who was the prophet","raven prophet","medivh third war"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the night elves part of the Alliance now?",a="The night elves had lived in strict isolation for ten thousand years. The Third War brought the Legion back to their sacred forests and made them sacrifice their immortality to slay Archimonde at the World Tree. In a changed world, with resource conflicts growing between them and Thrall's Horde and Scourge corruption still present, they left their solitude and allied with the races of the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why did night elves join alliance","night elves third war","kaldorei joining alliance"},it="allies"},{q="How did the Horde escape the war in Lordaeron?",a="Warchief Thrall trusted Medivh's prophetic dreams. He rallied the freed clans from the internment camps, raided human ports for sailing ships, and crossed the Great Sea before the Scourge or Legion fully consumed Lordaeron.",al={"how did thrall leave lordaeron","orcs sailing west","horde kalimdor flight"},it="motive"},{q="What was the Third War?",a="The Third War was a catastrophic global conflict that saw the demonic Burning Legion launch its second invasion of Azeroth, aided by the undead Scourge. Beginning with the Plague of Undeath in northern Lordaeron and the betrayal of Prince Arthas Menethil, the war quickly spread across the Eastern Kingdoms and into Kalimdor. Unlike earlier conflicts between just orcs and humans, it engulfed nearly every major race on Azeroth before culminating in a desperate, united stand atop Mount Hyjal.",al={"what is the third war","third war summary","explain third war"},it="identity",add="b67a3dac"},{q="Why is it called the Third War?",a="It is named the Third War because it followed the First and Second Wars fought between the original orcish Horde and the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron. Because this invasion brought unprecedented global devastation and demon armies, it is also known as the Third Great War, the Chaos War, and the Reign of Chaos.",al={"third war name origin","why called third war","reign of chaos name"},it="name",add="4a458aae"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lordaeron's fall moved Alliance leadership south to Stormwind and Ironforge. Survivors look north, longing to reclaim their homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="For Thrall's Horde, the war brought redemption. Grommash Hellscream slew Mannoroth and broke the demonic blood curse, so the orcs could build a sovereign nation in Kalimdor.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken are Lordaeron's people, slain by the plague and forced to serve the Scourge. They broke free and claimed the Undercity.",["race:NightElf"]="Defending Nordrassil cost the kaldorei their immortality. It also opened their ancient homelands to the wider world for the first time in ten thousand years.",["class:Paladin"]="The Knights of the Silver Hand were torn apart in the war. Arthas disbanded them, murdered Uther the Lightbringer, and turned their holy halls into charnel houses."},kw={"archimonde","arthas","hyjal","mannoroth","medivh","nordrassil","scourge","stratholme","terenas","third war"},rel={"topic:scourge","topic:burning-legion","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:nordrassil","topic:lordaeron","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:medivh","topic:new-horde"},src={"Third War"}}
E["topic:titan"] = {t="topic",n="Titan",z="general",s="Across the Great Dark Beyond, the titans travel from world to world, seeking places to shape and order. Long ago, they came to Azeroth, defeated the Old Gods, raised great works, and prepared the world for life before departing among the stars.",h="Across the Great Dark Beyond, the titans travel from world to world, seeking places to shape and order.",sec={{t="Architects of the Cosmos",b="Vast are the titans, cosmic giants of primordial matter and arcane magic. They carry the forces of order and creation, seeking sleeping worlds to cultivate. There they raise continents, calm the elements, and shape life. Stone, iron, and sea constructs guard their works and keep the balance they sought.",sp=0},{t="The Ordering of Azeroth",b="When the Pantheon found Azeroth long ago, chaotic elemental lords and the horrific Old Gods held the world in their grip. The titans drove the elementals into pocket planes and sealed the Old Gods beneath the earth. They shaped great biomes and built vaults such as Uldaman. Then they entrusted five great dragons, the Dragon Aspects, with the land, magic, time, and life, and journeyed back among the stars.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Champion",b="Sargeras once stood among the titans as their greatest warrior and defender. Yet the deep cosmic darkness and demonic malevolence he fought filled him with fear and despair. He rejected his kin's work and embraced nihilism. To extinguish all creation rather than let it fall to corruption, he founded the Burning Legion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Are the titans still alive and on Azeroth?",a="The titans departed Azeroth long ago for the Great Dark Beyond, after defeating the Old Gods and ordering the world. They left watchers, stone and iron constructs, and buried vaults to oversee their design.",al={"where are the titans","are titans on azeroth","titan locations"},it="place"},{q="Why do the dwarves care so much about the titans?",a="Dwarves descend from the earthen, subterranean stone beings the titans fashioned to carve the world's foundations. Through archaeology and the excavation of ruins such as Bael Modan and Uldaman, dwarves seek their forgotten lineage.",al={"dwarf titan connection","why dwarves dig","dwarves and the creators"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Pantheon?",a="The Pantheon is the titans' governing council, led by the Highfather Aman'Thul. Its members include Khaz'goroth the shaper of worlds, Eonar the life-binder, Norgannon the keeper of celestial magics, Golganneth the lord of skies, and Aggramar, who replaced Sargeras as champion.",al={"titan pantheon","who leads the titans","titan leaders"}},{q="Did the titans create the Dragon Aspects?",a="Yes. Before leaving Azeroth, the Pantheon sent its power through the keepers to bless five proto-dragons. Alexstrasza, Ysera, Malygos, Nozdormu, and Neltharion received immense power to safeguard life, nature, magic, time, and the earth.",al={"titan dragons","aspect origins","who made the aspects"}},{q="Is Sargeras a titan?",a="Sargeras was once the Pantheon's champion, defending the cosmos against chaos and demons. The darkness he witnessed drove him to despair and madness. He broke with his brethren to form the Burning Legion and burn down the ordered universe.",al={"who is sargeras","is sargeras a god","sargeras origin"}},{q="Did a titan fall in Silithus?",a="The Qiraji Prophet Skeram recorded prophecies claiming that a titan battled an ancient evil in Silithus's southern deserts and fell. Scholars and explorers still debate whether the fallen being was a true titan or one of their constructs.",al={"silithus titan","prophecy of c'thun titan","did c'thun kill a titan"},it="history"},{q="What are the titans?",a="The titans are colossal, godlike beings of the cosmos, the supreme champions of Order and creation. Wandering the Great Dark Beyond, they bring structure to formless worlds and foster life wherever they travel.",al={"who are the titans","what is a titan","titan lore"},it="identity",add="f6eb9ea0"},{q="Where did the titans come from?",a="No mortal knows where the titans came from. They are ancient beings of the Great Dark Beyond who travel the cosmos to bring order to newborn worlds, as they did when they came to Azeroth, defeated the Old Gods and shaped the land.",al={"titan origin","origin of titans","how were titans created"},it="history",add="23c22d21"},{q="Who leads the titans?",a="The titans are led by Highfather Aman'Thul, the eldest among them and the head of their governing council, the Pantheon. Wielding immense temporal and cosmic power, Aman'Thul guides their mission across the Great Dark Beyond to order worlds.",al={"who is the titan leader","leader of the titans","leader of the pantheon"},it="leader",add="91d84aea"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you revere the titans as the divine Makers. The Explorers' League and King Magni Bronzebeard seek your origins among titanic relics.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you share a mechanical legacy from titanic creations. That legacy drives your affinity for clockwork design and excavation.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you wield arcane magic, the titans' fundamental lifeblood. Its ordered principles trace to enchantments the Pantheon wove across the world.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you dig deep into the earth and may uncover pristine titan-forged metal and foundations older than recorded history."},kw={"aman'thul","earthen","eonar","khaz'goroth","makers","norgannon","order","pantheon","titan"},rel={"npc:magni-bronzebeard","topic:old-god","topic:sargeras","topic:burning-legion","topic:emerald-dream","npc:deathwing","zone:silithus","npc:greatfather-winter"},src={"Titan"}}
E["topic:trogg"] = {t="topic",n="Trogg",z="general",s="Deep beneath the earth, Troggs have clawed their way into the world above. Dwarven excavations disturbed their ancient vaults, and now they overrun quarries and hold Gnomeregan after driving its gnomes out.",h="Deep beneath the earth, Troggs have clawed their way into the world above.",sec={{t="The Flawed Predecessors",b="The first stone servants were a flawed design. Long before mortal races kept records, titan-forged keepers tried to shape servants from stone. They made brutish creatures with stone skin, little sense, and savage tempers. The keepers refined their design into the earthen, ancestors of the dwarves. Ironaya, a giantess, spared the flawed troggs and sealed them deep within Uldaman, hoping they would sleep without end.",sp=0},{t="Awakened by the Pickaxe",b="Dwarven excavations woke the troggs after countless millennia. The Explorers' League of Ironforge broke into ancient underground complexes in Khaz Modan, and furious swarms poured out to hunt their distant dwarven kin. The bright surface world drove them to dig tunnels beneath Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and the Badlands. From below, they ambushed quarries, archaeological dig sites, and trade outposts.",sp=0},{t="The Catastrophe at Gnomeregan",b="Troggs followed underground vibrations and noise into Gnomeregan. Outnumbered and overpowered, the gnomes fought them through the city's corridors. Mekgineer Thermaplugg devised a desperate plan. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque released radioactive gas to kill the invaders, but it killed roughly eighty percent of the gnomish people and only enraged the troggs. The great city was left irradiated and under trogg control.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What exactly are troggs?",a="Troggs are underground humanoids, the first flawed stone servants made by the titan-forged keepers. The keepers sealed them in stasis vaults such as Uldaman instead of destroying them. Dwarven miners later unearthed them.",al={"trogg origins","what is a trogg","trogg lore"},it="identity"},{q="Are troggs related to dwarves?",a="Yes. The titans' keepers shaped both races. Troggs were their crude first design, while the earthen, ancestors of the dwarves, were the refined design.",al={"are dwarves and troggs related","trogg dwarf connection"},it="ties"},{q="How did troggs capture Gnomeregan?",a="Troggs followed the vibrations of heavy machinery and tunneled up into Gnomeregan. Their numbers overwhelmed the gnomes despite their defensive inventions. Radioactive gas meant to drive out the invaders killed most of the gnomes, leaving the city in trogg hands.",al={"why are troggs in gnomeregan","gnomeregan trogg attack"},it="conflict"},{q="Are troggs capable of speech or advanced culture?",a="Troggs have little intellect and mostly communicate with grunts and roars. They prize brute strength and choose tribal chieftains through violence. Some show simple shamanistic magic, but their craft remains crude, from clubs and stone arrows to stolen relics.",al={"can troggs talk","trogg culture","trogg intelligence"},it="power"},{q="Why do troggs collect ancient relics?",a="Explorers believe troggs hoard ancient titan relics because of an instinct left from their origins. Troggs rarely understand the objects, using priceless artifacts as clubs or simple charms for luck.",al={"why do troggs hoard artifacts","trogg treasure"},it="purpose"},{q="Are there troggs outside of Khaz Modan?",a="Yes. Trogg clans live underground across Azeroth, including the Ragefire troggs deep in Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar, the Gravelflint troggs in Darkshore, and groups in the Badlands and Alterac.",al={"trogg locations","troggs in durotar","troggs in kalimdor"},it="place"},{q="Why are troggs so hostile to other races?",a="Troggs are driven almost entirely by raw instinct, cunning, and sheer aggression. Upon being disturbed from their ancient slumber deep underground, their immediate impulse was to vent their fury on the surface dwellers, particularly their dwarven cousins who broke into their vaults. Simpleminded and territorial, they view other living beings either as threats to be crushed or as meals to be eaten, readily resorting to violence and even cannibalism without provocation.",al={"why troggs attack","are troggs aggressive","why do troggs hate dwarves"},it="hostile",add="0f8118fe"},{q="Who leads the troggs?",a="Troggs have no unified ruler or central civilization. Instead, they organize into scattered tribes and clans, such as the Rockjaw, Stonesplinter, and Stonevault troggs. Within each tribe, leadership belongs solely to the strongest, largest, and most vicious brute who can enforce rule through intimidation and bloodshed, such as Grimlok within Uldaman.",al={"trogg leader","trogg chieftain","trogg king"},it="leader",add="9c157b85"},{q="Do troggs have any allies?",a="Almost universally, troggs fight alone. Their savagery, cannibalistic tendencies, and hostility toward other races make diplomacy impossible, and they despise outsiders. A rare exception exists among the Stonesplinter clan, who have established loose ties with the kobolds of the Tunnel Rats, but genuine allegiances beyond their own kind are practically nonexistent.",al={"trogg allies","who works with troggs","trogg factions"},it="allies",add="21373546"},{q="Where did troggs come from?",a="Troggs were the first generation of titan-forged crafted by the titanic keepers. The design proved flawed and overly complex, producing stone-skinned, brutish creatures lacking higher intellect. Distressed by the result, the keepers refined their subsequent efforts into the earthen and sealed the defective troggs in stasis vaults like Uldaman. Over millennia, they slept beneath Azeroth until dwarven miners unwittingly excavated their tombs.",al={"origin of troggs","trogg history","how were troggs created"},it="history",add="638bdf0a"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Troggs are the bitter bane of your people. They shattered your underground home and scattered the survivors to Tinker Town in Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your people unearthed these savage cousins while seeking titan ancestry. Their incursions across Khaz Modan followed from dwarven archaeology.",["profession:Mining"]="Troggs often occupy rich mineral veins and deep mines such as Gol'Bolar. Miners must defend their claims with pickaxes and hammers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Defending Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and Gnomeregan from trogg infestations helps protect the mountain kingdom and its refugees."},kw={"caverndeep","earthen","gnomeregan","grubbis","oggleflint","rockjaw","stonesplinter","trogg","uldaman"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:uldaman","zone:dunmorogh","zone:lochmodan","zone:ragefire","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","topic:explorers-league"},src={"Trogg"}}
E["topic:troll"] = {t="topic",n="Troll",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, the troll empires lie divided, while the Darkspear now live within Thrall's Horde. Trolls are among the world's oldest peoples, born near the Well of Eternity before the Sundering. They heal swiftly and honor primal spirits called loa through voodoo.",h="Across Azeroth, the troll empires lie divided, while the Darkspear now live within Thrall's Horde.",sec={{t="Children of the Wilds",b="Trolls first arose near the Well of Eternity, long before the Great Sundering broke ancient Kalimdor. They lived by hunting and gathering, swift and agile, and their bodies healed grievous wounds with astonishing speed. Given time, they could regrow even severed limbs. Around the sacred mountains of Zandalar, they turned to primal spirits called loa. Shadow hunters and witch doctors guided these rites, which grew into voodoo.",sp=0},{t="War Against the Aqir",b="In ancient times, troll empires fought a long war against the insectoid aqir, whose swarms threatened to overrun the continent. The Amani and Gurubashi led the struggle and drove the aqir to the land's far reaches. Some fled north to what became Azjol-Nerub. Others went south to the deserts where Ahn'Qiraj would rise.",sp=0},{t="A Fractured Legacy",b="With the aqir broken and contained, the trolls lost their common cause. Their great factions withdrew into separate empires, shaping distinct cultures, physical traits, and tribal orders for forests, jungles, and frozen wastes. Millennia of separation and rivalry followed, along with territorial wars against younger races.\n\nThese struggles wore down troll dominion. Most surviving troll kingdoms now meet other races with fierce hostility, clinging to the ruins of their former greatness. The Darkspear, jungle trolls driven into exile, chose another path and joined the Horde with orcs and tauren.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can trolls really regenerate lost limbs?",a="Yes. Trolls heal physical wounds faster than most other mortal races. Given time, they can regrow lost fingers and even entire limbs.",al={"troll healing","troll limb regrowth","how do trolls heal"}},{q="What are loa?",a="Loa are primal deities worshipped by trollkind across nearly every tribe. Many take the form of powerful animal spirits, honored with offerings, meditation, and ritual magic. Priests and shadow hunters call on them for blessings, guidance, and strength in battle.",al={"who are loa","troll gods","what do trolls worship"}},{q="Why are most trolls hostile to players?",a="Many troll tribes, including the Amani forest trolls and Gurubashi jungle trolls, keep insular traditions and deep hostility toward outsiders. Long conflict with encroaching races has made them fiercely protective of their ancestral lands, and they attack trespassers on sight.",al={"why are trolls bad","hostile trolls","evil trolls"}},{q="How did the Darkspear join the Horde?",a="The Darkspear jungle trolls were driven from their ancestral lands and trapped on an island under attack by murlocs and sea witches. Warchief Thrall and his orc fleet rescued them from annihilation. Their chieftain pledged the tribe's loyalty to the newly formed Horde, out of gratitude and shared need.",al={"why are trolls horde","darkspear horde origin","thrall and trolls"}},{q="What is voodoo?",a="Voodoo is an ancient practice of spiritual and dark magic used by troll witch doctors, shadow hunters, and priests. It joins communion with ancestors and loa worship with curses, hexes, and potent herbal brews to harm foes and strengthen allies.",al={"troll voodoo","how does voodoo work","witch doctor magic"}},{q="Which classes can trolls be?",a="Trolls train as warriors, hunters, rogues, priests, shaman, mages, and warlocks.",al={"troll classes","what classes can trolls be","can trolls be warlocks"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Your heritage reaches back further than almost any civilization on Azeroth. While your cousins in Zul'Gurub and Zul'Aman hold to bitter, isolationist pride, the Darkspear carry their legacy forward through the strength of the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="The Darkspear trolls bring cunning, agility, and spiritual strength to the warchief's banner as scouts, shadow hunters, and shamans.",["race:NightElf"]="Elven history and ancient myths trace bitter rivalries to troll kingdoms. Elves regard troll voodoo and sacrificial rites with deep wariness.",["class:Priest"]="Troll priests are bound to the loa and shadow hunting. They commune with animal spirits and primal dark forces instead of the Holy Light."},kw={"amani","aqir","darkspear","gurubashi","loa","regeneration","troll","trolls","voodoo","zandalari"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:vol-jin","topic:horde","topic:old-god","topic:alliance","topic:titan"},src={"Troll"}}
E["topic:twilight-s-hammer"] = {t="topic",n="Twilight's Hammer",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Twilight's Hammer works in secret to bring Azeroth to its end. Its creed calls for the Old Gods to awaken and all things to end.",h="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Twilight's Hammer works in secret to bring Azeroth to its end.",sec={{t="Origins in Shadow",b="On Draenor, Twilight's Hammer began as an orc clan of the Old Horde. Two-headed ogre-mage Cho'gall led the clan and served as one of Gul'dan's chief lieutenants in the Shadow Council. Under Cho'gall, its members embraced a grim creed that looked toward the end of all things. They came to see the Horde as a force of destruction for that purpose.",sp=0},{t="Arrival on Azeroth",b="Twilight's Hammer crossed the Dark Portal during the First War, and its apocalyptic zeal deepened on Azeroth. Its cultists heard the true whispers of the Old Gods, ancient horrors chained beneath the earth. Blackhand tolerated their erratic rituals because Cho'gall kept their bloodlust in check. He sent them with Kilrogg Deadeye's Bleeding Hollow clan in early assaults on Stormwind Keep.\n\nDuring the Second War, the clan worked deep inside Grim Batol, overseeing critical refineries until Gul'dan's betrayal fractured the Horde. Orgrim Doomhammer ordered the traitorous clan slaughtered near the Tomb of Sargeras. A core of zealots survived.",sp=0},{t="A Spreading Cancer",b="On Kalimdor's forgotten shores, Twilight's Hammer grew from a broken orc clan into a secret, multiracial conspiracy. It draws disillusioned members from both the Alliance and the Horde, recruiting any soul broken enough to welcome oblivion. In northern Kalimdor, Twilight Lord Kelris leads cultists entrenched in the submerged halls of Blackfathom Deeps. There they feed sacrifices to Aku'mai, a monstrous servant of an Old God.\n\nFarther north in Darkshore, their excavators disturb the colossal fossilized remains at the Master's Glaive. In Silithus's southern deserts, robed fanatics tend abyssal windstones and listen for ancient horrors stirring beneath the sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Twilight's Hammer trying to achieve?",a="They seek to end all life and order on Azeroth. The cult calls oblivion a sacred blessing, not a path to conquest or wealth. It works to free the ancient Old Gods chained beneath the world.",al={"what do cultists want","twilights hammer goal","twilight hammer purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Are they an orc clan or a cult?",a="They began on Draenor as an orc clan led by Cho'gall. After fleeing the Second War, they left clan boundaries behind and became a secret, multiracial cult. They recruit humans, night elves, dwarves, and anyone willing to worship the Void.",al={"are they orcs","is twilights hammer a clan","twilights hammer races"},it="identity"},{q="Who leads the Twilight's Hammer?",a="Cho'gall founded and oversaw the cult. He is a cunning, two-headed ogre-mage and former apprentice of Gul'dan. Regional commanders lead local chapters, including Twilight Lord Kelris in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who is twilight hammer boss","twilights hammer leader","cho'gall"},it="leader"},{q="Why are they in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris leads cultists occupying a sunken night elven temple along the Zoram Strand. They worship Aku'mai and feed sacrificial victims to the primordial three-headed hydra, a servant of an Old God.",al={"blackfathom cultists","kelris bfd","what are they doing in ashenvale"},it="place"},{q="What are they doing at the Master's Glaive in Darkshore?",a="The Master's Glaive is a massive glaive embedded in a colossal creature's skull. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says an old, old lord of the earth fell there. Cultists gather to commune with lingering dark energies and seek signs of their masters' awakening.",al={"masters glaive cultists","darkshore twilight hammer"},it="place"},{q="Why did Orgrim Doomhammer try to wipe them out?",a="During the Second War, Cho'gall and Gul'dan abandoned the Horde's march on Lordaeron to seek godhood at the Tomb of Sargeras. Their treachery cost the Horde its victory. Warchief Doomhammer sent loyal troops to slaughter the clans that had defected.",al={"doomhammer twilights hammer","second war betrayal"},it="history"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer hostile to outsiders?",a="The Twilight's Hammer serves the Old Gods, seeking the utter annihilation of Azeroth. They view all outside civilizations—Alliance, Horde, and neutral alike—as obstacles to their apocalyptic grand design. Anyone not pledged to their nihilistic cause is an enemy to be eliminated or sacrificed in their dark rituals.",al={"why is twilight's hammer hostile","twilight hammer attack on sight","why do cultists attack me"},it="hostile",add="4ab30bd1"},{q="Who are the Twilight's Hammer working for?",a="Their true masters are the Old Gods, ancient beings of void and shadow imprisoned deep beneath Azeroth. The cult works to shatter those prisons, awakening entities like C'Thun in Silithus. They also revere the servants of these dark masters, such as the hydra Aku'mai in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who do twilight hammer serve","twilight hammer masters","who are twilight hammer allied with"},it="allies",add="301a24e8"},{q="Where did the Twilight's Hammer clan originate?",a="They began on Draenor as an orc clan of the Old Horde, led by the two-headed ogre-mage Cho'gall, one of Gul'dan's chief lieutenants. Under him the clan embraced an apocalyptic creed, and it crossed through the Dark Portal into Azeroth with the rest of the Horde.",al={"twilight hammer origin","where did twilight hammer come from","history of twilight's hammer"},it="history",add="23bd082e"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer called that?",a="The name dates back to the clan's days in the Old Horde under Cho'gall. Its origin is not recorded, but it fits a creed bent on bringing the world to its end.",al={"why are they called twilight's hammer","twilight hammer name meaning","origin of twilight hammer name"},it="name",add="74c580c8"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you draw on the same Void and shadow magic that Twilight's Hammer manipulates. The cult warns what can happen when communion with the whispers overwhelms mortal sanity.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you share the cult's past ties to Gul'dan's Shadow Council. Twilight's Hammer abandoned demonic fel mastery for the Old Gods' primordial madness, making its followers unpredictable rivals rather than allies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you inherit a shameful relic of the Old Horde's darkest days. Thrall's new Horde rejects the cult's madness and executes zealots who try to draw young orcs back into nihilism.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see alien cultists defile sacred sites in northern Kalimdor, including Blackfathom Deeps and the Master's Glaive. Their presence assaults those lands in spirit and body."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","cho'gall","kelris","master's glaive","old gods","silithus","twilight's hammer","void"},rel={"npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","subzone:master-s-glaive","zone:blackfathom","topic:old-god","zone:silithus","topic:shadow-council","npc:orgrim-doomhammer"},src={"Twilight's Hammer"}}
E["topic:varian-wrynn"] = {t="topic",n="Varian Wrynn",z="multi",s="Across the Great Sea, Varian Wrynn has vanished on the voyage to Theramore. His ten-year-old son Anduin wears Stormwind's crown under the guidance of Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and Lady Katrana Prestor.",h="Across the Great Sea, Varian Wrynn has vanished on the voyage to Theramore.",sec={{t="A Boyhood in Ash",b="Varian's boyhood ended when the First War shattered his life. He watched Garona Halforcen, the assassin, kill King Llane Wrynn as the Old Horde stormed the capital. Anduin Lothar rescued the orphaned prince and fled north with the kingdom's survivors to Southshore.\n\nIn Capital City, King Terenas Menethil II took Varian in like a second son. The young prince grew up in exile beside Prince Arthas Menethil, carrying the memory of his burned home. Then the Alliance of Lordaeron broke the Horde and reclaimed Stormwind.",sp=0},{t="A Troubled Restoration",b="At eighteen, Varian took the crown and faced the immense task of rebuilding his ruined kingdom. He hired Edwin VanCleef and the Stonemasons Guild to restore the capital. When the great work was done, the corrupt House of Nobles refused to pay the promised wages.\n\nThe stonemasons would not back down, and Varian could not settle the dispute between the entrenched nobility and the furious artisans. Soon, violence filled Stormwind's streets.",sp=0},{t="The Vanished King",b="Varian recently sailed from Stormwind toward Theramore Isle for peace talks arranged by Lady Jaina Proudmoore. He sought to ease tensions across the sea, but never reached the summit. During the crossing, the king vanished without a trace.\n\nStormwind is left vulnerable. Whispers of conspiracy spread through the court, and Highlord Bolvar holds the regency.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is King Varian right now?",a="No one in Stormwind knows where Varian is. He vanished while sailing across the Great Sea to Theramore for secret diplomatic talks.",al={"where is varian","where did the king go","is varian alive","varian location"},it="place"},{q="Who is currently ruling Stormwind in his place?",a="Anduin Wrynn, Varian's ten-year-old son, holds the throne as child-king. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon carries the real administrative and military authority as regent, heavily influenced by royal counselor Lady Katrana Prestor.",al={"who rules stormwind","who is king now","stormwind leader"},it="in_charge"},{q="What troubled Varian's rebuilding of Stormwind?",a="When the Stonemasons Guild finished rebuilding Stormwind, the House of Nobles refused to pay the promised wages. Their dispute erupted into violent riots in the city's streets, and the exiled masons later became the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"varian stonemasons","stonemason riots varian","varian and the nobles"},sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="Why was Varian going to Theramore?",a="Varian was traveling to Theramore Isle at Lady Jaina Proudmoore's invitation for a high-level diplomatic summit. The talks aimed to ease hostilities between the Alliance and Thrall's Horde.",al={"why did varian leave","theramore summit","varian peace talks"},it="purpose"},{q="How did Varian escape the First War?",a="After King Llane was assassinated and the Horde burned Stormwind, High Commander Anduin Lothar evacuated Prince Varian and the remaining civilian survivors by sea. They sailed north to Lordaeron, where King Terenas Menethil II took the young prince into his court.",al={"varian first war","young varian","fall of stormwind varian"},it="history"},{q="What was Varian's relationship with Arthas Menethil?",a="Varian and Arthas Menethil grew up as close companions and rivals in Lordaeron while Varian lived in exile. The two princes often sparred together. Arthas's descent into madness, the murder of his father Terenas, and his betrayal of Lordaeron turned their past friendship to bitter hatred.",al={"did varian know arthas","varian and arthas","were arthas and varian friends"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Varian Wrynn?",a="King Varian Wrynn is the rightful ruler of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the heir of the House of Wrynn. As a boy, he witnessed the fall of his kingdom and the assassination of his father, King Llane, during the First War. Exiled to Lordaeron, he returned years later after the Alliance reclaimed his homeland, taking the throne at eighteen to rebuild Stormwind. Recently, however, the king vanished under mysterious circumstances while traveling on a diplomatic voyage, leaving the kingdom in turmoil.",al={"who is varian","king varian","king of stormwind","who is king wrynn"},it="identity",add="4f50c804"},{q="Who are Varian Wrynn's allies?",a="Varian stands at the heart of the Grand Alliance. His closest counselors and protectors include Highlord Bolvar Fordragon, who rules as regent during his absence, and the royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor. His greatest historical bonds lie with the kingdoms of the Alliance of Lordaeron, fostered by King Terenas Menethil II, who fostered young Varian after Stormwind's fall. As Stormwind's king, he commands its armies and knights.",al={"varian allies","who does varian work with","varian wrynn faction"},it="allies",add="4a21f8ea"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you remember Varian as King Llane's beloved son, returned from exile to rebuild your home. His sudden disappearance casts dread over the realm.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know King Varian trained with veteran knights and endured the horrors of the First War. Across the Alliance, he is admired as a formidable warrior and fierce martial leader.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face a political vacuum with Varian absent. His absence emboldens dissidents and threatens border security from Westfall to Redridge."},kw={"anduin","king","missing","stonemasons","stormwind","theramore","varian","wrynn"},rel={"zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:anduin-lothar","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:terenas-menethil-ii"},src={"Varian Wrynn"}}
E["topic:venture-company"] = {t="topic",n="Venture Company",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Venture Company crews strip-mine and clear-cut land, heedless of its people and nature. Mogul Razdunk directs the ruthless goblin cartel from afar. Its crews seek raw materials with heavy machinery, away from major goblin ports like Booty Bay and Ratchet.",h="Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, Venture Company crews strip-mine and clear-cut land, heedless of...",sec={{t="Industrial Plunder",b="Venture Company crews tear into the land for raw materials. Mogul Razdunk directs the cartel from afar, and workers wield heavy machinery across Azeroth. Shredders harvest timber, drilling rigs bore into the earth, and refineries process what they find. The cartel takes resources by force, ignoring treaties, borders, and local rights.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching on Kalimdor",b="Across Kalimdor, Venture Company crews have made enemies. In Mulgore, Supervisor Fizsprocket sent drills and mining rigs into the eastern bluffs, though the tauren had denied the cartel mineral rights. The work polluted water wells across the plains. Farther north, the cartel turned the Barrens' Sludge Fen into a chemical sewer for its oil pumps. It also claimed the Horde's former Boulder Lode Mine, where it conducted dangerous experiments with samophlanges and toxic brews.\n\nAt Windshear Crag in Stonetalon, Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle directs the logging crews. The mad leper gnome's colossal Super Reaper 6000 machines have felled whole groves.",sp=1},{t="Corporate Rivalries and Shady Contracts",b="Venture Company has angered fellow goblins and made other enemies. Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay often hires crews to strike the cartel's base camp and oil rig at Lake Nazferiti. He means to halt their encroachment and take their advanced shredder fuel regulators. Ratchet's Tinkers' Union spies on the cartel to steal engineering plans.\n\nSI:7 and the Shattered Hand have uncovered the cartel's trade in dangerous alchemical compounds. It sells Zanzil's mind-altering poisons to Defias necromancers in Westfall. Toxic fumes also help it breed mutated drone laborers.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who leads the Venture Company?",a="Mogul Razdunk leads Venture Company from afar and directs its larger ventures. Regional supervisors, foremen, and hired overseers run work sites across Azeroth. They include Supervisor Fizsprocket in Mulgore, Supervisor Lugwizzle at the Sludge Fen, and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle in Stonetalon.",al={"venture co leader","venture company boss","who runs venture co","mogul razdunk"},it="leader"},{q="Why does the Horde hate the Venture Company?",a="The Horde hates Venture Company for exploiting lands it considers ancestral. In Mulgore, the cartel entered the eastern mountains without permission and fouled the tauren's sacred water wells. In the Barrens, it seized the Horde's Boulder Lode Mine and fouled the Sludge Fen with a noxious oil slick.",al={"tauren venture co","why horde hate venture co","mulgore venture company"},it="conflict"},{q="Are they affiliated with the Steamwheedle Cartel or Booty Bay?",a="No. Venture Company is separate from the Steamwheedle Cartel, and the two are fierce corporate enemies. Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay often hires mercenaries to disrupt its logging in Stranglethorn Vale. Sputtervalve of Ratchet sends operatives to sabotage its shredders and steal its blueprints.",al={"are they steamwheedle","venture co booty bay","ratchet venture co"},it="ties"},{q="Why is a leper gnome running operations in Windshear Crag?",a="Venture Company hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle for his ruthless mechanical skill and his design of the massive Super Reaper 6000. His hiring angered goblin engineers such as Ziz Fizziks and the Trade Princes in Undermine. They disapproved of Razdunk dealing with the outcast gnome.",al={"gerenzo wrenchwhistle","gnome in stonetalon","why leper gnome venture"}},{q="What is the Venture Company doing in Westfall?",a="Venture Company traded illicitly with the Defias Brotherhood. The cartel acquired Zanzilli poisons and sold the mixture to Defias operative Klaven Mortwake in Westfall. He used it to make mindless Defias Drones like the laborers found at Venture Company sites.",al={"venture co westfall","klaven mortwake venture co","venture defias"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="What is being produced at the Sludge Fen?",a="Venture Company built an industrial drilling rig over a spring that was once clear. It pumps and refines oil while dumping toxic sludge across the northern Barrens. Researchers there also test complex mechanical samophlanges and synthesize toxic mixtures.",al={"sludge fen oil","barrens venture co oil rig","samophlange sludge fen"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Venture Company?",a="The Venture Company is a ruthless, goblin-run cartel dedicated to plundering Azeroth's natural resources for maximum profit. Specializing in heavy machinery, mining, and clear-cutting, their philosophy is simple: if you can dig it up, chop it down, or blow it out of a mountain, they will. They operate entirely outside local laws and traditional ethics, using shredders, drills, and armed enforcers to extract wealth from wilderness frontiers.",al={"who are venture co","what is venture company","venture co lore"},it="identity",add="f7d6a0aa"},{q="Why is the Venture Company hostile to travelers?",a="The Venture Company operates illegal, aggressive resource grabs across contested and sovereign lands, from the sacred hills of Mulgore to the forests of Stonetalon. Because they routinely trespass, steal claims, and cut out competitors, their operations are heavily fortified. Their foremen view any outsider as an industrial spy, a rival claimant, or a vengeful local come to sabotage their machinery, and they instruct their enforcers to shoot first.",al={"why does venture co attack","venture company aggro","why is venture company hostile"},it="hostile",add="36300444"},{q="Who are the Venture Company allied with?",a="The Venture Company primarily works for its own profit, but it frequently cuts shady deals with outside factions when coin is on the table. They have established under-the-table trade with the Defias Brotherhood, selling them Zanzil-derived alchemical mixtures and toxic concoctions. Aside from such mercenary transactions, they maintain few friends, routinely stepping on the toes of neutral cartels like the Steamwheedle Cartel and drawing outrage from the trade princes in Undermine.",al={"venture co allies","who does venture company work with","venture co partnerships"},it="allies",add="48d27ccb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know Venture Company invaded Mulgore's sacred hills without permission. Its crews poisoned ancestral wells and cut timber against the Earth Mother's will.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the harm in Venture Company's heavy logging in Stonetalon and its pollution of natural springs in Mulgore and the Barrens.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the Shattered Hand and SI:7 watch Venture Company's poison trade closely. Their agents infiltrate its towers and sabotage high-ranking foremen to seize deadly chemical mixtures.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know Venture Company builds some of Azeroth's finest shredders and mechanical regulators. Other companies prize its blueprints and seek to steal them."},kw={"fizsprocket","gerenzo","puzik gallywix","razdunk","samophlange","shredder","sludge fen","super reaper","venture co","venture company","windshear crag"},rel={"zone:stonetalon","zone:barrens","zone:mulgore","zone:stranglethorn","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:goblin","quest:764","quest:1093"},src={"Venture Company"}}
E["topic:war-of-the-ancients"] = {t="topic",n="War of the Ancients",z="general",s="As Queen Azshara and her Highborne opened the Well of Eternity, the Burning Legion entered Azeroth. Malfurion Stormrage, Illidan, and Tyrande Whisperwind led the resistance that drove the demons back. The Well's destruction brought the Great Sundering, breaking ancient Kalimdor and changing the world.",h="As Queen Azshara and her Highborne opened the Well of Eternity, the Burning Legion entered Azeroth.",sec={{t="The Highborne's Folly",b="At the height of the ancient Kaldorei Empire, Queen Azshara and her Highborne sorcerers drew deeply on the Well of Eternity's arcane power. Their spells reached into the Great Dark Beyond and caught the notice of Sargeras, master of the Burning Legion. He promised power and perfection. Then Azshara and her advisor Xavius opened a rift within the Well.\n\nFelHounds, felguard, doomguard, and monstrous commanders poured into Zin-Azshari. They slaughtered those who were not Highborne and began a crusade to purge the world of life.",sp=0},{t="The Kaldorei Resistance",b="Night elves beyond the Highborne caste rose against the slaughter. Three remarkable leaders gathered the resistance: Malfurion Stormrage, the first mortal druid; Tyrande Whisperwind, a devoted priestess of Elune; and Illidan, Malfurion's gifted brother. Together, they brought common night elves to a desperate frontline against the Legion's onslaught.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Victory",b="The war grew to world-shattering proportions when Cenarius rallied the ancient Wild Gods and dragonflights to the fight. To keep Sargeras from setting foot on Azeroth, Malfurion and the resistance tried to collapse the portal over the Well of Eternity. Their desperate gambit cast the demonic host back into the Twisting Nether, but the strain proved too great.\n\nThe Well violently imploded and triggered the Great Sundering. Kalimdor broke into separate continents, the world's center flooded to form the Great Sea, and Kaldorei culture changed forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What caused the War of the Ancients?",a="Queen Azshara and her Highborne sorcerers drew on the Well of Eternity's arcane power. Their spells reached across the cosmos and drew the dark titan Sargeras. He persuaded the Highborne to open a gateway in the Well so the Burning Legion could enter Azeroth.",al={"why did the war start","who caused the war of the ancients","well of eternity portal"},it="origin"},{q="What was the Great Sundering?",a="The Great Sundering was the cataclysm that ended the war. To keep Sargeras from entering the world, the resistance collapsed the portal inside the Well of Eternity. The Well imploded, tearing Kalimdor's single supercontinent into separate landmasses and forming the Great Sea.",al={"what is the sundering","how did kalimdor break","well of eternity explosion"},it="conflict"},{q="Who led the mortal forces against the Legion?",a="Malfurion Stormrage, his brother Illidan, and the priestess Tyrande Whisperwind rallied the night elves against Azshara and the Legion. The demigod Cenarius brought the ancient spirits of the wild to their side.",al={"who led the resistance","kaldorei resistance leaders"},it="leader"},{q="Did other races fight alongside the night elves?",a="Yes. The great dragonflights joined the struggle, and Cenarius led his wild brethren into battle beside the night elves against the demonic invasion.",al={"tauren in war of the ancients","who helped the night elves"},it="allies"},{q="What happened to Queen Azshara during the war?",a="Queen Azshara stayed in her palace at Zin-Azshari until the bitter end, obsessed with bringing Sargeras into Azeroth. When the Well imploded and the oceans swallowed the capital, the queen and her surviving Highborne loyalists sank into the churning depths.",al={"where is azshara","did queen azshara die"}},{q="Why is arcane magic mistrusted by night elves today?",a="The Kaldorei saw the Highborne's unchecked hunger for arcane magic summon the Burning Legion and destroy ancient Kalimdor. Afterward, the night elves outlawed arcane sorcery and turned to druidism and faith in Elune to protect their lands.",al={"why do night elves hate mages","kaldorei magic ban"},it="today"},{q="What was the War of the Ancients?",a="The War of the Ancients was Azeroth's first major war against the demonic Burning Legion, fought roughly ten thousand years ago. Corrupted by promises of godlike power, Queen Azshara and her Highborne cast spells through the Well of Eternity to bring Sargeras and his demonic legions into the world. The night elf resistance, joined by early mortal races, the dragonflights, and the Wild Gods, fought desperately to halt the invasion, culminating in the destruction of the Well and the Great Sundering.",al={"what is war of the ancients","war of the ancients explained","first legion invasion"},it="identity",add="c481acb5"},{q="Why is it called the War of the Ancients?",a="The conflict earned its name both from the ancient era in which it took place—ten millennia before the modern age—and the pivotal role played by the Ancients themselves. Demigods and Wild Gods like Cenarius, alongside the ancient dragonflights, marched to war alongside mortal defenders to save Azeroth from demonic annihilation.",al={"why called war of the ancients","name war of the ancients meaning","war of the ancients name"},it="name",add="9e83d11f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the war behind your people's deep mistrust of arcane magic, reverence for Cenarius, and enduring leadership under Malfurion and Tyrande.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you inherit a path born in this conflict. Malfurion Stormrage learned the ways of the wild from Cenarius and showed that nature's power could defeat cosmic ruin.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the Highborne's reckless arrogance is a warning across Azeroth about the dangers of unchecked arcane power.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can honor Cenarius and the demigods of the wild. Their forest spirits fought the Legion beside the night elves ten thousand years ago.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you follow a tradition shaped by Tyrande Whisperwind. Her mastery of Elune's grace brought the Priesthood of the Moon to the heart of night elven military and civic leadership."},kw={"azshara","burning legion","cenarius","highborne","malfurion","sargeras","sundering","tyrande","war of the ancients","well of eternity"},rel={"topic:burning-legion","npc:malfurion-stormrage","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:cenarius","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf","topic:sargeras","zone:azshara"},src={"War of the Ancients"}}
E["topic:warlock"] = {t="topic",n="Warlock",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Warlocks wield forbidden powers that bring fear and distrust. They command demons and cast curses, fire, and shadow magic. Some turn these arts against the Burning Legion and its servants.",h="Across Azeroth, Warlocks wield forbidden powers that bring fear and distrust.",sec={{t="Forbidden Arts",b="Where ordinary spellcasters see ruin, warlocks see a path to victory. They strike from afar with shadow and fire, and drain the vital essence and souls of their enemies to fuel their fiercest rites. Brimstone falls from the sky, and agonizing curses break the mind.\n\nWarlocks wear simple cloth and have little strength to withstand a blow. They call horrors to meet danger and sacrifice demonic thralls to preserve their own lives.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Servitude",b="A warlock's hold over the Twisting Nether begins with small bargains and grows into iron dominion. Novices command mischievous imps to hurl flame. With deeper knowledge of fel magic, they bind voidwalkers from shadowy depths to bear physical punishment, succubi who beguile enemy minds, and ravenous felhunters that devour magical energy.\n\nEach summon demands dangerous focus. The Nether's denizens are ever testing their masters for weakness.",sp=0},{t="A Legacy of Ruin",b="Orcish demonology began on Draenor, where Kil'jaeden, a demon lord, tempted Gul'dan with the promise of supreme power. Gul'dan founded the secretive Shadow Council and turned many shaman into masters of fel magic. Demonic magic withered Draenor's fertile plains into a barren red wasteland, and the Old Horde invaded through the Dark Portal.\n\nAmong humans, the Kirin Tor forbade demonology and hunted illicit summonings. Yet ambitious mages still fell to the lure of untamed sorcery.",sp=0},{t="Tolerated Pariahs",b="Warlocks now walk a narrow path between usefulness and execution. In Stormwind, they meet in hidden, gloomy tavern basements, away from the Cathedral of Light's watchful eyes. In Orgrimmar, they gather in the shadowed chasms of the Cleft of Shadow, watched by Thrall's shamanistic regime.\n\nTheir methods inspire revulsion, yet neither the Alliance nor the Horde can dismiss the edge warlock magic brings to a hostile battlefield.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes a warlock different from a mage?",a="Mages use the ordered structure of arcane magic to shape fire, frost, and energy. Warlocks cross its safe bounds for chaotic fel magic, shadow, and demons. Many began as mages, then grew impatient with academic limits and sought forbidden shortcuts to power.",al={"warlock vs mage","difference between warlock and mage","mage or warlock"}},{q="Are all warlocks evil?",a="Not every warlock is wicked, though warlock magic is dangerous and corruptive. Many fall into madness or join demonic cults. Others pledge loyalty to their faction and wield dark sorcery, stolen souls, and bound demons against threats such as the Scourge and the Burning Legion.",al={"are warlocks evil","can warlocks be good","why does the alliance allow warlocks"}},{q="How do warlocks summon and control demons?",a="Warlocks draw creatures from the Twisting Nether with ritual circles, dark incantations, and soul energy. They must break each demon's will and bind it through sheer mental dominance. If their focus slips, the demon may slaughter its master.",al={"how do warlock pets work","demonic summoning lore","binding demons"}},{q="Where did orc warlocks come from?",a="Orc warlocks began on Draenor, when Kil'jaeden turned Gul'dan from shamanism to demonic sorcery. Gul'dan formed the Shadow Council and trained other orcs. Fel corruption spread across their homeland until Draenor's soil withered and died.",al={"how did orcs become warlocks","gul'dan warlocks","orc fel magic origin"}},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde tolerate warlocks in their cities?",a="Neither faction trusts warlocks. In Stormwind and Ironforge, they practice in secret basements and forgotten tunnels to avoid public outrage. In Orgrimmar, they are kept in the Cleft of Shadow. Leaders tolerate them because their curses and summons are effective weapons in wartime.",al={"why are warlocks allowed","are warlocks legal","warlock legality"}},{q="What are soul shards used for?",a="Warlocks drain the living essence of defeated enemies to make crystallized soul shards. These fragments hold the raw power to bypass natural magical laws, summon monstrous demons, and cast their most destructive spells.",al={"why do warlocks take souls","soul shard lore","harvesting souls"}},{q="Which races can be warlocks?",a="Humans and gnomes practice as warlocks in the Alliance. In the Horde, orcs, trolls, and the Forsaken do. Dwarves, night elves, tauren, and the Skyborne do not. Wherever they live, warlocks are tolerated rather than trusted.",al={"who can be a warlock","warlock races","can trolls be warlocks","troll warlock"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may view warlocks with contempt and fear. Their dealings with the Nether seem undisciplined and put all mortal life at risk.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you remember how Gul'dan's fel sorcery severed your ancestors' ties to the spirits and killed Draenor's land. That is why shaman despise warlock magic above all else.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you bear the bitter stain of the Old Horde's blood curse when you practice demonology. Some orcs keep these arts to survive in a hostile world.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you consider demonic summoning an abominable heresy. You watch warlocks who practice it with open hostility.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you begin warlock training beside orc initiates in the Valley of Trials. Thrall's Horde watches every wielder of fel magic with the same wariness."},kw={"affliction","demonology","destruction","fel","felhunter","gul'dan","imp","shadow council","succubus","twisting nether","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"topic:burning-legion","topic:shadow-council","topic:first-war","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:mage","topic:shaman"},src={"Warlock"}}
E["topic:warrior"] = {t="topic",n="Warrior",z="general",s="Across Azeroth, Warriors take their place at the front with steel, discipline, and battle rage. They wear heavy plate and wield many weapons, shielding allies or breaking enemy ranks. Every race and civilization has its Warriors, from city guards and royal champions to wandering mercenaries.",h="Across Azeroth, Warriors take their place at the front with steel, discipline, and battle rage.",sec={{t="Masters of Steel and Shield",b="Warriors rely on strength, discipline, and skill with weapons, not prayers or spells. Heavy plate helps them hold the front. Some brace behind tall shields, enduring blows and drawing danger away from spellcasters and archers. Others carry two-handed polearms, axes, or greatswords. Some fight with a blade in each hand and cut through enemy ranks.",sp=0},{t="The Power of Battle Rage",b="In battle, pain and blood kindle a Warrior's rage. It grows as Warriors strike foes and endure their attacks. Skilled fighters shape that force into crushing blows and sweeping weapon strikes. Their battle cries hearten nearby allies and break enemy morale.",sp=0},{t="A Universal Tradition",b="Every race on Azeroth has its Warriors. Stormwind fields disciplined knights and footmen, while Ironforge calls on its stout mountain guard. The Horde rallies around orcish blademasters, tauren braves, and Forsaken Deathguards.\n\nHonor, defense of their lands, or the promise of coin can lead Warriors to arms. They form the backbone of every standing army.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What powers a warrior if they do not use magic?",a="Warriors draw strength from martial skill, training, and rage. They build rage by striking foes and taking blows, then unleash it in sweeping attacks, shield strikes, and fierce shouts.",al={"how do warriors fight","warrior resource","what is rage"},it="power"},{q="What races can become warriors?",a="Every race in Azeroth can become a Warrior. All mortal cultures need armored fighters at the front, from the dwarven defenders of Khaz Modan to the orcish shock troops of Durotar.",al={"who can be warrior","warrior races","can every race be warrior"},it="people"},{q="What role do warriors serve in a combat party?",a="Warriors usually fight at the front. Those who favor protection use plate and shields to endure attacks and keep dangerous foes focused on them. Those who favor arms or fury wield heavy two-handed weapons or paired blades to overwhelm enemies with physical force.",al={"warrior role","do warriors tank","arms vs fury vs prot"},it="purpose"},{q="What weapons are warriors able to wield?",a="Warriors wield almost every weapon used in mortal warfare: swords, maces, axes, polearms, daggers, and staves, either one-handed or two-handed. They also carry heavy shields and use bows, guns, and crossbows.",al={"warrior weapons","can warriors use bows","what can warriors equip"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who are some famous warriors in Azeroth's history?",a="Renowned Warriors include Lord Anduin Lothar, Champion of Stormwind and Supreme Commander of the Alliance of Lordaeron; Grommash Hellscream, chieftain of the Warsong clan; and Cairne Bloodhoof, High Chieftain of the united tauren tribes.",al={"famous warriors","legendary warriors","who are warrior heroes"},it="fame"},{q="Where do new warriors receive their formal training?",a="Warriors train wherever soldiers gather. Human recruits drill in Northshire Abbey; dwarves and gnomes learn at Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley; and night elves train in Shadowglen. Orcs and trolls practice in the Valley of Trials, Forsaken fighters report to the Deathknell barracks, and the Skyborne begin on Zephras Isle.",al={"warrior trainers","where do warriors learn","warrior trainer locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a warrior?",a="Warriors are the quintessential frontline combatants of Azeroth, relying on sheer physical prowess, mastery of arms, and heavy armor rather than mystical arts. They come from every culture and background, serving as stalwart city guards, fearsome berserkers, mercenary soldiers, and seasoned commanders. Equipped with shields and a vast array of weaponry, warriors charge directly into the fray to draw the enemy's wrath and shield their more fragile companions from harm.",al={"what is a warrior in lore","warrior lore identity","who are warriors"},it="identity",add="2a49f247",nx={8}},{q="What does it mean to walk the path of a warrior?",a="Choosing the warrior's life means dedicating yourself to constant training, discipline, and uncompromising martial perfection. You step onto the battlefield without spells to shield you, putting your faith entirely in heavy plate, your chosen steel, and your instincts. Whether seeking glory, fortune as a mercenary, or defending your people from looming perils, you are the living wall that meets danger head-on, turning raw combat fury into decisive strikes.",al={"becoming a warrior","what does it mean to be a warrior","life of a warrior"},it="for_you",add="2e549509"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Every battle tests your stamina and nerve. Turn the pain of incoming blows into rage, and you can hold the front line.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a Warrior, you rely on blacksmiths for heavy plate, sturdy bucklers, and keen blades to help you survive combat.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance Warrior, you join the footmen and knights who defend human kingdoms, dwarven mountain holds, and elven forests.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde Warrior, you join a martial way of life, where grunt shock troops and tauren fighters lead each territorial advance."},kw={"arms","berserker","fury","melee","plate","protection","rage","shield","vanguard","warrior"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:tauren","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","subzone:anvilmar"},src={"Warrior"}}
E["topic:warsong-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Warsong clan",z="general",s="Across Kalimdor, the Warsong clan cuts timber for the young Horde. Once led by the revered chieftain Grommash Hellscream, the clan endured exile, internment camps, and demonic corruption. Now its Outriders work chiefly in Ashenvale, where they clash ceaselessly with the night elves.",h="Across Kalimdor, the Warsong clan cuts timber for the young Horde.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Defiance",b="On Draenor's open plains, the Warsong earned their name through swift attacks by wolf riders. After the Horde fell, the clan evaded capture while other orcs languished in Alliance internment camps. The Warsong wandered the wilderness and kept to their warlike ways. At last, Thrall united with Hellscream, and together they forged the New Horde.",sp=0},{t="Blood and Redemption",b="During the Third War, the Warsong reached Kalimdor. Thrall sent Hellscream and his clan into Ashenvale to cut timber and build an outpost. Their intrusion enraged the night elves and the forest demigod Cenarius. Facing slaughter, the Warsong drank once more from Mannoroth's demonic blood and killed Cenarius in a frenzy of fel corruption.\n\nThrall and his allies purged Hellscream of the curse. Grom then gave his life in a fateful fight that destroyed Mannoroth. His sacrifice broke the demon blood curse forever and secured the Warsong's place in Horde history.",sp=0},{t="The War for Ashenvale",b="Today, the Warsong Outriders carry on Grommash's mission in Ashenvale. From Splintertree Post and logging camps, they cut timber for the young Horde in Durotar's arid wastes. Their presence has brought them into bitter conflict with the night elven Silverwing Sentinels. The Warsong hold Warsong Gulch and keep cutting into the ancient forest despite the endless ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the Warsong clan right now?",a="Since Grommash Hellscream died at the end of the Third War, the Warsong clan has largely joined Thrall's New Horde. In the field, Warsong Outriders in Ashenvale answer to local commanders and ultimately to Warchief Thrall.",al={"warsong leader","who is warsong chief","current warsong chieftain"},it="leader"},{q="Why are the Warsong logging in Ashenvale?",a="The New Horde is based in the arid plains of Durotar and the Barrens, where substantial timber is scarce. The Warsong gather lumber in Ashenvale to build cities such as Orgrimmar, maintain military fortifications, and support the growing Horde.",al={"why harvest ashenvale","warsong lumber","orcs cutting trees ashenvale"},it="why_here"},{q="How did the Warsong kill Cenarius?",a="During the Third War, Cenarius led the night elves in a fierce defense of Ashenvale and drove the Warsong to desperation. The clan drank from a pool tainted with the blood of the pit lord Mannoroth. The blood made them demon-maddened chaos orcs, whose empowered fury overwhelmed and killed Cenarius.",al={"cenarius death","who killed cenarius","warsong vs cenarius"}},{q="How did the Warsong escape the internment camps after the Second War?",a="After the Second War, Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong hid in Lordaeron's remote wilderness and evaded Alliance capture. They waged guerrilla warfare and kept their fighting spirit until Thrall found them.",al={"warsong internment camps","grom evasion","warsong escape"}},{q="What is Warsong Gulch?",a="Warsong Gulch is a canyon valley in southern Ashenvale, where the Warsong Outriders clash with the night elven Silverwing Sentinels. The Outriders fight to protect their lumber operations, while the Sentinels seek to drive the orcs from their sacred woodland.",al={"wsg lore","what is warsong gulch","warsong battlefield"}},{q="Who was Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash 'Grom' Hellscream was the legendary Warsong chieftain and a mentor to Thrall. He was the first orc to drink demon blood on Draenor, but later redeemed himself by slaying Mannoroth and freeing all orcs from demonic bondage. He gave his life in the deed.",al={"who is grom","grom hellscream","grommash"}},{q="What is the Warsong clan?",a="The Warsong clan is a fiercely martial orcish clan renowned for its aggressive nature and mobile wolf riders. Long led by the legendary chieftain Grom Hellscream, the clan now serves as an integral pillar of Thrall's Horde, spearheading logging and military campaigns in the dense forests of Ashenvale.",al={"who are the warsong clan","who are the warsong","warsong clan info"},it="identity",add="ab40120e"},{q="Where did the Warsong clan come from?",a="The Warsong originally hailed from the plains of Draenor, where they earned renown as fierce, mobile wolf riders, and crossed into Azeroth with the Horde under Grom Hellscream. Evading human internment camps after the Second War, they later followed Thrall across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.",al={"warsong clan history","warsong origin","where are the warsong from"},it="history",add="b8b233bd"},{q="Who is the Warsong clan allied with?",a="The Warsong clan is fully pledged to Thrall's New Horde. They fight shoulder-to-shoulder with their fellow orcs, the Darkspear trolls, the tauren of Mulgore, and the newly admitted Forsaken, harvesting vital lumber to supply the Horde's growing settlements across Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"warsong allies","who do the warsong fight for","warsong faction"},it="allies",add="f1dd8797"},{q="Why is the Warsong clan hostile to Alliance travelers?",a="As a central military force of the Horde, the Warsong clan views members of the Alliance as mortal enemies. Their deep-seated hatred is further inflamed in Ashenvale, where night elven Silverwing Sentinels and their allies fiercely contest the clan's aggressive clear-cutting of the sacred ancient woodlands.",al={"why do warsong attack","why are warsong hostile","are warsong enemy"},it="hostile",add="5b3f6a6c"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs, the Warsong carry both their people's deepest shame and greatest redemption. They were the first to drink Mannoroth's blood, and their chieftain died to break the demon's hold over all orcs.",["race:NightElf"]="The night elves hate the Warsong for cutting sacred Ashenvale woodlands and killing the demigod Cenarius.",["faction:Horde"]="The New Horde depends on timber the Warsong Outriders cut in Ashenvale to fortify settlements and expand across Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="To many in the Alliance, the Warsong's relentless aggression shows that peace between the factions remains impossible while their axes swing in Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarius","grommash","hellscream","mannoroth","outriders","splintertree","warsong"},rel={"topic:grommash-hellscream","zone:ashenvale","npc:thrall","topic:cenarius","topic:new-horde","npc:warsong-outrider","subzone:splintertree-post","topic:sentinels"},src={"Warsong clan"}}
E["topic:wildhammer-clan"] = {t="topic",n="Wildhammer clan",z="general",s="In the Hinterlands, the Wildhammer clan holds to its freedom among the wooded peaks. Driven from Grim Batol centuries ago, the dwarves made Aerie Peak their home and learned to ride wild gryphons. They remain friends of the Alliance and stand ready to defend its skies.",h="In the Hinterlands, the Wildhammer clan holds to its freedom among the wooded peaks.",sec={{t="Exile from Grim Batol",b="Before the War of the Three Hammers, the Wildhammers lived near Ironforge. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died, civil war followed, and the victorious Bronzebeards claimed the city. Thane Khardros led his clan north and built a hold within Grim Batol. Soon, the defeated Dark Irons laid siege to it.\n\nKhardros slew the sorceress Modgud, but her dying curse blighted the mountain and left its halls uninhabitable. The Wildhammers refused an invitation to return under Bronzebeard rule. They chose their freedom and traveled north to the forests and rocky crags of the Hinterlands.",sp=0},{t="Riders of the Storm",b="The Wildhammers built Aerie Peak in the highlands of their new home. Unlike their kin beneath the earth, they embraced open skies and living rock, and formed a deep spiritual bond with the native gryphons. In secluded aviaries, they forged enchanted stormhammers and became Azeroth's finest aerial cavalry.\n\nDuring the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer marched toward Quel'Thalas and attacked Aerie Peak. Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar and the Alliance came to the clan's aid. In gratitude, High Thane Kurdran Wildhammer pledged his gryphon riders to the coalition. They fought the Horde's enslaved red dragons above Lordaeron and the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Loyal to the End",b="When the Dark Portal reopened, Kurdran Wildhammer led his riders into Draenor with the Alliance Expedition. He gave up his return to seal the rift, and a colossal statue in Stormwind's Valley of Heroes honors his deed. In Aerie Peak, High Thane Falstad took command.\n\nThe human kingdoms later quarreled and fractured, but the Wildhammers remained loyal partners of King Terenas Menethil II. During the Third War, the Scourge swept across Lordaeron. Wildhammer flyers took to the skies again, fighting to defend allied lands and innocent refugees from the walking dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Wildhammer clan based right now?",a="The Wildhammer clan is based at Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands, north of the Wetlands and the Thandol Span.",al={"wildhammer home","where do wildhammers live","wildhammer location"},it="place"},{q="Why don't the Wildhammers live in Ironforge?",a="The Wildhammers lost the civil war for Ironforge to the Bronzebeards after High King Modimus Anvilmar died. Thane Khardros led the clan north to Grim Batol rather than live under Bronzebeard rule.",al={"why did wildhammer leave ironforge","war of the three hammers wildhammer"},it="why_here"},{q="What happened to their fortress at Grim Batol?",a="The Dark Iron sorceress Modgud besieged Grim Batol during the War of the Three Hammers. Thane Khardros slew her, but her sorcery corrupted the halls and made the mountain uninhabitable, driving the clan to the Hinterlands.",al={"why is grim batol abandoned","grim batol curse","modgud grim batol"},it="ruin"},{q="Who leads the Wildhammer clan today?",a="High Thane Falstad Wildhammer leads the clan from Aerie Peak. He took command after Kurdran Wildhammer joined the Alliance Expedition through the Dark Portal.",al={"wildhammer leader","high thane wildhammer","who rules aerie peak"},it="leader"},{q="How did the Wildhammers join the Alliance?",a="During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer attacked the Hinterlands as he marched toward Quel'Thalas. Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar led the Alliance in defense of Aerie Peak, driving off the Horde and forest trolls. The Wildhammers joined the Alliance of Lordaeron in gratitude for their aid.",al={"why are wildhammers alliance","wildhammer alliance history"},it="allies"},{q="Are the Wildhammer dwarves closely allied with Ironforge?",a="Yes. Though the clans fought during the War of the Three Hammers, they united against the Dark Irons. They built the Valley of Kings in Loch Modan to honor their friendship and have kept a firm alliance ever since.",al={"bronzebeard wildhammer relationship","do ironforge and wildhammer get along"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Wildhammer clan?",a="The Wildhammer clan is one of the three great dwarven peoples of Azeroth, renowned for their close bond with nature, their independence, and their fearless aerial mastery. Unlike their Bronzebeard cousins who prefer subterranean halls, the Wildhammers dwell openly among high peaks and lush forests. Renowned across the world as peerless gryphon riders, they take to the skies wielding mystic, lightning-infused stormhammers to defend their homelands and aid their long-standing allies.",al={"who are the wildhammers","wildhammer clan overview","wildhammer dwarves"},it="identity",add="eadee6c6"},{q="Where did the Wildhammer clan come from?",a="Long ago, the Wildhammers lived in the crags and foothills around Ironforge under High King Modimus Anvilmar. Following his death, the civil strife of the War of the Three Hammers erupted. Banished from Ironforge by the victorious Bronzebeards, Thane Khardros led his clan north to carve out the grand fortress of Grim Batol. After surviving a harrowing siege by the Dark Irons that left Grim Batol cursed and uninhabitable, the Wildhammers migrated further north into Lordaeron, eventually settling throughout the forested mountains of the Hinterlands.",al={"wildhammer history","wildhammer clan origins","origin of the wildhammer clan"},it="history",add="f21b0698"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you share kinship with the Wildhammers through old oaths. They favor windy crags and open skies over deep mines, and their stormhammer bravery commands deep respect.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance owes much of its strength in the skies to Wildhammer gryphon riders. Their lightning-infused mounts helped turn the tide against the Horde's red dragons during the Second War.",["class:Hunter"]="The bond Wildhammer mountaineers share with wild gryphons shows beast mastery built on lifelong partnership rather than simple dominion.",["class:Shaman"]="Wildhammer tradition channels raw storm energy through mystic hammers and keeps a bond with elemental lightning and nature, older than Ironforge's modern church traditions."},kw={"aerie peak","falstad","grim batol","gryphon","hinterlands","khardros","kurdran","stormhammer","wildhammer"},rel={"topic:dwarf","zone:hinterlands","topic:bronzebeard-clan","subzone:grim-batol","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war","subzone:valley-of-kings"},src={"Wildhammer clan"}}
E["topic:worgen"] = {t="topic",n="Worgen",z="general",s="Across Silverpine Forest, Ashenvale, and Duskwood, Worgen now hunt with bestial swiftness and a fury they cannot master. Once feared as nightmares from another realm, their beginnings remain uncertain.",h="Across Silverpine Forest, Ashenvale, and Duskwood, Worgen now hunt with bestial swiftness and a fury they...",sec={{t="Whispers and Folktales",b="Long before Worgen appeared in Lordaeron and Kalimdor, people told folktales and cautionary tales of wolf-men. Their beginnings remain a mystery. Scholars who have studied them believe they came to Azeroth from another realm. Archmage Arugal and the night elves' Scythe of Elune have both been shown to summon them.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Folly",b="During the Third War, the Scourge overran Lordaeron, and slain Kirin Tor wizards rose again as undead. Archmage Arugal sought a weapon to strengthen Dalaran's dwindling ranks. He used forbidden research by the Dalaran wizard Ur to pierce the veil and summon Worgen into Silverpine Forest. They savaged the undead invaders, but Arugal could not master their fury. The beasts turned on the wizards and spread their curse with fang and claw.\n\nMad with guilt and fascination, Arugal claimed the monsters as his children. He seized Baron Silverlaine's ancestral seat and renamed it Shadowfang Keep. There, he cursed nearby villagers into monstrous nocturnal servitude.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe Awoken",b="Across the sea in Kalimdor, the night elf Sentinel Velinde Starsong sought to purge Felwood of the Burning Legion's lingering demonic remnants. She unearthed the Scythe of Elune and used the ancient relic to summon Worgen against the demonic satyrs.\n\nAs the battles raged, Velinde realized the scythe had slipped beyond her command. Worgen began appearing without her consent, slipping into Ashenvale's dark forests and beyond. Wild packs now roam, spreading terror wherever their moonlit hunts reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are worgen?",a="Worgen are fierce, upright lupine humanoids with terrifying strength, predatory senses, and dark shadow magic. They dwell mainly in secluded woodlands and ruins, hunting in packs under the pull of an uncontrollable bestial fury.",al={"what is a worgen","worgen lore","wolf men"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the worgen originally come from?",a="No one knows for certain where Worgen came from. They seem to come from another realm: Archmage Arugal summoned them into Silverpine from beyond, and the night elves' Scythe of Elune drew them forth in Kalimdor.",al={"worgen origin","who made worgen","how were worgen created"},it="origin"},{q="How did worgen end up in Silverpine Forest?",a="During the Third War, Archmage Arugal summoned Worgen with research by the late Dalaran wizard Ur. He hoped they would strengthen the Kirin Tor against the Scourge, but the beasts turned on everyone.",al={"silverpine worgen","why are worgen in silverpine","who summoned worgen"},it="why_here"},{q="How does someone become a worgen?",a="Worgen spread a supernatural affliction. A bite or scratch from an active Worgen infects humanoids, and victims eventually succumb to feral urges and become wolf-beasts unless held back by potent discipline or specialized sorcery.",al={"worgen curse","can you turn into a worgen","worgen bite"}},{q="What is the Scythe of Elune?",a="The Scythe of Elune is a powerful night elf relic. It holds deep, volatile dominion over Worgen and can summon and agitate them.",al={"scythe of elune","scythe elune lore"}},{q="Who is Archmage Arugal?",a="Archmage Arugal was a Kirin Tor archmage of Dalaran. After summoning Worgen to fight the Scourge, he succumbed to madness and came to rule the haunted ruins of Shadowfang Keep with his monstrous children.",al={"arugal","who is arugal"}},{q="Why are worgen in Ashenvale and Kalimdor?",a="Worgen packs now prowl Ashenvale and Felwood, and the Sentinels of Darnassus still seek to learn how they came to Kalimdor. Their search follows the trail of the vanished Sentinel Velinde Starsong and the Scythe of Elune.",al={"ashenvale worgen","kalimdor worgen","terrowulf"}},{q="Why are worgen hostile to travelers?",a="Most worgen you encounter are consumed by feral, primal fury. The curse strips away reason and self-control, driving those afflicted into a frenzy where they view outsiders as prey or threats to be torn apart. Even those who follow the mad Archmage Arugal view mortals as enemies to be slaughtered or cursed into joining their packs.",al={"why do worgen attack","are worgen hostile","why are worgen aggressive"},it="hostile",add="d99a4888"},{q="Who leads the worgen?",a="The worgen do not answer to a single master, but gather in packs under powerful figures. In Silverpine Forest, many serve Archmage Arugal at Shadowfang Keep, who summoned them into the world. Independent packs run wild across Lordaeron, Duskwood, and Kalimdor, answering only to their alpha or primal instincts.",al={"worgen leader","who controls the worgen","worgen master"},it="leader",add="92f4d7ca"},{q="Who are the worgen allied with?",a="The worgen have no broad alliances. In Silverpine, certain packs answer to the renegade Archmage Arugal out of Shadowfang Keep. Otherwise, these feral beasts run rampant across the wilderness, attacking Scourge, Alliance, and Forsaken without distinction. They serve only their primal hunger and the leaders of their individual packs.",al={"worgen allies","who do worgen serve","worgen factions"},it="allies",add="52984533"},{q="Where did the worgen come from?",a="Their true origins are unknown. The beasts appear to come from another realm: Archmage Arugal summoned them into Silverpine from beyond during the Third War, and how packs came to prowl Kalimdor's forests is a mystery the night elves are still investigating.",al={"history of worgen","worgen backstory","how were worgen created"},it="history",add="b6544cd9"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Worgen show the danger of summoning savage power without the wisdom to control it. Their spread through Kalimdor's forests troubles the Cenarion Circle.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Worgen remain a troubling mystery. Sentinels now find the beasts prowling Ashenvale and Felwood.",["race:Undead"]="In Silverpine Forest, the Forsaken battle feral Worgen packs and Arugal's twisted cultists for control of the region south of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="Dalaran's Kirin Tor long debated the research in Ur's mystical treatises. Arugal's catastrophic summoning proved Ur's warnings that these nightmare creatures should never be called forth."},kw={"arugal","pyrewood","scythe of elune","shadowfang keep","silverpine","ur","velinde starsong","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","quest:1043","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","npc:baron-silverlaine"},src={"Worgen"}}
E["topic:world-of-warcraft-forever"] = {t="topic",n="World of Warcraft: Forever",z="general",s="World of Warcraft: Forever takes place in the year after the Third War. Thrall's Horde has settled Durotar, and a regent rules Stormwind for its boy-king. The Forsaken hold the Undercity. The world reaches from the Skyborne of Zephras Isle to the contested Riverglades and Shen'dralas, sacred Mount Hyjal and the city of Dalaran rising from its ruins in the Alterac Mountains.",h="World of Warcraft: Forever takes place in the year after the Third War.",sec={{t="The World After the Third War",b="The Burning Legion has been driven back at Mount Hyjal, yet the world bears the hurt it left behind. Thrall's Horde of orcs, trolls and tauren has made its home in Durotar and Mulgore. The Forsaken under Sylvanas Windrunner have joined the Horde from the ruins of Lordaeron.\n\nIn Stormwind, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon rules as regent for the boy-king Anduin Wrynn while King Varian is missing. The dwarves of Ironforge, the exiled gnomes and the night elves of Teldrassil stand with the Alliance. The Scourge still holds the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="The Skyborne",b="The Skyborne, or shen'dorei, descend from night elves who rebelled against Prince Tortheldrin of Eldre'Thalas. Wind spirits carried their island, Zephras Isle, into Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air, and the Skyborne escaped with it. Ages there made them high elves, and more are now born blue-skinned.\n\nThe spirits vanished centuries ago, and Zephras Isle is slowly breaking apart. The Skyborne look back toward Azeroth. Their airships reach the Alterac Mountains near Dalaran and Mulgore's Skywatcher Plateau. They fight for both the Alliance and the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Lands to Explore",b="Zephras Isle floats in Skywall as the Skyborne's homeland. East of the Burning Steppes, the Riverglades is an old Stormwind frontier lost in the First War. Loyalists at Farholde Keep hold out against the wilds, Horde outposts and the Twilight's Hammer at Sunnyglade.\n\nShen'dralas is a rugged borderland between Desolace, Feralas and Mulgore, contested by centaur, quilboar and outcasts. Mount Hyjal, sacred to the night elves, still bears the scars of Archimonde's defeat. In the Alterac Mountains, the Kirin Tor have lowered Dalaran's shield and are rebuilding their city. Off Kalimdor's coast, the Horde and the Alliance battle over the Darkspear Islands.",sp=0},{t="Dungeons and Raids",b="Danger waits beneath cities and in the world's far corners. There is the Hall of Thanes deep under Ironforge and the haunted Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity. An excavation site lies in the Wetlands, alongside the City of Dalaran itself.\n\nFarther afield are the Drowned City in Stranglethorn Vale, Krol'dok Stronghold in the Riverglades, Alcaz Prison in Dustwallow Marsh, Blackmaw Hold in Azshara and the Shaper's Terrace in Un'Goro Crater. On Mount Hyjal, the Barrow Deeps and Hyjal Summit test the mightiest war bands.",sp=0},{t="Who Walks Which Path",b="Warriors come from every race. Paladins are human, dwarf or Forsaken, while shaman are orc, tauren, troll, dwarf or Horde Skyborne. Priests are human, dwarf, gnome, night elf, troll or Forsaken. Mages are human, gnome, orc, troll, Forsaken or Alliance Skyborne.\n\nWarlocks are human, gnome, orc, troll or Forsaken. Hunters are human, dwarf, night elf, orc, tauren, troll or Skyborne. Rogues come from every race but the tauren. Druids are night elf, tauren or Skyborne.",sp=0}},faq={{q="When is World of Warcraft: Forever set?",a="World of Warcraft: Forever is set in the year after the Third War, once the Forsaken have claimed the Undercity. Thrall leads the Horde from Orgrimmar. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is regent of Stormwind for the boy-king Anduin, and the Scourge still holds the Plaguelands.",al={"when is wow forever set","wow forever timeline","what year is wow forever","when does forever take place"}},{q="What lands can I explore in WoW Forever?",a="You can explore Zephras Isle, the Skyborne's floating home in Skywall, and the old Stormwind frontier of the Riverglades. Shen'dralas lies between Desolace, Feralas and Mulgore, while Mount Hyjal is sacred to the night elves. Dalaran is rising again in the Alterac Mountains, and the Horde and Alliance fight over the Darkspear Islands.",al={"what's new in wow forever","what's new in forever","new zones in wow forever","wow forever zones","what is in wow forever"}},{q="Who are the Skyborne?",a="The Skyborne are high elves descended from night elves who fled Eldre'Thalas ages ago and lived on Zephras Isle in Skywall, the Elemental Plane of Air. With their island crumbling, they look back toward Azeroth and fight for both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"skyborne","shen'dorei","new race wow forever"}},{q="Where is Dalaran?",a="Dalaran stands on the shore of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. Archimonde shattered the city in the Third War. The Kirin Tor raised a shield over its ruins, and have now lowered it as they rebuild the city.",al={"dalaran wow forever","is dalaran rebuilt","dalaran alterac"}},{q="What dungeons and raids are there?",a="Among the dungeons are the Hall of Thanes under Ironforge, the Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity, an excavation site in the Wetlands and the City of Dalaran. Others include the Drowned City in Stranglethorn Vale, Krol'dok Stronghold in the Riverglades, Alcaz Prison in Dustwallow Marsh, Blackmaw Hold in Azshara and the Shaper's Terrace in Un'Goro Crater. The raids are the Barrow Deeps and Hyjal Summit on Mount Hyjal, and Onyxia's Lair in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"wow forever dungeons","wow forever raids","new dungeons in wow forever","new raids"}},{q="Which classes can each race be?",a="Humans can be warriors, paladins, hunters, rogues, priests, mages or warlocks. Dwarves can be warriors, paladins, hunters, rogues, priests or shaman. Night elves can be warriors, hunters, rogues, priests or druids. Gnomes can be warriors, rogues, priests, mages or warlocks.\n\nOrcs can be warriors, hunters, rogues, shaman, mages or warlocks. Forsaken can be warriors, paladins, rogues, priests, mages or warlocks. Tauren can be warriors, hunters, shaman or druids. Trolls can be warriors, hunters, rogues, priests, shaman, mages or warlocks.\n\nSkyborne can be warriors, hunters, rogues or druids. Alliance Skyborne can also be mages, and Horde Skyborne can also be shaman.",al={"race class combinations","what class can i be","can undead be paladins","undead paladin","dwarf shaman","gnome priest","human hunter","orc mage","troll warlock","skyborne classes"}}},ang={["race:Skyborne"]="Your people have only begun to return to Azeroth. Both the Alliance and the Horde have taken Skyborne into their ranks.",["race:Undead"]="Some Forsaken still wield the Holy Light as paladins, though it burns them. Tyr's Watch holds Bandarion Keep in western Tirisfal.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarves of Ironforge walk the shaman's path as well as the Light's. They call on stone and storm."},kw={"class combinations","dalaran","darkspear islands","mount hyjal","riverglades","shen'dralas","skyborne","world of warcraft forever","wow forever","zephras isle"},rel={"topic:skyborne","zone:zephras","zone:riverglades","zone:shendralas","zone:hyjal","subzone:dalaran","zone:darkspearislands","topic:third-war","zone:hallofthanes","zone:ruinsoflordaeron"},src={"World of Warcraft: Forever","Template:Forever class by race"},fv=true}
